INSERT INTO `listings` VALUES (1,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12899','Alberta Arts 2 bedroom suite, charming 1906 house','Please know that we are fully vaccinated, will practice social distancing and will be masked when we greet you.  Thanks!<br /><br />     Settle in to a space of your own. You\'ll have 2 bedrooms  as well as a seating area, a private bath with shower, and a galley kitchenette with microwave, toaster oven, induction cook top, Instant Pot and a fridge.  Access to the space (that is on the top floor of our home) is via a private, exterior staircase.','We\'re within walking distance of a grocery and drug store, and the Alberta Arts district, with galleries, pubs, restaurants, music and people watching. If you\'re a foodie, check out Beast, just a few blocks away, or some cheaper but equally tasty options like Authentica, Wilder or Dame. A few blocks further you have a wide variety of options on Alberta, including Salt and Straw. Catch a show at the Alberta Rose Theater or borrow our bikes and go further afield. We\'re happy to help you find what you\'re looking for in our beautiful city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/225005/cf00832d_original.jpg',49682,1,'45.56488','-122.63418',1,3,1.00,2.00,2.00,80.00,3,730,616,4.93,12899),(2,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37676','Mt. Hood View in the Pearl District','This rare and relaxing 1,000 SF loft is located in the heart of the Pearl District, Portland\'s premier location for siteseeing, dining, shopping and exploring.  Pristine accommodations with high ceilings, wood floors, giant flat screen TV, wall of windows, lots of art, and fully-equipped kitchen.  Enjoy access to the 5th floor deck!','The Pearl district enjoys a walkability score of 99!  Nationally acclaimed restaurants within three minutes walking include Andina and Voodoo Donuts. Not hungry? Walk 50yds to Powell\'s Books - the world\'s largest independent bookstore. Or venture a bit further to Forest Park - the nation\'s largest urban park or the NW 23rd Shopping District full of independent retailers.  Or catch a Timbers game!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/212298/16fb6b9f_original.jpg',162158,2,'45.52676','-122.68123',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,125.00,30,730,132,4.89,37676),(3,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/61893','Perfect Portland Place','Amazing for a long stay in<br />Portland\'s perfect location!<br /><br />City — Hike —Work — Cook — AC <br /><br />40% Monthly discount included, <br />30 night min. <br /><br />Studio with wall-bed <br />- Feels like a one-bedroom <br />- Walk around the city<br />- Hike in Washington Park<br />- Fast + reliable WiFi <br />- USB charging ports<br />- Apple AirPlay 2 + Chromecast RokuTV <br />- Luxurious bed + linens <br />- Cooks kitchen<br />- Warm cozy lighting<br />- Alexa enabled music<br />- FREE & easy laundry<br />- FREE on-street parking with city permit (fees may apply)','Restaurants, bars, shops, and culture of <br />NW Portland, Alphabet District, Pearl, Downtown are steps away. Washington Park foot trails are next door to the building. Walk out of the building and turn left to go hiking or turn right for city fun. <br /><br />Portland places<br />- Washington Park - next door<br />- Ken’s Artisan Bakery - 8 min walk <br />- Salt and Straw Ice Cream - 9 min walk <br />- Powell’s Books - 7 min bus or 15 min walk<br />- VooDoo Donuts - 10 min bus or 21 min walk <br /><br />Grocery stores<br />- Zupan\'s Market - front of the building<br />- Trader Joe\'s - 8 min walk <br />- Fred Meyer - 8 min walk <br />- New Seasons - 6 min bus or 18 min walk','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/993af180-c56e-4c75-9242-b77972fa8e7a.jpg',300391,3,'45.52258','-122.69955',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,118.00,30,300,25,5.00,61893),(4,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/67036','Historic Home Located in Central City','Welcome to Multnomah House, a classic Portland guest home located in the central city. Built in 1904 this home maintains all historic charm but with the amenities of a modern home. Perfect for visitors who want the convenience and close proximity to all Portland has to offer with the quaintness of one of Portland’s oldest historic neighborhoods. <br /><br />Multnomah House is located in near the Oregon Convention Center, the MAX Lloyd Station and shopping and entertainment along NE Broadway.','Sullivan\'s Gulch is a central east side neighborhood that has shops, restaurants and bars all in walking distance. It\'s also central so getting to other neighborhoods and attractions is a snap.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-67036/original/363bd104-1a1e-4ebc-8f30-166d8f5511d2.jpeg',329777,4,'45.53103','-122.64448',1,10,2.00,4.00,5.00,425.00,3,365,71,4.96,67036),(5,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/77522','Spacious Suite in Eastmoreland/SE. Hot Tub Dogs OK','Our private spacious suite is in a beautiful residential area near Reed College. Relax in our hot tub on our covered back deck. Sleep in a comfy queen bed with an organic mattress on our lower level, have your own bathroom, shower,  full kitchen,  cable tv, laundry, office. Enjoy a complimentary bottle of wine, fruit basket. sparkling water. A 15-minute drive to downtown. Near restaurants, coffee shops, grocery stores. a golf course hiking trails. Dogs welcome. No cats. Long term guests welcome.','Our neighborhood is very quiet and subdued with beautiful Tudor and other English style homes. Eastmoreland is a quiet neighborhood with little traffic.  We\'re walking distance to Reed College, the Eastmoreland Golf Course and Crystal Springs Rhododendron Gardens. There are designated bike lanes nearby. This is a very friendly and safe neighborhood and a great place to jog or ride a bicycle.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-77522/original/a9282eab-8cdf-4bb4-b7a2-dc3af8aebbc2.jpeg',345461,5,'45.47086','-122.63273',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,95.00,2,365,136,4.84,77522),(6,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/93613','Sunny Queen Room FUN Alberta Arts','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2f8fe630-fb9b-45c4-b63a-2ffe6d3b422c.jpg',501715,6,'45.55536','-122.65106',2,2,4.00,1.00,1.00,40.00,30,180,67,4.51,93613),(7,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/99355','Beautiful Apt near City Center!','A beautiful 1908 Craftsman home in a historic neighborhood, safe and walkable.  Beautiful historic homes, gorgeous tree lined boulevards, wonderful people, and extremely close to many wonderful restaurants and shopping.  There are wonderful neighborhoods surrounding Historic Irvington, but she is the Grand Dame of them all!<br /><br />Irvington neighborhood is on the National Register of Historic Places, and it\'s very central to everything in Portland.','Irvington is the best neighborhood in PDX. Its on the national register of historic places. Beautiful houses and gardens abound. Wonderful eateries surround Irvington, easy access to anything you want!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/79983a33-e01c-4660-87df-385f0b09b0cc.jpg',523311,7,'45.53836','-122.65159',1,6,1.50,3.00,3.00,189.00,1,730,314,4.93,99355),(8,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/114086','Bright Friendly Home- Alberta Arts','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7ba28173-ffa4-4db8-9fd3-28cc9090407d.jpg',501715,6,'45.55593','-122.65029',2,1,4.00,1.00,1.00,32.00,30,180,71,4.41,114086),(9,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/117969','Beautiful Remodeled Apartment','Our carefully-remodeled downstairs apartment has a gorgeous bathroom & kitchenette, big windows and a separate entrance that opens onto a shady side yard and sunny patio.   It\'s on a quiet, leafy street a short walk from lots of great restaurants.','Our neighborhood is quiet, friendly and full of kids.  We have an oversized lot and an outdoor play house, and we\'re a block from Sewallcrest Park, which has a big play structure, a basketball court and playing fields.<br /><br />Our house is 2-3 blocks from SE Hawthorne Boulevard, with restaurants including Farmouse (Thai) Tarboush (Lebanese), Cafe Castagna, Bread & Ink, Hot Lips Pizza, Two Doors Down, Porque No? (Mexican), Lardo (Pork!), Apizza Scholls,  Cha Cha Cha (Mexican), Grand Central Baking, Jam on Hawthorne, Blue Star Donuts, The Waffle Window, Little Big Burger and (about a mile toward downtown...) Burgerville, which is a pretty solid local fast food chain.<br /><br />And there\'s more...<br /><br />A 10-minute walk south (the opposite direction from Hawthorne) and you\'ll find SE Division Street, with Pok Pok (Thai), Ava Gene\'s, Cibo (Italian), Xico (Haute Mexican), Pizza Maria, St. Honore Bakery, Sunshine Tavern, The American Local, the Richmond Bar, SE Wine Collective, Boll','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/952cdcb3-ea8f-4b73-87e5-05d81184aae8.jpg',589016,8,'45.51061','-122.63257',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,2,31,350,4.84,117969),(10,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/134282','Daylight Foodie\'s Paradise & Everyone\'s Fun Zone','Portland\'s Mississippi District. With eats treats and beats right around the corner, you\'ll have endless fun in our private tastefully finished basement daylight duplex!  We have another listing upstairs.  Walkscore says 92, Walkers\' & Bikers\' Paradise. Great public transit and freeway 2 minutes away!  <br /><br />BOOKING TIP:  Verify that with your 31+days booking, you have no govt short stay tax.','With eats treats & beats around this corner, this ever popular destination location, Mississippi Historic District.  This duplex is in a friendly residential neighborhood. <br />NEIGHBORHOOD:  Our nearby neighbors are in their owner-occupied homes.  Use typical urban precautions at night, like stay in well-lit area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-134282/original/fd85145e-80e4-495c-a97c-09567a808959.jpeg',659137,9,'45.55273','-122.67524',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,78.00,31,365,35,4.39,134282),(11,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/143483','Garden Hideaway near City Center!','A beautiful 1908 Craftsman home in a historic neighborhood, safe and walkable. Beautiful historic homes, gorgeous tree lined boulevards, wonderful people, and extremely close to many wonderful restaurants and shopping. There are wonderful neighborhoods surrounding Historic Irvington, but she is the Grand Dame of them all!<br /><br />Irvington neighborhood is on the National Register of Historic Places, and it\'s very central to everything in Portland.','Irvington is on the national register of historic places. Its a wonderful neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a930307f-67f4-497c-8b54-82be83644ea3.jpg',523311,7,'45.54005222601903','-122.64988089596142',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,1,730,185,4.84,143483),(12,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/145199','Two private bedrooms with bath and kitchenette','Guests have exclusive use of upstairs floor, including two bedrooms with bathroom and kitchenette (refrigerator, freezer, toaster and microwave).  This area is private and not shared with owner.  It also includes cable television, air conditioning, air purifier, towels and sheets.  Guests are welcome to use main floor kitchen for more extensive cooking, landscaped backyard, patio with gazebo, charcoal grill and fire pit.','Very quiet, within walking distance to groceries, buses, restaurants, bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/17d852dc-da6a-4978-b37a-c63185975475.jpg',683139,10,'45.53034','-122.59138',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,85.00,3,180,86,4.75,145199),(13,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/182450','Luminous, Cosy Home near lively SE Division Street','Quiet, comfortable, fully furnished house 2 blocks from Division Street and the heart of SE Portland -- great restaurants, bus, and shopping. Two bedrooms garden and deck, remodeled kitchen.   Great place to relax while being close to a lively area. Wifi. Breakfast is not included. I have two friendly young indoor cats that you would be caring for. I welcome all races and nationalities, LGBT friendly. All guests required to be fully vaccinated and boosted. City of Portland permit no 14-212846','My neighborhood is between two lively streets - Hawthorne and Division, but still is quiet and lovely with plenty of on street parking. Very safe to walk night and day with nearby park and playgrounds','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/47e6f68a-7197-4a2f-9be1-ba16b92f8244.jpg',52505,8,'45.50529','-122.63201',1,4,1.50,2.00,2.00,90.00,5,29,33,4.88,182450),(14,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/182465','Quiet room next to lively Division St','Quiet, comfortable home with garden.   I live near one of the food hot spots of Portland. Private room with queen bed with possible trundle. Free wifi. Continental breakfast provided.  Street parking and access to bus. I have two young cats who are kept out of the guest bedroom. City permit 14-212846. I welcome all races and nationalities, LGBT friendly.<br />Note: I no longer serve a full breakfast.','My neighborhood is green and quiet, but lively. Division Street, two blocks away, is sizzling with excellent restaurants, bakeries, bars and coffee shops. Hawthorne Street, 7 blocks away has shops, a movie theater, vintage stores and restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-182465/original/d3da9fc1-9a2c-4ab1-9c80-fc6dbc9531c2.jpg',52505,8,'45.50582','-122.63389',2,2,1.50,1.00,2.00,68.00,2,5,346,4.95,182465),(15,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/195632','Foodie\'s Paradise & Everyone\'s Playground!','Welcome to your vibrant yet cozy haven in Portland\'s lively neighborhood! Just a 3-minute walk away, enjoy dining, unique shops, and cozy cafes.<br /><br />Our duplex offers comfort and convenience on both levels. Explore Portland\'s bike-friendly atmosphere on Bike Greenway. With a walk score of 91, exploring is fun & easy.<br /><br />New Seasons Health & wellness grocery store is an 8-minute walk, with wholesome options. Experience the perfect blend of comfort & convenience at our duplex haven.','With eats treats and beats right around the corner, you have a full array of restaurants, bars, shopping and healthy groceries within 10 minute walk.   This is a walker and bikers paradise with a 91 walkscore.<br /><br />N.Michigan Av at N. Shaver, 1 block west of N.Mississippi Ave is part of Portland\'s Bike Green-way Program. This is a walker and biker paradise! <br />A super healthy grocery store “New Seasons”.  Mind boggling food choices,  housewares, etc . It\'s a leisure 15 min walk from here. <br />Walk, jump on a bike, bus, light-rail or car!  <br />1.1 miles to Emanuel Hospital<br />1.4 miles to Adidas Headquarters<br />2.3 miles to the center of downtown<br />2.4 miles to Portland\'s Convention Center<br />8.5 miles to the airport.<br />40 miles/50 minutes to Multnomah Falls in the Columbia Gorge<br />Our walkscore rating is a hefty 94.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2215614/04804706_original.jpg',659137,9,'45.55083','-122.67567',1,3,1.00,1.00,3.00,86.00,4,1125,89,4.69,195632),(16,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/199683','Authentic Portland Flavor, Central!','*Private queen-sized-bedroom in a lovely, soulful, snazzy old NE Portland craftsman home and central neighborhood!  <br />Happy & peaceful feeling place <br />Near parks, golf course, restaurants, pubs, music venue, public trans., food markets & airport!','~The Neighborhood elaboration:<br />The Rose City Park neighborhood is a sweet one, adjacent or near to the Beaumont-Wilshire/Fremont Street, Alameda, Hollywood, Alberta Arts and Cully areas. <br />A clear day stroll a few blocks southeast of this porch brings you to the ridge of city owned Rose City Golf Course and a beautiful view of Mount Hood!<br /><br />Very comfortable, safe, tasty (walking distance food, pubs, jazz, all convenient! Great neighbors, vibe) neighborhood close enough to all \"quadrants\" of our fair Rose City to be a handy central point for sampling the nuances of all Portland\'s flavorful pockets.<br /><br />Easy Public transportation (tri-met bus) access just a half block away. Hollywood Max station a ten-minute stroll (unless you stop to sample beer from the brew pub en route i.e. BTU, Laurelwood Public House, Moon and Sixpence Pub, Gustav\'s or any of the dozens of restaurants, shops and markets along the way... NE Sandy Blvd, NE Fremont Avenue and NE Alberta Street','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4918344/c32173f2_original.jpg',975606,11,'45.54458','-122.60223',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,40.00,31,730,50,4.94,199683),(17,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/218708','Vintage Charm *King* at Opal 28 Apt 3','1 of 4 Opal 28 Apts, originally built in 1908, our building is boasting with vintage charm. This spacious one bedroom apartment includes the amenities of home.  Located on NE 28th Avenue, one of NE Portlands best neighborhoods. Bustling with food, drinks and shopping right out the door!  A short walk to Laurelhurst Park and a very central location to all of the regions best places to visit via car, foot or bus. There is ample street parking that is not metered nor monitored.','We are located in Laurelhurst / Kerns,  prime and very central Portland neighborhood for taking in the pride of the Pacific Northwest. With in walking distance are great restaurants, shops, parks and Portland culture. <br /><br />Here are a handful of our faves with in walking distance....<br /><br />Migration Brewery - great beer and if the patio is open you can watch the world of Burnside go by! <br />Dove Vive - best pizza in town<br />Guero - best torta in town<br />Basilisk - best fried chicken <br />Cheese & Crack Shop - cheese & charcuterie plus soft serve! UNIQUE FIND*<br />PaaDee- Authentic Thai<br />Montelupo Italian Market  - new on the scene! <br /><br />UNIQUE PDX<br />28th & Sandy is the Zipper - multiple micro restaurants to choose from<br />24th & Glisan is the Ocean - multiple micro restaurants to choose from<br /><br />GROCERY<br />Whole Foods - NE 28th and Burnside (out the apt door to the left) <br />Providore - NE 24th and Sandy, fancy food store <br />Fred Meyer* ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjE4NzA4/original/e081da56-4b2e-4ea5-afff-e879d355b879.jpeg',6313800,12,'45.5236','-122.63458',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,58.00,30,365,274,4.81,218708),(18,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/222298','Blues, Brews & Bicycle Guesthouse','','This guesthouse is on a cliff overlooking Swan Island- very close to the Adidas World Village.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2132446/caf75dca_original.jpg',1153902,13,'45.55815','-122.69218',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,2,14,117,4.85,222298),(19,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/231732','large, sunny room in farmhouse','','This is a walkable and bike friendly neighborhood and the guesthouse is a 3 minute walk from the Adidas campus. There are pubs and eateries close by, and it takes about 24 min to get downtown by bike or public transportation.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7274529/fe4f9e3e_original.jpg',1153902,13,'45.55629','-122.69042',2,1,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,48,4.96,231732),(20,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/231734','Private, sunny room in farmhouse','This is a hundred year old, light- filled farmhouse on a half-acre; with rain gardens, fruit trees , berries and bees. It’s a peaceful, green oasis ; be sure to try hanging out in one of the hammocks !','This guesthouse is close to the Adidas campus, overlooks Swan Island, and is a 20 min walk from the river.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2132831/32cdabe5_original.jpg',1153902,13,'45.55748','-122.69207',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,2,14,60,4.98,231734),(21,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/236108','Large COMFY Room in Alberta Arts','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-236108/original/cd1777a0-70e5-4b40-879f-00ff64ed0e37.jpeg',501715,6,'45.55645','-122.64854',2,2,3.00,1.00,1.00,49.00,30,180,59,4.54,236108),(22,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/269339','Sweet Apartment in Alberta St. Area','We\'d love to have you as a guest in our renovated above ground basement studio apartment in our updated 1910 home in NE Portland. The home is located a short walk away from Alberta St., Williams St. and Mississippi St. and across from Two Plum Park.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2707833/6fce059c_original.jpg',960864,14,'45.55033','-122.65798',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,29,375,4.72,269339),(23,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/317797','Condo in the Courtyard','No Lodging Taxes if you book for thirty-one (31) nights!<br /><br />Located on SE Hawthorne Blvd in beautiful Mt. Tabor. Each home is vintage mid-century. With wood floors, tiled kitchens and bathrooms. The location is fabulous. Restaurants, shopping and parks are close by.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b588205a-936b-4f03-9735-62a7e453c46d.jpg',828435,15,'45.510918377814114','-122.61128317425442',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,48.00,30,150,42,4.79,317797),(24,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/332420','Vintage Artist\'s Home, walk/bike everywhere!','Enjoy SE Portland\'s best walkable neighborhood, Sunnyside. You\'re 3 blocks Belmont Street\'s local restaurants, small bars, coffee shops,  and H-Mart Grocery. Laurelhurst Park (designed in the Olmsted style in 1912) is 4 blocks away. Our 1908 house has a spacious floor plan, wood floors and updated kitchen. We have a great covered patio living room with several seating areas in the garden. We\'re on a quiet street with a fenced-in yard. Once you get here you won\'t want to leave the property!','You will be 3 blocks from the Belmont District, which has shops and great restaurants. A 10 minute walk will get you to Hawthorne Boulevard, Portland\'s original shopping street with lots of small shops and food options.<br /><br />We\'re also 4 blocks from Laurelhurst Park, a large historic park with a pond and play areas including tennis and basketball courts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-332420/original/bf0f9a3a-8506-4eb9-a0c6-07464d68b159.jpeg',1206902,16,'45.51832','-122.6318',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,30,61,4.98,332420),(25,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/345650','GUEST SUITE SURROUNDED BY NATURE','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5826920/9a024f50_original.jpg',38860,17,'45.48203','-122.71903',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,335.00,2,60,139,4.87,345650),(26,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/357732','Cheerful, musical, eclectic home','Airy, bright, furnished bedroom, on the main floor, with queen bed, and bathroom next door (partially shared).<br />For all stays, long or short, I hope you will feel that this is your temporary \"home away from home\".<br />PLEASE MAKE INQUIRY BEFORE ASKING FOR RESERVATION. I like to know a little about my guests who are asking to live in my house for a month or more, and often it is difficult to complete a dialog within the time period of 24hrs that Airbnb gives me to accept or decline a reservation.','This location is in a quiet neighborhood close to a large park, and only a 5 min walk to local coffee shops, restaurants, and funky stores, in what is called Multnomah Village.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4149108/c49b2242_original.jpg',1810476,18,'45.46623','-122.71432',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,40.00,30,240,35,4.35,357732),(27,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/362775','Kuza Cabin + Fine-Dining Village','1 Bedroom Sleeping Nook<br />1 Bathroom (separated from the bedroom nook by a curtain, no door)<br />350 sqft<br />WiFi and Roku TV<br />Full Kitchen<br /><br />Located in the heart of the Alberta Arts District:<br /><br />#72 bus stop right at your doorstep<br />Just steps away from Gabbiano\'s Patio Lobby Bistro<br />Walking distance to Gabbiano\'s, Dame, Lil Dame + Pop-Ups, Expatriate, Take Two, Wilder, Jet Black Coffee, and New Seasons Market','Within 2 blocks is a plethora of restaurants, cafes, bars, and other venues, with recommendations including Gabbiono\'s Italian Kitchen, immediately downstairs, as well as , Dame, Lil  Dame + Pop-Up\'s , Expatriate, Toy Shop Ramen, Wilder,  and Flour Market to name a few . Visit  Peoples Yoga and galleries in the Alberta Art District not to mention some of the best coffee in town. Try Jet Black Coffee just up the block on 30th','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/049218b0-0836-4792-aa9f-b7eb6575ffa9.jpg',1213257,19,'45.54903','-122.63423