he most popular areas of SE portland, Hawthorne st and Division st. There are cafe\'s and restaurants galore. This is such a wonderful part of town and extremely walking and bike friendly. There are three bus lines within walking distance but the cottage is in such  perfect place as to never hear any buses or much traffic. You will hear and see many birds however!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4731175/a773b192_original.jpg',2034859,8,'45.50964','-122.61787',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,78.00,2,1125,134,4.95,408577),(33,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/413956','Beautiful, Clean 1920 NoPo Bungalow','Hello travelers,<br /><br />I have a comfortable and spacious three bedroom house available for short term stays. I\'m very near the lovely Peninsula Park, a nice upscale grocery store, Max train (for quick trips downtown, or to PDX), and not far from several neighborhood business districts (Mississippi, Williams, and Alberta). Fiber optic wifi, a well equipped kitchen, designated driveway parking, and a selection of breakfast foods are included.','The house has a convenient location on Ainsworth street between I-5 and Interstate avenue in North Portland. Outside of rush hour it takes only about 6 or 7 minutes to drive downtown. There is an upscale grocery store called New Seasons market and a stop for the yellow line Max train just 3 blocks away. New Seasons is like a smaller and more locally-focused version of Whole Foods, with an excellent bakery, high quality butcher and seafoods, and a nice hot / cold deli. <br /><br />A few blocks east is the gorgeous and historic Peninsula Park. Also not far away are bustling Mississippi, Williams, and Alberta streets, the Killingsworth food cart pod, and P.C.C.\'s Cascade campus. Within a mile or two are the University of Portland, Adidas North America headquarters, and Legacy Emmanuel Hospital.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-413956/original/47df9fd7-282f-469c-aa03-1a0d301c940f.jpeg',1099616,13,'45.56557','-122.67893',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,115.00,3,9,161,4.70,413956),(34,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/448195','The Wisteria… Portland Craftsman','• Great location! Close in NE PDX!  Hollywood/Rose City Park  <br />• Suited for families up to 8. <br />• 4 bedrooms, two baths, five comfortable beds. <br />• Gourmet chefs kitchen, high end appliances, nook, table and tv. <br />• Off street parking <br />• FAST 210+Mbps Fiber WiFi <br />• Central A/C<br />• Spacious living room / dining room<br />• Gas fireplace<br />• Shoes off house. Bring your slippers!<br />• No pet policy, allergy free environment.<br />• Fragrance free laundry detergent ￼is used.','Walking distance to many great restaurants, pubs, coffee shops, bake shop, and food carts!<br />• Case Study Coffee,  all 2 blocks - -<br />• Cabezon Seafood Bistro- 52nd & Sandy<br />• Vincenzo\'s Pizza<br />• Rose City Park FOOD CARTS! 53rd/Sandy...<br />• Bakeshop‎- Bakery<br />• Bubble tea shop<br />• Du\'s Grill-  Bento!<br />• Zien Hong- Chinese<br />• The Human Bean-Coffee Shop Drive-thru  48th/Sandy <br />• Clyde\'s Prime Rib and jazz night club- 54th/Sandy<br />• Cha Ba Thai, Pizzaria Otto at 67th<br />• Safeway<br />• New Deal Cafe - Breakfast cafe- 53rd / Halsey St.<br />• Killer Burger- Burgers- 47th / Sandy Blvd.<br />• Whole Foods Market- 43rd / Sandy Blvd. <br />• Trader Joe\'s- 41st/NE Halsey <br />• Petite Provence 3420 NE Sandy <br />• Fleur De Lis Bakery & Cafe- 40th & Hancock<br />• The local Hollywood \"Saturday Market\"- fresh local produce all year! 42nd / Hancock (located in the Grocery Outlet parking lot)<br />• Ambassador restaurant and lounge (karaoke!)<br />• Kill','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cd3efb5b-18da-45a1-812d-61c1d2cd8999.jpg',2226037,11,'45.546532','-122.612953',1,8,2.00,4.00,5.00,264.00,3,30,283,4.90,448195),(35,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/449461','Portland Soul, Central! Porch Time!','*Beautiful Bright Room in a snazzy old Portland craftsman, and neighborhood!.. Near parks, golf course, restaurants, pubs, music venue, public transportation, food markets...<br />Queen Bed, Peaceful. Friendly travelers and transplants Warmly welcome!','My favorite \'hood in Portland:<br />Cultural cuisine galore, super handy central locale to access the bohemian SE, Mt. Tabor, etc. as well as the nearby Alberta Arts \'hood. Funky, safe, fun!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/25023858/3830a52c_original.jpg',975606,11,'45.54244','-122.60331',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,40.00,31,999,42,4.85,449461),(36,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/450488','Alberta Arts Room Overlooking Lush Backyard!','Well-appointed room in the heart of the vibrant Alberta Arts district. Enjoy a well-equipped, small kitchenette, and clear-covered, second story deck covered with grapevines in the rafters!','The house is located in the heart of the vibrant and eclectic Alberta district. Starting 3 blocks away, there are great restaurants including Hat Yai, Pok Pok, Teote, Petite Provance, Podnah\'s Pit (former restaurant of the year), coffee houses (like Random Order named one of America\'s Best Pie Spots by Food&Wine), brew pubs, shopping and entertainment all within a 5-20 minute walk of the house.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0db8d4b8-ef6d-41ef-9b45-9581fbbde332.jpg',2236909,14,'45.56141','-122.65806',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,54.00,31,120,109,4.86,450488),(37,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/450660','Cozy Alberta Arts Room - TV, A/C, Wifi, Desk','A cozy bedroom with all the essentials and a bit of charm, located in the vibrant and eclectic Alberta Arts neighborhood.','The house is located in the heart of the vibrant Alberta Arts district. Starting 3 blocks away, there are great restaurants (including Podnah\'s Pit, 2011 restaurant of the year), coffee houses (like Random Order named one of America\'s Best Pie Spots by Food&Wine), brew pubs, shopping and entertainment.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b955c95d-6ce4-4e5f-9966-097678d3a508.jpg',2236909,14,'45.56186','-122.65834',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,54.00,31,120,104,4.83,450660),(38,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/483614','House w/ Wood Burning Stove and A/C - NE Portland','Enjoy this cozy one bedroom loft with a wood burning stove, full kitchen, washer/dryer, private patio, and more. Walkable to the Alberta Arts District, Beaumont Village, bakeries, coffee shops, local eateries and just a 15 min drive to down town Portland.','In addition to all of the great shops and restaurants, we have wonderful parks nearby. Kʰunamokwst (pronounced KAHN-ah-mockst)  is a Chinook wawa name meaning \"together\". Kʰunamokwst Park is the first PP&R park to enjoy a name indigenous to the land it sits on. Chinook wawa is the language commonly used by the original people of this area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/acebbc62-667d-4d97-906e-553a9c7f43ad.jpg',1387456,21,'45.55794','-122.61679',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,125.00,30,150,214,4.89,483614),(39,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/522334','A sunny separate studio w/skylights','Your own modern large studio on 2nd floor with separate entrance, full kitchen, sunroom, skylights, 14-foot ceiling, balcony, desk, full bathroom, washer/dryer, dishwasher, gas stove, lots of windows. All this in a vibrant neighborhood, short walking distance to multiple coffee shops, restaurants, a single-screen movie theater, the light rail station, an open-late grocery store, a small park with a salmon run. One mile to Reed College, where Steve Jobs took a calligraphy class.','The Westmoreland/Sellwood neighborhood was listed as the second hottest city neighborhood in the West by Sunset magazine about ten years ago. Very walkable, friendly part of town with some great parks, bars and restaurants and easy access to the Orange Max line. Not sure why but there are three coffee shops within a stone\'s throw of each other. Farmer\'s market on Saturdays (late Spring to early Fall). Great residential neighborhood. Five-minute drive to New Seasons (two of them) or Trader Joe\'s. Grocery store is four short blocks away. Take a walk along the nearby bluff to view the west hills, Oaks Bottom wetlands, a 100-year old amusement park (open during summer and weekends in Spring/Fall) and catch a glimpse of downtown skyline.<br /><br />Please note that Portland charges a hospitality tax and city tax on all licensed Airbnbs. Hosts do not get this money. Airbnb collects it and forwards it to the appropriate agencies.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7188923/49e393a6_original.jpg',19234,20,'45.47518','-122.64512',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,3,29,530,4.97,522334),(40,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/525395','Gorgeous Bungalow with Hot Tub close to Downtown','I really want you to enjoy yourself here:)This is a gorgeous house with a lot of separate outdoor and indoor spaces to gather together in. It was extensively updated in May 2021,  It\'s within minutes of downtown. Gourmet kitchen, hot tub, 70 inch TV Room, Sonos System TV upstairs, 1 gb fiber internet, Tesla charger, surround sound theater downstairs,  and plenty of room to spread out.  Located within steps to a gourmet grocery store, restaurants, block from the River and Willamette park.','Great walking neighborhood with great restaurants, a gourmet grocery store, microbreweries all a short walk away.  There is a bike path which takes you on a separate path along the river right downtown.  There are awesome Mountain bike trails one mile away.  Willamette park which has a boat ramp tennis courts etcetera is a block away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7dfed189-c367-46e5-aff9-6cb3527994a2.jpg',2555917,22,'45.47187','-122.67422',1,5,3.00,2.00,3.00,207.00,3,90,78,4.59,525395),(41,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/531553','Garden Oasis in Walkable Mississippi District','Our garden apartment is an urban oasis that is located smack-dab between the popular and historic Mississippi and Williams Avenues - mere blocks away from Portland\'s BEST restaurants, food carts, bars and music venues.','The coolest neighborhood in Portland.  Williams and Mississippi Aves. are chocked full of award winning restaurants and indie shops & boutiques.  <br />It has the quintessential Portlandia vibe that Portland is known for and loved.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ce780586-c348-4c51-9521-a849a68da7a8.jpg',1601890,9,'45.55232','-122.67048',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,2,30,394,4.91,531553),(42,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/543988','Quaint English Cottage Garden Private Apt.','A quaint downstairs apartment in a beautiful  historic home with a lovely English garden  in the heart of one of the most sought after neighborhoods in Portland.  This comfortable, charming  one bedroom apt. is tastefully decorated mid-century.  Beautiful   Laurelhurst Park and public transportation are minutes away with shops and  dining all within walking distance - 10 minutes to downtown and 15-20 minutes to the airport - an ideal guest cottage in an ideal location!!','Laurelhurst is an historic old Portland neighborhood with beautiful homes, street trees and a huge park a few blocks away designed by the Olmsted\'s who designed Central Park in NYC.  You will see how homes in Laurelhurst are each very different and unique from craftsmen with large porches to smaller  bungalows with beautiful gardens.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f0100ed1-6d2e-4ce8-9e4f-01dd3a8441f9.jpg',40759,23,'45.52417','-122.61865',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,105.00,2,30,346,4.92,543988),(43,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/546107','Hip, Tiny House in North Portland','The Tiny House is a clean and light place, in a perfect North Portland location. Super cozy, situated in between Alberta, Mississippi, and Williams nieghborhoods, and very close to downtown. Easy street parking and a beautiful, vibrant neighborhood. 31 day minimum stay. Pets with approval and deposit. Hot tub for rent certain hours via Swimply. Level 2 EV charging.','The Tiny House is located in a perfect neighborhood. It is within walking distance to great neighborhood streets (Mississippi Street, Alberta Arts District and Killingsworth Street) It is 10 min drive downtown and an easy ride to the river. <br /><br />1- 8 minute walk to Mississippi Ave, <br />2. 20 minute walk to the Arts district on Alberta St<br />3. 15 min walk to Williams Ave corridor. <br /><br />Mississippi, Alberta and Williams. These are the three vibrant neighborhood centers of North Portland, where you will find all the amazing authentic awesomeness that makes Portland, Portland. Friendly people, delicious restaurants, beer gardens, food carts, fun unique shopping, bikes everywhere, the best coffee and art galleries. <br /><br />Within the neighborhood, here are my suggestions for breakfast and lunch. I\'ve coded these on Mississippi (M), Alberta (A) or Williams (W). Or if it\'s (somewhere else) that\'s noted, the best restaurants for dinner are dotted all around the city. I\'l','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c6c9642a-a391-4a49-84d8-af1c68d350c9.jpg',307635,24,'45.55975','-122.67163',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,61.00,31,365,344,4.75,546107),(44,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/548557','NE  Concordia Cabin','New, clean, modern studio flat. Converted 25x20 garage with kitchenette and bathroom. Cool neighborhood walkable to coffee, beer, New Seasons, Kennedy School, Concordia University. 3 large skylights bathes the cabin in light all day.','Redfin rates Concordia \"hottest neighborhood\" in the USA (March 2014). Very trendy, upscale dining and shopping destination at NE 30th & Killingsworth is very hot and 5 blocks walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6978933/26d86c5a_original.jpg',2696498,1,'45.56973','-122.63153',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,109.00,2,90,139,4.79,548557),(45,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/557948','Pretty house, perfect location, EV-friendly','Our entire remodeled house in the quiet, historic Ladd\'s Addition neighborhood is available to Airbnb guests. Treelined streets invite a stroll from our front door to public parks, rose gardens and coffee shops. Our modernized cottage checks all the boxes: work-from-home, tourism hub and place to hunker down. Features: architect-designed dream kitchen, fast Internet, gas fireplace, available EV charging, off-street parking, mid-century furniture, home theater and bathroom jet tub.','Ladd\'s Addition is Portland\'s oldest planned residential development, and one of the oldest in the western United States. The neighborhood is known in Portland for a diagonal street pattern and public gardens. Ladd\'s is bordered by Hawthorne Blvd., Division St., 12th Ave. and 20th St. It\'s part of SE Portland\'s Hosford-Abernethy neighborhood association.<br /><br />A large traffic circle and enclosed park are at the center of Ladd\'s Addition. Streets are lined with American Elm trees. Each of the four smaller, diamond-shaped parks to the east, west, north, and south contains one of Portland\'s famous rose test gardens.<br /><br />The neighborhood was designated a historic district by the National Register of Historic Places in 1988.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-557948/original/94fe0bfe-3655-460a-bdf0-8bd7ce1b0133.jpeg',2690880,25,'45.51017','-122.64576',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,614.00,7,7,16,5.00,557948),(46,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/566103','Old Portland SE Clinton/Division','Handsome arts and crafts 3 bedroom, 2 full bathroom, fully furnished 1916 Old Portland home in the heart of Clinton neighborhood in inner SE Portland<br /> AC only available in 3rd floor attic. We welcome all guests, especially people of color, non-US citizens and other marginalized communities.<br /><br />For short-term stays, less than a month, we are restricted by city regulations to only rent out 2 bedrooms.','The Clinton/Division neighborhood is home to some of the best restaurants, bars and Cafes in Portland.  In spite of the recent gentrification, the old feel of gritty SE PDX is still visible at the Clinton St. movie theater, the oldest theater west of the Mississippi.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7275568/f46f4a28_original.jpg',1115782,25,'45.50601','-122.63986',1,5,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,31,54,4.89,566103),(47,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/580155','NE Portland Oregon Modern Victorian Duplex','1 bedroom, 1 bathroom, Ideal for 2, sleeps 3 max.  King size bed in bedroom and fold-out Queen size couch in living room.<br /><br />We adhere to the highest quality, professional cleanliness standards. The apartment is well cleaned and sanitized between guests. We provide additional cleaning supplies for guests to use while visiting. <br /><br />The apartment is completely private, with it\'s own front door entrance.<br /><br />ASTR permit #23-092838-000-00-HO','Eliot is one of the oldest neighborhoods in Portland. You\'ll see Victorian houses mixed with modern architecture. There is a mix of residential houses and commercial buildings.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7198010/b9d70053_original.jpg',2854451,26,'45.53814','-122.66166',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,105.00,2,365,96,4.95,580155),(48,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/584676','NW Portland Condo on Street Car Line','This well-kept and recently renovated condo is available in the heart of Portland\'s art community.<br /><br />This condo is professional cleaned after every tenants stay with Covid precautions in mind. If there are additional precautions that are needed/wanted - please feel free to reach out.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7275938/9924ddba_original.jpg',2881063,27,'45.52972','-122.69269',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,30,365,80,4.73,584676),(49,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/600976','SW 2 Bedroom/Private Bath - SUPER CLEAN','• Routinely disinfected door handles, counter, handrails<br />• Quiet, calm and safe neighborhood <br />• 7-10 min drive downtown, 15-20 min bus ride<br />• Super clean and comfortable<br />• Cleaned with natural products<br />• Easy street parking<br /><br />SW PORTLAND ADVENTURE:<br />• 2 local breweries a short walk/drive away<br />• Near local shops and eats<br />• Excellent Sunday Farmers Market<br />• 4 miles to downtown, 2 miles to SE<br />• 1.5 mile Walk to Lewis & Clark College & Tryon Creek State Park, quick bus ride to OHSU/Veterans Hospital','Burlingame is one of the few areas that has maintained its gracious charm and timeless elegance over the decades. A favorite among those wanting to remain close to downtown with the added benefit of lush greenery and neighborhood feel. Burlingame is adjacent to two main shopping areas - Hillsdale and Multnomah Village and has great places to dine, shop and drink nearby. Like most Southwest neighborhoods, this is a charming area with a mix of residential and business areas with a strong sense of local community.<br /><br />Nearby are Lewis & Clark College, OHSU, Veterans Hospital, PCC - and many places to shop and dine in between.<br /><br />Dine/Drink <br />Tryon Creek Bar<br />Chez Jose - awesome Mexican food<br />Baker & Spice<br />Starbucks<br />Verde Cocina<br />Sasquatch Brewery<br />McMenamins Brewery<br />Tastebud<br /><br />The area is filled with great grocery options which include nearby Fred Meyer, Food Front Co-Op, Elephants Deli, Zupans Market and Barbur World Foods. <br /','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-600976/original/55d00d0f-c2c6-463a-a168-b33e98814c24.jpeg',2974150,28,'45.46519','-122.68488',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,89.00,1,28,421,4.85,600976),(50,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/604270','Mt. Tabor studio with Mt. Hood view','This treehouse-like studio at the base of Mt. Tabor is a sunny detached structure in our backyard, walkable to Montavilla, and has an excellent view of Mt. Hood. The inside is well-decorated and inviting with one large room that sleeps up to four and has a full kitchen.','We are just a short walk east of Mount Tabor, a 190 acre public park and dormant volcano in southeast Portland - great for picnicers, birders, runners, kids, concert-goers... this park has it all. We are also within walking distance of the fabulous Montavilla neighborhood, which includes a movie theater, coffee shops, and multiple bakeries, boutiques, bars, and excellent restaurants.  Ask us for recommendations - we\'ve tried them all!   If coffee-drinking, beer-tasting, vintage-shopping, and people-watching are up your alley, a five-minute drive or short bike or bus ride gets you to the Hawthorne, Division, and Belmont neighborhoods. A 20-minute drive gets you to the Columbia Gorge, 60 minutes to wine tasting in the Willamette Valley, and 90 minutes to the beach!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/48156958/3410fccf_original.jpg',1493662,10,'45.51431','-122.58521',1,4,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,2,25,649,4.92,604270),(51,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/633385','Sweet Room in Charming Central SW Home SUPER CLEAN','• Routinely disinfecting<br />• Super clean and comfortable, cleaned with natural disinfecting products<br />•  Quiet, calm and safe neighborhood <br />• 7-10 min drive downtown, 15-20 min bus ride<br />• Easy street parking<br /><br />SW PORTLAND ADVENTURE:<br />• 2 local breweries a short walk/drive away<br />• Near local shops and eats<br />• Excellent Sunday Farmers Market<br />• 4 miles to downtown, 2 miles to SE<br />• 1.5 mile Walk to Lewis & Clark College & Tryon Creek State Park, quick bus ride to OHSU/Veterans Hospital','Burlingame is one of the few areas that has maintained its gracious charm and timeless elegance over the decades. A favorite among those wanting to remain close to downtown with the added benefit of lush greenery and neighborhood feel. Burlingame is adjacent to two main shopping areas - Hillsdale and Multnomah Village and has great places to dine, shop and drink nearby. Like most Southwest neighborhoods, this is a charming area with a mix of residential and business areas with a strong sense of local community.<br /><br />Nearby are Lewis & Clark College, OHSU, Veterans Hospital, PCC - and many places to shop and dine in between.<br /><br />Dine/Drink <br />Tryon Creek Bar<br />Chez Jose - awesome Mexican food<br />Baker & Spice<br />Starbucks<br />Verde Cocina<br />Sasquatch Brewery<br />McMenamins Brewery<br />Tastebud<br /><br />The area is filled with great grocery options which include nearby Fred Meyer, Food Front Co-Op, Elephants Deli, Zupans Market and Barbur World Foods. <br /','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5d0f3cb4-a520-490e-b45a-6ce211ab5669.jpg',2974150,28,'45.4705','-122.68506',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,53.00,2,28,237,4.83,633385),(52,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/637011','Eclectic, cheerful, musical home','Large, airy, upstairs bedroom with lots of storage, perfect for longer term stays.  Has shared bath with me (owner) but I mainly use downstairs bathroom.<br /><br />THE PRICE LISTED IS FOR ONE GUEST. FOR TWO GUESTS THE THERE IS AN ADDITIONAL $7/PER NIGHT CHARGE for long term guests. $15/night for occasional \'visitors\', payable to me.<br />I also list a smaller room, more ideal for shorter stays. This second listing is called\"Cheerful, musical, eclectic home\".','This location is in a quiet neighborhood close to a large park, but only 5 min walk to local coffee shops, restaurants, and funky stores, in what is called Multnomah Village. Easy bus access to downtown Portland, about 15 or 20min. Only a 10 min drive with car. On street parking.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8183930/3c3b6553_original.jpg',1810476,18,'45.46671','-122.71559',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,30,240,21,4.52,637011),(53,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/637362','Newly renovated Sellwood Sanctuary Guest House','Newly renovated Sellwood Sanctuary guesthouse complete with its own fully stocked bathroom, kitchen and queen sized bed with Dreamcloud Premier mattress that includes a luxurious foam topper.  Half a block from one of Portland\'s best parks and Springwater Bike Trail. Great shopping, coffee shops, bakeries, food carts and restaurants all within walking distance. New Seasons grocery store is a few blocks away.','We\'re biased, but we love our neighborhood! Sellwood/West Moreland is a well-established family neighborhood brimming with lots of great restaurants, coffee shops, food carts, parks, movie theatre and easy access to the Springwater Corridor. Downtown Portland is a 15-20 minute car ride or you can take the new MAX Orange light rail for nearly the same amount of time it takes to drive (ticket cost is $2.50 for two hours or $5.00 provides you with all day access, which includes bus, streetcar and riding OHSU\'s Aerial Tram).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3465e6ba-0303-4ac5-abcf-8695fb8363d1.jpg',869146,20,'45.46549','-122.65551',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,111.00,3,90,355,4.97,637362),(54,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/674866','Fantastic Loft in the Pearl (short or long term)','This furnished loft is in the heart of the Pearl District. Perfect for corporate housing, travelers, home buyers in transition, remodelers in need of temporary housing, vacations or business travel. It features 20 ft ceiling, 2 bedrooms/1.5 bath, 1,600 sq. ft., a gourmet kitchen with all the amenities, washer/dryer, a patio & amazing natural light.  2 story building in a no-elevator building. It also includes a private garage for one vehicle.  The unit also has a bonus loft great for being cozy!','The Pearl District is loaded with everything you will need and want to do - all within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c049b4a6-30be-4f56-a601-eb7d493e31ba.jpg',1731137,2,'45.52667','-122.68242',1,6,1.50,2.00,2.00,200.00,90,1125,61,4.72,674866),(55,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/687927','Heart on Hawthorne ,  SE Portland','Shared bathroom!! I have guests that want to be here at least a week.  I am open to changes as I have another Airbnb room, for anyone wanting to extend their stay, this is now possible, although not always (negotiable).  Twin bed in each room, so solo travelers only. No washer dryer. No curfew. May be 1-2 other guests.','It is rated a 9 or 10 in the walkability scale.  I can have a really fun day without being too far from home, and the car stays in the driveway.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-687927/original/f768572d-b4e7-456b-acb3-5d96b6365d0f.jpg',3425231,16,'45.51336','-122.62062',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,40.00,7,60,184,4.75,687927),(56,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/696955','Alberta Arts House - Hip Portlandia','','Where do you start in Alberta Arts?!! Food trucks, great restaurants, locally owned boutique shops, cool bars, awesome coffee, lush parks are a few blocks away with towering Douglas Fir Trees, the cool Kennedy School conversion is a walk or quick bike ride away and if you want access to downtown or The Pearl, it takes us about 15 minutes on our bikes or 5 minutes by car. Our neighbourhood is very chilled, young families and couples abound and everyone is super friendly and social. The location is amazing with all the cool shops, bars, restaurants and food carts just one block walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9721491/3814afbc_original.jpg',3569549,29,'45.55823','-122.64626',1,6,1.50,3.00,5.00,199.00,30,210,215,4.95,696955),(57,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/697115','Classic Bedroom/Private Vanity','Bedroom is located on a separate level within a larger home. Smaller Kitchen and outdoor deck is off of 3 bedrooms perched 28\' on a larger deck in a forrested 1/2 acre property. Nature abounds w deer, hawks, eagles, bunnies, deer & squirrels.','Within 1/3-mi. of restaurants, bakery, starbucks, pizza, dry cleaners, nail salon<br />Near walking Trails <br />Near Council Crest Park<br />Near OHSU<br /><br />A 5-minute drive into downtown SW Portland<br />A 7-minute drive to NW 23rd and NW Pearl District','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-697115/original/b0036762-636e-4890-8668-5d16dc51df08.jpeg',3190134,30,'45.48684','-122.68875',2,1,1.50,1.00,1.00,56.00,30,120,3,5.00,697115),(58,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/699605','Adorable Alberta Arts Bungalow','Fall in love with Portland in our cute, clean, and newly renovated 1925 Craftsman bungalow in close-in NE. Full of art and plants, the house has an open floor plan, providing a nice “flow” and abundant natural light. The location is superb - with a walk score of 86, it\'s a short walk to shopping, lively nightlife and restaurants, and several lovely parks. The area is very bike friendly, with two major bike routes nearby.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9373587/e3adc2bd_original.jpg',2605790,14,'45.56611','-122.65743',1,4,1.50,2.00,3.00,157.00,30,240,47,4.76,699605),(59,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/704753','Near OHSU. Choice of Clean Rooms. Private Baths.','INQUIRE in order to send a Reservation Request. We both need time to ask & answer Q\'s before Airbnb CUTS us off!! 24 HOUR limit. Available for Medical Students on Rotations!  Monthly stays are the best deal. Available to NON-smokers ONLY. No Smoking, No drugs, No pot, No pets, No drama in or within 200 feet of this home. Not accepting \"work from home\" stays. Period.<br />Clean Healthy Home.  In order to stay, See house rules upon YOUR ARRIVAL. Mature responsible working individuals reside here.','Well-established neighborhood. <br />Surrounded by nature in this amazing hillside setting 5-minutes from downtwon.<br />Birds are heard chirping every morning. Tall firs, ferns.<br />Wildlife are seen if you keep your eyes peeled. Mostly deer. <br />Lots of walkers, joggers, runners & cyclists are seen along the street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-704753/original/df2c8408-7a42-4b75-893b-db93ffeec2cf.jpeg',3190134,31,'45.48699','-122.69223',2,1,1.50,1.00,1.00,53.00,30,1125,11,4.73,704753),(60,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/714773','ArtFulLife','Three months minimum!  ArtFulLife is situated just 75 feet off NW 23rd, Portland’s iconic neighborhood street. An easy walk to the streetcar (3 blocks away), to the Pearl District to downtown, Washington Park, and much much more. It is all best experienced without a car! Parking is available for $150 a month additional.','ArtFulLife is situated about 75 feet off NW 23rd, Portland iconic shopping and eating street. From this location it is an easy walk to the streetcar (3 blocks away), to the Pearl District (10 blocks away), to downtown (1 mile), Washington Park (less than a mile - up a hill), and much much more. It is all best experienced without a car!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9753947/7a6d0d4f_original.jpg',1186353,27,'45.52837','-122.69799',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,49.00,90,1125,135,4.78,714773),(61,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/760737','Remodeled basement studio in central Portland','Basement studio apartment in a house built in 1900. The studio was completed in June 2018 and has everything you need for one or two people. Whether you\'re here for work or enjoying vacation, the studio\'s convenient location will make it all easy. The Buckman neighborhood provides the perfect Portland experience. The studio is private and has it\'s own entrance. Guests are welcome to use the small forested backyard. Feel free to contact me with any questions or suggestions','Our house is across the street from the historic Lone Fir Pioneer Cemetery. We are centrally located in the Buckman neighborhood and closest to bus lines 20 and 15. <br /><br />All necessities are within walking distance, including shopping, bars, coffee shops, grocery, restaurants, and movie theaters. We\'re located close to the Central Eastside Industrial, Hawthorne, NE 28th, Belmont, and East Burnside business districts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-760737/original/b9261d7a-f752-46dc-8f4b-9ea2887b8018.jpg',2646777,32,'45.51851','-122.64196',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,80.00,30,1125,282,4.97,760737),(62,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/774924','For humanitarian aid or medical vacations only','ONLY available to those seeking medical help with women’s care, and refugees for short term stays (maximum 2 weeks). I will help you find resources to help you resettle. Free to you if you qualify.<br /><br />Very kid- and pet-friendly, culturally-inclusive, and one block from an off-leash dog park, two playgrounds, tennis courts, new running track, and a public swimming pool, open June-Sept.<br /><br />I’m MORE than happy to welcome your pets! But they do entail extra cleaning so add each pet as an extra guest.','Best neighborhood! Two playgrounds, dog park, swimming pool, a church, and several hidden\" outdoor staircases in a well-maintained neighborhood. Three bus lines in easy walking distance. A little further, but still a 10-15 minute walk are four grocery stores, a terrific bakery, three pizza places, a movie theater, multiple nail salons, a public library, some pubs, a bike shop, a pharmacy, excellent restaurants, and pet stores. And, the Max (light rail) to take you to the airport, downtown, the convention center, Zoo, or Beaverton/Hillsboro.<br /><br />Follow us on Instagram #visitpdxwithpets for more restaurant/activity ideas around Portland, but here are a few to start:<br /><br />Dog-friendly bars and restaurants:<br />- Velo Cult bike shop and bar<br />- Fifth Quadrant<br />- Tin Shed<br />- Lucky Lab (3 locations)<br />- and many more: https://pdx.eater.com/maps/portlands-best-dog-friendly-restaurants-bars<br /><br />Dog-friendly Activities:<br />- International Rose Test Garden<br','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dd31da0d-0859-45d6-83b6-81a1f44ca4c2.jpg',3622006,33,'45.54129','-122.62691',1,5,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,14,59,4.93,774924),(63,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/775426','Incredible Location in Alberta Arts District','Make your experience in Portland as unique as the city itself by staying in our beautiful eco-friendly remodeled 3 bedroom space.','The Alberta Arts District is incredible! It\'s filled with independently owned restaurants, bars, stores, and cafes. The house is located in the heart of the area, so you can walk across the street to Tin Shed one of Portland\'s best breakfast spots. Or next store to Frock Boutique an adorable clothing store.  Our past guests have loved being so centrally located and hanging on the porch to watch the creativity of Portland flow by!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/59475535-5de6-44d3-99e5-62b8b726b3f6.jpg',1150082,14,'45.55841','-122.65152',1,7,1.50,3.00,4.00,157.00,1,1125,238,4.92,775426),(64,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/781710','House near Mt Tabor, SE Portland','A Four Square house built in 1904, our home has wood floors downstairs and carpet in the bedrooms. It is located in a corner lot surrounded by trees, keeping it shaded and cool in the Summer. Scarcely 2 blocks from the commercial district of Montavilla, you will enjoy rapid access to restaurants, bars, a movie theatre and a diversity of shopping. Blocks away from several bus lines.','Montavilla is an old neighborhood located near Mt Tabor Park. A distinctive feature is having many amenities (see list of restaurants, bars and other shops mentioned in description of the house), yet remaining family friendly and quite.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-781710/original/92f030ba-ebc6-484f-a591-ea660ea24da8.jpeg',4123246,10,'45.5219','-122.58296',1,4,2.00,3.00,3.00,120.00,30,115,4,5.00,781710),(65,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/784126','Portland condo near OHSU, VA Hospital & downtown!','Cute cozy condo near downtown Portland with Marquam nature park just a step away.','Situated amongst hiking and biking trails and lush greenery, and across from Oregon Health and Science University. 6 minute walk to VA hospital.<br /><br />The unit is about a 7 minute drive to portland state university and pioneer square. <br /><br />12 minute drive to pearl district and NW 23rd.<br /><br />It’s a little retreat near the heart of town.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/10995664/09d21496_original.jpg',4134978,30,'45.49608','-122.68884',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,70.00,30,1125,58,4.84,784126),(66,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/789798','Artsy, private lower level. Minutes from downtown.','Rhonda, an architectural designer, lends a creative vibe to this 1940 home. She created this spacious 525 sf. basement studio - leopard skin carpet, queen bed, sitting area, table, private bath and closet. Doug\'s show biz background\'s reflected with his movie memorabilia throughout. Quiet, safe SW Portland neighborhood, close to downtown. <br /><br />SPACE: Entrance & main floor is shared by us.<br />LONG STAYS: We request a chat before booking.<br /><br />City of Portland ASTR Type A Permit','SW PORTLAND: <br />• Ashcreek neighborhood, next to Multnomah Village<br />• Quiet, safe, middle class, wooded, residential<br />• 3 minutes to quaint Multnomah Village<br />• 3 minutes to the interstate<br />• 15 minutes to downtown on I-5, depending on traffic <br />• 30 minutes to scenic wine country <br />• 40 minutes to Columbia Gorge and Multnomah Falls <br />• 90 minutes to the beautiful Oregon Coast','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-789798/original/e321fdbc-cb8e-4dba-90a1-d33f9970590f.jpeg',4161754,34,'45.45631','-122.73765',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,82.00,3,30,235,4.93,789798),(67,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/798113','Kinley Manor Coach House Experience','THE KINLEY MANOR COACH HOUSE, \"Portland\'s Most Talked About Well-Kept Secret\" is an award-winning bright, spacious, furnished, two-level guest home that serves as a great retreat for business people or travelers interested in extended stay lodging.','Centrally located one block off NE Broadway, one of Portland\'s most popular thoroughfares, we are one block from Safeway. The Lloyd Center (Portland\'s oldest and biggest shopping mall), the Convention Center, The Rose Quarter, some of Portland\'s most popular restaurants, movie theaters, and there is also a MAX light rail station are also near by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/42c84403-a97e-48a2-bb08-c10c079a51d3.jpg',4203145,7,'45.53693','-122.65713',1,2,1.00,1.00,3.00,120.00,1,28,145,4.89,798113),(68,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/801318','Ideally Located, Modern & Artistic Large House','This amazing rental is located in the heart of Portland\'s most unique neighborhoods, the Alberta Arts District. With 4 bedrooms, 2 full baths, a large living room, and all of the amenities you need to feel directly at home.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-801318/original/f7b07033-e174-4580-a841-a006cfb12cdb.jpeg',1150082,14,'45.55859','-122.65161',1,11,2.00,4.00,4.00,228.00,1,1125,100,4.95,801318),(69,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/822105','Beautiful eco house in an excellent area','Our home is available for rent for the dates of May 22- June 24, 2024. As well as September 9th- October 26th. Fee includes all utilities. Ideally we are looking for someone who wants to rent the entire month. This beautiful home is located in the heart of the Alberta Art\'s Area and is filled with designer touches and warmth.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-822105/original/ff9e3047-2235-4959-958a-97298ade13d9.jpeg',1150082,6,'45.55596','-122.64804',1,6,2.00,3.00,3.00,82.00,30,60,4,4.75,822105),(70,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/838961','Studio Apartment - Private Entry','Private Full Kitchen, with shower , Laundry and Parking on the public street.','Walk to Park , Mall and Grocery Stores','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/35876219/f311d872_original.jpg',4382924,35,'45.54385','-122.54355',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,30,730,38,4.84,838961),(71,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/857220','Spacious, Comfy Downstairs Suite & Garage parking!','I\'ve achieved 40 consecutive Superhost statuses, representing over a decade of hosting experience.  I\'m also one of the first to earn the coveted \"GUEST FAVORITE\"<br /><br />You will enjoy a SPACIOUS 1200 square feet of downstairs area.<br /><br /> I stand as one of the rare AirBnB hosts in PDX with full short-term rental permits, having successfully passed a city inspection and covered all necessary fees for short-term renting.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6ODU3MjIw/original/11543f42-f72a-4805-bda0-e0f6364129b6.jpeg',4440080,36,'45.49162','-122.58212',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,74.00,1,28,403,4.95,857220),(72,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/871985','Beautiful Alberta Arts District Apt','This beautifully renovated, light and spacious basement apartment is located in a classic 1923 home 2 blocks from the exciting Alberta Arts District.  The space is contemporary in style and yet peaceful in ambience.  Please note that no animals/pets allowed in the apartment.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/13486917/1ba37d0f_original.jpg',3528646,6,'45.55677','-122.64898',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,110.00,1,1125,617,4.96,871985),(73,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/921597','Pearl District Loft: Urban Oasis','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/14598105/a7c83513_original.jpg',4955336,2,'45.53083','-122.68418',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,20,5.00,921597),(74,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/927432','Spacious, charming, & well-located Portland house','Beautifully renovated 1911 home in a great neighborhood with easy access to all Portland has to offer. Three bedrooms, 2.5 bathrooms; a spacious and light-filled living room, dining room, and kitchen; plus an office upstairs and a cozy TV/family room in the basement. Mere blocks from a wonderful park and rose garden and very close to the shopping/dining on Mississippi, Alberta, and Williams Avenues, with a direct bike path and multiple public transportation options to get downtown.','Our house is a short, pleasant walk to Peninsula Park, where there is a beautiful rose garden as well as a playground, tennis courts, and a swimming pool. Famous Mississippi Records is just a few blocks away, right next to Sweedeedee Cafe, a perfect spot for breakfast or lunch. There are grocery stores within walking distance, and historic Mississippi Avenue, with its cute restaurants, bars, and shops, is less than one mile away. We are also just around the corner from Williams Avenue, where new bars and restaurants seem to open every day. The Alberta Arts district is also nearby. Finally, because we are just a few minutes from I-5 and surrounded by great transit, you can get downtown or to pretty much any other part of Portland really quickly and easily.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/13629063/00a96e16_original.jpg',1916182,24,'45.56438','-122.67032',1,5,2.50,3.00,3.00,139.00,30,90,9,4.89,927432),(75,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/929954','Authentic Portland, Levity Lodge #3','Bright, Private room with Queen size bed, lightly Shared bath,  adjacent a flavorful, Peaceful feeling, owner-occupied central NE craftsman Home.  <br />Welcome!','I love it all. I have lived and most quadrants of Portland and purchased a house in my favorite area, very central to all of the juicy east side neighborhoods...<br />Lots of wonderful eats are walking distance and 10 blocks either direction On Sandy will lead you to large grocery stores. Case study coffee, Bake Shop, Du’s Korean barbecue,  are all just a couple blocks away as well as live music at Clydes prime rib (no cover charge).<br />Chaba Thai is half a block away and scrumptious- as is Arrowood- neighborhood restaurant/bar that features the beers of second profession brewery .<br />Rose city park playground is just a few blocks away as is $1 million view of Mount Hood on Northeast Sacramento if you walk to the south 2 blocks and to the east A few more..','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/14462923/7aa084d1_original.jpg',975606,11,'45.54433','-122.60348',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,31,600,14,4.93,929954),(76,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/938257','Pink House off Mississippi-ask for DEALS 4-6nights','MURPHY BED w/ comfy mattress.<br /><br />Great little tiny house in a fantastic neighborhood. It is cozy and modern. It\'s a tiny, stand alone house with a private bathroom, but no real kitchen.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-938257/original/86cd9295-b38e-4be4-bd00-f136c06c023c.jpeg',1515905,9,'45.55039','-122.67497',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,2,1124,560,4.77,938257),(77,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/938283','Green House Mississippi-ask for DEALS on 4-6nights','MURPHY BED with comfy mattress!<br /><br />Great little tiny house in a fantastic neighborhood. It is cozy and modern, with a great layout. <br /><br />It\'s a tiny, stand alone house with a private bathroom.<br />Short Term Rental Permit Number<br />15-163887-000-00-HO','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6db6c7ef-eef7-467d-a2ed-b8b32845ea75.jpg',1515905,9,'45.54884','-122.67389',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,2,730,544,4.77,938283),(78,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/942885','Simple and Spacious on NW 23rd with driveway','Located in the heart of Portland\'s Alphabet District off NW 23rd ave. <br /><br />This historic home features high-ceilings, hard wood floors, new accoutrements and spacious surroundings throughout.','With NW 23rd Avenue half a block away some of the best Portland has to offer is literally right outside the doorstep.  <br /><br />We live in a trendy fun-filled neighborhood with a 100% Walk Score and almost anything you could need within walking distance.  From flavorful restaurants & lively watering holes to boutique street shopping & beautiful scenic parks this location has it all.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-942885/original/ad51e547-79ab-4756-81b0-88924671a93c.jpg',5097860,27,'45.52934','-122.69961',1,5,2.50,2.00,3.00,217.00,3,120,235,4.88,942885),(79,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/951387','Quiet Private Studio in Inner NE near Bus & Bike','Come stay in our cozy studio apartment. You\'ll have a separate guest entrance,   a cheerful kitchen, a fully-tiled bathroom with tub and access to our little backyard oasis. We are located in a quiet neighborhood within short walking distance to restaurants and bars of N. Williams, Historic Mississippi and Alberta Arts. You can easily get around by using bikes from Biketown, Portlands bike share program, by public transportation (about 250ft to bus stop) and/or your car with free street parking.','The house in in a quiet residential neighborhood with a Walk Score of 85 and a Bike Score of 95. Its only a few blocks from upcoming Williams Ave, Historic Mississippi,  and Alberta Arts night-life, as well as bike paths, bus routes and light rail. <br /><br />Portland’s known for great food, and you can find restaurants like Thai BBQ \"Eem\", pizza at \"Life of Pie\", Argentinian barbecue at the Ox, brewpubs like Migration Brewing, German beer at Prost, and cafes like Honey $ Bread and Poa fit for your palate close by. Or you can cook up a storm in your own kitchen or grab a bite from one of the many food carts nearby. <br />New Seasons (a local grocery chain) and Natural Grocers are nearby and provide an easy walk for groceries or a gourmet buffet (New Seasons) when you don’t feel like messing up the kitchen.<br />You can easily get around by using one of the bikes available from Portland bike share Biketown.  The closest bike station is about 600ft from the studio, the closest kiosk to ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-951387/original/5465aadd-52bb-4a2c-8e64-b63811017563.jpg',5161731,9,'45.553','-122.66629',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,75.00,2,90,624,4.86,951387),(80,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/958634','Spacious Private Suite for Extended Stays','Private, quiet, furnished space with storage. Two large rooms and a half bath are exclusively for guest use.  Shared spaces are open and bright. Neighborhood is the hip South Tabor neighborhood with a Walk Score of 83 and is rated Bikers Paradise (score of 99). Three bus lines are within 3 blocks.  Quick bike ride to inner Division Street featured in Sunset Magazine and trendy Montavilla and Hawthorne neighborhoods. Available for 30 nights plus only. Host and her dogs share the common areas.','It\'s very walkable and I know all my neighbors. It\'s quiet and safe with ample parking. Mt Tabor (large park with trails ) is less than a mile away. There is a local coffee shop on the corner, Starbucks two blocks away and several restaurants within walking distance.  It\'s a 5-10 minute drive to the popular Hawthorne, Montavilla, and Division neighborhoods.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/85fc6f17-6f73-47bc-82f9-460a287d6d3d.jpg',5216499,37,'45.50315','-122.58148',2,1,1.50,1.00,1.00,85.00,31,250,31,4.87,958634),(81,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/967959','Authentic Alberta Arts Abode','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/19306020/58face15_original.jpg',1507209,14,'45.55715','-122.65553',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,76.00,2,30,698,4.88,967959),(82,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/993073','PDX Eco Cottage','Winner of Sunset Magazine\'s \'Small Space, Big Dreams\' contest for best Small House, this private midcentury cottage, built in 2013, is  located in tree-lined historic Ladd’s Addition, two blocks from Portland\'s hottest bar and restaurant row - Division Street.  Check out our other listing, the 2 bedroom PDX Urban Barn, https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15094467 for a two bedroom guest house just a few short blocks away.  Please don\'t book if you have a service animal as our cleaner is highly allergic','Ladd\'s Addition has a \'Walk Score\' of 92 - perfect for strolling around the rose gardens or using the nearby bike route to get around the city. Funky Hawthorne Blvd. is the northern border of Ladd\'s with culinary-rich Division St. to the south, gaining prominence for its growing and innovative restaurant scene and unique shops.  Nearby Clinton St.\'s bars and coffee shops as well as restaurants round out why this area lands you in the heart of what makes Portland unique - small, boutique restaurants, an independent movie theater and one-of-a-kind businesses for shopping.  We are a block from a children\'s playground.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/62541700/bf842146_original.jpg',5455260,25,'45.50661','-122.64996',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,142.00,2,28,375,4.95,993073),(83,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/997150','Cozy Kerns 1 bdrm Apt - Best PDX Neighborhood!','Portland’s own Kerns neighborhood has been written up as one of the best spots in the US! For good reason, tons of charming shops and restaurants within walking distance with everything you\'d need for your short or extended visit. <br />Located off the bustling 28th and Burnside strip with a Whole Foods grocery store, park, movie theater, food cart pod and variety of cuisines to choose from. This is a private, first level apt in a craftsman house duplex. Pets allowed with an additional $75 cleaning.','I\'ve lived all over the city and believe this to be the best neighborhood. Its a central location, two blocks to Whole Foods, and a multitude of other restaurants, and coffee shops. <br />To eat - Bamboo Sushi, Kens Pizza, Paadee, Navarre, Laurelhurst Market, and Pambiche are my immediate favorites. For inexpensive bites head to the food carts on 28th or a sandwich at Meat Cheese Bread. Coffee and bakery best found at Crema. <br />Head up to Laurelhurst Park for a stroll or catch a movie at Laurelhurst theater - $4 tickets and beer!<br />More then happy to give any other recommendations per request, from shopping to haircuts etc, I\'ve done everything there could possible be to do within a two mile radius of this house and its an extensive list.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-997150/original/e0235f60-cea2-4fc0-a37d-d9c83735df1d.jpeg',3041678,32,'45.52159','-122.63738',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,1,1125,569,4.84,997150),(84,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1003617','The Portland Villa on Alberta St','In the heart of NE Portland\'s vibrant and bustling Alberta Arts district. Endless options for dining, drinking, shopping and entertainment within walking distance. The main home is 2800 sqft plus an additional 1200 sqft on a private rooftop deck (that we built ourselves!). There is natural light (and plants) galore. Prepare meals in our chef’s  kitchen. We don’t skimp on linens, supplies, cozy mattresses or bedding. A legally permitted rental by the City of Portland. 1% for The Planet member.','The Alberta Arts district (Concordia) is thriving. There is so much in Portland but you have found the hottest hood in PDX. Wonderful restaurants, bars, shops and boutiques line Alberta Street from 9th street to 30th. The shops are all small, local businesses and its simply a friendly and unique place to be. We are a quick 15 minutes from the airport, downtown and the convention center. We would say there is no better spot to experience a city that we have grown to love :)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/818aac4a-f9e1-46da-b06b-ed59d5f6525d.jpg',4430753,1,'45.55856','-122.63717',1,9,2.00,4.00,5.00,398.00,1,1125,308,4.95,1003617),(85,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1007277','Feels Like Home','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/21d67084-8f2e-49bb-8a75-d2ee722d1838.jpg',3978304,38,'45.4889','-122.62173',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,30,365,433,4.82,1007277),(86,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1009218','Perfect SE Location: Classic Portland Experience','A classic 1904 foursquare Portland duplex that is within walking distance to everything - local cafes, restaurants, shops, music venues, boutique stores, wine bars, coffee roasters, parks, and a local volcano! This characterful apartment is cozy and comfortable for a single person or a couple.','Buckman is a cool and very walkable neighborhood.  It has a walk score of 90 and a bike score of 99!  Neighbors are friendly.  Restaurants include Screendoor, Navarre, Matador, Ken\'s Artisan Pizza, Tusk, Pix, Bamboo, Paadee, and many more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0c59898e-c381-4a5a-acc7-dd64cc8b4d4d.jpg',1284016,32,'45.52286','-122.64743',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,123,4.95,1009218),(87,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1036774','\"The Portland Purple House 1\"','An area filled with charm, older homes, pride in ownership.  Dogs walking their owners, and squirrels running to and fro.  Two blocks from a major grocery store, and the Trimet bus line, Max light rail on 42nd.<br />Centrally located to Downtown, Airport, Moda  Center.','My neighborhood is very \"Portland\" coffee bars, little family owned fooderies, Awesome pizza places galore.  No need to call for Dominos.  When you got Blind Onion, or Otto a phone call away. <br />Very quiet, family owned homes, with pride in ownership and pet happy people.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTAzNjc3NA%3D%3D/original/58d04f17-ac57-480e-a9c1-cfbf1793ef5d.jpeg',5707629,39,'45.55121','-122.59294',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,105.00,2,7,35,4.40,1036774),(88,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1046001','Alberta Arts Basement Room - Wifi, A/C!','Custom-finished room in a semi-secluded area of the house. The basement has a separate outside entrance and walkway so guests can come and go with privacy.','The house is located in the heart of the vibrant Alberta district. Starting 3 blocks away, there are great restaurants (including Podnah\'s Pit, restaurant of the year), coffee houses (like Random Order named one of America\'s Best Pie Spots by Food&Wine), brew pubs, shopping and entertainment.  Walkscore rating for our house is an amazing 96! It describes our location as a Walker\'s Paradise.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8500a3d6-1a46-48fa-88b0-58957243e2b8.jpg',2236909,14,'45.55965','-122.65729',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,57.00,30,180,88,4.69,1046001),(89,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1086146','Spacious Urban Retreat','Located in a quiet safe neighborhood, our spacious urban retreat is your perfect home away from home.  Its clean and beautiful, just minutes away from the airport, and is ideal for weekend getaways, family get-togethers, business travel, or extended stays over 30-days. Play in the fenced backyard, or just relax under the shade of the front porch with our custom-made swings.  If you want to adventure outdoors, hike some beautiful trails, or visit downtown, we’re a short drive away.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTA4NjE0Ng%3D%3D/original/883d0e68-247e-453b-9367-d1cf02421914.jpeg',5970172,40,'45.55796','-122.55871',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,225.00,2,60,183,4.81,1086146),(90,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1100793','Walker’s Paradise w/ projector, kitchenette','Sound-proofed Basement in Sellwood-Westmoreland w/ PRIVATE outdoor entrance, big windows, workspace, heated carpet, heated toilet seat and BIG screen  w/ Bose soundbar. Coffee, tea, snacks, drinks provided. <br /> <br />* a tiny nook in the main room w/ 2nd bed. <br />* 2 adults Max, 1 child<br /><br />2 blocks to grocery, restaurants, theater, coffee, parks, mountain views <br /><br />.5 mi to Bybee MAX Train station, orange line. Reed College & Crystal Springs 1 mi. Trackers  1 mile. Downtown 4.5 mi/ <10min by car.','90+ walkscore says about half of it. Here are some other great factors:<br /><br />1. Light Rail (MAX) is open! Less than 1/2 mile (10th mins walk) from our house. You can take it to/from the airport, downtown, Powell\'s books, expo center, you name it. It rocks! <br /><br />2. River access 1 mile from the house, take our kayak for a spin- if you know how to use it! We have a single.  There\'s also a kayak rental place across the river if you need additional or tour guide. <br /><br />3. One mile north to entrance to the bike corridor that loops the city. Take our bikes (please rent through Spinlister)!<br /><br />4. These things are within a 5 min walk:<br />-Movie theater<br />-Restaurants<br />-Coffee shops<br />-Grocery store<br />-Yogurt shop<br />-Hardware store<br />- 3 Banks (US Bank, Wells, BOA)<br />-Westmoreland Park (1 mile long with new, innovative kid\'s area) <br />-Elementary School Park (with play structures)<br />- Tiny Park (with play structures)<br />-View of Mt. Hood ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-1100793/original/6d1cb6b6-3534-4058-9337-f9779df7a622.jpeg',496929,20,'45.47911','-122.64506',1,2,1.00,2.00,2.00,95.00,3,21,59,4.90,1100793),(91,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1103529','The Hen House: Private unit in NE','The Hen House is a converted garage, built from mostly salvaged material, and has everything you need for an easy visit. The loft has a queen bed but stairs are very steep so I recommend the pullout single bed downstairs if uncomfortable with steps. I\'m near Mississippi area, Williams and Alberta Arts District with 2 grocery stores within walking distance. Unit stands alone and there is a garden and friendly animals to hang with outside. Dogs allowed.','Fun and quiet neighborhood but you can walk to a bar, park or a really good restaurant within minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c67397f7-baad-449b-bcb8-525df08bc441.jpg',6060622,14,'45.55192','-122.65726',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,78.00,1,1125,896,4.94,1103529),(92,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1107789','Cozy Portland Studio Apartment','The space is a well appointed, comfortable studio apartment. It is an ADU at the back of the main house. All the amenities that one would desire are provided (wifi, internet, cable TV, washer & dryer, fridge, dishwasher, stove, microwave, AC, cooking utensils,  etc., etc).<br /><br />It is also very modern and clean, with a private entrance and keyless entry.  Close to many restaurants, bars and coffee shops.','Buckman is close in on the SE side of town. We are about 2 miles from downtown. There are several restaurants, bars and coffee shops within walking distance, plus a park in which one can walk or run.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/53007259/a1d8e064_original.jpg',6000443,32,'45.51904','-122.64412',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,3,29,842,4.98,1107789),(93,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1119763','Maple Cottage PDX/ Fun Historic Mississippi Ave.','The Maple Cottage is located in the Historic Mississippi district of Portland. It offers a full kitchen, bedroom and generous dining room table that doubles as a work area. Just outside, is a small patio great for enjoying the garden. Restaurants and pubs are just a step away.  Let\'s not forget Blue Star donuts!<br />Downtown Portland is just a short distance and our city is widely known for it\'s excellent transit system. Bikes are available for rent just a few blocks away.<br />Welcome to our home!','Where to begin! <br />Have to mention the upcoming Mississippi Street Fair this July 8, 2017. Handcrafts, bands, BBQ, beer garden -- go crazy in the street! <br />There are so many fun and funky restaurants on the Mississippi Ave! Generous plates of biscuits and eggs at Gravy, crepes at FlapJak, scrumptious street tacos at Porque No, UCHU Sushi has many great happy hours and the Stormbreaker and the Ecliptic are great brew pubs with outdoor seating and all the interesting locally produced microbrews.<br />For live music, peruse the lineup at Mississippi Studios for rap, retro, folk and indy.  Or just pop into the Mississippi Pizza pub and see who\'s playing! All summer Portland hosts free concerts in the park -- picnic and dance! This is something we love and always have the full concert schedule on hand. Watch a sunset at the Overlook Park just minutes away.  Rent bicycles just 2 blocks away and peddle to McMenamin\'s Kennedy School for a meal or a movie or just check out the amazing lo','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0f492c55-53c8-4be9-bb1d-b7eddca38d30.jpg',2749411,9,'45.55299','-122.67411',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,69.00,3,30,370,4.98,1119763),(94,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1151857','Vintage Charm *Queen* at Opal 28 Apt 2','1 of 4 Opal 28 Apts, originally built in 1908, our building is boasting with vintage charm. This spacious one bedroom apartment includes the amenities of home.  Located on NE 28th Avenue, one of NE Portlands best neighborhoods. Bustling with food, drinks and shopping right out the door!  A short walk to Laurelhurst Park and a very central location to all of the regions best places to visit via car, foot or bus.','We are located in Laurelhurst / Kerns,  prime and very central Portland neighborhood for taking in the pride of the Pacific Northwest. With in walking distance are great restaurants, shops, parks and Portland culture. <br /><br />Here are a handful of our faves with in walking distance....<br /><br />Migration Brewery - great beer and if the patio is open you can watch the world of Burnside go by! <br />Dove Vive - best pizza in town<br />Guero - best torta in town<br />Basilisk - best fried chicken <br />Cheese & Crack Shop - cheese & charcuterie plus soft serve! UNIQUE FIND*<br />PaaDee- Authentic Thai<br />Montelupo Italian Market - new on the scene!<br /><br />UNIQUE PDX<br />28th & Sandy is the Zipper - multiple micro restaurants to choose from<br />24th & Glisan is the Ocean - multiple micro restaurants to choose from<br /><br />GROCERY<br />Whole Foods - NE 28th and Burnside (out the apt door to the left) <br />Providore - NE 24th and Sandy, fancy food store <br />Fred Meyer* - ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTE1MTg1Nw%3D%3D/original/d3e85f6d-bb11-43f8-bd8f-a82a4cab6a70.jpeg',6313800,12,'45.5262','-122.63684',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,52.00,30,1125,191,4.63,1151857),(95,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1193068','Rosie Room at Farmhouse Cottage','The elevated bed is built into the nook of a large window, a step up from the garden outside. The double bed is comfy for two who care to cuddle.  There\'s a door to the south covered porch with theater seats overlooking the garden.  The vintage kitchen, custom bathroom, warm common spaces and heirloom garden are all yours to enjoy.','The big trees.  The singing birds.  The sound of the creek.  The friendly humans.  The proximity to town.<br />These are a few of my favorite things.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-1193068/original/cb0fb39a-9b0c-4635-a775-a4ce9f9325b5.jpg',1996078,41,'45.45896','-122.69126',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,30,1125,13,5.00,1193068),(96,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1194370','Cozy mud hut with big bridge view','Nestled in the private backyard of our family home, a neighborhood hub. The round, rustic, romantic MudHut hides in a secret garden overlooking the St. Johns bridge and sparkling river, near Cathedral Park, Forest Park, downtown St. Johns, canoe and hiking trails... Firepit, permaculture gardens, loaner bikes, community life, view!','We\'re in St. Johns, Portland\'s northern-most neighborhood and a small town of its own with a strong community identity here. Many families here trace their roots back to James John, the pioneer founder of St. Johns who is memorialized all over the neighborhood. Downtown St. Johns is a few blocks away, with plenty of restaurants (Thai, vegan, soulfood, chinese, pub grub, pizza, deli, breakfast, coffee & gelato), an old movie theater and shopping (lots of vintage). <br />Cathedral Park, three blocks away, is gorgeous and photogenic with access to the Willamette River and the awesome overhead presence of the gothic St. Johns Bridge that you can see from the hut. <br />We\'re also close to a lot of natural areas for urban hiking and paddling. Forest Park, full of trails and old growth forest, is right across the bridge. Just north of here is Kelley Point Park, the confluence of the Willamette and Columbia Rivers; Smith and Bybee Lakes, a wetlands for birding and paddling; and Sauvie Island,','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/22623807/9dbebaee_original.jpg',6526820,42,'45.58991','-122.76046',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,72.00,30,1125,498,4.78,1194370),(97,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1194589','Artisan Sanctuary','Cozy, quiet, artistically appointed basement apartment in great NE Portland location.  Separate entrance.  Parking available on street in front of house. Fully furnished and on the bike route.  2 vintage bikes available for your use free of charge.  Located on a quiet street within walking distance of Alberta Street, N. Williams and Mississippi  Ave.<br />I personally clean my apartment for each guest. In light of recent events, I\'m being extra meticulous for the comfort and well-being of my guests.','A lovely older established neighborhood that is undergoing a major transition.  There are still many people who have lived here for years, but it is also being developed.  There are now 3 area within walking distance that offer housing, shops, restaurants and bars etc.  I  am on the bike boulevard system and not far from the highway access.  It is also easy to get around on public transportation which is at the end of the street.  I have loved living here for these 20 years.  One of the nicest neighborhoods in Portland, I think.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fb6c86c1-1e58-4fdc-a4ed-a8ffa7f715ad.jpg',5927807,24,'45.56037','-122.6684',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,199.00,2,1125,406,4.93,1194589),(98,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1209612','WATERFRONT, NW  DISTRICT CONDO','','Portland, in general, is a great walking city. We love that we are close to great shopping, great parks to laze around in, great neighbourhood dining spots...','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/34690876/8950b7d7_original.jpg',6510017,43,'45.52622','-122.67284',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,1.00,30,60,54,4.78,1209612),(99,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1213052','Alberta Arts Bungalow - 4 Bedroom','We are a legally permitted 4 bedroom short term rental house. <br />Alberta Arts district is unique; rich in culture, excellent food and drink, on transit lines and totally walkable. We\'re half a block from it all. At home, enjoy the whole single level house, impeccably clean, modern and comfortable, with solid bamboo floors. Enjoy the front porch and private back yard.<br />Our tenant lives upstairs in a separate apartment.','Just read the reviews to see how much people enjoy this neighborhood.  Just for starters, good coffee choices within blocks,  the Tin Shed and Fuel Cafe at the corner, and dozens of breakfast, lunch, dinner, and bar choices awaiting within walking distance. Want to cook? The Alberta Co-op in one block, Whole Foods, New Seasons, and Safeway all within a mile or so.  Galleries and boutiques are on Alberta Street too.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ec7153af-fcbc-4855-828b-c4633cf66260.jpg',6621964,29,'45.5585','-122.65001',1,8,2.00,4.00,5.00,289.00,2,30,225,4.94,1213052),(100,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1242928','Modernist Loft in NE Portland (30-day minimum)','This modern loft is located just a block South of Northeast Portland\'s Historic Alberta District and just 1 mile from great shops and restaurants on both Williams and Mississippi Avenues. Whether on a business trip or Portland vacation, this modern loft is a great stay. The open floor plan allows you to spread out and relax while a fully equipped kitchen is ready for entertaining a small group.<br /> <br />✓  5 minutes away from Adidas Corporate Office','You\'ll be located in Portland\'s most up-and-coming neighborhood. The expanding Williams Ave is home to restaurants like Tasty & Sons and southern cuisine spot: The People\'s Pig. <br /><br />🗸  Catch a live show, get brunch or shop on Mississippi Ave. <br />🗸  Enjoy the Last Thursday Art Walk on the popular Alberta Street where <br />     there\'s more than enough to see and eat, especially at places like Tin Shed <br />     and Pine State Biscuits. <br />🗸  The I-5 and 405 are both 1 mile away for easy access around the city. <br />🗸  Supermarkets Safeway and New Seasons are 1 mile north and south, respectively. <br />🗸  Downtown Portland is a 5-10 minute ride. <br />🗸  Bike lanes and bus routes are located literally just steps away on Williams and Vancouver Avenues.<br /><br />You are just minutes away from enjoying the gorgeos Peninsula Park and Portland\'s Washington park which contains a number of tourist attractions, including the famed international Rose Test Garden, zoo and museum','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-1242928/original/9d3ecbf9-2a88-4c03-83f2-f5cc7f5deacf.jpeg',6774413,24,'45.55915','-122.66811',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,113.00,30,1125,104,4.72,1242928),(101,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1242968','Urban Sanctuary near Shops, Dining & Downtown!','Accepting guests and implementing extra cleaning protocols.<br /><br />Bright and clean one bedroom main floor of gorgeous bungalow just one block off of Mississippi St. Thousands of happy guests! Dozens of shops, bars, restaurants and things to do just outside your door!!! Free parking no permit required.<br /><br />Full kitchen and charming shared courtyard!<br /><br />Minutes from downtown via bike, light rail or car. Easy access to/from the Airport too! Ten years in and our five star rating is going strong!','Portland\'s Historic Mississippi District is definitely where you want to stay when visiting the city. A gorgeous  and funky stretch full of great shops, award-winning restaurants, an incredible music venue and amazing bars with outdoor patios and inspiring craft cocktails. SUPER easy to get to other parts of the city from here too!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/033140b7-9da2-4ebb-9dd0-669c1b55f5a8.jpg',6416589,9,'45.5537','-122.67645',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,1,1125,914,4.94,1242968),(102,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1261196','Vintage Portland Home—8 Minutes to Downtown!','Get a taste of Portland charm when you stay in this spacious, private 1913 Craftsman bungalow set in one of the most renowned neighborhoods in the city, boasting over 80 restaurants, bars, and cafes within a mile stroll! Kerns ranks #5 on Time Out\'s recent list of World\'s Coolest Neighborhoods. Fancy a trip downtown? This house is just a short 10-minute drive over the river, or if you\'re needing to burn off the praline bacon from Screen Door down the street, a leisurely two-mile stroll.','Great location in the Kerns neighborhood, three blocks from \"Restaurant Row\"—a fabulous lineup of dozens of restaurants, cafes and bars, along with Whole Foods, good ol’ Starbucks, an independent movie theatre, and tons of unique shops and boutiques. More restaurants and bars are opening up all the time, including top eateries like Luce, Screen Door, Navarre, and Tusk, all just a few blocks away. It\'s a wonderful walking neighborhood (Walk Score 93!), a 15-minute stroll from lovely Laurelhurst Park, even closer to Oregon Park and the school playground down the street. Voodoo Doughnuts Too is a 10-minute walk, and there\'s a beautiful hot tub/float tank spa (Everett House) just down the block.<br /><br />WALK TO<br />-Screen Door+<br />-Pix Patisserie<br />-Navarre<br />-Ate Oh Ate<br />-Tusk*++<br />-Davenport<br />-Luce+<br />-Stammtisch<br />-Nomad PDX<br />-The Pie Spot+<br />-Pambiche+<br />-Laurelhurst Market*<br />-Basilisk<br />Beulah Land+<br />-Crema+<br />-Guero<br />-Pollo No','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f0bf986d-5d1f-455a-997f-ad9eedffd1d6.jpg',234549,12,'45.52485','-122.64315',1,5,2.00,3.00,4.00,207.00,90,365,243,4.75,1261196),(103,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1288320','Thompson Hideaway - walk to Convention Center','Step away from world class restaurants, shops and public transportation. Nestled in a quiet neighborhood setting. Walk to the Convention Center, The Moda Center (Blazers), The Wonder Ballroom, the Pearl District, the Lloyd District, and Legacy Emanuel Hospital. Sleeps 4, with queen bed, and a convertible comfortable futon in the main room.','You\'ll find it easy to explore Portland from this close-in location by streetcar, on foot, or by bike.  You\'ll be walking distance to the Convention Center 0.7 miles, the Lloyd District 0.5, Williams Avenue, the Pearl District 1 mile, the Moda Center 0.75, Powell\'s, and of course Voodoo Donuts.<br />There is a great marijuana store, Mary Jane\'s at the end of the block.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/da0644fb-6d08-4b39-be55-cd3237ed26cc.jpg',5037209,26,'45.54057','-122.66377',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,76.00,2,15,609,4.77,1288320),(104,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1297869','5th Ave Townhouse','If you want to experience Downtown Portland & live in a spacious house with a backyard to sit out in too, this is it!<br />You\'re a hop & a skip from local transport or you can easily walk to anywhere within the city center.','We are in a vibrant, ever changing & improving section of the Downtown where the  Portland State university has its campus as well as an excellent year round Saturday Farmers market, Portland Art museum, Oregon Historical museum and the Marina on the Willamette River. There are a number of great restaurants, bars & cafes within a 5 min walk.<br />Portland\'s famous food carts are one street away!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-1297869/original/de6378e6-7640-4613-ae5c-7e7e4be29b5e.jpeg',7055900,44,'45.51032','-122.68208',1,8,2.00,4.00,5.00,395.00,2,1125,432,4.90,1297869),(105,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1313694','Work & Stay at The Green Fairy','Come have a work/staycation at The Beautiful Green Fairy.<br />Vintage Gorgeous 1,500 sq ft lovingly hand restored 1899 duplex in vibrant desirable neighborhood. Corner lot with wrap around garden. Walk to restaurants, shops, brewpubs, coffee, yoga. Beautifully furnished with everything possible to make your work/stay as comfortable & memorable as possible. Fast WiFi.  Sit/stand desk in 2nd bedroom, Across from park, Near major bike lanes & mass transit. <br />Please reach out For stays of 6 mos. or more.','I love the Boise Elliot (Mississippi/Williams corridor) neighborhood for its walk ability to great food, shopping, yoga etc. Also- it\'s very close to the Alberta arts district, Hawthorne, and close access to the freeway and the max line. Oh- and the Vancouver/Williams bike corridor is right there as well.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/63e9aaba-63bc-4253-9bf5-039724f51446.jpg',6153335,9,'45.55014','-122.67192',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,136.00,30,300,122,4.82,1313694),(106,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1332422','Salmon Street Farmhouse','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/20070961/5e9703f9_original.jpg',1616228,25,'45.5119','-122.64345',1,5,1.50,3.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,15,4.87,1332422),(107,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1386231','Cozy Basement Alberta Arts Room','Private room in a secluded part of the house. New tiled bathroom and granite kitchen counters. 3 blocks walk to the start of the vibrant and famous Alberta Arts district.','The house is located in the heart of the vibrant Alberta district. Starting 3 blocks away, there are great restaurants (including Podnah\'s Pit, restaurant of the year), coffee houses (like Random Order named one of America\'s Best Pie Spots by Food&Wine), brew pubs, shopping and entertainment.  Walkscore rating for our house is an amazing 96! It describes our location as a Walker\'s Paradise.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/078e1f86-cfe7-4cfc-886d-608de1bb5482.jpg',2236909,14,'45.56239','-122.65649',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,53.00,30,180,72,4.77,1386231),(108,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1386922','Mississippi Ave Basement Studio','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b4f196e5-e2e1-4929-8687-10d8bfbf658b.jpg',3859198,24,'45.56328','-122.67523',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,30,1125,212,4.60,1386922),(109,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1408895','Bright & Modern Home in Lovely Roseway','','So many awesome things in and nearby my neighborhood!  Feel free to check out the guidebook for restaurant or sightseeing suggestions.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/29603880/34d42a04_original.jpg',942377,39,'45.54872','-122.58744',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,99.00,30,50,77,4.84,1408895),(110,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1411299','Cozy, yet Spacious Division 1BR Apt','Immaculate, homey, 1-BR apartment w/separate entry. Great for parents visiting kids, business folk & tourists. Spacious & light w/full kitchen. Separate router, so fast Wi-Fi. Many guests note: \"Great shower water pressure!\" in snug but full bathroom. If you like to nap, bedroom feels far away from kitchen.  Neighbors are out & about, but quiet at night.  <br /><br />A 5-minute walk to popular Division restaurants & buses downtown or a 15-minute walk to Hawthorne through sweet Portland neighborhoods.','The neighborhood is bustling with kids and families, but it is not noisy at night.   <br /><br />We are located two blocks from busy Division St which is exploding with restaurants of every variety.  A very pleasant ten-minute walk north is the Hawthorne District, with an equally dizzying array of restaurants and shops.  <br /><br />Nearby Cleveland HS has a refurbished track for joggers and space to play other sports.  <br /><br />New Seasons, Safeway, Fred Meyer and Trader Joe\'s grocery stores are close by to stock your kitchen, along with a friendly wine shop w Happy Hour seating two blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-1411299/original/b6fdf277-16ce-40b2-ad09-4564f72ec583.jpg',6960996,8,'45.50152','-122.62856',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,2,21,259,4.96,1411299),(111,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1420478','Chez Rosette Tiny House','This is a centrally located, bright, airy, comfortable and separate 320 sq ft tiny guest house. It comes equipped with a memory foam mattress in the sleeping loft, a kitchenette (mini fridge, induction stove, microwave, toaster oven, hot water kettle, french press), claw foot tub/shower, WiFI, and TV, and outdoor patio/garden access. Close to bus/ MAX/bike paths. Sleeps 2 comfortably, +1 on couch or extra mattress. Recommended for adults. No children under 8. COVID NOTE: Patio not available.','Beaumont Wilshire is a lovely, residential neighborhood with great shopping, restaurants, bars, parks and Beaumont Market, which is open til midnight.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/21229581/2bd44fe2_original.jpg',7647618,19,'45.5443','-122.62612',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,107.00,3,120,167,4.87,1420478),(112,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1429073','Lovely Private Room & Bath in SE (South Tabor)','I offer a comfortable, clean & quiet guest bedroom & private bath in my cozy cottage-style home in SE Portland less than a mile from beautiful Mt. Tabor.  I have had the pleasure of hosting people from across the country and world for nearly ten years and take great pleasure in meeting new folks and offering them an affordable and welcoming place to call “home” (however temporarily) during their stay in the Rose City.','The South Tabor neighborhood is a relatively quiet one consisting of a diverse collection of single family homes and higher density housing.  It is close enough to walk to Division Street (12 blocks) and to Hawthorne (1 mi.), both of which are teeming with a diverse collection of shops and restaurants, but far enough away to not be affected by the noise and parking that accompanies these busier streets.  Easy access to one of Portland\'s most established \"bike corridor routes\" to downtown Portland.  One mile from various entrances to Mount Tabor -- a lovely, forested park within the city with a variety of hiking trails.  And since it\'s Portland, I can not too surprisingly report that I am located within five blocks of at least one cannabis store, tattoo parlor and strip club.  Something for everyone!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/84329664-9300-495a-9308-9bfee8596230.jpg',7656277,37,'45.49991','-122.60654',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,48.00,2,30,215,4.99,1429073),(113,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1438618','One block from everything. Purely Portland stay :)','My gem of a mid-century 1942 bungalow captures  Portland\'s unique character. A comfy oasis one block from unique restaurants, coffee shops, boutiques, a neighborhood market, and more!  Authentic vintage furnishings bring you to a simpler time. Gas fireplace keeps you cozy on cool nights. Large backyard patio surrounded by birds & plants. Flowers, fruit trees, and a vegetable garden out front. <br /><br />Every bit of my cleaning fee goes directly to my cleaning person :).','Beaumont-Wilshire is the ideal place to stay! Lots of shops and restaurants with well-appointed outdoor seating, and without the crushing crowds and painful waits. There is always parking within a few car lengths of my house. We have old school bars and burger joints, Thai and Thai fusion, incredible outdoor seating and live music at Amalfi’s, legendary Jim & Patti\'s coffee, the ever-delicious Pips made-to-order donuts, sushi, local bakery, bagels, and more!  Beaumont Market is a quick walk up the street, where you\'ll find everything you need, including a walk-in beer cooler ;). Hollywood, Alberta, and Mississippi districts are just a 5-10min drive, but if you want to know where the locals go to avoid the crowds, I\'ll be happy to share! Walking this neighborhood, the shop-owners will greet you warmly and help you find whatever you need. You will experience the uniqueness of a very Portland neighborhood while feeling very much at home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6c04d6fd-c6a5-46d4-af4e-afb25fb7e218.jpg',7727691,21,'45.54883','-122.61489',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,195,4.88,1438618),(114,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1525272','The Irvington off Broadway studio condominium','Located in the beautiful, historic Irvington neighborhood.  2 block walk to Broadway St. restaurants and cafes. This is a private basement studio. Photos give an accurate depiction of the space.<br /><br />Enjoy free wash & fold laundry service at a local cleaner, and monthly room cleanings for multi-month stays.<br /><br />The Irvington off Broadway requires a minimum stay of one month (31 nights).  Please avoid booking for 30 nights, as this will result in you paying (Airbnb-required) significant rate upcharges.','Historic Irvington Neighborhood<br />NE Broadway Street Cafes, Restraunts, Shops<br />Bike Town PDX<br />TriMet public transportation<br />Lloyd Center Mall and Movie Theater<br />Milo\'s City Cafe<br />Starbucks<br />Safeway Grocery Store<br />Portland Convention Center','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-1525272/original/5617889e-b402-414e-a1b4-c4278c5a065f.jpeg',8138263,7,'45.5373','-122.65571',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,60.00,31,365,19,4.58,1525272),(115,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1539452','\"The Hermitage\", Historic Hafner Haus 2nd unit','On Portland\'s registry of \"Historically Significant Buildings\", The Hafner Haus is the most central remaining single family home in the center of Portland. It was built for Pastor Hafner and his family in 1907. Price is a suggested nonprofit donation','We are in the middle of Everything! There is a police rest stop in the church next door, so this area is very safe. Downtown Portland is generally a safe place, but the extra presence is nice.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTUzOTQ1Mg%3D%3D/original/e837fc7c-8f87-41f6-b267-6bd7e55d0edb.jpeg',8207605,44,'45.51637','-122.68821',1,5,1.00,2.00,7.00,44.00,30,180,166,4.58,1539452),(116,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1542659','Bright Beautiful Mid-Century Style Loft in N.E.','Our beautiful, spacious loft is in the Eliot/Irvington neighborhood.  Featuring a high vaulted ceiling and lots of light, its spacious and cozy at the same time. It’s fully furnished with our family’s art and mid century furniture. It’s tasteful and home-y. <br /><br />NE Portland is known for it\'s vibrant restaurant and bar scene, arts districts, hip food carts, shops, beautiful houses and parks. Immediate access to public transportation, and walking distance to the Lloyd district.','We are located in a historical neighborhood, with beautiful parks & shopping destinations, very close to the Convention Center & Moda Center. <br />Whole Foods & New Seasons, farmer\'s markets & amazing restaurants abound, which makes for wonderful shared culinary experiences. <br />We are within a block of gourmet pizza & beer), Bunk Sandwiches - best in town, plus cocktails, Cafe 26 ~ (coffee bar with great pastries & small food items), Bella Flora (adorable vintage, handmade crafts & fairy furniture), a dry cleaner, a laundromat, and the Nike Outlet store. <br />-Some of the BEST RESTAURANTS in Portland are within a few blocks, including last year\'s restaurant of the year -\"OX\" (think nouvelle Argentinian fusion), Toro Bravo (former restaurant of the year, famous for it\'s tapas menu), Russell Street BBQ, Queen of Sheba (Ethiopian, best in town!). <br />Tasty and Sons, Pok Pok Noi, Por Que No, Grain & Gristle, Widmer Brewery & Mint are close by. <br />Many eclectic and highly regarded','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-1542659/original/f21d98aa-3fbd-47ed-a191-7b3dcbddee15.jpg',2722503,26,'45.5425','-122.66028',1,5,2.00,2.00,4.00,185.00,2,1125,368,4.91,1542659),(117,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1560267','Pearl District Private Suite','A large, bright bedroom/bathroom suite above a two-car garage that allows guests to park off the street. The unit is across a private courtyard from a townhouse, all part of a  rectangular building with 14 townhouses in a vibrant neighborhood abutting Portland\'s downtown commercial and cultural districts. Guests come and go through the garage rather than through the owners\' townhouse, affording privacy to the guests and the owner.','The Pearl District is a reconstructed industrial area, close to downtown Portland. Old buildings have been renovated. New ones have been built. It is well-planned with multiple parks. It has become a destination area for shopping, eating, and wandering.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/23769036/cc0208d6_original.jpg',2655510,2,'45.52894','-122.68338',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,105.00,2,1125,678,4.97,1560267),(118,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1584433','Historic Northwest Portland Home','Cute NW 23rd home with guest bedroom and bathroom for rent. Walking distance to bakeries, coffee shops and breweries. Only a 1/2 mile from Forest Park. Easy access to bus and streetcar lines. A great spot to enjoy the amenities of Portland!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/37047065/c0940c46_original.jpg',8441694,27,'45.53822','-122.69943',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,120.00,2,730,108,4.85,1584433),(119,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1625075','Sellwood Garden Studio pet friendly','The 400 sq ft Studio sits in the middle of a garden and backs up to Sellwood  Park. Best location in Sellwood with the Willamette River & Springwater Bike Trail out the door. A stand alone private studio-with sun & light, NOT a basement. Downtown Portland is just 15 minutes away via Orange Max line or use Uber or ride a Bike!','Sellwood is a nice neighborhood on the Willamette River. It has several parks, and access to the popular Springwater Bike trail.<br />Walkable and friendly with shops and restaurants and easy access to downtown. It is called Sleepy Sellwood but is quickly being discovered!<br />New York Times just listed it as one of the top 50 places to visit!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/101121397/43323027_original.jpg',1178070,20,'45.46711','-122.6597',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,150.00,30,1125,421,4.86,1625075),(120,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1641735','Zen Suite Private Bath-Alberta Arts','Cozy home just blocks away from the funky Alberta Arts District.  You have your own floor complete with bed, desk, and private bath.  Great coffee, restaurants, and microbreweries all by foot! For visiting other areas, public transport is breeze!','We live 10 minutes walking from the Alberta District-one of the funkiest and hippest neighborhoods in Portland.  Tons of top notch restaurants and cheap eats (including a fun food cart pod).  We also are only 4 blocks from McMenamins Kennedy School which houses a movie theater, 3 restaurants, 5 bars, music, and a soaking pool!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b7842e9f-eb28-49a8-80d1-e2501a67c1e6.jpg',8703941,1,'45.56696','-122.63339',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,73.00,30,1125,57,4.89,1641735),(121,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1641774','Walk to OHSU/15-min drive to Intel. Pristine Room!','CHOOSE A ROOM! Private BATH? Monthly STAYS: ●GreenRM+Priv Bath $1700... ●ClassicRM or ●PristineRM ea w Private Vanity $1400...<br />●TREETOPBonusRM above Garage $1250 ... ●Easy/Quiet: Small BDRM adjacent Bath. $1250. HOME: Well-maintained Clean, Upscale, nestled in the Hills above DT. Near OHSU. Scenic location that feels miles out yet located a 5-minute drive from heart of DT Portland. Mature Guests ONLY. All Guests shall sign House Rules','Q\'s, please ASK! Airbnb allows only 24hrs for Q\'s. Do I RESERVE OR NOT?  <br />GREAT space for those wanting to be near OHSU or the VA! Doing a Medical Rotation? Hiking Trails/Parks.<br />MONTHLY STAYS Only. ASK! <br />NO Smoking, drugs, pot, pets, drama in or within 200 feet of this Home. <br />Clean Healthy Home<br />UPON YOUR ARRIVAL: Meet Jenna/Go thru basic rules. Mature responsible working individuals. <br />Thank you','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-1641774/original/aca72ce9-ba6a-40db-976c-7a31bc05be6a.jpeg',3190134,31,'45.48784','-122.69288',2,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,60.00,30,90,1,5.00,1641774),(122,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1650401','Sunny and family friendly - just off Hawthorne!','Beautiful Hawthorne space filled with skylights. Provides a great reprieve with the pitter patter of rain during the stormy months, and sunshine streaming in on a breezy summer day.','Family friendly, walkable neighborhood with many parks, restaurants, bars, bookstores, shopping, etc.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/23726255/c0d8367e_original.jpg',1178421,8,'45.51155','-122.61581',1,3,1.00,0.00,3.00,50.00,30,90,459,4.91,1650401),(123,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1651319','Charming home in great NE location','Enjoy your visit or longer stay in Portland in this cute, open-floor plan 1950s one-story home in the lovely Woodlawn neighborhood.<br />There are several places to walk to, including the local and popular Breakside Brewery, FireHouse (great for dates!), Woodlawn coffee shop, and a park with movies in summer. Walk just a few more blocks and you\'ll find more restaurants including Tough Luck (open late), Tamale Boy, Ranch Pizza, and more.<br /><br />Quick access to the rest of Stumptown!','The lovely Woodlawn neighborhood is expanding rapidly with new businesses and families. Right around the corner is Breakside Brewery, Good Neighbor Pizza, Woodlawn coffee shop, Firehouse, The Non-Profit Oregon Public House (beer profits go to charity), Tamale Boy, Ps & Qs Market & Cafe, Tough Luck & many more.  Woodlawn Movement provides yoga and martial arts classes, as well as massages and body work. Also around the corner is a lovely park with a jungle gym and basketball courts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fd09ce8d-9be7-4d24-aad6-227db187588b.jpg',8017624,45,'45.57014','-122.65646',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,3,200,74,4.96,1651319),(124,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1661004','Charming Irvington Cottage - historic neighborhood','Private, Bright, spacious, guesthouse in historic neighborhood is walking distance to grocery, coffee shops and more plus lots of great take out and food delivery options! Great for visiting nearby family, or a vacation getaway. Close-in to shops and restaurants, plus bike share rental, MAX & Streetcar all just blocks away. Features private, beautifully appointed interior, pro kitchen and memory foam beds. Outdoor patio seating, grassy yard, fruit trees. Access to 2nd floor is by ships-ladder.','Irvington is a historic neighborhood in Portland, OR. It is filled with beautiful tree-lined streets, sidewalks for jogging or meandering about. Beautiful historic century old homes abound and gardens in the spring, summer and fall overflow with flowers, fruit trees and shady big oaks, maples and evergreens.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-1661004/original/ab2074b5-2dc5-4bf4-8338-5e85fded6f7f.jpeg',4426731,7,'45.53847','-122.65533',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,104.00,2,30,317,4.89,1661004),(125,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1665757','Cosy Basement Apt on East Mt Tabor! City Permitted','Warm & spacious basement apt. accessed thru house garage. Comfy antique 4 poster full bed in master bedroom, full bed in living room, full bathroom, big living room w/kitchenette (NOT full kitchen): small fridge, toaster oven, microwave, tea & coffee pot. Heat/cooling separate from main house.  <br />Lockbox w/key for arrival. Free internet.<br />Apt entrance is awkward-  extra door added for covid safety, so it’s tight on the way in/out. <br />No T. V., pets/smoking/scents. <br />Laundry in apt<br />Enjoy the garden!','Our neighborhood is beautiful! Feels more like country than city. Peaceful, walking distance to public transportation and many restaurants and shops and best of all on the side of Mount Tabor, a beautiful park on an extinct volcano!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3b4a2a66-f6ee-45f8-8108-5ae41efd9d5e.jpg',4243978,15,'45.50829','-122.58815',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,75.00,5,180,250,4.79,1665757),(126,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1682154','Beautifully remodeled house in Beaumont-Wilshire','Located on a quiet block in the Beaumont-Wilshire neighborhood, this newly remodeled bungalow is thoughtfully designed and furnished with everything you will need for a comfortable stay in Portland. Enjoy climate control in every room, blazing fast wifi, comfortable bedding and a Japanese-style walk-in shower and soaking tub. Walking  distance to Wilshire Park, The Kennedy School, New Seasons and the Alberta and Killingsworth business districts.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTY4MjE1NA%3D%3D/original/1e50db47-557d-4520-be2c-03fb0ddd0859.jpeg',84148,46,'45.55587','-122.62896',1,8,1.50,3.00,5.00,156.00,5,180,2,5.00,1682154),(127,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1703888','Cool tiny home near wooded park, transit, dining','A sweet retreat in the heart of a walkable, bikeable neighborhood, just steps away from a 170-acre forested park and a transit stop. The little purple house is a great home-base for exploring the city, and a wonderful place to savor time alone or with one close friend.  Shops and nightlife are 0.5 miles away on Hawthorne and Division streets, or stay home with coffee beans and linen bedding.  There are substantial discounts for stays of 30+ days -- put in your exact dates for an exact price.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/24807734/33510aac_original.jpg',8036326,15,'45.51064','-122.60206',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,31,93,128,4.94,1703888),(128,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1728844','Hawthorne Hideaway: center of SE','Welcome! Eco-friendly, newly-renovated 1 bedroom garden apartment located  in the heart of Portlandia: the Hawthorne/Belmont neighborhood. Be in the middle of it all and walk to restaurants, theaters, coffee, shopping.  ','You\'ll be in the heart of Southeast Portland.  Your place is in the desirable neighborhood of Sunnyside, between the commercial streets of Hawthorne and Belmont.  These two quintessentially Portland corridors are filled with local restaurants, shops, and grocery stores. Within 5 blocks you have Portland institutions such as Stumptown Coffee, Powells Books, and the Baghdad Theatre. A 10 minute walk north takes you to Laurelhurst Park, designed by Frederick Law Olmsted, of New York Central Park and Prospect Park fame.  A 10 minute walk south will take to the Division Street corridor with Pok Pok, Salt and Straw and a booming restaurant scene.  ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/31483451/4e90a829_original.jpg',9110094,16,'45.5131','-122.62704',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,310,311,31,4.76,1728844),(129,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1732272','Hollywood One Bedroom Home','Located on the edge of Hollywood and Rose City Park. The neighborhood is quite with households of families and working professionals. The #12 bus line and the Hollywood Max serve the neighborhood and downtown. You are just two miles from city center if you follow Sandy Blvd.','Hollywood and Rose City are well established neighborhoods.  Food and shopping are close by and if you wander into Sandy and head north you will soon come to the Laurelwood Public House and Brewery, Hogan\'s Goat Pizza, Cabezon Fish Restaurant, Case Study Coffee, and the Bake Shop.  You might also like to try the food cart pod just steps beyond the brewery.  Heading down Sandy you will find Killer Burger and Hot Lips Pizza on the corner at 47th. Continuing down Sandy into the heart of Hollywood you will come to Sizzle Pie, Chimcking, Reo\'s Ribs and other alternatives to fast food. If you are more interested in cooking, Trader Joe\'s, Whole Foods, and the Hollywood Farmers Market (on Saturdays) are just a short walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/110083542/153555f0_original.jpg',102666,11,'45.54172','-122.61113',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,96.00,3,14,96,4.96,1732272),(130,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1751672','NE Portland Craftsman 3 bdrm','This elegant three bedroom, two-and-a-half bathroom fully furnished craftsman home in Northeast Portland\'s desirable Beaumont Village neighborhood has the amenities you\'re looking for in an excellent location on a quiet neighborhood street.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTc1MTY3Mg%3D%3D/original/6bbc390e-623f-4d64-91d3-bef483553e05.jpeg',4912906,11,'45.5443','-122.61122',1,6,2.50,3.00,3.00,233.00,3,28,7,5.00,1751672),(131,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1826250','Urban Garden Studio','Experience the best Portland has to offer from a private studio in a lush, backyard garden. Our beautiful, eco-home on a quiet street is conveniently located in Southeast Portland\'s best and most walkable neighborhood.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/26000793/16e7fd68_original.jpg',2592211,8,'45.50769','-122.62844',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,72.00,30,90,162,4.93,1826250),(132,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1851090','Inn Off Hawthorne','Cozy and elegant three-bedroom.  A great HOME base to explore the entire funky Southeast side.  After an extensive remodel and renewal this home is finally back!! Yay! Convenient to take in Hawthorne, Belmont and Division Districts by foot with public transit in all directions just two blocks away.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7a0393e4-5676-48ed-8fda-d94e881128dc.jpg',4966686,16,'45.51256','-122.62489',1,6,2.00,3.00,3.00,125.00,30,730,36,5.00,1851090),(133,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1851145','Hawthorne/Division Beautiful Suite','Beautiful newly remodeled space for 2 in great walkable neighborhood close to tons of wonderful restaurants and shopping. This garden level apartment is very comfortable and beautifully furnished and decorated. We follow all Covid Cleaning protocols for yours and our safety.','We are walking distance to just about anything a person can need, and yet our street is quiet. We have wonderful neighbors and our neighborhood is VERY safe.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-1851145-unapproved/original/38567505-92e8-47f6-9e45-3ec3f03593b7.JPEG',3379729,8,'45.50933','-122.61885',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,30,304,4.96,1851145),(134,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1856414','Comfortable Hip Downtown Loft','Walking score 98. This bright spacious, centrally located, nicely decorated loft is in downtown Portland, it is an excellent place to experience what our amazing city has to offer.  The loft is steps away from the Portland street car, Portland Art Museum, Portland State University, Farmers Market, numerous restaurants and shops.  My Loft is available 31 nights or longer. It is perfect for an extended stay or business traveler.','The unit is in a great location. Close to Portland State University.  Walk out the front door and in minutes you can walk to Pioneer Square, Jen-Weld Field and watch a Timbers game, or to one of the many fantastic dining establishment in the area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/43825879/9f5fad5e_original.jpg',5907304,44,'45.51462','-122.68498',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,65.00,30,1125,86,4.87,1856414),(135,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1880649','Cozy/Modern Casita','Our cool and cozy little abode has everything you need for your getaway. Sleeps two to four comfortably has a great little kitchen ( no dishwasher ) and a full bath. Nestled in and off the street,  just blocks from Johnson Creek and The Spring Water Trail.','Eastmoreland is a very charming and quiet neighborhood. It is within walking distance to Sellwood and the Woodstock neighborhoods. A quarter mile from Reed College. It is close to many parks and trails. If a peaceful experience is what your after then this is the right place. The light rail Max station is one mile from the casita. It is the orange line that will take you all over town.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/40041113/6aa4fd88_original.jpg',9319397,47,'45.4643','-122.62437',1,3,1.00,1.00,3.00,95.00,30,1125,242,4.93,1880649),(136,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1887261','Clean, private suite w/garden entry','This bright, basement-level suite in Piedmont is a restful spot to enjoy while visiting Portland! It’s part of my home, located between Airport and Downtown, near public transportation, with free street parking, bike routes, groceries and other conveniences.<br /><br />We are powered by green energy, strive for a small carbon footprint, have organic garden, patio, fruit trees, veggie beds, herbs and flowers. I love hosting stays! I\'m around if you need me and leave the amount of interaction up to you.','Piedmont is a typical North Portland neighborhood filled with bungalows from a variety of eras and a variety of wonderful neighbors. You\'ll find some great resources in walking distance from the suite, and it\'s a short drive or bus trip to the popular Mississippi and Alberta Arts districts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1686f501-fd5b-4a76-acbb-8c7da93340b4.jpg',2916925,48,'45.57657','-122.67554',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,83.00,2,29,71,4.92,1887261),(137,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1917726','Northeast Portland Studio with Private Entrance','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/27882282/1959afbf_original.jpg',9943209,11,'45.52764','-122.60969',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,73.00,30,30,619,4.94,1917726),(138,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2003568','Historic Irvington Basement Apt','Transportation: <br /> 4 blkMAX rail: http://ride.trimet.org/?tool=routes&find=90#/<br />Street car: http://trimet.org/streetcar/index.htm<br />1 block to Bus stop/ schedule: http://trimet.org/schedules/r077.htm  - Bus #77<br />Uber: https://www.uber.com/cities/portland','Pedestrial friendly and within minutes of downtown Portland.  There are cafes, shops, wine shops, boutiques, etc. within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6c623f45-2483-4d18-96bb-d8d9c9c92944.jpg',3519465,4,'45.53456','-122.64903',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,30,365,97,4.88,2003568),(139,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2020429','Modern Apt. Close in SE, LOCATION!','Our private entrance, lower level suite is newly remodeled with a spa shower, calming hues, organic linens, down comforter, queen bed, and kitchen (plus Free WIFI). It comfortably sleeps two, and is centrally located in close-in SE Portland.  Just walk around the corner to rose gardens, shopping, brunch, you name it!','We are located in the heart of SE just a few blocks from food carts and shopping on hawthorne.  The famous rose gardens in Ladd\'s addition. Across the street from Apex brewery and around the corner from Pine State Biscuit. On Saturday night you can walk across the street to Double Dragon.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/76022954-d0ff-4b05-9c6b-1024a2044a0d.jpg',10385699,25,'45.50453','-122.65446',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,101.00,30,1125,338,4.84,2020429),(140,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2020615','Sellwood Detached Studio Loft','Self contained cozy yet bright studio apt located above our garage in the heart of charming Sellwood!  Though no interaction is required, hosts are close-by and available as needed!  Steps away from shops, restaurants, coffee, bars, parks, trails, and the river.  Within a few miles of both Reed and Lewis and Clark Colleges. You will have all the privacy you need in this detached unit!  Sleeps 2-4.','Lively and friendly neighborhood bursting with great restaurants, bars, coffee shops, boutiques, antiques stores, etc.  Within 1-2 blocks you will find Grand Central Bakery, New Seasons Market, Starbucks, Gino\'s Italian Restaurant and Bar, Bottle Shop Wine Bar, and Either/Or Coffee!   Just a few more blocks away and you\'ll be able to enjoy Jade, Espiritu, Reverends BBQ, A Cena, the Library, killer Food Carts, and Blue Kangaroo Coffee!  To retreat to the beauty of nature, we are just 5 blocks away from Sellwood Park, the Willamette River, the Sellwood Bluff, and the peaceful wooded trails of Oaks Bottom for hikes or trail runs. Cyclists can rent bikes at Sellwood Cycles (2 blocks away) and make our place the start of long rides down the Springwater Trail, or get mountain bikes for use in more remote locations, including Sandy Ridge, a nationally recognized mountain bike trail network.  We are 1.5 hrs away from glorious Mt Hood, and 2 hours away from the beauty of the Oregon coast.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/82762398/2bfcf936_original.jpg',10386316,20,'45.46587','-122.65336',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,60.00,2,35,518,4.91,2020615),(141,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2033589','Cozy Room Near Airport, Alberta','Cozy room for a good night\'s sleep.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/46143861/ad09eb30_original.jpg',10438539,21,'45.56069','-122.59966',2,2,1.00,2.00,1.00,40.00,1,7,547,4.74,2033589),(142,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2038802','2 story, 2 bath Downtown View Condo','Long term rental. Secure keyless entry building w/2 gas fireplaces on each level. Minutes from Pioneer Sq, PSU, Art Museum, Saturday Market, South Park. Great city views.  Queen size memory foam bed.  Open floor plan.  All new modern furniture.  Near Safeway store.  Portland Streetcar stop near by.','Great restaurants within walking distance; Art Museum one block away along with Portland State University; South Park; Starbucks; Safeway grocery store across the street.  Pioneer Square about 4-5 blocks away; Portland Street car is nearby, so it is reliable transportation.  Portland Saturday Market one block away at Portland State University.  All of Portland downtown area readily accessible.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0ea98e2a-6d09-4be9-adb1-fd23b1d9ae65.jpg',2687437,44,'45.51564','-122.6844',1,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,115.00,30,1125,171,4.94,2038802),(143,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2101856','Cute Overlook Studio Cottage','Private studio cottage central to public transportation, restaurants, bars, shopping and several parks. 3/4 bathroom, queen-size bed, kitchenette with mini fridge, coffee maker, toaster oven, and microwave. Great neighborhood with free street parking.','This space is in the perfect location to explore Portland.  North and Northeast Portland are known for awesome bars, restaurants, specialty shops, and our home is right in the middle of it all.  Our neighborhood is full of great little shops, markets and restaurants for Thai, Asian, Mexican and Ethiopian food, dive bars, fancy bars, hipster bars, the hipster grocery store, the local fresh produce market, a Dr. Who themed British pub, sushi, a Buffalo wings place that serves meat and vegan wings, food carts, several coffee shops, the smallest park in Portland which houses a community theater space, Portland Community College, all within 3-10 minutes walking distance.  <br /><br />We are easy on/off of I-5, and a great neighborhood full of parks, bike lanes, and entertainment. <br /><br />Our neighborhood is friendly, diverse, and full of interesting places to see and things to do.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-2101856/original/90d0dcc2-f448-421b-9914-4529d83f8521.jpeg',729625,13,'45.56142','-122.68037',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,59.00,1,29,741,4.91,2101856),(144,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2241274','Modern Artistic Three Bedroom Bungalow','A 1920s Grant Park bungalow with a contemporary interior that sits one block from Hale Pele, the 2019 tiki bar of the year and 5 minutes to a nearby Voodoo Doughnuts. This 3BR bungalow has a fully stocked kitchen on the first floor and the second floor features a master BR with bathroom.<br /><br />This home is centrally located (10-15 minutes) from anything you want to do in Portland.<br /><br />--> Note: My home has a friendly, quiet, small cat. Her food and water are taken care of while you are here.','Grant Park is central to virtually all things Portland. It is a quieter neighborhood within a 3 minute walk to restaurants on NE Broadway, a 20 minute walk to Laurelhurst or a 5 minute car drive to Alberta Street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f5cf5084-ecb1-4c32-ba41-bdbd5717ace4.jpg',11446106,33,'45.53638','-122.63538',1,6,2.00,3.00,0.00,0.00,2,7,28,4.86,2241274),(145,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2243045','Enjoy Living Right on the Riverfront!  2b/2b','Enjoy a glass of wine on the deck as you watch the boats float by and the ducks on the Marina.  Watch or join the runners, walkers and bikes pedal by as they enjoy the Willamette Greenway path down below.<br />Master bedroom is loft style with a queen size bed bathroom, and large private deck with expansive view of the river and 2 bridges.  <br />Kitchen stocked. All linens included, Washer/Dryer. Second bedroom; queen size bed with detached bathroom and a Spectacular river/bridge view. Sleeps 5. 1 pet','Walk along the waterfront to restaurants, Chinese Garden for tea, light rail or streetcar all over Portland to museums, theater & opera.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5bc7d086-e6d0-4444-9cb5-967c2cb0d589.jpg',11456606,43,'45.52593','-122.67209',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,115.00,30,1125,22,4.50,2243045),(146,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2281775','1 Bed Apt W/Laundry. Close to Moda & Convention','Super central and clean hideaway in N.E. Portland\'s Irvington/Lloyd Center neighborhood. <br /><br />This cozy apartment lives under our brownstone home, with it\'s own entrance, free wifi, queen bed, washer/dryer and kitchen appliances. <br /><br />Street parking is easy, no restrictions or permits required! <br /><br />We have many guests in town to attend an event at the convention or the Moda Center, if that’s you, we are under one mile from both, and three blocks from the bus that takes you there!','Nestled in the classic and charming Irvington  neighborhood and close to many shops, restaurants as well as major business centers, this apartment sits in a great spot to serve as a hub for any Portland getaway. If you’re looking for a place to stay during your work trip, we are one mile from the convention center and Moda and a half mile from Doubletree.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/38485236/68bc95a5_original.jpg',829833,7,'45.53646','-122.65738',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,69.00,1,28,676,4.87,2281775),(147,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2291626','Private Haven-private bath&entrance','Spacious master bedroom with private bath, entrance & deck; easy access to transportation, walking distance to N Williams, N Mississippi, The Pearl, Rose Quarter/Convention Center, east side amenities, & Emanuel Hospital.<br />All are welcome! airbnb.com/rooms/2291626?s=51','Eliot neighborhood is full of popular dining establishments, coffee shops, music venues, parks, and the Matt Dishman community center with in-door swimming pool.  This is a great close-in Portland community with access to everything you need. <br />Several places for live music include the Secret Society, White Eagle Saloon, Wonder Ballroom and, of course, the Rose Garden Moda Center.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-2291626/original/ad2ca945-1a80-426f-932b-8c312280a193.jpeg',5229526,26,'45.54215','-122.66578',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,2,28,570,4.87,2291626),(148,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2349023','Victorian haven. Fun, walkable N Williams location','Gorgeous, one of a kind Victorian in the heart of Williams/Mississippi District. Smack in the center of entertainment, shops & parks - an incredible walking neighborhood close to both airport and riverfront.<br /><br />High ceilings, natural light, large deck and room to spread out for lounging, cooking or gatherings. The spacious living area is designed with simple, fun furnishings and make both work and play so enjoyable you’ll want to stay longer. <br /><br />Fully appointed sunny kitchen, gas range.','Smack in the center of the Williams District with a private, gated yard, this is one of the most popular neighborhoods in Portland. <br /><br />Award winning restaurants, food carts, shops, yoga studios, gyms, laundry, art galleries, parks, playgrounds New Seasons market and even a local hardware store are steps to a short walk away. You are next to a wonderful wine bar and across the street from one of the best brewpubs.<br /><br />And a few blocks from Mississippi Ave with even more shops, restaurants and eclectic spots and a half hour walk or short bus ride to Alberta Street. <br />Two miles to the Convention Center or Willamette River and less to the Moda  There are several different frequent stop bus lines that run along Williams Ave and a bike rental corral steps from the front gate. <br /><br />Seven miles or a twenty minute ride to PDX, our wonderful airport and a five minute drive to the I-5 Interstate entrance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-2349023/original/a18ce3fa-c5c3-432b-839b-f136a5256ea6.jpeg',11995752,9,'45.55194','-122.66569',1,5,1.50,2.00,3.00,173.00,2,28,31,5.00,2349023),(149,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2360923','Bright Wooded Apartment SW Portland','This private 1BR apartment in a quiet SW neighborhood provides a sanctuary from the City.  Its 800 sq ft features a private entry, your own deck, large bathroom, fully-equipped kitchen and living area. Clean and modern, with views overlooking the woods. It\'s just 5 miles to downtown Portland.','My area has a wooded, rural feel to it... don\'t expect sidewalks and manicured lawns.  There are woods and a creek in back.  It\'s a mile from a 600 acre state park with hiking trails.  It\'s close Lewis and Clark College, Tryon Creek State Park, and Lake Oswego, with all its beauty and amenities/restaurants and shops.  And a very easy five miles to downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-2360923/original/8623d987-6cea-4c6a-acc3-8803a2b4bef0.jpeg',3521268,49,'45.45718','-122.68622',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,7,31,26,4.88,2360923),(150,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2390685','Portland Tiny House','Welcome to Portland Tiny House! Featured in Airbnb Magazine, this cozy home is located in the Alberta Arts District, just steps away from award-winning restaurants, cafés, bars, art galleries, and shopping. You can reserve time at the Kennedy School soaking pool or catch a movie at their theater, enjoy a craft cocktail at Expatriate, take a yoga class at People’s Yoga, or shop locally at New Seasons Market. This is one of Portland’s most popular spots to make your home base for a memorable stay.','The house is a quick walk to the locally-sourced New Seasons Market and the Alberta Arts District. Walk one block for hand-crafted coffee at Extracto or a cocktail at Expatriate . Soak in the Kennedy School hot tub or take a class at People’s Yoga.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/101508624/1e1aaef5_original.jpg',2333787,1,'45.56464','-122.63583',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,76.00,2,28,831,4.97,2390685),(151,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2407080','Luxury Modern Newer Townhouse w/view in the hills','Gorgeous LUXURY  townhome in the beautiful west hills. Less than 3 miles to the center of downtown  tucked away in the hills over looking the city this  3000 Sq ft home has 3 br 2.5 ba + office+ oversized 2 car garage and nice private backyard with trees,  fountain,  and natural gas powered BBQ . You wont be disappointed! minimum 60 day rental.','Newer subdivision of very upscale homes. Mountain views and abundance of nature.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-2407080/original/617d6f22-438a-47e9-a191-896d0207dfee.jpeg',12272370,50,'45.52335739135742','-122.74468231201172',1,6,2.50,3.00,4.00,259.00,60,365,1,5.00,2407080),(152,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2440738','Laurelhurst Loft above the trees!','Entire 3rd floor, perched high in the trees of a beautifully restored vintage  building! Skylights and windows make this open loft feel bright and airy.  Quiet location within walking distance of Portland\'s finest coffeeshops, restaurants, and parks.','The Laurelhurst Loft is located in a quiet neighborhood and in a quiet building. This is an area known for its many high quality restaurants and eateries - descriptions are provided in the guidebook. All are easy walking distance from the loft. There is simple access to downtown Portland via the Tri-Met number 20 bus line.  Beautiful Laurelhurst Park is 4 blocks away - deep shade trees, grass-covered areas, a pond, walking paths.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/32387999/4135ddf1_original.jpg',8927355,12,'45.5218391418457','-122.63525390625',1,3,1.00,1.00,4.00,65.00,2,60,508,4.90,2440738),(153,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2458957','Alberta Arts Hideaway','Comfortable, cozy, clean. High ceilings and open spaces give this remodeled vintage Portland home has  a modern, airy feel. The house is all yours, no shared walls, ceilings, or floors. Addti that, off-street parking for two. Perfectly located on a quiet street adjacent to the thriving Alberta St., an easy and enjoyable walk to restaurants, bars, boutiques, galleries, and more. Close to North Williams Street corridor and the much-loved Mississippi St. A very easy 12 minute drive from downtown.','Alberta Arts is at the heart of Portland’s legendary indie business community. It’s a mile-long stretch of originality where you can buy a vintage skirt for $10 around the corner from a rare book shop that sells first editions for thousands. It’s where now-famous chefs became famous and where baristas get in shape for international competitions.<br /><br />If you want to try all of the great restaurants, bars, cafés, food carts and coffeeshops of Alberta Arts, you’ll need to stay a month. But if you don’t have that long, don’t worry. We can give you a short list of musts.  Here are a few highlights, for your Googling pleasure: Beast, Pine State Biscuits, Ciao Vito, Barista, Aviary, Salt & Straw Ice Cream, Pok Pok Noi (not technically on Alberta, but only a 13 minute walk).<br /><br />Alberta Street is home to Last Thursday, a monthly street festival that closes the street for a few hours in the evening for gallery hopping, live music, people-watching, fire dancing, street art and perfo','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-2458957/original/8a68257f-3f9a-42de-b0c2-4bef4ce7b27e.jpeg',12483794,14,'45.55619','-122.65703',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,145.00,2,120,192,4.88,2458957),(154,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2460265','Modern condo in heart of Downtown','Spacious, airy, loft-like, large true one bedroom.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjQ2MDI2NQ%3D%3D/original/9faa6e1f-013e-4e9e-80f0-e3cc820461b5.jpeg',12579841,44,'45.51622','-122.68524',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,31,180,26,4.96,2460265),(155,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2545810','Fully Restored 4-Level Grand Craftsman','1906 Craftsman, fully remodeled, furnished, decorated, outdoor living room & dining area with grill & smoker, huge front porch, stainless gourmet kitchen, formal dining & living rooms, Jacuzzi bathtub (no exterior hot tub), attic loft with four skylights, original woodwork and built-ins, basement theater, two fiber Wifi works, central location minutes to downtown & numerous neighborhood entertainment and retail areas.','The Piedmont neighborhood is an historic area boasting easy access to other popular Portland neighborhoods such as Humboldt, Alberta, Arbor Lodge, Boise, Eliot, Mississippi and Kenton. Piedmont runs alongside the Max light rail train allowing for a convenient commuting to downtown Portland and other Portland neighborhoods. Downtown by car is five - ten minutes in most traffic situations and by bike is about twenty-five minutes. I-5 is easily accessed as it runs adjacent to the neighborhood.<br /><br />Please visit the interactive Guide Book at the bottom of this profile to review all of the nearby attractions and services to accommodate your stay.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/35399531/85cc72c7_original.jpg',13032937,48,'45.5683','-122.66523',1,5,1.50,2.00,2.00,450.00,3,1125,63,4.89,2545810),(156,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2546099','Sunny spot on N. Mississippi Ave.','Sunny 1 BD apt. in the center of Historic Mississippi Neighborhood. This 2nd story corner apt. has great street views. Vintage 1930\'s era fixtures with a mix of mid century furniture make this apartment a peaceful retreat from the vibrant street.','The Mississippi District is diverse and lively. There are many independent shops, restaurants, bars and even a large natural foods supermarket (New Seasons) within walking distance on N. Williams, a street filled with bars, restaurants, and shops... The Alberta Arts District is also nearby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-2546099/original/276213a1-6fb1-4aec-8ead-dfe2ba45448b.jpeg',5074035,9,'45.55228','-122.6758',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,31,180,234,4.86,2546099),(157,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2559470','\"The Portland Purple House\" 2','The Space, Clean from ceiling to floor.<br />Centrally located in the N.E. Portland. In the Rose City area and Minutes to Downtown by Max, or Trimet. Close to the Moda Center, Convention center, Expo center, 205 fwy to Vancouver, Washington, or south to Lake Oswego, Beaverton.','My neighborhood is very \"Portland\" coffee bars, little family owned fooderies, like Ottos, Fire on the Mountain a phone call away. <br />Very quiet, family owned homes, with pride in ownership and pet happy people.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-2559470/original/21b4d64e-a5bd-4845-8f16-9c63514ccc06.jpg',5707629,39,'45.55121','-122.59294',2,2,1.00,2.00,2.00,125.00,2,7,30,4.53,2559470),(158,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2569391','Portland-1000sf basement apt./queen','Located in the Arbor Lodge neighborhood of Portland Oregon- our comfortable home offers guests the entire finished basement: queen bed, living room, full kitchen, full bath, pool table, ping pong and a gas fireplace in the bedroom. Our location is close to all our fabulous city of Portland offers.','Our home sits on a quiet, safe, tree-lined street and is close to almost everything.  At the end of the block is Arbor Lodge Park with plenty of space to roam and two lighted tennis courts (we have rackets you can borrow).  A short drive (10 minutes can take you almost anywhere in metro Portland) will take you to historic St. Johns, Kenton, the Alberta Arts district, Mississippi area, Fremont, PDX downtown, and more.  Throughout Portland, there are numerous brewpubs, restaurants, shops, and more.  Also, the Expo Center and Convention Center are right up the road.  And, if you like to stroll, these places are within a short walking distance to our home:<br />- 1/2 mile to the Max train line that can take you to downtown Portland, the Expo or Convention Center, the airport, or throughout the metro area.<br />- 1/4 mile to our local Thai, Mexican, or sushi restaurant.  There is also a unique coffee hut, doughnut shop, and a take out pizza establishment.<br />- 1/2 mile to our local sports','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f494a1eb-85b4-4a01-ba86-b52437f3421d.jpg',12807678,51,'45.57134','-122.68781',1,5,1.00,1.00,1.00,94.00,1,90,728,4.86,2569391),(159,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2575775','Walk to Se Division from a Sleek, Architect Designed Space','My wife, Raechel, and I originally designed and built this ADU ( accessory dwelling unit ) with the intention of living there full time, but due to a change of plans, it\'s available to you. The space was designed by Buckenmeyer Architecture, and was constructed by me. <br /><br />Our space features many unique elements such as: paper-composite counter tops and bathroom tiles, real copper backsplash and bathroom walls, polished concrete floors, cedar tongue and groove ceiling, burnt cedar siding, 16\' multi-slide window wall (please open and close slowly), moveable cedar slat screens, custom frosted glass pocket doors, and custom apple-ply kitchen cabinets by George Ramos<br /><br />We love to cook and put great effort into getting the kitchen space dialed in. The kitchen features: bosch speed oven (microwave and convection oven), bosch dishwasher, 2 burner gas range, and Pull-out exhaust and lighting<br /><br />We hope you enjoy the space and neighborhood as much as we do!<br /><br />Th','Nearby Division Steet is known as restaurant row and features some of the best food in Portland, including Pok Pok, Salt and Straw, and Ava Genes. On a warm summer night, there will be hundreds of people just going for a stroll up and down Division.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-2575775/original/0c8a9707-8bb3-402d-9f38-c02650efe6d5.jpeg',7409866,25,'45.50754','-122.63693',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,108.00,1,90,353,4.97,2575775),(160,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2578371','Sky Cabin, Modern Loft, Cozy, Clean','This light filled open concept Cabin in the Sky melts together the elements of nature, a touch of western spunk with the comforts and design of raw modernism. Blocks from the hub of North Portland’s food district, our Max Line. We love dogs and have a fully fenced backyard.  This is the second floor of a duplex property.  Guest will have entire unit.','EAT. WALK. ENJOY CULTURE. DISCOVER SOMETHING NEW. These are the things we love about our neighborhood. We think you\'ll fall in love with these same things that makes our neighborhood special. We are just a few walk-able blocks from beautiful parks (big and small), library, breweries, food carts, vintage clothing, live music, galleries, farmers market, some of the best bars and restaurants in Portland, yoga studios, massage/acupuncture clinics, coffee shops and much more. A quick bike ride will take you to Alberta Arts District, Emanuel Hospital, the Addis World Headquarters, Downtown Portland, and much more. PLUS we have big trees, clean air, and happy people in our little neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/90a13c33-56cd-4e33-bb92-8d99b24583a3.jpg',1483711,24,'45.56066','-122.67662',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,88.00,30,180,18,5.00,2578371),(161,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2636510','Modern Oasis in St Johns, Portland','Super convenient location.  Stunning views and walking access to Resturants, Bars, Live Music, Movies, Shopping, Biking, Forest Park, Hiking, Downtown St Johns.  Space has deck, full kitchen.  Great living space to relax.  ','Everything is walking distance!! Movie Theatres(2), multiple Grocery stores, Coffee Shops, Many Resturants and Bars featuring live music, Post Office, Bus Transit Downtown, Cathederal Park, Portlands Famous - Forest Park, St Johns Bridge.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f05b03fe-e93f-4830-b86f-986d73a9d8ea.jpg',13462816,42,'45.58892','-122.75687',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,81.00,30,1125,16,4.87,2636510),(162,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2637543','Mt. Tabor 1 Bdrm Apt. private comfortable and big','Sunlit basement apt. with private entrance. Convenient to MAX train, bus, airport, and Gorge access. Walk to Mt. Tabor park. 5 miles to downtown Portland. Two very nice grocery stores are within walking distance.  <br />The apartment has a kitchenette w/ full-size frig. For ambiance and warmth there is a gas fireplace. Easy on street parking. Excellent location for bicycling anywhere in the city. Many dedicated bike roads and bike lanes.','This is a walking neighborhood safe and friendly. Walking distance to grocery stores, pubs, restaurants, coffee houses, etc.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7f93d805-53fd-4854-9f4a-7a19f13b08ae.jpg',13506616,52,'45.52306','-122.60022',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,365,48,4.83,2637543),(163,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2660141','Portland Bungalow, A Happy House','Newly remodeled, comfortable basement quarters with private bath. Located on a quiet street, near Kennedy School, Alberta, Dekum Triangle and Killingsworth neighborhoods. Your stay will be a pleasant experience. Woman and couples friendly.<br /><br />Check in time is 2:00 pm<br />Check out is 10:00 am','The Vernon/Concordia neighborhoods are truly convenient to Portland\'s vast variety of entertainment. From the beautiful Japanese, Chinese and Rose Gardens to local breweries and top rated restaurants. Portland has it all. The Ocean and the Mountains are an hour and a half away in either direction. Amazing hiking trails and large parks are everywhere. For hikers Portland will offer you miles of trails suitable for all individuals from beginner to experienced. Forest Park, the longest hiking park within a US city will offer you 20 miles of extraordinary adventure. The Columbia Gorge and sites surrounding are must-sees on your visit to Portland. Explore local breweries, coffee shops, world class restaurants. If a quick bite is your goal Little Big Burger is a must; don’t leave without indulging in their french fries. You will truly enjoy your visit and your stay at the \"Little Purple House\".','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-2660141/original/33580e7d-b9c4-4562-a4f6-98df7a975e9e.jpg',2723562,29,'45.56561','-122.64757',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,63.00,2,21,245,5.00,2660141),(164,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2735985','Charming Southeast Portland Private Studio','Lovely private entry one room studio space with King bed and bathroom with a shower. Prime inner SE Portland location close to great coffee, bars, restaurants, shopping and minutes to Revolution Hall and downtown.','Very close to all sorts of amazing food, drink, parks, entertainment, shopping and quick access to downtown.<br /><br />Always good to check out Eater for the latest recommendations - pdx.eater.com<br /><br />Across the street from an arts-focused elementary school and park, family/quiet neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-2735985/original/f97fb86c-5877-4bc5-8795-a9cf94d8101c.jpg',5445817,32,'45.52001','-122.64671',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,86.00,2,1125,361,4.99,2735985),(165,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2919433','Quiet, Private Apartment Retreat','','This SW Portland neighborhood is situated close to land set aside by the Nature Conservancy and makes a nice half hour walk in the neighborhood and then woods. Just down the hill is Terwilliger Blvd., a two lane street with  bike and walking paths which is a favorite jogging route for Portlanders. Off of Terwilliger about one mile from the house there is a nature trail that will make you forget you are anywhere near a city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/37638888/3ed49925_original.jpg',13267370,31,'45.48261','-122.68722',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,145.00,3,1125,277,4.97,2919433),(166,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2950282','Portland Cottage with Kitchenette','Our cottage is in a quiet southwest Portland neighborhood. It includes a pillow top queen size bed, microwave, refrigerator, Keurig coffee maker, toaster oven, 2 burner hotplate, hair dryer, soap & shampoo.  Easy access to I-5 and downtown Portland by car or public transportation.','We are in a quiet neighborhood yet close to all Portland has to offer.  Whether you look for nightlife, restaurants, theater, farmers markets or outdoor activities like hiking, biking and skiing.  Portland has it all!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7ae8741c-d601-4d8b-9fc3-56b7b5cffff9.jpg',10873863,53,'45.448','-122.72277',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,67.00,2,28,639,4.95,2950282),(167,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2975954','Apartment in 1911 craftsman home','Separate entrance, modern interior, full bath, quiet setting, ground floor apartment, induction burner, microwave, small fridge, crib. Walk to coffee roaster, parks, Sunday farmers market, grocery, good restaurants. Three bus lines within 5 blocks.','Family friendly neighborhood. Walk to: Sunday farmers\' market, co-op, grocery store, coffee roaster, tap room and bottle shop, excellent local restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/38235303/d1538ae8_original.jpg',11551162,6,'45.55384','-122.65539',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,125.00,30,1125,119,4.67,2975954),(168,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/2988721','Urban Charm - NW Pearl/Nob Hill','This 1-bdrm Nob Hill condo is located in the heart of one of Portland\'s most vibrant and desirable neighborhoods. Handcrafted coffee, decadent food, pubs/bars, parks, museums, trails, and urban hikes are just all just steps away. 2 blocks to the street car, NW23rd ave, and the Pearl District.','Northwest and the neighboring Pearl District have a little bit of something for everyone. For all you foodies out there, get your refined palate ready for your pick of any cuisine for breakfast, lunch or dinner. Besaw\'s, Cafe Nell, or The Daily Cafe are excellent breakfast/brunch choices, on Sunday\'s the Pink Rose\'s patio is hard to beat with bottomless mimosas and killer scrambles. Laughing planet and Dick\'s Kitchen offer healthy options for the health conscious, kale for days! 23 Hoyt, N45, and Matador are great happy hour spots. And dinner at Cafe Mingo, Serrato, Andina, or Paragon, are sure to deliver a memorable meal and evening.   For the coffee lover, get the best espresso in town at Sister\'s Coffee Company, Lovejoy Bakers, or Sterling Coffee Roasters. And of course there are 100 Starbucks within blocks. <br /><br />For those who prefer to cook their own meals, Trader Joe\'s, Kroger/Fred Meyer, Safeway, Zupans, Whole Foods are in close proximity, with City Market literally across','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5b673775-6f9f-4419-b253-b91b8ece7721.jpg',15239348,27,'45.52983','-122.69503',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,109.00,2,365,129,4.91,2988721),(169,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3011519','Sweet Home/Walk to Bars, Restaurant, Downtown','Hip Buckman Neighborhood home with AC!  Enjoy the large living and dining rooms with friends or family. Perfect backyard for BBQ and front porch for relaxing.  4 big bedrooms so everyone has a quiet, comfortable bed. 2 bedroom are upstairs and 2 bedrooms are in the finished basement. Two large screen TV’s so everyone can watch their favorite shows. Walk to Revolution Hall, rooftop bar, urban winery, brew pubs, bakeries, food carts, restaurants and downtown.','We live in an awesome urban neighborhood with great neighbors. 2 blocks from a school playground, cafe, restaurants and wine bar. Walk downtown in 30 minutes or take the street car (2 blocks to the bus too). We have it all!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b7582be1-9ffb-4882-86ba-26ef5ff05eb6.jpg',15346651,32,'45.5196','-122.64994',1,8,2.50,4.00,0.00,0.00,2,31,21,4.86,3011519),(170,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3059314','420 Friendly: Tiny House Living with A/C','Close to the airport, Alberta, Hollywood, Concordia, and Mississippi Districts, this loft studio is perfect for tiny house living in the city. Queen Tuft & Needle  bed in the loft is reachable via custom-crafted ladder. The main floor has a fully-functional kitchen with a whimsical vintage stove and reclaimed touches. The spacious bathroom includes tub/shower combo with subway tile. The seating area includes room for a queen sofa bed and small dining table - try tiny house living here!','Located in the NE Cully neighborhood adjacent to Concordia, Alberta, and Fremont. I love my \'hood because it feels like the country in the city yet we are so centrally located.<br /><br />Nearby places to explore:<br />-- Alberta Arts: 5 minutes So much to do here! Endless shopping, more coffee, more yummy food, on and on. You could spend a whole day walking around Alberta. Be sure to check out the Last Thursday celebration during the summer months.<br />-- Concordia neighborhood: 5 minutes Here we have New Seasons (a great grocery store with loads of organic/healthy food options), McMenamins Kennedy School (cheap movies, bars, AND a outdoor soaking pool, Common Ground (clothing optional hot tub and sauna), yoga, amazing restaurants like Yakuza, DOC, and Beast (just to name a few). And a fantastic coffee shop: Extracto.<br />-- Downtown: 20 minutes Shopping, dining and breweries plus art, museums and fun!<br />-- Fremont neighborhood: 5 minutes Some attractions are Grand Central Bakery','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5b8af332-ab3a-4433-8581-ea5fb91310f2.jpg',1243625,21,'45.56161','-122.60821',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,75.00,2,28,408,4.89,3059314),(171,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3075414','Modern 2 Bedroom 2 Bath SE Hawthorne House','Cozy and recently renovated house centrally located in SE Portland that is walkable to everything you need.  There are dozens of restaurants, coffee shops and food carts that you can walk to in a few minutes.  Bagdad Theater and Powells books are only two blocks away.  New Seasons and Fred Meyer are also both one block away.  10-min walk to Laurelhurst park and 20-min walk to Mt. Tabor park. Off-street parking space in the driveway.','Southeast Portland is the place to be!  You can easily walk to everything:<br /><br />Convenient to everything you need-<br /><br />-1 Block to Fred Meyer - The largest grocery store in  SE Portland.<br />-1 Block to New Seasons - Portland\'s own version of Whole Foods.<br />-3 Blocks to a 24-hr Walgreens<br /><br />Also nearby-<br /><br />-3 Blocks to Bagdad Theater - Best movie theater in Portland!<br />-3 Blocks to some of the best food carts in SE Portland.<br />-3 Blocks from the best pizza place in Portland -Apizza Scholls<br /><br />-10 minute walk to Laurelhurst Park, 15 min walk to Mt. Tabor Park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-3075414/original/bb714852-6432-4d4c-89dc-1bdc9878e1c2.jpeg',2051547,16,'45.51374','-122.62179',1,3,2.00,2.00,2.00,250.00,30,150,4,5.00,3075414),(172,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3104395','~..++ Sweet N. Portland Loft ++.._~','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/42116785/6720b983_original.jpg',4333411,24,'45.56011','-122.66716',1,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,190.00,30,1125,5,5.00,3104395),(173,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3122190','Studio Apartment PandaCrystalCave','Studio basement apartment features eco-floors, zero VOC paint, legal egress. Ceiling height: 80\" -- Aesthetic features Asian influence. Fits 2 adults well. Leather sectional. Mt.Tabor park 1-block away. Dogs welcome!<br /><br />50” UHD TV with Netflix & Amazon Prime included.  We have a PLEX media server with lots of movies and shows.  A 4K HDMI cable is provided for your gaming console, Blu-Ray player, or HDMI-equipped media player/streaming device.','What we love the most is that our block of Belmont Street is an unimproved, narrow gravel roadway that magically and instantly takes you out of the city environment into a quiet garden of flowers standing in a crown of cedar trees from the neighboring Mt. Tabor Park. Perpetual migrations of birds relaxing on the mountain share the songs with us in our little oasis.<br /><br />We live in an epic Portland neighborhood (Tabor Heights), on top of Mt. Tabor - a dormant and lovely volcano covered with delicious Cedar trees and home to large birds of prey, owls, rabbits, woodpeckers and a multitude of songbirds. Mt. Tabor is one of Portland\'s destination parks - extensive hiking trails, awesome dog park and kids park.<br /><br />Top Portland eatery, coquinepdx.com is across the street. They\'ve recently occupied the adjacent space, where they\'ve established a delightful, brilliantly stocked Eurocentric market, with coffee and pastry service.  Their market is open Monday through Sunday, 9:30 a.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5edb7d5a-a3ba-4281-85c8-a3ff14a41f22.jpg',11158071,15,'45.51569','-122.59269',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,81.00,1,90,608,4.91,3122190),(174,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3133331','Guest-suite,king bed,near downtown, free-parking','*This is a guest-suite attached to a townhome where the host lives. The suite has its own private entrance, balcony, and bathroom.','Southwest Hills neighborhood is a great mix of suburban and urban living. Many of the homes are built on the side of the hill and are cantilevered over the forest floor below. As many of the streets in this area wind through the tree-lined forest, this makes the Southwest Hills an interesting place to drive, and a serene and beautiful place to live.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/74d0e7c2-5c83-4dce-8c7b-854d5a6adbf3.jpg',15910930,54,'45.5079','-122.69002',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,1,14,847,4.92,3133331),(175,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3146964','Sunny, Modern Guesthouse South Tabor Neighborhood','A modern guesthouse with one bedroom, one bathroom, a living/kitchen space and a deck. The guesthouse is above our garage and was built in 2011.  There\'s a deck off the kitchen which is a nice place for relaxing. <br /><br />We are about 1.5 miles from restaurants and shops at SE Division. There are several bus stops within 1-2 blocks of our house. Downtown Portland is 30 minutes by bus<br /><br />We\'ve done a lot of traveling and enjoy meeting new people. We welcome folks from all backgrounds and places.','The South Tabor neighborhood is relatively quiet. It contains a mix of single family residence and rental properties. The house is a short walk to Division street shops and restaurants. Less than a mile walk to Portland\'s Stumptown coffee. About a two mile walk to shops and restaurants on Hawthorne st., or to reach the top of Mt. Tabor (a lovely Portland Park with lots of small hiking trails).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0812a909-1003-465a-a61d-fca6562131d6.jpg',15975696,37,'45.49891','-122.60763',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,100.00,2,60,210,4.94,3146964),(176,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3147877','Bright & Modern 2bdrm House In Kenton Neighborhood','This 1,000 square feet, bight, newer and spacious house is located in the quiet historic Kenton Neighborhood. Two bright & spacious rooms with one bathroom comfortably sleep for 4. FREE parking on-premise. The house is 7 miles to downtown and 8miles to PDX, 10-minute drive to Alberta and Mississippi district, 5-min walk to the bus stop and 12-min walk to the Max Transit Yellow line Kenton/N. Denver station. Cafés, bars & great restaurants (with outdoor seating) & organic grocery stores nearby!','The house is located in the quiet historic Kenton neighborhood. It is a leisure walk to the coffee shops and restaurants in central Kenton. Most of them have outdoor seatings. I recommend the following neighborhood restaurants - they are about 12-minute walking distance.<br /><br />Posies Bakery & Cafe for a great cup of coffee, fresh in-house made pastries and breakfast sandwiches. It has outdoor seatings.<br /><br />Swift & Union is a great refined yet casual pub-style restaurant. Great for all occasions. It has outdoor seatings.<br /><br />Pizza Fino - Gourmet Pizza. It has outdoor seatings.<br /><br />Poshine is a nonprofit Cajun & BBQ restaurant dishing up down-to-earth soul food.<br /><br />Parkside Restaurant and Lounge is a pub by the Kenton Park, a little gem in the neighborhood, has delicious food and drinks. It has a 4.5-star rating on Yelp. It has outdoor seatings.<br /><br />Casa Maya Taqueria & Cantina - It opened in August 2020. It has outdoor seatings.<br /><br />Mayfly','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/40128898/78ceaf71_original.jpg',9260383,55,'45.58557','-122.69488',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,0.00,30,30,8,4.63,3147877),(177,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3186591','Bright and Cozy Home in NE Portland','Come enjoy this bright and cozy home in the Woodlawn neighborhood and explore Dekum Triangle. Quiet neighborhood just a 5 minute walk to a park, bus lines, great restaurants, coffee and more. Enjoy a great kitchen, big yard spaces, central AC, and family friendly amenities. NEW 100% NATURAL LATEX BED! Super comfy.<br /><br />Great backyard space with a propane grill, Traeger, deck, shaded grape arbor, and garden.<br /><br />This listing is for 2 bedrooms with 5 beds but there is another bed in a third office room.','The Woodlawn neighborhood is a delightful neighborhood of Portland. Within 5 minutes walk you will find Woodlawn coffee shop, Good Neighbor Pizzeria, Oregon Public House (a non profit pub), Breakside Brewery, Grand Army Tavern, Firehouse restaurant (upscale dining), P\'s & Q\'s Market, Tamale Boy (local Mexican), and more. You may never want to leave the neighborhood!<br /><br />The local park is 3 minutes walk and has tons of wide open spaces, great shaded areas, a basketball arena, of course a playground and a water park!<br /><br />There is also a full supermarket and drug store within a 10 minute walk.<br /><br />Our street is quiet and peaceful and our neighbors are great.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6704a486-5312-49c5-bfc4-21c26cf49082.jpg',8637203,45,'45.57378','-122.65878',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,1125,19,4.95,3186591),(178,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3198698','Private 2 bedroom near Airport','Two private rooms & bathroom in the basement of my home in the Roseway neighborhood, centrally located between downtown and the airport.','My place is about 5 miles from downtown. The neighborhood is quiet and within walking distance to coffee shops (Fresh Love), grocery stores (Safeway) and restaurants (Namaste, Reevas, Mekha, Fresh Love). It\'s easy and convenient to bus or bike to Portland destinations from my house.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/42116526/d3b3d4f7_original.jpg',9132065,39,'45.55301','-122.58236',1,3,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,20,240,4.78,3198698),(179,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3246662','Entire 3rd floor in historic home','This is a 1200 sq ft area with bedroom, large living area and private bath with the original old clawfoot tub, and a shared kitchen on the first floor. It has views of all the mountains.  It is quiet.  It feels like you are out in the forest at night.<br />There is central heating in the bedroom with the double bed and in the bathroom.  There is a space heater in the living room.  There is no central heating in the room with the single bed.<br />There is easy parking in our driveway.','This neighborhood is called the Alphabet district because all the street names are in alphabetical order.  It is just adjacent to downtown so there is easy public transportation, but parking is also easy.  Our neighborhood was built up after the World\'s fair exhibition in 1905','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/53299920/2c6f6f77_original.jpg',3022845,27,'45.53066','-122.7031',2,3,1.00,2.00,3.00,95.00,30,30,117,4.82,3246662),(180,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3280928','Onsen oasis + Portland\'s finest at your feet','Elegant 2-bedroom loft in Alberta Arts District\'s culinary haven. Sleeps 4, 1 bathroom, 1,200 sq ft.<br />Highlight: Private onsen garden soaking tub for ultimate relaxation.<br />Amenities: WiFi, Netflix, fully-equipped kitchen.<br />Steps from acclaimed eateries: Gabbiano\'s, Dame, Lil Dame Nearby: Expatriate, Take Two, , Wilder. Jet Black Coffee.<br />#72 bus stop at doorstep.<br />Immerse in Portland\'s finest dining and arts scene from your sophisticated retreat.','Within 2 blocks is a plethora of restaurants, cafes, bars, and other venues, with recommendations including Gabbiono\'s Italian Kitchen, immediately downstairs, as well as Ripe, Dame, Expatriate, Jinx, Wilder, Yui and Flour Market to name a few . Visit galleries in the Alberta Art District not to mention some of the best coffee in town.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/02bd39eb-8925-4876-92b6-3c8e459ca2d6.jpg',1213257,1,'45.56203','-122.63457',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,226.00,1,90,487,4.92,3280928),(181,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3282776','Comfy room near Alberta, Airport','Relaxing room is perfect for anyone looking for a cozy night\'s sleep. Just 12 minutes from airport and 7 minutes to the Alberta Arts District. Plush queen bed, desk, and tv.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/41685703/b0d14683_original.jpg',10438539,21,'45.56197','-122.60037',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,48.00,1,7,395,4.68,3282776),(182,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3340282','Modern, quiet, comfortable Suite. Trained dogs ok!','Our Underground Oasis Suite is a beautiful 800 sq ft grand basement space, designed for comfort. It is perfect for up to four adults and one child. You have your own private entrance with a keypad access to downstairs. Located four miles from downtown Portland with easy freeway and transit access. Lovely, quiet neighborhood with plenty of street parking with access to park/golf course a block away. We have a City Permit, so you know you are safe. The Underground Oasis Suite is the place for you!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/56045998/2ee51a13_original.jpg',10160131,11,'45.53435','-122.59838',1,5,1.00,1.00,2.00,115.00,2,28,196,4.93,3340282),(183,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3378558','Modern Corner Unit Condo at 34th and Hawthorne','One-of-a-kind modern condo, floor to ceiling glass, right in the best section of Hawthorne. Endless cafes, shops, and restaurants and two grocery stores within short in walking distances. There are no bars or businesses on this block open past 8:30 pm so it\'s quiet at night.<br /><br />Excellent configuration with the kitchen, eating nook, living rooms downstairs and two bedrooms and full bathrooms upstairs. <br /><br />Tons of glass and skylights provide wonderful light, even during the rainier season!','In the heart of Hawthorne, but with no bars or restaurants on our block.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-3378558/original/9bd21532-5013-4afa-862c-ec71acbdbad0.jpeg',5462607,16,'45.51293','-122.63066',1,4,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,150,0,1.00,3378558),(184,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3379920','Your Hawthorne Home. Walk everywhere!','A charming home blocks from the shops, restaurants and excitement of Hawthorne set on a quiet street in a great neighborhood.<br /><br />Experience all Portland has to offer in a place to call home.','This house is close to so much Hawthorne has to offer, as well as grocery stores, bars, restaurants, coffee joints... it\'s all within a quick 10 minute walk in both directions.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-3379920/original/b6bf1c56-3f32-48aa-828c-d8c0d498a339.jpg',887013,16,'45.51318','-122.61805',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,170.00,3,185,104,4.88,3379920),(185,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3395521','The Cottage. Close-in. Near River/Downtown/MAX','Experience Portland in Comfort from a Convenient and Central Location. Beautiful, spacious 2 bedroom, 1 bathroom, home that sleeps up to 4 adults and 1 child (unless child is under 2, we don\'t count them in the guest count!). There is full modern kitchen with a full-size dishwasher, oven, and fridge. The AirBnB is a standalone building with a private entrance and behind the main house on the property where the owners live. Close to Downtown Portland and everything on the EastSide.','We choose this property because of its proximity to downtown Portland and so many other amenities like restaurants, grocery stores, bus lines, bike trails, running trails, Oaks Bottom Wildlife refuge, museums, and other activities and conveniences.<br /><br />The Brooklyn Cottage is central located and very close to downtown Portland, the Oregon Zoo, Portland Art Museum, Oregon Museum of Science and Industry, Portland Children’s Museum, Portland Children’s Theater, Hoyt Arboretum,  Portland Rose Garden, Forestry Center,  Chinese Garden, Japanese Garden,  Oregon Historical Society Museum, Oregon Convention Center, Rose Garden Arena and Memorial Coliseum,  Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge, Portland Willamette Waterfront recreation area, Oaks Amusement Park, Reed College, Oregon Health Sciences University, Lewis and Clark College, National College of Natural Medicine, Portland State University, and a number of restaurants, grocery stores, boutiques, museums, gyms, spas, farmers markets, parks,','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bb83f293-ce64-4393-8823-cf386f6b38ff.jpg',7239911,56,'45.49211158502245','-122.648358219535',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,89.00,2,29,185,4.95,3395521),(186,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3431587','Private Studio Mount Tabor/Division','Private ground floor Studio. Newly built modern and airy building w high ceilings. Gated cedar fence, with private sunny patio area in front, private entrance. Natural lighting with large south facing and garden windows.  Main lighting on dimmers. Full kitchen. Queen bed. Washer dryer. Mix of Midcentury vintage and modern furniture. This is not a basement. Very quiet easy going neighborhood . Parking in front. 3 blocks to Mt. Tabor park, fun Division St., 5 min to Hawthorne, & the 205 & 26 hwys','South Tabor neighborhood is relaxed and safe, along with a view of Mt. Tabor mountain from our yard and street.  <br />We are a super short drive, a fun bike ride, or nice walk to the mountain park, and near some of the best shops and restaurants in Portland right on Division St. They start about 10 blocks away. Which is perfect, as it keeps our area quiet with plenty of easy parking.<br />We are also very near the famous and fun Hawthorne neighborhood. The best Asian restaurants and grocery stores along 82nd Ave are nearby too! <br />The South Tabor neighborhood is the best of both worlds! It can feel like country living in the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/304943d8-24d8-4594-b383-6223fb1334d6.jpg',17293984,37,'45.50174','-122.59021',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,30,1125,178,4.79,3431587),(187,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3433479','Cozy art studio hideaway','Formerly a work shop and art studio, now an intuitively designed example of creativity and innovation. Many reviews call this the best AirBnb they\'ve seen. A unique local experience awaits you in this cozy, one of a kind artistic space that is close to everything in Southeast Portland’s Hawthorne district. Safe, clean, quiet. Ping pong, vinyl, high speed wifi, tv, air purification system, free and safe parking, washer and dryer, bikes to ride. No Parties. No Smoking. No small children. No pets.','Historic Ladd\'s Addition neighborhood in Portland\'s eclectic and vibrant southeast. Located between Division and Hawthorne near SE 20th. Surrounded by gourmet food carts and brewpubs. Walkable and pretty tree-lined neighborhood close to everything. Easy 1 mile bike ride or walk to Portland\'s downtown and waterfront.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-3433479/original/c70615fc-f776-4b73-9488-720ce1e5a291.jpeg',17264703,25,'45.51117','-122.64579',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,123.00,1,7,1269,4.98,3433479),(188,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3439204','Wooded Getaway w/City Access','1000 sqft. all for you! In a beautifully wooded area, close to hiking trails, but minutes from downtown. The bottom floor of our home w/ a private entrance. The bathroom has a walk-in shower & double sinks. There is a great room with a sectional couch, kitchenette w/microwave, fridge, & toaster oven  (no burners, oven, or freezer) & flat-screen tv (streaming, no cable). Bedroom has a queen bed & garden views. Family & pet friendly. Centrally located between NW 23rd, downtown, Beaverton and OHSU','Centrally located between downtown Portland, Beaverton, Washington Square and Multnomah Village.  Council Crest is recognized as one of the most exclusive neighborhoods in the area with wooded drives, incredible views, and city access, all among some of the nicest homes in Portland.  The house itself is at the end of a cul-de-sac and very peaceful.  There is a wooded trail immediately outside your door leading to Council Crest park (the highest point in Portland and great views!) and a moderate/longer hike to the Zoo. <br /><br />We are in the Southwest hills above downtown and the Alphabet District (aka Nob Hill, NW 23rd Avenue and NW 21st Avenue). It is a steep and curvy drive, but beautiful and full of interesting views, and only 10-15 minutes from most attractions and restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ebe8a6a5-93e0-4a01-b1ce-cad3a42e7dac.jpg',11853939,54,'45.49621','-122.71122',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,503,4.85,3439204),(189,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3441025','Updated Woodland Garden Retreat & Spa','Completely remodeled in 2017, this breathtaking private space has a full kitchen, bedroom and luxurious bathroom spa with a shower and jetted hot tub.  Other features in this secluded apartment include bamboo flooring, vaulted ceilings and skylights overlooking a lush yet private Pacific NW backyard landscape.  This apartment has a private entrance and street parking right in front of the house.','Additional  information about your stay here..<br /><br /> • Quiet, safe and friendly neighborhood. <br /><br />• Wide street with plenty of free parking. <br /><br />• A short walk to the beautiful Mt. Tabor Park.  <br /><br /> • The Montavilla Neighborhood cafe\'s, restaurants, pubs, shops, parks, library and movie theatre are also just a short walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4d14bf53-10ad-48a3-91dc-41bb387128ea.jpg',6864209,37,'45.49888','-122.58735',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,116.00,2,1125,242,4.87,3441025),(190,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3448571','Peaceful studio space.','Basement studio space located in one of Portlands classic older neighborhoods.  Space created for guests to have a peaceful and relaxing place to rest after a day exploring Portland.  Good location to hop on public transportation (max and bus lines) for exploring the city.','Sweet Rose City Park.  One of Portland\'s older neighborhoods. It is a close in, relatively quiet residential area. Walking distance to some restaurants, breweries, coffee shops, bakeries, farmers market and grocery.  We are also close to many other happening neighborhoods. We have a lot of families that live in our neighborhood. Close to a huge park that has tennis courts and golf.  Take a walk down any street in Rose City Park you\'ll be rewarded with well-maintained older homes, tree lined streets and beautiful gardens.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/124cbe28-0289-4a37-9c32-169837af61cd.jpg',4241752,11,'45.53677','-122.6032',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,2,7,286,4.99,3448571),(191,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3476238','Bright and Beautiful One Bedroom Apartment','Enjoy Portland while staying in our light and bright basement apartment in the University Park neighborhood of St. Johns. Walking distance to the University of Portland, and a great food truck pod. We are less than 5 mi from the Moda Center. It\'s a nice get away from downtown Portland, but only a 15 minute drive. Also close to the beautiful St. John\'s bridge/park and the Alberta Arts District. The apartment has one bedroom with a queen-sized bed and a sleeper sofa. There\'s a separate entrance.','University Park neighborhood in the St. John\'s area. Three blocks from The University of Portland, close to food truck pod and the Overlook path that looks over the Willamette River. Close to the downtown area of St. Johns, Alberta Arts district, St John\'s Park/Bridge. Quick drive to the Portland downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-3476238/original/f33e5d55-b23c-4c22-811a-555a85e8c84f.jpeg',17509708,57,'45.58251','-122.73612',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,90.00,2,90,65,4.92,3476238),(192,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3480082','Great location, relaxed vibe & flex cancellation','Solo travelers only for housemate-style living in my small 2 bedroom/1 bath bungalow. The bath is shared with me; the guest room is private w/lock. Centered between Mississippi Ave and Williams Ave in the historic Boise neighborhood, my place is within walking distance of great dining, shopping, bars, music, comedy, and breweries. New Seasons Market is 3 blocks away.  It\'s a short walk to transit lines that take you all over the city.','I live in the fast-growing and busy Boise-Eliot neighborhood, almost directly centered between historic Mississippi Ave and the Williams Corridor. There are many shops, pubs, breweries, specialty bars, restaurants, and music venues within walking distance, and our local New Seasons Market is just three blocks away!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-3480082/original/7eed5629-8465-409a-847e-8894efed1170.jpeg',17530443,9,'45.5495','-122.669',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,48.00,1,6,530,4.99,3480082),(193,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3498642','Artsy, Lofty, Open 1BR comfort in Converted Church','Adorable rear duplex renovated in former 50\'s Baptist Church. Bright, open floor plan, high ceilings and three skylights, separate 900 SF apt with a private backyard, kitchen, wood stove, TV/cable, D/W, W/D, A/C, Wifi, bus. Well located blocks from Alberta Arts, Williams Hub, Mississippi shops & so many amazing restaurants.','The North Williams corridor is historically the jazz/blues/speakeasy section of town back in the 50\'s and 60\'s. Since then N. Williams has undergone a transformation in urban renewal, the HUB shopping district about 8 blocks south of us is a recent development and home to several fabulous restaurants yoga studios, wine-bars, coffee shops and great boutique shopping. It\'s definitely an up-and coming area with several new apartment buildings and mixed-use retail developments just in the last few years.  There is a great small indie grocery store called Cherry Sprout blocks away for local produce 3 blocks away, a convenience store 2 block away, a Natural Grocers  three blocks away, and a New Seasons giant awesome grocery store to the south about 15 blocks down Williams.  Williams is a north running one-way, known for being the main bicycle super-highway connecting the Central east-side to North Portland.  (Make sure you check behind you for bicycles before parking out front and opening yo','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-3498642/original/3583ce7e-821d-49fd-a638-5b3ece32fb90.jpg',4716299,24,'45.55757','-122.66546',1,4,1.50,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,30,563,4.97,3498642),(194,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3518220','Urban Retreat for 1-4 Near Airport & Alberta St','Squash Blossom is 12 min to the airport, 20 min to downtown and walkable to popular NE Alberta & NE Fremont districts. So close to the city, yet, this peaceful home feels like it\'s nestled in the country as it is a large lot hidden from the street.  The guest apartment is attached to our ranch-style house and sleeps up to 4 people: 1 bedroom with a deliciously comfy queen bed and a family room with a sofa bed and giant couch.  Space includes a kitchenette w a lovely bathroom. Pls no smokers.','Squash Blossom is a block away from an awesome park with a place for skateboarders to play, and children of all ages to enjoy.  It\'s also a 10 block walk to a variety of international cuisine, coffee shops, yoga, children\'s bookstore, and self-serve frozen yogurt (yum!). It\'s a 20 block walk to the local New Seasons grocery store and Alberta District, where you can find even more of the Portland culture.. including gluten free bakeries, craft stores, and the Alberta Rose Theater, a venue with fantastic shows nearly every night of the week. This neighborhood is delightful to walk around. There\'s also an Albertson\'s grocery store just a few blocks away for last minute needs.  I love this place.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/53673f32-744b-4600-9a50-3af09f93480c.jpg',891590,21,'45.55669','-122.60913',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,65.00,2,14,383,4.92,3518220),(195,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3551900','Spacious room w/ attached bath- monthly discounts','\" The Oak \" <br /><br />Large, sunny bedroom in North Portland with a large connected private bathroom in a updated 1922 Craftsman home.  <br />The bathroom has its own washer and dryer, small refrigerator and microwave for privacy and convenience.   Lots of windows and natural light. There is a desk in the room to work from home and also a large Internet TV.   House and room have keyless coded entry.<br /><br />Book for 31 days or more to avoid the 11.5% city occupancy tax!','At 5-10 min walking distance are the beautiful St. John\'s bridge, McMenamins , Soma Kombucha Speakeasy, Occidental brewing company, Stormbreaker brewpub,  St. John\'s twin theaters, many local  food carts offering delicious, diverse and affordable food options and numerous other restaurants and coffee shops. Right across the iconic St. John\'s bridge is Forest Park,  a 5100 acre park with numerous hiking and biking trails.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-3551900/original/914a99e8-8306-4d15-9443-bb41f153f6fa.jpg',8587273,58,'45.59045','-122.74738',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,28,1125,22,4.95,3551900),(196,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3562068','Sunrise studio with Mt. Hood view','Private entrance to beautiful, new, hilltop studio with private patio and Mt Hood view! Sleep well in this new, comfortable queen sized bed. A spacious en suite bathroom is included. <br />Relax and enjoy expansive views.<br />You will have close proximity to everything Portland has to offer.<br />Scenic Terwilliger Parkway is steps away. It\'s easy to get to Portland\'s many cool neighborhoods/districts, breweries, unique restaurants and shops, fabulous parks and wilderness trails.','Our neighborhood is on a tree covered hillside close-in to downtown Portland. The views of the Willamette River and the Cascade Mountain Range make this a very unique spot. We have easy access to getting around Portland and to the freeways.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b6f77018-48e9-4f1c-8e81-4101c4f2fb45.jpg',17934290,30,'45.49156','-122.68208',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,96.00,2,28,358,4.96,3562068),(197,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3562307','Navajo Suite','Bedroom with door, full privacy, and queen size bed, wifi, The West Hills/Northwest SAFEST, quietest neighborhood in PDX, Streetcar Pass. Right by many entrances to Forest Park, all the hikes, including to Pittock Mansion and many other parks. Im surrounded by forests, mountain views, and hills with beautiful views and old victorian and craftsman homes. I\'m only taking monthly bookings, it\'s 5% off for those who book a month! Send me a message :)','There\'s a place you can park for FREE by here,  1 car only and street parking but it\'s free or I could arrange a free space but that\'s not guaranteed but a free spot near here is. Street parking in this neighborhood can be a nightmare and there\'s also the expensive parking tickets but your car will safe here. There are so many parks/dog parks, Forest Park, hiking trails, Amazing view of the Cascade Mountains towering in the background, the NW Waterfront along the Willamette River, Boutiques, shops restaurants, cafes, of NW 23rd convenient stores, co-ops, grocery stores, the bars that line NW 21st with great happy hours all easily within walking distance in a classic victorian and craftsman neighborhood of NW Portland. Chinatown, The Pearl, and Downtown are all easily within walking distance or you can take the streetcar or Max that\'s located right by here. North and Northeast Portland is just right over the Fremont Bridge which is a located 6 blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0ef99069-db9e-4f9d-933c-9322f625485a.jpg',17615383,27,'45.5329704284668','-122.7051773071289',2,1,1.00,2.00,0.00,40.00,30,1125,277,4.82,3562307),(198,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3604698','No cleaning fee, Private bath, Free Parking for 4!','The house is located in the quiet historic Kenton Neighborhood.  A bright & spacious room with a private bathroom comfortably sleeps for 4. FREE & easy street parking. The kitchen & laundry are not included. The house is 6 miles to downtown and 8miles to PDX, a 10-minute drive to Alberta and Mississippi district, 5-min walk to the bus stop & 12-min walk to the Max Transit Yellow line Kenton/N. Denver station. Cafés, bars & great restaurants (with outdoor seating) & organic grocery stores nearby!','The house is located in the quiet historic Kenton neighborhood.  <br /><br />#The following recommended restaurants are all round 12 min walk distance—<br /><br />* Swift & Union, is a bright, airy gastro pub with outdoor seating offering seasonal New American plates, craft beer & house cocktails  Rated 4.5 on G.<br />* Casa Maya.  4.5 rating on G.    <br />* King Burrito. 4.6 stars on G.!<br />* Posies Bakery & Café is for a great cup of coffee, fresh pastries & breakfast sandwiches. 4.6 G. rating.<br />* Pizza Fino. 4.4 star rating on G.<br />* Po’ Shines Cafe De La Soul, southern food. 4.3 G. rating.<br />* Parkside Restaurant and Lounge is a pub by Kenton Park. It has outdoor seating. 4.3 G. rating<br /><br /># 1 mile away is Tiny Bubble Room, with southern-style food, and good drinks. 20-min walk.  4.8 rating on G.<br /><br /># Mayfly Taproom And Bottle Shop offers a great selection of wine and beer. It is 0.7 miles from the house or a 15-minute walk.  4.9 G. rating.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/54065907/1042c77c_original.jpg',9260383,55,'45.58738','-122.69598',2,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,1,2,85,4.55,3604698),(199,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3617607','Private studio Casita - walkable, Sellwood, SE PDX','This entire space is yours. It sits on top of the garage and it has a private entrance, bathroom, shower, and wet-bar setup. It is like staying with your in-laws, but with some  breathing space. Just steps to the Sellwood-Westmoreland neighborhood, with coffee shops, antique row, restaurants, and great little shops.<br /><br />Queen Bed, dining table for 2, couch, and club chair for reading','I love the walkability of our neighborhood, Sellwood-Westmoreland. You can grab groceries, coffee, baked goods, farmers market (in the spring-late fall), antiques, great food, library, parks etc. Close to two bus lines (19 and 70) that can take you to other parts of Portland and Max (in between Bybee and Holgate)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-3617607/original/88369ed0-c47b-491e-b80c-1a8b8ed4cb75.jpeg',10433870,20,'45.47858','-122.64884',1,3,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,1,365,84,4.89,3617607),(200,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3627515','The Downtowner','A Hidden Gem in Portland\'s Downtown area!<br />A newly remodeled historic home with Public transport & light rail  across the street.<br />Everything you could possibly want is within walking distance & everything is provided for your comfort - Just like home!','Easy accessibility to all of Portland\'s main attractions is without doubt the Reason D\'etre for you to stay at the Downtowner!<br />The Willamette River front promenades, urban forests, Theaters, shops, Restaurants, food carts,  the farmers markets & much more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-3627515/original/4ac3566d-ef47-484e-9182-98d568b27840.jpeg',7379278,44,'45.50792','-122.68358',1,8,2.00,4.00,5.00,395.00,2,60,414,4.94,3627515),(201,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3635579','Gorgeous Art Filled PDX Craftsman','An artist\'s home filled with art I have created and collected with  2 spacious bedrooms with cotton sheets and duvet covers, (frankly, I can’t stand the microfiber stuff) 1 1/2 bathrooms. Come here to experience this centrally location in the heart of Portland.','Sullivan\'s Gulch Neighborhood is located near numerous coffee shops, bakeries, restaurants, brew pubs, book stores, a wine shop and boutiques. My house is at the west end of Sullivan\'s Gulch, two blocks from the Lloyd Center Mall, and very close to the Convention Center, the Lloyd Center DoubleTree, the Rose Quarter, and downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-3635579/original/f7a7c949-904d-4bce-b7d3-1537db36d8a4.jpg',274455,4,'45.53204','-122.64758',1,5,1.50,2.00,3.00,172.00,1,27,462,4.93,3635579),(202,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3646070','Private Garden Studio in great location!','This bright  studio in the heart of Portland\'s historic Irvington neighborhood is not to be missed. Tree lined streets with big beautiful homes nestled in the heart of North East Portland.  Comes with a full kitchen, a private bathroom,  Xfinity Flex streaming service with local TV and a platform Queen Bed with  a hot tub in the back yard! <br />Free street parking in front of our home if you have rented a car.   <br /> A home for every travelers needs.','The Irvington neighborhood, now only a ten minute bike ride from downtown, was once a trolley-car suburb to the just-fully-developed West side. Designated a historic district by the National Register of Historic Places in 2010, Irvington is filled with early 20th century homes that have been preserved in their original states. Irvington has become a livable hub of Northeast Portland as a whole, with shops and restaurants of all kinds, within walking distance, surrounding the neighborhood. Irvington proper boasts more than a few community and culinary destinations of its own.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b7196fd0-ea04-4e7c-a20e-91d8bc83b814.jpg',13695963,7,'45.54121','-122.64967',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,30,90,606,4.75,3646070),(203,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3666651','5BD in the Heart & Soul of Portland','Enjoy our permitted, light-filled 5 bedroom/3 bath home. Great backyard, next to Sewallcrest Park. Walk to everything! Eclectic Hawthorne is 3 minutes on foot. Division & Belmont Sts are 10 minutes. 2 supermarkets.  Tons o\' food & pubs. Easy...','We are biased, of course, but our neighborhood is the best in the city. In one of the country\'s best cities. We feel incredibly privileged to call it home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/30f6dfca-b26d-4970-8a07-3d88d11fafa1.jpg',18590525,8,'45.50935','-122.63333',1,10,3.00,5.00,5.00,354.00,1,29,77,4.79,3666651),(204,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3667515','Great Space in Heart of Hawthorne','Enjoy a safe, secure, comfortable(!) bedroom in the heart of Portland’s most iconic neighborhood.','Our neighborhood location is ideal. So much is so close. Whether you\'re on the hunt for the best beer in world famous \"Beervana,\" a uniquely fantastic meal in \"foodie\" Portland, or looking for a quiet, secure place to rest, our neighborhood provides it all.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-3667515/original/47c1a57c-99f1-4181-a415-66c5fd016613.jpg',18590525,8,'45.5076','-122.6348',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,47.00,1,7,678,4.86,3667515),(205,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3677614','Cozy Charming Apartment in Ladd\'s off Hawthorne','A cozy space just steps to anything you want to experience in Portland: great coffee, local micro brews, late night food carts, casual and fine dining, movies, comedy, shows, parks, distillery row, wine bars, pubs, and so much more.','Ladd\'s Addition is arguably one of the most unique neighborhoods in Portland. It is one of the closest neighborhoods to downtown Portland, and also one of the oldest. It is truly a historic district. It is a delight to spend time in the neighborhood, which has hundreds of enormous trees, four rose gardens, and a large central garden. It can sometimes be confusing to navigate, but is a great pleasure to explore!  If you love maps, you\'ll love the way the neighborhood looks on the map :)<br />For a cup of coffee or a rich slice of German chocolate cake in a cozy environment, try Palio\'s (right on the main circle). New Seasons market is also just outside the neighborhood, and is a great choice for lunch or groceries, or try the farmers market up Hawthorne, open 7 days a week.<br />There are other grocery and coffee options, as well as countless classic or new dining and entertainment options within blocks of the neighborhood. Most everything is easily walkable!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ca82f473-2620-47bb-93e7-3d49ea943f9c.jpg',13351238,25,'45.51186','-122.65171',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,87.00,1,1125,702,4.81,3677614),(206,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3678338','Portland\'s best kept secret...','This private apartment is centrally located in the heart of Portland.  We are walking distance to the Convention Center, Max line, and great bars and restaurants.  Downtown, Hawthorne, and Alberta neighborhoods are all only a 15 min bike ride away!<br />We do have young children so be prepared for the pitter patter of little feet. We are usually up from 6-8 in the morning getting ready for work and school and in bed by 9pm.','Sullivan\'s Gulch is truly one of the best kept secrets in Portland.  We live in a quiet, friendly neighborhood that is close to everything good about Portland.  Win, win!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/74198078/73dd4036_original.jpg',1795731,4,'45.533957482359725','-122.64123097122949',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,30,360,339,4.87,3678338),(207,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3696524','Purple bedroom in cute artsy Home','The Location is perfect, you can be almost anywhere in the city within 5-20 minutes. Very easy to get places from here by bus or car if you have one.<br />Close to number 6 bus line.  Free street parking.  Walk to cafes. 5-8 minute bus ride to convention center.  Near Fremont and MLK<br />NON SMOKERS  only  DO NOT REQUEST THIS ROOM IF YOU SMOKE CIGARETTES<br />1 person only <br /><br />The neighborhood is safe and there is plenty of street parking. <br /><br />Non Smokers only please.','Neighborhood is safe.  It\'s peaceful and there is a good breakfast spot down the street and a sweet cafe. Nike outlet store is a a couple blocks away. Parking is easy on our street after 5pm weekdays and easier on weekends.<br /><br />Though it\'s a safe neighborhood, this is Portland.  In Portland no one leaves anything valuable in their cars.  Car break ins are common in Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-3696524/original/813414cd-dd79-423f-bf3a-03f030fb4fb2.jpeg',2410278,9,'45.54935','-122.66253',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,37.00,2,14,101,4.91,3696524),(208,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3698451','The Serene Hideaway','This is a beautiful, 1st story, flat style studio, very modern, sleek, and edgy. Located in a historical Victorian neighborhood, central to everything. 5 minutes from downtown Portland, walking distance to Rose Garden, Convention Center and more!!!','This cozy space is centrally located literally to everything and only 5 mins from Downtown/Pearl district. Walking distance to the Moda Center formally known as Rose Garden and the Pearl district,  a 1/2 block from eateries and two cycle shops.  You can also find within 5 minutes more breweries, unique cafes, grocery stores and the Mississippi/Fremont experience which include restaurants, shopping, and entertainment.<br /><br />Family: Kid friendly: parks, Oregon Zoo, Omsi, Water Front Park, Saturday market and much more<br /><br />Description of Neighborhood:  Slightly industrial/neighborhood<br />(almost like an extension of downtown). Though its a neighborhood you will find a lot of close businesses/restaurants within walking distance','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/80515604/55d70267_original.jpg',18846362,59,'45.53452','-122.6659',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,83.00,1,1125,427,4.86,3698451),(209,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3738840','Private King Studio w/fireplace in great location!','With just the right amount of space for two, this studio has everything that makes a house feel like a home: a fireplace, a full kitchen, King Memory foam Bed, oak floors, handmade furniture, Local TV with Xfinity flex streaming and a private entrance.','The Irvington neighborhood, now only a ten minute bike ride from downtown, was once a trolley-car suburb to the just-fully-developed West side. Designated a historic district by the National Register of Historic Places in 2010, Irvington is filled with early 20th century homes that have been preserved in their original states. Irvington has become a livable hub of Northeast Portland as a whole, with shops and restaurants of all kinds, within walking distance, surrounding the neighborhood. Irvington proper boasts more than a few community and culinary destinations of its own.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8c8ddbe2-f0c3-469e-a159-9db21c362800.jpg',13695963,7,'45.54143','-122.64832',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,46.00,30,90,573,4.75,3738840),(210,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3755902','Private apartment! Fast WiFi. Central NorthPDX','Selected for Portland\'s 2015 ADU tour, this new, modern space is fresh, clean, and perfect for your stay. It\'s on a quiet street just blocks to the MAX rail line, great restaurants, and coffee shops. Enjoy the new bedroom, bathroom, and full kitchen!<br /><br />Use of washer and dryer is available for long term  (28 days +) guests only. A $60 fee per month for use. Ask Stephani!','Overlook is named for the nearby bluffs that look down onto the city center and the Willamette River, offering great sunsets and activity areas (lots of dogs, running and biking). There\'s a strong core of restaurants, bars, grocery stores and coffee.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/99844973/fc256432_original.jpg',847543,13,'45.56547','-122.68705',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,71.00,2,400,411,4.84,3755902),(211,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3774635','Cozy for 1 in Portland\'s Safe Central NE Portland','Start your day with a  complimentary \'continental\' breakfast Tues-Sat in lovely, clean, safe, central NE Portland. READ THE LISTING ‘BEFORE ’ BOOKING. Thank You 🙏🏼','NE Portland is Portland\'s  trending/hip adult playground.—it\'s become a destination for eating, drinking and window shopping, thanks in large part to the Alberta/Mississippi/Williams Arts districts. This safe/upscale residential neighborhood is very close, (walking distance), to a couple of parks, several great coffee shops, great restaurants, bars, McMenamins Kennedy school, and healthy grocery stores, just 2 miles from a shopping mall, Forest Park which in one of the largest inner city parks in the world. You can take a bus to Forest Park and hike there all day. The Portland Zoo, rose gardens and Japanese gardens are all in Forest Park.<br /><br />Alberta St is 6 1/2 blocks from my door, 15 min walk, 3 min car ride and 5 min bike ride.   You\'ll find great bars, restaurants, art galleries and shopping on Alberta as well as coffee, yoga and the stuff that make Portland pleasantly \"weird\"<br /><br />Mississippi 30-45 min walk and Williams, 20-30 min walk are must do streets as well for ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cf6efecd-4673-403a-adc3-c975400cddf4.jpg',748943,46,'45.54796150286919','-122.63007201249582',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,1,21,337,4.87,3774635),(212,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3775190','Beautiful house in Portland Heights','Beautiful spacious house in Portland Heights. Brand new renovation and remodel of the entire house. 1.2 miles to downtown and 1 mile to 23rd street/uptown. 5 minute drive to OHSU. <br />We are looking for responsible tenants to take very good care of this home. Long term tenants would be ideal for us. <br />We have a strict no pet policy. <br />Please message me if you are interested. Thanks!','Vista Hills is one of the most conveniently located neighborhoods in Portland. Only being a mile away from downtown and NW 23rd street, its perfect for OHSU residents or young professionals who don\'t want a long commute. The house has a really open air feeling, with lots of green happening around it!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/68086b75-d938-41ab-9d22-5dd0b3dcb5b4.jpg',2738309,54,'45.50722','-122.6987',1,4,2.50,4.00,4.00,243.00,30,300,0,1.00,3775190),(213,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3825370','The Bourbon Rose','Spacious, newly built,  & freshly furnished 3 bedroom/1.5 bathroom condo unit with lots of natural sunlight and your own patio!<br /><br />The property is located in the vibrant and exciting Alberta Arts district neighborhood- right in the heart of all the action! Close to plenty of food options, great coffee, shops & easy access to the frequently running 8 & 72 bus lines. The owner’s car is in the driveway, but there is plenty of easy street parking available right in front of the home.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-3825370/original/5afb26d6-cb71-44f5-a8f9-071ee26d5f5b.jpeg',7409866,29,'45.56047','-122.64892',1,5,1.50,3.00,0.00,0.00,1,28,76,4.93,3825370),(214,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3842427','Woodlawn Retreat','Get comfortable in your own home while visiting northeast Portland\'s charming Woodlawn neighborhood.  The guesthouse was built in 2018 and boasts quality construction, craftsmanship, and attention to detail with a modern aesthetic. The guesthouse is detached from the main house on the lot, and due to it being a corner lot, has its own street facing view.','Woodlawn, aka the Dekum Triangle, is a cozy residential neighborhood with a small commercial district.  There are restaurant and bar options within two blocks of the guesthouse, with many more a bit further afield. Alberta St in particular is one of East Portland’s best commercial districts and is about a mile away.  The airport is conveniently 15 minutes away, as is downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ac93ecd5-d04c-41a6-a68c-cbdb5fb619d6.jpg',76618979,45,'45.5714','-122.64785',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,1,14,628,4.96,3842427),(215,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3844595','Great Two Bedroom Apt. in Portland!','Spacious and clean 750 sq. ft. two bedroom apartment available in inner north Portland. Two blocks from Columbia Park, close to the University of Portland, Kenton, Williams and Mississippi Ave. hotspots. Also, 10 minutes from The Pearl District and downtown. Quiet and stress-free!<br /><br />No cleaning fee!!<br />Added fees can be annoying, so we won’t charge cleaning fees. <br />We also don’t like doing chores while on vacation, so we only ask that used towels go in the tub before you leave.','Portsmouth is close to all of the amenities, activities, and great food that Portland has to offer. But, it\'s quiet and relaxed when you are ready to get a good night\'s sleep in preparation for the day ahead. Conveniently close to the University of Portland and St. John\'s neighborhood!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/83161471/dd506379_original.jpg',19817453,60,'45.58493','-122.70797',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,159.00,3,5,147,4.95,3844595),(216,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3875448','Blue FoPo House','Stay in our craftsman house  in the heart of the Foster-Powell neighborhood. The room is the only bedroom on the main floor with a bathroom designated for guest use only and a garden view with small deck.','The neighborhood is really a residential area that is close to popular areas and about 3 miles from downtown. I provides good access to these area but is also far enough away to provide a quiet, residential experience. We are in a working class neighborhood that has changed a lot over the last few decades. There are two foodcart pods nearby, the nearest  just three blocks. Foster has some bars, restaurants and other businesses. There is grocery shopping and a great brewery within a mile. There is also access to SE Hawthorne and Division neighborhoods with lots of exciting, new as well as established restaurants and businesses.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1ab3b19a-4b87-44db-ad9e-cc05689b3ab8.jpg',19252862,36,'45.49751','-122.60455',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,40.00,7,100,69,4.80,3875448),(217,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3884940','Arbor Lodge Guest Suite','Welcome to our cozy and charming Arbor Lodge home in Portland!  Nestled in a quiet and family-friendly neighborhood, our house is the perfect retreat for your PNW getaway.  This private space features - one  bedroom, a spacious living room, full private bath and a fully equipped kitchen.  Beautifully decorated with mid century furnishings, creating a warm and inviting atmosphere.  This home is conveniently situated near public trans for easy access to downtown and other attractions.','Located in Arbor Lodge neighborhood w/ lots of amazing local restaurants, coffee shops and groceries within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6Mzg4NDk0MA%3D%3D/original/5333f5da-33c9-4ff8-aefb-17786f5053a7.jpeg',20091250,51,'45.57118','-122.68578',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,114.00,2,30,8,4.63,3884940),(218,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3898216','SE PDX Apt, great location, full kitchen, private!','Awesome updated apartment in Old Portland home. <br />Great amenities! 24 hr keyless, private entry. Completely separate apartment.<br /><br />10 years as a LEGAL Airbnb, legit not fake Permit (many aren\'t); and Super Hosts.<br />Quiet, shaded courtyard sitting area. Quiet apt. No kids, pets, or smokers live here.<br />Fast WIFI, full kitchen, HDTV, CATV, W/D. 2024 laminate; tile.<br />Unusual perks: Well-lit, level, easy street parking. Quiet street. 15-20\' to PDX 24/7.<br />Walkable to SE Portland\'s best food, pubs, shops, etc.','The Richmond neighborhood has mostly older homes, dating from 1890 close by us; ours was built in 1910. Lots of huge old trees and wide sidewalks set off from the street. No retail here on our street, but the heart of SE Division Street is less than a 5-minute walk away (4 blocks).  Ava Gene\'s (Portland Monthly’s 2013 Restaurant of the Year and ranking fifth on Bon Appetit’s Best New Restaurants in America), Salt & Straw Ice Cream, Oma\'s Hideaway (Portland\'s Eater Award Restaurant of the Year 2021), Kim Jong Grillin\', Olympia Provisions, Lauretta Jeans (best pie and desserts in town, go early, they often sell out),  Cibo\'s, La Provence French Bakery and Cafe (one of our favorites for brunch and French pastry!), Bollywood Theater, several eclectic food cart pods, the original Stumptown Coffee location - all here, and much more. John\'s [Beer] Marketplace - best selection in the PNW, and the food cart pod is 10\' away on SE Powell. Also, Safeway, Natural Grocer, and New Seasons Market are ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/49262623/34219927_original.jpg',20180480,8,'45.50307','-122.62072',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,62.00,2,28,661,4.93,3898216),(219,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3898931','Pearl Extended Stay w/ Downtown View','Whether here for work, transitioning, or just enjoying extended visit to Portland you will find no better option than this great space overlooking the entire city - right by the Willamette River and close to all the great things the Pearl has to offer.','Close to everything that Portland has to offer.  Step into the Pearl for great food, cafes, and nightlife.  Leave the car in the secured garage and jump onto the street car to check out the scene on the East Side, shop in NW, or take a look downtown.  Everything you need to get to is an easy few minutes away...Moda Ctr, Rose Qtr, Business Ctr, I-5, I-84, Waterfront, shopping, great restaurants...you name it...it\'s right near by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-3898931/original/bf4a5e57-dd4c-4a34-9185-06937781b699.jpeg',4701601,2,'45.53389','-122.67867',1,3,1.50,1.00,2.00,95.00,60,600,22,4.95,3898931),(220,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3899124','Alberta Arts 1 Bedroom Suite','Located in the heart of the Alberta Arts District, one of Portland\'s great neighborhoods. This clean and comfy one bedroom apartment is the perfect spot to stay while you explore Portland and Oregon.<br /><br />With outstanding walkability, this apartment is within three  blocks of some of the best parks, shops, galleries, bars, coffee and food the city has to offer.','The neighborhood is one of the best in Portland. Within three blocks you\'ll find some of the best parks, shops, galleries, bars, coffee and food the city has to offer.  <br /><br />Across the street is Alberta Park. Two blocks down is the one of the cities infamous BBQ spots, Podnahs. And three blocks away is the best coffee in the city at Roseland Coffee. Those three spots are just the start. There are more restaurants, food carts and must stop spots than you\'ll have time to see, all within walking distance.  <br /><br />Also it\'s only about 15 minutes from the airport.<br /><br /><br />For the Foodies:<br />A list of some (of the many) amazing restaurants all within walking distance:<br /><br />Bamboo Sushi<br />Proud Mary<br />Salt & Straw<br />Hai Yai<br />Podnahs<br />Bollywood Theater<br />Expatriate <br />Pine State Biscuits<br />Boxer Ramen<br />Gabbianos <br />Gumbas <br />Urdaneta <br />Thom<br />GrindWitTryz<br />Toy Shop Ramen <br /><br /><br />Vegan hotspots (all walkable)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/49060698/d2084e8d_original.jpg',9494168,29,'45.56107','-122.64625',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,106.00,3,1125,107,4.93,3899124),(221,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/3939886','Beautiful apartment near the heart of Sellwood','Beautiful downstairs apartment - walk to the best of Sellwood!<br />Offering a prime location near the heart of Sellwood-Moreland, this beautifully decorated, two-bedroom apartment will provide you with wonderful walking access to one of Portland\'s most charming and inviting neighborhoods. Come see why PDX monthly calls our neighborhood \"Mayberry in Portland\"!<br />Private entrance, contact-less check-in, free and fast WiFi, full kitchen, workspace with desk and chair.','This apartment is located in the Sellwood-Moreland neighborhood of Southeast Portland, an area known for its eclectic small businesses, great restaurants, and proximity to the Willamette River. Just around the corner you\'ll find coffee, brunch, several restaurants (and a cake shop!) as well a convenience store. If you wander three blocks westward to 13th Avenue, you\'ll find all sorts of wonderful places to eat, drink, and shop, including a New Seasons Market, Gino\'s, A Cena, Wei Wei, and the always beautiful Notary Ceramics. The sprawling green space of Westmoreland Park is half a mile northeast, with the manicured Eastmoreland Golf Course approximately half a mile beyond.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fbdbad8a-283a-4ec3-ab0c-a7a1df1d5980.jpg',8761908,20,'45.46295','-122.64759',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,115.00,2,30,158,4.90,3939886),(222,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4014812','Large 1-bdr Condo in Walkable Hawthorne','Experience the iconic Hawthorne area with breweries, cafes, restaurants, music venues, two of Portland\'s largest food-cart pods and a park, all within short a short walk (3-10 minutes). Two miles from downtown. 90 minutes to Mt Hood skiing. <br /><br />This is no sterile investment property; It\'s my actual home styled for living! At this time, only guests with a complete/informative profile and at least 5 reviews accepted. Thanks for understanding :)','Popular Buckman neighborhood between Belmont and Hawthorne Blvd. Walkable to cafes, food carts, vintage shops, movie theatre, great restaurants, bars, etc.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-4014812/original/08ef65ba-771b-415a-b40a-98c774ce5c7e.jpeg',7029980,32,'45.51354150266015','-122.65066612072778',1,4,1.50,1.00,2.00,179.00,3,15,4,5.00,4014812),(223,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4025399','Clinton / Division -the best of SE!','Spacious, comfy basement apartment in the hip Clinton / Division area of SE.  Easy access to west side/downtown. Walking distance to restaurants, food carts, bars, shops, New Seasons grocery, MAX line. Bus stops, bike rentals, bike routes just outside the door.','We live in the trendy Division-Clinton neighborhood of Southeast Portland. You can walk to it all, from Portland\'s famous food carts to hidden gems to four-star extravaganzas -Pok Pok, Ava Gene\'s, Bröder, Bollywood Theater and American Local. You know that dive bar famous for its fried chicken? Mere blocks away...ask and we\'ll tell you where ;) .<br /><br />It\'s also terrific for cyclists, with a Nike Bike stand two blocks away and bike streets and urban greenways all around.<br /><br />On chilly, gray days, you might want to hit the beautiful sauna and steam spa Löyly --it\'s just a short walk away, is reasonably priced and is a neighborhood treasure. <br /><br />The Orange Max line crosses the Tillikum Bridge --an activity in and of itself. OMSI, the Oregon Museum of Science and Industry is a great resource for kids and is a short bike/drive or a longer walk from our house.<br /><br />And we are also not far from Hawthorne Ave. for Powell\'s, etc. On the SE river esplanade you can walk','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/75739145/ddedbd78_original.jpg',128686,25,'45.50408','-122.64265',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,70.00,2,40,196,4.88,4025399),(224,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4026064','Custom Studio w/AC , Alberta Arts District','Artist created studio in the heart of the Alberta Arts district, features lots of reclaimed wood & steel. Situated one block off the bustling Alberta street, this gorgeous studio accomodates 2, or can squeeze in a family of 4.<br /><br />\"I\'ve stayed in roughly 30 different AirBNB\'s and Alex\'s is the best I remember\"<br /> Kris, recent guest<br />\"Alex\'s place was my all time favorite Airbnb. Super thoughtful special touches\"<br />Michelle, recent guest<br />\"Beautiful little gem in the heart of Alberta!\"<br />Jodi, recent guest','Alberta is a thriving artist community, with a quirky mix of fun and eclectic cafes, restaurants, bars, shops, art galleries, music venues, movie theatre & theatre.<br />Last Thursday is a wonderful experience, especially in the summer months when Alberta street is closed to traffic from 6pm -9pm. Artists of all genres sell their wares. Wander up & down, then find an outside spot to people watch! (Please note: this is an occasion where parking becomes scarce and my (usually) quiet corner can get a little loud.)<br />There are several parks within walking/biking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/55eeffe0-84eb-451e-ba8f-f76c1e0f5260.jpg',14055038,1,'45.55896','-122.63895',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,95.00,1,30,1100,4.95,4026064),(225,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4041500','Heart of Southeast - Spacious 2 bedroom Craftsman','No added cleaning fee. Modern amenities in a beautiful, spacious century-old Portland Craftsman home.<br />*Please note that hardwood floors throughout the house above our co-hosts make this accommodation not appropriate for guests traveling with toddlers and other children under 12 years of age','This is a quiet neighborhood within walking distance to such local favorites as Ava Genes, Cibo, Bollywood Theater, Salt n\' Straw, Division Wines, Harlow, Apizza Scholls, Fried Egg I\'m In Love, Farmhouse Kitchen, Powell\'s Books,  Porque No?, the original Stumptown Coffee location, the Baghdad Theatre, and New Seasons market.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-4041500-unapproved/original/a77ec198-f952-4f60-b4b6-1a66c7a28257.JPEG',20955728,8,'45.50864','-122.62255',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,183.00,2,21,488,4.86,4041500),(226,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4054099','Modern Reed College Apartment','Apartment with private entrance & patio. Light & airy with 2 bedrooms, full kitchen & living room. Located blocks from Reed College, close to the Eastmoreland Golf Course & Crystal Springs Rhododendron Garden. Newly renovated bath (2021) with a walk in shower. Between Sellwood/Westmoreland & Woodstock. Gigantic Brewery and food carts are nearby. Downtown is 15 minutes.<br /> <br />We follow COVID 19 guidelines in cleaning between guests, disinfecting high touch areas.<br /><br />ASTR Permit on file','Great walking neighborhood. Blocks to Reed College. Close to the Eastmoreland Golf Course and the Crystal Springs Rhododendron Garden.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-4054099/original/d522e7a4-5b0d-4188-9667-054c39303865.jpeg',21024600,61,'45.48816','-122.62806',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,106.00,3,30,60,5.00,4054099),(227,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4084311','Convenient, Comfortable and Private','Private guest suite for 1 or 2; separate entrance w/full in room bath, mini-fridge, & microwave.  Short walk to Trendy Alberta Arts District, little longer walk to Historic Mississippi Area.  Ten minute drive to Downtown Portland & the Pearl District for amazing restaurants, shops/night Life.  Bus stop across the street. #72 drives up Alberta.  #8 goes past the MODA and Convention Center. Close to I-5.  Great neighborhood.  PDX Airport 15-20 min. drive.  Quiet time from 10:00 p.m. to 8:00 a.m.','15 to 20 minutes from PDX Airport. Close to parks, walking distance to coffee shops, great restaurants, food carts and grocery stores.  Ten minute drive to downtown. Yellow Max line easy walking distance.  Close to Alberta Art and Mississippi Districts with great restaurants and shopping.  Historic NE Neighborhood on tree lined street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/54516832/0b784cdc_original.jpg',18861712,14,'45.564092046398784','-122.66287918412279',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,2,30,306,4.95,4084311),(228,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4198752','Live like a local in Laurelhurst—family friendly','This beautiful apartment features everything you need to enjoy Portland like a local in the heart of the popular Laurelhurst neighborhood. Enjoy a gourmet kitchen, 2 comfortable bedrooms, shared backyard, safe, quiet street and easy access to public transit.','Centrally located on a quiet street between Mt Tabor Park and Laurelhurst Park, it offers urban living at its finest--walk to everything--transit, restaurants, night life, grocery stores and more. We\'re just 5 blocks from the popular Belmont corridor and 12 short blocks from the  Hawthorne neighborhood shops. We are 15 minutes from downtown and yet 30 minutes from the incredible scenic Columbia River Gorge!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/07bf0568-6720-4a5d-b625-f02289373827.jpg',13825879,52,'45.52113','-122.61685',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,120.00,2,28,552,4.89,4198752),(229,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4204652','Soothing Studio Among the Trees (1)','This is a renovated studio with a private, south-facing deck in a historic Buckman home that was converted to apartments in the 1920s. It is on a quiet, tree-lined street, but is central to everything Portland has to offer. Go out on the town or enjoy a meal in and feel right at home.','We are two blocks from Colonel Summers Park and the legendary, original Cartopia food carts and the new Asylum food carts. Also within walking distance is a year-round farm stand, two grocery stores, and a plethora of excellent restaurant and entertainment venues. We\'re happy to offer recommendations.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/81615070/813553f4_original.jpg',3867866,32,'45.51291','-122.64946',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,87.00,30,1125,83,4.88,4204652),(230,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4210084','Portland Belmont House—Main Floor','Our Urban Victorian, close to restaurants, gourmet markets, and food carts has easy access to anywhere! Enjoy quiet porch off main bedroom, lush yard, stone patio. It is an eco-renovated, solar powered, gem in quirky, close-in Portland neighborhood.','I love that our neighborhood is a walkable, vibrant neighborhood only a few minutes to everything.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/67314796/c8e7830b_original.jpg',21846830,16,'45.51616','-122.63398',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,132.00,1,180,229,4.96,4210084),(231,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4210881','Portland Belmont House—Eco Studio','A clean, modern step-down, lower floor space with 9\' ceilings and radiant heat. It is located in a beautifully renovated 130 year old house. Our spacious eco-room ( solar energy space) is minutes to downtown, short walk to Hawthorne, a stones throw to Belmont Dairy Block. Charming & tucked away.','Vibrant and quirky.  Beautiful parks, shopping, gourmet grocery stores, world class, affordable restaurants, and food carts galore.  Public transportation a stone\'s throw away and minutes to downtown Portland. Described by Portlanders as \"Close-in, Southeast\", or better known as the Belmont/Hawthorne area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/52910847/6ccbb846_original.jpg',21846830,16,'45.51794','-122.63292',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,99.00,1,90,254,4.94,4210881),(232,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4256044','Thoughtfully Detailed & Appointed Guest Suite','Private Queen ADU guest suite, with \"Kitchenette\", in lovely, safe, clean, aesthetically beautiful NE Portland.  PLEASE DO NOT  BOOK BEFORE READING THE LISTING to insure this \"Airbnb Home Share\"  is the perfect fit for your optimum comfort and needs.','NE Portland is Portland\'s  trending/hip adult playground.—it\'s become a destination for eating, drinking and window shopping, thanks in large part to the Alberta/Mississippi/Williams Arts districts.  The neighborhood is very close, (walking distance), to a couple of parks, several great coffee shops, great restaurants, bars, McMenamins Kennedy school, and healthy grocery stores plus just 2 miles from a shopping mall. There\'s a Park called Forest Park which in one of the largest inner city parks in the world; you can take a bus and hike around there all day. The Portland Zoo, rose gardens and Japanese gardens are all in Forest Park.<br /><br />Alberta St is a 6 1/2 block walk, 3 min car ride and 5 min bike ride.   You\'ll find great bars, restaurants, art galleries and shopping on Alberta as well as coffee, yoga and the stuff that make Portland pleasantly \"weird\"<br /><br />Mississippi 30min walk and Williams, 20 min walk are must do streets as well for all the same reasons Alberta is on','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/637048c4-86d9-4f81-acab-4b7934bb6607.jpg',748943,46,'45.54749','-122.62853',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,79.00,1,28,289,4.87,4256044),(233,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4257909','Private Studio, Lofted Bed, Soaking Tub & Patio','Located in SE near the Hawthorne & Belmont districts, just a skip away from Division, this tiny house was crafted with efficiency, comfort and style in mind - perfect for vacation, business travelers or for folks who want to try out the minimalist lifestyle. With a cozy lofted sleeping area, queen sofa bed below, fully-equipped kitchen, bathroom with deep soaking tub/shower, and efficient HVAC unit to keep you comfortable in any weather, you\'ll have everything you need for your Portland stay!','The residential neighborhood provides a lovely place to rest. You\'ll also have the best of Southeast Portland right out your door: Laurelhurst and Mount Tabor parks; the commercial buzz of the Hawthorne and Belmont districts (thrift stores, Powell\'s Books, bars, restaurants, food carts, Stumptown Coffee, Lucky Strike, Apizza Scholl\'s, Tabor Bread, Albina Press, and more); the People\'s Yoga Southeast; Belmont Library; two grocery stores (Fred Meyer and New Seasons) are in walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-4257909/original/65469e96-5a55-4c6a-b459-bd524a6f205d.jpeg',22096995,16,'45.51741','-122.6204',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,85.00,30,1125,396,4.85,4257909),(234,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4263742','Roomy suite with kitchenette','Spacious basement suite in residential north Portland neighborhood. Queen bed, kitchenette, bathroom, and dining / living area all to yourself. <br /><br />Central AC keeps the space cool even on the hottest summer days days. Friendly hosts who are committed to professional, equitable, safe and responsive hospitality.<br /><br />Laundry shared with hosts down the hall from your suite.','Portsmouth is a residential neighborhood of working people with green yards, walkable streets, and single family houses. It\'s home to beautiful 35-acre Columbia Park and New Columbia, one of Portland\'s most diverse communities. <br /><br />There\'s very little that is trendy or even commercial about Portsmouth itself, but it lies between North Portland town centers St. Johns and Kenton, which offer restaurants, coffee shops, movie theaters, and shops. These town centers are each about 2 miles away. Downtown Portland is about a 15-30 minute drive, depending on traffic.<br /><br />Village Market is a small convenience store about 4 blocks away and offers healthy groceries, staples, and a small cold deli case. <br /><br /><br />The Charles Jordan Community Center is 1 block from the house and offers simple public gym facilities for a small fee. <br /><br />See \"Guide\" for more on local attractions.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6NDI2Mzc0Mg%3D%3D/original/daebac54-f394-416d-a2e0-5f89c400cfdd.jpeg',22131920,60,'45.58635','-122.71368',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,63.00,2,21,69,4.81,4263742),(235,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4264248','No Cleaning Fee, Private-bath, Free Parking for 2!','The house is located in the quiet historic Kenton Neighborhood.  A bright & spacious room with a private bathroom comfortably sleeps for 2. FREE & easy street parking. The kitchen & laundry are not included. The house is 7 miles to downtown and 8miles to PDX, a 10-minute drive to Alberta & Mississippi district, 5-min walk to the bus stop & a 12-min walk to the Max Transit Yellow line Kenton/N. Denver station. Cafés, bars & great restaurants (with outdoor seating) & organic grocery stores nearby!','The house is located in the quiet historic Kenton neighborhood.  <br /><br />#The following recommended restaurants are all around 12 min walk distance—<br /><br />* Swift & Union, is a bright, airy gastro pub with outdoor seating offering seasonal New American plates, craft beer & house cocktails  Rated 4.5 on G.<br />* Casa Maya.  4.5 rating on G.    <br />* King Burrito. 4.6 stars on G.<br />* Posies Bakery & Café is for a great cup of coffee, fresh pastries & breakfast sandwiches. 4.6 G. rating.<br />* Pizza Fino. 4.4 star rating on G.<br />* Po’ Shines Cafe De La Soul, southern food. 4.3 G. rating.<br />* Parkside Restaurant and Lounge is a pub by Kenton Park. It has outdoor seating. 4.3 G. rating.<br /><br /># 1 mile away is Tiny Bubble Room, with southern-style food, and good drinks. 20-min walk.  4.8 rating on G.<br /><br /># Mayfly Taproom And Bottle Shop offers a great selection of wine and beer. It is 0.7 miles from the house or a 15-minute walk.  4.9 G. rating.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d7c4aa4b-1459-4f8a-b78c-0e49a4ee320e.jpg',9260383,55,'45.58717','-122.69465',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,1,3,571,4.76,4264248),(236,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4276758','Zen Modern in Historic N Miss. area/ Sanitized!!','Enjoy urban life in this luxurious newer constructed 3 bedroom, 2.5 bath home.  Located in the vibrant historic N. Mississippi area, you will enjoy a real taste of Portland, surrounded by cafes, boutiques, live music, and exciting culture... ENJOY! We also have a fabulous central A/C unit in the house.”, as well as a beautiful gas fireplace for cooler weather.','This property is located blocks away from the very popular North Mississippi area, which is filled with vibrant businesses of all sorts.<br />In addition, our home sits two short blocks away from beautiful Peninsula Park. This park has a lovely fountain surrounded by one of Portland\'s oldest rose gardens. The park also has tennis courts, a great children\'s play ground and public pool.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/53725721/da7678fc_original.jpg',20090994,24,'45.56436','-122.67561',1,6,2.50,3.00,3.00,330.00,3,1125,71,4.92,4276758),(237,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4315756','Private Room, Bath, Kitchenette & Garden Paradise','Just a few blocks to coffee shops, restaurants, bars, Whole Foods, Irving Park and lovely walking neighborhoods. 15 min. walk to the popular N Mississippi Ave and the Alberta Arts dist. Garden-level suite within warm and inviting art-filled house, with very private guest room, leafy and private yard with tables and chairs. You\'ll appreciate the cool of the daylight-basement space. My place is ideal for the solo traveler coming to town for work or adventure or for couples exploring the area.','This block is the best in the neighborhood! It is quiet without being uptight and there\'s always plenty of parking. There are other airbnb\'s and it\'s very neighborly. We\'re just 3 blocks from Whole Foods and a hub of other businesses, as well as a few good bars, coffee and brunch spots and are also a reasonable walk to the bustling shopping districts of N Mississippi and Alberta Streets.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-4315756/original/28ac6ba5-9933-40e9-9a9a-222fc8af10aa.jpeg',22404852,6,'45.55324','-122.6532',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,30,30,80,4.93,4315756),(238,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4325619','Mt Tabor, Lincoln Suites ~ Private and comfortable','A private entrance will take you (in basement) to this comfortable, quiet space with a sitting area with a 50\" TV with Netflix, mini fridge, microwave etc. <br /><br />The bedroom has reading lights and a queen size bed. Updated linens/towels are provided along with room to hang your clothes. En suite bathroom with amenities including a bidet.<br /><br />The home is situated within walking distance from the best city park, restaurants and shopping! Mass transit is steps away and on a main bike thoroughfare.','The Mt. Tabor neighborhood is a perfect blend of residential, the best restaurants, shopping and sightseeing. You can walk to get to most places or a quick Uber/Lyft or mass transit ride is also easy.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-4325619/original/ef9bc09e-ba4e-4955-b38e-717e83026c98.jpg',22461545,15,'45.50857','-122.60111',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,78.00,1,30,372,4.94,4325619),(239,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4333005','Cozy Room in Vintage Belmont Home','Great base to explore Portland!  Easy walk to over 70 restaurants, shops, and bars in the vibrant Belmont/ Hawthorne area.  The 1910 renovated house includes a Moroccan arched bathroom with clawfoot tub and spacious garden.  Has fan, but no a/c.  I only accept guests who have previous reviews from airbnb.','The Sunnyside area  is one of the most attractive and accessible in Portland.  It is great for walking and biking.  It is full of \"keep Portland weird\" spaces in common places and has a friendly neighborhood spirit.  People say \"hi\" to others as they walk past their homes.  You can walk to many excellent, ethnic restaurants, 3 small privately owned, movie theatres, breweries to sample our renowned craft beers,   unique shops, and a smaller model of Powells book store on Hawthorne.  It\'s a mixed neighborhood with all ages and types of people.  I love just walking around my neighborhood and noticing what people are doing with their gardens and houses.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/96651954/fc4774f1_original.jpg',9624551,16,'45.51495','-122.63221',2,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,78.00,3,1125,87,4.85,4333005),(240,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4341988','Bright Hawthorne Cottage Available','Our newly built cottage set in a private rose garden sleeps four comfortably and features a full kitchen & bathroom. Located two blocks from the trendy Hawthorne District  / Division Street, this little house is great for exploring Portland shopping and dining and all it has to offer!','The cottage is located in a very quiet, family-friendly neighborhood, only a short distance from downtown and other trendy neighborhoods in Southeast and Northeast Portland. Guests of all ages can also enjoy the public park directly behind the house.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/54535478/a005f9c1_original.jpg',22541617,8,'45.50896','-122.63088',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,130.00,30,30,195,4.93,4341988),(241,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4363868','Spacious Home in Alberta Arts!','Enjoy a stylish stay at this centrally-located, 2br/2ba home in the Alberta Arts District, walk to many restaurants and shopping, perfect for digital nomads, traveling professionals, or those displaced for temporary periods. Bright sun highlights a modern and updated Chef\'s Kitchen, with extensive counter space, new gas range/hood, and an open and inviting layout between kitchen and dining/living area, excellent for cooking and entertaining in your Home away from Home for the Holidays!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-4363868/original/e70becce-36ce-4cf2-9128-82db67164edf.jpeg',18163672,14,'45.558103510801416','-122.65534264213844',1,3,2.00,2.00,2.00,113.00,31,365,0,1.00,4363868),(242,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4372088','Portland Perfection','Amazing standalone unit in the Sellwood neighborhood of SE Portland.  Every amenity you can imagine, along with period details and decor.  Gas fireplace, gas range, AC, custom cabinets and more.  Nearby coffee, restaurants, shops and parks.','I know, we\'re biased.  But we\'re staunch believers that Sellwood/Westmoreland is one of the best neighborhoods in America.  <br /><br />Located just three miles south of downtown Portland and over the Sellwood Bridge, the Sellwood/Westmoreland neighborhood is brimming with unique shops, delicious dining and fabulous adventures.<br /><br />Approximately two miles in length and a mile wide, the teardrop-shaped area is rich in natural and recreational amenities. We have four public parks (Westmoreland, Sellwood, Sellwood Riverfront & Johnson Creek), hiking paths (Oaks Bottom Refuge), a public golf course, a bicycle/pedestrian-only thoroughfare (the Springwater Corridor) and the center of Portland\'s antique shopping.<br /><br />With a wide variety of shopping and dining choices, our two historic neighborhoods dating from 1876, make it easy to enjoy everything that Sellwood/Westmoreland has to offer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3de9cfee-abf7-4a36-9a38-429095750dea.jpg',4099316,20,'45.46839','-122.65457',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,159.00,3,1125,97,4.98,4372088),(243,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4412762','Clean, cozy \"mother-in-law\" apt. in newer home!','Cute, clean, cozy private apartment that is your private sanctuary.  No shared spaces or amenities -- it\'s all yours!  <br /><br />Huge king bed, queen sleeper sofa, private entrance, kitchenette, full bath, back patio.  Convenient to everything.  Find your home away from home in Portland!','Kenton is an old neighborhood, and one of the few places left in Portland that still feels like Portland of 20 years ago.  It\'s tiny and quaint, but somehow you can still do all the shopping, eating, drinking, strolling and ig pic snapping you need without walking more than 5 blocks from my front door.  And when you do want to slide downtown or to parts farther afield, the I-5 onramp is close enough to be convenient (but far enough to not be subjected to highway noise and exhaust), and public transit is (lightrail and bus) is within easy walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/59213297/4cd8571d_original.jpg',22906371,55,'45.58003','-122.68684',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,237,4.87,4412762),(244,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4440990','Multnomah Village Studio','Come visit beautiful Portland and stay in our private studio. Just 15-minutes from Downtown, the studio is perfect for two with a full bath and kitchen. Explore Multnomah Village or just hang out and listen to the wind in the trees.','Multnomah Village has everything that\'s great about Portland without being right in the middle of the chaos. We\'re walking distance to food carts, a farm stand, great coffee, breakfast joints, fro-yo, bars (from classy to divey) and a Safeway. There are only two measly blocks standing between you and one of Portland\'s best selections of beer and wine! If you\'re into fresh air, check out nearby Gabriel Park. It\'s amazing.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9658a14d-8a44-49ed-ad9a-901ef9ef0fa6.jpg',23051392,18,'45.46553','-122.71113',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,2,22,336,4.91,4440990),(245,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4457868','Modern Garden Studio Self Check & Private Entrance','Newly remodeled detached studio located one block from Division, the food hub of Portland. Bright and clean, self check in, private entrance, private garden nook, queen size bed and free on site parking and one block from the bus.','We are located in the Richmond neighborhood, voted \"Best City Neighborhood\" in Sunset Magazine\'s article \"24 Best Places To Live & Work\".<br /><br />Conveniently located within walking distance to some of the best restaurants in Portland and a short drive/15 walk to all the shops on Hawthorne street. We are 10-15 minute walk from the base of Mt. Tabor park, which boasts public tennis courts, jogging trails, children\'s play structure, basketball courts, and a spectacular view of Portland on a clear day.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/57343971/e98a81c6_original.jpg',3022438,8,'45.50583','-122.61383',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,76.00,1,31,737,4.90,4457868),(246,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4469025','Cozy bedroom in N. Portland ranch','Room available in North Portland 2 bdrm/1 bath one-level home situated between Univ. of Portland and St. Johns, only 15-20 minutes to downtown by car, 35 min by transit. St. Johns and nearby area has a small neighborhood feel w/ bars restaurants and coffee shops. <br /><br />My street is quiet, safe and the neighbors are friendly.<br /><br />I am a middle-aged white male, empty-nester that has an extra room, check it out for a short-term or middle-term stay! I\'ll be at work during the week and out of the way!','I live in the Portsmouth neighborhood, which is flanked by University Park to the south and St Johns to the west. It is a mix of white collar professionals, students, families and blue collar workers. This part of town has historically been working-class, but with the influx of new Oregonians that demographic is changing. <br /><br />Housing in this area is still one of the relatively close-to-downtown neighborhoods that is somewhat affordable, though that is changing, enabling some young families to move here. <br /><br />St Johns has a small town feel with businesses clustered together and is very walk-able, and is also going through a demographic shift. During the summer there is a small farmers market on Saturday mornings at the \"downtown\" public plaza. Other offerings include an old movie theater playing first-run movies cheaper than you\'ll find anywhere else in town (St. John\'s Twin Theater), as well as multiple restaurant/food options (including vegan/vegetarian), coffee options','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-4469025/original/713bb3ed-1044-4dfb-bea0-3e0782322fcd.jpeg',2623945,60,'45.58538','-122.72375',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,30,365,102,4.85,4469025),(247,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4481444','Cute Cottage in SE Clinton area!','The Queensway Cottage is tucked back in our large South East back yard complete with a small kitchenette, queen bed, a small smart tv with no cable and a bathroom with tile shower. Located just a few blocks from the Clinton and Division street restaurants and bars!','Close to popular South East Portland restaurants, Get downtown in minutes!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/56334797/8ef3e6a1_original.jpg',66254675,25,'45.50057','-122.64392',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,67.00,2,14,517,4.82,4481444),(248,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4483736','Cozy, bright, spacious studio house','Recently remodeled single bedroom house, rebuilt for natural light, efficiency (solar panels, cellulose & foam insulation, mini-split heating/cooling, all new appliances) and comfort w/ oversized clawfoot tub and bidet toilet.','Arbor Lodge is a family-friendly neighborhood, quiet at night, bustling through the day with joggers, cyclists and people of all ages strolling down our tree-lined streets. Great coffee shops, grocery stores, restaurants and bars are all within a 10-minute walk.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/58878077/4636ac78_original.jpg',17225282,51,'45.57474','-122.68913',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,185.00,30,1124,12,4.83,4483736),(249,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4491259','Bright Mississippi AC MAX 2 Dwntwn Portland, OR','Welcome to my Portland Sunny 1st floor apartment.  Modern and well equipped private 1 bedroom 1 bath apartment.  This home features a comfy, spacious bedroom + private bathroom  with tub and shower and full kitchen.  SMART TV, Wifi in a charming 1908 Craftsman Duplex. Located on the 1st floor. Perfect for long stays. Great front porch. 1 Mini split A/C & Heat. Street parking .2 blocks to Yellow Line MAX lite rail 15 minutes 2 DOWNTWN Walk to Mississippi Historic District Shops, Bars, Cafes','Overlook Neighborhood - Historic Mississippi Avenue District.  The neighborhood has over 60+ shops and restaurants. Downtown is a 10 minute drive or quick public transport trip (Max Light Rail)  and the airport is 20 minutes away, so you can live in a fun, artsy, beautiful, tree lined neighborhood while still being close to everything! Please note just like any city it\'s best to keep all property doors and cars locked while visiting Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-4491259/original/d17e95e1-03b6-48f7-bc1b-d7f269faf40e.jpeg',477663,13,'45.55255','-122.67941',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,101.00,31,180,69,4.61,4491259),(250,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4493001','Mad Court House - Private Apartment','I live in a two-story ranch home with a full daylight two-bedroom apartment on the lower level. With full southern exposure to a forested green-space, it\'s anything but MAD! After goings on about town, come here to relax and revitalize.','Secluded inner city home which abuts a forested area with walking trails. Very quiet safe neighborhood with occasional wildlife sitings. Great location for guests seeking a balance of Portland\'s natural beauty and city life.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/67480269/d3601d3e_original.jpg',22904946,62,'45.51292','-122.73847',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,133.00,2,90,91,4.76,4493001),(251,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4494541','Modern Home - KING BED - 15 Minutes to Everything','Welcome to our stunning Portland home! Our contemporary rental is the perfect place for your next corporate housing need or family gathering with 5 bedrooms and 3 bathrooms, and unique decor that sets it apart from the rest. The modern and sophisticated design features an open floor plan and numerous large windows. The living room is great for entertaining, and the kitchen is a chef\'s dream.','Cherry Park is a well established pocket neighborhood in a great location close to shopping with easy access to the freeways. On the SE side it\'s a short trip to the popular hot spots such as Alberta Arts, Hawthorne, Woodstock and Montavila. Just 15 minutes to airport or downtown. The Woodburn Outlet Mall is a straight shot from the I-205.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b2d67f32-646c-42cd-bb68-fc69c152482d.jpg',4702598,63,'45.50454','-122.55554',1,10,3.00,5.00,9.00,499.00,1,400,45,4.80,4494541),(252,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4512280','1,615 Great Reviews: Heart of Sellwood','Read our reviews! We love helping people plan their visit to our city! Please be aware that unfortunately we cannot host guests with animals.','When visiting Portland, where you stay is critical. You want to have easy access to everything. We have that. Our neighborhood is Sellwood- you can look it up online and see why it is such a desirable place to be. There are lots of antiques shops, coffee and tea houses, a Columbia Sportswear Outlet, restaurants, parks, bars, microbreweries and river access to the Willamette River all within a few blocks. We are also just minutes away from the bus and the Orange Line (light rail) that will take you right downtown. We are also close to Reed College, Lewis & Clark College, Oaks Park and Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-4512280/original/bcf69bb6-671b-46da-b990-dece65a114b2.jpeg',8474325,20,'45.46573','-122.65208',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,61.00,1,21,347,4.93,4512280),(253,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4518904','Cozy SE home with an 80 Walk Score!','Enjoy being steps away from countless restaurants, bars and coffee shops. Or don\'t move at all and enjoy a beautiful patio that is perfect for morning coffee or an evening cocktail.<br /><br />A ton of space including two bedrooms and 1.5 baths. A large kitchen is available stocked with everything you need to cook a feast.','SE is developing into \"the spot\" to be in Portland.  You can get to some of the best restaurants in town in just a few minutes and spend your days exploring the city or you can find the ocean and Mt. Hood only about an hour away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-4518904/original/bd69ce3e-afde-4f14-a6c1-5272c8780480.png',2312710,36,'45.49475','-122.59745',1,4,1.50,2.00,0.00,90.00,30,1125,85,4.84,4518904),(254,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4519533','Upstairs BR in Vintage Belmont Home','My cozy, upstairs bedroom is a great base to explore Portland.  You can walk to over 30 restaurants, shops, bars, and cafes in the vibrant Belmont/Hawthorne neighborhood.  My 1910 house has been lovingly renovated, while retaining its vintage charm. Please note:  I only accept guests who have previous reviews from airbnb.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/96647644/83b1c991_original.jpg',9624551,16,'45.51493','-122.63408',2,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,86.00,3,1125,91,4.92,4519533),(255,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4536608','Historic Hafner Haus, British Style Bed+Breakfast','The most central single family residence in downtown Portland, the Hafner Haus was built as a manse for Rev. Hafner and his family over a hundred years ago. We are a nonprofit organization and the price is a tax deductible suggested donation which enables us to maintain our historical church.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6NDUzNjYwOA%3D%3D/original/3f0024f5-5242-47da-9a3e-cafdc8d34b77.jpeg',8207605,44,'45.51527','-122.68647',2,4,1.00,1.00,6.00,33.00,30,125,52,4.73,4536608),(256,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4558343','Moving to Portland Central','Lovely, comfortable, tastefully decorated, sweet suite can be your base for exploring Portland. Close to parks, shopping, OHSU, L&C and downtown. Hood views from decks. Full amenities. Special discounts to those looking to buy a house in Portland.','Tucked in the hills between downtown Portland and the Willamette River, Terwilliger Heights is one of Portland\'s most desirable neighborhoods. Known for its unique homes, panoramic views, access to trails, and convenient location.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/60813964/984728bf_original.jpg',8530650,31,'45.48465','-122.68692',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,95.00,30,1125,135,4.90,4558343),(257,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4559235','Great Reviews! Heart of Sellwood','Read our reviews! We love helping people plan their visit to our city! Please be aware that unfortunately we cannot host guests with animals.','When visiting Portland, where you stay is critical. You want to have easy access to everything. We have that. Our neighborhood is Sellwood- you can look it up online and see why it is such a desirable place to be. There are lots of antiques shops, coffee and tea houses, a Columbia Sportswear Outlet, restaurants, parks, bars, microbreweries and river access to the Willamette River all within a few blocks. We are also just minutes away from the bus and the MAX (light rail)that will take you right downtown. We are also close to Reed College, Lewis & Clark College, Oaks Park and Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-4559235/original/f09c4011-48ee-462c-9173-21e4372efb2c.jpeg',8474325,20,'45.46636','-122.65195',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,61.00,1,21,460,4.85,4559235),(258,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4572931','St. Johns Farmhouse','Our home is simple, cozy and welcoming and people generally feel immediately at ease. It is walking distance to historical St. Johns, and 1-3 blocks from bus lines. By TriMet it\'s 25 minutes to downtown and 50 minutes to the airport. This is a peaceful street with great neighbors who all know each other and look out for one another. <br />The bed is very comfortable, and most guests say they\'ve gotten a great night\'s sleep!','Close to University of Portland, so great for family visiting students. This area is quite old and many of the houses on this street are from the early 1900\'s, so its got a certain charm to it. Very quiet and all the neighbors look out for each other.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-4572931/original/47c069a7-49dc-47dd-96bb-a48da478a6c4.jpg',21691680,42,'45.58494','-122.74654',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,39.00,2,21,173,4.96,4572931),(259,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4623759','Serene Alberta Arts Garden Casita.','Detached casita in one of the hippest neighborhoods in NE Portland; The Alberta Arts District.    3rd party bookings will not be accepted. The cleaning fee is based on the duration of long-term guests and due to COVID-19  deep cleaning protocols.   The cleaning fee will be reduced for guests staying one week or less.   There is a kitchenette; no oven.   The space is ideal for smaller breed dogs, and no cats.','Check out Petite Provence Bistro, The Tin Shed Cafe, Gumba, Proud Marys, Tumbleweed local made Boutique, and so much more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/27c84ea1-b508-441c-a848-77f7600e09e5.jpg',15693905,29,'45.5593','-122.64603',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,99.00,2,1125,197,4.94,4623759),(260,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4623988','Ate my way through Portland, Oregon','New and modern backyard cottage. All the conveniences of your own house. Great, central urban location near bars and restaurants. Walking distance to downtown, Oregon convention center,and Moda center. Easy access to all MAX, bus and streetcar lines. <br /><br />I have taken the time over the past 4 years to establish a lush and inviting back yard garden and patios, featuring many varieties of local species of plants and feeders to attract the fauna<br /><br />One way to visit and live the true Portland experience.','I love the proximity and access to everything! Located in Eliot, a quirky yet up-and-coming coveted Inner NorthEast Portland.  <br /><br />You\'ll be walking distance to many of the best attractions in Portland. A 30 minute walk downtown.  Lloyd Center mall, the Convention center, Emanuel Hospital all within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/32031198-53e1-42d7-bbbe-c7828c9a2d51.jpg',9032075,26,'45.53926','-122.66074',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,30,90,485,4.87,4623988),(261,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4624844','Private room, entrance + bath-Historic Hafner Haus','This listing is for a studio bedroom with a queen size bed and a twin.<br />You will have a private entrance and a private bathroom.<br />Your studio is on the main ground level of one of Portland historic homes. It is a large Portland style house in the very center of the city.<br />Your studio has a pocket door which is securely locked and private with regard to the remainder of the main house.<br />Upon request, we may be able to give  access to the main house + kitchen.','We are close to everything downtown. You might also be interested to know that there\'s a police rest stop in the church next door so it\'s a very safe neighborhood as well.<br /><br />Portland has a significant homeless population but in this corner of the city, we have good relationships with the individuals in transition.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6NDYyNDg0NA%3D%3D/original/564dfb79-8db8-4d4e-96a1-9f8f0b43d51a.jpeg',8207605,44,'45.51668','-122.68769',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,79.00,30,200,81,4.68,4624844),(262,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4638242','Belmont Dairy - Portlandia Central','Sunny southern exposure room with private bath in Belmont Dairy/Sunnyside area of  Southeast Portland. Our neighborhood is one Portland\'s of oldest and rich in Victorian homes with great restaurants, cafes, shopping all within minutes walk..','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/60971947/fc9bef55_original.jpg',23159593,16,'45.51585','-122.627',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,14,4.93,4638242),(263,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4644858','Central Historic Irvington Suite','Stay in a lovely remodeled basement apt within a 1905 home in the Historic NE Irvington area! Suite includes: 1 bd (queen), 1 ba, living room (with full-sized sofa sleeper available upon request) and kitchette/laundry room.  Walkscore 87, public transit 71 and biking 98! Walk to the OR Convention Center and the Moda Center (20 min). All are welcome. This unit is a great fit for those out and about during the day, but want a quiet place at night. Support local Portland teachers by booking here!','We are on the edge of the Irvington neighborhood which is formally registered as historic and \'amazing\' (not really the latter).  All the homes within the Irvington area itself, with a few exceptions, date from the early 1900s or late 1800s.<br /><br />We are a ~15 minute walk to the Oregon Convention Center and have had many guests stay attend events and avoid renting a car.  It is very centrally located.  Our guests are able to walk to the streetcar stop which can take you to the Pearl District in Downtown Portland.  We are biking distance to almost all the \"fun\" neighborhoods such as the Alberta Arts, Mississippi and Hawthorne districts.   There are cafes, restaurants and a non-profit brewery all within a 15 minute walking radius.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-4644858/original/ad68616b-7ca3-4af2-b6d8-b1502f104bba.jpeg',2200022,7,'45.53994','-122.65787',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,57.00,2,31,787,4.93,4644858),(264,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4648534','The perfect spot!','Fully furnished, stylish, modern, 600 SF, 1 bedroom  ADU <br />(in-law apartment ) located in historic, close-in Sellwood','Sellwood is a close-in historic neighborhood located in SE Portland. It has a small neighborhood vibe with tons of choices for food carts, restaurants, brew pubs, and shopping within a short walking distance! It is also blocks away from the Willamette river, Oaks Bottom wildlife refuge, and an extensive bike path system for outdoor activity. It is a very comfortable and low key place to relax and recreate with the bonus of being just minutes away from any other neighborhood you want to explore.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6NDY0ODUzNA%3D%3D/original/54282904-430b-4034-8f8c-04b3f1237480.png',24064951,20,'45.46455','-122.65481',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,30,1125,13,5.00,4648534),(265,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4671958','60\'s Modern Home with Hot Tub, Art, Chef\'s Kitchen','Charming St Johns saltbox with vintage details throughout. Large open living spaces, lots of natural light, huge living room, hardwoods on main floor. Comes with patio + hot tub. Great beds. Proper kitchen. Quiet, safe, lovable neighborhood.','The Cathedral Park neighborhood of St. Johns is a tightly knit community of old timers and young families. Our sweet street neighborhood watches out for each other. It\'s a short walk down to Cathedral Park, where you will surely enjoy hours under the beautiful St. Johns Bridge. Downtown, four coffee houses vie to pull the perfect espresso shot, two first run movie theaters sell beer and pizza along with the regular fare. You\'re a traffic-free 20 minutes away from downtown Portland and a world away in terms of peace, safety and quiet.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8842ca23-b0e3-460d-b4c3-c7b130b9435f.jpg',24167390,42,'45.59612','-122.76363',1,4,1.00,3.00,3.00,100.00,30,80,0,1.00,4671958),(266,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4742398','Cozy/quiet house, walkable to all things great!','Hello, front porch! This place is close to everything no matter how you choose to get there. Everything you need. No more, no less. Warm and  comfortable, the bed alone is worth it.<br /><br />Please read our reviews, we\'ve been doing this a while and they speak volumes. Y\'all will feel right at home here. Every single person that stays here, loves it. We are both very experienced AirBnB Hosts and Guests. <br /><br />Our neighborhood is rad and we stoped trying to keep up with our online AirBnB guidebook.','We are a 25min bike ride, 15 min drive or a 30 min straight-shot bus ride to downtown. Although, there is a lot of fun to be had on this side of the river.  We bought our house because of it\'s location.  We\'re close enough to everything.  Our neighborhood itself is awesome.  We are within walking distance to many small businesses,  great parks with a Saturday Farmers Market and the Alberta Arts district (And all of the concerts/ galleries/ cafe\'s/ pubs/ shops that come with that.) We are even closer to the Dekum commercial district (Coffee/ restaurants/ massage/ bars.) <br /><br />Please check out our guidebook, as it will get updated often.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/eb65691c-739a-479f-8282-8d49add4690b.jpg',24465004,45,'45.56914','-122.65323',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,96.00,2,1125,337,4.92,4742398),(267,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4767262','60\'s Modern w/ Separate Art Studio','Turn of the century St Johns Saltbox with vintage details throughout. Large open living spaces, lots of natural light, a huge living, hardwoods on the main.','St. Johns is kid and family friendly. Perfect for dog owners, as you\'re within easy walking distance of two great dog parks and Forest Park. Our street is safe and quiet. Downtown St. Johns is known for its vintage shops, coffee and cocktail bars, movie theaters and restaurants. ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6NDc2NzI2Mg%3D%3D/original/13f12142-b72e-4e56-a1f5-b5abcdc69381.jpeg',2695720,42,'45.59712','-122.76369',1,4,1.00,3.00,3.00,171.00,30,60,0,1.00,4767262),(268,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4787390','Terry Street Retreat - Kenton Studio near MAX','Come explore North Portland! Finished basement studio with large kitchen, local art, and private entrance on a quiet street five minutes walk to MAX light rail and bars, shops, and restaurants on Denver Avenue, Kenton\'s main street in North Portland.','Kenton is a historic and happening neighborhood with very loyal and friendly residents. We are a five minute walk to Downtown Kenton which features two coffee shops (Posie\'s and Prince), three bars, several haircutting places (for some reason), library, post office, Paleo restaurant, pizza joint, awesome re-sale shop, antique stores, and more. <br /><br />If you walk seven minutes in the other direction, you come to our light rail station and a huge Fred Meyer, where you can buy pretty much anything.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/760b392d-d383-4ebf-9791-bdf51404a4e0.jpg',1007790,55,'45.58071','-122.68322',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,75.00,90,200,146,4.92,4787390),(269,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4794805','Cozy charming room quiet neighborhood.','Cozy Old Portland charm!  Bright, clean, safe & quiet neighborly street, central NE location, easy ride from airport.  <br /><br />On Neighborhood Greenway quiet streets. Close to bike rental, Hollywood, Alberta Arts District.  Walking trail, tennis courts, children\'s park, food carts, restaurants & coffee shops.<br />   <br />Full kitchen, access to grand piano & covered porches.  Shared with two cats & an occasional dog visitor, hosts sleep on 2nd Fl.  You\'ll have a PRIVATE room & bathroom with bath tub.','We are two blocks from Sacramento Street which has a trail that over looks the Rose City Golf Course, with stunning views of Mt. Hood.  You will also find a a walking trail along side the golf course, children\'s park, tennis courts, and baseball Dimond.  You can walk through the garden filled neighborhood to Pizza Otto\'s, Thai Season, Pho Corner, Mekha Restaurant, Petite Provence, Swiss Hibiscus, Clyde\'s Prime Rib Restaurant & Bar, Piccone’s Corner, Cabezon, Laurelwood, Basilisk, Ohana Hawaiian Cafe, Blue Diamond.  WE love Kianos coffee house, Bison coffee, Pips Donuts and Chai, The Barley Pod Food Park, Mom and Pop Wine Shop, Ben and Esther\'s Vegan Jewish Deli, Nicos Ice Cream shop, Peter\'s Cafe Bar, Tacovore, Hollywood Farmers Market and so much more!!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-4794805/original/cb064467-ba6f-4bf1-80c4-a1b925f0f75f.jpg',14802436,11,'45.54337','-122.60031',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,74.00,2,7,101,4.96,4794805),(270,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4795239','Exquisite Historic Suite- uptown','Located within walking distance to downtown Portland, NW 23rd and the Pearl district, this romantic private suite is appointed with all of the little luxuries found in a fine hotel.  There is a communal deck with mt. and river views available. 1 queen bed and a queen sofa bed available.','Portland Heights neighborhood is one of the most prestigious in Portland and a walker\'s dream.  Historic homes with rich interesting details are everywhere and Washington Park is a nice walk from here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-4795239/original/fdd32dad-6372-4d4c-aa16-32cbad87977a.jpg',24711856,54,'45.50761','-122.69855',2,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,135.00,1,1125,386,4.97,4795239),(271,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4862779','Buckman Garden Suite','Our private downstairs suite is infused with warmth and tranquility. It has a living room and a bedroom, a full bathroom, and a kitchenette. From our peaceful home you can easily walk to  Portland\'s best bars, restaurants, brew pubs & urban wineries.<br />If you have a car, let us know and we will reserve our driveway for you. This saves you from having to park a block or more away or from the risk of getting a ticket.','There is no end to how you can choose to experience Buckman, our innermost SE neighborhood. You can go to just breweries, or dive bars, vegan restaurants or just top rated restaurants, you could do a tour of our local distilleries, neighborhood breweries or urban wineries. You can walk to Revolution Hall or small theaters, or bus downtown to see a show at bigger theaters and venues. You could even just stay close in - all the amenities you would need are within blocks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/66307674/b5d270ad_original.jpg',4817279,32,'45.52235','-122.65012',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,105.00,4,30,299,4.86,4862779),(272,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4863271','Private guest suite in central SE','You get the second floor of our house to yourself, including a calm and cozy bedroom, a second bedroom/sitting room, and a spectacular bathroom. It\'s the best of both worlds: the privacy and self-check-in of a stand-alone space, plus all the access to your hosts that you want (or don\'t want!).<br /><br />You\'ll feel like a local staying on our quiet residential street in the walkable Brooklyn neighborhood. The house is on several bus lines, and it\'s only a 5+ minute drive to downtown and OHSU.','We love our mellow and modest little neighborhood that is close to everything. In under 10 minutes, you can walk to several coffee shops, a little organic market, a bottle shop, a public park, several dive bars, and the Aladdin Theatre for live music. If you venture a few minutes more, you can also walk to some of the best restaurants in the city on SE Division. We\'re also a 5-minute drive or a 20-minute bus ride away from downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/69933175/6a34ade1_original.jpg',25016067,56,'45.49752','-122.65793',2,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,1125,208,4.96,4863271),(273,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4894613','Cozy 2BD Hawthorne Guest Suite for Vacation or WFH','Our house is nestled in the heart of SE Portland on a quiet street one block off popular Hawthorne Blvd. Surrounded by parks, cafes, funky shops, restaurants, grocery stores and public transportation--all within walking distance.  You\'ll find your apartment is perfectly situated for exploring the city of roses.','Sunnyside Neighborhood in SE Portland is the sweetest spot to be. Situated one block off eclectic Hawthorne Blvd, you\'ll find yourself surrounded by some of Portland\'s finest places- Stumptown Coffee, Powell\'s Books, Por Que No, Apizza Scholls, Baka Ramen, Horse Brass, Belmont Station Bottle Shop, Gigantic Brewing, Baghdad Theater- to name a few. Many more lesser known, but equally stellar restaurants, shops and cafes await your visit, and we\'re more than happy to point you in the direction of a few we love. New Seasons Market and Grocery is just a few blocks away, if you need to grab a few food/drink items for the fridge. <br />Just up the street to the east of us is Mount Tabor Park, a huge forested park on an extinct volcano. It\'s loaded with trails to explore and an awesome view of the city. To the west lies beautiful Laurelhurst Park with paved paths that curve amongst huge Douglas fir trees and around a pond. Both parks are nice destinations for a stroll or run. All in all, our n','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-4894613/original/a4ae5f40-e22c-4ddc-bb1e-697d17d0efb1.jpeg',2111718,16,'45.51289','-122.61472',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,107.00,1,60,278,4.91,4894613),(274,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4907548','Sellwood Luxury Studio Home','Detached studio stand-alone home (17ft x 20ft), built by us in 2008. It has a king bed with kid gear if needed. It also has a full bath and a full kitchen (convection microwave oven instead of a conventional oven). Queen air mattress also available for extra guests. <br /> Location is fantastic!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/63118891/13efe5e6_original.jpg',25267321,20,'45.46015','-122.65385',1,4,1.00,0.00,1.00,100.00,2,30,222,4.89,4907548),(275,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4914388','Artful studio, Ladd\'s Addition, PDX','My charming artist studio space is located in the historical Ladd\'s Addition neighborhood. Once a garage that held the tools for restoring the 1925 home, it is now your key to exploring Portland on foot, bike or car.','Ladd\'s Addition is a great neighborhood for strolling around the rose gardens and is connected to the city bike route. It is a 10-20 minute walk to explore shopping on Hawthorne Boulevard or sample the food on  bustling Division St.  A fantastic grocery is only three blocks away (New Seasons) and is open 8am-10pm).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/73049014/d60efb9e_original.jpg',25307230,25,'45.50479','-122.65127',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,103.00,1,30,397,4.90,4914388),(276,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4921212','North Tabor Charming and Restful','I love that you walk through a garden to get to your spacious room. That it has a private entrance and access to veggie garden. Every thing you might need for your comfort is provided. I love the wooden soaking tub,soft bathrobe and comfey bed!','This is a quiet neighborhood with beautiful trees and yards fairly close to the beautiful Mount Tabor and its walking trails.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/63046612/dc96f810_original.jpg',25347302,52,'45.52576','-122.59789',2,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,79.00,2,30,53,4.91,4921212),(277,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4923100','New Cozy Basement Suite, Private Entry, Hawthorne','Warmth and comfort in winter.  Cool and soothing in summer. Sleeps 4+, has radiant floors, TV/Wi-Fi, washer/dryer, private bath and entrance. We are blocks from Hawthorne/Division food carts, Mt. Tabor Park. Transit to downtown. Enjoy home-roasted coffee and our fruited backyard!','We live 4 blocks from Mt. Tabor Park; 180 acres of huge trees, walking trails, open reservoirs, tennis and basketball courts, picnic areas and playground.  Every Wednesday, the park is closed to vehicular traffic. Hawthorne district is 5 blocks the other direction, with shops, restaurants, and theaters.  Food cart pods are also within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/86065280/c7d49cc5_original.jpg',25357111,15,'45.5114','-122.60498',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,95.00,1,30,802,4.88,4923100),(278,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4935985','Beautiful, Meditative House','Close in Mississippi/Williams area Victorian. Excellent  bus access from airport ; to downtown, the convention & MODA centers.  Quiet, peaceful and green,  but a short walk to all the restaurants, bars. boutiques, food carts, coffee shops and venues. Some of the highest rated and most popular eateries are on either street.<br />Large garden with lots of botanical interest and gathering spots.','Super convenient to get anywhere, fun to walk to Mississippi and Williams Avenues and New Seasons Market, food carts, park is two blocks away, quiet and verdant.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/82791638-cb38-495a-8248-9ef6ba2e0c7b.jpg',7389792,9,'45.54964','-122.67157',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,110.00,1,29,555,4.86,4935985),(279,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4958064','Portland, OR steps to Oregon Health and Sciences U','This charming and completely private studio has a king-size bed, a recently upgraded kitchen with a gas range, a TV with Roku, local channels, Wi-Fi, and a stacked Washer-Dryer.<br />There\'s a parking permit fee of $75.<br />Let me know if you have questions.<br />A parking permit allows you to park on the street, however, parking can be very limited. I Highly recommend not bringing a car.<br /><br />If you rent for 30 days you have to pay$465 in Taxes. If you rent for 31 days you pay Zero in tax.','Marquam Hill is also known as Pill Hill, because it is home to:<br /><br />-Oregon Health and Sciences University. <br />-Doernbecher Children\'s Hospital. <br />-VA Hospital <br />-Nursing School. <br />-Shriner\'s Hospital. <br />-Casey Eye Institute. <br />-The Dental School.<br /><br />Access to the Aerial Tram which leads to the Portland Streetcar and south waterfront, is just inside the hospital.<br /><br />Downtown Portland is an easy one mile drive. Or catch the number 8 bus, there is also a free shuttle to Downtown, and Portland State University.<br /><br />While in Portland, you may want to visit: <br />Pioneer Courthouse Square <br />The Portland Art Museum. <br />Chinese Gardens <br />The Gerding Theater <br />The Grotto <br />OMSI <br />Pittock Mansion <br />Living Room Theater <br />During the summer is Tom McCall Waterfront Park. <br />Multnomah Falls-- (website hidden) <br />Forest Park <br />Willamette Valley','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/66671279/c31fa51f_original.jpg',375683,30,'45.49694','-122.68854',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,45.00,30,1125,168,4.70,4958064),(280,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4963976','Handbuilt Alberta Arts Cottage','Featured in the NY Times! <br />This gorgeous custom home is the biggest little house on the block with raw wood throughout, a chefs kitchen, and a bed you won\'t want to leave. In the heart of Alberta you\'re a short walk from food, drink, parks and art.','Alberta Arts offers a wonderful mix of quiet streets and family homes with easy walking access to exceptional restaurants, bars, theaters, grocery stores, and coffee shops.<br /><br />The home is on Going Street, which is one of portland\'s \"bike boulevards\" optimized for biking around the city without heavy interaction with car traffic.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/62186231/8ee4277e_original.jpg',15103041,1,'45.55716030353737','-122.63480357971446',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,113.00,2,1125,746,4.96,4963976),(281,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/4975966','Cozy SE Portland Apartment','Spread out in our basement apartment! Separate entrance provides privacy. Plenty of amenities with easy access to the rest of Portland. Check-in is flexible.','Woodstock is a pretty great area to explore! A few bars, restaurants, and grocery stores nearby. Plus Reed College is just down the street offering a great hike through Reed Canyon.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0bb8ca8b-a4e7-4eb4-bd02-b72d8cc268e1.jpg',4497071,38,'45.4855','-122.61527',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,1125,195,4.88,4975966),(282,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5012460','Cozy 2 Bdrm In Popular SE Hawthorne','Take some time to relax in this cozy two bedroom house, only steps away from the popular Hawthorne St District\'s, Pok Pok, Salt & Straw, Por Que No, Stumptown Coffee, Laurelhurst Park and more. Enjoy the large deck, wifi & free street parking.','The house is located on a quiet, tree lined and designated bike route street in SE Portland. It is walking distance to Stumptown Coffee, popular food carts, Hawthorne St. shopping, Fred Meyers, New Seasons Market, Laurelhurst Park, Division St restaurants, and more... Enjoy free street parking or easy access to public transit, leading directly to The Pearl District, NE Alberta St, and The Portland PDX Airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/62751810/bd36f5b8_original.jpg',23400410,16,'45.51395','-122.62442',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,90.00,31,180,183,4.74,5012460),(283,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5041164','The Green Door Garden Cottage','Located in Concordia/Alberta Arts neighborhoods within walking distance to the Alberta Arts District, McMennimans Kennedy School Hotel and Pub, locally owned New Seasons Market and Concordia University. This newly constructed cottage has it all!  ','We love how our Neighborhood  feels like a small town yet we are close to city life and everything you want is with in easy reach. The well known Alberta Arts District is within walking distance offering great dining and shopping experience. Several beautiful parks and the Columbia Gorge is nearby for hiking and sight seeing.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/63109114/4dadca22_original.jpg',25897935,1,'45.56931','-122.62854',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,118.00,2,30,359,4.98,5041164),(284,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5051347','Inner SE Div/Clinton Modern/Private 5-Star APT','Situated just off Inner SE Division St, this remodeled, clean and sanitized, quiet, private 1-bedroom apartment is perfect for overnight stays or for use as a daily home-office. With ample parking, it is 1-block to some of Portland\'s finest restaurants, public transit & close to downtown. Walk score of 91! <br />Easy access to freeways, The Gorge and just about any part of town makes this the ideal spot for your Portland adventure.','Situated off Southeast Division St, as the New York Times wrote, ‘a formerly gritty strip of southeast Portland, [turned] into a gourmand’s wonderland of taverns, specialty markets, coffeehouses’, our neighborhood is one of Portland’s most vibrant. Retaining it’s classic charm of tree-lined streets this coveted residential neighborhood claims some of Portland’s best amenities. One block to several world-renowned restaurants and just a few more steps are a variety of bars, bakeries and restaurants. There is something for every palate including Ava Gene’s, Olympia Provisions, Broder, Nuestra Cocina, St. Honore Boulangerie, Bollywood Theatre, Cibo, and several Food Carts! Follow it up with some of the best artisanal ice cream at Salt and Straw or Pinolo Gelato. Need to pick up some groceries or snacks to have around the apartment? New Season’s Market, People’s Food Co-op, or the Clinton Corner Market are just a short stroll away. Looking for exercise? Take a run through the neighborhood o','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/64966837/6bf0c8fc_original.jpg',26081771,8,'45.50392','-122.63253',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,680,4.94,5051347),(285,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5103651','Graham Street Garden Suite','Garden level, light-filled studio with private entrance and private patio located in Portland’s Eliot neighborhood. Ideal for those on work assignment, medical/education rotation, between homes, or visiting the beautiful Pacific Northwest!','The Elliot Neighborhood, nestled in the heart of North Portland, is a vibrant and eclectic community known for its rich history, diverse culture, and a strong sense of togetherness. This dynamic neighborhood offers a blend of urban convenience and a welcoming, tight-knit atmosphere.<br /><br />The neighborhood supports a range of local businesses, from cozy cafes to unique boutiques. You can explore a variety of dining options, whether you\'re in the mood for artisanal coffee, international cuisine, or classic comfort food. Elliot is a foodie\'s paradise.<br /><br />Perhaps the most cherished aspect of the Elliot Neighborhood is its strong sense of community. Neighbors frequently come together for events, block parties, and community initiatives, making it an inviting place to call home.<br /><br />In the Elliot Neighborhood, you\'ll experience the best of Portland – a friendly, diverse community with a deep appreciation for history, culture, and creativity. It\'s a place where you can emb','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/91587438/6a3bf1cf_original.jpg',21379161,26,'45.54325','-122.6648',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,2,1125,116,4.91,5103651),(286,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5105762','Storybook Cottage with Beautiful Landscaping & Private Deck','Bring the kids to share in this thoughtfully crafted guesthouse. Say hello to resident chickens and hang out on a beautiful, private deck. Admire a framed insect collection on the way to bedrooms warmly decorated in a modern take on traditional comfort.<br /><br />You may be worried about traveling during this uncertain time of Covid-19. We understand! Please know that, as always, we\'re taking extra care to disinfect our Airbnb due to COVID-19. In addition, we will also be staggering our guests so that there is a 48-hour time period between groups. Your health and safety are our #1 priority.<br /><br />Being on a flag-lot, this home is extremely private with a great location to town. It\'s easy to hop on to I-5 North and be downtown in minutes or just stay in the Village or Hillsdale if you like a cozy neighborhood feel. Getting downtown can take anywhere from 10-25 minutes depending on the time of day. The lot is newly landscaped and we have a small urban farm with 6 chickens. Our gues','The cottage—McHoof Haudin Haus—is in quaint Multnomah Village, just south of Downtown Portland. Stroll down the street to restaurants, bars, and shops. Walk to Gabriel Park, where there\'s a picnic area, playground, and lots of sporting facilities. We\'re only 10min from downtown and in a great location to head West to the coast, South to the wine valley, or East to the scenic Gorge. We\'re happy to share advice on day trips!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e930fe17-59fb-47eb-b7a3-bbd1bfd67590.jpg',26381987,18,'45.47245','-122.70858',1,6,2.00,3.00,0.00,0.00,3,1125,267,4.97,5105762),(287,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5127548','Sweet Suite in Alberta Neighborhood','Enjoy a private 3-room suite: living, bedroom & bath, in our lovely 1910 Craftsman home. Residential, centrally located NE neighborhood. Close access to public transit or walk to great shopping/food districts. <br />Explore like a visitor, live like a local!','This neighborhood is called Piedmont, located 1/2 block off of Alberta Street, which is an active commercial strip. We\'re in NE Portland, on the residential east side of the Willamette river, which means the culture of downtown Portland is just on the other side of the river (10 minutes by car). The street is residential & homey, but you\'ll be just a close walk, bus or car ride to several fun hubs in every direction-Alberta Arts, Dekum, Williams & Mississippi.  Great shopping, dining and people watching is right at your doorstep.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5127548/original/e0510021-4763-43e9-882d-38da15963779.jpeg',7630516,14,'45.56101','-122.66292',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,1,7,485,4.97,5127548),(288,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5145373','Oasis NW Portland One Bedroom','Welcome to your bright, spacious one bedroom Oasis tucked off bustling NW 23rd Ave in the heart of the restaurant and shopping mecca of PDX. <br />Clean apartment with free W/D on site and plenty of comfortable space to enjoy Portland to the fullest! Mid-stay cleaning service available-message me for details.','All the eating, drinking, shopping you could want are at your finger tips in NW Portland.  <br />Portland is a foodies paradise and this apartment has easy access to all of it! St Honore Boulangerie french bakery, lunch of every style from food cart to sit-down, dinner theaters and dive bars, hand-made ice cream, classy pool halls...and that is just the beginning located just steps from your apartment door.  <br /><br />Shopping is top notch too.  Vintage jewelry, clothing boutiques galore, keepsakes and high-class home furnishings, and the list goes on.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5145373/original/bcd7c13d-1284-46d0-a631-4cd4af5bdc49.jpeg',14540855,27,'45.53512','-122.69776',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,235,4.87,5145373),(289,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5159896','Charming Four Square.   Pet friendly.','This is our home. We have flexible schedules, so we either plan a getaway or we might have discount time slots  based on a pre-planned trip. <br />We require advanced notice on most reservations.  However, please inquire for a short notice reservation.  We have made exceptions.<br />Modern kitchen and bathroom. <br />Bedroom has new windows, blinds, black out curtains.<br />New exterior paint as of May 2020.<br />A/C units during summer for upstairs and downstairs','Fantastic Sunnyside area neighborhood.<br />Three blocks from Laurelhurst Park.<br />Belmont from 32 to 45th, Hawthorne from 10th to 52nd,<br />and Division from 10 to 37th are all walking distance and have<br />some of the top eateries in Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5e0287e7-476c-402c-bb22-a96d3df1aca4.jpg',4611659,16,'45.5181','-122.6319',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,29,18,4.83,5159896),(290,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5159912','Fenced yard, covered patio, and pet friendly','Private pathway to the studio apartment. <br />The unit is a separate space below our main living area.<br />There is a fan and a swamp cooler.<br />Pavers and outdoor furniture<br />Queen size bed.<br />Fold out standard size extra bed.<br />Kitchenette.<br />Washer dryer available.<br />Chrome device for HDMI connection. Fiber optic cable for fast internet. <br />Pet friendly pricing: 1 night $10, 2 nights $20,  Maximum $30. Payment can be made during your visit for the balance.  I pass this fee to the cleaning personnel.','Three blocks from Laurelhurst Park.  The park is about 6 blocks long and 3 blocks wide.  Great for dog walks or just walking around. Kid area too.<br />Two blocks South is Belmont. Many dining options are available as well as several music venues.   Three great pizza places with Ken\'s Artisan, NY NY and Baby Dolls.  Sushi within 5 blocks.  Hawthorne has many options from 11th to 49th.  Division from 11th to about 37th.   No shortage of good food in the SE area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4251f7ff-f786-4c68-9d5f-03ff4cff604d.jpg',4611659,16,'45.5181','-122.6319',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,118.00,1,29,257,4.90,5159912),(291,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5185383','Casa Mágica  / Walk Score 93!','Everyone\'s safety is our top priority.  We are following Airbnb\'s enhanced cleaning protocols. <br /><br />The Magic House, circa 1909, is in the heart of a peaceful, charming restaurant and boutique district, 3 blocks to SE Hawthorne and Division, 15 mins to Airport, Convention Center and Downtown.  <br /><br />The Magic House was Todji\'s sculpture studio for 17 years, and we have done the restoration ourselves.  We hope that you enjoy her unique character, up cycled furnishings and artistry.','The Magic House is centrally located in one of the most beautiful, charming, and safest neighborhoods in Portland.<br /><br />There is an abundance of restaurants, grocery stores, neighborhood strolling, boutique browsing and hiking options within walking distance. <br /><br />See a movie, or just step in to witness the beautiful and iconic McMenamin\'s Bagdad theater, accompanied by an incredible restaurant/bar/pool hall in the back called the \"Back Stage Bar\", at SE 37th and Hawthorne.  It will give you a feel for classic Portland! <br /><br />We are minutes from Mt Tabor park which has a lovely forest with walking trails sitting upon a dormant volcano, and we are 45 minutes to the spectacular 600 foot tall Multnomah waterfall in the gorgeous Columbia River Gorge scenic area. <br /><br />Division is the new up and coming Southeast neighborhood. With lots of modern architecture, new restaurants and shops you will get a feel for the freshest vibe Portland has to offer. <br /><br />Here ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/34ab29a3-c35f-4321-8308-4780d1f635f3.jpg',26822355,8,'45.50959','-122.6233',1,4,1.00,2.00,1.00,39.00,1,7,411,4.85,5185383),(292,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5205479','❤ Vintage Jewel in Historic Mississippi!','3-bdr, 2.5 bath vintage home available on a quiet street that sleeps 8 located just blocks from the bustling Williams Corridor and the Historic Mississippi District!  Enjoy soaking tub, modern kitchen and enclosed patio.','From the food to the beer to the mountain to the people, Portland has become a destination for world-travelers, foodies, beer enthusiasts, adrenaline junkies and book lovers alike... and we are in the middle of it! <br /><br />The Historic Mississippi District is considered one of the hippest in the entire city with unique vintage shopping and is just 3 blocks away in one direction.  In the other direction just 4 blocks away is the bustling Williams Corridor with award winning eateries!  The Alberta Arts District is not much further away.  We also have food carts galore just steps away from our home in all directions.  Downtown Portland is just 5 minutes away.  Feeling like a taco? World-famous ¿Por Que No? is right around the corner down the street. Need a beverage? There\'s ten bars within a 5 minute walk. Want to jet downtown? No problem, the MAX is a short walk away. You can walk, MAX and bus your way to anything your heart desires, and getting home will be equally easy.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/68210206/2d477feb_original.jpg',26929359,9,'45.5483','-122.67164',1,8,2.50,3.00,4.00,289.00,30,93,120,4.93,5205479),(293,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5221169','Alberta hideaway','(URL HIDDEN)This comfortable basement apartment is located in the hip Alberta Arts neighborhood and is ideally located for exploring Portland.  Dozens of restaurants and shops within walking distance. (Due to it being in the basement, the doorways and ductwork are not suitable for guests over 6 feet.)','I love this neighborhood.  It\'s quirky, hip, and happening.  I live three blocks from Alberta Street with its numerous restaurants, eclectic shops, and art studios.  I\'m about 15 minutes from the airport and downtown.  90 minutes to the west are our beautiful beaches and 90 minutes east is magnificent Mt. Hood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/66189932/874da12d_original.jpg',16217416,6,'45.55627','-122.64373',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,2,365,76,4.99,5221169),(294,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5269402','Private Garden Suite for 1 or 2 Guests.','We offer an elegant, cozy, private guest room with private ensuite bathroom, it\'s own private entrance and private arbored deck. The carrera marble bath tiles are heated for winters, and the deck and garden have seating areas for summer. Like a little hotel room, this queen-bed suite is ideal for 1 or 2 who would like an entirely separate space, but don\'t need a full kitchen. The room features microwave, mini-fridge, teakettle & basic flatware - ideal for simple breakfasts or reheated leftovers.','Food in our immediate walkable neighborhood is insanely awesome:<br /><br />#1:  Ps & Qs Market: Go for lunch or dinner any day, or brunch on the weekends; go early in your stay, because you\'ll want to return for more. This is a hipster bodega, with a deli case and full kitchen, like a Vermont country store.  It\'s a hit through Portland, and people travel to our neighborhood just to eat there.  5 blocks away.<br /><br />#2: Woodlawn Cafe and Bakery: Super baristas and pastries. Also serving artisanal breakfast and lunch plates until about 5 or 6pm.  3 blocks away.<br /><br />#3: Breakside Brewery: This might be number 1 if you\'re a beer fan, as it is a famous regional brewery with decent brewpub cuisine.  3 blocks away.<br /><br />#4: Tamale Boy: Awesome and unique Mexican food, specializing in tamales, but with a broad menu.  8 blocks away, and adjoined by a decent gelato place and a funky meed bar.<br /><br />#5: Firehouse Restaurant: Upscale Italian restaurant featuring wood-fired p','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/18e3d3bb-c082-41f4-a388-4438c7a58db0.jpg',7358871,45,'45.57081','-122.65682',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,55.00,1,18,688,4.96,5269402),(295,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5296454','Sunny  2BR Mt Tabor home-Hood View-MontavillaWalk!','★ ★ CORONAVIRUS UPDATE:  This is a PRIVATE entire home, which is PROFESSIONALLY CLEANED AND STERILIZED before each booking, based on the latest guidelines for cleaning and disinfecting from Airbnb.  This lovely street level home is in the heart of SE PDX!','When visiting Portland, where you stay is critical.  You want to have easy access to everything.  We have that here.  The neighborhood is Mt. Tabor, you can look it up online and see why it\'s such a great place to be.  We are literally surrounded with great food and pubs.  Walk 5 minutes to the Coquine Cafe, or 10 minutes to the Montavilla pub area with restaurants, pubs, dive bars, a cocktail lounge, a brewery, coffee and tea houses, the best Pizza in town, vintage stores, and a theater where you can have Pizza and Beer while you watch a current movie for $4!!  Walk 5 minutes to SE 82nd Ave (the Jade District), which has some of the most authentic Asian food in the city.  Walk to the other side of the park and you end up on Division St.(one of the 10 hottest food streets in the country), or Hawthorne Blvd (TONS of different ethnic and pricing options).   Portland is not called \"Beervana\" for nothing, it has more brewpubs per capita than any other city in the United States, and believe','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/67111165/27c4f912_original.jpg',27071792,15,'45.512062','-122.588821',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,109.00,1,1125,342,4.93,5296454),(296,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5309890','\"The Getaway\" modern cottage SE Portland Division','This beautifully bright studio loft is in hip SE Portland where exceptional restaurants, bars and boutiques are within close reach. The space comfortably fits two with a sweet garden patio under the dogwood tree.','Our neighborhood is eclectic and going through a heyday of sorts.  We are on the edge of a historic neighborhood- Ladds Addition and that edge is Division Street. Traditionally a more earthy neighborhood with infamous People\'s Co-Op and Mirador Community Store, New Seasons, a local version of Whole Foods has helped attract a more yuppie side.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/67125995/c0704893_original.jpg',27506814,25,'45.50505','-122.64355',1,2,1.00,0.00,4.00,100.00,2,31,244,4.93,5309890),(297,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5362928','Charming Kerns Apt - Times Out \"Best Neighborhood\"','Portland’s own Kerns neighborhood has been written up as one of the best spots in the US! For good reason, tons of charming shops and restaurants within walking distance with everything you\'d need for your short or extended visit. <br />Located off the bustling 28th and Burnside strip with a Whole Foods grocery store, park, movie theater, food cart pod and variety of cuisines to choose from. This is a private, 2nd floor upper level apt in a craftsman duplex. Pets allowed with addtl $75 cleaning.','Where to start… ;) <br />Having lived all over the city, we consider this to be the best neighborhood in Portland. Close to so many amenities, we found ourselves walking everywhere we went. <br /><br />Within a 5 minute walk - <br /><br />Activity - <br />Laurelhurst Park -  beautiful and also has a great dog run/off leash area.<br />Laurelhurst Theater - Second-run movie theater.<br />Food cart court - all of the vendors are pretty good actually.<br /><br />Groceries - <br />Whole Foods - organic grocery store<br />Vino - Wine shop with wine tastings every friday<br /><br />Restaurants - <br />Navarre - small tapas plates<br />Ken Artesian Pizza - wood fired pizza <br />Bamboo - sustainable sushi, great happy hour<br />Laurelhurst Market - steaks<br />Pambiche - Cuban plates<br />Canteen - healthy organic bowls and fresh juices<br />Those are just my favorites, a bunch of others around too. For specific interests - brew pubs, vegetarian etc just reach and I\'m happy to give recommendat','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5362928/original/e1b7e295-a452-4d50-8780-f635aafea241.jpeg',3041678,32,'45.52214','-122.63847',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,89.00,1,1125,523,4.85,5362928),(298,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5387093','Portland Belmont House—Bird’s Nest','San Francisco-like two bedroom apartment with balcony in vibrant Belmont/Hawthorne neighborhood. Half block to bus stop--great walking district with easy transit to downtown or light rail. Groceries, restaurants and food carts nearby.','I love that our neighborhood is a walkable, vibrant neighborhood only a few minutes to everything.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e12ea94f-bcd2-4c94-87fb-94a79441d24a.jpg',21846830,16,'45.51552','-122.6333',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,134.00,1,365,255,4.93,5387093),(299,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5393534','Beautiful Treetop Loft','Lovely, light-filled studio among the trees above a family home. Private entrance.  Located near vibrant NE 28th Ave with lots of wonderful restaurants & cute shops. Easy access to public transportation.<br /><br />Our neighborhood was recently named as one of the five best in the world!  <br /><br />The Time Out magazine ranked the Kerns neighborhood at No. 5 because \"it feels like a perfectly-formed small town\" inside a major city.','It\'s a lively, fun place where the TV series \"Portlandia\" has recently been filmed.  Close to Laurelhurst Park and Whole Foods as well as Laurelhurst Movie Theater where you can eat pizza and drink beer while watching a great film for $4! There are some awesome brew pubs like Migration Brewery.  We are also one street over from the Everett Healing Spa.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-5393534/original/19f86488-0fb9-49de-9b73-741bd8364328.jpg',27956806,12,'45.52625','-122.63636',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,2,1125,488,4.96,5393534),(300,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5394124','Beautiful Mt Tabor Home with Mt Hood View - 2b/2b','This is a 2 bed/ 2 bath but we also have a large office room, and a large den with a queen sofa bed.  It is fully furnished and set up with everything you need in the kitchen, linens etc.<br /><br />We are in a nice, quiet neighborhood minutes to downtown, restaurants, shops, bars, movie theaters and more.  We are 2 blocks to the sublime Mt Tabor park where you can picnic, walk on the trails and wander through the trees.','We\'re located close to \"Restaurant Row\" on SE Division street, near tons of cute little shops and restaurants in Montavilla, SE Belmont street, SE Clinton Street and SE Hawthorne street. We\'re also very close to downtown - about a 10-15 minute drive. Despite the great proximity to the hustle and bustle, we are in a quiet neighborhood, just a couple of blocks to Mt. Tabor Park - a wonderful city park full of walking trails and great views of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5394124/original/090b8f79-232f-4447-a22d-3aa06ca2a48b.jpeg',6298174,15,'45.51166','-122.58811',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,200.00,30,31,6,5.00,5394124),(301,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5404942','Updated Mid Century Modern Close-In','Our 1957 custom built mid century modern home is close to all that is Portland. We are less than 5 minutes from downtown, OHSU and Lewis and Clark.  We are walking distance to great food, community pool and parks! The modern open concept is great!','We LOVE our neighborhood. We are an easy walk to the library, parks, restaurants and the best bakery in portland, Baker and Spice. In the summer there is a portland parks pool within a 3 min walk from our house that is fabulous.  We are also very close to downtown and easy access to freeways whichever direction you are going.  There are also great hikes on the SW Trails right from our house.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0c863345-67ef-4621-95e9-f4e86301f9e6.jpg',28017147,31,'45.47624','-122.6881',1,10,3.00,4.00,7.00,1.00,30,1125,11,4.91,5404942),(302,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5434216','Downtown  Nest','Spacious, modern living right in downtown Portland. Located within walking distance to the waterfront, PSU, parks, restaurants, bars and entertainment. The Portland Streetcar stops right in front of the building for public transportation throughout the Portland Metro area.<br /><br />Great homebase to get to know Portland. Office area and GB internet are great for business travel.','Downtown location near Portland State University, OHSU and southern waterfront. Easy access to freeways, hiking and parks.<br />The neighborhood has a hearty mix of of college students, visitors and long-term residers, young professionals and retirees.  Adjacent to the university, there are plenty of walkable food and drink options, concert and theater venues, and several parks.  The MAX and light rail offer convenient access to the airport and the rest of the city.  There is literally something for everyone.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d36807f7-9ce8-4e99-909d-13df3b29e41e.jpg',28190369,44,'45.51106','-122.67838',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,30,125,35,4.97,5434216),(303,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5477710','Rose Garden Room! Amazing Location!','Newly remodeled room with the same great amenities!  A romantic getaway for two. Enjoy your beautiful bathroom with a clawfoot tub and the tranquil, amazing yard.  Walking distance to the Japanese Gardens and the International Rose Garden as well as minutes from downtown.','Arlington Heights is the Portland Neighborhood ideally suited for the traveler who seeks the most convenient and authentic Portland experience available. Historically, Arlington Heights was developed with less than 250 homes between 1911 and 1980. Of these 250 residences, 100 were constructed during the “Roaring Twenties,” a period of unprecedented prosperity following World War I. <br /><br />Arlington Heights also lies within the densest aggregation of attractors in the city: the Oregon Zoo, the Children’s Museum, the Forestry Center, Hoyt Arboretum, the Viet Nam Memorial, the Holocaust Memorial, the Rose Garden, and the Japanese Garden, all linked by frequent shuttle buses that route past these venues to region-wide light rail <br />Tri-Met service and pass within 2 blocks of the Boly House.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5477710/original/b9c89b35-2225-44fa-a9ac-d1d24da6f5a9.jpeg',22375978,64,'45.52113','-122.70881',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,54.00,1,1125,619,4.90,5477710),(304,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5536388','Pearl District Condo | Quiet, clean, contemporary','Beautifully furnished condo in an unbeatable location!  Condo has all of the amenities you’d expect - including two extra  wall-beds for guests.<br /><br />Walk score 94 / bike score 98!!!<br /><br />**30 Days minimum stay** <br />All guests agree to abide by the Declaration, Bylaws, and all Rules and Regulations adopted previously or in the future by the Encore Condominium Association. Failure to comply with the Declaration, Bylaws, Rules and Regulations will be considered a violation of the terms of this stay.','Pearl District is a diverse blend of restaurants, art galleries, striking architecture and easy access to all that Portland offers. Riverfront paths, forested trails, cafes, yoga, groceries, and more! <br /><br />Fields Park is a gem and this unit looks right out onto the Park!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f157dcb1-cd74-4c19-8a03-36e2298aecee.jpg',22576469,2,'45.53304','-122.68156',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,112.00,31,730,25,4.96,5536388),(305,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5589595','Cozy 1Br apt. beautiful park view','Attached 1Br apt. with its own entrance and a private courtyard. Columbia Park (across the street) is in full view from the living room.','Columbia Park is across the street. It has a walking path and picnic tables, as well as a small meadow for spreading a blanket.<br />We are in the Portsmouth Neighborhood, which is 5-15 minute drive to just about everything in Portland.<br />Alberta, Mississippi, St John\'s: 10 minutes<br />these three area\'s have shopping, restaurants, galleries, arts, music, pubs.<br />Downtown: 15 minutes<br />Forest Park: 12-15 min. Our amazing 5,000 acre urban park.<br />The apartment is 5 minutes from U of P for parents visiting their kids.<br />New Season\'s our big health food store is a 5 minute drive and a 10 minute bus ride.<br />Fred Meyer is just a 7 minute drive. This is a big grocery store/department store that has everything you might need.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/71961527/710c001a_original.jpg',2783582,60,'45.58124','-122.71235',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,3,14,395,4.98,5589595),(306,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5604467','The Perch - Relax in style/Walkable Location!','An Architectural staircase leads to your private birds-eye deck as you enter your airy urban sanctuary. Bright, clean, elemental decor offer the perfect retreat -  just one block off of fabulous Mississippi St.  Restaurants, bars, shopping and entertainment venues at your doorstep!<br /><br />Fast Wi-Fi and extra cleaning protocols.<br /><br />Minutes from downtown via bike, bus, light rail or car. Easy access to/from the Airport too! Ten years with a consistent five star rating says it all.','Portland\'s Historic Mississippi District is definitely where you want to stay when visiting the city. A gorgeous  and funky stretch full of great shops, award-winning restaurants, an incredible music venue and amazing bars with outdoor patios and inspiring craft cocktails. SUPER easy to get to other parts of the city from here too!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5604467/original/f4579f1a-ad84-41ef-86ea-a0702eb7986e.jpeg',6416589,9,'45.55406','-122.67662',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,110.00,1,1125,1075,4.97,5604467),(307,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5607847','The East Wing','Relax in this quiet wing of a family home among old growth trees on the western side of Mount Tabor. We are offering a reduced rate as we are new to hosting and open to advice and requests from guests to make this place perfect. <br /><br />Dedicated separate entrance, two decks, and a shuffle board table! Luxurious king size bed in the main room and a twin sized couch in the bonus room that opens out into a second king to suit your needs. Instahot faucet at the kitchen sink.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-5607847/original/aeec06bc-8f12-4c5b-95b8-6c73191ace7c.jpeg',11358484,15,'45.51627568649434','-122.60418478399515',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,37,5.00,5607847),(308,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5615066','Hideaway NW Portland One Bedroom','Welcome to your bright, spacious one bedroom Hideaway tucked off bustling NW 23rd Ave in the heart of the restaurant and shopping mecca of PDX. <br />Clean apartment with free access to W/D on site and plenty of comfortable space to enjoy Portland to the fullest! Mid-stay cleaning service available-message me for details.','All the eating, drinking, shopping you could want are at your finger tips in NW Portland.  <br />Portland is a foodies paradise and this apartment is easy access to all of it! St Honore Boulangerie french bakery, lunch of every style from food cart to sit-down, dinner theaters and dive bars, hand-made ice cream, classy pool halls...and that is just the beginning located just steps from your apartment door.  <br /><br />Shopping is top notch too.  Vintage jewelry, clothing boutiques galore, keepsakes and high-class home furnishings, and the list goes on.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5615066/original/489579ea-bb1b-4250-99c0-83f5e6d35907.jpeg',14540855,27,'45.53638','-122.69894',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,72.00,30,1125,218,4.85,5615066),(309,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5619130','Dog Friendly 2B/ 2b Condo - Heart of Belmont','Live like a local in this vintage-style condo in the heart of Belmont/ Hawthorne area. Walk or bike to all the great restaurants, coffee shops and parks.  <br />Ideal setup for someone transitioning in or out of the city, or coming for an extended stay.<br /><br />You\'ll get both levels:<br /><br />Upstairs: 1 bedroom/ 1 full bath/ living room/ full kitchen <br /><br />Downstairs: 1 Murphy bed/ 1 full bath/ office area/ kitchenette','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5619130/original/99491e29-7360-497a-99cb-b2464ea6b3ef.jpeg',4701601,16,'45.51684','-122.63291',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,91.00,30,1125,36,4.97,5619130),(310,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5630762','SW PDX Artist\'s Retreat','A light-filled lower level studio apartment nestled in a quiet & beautiful neighborhood.  This lovely little apartment features original art by Portland artists and is designed for relaxation and comfort.  Features a full kitchen, laundry room, smart tv  &  queen-sized bed w/ cushy memory foam mattress.  Cozy, Private and Serene! Near OHSU and Lewis & Clark College.','It\'s peaceful, quiet, safe and beautiful! <br />There is an enchanting park in the forest a half mile away, that is a little gem, yet we are so close to downtown - the very best of both worlds.... I think it\'s heaven!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-5630762/original/b884c8b9-bec7-404d-8b6c-64de6866c6b6.jpg',19711951,28,'45.4638','-122.68952',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,76.00,14,730,179,4.93,5630762),(311,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5632832','Airy and Light filled 1 Bd in a newer Home','Airy and light filled 1 bedroom with newly added hybrid queen foam bed & bed frame.<br /><br />Excellent location near downtown, Broadway, Alberta, Mississippi and Williams neighborhoods & 2 blocks to TriMet Bus Service. The local area has a WalkScore of 87 out of 100 which is very walkable so some errands can be accomplished on foot.<br /><br />Our location is in the Sabin area near numerous parks, restaurants, bars & cafes.  Groceries nearby include Whole Foods along with New Seasons, Natural Grocers & Safeway.','This is a very centralized neighborhood relative and convenient to many parts of Portland. Were located in a quiet, very walkable neighborhood with easy street parking. And close to Whole Foods, New Season\'s (similar local natural grocery) and walking distance to Alberta Street, Mississippi neighborhood\'s. Also near Williams street restaurants and shopping and in addition Lloyd center where there is a major mall, nearby movie theater and transportation hub. Are location is centrally located to downtown, with a bus stop 2 blocks away. Portland has a good and efficient public transportation system so if your not driving its simple to get around. Also nike is putting up orange bicycles all over the city for hourly use.<br /><br />--','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/75a918d6-a0b1-435d-b436-cd49e629c758.jpg',3519870,6,'45.5498','-122.65159',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,78.00,30,90,54,4.83,5632832),(312,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5641892','Forest Park Room! Spacious and Comfortable!','Come experience the best of Portland! Amazing location in the most prestigious neighborhood in Portland, just minutes away from everything.  Wake up & enjoy the view that you won\'t get anywhere else. This room features a brand-new bathroom with double sinks, plenty of storage, and a huge tub/shower. It also has heated tile floors and a water closet.','Arlington Heights is the Portland Neighborhood ideally suited for the traveler who seeks the most convenient and authentic Portland experience available. Historically, Arlington Heights was developed with less than 250 homes between 1911 and 1980. Of these 250 residences, 100 were constructed during the “Roaring Twenties,” a period of unprecedented prosperity following World War I. <br /><br />Arlington Heights also lies within the densest aggregation of attractors in the city: the Oregon Zoo, the Children’s Museum, the Forestry Center, Hoyt Arboretum, the <br />Viet Nam Memorial, the Holocaust Memorial, the Rose Garden, and the Japanese Garden, all linked by frequent shuttle buses that route past these venues to region-wide light rail, Tri-Met service and pass within 2 blocks of the Boly House.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5641892/original/97b1ea5b-0764-43dd-8a89-035fb68e7290.jpeg',22375978,64,'45.52309','-122.70864',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,73.00,1,1125,563,4.92,5641892),(313,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5762158','Cozy Nest in the Heart of Portland','A cozy studio in a beautiful 1928 brick building.  <br />Top floor, east facing windows.<br />Murphy Bed tucks away during the day.<br /><br />Fun and bright decor with personal touches.<br />Minimum 30 day rental (required by HOA).','It is centrally located near all downtown areas, and you can walk to a hundred wonderful restaurants in 15 minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e80e802e-b2bf-4c9c-89fa-ea11789b8d3c.jpg',26905222,3,'45.52071','-122.68734',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,54.00,30,1125,15,4.93,5762158),(314,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5820909','Light & bright-Close to EVERYTHING!','This bright and open upstairs apartment features two spacious bedrooms, living room a full bath and kitchenette. Located blocks from the light rail and bus line and walking distant to restaurants and shops on Killingsworth as well as the Mississippi district plus you can be downtown in minutes.','Walk ride or drive anywhere in minutes, we love the accessibility of our neighborhood. <br /><br />There are awesome restaurants within blocks and great shopping in the Alberta and Mississippi districts only minutes away.  <br /><br />Our neighborhood is quiet and respectful yet extremely friendly. <br /><br />Feel at home even though you\'re away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-5820909/original/6b970040-3f5d-44dc-9c0f-573d18a4b0a5.jpeg',17783032,13,'45.55781','-122.68059',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,74.00,7,93,235,4.88,5820909),(315,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5874084','Private apartment in historical Irvington','A private-entrance, finished and dry sub-main, apartment.  Enjoy a private bedroom, full bathroom, sitting area, and large screen TV.  Guests also have food storage and preparation space with sink and countertops). The neighborhood is very safe and close to eateries, shopping, and outdoor spaces (track, park, tennis). Broadway and Hollywood district are walking distance.','Broadway Ave and shops are 5 blocks away to the South. To the East is block after block of charming houses in historic Irvington, great for morning or evening strolls. Alberta Arts district is 1 mile to the North. Grant High School is 7 blocks East and has a running track and field plus 6 tennis courts for public use.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/107694282/c5cccbfb_original.jpg',20930553,33,'45.54047','-122.63863',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,30,365,215,4.94,5874084),(316,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5882940','*Amazing Guest Suite - by river, OHSU, river trail','Newer  - lower level guest suite located within walking distance fr Willamette River in Portland, OR and OHSU Tram-  1 mile from Dtwn.   Private Guest Space in lower level of 3-story 2010 home w priv bth new GE fridge, sink, microw, hot plate, private entrance.','The area is residential; quiet - but only minutes away from the Willamette River, many restaurants, nightspots, and shopping areas.  OHSU staff (MDs, nurses, residents, other non medical) staff live in area.  A couple blocks away from guest suite is Elephants Deli, Starbucks, Growlers etc.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/102424558/c32fbc8b_original.jpg',30549717,22,'45.48604','-122.67867',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,52.00,30,1125,43,4.74,5882940),(317,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5912939','Lyle Room @ 1234 HOUSE in SE PDX','An artist-made guest room in a renovated 1902-built house near Hawthorne, Belmont, Division & Downtown. Walking distance to variety of restaurants, bars, theaters, shops, grocery stores, parks & public transit. PRIVATE BALCONY. Memory-foam queen bed, number-code locks, WiFi, two shared restrooms. Shared kitchen, dining room, living room, laundry, canoe, outdoor patios, record collection, piano/musical instruments.','1234 House is in the Buckman neighborhood of Southeast Portland, which is dense with homes 100-plus years old, and, like most of Portland, is experiencing a wave of new, modern consruction. 1234 House is a mile from the Willamette River, which separates the eastside of Portland and the westside city center. The house is nestled between Hawthorne Boulevard and Belmont Street, both lined with restaurants, bars, shops, theaters and music venues. A few blocks down the street is Col. Summers Park, a popular meet up spot to hang in the summer, especially on Monday Funday, and especially if you are down to play a mean game of dodgeball.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/90905331-3505-40d0-a40a-7e2026630224.jpg',30708290,32,'45.51307','-122.6462',2,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,71.00,1,730,385,4.83,5912939),(318,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5914549','Close in - Southeast Belmont/Hawthorne Home','My place is good for couples, solo adventurers, business travellers, and visiting parents, and grandparents.<br /><br />New, private studio located in Sunnyside Portland neighborhood. Close to restaurants, coffee shops, grocery stores, and parks. Includes comfortable queen bed with high end linens, full kitchen including refrigerator, oven/stove, dishwasher and coffee/tea making equipment, washer/dryer, living room with Firestick tv and wifi.\" Private garden area.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/105cc1f8-dd8f-409f-ab3c-04516dd21de8.jpg',24909901,16,'45.51917','-122.62782',1,2,1.00,1.00,5.00,2.00,30,1125,0,1.00,5914549),(319,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5964484','Private room with shared bath','Large private room with large balcony facing North and the back yard with itäs multiple seating areas, very centrally located, near the street car and buses. There is easy parking available, in the driveway<br />Shared bathroom with a shower.<br />We have a 7 yr old standard poodle, Maggie who coat is hypo allergic and should not cause any problems.  She is delightful','This neighborhood is called the Alphabet district because all the street names are in alphabetical order. It is just adjacent to downtown so there is easy public transportation, but parking is also easy. Our neighborhood was built up after the World\'s fair exhibition in 1905','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/76297331/d5c9be44_original.jpg',3022845,27,'45.53027','-122.70493',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,30,31,36,4.94,5964484),(320,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5979427','Private Apt. Comfy & Clean in a Great neighborhood','Daylight basement apt. with private entrance in the peaceful neighborhood of Montavilla - Forbes travel lists as a top 10 U.S. neighborhood. Great home base for exploring the Pacific NW. One block from two bus lines & an easy walk to the MAX line. PERFECT for getting to events of the ROSE FESTIVAL or THE BLUES FEST. An easy morning walk to Mt. Tabor will take you up the side of an extinct volcano! Great coffee shops a block away. Experienced hosts - your comfort is important - come stay with us!','North Tabor/Montavilla Neighborhood offers some very PDX restaurants, bars and a neighborhood movie theatre. We have a binder with information on plenty of dining ideas (remember, we LOVE to explore restaurants).  Within walking:  Fillmore cafe, Mt. Tabor Roasters, Tabor Tavern, The Tannery, Country Cat, BiPartisan Café, Redwood and more! What are you hungry for?','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/76547246/79e929be_original.jpg',31042891,10,'45.52579','-122.59055',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,126.00,2,28,167,4.98,5979427),(321,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/5988930','Upscale 1 bdrm /Apart/ SW Hills- Util incl.','One bedroom apartment -Hide-a-bed in living room for extra guests. Full kitchen, 2 bath.<br />Bedroom is on the 2nd level. 6 minute drive downtown Portland and on major bus route But buses are slow and do not run on weekends.<br />Full shower bath main level.<br />The apart has its own entrance is is completely self contained.<br /><br />There is only one airBNB parking space.  Preferring small vehicles. No room for camper vans or 4x4 pickups.  A 2nd space for visitors is shared by all of us.<br />5 min walk to Park.','In the Southwest hills.  Walk to  Council  Crest  Park. The park offers an incredible view of the city, Mt. Hood and Mt St Helens.<br />Hiking trails including  to the zoo and parks.<br />6 minutes drive to Downtown Portland. Hiking Trails within walking distance from the apartment.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/79390055/f1863862_original.jpg',31093263,54,'45.499610900878906','-122.71192932128906',1,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,31,150,43,4.93,5988930),(322,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6132497','Charming! Great location!','Modern private studio getaway that includes a comfy Queen bed & Queen sofa sleeper, living room & kitchen area with private entrance.  Beautiful garden patio.  Easy access to transportation, close to dining & shopping!  Free Wifi, coffee, tea, tennis courts, park for kids & dogs and free parking too!  <br />PS.  Your dog may not be left alone unless in crate.','This getaway  is located near downtown Portland, Oregon.  Catering to both outdoor enthusiast and city lovers, Portland is known for its natural beauty and exciting night life. Enjoy the hiking and biking trails outside the city, or head to town for the world-class restaurants and shops. Explore all the wonderful Portland attractions just minutes away from your getaway.<br />You are steps away from outstanding restaurants, coffee shops and boutiques.  Just take the street car to a professional soccer game, the Oregon Ballet or  the Chinese Gardens or in the evening go the Crystal Ballroom to hear and dance to some great bands.  Step out in the other direction and you could have a picnic in Wallace Park or enjoy a day hike into Forest Park to visit the Audubon Society or Pittock Mansion.  Kids will love the soccer field and play structure and your dog will love the doggie park.  Bring your tennis rackets and use ent isone of the two courts that are steps away.<br /><br /><br />THINGS TO','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d71417ee-b33f-4d25-bcbb-17062abb2da2.jpg',31813936,27,'45.5337','-122.708',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,66.00,3,28,530,4.88,6132497),(323,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6165708','Your Portland Bungalow Apartment','Our daylight apartment sleeps 4 with its own entrance, easy freeway access, blocks from light rail, and buses. Walk to groceries, Dekum Triangle, coffee shops, bars, and two great parks. It\'s also just a 10-15 minute bike ride to the Mississippi, Williams, Kenton, and Alberta hot spots.','We love our neighborhood! It\'s close to plenty of great things, but it is far enough away to be quiet. We\'ve got rose gardens, coffee shops, good brunch spots, neighborhood watering holes, and easy access to public transportation, car shares, and bike rentals.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-6165708/original/51a557cd-d018-48ad-9c2b-806228c08e9d.jpeg',4635967,48,'45.57485','-122.6713',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,61.00,2,9,613,4.91,6165708),(324,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6210573','Modern apartment at a fantastic location','A *lower unit* apartment in a custom-built modern house in a buzzing neighborhood filled with restaurants, boutiques, parks and grocery stores.  <br /><br />The NE 28th restaurant row is one block away and there are around two dozens restaurants within walking distance from the apartment.   You can walk to the beautiful Laurelhurst Park.  The Whole Foods is four short blocks away.   There is a 24-hr convenience store right around the corner.','Sits on a quiet corner but is only one block from a very buzzing part of the city well known for its vibrant restaurant and bar scene, hip food carts, music venues, and vintage boutiques. Walk to the beautiful Laurelhurst Park, movie theater, Whole Foods, New Seasons and Fred Meyer!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/79561294-34b5-4211-a56e-7d2222bc7eec.jpg',851489,12,'45.52502','-122.63904',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,96.00,2,1125,132,4.86,6210573),(325,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6255911','Private Mt. Tabor Guest Quarters','A 500 sq. ft. 1BR Apt. inside a Mt. Tabor Craftsman home features a queen bed, pull out sofa, luxe linens, kitchenette, fast wifi, 55\" TV, and in-unit washer/dryer. Perfect for couples, friends, and remote workers, comfortably sleeps up to 4 guests. Walk to some of SE Portland’s best cafes, bars, shops, restaurants, food carts, and Mt. Tabor park. Electric bike and scooter shares are nearby and the public bus is two blocks away which will take you to the heart of downtown in just 20 minutes.','Mt. Tabor is one of Portland\'s most beloved neighborhoods located in the Southeastern part of the city. It\'s mostly residential but is home to tons of great bars, restaurants, cafes, and shops. Not to mention its namesake - the inactive volcano turned urban park full of trails, playgrounds, and reservoirs.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-6255911/original/488f9e8e-003e-4a09-8b28-8910ae0f8243.jpeg',30384117,15,'45.5061534','-122.607831',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,78.00,2,90,114,4.97,6255911),(326,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6262850','Quite Upstairs Studio in NE PDX.','Our upstairs studio is quite,roomy and gets great natural light.<br />Out guests love how impeccably clean the studio is.<br />It’s very cozy and relaxing sipping tea or coffee at our large kitchen table while you plan your PDX adventure.<br />Carl is a clean freak, he even irons the sheets.','We love walking to coffee and breakfast at the New Deal Café.Our neighborhood is family oriented and it  provides lovely walks in any direction. We enjoy urban walks  to Trader Joe’s,Whole Foods,Brew Pubs and transit.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/15da20c8-273f-4f22-a9d1-a318fe31e091.jpg',9681458,11,'45.53396','-122.61039',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,3,30,357,4.96,6262850),(327,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6277852','2+ Bedroom Urban Home in SE Portland','Welcome to SE Portland... the best part of the Rose City!<br /><br />In the Woodstock/Mt. Scott neighborhood, you\'ll have quick access to great shops, the best restaurants (Double Mountain Brewery, New Seasons Market, Cloud City Ice Cream, Zoiglhaus Brewing Company), food carts (Portland Mercado), a few farmer\'s markets, and a great park and recreations center (Mt. Scott Community Center... they even have a killer indoor pool!).','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/de7cbd13-0b2e-4924-ab34-08b79970b932.jpg',2519473,65,'45.47964','-122.58028',1,5,1.50,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,23,4.87,6277852),(328,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6287392','Waterfront condo in SW Portland','Willamette River and Mount St Helen views with the Willamette Greenway biking and walking path right out my door.  2 bed/2 bath condo located in John’s Landing/Lairs Hill SW Portland neighborhood and 1.5 miles from downtown--walk or bus there.','John\'s Landing is located 1.5 miles from downtown Portland, which has many food choices. Eating in John\'s Landing is convenient yet delicious. Dining-in or picnic supplies are easily purchased at Zupan\'s Market (about 1.5 miles).  <br />John’s Landing has a few select restaurants that have become quite famous in the Portland area. Those are Buffalo Gap, Corbett Fish House, Fulton Pub & Brewery, Jolly Roger at John’s Landing, and Reo’s Ribs. Elephant’s Deli (3 blocks) is an excellent café and coffee shop. <br />Willamette Park is a convenient and plentiful picnic place with views of the Willamette river.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4f45a3b7-61a9-4e3b-8de9-a542225e52a4.jpg',19632445,22,'45.4865','-122.67145',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,150.00,30,30,6,5.00,6287392),(329,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6290791','Spacious Sellwood 2 bedroom Suite','Welcome to our gracious, art-filled home, built in 1892 and located in historic Sellwood.  You will have the entire second floor with your own private entrance,  living room & 2 full bedrooms, spacious bathroom and kitchenette.  See photos for detailed descriptions. **PLEASE SEE OUR HOUSE RULES FOR DETAILED DESCRIPTION OF CLEANING PRACTICES AND DISINFECTING PRODUCTS IN LIGHT OF COVID-19.  FEEL FREE TO CONTACT US WITH ANY QUESTIONS OR PREFERENCES.','Sellwood is a wonderful, historic neighborhood convenient to parks, hiking trails, Willamette River, Oaks Bottom (blue heron refuge) and there is a community center with a small play park right on our block..   We boast a WALK SCORE of 94 and a BIKE SCORE of 84!!  There is a great bike trail, Springwater corridor, and we have bike maps.   There is a bike rental available nearby.  You can ride all the way downtown on bike paths and hook up with multiple trails en route.  We will have plenty of information and more details in our book, including some coupons for local businesses.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/78768492/155ce5a8_original.jpg',21134004,20,'45.46558','-122.65133',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,129.00,2,10,382,4.94,6290791),(330,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6293687','The Oasis in the City','This is a beautiful UPSTAIRS UNIT, very modern, sleek, and edgy. Property is located in a historical Victorian neighborhood central to everything. 5 minutes from downtown Portland, walking distance to the Rose Garden and much more!!!','This cozy space is centrally located literally to everything and only 5 mins from Downtown. Walking distance to the Moda Center formally known as Rose Garden, Convention Center and the Pearl district, and 1/2 block from eateries and two cycle shops. You can also find within 5 minutes more breweries, unique cafes, grocery stores and the Mississippi/Fremont experience which include restaurants, shopping, and entertainment.<br /><br />Family: Kid friendly: parks, Oregon Zoo, Omsi, Water Front Park, Saturday market and much more<br /><br />Description of Neighborhood:  Slightly industrial/neighborhood<br />(almost like an extension of downtown). Though its a neighborhood you will find a lot of close businesses/restaurants within walking distance','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/106061154/32c91e1c_original.jpg',18846362,26,'45.53595','-122.6651',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,77.00,1,1125,315,4.84,6293687),(331,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6346680','Room in lovely home, near airport.','Lovely Argay Terrace neighborhood, near airport and 15 minute drive to downtown Portland.','You’ll also find access to several bike and pedestrian paths that traverse the area and allow people to travel along the Columbia River, east to Gresham and south to the Gateway Transit Center.<br />Argay Park on 141st offers areas to exercise pets, play tennis, basketball, baseball and soccer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/79406736/a2069bc7_original.jpg',33056989,66,'45.54765','-122.52593',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,39.00,30,1125,32,4.84,6346680),(332,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6364401','Charming Cozy Home Right Off Alberta & Boise','This cozy 1901 craftwork is newly renovated with family-friendly amenities. Located in the heart of Portland’s hottest neighborhood, minutes of walk away from prime breweries, food carts, and restaurants in Portland. Perfect location to connect with friends and families with our fully renovated kitchen, explore the hippest breweries & restaurants in town or experience the majestic PNW wilderness nearby.<br /><br />The house also features dedicated office space and is pet friendly (please see house rules)','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-6364401/original/48a6241b-a14a-49dc-ab5b-dc78cf4d10c6.jpeg',32509067,14,'45.55518787676244','-122.65971725317026',1,7,2.00,3.00,5.00,110.00,1,60,72,4.85,6364401),(333,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6376373','Waterfront Pearl District Condo!','Pearl District. Great for business or pleasure. Contemporary yet comfortable, sophisticated yet fun, this unit has it all. <br />this condo is WATERFRONT with a fantastic view of the Wilamette River and easy walk to the Pearl District!<br />HDTV, WI-FI, IPOD Doc station. Comfy KING Bed, w/d in unit, parking space, Walk everywhere. Steps to everything..','FANTASTIC walkability to so many restaurants, shops and all things in the Pearl District! great location if you want to walk, or ride','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cf96b791-93d5-4870-9388-46b5a7d51b0f.jpg',5744484,43,'45.5281','-122.67391',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,100.00,30,1125,2,5.00,6376373),(334,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6389996','La Petite- BRAND NEW!','ELEGANT URBAN OASIS IN PORTLAND\'S DIVISION NEIGHBORHOOD.<br /><br />Step into an enclave of opulence and comfort in our newly designed Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU). This private haven, sculpted with attention to every detail, stands as a testament to luxury and comfort, offering you Portland\'s finest in an intimate, and sleek setting. You\'ll cherish our ADU\'s tranquil ambiance and our foodie forward neighborhood.','We are located in the BEST neighborhood in all of Portland. You can walk to two of Portland\'s most popular streets (SE Division and SE Hawthorne) lined with coffee shops, bike rentals, restaurants, and bars!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-6389996/original/ca5ee77f-d212-4a86-b828-4895b0de4b47.jpeg',1825887,8,'45.50827','-122.61406',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,94.00,2,60,97,4.80,6389996),(335,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6402773','The Hawthorne Hideaway','Located a few blocks from Hawthorne, this charming basement apartment sleeps up to 4 people, includes a full kitchen and washer and dryer.  Super close access to downtown and all that Inner Southeast has to offer!<br /><br /><br />Walk Score of 96%','Hawthorne and Inner SE is the best for walkability, close to downtown and plenty of restaurants in the area!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c0458060-bc0c-4517-b34d-2c3a862d4cd6.jpg',16113117,32,'45.51412','-122.64916',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,80.00,2,29,327,4.87,6402773),(336,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6426141','Cozy Room (with Bicycles!)','As fellow travelers we deliver a unique and authentic Portland experience. Relax in our quiet home and immerse yourself in the fabric of our fair city through our quiet, eclectic neighborhood. We offer free bike rentals so you can enjoy our city like a local and get around easily. <br /><br />Come visit us. Your room is ready!','The North Cully neighborhood is a quiet, beautiful and slow little corner of Portland that was once mostly covered in filbert (those are hazel nuts to non-Oregonians) orchards. The area still thrives with urban farms, charming houses and quiet streets. Though there are no sidewalks (or maybe because of the lack of them) there is low vehicle traffic but a constant stream of dog walkers, runners and cyclists on our street.<br /><br />Our neighborhood is a little \"Portlandia\": Tori runs a business teaching bicycle riding and repair skills called \"Gracie\'s Wrench\" while the next door neighbor has a school for fire dancing and stilt walking (as well as performances) called \"Flamebouyant\"-- not to mention the goat herds.<br /><br />This place is also very down to earth. We know and appreciate our neighbors and love the old-school charm that can\'t be found everywhere.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/81574425/f227b046_original.jpg',347470,21,'45.56605','-122.61166',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,225,4.87,6426141),(337,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6433274','Historic Home - Walk to Hawthorne!','Experience the feel of Portland\'s history while you stay in this amazing National Historic Home built in 1892 by Gustave and Mina Bartman. Located three blocks south of Hawthorne the Bartman is a rare remaining example of urban living 125 years ago.','The Bartman is located minutes from downtown in the heart of what we in Portland call \"Inner South East\" on the main avenue connecting with the hub of SE Hawthorne and 12th. The neighborhood of Hosford-Abernathy is one of Portland\'s most beloved neighborhoods. <br />This is a wonderfully active urban (in the Portland sense) area (SE 12th avenue is a busy inner residential street): you\'ll be amused to watch one of the many \'pedalounges\' cruising by with revelers aboard. Within two blocks are two of the best of the many fantastic restaurants at your finger tips: (Junior\'s cafe for incredible breakfasts and Teote for amazing Latin American food and both with excellent atmosphere) and all around the neighborhood with an easy walk your choices for excellent dining are practically unlimited.<br />You can experience the pulse of the neighborhood from the comfort of the beautiful parlor while relaxing by the fire. I want to be sure to let you know that 12th avenue is a main residential avenue ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/82331871/b1fee115_original.jpg',32342870,25,'45.50976','-122.65401',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,103.00,1,1125,582,4.85,6433274),(338,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6506905','Lola house, Historic Irvington, California King','Located in Beautiful Historic Irvington, less than 20 minutes from the airport and 5 minutes from downtown by car,  Irvington is the gem of Portland and popular among locals and tourist.','The Lola House is on a popular bustling thorough fair.  Enjoy the street traffic from a Porch swing or lounge. Or  walk down any street in Irvington and enjoy viewing historical homes, yards, and trees. Irvington Classic Homes and Heritage Trees is a 2.8-mile loop that tours more than 75 homes (including Lola House) that have been designated as historically significant, ranging from Mediterranean mansions to English cottages to Prairie Craftsman. Great shopping and eating places on NE Broadway offer a way to end the walk. <br />Portland is the 14th most walkable city in the U.S. with a Walk Score of 63, a Transit Score of 50 and a Bike Score of 72. There are over 3,000 restaurants and coffee shops in Portland. People in Portland can walk to an average of five restaurants and coffee shops in five minutes.The Walk Score for the Irvington neighborhood is 83, the Transit Score is 62, and the Bike Score is 93.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/84f920fb-ee18-4636-b7cb-115e75b3c566.jpg',26263678,7,'45.54355','-122.65184',2,2,2.50,1.00,1.00,175.00,30,1125,78,4.94,6506905),(339,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6545849','Plum Room, Hummingbird Farm','Visiting Portland and curious about our mini farms, sustainable living, slow foods? Come stay in our lovely room with south facing french doors, private yard of fruit trees, grape arbor, and verdant gardens,. We used to raise goats, chickens and bees here too, but with the changing landscape of our lives, those dear companions no longer live here (:','The Kerns neighborhood is blessed with several excellent restaurants including Pembiche (ever popular Cuban) and Bamboo (one of the best sushi restaurants in Portland). There are many other amazing choices - intimate to raucous; quirky and fast. We are blocks away from breweries like Migration and coffee roasters like Heart. We have neighborhood parks (Oregon Park, Laurelhurst Park) and several music stores. We are just up the street from two climbing gyms and numerous dance venues (Tango, Salsa, Swing, Walz at the Viscount, the Norse Hall, Club 720, Ankeny Str club) and there are great bands at the Doug Fir Lounge and the Laurelthirst Pub,<br />Bike shops abound and there are grocery shops nearby.<br />Basically, we are a little slice of Portland itself, all within 10 blocks or so.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-6545849/original/75a87b21-1240-4f43-b832-992758e362a7.jpg',14954072,12,'45.52728','-122.6326',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,1,14,246,4.94,6545849),(340,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6555772','Spacious SE- Air/Con, toy room, crib, walk to food','Family friendly, Walk to food, central A/C<br /><br />4 bedroom and 3 full bath house. Full access to the entire 2700sq ft house. This house is right by a park.<br /><br />Walk to bars/restaurants/food carts. This house is in Foster-Powell neighborhood in SE Portland. Downtown is approx 6 miles. <br /><br />**Due to severe allergies, no pets are allowed. If you bring a pet, you will be asked to leave and will be charged $200 for extra cleaning. <br /><br />See my other listing “The Pickle Cabin” in Mt Hood and split your stay!','Located in the Foster-Powell neighborhood. Quiet, yet many local bars, restaurants and food carts within walking distance. Grocery store 0.7 miles away. Everything you could need within a short distance. Trader Joe’s about 1.5 miles away. <br /><br />The house is directly opposite a neighborhood park with basketball court and playground. <br /><br />Also, not far from Woodstock neighborhood with New Seasons, Safeway. <br /><br />Bus lines very close to get you downtown easily. Max light rail also not far - about 1 mile. <br /><br />* Downtown - 15 min <br />* OMSI - 10 min <br />* OHSU - 15 min <br />* Multnomah Falls - 40 min <br />* Timberline Lodge - 75 min<br />* Beaverton - 30 min<br />* Portland Airport - 15 min<br />* Oregon Coast - 95 min<br />* Wine Country - 60 min<br /><br />This is a fully permitted rental. Portland requires a LU permit for 3 bedrooms or more. Many others are not permitted and guests risk being cancelled if the city finds out. <br /><br />Th permits require','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-6555772/original/3d83dd83-51ce-4613-87fe-4d73957d90d7.jpeg',34286584,36,'45.49394','-122.59428',1,8,3.00,4.00,5.00,414.00,4,500,99,4.97,6555772),(341,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6560720','Portland’s “fake fall” is cool and comfortable.','Enjoy the modern conveniences of city living while experiencing a slice of history, just steps from the streetcar line!  This convenient Victorian apartment features private front and back decks, a full kitchen and remodeled bathroom with an accessible shower.  Walk  to Salt & Straw ice cream and extensive take-out and dine-in options! Near parks, shops, restaurants, hiking, the Pearl District and Powell\'s City of Books.  <br /><br />Check in at your convenience, using a coded lock and private entry.','The neighborhood is on the National Register of Historic Places, dubbed The Alphabet District.  It was one of the first neighborhoods built in Portland and is rich in history.  Our section is called Goldsmith\'s Addition, named after an early mayor. <br /><br />On the bulletin board in the kitchen are brochures for walking tours of the area.  They are given by my dear friend and knowledgeable historian Tanya March.<br /><br />We have several grocery stores within walking distance:  Trader Joe’s ($$) at 21st and Glisan, Fred Meyer ($) at 20th and Burnside and Food Front Co-operative Grocery ($$$) at 23rd Place and Thurman.<br /><br />Just around the corner to the south on 23rd is the Lovejoy Grocery; very convenient for groceries, sundries, sandwiches, beverages and GREAT baklava.<br /><br />The neighborhood and Portland in general are full of great restaurants.  Two doors down on the corner is Red Onion, which has tasty Vietnamese food and a nice atmosphere.  If you arrive late at night','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/84767722/a5b409f1_original.jpg',3440675,27,'45.52978','-122.69994',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,133.00,30,1125,397,4.70,6560720),(342,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6599733','NE Portland Beauty','Spacious two bedroom house with curated design details. Within 15- 20 minutes of everything Portland has to offer. Perfect for artists, musicians and families alike. Comfort & convenience await!','Sweet NE Portland Neighborhood with Park in walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/96692381/e3d09837_original.jpg',6621463,39,'45.55402','-122.58672',1,4,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,5,30,33,4.81,6599733),(343,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6609741','Private Studio Right Off Hawthorne!','Come live like a local in Portland\'s Hawthorne District.  One block off Hawthorne and four blocks off Division, private studio space with queen bed, twin sofa bed, full bathroom,  kitchenette with induction cooktop, and wifi.','We are right in the middle of the bohemian Hawthorne District of SE Portland.  Walk 1 block to Hawthorne and you’ll find restaurants, boutique shops, a movie theater and a grocery store all within a few blocks.  It’s easy to catch a bus or ride a bike to downtown, OMSI on the river, or over to beautiful Mt. Tabor park.  We are also a 5 minute walk to Belmont and a 10 minute walk to Division, other popular streets that have restaurants and shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/374b6a41-8bc6-4a74-87be-08e8c361079c.jpg',2711731,8,'45.5118','-122.62902',1,3,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,2,29,290,4.87,6609741),(344,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6712131','Magnolia House: sunny and bright','This is a home: warm, cozy, interesting and comfortable home. The house is very Portlandy, full of plants, with clayed walls and warm carpets. It has comfy places for folk who want to gather as well as for those who crave privacy, including two porches, a half-light basement and a lovely garden. Enjoy the well-stocked kitchen and many thoughtful details.  The sun porch has a new full bed and all the mattresses have memory foam toppers. Come here for easy access to all Portland has to offer.','The Hollywood District is beautiful--mostly Craftsman style houses with lots of trees and flowers. Because the nearby-highway is built into an old streambed, your immediate neighborhood is urban-quiet and feels sheltered from city buzziness, but within 6 blocks you can find 3 large grocery stores, 5 restaurants, 3 bus lines and a beautiful park. There\'s a french pastry store with excellent coffee one block away, side-by-side with a reasonably-priced and good sushi place and now a brand new butcher shop/deli as well. (Their meat-ish food is good, of course, but actually their mushroom version of a french dip/philly is one of the best dishes in town, and totally meatless.)<br /><br />We\'re just off I-84, but the highway noises are minimized by the fact that the highway follows an old stream bed, so it is naturally walled in by the old stream bench.<br /><br />The Hollywood Transit Center\'s light rail line (which runs directly to the airport) is about a quarter of a mile away from the hou','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-6712131/original/cd312ca5-20e5-4218-b7e4-7fc726d9d466.jpeg',4256569,23,'45.5329','-122.62925',1,10,2.00,5.00,5.00,159.00,3,30,86,4.88,6712131),(345,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6731334','Chic Mississippi District -Fresh, Bright & Modern','4 bedroom historic house with a bright modern interior steps away from hip and trendy Mississippi District in Portland.','The many independent retailers of North Mississippi Ave. reflect the city’s eclectic tastes and DIY ethic. This is the neighborhood that embodies the essence of what makes Portland, Portland. Colorful, independent, and oozing with creativity Mississippi isn\'t to be missed. <br />Food carts, bars, cute stores, music venues are all within a short walk from Shift.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ddbd2b4d-9ef8-49ea-b07e-c15bd7833544.jpg',1150082,24,'45.55704','-122.67591',1,10,2.00,4.00,4.00,231.00,1,1125,71,4.90,6731334),(346,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6777992','Cozy, Creative & Spacious! Historic Portland Home','Just a few minutes from downtown Portland & the Pearl in the historic neighborhood of Irvington. Within walking distance from beautifully stunning parks like Irving Park, and great world-class restaurants, and shops nearby. <br />Travel by street car all around town and shop at great local produce and meat markets like Cherry Sprout and Sheridans (the oldest fruit market in the city!)  Lovely area with vintage charm.','We live in a beautiful, quiet neighborhood which is surrounded by giant shady trees, and gorgeous old houses with true Portland charm. Spend some time walking up to beautiful Irving Park and admire historic homes and beautiful gardens.<br /><br />It\'s a truly centrally located area, just a few minutes drive from downtown, Alberta arts district, Belmont, and Hawthorne. Public transportation is also just a few blocks away. Our home is within walking distance to some amazing restaurants too- Toro Bravo, Ox, Bunk Bar, Russell St BBQ & Wonder Ballroom!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-6777992/original/673a9d38-6901-4f2e-bb96-6b03c67ce8fb.jpeg',35482861,7,'45.53685','-122.65791',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,87.00,1,20,269,4.83,6777992),(347,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6799955','Historic Private One Bedroom Condo','LOCATION <br />• Centrally located<br />• Between popular streets of NW 21 & NW 23<br />• By Timbers stadium, downtown life, grocery store<br />• Off W. Burnside<br /><br />CONDO <br />• Vintage <br />• Secure access building <br />• Hardwood <br />• 1 Bedroom <br />• Real queen bed <br />• Extra queen airbed','BREAKFAST<br />• The closest breakfast place is a 1 minute walk -- the B Street Cafe. It\'s a VERY small restaurant, and there are larger breakfast/lunch places that are about a 5-10 minute walk.<br />• There are lots of coffee shops close by -- the closest being the Coffeehouse Northwest.<br /><br />GROCERY STORE<br />• The grocery store is a 3 minute walk from my condo. It is a Fred Myer (100 NW 20th Pl, Portland, OR 97209)<br />• Feel free to cook at my condo and store food in the fridge/freezer!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/85901158/b3f40e34_original.jpg',35596135,27,'45.52375','-122.69653',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,160.00,30,1125,15,4.93,6799955),(348,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6811607','LUX Lava Lounge in downtown Kenton.','The LUX Lava lounge is located in the lower level of a mid-century ranch.  It\'s been fully remodeled and includes over 1000ft with 2 bedrooms, 1 Full Bath, Laundry, Fireplace, oversized living room with pool table and much more! Also includes a private fenced yard and off street parking!  Fun colors and groovy designer patterns in the kitchen provide flavor to your vacation or extend stay experience.','The neighborhood keeps growing and creating more new local places to visit.  At one end of my block is a new Tap Room called Mayfly and I am only a 2 minute walk from here to the cute downtown area of Kenton in North Portland. There are coffee shops, restaurants, resale and fun boutique\'s.  There is also a Library and Post Office.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/68d66ed0-f033-44ff-994a-6cc0e03137b8.jpg',1495776,55,'45.58245','-122.6827',1,3,1.00,2.00,2.00,0.00,30,179,1,5.00,6811607),(349,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6820353','Portlandia Pad','Bright, clean, colorful and central!  Completely contained and separate space.  This apartment is located in a beautiful, historic, Victorian home in the heart of Buckman.  Across from a park/playground/community garden and near cafes, bars, venues & restaurants.  Near buses, bike rental, and bike routes.  Bike score 100/100.  Kitchen with gas range, oven, microwave,and quality cookware. Gorgeous & large newly renovated shower.   We prefer that guests share bed.','Buckman is a central and historic neighborhood.  Our house is 1 mile from downtown and close to Burnside (5 blocks) and Morrison (4 blocks) which have frequent buses.  Walking distance to many destinations spots: Revolution Hall, Screen door, Tusk, Crema, Ken’s Artisan Pizza, Bamboo sushi, Kachka, Doug Fir, Le Pigeon, Nostrana, Heart, Push/pull coffee, Belmont and Hawthorne shopping districts and 28th restaurant row.  Across from a large school park/playground.  I only clean with environmentally friendly products, so no fumes for those who are sensitive to bleach or ammonia!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/95019499/dcc8717f_original.jpg',35716158,32,'45.51464','-122.6474',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,82.00,2,28,327,4.89,6820353),(350,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6836688','Sweet Garden Perch! Ideal Spot.','Fab Division/Clinton Dining District! Lovely, fresh, private apartment. Downtown, breweries, science museum, shops, fabulous restaurants/cafés, parks, grocers, bars, super close. 1BR, 2 new beds, fireplace, w/d, full kitchen, balcony, treetop views.','The space is in the Division/Clinton Street dining district, renowned for outstanding cuisine. Known for its gardens, bioswales, solar projects, etc, this area is also known as \"Sustainable SE.\"<br /><br />Many fantastic bars and restaurants, some reviewed in Bon Appetit and The New York Times, are just blocks away, as are organic grocers, a farmers\' market, food carts, ice-cream parlor (like the trendy Salt and Straw), bakeries and cafés.  Parks, pool, cinema, museums, downtown and boutiques quite close.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/92351277/3f04996e_original.jpg',6744152,25,'45.5003','-122.64118',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,92.00,3,120,398,4.92,6836688),(351,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6967714','Stunning Home In Trendy Mississippi District','5 bedroom stunning eco modern house steps from hip and trendy Mississippi District in Portland.','The Historic Mississippi District is incredible. You are walking distance to some of Portland\'s best bars, restaurants, and stores. It is the kind of street that makes you feel that you are in a one of a kind neighborhood, typical Portland flair from the street art to the food carts. You will adore this area!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-6967714/original/952142f6-510a-4841-887f-26ac15f75719.jpeg',1150082,24,'45.55604','-122.6757',1,12,3.00,5.00,5.00,357.00,1,1125,89,4.92,6967714),(352,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6974214','Stunning SE 1920\'s Craftsman near Kenilworth Park','Built in 1924 by a relative of Meriwether Lewis, the \"Gladstone House\" boasts original Mahogany built-ins, hardwood floors and a classic front porch. The kitchen and baths have been updated but retain the historic character.  The home is spacious and inviting, complete with full-size office and private patio. Highly walkable location.','Gladstone is quickly becoming “Little Division” with coffee shops, pubs, wine bar and a few hot restaurants is still tucked away with numerous parks and much quieter than it’s neighborhoods to the north (Division and Hawthorne). Scores: VERY walkable (74) VERY Bikeable (84) and GOOD Transit (51).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dc9fde73-d396-4e26-a2c8-521cb4c38fab.jpg',13818089,67,'45.49286','-122.63071',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,120.00,3,1125,267,4.91,6974214),(353,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6976600','Granny Flat in leafy SW Portland','One bedroom flat above house with separate entrance and private deck. Close to freeways to quickly get around Portland and all the beautiful and unique sights of this city. Less than 3 miles to trendy Multnomah Village. Minutes from downtown Portland.','We are on a small cul-de-sac with the back of the unit facing a beautiful green space.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5cd7dff2-7256-4e40-aa5c-8adc09012765.jpg',31117446,68,'45.44227','-122.73681',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,1,30,813,4.91,6976600),(354,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6990644','Modern & Private 1 Bedroom in NE Portland','Built in 2015, this new one bedroom apt is centrally located in inner NE Portland. Easy to walk, bike, or take public transit to great restaurants & shops.<br /><br />Free WiFi, memory foam queen bed, pull-out couch, Apple TV, full kitchen, dishwasher, full bath with washer/dryer. Clean comfy living in a private apartment separate from the main house.','We are located on the border of the beautiful Irvington and Eliot neighborhoods.  It was so important for us to find a house that was walking distance to almost anything and we found it (\'Walk Score\' gives it an 84 out of 100)!<br /><br />Distance of neighborhoods: <br />Downtown / Pearl District & NW 23rd (less than a 10 minute drive)<br />N. Williams (10 minute walk or 3 minute drive) <br />Mississippi (20 minute walk or 5 minute drive) <br />Alberta Arts (5 minute drive) <br /><br />Outdoors: <br />Irving Park (5 minute walk) <br />Forest Park (10 minute drive) <br />Mt. Hood, Mt. Saint Helens, and the Coast (~90 minutes away) <br />The Columbia River Gorge, Multnomah Falls, and Hood River (30-45 minute drive)<br /><br />Business Travel: <br />The Oregon Convention Center is a short 5-10 minute bus ride away and the PDX Airport is a 15-20 minute drive.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-6990644/original/2b5f080d-5f3c-4d7c-aa56-a5989fca7986.jpeg',14933969,26,'45.54295','-122.66003',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,15,120,390,4.93,6990644),(355,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6991450','Gorgeous craftsman in Sellwood!','Our lovely home offers a gourmet kitchen, media room, fireplace, outdoor dining, & firepit. Family-friendly, quiet Sellwood is minutes from downtown PDX & offers cafes, restaurants, the river, a pool, park, movie theatre all within walking distance.','Sellwood is a unique, desirable neighborhood in SE Portland. We love living here because of our easy (10 minutes) access to downtown but more so because of the incredible walkability of this neighborhood.  The new Orange Max (light rail) line is just a short 8 blocks away.  Within 5 minutes walking you can be at our neighborhood grocery store, one of several cafes, incredible award-winning dining (casual or more upscale options), a wine bar, one of the most amazing parks Portland has to offer, the Willamette River, or even an old-fashioned amusement park (Oaks Park on the river). Sellwood is truly one-of-a-kind. Despite all it has to offer, it is quiet and family friendly, and strollers, bikes, and dog walkers are more common than cars most times of the day.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/110252277/3624b08d_original.jpg',15850938,20,'45.46553','-122.65706',1,8,2.50,3.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,13,5.00,6991450),(356,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/6992895','The Kinley Manor Guest House','THE KINLEY MANOR COACH HOUSE, \"Portland\'s Most Talked About Well-Kept Secret\" is an award-winning bright, spacious, furnished, two-level guest home that serves as a great retreat for business people or travelers interested in extended stay lodging.','The lower level unit of this duplex is perfect and affordable. Located in the Irvington/Lloyd Center districts, near the Convention Center, Moda Center, the lightrail, Portland Streetcar, the Lloyd Center Mall, supermarket and more, we are equipped with every amenity you could hope for.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/50c03e99-28c8-4b5f-ab6c-a0d10fe29acf.jpg',4203145,59,'45.53448','-122.65498',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,126.00,28,120,274,4.94,6992895),(357,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7039107','Sunny, Private, Elegant---Pet Friendly','Bright, beautiful and fully furnished. This is a pet-friendly private house with an attached deck and a completely fenced, landscaped yard. Located in the heart of the Piedmont neighborhood. Walk to shops Max and bus. Less than 1 mile from both New Seasons and Fred Meyer. This is a two bedroom, one bathroom. The house features an open floor plan and would be comfortable for up to 4 people.<br />Minimum 30 days stay.','Walk to Max and bus--easy access to downtown. Close to New Seasons, Fred Meyer, Peninsula Park, Alberta Arts, Mississippi, and Dekum Triangle.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/89283680/878f472e_original.jpg',36909902,48,'45.57731','-122.67427',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,110.00,30,1125,1,5.00,7039107),(358,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7068422','The Garden House','The Garden House and guest bath are your private spaces. Location is at the base of Mount Tabor. The garden is available for lounging. Walking distance to Belmont and Hawthorne Districts.','Mount Tabor. Belmont Street. Hawthorne District. The Garden House backs up to The Portland Nursery. (Most amazing nursery ever!). The famous Horse Brass Pub is a 5 minute walk. There are food opportunities galore. Restaurants with great happy hours and/or food carts right in the neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/89666509/b546b1cb_original.jpg',37060525,16,'45.51761','-122.61327',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,94.00,1,1125,542,4.91,7068422),(359,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7072485','Modern Treehouse in Historic Spanish Turret House','This is not your typical short term rental with IKEA furniture and misleading photos! The Turret House is located on a large corner lot in Portland\'s most beautiful Eastside neighborhood (Irvington) and surrounded by gorgeous properties and tree-canopied streets. The unit was meticulously updated, while maintaining its Spanish Californian architecture and wide open circular floor plan. My partner and I are both designers and we’ve worked hard to blend tradition and modern simplicity.','The Irvington neighborhood is one of the largest Historic Districts in the country and features some of the most beautiful homes in Portland dating back to the 1920\'s. It is an architectural dream that spans a large swath of Portland. Most of the neighborhood, including my streets, are lined with old growth deciduous trees that create gorgeous canopies of green. The property has 5 giant old growth trees that feel like quintessential Portland. <br /><br />The apartment is ideal for anyone wanting to access all the culture of the Eastside while staying in a tranquil setting with a BBQ, hammock, and patio. The apartment is 2 miles from downtown Portland and less than a mile from the Convention Center and Moda Center.<br /><br />If you like taking walks with your family, friends, or dog, you couldn\'t choose a better location for natural and architectural beauty.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-7072485/original/31941938-45da-4d1b-9434-9ecd41633611.jpeg',373733,7,'45.53876','-122.64476',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,142.00,1,1125,383,4.89,7072485),(360,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7074345','Spacious Modern home in Mississippi Neighborhood','Keep Portland weird & the spirit of Portlandia alive while you relax in your Unique, modern home right in the heart of Mississippi North Portland neighborhood. Portland Flair,  funky boutiques,  coffee shops,  bars and restaurants at your fingertips.<br /><br />The home has lots of windows and natural light, dramatic ceiling lines, artistic Craftsman touches, and a comfy, livable feel. We hope you\'ll love it as much as we do.','We’re a N. Portland neighborhood with a lot of history and a ton of love. All sorts of restaurants, shops, boutiques, cafes, and night life!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/513f08d9-6fbf-405d-a221-8e6f62dc8262.jpg',3220022,9,'45.5501','-122.67553',1,4,1.50,2.00,2.00,219.00,30,180,44,4.82,7074345),(361,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7092722','Casita Sarita, Your Urban Escape! NO Cleaning Fee!','Welcome to Casita Sarita, Your Urban Escape!  A large, beautiful,  light-filled studio in the heart of SE Portland, walking distance to everything.  I have eliminated my cleaning fee for 1-2 night stays because I understand the frustration of so many  fees, and short stays tend to need less cleaning time. This is the only fee I can control, so I hope it\'s helpful.  On site professional MASSAGE(by me!) available. Please make yourself at home, relax, and rejuvenate.  I look forward to hosting you!','Oh there is so much to do in this neighborhood! Check out my \"guidebook\" for more detailed explanations, and my top recommendations. <br /><br />Just on this corner is Double Dragon Bahn Mi sandwiches (delish!) and cocktails, Apex, a watering hole with craft beers and outdoor seating galore (great people watching), Beermongers, a bottle shop where you can drink there or take beers to go, Genies or Pine State Biscuits for excellent breakfast, Los Gorditos is a taqueria, Virtuous Pie (vegan pizza), Baker\'s Mark (great subs), a couple coffee shop choices, a tattoo shop, a hair salon, and much more!!  Walking distance to food carts, restaurants, drinks, and shopping of all kinds on Division, Clinton, and Hawthorne streets. I\'ve lived in Portland for 25 years so I have lots of suggestions on restaurants, food carts, bars, music venues, and excursions. Bicycle rental also just out front, and the Spring Water Bike Trail is maybe a half mile away. Downtown is just across the bridges, about a 1','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/89972351/679b8455_original.jpg',13322905,25,'45.50624','-122.65393',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,99.00,1,730,819,4.95,7092722),(362,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7162521','Studio Basement Apt/Private/Mt. Tabor Neighborhood','Patio entrance door opens to down the stairs to the basement studio apartment with all the items you likely will need for your stay.  It\'s a mini home away from home. Owner lives in the house above the apartment. Bistro table with 2 chairs, Cable TV & WiFi; mini fridge; microwave, coffee maker. Plentiful, unrestricted street parking in front of my house.  Quiet neighborhood (quiet time 10pm to 6am respecting neighbors and homeowner.) One block off major street bus line.','The Mt. Tabor Neighborhood is one of Portland\'s oldest, safest, and most desired for living and enjoying.  A glimpse of how Portland appeared 200 years ago is minutes away.  A beautiful, heavily forested park, Mt. Tabor City Park, is a 10 block walk with it\'s numerous paved and graveled pathways for running, walking and biking.  The park is an icon within our city and loved for it\'s open air reservoirs, old growth trees, and abundant, natural wildlife. Mt. Tabor itself is an extinct volcano offering gorgeous views of downtown Portland to the west and Mt. Hood, Oregon\'s tallest peak, to the east.  Come and explore.  You\'ll find people friendly and welcoming.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b66ffc73-9396-49cd-abd9-4382d5d28577.jpg',29874534,15,'45.50625','-122.60527',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,1,30,593,4.96,7162521),(363,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7173741','Multnomah Gem - beautiful, pampering, mins to dntn','Perfect downtown \"alternative\" (less than 10 min away during light traffic times, or a little more with traffic). Absolutely gorgeous, fantastic kitchen, top-notch tiled bathroom, beautiful art on the walls and much more.  Coveted neighborhood of Multnomah Village.  Ditch that noisy hotel and get free parking and available late night check-in.','Quaint. Charming. A bit off-center and quintessentially Portland. Call it what you will, southwest Portland’s Multnomah Village is filled with character – as well as dozens of unique shops, galleries, restaurants, a wine bar and a brewpub.<br />Annual events include the Multnomah Days Parade and ensuing street fair on the 3rd Saturday in August, an afternoon Halloween in the Village and Holiday Gala on the First Friday and Saturday of December.  So get over here and see what all the fuss is about!<br />There is a very close-by gym in the Mittleman Jewish Community Center, located at 6651 SW Capitol Hwy.  It costs $15/day to use the gym.  Their hours are:  Mon-Thur 6am-10pm, Fri 6am-9pm and Sat-Sun 8am-6pm.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9b8610f5-fa5e-4e0f-bf51-08e84e67a612.jpg',37575586,18,'45.47175','-122.70289',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,82.00,1,1125,489,4.87,7173741),(364,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7202320','The Rabbit Hole - A Downstairs Guest Suite','Downstairs guest suite in my family home in the heart of the Portland culture, walking distance to downtown, Hawthorne, Natural Markets, Aladdin Theater, great little shops, local food carts, brewpubs & eateries. Public transit is nearby & frequent.','Walking distance to nightlife, restaurants, food carts, cute shops, community gardens, parks, rose gardens, theaters, cinemas, coffee & beer joints. Overall it\'s a pretty sweet spot!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ac2f92ac-7426-4db0-a809-1dec82b0692c.jpg',37410089,25,'45.50439','-122.65291',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,81.00,1,27,532,4.77,7202320),(365,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7207295','Scandinavian-modern private studio','Studio apartment designed with the essentials for relaxing. Get cozy by the gas fireplace with a book from our little library, work on your laptop in the desk nook or make an outdoor fire + star-gaze on the patio. Enjoy the mid-century furnishings, the nice sheets + towels and be sure to write a letter - letterpress cards + stamps are for your use. Quiet neighborhood with good coffee (Bison!), steps from breakfast (Beeswing), and near Beaumont Village (Pip\'s Donuts!). Only 10 mins to airport!','We\'re located in the Roseway neighborhood in NE Portland, Or. <br /><br />It\'s a quiet pocket of town though we\'re in proximity to some great hubs:<br /><br />Beaumont Village / approximately 1 mile away<br />NE 42nd Ave / approximately 1.5 miles away<br />Alberta Arts / approximately 3 miles away<br />Williams Ave / approximately 4 miles away<br />Hawthorne Blvd / approximately 4 miles away<br />Downtown / approximately 6 miles away','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/106590407/df323822_original.jpg',1312929,39,'45.55378','-122.59778',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,70.00,2,29,203,4.97,7207295),(366,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7224016','Purple House PDX- HUGE SW Apt. 10-15 min to town','ALL fully vaccinated/boosted guests are welcome to our city permitted, private, close-in RESIDENTIAL studio <br /><br />•Up to two well-trained, vaccinated dogs are welcome (extra fee(s))<br />•Separate EASY keyless entrance<br />•Free parking <br />•420 friendly OUTSIDE<br />•One street from public transportation<br />•Planter benches to wait for rides<br />•FULL Kitchen w/essentials & breakfast items<br />•Smart TV, blue ray<br />•Dedicated high speed Wi-Fi <br />•Private balcony <br />•Laundry<br />•Musical instruments/drum set for YOUR music!','Since we clearly cannot control where our house is located, please make sure that YOU want to be here, in a quiet RESIDENTIAL neighborhood that is close to everything. Almost every guest has rated us five stars for location since Purple House PDX has the best of both worlds. West Portland Park is a very friendly, safe and quiet Southwest RESIDENTIAL neighborhood.  We\'re just 6 miles/10-15 min drive (depending on time of day), from downtown, yet close to nature all around.  A short walk rewards you with a spectacular 360 view from Mt. Sylvania, parks, running trails and tracks. Tryon Creek Nature Park is also close.<br /><br />We are a great home base to explore nearby villages (Multnomah Village is a nice walk away on Capital) and cities, since we\'re close to Beaverton, Tigard, Tualatin and Lake Oswego. Near Lewis & Clark College and Oregon Health and Science University (OHSU), Shriners Hospital and Doernbecher Children\'s Hospital. We\'re also just five blocks or so to Portland Communit','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/80b64e16-bb5c-4f5b-a59e-28bc6b944b77.jpg',5401489,53,'45.44312','-122.7263',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,74.00,2,29,251,4.97,7224016),(367,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7225293','Morel Room @ 1234 HOUSE in SE PDX','An artist-made guest room in a renovated 1902-built house near Hawthorne, Belmont, Division & Downtown. Walking distance to variety of restaurants, bars, theaters, grocery stores, parks & public transit. PRIVATE ATTACHED SUNROOM AND LARGE BALCONY. Memory-foam queen bed, number-code locks, WiFi, two shared restrooms. Kitchen, dining room, living room, laundry, canoe, outdoor patios, record collection, piano/musical instruments.','1234 House is in the Buckman neighborhood of Southeast Portland, which is dense with homes 100-plus years old, and, like most of Portland, is experiencing a wave of new, modern consruction. 1234 House is a mile from the Willamette River, which separates the eastside of Portland and the westside city center. The house is nestled between Hawthorne Boulevard and Belmont Street, both lined with restaurants, bars, shops, theaters and music venues. A few blocks down the street is Col. Summers Park, a popular meet up spot to hang in the summer, especially on Monday Funday, and especially if you are down to play a mean game of dodgeball.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/838ec6ae-45c8-4335-b67b-7618fd5053fa.jpg',30708290,32,'45.51516','-122.64451',2,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,59.00,1,730,428,4.87,7225293),(368,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7228375','Welcoming 2 Bedroom, dog friendly','Get immersed in Portland culture! Dog-friendly in an easy-going residential area.<br />We are near a number of coffee shops, bars, restaurants, and wine tasting rooms. <br />Near public transit, a short drive/bike ride to downtown or trendy SE strips.','Just a few blocks from our house are a fantastic coffee shop, bakery, several restaurants, and bars. <br /><br />Everything is conveniently located a short drive or bicycle ride away. <br />The apartment is about 10 blocks South of the up and coming Division Street area where you will have your pick of trendy restaurants and bars. Also nearby are trendy SE strips like Hawthorne and Belmont.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/106746172/9d7815bb_original.jpg',34867239,67,'45.49419','-122.63901',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,125.00,30,90,270,4.93,7228375),(369,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7228938