d and the westside city center. The house is nestled between Hawthorne Boulevard and Belmont Street, both lined with restaurants, bars, shops, theaters and music venues. A few blocks down the street is Col. Summers Park, a popular meet up spot to hang in the summer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/da41e416-401e-4431-a6cd-c825f744a913.jpg',30708290,32,'45.51462','-122.64595',2,2,3.00,1.00,1.00,77.00,1,730,372,4.87,7231930),(371,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7245156','Division/Hawthorne Getaway','Join us in one of Portland\'s hottest neighborhoods. Blocks away from SE Division street (home to Salt and Straw, Ava Gene\'s and Stumptown Coffee), SE Hawthorne Street (historic hippie district) and Mt. Tabor Park (perfect for hiking and summer picnics).','Our home is in one of Portland\'s best & most historic neighborhoods, nestled between two of the city\'s most active, restaurant and bar filled streets. A family friendly, walkable, beautiful area. Division street sits two blocks south of our home where you can find Portland\'s most acclaimed & nationally recognized restaurants, such as: Pok Pok, Ava Genes, Woodsman Tavern and Salt and Straw. It\'s also home to Stumptown Coffee Roaster\'s very first coffee shop. This street is super chic but laid back, with many cute boutiques and upscale bars.<br /><br />Just two blocks north of our home sits SE Hawthorne Street-- historically known as Portland\'s \"hippie district.\" Lots of brew pubs, second hand and vintage shops, along with the famed Por Que No Mexican restaurant.<br /><br />And for a killer view of the city and some beautiful nature, just head twelve blocks east, to Mount Tabor Park--a volcano cinder cone! You can hike, picnic, bike, and enjoy summer concerts here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b9842e52-0449-4861-a390-c901b80d9938.jpg',1825887,8,'45.50722','-122.61292',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,104.00,2,30,584,4.81,7245156),(372,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7246397','Renovated Alberta Arts Sun-Filled Tiny House','This 1904 garage-turned studio apartment is fully equipped with comfy queen bed, compact kitchen, full bathroom including bath/shower combo and washer/dryer. The studio is set back from the road, private, vaulted and light-filled and surrounded by trees and greenery.  It features a comfortable outdoor area for those wonderful Portland evenings.  An easy walk to all kinds of good food and drink.  Alberta Arts, Mississippi, Fremont, PDX airport and Williams Avenue are not far away.','Inner Northeast Portland is one of the area\'s most vibrant neighborhoods.  In addition to Alberta Arts, nearby Mississippi Avenue is alive both day and night. And downtown Portland and the Pearl District are only 10 to 15 minutes away by car.  Also, we are only 15 minutes from PDX via a back way so take advantage of a quick trip to the airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-7246397/original/a3016f14-1f7b-4b59-8358-e3b9e651cf60.jpg',12923876,6,'45.55614','-122.65138',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,101.00,1,1125,840,4.96,7246397),(373,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7272984','The Black House Studio Unit #8 (North Portland)','The Black House Studio are cozy/serene spaces idea for the solo or duo traveler. They are situated in the Overlook neighborhood, one of the city’s many desirable neighborhoods and are close in proximity to the Mississippi and Albert Arts District. <br /><br />Located less than 10 minutes from downtown off the  I-5, you are in the middle of everything that PDX has to offer. The studios are just a short walk, bike ride or Lyft from local grocery stores, restaurants, nightlife, parks, entertainment and more.','The Overlook neighborhood in Portland is one of the city’s many desirable neighborhoods. Located north of the Pearl District across I-5, staying in Overlook puts you in the middle of everything that PDX has to offer, including great restaurants, nightlife, parks, entertainment and more. <br /><br />The studio is also located near the Mississippi & Alberta Arts Districts, the Adidas US Headquarters, University of Portland, Swan Island, the Kaiser Permanente Interstate Medical campus, and minutes from the Moda arena and Oregon Convention Center.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/494396ea-a217-45bb-8714-f1895cfb43d5.jpg',38007422,13,'45.55691599481316','-122.68331714092297',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,1,30,67,4.97,7272984),(374,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7279243','Charming Studio in SE PDX','Charming and bright private studio apartment in inner SE Portland, 4 blocks from  \"7-Corners\".  Walking distance to cafes, bakeries, shops, food carts, natural food markets, movie theater, restaurants and pubs.<br />Bike friendly<br />Washer/dryer<br />Secure storage<br />Private entrance<br />Kitchen with pantry basics/refrigerator <br />Freezer/ice<br />WiFi<br />Sleeps 2 in standard queen bed<br />An air mattress is available upon request if more than two guests<br />Hydronic radiant floor heat','Inner SE Portland is an established older mixed use residential urban neighborhood with narrow streets, sidewalks, single family houses, apartments and schools. The main corridor -Division Street- has been experiencing moderate retail and service re-development which has energized the neighborhood with a wide range of restaurants and food-cart vendors as well as natural food markets and coops, and boutiques. Overall livability is excellent as public transport and bike lanes are accessible and convenient.<br /><br />In summary, there is:<br />public transportation, retail, restaurants, markets, bakeries, parks, rose gardens, nightlife, theaters, and live entertainment within walking distance and/or a few minutes ride.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/108356183/9335d2b2_original.jpg',38113379,25,'45.50573','-122.64087',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,84.00,3,29,558,4.98,7279243),(375,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7292504','Saratoga Sweetness: cozy, quiet with private bath.','Superhost rated 1 bedroom with own private bath LGBTQ friendly (I am family). <br />I provide a dedicated work space with desk  right next to your room. This is a green and Eco-friendly space. If looking for a quiet restful night\'s sleep, you\'ll find it here!   No smoking/vaping on-premises.<br />Located in North Portland within desirable Arbor Lodge; quiet residential neighborhood. Organic coffee/tea available. Near parks and neighborhood restaurants. <br />Safe disinfectants are used for cleaning.','My Super Host (AirBNB rating) home is located near the Arbor Lodge neighborhood park, and light rail (MAX) is 6 blocks away. Bus lines are within 2 blocks. Travel time into downtown is about 15 min. <br />This neighborhood is quiet with many large old trees. Portland is a friendly,  easy to navigate city. There\'s always an opportunity to hear music, taste beer or sip wine.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-7292504/original/864634c6-07f8-4451-b037-6b797cee9403.jpeg',36446072,51,'45.57253','-122.68793',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,49.00,2,1125,254,4.92,7292504),(376,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7306750','Artist haven/historic Laurelhurst','During these unusual times I am very conscious about keeping keeping things scrupulously clean and am taking extra precautions to ensure my visitors safety.<br /><br />Beautifully remodeled spacious basement apartment in historic Laurelhurst with separate entrance and off street parking.  Near Hawthorne & Division neighborhoods and public transportation.<br />There is also a brand new “sister” cottage which makes this the perfect location for multiple guests.<br /><br />View:<br />https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37038333?','Historic Laurelhurst is one of Portland\'s most desired neighborhoods. It is a quiet family orientated area grounded by beautiful Laurelhurst Park which features serene walking trails, a lagoon, tennis and basketball courts. Within walking distance are trendy Hawthorne and Division Street neighborhoods. There is easy and quick access to downtown Portland, where you can become acquainted with the waterfront, the Pearl, NW 23rd Street and other points of interest. While exploring be sure to check out museums, theaters, restaurants and great shopping. <br /><br />If the city is not your thing, think about heading to Mt. Hood, Multnomah Falls, the Oregon Coast or spending the day visiting Oregon\'s renowned wineries.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/92751415/538d3871_original.jpg',22112041,16,'45.51903','-122.61924',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,115.00,2,730,112,4.87,7306750),(377,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7320844','The Cedar Cottage','Located in a quiet urban neighborhood close to unique eateries and the famous Hawthorne District. Short walk to hiking Mt Tabor park. This charming cozy studio cottage feels spacious and includes its own private deck.  It has easy parking and access.','The neighborhood is Mt. Tabor and is a few blocks from the eclectic Hawthorne District filled with interesting shops, New Season\'s Grocery, and a wide variety of delicious eateries.  Mt. Tabor park is less than a mile away and has hiking trails and historic reservoirs and a large beautiful off leash dog park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8a87ac1f-53ed-4af7-a79a-903d2ec05311.jpg',2135653,15,'45.50843','-122.60755',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,2,1125,854,4.94,7320844),(378,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7330215','Travel nurse friendly Portland Nice Condo','My place is in SW Portland, walking distance to synagogues, on the bus lines & is kosher/vegan/veggie friendly.  It is a 1 bedroom, 1 bath unit with 900 sq footage.  Was completely redone 7 years ago.  I have an extra air mattresses.','Super close to Multnomah Village and Downtown Hillsdale, for lots of restaurants, bars, and cute shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ee79f35b-6194-42d6-9312-21ecf4946c1a.jpg',23955222,31,'45.4747','-122.69736',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,159.00,30,60,20,4.75,7330215),(379,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7383236','Cozy 2nd floor Studio on gorgeous street','This newly updated small studio is perfect for the solo traveler with everything one would need to stay for awhile.  Private stocked kitchen with all cooking essentials, extra cozy full bed with fresh linens, and a work space that looks out big beautiful 4 square windows onto an urban forest with century old homes framing the very desired Irvington neighborhood.  It features a kitchen, full bed, walk in closet, with a spacious bathroom (shared with 1 person) with clawfoot tub.','The Irvington neighborhood, now only a ten minute bike ride from downtown, was once a trolley-car suburb to the just-fully-developed West side. Designated a historic district by the National Register of Historic Places in 2010, Irvington is filled with early 20th century homes that have been preserved in their original states. Irvington has become a livable hub of Northeast Portland as a whole, with shops and restaurants of all kinds, within walking distance, surrounding the neighborhood. Irvington proper boasts more than a few community and culinary destinations of its own.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4492eaff-b888-4b26-aa6e-023eaf0cce2c.jpg',13695963,7,'45.54245','-122.64835',2,1,1.00,0.00,2.00,31.00,30,1125,109,4.85,7383236),(380,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7402676','Retreat on Mt Tabor','Stay steps from Mt Tabor Park in your own private apartment area with a bedroom, bathroom and spacious living room with a well appointed kitchenette, enjoying shared outdoor decks, hot tub and a garden with meandering paths. We offer this space by the month while we are traveling.  Our roommates who live in another part of the house will be available to help you with any in-person house sharing questions and needs that you have.','We are right on the edge of Mount Tabor Park, a 10 minute walk from all the restaurants and shops in Montavilla.  Many outstanding restaurants and food carts at every price point are a 30 minute walk or 10 minute drive from the house.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-7402676/original/b58b1cba-2c69-4cfa-8be6-1a256598ddad.jpeg',8179306,15,'45.50982','-122.5908',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,45,31,4.81,7402676),(381,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7429660','Two bedroom standalone home Mt Tabor, Dog friendly','Cute home on quiet street in Mt. Tabor neighborhood.  Located on bikeway between Hawthorne and Division streets.  Easy walk to restaurants, cafes, and bars on  Hawthorne and Division streets.  Good central location for enjoying everything the Portland area has to offer.  This is a dog friendly home.','About 10 blocks from Mt. Tabor Park.  Walking distance to restaurants and bars on Division and Hawthorne streets. Located on both 50\'s bikeway and Lincoln street bikeway.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ec16ff61-8894-494e-bf7d-eaee0dec3d21.jpg',1377982,15,'45.5087','-122.60776',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,1125,61,4.84,7429660),(382,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7452129','New 1bd/1 BA Across from Park','The apartment is new construction (2015), super well maintained, 550 sq ft, 1bd/1ba unit above our garage. The outdoor space is very private. it is directly across the street from Sellwood park and just a few blocks from the bustle of 13th Ave which has restaurants, bars, coffee shops, etc.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-7452129/original/2e46ba62-a2b7-493e-9590-03dcc62e17ae.jpeg',39028080,20,'45.46884','-122.65812',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,125.00,2,1125,69,4.91,7452129),(383,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7486149','NoPo Boho','Quiet residential neighborhood in North Portland with easy access to public transport.  On street parking.  Quick walk to coffee (on the corner), restaurants and bars.  Private room with comfy queen bed.  Shared bathroom adjacent to bedroom.','Classic old Portland neighborhood without being super hipster.  Easy access to more hipster. Two mellow dive bars a block away.  Two coffee shops same with sushi and thai and tacqueria a three block walk. 10 to 20 minute drive to total Portlandia.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/536109bc-dc33-410e-9829-bf7346a4a2c8.jpg',13531661,51,'45.56689','-122.69746',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,51.00,30,1125,247,4.83,7486149),(384,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7547444','Near Oregon Convention Center','Please read entire listing before booking  ;o} <br /><br />It\'s my hope that you\'ll feel like a princess (or prince) sleeping in a jewelry box, in this sweet little jewel of a room. Perfect if you\'re traveling alone and plan to enjoy this great city.','You will be in the historic Sullivan\'s Gulch neighborhood where birds sing and trees line the streets but downtown is just ten minutes away and on Saturday night you\'ll find salsa dancing just 4 blocks away. <br />We are centrally located right in between some of Portland\'s most popular neighborhoods, Hawthorn, Division, Alberta arts, Mississippi arts, the Pearl and if you want to venture out a little further, an hour and a half to the east is Mt Hood and an hour and a half to the west is the beautiful Oregon coast.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/99088510/da59537f_original.jpg',1770933,4,'45.53368','-122.64487',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,55.00,30,1125,284,4.53,7547444),(385,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7591432','Live like a PDX local in this private apartment!','Getaway to Portland!<br /><br />This fully furnished unit will give you all the privacy and amenities that you need to live like a local.<br /><br />Work remotely? It\'s a great setup with lots of natural light and quiet for those video calls.','This North Portland neighborhood has a tremendous amount of conveniences within a short walk. Grocery stores, bars, restaurants and coffee shops all nearby.<br /><br />Take a walk annnd:<br /> - see the sunset overlooking downtown Portland<br /> - over to the downtown Kenton area for shops, bars and restaurants<br /> - lie in the grass at Peninsula Park or walk around their magnificent rose garden<br /> - have a coffee at Arbor Lodge, a burrito at Burrito Azteca, sushi at Sushi One, a beer at Look Long Brewing,...','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-7591432/original/bd6784a6-1b6d-4f52-8a03-ad4aa6b2cb5d.jpeg',12340051,51,'45.57629','-122.6802',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,45.00,30,200,33,4.61,7591432),(386,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7616616','Modern Rustic Zen  SE Studio Loft','Enjoy the early evening sunset and tree tops; a quiet resting spot! <br />Enjoy the SUPER King Bed: Romantic, warm and cozy, with a modern design Smart TV, and breakfast bar. Remodeled bathroom with waterfall faucets  for a \"get away\" experience.<br />Price reflects quiet though non-central local!<br />Please note: due to the stairs and partially open loft, the space is not safe for toddlers.','Food:<br />Very close by is Cartlandia! Another Hip, Cheap, Quick and Exceptional Food Value Deal. Clackamus Town Center is nearby. SE 82nd Ave. has anything and everything you need from Best Buys to Trader Joe\'s. The neighborhood is not a walking neighborhood. It is better to have a car to easily access the nearby sites.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/96669473/8c0a017f_original.jpg',23836921,69,'45.46686','-122.59751',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,65.00,30,60,67,4.36,7616616),(387,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7620997','Bright, Spacious Heart of Portland','Enjoy a safe, secure, comfortable(!) bedroom in the heart of Portland’s most iconic neighborhood.','We are blessed to live in such a convenient neighborhood. We live the \"village lifestyle\": we are so close to so much but without the cacophony usually found in big urban centers. All the convenience, none of the hassle. <br /><br />Whether you\'re on the hunt for the best beer in world famous \"Beervana,\" a uniquely fantastic meal in \"foodie\" Portland, or looking for a quiet, secure place to rest, our neighborhood provides it all.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-7620997/original/cadfcc9b-958e-474f-ab39-e4f39d4dd750.jpg',18590525,8,'45.51113591846699','-122.63356607310152',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,46.00,1,14,656,4.86,7620997),(388,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7644915','Lovely Northeast Portland Oasis','Peaceful private getaway in NE PDX neighborhood perfect for walking to restaurants, stores, parks and public transit. Beautifully equipped for extended stay with comfortable and eclectic furnishings and kitchen wares.','Within easy walking distance there are multiple grocery stores, coffee shops, donut shops, restaurants of many varieties, brew-pubs, sports-bars, wine-bars, food cart pods and the best frozen yogurt ever (Eb & Bean- locally sourced and organic).  The local Farmers\' Market is open on Saturday mornings throughout the summer and is a great spot for locally sourced edibles of all kinds (fruit, veggies, meat, fish, baked goods, honey, wine tasting, cheese, etc) with entertainment and hot food vendors. We love our local independent book store (Broadway Books) and historic non-profit movie theater, Hollywood Theater,  where you can see first run movies for $10. There is easy access to downtown Portland with all there is to see and do there (please don\'t miss Powell\'s Books). For Blazer fans, we\'re a half hour walk from the Moda Center. For Portlandia fans, many of the scenes were shot in the neighborhood so you might spot a home from your favorite segment while walking around.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/107414277/8a632ec8_original.jpg',19538819,33,'45.53756','-122.63737',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,144.00,5,100,102,4.96,7644915),(389,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7650094','99 Walk Score | NW Home for Long-Term Stays','Charming studio condo conveniently located in a historic NW building steps from the Pearl, 21st and 23rd Avenues, and downtown core. Great walk/bike score and access to public transit. Full kitchen, including gas range stove, dishwasher, toaster and microwave. Bathroom with clawfoot tub/shower. Washer and dryer in unit. Oversized walk-in closet.<br /><br />The condo is fully furnished and decorated, clean and private; fully stocked with all the necessities.','Steps away from restaurants, Trader Joe’s, two movie theaters, and trendy bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/45271b67-2947-4ca5-a3f5-bc987a7d219a.jpg',1197719,27,'45.52446','-122.68876',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,59.00,31,1125,15,5.00,7650094),(390,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7676079','5428 B - Interstate Max Line Monthly','BOOK FOR 31 DAYS OR MORE AND AVOID PAYING LODGING TAXES:<br />Newer fully furnished studio unit one block from the interstate Max light rail line in North Portland. Comfy queen size bed, washer and dryer in unit, air conditioning, dishes, linens, towels, etc. Utilities included, power, water, trash, wifi, no cable tv, smart tv only. Sorry no pets. Monthly housekeeping included. This is a separate apartment, this is not part of a house. Monthly housekeeping is included.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8490b214-6a57-493e-b6b5-84b59579d518.jpg',770134,13,'45.56136','-122.68032',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,19,4.84,7676079),(391,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7676080','5422 B- interstate Max Line','BOOK FOR 31 DAYS OR MORE AND AVOID PAYING LODGING TAXES:<br />Newer, fully furnished studio unit one block from the intestate Max light rail line in North Portland. Comfy queen size bed, washer and dryer in unit, air conditioning, dishes, linens, towels, etc. Utilities included, power, water, trash, wifi, no cable tv. There is a smart tv, sorry no pets. Parking is on street, free, no time limit. This is an independent apartment, it is not in someone’s house.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/791aa19a-ed81-4972-a03b-ea1001804220.jpg',770134,13,'45.56144','-122.68194',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,43.00,30,1125,26,4.96,7676080),(392,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7678990','Yellow Door / Heart of NW District /  Free Parking','THE BEST NEIGHBORHOOD IN PORTLAND/NW PORTLAND/NOB HILL/ALPHABET DISTRICT/ PRIVATE ENTRANCE AND FREE NEIGHBORHOOD PARKING PERMIT/SAFE NEIGHBORHOOD.   Wonderfully appointed kitchen and beautifully lit and maintained comfortable and roomy daylight basement apartment in the heart of Northwest Portland\'s most walkable neighborhood.  Prime location!!!','The NorthWest Neighborhood/Alphabet District/Nob Hill is Portland\'s Prime shopping, eating, and walking neighborhood.  We are in the Heart of one of the Best city neighborhoods in the country! Walk to Rose Garden, Forest Park, Riverfront....all within 10 to 20 minutes walk!!!!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/59a0f90a-98cd-4031-91ec-6938512329b5.jpg',33149703,27,'45.52894','-122.69859',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,138.00,3,30,353,4.95,7678990),(393,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7679227','Mid Century View Ranch w/ Covered Deck & Fireplace','Entire home rental for Sylvan Highlands view property.  Scenic outdoor spaces and tastefully furnished interior.  Ample parking, 5 min. to downtown and close to public transportation.  Enjoy Portland in style!  See details below.<br /><br />ASTR # on request','Plentiful nearby walking and hiking trails, grocery stores and restaurants.  Please inquire with hosts for details.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9c6cf00e-49a6-4063-a6d9-b5e0a629a731.jpg',2000049,62,'45.51374','-122.73534',1,10,3.00,4.00,7.00,425.00,30,90,147,4.82,7679227),(394,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7699029','Convenient, Secure, Comfortable. Pets Welcome!','This is a safe, cozy, quiet, fully remodeled basement suite perfect for traveling professionals and Portland visitors alike. It’s an ideal space to stay if you’re moving here and need time before settling into your own home.<br /><br />All you need is at your fingertips, including office workspace, full bathroom, full kitchen, common area, laundry.<br /><br />Close to bus, shopping, airport, downtown and MAX.','This is typical Portland! Want to know what it feels like to live here? This is it. Close to Parkrose High School, where you will find a state of the art rubberized track, public tennis courts, swimming facility, and if you are really lucky, a good ol\' hometown basketball or football game complete with marching band; or if you are really REALLY lucky, you\'ll be here when one of their plays or musicals is happening.<br /><br />Shopping, restaurants, freeway access, and one of Portland’s premier attractions (The Grotto) is within a 5 minute drive.<br /><br />Ample street parking around our corner home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d44c7c80-1301-4010-b134-e6e08a411baa.jpg',38953564,40,'45.54811','-122.5459',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,87.00,30,180,161,4.93,7699029),(395,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7701258','Charming 1922 Restaurant Row Bungalow Home','Built in 1922 and located on a charming, quiet residential street in the Laurelhurst neighborhood of NE Portland.  Our home is within walking distance to the restaurants and bars of vibrant NE Burnside and 28th Avenue. Our two bedroom bungalow  makes for the perfect place to call home during your stay in Portland.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-7701258/original/36be8e69-f53e-48bb-a024-94b923ec1f94.jpeg',40454925,12,'45.52586','-122.63976',1,2,1.00,2.00,2.00,116.00,2,6,245,4.91,7701258),(396,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7729130','Magic Barn  / Walk Score 93!','Everyone\'s safety is our top priority.  We are following Airbnb\'s enhanced cleaning guidelines.  Our neighborhood is safe and peaceful.<br /><br />The Magic Barn is centrally located 3 blocks to SE Hawthorne and Division\'s charming restaurant and boutique district.  Walk score 93!<br /><br />The Magic Barn was built in 1936 and was Todji\'s sculpture studio, which he transformed in 2015 with old growth barn wood, upcycled furnishings, kitchen, claw foot tub (not a hot tub), baby amenities, and a sculpture garden!','The Magic Barn is centrally located in one of the most charming and hip neighborhoods in Portland.<br /><br />With the center of both SE Hawthorne and SE Division St within 3 blocks, there is an abundance of restaurants, boutique browsing, grocery stores, neighborhood strolling, and park hiking options within walking distance. <br /><br />See a movie, or just step in to witness the beautiful and iconic McMenamin\'s Bagdad theater, accompanied by an incredible restaurant/bar/pool hall in the back called the \"Back Stage Bar\", at SE 37th and Hawthorne.  It will give you a feel for classic Portland! <br /><br />We are minutes from Mt Tabor park which has a lovely forest with walking trails sitting upon a dormant volcano, and we are 45 minutes to the spectacular 600 foot tall Multnomah waterfall in the gorgeous Columbia River Gorge scenic area. <br /><br />Division is the new up and coming Southeast neighborhood. With lots of modern architecture, new restaurants and shops you will get a feel','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e5618a35-c16f-470f-8642-af857681e068.jpg',26822355,8,'45.50953','-122.62238',1,10,1.00,1.00,1.00,82.00,1,14,1080,4.92,7729130),(397,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7764019','Private Bedroom Studio with Kitchenette','*smile*<br /><br />Conveniently located (airport, biking, walking, bus, MAX, Hollywood, Beaumont Village, restaurants, coffee shops), charmingly decorated, beautiful garden to enjoy. A private entrance to your studio bedroom with kitchenette and keyed entry.','We are located two blocks from Beaumont Village and an easy walk to the Hollywood Theater, 24 HR Fitness, yoga, stores and restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/40714714-3325-4aaf-83f1-2a61d467fced.jpg',40829795,11,'45.54615','-122.61449',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,1,1125,177,4.80,7764019),(398,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7769491','Minimalist Basement Unit in Historic Irvington','Beautiful  basement apartment in the historic Irvington neighborhood of north east Portland.  Perfect for a couple or solo traveler.  You will have your own entrance and side yard.  This unit has a temperpedic queen bed(firm), stove, dishwasher, bar table with stools, projector screen for movies, tea, and french press for coffee. The unit is centrally located with easy access to all that Portland has to offer.  Enjoy beautiful walks through the Irvington neighborhood or to Irving park.','Historic Irvington is known for the old craftsman and victorian houses, many which are over 100 years old.  Our house was built in 1924 but the basement was recently updated.  To the east of the house a few blocks are large historic houses with beautiful landscaping and massive heritage trees worth the stroll.  The closest coffee shop is a few blocks away to the west, Twentysix Cafe.  Irving Park, a short walk north is also a great park to stroll through.  If you want to keep close by, 15th and Broadway is a few blocks east and has a few bars Capitol and Swift lounge, as well as Eb and Bean frozen yogurt spot with dairy free/vegan options.  To the north less than a mile away is Whole foods Market and Free House one of our favorite little bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c34a49de-52db-4417-921e-7ba6fd15175c.jpg',4112255,7,'45.53954','-122.65502',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,120.00,2,1125,71,5.00,7769491),(399,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7790853','Charming craftsman blocks from Univ','1911 craftsman house blocks from Univ of Portland.This listing is for a private suite with 1 br (2 queen beds), lg family room (w/ desk and optional queen air mattress), mini fridge/ sink and bathroom. 1/2 block walk to bus access. Addtl space avail under different listings!  The back patio is a shared space with the owners (no other guests).','We are just a few blocks from Univ. of Portland with convenient access to grocery stores, parks and mass transit.  We are also close to the cute downtown St. Johns area with beautiful St. Johns Bridge and great restaurants.  Several restaurants within a couple of blocks.<br /><br />The house is in a residential neighborhood, with green yards (except in the summer), walkable streets and single family houses. It\'s nearby many playgrounds and a couple of big, beautiful parks (Forest, Columbia and Pier).<br /><br />Portsmouth lies between North Portland town centers St. Johns and Kenton, which offer restaurants, coffee shops, movie theaters, and shops. These town centers are each about 2 miles away. Downtown Portland is about 7 miles away / a 15 minute drive (with no traffic).<br /><br />New seasons is about 2 blocks  away and has a wide selection of wine and beers in addition to organic groceries and a large hot deli and salad bar.  We also have a Fred Meyer nearby.  <br /><br />Starbucks','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/99125903/1b739b75_original.jpg',13938342,57,'45.58356','-122.72838',1,5,1.00,1.00,2.00,132.00,2,1125,126,4.83,7790853),(400,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7837939','Close To Everything-Private Apt.','Clean & modern 1 bedroom private apartment in inner NE Portland. It has a private entrance, full kitchen, private bathroom (narrow shower stall), double bed, TV,  internet  & near grocery stores, dining, the Convention Center, transit and downtown.','Close to everything! Located in the historic Irvington neighborhood, in inner NE Portland (so it\'s close to downtown Portland). One mile away from the Oregon Convention Center and two miles away from downtown. Lloyd Center mall is close as well as many dining options and the Moda Center (where the Blazers play). There is a post office about five blocks away and many banks near by. We love the neighborhood in part because we love city living. This is in a walkable, busy and dense tree-lined community. You will be living as the locals live in one of Portland\'s best neighborhoods.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/108093637/f219a27b_original.jpg',344295,7,'45.53778','-122.65428',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,448,4.89,7837939),(401,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7844086','5422 A - Interstate Max Line Monthly','BOOK FOR 31 DAYS OR MORE AND AVOID PAYING LODGING TAXES:<br />Newer fully furnished studio unit one block from the interstate Max light rail line in North Portland. Comfy queen size bed, washer and dryer in unit, air conditioning, dishes, linens, towels, etc. Utilities included, power, water, trash, wifi, there is no cable television, but there is a smart tv. Sorry no pets. Monthly housekeeping included.','Great North Portland neighborhood close to public transit and multiple restaurants. New Seasons natural grocery is nearby as well as a Fred Meyer','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1f4c45a1-fd23-4db2-87b6-c029fd634799.jpg',770134,13,'45.56267','-122.68054',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,43.00,30,1125,19,4.89,7844086),(402,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7885712','Hawthorne Wisteria Retreat','A private studio in a garden courtyard located in the heart of bustling Hawthorne and Division neighborhoods, this retreat offers walking access to countless top restaurants, boutiques, vintage stores, book stores independent movie theaters and more. There is ample street parking right infront of the house or very near.','This delightful retreat, nestled under lush wisteria, is located in the heart of the most desirable part of inner Portland and is within walking distance of (just to name a few):<br />•Unique boutiques and vintage shops on Belmont, Hawthorne and Division streets<br />•A wide variety of restaurants including some of the most sought after, fine dining establishments-Ava Jean’s, Bollywood Theater, Nuestra Cocina, Three Doors Down, Jacqueline and many more<br />•Powell’s Books on Hawthorne <br />•Bakeries- Grand Central, Little T’s, St. Honore, <br />•Independent movie theaters- Clinton St. Theater, Cinemagic, and Bagdad theater and pub<br />•Grocery stores- Safeway, New Season’s, Fred Meyer and H-Mart<br />•Ice cream- Salt and Straw, 50 Licks<br />•Breakfast cafes- Jam, Genies, Pine State Biscuits, Waffle window, Bread and Ink, Slappy Cakes<br />•One of the newest and BEST Food Cart Pod’s in Portland (The Asylum- 11th and Main)<br />•Bus and Max train lines to downtown<br />•Easy walk or ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/107673448/bf13b846_original.jpg',41571033,25,'45.50977','-122.64226',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,106.00,1,28,610,4.92,7885712),(403,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7915941','Newly Remodeled, Modern Retreat','Our place is close to Adidas, Portland State University, and major bus lines. You’ll love our custom basement from the moment you walk in the door.  Our place is good for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, and families.','Very safe and quit neighborhood.<br />Great local restaurants and pubs close by.  Location is in the middle of everything, it\'s just a few minutes driving to downtown, Portland State University, Addidas, Mississippi, St Johns, Jantzen Beach.  <br />Great park for kids 4 blocks away.  <br />Dog parks close by.<br />Bike paths close by, <br />Max Station 10 blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3413f987-ad09-44ab-9478-af920c02e31a.jpg',32847442,51,'45.56806','-122.69564',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,79.00,1,90,311,4.96,7915941),(404,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7922813','Ash Street Private Penthouse off Restaurant Row','A penthouse studio  in one of Portland\'s amazing spots! Private entrance, large deck, and kitchenette! Whether you\'re visiting the city, here on business or visiting family, our spot is perfect. We are one block from everything: eateries, cafes - minutes from Mt. Tabor and just over the bridge from downtown.<br /><br />Please read house rules before booking. Sounds carry in our old house. We ask everyone to please be aware that although the space is a private space, you’re still in a home with kids.','We are in the heart of Portland. Portland is famous for a few things by now: food pods, foodie spots, the Laurelhurst Theater, Laurelhurst Park, bike routes, Powell\'s bookstore... you name it, we are located in the popular Kerns neighborhood, just minutes away either by foot bike, or car. Please check out the Guidebook here on the listing for what is within walking distance - so much!!<br /><br />We love to chat about Portland and what makes our city special. See the Guidebook as to where we are located and you\'ll be in for a treat.<br /><br />Step outside the house and you can easily walk to almost anywhere. If you don\'t have a car we are two blocks from a major busline that takes 5 minutes to downtown and elsewhere. There are now bike and scooter rentals nearby as well, and Uber or Lyft of course. <br /><br />We are near nightlife, eateries, both urban and green spaces like the sprawling, gorgeous Laurelhurst Park and Mt. Tabor. There are plenty of options for the meat eater, the veg','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d5422a35-5bf7-4c7c-bc24-d251948afc5e.jpg',41780011,12,'45.52167','-122.6354',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,85.00,2,29,125,4.93,7922813),(405,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/7924119','Ash Street Big Studio off Restaurant Row','Incredibly cozy, large studio with private bathroom, full shared kitchen, radiant heated floors, washer and dryer in the heart of Portland! <br /><br />Come enjoy our cozy studio! We are close to everything - the historic Laurelhurst Theater is 2 blocks away, as well as eateries, bars, boutiques!<br /><br />Please read house rules before booking. Sounds carry in our old house. We ask everyone to please be aware that although the space is a private space, you’re still in a home with kids.','Our neighborhood IS so much. Technically, we are in Kerns which was recently named one of the BEST neighborhoods in Portland! We have the sprawling Laurelhurst Park, one of the nicest and largest parks in Portland. We are two blocks from Laurelhurst Theater, made famous by Portlandia where you can get beer and pizza with your movie! We are also a half a block away from shops, restaurants, food pods, and bars. Basically we are in the heart of the hip and urban Portland and happy to call here home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/20818ecf-f87e-4e2f-b2e5-4c60a025da1c.jpg',41780011,12,'45.52212','-122.63615',2,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,65.00,2,20,122,4.93,7924119),(406,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8015598','Quiet Retreat Steps from Bustling NE Broadway','Find economical luxury for long or short stays in our bright, beautifully furnished 1-bedroom apartment in the Irvington Historic District, close to the NE Broadway shopping and dining area, and well served by TriMet transit.  You\'ll like the new construction, modern appliances, super comfy beds, two TVs and high speed WIFI.  The unit is a separate sound insulated space giving you total privacy, with no air circulation to the main house and a private entrance directly from the street.','The unit is in the Irvington Historic District, Oregon\'s largest historic district, and a treasure trove of lovely historic homes and lush gardens along tree-lined streets that are perfect for strolling or biking and have won plaudits in our guest reviews.  Just two blocks away is the NE Broadway commercial area with its many restaurants, shops, and services.  Supermarkets, convenience stores, and one of Portland\'s best bakeries are near at hand.  Our \"house manual\" lists over 30 restaurants within walking distance.  Downtown Portland and its many attractions are 15 minutes by car and convenient by TriMet bus or Light Rail.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3a51b603-4cd9-45ce-a802-650dc47e2a34.jpg',3849293,7,'45.53625','-122.6469',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,88.00,1,90,408,4.98,8015598),(407,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8018480','Private Garden Guest House - one bedroom','Detached one bedroom  abode just behind main house with off street parking and private entry. Features a full private bath & kitchen that easily accommodates 1 person or two people who like each other a lot ;) Located in inner North Portland, there is easy access to freeway, mass transit, and bike routes. Neighborhood is highly walkable with parks, library, shopping, and restaurants near by.','Full of activity and venues, the inner North Portland Corridor is bound to please. The major hubs are located on N. Williams, N. Mississippi and NE Alberta Avenues but the adventurous will delight in finding small gems along the way. Consistently known for the finest coffee houses, small craft breweries and a bustling food scene - there is something for all tastes within walking distance of the house. The listing is complete with a directory to establishments plus walking and biking maps to make your travels easier.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6ODAxODQ4MA%3D%3D/original/ee9c429f-e50b-4974-ba2b-ba79716a38c1.jpeg',12099165,24,'45.555538177490234','-122.67086029052734',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,47.00,30,90,69,4.94,8018480),(408,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8035910','LONG TERM LUXURY IN THE PEARL','Industrial Lux meets Swankiness in our haven in the Pearl. We are walkable to bistros and  coffee bars, the latest craft beer emporiums, bars, boutiques, clubs, transit, groceries, theatres, books, beards and lots of flannel.  Enter 750 sq \' of fully equipped urban comfort chic.  Lounge on our bronze leather furniture while watching the 55\" smart TV. Don a complementary plush robe, shake yourself a cocktail, walk through French doors and sit in calm repose on our balcony. Welcome!','The Pearl is frequently sited as one of the hippest neighborhoods in North America.  Markets, festivals, parades, galleries, live music venues, bars, boutiques and a wide variety of services all contribute to create the vibrant culture that surrounds our condo and is just steps away.  Around the corner from our condo is the eclectic World Foods Market Grocery with a fabulous bakery, gourmet deli and soup bar, wine bar and outdoor seating. Very close for coffee are favorites Barista, Umbria and Sisters. Favorite breakfast and brunch places are  Lovejoy Bakers and Daily Cafe and for a true diner breakfast experience (with very good food) is Fullers Coffee Shop, also 1 block away. Cha Cha Cha serves Mexican food in a colorful intimate space and Hotlips Pizza and Little Big Burger are all great choices for an inexpensive fun meal.  If you would like to hit a chill place to try some local craft brews and fill your growler,The Big Legrowski is a block and a half away on Couch St. The famous ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/109604039/df3f1773_original.jpg',42431331,2,'45.52452','-122.6803',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,30,180,21,4.95,8035910),(409,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8035987','Lark About Downtown from Here!','Hip & Homey -- Cultural Arts District in the Heart of Downtown <br />Pulse of Downtown -- Unbelievable location!!   <br />We call it Lark About - meaning:  to play boisterously, to engage in harmless fun or mischief.  You can do exactly that as you are out and about during your stay!<br />Open plan with floor to ceiling windows<br />Excellent interior design, comfortable furnishings and ingredients for cooking and living.  Views of downtown & west hills.... looks out to PSU & Parks Blocks','It is in the heart of the Cultural Arts District, but is also close to what could be called the Financial and Legal District. <br /><br />Shopping, dining, Farmers Market, Museums, Theaters, Providence Park -- all within walking distance.   Walk to Timbers & Thorns Games!  Portland State University, Lincoln High School and St. Mary\'s also within a few blocks!<br /><br />Lark About is close to almost everything of fun in the downtown area: Park Blocks and its famous Saturday morning Farmer’s Market, Portland State University, McCall Waterfront where most festivals are held, Pioneer Place, Powell’s Books, the beautiful Central Library, Art and History Museums, Providence Park for Timber and other sports events.  <br />A Safeway is across the street!  <br />The Old Church, venue for concerts and weddings, is next door.  <br />The famous Saturday Market (near VooDoo Donuts) and the Pearl District are not what could be considered “close,” but they are also easily reachable on foot, bike, st','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b57e9dee-2cc2-4afe-aa49-47375a8fb685.jpg',42139754,44,'45.5159','-122.6867',1,4,1.00,1.00,4.00,250.00,30,90,54,4.81,8035987),(410,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8051993','North Tabor Victorian/Modern 2BD','Beautiful North Tabor Victorian with modern appointments. Wonderful updated bathroom and kitchen. Numerous amenities including outdoor deck and lounge space with backyard fire pit and professional outdoor gas grill. Lots of great natural light.','North Tabor is centrally located to many neighborhoods in Portland\'s east side, including Hawthorne, Belmont, Laurelhurst and the inner Eastside Industrial District - and a close jaunt from downtown and the Mississippi/North Portland Neighborhood. Close to everything without the noisy nighttime traffic!  Walking distance to two great restaurants as well as a grocery store.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/109958633/4548aab4_original.jpg',1735359,52,'45.52624','-122.60858',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,124.00,2,1125,574,4.94,8051993),(411,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8053707','Sunny bedrooms  Craftsman style home NW Portland','This listing has  sunny, lovely  private bedroom with 4 poster double bed and dresser, private bathroom, with use of  kitchen and outdoor decks, in historic NW neighborhood convenient to shops, galleries, cafes, restaurants and all public transportation.  We ask that all guests be vaccinated for COVID.','My home is only two blocks from NW 23rd Ave, bustling with cafes, restaurants, galleries, shops, library and public transportation. The neighborhood is friendly and an easy walk to either the Pearl District or forest park with miles of forested wilderness trails. Parking is limited but available on the street but public transportation (bus and street car) is right here and makes us so convenient to Portland\'s other neighborhoods.... also this is a great walking neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/102640955/d589b0f5_original.jpg',42533657,27,'45.53286','-122.70142',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,125.00,3,30,22,4.55,8053707),(412,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8072092','Designer\'s Home in Rose Garden!','You are simply going to love this beautiful house, which has been perfectly styled by the home owners -- two minimalist designers -- to be a sleek, modern rental, while still being comfy enough for the whole family. With two queen-sized beds and bunk beds, a bonus room, a brand new kitchen, remodeled bathroom, and small yard, this home has all the amenities of a high-end hotel plus much more. You\'ll feel like a mid-century movie star in this house!','The beautiful Peninsula Park and Rose garden is nearby with playground and a swimming pool in the summer. Easy 1-5 access just 10 blocks to ramps north or south. New Seasons grocery store is a short 15 minute walk from the house and has all the essential grocery items you may be searching for.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-8072092/original/736c18bd-4f13-4165-b627-d10ea1cf252f.jpeg',27974994,48,'45.56884765625','-122.66822052001953',1,5,1.00,3.00,6.00,119.00,30,1125,121,4.93,8072092),(413,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8118223','Spacious & Stylish Portland  Beauty! Close-in!','Professionally cleaned after each and every guest stay! Dreamy updated Portland Classic Bungalow- she\'s a real gem. Close-in and easy walking distance to public transportation, food trucks, historic Mississippi, the best brunch in town, amazing pizza, the list goes on.  For families with children, picturesque Overlook Park is one block away(with a large playground!).  For foodies, options abound!  Kick back and relax on the deck with a coffee or around the fire pit in your private back patio!','Charming Portland Overlook neighborhood! Very safe, sweet neighbors, close to everything. 10 minutes drive to downtown Pearl and walking distance to Mississippi neighborhood! Historic Overlook Park is one block down the street with a big field, running track, and large playground. Beautiful views of bridge city!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a9691f81-6aaf-4d1c-bad5-5d439cb772a2.jpg',1022102,13,'45.55054','-122.68304',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,225.00,2,30,310,4.89,8118223),(414,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8149676','Just Remodeled NE Cottage w/new King Bed','Just remodeled cozy cottage with new king bed in NE Portland Irvington neighborhood, five minutes from downtown, Convention Center, Moda Center, restaurants, coffee shops, and on major bus lines.  Carport parking. Full kitchen & excellent AC!  Private back yard deck. A ten minute drive to major Portland attractions such as the Pearl, Powell bookstore, the Japanese garden   Relax in our mid century modern living room or walk in our treelined neighborhood to coffee shops and restaurants.','The unit is perfectly located in a safe and historic neighborhood a few blocks walk from Broadway St., with many restaurants, coffee shops, bars, and boutiques. Two nearby parks offer tennis courts, running track, playgrounds and seasonal swimming pool/water park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-8149676/original/1854628d-0408-490b-bd38-1f0565958e2a.jpeg',869605,7,'45.53732','-122.64664',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,109.00,2,30,266,4.89,8149676),(415,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8194988','Private, airy & super-clean guest house','Newly constructed cottage. Ideal location, close to I84, bus, MAX. 15 min to Downtown or Airport. Close to some of the best food and drink in town. Located in Portland\'s safe & quiet Hollywood neighborhood. Bright, luxurious & private. It is a comfortable, charming modern bungalow that will make you feel like you\'re at home!<br /><br />*Please note: the no cleaning fee applies to all reservations booked after February 15, 2024.','Our house is nestled within a friendly and safe neighborhood. Enjoy short walks to the Hollywood Farmer’s Market, Trader Joe’s, Whole Foods, Rite Aid, Hollywood Theater, and a variety of restaurants including brew pubs, coffee shops, family-friendly and fine dining. The neighborhood is named for the glorious art house, the art deco Hollywood Theater, just a few minutes\' walk from our cottage.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d640d7b4-3089-43d1-b6a5-e8e7a2f169c2.jpg',13303946,11,'45.53562','-122.61419',1,4,1.50,1.00,3.00,139.00,1,365,290,4.93,8194988),(416,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8236018','Woodstock modern apartment','Fully-furnished, standalone one-bedroom apartment with queen bed, full kitchen, washer/dryer, A/C and on-site parking. High quality finishes, non-toxic cleaning products, native landscaping and grid-tied solar power.','The house is located in a rural-feeling area near Errol Heights Wetlands and Community Garden. It is a peaceful, friendly, and funky neighborhood near Woodstock. <br /><br />Please note that wild peacocks roam the neighborhood and can be noisy at times.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/279c26ce-05e0-4821-b2fb-2a49c0b70994.jpg',15280606,69,'45.4652','-122.61292',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,2,30,326,4.96,8236018),(417,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8256301','NW 23rd (Nob Hill) - Cozy Apartment','This comfy and cozy two-bedroom apartment is in the basement unit (with separate entrance!) of a beautiful Victorian home and just a half a block from the restaurants, cafes, bars and boutiques of gorgeous NW 23rd Ave.','Smack dab in beautiful NW Portland/Nob Hill/Alphabet District/The Flats. You will be half a block away from arguably Portland\'s most charming commercial strip, NW 23rd Ave.  Seemingly endless bars, restaurants, cafes, and shops of all kind.  Neighborhood full of tree-lined streets, flowers, and Victorian homes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-8256301-unapproved/original/5e030207-92b9-4f7d-a089-d90f64533df8.JPEG',37100855,27,'45.52698','-122.69794',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,60,484,4.75,8256301),(418,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8290529','Hawthorne/Belmont Retreat - East bd','This is the EAST room. The other room is WEST. They are the only 2 upstairs bedrooms in our home, and we try to keep both free of chemical scents. (See house rules) The West bd has an office/sitting room and kitchenette. Both rooms are peacefully quiet, yet only 2 blocks from a popular foodie and shopping district with many local restaurants, shops, and lots of vintage clothing stores. Guests share a large bathroom, but not with us since we and our 3 cats live on the main floor. Come meet us!','Our southeast neighborhood is close-knit and quiet but only blocks from a trendy, bohemian-style shopping district with excellent restaurants. Free street parking is available across from our driveway. No city permit is required. We have several beautiful parks close by with duck ponds, tennis courts, and jogging paths.  Portland has an active arts and music scene with styles for all tastes. The downtown is on the water and a great place for sailing or a dinner-cruise on the river.  The Columbia George is about a 45-minute drive from our home. The Oregon coast is about an hour and a half from here by car.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-8290529/original/b9a14f47-ca15-4dc3-93e9-271473b56119.jpeg',456853,16,'45.51347351074219','-122.63191986083984',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,1,7,825,4.97,8290529),(419,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8290549','Urban Oasis / Private Guesthouse','Located just minutes from downtown, but you\'ll feel like you\'re nestled deep in the woods. Relax and enjoy our private guesthouse in the Overlook neighborhood. Within close walking distance to public transportation, and a short drive to restaurants, bars, shopping. Mississippi Ave, Williams St, and the Alberta Arts District are nearby.  The MAX line is an eight minute walk away.','Overlook is a charming and historic residential neighborhood located just 2.5 miles north of downtown Portland. We are situated on a bluff above the Willamette River, which offers beautiful views of Forest Park, the Fremont Bridge and downtown. There are a handful of restaurants, bars, and coffee shops within a few blocks of our house on Killingsworth St., and we are a short walk to Mississippi Ave. where you will find some of Portland\'s best restaurants, food carts, bars, music venues, and shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/74befb20-91fc-4ffd-a061-7aec068871c8.jpg',43706954,13,'45.55697','-122.68691',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,157,4.92,8290549),(420,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8291362','Hawthorne/Belmont Retreat - West bd','This is the WEST room and has an office/sitting room and kitchenette. The other room is EAST. They are the only 2 upstairs bedrooms in our home, and we try to keep both free of chemical scents. (See house rules) Both rooms are peacefully quiet, yet only 2 blocks from a popular foodie and shopping district with many local restaurants, shops, and lots of vintage clothing stores. Guests share a large bathroom, but not with us since we and our 3 cats live on the main floor. Come meet us!','Our southeast neighborhood is close-knit and quiet but only blocks from a trendy shopping district with excellent restaurants, lots of local shopping, and many vintage clothing stores. Free street parking is available across from our driveway. No city permit is required. We have several beautiful parks close by with duck ponds, tennis courts, and jogging paths. Portland has an active arts and music scene with styles for all tastes. The downtown is on the water and a great place for sailing or a dinner-cruise on the river.  The Columbia George is about a 45-minute drive from our home. The Oregon coast is about an hour and a half from here by car.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-8291362/original/71b8e538-3614-4287-bb04-b17347b0b457.jpeg',456853,16,'45.51347351074219','-122.63191986083984',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,1,7,886,4.95,8291362),(421,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8312174','Near Providence Hospital - Sunny Tabor 1100 Sq Ft','Welcome to your charming 2-bedroom home in the heart of Portland! Nestled in the North Tabor area, this cozy retreat offers a perfect blend of comfort & convenience for your stay. This private apartment on the main floor (w/private entry!) has over 1,100 sq ft. Living room, kitchen, 2 bedrooms, dining room & 1 bathroom for your EXCLUSIVE use with central air conditioning & heating. Close to downtown & extremely easy access to public transportation.  Inspected & permitted by the City of Portland.','Neighborhood is very safe, convenient, and there are cool bars and restaurants within walking distance. Leikam Brewing and Salvi PDX are just a block away.  The Tabor Tavern is nearby and has great fish and chips and a nice selection of beers.  Oly\'s Pizza is in easy walking distance. There is a QFC grocery store (with pharmacy) and nail salon 3 blocks away.<br />You can get downtown by car in about 10 minutes (depending on traffic/weather) or by bus in about 20 minutes.  <br />I am a short distance from the following areas: Mt Tabor, Belmont, Montavilla, Hawthorne, Hollywood District, Lloyd Center.  I am just a few blocks from the Providence Hospital complex.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5e888c90-c745-4534-8d5c-b28d4b054c62.jpg',9603365,52,'45.52437','-122.60473',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,136.00,3,26,87,4.92,8312174),(422,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8355231','Home away from home in SW Portland!','Enjoy your stay in my simple, bright 50\'s ranch. 2 bdrms with queen beds, bath, shower, stocked kitchen, deck. Walk to Gabriel Park or Multnomah Village. Short commute to OHSU, PSU, L&C College or NCNM. Nice, quiet hood 10 minute drive to downtown.','Gabriel Park<br />Southwest Community Center (drop in yoga classes, swimming and more)<br />short walk to Laughing Planet, Sunnys Legendary Frozen yogurt or Lighthouse Coffee shop<br />30 minute walk or 5 min drive to Multnomah Village where you will find:<br />Marco\'s restaurant<br />Journey\'s restaurant and pub<br />Lucky Lab Microbrewery and Pizza Pub<br />Sip d\' Vine wine bar<br />O\'Connors restaurant and pub<br />Acapulco\'s Southwest Gold<br />Down to Earth Cafe<br />Switch Shoes<br />Multnomah Arts Center','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cbca4d70-dc0c-4154-8325-97e05892e1ec.jpg',2381917,17,'45.47973','-122.72654',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,127.00,2,14,79,4.89,8355231),(423,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8391434','Mississippi District Private Suite','Nestled in the quaint Mississippi District and less than a mile to downtown this is an upstairs suite with a bedroom that will allow up to 4 people, a full bath and a sitting area.<br />PDX airport is 25 minutes away. Public transport and Nike bike rentals within a block.<br />Old & new with asian touches blend together in our restored craftsman bungalow. The home is as much a working sanctuary as possible. <br />Cute shops, restaurants and brewpubs just around the corner. <br />Fabulous Portland beyond!!','The Mississippi District is a very quaint neighborhood with many unique shops and restaurants.  It is tucked up into a <br />a kind of bluff just a mile from the center of town but far enough to feel like it’s own little town. It is generally quite peaceful but can  become bustling and exciting. Quiet at  night and is not a major thoroughfare.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9887282b-46f3-4845-befd-1271a5137970.jpg',44216258,9,'45.55176','-122.67562',2,3,1.00,1.00,3.00,81.00,4,10,204,4.90,8391434),(424,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8408240','Charming Rooms in Eastmoreland Contemporary Home','I live in this home in Eastmoreland, a great neighborhood! This ranch style home is furnished in contemporary decor. Walk to Reed College, Crystal Springs Rhododendron Garden, Woodstock, and Sellwood. I moved here from the south and I extend my southern hospitality to all of my visiting guests!  My son has a photography studio in my basement and works there some days. His business will not interfere with your stay.','Eastmoreland is a family neighborhood with a great community spirit.  Woodstock and nearby Sellwood have excellent options for dining and shopping.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/02c64f66-1a88-4c0c-b466-810a850f3ba9.jpg',44293276,5,'45.46597','-122.62614',2,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,1,10,165,4.93,8408240),(425,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8429119','Modern Loft Living in Central SE PDX','Over the past 12 years, we have extensively renovated our 2-story 10,000 sf warehouse from a cluttered loading facility into a bustling wedding & event venue and an open-concept loft home. <br /><br />The building\'s industrial architecture sets the stage for the modern decor, and the spacious layout is ideal for a cityscape vacation, wedding prep, and a family looking to spread out and relax. <br /><br />In one of the hottest neighborhoods in town, you can\'t beat our location in the heart of Central SE Portland.','Sharing a block with James Beard winning restaurant, Kann, and a popular ceramic studio, our building is in one of the most accessible and central neighborhoods in the city. <br /><br />Within a few minutes walk are Portland’s best hotels (Jupiter, KEX, Hotel Grand Stark), bars (Scotch Lodge, Rontoms, Pacific Standard), an incredible wellness spa (Knot Springs), as well as yoga studios, retail,  restaurants, coffee shops, and so much more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-8429119/original/f105b25e-8fb5-4f8a-8355-6c1adf603e52.jpeg',1511460,32,'45.52066448187114','-122.66113566449326',1,6,2.50,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,5,21,4.76,8429119),(426,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8458004','Multnomah Village Petite Maison','Cozy private apartment studio above detached two-car garage behind our house sleeps 2 adults. Queen bed, kitchenette, full bath w/ shower. All necessities included. 10 minute walk to the village, 10 minute drive into downtown Portland.','Our location has great access to Barbur or I-5 for quick access into downtown or Eastside. We\'re also walking distance to both Multnomah Village and Hillsdale, the cutest gems of Southwest Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-8458004/original/bd9250c9-ee7f-4029-b0c5-bc668dae1949.jpeg',44519913,31,'45.47334','-122.70233',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,99.00,1,14,222,4.87,8458004),(427,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8475095','The Artist’s Nest','You\'ll love this private and comfortable artist\'s studio complete with your own outdoor deck and pergola. Enjoy a King size Casper bed to relax on. You can walk to the Montavilla bars/restaurants or up to the top of Mt. Tabor and grab a city view while you picnic. Located conveniently near the airport, downtown, public transit and freeways, whatever you have planned for Portland, this is a perfect launchpad.','Come check out any one of the several bars and restaurants located only a couple of blocks away including The Observatory, Lazy Susan, Academy Theater, Bipartisan Cafe, Roscoe\'s, Montavilla Farmer\'s Market, Miyamoto Sushi, Flying Pie Pizzeria, Bipartisan Cafe, Beer Bunker, Redwood, Tinker Tavern, Vintage Cocktail Lounge, Beer Bunker, and Thatchers. The well known Mt. Tabor Park is just several blocks away also - walk up to the top and watch the sunset over the city!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-8475095/original/aa18de20-c3b2-49a6-971e-9fa2f24d0a16.jpeg',2884284,10,'45.51899','-122.57611',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,60.00,30,1125,326,4.94,8475095),(428,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8597145','GREAT NOB HILL NEIGHBORHOOD - 21','NORTHWEST PORTLAND: Completely furnished studio in a beautiful Mediterranean building located in friendly, close-in Northwest Portland. <br /><br />This convenient location with a 98 Walk Score is close to some of the best restaurants, bars and cafes in town. <br /><br />Fast wifi included so you can work from home.','Close-in Northwest Portland- Nob Hill.<br /><br />This convenient location, with a 98 POINT WALK SCORE is blocks from trendy NW 23rd AVE, Dragonfly Coffee House, St. Honore Bakery, McMenamins Pub, a natural foods grocery store, the public library, as well as the post office. <br /><br />Window shop at all the lovely boutiques located just blocks away or hike/bike/run/explore the 80 miles of trails and over 5,000 acres of Forest Park; one of the largest urban parks in the United States! <br /><br />You can quickly and easily reach the Pearl District, the Brewery Blocks or Downtown Portland in minutes by foot, bike or streetcar; no need for a vehicle when living here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7b31ace3-80f0-4578-bf82-50e0b37528a9.jpg',21655715,27,'45.53697','-122.70296',1,2,1.00,2.00,1.00,56.00,30,365,25,4.56,8597145),(429,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8630512','Cozy Attic Apartment','Headed to Portland and need a cute, comfortable, well-located place to serve as headquarters? Search no further! I live in one of the best neighborhoods in town. It\'s very safe, comfortable, and easy to maneuver on foot, on bike, by bus, or by car. 2 blocks from New Seasons, one of the best grocery stores in the country (think Whole Foods, but better), 2 blocks from prime Alberta arts district.','I live in one of the best neighborhoods in town. It\'s very safe, comfortable, and easy to maneuver on foot, on bike, by bus, or by car. 2 blocks from New Seasons, one of the best grocery stores in the country (think Whole Foods, but better), 2 blocks from prime Alberta Street bars, restaurants, coffee shops - and 1 block from Killingsworth bars/restaurants (Beast, Yakuza, Wilder, Vita Cafe, Pine State Biscuts, Cup and Saucer, Expatriate, Extracto, etc…) and 4 blocks from Kennedy School, which has a range of different bars and things to do including a spa, soaking pool and second run movie theater. PDX airport is a 15 minute drive away; 25 minutes will get you to the Gorge; and Hood River can be reached in an hour.<br /><br />http://www.portlandneighborhood.com/alberta-street.html','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b22b6e96-47cb-4f62-847d-d23e83071762.jpg',41290032,1,'45.56172','-122.63126',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,84.00,1,30,361,4.91,8630512),(430,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8687026','SE Woodstock 1 BR vintage 1930s updated apartment','This is a is charming and quiet comfortable 1 bedroom apartment that is autonomous and readily equipped for long term stays - including full kitchen (sans dishwasher) and washer/dryer. Often guests stay 6-12 months. It\'s just a few blocks from Woodstock’s commercial area, the best neighborhood in Portland! I accommodate short term stays, but there is no tax for stays 31 days or longer. I\'ve always had great, open, friendly relationships with our guests, making great new connections and friends.','This apartment is just a few blocks from the commercial center of Woodstock, with shops, bakery, restaurants, cafes, grocery stores, library, parks, and shops. It is also a 10 minute walk to Reed, and you can get there via Reed Woods.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/110212407/a72d5f9f_original.jpg',45613100,38,'45.4823','-122.62039',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,70.00,3,1125,82,4.82,8687026),(431,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8700497','2 bed/2 bath Contemporary Condo','Ideal location. 2 blocks to everything in Hillsdale Village. Privacy & peacefulness, AND easy commute to OHSU, Downtown Portland, Beaverton, PSU, & more! Spacious w/ covered private deck overlooking green space in well maintnd Hillsdale Village Cmplx nestled in private setting surrounded by trees&native plants. 1 Reserved Parking space. No pets/smoking, or loud guests.','Hillsdale /Multnomah Village at your fingertips. Walk Score 77 /Bike Score 69!! Blocks from Hillsdale Farmer\'s Market, shops, eateries, and library. One block to public bus transportation.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/38e0256e-2b47-4484-b27c-47852044bb6f.jpg',45394187,31,'45.47875','-122.70274',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,144.00,90,180,21,4.90,8700497),(432,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8703224','Bedroom in NoPo N. Mississippi Ave Home','Bedroom right in the middle of Mississippi neighborhood. Chill in living room or backyard, if you can peel yourself away from the tons of great restaurants, coffee shops, boutiques, & breweries nearby - Portland spirit! Public transit very close - both MAX & bus lines. About 10 min drive (and 20 min on bus) from Downtown hot spots like Powell\'s Books. Very close to other Williams, Interstate, Killingsworth and Alberta St. Ask about complimentary BikeTown usage for guests!','In the city that likes to “keep it weird,” Travel Portland has coined the phrase, \"You can, in Portland.\" North Portland is a prime example with delicious meals, tax-free shopping, one-of-a-kind bars and much more off the beaten path. Enjoy live music, tons of local shops, popular restaurants, breweries and great hang out spots on N. Mississippi Ave, one block from home. The many independent retailers of North Mississippi Avenue reflect Portland\'s eclectic tastes and DIY ethic. North Mississippi provides this vibrant neighborhood with ample watering holes and entertainment, one of the city\'s best concentrations of quality craft beers and brewpubs, and lots of yummy eateries.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8a9ce9ac-6c13-4051-b9c2-fae731b85f00.jpg',3220022,9,'45.54955','-122.67614',2,1,2.00,1.00,1.00,38.00,14,1125,37,4.81,8703224),(433,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8714815','NW Neighborhood Cabin in the City','Fully refinished inside, a light filled studio with loft.  Surrounded by coffee shops, library, restaurants and walking distance to street car stop.  Large open kitchen, deck over a garden, claw-foot tub,  woodstove and natural gas, cozy and sweet.  Reviews are 5 star for location, cleanliness, communication and overall experience.','Nw Nobb Hill','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4ffbceea-a190-40ad-817c-2f91351e6b87.jpg',6544470,27,'45.5362','-122.70008',1,3,1.00,1.00,4.00,140.00,3,1125,367,4.82,8714815),(434,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8740782','Modern spacious private studio overlooking bamboo','Safe and completely private, large studio with separate entrance, located in a peaceful rainforest location, with convenient access to all the city has to offer.<br /><br />We just installed all sorts of brand new features, including a modern A/C & Heater mini split with remote, a smart anti-fogging mirror, modern electric stove/oven, larger fridge, and new driveway and sidewalk entrance! <br /><br />Queen, full-sized, and twin beds with comfortable new mattresses. Full Bathroom with Shower, Wifi, Fireplace.','Our location offers great access to downtown Portland, while getting to escape the urban grime and spend the night in a beautifully forested environment more like Washington Park. Guests have said they feel like they are in a rain forest, perched up in the trees. The space is spacious, quiet, clean and private. Recommended nearby are Wine and Growl, Salvador Molly’s, McMenamins, and the Hillsdale food trucks. Hillsdale Farmers market is on Sundays until 1pm and the food trucks are open for lunch and most of the day. Dutch Bros coffee shop is a nice walk down the hill, across from the Albertsons grocery store. Wine and Growl has nighttime ambiance, a top notch chef for affordable prices, and a wide assortment of local wines and beers. After you arrive and are exploring Portland, you can try this new online tool to find other nearby attractions: <br /><br />https://www.travelportland.com/near-me-now/','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-8740782/original/68eba129-b5ea-4461-8c3a-8bbfc70c197f.jpg',45007538,70,'45.49008','-122.72925',1,5,1.00,1.00,3.00,84.00,1,27,402,4.82,8740782),(435,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8742729','Hawthorne Sauna Studio & Garden','Clean, beautiful, and private garden studio in the bustling Hawthorne neighborhood. Walk to restaurants, coffee, music venues, theaters, bars and food carts. We are located on a quiet street across from a city park. The studio has a private entrance, private sauna, kitchenette, comfortable queen bed, tile shower and wifi. Tons of free street parking!','Location! With virtually everything you might need within walking distance and the rest of the city easily accessible by bus, bike or Lyft, this area is thought of by many as the heart of Portland. Come stay and enjoy this cozy place while taking in the lively Hawthorne District.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b685572c-a27b-4430-ad60-a94708586639.jpg',45865050,8,'45.51036','-122.63466',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,82.00,2,21,746,4.90,8742729),(436,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8758093','Beautifully Restored SE PDX Duplex','Portland Duplex with 2 Bedrooms, 1 Bath in the close-in area of SE Portland.  Just a 20 minute walk to Downtown Portland and a short distance to all the desired restaurants & bars in Portland.<br /><br />Pets are negotiable but must be approved by owner prior to booking.','Located in the heart of the Belmont/Hawthorne district, a central, SE location of Portland.  <br /><br />You\'ll find it\'s just a 20-minute walk to downtown Portland and you are just minutes from some of the most desired restaurants & bars the city has to offer.  <br /><br />Colonel Summers park is 2 blocks away with paved walking paths, picnic areas, playground & basketball/tennis courts.    <br /><br />You\'ll find most of the amenities you could need right in the area.  Market of Choice is less than a mile away and New Seasons Market is just 1.5 miles away.<br /><br />Pets are negotiable but must be approved by owner prior to booking. There will be an additional monthly cleaning fee of $150 per month for guests with approved pets.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-8758093/original/4f661a1b-7e65-4418-ab07-54b54510baa8.jpeg',45926254,32,'45.51597','-122.64349',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,85.00,30,1125,39,4.87,8758093),(437,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8813922','Modern Guest House - Concordia','Wonderfully bright, spacious and modern guest house in the popular Concordia Neighborhood. Just one block from McMenamin\'s Kennedy School and a quick walk to New Seasons, Walgreen\'s, Extracto Coffee, 2 parks and lotsa other cool stuff.','The Concordia Neighborhood is home to one of Portland\'s finest gems: The Kennedy School. An elementary school converted into a marvelous mix of restaurants, pubs, movie theater and more, this well-preserved institution is a must-visit. <br /><br />Concordia is also home to Fernhill Park (5 blocks away) and Alberta Park (12 blocks), two large greenspaces you can lose yourself in. Figuratively speaking. Throw in an eclectic mix of outstanding restaurants, coffee houses and drinkeries--all within walking distance--and you\'ve got days of exploration awaiting you.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5839b9e5-7277-44b6-8934-2624c1a153b0.jpg',46173088,1,'45.56577','-122.62971',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,109.00,30,1125,96,5.00,8813922),(438,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8849753','Hattie\'s Cactus and Rose Garden','Serene and very beautiful park setting adds to the allure of this spacious one bedroom apartment.  Blocks from the freeway, close to bus lines, walking distance to the ever popular Mississippi Street, Williams Avenue and Alberta Arts district shops and activities, blocks from grocery store.','This is a very nice neighborhood in North Portland with numerous amenities including the Pennisula Park Rose Garden directly across the street, close access to a grocery store, close proximity to Mississippi Avenue with it\'s many splendid shops and activities.  Ten minutes from the Alberta Arts district.  Two bus lines within blocks of the apartment and five blocks away from the freeway.  Fifteen minutes from the airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e2195b44-78d8-4bba-9fea-5a5824c79104.jpg',46341450,24,'45.56598','-122.67273',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,105.00,30,1125,157,4.75,8849753),(439,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8863377','Modern Studio in Mt Tabor /Hawthorne area','Conveniently located close to Hawthorne restaurants, bars and shops yet nestled in a popular, quiet neighborhood/ street.  Just off the 52nd Ave bike path and a 5 minute walk up to Tabor. <br /><br />Enjoy a cocktail at Sapphire Hotel, tacos at Por Que No, or a walk around Mt Tabor Park. All are just a few blocks away.  If you prefer a night in, HBO, AmazonPrime, Netflix, Hulu/YouTuibe TV and Peacock all are available to you free of charge  <br /><br />Good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3ce4bed5-4623-479b-8d24-cf00efe50481.jpg',7810808,15,'45.5144','-122.60984',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,99.00,2,90,161,4.84,8863377),(440,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8956997','Urban retreat in historic Irvington','Fellow travelers, this is a newly constructed home on the border of Sabin/historic Irvington in NE Portland.   Conveniently located next to 3 bus lines and a quick bike ride or Uber to downtown, across the street from Whole Foods, a block from 2 coffee shops and close to dozens of restaurants.  Amazing, residential, safe walking or biking location!','Want to have coffee in the morning?  Starbucks and a local cafe are down the block.  Need breakfast or a quick meal?  Cross the street to Whole Foods.  Need to print something?  UPS store across the street.  Hungry for a meal?  There are literally dozens of restaurants and food trucks within less than a mile radius--we are close to the infamous N. Williams St as well as N. Mississippi avenue and also Broadway street and the Alberta arts district.  You can walk to any of these within 15 minutes.  Looking for a picnic or water park?  Irving city park is about half a mile.  Want to walk through a historic part of Portland and ogle beautiful houses?  Cross Fremont street a block away and you\'re in historic Irvington.<br />Bike or uber to downtown super fast too.  This is a very centrally located neighborhood with lots to do, but still with the family friendly Portland atmosphere and neighborhood feel.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7b8daf56-ad4f-4189-895c-81ab53e5bbb2.jpg',46814135,6,'45.54887','-122.65242',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,75.00,1,39,285,4.79,8956997),(441,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8974083','NE Alberta Area - Great Walking Area, with Parking','Amazing NE location, walking distance to some of the best food, coffee, and beer in Portland and a quick commute to downtown. Enjoy your longer stay with a fully stocked kitchen, private yard, 2 queen beds, and local art. You\'ll find coffee, tea, beer, wine, BBQ, Thai & Indian food, a bakery, conv. store, vegetable stand, and one of the best sushi restaurants in Portland within 1 block. And, you\'re only 3 blocks to Alberta St with tons of locally owned retail, music, art, and more restaurants!','The neighborhood is creative and lively with lots of great options to explore the Portland foodie scene. (Check out the guidebook and house manual for recommendations and their proximity to the house.)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/41ff97dd-2d64-48b7-b826-4bfcc689f09e.jpg',4609035,29,'45.5622','-122.64789',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,86.00,30,1125,74,4.69,8974083),(442,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8981600','Cute*Cozy*Clean NE Studio','Beautifully hand crafted lower level studio, just one block from the lovely Woodlawn neighborhood nook. A private entrance, organic mattress, down bedding, wood floors & vintage accents make this the perfect home base for your Portland adventures!','Woodlawn has a small center of business, mostly filled with delicious food options. We live just one block from this area which includes Woodlawn Pastry, Good Neighbor Pizza, Breakside Brewery, Firehouse Restaurant and more. Our neighborhood favorite is four blocks away, P\'s & Q\'s Market and Deli, serving delicious food and a small selection of groceries. Woodlawn Park is also just two blocks away, a great place for a walk or picnic.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9387c284-f6dd-43ea-9ed4-4cef9981ab48.jpg',7644885,45,'45.57044','-122.65609',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,65.00,2,1125,299,4.92,8981600),(443,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8982859','Tiny House, Big Charm','This cute and comfortable studio apartment used to be our detached double car garage! We worked tirelessly to curate the perfect Portland experience to compliment your vacation. With art and photography from NW artists, to locally sourced materials and treats, we are honored to host you during your trip.','Our favorite places are within 10 minute walk!<br />Rosoce\'s - 20 beers on tap, can order sushi from Miyamoto next door.<br />Hungry Heart - bakery, breakfast and lunch<br />Redwood - Amazing brunch<br />Observatory - upscale dinner with emphasis on local ingredients<br />Academy Theater - great local theater that offers pizza, beer, and wine. <br />Stark Street Pizza - over 50 years of making pizza, funky dark booth interior. <br />Ya Hala - Mediterranean amazingness. <br />Montavilla Brew Works - the brew master Michael is passionate about his beer and the community!<br /><br />Weekly Farmer\'s Market on Sundays through  May - September (10 min walk)<br /><br />Fred Meyer, Target, Winco within 1 mile. 7-11 two blocks away.<br /><br />Montavilla is a neighborhood in transition. Some of the homeless population that was pushed out of central Portland have found this neighborhood. It is very common to see tent camping within a few blocks of our location, and in most of Portland. We unders','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-8982859/original/b799e0d3-7c7a-4a9c-9e1b-87a52e2b5290.jpg',20410856,10,'45.52084','-122.56984',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,1,1125,596,4.98,8982859),(444,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/8989294','Portland House with Sunset View','This large view home is perfect for a family vacation or romantic getaway.  The home has a panoramic view over to the SW wine country and faces the setting sun.  You\'ll love enjoying a drink on the deck or the view from the hot tub. Close to Providence Hospital, Intel, Nike, or downtown Portland-- it\'s also a perfect location for traveling nurses or business trips. The home is fully stocked down to the wine bottle opener. The neighborhood is quiet with no traffic and close to hiking trails.','Panavista is a small neighborhood off Skyline Road that hugs the ridgeline above Forest Park. Close to hiking trails, downtown Portland or Beaverton, you will enjoy a quiet space with no traffic (street ends in a cul de sac). You will see nice neighbors strolling by with their kids or dogs. Very safe area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4fc0d084-eae3-4e17-9b89-077c58950155.jpg',44211105,50,'45.5423','-122.76146',1,5,2.50,3.00,0.00,0.00,30,32,3,5.00,8989294),(445,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9059118','The Jacobberger House Portland\'s Historic 5 star','Discover the abundance of old world charm and architecture in this beautifully restored Craftsman  home.  Built in 1904 by Joseph Jacobberger, this home is  perched on the hill with stunning city & mountain views.  This extra spacious 3500 sq foot 5 bed hillside paradise awaits you. GIGABIT WIFI with NETFLIX included.   A central location with easy access to beach, mountains, and wineries.  A great place to make memories with friends or family.  All rooms passed safety Inspection & B&B licensed.','I love the location. There is something special about waking up to the view of the Mountains. . Or hang out on the deck and watch the sun go down.<br />Or take an afternoon walk up the hill .','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/73dc65c7-87ba-4e0a-b901-7acb880db863.jpg',12846561,44,'45.50945','-122.68692',1,8,2.50,5.00,6.00,480.00,3,1100,117,4.96,9059118),(446,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9076254','Hawthorne Guest House - heated king bed','Romantic light-filled apartment in the heart of the Hawthorne/Belmont neighborhoods.  Enjoy vinyl records from your heated King size bed and shower in a sky-lit bathroom with a heated floor and a spacious stone tiled shower.  Located behind the host’s house, the guest house is a private space, separated by a fence and with its own entrance and private patio. A walkable neighborhood, there are so many nearby restaurants, bars, and stores in the Hawthorne, Belmont and Division neighborhoods.','Just step out the door for a bona fide Portland experience. Hawthorne features block after block of boutiques, vintage stores, cafes, restaurants, theaters, pubs, and Powell\'s Books store. There is a New Seasons Market for groceries three blocks away, and everything you could need is within walking distance.<br /><br />Mt. Tabor Park is  a great place to hike with breathtaking views of Mt. Hood and downtown Portland, and is just 20 blocks away. Only 10 blocks away is the stunning Laurelhurst Park, once named the most beautiful park on the west coast, and the first city park to be listed on the national register of historic places.  During the summer the park hosts many events - movies, theatre, and music performances.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/55399605-ae23-42f4-9c62-4e29927cb989.jpg',137869,16,'45.51593','-122.62146',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,1,1125,579,4.90,9076254),(447,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9115424','Charming St. John\'s Getaway','This is a room in a new three bedroom house in the charming St. John\'s neighborhood in North Portland.  The space has a Queen bed and is furnished.  There are both a private full bath and shared half bath available. I live here with my dog.  Looking for month-to-month renters- we can negotiate lengths of stays if you need something longer or shorter.   Great spot if you\'re in-between places or looking to move to Portland and need time to find a spot.  Who knows, maybe this will work out!','St. John\'s is awesome.  It\'s got it\'s own flavor, just like most other neighborhoods in Portland.  There is a great \'downtown\' strip with shops/restaurants/movie theater/coffee shops/bars.  The Farmer\'s market happens downtown on Saturdays, and there\'s a fun food cart/market space complete with beer garden that\'s open every day.  <br />There is also Pier Park, which has beautiful trails and a pretty great disc golf course.  Sometimes you can even catch them filming Grimm.  The park also has one of the best skate parks in Portland.  <br />Forest Park is an easy walk across the St. John\'s Bridge (an experience in itself), where hiking trails can go for as long as you\'d like.  Cathedral Park, under the bridge, is home to some very famously photographed spots, and a peaceful place to walk around, sit for awhile, or people-watch.  Kelly Point Park offers some great bike trails and water access to the Columbia River.  Sauvie Island is it\'s own little farmer paradise and Columbia River beach ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b761071a-7094-45b2-b75b-d9898129af0f.jpg',25200663,60,'45.58994','-122.73032',2,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,58.00,30,30,42,4.93,9115424),(448,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9118702','2BR Renovated Craftsman by Sellwood Park','1913 beautifully renovated craftsman in historic Sellwood neighborhood, 12 minutes from downtown.  100 yards from Sellwood park and wildlife preserve with nature trail & lake, public pool, and short walk to the river.  Sellwood neighborhood has many restaurants, pubs, coffee shops, grocery stores, vintage shops, golf course, as well as public transport (bus and train) and bike paths to downtown.  Enjoy an authentic Portland experience in this charming, walkable neighborhood near downtown.','Sellwood is an old neighborhood popular for its close proximity to downtown Portland.  It overlooks the Willamette river and has the oldest and some believe most beautiful park in Portland.  You can walk to many coffee shops, restaurants, pubs, and grocery stores.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6OTExODcwMg%3D%3D/original/cc2de9bb-3149-4dec-a838-846407cd9a25.jpeg',47514269,20,'45.4691047668457','-122.65819549560547',1,4,2.50,2.00,2.00,295.00,5,365,36,4.64,9118702),(449,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9119299','The Firebird','Artisan masterpiece created from reclaimed materials.  Inspiring design for the tiny house enthusiast.  Close to hip NE areas, easy access to downtown and PDX Airport.  Tucked away with covered outdoor area, fire pit and grill.  Super friendly hosts.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6037f38a-7ffc-4b07-9fbf-cea8e35c0d1f.jpg',47516888,21,'45.56056','-122.60258',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,30,1125,192,4.94,9119299),(450,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9119792','Bamboo Garden Apt, a quiet, cozy getaway','Just a 15 min walk to the Convention Ctr and a 10 min Lyft  or 30 min walk to downtown and the Pearl District, this is a new, light-filled 2 story separate apt with views of bamboo groves and organic gardens. Full kitchen, bathroom with shower, and AC. New hot tub ( shared with big house). Location is tops: close to all 4 quadrants of the city in a quiet, lovely, safe and historic neighborhood. Walk score is 87; bike score 99. MAX light rail, street car, bus are 5-10 min walk; no car needed.','The quiet, tree-lined historic Irvington neighborhood contains the largest collection of Queen Anne, Arts and Crafts, and Colonial Revival style homes in Oregon. You are close to downtown; it is only a 20 minute walk or a 5-10 minute walk to the MAX light rail, street car (line B to downtown, line A to points on the eastside like OMSI) or bus. I am just a 15 minute walk to the Convention Center as well. I provide walking and bike maps in the apt, as well as guide books to the city plus the Gorge, the Oregon Coast and Wine Country.  Other neighborhoods you can reach within a 20-30 minute walk or a 10 minute drive are:  Mississippi, Alberta, Hollywood, (all east side) and the Pearl District (west side.)   Be sure to check out our famous food carts; there are pods throughout the city and many even have tents with heaters and fire pits.  The closest Farmer\'s Market happens on Sunday 10-2 at NE 7th and Wygant, open May-Nov. The biggest, busiest Farmer\'s Market is downtown by Portland State ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f25250ca-2552-44f3-adae-8fcbca3464b8.jpg',263312,7,'45.53586','-122.65583',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,103.00,2,1125,492,4.88,9119792),(451,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9131283','Alberta St. Modern Craftsman','Uniquely updated 1922 craftsman style house with 1500 square feet with 2 bedrooms, 1 bath, extra attic room and a sun porch. The living/dining/kitchen/sun porch are interconnected via the open floor plan. House is centrally located near 4 separate business districts (Mississippi Ave, Williams Ave, N. Killingsworth St. and Alberta St.)<br /><br />Please Note: You MUST make the reservation request for an accurate number of guests...there are added guest fees when more than 2 guests are staying.','The Humbolt neighborhood is situated between the NE Alberta Arts, North Williams St. and  Mississippi St. districts.  There are 3 nearby convenience/small markets but the Cherry Sprout on N. Albina is the best.  \"The Red Fox\" , \"Chapel Pub\" or \"Victoria\" are the closest Bar/Restaurants.  Many options for delicious food/drink within a 5-15 min walk...you can easily quadruple your options within a 10 min bike ride.  Lots of bike lanes throughout the neighborhood to ease your exploration on two wheels. There is shopping aplenty on Mississippi Ave, Williams Ave and Alberta St  if you want something cool to take home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/521ea734-4f21-4c52-a2c7-c4b98a50bce4.jpg',40548274,24,'45.55828','-122.66917',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,107.00,1,20,1143,4.90,9131283),(452,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9131630','Enchanted Loft in the Absolute  Center','This is a unique opportunity to be at the literal center of the Pearl District, directly across the street from everything!','This is a unique opportunity to live at the literal center of the Pearl District, directly across the street from what is considered to be the best coffee shop (Barista), best Yoga (Yoyoyogi), 13 restaurants within a block, Whole Foods, shopping, freeway access, bars etc etc are truthfully out your door...(it get\'s a 99 out of 100 on walkability using websites that measure this sort of thing).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6OTEzMTYzMA%3D%3D/original/9c9ad5a7-65d9-4365-978a-694c63fa4640.jpeg',10255733,2,'45.52611','-122.68353',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,174.00,30,275,10,5.00,9131630),(453,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9153419','Beaumont Village Private Hideaway','A 1-bedroom permitted basement unit is in our 1920s bungalow. We are located in a quiet and beautiful neighborhood in NE (Beaumont) Portland, only a couple blocks from Fremont Street\'s restaurants, shops, fitness studios, and local market. Feel free to use the sideyard through the gate opposite your front door for a breath of fresh air, drinks, and meals until 10 PM.','We are centrally located and in one of Portland\'s vibrant, close-in residential neighborhoods with beautiful tree lined streets. Only 10 minute drive from downtown, 5 minute car ride from the Alberta Arts district and Hollywood district. Street parking in front of the house is available and free.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-9153419/original/d919ff07-343e-43b1-b6f5-213d86aec00b.jpg',35075353,11,'45.54457','-122.61415',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,94.00,2,29,189,4.95,9153419),(454,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9154349','City/Mtn Views, Parking, and 24-hr Concierge','(Note that pricing is variable based on dates but we can adjust). <br /><br />Beautiful high rise condo with east facing City and mountain views and all luxury amenities including 24-hour concierge and secure underground parking. Desirable location and walk score >98 with Washington Park, restaurants, Timbers, and downtown all nearby!<br /><br />Minimum 3-month rental desired (1-month possible) and max of 12-months. Murphy bed in living room for guests but otherwise unfurnished (furnished photos for example only).','Close to (as in walking distance!) Timbers/Thorns soccer stadium, Crystal Ballroom, Oregon Symphony, Washington Park, bars, eateries, and nightlife!<br /><br />Washington Park includes hundreds of acres of trails and forest areas, Japanese Garden, International Rose Test Garden, Oregon Zoo…<br /><br />1 hour from Mt. Hood and 1 hour from the Pacific Ocean!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d273e595-f259-4f5d-bc77-15b84b3778b9.jpg',47656356,3,'45.52291','-122.69153',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,92.00,31,365,0,1.00,9154349),(455,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9171996','Modern, walkable, Kerns apartment','We hand built this beautiful basement apartment in our 1908 home featuring exposed beams and reclaimed wood throughout. It includes a full kitchen, large bathroom and a cozy outdoor nook.  Walking distance to bars, restaurants, transit and more!','The Kerns is a small neighborhood close to downtown that best know for its old style Portland homes and \"restaurant row\" on NE 28th Avenue.  In addition to eclectic restaurants there are also locally own shops, food carts and bars nearby. Check out Yelp for a listing of all the great restaurants in Kerns. <br /><br />If you like cinema, the historic Laurelhurst and Hollywood movie theaters (which serve pizza and beer!) are both walking distance from the house.<br /><br />The famously beautiful Laurelhurst Park is just a 10 minute walk from the apartment. There you will find a great soft surface running trail, a pond filled with ducks, huge trees and many places to relax or picnic. Though much smaller, Oregon Park is just a minute walk from the apartment and includes a large open field, play ground and basketball courts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/62ea0a10-1ca2-4757-8476-c1a1ba3950f4.jpg',47731731,12,'45.52774','-122.63541',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,59.00,30,90,265,4.75,9171996),(456,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9200540','NEW:Top 2 levels twnhse2 Bdr-2.5 bth by OHSU/River','Relax with the whole family at this peaceful, centrally located townhouse by OHSU, Willamette River, and all major freeways.   The townhouse is 3 levels but we are only renting top 2 levels that include 2 bedrooms, full kitchen, living room.  First floor has a mother in law studio with its own separate entrance - this is not part of the rental but houses another guest. Modern offers 2-bedroom suites all with en-suite bathrooms.   A great place to stay, and call home during your stay in Portland.','Great neighborhood- close to Willamette River, good restaurants and OHSU. Close to major freeways.   Quiet residential area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d56ecfae-3533-4668-b135-f875a1169591.jpg',30549717,22,'45.48688','-122.67778',2,2,2.50,1.00,1.00,83.00,31,365,1,5.00,9200540),(457,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9216829','Stylish house, Mississippi Neighborhood','Fully renovated craftsman with all the modern touches including a private fenced yard for pets, BBQ, and garden. 3 bedroom home in the Mississippi District, in the heart of Portland with craft breweries, funky shops, restaurants, Art, wine shops, food carts & more! 5 minutes from downtown Portland & the Pearl. 3 blocks from the max and bus stops. There is a $200 cleaning fee for pets. There is a separate basement unit where another guest lives. They have their own entrance and separate patio.','The house is 2 blocks from one of the most popular and famous streets in Portland. Mississippi Ave. is filled with bars, restaurants and shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-9216829/original/67b75fde-461f-45c3-a524-2801d80c24b8.jpeg',6063183,24,'45.55583','-122.67533',1,4,1.00,3.00,3.00,114.00,31,365,143,4.83,9216829),(458,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9232236','Private and Cozy Two Bedroom Suite Walk to Reed','My place is close to Max Orange Line and 3 bus lines. Two blocks from bike lanes. Trader Joes is a 5 minute walk. Reed College is 6 blocks. Woodstock District is a 15 minute walk. The space is homey, clean and comfortable on the second floor. Its private and both bedroom doors lock. My house is peaceful and relaxing. My dogs love to meet my guests but are always kept in my space exclusively when guests are staying. I am always available 24 hrs a day either in person or by text or phone.','You can walk to most services from my home. Trader Joe\'s is 3 blocks away. I do a lot of walking in my neighborhood and Reed Canyon trail is a favorite just a few blocks from my home. The trail goes around a lake and up onto the beautiful Reed campus. Take my street up to Steel (south). Take a right at the light. Walk down to 37th St and cross over Steel. Head down the hill and you will see the trail on your right. You can also take the trail to Crystal Springs Rhodedendron gardens located on the West side of Reed campus. The gardens are free on Monday and other days 5.00/person. The Woodstock neighborhood on Woodstock Blvd has multiple excellent restaurants/coffee shops and two grocery stores. Grand Central bakery is a favorite!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/46a79847-6f35-485f-bfb4-78fd8bdca8d9.jpg',41571405,38,'45.48526','-122.6217',2,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,57,4.95,9232236),(459,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9236071','Fortune 503 - UofP Perfect Stay','Fortune Haus apartment home is tucked away in a friendly St. John\'s community neighborhood near the University of Portland. Above our detached garage, our space gives you a feeling of home while allowing quiet and privacy.  Due to Covid-19, we are taking extra steps to clean and sanitize frequently touched surfaces between reservations. We look forward to hosting you!','We love Portsmouth/St. John\'s! The community of people are very friendly and we are within walking distance to many shops and restaurants. Even though we are a bit north of Downtown Portland, we get to drive over the beautiful St John\'s Bridge to get there (takes about 20-25 minutes to get to downtown depending on time of day and where you are going). We are only about a mile away from the University of Portland, and less than a mile to downtown St. John\'s, where you can find cute shops, coffee, 2 theaters, many restaurants, food carts, and get to Cathedral Park (a favorite). A bit further up is Pier Park, where you can walk among tall trees and even play disc golf.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/195a9c8b-d908-44a9-b6e0-178162a2f5a2.jpg',10088347,60,'45.58832','-122.72944',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,68.00,1,1125,510,4.91,9236071),(460,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9254568','Charming Craftsman in the heart of Arbor Lodge','This house is located within walking distance of Adidas, University of Portland and 5 minutes to Daimler HQ and Vigor Shipyard. Only 10 minutes to downtown.    Fully fenced yard and close proximity to scenic Willamette Street which has great sunsets and scenic views.','I love this neighborhood! It is one of the reasons I decided to invest and build a second house. It is convenient to all of Portland via car and has above average connections via transit. <br /> <br />The house is located between the Overlook and Arbor Lodge Neighborhoods (technically Arbor Lodge, but Overlook neighborhood is two houses down). <br />What I love about this neighborhood? I could go on forever, but here is a good list:<br />1). Scenic walks or runs are just around the corner on the quietest park of Willamette Blvd. See sunsets, city lights, views of the marine terminals, and Forest Park.<br /><br />2). Location:  Relatively close to transit, 10 to 15 minutes to downtown,  plenty of restaurants are within walking distance, Adidas is five minute walk and University of Portland about ten. New Seasons, and Fred Meyers is close by for grocery shopping. <br /><br />3). Food and Brews: Portland is well known for its great food and brewery culture. The house is close to many good','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-9254568/original/33c797b3-a8bc-4c9e-8bb6-5f6c716b8fc9.jpeg',43717096,13,'45.56616','-122.69773',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,145.00,3,1125,259,4.84,9254568),(461,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9272043','Stumptown Cottage in Eastmoreland','Newly built modern studio space in our beautiful historic Eastmoreland neighborhood. Loft like space with modern amenities in a quiet setting. Close to Reed College, Woodstock, Division and Sellwood-Moreland neighborhoods. Easily accessible via public transit.<br /><br />Due to the coronavirus, we’re taking extra care to disinfect frequently touched surfaces between reservations.','We live in one of the oldest neighborhoods in Portland and it is one of the most beautiful with 100 year old trees and homes. Easily one of the most scenic neighborhoods to walk in.  We are located 3 blocks from the Springwater Corridor, a bike/run path that will take you West to ride around our downtown area. This is a must if you are a cyclist and a great way to view our city from two wheels.<br />We are adjacent to the Woodstock neighborhood which has lots of shopping, restaurants and a local library. We are also adjacent to the Sellwood and Westmoreland neighborhoods, which have boutique and grocery shopping, restaurants,  antique stores, etc. Both neighborhoods are a 20 min walk or 5 min drive from our home.<br />We will provide you with lists of restaurants, our favorite Farmer\'s Markets, supermarkets, including our favorite local New Seasons market that just opened in the Woodstock neighborhood, just a 5 min drive or 20 min walk. Think natural, organic, with a bakery, deli, rame','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-9272043/original/3ab9aaa8-a777-424c-8727-4b1cafdcf8b7.jpg',28235833,5,'45.46622','-122.62567',1,3,1.00,0.00,4.00,85.00,3,365,293,4.94,9272043),(462,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9276925','Lovely FURNISHED riverfront condo','Waterfront Pearl condo Portland - Totally decorator FURNISHED, 2 br/2bath-(1 King suite, 1 Queen suite) awesome river view, best neighborhood, walk downtown, 1 reserved garage pkg space. Huge selection near restaurants, shopping, river walk.','Waterfront Pearl located on Willamite river at foot of Pearl District the cities most vibrant neighborhood, walk to financial/downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/418c1e4c-8f82-4a1e-9372-00c41f218e09.jpg',31927943,2,'45.53338','-122.68003',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,167.00,90,1125,1,5.00,9276925),(463,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9296543','Beach themed cozy retreat.','Very hip neighborhood village just a few blocks away.<br />Good eateries within walking distance into village, also two markets, library, bottle shoppe,<br />delis, coupla coffee shoppes, yes, the astral male deer one, too..<br />Cool mix of ages and whatever.<br />The name is Woodstock, for heavens sake!  But grown, evolved.','My Woodstock neighborhood is very hip, vibrant and charming.  Al fresco dining and handmade ice cream<br />Two grocery stores, one is New Seasons, two bakeries,fresh fish mkt. with fish and chips take out. <br />Sunday farmer\'s market. <br />Explore, you\'ll find more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f91d923c-31ce-452e-a8eb-6eee12849157.jpg',22412761,38,'45.47654','-122.60972',2,1,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,18,4.17,9296543),(464,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9319598','Cool apartment in middle of it all','Centrally located apartment off trendy 21st ave in NW Portland. Steps from great local bars and restaurants. Short walk to the Pearl District and forest park.  <br /><br />This building is old but well built. Perfect for a couple or three friends.  Plenty of space, with a cozy feel!','This is easily one of the best neighborhoods in Portland. It\'s a block off NW 23rd with great shopping and restaurants. It\'s a few minute walk from trendy Pearl District. Forrest park is also right down the street. Feel free to ask for ideas for places to go or things to do.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2b453378-980d-4926-84d4-1e24a7a579c3.jpg',48026802,27,'45.52346','-122.69341',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,500.00,30,1125,344,4.65,9319598),(465,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9350743','Laurelhurst Gem! Lovely bright 2 bedroom home','Plant Lovin\' - Our very bright - south facing living and dining room windows - and warm place offers comfort, including a spacious backyard with deck and outdoor seating. It is located in a quiet, residential area near Laurelhurst Park, Whole Foods, plenty of bars and restaurants.','Everything you need in walking distance: parks, Whole Foods, bars, restaurants, movie theater.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7f3debd0-83ce-4fe5-a392-a07d52c7219a.jpg',10928596,12,'45.52638','-122.63214',1,3,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,31,31,1,5.00,9350743),(466,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9365410','Harmony House','Featured on the Portland Build Small Live Large ADU Tour, the guest house has full kitchen, washer/dryer, parking space, high ceilings, queen beds and lots of high windows giving lovely natural light.','This home is located 15 Minutes from the PDX Airport in an eastside residential neighborhood about 30 minutes from downtown, and one hour from Mt. Hood. A short distance away is a community walking trail at the Glendoveer Golf Course.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8db8873d-d1ac-424c-8a2d-7f4e4994a173.jpg',48595009,71,'45.52815','-122.50139',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,141.00,3,365,381,4.86,9365410),(467,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9369142','Private Studio with Kitchenette','Conveniently located (airport, biking, walking, bus, MAX, Hollywood, Beaumont Village, restaurants, coffee shops), charmingly decorated, beautiful garden to enjoy. A private entrance to your studio bedroom with kitchenette and keyed entry.','We are located two blocks from Beaumont Village and an easy walk to the Hollywood Theater, 24 HR Fitness, yoga, stores and restaurants and of course Starbucks. Sweet shoppes for browsing are all along Fremont Street with many fun eateries in between.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-9369142/original/ce771f6f-f3d8-458d-a7ae-0c7d680d4e1e.jpg',40829795,11,'45.54452','-122.61446',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,76.00,1,1125,110,4.85,9369142),(468,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9384461','Cozy Tiny House in SE Portland','Modern and private guest apartment! This beautiful studio space works great for one or two in the popular SE Division neighborhood of Portland. Bright, airy, and modern this micro-apartment boasts smart use of a Murphy Bed,  workspace, and options for dining al fresco. Walking distance to many of PDX\'s best restaurants.','This charming studio is in the heart of a Classic SE Portland Neighborhood, with everything you need only a short walk or bike ride away.  New Season\'s Market, People\'s Organic Coop, coffee shops, and our beloved food carts pods all about 10-15 minutes walking.  Additionally, just a stone throw away from nationally recognized dining (Ava Gene\'s, Salt & Straw, Stumptown, & more!). (See our guest book!)      <br /><br />The house and studio itself is in an exciting mixed use residential urban neighborhood with narrow streets, large trees, sidewalks, single family houses, apartments and schools.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-9384461/original/1be2cd6b-3140-4895-bb54-7b8140b8775d.jpeg',20414851,25,'45.50534','-122.64086',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,75.00,30,31,338,4.89,9384461),(469,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9475332','Light and Bright, Cozy Woodstock Cottage','This beautiful 1bd, 1ba house is spacious and bright. It\'s in a quiet neighborhood, just a short walk to  restaurants, coffee shops, farmer\'s market and gourmet grocery stores. Close to Reed College and several parks. It\'s also only 2 blocks from 2 bus lines, which makes getting around town a breeze. We are very family friendly and happy to help answer any questions,  or give recommendations in order to ensure you enjoy your stay!','The Woodstock neighborhood is a vibrant, family friendly area. Our house is just a short walk to numerous restaurants, coffee shops, parks, bars, breweries, the farmer\'s market in the summer, as well as New Seasons Market and Safeway. We are also close to Reed College,  and a short drive to Sellwood, downtown and the rest of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1cce1b50-3072-4085-9862-baffec5fd31e.jpg',49110034,38,'45.480094252636086','-122.6041601847713',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,125.00,2,29,193,4.89,9475332),(470,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9506971','Designer Alberta Bungalo-Walk to Everything!','The house is a 1900 redone bungalow with newer furniture. Designer touches throughout. You get the whole main floor of the house (minus 1 vacant room), not an apartment, and no other guests.<br /><br />Super comfy power leather recliner in living room to enjoy the 4K curved TV.<br /><br />The bedroom has a Queen Westin Heavenly Bed, windows on 2 sides,  new curtains, and plenty of storage. The bedroom is my guest room that i rent when im away.<br /><br />Note, no recent reviews cause i haven\'t been AirBnB\'ing for a while.','If you are coming to Portland you have likely heard of Alberta St. The house is about a 10 minute walk to Alberta, which is a plus in that its not as busy and loud on the house\'s street. Alberta has everything from multiple bars to live music every night, Salt and Straw Ice Cream, cool boutiques, all the best of Portland in a non pretentious area.<br /><br />Vancouver/Williams Street is has newer buildings and is only about 10 minutes away too. I like the Shine restaurant with a rooftop patio there.<br /><br />As mentioned, from May to November there is a Farmers Market on Sundays directly across the street!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/70943cac-0b62-4676-9ff1-d7778fb5b916.jpg',1886383,14,'45.55672','-122.65743',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,30,25,4.92,9506971),(471,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9543693','Inner NE  Private Apt 1BR','Amazing location in Inner NE Portland.  Private space and entry in charming and remodeled 1920s craftsman.  Everything you need for a comfortable stay.  Walkable neighborhood close to everything.  Less than a mile to Alberta arts, Williams-Vancouver, Mississippi, farmers market less than three miles to downtown ,15 minutes to airport.','The Sabin neighborhood is diverse and lively.  There are many restaurants, bars, independent shops, natural food markets, a weekend farmers market and parks all within walking distance to the apartment.  Williams, Alberta Arts, Mississippi, Rose Quarter all within a mile.  Walk or bike to anything to make your stay memorable.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6ca4b2fa-991c-4ddd-b604-a73355b191ef.jpg',49426376,14,'45.54908','-122.6616',1,6,1.00,1.00,4.00,89.00,30,1125,349,4.63,9543693),(472,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9551967','Newer Home in SW Portland!','Built in 2015, this detached home is in close-in SW Portland.  Scenic location on a quiet neighborhood street next to a park.  Walk to Multnomah Village or Hillsdale neighborhood centers, with coffee shops, bookstores, breweries, and bakeries.  Minutes to downtown or OHSU.  Queen in master.  Full bed in 2nd bedroom.  Sofa converts to full bed.  Furnished.  Perfect for a family.','This new home sits right above a park (grass fields, ball fields, playground, etc.).  The private deck and living room enjoy views of the park. The restaurants and shops of Hillsdale and Multnomah Village are about a 10-minute walk from the home.  Nearby neighbors are very friendly and quiet.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7710d858-455d-409f-b1a9-75f16e931732.jpg',47141750,18,'45.47136','-122.70207',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,120,130,4.92,9551967),(473,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9578248','Little House near Alberta Arts','New little house!  Beautiful high exposed wood ceilings, fully equipped kitchen. Quiet, cozy and private. Few blocks to a hub of restaurants, Kennedy school, Alberta Arts Districts, New Seasons and the amazing Extracto Coffee. Pets very welcome!','Quiet but close to lots of stuff. Restaurants (Beast, Expatriate, Nono\'s, Doc, Athentica, Extracto), close to downtown Portland. Kennedy School hot tub and brewery 2 blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-9578248/original/014e2dc1-f82b-4aa0-83c3-f40242120fc5.jpg',25235410,1,'45.56392','-122.63373',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,2,730,630,4.96,9578248),(474,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9632943','Fashionable Flat Close-In East Side','Fashionable city flat in Portland\'s close-in east side Laurelhurst Neighborhood.  Walkscore of 82, blocks to Whole Foods, Bamboo Sushi, Navarre Wine Bar, Tapalaya, and many of Portland\'s best restaurants.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6d9dc66c-00b3-40c9-986a-2924c87a2fb5.jpg',46497916,12,'45.52316','-122.63194',1,6,1.00,2.00,3.00,99.00,30,240,120,4.78,9632943),(475,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9729366','Private Garden Room with Bath. No cleaning fees.','Accessible, quiet, and modern space with a beautiful back yard, bedroom, and guest-use only bathroom. No cleaning fees. We are both vaccinated. For Covid-vaccinated guests only, we are now sharing our kitchen and living room. You will still have a mini-fridge, tea and coffee station in your room. We are a Canadian/Hungarian couple and a border collie/lab mix pup who are your guides to outdoor adventure and Portland sightseeing. See you soon!','We are just north of Sellwood (about a mile walk), which has an abundance of cute shops, restaurants, and yoga studios, and is highly walkable. Also, it is three minutes from the Oaks Bottom bike path, and at the South end of the Brooklyn Neighborhood. It is easy to access main roads, or the tranquil park by the Willamette River.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-9729366/original/276dc2e8-54b8-48aa-b548-d9f3549bc09d.jpeg',15310395,56,'45.4882','-122.65021',2,3,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,2,20,221,4.93,9729366),(476,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9732892','Quiet, convenient & comfortable!','Whether in town for work or pleasure, this townhome sits perfectly between downtown and the Nike/Intel corridor in a quiet gated neighborhood of working professionals.  Walking distance to Sylvan Starbucks & restaurants, MAX and the hwy 26 bike path.','Super quiet, GREAT location!  Backs up to greenspace but is also just a few blocks to HWY 26.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8d2117cb-a696-43d8-b39a-cbb336ecf69f.jpg',22298379,62,'45.51168','-122.73592',1,4,2.50,2.00,3.00,345.00,7,1125,59,4.92,9732892),(477,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9736647','Sunnyside Sanctuary_Belmont/Hawthorne/Laurelhurst','Lovely comfortable home just 1/2 a block from Laurelhurst park & walking distance to bus lines, restaurants, markets, coffee shops, Belmont, Stark, Hawthorne, 28th, & 10 mins from downtown. Fully equipped with all you could need including a spa!','We\'re in the SE Sunnyside neighborhood, which is central to Portland\'s  Hawthorne, Belmont & 28th/Burnside districts. With this proximity comes endless dining, shopping, drinking, and site seeing as well as being close to two of Portland\'s best parks - 1 block from Laurelhurst & a 10 minute bike or car ride to Mt. Tabor. Grocery stores New Seasons and Fred Meyer are all minutes away. Its a very walkable neighborhood & location and super bike friendly.  We have a couple of bikes you could borrow if we plan ahead of time and we\'ll include our favorite bike shops where you can rent bikes if you\'d like.<br /><br />A few local favorites: PaaDee/Laangbaan (Thai restaurant), Laurelhurst Theater, (on 28th) Porque No (tacos+), Blue Goose (Southwestern food), Powell\'s Books, Fried egg I\'m in Love (food cart on Hawthorne), Tao of Tea (tea shop), the Liquor store (bar/restaurant), Circa 33 (bar/restaurant) the Sweet Hereafter (bar & restaurant), Dick\'s Kitchen (Organic Burgers+) (on Belmont). Ther','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e368ed01-136d-49ea-bf32-46df8b1df91f.jpg',33451922,16,'45.51795','-122.62498',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,300.00,30,1125,6,5.00,9736647),(478,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9759612','Room/ B_Green','Large room, 1 of 2 bdrms with a shared separate living room, kitchen & bath room clothes washer/dryer in a quiet neighborhood, near natural areas.  Located 20 minutes from Airport, walking distance from MAX train and bus station , 420 friendly.<br />Pets are allowed $10 a night per pet no more than 2 please make a additional pets fees to Airbnb .','Close to lots of shopping, local shops and Clackamas Towncenter Mall, Cartlandia (food carts). The Springwater bike trail is at the end of the cul-de-sac, many recreational, scenic and music activities nearby.  Less than 3 minutes to Freeway I205.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/92775477-90bc-4e4a-b6a0-8e306be37f67.jpg',50332020,72,'45.4702','-122.57291',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,35.00,30,270,132,4.62,9759612),(479,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9760306','Room/A_Green','very Large bedroom with walk in closet, 1 of 2 bdrms in private bsmt apt, in a quiet   neighborhood with a queen bed we have computer desk in the room. Furnished kitchen, clothes washer/dryer. Bathroom and TV and we are 420 friendly.  No pets allowed in this room,  other bedroom room B  ok.<br />We are at 3 blocks from the Bus,and Train ( Max) stations.','Quiet neighborhood where most houses have children and know each other.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8599423f-3875-4d76-8117-86a8867c9280.jpg',50332020,72,'45.46906','-122.57273',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,40.00,30,270,108,4.55,9760306),(480,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9770224','Modern, NEW Home in HOT Spot. CLOSE 2 Everything!','FUN GETAWAY FOR FAMILY, FRIENDS OR COUPLES IN CENTRAL LOCATION!!!<br /><br />Beautiful, boutique home with high-end finishings, designed for entertaining. BBQ, shuffleboard, arcade & boardgames.<br /><br />CLOSE TO EVERYTHING! 1 mile from the popular Alberta District with incredible restaurants, art galleries, shopping, and nightlife. Close to Mississippi St. (1.5 miles) and Downtown (3 miles). Easy access to grocery stores, bike rentals, Moda Center, and the Airport.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-9770224/original/cb9c0c86-a254-4fa9-abab-8b3b1c7b7135.jpg',7858592,14,'45.56107','-122.65886',1,7,2.50,3.00,5.00,223.00,2,1120,406,4.96,9770224),(481,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9812111','10 min to NW, downtown, private-suite w gardens','Beautiful 1000-sq. foot downstairs suite has huge windows you\'ll look out to our manicured lawn and garden beds.  <br />We\'re currently offering a 3-night minimum and a 10% Weekly & 20% Monthly Discount.  <br />Remote workers will love the two large desks, Aeron chairs, and fast WiFi.  <br />The suite is beautifully appointed with wall-to-wall wool carpeting and artwork. The kitchenette is well-appointed with appliances.  Separate bedroom and bathroom.  <br />This location is serene and quiet, if you need to rest.','Hillsdale is one of the top neighborhoods in SW Portland. We\'re 10 min from OHSU and 15 min from downtown Portland.  Hillsdale has its own shopping area 5 minutes away with a fabulous bakery, Starbucks, restaurants, Basics grocery store, gas station and library.  If you have a car - it\'s just 15 minutes over the hill to downtown Portland, the  NW shopping district and the Pearl District.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-9812111/original/9869253d-19be-4f9f-9745-a1d5c2468e77.jpg',13676520,31,'45.49118','-122.70607',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,115.00,3,90,189,4.97,9812111),(482,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9825819','Sunny  Mt Tabor 1 BR Suite. Walk to HIP Montavilla','★ ★ CORONAVIRUS UPDATE:  This is a PRIVATE entire apartment, and it is THOROUGHLY CLEANED AND STERILIZED before each booking, based on the latest guidelines for cleaning and disinfecting from Airbnb.  Additionally, we block out at LEAST one full day between each booking, just to make sure it is TOTALLY germ-free.   We\'re just starting listing again, so we DRASTICALLY slashed the price!   This NEWLY BUILT private entrance, street level apartment is in the heart of SE PDX!','When visiting Portland, where you stay is critical.  You want to have easy access to everything.  We have that here.  The neighborhood is Mt. Tabor, you can look it up online and see why it\'s such a great place to be.  We are literally surrounded with great food and pubs.  Two James Beard Nominated restaurants are within walking distance!  Walk 5 minutes to the Coquine Cafe, or 10 minutes to the Montavilla pub area with restaurants, pubs, dive bars, a cocktail lounge, a brewery, coffee and tea houses, the best Pizza in town, vintage stores, and a theater where you can have Pizza and Beer while you watch a current movie for $4!!  Walk 5 minutes to SE 82nd Ave (the Jade District), which has some of the most authentic Asian food in the city.  Walk to the other side of the park and you end up on Division St.(one of the 10 hottest food streets in the country), or Hawthorne Blvd (TONS of different ethnic and pricing options).   Portland is not called \"Beervana\" for nothing, it has more brewp','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6OTgyNTgxOQ%3D%3D/original/70f45a86-9924-4236-88ee-61f10a4f2591.jpeg',27071792,15,'45.51206','-122.58882',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,88.00,1,90,282,4.90,9825819),(483,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9842582','Historic Laurelhurst Residence Extended Stay','1 to 6 month stay in historic twin palm Laurelhurst residence – Fully furnished, recently interior remodeled with new flooring and bathrooms, 4000 sq feet, 4 bedroom 3.5 bathrooms + office (or 3 bedrooms + 2 offices), basement w/ entertainment center.  Gorgeous, spacious chef\'s kitchen.  Large sundeck with outdoor furniture.  Pets allowed and backyard is full fenced!<br /><br />Home overlooks Laurelhurst park with historic charm and modern amenities.','Great family-friendly neighborhood with excellent school district. Beautiful Laurel Hearst park is around the block. Few business districts are in a walking distance. Whole Foods market are few blocks away with 28th street restaurant row.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9514b112-3337-4aea-9a32-8efb4b9d9db7.jpg',2409849,12,'45.52203','-122.63231',1,8,3.50,4.00,4.00,166.00,30,180,21,4.95,9842582),(484,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9887235','Tranquil/Bright 2 Bedroom, home in NE Portland','Very Quiet, tranquil home in NEPO (Northeast Portland). Close to the Alberta Arts neighborhood and many restaurants on NE 42nd Ave, one block away. Great pizza, pubs, cafe, bakery and Mexican food within a couple blocks. You can walk to easy, delicious meals or have UBER deliver with ease.. You’ll love my place because of the outdoors space, the neighborhood, the light, the comfy bed, and the kitchen. My place is good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.','A great quiet neighborhood with great places to eat and to enjoy yourself.<br />Great food, and only 1/2 block from the bike path downtown. Lots of great resources and I may have a bike that will just fit you.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-9887235/original/44ba613c-c03f-4ebc-a4e3-e714ef876c27.jpeg',50860253,21,'45.55861','-122.61386',1,3,1.50,2.00,2.00,115.00,30,1125,34,4.53,9887235),(485,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9899175','2BR/1BA: Amazing location! Available monthly','Private, main-floor apartment has 2 bedrooms with queen bed in each. Queen Aerobed available upon request. Full bathroom with tub and shower. Eat-in kitchen. Private back deck + shared porch and back patio.  One parking space included.  Laundry in basement. Month to Month.  30-day minimum.','The neighborhood goes by many names - Northwest District, Nob Hill, Alphabet District are a few. But whatever you call it, you\'ll find the best of everything Portland has to offer right here!<br /><br />Within 3 blocks:<br />- NW 23rd Ave (restaurants, shops, ice cream)<br />- NW 21st Ave (bars & nightlife)<br />- Trader Joe\'s grocery store<br />- Plaid Pantry convenience store<br />- Street Car & Bus Stops (easy transfer to Max to/from Portland International Airport)<br /><br />Short walk to:<br />- Timber\'s Stadium (Providence Park)<br />- Providence Park Max Station<br />- Fred Meyer, Zupan\'s, Walgreens, Starbucks<br />- Parks, playgrounds, basketball courts & more<br />- Forest Park (5,000 acre urban forest with hiking & biking trails)<br /><br />\"City Hike\" or 5-Minute Transit to:<br />- Pearl District, Old Town, Downtown<br />- Saturday/Sunday Market, Waterfront<br />- Washington Park/Rose Garden<br />- Oregon Zoo, Children\'s Museum, World Forestry Center','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7ff24eee-7a73-42ef-9e48-c589620d62b6.jpg',20727837,27,'45.52635','-122.69735',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,175.00,31,365,104,4.88,9899175),(486,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9904327','Great Home in Lake Oswego','This unique place has a style all its own. Come and enjoy the best that Portland has to offer, in the most fashionable neighborhood in the city. Close to downtown Portland and yet you can feel the small town atmosphere of Lake Oswego. It is also close to all the natural attractions Oregón has to offer: the Columbia Gorge; the beautiful Oregón coast and the vineyards along the Willamette valley. This house has all the comforts of modern life even a pickle ball court and a basketball hoop.','Located on the northern edge of Lake Oswego, this wooded refuge is nestled cozily into the southern portion of the Western Hills and provides easy access to Portland without any of the noisy urban density.<br /><br />Outdoor lovers will instantly fall in love with the large parks in this area. A robust system of hiking, cycling, and even horse trails crisscross Tyron Creek and River View parks, while the smaller Pine Cone and Woodmont Natural parks provide excellent lunch-time escapes. For those who love to get lost in nature, but still have a demanding schedule, the convenience of these easily accessible parks is impossible to beat.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-9904327/original/56d1a548-9fa3-42a7-af6e-c90eebca7d77.jpeg',50929838,73,'45.43407','-122.69763',1,6,3.00,3.00,3.00,260.00,30,365,0,1.00,9904327),(487,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9905408','Nan\'s North Portland Crepe Myrtle Cottage','Nan\'s Cottage is newly built, combining old world charm with modern convenience. In the beautiful Historic Mississippi District, you are close to everything in Portland. The cottage is fully furnished with everything you need whether you are a short or long term visitor. Bring your toiletries and enjoy. Your place is private, cozy, and restful. Separate from my main house, it is tucked in my backyard surrounded by gardens. You have your own private getaway, but close to advice/backup if needed.','Located in the Historic Mississippi District, you are close to many restaurants, bars, coffee shops, bookstores, boutiques & activities within walking, biking or public transportation distance.  <br />It is just 5 minutes to the heart of Downtown by car<br />It is also bike friendly ~ right on the North Portland bike corridor <br />10 blocks to Alberta Arts District<br /> 5 blocks to 1-5 Access & I-405','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8e26c265-be5f-4106-9d53-4ff4f403624a.jpg',50933310,9,'45.55052','-122.67599',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,30,1001,4,5.00,9905408),(488,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9925170','Explore Trails & Northwest Nob Hill From Guesthouse Getaway','This clean, chic Northwest Portland guesthouse is perfect for being close to the action yet staying separate  from other people. It’s just right for experiencing the best this city has to offer. Walk to marvelous Forest Park or NW 23rd. Take a short ride to Downtown, The Pearl, The Blazers Rose Garden Arena or the Rose Garden and Japanese Garden in Washington Park!<br /><br />The Guesthouse Getaway was designed and constructed in 2008 to reflect the charm of the property\'s 1926 main house. Its elevated simplicity is welcoming and homey  while still achieving that pristine quality you desire. This upscale lodging is situated in the West Hill\'s prominent Willamette Heights neighborhood where historic classics meet the urban edge.<br /><br />The best part? The place is all your own! No worries about whether the TV will wake your host; no sounds of snoring will come through the walls; no need to tippy toe around to keep from bothering light sleepers and there will be no wake-up blast of so','The Guesthouse Getaway is in a fun area with over fifty exceptional restaurants within a mile of the home. Go for a hike in the surrounding nature,  check out some of the breathtaking galleries, and catch a live sporting event or show in the evening.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3dce6bd5-0a29-4bb8-8aa0-4bb26671b3a2.jpg',51019210,27,'45.536445403800045','-122.71430891317755',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,178.00,2,29,231,4.93,9925170),(489,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9941118','Sellwood - nature, food & fun!','This home is in a safe, vibrant, friendly neighborhood!  It has easy access to nature, food, and entertainment. We just added a new addition...a large room that could be anything! An exercise room? Office? Play space? Extra bedroom? There is a shared outdoor space with seating and fire pit. A private fenced in yard was recently added.<br /><br />I will add some more photos soon.  Feel free to message me with any questions!','You can easily walk to restaurants, coffee shops, food carts, the library, shopping, Sellwood pool, and the best grocery store in town (New Seasons). <br /><br />Walk or bike to some of Portland’s best parks! The home is 2 blocks from the river and the Springwater Corridor bike trail. Bike to OMSI or downtown in about 20 minutes.  Launch your kayak or SUP at Sellwood Riverfront, picnic under the big trees at Sellwood Park, look for otters and eagles at Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge, let your little ones splash in the stream at Johnson Creek City Park, or explore the “Nature Playground” at Westmoreland Park.<br /><br />In the summer and early fall, street trees are dripping with fruit, there are music festivals in the park, and Oaks Amusement Park is open.  During the fall and winter holidays, homes are decorated with lights.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9edabe2e-a9db-4073-89f1-de332df3ceb4.jpg',28029219,20,'45.46015338427668','-122.65505992588058',1,4,1.50,2.00,4.00,100.00,30,365,2,5.00,9941118),(490,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9954390','Charming Sellwood Apartment','Modern 1BR Apt in Historic Sellwood. This new, charming upper level apartment, with a private entrance is located in Portland’s Historic Sellwood neighborhood. Unique shops, food carts, restaurants, coffee bars, parks and more await you.','We are on a quiet tree lined street just a block from 13th ave, a great neighborhood street full of wonderful local restaurants, coffee shops, boutiques, a bike store, bakery, bottle shop, etc.. Just a block the other way is Sellwood Park, with its outdoor pool, tennis courts and beautiful old Fir trees and picnic areas overlooking the Willamette River. Walk 5 minutes and you are on the banks of the river or Oaks Bottom natural area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ba613dc9-94f6-4596-94b3-2de53f7b5966.jpg',51154190,20,'45.46521','-122.65475',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,135.00,2,1125,288,4.96,9954390),(491,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9960778','Alberta Arts Craftsman 4 Bedroom','Enjoy family-friendly modern accommodations within walking distance to all Alberta has to offer! The 1st floor has an open floor plan including a modern kitchen with stainless appliances, dining space for 8+, living room, and all bedrooms upstairs.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d33865cb-da0a-4831-a603-e81fd594a95b.jpg',27447858,14,'45.56277','-122.6564',1,10,2.50,4.00,0.00,0.00,30,120,30,4.90,9960778),(492,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9978138','Charmer 1894 Rowhouse 94 walk score / Max train','Historic Brooklyn neighborhood row house,  close to everything!  No need for a car, as its just 2 blocks from Max station, and feet from bus lines.  Just steps to the Alladin theatre. Just a few short blocks to coffee houses,  pubs, and restaurants. 94 walk score.','Brooklyn is a great neighborhood, close to everything!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dca35dbf-4a4b-44ae-aa6d-6eb628a868d3.jpg',51273080,56,'45.49989','-122.65575',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,200.00,30,62,452,4.85,9978138),(493,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/9995993','Logan Home on Gladstone','A charming 2nd-floor Victorian getaway with private entrance, full kitchen, bedroom, living room that doubles as a second bedroom, bathroom w/clawfoot tub, and sunroom, located in a quiet street that dead ends into a beautiful park, 2 blocks from major bus lines.  A shared wrap-around porch and BBQ area are included. The neighborhood is filled with great restaurants, bars, and markets.  Free washer and dryer in the foyer.  Licensed by the City of Portland.','The neighborhood is full of fun places within a 10 minute walk or short drive.  Kenilworth Park is a beautiful space with huge trees, tennis courts, baseball diamond, and playground, right at the end of our block.  The Gladstone Pub (The Stone) is a 5-minute walk to the friendliest drinks anywhere.  Just tell \'em you\'re staying with us, and they\'ll take care of you!  Other neighborhood spots are the C Bar (best pinball selection around), Yoko\'s Sushi (best in town), Rocio (mexican), and Di Nicola (great family Italian restaurant).  The Division St. district is a 5-minute drive, with dozens of the best bars and restaurants in the city, including Pok Pok, Maru, Tom\'s Restaurant, Double Barrel Saloon, etc.  Safeway is a 2-minute drive, and Trader Joe\'s and New Seasons are 5 minutes away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4e7f7bce-54ab-4ca6-9c1f-03124174ff21.jpg',51352005,67,'45.49411','-122.63088',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,99.00,2,730,201,4.95,9995993),(494,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10153895','Cozy one bedroom, awesome location','A compact cute one bedroom with all conveniences. Walking distance to cute boutiques, restaurants and bars on Alberta and Williams. Next to Whole Foods, and coffee  shops. About 20 min to PDX Airport, and 10-15 min drive to downtown.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d214fb16-0271-4875-a6c1-9e239049f9b2.jpg',1586097,6,'45.54854','-122.65248',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,78.00,30,120,133,4.90,10153895),(495,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10230029','Cozy Studio In the Woods','This quiet cozy studio with your own kitchen, private bathroom and deck is  located  10 minutes from downtown , 1 mile to Tryon Creek Park with miles of trails and 5 minutes to  quaint Multnomah Village with coffee and artsy shops.','Here, you\'ll enjoy the option of a a morning hike at Tryon Creek before you head off to work, or school, or to hunt for your own permanent place to live in Portland . You\'ll be centrally located to make exploring the city easy.  Then return home to the woods and a retreat-like feel.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d939de9d-b5e9-4d67-9b92-8f4f12278789.jpg',141076,73,'45.44566','-122.70959',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,120,3,5.00,10230029),(496,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10294233','Comfy Convenient Home in Lovely Montavilla','Located in the heart of historic Montavilla neighborhood, enjoy the sweet life in this refurbished solar-powered 1900\'s PDX home. <br /><br />Steps away from over 23 bars & restaurants (beer lovers\' paradise), farmers market, movie theater, yoga studio, Mt. Tabor Park, & more!<br /><br />About 10 minutes by car to the airport & to Downtown PDX. An hour from Mt. Hood & the Oregon Coast. Conveniently access Oregon Wine Country, dozens of hiking trails/waterfalls/rivers, & tax-free shopping in under an hour.','Centrally located in SE Portland. The Montavilla neighborhood was named by Lonely Planet as one of the \"Top 10 Neighborhoods you need to visit in America.\" YOU CAN WALK TO ALL OF THIS!<br /><br />Restaurants | Bars | Breweries | Cafes & Coffee Shops<br /><br />- Lazy Susan<br />- Tinker Tavern<br />- Sebastiano\'s Italian Deli<br />- The Observatory<br />- Over & Out<br />- Redwood<br />- Ya Hala Lebanese Cuisine<br />- Roscoe\'s<br />- Miyamoto Sushi & Sake<br />- Thatchers<br />- Hungry Heart Bakery<br />- Bipartisan Cafe<br />- Montavilla Brew Works<br />- The Beer Bunker<br />- Montavilla Station<br />- Vintage Cocktail Lounge<br />- Vino Veritas Wine Bar and Bottle Shop<br />- Flying Pie Pizzeria<br />- Coquine<br />- Heartbreaker Neighborhood Kitchen<br />- Little Saigon Noodles & Grill<br />- Bánh Mì Nam Lộc<br />- Santa Cruz Bakery & Taqueria<br />- Giant Gyros<br />- Bui Natural Tofu<br />- Threshold Brewing & Blending<br />- PDX Cookie Co<br />- Su Casa Taqueria Cart<br />- Mon','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTAyOTQyMzM%3D/original/1d0a68ca-091f-4f96-a559-1d0106973f53.jpeg',52959802,10,'45.51974','-122.58252',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,60,66,4.91,10294233),(497,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10343033','Cozy Room in Bike-Friendly Craftsman + Free Bike','Bike\'N\'Roll Craftsman: Bicycle Tourism, Beautiful Front Porch<br />See Portland by bike - Biking Score 95!<br /><br />GUESTS RAVE: \"I can bike everywhere!\"<br /><br />*Beautiful, cozy bedroom <br />*Bright - lots of windows - high ceilings <br />*Near bus & max train - so you can bicycle even farther! <br />*100s of shops, restaurants, and everything you want to see within biking distance!<br />*Ranked 2nd in the CNBC\'s most bicycle-friendly cities in the US!<br />*Free on-street parking<br />*I don\'t charge a cleaning fee','There are some antique shops, restaurants, and the Aladdin Theater.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTAzNDMwMzM%3D/original/de071eb1-7988-4c12-a50e-b7f1ee5ad970.jpeg',53232555,56,'45.49377','-122.65446',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,63.00,3,28,150,4.77,10343033),(498,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10366008','Near Airport/15 mins to Downtown -Boho Artist Room','This is the master bedroom in a 1931 home, a bright 13\' x 13\' space with a vintage full-sized bed (owner lives upstairs).  Plenty of heat, light, comfort and closet space if you need it.  Only 10 mins from PDX Airport.  Nestled at the foot of beautiful Rocky Butte - 20 min walk to the top and an awesome 360-degree view of Portland and the Columbia River Gorge.  Neighborhood is rich in excellent Asian, Latin American, Russian and African-American food.  Near bus and MAX stops.','Located at the base of Rocky Butte, there\'s hiking trails, rock wall climbing and panoramic views of the Gorge within a 20 minute walk uphill.  A few blocks to the south is a giant Buddhist retreat center with trails, ponds and a million frogs that sing at night. It\'s a cute, central NE neighborhood with lots of gardens and easy access by public transportation to all of Portland.<br /><br />We are around the corner from the Beech Street Urban Farm and several Village Building Convergence sites. It\'s a diverse, semi-urban neighborhood with a wide range of interesting people, yet still quiet at night.<br /><br />I live in what was the center of a vortex, 15,000 years ago when the Missoula Flood sent a 100-foot high wall of water swirling around Rocky Butte and depositing boulders pulled from what is now Montana, Idaho and Washington. The energy is still here. In the winter when the icy wind barrels down the mountain, it follows the same path, like a 15,000 year old echo, making the walls','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/227bd582-849c-47f0-8ce1-dcc6d9812c67.jpg',42719900,74,'45.54657','-122.57281',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,24.00,1,5,155,4.90,10366008),(499,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10387521','NowStayingPDX / Inner SE Portland Guest House/ADU','Our rental is a newly constructed 1 bedroom ADU located in the SE Division/Clinton neighborhood. It\'s a 1 bedroom (queen bed), 1 bath (walk-in shower), second story unit located on the back half of our property. The backyard is a shared space is available upon request.','Walking distance to a plethora of Portland\'s finest eateries, bars and coffee shops.  For any last minute needs, New Seasons, our local grocery store is two blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-10387521/original/17e6d8c3-869a-4267-854f-b02fb6f92d1f.jpg',45402529,25,'45.50371528642422','-122.64246839837989',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,204.00,2,14,96,4.98,10387521),(500,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10406727','Front Bedroom in Cozy, Artsy, St. Johns Bungalow','Comfy bedroom with 1 full size bed in cheery, light infused home filled with oil paintings by host. Empty closet and dresser in room.Located in quaint and charming St. Johns with restaurants, shops and parks all within walking distance.  <br /><br />All guests much submit proof of  Covid-19 vaccinations.<br /><br />Please note I am LGBT-friendly and have no age, gender, racial or religious biases - everyone is welcome here!<br /><br />Traveling with a child? Let me know if you have baby proofing needs.','St. Johns is an up and coming neighborhood 8.3 miles from downtown Portland. There are shops and restaurants serving local food and locally made goods. Just 3 blocks away is a food cart pod with a fire pit and outdoor market. Nearby Cathedral Park is beautifully located under the St Johns Bridge, right on the river. We have 2 cinemas within walking distance that serve food and beer in the theater.  A small local health club 3 blocks away offers day passes.  Easily accessible are 2 different bus stops that connect you to downtown and all the colorful and interesting neighborhoods around Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-10406727/original/4e3c02e2-c1f3-447b-98f7-48cc165cc5ed.jpg',13263099,58,'45.58838','-122.74464',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,71.00,2,28,122,4.90,10406727),(501,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10430299','Northwest Nob Hill Alphabet District! Free Parking','Spacious 1,100 sq ft first floor 2 bedroom unit in prime Northwest Nob Hill location, just 2 blocks from 23rd Ave. It features full kitchen, island and new appliances including dishwasher, dining area, spacious living room with sleeper sofa, flat screen TV, fireplace, AC, desk, internet and laundry room with washer and dryer. The oversize open living area has two French doors that lead out onto your own balcony. Free street parking.  Nob Hill, Alphabet District, Walk score 97.','The unit is located on a quiet dead end street with lots of street parking plus a path at end of street for direct access to Thurman where the coffee shops, bakeries and boutiques begin.   <br /><br />The unit is in a prime, highly desirable location close to it all! It\'s just a few blocks from NW 23rd Avenue (near Thurman) featuring retail boutiques, home design shops both local and well-known, restaurants, bakeries, breweries, coffee shops, antiques, galleries, parks and hiking trails (just blocks from Forest Park) )... just about everything for an enjoyable visit to Portland! It is very close to public transit and the street car for quick access to the Pearl District (also within walking distance), Willamette River and Downtown, making this a great place to stay whether for work or fun!   <br /><br />Parking is on the street and pretty easy as it is located on a quiet, dead-end street. We provide free parking on the street for one car.  If you have an extra car please let us know as','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-10430299/original/c36681d1-ba0c-4d4a-97f3-f7108a3cdb6a.jpeg',45609473,27,'45.53629','-122.7017',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,153.00,2,28,35,4.91,10430299),(502,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10546918','Private Room in Fanatical PDX Tour Guide\'s Home!','Located in the heart of Hawthorne, the main artery of Southeast Portland!<br /><br />This district\'s a showcase of Portland\'s culture - tons of bars, cafes, food spots, vintage stores, and scenic parks within walking distance!<br /><br />You’re not only renting a room, you’re signing up to MEET A LOCAL GUIDE who wants to make the most of your time here!<br /><br />I host the Airbnb Experiences Weird-Bar Crawl and Explore Local Oddities, so I\'ve got an insider look at where to go & what to do - I\'m eager to share it with you!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-10546918/original/d1f7e73e-c064-458d-9afc-99051d1bc985.jpeg',54390576,8,'45.51137','-122.62155',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,42.00,2,31,72,4.96,10546918),(503,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10596867','Clean, Modern Townhouse w/ Patio in walkable area','Love your time in Portland in my newly constructed, modern townhome fully equipped with anything you may need and located in a close-in SE neighborhood. <br />Convenient to all the wonderful SE neighborhoods, Downtown, The Pearl, & Moda Center.  Bring your car, but you won\'t need it - the house is right on the main Ankeny bikeway and walking distance to lots of great restaurants, bars and retail shops! Park your car and leave it behind to get a feel for the real heartbeat of the city!','I live in the heart of Portland near SE 14th and Ankeny - a quick walk or bike ride from almost everything in the city! Our street is a relatively quiet, residential one with apartments and individual homes along with my modern townhome on the corner. There are a ton of excellent restaurants, bars and retail just blocks away!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTA1OTY4Njc%3D/original/17a4aaae-32c9-4560-bfbb-0d663e898624.jpeg',31480744,12,'45.52301','-122.64867',1,2,2.50,1.00,1.00,278.00,2,31,1,5.00,10596867),(504,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10632817','Charming home in Sunnyside—blocks from Hawthorne','Beautifully renovated 1902 house with high ceilings, bullseye moldings, and modern kitchen. Backyard deck is perfect for an alfresco dinner overlooking our garden. Our raised bed garden is bursting with herbs and berries and we often get visits from hummingbirds in summer. Within walking distance of Belmont and Hawthorne, two lively shopping streets lined with cafes, restaurants, and shops. Downtown is a short bike or bus ride away.','We are within walking distance of Stumptown Coffee, Los Puñales (tacos), Laurelhurst Theater, Crema, Cheese & Crack, Powell\'s on Hawthorne, Fried Egg I\'m in Love, several bustling food cart pods, and much more.  <br /><br />All the fantastic restaurants, bars, and shops that line Division St.—including Bollywood Theater, Ava Gene\'s, Olympic Provisions, Little Beast, St. Honoré bakery, and Salt & Straw—are a 10-minute walk to the south. <br /><br />We also love Canteen for their vegan rice bowls—especially the Bangkok bowl (with brown rice, adzuki beans, broccoli, and red cabbage with a red curry peanut sauce with kimchi and avocado); Crema, which serves coffee from Coava and Stumptown, homemade croissants, muffins, cookies, and quiches.<br /><br />We\'re a short walk/run from beautiful Laurelhurst Park, a 31 acre oasis designed by Emanuel Mische, which is full of majestic Douglas Fir, blue spruce, rhododendron, and linden trees. It\'s the perfect place for a morning jog or walk, or to sp','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d5ace2c5-5ccb-4615-a26d-22d2fe5077a0.jpg',6486134,16,'45.51576','-122.63468',1,4,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,7,21,13,4.92,10632817),(505,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10747692','Big, quiet, private apartment in Alameda/Irvington','This is a pet-free zone. Lovely walk through a quiet neighborhood to shops & restaurants. 10-min drive to city center. Public transit to everywhere. Ultrathick, comfy California-king mattress in the bedroom, and a comfy queen sofa bed in the living room. Plan to sleep well!','Share our 1926 Craftsman home in Alameda—one of Portland\'s loveliest, quietest, most architecturally rich neighborhoods. If you seek a sanctuary in this city of stunning natural beauty, unforgettable food, delicious coffee and tea, lively bars and brew pubs, cultural excellence, and famous weirdness—Voodoo Doll doughnut, anyone?—you\'ll find it here. Our neighborhood of historic homes, serene gardens, lush trees, and very little car traffic is a favorite of walkers and cyclists.<br /><br />We\'re a 15-minute walk from lots of restaurants, bakeries, and small shops, and we\'re a 45-minute walk from Portland city center.<br /><br />Starting in late January and ending in November or December, our gardens in the front and back always have something outrageous blooming. From March to September, they have LOTS of somethings blooming.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d1483fb9-dc26-45e7-98c5-a8ac269318e7.jpg',18516233,19,'45.54404','-122.63776',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,31,366,44,4.98,10747692),(506,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10752148','Hawthorne Hobbit Hole: special Portland experience','The Hobbit Hole is a cozy, comfortable sculpted suite to stay. It\'s an enchanting oasis, crafted with love and with guests in mind. <br /><br />This is a walking, biking, and transit paradise with easy curbside parking. We are around the corner from an organic grocery store, iconic restaurants, shopping, bike share programs and entertainment on perfectly Portland Hawthorne and Division streets.  We are an open and affirming household who welcomes all. We do allow smoking/vaping outside, including cannabis','\"Where there\'s life there\'s hope, and need of vittles.\" And you\'ll find some of the best Portland has to offer just outside our doorstep!<br /><br />Smack dab in the heart of the trendy Hawthorne shopping, dining and exploring strip, we are just footsteps from everything you need including New Seasons organic grocery store around the corner and a ton of excellent dining options nearby. We are walking distance from the Division and Belmont Street commercial corridors with even more things to do and eat. If you\'ve always wondered what it\'s like to live in Portland, check out our neighborhood. <br /><br />We are allowable of marijuana use in the backyard but please, no smoking or vaping inside the house. Take your pipeweed, tobacco and cannabis outside to our amazing Tin Lotus gazebo!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ef56bd02-5c88-4ab0-80ea-b6ee8de614ea.jpg',7380909,8,'45.51095','-122.62004',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,53.00,2,29,392,4.96,10752148),(507,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10787836','Sellwood Guest Home','SPECIAL OFFER: JANUARY 2025, $3,200/MO. Longer term rental available starting MARCH 1st @ $3,100/MO. Contact hosts for details.<br />Newly built, fully furnished, luxury 2BR/2Ba Guest Home in historic Sellwood neighborhood. Two blocks from Sellwood park, short walk to many restaurants, cafes, and shops. Bus, train and bike to downtown.','Sellwood is one of Portland’s oldest and most walkable neighborhoods, popular for its close proximity to downtown. It overlooks the Willamette River and has some of the most beautiful parks in Portland.<br /> You can walk to 3 different parks and the Willamette River all within just 10 minutes. Sellwood Park is just 3 blocks, New Seasons organic grocery store is also nearby along with numerous coffee shops, wine bars, pubs, bakeries, food carts, yoga, pilates, antiques stores and restaurants in the surrounding area. There is a bike path just a few blocks away- the Springwater Corridor trail - that goes straight to downtown in just 3 miles ride - or it will take you 15 minutes to drive to downtown. Our neighborhood has the soft, green comfort & safety of a charming small town, but with the style, excitement and access of city life.<br />Westmoreland Park & Golf Course, Moreland Movie Theater, Reed College Campus, Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge, Sellwood Library, Cork Screw Wine Bar, Bottle','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b0200946-236b-4ad2-beff-f3726f7d237d.jpg',21848715,20,'45.46629','-122.65748',1,4,2.00,2.00,3.00,152.00,3,90,123,4.98,10787836),(508,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10886050','Hawthorne Blue Jewel','Restaurant Heaven!  2 blocks to vibrant Hawthorne. 5 blocks to exciting Division. 600 sq ft basement apt in 1912 Craftsman. Queen bedroom, living room with big screen TV and very comfy memory foam sofabed, shower/soaker tub bathroom. No kitchen, but fridge, microwave, toaster, coffee maker, utensils.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c4d9bbf2-18a7-4057-baca-c7d8a68a1c06.jpg',30814658,8,'45.50939','-122.62365',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,90.00,2,30,180,4.88,10886050),(509,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10964177','GreyPort:  Peaceful, Upscale,  High-Speed Internet','A beautiful, professionally-designed studio apartment with attention to details. Varying art from local artists & styled with personal collections we have curated. The bathroom has an updated walk-in shower with a focus on being spacious, bright, and light. The great room is thoughtful in its layout & includes a relaxing area with TV, a sleeping area, & a remote work desk space. Large windows in the great room & kitchenette allow ample daylight & extreme privacy when needed.','This is a quiet residential neighborhood just South of downtown Portland.  A peaceful oasis near the heart of the bustling city.  A short walk to a couple of restaurants, coffee shop, dry cleaner, and nail salon.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-10964177/original/22991b59-dedc-41fa-9d8e-7a07c691c1d8.jpg',28179125,28,'45.46729','-122.68026',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,110.00,3,30,86,4.99,10964177),(510,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/10971248','NE Portland, Large Groups, walkable /pets allowed','Welcome to The Ginkgo House, centrally located in Alberta Arts district/ NE Portland. Our 3 bedrm /3 bath has all the amenities that you could ask for. It\'s ready to house your family vacation or work retreat. <br />We are steps away from great restaurants, coffee shops, groceries, liquor, & boutiques. The house has fast WiFi. We\'ve designed the home to reflect the Pacific Northwest and the fun it\'s known for. Our block boasts free street parking. Pets allowed for monthly rentals.','As far as Portland locations go, ours is perfect!  Tucked into a residential neighborhood of NE Portland, just 10 minutes to the Convention Center, MODA, or PDX, the Alberta Arts District is a vibrant arts and foodie paradise – quintessential Portland and a destination unto itself. Yet also easily accessible to downtown, to the Coast and the Gorge, and to the greater Portland area.<br /> <br />We are just three blocks to vibrant Alberta Street, Kennedy School, New Seasons Grocery, Walgreens, bakery, the dispensary and the liquor store. Minutes on foot to coffeehouses, bars, and restaurants headlined by well-known chefs: farm-to-table cuisine, fusion meals, craft cocktails, and so much more – a real foodie haven !<br /><br />❤︎ Here, we’re a city not just of eaters, but of explorers: in Portland and the Alberta Arts District, in particular, we brew, we ferment (kombucha, cider, wine, whiskey), we frequent taprooms, we offer growler fill-ups, and we even have family-friendly brewpubs. An','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-10971248/original/15f280d6-7c89-49c4-b480-07681a711d11.jpeg',56920726,1,'45.56242','-122.63363',1,8,3.00,3.00,6.00,229.00,3,180,21,4.90,10971248),(511,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11073083','Lucky\'s Place - New Listing 2-BR Apartment SE PDX','Welcome to Lucky\'s Place! 🌟 This freshly renovated, one-level 2-bed, 1-bath apartment 🏡 centrally located in a quiet neighborhood setting, just minutes from the vibrant Woodstock neighborhood 🌳<br /><br />Enjoy easy self check-in, secure gated parking, and a laptop-friendly workspace—perfect for couples, solo travelers, small groups, or families 💻🚗. We’re pet-friendly, so don’t forget to bring your furry buddies 🐾 It’s the perfect budget-friendly spot for exploring the PDX Portland has to offer 🏙️.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-11073083/original/5a8b62fa-511f-4538-a00d-ba24ed44a17c.jpeg',53497477,38,'45.47624','-122.60485',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,95.00,2,1125,29,4.90,11073083),(512,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11089716','Casa Solárium ~ Local Eateries, Parks & Espresso','Located in the heart of Portland\'s renowned Sunnyside Neighborhood, this 3BR apartment is just a short walk from many desirable spots. Notably, it\'s only two blocks from the eclectic SE Hawthorne Blvd! Enjoy this cozy, spacious getaway with family and friends, and immerse yourself in the splendid local attractions on the beautiful east side of town.','Welcome to Central Southeast Portland, a foodie\'s paradise where the options are endless! As a food fanatic myself, I can assure you that you\'re just a short walk away from some of the city’s best restaurants, delicious bakeries, renowned local coffee and tea shops, lively bars, and vibrant nightlife. You\'ll also find boutique shops, grocery stores, and so much more right at your doorstep.<br /><br />Beyond the culinary delights, the neighborhood offers a wealth of parks and recreational opportunities. Take a leisurely stroll or enjoy a picnic at Laurelhurst Park, known for its beautiful landscapes and serene pond. For those who love to stay active, the Eastbank Esplanade provides a scenic path along the Willamette River, perfect for walking, running, or cycling.<br /><br />Art enthusiasts will appreciate the local art scene, with numerous galleries and murals adding a splash of creativity to the area. Don\'t miss a visit to the Portland Art Museum or the quirky, yet fascinating, Indepe','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-11089716/original/d205c3a2-47fa-43a3-9e6a-7ccd7f097ef7.jpeg',33606696,16,'45.51671','-122.637',1,9,2.00,3.00,4.00,265.00,2,365,875,4.78,11089716),(513,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11097586','Warm and Welcoming in St. Johns','Completely updated with new lighting, paint, and remodeled kitchen and bathroom! This cozy ranch-style house has all the amenities. With great outdoor spaces, light and bright rooms, and comfortable furnishings, you\'ll feel right at home.','Less than a mile into downtown St. Johns, this is a wonderful and diverse working-class area of Portland. You\'re close to all the great shops in St. Johns (coffee shops, boutiques, natural grocer, movie theaters, etc.), a few blocks to Pier Park, just over a mile from the University of Portland, and a 15 minute drive into downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f8db6ac4-e9ca-449e-a8f1-751ad172b822.jpg',20227116,58,'45.5962','-122.7446',1,6,1.00,3.00,3.00,145.00,31,1125,65,4.97,11097586),(514,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11101624','Cozy, vintage Bohemian bus','Cozy converted bus with plenty of Bohemian charm, privacy, comfy memory foam mattress, dresser, electricity, lights, and heater. Bus is parked next to a 1907 farmhouse on a quiet cul de sac, close/easily accessed from airport and downtown Portland.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cdb23992-6cc0-4d1c-9252-8647a9384c5c.jpg',57657995,72,'45.48004',