e in a great location in the Beaumont-Wilshire neighborhood in NE Portland, which provides access to a variety of places to eat and drink. <br />We are walking distance from restaurants, grocery stores, shopping, art galleries, entertainment, public parks and awesome people watching.  Beaumont-Wilshire is an older, well established neighborhood with a strong sense of community. It has a nice mix of residential and commercial property.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-11238107/original/1a4508e5-d691-427c-b4a7-6cafddd03ea5.jpg',36040407,46,'45.55813','-122.62315',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,117.00,1,7,1033,4.93,11238107),(518,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11242427','Bright Spacious Studio-Close to PDX Airport','Feed your wanderlust and explore a new city on your terms when you stay at this adorable 2nd-story Portland vacation rental. The charming studio features 1 bathroom, chic decor, a Smart TV, a well-equipped kitchen, and your own 2nd story deck perfect for relaxing after a day out on the town. <br />With 3 bus stops within walking distance, you can tailor your getaway to your interests and explore local hot spots like Powell\'s Books, the Portland Japanese Garden, or one of the city\'s many food pods!','Many grocery stores and shopping are less than a 5 minute drive, and the max train is also 5 minutes away. The airport is about 10 minutes away. We are only 3 mins off Interstate 84 at exit 9 so it is super easy access from downtown.<br /><br />Location Details:<br /><br />BUS STOPS: NE Stanton & 117th (0.3 miles), NE Morris & 111th (0.3 miles), NE 111th & Knott (0.4 miles)<br /><br />PARKS & TRAILS: Knott City Park (0.5 miles), Luuwit View Park (1.1 miles), Powell Butte Nature Park (6.4 miles), Happy Valley Nature Park (8.0 miles), Spring Water Trail (9.6 miles), Woods Memorial Natural Area (14.2 miles), Tryon Creek State Natural Area (14.4 miles), Multnomah Falls (21.8 miles), Mt Hood (60.3 miles)<br /><br />DOWNTOWN PORTLAND (~9 miles): Oaks Amusement Park, Portland Art Museum, Washington Park, Lan Su Chinese Garden, Oregon Zoo, Portland Japanese Garden, International Rose Test Garden, Powell\'s Books<br /><br />REGIONAL WINERIES: Fullerton Wines (10.5 miles), Hawks View Winery (24.8','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3e4c9cb8-42f6-4287-9acb-cf9fd17f081e.jpg',501715,35,'45.54524','-122.54573',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,30,1125,68,4.74,11242427),(519,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11340920','Tiny Gem guesthouse at two rivers portland','Our house is nestled on a quiet tree lined residential street in the amazing Alberta Arts neighborhood.  We offer a newly built beautiful 450 sq ft spacious unique tall ceiling stand-alone studio home with beautiful and relaxing chemical free home with views of our garden, walking to coffee, food and grocery, or just relaxing.','alberta arts district is full of everything','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d50ad22a-c6a8-41bd-bb4d-51ab03ed552b.jpg',13602640,1,'45.5638313293457','-122.6346206665039',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,1,1125,185,4.88,11340920),(520,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11346138','\'Mallory homestead\' private garden apartment','A  garden oasis and your own entrance to a private daylit ground floor apartment with a queen size bed, a fold out queen futon sofa bed in the common area and its own bathroom. Within easy walking /biking distance1.7 miles  to hip strolling neighborhoods Alberta, Mississippi and Williams  of north Portland. Light and airy with full kitchen half mile from train, 10 minute train ride from downtown. <br />Cats on propertydo not enter rental','We are walking distance to restaurants, cafe, brew pubs, yoga studio and park in the woodlawn  triangle area...<br />Woodlawn cafe is my personal<br />Favorite as is P and Q market. Eleven cafe is close also and faces south so sunnier <br /><br /><br />within a mile of arbor lodge new seasons, max line station and cafes and shops<br /><br /><br /><br />Also Peninsula park and rose gardens with   tennis courts and 