892),(522,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11438533','Delightful Downtown Large Studio','Delightful large studio (477 sq.ft) apartment in the heart of everything: SW Morrison and 16th. Walk to the Pearl, 21st and 23rd streets, the Portland Museum, the Schnizer Concert Hall, endless cafes, restaurants, breweries. Right by a Blue Line/Red Line Max Light Rail station (Beaverton/Hillsboro/Airport). Big windows, eat-in kitchen, wonderfully maintained apartment building. In-building bicycle parking. Free washer/drier in basement.  Utilities included.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1e3be264-5471-42bd-8049-b4935cad7553.jpg',5790741,3,'45.52054','-122.68758',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,31,1125,10,4.80,11438533),(523,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11454745','Quiet Getaway in the Forest | Close to Downtown','Cute + Cozy Apartment in the Forest. 800 sq ft 1 bedroom/1 bath daylight basement apartment. Private entrance, spacious living room w/ sofa bed, balcony and deck, plus a quaint kitchenette. A perfectly peaceful retreat, nestled in the forest yet close to the city. <br /><br />IG: @owlcreekretreat<br /><br />Located in a quiet neighborhood, close to Woods Memorial Park. Just a 3 minute drive to popular Multnomah Village; 15 minutes from Downtown Portland; less than 10 minutes from Lake Oswego.','The apartment is located in SW Portland, just a 3 minute drive to super cute Multnomah Village. Multnomah Village offers a great selection of popular restaurants and bars (ask us for recommendations!). Take a 15 minute Lyft/Uber to Downtown Portland. We are also very close to lush Memorial Woods Park for a beautiful hike through the forest.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/46750d05-8732-4180-915c-d1f100ec2973.jpg',3040408,34,'45.45858','-122.73418',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,29,250,4.93,11454745),(524,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11480894','Historic Irvington 2 bd/NE Broadway (Parking + AC)','Spacious 2 bedroom apartment with private street level entry. Beautiful apartment with hard wood floors. Decor from my various travels in Mexico, Morocco, and Egypt. Full kitchen. Queen beds in each bedroom. Full bed in 2nd bedroom. A single bed is available per request as a 4th bed. Many shops, cafes, restaurants 1 block away on NE 16th/Broadway. Historic Irvington Neighborhood. Central Portland location. AC. Free street parking','One block off of bustling NE Broadway. Lots of cool restaurants, shops, cafes all the way from about 14th Ave up to 28th Ave','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8271671e-c2bb-4cba-b02c-a1c784060378.jpg',1602024,7,'45.53591','-122.64961',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,88.00,1,360,827,4.79,11480894),(525,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11491022','Riverfront Condo Downtown Portland','Condo offers stunning water views with great natural light and a location that allows you to walk into downtown Portland or Pearl district.  Condo is fully stocked, Flat screen TV in living room and bedroom, high speed WiFi,  and every essential you need to make your stay comfortable. Unit also come with a parking spot however public transit is great in Portland and a car is not always necessary.<br /><br />**There is a 30 night minimum on this property due to my HOA rules, however it is best to reserve','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3e34873c-c35d-4df1-b824-328a6a8b34b8.jpg',60500778,43,'45.5293','-122.6726',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,82.00,31,1125,18,4.83,11491022),(526,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11505470','Garden Tiny House, Woodstock','Our tiny cottage in is SE Portland near Reed and Woodstock.   The 200 sq feet of self-contained space is located between our home and a sweet elementary school.  We love the space for it\'s cheerful energy and quiet.  It is cozy and full of light.','Woodstock is the new up and coming sweet spot in Portland.  There is a New Seasons recently added and many restaurants, bars, and good coffee.  There are also some wonderful walking/biking nature paths close.  Reed Canyon is beautiful and peaceful and we are also close to Springwater Corridor for longer running or biking trips.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/61301d0a-5a24-4839-a5dc-5eb3f3870d56.jpg',8762054,38,'45.47332','-122.61922',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,238,4.97,11505470),(527,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11531147','Spacious Guesthouse with Creative Style and Local Charm','The house is adjacent to our home. It sits quietly in the back yard and above our painting studio. It\'s an open, airy and modern loft-style home with reclaimed fir floors, shelving, vanity, and doors. The reclaimed Doug Fir wood was sourced locally and has the beautiful patina of time. The queen size bed has a super comfy natural latex foam mattress and in the loft there is a fold out sofa with a full size memory foam sleeping pad (Please note that the loft is not an appropriate sleeping area for younger children due to the stairs and railing). The loft also boasts wonderful views looking out over the neighborhood and is a wonderful spot to chill out with a book or watch a movie. The art collection includes works created by the two of us (we are painters/photographers) and by other local artists. You are also welcome to come visit the art studio downstairs. The kitchen is fully loaded with brand new appliances and cookware and each guest is treated with coffee, creamer, chocolate, frui','The neighborhood was first settled in 1872 by Volga Germans and in 1891 was incorporated into Portland. Today, it\'s a thriving multi-cultural, socially conscious community. One of the best farmers\' markets in town is only a few blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8fa3d359-b339-44ac-86bf-7231ee3e3146.jpg',6805954,14,'45.55173','-122.6577',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,119.00,1,60,531,4.99,11531147),(528,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11669364','Bright Studio in Historic Brooklyn (Inner SE)','Wake up in this cozy and bright studio apartment on a quiet, tree lined street in the heart of Portland. Enjoy your your private entrance and private space with this beautiful studio apartment built in the basement of a historic 1923 Portland bungalow. You\'ll be tucked away in a quiet neighborhood but still within within easy access of all the hotspots in inner southeast Portland and the Rose Quarter. The studio has a queen size bed, cozy seating area and full-size kitchen for quiet relaxation.','The location of the Brooklyn neighborhood is what sets it apart! Incredible proximity to so many amazing shops and delicious restaurants! It\'s all a short walk or bike ride. Easy public transit or a short car ride from downtown or the Rose Quarter. Go Blazers!<br /><br />Coffee shop, restaurants and breweries all within walking distance. About 5 minutes from Oregon Museum of Science and Industry, and about 10 minutes from downtown and the Rose Quartern. Short hop to Sellwood antique district, SE Division (SE Portland\'s Restaurant Row), or Hawthorne Street. Great home base for exploring Mt. Hood, the Gorge, or the Willamette Valley wine country.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-11669364/original/fe4fe2d7-8d58-4fd4-9e80-fe802fe06b27.jpeg',19264481,56,'45.49485','-122.65221',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,85.00,2,120,8,5.00,11669364),(529,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11711660','Welcoming retreat with tree views!','This is a lovely two bedroom apartment in a fourplex with its own private deck overlooking a grove of lush trees. Vaulted ceilings, well insulated from sound and temperature, close to major bus lines, and a five minute drive to PSU, OHSU and downtown. The apartment is close to the South Waterfront, several parks, and nearby shopping centers and restaurants. It is practically downtown, yet situated on a quiet street with no outlet. Bring your bike and store it safely on your private deck.','Cozy residential neighborhood in a natural setting on a Court, not a thru-street.  Just a couple of blocks from a privately owned convenience store. Lots and lots of trees around. Very close to Barbur Blvd and public transit.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/878fb67f-8eb7-4bda-9b8f-e355443518e5.jpg',62203396,22,'45.49258','-122.67422',1,6,1.00,2.00,3.00,83.00,2,364,118,4.84,11711660),(530,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11759912','Quaint & peaceful room near PDX','We would love to have you come and stay in one of our charming guest bedrooms in our Sunny and comfortable 1914 remodeled farm house. Our home has all of the original architecture & is quite unique & artistic looking.  We are in quaint Parkrose.','Parkrose is a neighborhood in the Northeast of Portland. Parkrose was a small residential farming community until it was incorporate into the city of Portland in 1980. Rossi farms is still quite close, and a regional Farmer\'s Market occurs during the spring and summer. The Oregon Journal noted, “It is the most progressive and promising commuting districts on the eastern border of the city.\"<br /><br />There is a Parkrose transit center, which is served by the Red Line of the TriMet\'s Max Light Rail. We are close to the I 205 & I 84. There is a Parkrose school district and we happen to be close to Parkrose High School. This a beautiful high school with a great track for running or walking.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/72cd459d-7759-4a05-b1e8-b6992fcddefe.jpg',803501,40,'45.55246','-122.55334',2,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,48.00,30,1125,47,4.81,11759912),(531,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11760746','Charming Room near PDX','We would love to have you come and stay in one of our charming guest bedrooms in our Sunny and comfortable 1914 remodeled farm house. Our home has all of the original architecture & is quite unique & artistic looking.  We are in quaint Parkrose.','Parkrose is a neighborhood in the Northeast of Portland. Parkrose was a small residential farming community until it was incorporate into the city of Portland in 1980. Rossi farms is still quite close, and a regional Farmer\'s Market occurs during the spring and summer. The Oregon Journal noted, “It is the most progressive and promising commuting districts on the eastern border of the city.\"<br /><br />There is a Parkrose transit center, which is served by the Red Line of the TriMet\'s Max Light Rail. We are close to the I 205 & I 84. There is a Parkrose school district and we happen to be close to Parkrose High School. This a beautiful high school with a great track for running or walking.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/877b089f-3217-42f4-86ab-2447553742cc.jpg',803501,40,'45.55243','-122.55392',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,61.00,30,1125,31,4.68,11760746),(532,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11822724','Walk in NE. Light, private, hot tub, 420 friendly','This is a small carriage house in a quiet residential neighborhood.  Walk to restaurants, coffee shops and bakeries, member-supported historic movie theater. Three blocks to bus direct to downtown. Use hot tub (clothing optional), grill, garden.<br /><br />No pets','Highly walkable neighborhood with many young families and good schools. Two popular shopping/dining districts are a few blocks away (Hollywood, Fremont St.). Many legal recreational marijuana shops nearby, the closest being on NE Fremont at 51st (4-5 blocks).<br /><br />The Oregonian has a searchable database of its \"top 101\" restaurants at (URL HIDDEN)  We find the Oregonian\'s restaurant reviews to be reliable and its selections ones we agree with.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-11822724/original/98985c53-1a6f-40df-89f9-032ef01e2c62.jpg',58609749,11,'45.54589','-122.60803',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,83.00,2,1125,274,4.98,11822724),(533,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11825547','Portland Private 2 bedroom','Enjoy your stay nestled in the trees on 1/4 acre.  Only 2 minutes from I-5 South and Capitol Hwy.  Minutes to downtown, Multnomah Village, PCC Sylvania, NIKE, Lewis and Clark College, OHSU and PSU.<br /><br />Two bedrooms -  both with new pillowtop queen beds, living room with couch and loveseat, lamps, end tables, coffee table, dining area with seating for 4.  Open concept kitchen, spacious bathroom and laundry room with washer and dryer, outside balcony. Digital access.  Dedicated parking space.','Located in West Portland Park this popular area  is close to downtown without all the hassles of parking and noise.  Neighborhood of working professionals who enjoy being out of the city.  Barbur World Foods and Holly Park are just a mile away. Multnomah Village with all of it\'s restaurants and shopping is less than 5 minutes away','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4959a7db-627e-43ac-8d6f-42d4c543b9d1.jpg',62992553,53,'45.44628','-122.7208',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,164.00,1,730,25,4.88,11825547),(534,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11852482','IndigoBirch: Luxurious Zen Garden Retreat: Hot Tub','Look no further- as a member of The IndigoBirch Collection™️, our guest home stands as a top-tier experience on Airbnb. Located two blocks away from Reed College, IndigoBirch is nestled on a quiet tree-lined street in the highly desired & historic neighborhood of Eastmoreland. Our location is perfect for the adventurer looking to explore Portland. The guesthouse is two blocks away from public transportation, 12 minute drive to downtown Portland, and 20 minutes to PDX Airport.','The IndigoBirch™️ is located in the historic and quiet tree-lined neighborhood of Eastmoreland. It’s a desired neighborhood and was recently voted #1 neighborhood in Portland in 2020. One of our favorite things to do is to walk around and look at the beautiful homes and take in all of the sights and sounds. We are also located within a 10 minute walk to the Rhododendron Garden and two blocks from the stunning campus of Reed College! Both are a must see during your visit and known for their nature trails!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-11852482/original/ba652c65-541c-4a59-82ab-a1664bc3b336.jpeg',38404817,5,'45.478295395862794','-122.62678569062918',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,157.00,1,28,447,5.00,11852482),(535,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11929020','Furnished Condo','Located in beautiful Mt. Tabor. Each home is mid-century vintage. With wood floors, tiled kitchens and bathrooms. The location is fabulous. Restaurants, shopping and parks are close by. The close in location provides easy access to downtown.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTE5MjkwMjA%3D/original/28e2c663-c264-45a0-9e49-2d65d9e4ab7b.jpeg',828435,15,'45.51176','-122.61019',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,83.00,30,120,16,4.81,11929020),(536,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11991275','Handcrafted Blue Door Micro-Loft in Hip and Arty Location','Discover a unique, custom-built tiny home with a big feel. The residence features an open-plan layout, a mezzanine bedroom, rustic wood finishes, industrial accents, cathedral ceilings, and access to a shared garden patio with a BBQ.  Low cleaning fee & easy checkout.<br /><br />Close to action in fun Mississippi district, yet quiet & private. Self check-in. Close-in to downtown & Convention Ctr.<br /><br />As seen in “best of portland airbnb” online reviews:  wheatlesswanderlust, roadaffair, & bridgesandballoons.','Close to many things & easy access to everything else. The Historic Mississippi District is bustling with things to do, but also quiet & tucked away. A 10 minute bike ride to downtown or an equally short bus ride. The Alberta Arts district and the Williams corridor are a few blocks away, too. Within easy walking distance of local favs Por Que No?, Grand Central Bakery, New Seasons, Mississippi Studios, Interurban, Stormbreaker, & Gravy, to name a few. Short bus ride to Convention Ctr & downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9204cee0-6387-4a8f-90fa-7a33814860f6.jpg',585047,9,'45.548108586669315','-122.6741695620501',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,96.00,2,1125,670,4.99,11991275),(537,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/11991493','Live Like a Local in Artful Craftsman by Division','Beautiful 1916 Portland bungalow - bursting with character, original woodwork & striking local artwork. Located on a quiet residential street, it is steps away from the bustling Division/Clinton corridor filled with restaurants and bars! Easy street parking surrounds the whole house that you will have to yourselves. It\'s only available for rent when I travel so you\'ll have the home and the charming backyard to yourself - spread out and enjoy all Portland has to offer!','The house is on a quiet, tree-lined street, that is perfectly situated between Division and Clinton.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cb23b683-5f14-4ea8-b17c-710377708335.jpg',474837,8,'45.50475','-122.61705',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,145.00,2,21,118,4.97,11991493),(538,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12002530','Northberry PDX | Bright 1 BR Guesthouse | Balcony','Bright, light filled 1 bedroom apartment over garage with deck in close-in North Portland Overlook Neighborhood.  Close to light rail (6 blocks) and bus lines (1 block).  Sleeps four (2 in queen size Sleep Number Bed, 2 in pull out couch). Combination of salvaged housewares with clean modern lines creates a charming unit to serve as your base for Portland and/or Western Oregon exploration.  Hosts are Portland Natives that love their city and neighborhood and can\'t wait to share it with you.','Our neighborhood is filled with real people having a great time living in a wonderful part of Portland.  Close to everything and a lot of good restaurants, bars and coffee shops right down the street!<br />Try out Milk Glass Market, Old Gold, and Spitz all on Killingsworth and right down the block.<br />Great coffee shops a little farther away are Blend on Killingsworth at Greeley and Arbor Lodge on Rosa Parks Way at Interstate Ave.<br />Need a grocery store?  New Seasons has a great deli, beer, wine, bakery and cheese sections and is also walking distance at Rosa Parks Way and Interstate!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/eddd58f8-f0f7-49db-9e34-867cc13e1ea3.jpg',64184222,13,'45.56509','-122.68872',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,135.00,30,1125,221,5.00,12002530),(539,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12022574','Dolphin House','Welcome to Dolphin House! This is our family home full of light and character. Wonderfully decorated, with everything you will need for your time in Portland. Stylish living room, large dining room, lounge/beanbag room, eat-in kitchen, master bedroom with a king bed and a great view, upstairs bathroom and two sleeping nooks. It is warm and cozy with tons of light, eclectic decor, lots of books and records and close to everything Northeast Portland has to offer.','This neighborhood is called Woodlawn or Dekum Triangle. We are literally down the street from one of the best cafes around: Woodlawn Cafe. In that same area there is a beloved Brew Pub, a Weed Store, a nice restaurant called The Firehouse and our favorite local spot Ps&Qs Cafe and General Store. We are also walking distance to a Safeway and Walgreens as well as two generous parks. Within walking distance are the commerical areas of Killingsworth and Alberta Arts District.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/74dacabb-c12e-4641-b6b7-effacdf1646e.jpg',64329418,45,'45.56939','-122.65584',1,6,1.00,2.00,4.00,100.00,30,1125,18,4.94,12022574),(540,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12022874','Private Overlook Home (Near Miss & Downtown)','Sunny and spacious private Albina Victorian home in the central Overlook neighborhood. Full kitchen, living room, dining room, bathroom, two bedrooms upstairs. Private backyard and front porch.<br /><br />Great location! 5 min walk to Mississippi shops, carts and restaurants, or 15 min walk to Vancouver corridor, 2 blocks to MAX line,  just off the I-5 entrance (10 min drive to downtown).','The area is a nice mix of old and new Portland: tons of excellent food carts, cafes, bars, parks, and restaurants within blocks of the house. 5min walk to the Mississippi corridor, also near Vancouver and Alberta Arts districts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0f43558c-5d4d-46f3-90df-a1cf66d469f7.jpg',53357613,13,'45.55301','-122.67886',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,1125,36,4.89,12022874),(541,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12025458','Mississippi District Bungalow','Old & new with asian touches blend together in our restored craftsman bungalow. <br />We attempt to keep our house as much a working sanctuary as possible. Cute shops, food & pubs within a block,<br />Portland beyond!!','The house is located in the heart of the wonderful  Historic Mississippi District. <br />It is a quaint but exciting place perched a short distance north of downtown.<br />Full of restaurants, breweries, specialty coffee shops, a music venue, interesting shops and boutiques, food cart lots and more,  the area is also adjacent to The Williams and Interstate Corridors and the famous Alberta Arts district.<br />We are a quick bus or train ride to the center of downtown, an hour or so to the Pacific Ocean, 45 minutes to the Mt. Hood wilderness.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e2d2993d-151b-44c4-83e0-100e4a10107a.jpg',44216258,9,'45.55334','-122.67586',1,5,2.00,2.00,5.00,171.00,3,12,97,4.91,12025458),(542,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12025679','Furnished Condo near Mt. Tabor','No Lodging Taxes if you book for thirty-one (31) nights!<br /><br />Located near Mt. Tabor. Each home is mid-century vintage. With wood floors, tiled kitchens and bathrooms. The location is fabulous. Restaurants, shopping and parks are close by.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a8bb0d3a-414e-4c09-93ed-bf5f45f19862.jpg',828435,15,'45.51211','-122.61073',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,300.00,30,140,22,4.59,12025679),(543,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12028438','Walkable Alberta Arts- NE/ Family & Dog Friendly','Welcome to The Ginkgo House, centrally located in the coveted and easily accessible neighborhood of Alberta Arts in NE Portland. <br />Steps from the home, you\'ll find lots of restaurants, coffee shops, entertainment, groceries, pharmacy, liquor store, art galleries and much more. Our residential block boasts free street parking. Family and pet friendly.','❤︎  As far as Portland locations go, ours is perfect! Tucked into a residential neighborhood of NE Portland,  just 10 minutes to the Convention Center, MODA, PDX, and downtown, the Alberta Arts District is a vibrant arts and foodie paradise – quintessential Portland and a destination unto itself, and yet also easily accessible to downtown, to the Coast and the Gorge, and to the greater Portland area.<br />We are just three blocks to vibrant Alberta Street, Kennedy School, New Seasons Grocery, Walgreens, the dispensary and the liquor store. Minutes on foot to coffeehouses, bars, and restaurants headlined by well-known chefs: farm-to-table cuisine, fusion meals, craft cocktails, and so much more – a real foodie haven!<br />❤︎ Here, we’re a city not just of eaters, but of explorers: in Portland and the Alberta Arts District, in particular, we brew, we ferment (kombucha and cider), we frequent taprooms, we offer growler fill-ups, and we even have family-friendly brewpubs. And, did I mentio','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTIwMjg0Mzg%3D/original/abfdfeb8-08ea-4b2c-b255-679a1f0d1470.jpeg',56920726,1,'45.56181','-122.63371',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,149.00,3,180,30,4.97,12028438),(544,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12040912','Rose City Retreat','Newly constructed basement studio with private entry in 100+ year old NE Portland home in park-like setting. Trendy Beaumont Village neighborhood, walking distance to restaurants and shops, 90 minutes to the coast, one hour to skiing on Mt. Hood. Triple lot, gardens, swimming pool, hot tub and patio with BBQ.  Non-smoking household.','Right in the middle of it all. Walking distance to shops and restaurants on Fremont and Sandy, just a few minutes drive to downtown. Great biking neighborhood; our cross street Klickitat is a bike thoroughfare. 2 minute walk to Fire on the Mountain and Peter\'s Bar and Grill, short drive to Hawthorne, Alberta and Mississippi neighborhoods. The beach is 90 minutes west, the mountains about an hour east. The gorge is less than 30 minutes away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2462faef-fa41-48f0-8827-85245a17afe3.jpg',27382737,11,'45.54636','-122.60378',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,75.00,2,31,426,4.96,12040912),(545,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12111041','Garden Studio w/ Deck & Sauna','Large 20\'x12\' private studio with big private bathroom, supplied kitchenette, walk-in closet, and relaxing deck with access to a sauna, fire pit, and yard. Quiet, authentic FoPo neighborhood near many delicious and affordable restaurants, bars, dispensaries, and food carts. Borrow bikes to access the Hawthorne, Division, Woodstock and Belmont areas within 15 minutes. <br /><br />All are welcome. LGBTQ+ friendly. 420 friendly. Owner is comfortable communicating with internationals of all English abilities.','Foster-Powell is a diverse and friendly neighborhood. It has lots of bars, restaurants, cafes, live music venues, a tango dance hall, great dispensaries, a CBD libations bar, small grocers and convenience stores. We are located within 2 miles of Mt. Tabor and the Hawthorne district, Division shops, and Woodstock.<br /><br />You can borrow bikes to access more parts of the city.<br /><br />It\'s only a 5 minute walk to the small grocer of Bread and Roses Market on Foster. We are 1-mile away from the major grocery stores: New Seasons, Safeway, Natural Grocers, and Trader Joe\'s.<br /><br />Eastport Century 16 Movie Theater is right behind the Wal-Mart, also only 1-mile away. They have $6 deals on Tuesdays for new releases, and their seats are amazingly comfortable and you can reserve your seat ahead.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ce8110eb-d2eb-4f7b-aac6-5574e94a83f1.jpg',64693840,36,'45.49278','-122.6021',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,77.00,2,28,337,4.95,12111041),(546,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12223710','Elegant, Modern Garden House','Perfect location to explore the city! Steps to public transportation and nestled at the base of celebrated  Mt. Tabor Park and blocks to the best the city has to offer in dining, coffee,  and bars, parks and more!','We are just steps away from beautiful Mt. Tabor park and the Montivilla shopping area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ee75d381-5061-46e1-a738-0098fec53aaa.jpg',65753023,15,'45.51867','-122.58858',1,4,2.00,1.00,1.00,200.00,30,1125,13,5.00,12223710),(547,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12233092','South Tabor Bungalow','This spacious 1910 charmer is a comfortable, clean, stylish and cozy home base for your Portland stay! Nestled perfectly off the ever popular Division Restaurant Row and situated within a short walk to 4 city parks - including beautiful Mt Tabor Park...and much, much, more will enhance your enjoyment here.','What a great location!  South Tabor is nestled in between glorious Mt Tabor Forest/Park and Division Restaurant row. It\'s quiet, family friendly and is easy to get to. <br />The house is a short walk to Division Street, where you will find the original Stumptown Coffee, Roman Candle cafe, Ava Gene\'s Italian(voted best restaurant!) , Pok Pok, Salt n\' Straw Ice Cream, Xico,  Nuestra Cucina, Bar Avignon, a bustling food cart  corner and much more.<br />You can burn off those calories by shopping in high end boutiques or thrift stores galore. Tattoo parlors and funky bars are also fun. <br />The Clinton Bike avenue is just a block or two away. This begins a nice bike ride down to the waterfront, downtown, and all of SE neighborhoods. A fun way to see Portland!<br />Forest Park is 3 miles away and a gem of a forest to hike/bike/run/explore the 80 miles/over 5,000 acres of trails, one of the largest urban parks in the United States!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/987b7b5c-fd3e-4868-b4e3-674b0245dcc9.jpg',14477524,37,'45.50007','-122.60422',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,142.00,2,730,193,4.97,12233092),(548,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12293322','One Bedroom/One Bath Furnished','Located near Mt. Tabor. Each home is mid-century vintage. With wood floors, tiled kitchens and bathrooms. The location is fabulous. Restaurants, shopping and parks are close by.<br /><br />When you book for thirty-one nights or more you will not be obligated to pay Portland Lodging Taxes.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/89af3e1b-89b9-4025-ae13-0bcc5a73c365.jpg',828435,15,'45.51211','-122.6108',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,30,120,26,4.54,12293322),(549,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12319356','Peninsula Haven-Private, Quiet, and Cozy','Relax at the gorgeous, private & quiet mother-in-law apt, mere minutes from U of P, funky DT St. Johns and Kenton. Two nearby bus lines & a freeway provide great access to all Portland has to offer. Food carts, organic markets, coffee shops, dive bars & great food are all close by. <br /><br />Comfortable design & a rich amenity list are there to satisfy your every need.<br /><br />✔ LGBTQ & 420 Friendly<br />✔ 50\" ROKU TV w/ Netflix, Hulu, Prime, and Peacock<br />✔ Comfy Queen Bed<br />✔ Private Deck<br /><br />See more below!','The apartment is situated on the North Peninsula, in Portsmouth, one of the most diverse neighborhoods of Portland which still captures the feel of old Portland. Our home is situated right between St Johns, which has its own downtown area, and Kenton. These vibrant & lively neighborhoods are packed with cool shops, bars, cafes and restaurants. <br /><br />Please refer to the city guidebook below for more detailed recommendation of attractions and interesting places to visit.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/88a9967c-efa5-488b-8be2-7dc02aed65a6.jpg',327040,60,'45.58311','-122.7227',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,64.00,2,28,554,4.98,12319356),(550,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12361450','Cheerful Room in Friendly Alberta area home.','You will enjoy easy access to everything from this hot spot right off FUN NE Alberta Street.<br />Delicious coffee, bakeries and restaurants within a few block walk. Bus stops across the street and arrives downtown in 20-25 minutes.<br />Quiet, Friendly and spacious home with lots light and other fellow travelers, professionals or travel nurses. VERY high speed WiFi, 4 shared bathrooms, 2 laundry rooms, nice common areas and shared kitchen','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/af1616b2-5041-477f-8cdf-94e12f561c33.jpg',501715,6,'45.55605','-122.64859',2,2,4.00,1.00,1.00,47.00,30,365,3,4.67,12361450),(551,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12375526','Spacious Home, HUGE Yard, 10 Mins to PDX Airport','Wonderful Spacious Home with tons of light from the many big windows and French doors looking out on huge private yard with Firepit. <br />2 bedroom 1 bath home with a bonus room off the sun porch and with an outdoor/shop bathroom with a great rain shower!<br />The main bathroom is very large with double sinks, huge jacuzzi bathtub and separate shower.<br />There is a large Laundry room with washer and dryer.<br />The upstairs bedroom has a KING size memory foam bed.<br />Join the honey bees and enjoy a peaceful oasis!','This is a great location just a few minutes from exit 9 coming the 10 minute drive on I84 from downtown. It is also only a 5-10 minute drive from the airport. Winco, my favorite grocery store is 5 mins away among any other shopping you might need. It is also a really nice quiet family neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1eef54bc-1b31-4f6e-95bb-fc669906aed4.jpg',501715,35,'45.54421','-122.54487',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,195.00,30,360,12,5.00,12375526),(552,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12388588','Spacious living near Downtown. Trendy Williams Ave','Best deal in the neighborhood! Spacious basement apartment located below the main house with a separate entrance. Includes a full kitchen (stocked with everything you need), living room, dining area, and bathroom.<br /><br />Located blocks from Portland\'s Moda Center, Convention Center, Nike discount shop Mississippi district and Williams St. Feat. PDX\'s elite restaurants/bars.<br /><br />Downtown Portland a 5 min taxi away, and we have several Biketown hubs where you can rent a bike for the day/week/month.','The neighborhood is quiet yet is within walking distance of some of Portland\'s best restaurants including OX and Ned Lud.  Neighborhood highlights include:<br />- Walking distance to trendy Williams Ave, Irving Park (which includes basketball courts, running trail, playground and tennis), Moda Center, New Seasons Grocery, and Legacy Emanuel Hospital<br />- 5 minutes Uber to progressive Alberta Arts District, Mississippi Ave, downtown Portland, and Pearl District<br />-  Very bike friendly neighborhood with easy access to public transportation including MAX, Street Car, and bus.<br />-  Near popular Lloyd District which includes large shopping mall<br /><br />Perfect spot for guests seeking the Portland experience with everything conveniently located or for those with events at either the Moda or Convention Center.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7560ba5e-40ec-49d5-8e54-488fc3c4bfe2.jpg',24772821,26,'45.54141','-122.66338',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,27,199,4.85,12388588),(553,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12390197','Close in SE PDX! Historic Sellwood Basement Apt','Welcome to a 1912 landmark home in beautiful Sellwood/Moreland. Formerly the beloved Candyland restaurant, the light and bright basement apartment sits in front of the Springwater trail with views of Mt Hood.<br /><br />This is a 1 bedroom with kitchenette (stove burner and mini toaster oven) living room and dining room fit for 3! <br /><br />We are close to great shopping, dining and breweries get there by bus, the Max or bike in minutes. <br /><br />We welcome you to a safe and inclusive home and we are vaccinated!','Sellwood Moreland is a historic and well established neighborhood with it\'s own downtown area. Home to great restaurants, bars and antique shops  it draws many people to this part of Portland.  Our favorite dessert place is Papa Hayden\'s a mere short blocks away. A very walk and bike friendly part of Portland, there\'s easy access to downtown and our many bridges. Ubers and Lyfts arrive within minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/efd5953f-e390-4f85-a44d-16813b2b363b.jpg',66990216,20,'45.48362','-122.65024',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,1,10,804,4.89,12390197),(554,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12403226','Private Spacious Basement Suite & Full Kitchenette','Contemporary LARGE private basement suite w/ bathroom and full kitchenette. Washer/dryer access. Separate entry through garage (homeowner lives upstairs). Across the street from lovely Creston Park, 1 mile from shops/bars/food on Division. Easy walk to grocery store, coffee, ramen, pho,  Gladstone Pub, and more! Steps from Powell Blvd  with #9 (downtown) & #75 (SE/NE/N Portland) bus lines. Access to large back yard w/ fire pit.<br /><br />*note: extra cleanliness remains top priority regarding COVID-19*','Creston-Kenilworth is a wonderful neighborhood in SE Portland. There is a huge public park across the street with a public pool (open swim and lap swim; hours vary). Safeway (large grocery store) and Natural Grocers (smaller organic grocery store) are both a 4-minute walk from the front door. A variety of cuisine (Chinese, Thai, Vietnamese, Mexican, pizza, and ice cream!) are close walking distance, as well as multiple coffee shops and bars. Division Street (a hot spot packed with restaurants, bars, and shops) is less than a mile away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/03185437-51ad-4c45-bc55-fc97b394dd83.jpg',20320140,8,'45.49769','-122.61821',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,4,21,171,4.90,12403226),(555,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12420588','The Crystal Room - The House of Healing & Love','Would you enjoy relaxing in a garden full of berry bushes? How about a meal outside on our mahogany deck with a waterfall, bubbling brook and Koi pond? At night, under the stars, grab a blanket and sit on our stone patio in front of our gas fireplace.','We are located in Southwest Portland, in a cute neighborhood called Multnomah Village. Multonomah is about a five-minute drive from downtown Portland, and 20-minute drive to PDX. With tree studded windy roads, and a charming and eclectic business district, Multnomah developed in the 1910s around a depot of the Oregon Electric Railway of the same name. From our home, you can walk to Multnomah in 15 minutes (or drive in 5 minutes) and go shopping, as well as grab food, coffee, or a beer.<br /><br />Our street itself is quiet, safe, and the neighbors are quite friendly. There is a park directly across the main access road to our home, and Gabriel Park and Lewis and Clark College are an 8 minute drive.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-12420588/original/1081d8db-f58b-4718-81ad-d13a78a28f13.jpeg',31761206,34,'45.45786','-122.71944',2,2,1.50,1.00,2.00,80.00,1,1125,15,4.67,12420588),(556,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12482738','Light Airy Bedroom for Two Close to the Airport','Light airy home in the Overlook neighborhood. Private bedroom upstairs  with a queen size bed. The room has a dresser, closet and desk. Shared bathroom right outside the door. Down pillows and comforter on the bed. <br />Located in a quiet North Portland neighborhood close to restaurants, bars, coffee houses and parks. Light rail with service to the airport and downtown is only three blocks away. Bus service is one block away and it is within walking distance of the Adidas Campus.','There are quite a few very good restaurants with in walking distance of the house with a sprinkling of coffee houses and bars. Well lit and quiet there are also a couple of parks with in a few blocks and there are a couple of great grocery stores is near by.<br />Kitchen use is communal so it is restricted to light occasional use not full time three meals a day. Also no foods with lingering odors like fish or broccoli are to be cooked.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2f47543f-11c9-4c97-948f-1e1946b1a255.jpg',67395194,13,'45.56451','-122.68862',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,45.00,1,5,427,4.95,12482738),(557,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12508461','Alberta Arts retro fun studio apt.','Come stay in your own retro-modern apartment in the hip and eclectic Alberta Arts neighborhood.  The space is the light-filled basement level of a recently-built home,  1/2 block from NE Alberta St. and minutes from downtown Portland.  Walk score = 92 City Permit #16-157375-000-00-HO.','The Alberta Arts district is full of unique art galleries, restaurants, boutiques and pubs.  The area hosts a vibrant and fun street fair the evening of the last Thursday of each month with a focus on the arts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6d936b20-97d6-4134-9a74-3a3410a06b7e.jpg',45543392,14,'45.55898','-122.65827',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,1,28,399,4.97,12508461),(558,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12544586','Alberta Guest House','Clean, modern, comfortable Alberta Arts District guest house located 1.5 blocks from Alberta Street. The one bedroom + sleeping loft  guest house is situated in our beautiful quiet, private backyard oasis and includes access to our outdoor kitchen, gas fire-pit, hammock and patio.','We live in the Alberta Arts District and are just blocks from great dining and shopping. 6 blocks to Pine State Biscuits, 4.5 blocks to Salt & Straw Ice Cream & Bollywood Theatre Indian restaurant, 1.5 blocks to Podnah\'s BBQ and the list continues. Check out the Alberta Main Street site for more details. Check out the Travel Portland site for great dining ideas.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4c9a2843-9e53-4a2d-95d1-444cea29f5ba.jpg',11430120,29,'45.56084','-122.6477',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,105.00,2,1125,387,4.96,12544586),(559,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12574565','Lents Guesthouse - Nice Home in Southeast Portland','Nice & Private Guests\' Suite centrally located in SE Portland at a convenient location.<br />_Walk to Foods, Pubs, Shops, Malls, Park, Public Transits<br />_Short drive to PDX, Downtown<br />_Near I-205, US-26, OR-213<br /><br />_A Comfort of a home-away-from-home with cozy living room, a spacious master bedroom, fully equipped kitchen, nice bath with washer/dryer<br />_A perfect corporate rental, a comfortable stay for business travelers or guests needing an extended stay<br />_A nice place for friends, or family get together','This property is located in a Lents Historic District near Eastport Plaza Shopping Center in an old established neighborhood in SE Portland. In recent years, this area has become a reviving and thriving multicultural community. This home is located close to many amenities that Portland has to offer. It is only a short drive to Downtown Portland and Portland International Airport. It is an excellent hub to many of Portland\'s Must See Neighborhoods, less than a ten-minute drive to many trendy places like Hawthorne District, Division/Clinton District and Montavilla Districts.<br /><br />The location is very accessible as it is near Portland Major Roads, Highways and Interstates. It also has easy access to Portland Suburban Cities East and South of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d7ad5a5d-ca31-4bf9-894e-2c54819f3679.jpg',12523076,72,'45.4876','-122.57814',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,150.00,30,180,7,4.86,12574565),(560,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12679370','Modern Guesthouse in Portland\'s Central Eastside','Tall ceilings, an open staircase and walls of windows flood the space with light (even in Portland), while molded plywood Eames chairs add mid-century style. Located in the heart of Portland within walking distance to great restaurants, coffee and parks. Fast, gigabit fiber internet, full kitchen, large table, and private outdoor spaces help maximize your stay and comfort, whether you\'re alone or with a group. Editor\'s pick in Dwell.','From local, casual hot spots like Fire on the Mountain and hidden gems receiving national attention like Han Oak and Güero to high-end farm to table options like Nodoguro, there\'s a multitude of options within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/monet/Select-12679370/original/b367a74c-da06-46b2-800e-c19ab1e5ea3d',47289428,12,'45.52391','-122.64565',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,220.00,2,30,387,4.99,12679370),(561,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12699642','ROSE CITY PARK Guesthouse!','Welcome to our little house! Located in the wonderful Rose City Park neighborhood and close to the 60th Ave. MAX station, Hollywood District, and downtown Portland - this little house is great for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, and families. With a short 10 minute drive to downtown Portland and the convenience of public transportation, enjoy everything our city has to offer - your home away from home.','Located in NE Portland\'s Rose City Park Neighborhood, our sweet little house is near a park, several restaurants, and a short walk to the 60th Ave. MAX station. With easy access to the freeway, downtown is a quick 10 minute drive. We are also a short 5 minute drive to Rose City Golf Course and are within walking distance to the Hollywood District.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6b1c4b8e-0a32-4f3c-9ae6-23a71ba7b6cf.jpg',69029284,11,'45.53265','-122.60379',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,92.00,2,28,513,4.97,12699642),(562,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12796469','Bungalow Vibes in Nob Hill','Enjoy the Portlandia vibes from the heart of North West Portland. You’ll love the location and the charming front porch swing is perfect for people watching in the Alphabet District. The neighborhood is full of wonderful restaurants, bars and adventure. The space is good for couples, solo adventurers and business travelers. My place is the perfect basecamp for a Portland getaway!','The Alphabet district is a walkers paradise, close to Washington Park, Forest Park, The Rose Gardens, The Japanese Garden and Providence Park where the Timbers play. The apartment is just steps away from trendy 23rd  street that has lots of cute shops, trendy restaurants and bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/34c8687c-e792-43da-b4b1-229200de746b.jpg',7008585,27,'45.52676','-122.69491',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,30,100,441,4.86,12796469),(563,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12844862','South Portland Sanctuary','This spacious mid-century ranch is located in South Portland one block from the Willamette River and 1.8 miles to downtown. When you\'re done for the day this  is a great space to unwind and call home.  This clean and cozy ranch  boasts two bedrooms, two baths, two fireplaces, forced heat and A/C, high speed internet TV ,  and an attached garage to park your car safely at night.  Enjoy a six burner Wolf range or  private yard perfect for all season grilling, HE W/D and everything else you need.','The house is located one block from<br />the Willamette River and a park with the same name. The park offers access to the river with a four lane <br />boar launch. There is a soccer field, and in the summer the city hosts live music events and movies in the park. There is a firework show each 4th of July put on by Oaks Amusement Park which is directly across the river from where we are. It’s a great time for families and amazing that the trip home is a short block considering the traffic everyone else has to endure to return home.  The park also offers four regulation tennis courts open to the public for free and the courts are lit at night. There is a playground for kids and picnic tables.<br /><br />For runners and bikers, there is a path that runs through the park that will take you into downtown and if you still want to build your endurance you can cross a pedestrian bridge over the river and continue along the rivers eat bank on a maintained designated bike and running path.  You','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e17e0fcc-4a78-4c08-ac79-e757a1895036.jpg',57521274,22,'45.47486','-122.67459',1,3,2.00,2.00,2.00,285.00,30,1125,0,1.00,12844862),(564,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12854038','Spacious Portland Loft','Walking score 98. This bright spacious, centrally located, newly remodeled loft in downtown Portland, is an excellent place to experience what our amazing city has to offer. The loft is steps away from the Portland streetcar and Portland Art Museum. My Loft is available 31 nights or longer. It is perfect for an extended stay or a business traveler.','The Loft is located just outside of the core of Downtown.  You will be within walking distance to the West End, Portland State University, The Pearl and Goose Hollow.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4ce7ed07-4e7d-4e09-bed4-ec63f638c617.jpg',5907304,44,'45.51561737060547','-122.68614196777344',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,60.00,30,1125,20,4.70,12854038),(565,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12893173','Recently Remodeled House in Popular Montavilla','Lovely recent remodel, detached on lot with closed store but you will have the entire house and yard to yourself. Short walk to popular Montavilla shopping, food/drink, theatre and more. Very close to Mt. Tabor, one of PDX\'s most iconic Nature Parks for biking and views. In a quiet but trendy neighborhood setting that is very walkable. You are nearby nature destinations for the PNW as well as the popular areas of PDX metro.  2 bedrooms with queen beds, living room futon, nice kitchen and bath.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/05438298-e4d8-4d59-b658-637a5f28cc1a.jpg',39078640,10,'45.51623','-122.58193',1,6,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,41,4.98,12893173),(566,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12900085','Quiet Neighborhood near Glendoveer','Great single story home with two-car garage and a fenced back yard, one block from Glendoveer golf course, and its surrounding nature trail. Ten minutes to the airport and Cascade Station, 20 minutes to downtown. One block to TriMet bus lines. <br /><br />The City of Portland requires a minimum 31 day stay at this home.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-12900085/original/7cc1e3e2-7d80-47b9-bb24-7d84e9c40681.jpeg',40218250,71,'45.53506','-122.51303',1,6,2.00,3.00,4.00,135.00,31,120,3,5.00,12900085),(567,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12954149','Tortoise Room @1234 HOUSE in SE PDX','An artist-made guest room in a renovated 1902-built house near Southeast Hawthorne, Belmont, Division & Downtown. Walking distance to variety of restaurants, bars, theaters, shops, grocery stores, parks & public transit. OUTSIDE ENTRANCE & PRIVATE LUXURY RESTROOM. Memory-foam queen bed, number-code locks, WiFi. Shared kitchen, dining room, living room, laundry, canoe, outdoor patios, record collection, piano/musical instruments.','1234 House is in the Buckman neighborhood of Southeast Portland, which is dense with homes 100-plus years old, and, like most of Portland, is experiencing a wave of new, modern consruction. 1234 House is a mile from the Willamette River, which separates the eastside of Portland and the westside city center. The house is nestled between Hawthorne Boulevard and Belmont Street, both lined with restaurants, bars, shops, theaters and music venues. A few blocks down the street is Col. Summers Park, a popular meet up spot to hang in the summer, especially on Monday Funday, and especially if you are down to play a mean game of dodgeball.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-12954149/original/dd30de5a-8122-4c8e-a16a-8723b046d64d.jpeg',30708290,32,'45.51437','-122.64566',2,2,3.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,1,1125,267,4.84,12954149),(568,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12955575','Historic Mississippi District - Centrally Located','Located in the heart of the Historic Mississippi District. Fantastic destination neighborhood with many retail shops and restaurants and centrally located to everything Portland has to offer. <br /><br />Main level unit of 1920\'s duplex. Make yourself at home! Charming, comfortable and clean. <br /><br />Max Yellow Line: 10 minute walk west.<br />Vancouver / Williams Corridor: 10 minute walk east<br />Downtown: 10 minute drive or 20 Max ride <br /><br />Perfect for 2 - 4 adults. May not be best suited for children.','Historic Mississippi Neighborhood has become a destination over the years. Full of restaurants, bars and shopping. Walking distance to the Williams / Vancouver Corridor and close to Alberta Arts District.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/749dcff3-5019-4263-bf30-d35b3d0c3826.jpg',44840316,9,'45.55043','-122.67313',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,136.00,2,30,301,4.93,12955575),(569,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12970336','Spacious modern and private in Alberta Arts Area','Foodies paradise in quintessential hip neighborhood of Portland. Walking distance to Alberta Arts District with the best restaurants in Portland, unique shops and galleries. Two blocks to famous Kennedy School. 1/2 a block to a major bus line. 10 minutes from the PDX Airport and Downtown.  Apartment is clean, new and modern. High speed internet. HDTV\'s in bedroom and living room. Private entrance. Beautiful private garden. Our place is good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.','Great part of town for foodies. Ripe, Gumba, Wilder, Urdeneta, Salt and Straw, Bollywood Theater, Bernie\'s Southern Bistro, Kennedy School, Common Ground Wellness Center plus dozens of other restaurants are within walking distance. One block from main bus line. 10 minute drive to downtown and airport. Portland’s most eclectic and best loved neighborhood.<br /><br />Concordia is one of Portland’s most diverse neighborhoods, we pride ourselves on that face, as well as our neighborhood’s reputation for being a hub for the arts. Alberta Street Arts District is located within Concordia with dozens of Portland\'s best restaurants, food carts, shops and galleries. McMenamin\'s Kennedy School is also a short walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-12970336/original/8ed73558-d1af-4b2e-9a7d-0a500e1a2dd0.jpg',3888703,1,'45.56351','-122.62566',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,115.00,2,30,170,5.00,12970336),(570,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/12972054','15 minutes to downtown -Short Term Available','Quiet neighborhood, on bus line, <br />New Queen bed./Cotton Sheets. Nice eastern light in room. Comfortable place to enjoy the city.  15 minutes from downtown.  30 minutes from Pinot Noir Wine Country.  Sit on the front porch with coffee in the morning or a glass of wine in the afternoon.  Light breakfast available, usually something fresh from the oven.<br />For longer stays: Kitchen available before 8:30PM. Please leave kitchen as you found it—Be respectful of my home','Maplewood Coffee house is a short walk. Serving breakfast & lunch. Good wine & beer selection and great prices. Open 8am-2pm -Sunday, Monday, Thursday <br />Closed Tuesday/Wednesday <br />8am-6:00pm Friday/Saturday <br />Old Market Pub is also a nice walk away. Pub food, micro beer, pool, outside seating. 11am-10pm daily.<br />Multnomah Village is nearby with many restaurants choices.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1af02117-cd66-43d3-b4b6-e12195c23e03.jpg',71376038,75,'45.47448','-122.73908',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,1,120,146,4.93,12972054),(571,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13015826','Walkable Hawthorne guest suite - Cute and cozy','Our house is located in the heart of the eclectic Hawthorne District, within walking distance to some of Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brew-pubs, distilleries, craftspeople, and just over a mile from downtown via bike, walking, or frequent bus service.','This neighborhood is quite unique, even by Portland standards. The primary reason why Sunnyside is such a remarkable area is that it encompasses two of the most vibrant and well-known streets (also known as Districts) in the city – Belmont and Hawthorne.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13015826/original/a7a4907e-506d-4bb9-b5d1-4977abcb1304.jpeg',19266,16,'45.5148','-122.61906',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,2,1125,75,4.96,13015826),(572,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13018859','Wes Anderson inspired historical private apt.','Turn of the century/Wes Anderson Inspired converted lower level basement of an 1890s house.  Great proximity to Downtown and public transportation, as well as all the cool stuff to do in N Portland. We are a block  away from Mississippi Ave. and close to N. Williams and Freeway access to I-5.<br />You will have a private entry from the front of the house. Our place is good for couples, business travelers, friends, and families (with kids). We do not allow smoking of any substances in the home.','Into music? Check out the Mississippi Studio Calendar to see if your favorite band is playing just down the street during your stay.  Foodie? Gluten-free? Vegan or vegetarian? - We have plenty of options within a few blocks! The N. Mississippi area is a great spot for anyone who wants to eat, drink, and browse local shops.<br /><br />Love vegan or vegetarian food?  We have several top-quality local spots for veggie dishes close by: Victoria, Moberry, and The Sudra.<br /><br />Love local beer?   We have fantastic local breweries in the neighborhood: Stormbreaker, Ecliptic, Ex Novo,  Migration, and Grains of wraith.  Head to the nearby Alberta neighborhood for Great Notion (Our favorite).  Also,  We have a recently opened distillery (Shine) just a few blocks away.  They are the only distillery + grill in the city (we LOVE their homemade gin options)<br /><br />Love coffee?  We have several great options for local coffee.  Our favorite standby is Fresh Pot, just around the corner, but we ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7d5221c1-2474-475d-a69a-b22c8bfb9f20.jpg',25461561,9,'45.55041','-122.67392',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,110.00,2,30,472,4.98,13018859),(573,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13066954','Warm,inviting,home in heart of Multnomah Village.','The home is in quaint Multnomah Village, walk to Gabriel Park, and the village, for fun places to eat and shop. Perfect for the weekend getaway or business trip. Home is very charming with many fountains and serene atmosphere.','You will enjoy the quietness of our beautiful little neighborhood. Have a nice stroll to the park while taking in the scenery. Or grab a bite to eat in the many restaurants available within walking distance','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d021ac0b-f1a3-465f-b4fc-