on. A comfortable home thoughtfully designed for work or play with modern decor, warmth and tranquility. Nature and city on the Willamette River. Calm, positive vibe. High speed internet, TV, pool & hot tub, deeded parking, private washer/dryer. Onsite security & convenience store. Located on 15 mile riverwalk close to transit. No chores, no fees, no taxes on 31+ nights, no smoking, no children, no pets.','This Portland waterfront condominium is on the banks of the Willamette River in a convenient location. City center, NW Portland & Pearl District, and south waterfront medical community (dental school, Oregon Health Sciences University, etc) are easily accessed by car, bike, on foot, or by street car. Nearby MAX light rail lines provide easy connections to airport or suburbs. Safe, gated condo complex with secure parking and patrols. Easy access to work or play. Nature in the city, stunning views, modern tranquility, perfect location.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTMwNzkxNTQ%3D/original/235c88c6-b7da-42e5-b913-f6c3096029c9.jpeg',17264703,43,'45.527034759521484','-122.67161560058594',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,79.00,31,350,89,4.94,13079154),(576,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13097045','Modern Tiny House in Portland','Come stay in our award winning tiny house, featured in Portland Monthly, Dwell, and Curbed! Our home was featured on the  AIA Modern Homes Tour of Portland in Spring 2016.<br /><br />250 sq ft., 1 block away from restaurants, locally owned shops, bars, a Whole Foods, and great access to public transportation.<br /><br />You have your own private entrance to the tiny house, so you don\'t ever have to worry about hearing footsteps overhead from being in a basement apartment.','We have a great neighborhood!  We are one block away from some amazing bars and restaurants. There are convenience stores, supermarkets, and coffee shops within walking distance. We are very close to public transportation (downtown busses are both 1 block and 4 blocks from the house).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/542c99cd-4eb7-4a4f-88b7-45c2827efd2f.jpg',24172332,12,'45.52501','-122.63472',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,378,4.98,13097045),(577,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13097670','Tibbetts Coop - A beautiful SE Portland urban farm','Tibbetts Coop is located on a double cul-de-sac, where you will feel like you are in the country when you are really in beautiful inner SE Portland. Bring your walking shoes so you can walk through the neighborhood to SE Division to find coffee shops, cart pods, tap houses, cafes, restaurants, and bars to suit everyone, or stay at the coop to relax under a tree or on the deck.  Small dogs can be approved on a case-by-case basis (fees apply).','Our neighborhoods are what makes Portland so wonderful. I live in a close-knit neighborhood where it is peaceful. It\'s a pleasure to walk through the neighborhood to SE Division where you can eat at some of the best restaurants Portland has to offer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e406c123-6e56-41b3-a1d8-8cff314d1c37.jpg',62110493,8,'45.500511','-122.620216',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,87.00,2,1125,165,4.97,13097670),(578,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13102888','Sabin Neighborhood home-month to month rental','This apartment is about 800 sq ft with 2 bedrooms and one bathroom.','Our place is close to Extracto Coffee Roasters, grain & Gristle, Pok Pok Noi, Vendetta, Prost!, Tasty and Sons, Tin Shed, Bamboo, Pine Street Biscuits, Bye and Bye and Whole Foods.. You’ll love our place because of the location, the outdoors space, and the ambiance. Our place is good for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, families (with kids), and furry friends (pets).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5a0b7b5e-94fa-4632-af05-e61f06ffdfba.jpg',21193811,14,'45.5541','-122.65974',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,135.00,30,365,24,5.00,13102888),(579,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13117227','Perfect Cozy Get Away, close in SE Portland','The private guest suite is in our newly remodeled, earthquake retrofit lower level with a separate entrance at the back of the house.   The kitchenette includes: microwave, toaster oven, hot water kettle, mini refrig, plates and utensils.  An Instant Pot is available upon request.<br /><br />We are located on a quiet family friendly street, but with quick access to the rest of the city.  Walking distance to restaurants, 2 parks, groceries and bus or Max train downtown or to the airport.','We are within walking distance to restaurants/coffee shops on Gladstone (4 blocks) and hipster dining and shopping on Clinton/Division (10-15 blocks).  There are sweet kids on the block for playing and very kind neighbors if needed.<br />Powell Park is around the corner and across 1 street (26th and Powell).  There is a public, outdoor swimming pool at Creston Park (42nd and Powell).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bc43b171-ba36-4081-b505-c2ad60b49448.jpg',72968932,67,'45.49617','-122.63833',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,68.00,3,1125,84,4.92,13117227),(580,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13127022','Updated basement apartment, close in NE Portland','Come enjoy Portland!  We have a basement apartment with separate entrance blocks from Alberta Arts District, the Peninsula Park Rose Garden and the Dekum Triangle where Breakside Brewery lives.  10-15 minute drive from the airport, Mississippi Street, downtown and the Moda Center (formerly known as the Rose Garden).   Cable television and 1gig wifi.<br /><br />Accessory short term rental expires 08-26-26<br /> 24ASTR-PER-00302','Our neighborhood is the best, new great restaurants open up all the time near us, it is an area of Portland that is exploding.  If you are thinking about moving to Portland this is a good opportunity to see everything that NE Portland has to offer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dd7e801e-ab92-45a8-9821-0093cdde7692.jpg',8119693,29,'45.56586','-122.6547',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,59.00,2,30,446,4.92,13127022),(581,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13192008','Bike\'N\'Roll Craftsman + Free Bikes for Your Stay','Bike\'N\'Roll Craftsman: Bicycle Tourism, <br />See Portland by bike-Biking Score 95! <br /><br />GUESTS RAVE: \"I can bike everywhere!\"<br /><br />■ Beautiful 900 sf w/the details of a 111 year-old Craftsman <br />■ Bright - lots of windows - high ceilings <br />■ Relax & rejuvenate on the front porch with a cup of coffee<br />■ Near bus & max train - so you can bicycle even farther! <br />■ 100s of shops, restaurants & everything you want to see within biking distance!<br />■ Ranked 2nd in the CNBC\'s most bicycle-friendly cities in the US!','Brooklyn is a unique working class neighborhood with beautiful 100 year old houses. We are near the Spring Water Corridor, the Rhododendron garden, West Moreland, Division Street, Brooklyn neighborhood park, Aladdin Theater, and Rose City Coffee.<br /><br />Brooklyn neighborhood has a biking score of 98!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTMxOTIwMDg%3D/original/5b726e55-05c0-4552-8607-18c8b047a669.jpeg',53232555,56,'45.49332','-122.6549',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,14,6,5.00,13192008),(582,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13247486','Creative & Clean Bungalow in Portland Hot Spot','Welcome to The ArtHaus. Soak up the sun on the patio of this creatively crafted home. Inside, polished concrete floors combine with classic finishes and attention to detail, including a sliding timber door. Vibrant color pops abound, not least from the original artworks. Accepting guests and implementing extra cleaning protocols. Excellent wireless internet speeds!','The Mississippi neighborhood has quickly become one of Portland\'s most coveted foodie areas, with such names as Por Que No, Tasty and Sons, Ox, Gravy, Samurai Blue, and Mee Sen minutes from the doorstep. Great breweries, coffee shops and lots of shopping too! Portlands Original Food Carts are just a block away!!! Reach downtown in just minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13247486/original/9c2f55ed-c28e-4a43-8cdd-7f754f8e6e3c.jpeg',6416589,9,'45.55453','-122.6777',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,109.00,1,1125,1078,4.97,13247486),(583,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13260893','Secret Garden Guest House, Multnomah Village','2016 renovated backyard cottage located in \"The Heart of Portland,\" the historic, now trendy Multnomah Village neighborhood next to The French Quarter! A quiet residential area in the Southwest quadrant of Portland. It\'s a quick walk to unique shops and great restaurants. It\'s a 5-mile drive to downtown. It\'s complete w/ radiant floors, 2 bedrooms, full bathroom, full kitchen, dining & living room. Wireless Smart TV w/ Netflix, and an entertainment cabinet with games, puzzles, etc.','☆ We are in the historic Multnomah Village neighborhood, Portland\'s family friendly village in the heart of the city.  There are plenty of restaurants, cafe\'s and shops to explore! We are also walking distance to the beautiful Gabriel Park, a 90 acre park with stunning views of the Coast Range. We are only 5 miles South of downtown\'s center. George Rogers Park river access is 6.9 miles away, and refreshing on a hot day!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/22bd88a3-dd79-423a-8a42-020014a022a2.jpg',4441147,18,'45.46638','-122.71617',1,5,1.00,2.00,6.00,125.00,2,28,453,4.93,13260893),(584,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13264525','Private Apartment. Fully Stocked. Northeast','Brand new modern Portland apartment! This basement unit is in an historic neighborhood and close to great spots like Alberta Street, The Kennedy School, and New Seasons. You\'ll love the bright open layout and comfy couches, bed, and pillows. It\'s stocked with everything you need and perfect for your visit.<br /><br />Use of washer and dryer is available for long term  (28 days +) guests only. A $60 fee per month for use. Ask Stephani!','Great neighborhood close to Alberta corridor! Alberta park is only a few blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f28d7316-198f-41b2-b39c-795f8c170fca.jpg',847543,1,'45.56666','-122.6391',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,225.00,30,1125,107,4.71,13264525),(585,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13276888','Airy Alberta Bungalow','Portland home with 2 Bedrooms, 2 Bath and a den located close-in area of NE Portland.  Just a short walk to the heart of the Alberta Arts district, with many desirable restaurants and bars. A quick drive to Downtown Portland\'s desirable amenities.<br /><br />Pets are negotiable but must be approved by owner prior to booking. There will be additional monthly cleaning fee of $150 per month for guests with pets.','Located just a short walk to the heart of the Alberta Arts district with numerous restaurants, coffee shops, parks, retail and more! Just two blocks to Portland’s best BBQ restaurant Podnah’s Pit!   <br /><br />You\'ll find it\'s just a short drive to downtown Portland and you are just minutes from some of the most desired restaurants & bars the city has to offer.  <br /><br />Alberta Park is 2 blocks away with paved walking paths, picnic areas, playground & basketball/tennis courts.    <br /><br />You\'ll find most of the amenities you could need right in the area. New Seasons Market and Safeway are less than a mile away.<br /><br />Pets are negotiable but must be approved by owner prior to booking. There will be additional monthly cleaning fee of $150 per month for guests with pets.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13276888/original/919b8a07-99d0-4e69-a522-24b09a6c1a1a.jpeg',45926254,29,'45.56571','-122.64774',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,123.00,30,1125,36,4.92,13276888),(586,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13298544','MB’s Guest House.  Cozy 2 bedroom in SE Portland.','My place is close to restaurants, bars and shopping on Woodstock Avenue and Foster Avenue. My place is good for couples, business travelers, and families (with kids). There is a lovely patio surrounded by gardens where travelers can unwind and relax.<br /><br />My home is fully permitted/licensed by the city of Portland.  I am a completely legal, tax paying Airbnb host.<br /><br />I provide filtered water and metal water bottles.  Hope no one needs to buy bottled water.','We are just a 20 minute walk to the Woodstock neighborhood business district with many restaurants, coffee shops, bakeries, public library, hardware store and yes,  a great Goodwill.<br /><br />In the other direction we are 6 minutes from Foster street with its long line of coffee shops, restaurants and bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d0e9868d-1442-4a21-9788-3dfb66d36df4.jpg',75083765,65,'45.48725','-122.60121',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,171.00,3,28,187,4.96,13298544),(587,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13318747','Two Bedroom/One Bath Flat','No Lodging Taxes if you book for thirty-one (31) nights!<br /><br />This is a private two bedroom upstairs condo located above furnished rentals in Mt. Tabor.  <br />There are two bedrooms, a living room, full kitchen and three piece bath is locate off the entrance stairway with the bedrooms located on opposite sides of the living space.  The bedrooms do not share walls with each other.<br /><br />Keyless entry on the home\'s entrance and on each bedroom.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/89efbd46-fed5-4667-aaf8-e3bd6ff4a5ca.jpg',828435,15,'45.51225','-122.61089',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,60.00,30,90,12,4.67,13318747),(588,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13332861','StokeWood Lodge','Pet friendly!<br />StokeWood- Country in the City, within a 100 year old orchard. Stay in for Privacy & Solitude,  a respite from City Life. <br /><br />4 mile bike/drive to Portland Center & OHSU.  Walk to Multnomah Village for Food/Pubs, Shops Near Willamette River & The Pearl.<br /><br />Day trip the Columbia Gorge, Pacific Ocean, Wine Country, Cascade Mountains, Golf & Cultural events.<br /><br />StokeWood; for Couples, Solos, Business Travelers & Pets. Hosts offer as much, or as little, opinion as you seek!','Absolute quiet yet near the city.  <br />Multnomah Village and Hillsdale, our desirable little towns & restaurants are within walking distance in both directions.  Ours is the topmost property on the hill.  Peaceful and charmingly slow paced.  A few blocks from Gabriel Park, Southwest Community Center & The MJCC.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/17151afe-ba11-468e-a872-9493e29339b8.jpg',28410788,17,'45.47767','-122.71432',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,107.00,30,365,209,4.80,13332861),(589,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13342213','Bright & Fun loft in gorgeous central neighborhood','Sweet studio in the convenient,  beautiful, historic Irvington neighborhood. We\'ve used vintage furniture, found objects, and castaways to add charm and the \"Portland\" touch to our space. Perfect for one or two people to enjoy the best of Portland. It\'s only a 10 minute trip downtown, even less to the Moda or convention center and a short stroll from a multitude of coffee shops, restaurants, bars, pubs, theaters and boutiques. <br />We have a 2nd Airbnb! See the listing on my profile page','Irvington is one of grandest old neighborhoods in Portland and the most central. It features beautiful turn of the century homes, large lots, giant trees and and an awesome location. It is great for walking, biking, or a quick Uber or Lyft ride. Right down the street you can enjoy coffee shops, bakeries, several restaurants (35 within a 10 min walk), bookshops, happy hour, microbrew, groceries, boutiques and more. <br />We are also a short walk away from downtown, the MODA Center, and the convention center, 15 minutes from the airport, and 30 minutes from the Columbia River Gorge. <br />Close by neighborhoods within walk or bike distance are the Lloyd District, Mississippi Ave, Alberta Arts District, downtown, and the Central Eastside.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-13342213-unapproved/original/5bd7af17-0bce-44a3-89ae-aefde8362450.JPEG',66230687,7,'45.53534','-122.64635',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,98.00,2,8,230,4.97,13342213),(590,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13362534','The Alberta Arts Hideaway','This NEW 500 sq foot one bedroom apartment (outfitted for two) is steps away from Alberta Art District and close to Mississippi Ave, Dekum and Concordia. We are located in the HOTTEST arts and entertainment district in Portland! There are many restaurants, bars, arts studios, cafes, theatres etc in the area-- you\'ll never be at a loss for something to do!  We\'re also centrally located and a short bus/max ride from downtown or the airport!  Public transit is close and abundant! All welcome!','Alberta is one of the hottest and hippest entertainment/art centric districts in the city!  It is a MUST to see when coming to Portland!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13362534/original/9058bd67-3f51-41c3-aa90-b00100100628.jpeg',28894059,14,'45.5587','-122.65256',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,92.00,2,12,136,4.98,13362534),(591,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13381115','Craftsman with Hot Tub!','Come stay in the highly desired Laurelhurst Neighborhood for the summer! Our home is close (less than half a mile) to 15+ restaurants, a theater, a large (32 acre) park, and a host of fun shops and entertainment. The house can comfortable sleep 6 people and is perfect for a family (we are a family of 5), a couple looking for a getaway, or wanderers who want to explore the Pacific Northwest!','LOCATION, LOCATION, LOCATION!!!<br /><br />Our home is in the heart of Portland! <br /><br />We are: <br /><br />500ft away from Music Millennium (huge independent music store)<br />500ft away from Laurelhurst Market (Steak restaurant and butcher)<br /><br />0.2 miles away from Laurelhurst Park (beautiful 32 Acre public park)<br /><br />0.3 miles away from Laurelhurst Theater (Privately owned theater)<br />0.3 miles away from a plethora of restaurants that include <br />    Indian, Mexican, America, Diner, Ice Cream, Coffee, Italian, and French <br /><br />0.3 miles away from Whole Foods Market','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13381115/original/5ffa7091-fc60-