 Nature Play park. So much to LOVE about Sellwood!','Sellwood has a friendly village feel. It continues to evolve with new shops, restaurants, services and food carts moving in regularly. We find ourselves leaving the neighborhood less and less because most of our needs can be met right in our own neighborhood. Need coffee? There are 6 local coffee shops within walking distance. Tea, instead? Two blocks away, there is a red caboose that has been converted to a tea shop called Tea Chai Te! Hungry? Within easy walking distance, there are 2 cart pods with various cuisines represented, and MANY restaurants along SE 13th. Eating in? Our New Seasons Market is 4 blocks away. They have everything for cooking a full meal and also have hot nourishing prepared foods. And Grand Central Bakery has some of the best sandwiches around. Shopping? Sellwood used to be famous for its antique shops. It still has some, but now there are many other shops, including toys, clothing, gift, spice and craft supplies. There\'s even an inviting shop dedicated to board','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f372f60b-404d-4c2a-ab62-fc7961f69946.jpg',76194443,20,'45.465755462646484','-122.64928436279297',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,168.00,3,27,216,4.93,13394624),(594,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13415468','✿✿ Portlandia Garden Cottage ✿✿','Privacy in Portlandia.  Enjoy privacy in the heart of the SE Hawthorne/Division neighborhood.  My efficient home has peaceful patio and lots of natural light.  It is a stand-alone tiny house.  Level 2 EV Charging available<br /><br />TV.  Full Kitchen.  Heart of SE Portland<br /><br />Well furnished with the necessities for cooking splendid meals.  Or if you choose, it is a short walk to restaurants and food carts.<br /><br />Walk score of 89!  Downtown is close by car or bus.  Level 2 EV Charging station is also available.','My neighborhood close-in, so park your car and explore on foot.  With a walk score of 89, there are numerous shopping, eating and drinking establishments all within several blocks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13415468/original/188a334d-188b-44ab-a5ed-ca550f04f21d.jpeg',44210890,8,'45.50775','-122.6229',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,58.00,4,30,336,4.88,13415468),(595,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13434960','Stylish, Bright Townhouse - Nob Hill 2B/1B','Stylish and charming fully furnished two-story townhouse in Portland\'s historic Alphabet District. Outside: a peaceful courtyard in front and patio space out back. Inside: an updated and quiet space with two bedrooms, fully outfitted kitchen, in-unit laundry, and many special amenities.  Includes secure off-street car and bike parking.  Amenities include free wifi and cable TV.','This is Portland\'s most complete and charming neighborhood with a walk score of 95 \"Walker\'s Paradise\" and bike score of 96 \"Biker\'s Paradise\". There\'s easy access to many bus routes and the Portland Streetcar route that serves the Pearl, downtown and PSU. Easy freeway access connects you to the region. The unit is within easy walking distance to five major grocery stores, including New Seasons and the Co-op, just a short walk away. Virtually everything you need, from the basics (Post Office and groceries) to the many dozens of boutiques, bars and restaurants, can be found within a comfortable walking distance in and around famous NW 23rd Street. Just one block to Wallace Park, two blocks to a lovely branch library and a few blocks to award-winning Good Samaritan Hospital.   Walk to Forest Park an oasis in the City. The neighborhood is located in very close-in Northwest Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d57d7709-5dae-4db3-938f-b5ec44abdffa.jpg',14482835,27,'45.53537','-122.70468',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,115.00,30,60,33,4.97,13434960),(596,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13447534','Old World Luxury in the City.','My place is close to Downtown, Portland. The Pearl District. NW 23rd area. My neighborhood is filled with bars and restaurants but still quiet at night. You’ll love my place because of the high ceilings, the French gourmet kitchen, the comfy beds, landscaped backyard, luxurious bathroom. 3 beds total-1 King, 1 Queen & 1 Full. Dedicated workspace too. Nice outdoor space and large front porch.  My place is good for families (with kids) and big groups. 7 blocks from mass transit light rail, Max.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTM0NDc1MzQ%3D/original/ef623198-d6dd-425f-b05a-476d3515cfb6.jpeg',76780292,13,'45.56514','-122.69379',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,178.00,1,1125,11,5.00,13447534),(597,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13494359','The Homestead on 17th with Sauna add-on','The Homestead is a well-loved bungalow in the Sellwood/West Moreland neighborhood in SE Portland.  Don\'t be fooled, this is a big house!  Our place is only footsteps to Saburo\'s Sushi House Restaurant, Moreland Theatre, 13 Virtues Brewing, Westmoreland Nature Park, and Cork Screw Wine Bar. It\'s good for couples, business travelers, and families (with kids of all ages).  Public transportation is very close, too!<br />If you\'ve stayed before,  the basement remodel is ready and is now our guest space.','The Homestead is located in West Moreland, just north of the ever popular Sellwood neighborhood with all of it\'s delicious restaurants, the Wednesday Farmer\'s Market, and awesome West Moreland Nature park.   There is a lot to do and explore just footsteps away!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ac4b0940-37cc-4837-928f-27999e20d328.jpg',38278246,20,'45.474737432334514','-122.64920693309269',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,1125,199,4.83,13494359),(598,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13534643','Enjoy convenience &  class, Portland, OR','ENTIRE CONDO. <br />Close to OHSU, VA, Dental School , PSU and Downtown . You’ll love this large loft with its incredible location, excellent amenities including concierge services, FREE SECURE UNDERGROUND PARKING, biking and walking paths along the Willamette River.  The views are amazing . <br />Suitable for couples, solo and business travelers.<br />LONG TERM STAYS WELCOME - ask for rates as they can vary based on time of year and duration of stay. <br /><br />31 DAY MINIMUM STAY','Our vibrant downtown is yours to explore a short distance away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a3456a4e-8ac8-4d88-8cd4-06ccad4f8bbe.jpg',75800876,22,'45.49552','-122.67012',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,85.00,30,1000,24,5.00,13534643),(599,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13564185','Sunny Hawthorne Condo','No Lodging Taxes if you book for thirty-one (31) nights!<br /><br />Located in beautiful Mt. Tabor. Each little home is vintage mid-century. With wood floors, tiled kitchens and bathrooms. The location is fabulous. Restaurants, shopping and parks are close by.  Street parking usually within a block or so.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13564185/original/c96d507c-4a60-46ba-ae08-1cd11f252dc7.jpeg',828435,15,'45.51211','-122.61075',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,48.00,30,125,19,4.84,13564185),(600,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13566259','Alberta Arts Sweet Spot /Perfect for Groups,4baths','Welcome to The Ginkgo House, where the sweet independent nature of Alberta Arts welcomes our 5 bdrm. /4 bath home. It has all the amenities you could ask for, while being located steps from restaurants, coffee shops, bars, liquor, pharmacy, dispensary, groceries, & local boutiques. We offer fast WiFi and free residential street parking. Come enjoy The Ginkgo House where the whimsical, luxurious, and practical converge in our iconic close- in NE neighborhood. Our block boasts free street parking','❤︎ As far as Portland locations go, ours is perfect! Tucked into a residential neighborhood of NE Portland, just 10 minutes to the Convention Center, MODA, or PDX, the Alberta Arts District is a vibrant locally -focused arts and foodie paradise – quintessential Portland and a destination unto itself. Yet also easily accessible to downtown, to the Coast and the Gorge, and to the greater Portland area.<br />We are just three blocks to vibrant Alberta Street, Kennedy School, New Seasons Grocery, Walgreens, the dispensary and the liquor store. Minutes on foot to coffeehouses, bars, and restaurants headlined by well-known chefs: farm-to-table cuisine, fusion meals, craft cocktails, artisan bread, freshly roasted coffee, and so much more – a real foodie haven!<br /><br />❤︎ Here, we’re a city not just of eaters, but of explorers: in Portland and the Alberta Arts District, in particular, we brew, ferment (kombucha and cider), distill liqueur, frequent taprooms, offer growler fill-ups, and we ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13566259/original/f934375c-fd9c-4528-8863-243a1b71c0ec.jpeg',56920726,1,'45.56181','-122.63371',1,10,4.00,5.00,9.00,339.00,3,200,108,4.94,13566259),(601,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13573376','Cozy Hawthorne Condo','Located in beautiful Mt. Tabor.  Each home is vintage mid-century. With wood floors, tiled kitchens and bathrooms.  The location is fabulous.  Restaurants, shopping and parks are close by.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a60dd5fb-ec60-4f2d-8475-5b41e0f6a531.jpg',828435,15,'45.51211','-122.61083',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,49.00,30,240,36,4.92,13573376),(602,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13601516','Cozy, quiet private room and beautiful back yard','Charming and cozy private room with Queen size bed, private bath and quiet, beautiful, relaxing back yard. 10 minutes by car from Portland International Airport, 5 minutes to Hollywood District, 5 minutes to Alberta Arts District and Fremont Street restaurants, bars and coffee shops. Close to major freeways and transit centers, 15 min by car to downtown Portland. A serene neighborhood within easy walk to parks.<br />Ideal home away from home for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.','Several mature trees visited frequently by birds, and quiet streets with long blocks. It is easy to decompress here, and it can be easy to forget that the neighborhood is only 15 minutes away from the central city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1719379a-4f6f-47ad-8e66-427e63dfe59a.jpg',53052399,21,'45.55927','-122.58821',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,30,1125,76,4.95,13601516),(603,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13622008','Fully furnished ADU In Heart of Alberta Arts Dist.','New fully furnished ADU available for short term or long term stay. Right in the heart of Alberta Arts District. Access from 27th street or Alley parking. Custom queen wall bed. Full kitchen ~ hickory cabinets, granite countertops, fridge, range, microwave, disposal. Full bathroom inc. soaking tub shower combo. Private fenced patio with outdoor furniture. Washer/Dryer. Electric ductless heat and AC. All utilities included and high speed internet. HDTV with ROKU. 2195 per month or 99 per night.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0effd31f-e04a-4e12-a434-2ae26ee7f102.jpg',45164806,1,'45.55945','-122.63757',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,95.00,30,1125,171,4.94,13622008),(604,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13623856','a Sweet Studio in the heart of NE neighborhood','The cozy studio has its own entrance and a big window facing the garden that lets in lots of light and smells of herbs. Great for those looking for a peaceful space to stay. it is located in tbe basement level.','Quiet and peaceful yet accessible to Alberta arts district (15 -20 minute walk), 42nd restaurants. Great yoga studio, coffee shop and vintage store a few blocks away. It is 30-40 minute bus ride to downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/da37a8c0-041c-4f22-b4d1-39fb8c0bdc36.jpg',2038566,1,'45.5699','-122.62951',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,120,49,4.71,13623856),(605,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13624774','Cozy Vintage Cottage in the Woods','The studio cottage is located in an east Portland neighborhood bordering the city of Gresham. It is close to public transport (near a MAX light rail station), the airport and outdoor activities (the Columbia Gorge; Mt Hood) and is a 20-30 min drive to downtown. It\'s cozy (eclectic vintage style), a wooded 1-acre setting within the city limits, and has secure premises (electric gate). Our place is good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.','We are 20 minutes from the airport and on the eastern edge of the Portland city limits. We are about a half hour drive from Multnomah Falls and the Gorge and 10 miles from downtown Portland. Our one-acre property is in a developed neighborhood so it is not rural. But it has over 40 fir trees, many 150’ tall, and lots of other plantings that people say feels like an oasis.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-13624774/original/3b7fc571-e6ba-48dd-8579-5aedfe397003.jpg',18774457,76,'45.52269','-122.49979',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,120.00,2,30,529,4.99,13624774),(606,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13627002','Room in peaceful Montavilla home , private bath','Nestled between the Rose City Park and Montavilla neighborhoods, my serene home gives you a real taste of Portland neighborhood living, just 15 min. away from PDX and City Center. Work remotely by reserving the office adjacent the guest room + your private bath. Walk 3 blocks to the Rose City Golf Course (open to public) to be transported to an expansive green space, bursting with large oak trees. Drive minutes to Mt. Tabor or Rocky Butte  for phenomenal views of the city and its surroundings.','A quick trip over the I-84 overpass puts you in the lush and expansive Rose City Golf Course and Rosemont Bluff area, with a nice trail and beautiful views of Mt. Hood on a clear day. Great for long walks and fresh air. Head the other direction to check out bars and restaurants on Glisan Street. Easy access to the freeway means you can get anywhere pretty quickly.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cbe527f1-627c-4680-bdb9-8168a2486988.jpg',75240152,74,'45.53571','-122.58739',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,1,5.00,13627002),(607,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13660168','Clean, bright apartment in neighborhood home','You will feel at home in this bright, clean, cozy daylight basement apartment. Features include bedroom with gas fireplace, full kitchen, bathroom/shower, bonus room with large closet, and access to laundry room with washer/dryer, ironing board and iron. Located on a quiet residential street, you have a private entrance through the garden gate, on-street parking, and a 5-minute walk to restaurants, shops, and public transit downtown.','We live a block and a half from Multnomah Village; one of Portland’s many “near in” neighborhoods.  In the village you will find several restaurants, a book store, a bakery, shops for clothing, art, and antiques, and a store with an extensive selection of wines and craft beers.  We live a 15 minute walk from a large city park with walking and jogging trails, tennis courts, and a community center with indoor swimming pool and exercise room.  We love this neighborhood and we think you will, also.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/18ce20a2-8875-4450-9fb7-5630031831ae.jpg',5622521,18,'45.47037','-122.70991',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,2,14,281,4.96,13660168),(608,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13687944','Mt. Tabor Private Apartment','The apartment is close to trendy upper Hawthorne business district and Mt. Tabor Park. You’ll love the studio because of the location (close to downtown), the people, and the neighborhood. Perfect for walking, biking, and the use of public transportation to get you where you need to be. It is ideal for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.','Mt. Tabor/Upper Hawthorne is a great place to be. Located blocks from trendy shops and eateries, it\'s close enough to the \"action\" but situated far enough to be quiet.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/039451c9-24d9-4724-81bf-6aa103bfb9ed.jpg',79737835,15,'45.51454','-122.61178',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,2,30,399,4.92,13687944),(609,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13750038','Beautiful Pearl District Loft with On-Site Parking','3 mo minimum stay per HOA rules. This gorgeous west-facing loft, with balcony & french doors is located in the heart of the Pearl District. Rent includes 1 reserved garage space with EV Charger. 1 block from the North Park Blocks, and steps away from the neighborhood\'s premier art galleries, restaurants, bars, fitness studios, and shopping, including Whole Foods and Powell\'s Books. 100% non-smoking building, with daily on-site concierge service. Fob key/code secure with 3 high-speed elevators.','Easily one of Portland’s most desirable neighborhoods, the Pearl District is home to some of the city’s best known chefs and restaurants, world class art galleries, and vibrant shops and boutiques. Located in the heart of downtown, businesses ranging from finance and real estate to renowned advertising agencies and software firms can be found here, nestled among family-friendly parks that attract visitors and locals, many of whom call the neighborhood’s iconic residential buildings home. Formerly a neglected corridor of abandoned warehouses and railways, the Pearl District has earned a worldwide reputation for urban renaissance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0fdd9d70-09a8-420b-8c5f-0a89d202e96a.jpg',9510170,2,'45.52656','-122.68113',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,91,363,2,5.00,13750038),(610,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13790175','Historic Turret House w/ Gorgeous Modern Furniture','This isn\'t your standard rental w/ IKEA furniture & misleading photos! The Turret House sits on a large corner lot in Portland\'s most beautiful neighborhood (Irvington) and surrounded by stunning homes and tree-canopied streets. Broadway street is 3 blocks away & offers some of Portland’s favorite restaurants, bars, coffee shops, bookstores, grocers, & dispensaries. My partner & I are professional designers and we worked hard to blend traditional Spanish Californian design w/ modern simplicity.','Irvington is one of the country\'s largest historic neighborhoods and is centrally located for Eastside Culture while offering quick access to downtown via Broadway Ave. Irving Park is a 5 min walk from the house. Everything you would want to access in Portland is less than 2 miles away and most of it is within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dbbea51c-c54d-4244-a27d-16853c6b5607.jpg',373733,7,'45.53882','-122.64322',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,239.00,30,120,84,4.96,13790175),(611,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13790422','KERNS/ TimeOut\'s BEST Hood in US & 5th in WORLD!','Our place is very close-in to all things Portland, restaurants, shops, bars, movie theaters, etc. while still being a quiet garden oasis. Independent 1-bedroom apartment, one unit of a classic Portland craftsman duplex. Because of this, the property and large backyard is shared with us, so you may encounter children play and run around.','One of the best neighborhoods in town. Tree lined and unique landscaping every where. There are bars, restaurants, and even a movie theater are walking distance. Wonderful parks nearby too! This is a joggers paradise! Neighbors are friendly','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13790422/original/4bc09aae-b9cd-4fe7-90e6-2fb9cb2bdcfb.jpeg',10928596,12,'45.5262','-122.63326',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,91.00,4,90,59,4.85,13790422),(612,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13814896','Cozy Garden Cottage in the Heart of Richmond','A serene Guest Cottage nestled in a garden and located within walking distance to the local foodie restaurants. You’ll love the location and how quiet it is! The perfect set up for couples, solo travelers or business travel.<br /><br />It\'s open and bright. French doors, plenty of windows, and skylights to bring in natural light for an open feel. You\'ll be set up with a comfy mattress, quality linens and plush towels. Nothing more cozy than that! Don\'t forget about the Smart TV, work desk, and essentials!','We are located in a safe and quiet residential, tree-lined street in Portland\'s hottest neighborhood! Lovely and quiet, but just a few blocks from \"restaurant row\" (Division St.) and also easy walking to Hawthorne! Some local faves include Salt n’ Straw, the food cart alley off 37th, Blue Star Donuts, Little Big Burger, Atlas Pizza, Harlow, Waffle Window, Fried Egg I’m in Love, Olympia Provisions, Cibo, Farmhouse Kitchen Thai, St. Honore, Lauretta Jean’s, Stumptown Coffee, Petite Provence, The Automatic Bar, Sessionable, and SO much more. While we can\'t give out the address before booking for the safety of our team and Guests, you may view the approx. location on our listing or use nearby cross streets, SE Lincoln St. and SE 38th Avenue, as a point of reference!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13814896/original/aace05ac-9e9f-428f-ab49-1275b8ebaaa7.jpeg',3454923,8,'45.50643','-122.62425',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,1,21,593,4.93,13814896),(613,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13827370','Willamette Heights View','The Space: <br />Come experience quintessential PNW living at  Willamette Heights View apartment. Stay in our beautiful, light-filled, 2-story deluxe apartment perched .5 miles above NW 23rd Ave. and 2 doors down from Forest Park trails. Full kitchen,  backyard with mountains and river view, gas fireplace and hi-speed WiFi make this the ideal retreat/work  space.. My place is good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.  Please note that there is no TV :-)','Willamette Heights neighborhood is filled with old historic homes and nestled next to the largest urban park in the United States.  The amazingly beautiful natural area includes a multitude of wildlife and miles of walking paths.  Additionally,  my home is less than a mile away from great coffee shops, Dragontree spa, yoga studios, local grocery stores, and a plethora of trendy eating spots.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-13827370/original/18203321-7973-4173-9250-f7167a66f0c2.jpg',10354567,50,'45.53311','-122.71855',1,4,1.50,1.00,1.00,138.00,2,90,466,4.95,13827370),(614,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13856775','Sorta Summer House w/ sauna & outdoor shower','The guesthouse is a private oasis in the city. It\'s surrounded by fruit trees and tall Chinese Mountain bamboo. It\'s a quick walk to Woodlawn Park, great coffee, a bakery, pizza, whiskey bar, a brewery, seasonal farmers market, and minutes from Alberta Arts District.<br /><br />The airy, open floor plan is filled with natural light, mixed textiles and warm woods. A cedar-surround outdoor shower and private 5x7 Finnish sauna lend to the spa-like setting. Guests say it’s hard to leave!','Woodlawn\'s angled streets remind residents of a time when the streetcar depot was a major feature of the neighborhood. Our property is situated on a block of primarily 1920s bungalows, less than 2 blocks from an award-winning brewery, bakery, coffee shop, bars, and restaurants situated around a large city park. In the Summer, Woodlawn Park is known for movies on the lawn and Dekum Triangle hosts a small farmer\'s market. Less than 1 mile from our neighborhood are a couple of other shopping/dining destinations including on Killingsworth St/NE 30th Ave and the Alberta Arts District. Mississippi Avenue is just 2 miles West of us with more shopping and eating to explore. <br /><br />Even though this is a pretty quiet neighborhood overall, be advised that we are in the city so you\'ll hear the occasional siren, neighbors\' cars and music, neighborhood animals etc. We have blackout shades and provide earplugs if you\'re a light sleeper.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-13856775/original/daf8fc94-398a-4f4a-a7c7-bf4a52b942ea.jpeg',23464398,45,'45.56880569458008','-122.65646362304688',1,2,0.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,21,239,4.99,13856775),(615,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13900357','Woodlawn Cottage: Modern 2-br near Dekum Triangle','Woodlawn Cottage is a cozy, sleek, modern home for travelers of all kinds (couples, business travelers, travel nurses, & families!). Two well-appointed bedrooms flank a full bathroom, fully-stocked kitchen, and comfortable living room with a huge TV. We are walkable to the Dekum Triangle, Alberta Arts district, Mississippi Ave, and several parks. We provide everything you\'ll need, from shampoo to local coffee to blazing fast internet. We offer stays of 30-60 days. Welcome!','Located just blocks below the Dekum triangle, our home is in a quiet residential neighborhood but is walkable to a small neighborhood center with a variety of amazing brewpubs, restaurants, and coffeeshops. Just a little farther away, but still walkable, you can find the Alberta Arts district, which is home to dozens of restaurants, bars, boutiques, and beautiful shops. We are also close to three beautiful parks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/56ecd8d7-024c-4e53-b9a1-75903b21a082.jpg',10458442,45,'45.56939','-122.65227',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,99.00,30,60,202,4.81,13900357),(616,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13901912','Quaint & Cozy 1920\'s Bungalow','Our cozy 1920\'s Bungalow is nestled in-between Peninsula Park and the great restaurants, shops, and bars of North Williams, Mississippi Avenue and the Alberta Arts District.  <br />We allow pets on a case by case basis.<br />Washer and dryer and downstairs basement for storage is available to guests.','We are around the corner from Peninsula Park, and are within walking distance to great coffee shops & restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-13901912/original/d9b7d6d3-bbc2-4e2a-83b1-ca0f8601cd9d.jpeg',1332315,48,'45.56716','-122.67235',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,165.00,2,1125,84,4.94,13901912),(617,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13923118','Modern NW Apartment *free parking*','My house is on the street car line which runs between 5:30am-11:30pm depending on weekday or weekends, 3 blocks to Pearl District, 2 blocks to 21st/23rd Ave. Located close to the brewery blocks, lots of shopping, and dining! The neighborhood is easily walkable. Self check in, Full kitchen with basics for cooking, AC, W/D, Comcast cable with HBO in bedroom and living room with access to sign in to streaming services, WiFi, free street parking via digital residential guest pass will be provided.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/db5412d6-b4a1-438a-b298-a04dca38703e.jpg',52202264,27,'45.53157','-122.69081',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,129.00,2,29,300,4.94,13923118),(618,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13953547','★ 1 Block to Hawthorne! Remodeled! Walk Score: 92!','Centrally located in the Heart of Hawthorne, this gorgeous, newly renovated and spacious 1925 Craftsman home (with numerous upgrades and finishes) is within walking distance to some of the best eateries and coffee shops in Southeast PDX, including ¿Por Qué No?, Apizza Scholls, Fried Egg I\'m in Love, Dwaraka and Common Grounds. This incredible home is great for couples, business travelers and small families.','The Sunnyside neighborhood is located in Southeast Portland, which is home to plenty of locally-owned restaurants, bars, and shops. <br /><br />You can\'t get any closer to the action than at this house, which sits in the Heart of Hawthorne boulevard, with some of the city\'s most heralded restaurants, cafes, shops and bars just a block away, such as:<br /><br />-- The Waffle Window<br />-- ¿Por Qué No?<br />-- Apizza Scholls<br />-- Harlow<br />-- 3 Doors Down Café<br />-- Coava Coffee<br />-- Hawthorne Theatre<br />-- Crossroads Trading Co.<br />-- Buffalo Exchange<br />-- Powell’s Books on Hawthorne<br />-- New Seasons Market<br />-- ... and too many more to list!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-13953547/original/dc2b55da-bce1-461c-8dc0-5a3582b2bb9f.jpeg',70547018,16,'45.5123','-122.61768',1,5,2.00,2.00,5.00,155.00,2,1125,285,4.86,13953547),(619,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13973783','Inspired Hawthorne Craftsman','Beautifully furnished 1910 craftsman home with designer outdoor space in SE PDX with great kitchen and outdoor space.  The perfect place to get out and discover Portland\'s best or to just stay in and enjoy the comforts of the home in front of the wood-burning fire.<br />**Please read full description<br />2 bedrooms, 2 offices, 2 full bathrooms, Living room, Dining room, Kitchen','Our home is in one of the best locations in SE Portland. Just a half block off of Hawthorne, you get the benefit of a quiet home with a private backyard space, as well as being just steps from some of Portland’s most popular spots (¿Por que no?, Apizza Scholls, Baghdad Theatre, +)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e686c255-b487-4645-b551-86974a5977b1.jpg',1339136,16,'45.51263','-122.61412',1,5,2.00,3.00,3.00,292.00,3,1125,33,4.85,13973783),(620,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/13990506','Private Loft Apartment above my Photography Studio','A private loft apt with private entrance and  private Heat /AC system. It has  very quick access to the Portland International Airport, downtown Portland, and the epic Columbia River Gorge. The neighborhood offers dozens of diverse restaurants, brew pubs, wine bars, antique stores and delightful shops. A brief walk will take you to Mt. Tabor Park’s forested trails, beautiful open reservoirs and magnificent views of downtown Portland and Mt Hood.<br />Pets:  1 is acceptable dog,  I do not allow cats','Located just 10 minutes from the airport and minutes from downtown, in the vibrant Montavilla  neighborhood.  Relax and enjoy the private master bedroom, with a deck and private entrance. Located in the popular Montavilla neighborhood. Within a few blocks to restaurants, bars, shopping, and transportation.. The MAX line is an eight minute walk away. thin close walking distance to restaurants, bars, shopping, and transportation. Mississippi Ave, Williams St, and the Alberta Arts District are nearby. The MAX line is an eight minute walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/19249fa3-e884-453c-8e99-88b22fd8014b.jpg',13926479,10,'45.51953','-122.57447',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,12,120,228,4.93,13990506),(621,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14007930','Private room in Historic home in NW/Downtown PDX','Your private room in our 1905 Craftsman is only steps away from NW 23rd Ave. where you will find an endless amount of restaurants, bakeries, coffee spots and unique shops. Across from Wallace park and a couple blocks from Forest Park, with miles of forested hiking trails, streams and views. <br /><br />I am happy to help you with your visit and yet you will have all the privacy you want. It is a full size bed. You will pass through our common entry way to access your room. Limited shared kitchen use.','Our home is a classic 1905 Craftsman, located in the Alphabet District, a tree-lined downtown destination for shoppers searching unique experiences, European pastries, northwest coffees, Oregon micro-brews, art and five star dining. Just one block away, NW 23rd Ave. has endless shops, restaurants, night life and desserts. A few blocks in the other direction you can find yourself deep in the forest, hiking up to the Pittock Mansion (3.5 mile hike from our house) and enjoying the natural beauty of Forest Park. We live across the street from Wallace Park, an active greenspace destination.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9f4796d6-9a0a-41b6-a431-c54bcd1913b5.jpg',40342841,27,'45.53347','-122.70246',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,1,4,183,4.91,14007930),(622,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14055342','The Owl\'s Nest, NE Portland, Concordia','Located on a beautiful, quiet street popular with bikers, runners and walkers. Very private above garage apartment with separate entrance. Has its own small yard with deck, and BBQ. Minutes from PDX. Ample parking. <br />Walking distance to: The Kennedy School, New Seasons Market, Walgreens, Liquor store, Fernhill Park, Alberta Arts-shopping, restaurants, food, fun. <br />Great for: <br />Couples<br />Solo adventurers<br />Business travelers<br />Families-Pack n play, baby gate, car seat,high chair, books and toys!','Walking distance to many of NE Portland\'s destination spots such as The Kennedy School, Alberta Street, 42nd Ave and Fremont Ave. You will find some of the best restaurants, cafes, shopping and entertainment in Portland. Just a few blocks away you can spend the day at Fernhill Park where they have tennis courts, track, playground and lots of wide open space. Our neighborhood is filled with families, kids and people walking dogs. It\'s a super safe and friendly place to be.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/78c697cf-a966-45cd-b895-5aea7e3d0d21.jpg',1705386,1,'45.56917','-122.62751',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,139,4.95,14055342),(623,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14068580','F138','Freshly painted! Central A/C, hardwood floors. Fully equipped kitchen with vitamix, kitchen aid and other gadgets. You’ll love my place because of the ambiance. The house is kept simple and elegant for your relaxation and enjoyment. The kitchen is well stocked with anything you might need. Walking distance to an excellent paved biking/waking trail (springwater corridor), in a quite cul-de-sac, away from noise.','Clackamas Town Center - 6 miles (10 min)<br />Downtown Portland - 13 miles (20 min)<br />Government Camp (ski resort) - 44 miles (57 min)<br />MAX (Portland light rail) - 2 miles (5 min)<br />Seaside (closest Oregon beach) - 91 miles (1 hour 43 min)<br />Distance to Columbia River Gorge - 15 miles (19 min)<br />Airport - 11 miles (16 min)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-14068580/original/0c552c64-c5b8-4a6d-9980-e2b2e1bb78e7.jpeg',84485898,77,'45.47598','-122.52152',1,4,2.50,2.00,2.00,249.00,1,1125,189,4.67,14068580),(624,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14105781','Luxury Garden Cottage in Central PDX','✦ Beautiful new guest cottage located in the Historic Irvington neighborhood.<br />✦ Located a mere 6-10 minutes from downtown.<br />✦ Tall ceilings and gorgeous A-Frame house<br />✦Walk, bike or drive to the many cafes, shops and restaurants at nearby destination neighborhoods, including Alberta Arts District (1.5 miles), Broadway, (.5 miles) Williams District (.9 miles), Mississippi Ave. (1.5 miles)','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/44f10464-6e51-4861-b3e9-5b5d2158f6d3.jpg',1218855,7,'45.54229','-122.65664',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,71.00,1,365,515,4.90,14105781),(625,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14105943','✧ Chic Suite in Central PDX w/ Comfy King Bed ✧','• Secluded Guest Suite<br />• 7 minute drive to downtown & close to most cool spots in Portland<br />• Easy keypad entry<br />• Beautiful & safe residential neighborhood <br />• Cute coffee shop three blocks from house<br />• Well-appointed kitchenette<br />• Basement suite with private feel<br />• Highly-reviewed King bed<br />• Modern-chic design<br /><br />★ \"Great place to stay, and close to public transportation. Suja is a great host and wants to make sure your stay is perfect. Would definitely stay here again!\"','★ \"Just a couple blocks away from tasty cafes, hopping bars, and bus stops.  <br /><br />★ \"The location is not too far from downtown but also walking distance from other enjoyable neighborhoods!\"<br /><br />- Super beautiful and peaceful neighborhood. <br />- Central to almost all areas of Portland.  <br />- 7 minute drive to downtown <br />- Walkable to the Wonder Ballroom<br />- 20 mins drive to the airport, <br />- 5 minutes to Alberta and Mississippi<br />- 10 mins away from Hawthorne district!<br />- 3 blocks to Irving Park <br />- Amazing neighborhood for walks as the houses are beautiful<br />- Whole Foods and a Safeway not far from us<br />- Cute cafes and restaurants within walking distance!  My favorite is 26 Cafe, just three blocks away','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c93d74b6-ef08-47f3-93de-1eac8a113fd2.jpg',1218855,7,'45.54162','-122.65681',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,365,809,4.76,14105943),(626,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14180906','2Bd Bungalow with backyard sauna,  by Alberta Arts','Four blocks from Portland\'s iconic Kennedy School (with several cool bars, patios, a soaking pool and a movie theater!) two houses from beautiful Fernhill Park and some of the city\'s best restaurants — Beast, DOC, Expatriate, Dame — in walking distance. My place is good for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, families and furry friends. Watch a movie on the 92-inch screen. BBQ with the pellet grill on the back patio or SAUNA with a cold plunge tub. Central Air! Wood stove.','You\'re in one of the best neighborhoods in Portland. It\'s quiet, yet close to the bustling Alberta Arts District and some of the city\'s best restaurants. I’d love to tell you about  favorite places for coffee, yoga, cocktails, local beer, brunch, soaking pools, movies and more -- all within walking distance!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-14180906/original/6560b154-cb64-4357-b033-c7e9823e2180.jpeg',22320983,1,'45.56533','-122.62495',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,431.00,3,1125,85,4.78,14180906),(627,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14184963','The Clay House Portand','Centrally located on Portland’s Eastside, The Clay House is an enchanting 1 bedroom, 1 bath home that’s perfect for couples and business travelers. Freshly updated in spring 2024, the house features a luxurious bathroom, full kitchen, 2 office desks and a secret garden. From here, you can easily walk to Portland’s best restaurants and entertainment. We are one mile (1.6 km) east of the Willamette River, which you can cross via the Tilikum Crossing or Hawthorne Bridge to enter Downtown Portland.','We are in the middle of a gastronomic smorgasbord, in every direction within walking distance you can find great food, coffee, and other treats. There is a liquor store across the street, and several marijuana dispensaries in the neighborhood. There are beautiful rose gardens in Ladd\'s Addition, and we are close to the Willamette River, where you can hop on the Springwater Trail, which goes down to a wetland wildlife refuge. Or you can walk north along the river on the Eastbank Esplanade. If you\'re visiting during the weekend, be sure to check out Portland\'s Saturday Market via a pleasant walk over the Tilikum or Hawthorne bridges to the west side.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-14184963/original/8db0af3b-db46-4d67-9ed0-51606ed4e40e.jpeg',21571871,25,'45.51053','-122.65377',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,7,730,899,4.91,14184963),(628,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14210054','Immaculate Elegant House Downtown NW','Sanitized refuge from Covid19 fears. 5br/3ba home. 2200sqft of warm brick,leather,wood,polished brass, fine art. Big open kitchen.Walk to everything including Legacy GoodSam hospital. Heated floors,gas fireplace;sliding glass wall to deck,patio,fruit garden. AirCo. Beautifully furnished.Perfect for family events,business trips, groups. Walk to groceries,breweries,dispensaries, restaurants. Public transport 1/2block. 3blocks to Forest Park and 3blocks to NW23rd strolling, shopping & dining.','Northwest Alphabet district. One of the best vacation neighborhoods in downtown Portland. Right where visitors want to be. Very easy to find. Close to all major routes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f2b82291-87ca-4a29-8258-3fa752b2addc.jpg',73257018,27,'45.53584','-122.70604',1,10,3.00,5.00,4.00,487.00,2,1125,175,4.95,14210054),(629,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14254456','\"Crown Vic\" - sweet modern renovated Victorian','Message us if you don\'t see your dates we don\'t list all availability! Welcome to our sweet little crown jewel - a vintage Victorian lovingly restored by hand to bring out all her sweetness and light. She sits in the center of it all - Hawthorne, Division, Lardo, Teote, Cartopia, Coffee shops & more. Bikescore 100 (with Biketown station on corner)! Walkscore 92! You\'ll love our place because of the neighborhood, light, & clean modern vintage vibe blending old & new.','This neighborhood is wonderful. Near everything so no need to rent a car if you don\'t want to. In fact, you can rent bikes a block away! On same block or within blocks of restaurants, food carts, transportation, shops, grocery, and if you are looking for a little peaceful greenery, just head across the street and walk through the historic Ladd\'s Addition neighborhood which is known for its majestic elms, gorgeous houses, and rose gardens - just be sure to bring a gps - it is also known as the Bermuda triangle of Portland due to it\'s unique grid.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2e10830f-5c1c-44b7-b709-c6757aa6ddf7.jpg',5403721,25,'45.51072','-122.65309',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,168,4.77,14254456),(630,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14293805','Vintage Sunny Southeast 2 Bedroom','This is the first floor apartment of a duplex built in 1923. It is situated between Belmont St and Hawthorne Blvd in the desirable Southeast Portland neighborhood of Buckman. Interesting stores, cafés, restaurants and parks are within walking distance. Public transit to downtown Portland is a stone\'s throw away and free street parking is available. Good for couples, friends, families, business and academic travelers.','There are many interesting shops, cafés and parks which make it enjoyable to discover on foot. <br /><br />Places that are within walking distance:<br /><br />Coffee/Tea: Rocking Frog Cafe, Stumptown Coffee, Crema, Tao of Tea<br /><br />Breakfast/Brunch: Aviv (vegan), Blackheart, Zell\'s Cafe, Tusk, Fried Egg I\'m In Love<br /><br />Lunch: Rendez-Vous Off Belmont, Laughing Planet, Builicious Cart (SE 28th Ave and SE Stark), The food carts at SE 28th Ave and SE Ankeny, Guëro, Aviv (vegan), Olympic Provisions<br /><br />Ice Cream: Fifty Licks, Ruby Jewel, Pinolo<br /><br />Chocolate: Alma, Cloud Forest<br /><br />Happy Hour: Aalto Lounge, Gold Dust Meridian, Sapphire Hotel, Ankeny Tap & Table, Blackheart, Cibo, <br /><br />Nearby Bars: The Nest, Barebones, Blackheart, The Bonfire<br /><br />Dinner: Kala, Ken\'s Pizza, Ava Gene\'s, Cibo, Pok Pok, Han Oak, Guëro, Maruti (vegetarian), Noble Fish<br /><br />Dessert: Lauretta Jean\'s <br /><br />Groceries: Safeway, Fred Meyer, Whole Foods, New Sea','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a99d4e42-cc6d-4a5