mily friendly spacious basement apartment (700 square feet) with living, bath, kitchenette and bedroom, close to Creston park. Our house is a 5-7 minute drive from Reed College. It is within walking distance to several restaurants including Gladstone Street Pub and Food Carts on Foster. It is a 15 minute walk to Trader Joes; a 20 minute walk to many restaurants and shops on Woodstock Blvd. We have two security cameras on our property - one in the driveway and one on the front porch.','Creston park is a large park with a nice kids play area. It\'s a 5-7 minute walk from our house.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/abce5e26-cdf2-4a49-b6f5-61ad5ba873ad.jpg',88997237,67,'45.49275','-122.61132',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,75.00,2,35,98,4.93,14450148),(634,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14452990','Beautiful modern condo on SE Division','Enjoy all that SE Division Street has to offer in this beautiful, modern space with exposed beam ceilings, floor to ceiling windows, concrete radiant heated floors, gourmet kitchen with pro-series Wolf gas range, and in-unit washer&dryer. Highly walkable. Across the street from Tea Bar and half a block from the original Stumptown, we are also just half a mile from all the goodness Richmond has to offer (PokPok, Salt & Straw). Going downtown is just a convenient 30min bus ride.','-Reviewed by Sunset as 1/24 of America\'s best places to live and work, we are next to the original Stumptown and across the street from Tea Bar.<br />-Half a mile to the heart of Richmond including the famous: Salt and Straw and Pok Pok<br />-Other fun places include: Kim Jong Grilling, Cibo, Xico','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/026a9716-643a-4a31-9c56-545080c46026.jpg',1186587,8,'45.50696','-122.61744',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,30,1125,17,4.82,14452990),(635,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14475485','Portland Close to Downtown & Airport!','Everything you need to create amazing memories in Portland! Located in the Rose City Park Neighborhood in NE Portland. Close to groceries, cafes, and amenities, super easy access to downtown, public transportation, and the airport, free on-street parking, no parking meters!','I live in the great Rose City Park Neighborhood, easy to walk and get around, there is a golf course and a park 2 blocks away for a nice little jog, or you can just go to downtown and enjoy our great City!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-14475485/original/af5dffa1-e655-4831-a3c1-9576be9210bd.jpeg',18925199,11,'45.54426','-122.59727',1,2,0.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,3,365,212,4.79,14475485),(636,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14502584','Fresh North Portland Studio','Walk to Restaurants, Coffee Shops, Bars, Shopping, Mississippi Avenue District, MAX Yellow Line, Public Library, PCC-Cascade Campus. <br /><br />Beautifully furnished space with a fully stocked kitchen, high ceilings, comfy bed and custom-built features like the walk-in shower and kitchen bar.  Bright and open indoor/outdoor living with French doors that open to a private patio.<br /><br />Great for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.  Well-behaved dogs are permitted. No cats.','The studio is located in a vibrant, close-in neighborhood in North Portland.  There are plenty of restaurants, coffee shops, bars, parks, shops, and other attractions within walking distance!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/51ee1680-90f9-4e43-8495-e861d7e9f041.jpg',42715966,24,'45.561691','-122.675591',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,96.00,2,29,446,4.96,14502584),(637,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14505032','Clean, Modern & Cozy in NE Portland  (2bd, 1bth)','Our basement is a remodeled guest suite, with its private entrance.  This place has excellent walkability to great eats, bars and boutique shops. The nearby MAX makes Portland easy & accessible, no car needed. Popular nearby destinations are Convention Center and Moda Center. We are a 10 min drive from downtown (15 min MAX ride). You\'ll love that our location is central.  Our place is good for couples, friends, business travelers & families.(Note: lower ceilings)','We love the walkabilty in our neighborhood. It\'s pretty central for a Portland location. We are a perfect spot for Convention Center visitors. And personally, we love walking around Sullivan\'s Gulch and Historic Irvington to see the beautiful homes and gardens.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4512d7da-c18a-42bc-9dd8-b8696655820f.jpg',45410272,4,'45.53168','-122.64548',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,84.00,1,1125,619,4.89,14505032),(638,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14535161','Right on Hawthorne w/ 2 perfectly cozy king beds','This lovely, spacious, duplex, home is just about as centrally located as one could get. Sitting right on the bustling Hawthorne Blvd our guests have everything they could possibly need and want from a Portland visit without walking more than 5 blocks. From the historic Baghdad theater, countless bars and restaurants, shopping boutiques, amazing coffee shops, several food cart pods, grocery stores, bodegas, and very entertaining people watching! <br />We invite all to come stay!!','This is one of my very favorite neighborhoods in Portland. I grew up here and have found myself back (about 10 blocks from my childhood home) after living all around town. Hawthorne has this very chill old Portland vibe that is very distinct to the city.<br /><br />If you\'re looking up our neighborhood online we are located right between the Richmond and Sunnyside neighborhoods. Both are rich with Portland culture and offer a stunning amount of things to keep you busy - even in the rainy months!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-14535161/original/9220ed75-e14d-4b26-adca-9972dbecb7af.jpg',49123414,16,'45.51231','-122.63345',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,194.00,3,21,142,4.97,14535161),(639,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14551885','A Private Apartment in Inner SE Division-Clinton!','We are located directly on Clinton St, just one block to coffee shops, boutiques, a record store, an independent movie theater, multiple bars (including 2 classic dives!) and some of the best restaurants in the city. And even more a couple blocks up Division. Inside a classic 1906 house, the private apartment was newly built in 2022. We live upstairs with 2 kids ages 4 + 6. They sleep and mostly play in the opposite side of the house, but you will probably hear some kid footsteps during the day.','Situated on Clinton bicycle greenway corridor and just a block off SE Division. Walkable to heaps of great restaurants and coffee shops, a few breweries, New Seasons grocery store. A cute city park across the street. 1 block from the  FX Express bus that runs 24/7 to the heart of downtown park blocks (Powell\'s, Union Train Station, Chinese Garden, etc). Clinton greenway is a bicycle highway to connect downtown and everywhere. There is a BIKETOWN rack of rental e-assist bicycles across the street from us.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-14551885/original/607f9173-ec15-4861-bdff-a8cf66ffc063.jpeg',6446118,25,'45.503156298243674','-122.63854131562891',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,2,21,32,4.97,14551885),(640,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14592068','Charming Bungalow with A/C','Enjoy the entire main floor of this bungalow, with private main entrance, 2 bedrooms & 1 bath filled with natural light, hardwood floors, a comfortable living room that opens into a fully equipped kitchen and a cozy breakfast nook. Start your morning with coffee on the private deck and use the backyard & garden area to relax and enjoy a glass of wine. <br /><br />The downstairs of the house has an apartment for my family\'s use, with a complete separate entrance. <br /><br />Licensed by the City of Portland','The house is located in a quite residential neighborhood, within walking distance to coffee shops, several brew pubs, a Mexican restaurant, and one of the best sushi restaurants in town. <br /><br />A great park is only a few blocks away and several grocery stores are nearby. Within a mile are: Division St., Clinton/26th, Reed College, and the Crystal Spring Rhododendron Gardens. Parking on the street is readily available.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3dc65325-b43f-412a-9172-9d2e5b19be8b.jpg',51175099,67,'45.49166','-122.63607',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,116.00,1,1125,480,4.96,14592068),(641,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14632018','Portland vintage 2 br in heart of SE Woodstock','Thank you for considering our home for your stay! This adorable Portland space is in the heart of the Woodstock neighborhood. Just steps away from Portland\'s famous German deli (Otto\'s), locally roasted coffee from Loma, Oregon\'s favorite brewery Double Mountain and so much more. This quaint home is the perfect place to welcome you to the City of Roses. The place comes with off street parking, a fully equipped kitchen, great wifi, TV, and so much more to make you feel at home as you explore!','Megan describes the Woodstock area as the most walkable neighborhood in the city. In less than five minutes you can have a craft beer, local groceries, coffee, an amazing meal, golf the iconic Eastmoreland Course, visit Portland\'s amazing Rhododendron garden, or hike through the beautiful Reed College campus. If you want to get outside of the neighborhood, we\'re just 20 minutes from downtown and close to all of the main highways to get you in and out of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2a92a5bc-056e-48b5-b3d0-c8f60693d7a4.jpg',86128240,38,'45.4799','-122.61864',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,165.00,30,1125,47,4.45,14632018),(642,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14638923','SE PDX 2 Bed by Division, Hawthorne, and Woodstock','A short travel to a vast amount of restaurant, bar, and entertainment options, with some right around the corner.  Very cozy with full kitchen and laundry, cold central A/C keeps it cool in the summer. A half block from the park. Proximity to multiple hospitals great for travel nurses.<br /><br />As of September 2024:<br />Brand new kitchen with custom cabinets, quartz countertops,  and tile backsplash. New LVP wood floors throughout the house.','I love my neighborhood and you will too.  It is quiet, right around the corner from Mt. Scott Park, which is full of trees.  I\'m a block from Arleta Bakery Cafe which is an amazing brunch or lunch spot, Space Monkey Coffee, Old Gilbert Road Tavern if you are in the mood for a drink.  Also a block away is the Mt Scott Community Center which has a gym, basketball courts, waterslide, lap pool, and skating rink.  About five blocks away is the Portland Mercado, which has a coffee shop, many food trucks, market, carniceria, and a wine bar.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTQ2Mzg5MjM%3D/original/8929fa3a-9dba-4393-9c73-4d182deb8828.jpeg',37683790,65,'45.48085','-122.58937',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,85.00,7,1125,25,4.84,14638923),(643,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14654125','Come Home To A Place You\'ve Never Been Before','Our guests enjoy a private, completely restored Queen Anne farmhouse. The farmhouse features two large bedrooms, 1 1/2  bathrooms  (one with a clawfoot tub/shower), sunporch living room and mezzanine library, gas fireplaces and a large, well appointed kitchen on the main floor.<br /><br />Only Minutes from downtown, but a world away -  enjoy this quiet suite surrounded by an acre of spectacular gardens - the perfect respite from the urban life of Portland.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1ea95fd3-201f-4e90-b34a-5e9659df8319.jpg',6586631,38,'45.48843','-122.61037',1,5,1.50,2.00,2.00,380.00,4,1125,62,4.98,14654125),(644,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14686967','*On Alberta! Modern Artist Loft w/ Rooftop Views!*','Prepare to fall in love–this loft located in the heart of the Alberta Arts will have you immediately smitten! This newly designed and renovated 1BR/1BA apartment on Alberta Street includes a (wait for it!) rooftop deck with views of Mt. Saint Helens! Whether you’re looking for a cozy place to rest your head, easy access to bars, restaurants & shops, or a home away from home that has all the amenities you could ask for, this Alberta loft could be your next home away from home!','Vernon is one of Portland\'s hip neighborhoods that is located in close proximity to the Alberta Commercial Corridor, with restaurants, bars, coffee shops, theaters and awesome food carts! All you have to do is step outside this apartment and you are STEPS to some of Portland’s best dining, drinking and shopping!<br /><br />DRIVE TIMES TO LOCAL DESTINATIONS:<br />* Hawthorne: 15 minutes<br />* Division: 20 minutes<br />* Downtown: 10 minutes<br />* 23rd street: 13 minutes<br />* Sauvie Island: 34 minutes<br />* Wine Country: 43 minutes<br /><br />*Please note that this loft is located above a 24 hour gym. In our experience, this does not impact the majority of our guests.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ee5713e4-22f5-41e4-8eb6-90fac780abd3.jpg',51738043,14,'45.5592469','-122.6527726',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,105.00,30,365,336,4.78,14686967),(645,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14760381','Private Woodstock Retreat with Gorgeous Backyard!','This newly renovated apartment is in the heart of the popular Woodstock District and just blocks from shopping and restaurants.  Outfitted with everything you need, it\'s a great place to relax when you\'re not out exploring Portland.  Enjoy complimentary coffee and a welcome basket with your choice of goodies.  Your hosts are onsite, friendly, and ready to help with any needs! Newly back on the the Airbnb market after a pandemic pause.','Woodstock is a cute and quirky little neighborhood that centers on Woodstock St. from Cesar E. Chavez Blvd (39th St). to 60th St.  Its compact size combined with its density allows for most needs to be meet within a 10 minute walk from the apartment.  For all your grocery and hot deli needs, New Seasons is a wonderful store only a few blocks away (with Safeway being more pedestrian but cheaper and even closer).   <br /><br />For restaurants within walking distance, we recommend Double Mountain Brewery (some of the best beer in Oregon with great pizza too), El Gallo Taqueria (classic Taqueria experience) and The Delta Cafe (classic Portland institution for ribs and Southern food).  The best coffee/pastry option within walking distance is the Grand Central Bakery.  <br /><br />It\'s also located not far from the Reed College campus, which has a beautiful campus and canyon trails.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/06698b69-a716-46f4-869d-10121b9fc962.jpg',26701213,38,'45.4841','-122.61998',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,2,27,227,4.93,14760381),(646,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14772665','Ivon Garden Cottage','\"A true home away from home, this spot has all the details and little comforts you could ask for, along with a stellar location and a beautiful space. Just book it, you\'ll thank yourself as you sit on the patio sipping wine and figuring out how you can recreate this little Portland oasis in your own backyard.\" - Jordan, Missouri USA','The garden cottage is on a quiet street just two blocks from Stumptown Coffee and the incredible Division Street full of restaurants, boutique shops and other bustling activities. It\'s easy to get around Portland and has plenty of great spots to eat breakfast, watch people or enjoy a microbrew.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3d7d1604-c37a-40f6-a010-c7854306e4d8.jpg',1586012,8,'45.50386','-122.61675',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,116.00,2,29,637,4.98,14772665),(647,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14780717','Pension Portlandia: Close to Convention Center','Charming lower apartment in NE Portland.   Local coffee shops, restaurants, bookstores, and boutiques.  Extremely convenient for reaching ALL areas of Portland.  Two bedrooms with comfy queen beds w/ option of daybed.  Full bath and kitchenette.(fridge and a two burner induction hot plate, microwave, instant pot, coffee maker, toaster and  tea kettle. ) . Good for couples, solo adventurers, friends, business travelers, and families! Check inflexible .  There are steps both indoors and outside.','We are on the residential side of a block that includes terrific destination restaurants.  Before even crossing the street you\'ll encounter Costello\'s Travel Caffe (a neighborhood favorite for breakfast and lunch), The Rose and Thistle Pub (trivia every Monday), Spielman\'s Coffee and Bagels.  Just across the street from Rose and Thistle is The Taco Peddler.  And we have to exciting new restaurants, Steeplejack BrewPub is a stunningly remodeled former church right across the street.  The Sports Bra is a highly notable women\'s sports bar and restaurant....the very first of it\'s kind.  A few blocks down there are wonderful brunches, sports bars, Portland\'s favorite tiki bar Hale Pele, Broadway Books, carrying a wide selection of new releases, local authors, and used books, as well as traditional favorites  and children\'s books.  Saint Simon a few blocks west on Broadway has wonderful coffee, and Nicolas to the East has Mediterranean fare .  Blind Onion Pizza is a local favorite and there ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4ce938ca-4147-4a0c-9d79-c793632c7f01.jpg',5670387,7,'45.53519','-122.6409',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,95.00,3,365,224,4.95,14780717),(648,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14782685','Portlandia/Craftsman, Downtown, Food! Pet Friendly','Welcome to \"Portlandia\" Remodel!  <br /><br />Portland requires 30 days+ rental and restrict Vacation Rentals so we are looking for a longer-term guest.<br /><br />Perfect Vacation, Temporary Housing, Executives, Traveling Nurses, Back-Up Home<br /><br />Walking Score of 90!  <br /><br />Biker\'s Paradise (92)<br /><br />Super cool Irvington neighborhood with:<br />-Broadway Street<br />-Restaurants & Bars<br />-Supermarkets & Shops <br />-Minutes to Downtown<br />-Rose Garden Arena<br />-Close to Transportation<br /><br />Viva Beach Life website to save fees!','Irvington Portland Neighborhood<br />The Irvington neighborhood is located in Northeast Portland and is bordered by the Sabin, Alameda, Eliot, King, Grant Park, Sullivan’s Gulch, and Lloyd Center neighborhoods. Irvington is located on the East side of the Willamette River. Its boundaries are NE Fremont Avenue on the North, NE 7th Avenue on the West, NE Broadway on the South, and NE 26th Avenue on the East. As with some other Portland-area neighborhoods, the upper Northeast corner overlaps with Alameda and Sabin (for some unknown reason).<br /><br />irvington portland neighborhood map<br /><br />Click the image for a searchable Irvington neighborhood map including homes for sale.<br />Irvington Park<br />irvington neighborhood illustration<br /> <br />Irvington Park – This is a popular old park for Irvington residents, with big trees, plenty of green grass, ball fields, a water feature and playground for the children, and off-leash dog park section, basketball and tennis courts, and of ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f452ed49-d0b6-41de-8ae1-317c1d4f80fb.jpg',2503251,33,'45.53683','-122.6341',1,16,2.00,4.00,17.00,120.00,30,1125,62,4.37,14782685),(649,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14784937','Private floor, 2 bedrooms, close-in vintage modern','Located in the heart of inner SE Portland, walking distance to great restaurants, bars and cafes. Very stylish 2-bedroom suite with a private living room between the bedrooms. Rent both bedrooms or just one—perfect for one or two couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, and families with older kids. Exclusive use of the beautiful living room for relaxing. The private bathroom is one floor below beds (on the 2nd floor). You have to be comfortable walking up and down stairs.','Inner SE Portland is where it’s all happening. You can walk to several of the top restaurants in Portland:  Kachka,  Nostrana, Bollywood Theater, Xico and so many others. There are numerous brew pubs—Cascade Brewing, Hair of the Dog, Base Camp—and even a few distilleries.<br />If you want to leave the neighborhood, we’re only about a mile from downtown, which we often walk to. Go to the PSU Saturday Farmer’s Market, or bike to the new Pine Street Market food hall. No visit to Portland is complete without going to Powell’s Books and the Rose Garden.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c0092942-1339-4993-9212-6c9ecca29f2d.jpg',92302331,25,'45.51083','-122.65166',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,95.00,2,8,149,4.98,14784937),(650,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14785325','Alberta Arts Tree House','With great restaurants, bars and coffee shops just steps away, this bright and airy little house will be the perfect jumping off point for your stay in beautiful Portland Oregon.  <br /><br />Within a few block from your front door, there are Expatriate’s wonderful cocktails, Gabbiano\'s hand made pasta, Great North Coffee, FlourMarket, Vegan offerings at Jet Black coffee, and the lovely vibrancy of the Alberta Arts District.','The Alberta Arts neighborhood is a great place to base yourself for your stay. some favorite restaurants are within a 10 block radius.  There are plenty of little galleries, fun shops and nice cafes.  Extracto is a great coffee shop that is a block away, and Expatriate is a wonderful cocktail bar which is also super close.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/af8f4a6c-cfa5-4f74-aad2-be85c99b0e31.jpg',17456214,1,'45.56244','-122.63291',1,4,1.50,1.00,2.00,89.00,2,1125,348,4.98,14785325),(651,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14789940','Cozy and Bright Roseway Heights Cottage','A classic 1914 Portland home with lots of character, updated kitchen, and cosy bedrooms, you\'re gonna love it! Cook in our fully-equipped kitchen, or try some of the great restaurants in our neighborhood—the famous Pip\'s Doughnuts, or Otto\'s pizza just down the street! We\'re in a quiet neighborhood in NE Portland, not far from the airport (12 min) right near the popular Hollywood and Fremont neighborhoods.','Roseway is a beautiful walkable neighborhood, that runs along Alameda Ridge which sits just above a golf course, offering a nice urban hike with expansive views of Mt. Hood, Mt. Tabor, Powell Butte and parts of the city.<br /><br />Restaurants and grocery stores just a few blocks away!<br /><br />We\'re an 8 min drive from the popular Hollywood district, with it\'s historic Hollywood Theatre. Want to try out a cozy coffee shop? Case Study Coffee Roasters is one of our favorites, just 4 min down the road. Or even closer, the newly opened Kainos coffee is just a few blocks away! Doughnuts and house-made chai more your style? Don\'t miss the Portland-famous Pip\'s Original Doughnuts just a mile and a half down the road from us. And if you\'re coming from the airport, we\'re an easy 11 min drive away!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTQ3ODk5NDA%3D/original/23d4a375-0a4c-46cd-969f-81535e22e567.jpeg',3597843,11,'45.54472','-122.60062',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,124.00,2,28,50,5.00,14789940),(652,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14803761','Tiny House Off Hawthorne (Mt. Tabor) BLVD','Around the corner from Vibrant Hawthorne district 1900 circa carriage house converted into  tiny guest house. Brand new construction inside. Private entrance, gated backyard with 2 gated areas SMOKING Allowed outdoors ONLY. Close to Por Que No, A Pizza Scholls, Cana Connection, Quarterworld Mt. Tabor Bread, Albina Press, Whole bowl & Kure. Great for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers & families (with kids) and furry friends (pets) there is a fee for pets. Alexa and Keurig in unit.','We live in the epicenter of what makes Portland a destination TOWN Not a city. Think neighborhoods. Think WEIRD. That is what makes the city of bridges unique. Spitting distance from Hawthorne District. Boutique shops, diverse & excellent restaurants options, coffee shops bookstores , Pot dispensaries, music venues, cinemas a dive bar or two on and on. There is tons to do right outside your door. Two of the top Ten restaurants in town less than stone through..','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/53f07163-6b43-4b75-92aa-2c359eabc713.jpg',90701654,8,'45.51078','-122.61448',1,5,1.00,0.00,3.00,69.00,30,30,410,4.94,14803761),(653,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14809195','NE Portland Craftsman Guest House','Maximum of five (5) guests permitted. Our guest house boasts a feeling of a by-gone era, while also incorporating contemporary amenities and stylish furnishings. A conveniently located grocery store can be found just a stone\'s throw away. The house runs on renewable energy, as part of our dedication to lessening our ecological footprint. We eagerly anticipate hosting you in this lovely home away from home!','We are in the heart of the King Neighborhood, and a stone\'s throw away from great places to eat and visit; Alberta Arts District,  Radio Room, The Keys Lounge, The Bye and Bye are within easy walking distance. Old Town Brewing with their delicious Kolsch beer is one block away. Our neighbors are lovely people who are dedicated to their homes and each other.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7aba1137-0753-40d0-9f22-2f0a1d547cc2.jpg',62043803,14,'45.56084','-122.66424',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,160.00,3,25,188,4.98,14809195),(654,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14825708','SE Division Hideaway','The Hideaway is a clean, cozy and private, 700+ square foot basement apartment; located in the heart of SE Portland. The space has its own heating/AC system, independent of the rest of the house. An easy walk to SE Division Street provides great coffee, groceries, restaurants, brewpubs, boutique retail, theaters, parks, public transit and more. Street parking is ample. The location is urban & peaceful. This is a strictly<br />non-smoking property.','The Clinton/Division neighborhood is truly the best that Portland has to offer. Beyond being a short walk to Clinton and Division streets the apartment is within walking/biking distance to the Tillikum walking bridge which spans the Willamette river, the Eastside Esplanade, Laurelhurst and Mt. Tabor Parks, OMSI (Oregon Museum of Science & Industry), downtown, and an endless variety of other attractions.<br /><br />As per City of Portland permit regulations, all guests must provide full names, address and license plate numbers (if driving) upon arrival.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6069ec77-ac65-4c9a-a3a7-f4b3ef0d1bbd.jpg',1638505,25,'45.50097','-122.63882',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,2,29,348,4.97,14825708),(655,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14842356','Cute place near Powell’s Books','3 blocks to Whole Foods, Fred M, Powell\'s, Providence Park/train, Crystal ball room, Pearl & Alphabet district are within 5 mins walking. Tons of restaurants, parks, bars and people watching. If you want city living, this is it :)<br /><br /><br />Enterprise is right next door if you want to rent a car BUT no need to drive, streetcar and Max are 3 blocks away.<br /><br />Great for couples, solo adventurers, students and business travelers. 30 nights min and we can discuss to extend your stay after that for sure :)','The neighborhood is in the heart of everything, you can easily walk to Washington park (rose garden and Japanese gardens are a must) downtown, the Pearl, Alphabet districts, tons of bars, restaurants and people watching.<br /><br />It\'s convenient to walk to the waterfront and you could go to SE within a 5\' car drive.<br /><br />The apartment is located in an historic building from the 1920\'s, used to be a hotel.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3e893bf8-d528-4fc9-8a90-bb827b97dc0e.jpg',3611030,3,'45.52215','-122.68818',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,102.00,31,730,256,4.84,14842356),(656,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14885930','Modern Zen Haus - Mt Tabor','This small, modern Zen Haus is perfect for an individual or couple. Two levels, each floor is 400 sq ft. Open layout with bamboo floors, high ceilings, lots of light, balcony and stainless steel appliances. Fully furnished & minimalist with mid-century modern and Asian decor. <br /><br />Walk to restaurants, coffee shops, shopping along Division & Hawthorne. Close to bus routes & easy access to airport. Walk 5 minutes to Mt Tabor where you have lovely hiking trails & 180 acres to explore!','SE Portland is a very special place. Great places to hike, eat and discover new things. The Baghdad Theater and Powell Book Store are a short walk away in Hawthorne. Be sure to check out Porque No? for yummy tacos and Tabor bread for exceptional sour dough. New Seasons is a wonderful health food store with good quality produce. Grab a quick meal at Whole Bowl or Cure for a fresh juice.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-14885930/original/e2dcba5c-9a57-4725-9592-3faa74097083.jpeg',49343,15,'45.50883','-122.60158',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,119.00,31,365,15,4.80,14885930),(657,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14916909','Lincoln Loft','You’ll love this place because of the coziness, the high ceilings, the location to Portland and nearby neighborhoods, access to public transportation and the privacy. It is good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers. Parking is easy on the surrounding neighborhood streets and most often right out in front. of the house.','Mt. Tabor, Hawthorne, Montavilla, Woodstock, Laurelhurst are some of the neighborhoods within a couple miles - easily accessible by public transportation. Trimet bus lines 71, 14 and 4 are all within a few minutes walking distance from Lincoln Loft. Taxis, Uber, Lyft, Zipcar, Reach Now, Cars2Go and bike rentals are all available nearby. If you would like more information, I’m happy to answer questions.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2fdacdff-21b8-4d57-8d5f-b62d040f9a62.jpg',12095190,15,'45.50849','-122.60672',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,7,147,4.96,14916909),(658,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14936037','Cute, Private Apartment | Close to everything!','Our sunny basement guesthouse is your home away from home, walking distance to restaurants, coffee shops, grocery stores, and shopping. It has a private street entrance and all the comforts you need for a long or short stay in beautiful Portland, OR. Our place is great for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, and families with kids,.','One of the things we love about our neighborhood is that it is both residential and urban.  There are often kids playing out on the street and all the neighbors know one another and hang out.  But, we are also in a city and there are lots of stores and restaurants only a couple of blocks away.  It is usually pretty quiet, but sometimes the neighbors will have a party, sirens go by, or there may be a Naked Bike Ride going down the street.  We are right in middle of what makes Portland everything Portland is known for.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/49233469-d7ba-477e-9aa0-9694ed6d332b.jpg',25595028,9,'45.54927','-122.66427',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,60.00,3,28,230,4.89,14936037),(659,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14949147','Dog Friendly Motor Lodge, One Queen Bed','Bring your bestie! Four-legged family members are welcome at the Jupiter. We apply a one time $45 pet cleaning fee at Check-in and will explain our pet policy to you if you plan to bring your pup.<br /><br />Jupiter Hotel is a locally owned and operated, renovated, 1970\'s style motor lodge. Doug Fir Lounge is on site, with great food and beverage options and a music venue with performances most nights. Night owl? Early riser? You’ll feel at home here.','In the heart of the inner east side cultural district, Jupiter is surrounded by great places to eat, drink, shop and explore. We are a few blocks from the Burnside Bridge which can take you in to downtown or the waterfront with the Saturday Market. On site, in addition to Doug Fir Lounge, we also have Hey Love, which is an all-encompassing bar/restaurant/lounge/indoor jungle/neighborhood escape/all day hangout spot with hours from3pm-1am. Our neighborhood has locally owned boutiques, great food and beverage, as well as multiple theaters for live performances.  We are also a short jaunt form the Moda Center and the Convention center.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-14949147/original/07a775c8-e8fb-4279-95d0-81b6e9510174.jpeg',8873069,12,'45.52331','-122.65722',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,189.00,30,1125,74,4.65,14949147),(660,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14963860','Hidden Gem in Sellwood','Whether visiting family, on a work assignment, or considering moving to Portland this is your home away from home!  Fully equipped kitchen, driveway parking, your own storage, and laundry room.  High speed internet connection.  High walkability, blocks from the river, Oaks amusement park, biking trails, parks, health grocery stores, food carts, boutiques, restaurants, etc.   Bring along your small dog or ask for a case-by-case exception for larger pets.  I am looking forward to hosting you!','Historic Sellwood-Moreland boasts an array of shops, vintage vendors and restaurants, as well as a rambling wildlife refuge — all just minutes from downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ff555111-c064-401d-9dc0-56d114dc0703.jpg',2874362,20,'45.45845','-122.65352',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,94.00,14,1125,50,4.94,14963860),(661,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14963910','The Hydrangea House in Alameda','Our place is in the heart of NE Portland Beaumont/Alameda area. It is close to public transport, the airport, the city center, parks, and art and culture. We think you will love our place because of the comfy bed, the kitchen, and the coziness. The Hydrangea House is good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.','The Alameda/Beaumont area has so much to offer...Blocks away we have the cutest neighborhood market with the largest Beer Cooler as well as gourmet \"grab n go\" meals. Grand Central Bakery, McPeets Sports Bar, Sushi, Blackbird wine and small eats establishment, Batter (late night breakfast and bar) Mexican, Italian, Starbucks, Hawaiian.....and so much more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-14963910/original/4323e11a-1a15-49b8-899f-e7e7be8f2fe2.jpg',17366389,46,'45.54471','-122.62525',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,2,14,364,4.95,14963910),(662,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/14966304','Beaumont-Wilshire Charmer, NE PDX Close-in','This newly remolded Beaumont-Wilshire Charmer is ready to be your perfect home base to enjoy your stay in the Rose City. Perfect for couples, families, business people and those looking for a longer stay in PDX, this tastefully updated and well appointed home is in one Portland\'s best neighborhoods,  Ideally situated between the trendy Alberta Arts district, the rapidly expanding food scene of NE 42nd Ave and historic NE Fremont Street you will not run out of options for food & fun.','Located in the heart of Beaumont-Wilshire you\'ll be able to enjoy everything Portland has to offer.  A short 2 block walk to the gorgeous tree filled Wilshire Park , enjoy walking/running paths , picnic areas, baseball and soccer fields and wide open spaces. <br />Journey just a little further out by foot or bike and you\'ll find yourself at some of Portland\'s best shops and eateries. Great coffee, donuts, sushi, pizza and more can be found with ease and abundance less then 1 mile from your little slice of the Rose City.<br /><br />You\'ll find most of the amenities you could need right in the area. A New Seasons Market, Whole Foods, & Fred Meyers are all between  .5 -1.5 miles away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b54c81af-5f6d-4e92-a6e4-e00e482505ee.jpg',94248402,46,'45.55296','-122.62464',1,5,1.00,3.00,5.00,195.00,30,180,45,4.96,14966304),(663,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15040785','Lemon Door Micro-Loft Surrounded by Gardens in Hip Location','Discover a unique, custom-built tiny home with a big feel. The residence features an open-plan layout, a mezzanine bedroom, rustic wood finishes, industrial accents, cathedral ceilings, and access to a shared garden patio with a BBQ. Low cleaning fee & easy checkout.<br /><br />Close to action in fun Mississippi district, yet quiet & private. Self check-in. Close-in to downtown & Convention Ctr.<br /><br />As seen in “best of portland airbnb” online reviews: wheatlesswanderlust, roadaffair, & bridgesandballoons.','Close to many things & easy access to everything else.  The Historic Mississippi District is bustling with things to do, but also quiet & tucked away.  A 10 minute bike ride to downtown or an equally short bus ride. The Alberta Arts district and the Williams corridor are a few blocks away, too.  Within easy walking distance of local favs Por Que No?, Grand Central Bakery, New Seasons, Mississippi Studios, Interurban, & Stormbreaker, to name a few. Short bus ride to Convention Ctr & downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/48c393ab-7a00-4a33-a4e4-0eecfe57614b.jpg',585047,9,'45.54923116097722','-122.67255760046346',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,101.00,2,1125,641,4.98,15040785),(664,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15042822','Historic Portland Charm with Modern Comforts','Historic Overlook neighborhood is the most sought after. 2 miles to downtown, 20 mins to PDX, supreme location. Bus/max lines, bike rental, fwy access & walkability to parks, popular Mississippi Ave: coffee shops, boutiques, restaurants, bars.   Original Portland charm & central location to all of Portland. Perfect for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers. Newly constructed studio apartment, Queen bed. Kitchen is fully stocked, spacious bathroom, plenty of storage for your belongings.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f5b187f9-c914-410b-ad57-0cb58c7dcfbb.jpg',56903072,13,'45.55289','-122.68559',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,365,1125,10,5.00,15042822),(665,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15060409','Queen Private Room at NW Portland Hostel','Experience Portland’s top-rated, family-owned hostel, in the vibrant Northwest District! Enjoy a FREE breakfast and explore nearby downtown attractions, Washington Park, the Rose and Japanese Gardens, and hiking trails. Join our daily free events like walking tours, tap tastings, live music, and trivia nights. For over 25 years, our mission has been to provide a welcoming, affordable, and safe space, connecting Portland with travelers worldwide and making a positive impact locally and beyond.','We are located in the Northwest district, just a few blocks from popular shops, cafes, pubs, cinemas, and some of the city\'s best restaurants. Many area attractions, including the Pearl District, downtown Portland, Saturday Market, Portland Farmers Market, Powell\'s Bookstore, art galleries, the Lan Su Chinese Garden, museums, the MLS Stadium, and Pioneer Square, are within walking distance. The Rose Gardens and Japanese Gardens are a short bus ride or a 25-minute walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTUwNjA0MDk%3D/original/914babb1-1abb-4fd4-92e5-b8508db071b0.jpeg',2820851,27,'45.52658','-122.68891',2,2,3.00,1.00,1.00,78.00,1,365,122,4.73,15060409),(666,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15087305','NE Portland Charmer *Walk to Alberta & Williams!*','This beauty is a perfect blend of updated splendor and old world charm. Mere minutes away from Fremont, Mississippi, Alberta, Prescott, and Killingsworth, there is an infinite number of places to eat, drink, shop, and people watch. Easy freeway access makes other parts of Portland a quick drive, and if you want to get out into nature, that\'s not far off either! Relax on our comfy couches with a good book on those rainy Portland days,  or enjoy some local brews on our quaint front porch!','We love how close our home is to some of our favorite things! Like N Williams St, Alberta Arts district, Mississippi St, Irvington and Oldtown- Downtown Portland!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4e9ac8ca-fdc5-44b9-b921-05f164e4eb61.jpg',95484731,14,'45.55509','-122.66065',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,93.00,2,29,265,4.96,15087305),(667,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15094467','Modern Urban Barn Guesthouse','Featured in Portland Monthly Magazine, the Urban Barn Guesthouse, built in 2016, is a two bedroom gem in culinary-rich Division St. where you\'ll mix with quirky neighbors, track down nearby food finds and experience SE Portland\'s cultural richness. The Barn has cathedral-height ceilings in 800 sf of style and comfort - a full stocked gourmet kitchen and private, gated patio and yard.  Because you\'re on vacation the cleaning fee covers all cleaning. You don\'t have to strip the beds or empty trash','The Division-Clinton neighborhood has most everything a fun visit to Portland can offer. The property is in the heart of a cool and vibrant area with vintage homes, food cart pods with every imaginable cuisine, bars, grocery stores, and bakeries.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-15094467/original/0c3f6560-33c4-4e8c-a72c-f63933f70eb9.jpeg',5455260,25,'45.50267','-122.64462',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,193.00,2,28,252,4.98,15094467),(668,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15101133','Peaceful Artist\'s Retreat','Centrally located with access to bus and MAX train 10 min. from downtown and 10 min. from airport.<br /><br />It\'s a foodie neighborhood including cafes, pubs and food carts in 2 blocks. Easy walk to organic grocery.<br /><br />Our basement apartment has a spacious living- sleeping area with private entrance and garden view.<br /><br />Snack bar has microwave, hotpot, expresso machine and fridge. <br /><br />The king bed+daybed sleeps 4.<br /><br />We use unscented and non-toxic cleansers.<br />We enjoy the diversity of our guests!','The Hollywood-Rose Park neighborhood is crammed with food stores and restaurants and family style bars. We like to eat! <br />You can go neither direction on Sandy Blvd to fine numerous options.<br /><br />For fancy but fabulous dining try Cabezon, right across the street.<br />Expensive but high quality coffee is one clock away at Casestudy Coffee.<br />There is a gym that allows unlimited  access for 20./month!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5e091bf8-df2b-41aa-8f11-2c220b34000d.jpg',59002572,11,'45.53958','-122.60806',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,100.00,3,730,90,4.88,15101133),(669,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15113378','Views, close to OHSU and PSU.  Parking included.','Located two blocks from Portland State University, Riverplace Marina, Three Degrees Waterfront Bar & Grill, Trimet, and OHSU.  <br /><br />You’ll love this place because of views, location and relaxation!  Included underground parking.','This location to great restaurants, theater, music, running/biking and public transportation.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2acad2df-859a-4753-a786-73eebeb16339.jpg',50536855,44,'45.51164','-122.67977',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,30,1125,28,5.00,15113378),(670,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15147354','Cozy NE home: walk to parks, Dekum attractions','Our light-filled 1938 home is close to parks, craft breweries and one of Portland\'s best bakeries. Sip coffee on the patio, visit our hens, pick organic raspberries from the garden, or spend an afternoon with a book. The kids\' room is stocked with books, games, and toys. When you\'re back from a walk or run, make a home-cooked meal - we have all the tools and utensils you\'ll need.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-15147354/original/7c47facf-022c-4502-8f76-0ce6d3a02d4d.jpeg',218151,45,'45.56951','-122.6593',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,150.00,30,60,2,5.00,15147354),(671,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15147998','Lovely Laurelhurst Home','This tastefully decorated, spacious Portland home is centrally located & perfect for family gatherings. Terrific yard for relaxing, with a hot tub and studio space/gym. Located in a historic neighborhood with beautiful, tree-lined streets perfect for walking. Close to excellent shopping, cafés, and restaurants! The Laurelhurst & Hollywood theaters are also located nearby. Only 6 minutes to downtown, 10 mins to the airport by car, near the Hollywood max station & 4 bus lines.','This is a great are to walk to nice restaurants and shops. Beautiful Laurelhurst park is 4 blocks away','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-15147998/original/d5b44d06-ac72-4b48-b0db-3b8d3e362cf8.jpeg',237041,23,'45.52791','-122.62807',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,374.00,3,99,9,4.89,15147998),(672,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15162109','Studio Guesthouse SE Portland','New Memory Foam Mattress (Jan.2024) <br />43\" TV on an adjustable wall mount <br />AirBnB COVID-19 Cleaning in place w/cleaning supplies for your use.<br /><br />You will love our Southeast Studio with Private Entrance, patio, seating & garden. Near Mount Tabor Park,  restaurants and bus stop. The Studio is great for couples, solo adventurers, business travel, and small families. Quiet neighborhood vibes. Yummy snacks, Coffee and Tea<br />Portable A/C installed June - mid September<br />Fan in unit after A/C removed','Our Neighborhood is a mix of Families, Young Professionals and Empty Nesters.<br /> As in most Portland neighborhoods we are a short walk away from several parks, Kern Park, Essex Park and Mount Tabor Park are the closest.  If you are looking for dining options with in walking distance here are the closest options.<br /> If you like Chinese Seafood it\'s a very short walk to Powell Seafood where they have excellent Salt and Pepper Squid as well as many other tasty Chinese dishes.   Other Restaurants within a 2-10 min. walk are Local 66(sports bar and grill), The Lodge(bar), Lay Low(bar), Steakadelphia(Cheesesteak Sandwiches) and Rose VL (authentic Vietnamese soups and sandwiches).  El Campesino PDX is a 2 min walk and offers fresh Mexican Pastries, 3 types of fresh Chicharron, House made Chips and Salsa, and many other treats.  The Portland Mercado is also nearby offering Latin American food carts and grocery store as well as a bar and indoor seating. If you are looking for pizza Atlas ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9ea45df4-812a-4a0c-be9a-8c9f3890bee7.jpg',62035184,36,'45.49559','-122.59545',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,57.00,1,10,618,4.91,15162109),(673,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15207122','The Filbert - Garden Apartment in Inner SE PDX.','The Filbert is in the Division/Clinton Neighborhood close to Broder Cafe, Salt & Straw and dozens of other amazing restaurants and bars. Also close by is the New Season\'s Market, People\'s Food Co-op, bike shops, and boutiques.  It is quick to get to downtown Portland by car, bus or light rail. This renovated apartment is tucked into an urban eco-community. You’ll love the location and the ambiance. The Filbert is good for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, and families one child.','The Filbert is in the Division-Clinton section of Hosford-Abernethy, a charming Portland neighborhood that’s full of history and beautiful homes. The neighborhood is close to downtown and the tree-lined streets offer shops, restaurants, and cafes. Hosford-Abernethy is a convenient jump over the Hawthorne Bridge from downtown and close to the bustle of the Hawthorne District, yet it retains that quiet, residential feel. The neighborhood is well known for Ladd’s Addition, where the streets are liberated from Portland’s usual grid layout, and instead run diagonally in an 80-square-block, wagon-wheel-like display of roadway defiance. Ladd\'s Addition is a great area for an evening walk. Make sure to visit the four rose gardens in Ladd\'s Addition during May and June.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-15207122/original/41f09960-3f80-47ec-a142-56fb655dcb61.jpg',17575711,25,'45.50221','-122.64584',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,91.00,30,1125,339,4.92,15207122),(674,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15225078','LoftHousePDX w/ Sauna & Hot Tub','Debuted during Portland\'s Accessory Dwelling Tour, “Loft House PDX” is centrally located just off beautiful Alameda Ridge. Business and leisure travelers alike will find a peaceful retreat awaiting them in this tastefully-appointed, open and airy, modern loft house with all the accoutrements one might wish for—including a Finlandia Sauna, and STIL hot tub to enjoy after a long day of work or play, and a custom gas firepit for evening lounging...','Alameda-Beaumont is a very desirable neighborhood in Portland. Well-established, safe and quiet it\'s comprised of a wonderful mix of well-cared for homes from the 1900\'s to the present. Alameda Street ( a stones throw away ) is one of the most beautiful tree-lined streets in all of Portland. Wide and winding with architecturally significant houses on either side it\'s a destination route for cyclists, runners, and strollers alike. With neighborhood places to eat/drink within easy walking distance on Fremont ( Bang Bang, Wonderly... ) and Sandy ( Case Study Coffee, Cabezon...  ) and being conveniently located to the airport, downtown and the many close-in shopping districts ( Alberta Arts, Mississippi... ) I think you\'ll find Loft House PDX to be the perfect launching pad for all things Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTUyMjUwNzg%3D/original/8a53bba3-6361-4c82-998b-36e29e22ad24.jpeg',42092967,11,'45.54143','-122.61048',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,242.00,3,30,462,4.99,15225078),(675,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15252541','Chic modern apartment in heart of Pearl District','My place is close to Pearl District and Sisters Coffee Company - The Pearl. Looking for someone to rent over Thanksgiving please contact me for inquiry!! My place is great for couples, solo adventurers and business travelers.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-15252541/original/3bd45a0f-8504-4249-8af4-576d9e1ef066.jpeg',48430655,2,'45.53137','-122.68478',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,139.00,30,1125,1,5.00,15252541),(676,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15255217','Peaceful Sanctuary in Portsmouth','Warm and inviting, this two-story \"skinny\" has everything you need to relax in comfort.  Sun-filled rooms with whimsical touches throughout and an outdoor patio perfect for grilling.  A calming and peaceful retreat!<br /><br />In a great location, only 20 minutes from PDX airport and 15 minutes to downtown Portland.','Located in Portsmouth, you’re smack dab in the middle of two great historic neighborhoods: St. Johns to the west (about 2 miles away) and Kenton to the east (2.5 miles away) St. John’s was once a separate town and retains an independent and unique vibe.  Home to funky boutiques, cafes, a natural grocer, two movie theatres, and a food cart pod with fire pit and beer garden.<br /><br />The University of Portland is just a few minutes’ drive down N. Portsmouth Ave.  New Seasons, a locally owned grocery store, is a 10 minute walk from my home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ccdd0680-766b-4b7e-89af-6983a9d85ebc.jpg',2207146,60,'45.5905','-122.7232',1,4,2.50,2.00,2.00,160.00,7,16,127,4.98,15255217),(677,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15267499','Colorful One Bedroom Condo One Block Off Division','This colorful and cozy one bedroom condo is perfect for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.  Located just one block off of the hustle and bustle of SE Division St giving you just enough space to enjoy the quiet neighborhood and its surrounding. The location is ideal for anyone wanting to explore SE PDX.  It\'s about 10 mins from downtown and is close to many great restaurants and bars right in the heart of Division St. Enjoy!','Quiet, relaxing, and safe Hosford-Abernathy neighborhood. Take a walk around the block and explore. All side walks on Division St. are wheelchair friendly and accessible.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f22a2181-c975-4cdc-b007-b02ad63b5f4e.jpg',97118810,25,'45.50603','-122.6427',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,31,160,87,4.76,15267499),(678,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15285983','Portland Peaceful and Friendly Oasis','Our house is  block away from a wonderful Creston Park (olympic size outdoor municipal pool open in the summer), 5 mins walk from Gladstone\'s restaurants, bars and other stores, 5 mins walk from Safeway, 5 mins to great Portland food carts, 10 mins to  Woodstock and its great cafes and restaurants, 15 mins from downtown Portland. Great quiet and friendly neighborhood and cozy interior. This is a great place for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d2df7c7b-856b-429c-bbc3-e7633fd0c1ad.jpg',97295503,67,'45.49428','-122.61479',2,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,1,5.00,15285983),(679,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15287873','Adorable Backyard Cottage.  Near Beaumont Village','My place is perfectly located between the airport and downtown.  Walking & biking distance to the great neighborhoods of inner NE Portland, including Beaumont Village and Alberta Street. The house is on the Klickitat bike route.  Easy access to public transportation.  <br /><br />Perfect for a business traveler or anyone interested in exploring Portland.  The bed is a queen bed & guests have said it is very comfortable.  It has a full kitchen to cook, or walk to one of the many restaurants or bars nearby.','The cottage is in NE Portland.  There are several restaurants, food carts, shops, brewpubs and bars in walking distance.  If you feel like hoping on a bike, driving or catching public transportation, it is only a short commute to many of the most popular neighborhoods in NE and SE Portland.<br /><br />Portland Business License # 16-258922','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f3c8fa5c-e0a8-477f-88be-4132c4b698fd.jpg',24370022,11,'45.5478','-122.60267',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,115.00,2,730,276,4.98,15287873),(680,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15308248','Comfortable & convenient.','This place is great for one or two people looking for a comfortable & convenient place to stay for a minimum of 30 nights. The house is a single-story alone on a larger city lot (not an apartment, duplex, basement, or ADU). Convenient to public transportation and thorough-fares in Portland.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-15308248/original/4fcef48f-cf9e-42d8-be45-cb8ae5db142c.jpeg',43635238,36,'45.49285','-122.58813',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,30,1125,10,5.00,15308248),(681,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15308318','Victorian in the Hip Mississippi District','Guests rate this home the perfect home base for groups in Portland\'s premier dining and entertainment corridor.<br /><br />*BRAND NEW water heater installed August 2023!<br /><br />You\'ll love this delightful multi-level historic Victorian urban retreat full of charm.   With 5-bedrooms, 2-bathrooms, it offers a living room, kitchen with butcher block island, oversized den,  walk-in pantry, dining room, foosball table, back deck, and ample space to relax. The gated off-street parking makes everything easier.','One of Portland\'s premiere entertainment districts, all within a one minute walk from the house.  Let our Mississippi District home, full of character and charm be your home base for your Portland visit!<br /><br />Our neighborhood is the perfect example of quintessential Portland culture, combining creative originality and diversity with lots of independent energy.  Almost every business is locally owned and operated, including some of Portland\'s most talked about restaurants, entertainment venues, coffee shops, brew pubs, and boutique clothing stores.  This newly revived area has become one of the hippest places to shop, dine and imbibe. Colorful buildings line the main thoroughfare one block away,  and charming and bike friendly residential neighborhoods fill in the spaces around the central gathering spots<br /><br />This neighborhood, having evolved from its urban roots has a very pleasant boutique flair with ever-growing options continue to grow establish itself as one of the mos','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c1fb22d1-1edb-49bd-a9ed-24b84f24e957.jpg',71038689,9,'45.55304','-122.67529',1,9,2.00,5.00,6.00,251.00,4,120,156,4.86,15308318),(682,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15322001','Chicken Little Cottage: rustic cabin in the city!','This charming little cottage sits back on a large urban lot in quiet NE Portland, behind the owner\'s home. Just a 5-10 minute bike ride from urban gems: the famous Alberta Arts District, locally owned shops, a large natural grocery store, a non-profit yoga studio, bike shops, bars, bakeries, many coffee shops and restaurants in this food lover’s mecca. You’ll feel like you’re in a quiet country cottage, but you’ll truly be in the heart of the city: only a 10-15 minute drive to downtown Portland.','We are located blocks from the Alberta Arts District, in the quieter sister neighborhood of Cully. We are true Portland; in fact a scene for “Portlandia” was filmed just 3 doors down from our house!<br /><br />This delightful cottage, nestled on our urban farm, is located within walking or biking distance of (just to name a few):<br /><br />Unique boutiques and vintage shops on Alberta Street and Fremont Street. <br />A wide variety of restaurants including some of the most sought after, fine dining establishments and other truly “Portland” style casual restaurants-  Petite Provence, DarSalam, Beast, Tin Shed, Expatriate, Bollywood Theater, Cup & Saucer, Vita Cafe, Pine State Biscuits, The Waffle Window and many more.<br />Bakeries-  many to choose from including classic bakeries as well as a vegan bakery and a french patisserie. <br />Independent (and non-profit) movie theater, Hollywood Theater is just 2 miles away.<br />Farmer’s Markets: Cully, Hollywood, <br />Grocery stores within','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a42ee777-dbe1-43dd-9daa-bf202af3d3d6.jpg',54436471,21,'45.55856','-122.60355',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,1,14,637,4.86,15322001),(683,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15358320','Bohemian Escape','My place is located in the heart of the city, a minutes walk or bike ride to all of Portland\'s best amenities including cafes, theaters, shops and restaurants. It\'s also right near public transportation. You’ll love my place because, hidden behind the wooden front gates is a private and serene oasis, done in an eclectic bohemian/mid-century modern/Anthropology feel. <br /><br />Note that Iove animals and accept pets for an additional $10 per pet per night! fees can be paid separately upon arrival.','We live in Sullivan\'s Gulch, a tiny enclave which sometimes even Portland natives haven\'t heard of! However, it is literally bordered by some of the best neighborhoods in the city (Irvington, Grant Park, Hollywood, Kerns & Laurelhurst) and has easy walking access to shops, bars, restaurants, grocery stores, multiple movie theaters, parks, the library, and public transportation.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6003107c-6580-44d2-a53f-8f1669e300bd.jpg',78494301,4,'45.53191','-122.64146',2,2,0.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,2,30,192,4.78,15358320),(684,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15361775','Private Basement Apt in sought-out SE Neighborhood','Our home is a 1940\'s bungalow in the heart of Sellwood. This charming basement apartment is located in the heart of Westmoreland/Sellwood neighborhood. Private entrance, well-lit, mother-in-law basement suite with kitchenette, en-suite bathroom and laundry room.   Separate access and outdoor patio use.  Ample street parking in the neighborhood. Close to Trimet bus and orange line.  Great restaurants,shopping and Oaks Bottom park trails within walking distance.  Wi-Fi and Smart TV with Netflix!','Hip and upcoming neighborhood in the southeast tip of Portland proper. Great neighborhood with easy access to all Portland has to offer. 10 min car ride to city , bike and public transit access. Close to one of the top golf courses , Eastmoreland golf course. Westmoreland and Sellwood is a great walkable neighborhood, with everything here in one place!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/53ed72fd-14d2-4429-a0ad-8bf31a28c3f7.jpg',13580938,20,'45.48152','-122.64528',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,30,35,151,4.85,15361775),(685,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15375039','NE Suite Spot! Alberta/Williams/Mississippi','Welcome! This is a fully appointed, large private suite with sleeping, sitting, dining, and work areas, and a well-equipped kitchenette. Very comfy bed and plush carpet. Walk score-89/bike score-94; a short stroll/ride brings you to 3 of Portland’s most lively districts—Alberta Arts, Williams, and Mississippi—and dozens of the best restaurants, bars, shops, galleries, & music venues in town. Great for couples, solo travelers, parents w/kids, or groups cool with a little coziness!','With a walk score of 89 and bike score of 94, a short stroll/ride brings you to three of Portland’s most lively districts—Alberta Arts, Williams St., and Mississippi Ave.—and dozens of the best restaurants, bars, shops, galleries, and music venues in town. Peninsula Park & Rose Garden (the city’s oldest), a gem of our celebrated Parks system, is also a walk away, along with historic North Portland Library and a certain feminist bookstore made famous by the show Portlandia. You can also stroll the immediate neighborhood and admire the gorgeous, century-old Victorian homes and large mature trees.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-15375039/original/34b1c547-0996-47e7-9398-ea0eb48639e1.jpeg',4649264,14,'45.56276','-122.66411',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,62.00,1,100,516,4.88,15375039),(686,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15378341','Hawthorne / Tabor Getaway','Mt Tabor and Hawthorne Blvd are a 10 minute walk away. Tabor is a huge park, great for walking, running, hiking and biking.  Hawthorne has a great selection of bars, restaurants and cafes to choose from, along with the iconic Bagdad Theater and Powell\'s Bookstore, Hawthorne location. The house is good for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, and families (with kids).  The house has two bedrooms with queen beds, a kitchen, dining area, and living room. Off-street parking for one vehicle','Hawthorne has long been a hot spot for bars, cafes, and restaurants, and in the past five years, Division has also seen tremendous growth with more than 20 trendy new pubs and restaurants like Salt and Straw and Petite Provence while still retaining some of the old-school Portland haunts like Reel M Inn, Tom\'s and the Scoreboard<br /><br />Mt Tabor is a huge park with both paved and dirt hiking and biking paths.<br /><br />There is a yoga studio directly across the street from the house.  In the past, they have had introductory 2-week deals.  I think a monthly membership is around $100.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d0a567fc-8bfb-4e33-9fe6-831523c53c59.jpg',1610080,15,'45.50669','-122.61047',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,95.00,30,1125,9,4.33,15378341),(687,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15408554','Cozy Room in Eclectic Victorian-31 day min no tax','A comfy private room with lock and key inside a charming 1896 Victorian building set up for Airbnb guests-like a mini hostel.  Out front is a popular Mexican food cart and 2 blocks away is trendy~NW 23rd Avenue-a 1.5 mile strip of coffee shops, restaurants and unique shops. A bus stop is 2 blocks away or use Uber/Lyft/car to get downtown in 6 minutes. Also Forest park Is only a 15 minute walk away.<br />Part of your fee goes to help Ukrainians🇺🇦. Your host lives on premises in a different apartment.','The NW Alphabet District offers a variety of wonderful art, clothing, yoga, coffee, specialty shops, pubs, grocery stores and restaurants.  Walking down NW 23rd Avenue is a great way to interact with Native Portlanders. Take NW 23rd Avenue all the way to Burnside Street (turn left-East) then pass Powells books and other sights all the way to Voodoo donuts and explore the waterfront to get an even better feel of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7daa9e5a-006b-4769-b565-8926ded09192.jpg',98202133,27,'45.537888','-122.697311',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,31,180,595,4.95,15408554),(688,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15414261','Unparalleled City & Mtn Views','Sit on the deck for an uninterrupted view of Mt Hood and sip your coffee while enjoying the sun rise or enjoy the sun setting over the city & Mt. St. Helens.<br />Amazing views from all the windows but just walking blocks to  Dwntwn. Climb some stairs to this exceptional rooftop apartment and have the best views in town. Outfitted with high end linens and towels for your comfort. Perched atop a historic home this gem in the sky is perfect for your holiday or work.<br />Permitted and hold ASTR Short term.','Vibe and Style<br />This hillside paradise has a mix of young and established families as well as single professionals. The area contains some of Portland’s most spectacular high-end real estate, where many of the homes have views of downtown and Mount Hood. The neighborhood claims an abundance of classic older Portland homes in styles such as English cottage, Tudor, Colonial, Foursquare, Arts & Crafts and Queen Anne. Most of these homes were built in the early part of the 20th century. Great for walking around and checking out the wonderful architecture.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/13ec7e0b-30d6-4679-af8e-a52859209a28.jpg',12846561,44,'45.51038','-122.68686',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,175.00,2,1125,10,5.00,15414261),(689,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15422766','Charming Bungalow in Vibrant Neighborhood','Charming bungalow with urban appeal and lush garden space. You\'ll be warmly welcomed and feel immediately at home. <br /><br />North Mississippi Avenue features a long stretch of stores, bars and restaurants; the acclaimed eateries and bars on up-and-coming North Williams are just half a mile away.  <br /><br />You can pass a whole day pleasantly strolling and shopping on Mississippi, and when you\'re trying to decide what to eat you\'ll have more options than you can eat at during your visit.','A short but bustling commercial corridor, North Mississippi Avenue is most commonly known—to outsiders—for the one day a year when it bursts at its seams (seriously, some 30,000 people turn out) with music, merriment and local street vendors during the annual Mississippi Street Fair, held each July.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/deb6f4db-7457-415f-a551-30b187f76e65.jpg',98845081,9,'45.55233','-122.67535',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,30,1125,376,4.99,15422766),(690,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15456416','Vintage Portland Charm in The Heart of NE 30+ Days','Relax in this travelers paradise! Just blocks from N Williams restaurant and shopping strip and the famous Alberta Arts district! You\'ll never get bored, but when you\'re finally tired you can venture back to your cozy slice of Portland heaven and recharge in our fabulous home.','We love how close our home is to some of our favorite things! Like N Williams St, Alberta Arts district, Mississippi St, Irvington and Oldtown- Downtown Portland!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8560175a-a3e7-4aa9-b963-08a901f49a6c.jpg',99163732,14,'45.55505','-122.65727',1,2,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,59,4.98,15456416),(691,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15496107','Pearl District Condo-Prime Location! Free Parking','This amazing Pearl District condo is perfect for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers and small furry friends (pets). You simply can\'t beat the location! Within steps of the condo you will find three world-class parks, Portland Streetcar, Biketown bike share kiosks, Amtrak train station, a large grocery store and the beautiful waterfront walkway. No need for a car, but if you have one, there is a secured parking spot included. Newly painted and furnished in Nov.','Pearl District','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-15496107/original/de836908-85ac-4aca-a71c-cca976bf7398.jpeg',25596073,2,'45.53306','-122.68118',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,90.00,30,1125,31,4.87,15496107),(692,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15498447','Sun-filled charmer: Two full baths!','Welcome to Casa Felice (Happy House!) <br /><br />High ceilings, huge windows, 2 spacious bedrooms and 2 baths ,quality furnishings, TV room, fireplace, huge private patio in back yard, private driveway for parking. <br /><br />The best area. Charming quiet neighborhood. Short walk to restaurants, coffee shops, bakery, and a grocery store. <br /><br />An 8 minute stroll through Westmoreland Park, a block away, takes you to MAX Light Rail that can get you around Portland, even to the airport!','Our neighborhood is a very quiet, friendly place. The neighbors all know each other and will say hello. This is not the place for loud parties or late nights. We ask that you please be respectful and keep noise to a minimum, especially while enjoying the patio. <br /><br />You can walk to so many things!  If you want cute coffee shops, restaurants, movies, antique shops, wine bars, brew pubs, yummy bakeries,  famous Portland food carts -- it\'s all within a 20 minute walk. It is also a short walk to the highest rated municipal golf course in the Portland area.<br /><br />We are also one block from super lovely Westmoreland Park!  Reed College is about a 10 - 15 minute walk from our home, we’re a great base for visiting parents.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7139b23e-2f96-4690-b94f-8ef187de47d3.jpg',32619683,20,'45.46923','-122.64218',1,4,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,180,63,4.97,15498447),(693,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15500919','The Ladd - A Perfect Walkable Spot','Mid-century modern comforts in this duplex home with big windows and simple style. <br /><br />Perfect walking location to the best Portland has to offer with additional easy access to public transportation.<br /><br />Ample outdoor lounge and dining space available for guests to share with the owners, who live on site for quick and responsive service.<br /><br />Sleeps 4 adults comfortably with room to work from home if needed. Reliable and fast internet is provided.','Ladd\'s Addition is an inner southeast historic district of Portland, Oregon, United States. It is Portland\'s oldest planned residential development, and one of the oldest in the western United States. The district is known in Portland for a diagonal street pattern, which is at odds with the rectilinear grid of the surrounding area. Roughly eight blocks (east-west) by ten blocks (north-south) in size (by reference to the surrounding grid), Ladd\'s is bordered by SE Hawthorne, Division, 12th, and 20th streets.<br /><br />Close to some of the best food and drink in the city. It is also very connected to public transit and a short walk to the east side of the Willamette River. Mount Taber is just up the road.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-15500919/original/911cb930-a156-43b6-b1cd-91712289eccb.jpeg',5202775,25,'45.50719','-122.65298',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,139.00,1,45,27,5.00,15500919),(694,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15523295','Beautiful Basement Studio Mississippi Neighborhood','Perfect location with a walk score of 94.  This is a fully furnished daylight basement apartment in the Mississippi District, in the heart of Portland with craft breweries, funky shops, restaurants, art, wine shops, food carts & more! 5 minutes from downtown Portland. I used to live in this apartment and loved it as my home. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions! There is an additional $150 cleaning fee for pets.','Location, Location, Location!  My guests rave about the central location to everything Portland has to offer.  It is a great spot for people exploring the city and is close to all Portland neighborhoods.  It is within walking distance to shops, breweries, galleries, parks, bars, grocery stores, etc.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-15523295/original/e8280789-1ec3-4130-acaf-9b3287eead8c.jpeg',6063183,9,'45.55171','-122.6736',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,31,365,50,4.88,15523295),(695,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15524397','1920s Bungalow in NoPo','Located in North Portland, my house has easy access to I-5, downtown, Alberta Arts district and the trendy Mississippi district. The house is airy and bright with original features and modern appliances. Good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers. LGBT friendly.','Located in North Portland, my house has easy access to I-5, downtown, Alberta Arts district, Kenton and the trendy Mississippi district. There is a park within walking distance as well as a Fred Meyer for grocery essentials.  If you have a car, the home is close to highways that can take you to the Columbia River Gorge for hiking as well as to the coast for a day excursion.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-15524397/original/c6cffe6a-11a6-4079-8576-2ece4f25cfcc.jpg',9423242,48,'45.57816','-122.67294',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,42.00,2,7,236,4.96,15524397),(696,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15525083','Private Cozy Retreat, inner SE Portland/Reed Area','I\'m offering to you a Private 2 BR, 1-BA, w/ full Kitchen Basement-Apartment! Just blocks from Reed College, Restaurants & shops in Portland\'s Inner SE.  Walk to Starbucks, Marigold\'s, Trader Joe\'s & more! A Perfect, cozy place to relax after exploring Portland! You have a private separate back entrance & direct access to backyard & outdoor patio & fire pit! My place is great for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, & families (with kids)','Beautiful Reed College neighborhood!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/57b0106e-646c-4317-a819-50387b613269.jpg',91753188,61,'45.4889','-122.62782',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,70.00,30,730,364,4.67,15525083),(697,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15529938','Queen Studio, Comfortable Cozy Chic','Comfortable attached studio in beautiful wooded Hazelwood. Private entrance with outside patio area. Kitchenette with refrigerator, microwave oven, and coffee maker. Queen bed, full bath and shower. Ten minutes to airport and 20-30 minutes to downtown Portland. Easy access to I-205 and I-84. Bus 1+ block away.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/864451ed-e01e-47c1-a48c-90f38ad7fc93.jpg',39865353,63,'45.53085','-122.52799',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,324,4.84,15529938),(698,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15573458','Beautiful Oasis in NE Portland!','Relax in retreat-like space with giant Doug firs/Cedars in backyard and organic garden in front, while still 5 mins from all city activity.<br /><br />Hardwood floors, high ceilings, fireplace, hot tub, outdoor shower, awesome location. <br /><br />Room: Queen bed, Casper mattress, two big windows, dresser, vanity and closet.  <br /><br />Easy public transportation. Good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.  Well behaved dogs considered. <br /><br />Acupuncture/massage treatments available for additional fee.','Roseway is awesome!  <br /><br />5 mins to Alberta Arts District.  5-7 mins to airport.  Easy access to Columbia River Gorge and highways to Mt Hood, Hood River, and winery adventures.  <br /><br />We are close to amazing restaurants like Pizzeria Ottos, Kainos Coffee, Thai Seasons, lots of Pho shops, and BTU.  Unicorn Burger food cart is 2 blocks away.  Safeway and Walgreens are 4 blocks away for all your needs.  <br /><br />And dont miss the baklava and growler pours at Ira\'s deli!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/78f050c8-6518-4b55-b8dc-eace251a244f.jpg',2576419,39,'45.55237','-122.58542',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,61.00,30,1125,8,5.00,15573458),(699,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15590226','Cozy, eclectic SE Portland upside down penthouse','Enjoy the Reed College/Woodstock neighborhood in SE Portland.  Windows looking onto the yard with private entrance.  Furnished with knickknacks from my collection of modernist & antique furniture, art, curios, and books.  Also:  bathroom w/shower, fridge,  & hot pot (not a kitchen). Walk to nearby nature trails at Reed College , Trader Joe\'s &  New Seasons (groceries), vintage mall, Double Mountain & Gigantic breweries, , local restaurants, cafes & bars; bus line half block away.','Woodstock, Reed, Foster,  and Creston-Kenilworth neighborhoods all a short walk away.  Two great OR breweries nearby (Gigantic and Double Mountain), as well as my favorite Thai-ish restaurant, Nudi, Portland\'s southern food institution, the Delta,  and for meat-lovers, Otto\'s Sausage Kitchen (with outdoor grilling).  Also, Laughing Planet offers lots of healthy food and dinosaurs.  New Seasons Market with a rooftop cafe (complete with fire pit & wine/beer bar), Grand Central Bakery, and Shut Up and Eat for sandwiches, are all short walks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/67b2df03-4be0-4f15-9c15-f238e28925d9.jpg',100441836,38,'45.48576','-122.6217',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,82.00,2,7,245,4.91,15590226),(700,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15646823','Quiet Stay In Overlook near the Airport','My house is close to light rail and bus lines in a quiet and secure area. Many restaurants, coffee houses and bars are within walking distance and there is a large grocery store nearby in case you need provisions. There are parks within walking distance. My place is good for solo adventurers and business travelers. There is another bedroom that can sleep two and I have an air mattress available. Kitchen use is communal so it is restricted to light occasional use not full time three meals a day.','There are quite a few very good restaurants with in walking distance of the house with a sprinkling of coffee houses and bars. Well lit and quiet there are also a couple of parks with in a few blocks. Also a great grocery store is near by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b718f051-c05b-4962-9b20-970d6b99a7e7.jpg',67395194,13,'45.56296','-122.68875',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,38.00,1,5,453,4.91,15646823),(701,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15658660','The Traveler’s Cozy Retreat','Escape the road or your relatives into a peaceful spacious room with a private bathroom. We are located in the friendly SW Portland Maplewood neighborhood, 7 minutes from I-5 and 12 minutes to downtown.','Ours is a quiet friendly neighborhood in SW Portland, hills, views, lots of trees and parks. Two nice coffee places (Maplewood Coffee & Tea and Driftwood Coffee) within a 10 minute walk, also serving food.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/927064e4-8d61-4907-a95a-125b074af089.jpg',1495645,75,'45.47463','-122.73197',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,52.00,30,365,3,5.00,15658660),(702,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15724441','Adorable Craftsman Home! Inner SE Portland Reed','Offering my charming, air-conditioned, completely renovated 1920\'s home!  This 2 bedroom, 1 bath home also has landing area with pull out sofa, Sleeps 5+.  Near Reed College, Restaurants & shops in Portland\'s Inner SE.  You’ll love our clean, cozy home to relax after exploring Portland. Secure front door entrance.  Main & Upper floor are completely private.   Home is completely secure from a separate basement unit. My place is great for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, & families','Beautiful Reed College neighborhood! 10-minute walk to Woodstock neighborhood, 10 minute walk to Division neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/22a7fccd-104a-4e02-8011-cf35bd385139.jpg',91753188,67,'45.49056','-122.62585',1,6,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,730,326,4.74,15724441),(703,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15728518','Portland\'s Hawthorne Hideaway - 2 bdrms Own floor','Enjoy safe, secure, comfortable (!) bedrooms and common space in the heart of Portland’s most iconic neighborhood.','Our place is conveniently located in the heart of Portland\'s trendy Hawthorne District - full of fun Portlandia quirkiness.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/46765520-07a5-4a0b-bdcd-032205d4a62e.jpg',18590525,8,'45.51046','-122.63315',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,99.00,1,14,123,4.73,15728518),(704,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15734618','Huge Mt Tabor Studio with Courtyard Entry','Need to extend your stay? Ask about adding 60 days, 90 days and more!<br /><br />Open and airy 20\'x20\' studio with 2 queen beds. Minutes from Mt. Tabor. You’ll love it because we\'re pet friendly and a quick walk to Mt Tabor! A great spot for couples, adventurers, business travelers and furry friends.<br /><br />Private full bath.<br /><br />The entrance is accessible through the garage and opens onto a shared courtyard.<br /><br />If traveling with a pet they must be accompanied by their humans at all times.','Walk to Mt Tabor in 5 minutes, it\'s only 4 blocks away! Minutes from Salt and Straw on Division St. Or cook yourself up a meal with easy access to grocery shopping on SE 82nd, such as, Winco or FuBonn, the Asian market.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0460aa8e-3f7a-4139-adb0-87f3f6ec5300.jpg',8260857,37,'45.50382','-122.59359',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,68.00,30,60,421,4.74,15734618),(705,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15757243','The Westmoreland Lighthouse - Private studio in SE','We\'ve dubbed this stunning, newly constructed detached studio the \"Lighthouse\" because of the way natural light pours through the 550-square-foot studio\'s many windows and dances off its walls and vaulted ceilings. An open loft offers soothing views. We are tucked into the Westmoreland neighborhood\'s quiet residential area, but are only a five minute walk from more than 20 restaurants and entertainment features. Westmoreland Park, Reed College and downtown Portland are just minutes away by car.','Since you asked about the neighborhood, let us expound a bit: The Westmoreland neighborhood of Portland was platted in the mid-1920s -- a time of explosive growth in the greater Portland area. Our house dates to 1925 (our studio was completed in 2016). It\'s not uncommon for 100-plus kids to ring our bell on Halloween. Myriad strings of Christmas lights brighten our winter-night sidewalks. Westmoreland Park, just a five-minute walk from us, recently reopened after 18 months of renovation aimed entirely at making the stream that flows through it habitable for native fish. More than 20 restaurants and fun shops are a 10-minute walk from us, with scores more only a few minutes farther by car. Reed College and Lewis & Clark College are both nearby. Popular shopping and dining areas near us include SE Division, SE Hawthorne, and SE Belmont boulevards -- all popular destinations that are custom made for leisurely strolling. Beyond that, we consider ourselves fonts of information, able to poin','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/53b214f6-4699-449f-be22-d9d4edd9b533.jpg',11423234,20,'45.47605','-122.64326',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,84.00,2,1125,596,4.97,15757243),(706,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15774439','Home Should Be Your Favorite Place In The World!','North Portland Bungalow, located off N. Lombard in Historic Kenton neighborhood, classic 1928 architectural features blend with modern mid century.  This small home features the warmth of hardwood floors, sleek stainless steel wood burning fireplace, a freshly remodeled bath with Toto toilet / bidet system.  Outdoor firepit, herb garden, tropical plants. 10 minutes from downtown, accessible to TriMet lines, bike lanes & skateboard parks. Great space for those into art & music, & gay friendly.','North Portland is close to many fun, accessible adventures! <br /><br />Whether you are looking for Beaches, Hiking Trails, Running, Bike Riding or Skateboarding...<br />• It\'s nearby. Sauvie\'s Island, St. John\'s Cathedral Park, Columbia Park, & Chimney Park all are dog friendly.<br />Running, & Bike riding; try  scenic route on N. Willamette Blvd. or Marine Drive.<br /><br />•  5 minutes to Adidas North America HQ,<br />10-15 minutes to downtown, artsy NW Pearl District & hip NE Alberta & N. Williams streets. <br /><br />• Grocery? Check out Green Zebra & New Seasons  - both are minutes away.<br /><br />• Pubs & Music? Try Mock Crest Tavern for Blues, Lombard Pub for alternative music acts, <br />McMenamins in St. Johns, Chill & Fill  for the best in local craft beers, trivia nights & sports!<br /><br />• Want to get further away? North Portland is 5 minutes to I-5 North to Seattle. And  15 minutes to PDX Airport.<br /><br />• Need a bit of quiet, off the grid time?  My home can give ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3586f5ce-9946-439a-b62f-4208ef33ceda.jpg',99762997,55,'45.58193','-122.70356',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,58.00,1,1125,395,4.73,15774439),(707,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15788692','Alberta Arts Gem Brimming with Color and Light','Smell the cherry blossom from a corner-lot front porch. Inside, walls, floors, and furnishings pop with fun, fresh colors. Light pours into a sunny kitchen through windows, doors, and skylights. Plants and artful prints pepper the upbeat spaces.<br /><br />UPDATES: New updated HVAC system in November 2022, so now more comfortable temperature control for summer and winter months in second story!','The Alberta Arts neighborhood is one of Portland’s hot spots. Explore Alberta Street’s tasty restaurants, watering holes, coffee galore, and boutiques. Last Thursdays in summer are an excuse to share art, libations, crafts, and great conversation.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2fbed92d-b698-43e5-9219-20bf27bee20c.jpg',21621478,1,'45.55675','-122.63749',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,225.00,2,30,264,4.93,15788692),(708,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15803257','Portland Sunflower House','Step into this charming 1926 Craftsman Bungalow, where natural light streams through large picture windows, casting a warm glow on original hardwood floors. Nestled on a tranquil corner property in a quiet, family-friendly neighborhood, this home offers a comfortable, peaceful retreat.','Nestled within the serene enclave of the Piedmont neighborhood in N/NE Portland, this area offers a peaceful respite. A verdant park lies just a few blocks from your doorstep, providing a local natural getaway for humans and dogs alike! Additionally, within a mile radius, you\'ll discover charming cafes, boutique shops, a convenient USPS office, and a well-appointed library.<br /><br />For those seeking easy access to public transportation, the Max light rail station is a mere 15-minute stroll from this residence, ensuring seamless connectivity to the city\'s offerings.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-15803257/original/e1ac6d68-3715-4e2d-a8b0-3e6adcf23e68.jpg',9467415,48,'45.58031917898625','-122.67566641816826',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,195.00,2,1125,45,4.96,15803257),(709,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15804432','Center of PDX 2B+ loft w/garage!','Brand new remodeled classic Portland duplex. This 2 bedroom w/ bonus bed and pullout in unfinished basement is the perfect fit for anyone. Fully furnished with top of the line kitchen appliances, beautiful range, full size fridge, and a dishwasher! Loft master bedroom is massive with its own sitting area,  amazing light and bathroom. Backyard is completely fenced and private, perfect for hosting, grill and deck included! There is also a washer/dryer and all linens and kitchen wares are provided.','You have freeway access without the noise. Can walk across the street to a park, to the grocery store, to food, and anything else! It\'s family friendly with schools closeby but centrally located to bars and a quick hop to downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c9c21fb3-1d96-42d5-8865-bd43130171c9.jpg',9292540,33,'45.53624','-122.63264',1,6,2.00,2.00,1.00,99.00,30,1125,121,4.79,15804432),(710,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15817715','Foodie Fun at the Urban Owl - Division/Hawthorne','Foodie Paradise - Division, Hawthorne, Clinton. Walk to some of the hottest restaurants in Portland and the US, or cook your favorites in your own full gourmet kitchen.  Within walking distance to Salt & Straw, Oma\'s Hideaway, Ok Omens, Blue Star Donuts, New Seasons Grocery, the amazing McMenamins Bagdad Theater, and many more of our favorite neighborhood spots.','We are located between the Hawthorne and Division neighborhoods of Inner SE Portland.  According to Travel Portland: \"Eclectic is the norm on Southeast Hawthorne Boulevard, a walkable street with block after block of vintage shops, boutiques and cafés. Hippies and hipsters mingle on this busy Southeast Portland street.\"  Division/Clinton is described as \"A rich crop of noteworthy restaurants distinguishes this eastside district.  This pair of close-in Southeast Portland streets features block after block of must-see — and must-eat — destinations.\"','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fc0c5aed-5a31-41cb-b6d6-7ae2705fd7a0.jpg',8202650,25,'45.5108','-122.64102',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,93.00,2,13,427,4.98,15817715),(711,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15888715','Mod Cool Private Entrance Space in SE Portland!','Hello!<br /><br />Beautiful neighborhood<br />High ceilings <br />Large windows<br />Beautifully decorated<br />Plush King Bed in 1-bedroom-with a door.<br />2nd queen bed living room pull out<br /><br />Established Neighborhood 20 minutes of City Center.<br /><br />Discounts are a hassle so: no. <br /><br />There is a locked access door adjacent to the bathroom we use in between guests to service the space. We don\'t go in the Airbnb space when guests are there, obviously. There\'s a photo of the door, last photo, in the Addional Photos section of Photos.','Hello!<br />Our lovely garden level space is 20 minutes from city center on a larger tree lined street in a mature neighborhood. <br /><br />We are about a 20 minutes from downtown Portland on a larger street. Please try to understand this. Please look at the map of where we are in the city in relation to where you want to go. Please refrain from booking us and giving less than 5 stars for value and location when we have been completely transparent and upfront about our location. Our value absolutely reflects our location, availability and pricing compared to the closer in guesthouses. The stars mean a lot Airbnb so they mean a lot to us and our relationship with them. We are 20 minutes driving time plus parking from downtown Portland, Moda Center, The Oregon Zoo, Washington Park, Japanese Garden and the Rose Test Garden. We are an hour away from the beach and Mt. Hood. If there\'s somewhere you\'re interested in going please ask. If we aren\'t in the locale you need we\'ll tell you and tr','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ca954e73-7361-4163-a3f1-fc85f201541d.jpg',8825,65,'45.47869','-122.58293',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,100.00,3,16,294,4.94,15888715),(712,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15900501','Artistic Victorian Gem in a Trendy neighborhood','This 1883 Victorian is one of Portland\'s hidden gems. In its heyday, it operated as a boarding house. Old world charm will transport you to another time while providing modern comforts! Pine Manor is just a few blocks from coffee shops, eateries, bars and shops. Everything you need for a perfect visit is just a stone\'s throw away! Located between the Hawthorne and Burnside bridges, and within walking distance to the Convention Center, it is the ideal place to enjoy the best of Portland!','Over 140 years ago when this home was built, Portland was a quaint logging town and river trade gateway. The mode of transportation was horse and buggy. Boy, a lot has changed since then! Portland (or Portlandia) is now known for it\'s \"weirdness\" holding true to the word with its quirky skilled-craftsman type of inhabitants. <br /><br />We are located in the popular and safe Buckman neighborhood, which includes the southern border of the Hawthorn district. Trendy and hip, and walking distance to most everything including parks.<br /><br />The central east side of Portland is the heart of this lovely city. There are a great few vegan boutique grocers, micro-breweries, entertainment venues, juice bars, parks, community gardens, rock gyms and yoga studios. There are so many amazing restaurants to experience close by you won\'t miss the kitchen one bit. <br /><br />Portland is known for it\'s lush outdoor refuges. Laurelhurst Park is among the most beautiful in the city (20 blocks away)  Col','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTU5MDA1MDE%3D/original/8a8365e5-98d6-4256-ab7d-0b079f44f13b.jpeg',103138695,32,'45.52132','-122.65144',1,10,2.00,5.00,5.00,298.00,3,90,192,4.93,15900501),(713,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15930586','Two Palms: Spacious, central, remodeled 5bd beauty','• Brand new kitchen<br />• Central AC<br />• New washer/dryer<br />• High-speed gigabit wifi<br />• Walk Score 80 - short walk to groceries, restaurants, public transit<br />• 15min to downtown<br />• 2200 sq ft / 205 square m<br />• Front yard w garden (no backyard)<br />• Bike Score 95<br />• 2 levels, 2 living rooms<br />• HBO, premium cable<br />• Gas fireplace<br />• Safe neighborhood<br />• Free, easy street parking','Two Palms is centrally located in close-in NE Portland in Alberta Arts/Concordia - the best neighborhood in town!  We\'re 15 minutes from PDX airport (commercial airlines don\'t fly overhead so our neighborhood is tranquil!) and 15-20 mins from downtown Portland.  Excellent restaurants, cool bars and cafes are just steps away and a fabulous organic grocery store (New Seasons) is two blocks away. The neighborhood is home to the original Salt & Straw ice cream shop and Pine State Biscuits.  We\'re very close to a number of excellent urban parks.  Fernhill Park, just a few blocks away, has a brand new playground and summer splash pad for kids, running paths, and a track. Other Portland top spots (downtown, inner SE, Washington Park) are just a short drive away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/075fe51b-bd39-4a7f-a3ed-6273c30952f2.jpg',3158903,1,'45.56459','-122.62713',1,12,2.00,5.00,6.00,286.00,3,90,237,4.95,15930586),(714,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15974802','Waterfront Condo In The Heart Of Downtown Portland','A contemporary, cozy and centrally located ‘home away from home’ on the Willamette River.  The panoramic views are spectacular day and night! Easily explore all of Portland!','We love everything about this neighborhood!  You are ON the river, watching runners, bikers, dog walkers and river traffic go by from the living room or deck.  Perfect for runners, walkers and bikers.  Spectacular foodie town with everything from fine dining to food trucks - walk to The Pearl (a few blocks) or downtown.  Great shopping - walk or take the street car to trendy NW 23rd for unique boutiques, or walk downtown to Pacific Place mall for upscale shops - take advantage of NO sales tax!  Weekend \"Saturday\" Market (it\'s held on Sat. and Sunday) and excellent Farmer\'s Market by PSU are also walk distance.  We are in the perfect location for everything Portland has to offer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/44a75d1c-3eb0-4182-b903-8e0a4098bc09.jpg',27370966,43,'45.52868','-122.67388',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,30,730,6,5.00,15974802),(715,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/15987481','Modern Sanctuary in the heart of Concordia.','Our newly built in-law apartment is located on a quiet street close to McMenamins Kennedy School hotel, Extracto Coffee, Wilder restaurant, Dame, Gabbiano\'s restaurant, Bardo Tea (tea and meditation), The People\'s Yoga, Teote Tavern, New Seasons Supermarket. You’ll love our place because of the comfy bed, the neighborhood, the coziness, the light, the kitchen, the local joints. Our place is good for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, families (with kids), travelers with a pet.','Our place is located in a beautiful green neighborhood where people are nice and friendly, close to some of the best restaurants, bars, art galleries and coffee shops that Portland has to offer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/de29ee4e-94b7-4bbf-9d3e-14e11c7eb5f8.jpg',14968156,1,'45.5642','-122.63582',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,88.00,1,28,498,4.94,15987481),(716,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16017785','2 bedrooms plus office in vibrant Buckman','Available November 15th<br /><br />This newly-renovated, fully-furnished 1300 sq. ft. apartment is on the main-floor of a duplex in the heart of Buckman, close to downtown Portland and minutes to all of the action in SE Portland.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e6d4381b-782e-42bd-86e8-8bd199ec9fa0.jpg',3014197,32,'45.51658','-122.65151',1,3,1.00,2.00,2.00,95.00,30,90,2,5.00,16017785),(717,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16072598','Spacious Loft in the Heart of Southeast PDX','Enjoy Portland in this cozy and spacious bungalow in the heart of southeast PDX. Come stay in a private, loft apartment in our home with a separate entrance, keyless entry, 50\'\' smart TV, laundry and a kitchenette/bathroom. Public transit is easily accessible, city center 2.5 miles away & Division street - a restaurant and food cart hub - is a 10 min walk.<br />Permitted by the City of Portland Bureau of Development Services - Permit #17-156319-HO','Our home boasts an incredible walking score: Division street (amazing eating, drinking and shopping), bowling alley, Hopworks Urban Brewery (organic world class beer and food) and one of Portland\'s best food cart pods!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cf6cbfd8-28ef-4cfe-a0ec-cc2309c5a0da.jpg',2673359,8,'45.50012','-122.62348',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,53.00,2,30,325,4.94,16072598),(718,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16123022','1 BD Quiet & Light Filled Home / Truly Private','Welcome to the Little Blue House!<br /><br />•   Modern & Peaceful In Safe Neighborhood<br />•   Private Entrance & No Shared Walls<br />•   Filled With Sunshine and Lots of Windows<br />•   Unlimited Free Parking On Street <br /><br />Within Blocks Of The Best Of Portland!<br /><br />•  50 Beers On Tap / Craft Cocktails / Top Restaurants <br />•  Locally Roasted Coffee & Artisan Bakeries <br />•  Vintage Shopping & Cute Boutiques <br />•  Tall Trees / Rose Gardens / Willamette River','Located within the Ladd\'s Addition neighborhood which is a charming maze of rose gardens, huge elms trees and beautiful old homes. Just blocks to great cocktails, coffee, groceries and restaurants! <br /><br />•  Situated between SE Hawthorne and SE Division streets<br />•  Minutes to OHSU / South Waterfront / Downtown / Pearl <br />•  Walk to the Central Eastside & the Eastbank Esplanade<br />•  91 Walking Score / 100 Biking Score <br /><br />You will find street parking on our block easily, but no need for a car. You can walk to: <br /><br />•  Huge Assortment of Restaurants & Food Carts<br />•  Grocery Stores, Co-op & Year Round Farmers Market <br />•  Parks, Willamette River & Green Spaces   <br />•  Coffee Shops & Bakeries <br />•  Breweries, Urban Wineries & Distilleries','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-16123022/original/b852ad62-8d3e-41b8-88a8-55322b3af605.jpeg',672152,25,'45.50691','-122.65305',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,150.00,28,120,223,4.99,16123022),(719,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16132722','Cozy Two Bedroom Downstairs Living Space','When you book this quiet downstairs private space there are two comfortable bedrooms-one with a double bed and one with a queen bed. There is also a living room, dining area, laundry space, refrigerator, and single bath with shower/tub. There is an additional fee for a 5th guest. A cot can be provided.<br /><br />We live in a pleasant residential neighborhood of NE Portland with quick access to shops, restaurants, the airport, and Gateway Max line, which will take you about anywhere in the Portland area.','We have Shari’s, Starbucks, Winco grocery, BiMart, Taco Bell, Mod Pizza, Panda Express, Dollar Tree, Pizza Guys all 3 short blocks from the house, easy walking. There is also a private school with a big field and track that same distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/282b1b1c-3ecd-47d6-86e2-c1ade2ff2b08.jpg',52170945,35,'45.5357','-122.54052',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,100.00,30,30,62,4.85,16132722),(720,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16135056','Laurelhurst gem - directly across from Park!','Separate guest house apartment that is directly across from beautiful Laurelhurst Park.  It is clean, bright and cozy.  The apartment has it\'s own kitchen, washer and dryer, walking distance to multiple restaurants, coffee shops and boutiques.  The apartment is above the garage and separate from the main house.','Located across from 30 acre Laurelhurst Park with lovely walkways.  Just minutes to several fine restaurants and coffee houses.  The neighborhood has beautiful homes of architectural  and historic significance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a4452c47-394c-4415-810f-d0771bad74ed.jpg',105257516,23,'45.52019','-122.62542',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,111,4.98,16135056),(721,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16135714','Cozy Apartment by the Park-Newly Renovated','New renovation, October 2024!!!  Our home is beautifully situated across from a quiet park. We are located just a couple blocks walk to restaurants, coffee shops, boutiques and bus stops on trendy Hawthorne and Division streets. LGBTQIA2S+ safe space.','We are ideally situated between the popular Hawthorne and Division streets.  We are 2.5 blocks from the nearest bus stop and are walking distance to shops, restaurants, grocery stores, movie theaters.  Best of all we are located right across the street from a park.  There is ample parking as well.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTYxMzU3MTQ%3D/original/2a26d520-f539-4660-9c0f-6e58ef2c158f.jpeg',3901470,8,'45.51086','-122.63464',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,51.00,1,28,1049,4.89,16135714),(722,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16146098','Cozy Private Dwelling in Cathedral Park / St Johns','Welcome to the Nagel Nook! We are located in the Cathedral Park / St. Johns neighborhood of Portland. This private basement dwelling has a queen bedroom, full kitchen, bathroom, laundry facilities, and a spacious living area for leisurely coffee & wifi sessions or post-excursion relaxing. Easy access to downtown via car, public transportation or bicycle. We welcome guests from all backgrounds and are LQBTQ friendly.','St. Johns is Portland\'s northernmost neighborhood and one of the last to see major gentrification in the last few years. \"Downtown St. Johns\", as the main business area is known, is home to several eating spots, 2 movie theaters, breweries and bars, coffee shops and cute local shops. There are a few different grocery stores nearby (including local fave New Seasons where it is possible to grab a quick meal from the deli) and on Saturdays from May-October, the downtown plaza hosts a local farmers market. Nearby Cathedral Park is a great place to relax and take in spectacular views of the gothic St. Johns suspension bridge. Directly across the St. Johns bridge lies Forest Park, which offers numerous hiking trails. We are also located a mile and a half from the University of Portland campus.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/35477415-8e7d-4a77-b634-340089a72501.jpg',39660315,42,'45.58354','-122.75054',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,110.00,3,28,67,5.00,16146098),(723,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16159044','Waterfront dream home 10 min to PDX airport','Columbia River paradise 10 minutes from the Portland International Airport. Preferred guest =  travel nurse. WEEKLY & MONTHLY DISCOUNTS.  BUSINESS FRIENDLY!!  Keurig.  85\" tv and our favorite DVDs in living room as you are allowed access to living room, kitchen and deck. comfy queen bed in the airbnb guest room.Local menus for delivery. Sit on the deck and relax as the mighty Columbia passes by. Limit 1 Airbnb guest.  Free parking for your car. Security cameras on all external doors.','The Columbia river is the biggest draw! So peaceful and beautiful.  If you must leave to shop Winco and Costco are close by.  Gas stations within a mile.  (Costco is the closest store and sells gas.  It\'s just a few blocks away.)  Neighbors include osprey, beavers, a bald eagle, ducks, geese, bunnies and occasional water skiers and boaters on the river.  Across the river is Government island, a popular boating destination.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cd5e35df-f3cf-4cdc-964c-1a657d2b21d2.jpg',57792832,66,'45.56602','-122.52011',2,1,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,45,40,4.93,16159044),(724,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16159235','Portland International Guesthouse - Apartment','Our Flanders Apartment is a fully furnished, cozy, 1 bedroom garden level/basement apartment.  It has a large bedroom with 1 queen bed and carries a maximum capacity of 2 people.  This spacious apartment has a private entry, several big windows, a comfortable seating area, breakfast nook, fully stocked kitchen, private bath with shower and washer/dryer.  Free WIFI and Roku TV and all utilities are provided.','This apartment is located in Portland\'s historic Alphabet District also known as Nob Hill.  Our neighborhood is the city\'s most charming and vibrant. We are within walking distance or a short transit ride Downtown, the Pearl District, Powell\'s Books and most of Portland\'s major cultural institutions.<br /><br />One can meander through the neighborhood streets lined with Victorian homes, NW 23rd and 21st Avenues lined with shops and restaurants or walk up to Washington Park and the amazing Japanese Gardens. From there, it is possible to access over 40 miles of hiking trails.<br /><br />Some of the Portland\'s best restaurants, coffee houses and cinemas are only a few blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/83648541-55b3-4b5b-af03-b84323993e42.jpg',2915808,27,'45.525718688964844','-122.69625854492188',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,148.00,1,20,109,4.86,16159235),(725,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16174300','Sun-kissed room for 1-2 in historic Alberta home','This quiet, peaceful room in an historic, updated 1907 Foursquare house is just steps from Alberta Arts District and other neighborhoods, with local shops, bars, & eateries.<br /><br />(Also see QUIET PLACE, PATIO SUITE OR PATIO COTTAGE if this room is booked during your dates.)<br /><br />FEATURES:<br />• Queen Bed w/ memory foam mattress<br />• Organic cotton bedding, towels & toiletries<br />• Fully equipped kitchen<br />• High-pressure shower<br />• A/C & work space<br />• Large patio w/ gas fire pit<br />• LGBTQ+ Friendly','PERFECT CENTRAL LOCATION<br /><br />You couldn’t ask for a better spot to take in Portland’s charms, right outside the door:<br /><br />    • Just 15 minutes from the airport, and 10 minutes to downtown and the Convention/Moda Centers.<br />    • Directly off N Williams Ave and NE Alberta Street, right in the heart of some of Portland’s most popular shopping and restaurant districts – with easy access to all the rest of Portland’s star attractions.<br />    •  Within easy walking distance to a lot of shops, restaurants, pubs, cafes and food carts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-16174300/original/b1cd495f-b646-4329-8dd3-3e62c607ee11.jpeg',6946676,24,'45.558284759521484','-122.66563415527344',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,46.00,1,14,124,4.90,16174300),(726,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16207620','St. Johns Close-In Cozy  Studio','Great location, with easy walking to Cathedral Park,  St. Johns Village and bus connections.  <br />This is a cozy, unique space with original art. <br />Just minutes from Dwntn Portland. <br /><br />• Separate entrance<br />• Large closet<br />• Kitchenette w/microwave, small refrigerator, coffee maker, hot plate and electric kettle.<br />• Internet & TV<br />• Large Patio<br />• Built-in heating/AC<br />- Protected Bike Storage','The Studio is located in the St. John\'s / Cathedral Park area.  Just 3 blocks up the hill is the heart of St. John\'s Village with many unique restaurants, coffee shops & 2 theaters. <br /><br />My Favorites in the St. John\'s Neighborhood: <br />- Walk over the bridge to get the best views of the mountains and Portland!<br />-MCMENAMIN\'S PUB & THEATER. A Cool-funky pub with huge garden patio.<br />- GREAT SHOPS in St. John\'s Village:  Olive & Vine, Therapy, Hound & Hare.  <br />- THE FIXIN\' TO is a southern-inspired honky tonk with live music most nights of the week. <br />- CATHEDRAL PARK (on the waterfront) is only 1 block away. It is one of the most popular dog friendly parks in Portland.<br />- PIER PARK offers great green space and Disc Golf.<br /><br />https://www.niche.com/places-to-live/n/st-johns-portland-or/<br /><br />https://www.skyblueportland.com/portland-neighborhoods-north-porland-st-johns-neighborhood-guide/','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7605d207-278b-4891-8af2-6ed0e6a00d8d.jpg',7323422,42,'45.58677','-122.75606',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,59.00,4,90,100,4.83,16207620),(727,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16236488','The Place','The \"PLACE\" is on Williams Ave known as \"THE STEM\" close to I-5 in North Portland.  This is the street where the Night Life took place.','Located on WILLIAMS AVE in NORTH PORTLAND. Near MISSISSIPPI Ave & ALBERTA ST. There is a bar and several Eating Establishments<br /> There is a Store on our block.<br />Also directly across the street is a dispensary.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e165cc59-25f8-4873-9506-15546cc97e7b.jpg',60426753,24,'45.55475','-122.66781',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,94,4.71,16236488),(728,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16282853','Magnolia House, Birthday Room','Walk into this house and say \"Ahhhhhh. This is going to be a good visit.\" It is airy, light and beautiful. Thoughtfully arranged for real human beings. Comfortable. Inviting. Nestled in a classic Craftsman neighborhood, it is minutes from downtown by car, MAX or frequent close buses. It is an easy walk to grocery stores, great restaurants and the most comfortable bar in town. It is a convenient place for those attending events at the convention center and a single bus ride to PSU.','The house is nestled between the Laurelhurst and Hollywood neighborhoods. Conveniently, it is a stone\'s throw (maybe two stones\' throws) from the on-ramp to I-84. (Fortunately,  the highway here is sunk into an old stream bed--Sullivan\'s Gulch--so our space itself is very quiet.)  The street was developed in 1910 in classic Craftsman style--along our side of the street every other house is a variant of one design and the in-between houses are a variant of the other design. <br />There are four grocery stores within walking distance (two organic--it is Portland), good restaurants ranging from Arabian to gastropub (with cask ale), two large parks (Grant Park and Laurelhurst) and of course tons of good public transportation.<br /><br />The heart of downtown is three and a half miles away. Yes, you could walk downtown! Amble leisurely downhill through some of the old neighborhoods, cross the river on one of our beautiful bridges, enjoy the town and then Uber or bus home.<br />In our house ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/57027d87-60c7-4b63-acb6-e7c071a4b1ef.jpg',4256569,23,'45.53291','-122.62923',2,2,2.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,1,4,97,4.92,16282853),(729,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16287341','Bright. Sunlit. Craftsman home. Built in 1913.','2500 sqft foursquare house. Huge light filled windows. A grand dining room, 4 bedrooms (2 beds, office and a baby room) The house features original built in details, working fireplace, claw-foot tub, and beautiful hardwood floors. <br /><br />Located in Hollywood/Grant Park neighborhood. Best neighborhood in Portland for both going out and family time. Walk or bike to library, Farmer\'s Market, Whole Foods, dog park, historic movie theater, cafes, brew pubs & MAX stop.','Grant Park, NE Hollywood District is a historic neighborhood teeming with lively bars, restaurants, and shopping in a short walk. The historic Hollywood movie theater is four blocks away and it screens 70mm prints. Grant park is six blocks away with fountains, playground, public pool, and tennis courts. Whole foods and Trader Joe\'s is within a five block walk. The location is centrally located and equidistant to the North East and South East bars and restaurants. All within a ten minute drive.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2fe81f28-600f-4207-ba40-a01cc8280974.jpg',7698196,33,'45.53929','-122.62069',1,6,2.50,4.00,3.00,250.00,30,1125,12,4.75,16287341),(730,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16288502','Walk Everywhere • Foodie Paradise • Immaculate','Your separate, private space is in the vibrant Hawthorne District, one of the best neighborhoods for tourists in the city! Centrally located to nearly everything! From the great outdoors to world class restaurants, it’s all within reach. ⛰ 🌊 🍲🚶‍♂️🍕<br /><br />We provide a ton of curated recommendations on where to eat and drink, and activities to do. Take a minute to read our guest reviews: ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️.<br /><br />As a food blogger/influencer, and expert pizzaiolo I am happy to share my inside knowledge of the best spots. 😋','You will be a short walk to eclectic shops, coffee shops, bakeries, restaurants, bars, and parks...all virtually out your front door. Many are beginning to reopen, and most have pick-up or delivery options available. <br /><br />Other nearby highlights include (check our Instagram @airbnb.portland or our Guidebook for more):<br />- Mt. Tabor Park - ~10 minute walk. Beautiful, urban forest park on a dormant volcano, with great views of the Portland skyline. It is a runner/walker\'s paradise. <br />- Unique shops/restaurants on Belmont, Hawthorne, and Division streets. <br />- Many food options including: Por Que No?, Apizza Scholls, Tabor Bread, Saphire Hotel, and more within a 5 minute walk. Three of Portland\'s top 5 restaurants in the city are within a 5 minute drive (Coquine #1, Castagna #3, Nodoguro #4 ranked by The Oregonian). <br />- Several great coffee shops are just around the corner including: Albina Press, and Common Grounds. <br />- Powell\'s Books in a short walk down Hawthor','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9fd99287-a8c9-4311-9938-04f6d4981a20.jpg',1166453,16,'45.51445','-122.61536',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,9,357,4.93,16288502),(731,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16299536','Cozy Room(s) in St Johns with Private Bath','You will feel at home right away in our freshly remodeled contemporary house, located on a quiet street of St Johns historic neighborhood. The bedrooms are spacious and bright, and the open-space kitchen/dining room/living room is a comfortable area to hang out and relax. St Johns is Portland’s latest up and coming “hip” area–with a unique and eclectic feel. Close proximity to the University of Portland, St Johns’ restaurants, coffee shops, parks, and about 15 minutes from downtown Portland.','Come discover the lesser-known, up and coming St Johns neighborhood. It has a distinct and unique small-town charm, with its own historic downtown area, farmers’ market, many quirky locally owned shops, cafés, food carts and restaurants, and even theatre pubs where you can view movies while drinking beer/eating food.  Favorite activities nearby also include:<br />-Pack a picnic blanket for an afternoon in Cathedral Park, which features free open air concerts and a jazz festival each summer. The park has an amazing view of picturesque St Johns bridge. <br />-Grab some discs and go play frisbee golf at nearby Pier Park, one of the best course in the Pacific NW. <br />- Cross the picturesque St. Johns Bridge to explore downtown Portland and the Pearl District less than 15 minutes away. <br />-Go hiking in Forrest Park, one of the country\'s largest urban forest reserves with miles and miles of trails.    <br />-Or take a short drive to Sauvie Island’s for berry picking or walking on the be','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6cd82a16-1afe-47ff-8d3a-6d408da6349c.jpg',34947896,58,'45.59828','-122.74278',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,68.00,1,30,101,4.98,16299536),(732,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16323535','Stylish apartment in amazing location.','A very spacious, clean, quiet, private 1-bedroom apartment with ample street parking is within walking distance to trendy bars, local favorite restaurants, and public transit.<br />Easy access to freeways, The Gorge and just about any part of town makes this the ideal spot for your Portland adventure.<br />Great for the solo traveler, couples, friends, and family with kids. <br /><br /><br />..','In walking distance:<br />*Killingworth  - bars, restaurants, coffee shop.<br />5 min drive:<br />*Mississippi- vintage stores, restaurants, music venue, bars...','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ef1c980e-cb58-4d5c-9140-c7245176b67f.jpg',6628318,13,'45.56152','-122.69327',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,1,30,171,4.88,16323535),(733,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16345946','Relaxing santuary in inner NE Portland','Cute and Cozy bedroom within walking district of the Alberta Arts District and located just 3 miles from downtown Portland. Three nearby bus routes make transportation easy and several restaurants and grocery stores are within 1 mile.<br />*travel nurses or extended stay please contact for special pricing','Only 3 miles from downtown and within 7 blocks of the very diverse Alberta Arts District, offering many diverse options for dining preferences of all lifestyles. Stop at one of our famous food carts or go have dinner at one of our many restaurants that are inclusively to organic, vegan and vegetarian preferences. About 1.5 miles away is another must-see neighborhood offering several more tasty options; the Mississippi district. <br /><br />Located just 5 blocks away from Safeway and about a mile walk from Whole Foods which can easily be accessed by the bus route #8.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a622526e-c30d-44bb-abc5-a0c1002df6fd.jpg',4955204,14,'45.56567','-122.65575',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,1,5.00,16345946),(734,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16364330','Cozy Victorian Studio (31 day min-no taxes)','10% of your fee goes to help Ukrainians. <br />1A is a cozy studio apartment located in a in charming 1896 Victorian building with a popular Mexican food cart right out front.  We are located just 2 blocks away from one of Portland\'s most popular areas~NW 23rd (Trendy-third) Avenue where you\'ll find a huge variety of coffee shops, restaurants and unique shops. A bus stop is 2 blocks away or use Uber/Lyft/car to get downtown in 6 minutes. Enjoy Forest Park-only a 10 minute walk away.','The NW Alphabet District has all kinds of wonderful shops and restaurants.  There is a lot of hustle and bustle going on around here. We are situated amongst residential homes, commercial businesses and next to a highway overpass. There is a popular Mexican food cart located on the property typically open 10-6.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f5091d12-ff4f-4e7e-8d4c-587569546986.jpg',98202133,27,'45.53909','-122.69658',1,1,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,31,364,41,4.88,16364330),(735,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16368185','Cozy Private Retreat near Division Street','Our Richmond Retreat is located on a quiet residential street, just 3 blocks from popular Division Street restaurants and shopping. You’ll love this cozy bedroom & bath with a private outdoor entrance.  Great for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, families, and furry friends (pets).  <br /><br />Please note that pets count as an extra person, so there is a pet charge of $10/day if you have 2+ people and a pet. (More information under additional rules.)','Wonderful residential neighborhood with quiet tree-lined streets just a few blocks away from Division street with dozens of restaurants, bars, and shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0edc139f-4d1c-4e0f-9880-3bf2a13ad275.jpg',26701213,8,'45.501404','-122.626472',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,2,14,260,4.91,16368185),(736,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16413063','BEST NEIGHBORHOOD IN PORTLAND!!! #17','Completely furnished, modern, private. Located in friendly, close-in Northwest Portland. This central location with a 98 Walk Score and is next to some of the best restaurants, bars and cafes in town.  Full kitchen.  Private bath. Beats hotel pricing','Close-in Northwest Portland- Nob Hill.<br /><br />This convenient location, with a 98 POINT WALK SCORE is blocks from trendy NW 23rd AVE, Dragonfly Coffee House, St. Honore Bakery, McMenamins Pub, a natural foods grocery store, the public library, as well as the post office. <br /><br />Window shop at all the lovely boutiques located just blocks away or hike/bike/run/explore the 80 miles of trails and over 5,000 acres of Forest Park; one of the largest urban parks in the United States! <br /><br />You can quickly and easily reach the Pearl District, the Brewery Blocks or Downtown Portland in minutes by foot, bike or streetcar; no need for a vehicle when living here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3086b324-67f5-4683-b9e6-510477a936de.jpg',21655715,27,'45.53494','-122.70292',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,58.00,30,365,17,4.53,16413063),(737,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16416965','Private Modern Portland Home - KING BED','This house is located in Portland just a couple of miles from downtown. A few miles to the city center. One mile from I-5. Close to NIKE, OHSU, PCC Sylvania, PSU, and Multnomah Village.<br /><br />Ideal for corporate rentals  or relocation housing.  House is business travel ready.<br />All utilities and wifi are provided - you will need just your suitcase.','West Portland Park is conveniently located to all the hotspots, but far enough away to enjoy quiet and plenty of parking. You have a neighbor on one side and trees and forest on the other sides. It\'s only a couple of miles to Multnomah Village, Costco, Fred Meyer grocery store and AMC Theatres.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1daceec3-5f83-4162-be34-cb30655001ab.jpg',62992553,53,'45.4457','-122.72056',1,10,2.50,5.00,7.00,400.00,30,1125,3,5.00,16416965),(738,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16427538','Portland Southwest Suite Stay','Cozy suite in quiet, safe neighborhood with private, digital key-coded entrance for convenience. Private kitchenette & bathroom/shower, comfy queen sized bed, fold-out sofa, air-bed, pack & play, high chair & change table. Lots of closet space, included continental breakfast, and private covered outdoor sitting area.  Very close to bus stops, so you won\'t need car. Walking-distance to parks, grocery, and restaurants. Close to downtown, Zoo, Japanese, Chinese & Rose Gardens, OHSU, OMSI.','We\'re close to everything! Minutes from I-5, the Oregon Zoo, Japanese, Chinese and Rose Gardens, OMSI, Forest Park, Council Crest and downtown Portland. We\'re also walking distance to Gabriel Park and Multnomah Village and our quiet and safe neighborhood has a great view of Portland West Hills. You can also use TriMet to get around town as we\'re a stone\'s throw from bus stops #377 and #378 and minutes from Portland city center. There\'s a brewpub (IBU) with a spectacular selection of craft beers that\'s just a short walk down the street. The Oak and Olive, Tastebuds (wood oven pizza) and O\'Conners are all very close. There\'s grocery and a pharmacy a block away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c2bcaa46-caff-4402-a31d-15c2d539892f.jpg',107557224,17,'45.48496','-122.72776',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,70.00,2,29,383,4.96,16427538),(739,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16480376','Eclectic Urban Oasis, Relaxing Suite Near U of P','This is a charming Arbor Lodge Tudor surrounded by lush gardens with a gorgeous and cozy apartment-like unit in the bright basement. The driveway side entrance leads downstairs to the spacious and comfortable private suite. The house is in a quiet neighborhood conveniently located near MAX lightrail,  grocery stores, coffee shops and restaurants. The home is close to Alberta St and Mississippi Ave and a short MAX ride to Moda Center, Expo Center and downtown Portland.','This is a great place to launch your daily adventures in the North Portland and beyond. It is a very convenient spot for visiting family and friends in many North Portland neighborhoods, including University of Portland.<br />Arbor Lodge is a beautiful urban neighborhood. It is safe, quiet and very walkable. There are many coffee shops, restaurants and neighborhood pubs.  <br />My home is 4 block from New Season\'s market. <br />We are 20 minutes from PDX (Portland\'s airport).<br />The home is within walking distance to the Killingsworth and Kenton stores, restaurants and bars (1 block up to 1 mile). It is just over 2 miles to the hot spots on Mississippi Ave and the Alberta Arts district. The Moda Center and downtown Portland are just a short MAX ride away. For sports games and graduations,  University of Portland is just over 2 miles away.  It is also a short drive to St John\'s and Cathedral Park.<br />We are 5 miles south of the Oregon/Washington state border.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-16480376/original/98c9bc35-92da-463b-be36-acf15155bbfa.jpeg',108190308,51,'45.57138','-122.68684',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,82.00,2,30,75,4.91,16480376),(740,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16519704','Greenwich Place','New apartment nicely (Website hidden by Airbnb) block to light rail (Website hidden by Airbnb) block to <br />New Seasons grocery...Coffee Shop and nice bar and restaurant .<br />3 Blocks from I-5....lots of parks and good jogging paths.20 minutes from PDX .Easy on street parking.<br />Private entry with coded lock','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/320a6fee-a8cb-445b-8420-1bebd01624c3.jpg',108570373,51,'45.57099','-122.68386',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,76.00,30,30,119,4.96,16519704),(741,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16545380','Ash Street Little Studio off Restaurant Row','Incredibly cozy, small space with private bathroom, full shared kitchen, radiant heated floors, washer and dryer in the heart of Portland! <br /><br />Come enjoy our cozy space! We are close to everything - the historic Laurelhurst Theater is 2 blocks away, as well as eateries, bars, boutiques!<br /><br />Please read house rules before booking. Sounds carry in our old house. We ask everyone to please be aware that although the space is a private space, you’re still in a home with kids.','Our neighborhood IS so much. Technically, we are in Kerns, just named one of the best neighborhoods in Portland by Portland Monthly. We are just two blocks from the sprawling Laurelhurst Park, one of the nicest and largest parks in Portland. We are one block from Laurelhurst Theater, made famous by Portlandia where you can get beer and pizza with your movie! We are also a half a block from shops, restaurants, food pods, and bars. Basically we are in the heart of the hip and urban Portland and happy to call here home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b140032e-2679-4b05-98a3-51cde74e4562.jpg',41780011,12,'45.52151','-122.63618',2,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,60.00,2,12,123,4.93,16545380),(742,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16557751','Private Cottage in Laurelhurst Neighborhood','Located in one of Portland\'s most historic neighborhoods, the Laurelhurst Cottage is a great way to become acquainted with all Portland has to offer. You’ll love the comfy bed, private kitchen, private bathroom, and central location to shopping areas and public transportation. This accommodation is good for couples, solo adventurers and business travelers.','Laurelhurst Park is right around the corner from our rental and the old architecture is a delight to view on an evening walk. Just west of us, is the classic yet burgeoning 28th Ave with notable eateries, nightlife, and amenities such as grocery store and laundromat. No car necessary. It\'s all just 10 blocks away!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/24dfa41a-b0b4-419b-9a67-461940f61138.jpg',109032237,23,'45.52546','-122.62496',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,96.00,3,14,103,4.90,16557751),(743,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16568420','Waterfront Pearl Modern Large Home Away From Home','My place is close to Lovejoy Bakers - Pearl District Downtown Portland. Beautiful views, cozy, clean and modern condo. Comes with everything you need to get away from home, whether to work or play. Easily sleeps four with 2 brand news king beds. Updated appliances.<br /><br />Just bring clothes and food! We even have spices, sugar, coffee.<br />Relax on the private decks. <br />Want to see the sights? Jog down the river front trail to Saturday market, or cross the bridge. We have free, covered, assigned parking.','Our condo is walking distance to a lot of the amenities.  Would like to see a show, down town is close by, have a desire to go to a Happy Hour or wish to eat dinner, walk over to the Pearl District.<br />There is no dearth of entertainment in this area, we are very centrally located.<br />Beaches are about 1-1.5 hours away.  Mt Hood is not too far if you wish to ski.<br />We are close to the train, our local train \'MAX\' and to the bus line.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9301c11c-14c4-4300-ad43-aa4c136a3257.jpg',109143261,43,'45.5282','-122.67235',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,110.00,31,1125,6,4.50,16568420),(744,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16600030','Mid-Century Modern Meets Historic Streetcar Style','This second floor walk-up apartment is located in the Historic Mississippi Neighborhood. <br /><br />The apartment has fantastic views of the west hills and is a relaxing place to watch the sunset and enjoy the nightly golden glow.<br /><br />A perfect apartment for long term visits and business stays...','North Mississippi Avenue is a fun place to walk, eat, shop and wander. You can pretty much walk to everything including a grocery store.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTY2MDAwMzA%3D/original/7a1c0f93-58d7-47a8-8998-56822a716a24.jpeg',5074035,9,'45.55225','-122.67577',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,31,240,89,4.98,16600030),(745,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16617424','Eclectic Victorian Room with Private Bathroom','Close to South Waterfront, OHSU and NUNM.  Perfect for folks who are looking for a quiet and peaceful space while in Portland. The room is on the top floor of the house and you have this floor to yourself and it includes a private bathroom (shower and claw foot tub). The room has a mini fridge and electric kettle with a varied selection of teas and coffee. Free snacks provided.<br />Free parking for one vehicle.<br />We cannot accommodate service animals due to severe allergies.','The neighborhood is a mix of old portland and new development. <br />We are two blocks from the overpass to South waterfront area, which includes Transit Hub (Trimet Bus & Street Car, Bike town Kiosk) and Tillicum bridge. There are many food pods/carts, cafes and coffee shops in the neighborhood.Ross island cafe is a half block away- great breakfast and lunch options.<br />5 minute ride to downtown via Uber or Lyft. Transit to downtown is 10-15 minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/db8b192d-bed9-45b7-930e-5824ad72618a.jpg',50541937,22,'45.49682','-122.67523',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,2,14,430,4.98,16617424),(746,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16622422','The Bridge House: A Modern NE Portland Loft','Bridge House loft, named after our beautiful mural of Portland\'s own Steel Bridge, is perfect for a romantic getaway or a solo adventure. Located in the heart of NE Portland, it is mere blocks from the popular Williams and Alberta streets, and a few minutes from downtown. Bridge House offers all of the amenities you want with the privacy and comfort you require. Newly built and beautifully designed, we take pride in all the details we\'ve included to create a memorable experience for our guests!','We love how close our home is to some of our favorite things! Like N Williams St, Alberta Arts district, Mississippi St, Irvington and Oldtown- Downtown Portland!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e5b33459-3302-40f4-b26e-80684af3b94a.jpg',99163732,14,'45.55325','-122.65768',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,150.00,2,29,303,4.99,16622422),(747,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16712779','Sunstone House - Stylish 2 BR - Best Part of Town','Come stay at my amazing 2 Bedroom home built in 1939 and recently remodeled. The property is located in my personal favorite part of town, with a walking score of 78 and a bike score of 98! We are a 5 minute walk to Division St which is known for having the best restaurants in Portland. A little further north is Hawthorne blvd which is also packed with restaurants and bars. If you want to be within walking distance of great nightlife but also in a quiet nook to relax this is the place for you!','We love living in this part of Portland, our street is sleepy and quite but within a 10 minute walk you\'re in the bustle of a thriving neighborhood! Richmond will provide anything you might need during your stay (grocery stores, coffee shops, award winning restaurants, amazing bars, pharmacies, convince stores, vintage shopping, and beautiful parks) you could spend 3 or 4 days just exploring the neighborhood around our house and you would never see it all.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4ca0ac77-8f22-4d1b-8c94-343e41bdb827.jpg',16693663,8,'45.50043','-122.62155',1,6,1.00,2.00,2.00,350.00,30,1125,203,4.84,16712779),(748,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16770374','Hawthorne Hideaway-Close To Food and Fun!','Stylish apartment in Inner-SE Portland, located in the basement of a 1908 craftsman home. The apartment is near all of the amazing spots that Portland has to offer while being a true peaceful oasis from the hustle and bustle. There is a king size memory foam bed, spa-like bathroom, plus a kitchenette to warm up your amazing leftovers and enjoy a locally roasted morning coffee.','Enjoy exploring the area on foot! You are nestled between Division and Belmont stopping and restaurant districts and just two blocks off Hawthorne Blvd, the heart of southeast Portland! <br /> <br />Parks/Outdoors: <br />- Laurelhurst Park <br />- Mount Tabor <br /> <br />Historical: <br />- The Bagdad Theater <br />- Lone Fir Cemetery','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3f1cfaf4-e047-41ff-8b36-e62c0363be52.jpg',3794426,8,'45.51132','-122.62373',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,86.00,2,29,361,4.88,16770374),(749,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16779136','Hawthorne Area Artsy Home Away from Home','You’ll love our place because of its fantastic location! The Sunnyside neighborhood has been named one of the hottest in the country. We\'re close to so much: wonderful restaurants and pubs, Stumptown Coffee, McMenamin\'s movie theater and pub, grocery stores, beautiful parks. We\'re two miles from downtown with convenient public transportation. The comfortable, bright apartment has its own entry and kitchen is well-supplied. Our place is good for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers.','We are three blocks from the heart of both SE Belmont St. and SE Hawthorne Blvd. In each business district, you\'ll find charming shops; delicious cafes, pubs, and restaurants; fun coffee shops; and an array of vintage clothing stores. Even though we are so close to so many great services, our street is quiet and pleasant without a lot of traffic. It\'s a city-designated bike street so you\'ll see many people biking by. We\'re a half-mile walk through residential streets to the huge and beautiful Laurelhurst Park. Both Belmont and Hawthorne have bus lines that take you downtown, just two miles away, and you\'ll also find BikeTown bikes for rent to explore the neighborhood on wheels. We have a major grocery store, Fred Meyers, just 6 blocks away, as well as an Asian-focused super market, H-Mart, just 3 blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-16779136/original/f37918db-7370-4f91-9234-4eb21522d7c8.jpg',28000582,16,'45.51328','-122.63058',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,114.00,2,60,192,4.97,16779136),(750,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16795787','Mid-Century Woodstock Duplex','This is a beautifully remodeled mid-century unit, completely furnished. Shared back yard. Hardwood floors, stacked washer & dryer, window coverings. Corner lot, single level, walking distance from New Seasons and all Woodstock has to offer! <br />No smoking in unit or on property, please!','Near Reed College, First Cup Coffee House, Laughing Planet, Delta Cafe, Lutz Tavern, and Cloud City Ice Cream. . . Great for couples, business travelers, and furry friends (pets).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/158abd5b-5f8a-4058-b55a-7ba0df5dd426.jpg',111643390,65,'45.48088','-122.59648',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,72.00,30,120,25,4.84,16795787),(751,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16846942','Large Basement unit near Mississippi and Alberta','Our remodeled basement will be a great base for you to explore Portland. The large space is perfect for relaxing, but still provides anything that you need. You have your own private entrance from the street. <br /><br />Location: We are within walking distance of both Alberta and Williams, two popular streets with wonderful food and arts. Mississippi is a longer walk or an easy bike ride. Portland\'s renowned bike facility network and bike share rentals are within two blocks.','Prime location half a block from the Going Street Neighborhood Greenway, a very efficient bike boulevard, 2 blocks to Trimet Bus stop and less than 10 minutes to downtown Portland. You are truly within blocks of the Alberta Arts District and within walking distance to Williams Avenue shops and restaurants and a short bike ride to Mississippi Avenue! Not to mention that it is less than a half a mile to wonderful sushi and top rated restaurant Grain & Gristle!<br /><br />If you like theater, the renowned Portland Playhouse is within a block.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9943aa18-9496-406d-b697-a7b38051338e.jpg',53588039,14,'45.55491','-122.6596',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,1,14,213,4.95,16846942),(752,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16862950','The Laurel/Portland.Peaceful.Fun','Imagine walking into a beautiful cozy hotel room downtown that has been suddenly picked up by a gust of wind and delicately placed near an exquisite park in an extraordinary neighborhood only two miles away. Oh my!','Prohibition is over! With cannabis legal we have partnered with Farma, Portland\'s best and most award winning dispensary. We offer a $2 (plus tax) pre-roll and a coupon for a 10% discount when you visit Farma (only 2.5 miles from the studio) on lower Hawthorne. Please remember to smoke outside of The Laurel ;-).<br /><br />We are a block from major bus lines (75 and 20) and an 8 minute walk to the MAX rail system. <br /><br />Access to nature:<br /><br />Laurelhurst Park is two blocks away and Mt Tabor Park is only 1.5 miles with stunning views of downtown and Mt Hood. The Columbia River Gorge is a 20min drive from our house. Just walking in our neighborhood is pretty amazing, for the trees on either side of the street stretch to create a beautiful canopy overhead. <br /><br />Portland International Airport is a 15 minute Drive, take MAX rail, or a $17 Uber. <br /><br />Shopping and entertainment. These stores are all within a mile, with the closest being Whole Foods ten blocks away. <','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d49a311e-b0c1-4ac9-8458-7299e59f2e35.jpg',714512,23,'45.52294','-122.62382',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,47.00,1,30,596,4.87,16862950),(753,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16874105','The Nest: Very Clean & Peaceful N Portland Studio','Guest Testimonial: “If I could give this place 6 stars I would. I literally wanted to move in.” “Our favorite Airbnb ever. Very clean. Great location in an awesome neighborhood.”<br /><br />The Nest is nestled in N Portland, <br />15 minutes from downtown and 15 minutes from the airport. The space is a cozy 512SF studio with beautiful open floor plan, full kitchen and laundry. Solar powered home with 40amp EV charger.<br /><br />Walking distance to Portland’s famous food and historic districts.<br />All are welcome here.','The neighborhood includes three of the most vibrant food, drink, and walking districts in North Portland (Mississippi, Alberta, and Williams). <br /><br />Some of our favorite neighborhood restaurants, coffee shops, and breweries include:<br /><br />Breakfast: Tin Shed, Grant Central Bakery, and Coco Donut. <br /><br />Cocktails: Box Social<br /><br />Dinner: Bamboo Sushi, Por Que No, Life of Pie, and Monsoon Thai.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f01e6765-3e80-402c-8d73-ddb6928d51ee.jpg',49356222,24,'45.55527','-122.66881',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,81.00,1,99,608,4.96,16874105),(754,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16881037','Standard Private Room at NW Portland Hostel','Experience Portland’s top-rated, family-owned hostel, in the vibrant Northwest District! Enjoy a FREE breakfast and explore nearby downtown attractions, Washington Park, the Rose and Japanese Gardens, and hiking trails. Join our daily free events like walking tours, tap tastings, live music, and trivia nights. For over 25 years, our mission has been to provide a welcoming, affordable, and safe space, connecting Portland with travelers worldwide and making a positive impact locally and beyond.','We are located in the Northwest district, just a few blocks from popular shops, cafes, pubs, cinemas, and some of the city\'s best restaurants. Many area attractions, including the Pearl District, downtown Portland, Saturday Market, Portland Farmers Market, Powell\'s Bookstore, art galleries, the Lan Su Chinese Garden, museums, the MLS Stadium, and Pioneer Square, are within walking distance. The Rose Gardens and Japanese Gardens are a short bus ride or a 25-minute walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTY4ODEwMzc%3D/original/01f3cafa-d9de-49fb-9d45-bc17b6294682.jpeg',2820851,27,'45.52562','-122.68876',2,2,3.00,1.00,1.00,64.00,1,365,237,4.75,16881037),(755,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16972972','St Johns Urban Studio','Hey there! <br />Our quaint studio, located in N. Portland welcomes you with everything you need to have a classic PDX vacay.<br />A private entrance, as well as transit access to explore PDX (bus stop just outside your private gate), 4 full service markets (1 organic), trendy St. Johns, and quick access to downtown PDX via the St. Johns Bridge. The space is comfortable, squeaky clean, fast WiFi, private laundry, smart TV, along with many other amenities. Space for two, solo and business travelers.','My place is a 20 minute car ride from PDX airport and 15 minutes from downtown Portland via the St John\'s Bridge/SR30 (locals shortcut). As a bonus, I am also a 15 minute drive over the Columbia River to Vancouver, Washington and all that growing city has to offer.<br /><br />St. John\'s is one of the 95 listed Micro Neighborhoods that make up the City of Portland. It is a wonderful and diverse working-class area of North Portland. The neighborhood is literally developing around us with a new shop, bar or cafe opening seemingly daily! <br /><br />The Studio is a short walk to numerous cafes, bars, boutiques, supermarkets, 2 Movie Theaters, a food cart pod...and growing! From spring through fall we have our own Farmers Market on Saturday morning.<br /> <br />The centerpiece of the area (about a mile from my place) is the St. John\'s Bridge with Cathedral Park along the Willamette River below - imho, the most stunning of all the water-crossings in Bridgetown, USA. It was designed by David ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTY5NzI5NzI%3D/original/e945fc93-d97d-4d33-ab7a-7c7ddb4df5a9.jpeg',246080531,58,'45.59565','-122.74413',1,2,1.00,0.00,4.00,62.00,1,14,352,4.97,16972972),(756,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16974158','Work & Relax at the Treehouse Organic Modern Apt.','Come to work Forest Bathe & De-Stress! Modern private W.Hills daylight basement studio surrounded by Forest Park, abutting major hiking trails w/ beautiful forest views yet just 4 mins above the city! W/fast Wifi Close to Nike, Intel, OHSU, St.Vincent.<br />Priv. entrance, full kitchen, fireplace, Queen  & sofa bed, shower, laundry, covered patio private backyard, BBQ, table, swings, facing the forest.<br />Hike: Arboretum, Rose/Japanese Gardens, Washington Park, Hoyt Arboretum, Pittock Mansion& the city.','This self contained beautiful studio apartment is part of a 1970\'s daylight ranch surrounded by the lush old growth forest of Portland\'s west hills, with trail heads just below the house, yet you are just 4 minutes above NW 23rd, and the Pearl and downtown below! Immerse yourself in nature and experience the best of what Portland has to offer!<br />You can hike the trails from here to the arboretum, the Rose Gardens, the Japanese Garden, Washington Park, Pittock Mansion, and down to the city. We do this on weekends- go hike down for breakfast, walk around and window shop, take the tri-met back to the top of skyline Blvd., and walk back down to our home.  It\'s a great great way to get your cardio going, de-stress, immerse ourselves in nature, and get your city fix as well.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/64b1023e-d7a6-4b77-95ac-538dcce3ee39.jpg',113557299,50,'45.5251','-122.74252',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,90.00,30,365,39,4.90,16974158),(757,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16985036','Division Street Casita del Jardin ( garden home)','Our beloved purple house is an 800 sf cottage (ADU, or Accessory Dwelling Unit) tucked behind our primary residence in the heart of the happening SE Division/Clinton neighborhood.  It sits in a shared garden setting with pathways, sitting nooks and a covered area to grill and eat.  It\'s a perfect getaway for couples, families, and friend groups.  We provide a safe and welcoming place for all people regardless of gender, sexual orientation, ethnicity, nationality, or religion.','Our neighborhood has transformed drastically in the 30 years we have lived here, and we love the increasing density and the benefits that come with it.  Just around the corner, you can explore a huge variety of restaurants and bars, offering a wide array of exciting food and drink, with creative outdoor dining/drinking options for safety.  The neighborhood is a vibrant place to explore, with lovely neighborhood gardens and parks.<br /><br />Coming to eat and drink?  We are less than 5-10 minute walk to Salt and Straw,  Lauretta Jean, Cibo,  Richmond Bar, the Automatic, Bollywood Theatre, Tight Tacos,  the Cat\'s Paw, \"The End\"  bar, Oma\'s Hideaway,  St Honore (French Bakery), Blue Star donuts, Pinolo Gelato, Cicoria Pizzeria,   to name just a fraction of Division St culinary gems.  Farmhouse food carts is a new cart pod around the corner behind Cibo\'s.  And there are two other sweet little cart pod /bar hangouts with chill open patio seating and a hip vibe down alley ways on division.  ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-16985036/original/a2673043-a951-4aaa-a5dd-0e344854e347.jpeg',7281995,8,'45.50336','-122.62933',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,1125,186,5.00,16985036),(758,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/16995515','Vintage style and quiet comfort','Quiet, clean, comfortable home close to light rail and two neighborhood districts, this gracious home offers a stylish and peaceful respite from your city adventures with easy accessibility to downtown and the cool Eastside scene.  Located in the historic Eastmoreland neighborhood, there is easy access to bus lines and light rail, local neighborhood shops and Portland\'s extensive network of biking and hiking trails and nearby Reed College.','Eastmoreland is a classic early-twentieth century tree-filled neighborhood in inner Southeast Portland. Located between 3 neighborhood shopping districts - Woodstock to the east, the City of Milwaukie to the south, and Sellwood-Moreland to the west.  Restaurants, grocery stores, wine bars  coffee shops, bars, book stores, libraries, boutiques and a local movie house are all nearby. Reed College is a few blocks away as is the Crystal Springs Rhododendron Garden, Springwater corridor and the public Eastmoreland Golf Course.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4b0f9662-0866-433f-a7a0-69bfe2780dea.jpg',6789678,5,'45.46882','-122.63471',1,2,1.50,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,1125,101,4.94,16995515),(759,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17001341','Boho Digs in Heart of Portland\'s Hippest Hood!','Impeccably clean, incredibly comfortable walker\'s paradise with hip design and a caring and responsive host.<br /><br />Feel at home in a garden level 1-bed, built for AirB&B by two award-winning interior designers. Sleep soundly in new beds and block out the light with blackout curtains. Fantasize about epic Farmhouse Thai. Crave Tove cold-brew. Pine for Hazel Cafe biscuit sammiches. <br /><br />Then awake, and step outside. You\'re a short walk away from many of Portland\'s best restaurants, bars and shops.','The ideal place for a true Portland experience, this home sits in the heart of the Hawthorne Neighborhood. It is home to some most notable restaurants, cafes, shops and bars the city has to offer, such as:<br /><br />-- Blue Star Donuts<br />-- Fried Egg I’m In Love <br />-- Stumptown Coffee<br />-- Sapphire Hotel<br />-- Jackpot Records<br />-- Jam on Hawthorne<br />-- Martian Arts<br />-- Coava Coffee<br />-- Red Light<br />-- Chicken and Guns<br />-- Apizza Scholls<br />-- The Waffle Window<br />-- Powell\'s Book<br />-- El Cubo de Cuba<br />-- Crossroads Trading Co.<br />-- ¿Por Qué No?<br />-- Nakhon<br />-- Cup & Saucer<br />-- Potato Champion<br />-- The Gold Door<br />-- Gold Dust Meridian<br />-- Harlow<br />-- Nick\'s Coney Island<br />-- Chez Machin<br />-- Thanh Thao\'s<br />-- Cha-Cha-Cha<br />-- Pho Dalat<br />-- Happy Sparrow<br />-- Tov<br />-- ... and too many more to list!<br /><br />LOCAL DESTINATIONS: <br />------------------------------------<br /><br />- ½ mile from ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/322070ca-2b98-430b-b91e-8753407b4f15.jpg',7635902,16,'45.51359','-122.63292',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,63.00,30,364,136,4.84,17001341),(760,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17012262','The Little House in the Heart of Concordia','Our Little House started its life as a 2-car garage, on the alley behind our home, that we transformed into our vision of a cozy and peaceful retreat. This light filled studio is professionally designed, features art from local artists and designers, and is equipped with heating & AC, making it a very comfortable spot to relax and enjoy Portland. You\'ll have a fully detached private guest house with a fully equipped kitchen, outdoor space and be two blocks away from the vibrant Alberta district.','The Alberta Arts neighborhood is a vibrate yet easy going part of NE Portland. Enjoy some of the city\'s best dinning spots just blocks away: DOC, Beast, Dame, Aviary, Podnah\'s, Salt & Straw, Bollywood Theater....the list goes on. We\'re in walking distance to McMenamin\'s Kennedy School movie theater and soaking pool and the Alberta Rose Theater, plus several parks, and easy public transportation to the rest of the city. We are close to the Oregon Convention Center (12 minute drive or 1/2 an hour, by bus).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7a03eb41-babd-46ab-8012-0d18a16a973a.jpg',170065,1,'45.56119','-122.63916',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,76.00,2,28,401,4.96,17012262),(761,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17026805','Stephens Street Gallery & Guesthouse','Our place is in the heart of the Hawthorne neighborhood.  Located 2 blocks off Cesar Chavez blvd, it is walking distance to great restaurants and some of the best parks in the city, including Mt. Tabor.<br />You’ll love the place because of the abundant natural light and spacious feeling of the house. It is an ideal central location to experience the other quadrants of the city while being at the center of one of Portland\'s most vibrant neighborhoods.','Our neighborhood is in the heart of Southeast Portland and just a couple miles from downtown.  It is very walk-able and while it is a quiet neighborhood, shops and restaurants are just blocks away.  Craftsman bungalows and old Victorian houses fill our neighborhood, and with people\'s beautiful landscaping and front yard gardens a walk in the neighborhood is a must.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2f4749f2-51e7-4d4d-85aa-55671fc56611.jpg',14088213,8,'45.51022','-122.62356',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,179,4.92,17026805),(762,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17038994','Magnolia House, morning sunshine','Walk into this house and say \"Ahhhhhh. This is going to be a good visit.\" It is airy, light and beautiful. Thoughtfully arranged for real human beings. Comfortable. Inviting. Nestled in a classic Craftsman neighborhood, it is minutes from downtown by car, Max or frequent close bus. It is an easy walk to grocery stores, great restaurants and the most comfortable bar in town.','The house is nestled between the Laurelhurst and Hollywood neighborhoods. Conveniently, it is a stone\'s throw (maybe two stones\' throws) from the on-ramp to I-84. (Fortunately,  the highway here is sunk into an old stream bed--Sullivan\'s Gulch--so our space itself is very quiet.)  The street was developed in 1910 in classic Craftsman style--along our side of the street every other house is a variant of one design and the in-between houses are a variant of the other design. <br />There are four grocery stores within walking distance (two organic--it is Portland), good restaurants ranging from Arabian to gastropub (with cask ale), two large parks (Grant Park and Laurelhurst) and of course tons of good public transportation.<br /><br />The heart of downtown is three and a half miles away. Yes, you could walk downtown! Amble leisurely downhill through some of the old neighborhoods, cross the river on one of our beautiful bridges, enjoy the town and then Uber or bus home.<br />In our house ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/eaab56b0-ee3d-4385-b3ed-800165126be2.jpg',4256569,23,'45.53289','-122.62923',2,2,2.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,1,3,36,5.00,17038994),(763,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17159753','The Backyard Bungalow! Big Living; Small House','The Backyard Bungalow - featured on Portland\'s ADU tour - is the perfect hideaway amidst uncertain times. <br /><br />With its own secluded pathway, and detached from the main house, it offers as much privacy as desired. Once inside however, its 16ft vaulted ceiling and sunlit open-plan living area surprises with a sense of spaciousness and comfort. <br /><br />Its inner SE location is walking distance to Division St. restaurants and cafes, food carts, parks and playgrounds, as well as being a \"biker\'s paradise\".','The Backyard Bungalow is in the midst of Clinton, Division, and Mt Tabor neighborhoods. The area is quickly developing, with restaurants, shops, food carts and cafes in every direction, and a Green Zebra Grocery store a few minutes away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d778379e-6934-4fee-a76d-d9045d59d3cb.jpg',8584999,8,'45.50162','-122.61124',1,5,1.00,1.00,1.00,93.00,2,1125,402,4.95,17159753),(764,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17161133','Private Room (2 beds) at NW Portland Hostel','Experience Portland’s top-rated, family-owned hostel, in the vibrant Northwest District! Enjoy a FREE breakfast and explore nearby downtown attractions, Washington Park, the Rose and Japanese Gardens, and hiking trails. Join our daily free events like walking tours, tap tastings, live music, and trivia nights. For over 25 years, our mission has been to provide a welcoming, affordable, and safe space, connecting Portland with travelers worldwide and making a positive impact locally and beyond.','We are located in the Northwest district, just a few blocks from popular shops, cafes, pubs, cinemas, and some of the city\'s best restaurants. Many area attractions, including the Pearl District, downtown Portland, Saturday Market, Portland Farmers Market, Powell\'s Bookstore, art galleries, the Lan Su Chinese Garden, museums, the MLS Stadium, and Pioneer Square, are within walking distance. The Rose Gardens and Japanese Gardens are a short bus ride or a 25-minute walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTcxNjExMzM%3D/original/ddf8e923-c19f-4cf2-b916-3ff7ccac20b9.jpeg',2820851,27,'45.52734','-122.69084',2,3,3.00,1.00,2.00,93.00,1,365,93,4.73,17161133),(765,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17176362','Beautiful private Apartment','Our comfortable apartment is fully furnished.  It has a gas fireplace for a great cozy feeling with a fully equipped kitchen with full size appliances.  Full private bathroom and  laundry.  Fully equipped with a bedroom with a queen size bed.  The common area has two queen size futons with exra thick mattresses.   Complimentary wine, eggs, and chocolates','We are close to downtown, the Columbia gorge, Japanese gardens, the zoo, Omsi, and the Portland rose gardens or a day trip to the mountains for skiing or hiking. There are many breweries to visit as well or a quick day trip to the wineries.  We are about 12 minutes to the convention center. We live on a unpaved road that has some potholes thanks to the city so we apologize in advance. 2 miles to the golf course.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/03080529-a548-4d6d-9346-445d762062b9.jpg',79068987,78,'45.50122','-122.53778',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,14,5.00,17176362),(766,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17191505','Spacious and Clean NE Portland *Pet Friendly*','Get the chance to live like a Portlander! <br />Huge lovely space in a safe neighborhood, close to downtown, Portland airport, public transportation, grocery, and restaurants.<br />Private 24hr. keyless entry, fenced deck, and backyard.<br />Free street parking...perfect!','This is the great Rose City Park Neighborhood, easy to walk and get around, there\'s a golf course and a park 2 blocks away for a nice little jog, or you can just go to downtown and enjoy our great City!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-17191505/original/7c850ec8-dcbf-4a9a-91c5-a7da647e0294.jpeg',18925199,39,'45.54531','-122.59578',1,2,0.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,3,365,246,4.78,17191505),(767,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17193144','Modern Montavilla Studio','Renovated 2016.  This attached apartment is in Montavilla-close to shops on Stark St. Less than 20 min driving to downtown, about 40 min on public transit. It\'s ~320 sq ft.  It has a kitchen with basic items. It\'s bright and a great place to relax after a day in our beautiful city!  We have a cat and small dog that do not enter the space. Neighborhood has its quirks. There are apartments on the street and people are often out enjoying the weather.','The studio is in a simple and somewhat quirky residential neighborhood in Montavilla. There are a couple apartment buildings on the street and sometimes there are more people and children outside, especially in nice weather.  It is walking distance from Glisan St. and Stark St. where you can find cute shops, cafes, restaurants, and bars.  There is also a farmers market on Sundays (June-October).  Some of our favorite places in the neighborhood are Country Cat for a yummy brunch, Vintage for delicious cocktail, Bipartisan Cafe for coffee and a treat, Roscoes for beer and great sushi happy hour, and East Glisan Pizza for pizza, beer, and a basketball game!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/334d3e6c-507b-48fa-b32f-577c3c2ab604.jpg',10354978,10,'45.52867','-122.57093',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,162,4.90,17193144),(768,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17220608','Cozy home away from home in NE Portland','This renovated 1100 sq ft basement apartment in a house has great light, a private entrance, and a working fireplace. Two bedrooms can accommodate 4 people, plus additional sleeping options in the main area. We are close to PDX airport, and easily drivable to food and attractions. We are a block from a park with a playground, track, tennis courts, and ball fields. The Alberta Arts District, with gobs of restaurants, cafes and shops, is within a 15-minute walk or 5-minute drive.','You\'ll stay in the Cully neighborhood of Northeast Portland, near the Alberta Arts District, on a quiet neighborhood street. Our area is known for large lots and urban farms, although downtown is just a quick drive away.<br /><br />Within walking distance, food options include taquerias, pubs,  food trucks, coffee shops, and fish-n-chips.  Popular places to eat nearby include McMenamin\'s Kennedy School, Pizza Jerk, Salt and Straw, Pip\'s Original Donuts, and Bollywood Theater. <br /><br />New Seasons, Portland\'s natural foods supermarket chain, is just 9 blocks away. A convenience store is 3 blocks away.<br /><br />One block away, you have Fernhill Park - a huge green space with a track, sports fields, tennis courts, a playground, splash pad (summer months) and fenceless off-leash dog park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-17220608/original/9f409d1f-8b4e-49a0-911f-f8a8c20de033.jpeg',115783024,21,'45.56484','-122.61949',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,111.00,1,1125,343,4.94,17220608),(769,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17225450','Nest NW Portland One Bedroom','Welcome to your clean, spacious one bedroom Nest tucked off bustling NW 23rd Ave in the heart of the restaurant and shopping mecca of PDX. <br />Fully equipped apartment with free W/D on site and plenty of comfortable space to enjoy Portland to the fullest! Mid-stay cleaning service available-message me for details.','All the eating, drinking, shopping you could want are at your finger tips in NW Portland.  <br />Portland is a foodies paradise and this apartment offers easy access to it all! St Honore Boulangerie french bakery, lunch of every style from food cart to sit-down, dinner theaters and dive bars, hand-made ice cream, classy pool halls...and that is just the beginning located just steps from your apartment door.  <br /><br />Shopping is top notch too.  Vintage jewelry, clothing boutiques galore, keepsakes and high-class home furnishings, and the list goes on.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-17225450/original/9f8ce062-b7af-4552-911f-6088c36c0bf6.jpeg',14540855,27,'45.53495','-122.6992',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,62.00,30,1125,120,4.88,17225450),(770,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17238144','Cozy Cottage in Mt. Scott','The cottage has everything you\'ll need for your Portland adventures! It comes fully equipped with a well stocked kitchen, outdoor patio,  and lots of natural light. You\'ll have quick access to shops, restaurants and bars in the Woodstock/Mt. Scott neighborhoods. Highlights include Mt. Scott Park, Double Mountain Brewing, Bella\'s Italian Bakery, The Portland Mercado, Cartlandia, Cloud City Ice Cream and New Seasons Market.','Mt. Scott is a nice, quite neighborhood in Southeast Portland. There is lots to explore like Mt. Scott Park, the Mercado, Foster Street, and nearby Woodstock. Trendy areas like Division and Hawthorne are nearby as well!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5bdb5733-3206-489f-a093-bf8f0b3680d3.jpg',11236598,65,'45.476','-122.58604',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,70.00,1,1125,390,4.95,17238144),(771,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17257045','Woodlawn 2bed/1ba Only Steps to Pubs & Cafes','Clean and comfortable 2 bed/1 bath, queen beds in both bedrooms and a comfy sofa in the living room, 5-G Wifi, Roku TV.  Across the street from 2 great pubs, a tasty Mexican restaurant and Pizza shop.  A 5 block walk to 5 other restaurants/pubs and a coffee shop. Woodlawn Park is a lovely picnic/lounging/walk just 4 blocks away. Only 12 min from the Airport and 16 min from downtown! Our co-host Jacob lives in the basement apartment which has a separate entrance. He’s available via text or phone.','The Woodlawn neighborhood is served by the central business nexus of the Dekum St triangle.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b8d6c048-53a8-4a9a-9013-28feb439f47b.jpg',6628849,45,'45.57197','-122.64594',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,79.00,1,13,874,4.85,17257045),(772,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17269218','The Book House: Quiet Queen','Book here for the Quiet Queen ONLY-one queen bed/two persons only.<br /><br /><br />For Twin Bed/Balcony ONLY-go to Book House: Twin Bed w/Balcony.<br /><br /><br />Links:<br /><br />One queen bed: https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17269218?s=51<br /><br /><br />One single bed:https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17866124?s=51','Super-friendly neighborhood. Street parking.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/194d27c4-556c-41ad-b1fb-e8dd2496a159.jpg',42694776,60,'45.58656','-122.73021',2,2,1.50,2.00,2.00,59.00,1,7,72,4.82,17269218),(773,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17305201','Everything You Need Rain or Shine','Stay in this cozy and bright 2 bedroom basement apartment in North Portland with your own private entrance. Ideal for 4 guests, or a family of 5. This spot is a mile from University of Portland and the St. Johns neighborhood. Explore all Portland has to offer and trips to Mt Hood, the Coast and The Gorge. Restaurants, cafes and food carts are nearby or shop at the grocery next door and cook up your own feast.   <br /><br />Perfect for UofP visitors, PNW explorers, or anyone looking for a home base.','A city divided into quadrants, North Portland is the fifth quadrant of the city. 15 minutes from downtown Portland, the University Park/St Johns neighborhoods are one of Portland’s hidden gems. Walk down Lombard towards the St Johns bridge to check out boutique shops, unique craft beer taprooms, restaurants and food carts. Head down towards the University of Portland along tree-lined streets that lead to wooded green parks and views of the city center. Visit the many dive bars on a stroll towards Mock Crest and Kenton for a taste of old Portland. Grab a Lyft or public transit and head to the hip new Portland neighborhoods in Northeast just minutes away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/acaa3447-113c-4bbf-84cd-f8903306604f.jpg',8335229,60,'45.58539','-122.73102',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,127,4.97,17305201),(774,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17327332','Modern Oasis- hip/cute/walkable/close to downtown','Centrally located in one of the coolest neighborhoods in Portland- a light, hip airy, newly renovated modern space. Just blocks from some of Portland\'s best restaurants. New, stylish, with eclectic touches: full kitchen, large open space with TV/sitting room, dining table, full bath, queen, trundle bed (twin), convertible couch (twin ). Back yard is a sanctuary with pond - an oasis in the city. Blocks from \"restaurant row\", market,  theater, local coffee shops, public transportation.','A block from Whole Foods Laurelhurst, bustling cafe\'s, parks and trendy eateries.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dbb632aa-90bd-4076-bd1a-cc201ef5b672.jpg',940836,12,'45.52304','-122.63502',1,4,1.00,0.00,3.00,95.00,30,30,258,4.84,17327332),(775,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17348491','Heart of Arbor Lodge, Clean and Modern Retreat','Modern and beautifully crafted 800 Sq. Ft. space. We are located in the heart of the Arbor Lodge neighborhood in North Portland. Our 2 story guest house will be the perfect place to unwind during your visit to Portland. <br /><br />We are 6 blocks from the light rail transit (The Max) and a short ride to trendy breweries, cafes, and restaurants. We are also less than 5 mi away from attractions such as the Convention Center, Moda Center, Expo Center, Adidas NA Headquarters, and The University of Portland.','Our home is located near Arbor Lodge Park and Gammans City Park.  New Seasons and Fred Meyer grocery stores are less than a mile away.  Easy access to Kenton neighborhood (w/ local library and great coffee) and close to Alberta,  Williams, Woodlawn and Mississippi district.  NW 23rd and Pearl District are only 5 miles away!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e3a8e508-6bbf-48fd-91ee-261ef231720f.jpg',36014626,51,'45.57558','-122.68764',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,143.00,2,4,551,4.96,17348491),(776,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17381562','Home Sweet Home in St. Johns','Bright fully furnished 2+ bedroom, 2 bathroom two-story house in cute St. Johns neighborhood.  Right on bus route and walking distance to downtown St. Johns with shops, restaurants, grocery stores, and neighborhood parks.','Cute St. Johns is located in the northern peninsula of Portland.  It\'s like a small town within the city.  We have our own downtown area, that is about 15 minute walk away with restaurants, shopping, and grocery stores.  Travel over the iconic St. Johns bridge to access hiking trails or visit Cathedral Park located under the bridge for a relaxing afternoon or just a beautiful stroll.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/28a1df77-a67a-40cd-892f-0e3534e3b565.jpg',6514453,42,'45.58522','-122.74491',1,5,2.00,2.00,4.00,175.00,2,45,121,4.95,17381562),(777,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17386788','❤️ CLEAN ★ NEAR DOWNTOWN ★ PATIO ★ WALKABLE','☀ Featured on travel blogs!<br />☀ 10 Min from downtown + Airport <br />☀ Free parking<br />☀ Luxury queen bed • premium bedding <br />☀ 1 additional full size bed + sofa bed<br />☀ Fully stocked kitchen<br />☀ Outdoor patio + BBQ + garden<br />☀ Super Fast Wifi (200+mbps)<br />☀ 55” 4K Smart TV<br />☀ Smart Home <br />☀ Spa style shower<br />☀ Steps from public transit<br />☀ Safe walkable neighborhood<br />☀ Bikes for exploring Portland <br /><br /><br />★☆Learn More Below & Experience Portland With Us!★☆','•  Located in the historic Laurelhurst/Tabor neighborhood<br />• Extremely safe and peaceful for walking <br />•  A dream for bikers<br />•  Huge lush mature trees<br />•  Walking distance to public transit, restaurants, bars and coffee shops<br />• A Starbucks is 4 doors down','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0d61a692-afcf-4533-9c51-a1dc74c6944f.jpg',14008197,52,'45.52634','-122.61484',1,3,1.00,1.00,3.00,90.00,2,30,244,4.90,17386788),(778,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17422378','Charming apartment in the middle of Portland!','Welcome to this lovely apartment in the heart of Portland!  <br />     4 min-Crystal Springs Rhododendron Garden<br />     5 min-Oregon Museum of Science & Industry<br />     10 min-Powell\'s Books, Portland Art Museum, Lan Su Chinese Garden, Japanese Garden, Hoyt Arboretum, Children\'s Museum, International Rose Test Garden<br />     15 min-Pittock Mansion, Forest Park, Oregon Zoo <br />     30 min-Columbia River Gorge National Scenic Area<br />     90 min-Oregon Coast, Mount Hood Timberline Lodge<br />     1:40-Mount St Helens','We are within walking distance of People\'s Food Coop and New Seasons, two excellent organic food groceries.  There is also a large Safeway about 12 blocks away and Trader Joe\'s isn\'t far.  Every Wednesday afternoon People\'s hosts a farmer\'s market year round.  Also in walking distance are a wide variety of restaurants, pubs, a wide variety of shops, bicycle rentals, bakeries, coffee shops, unique theaters, etc.  Hop on the bus just a block away and you\'re downtown in ten minutes, or rent a bike a few blocks from here and ride.  Portland is the best biking city in the country!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9aa1102b-abe0-42ff-be03-7e19332decd2.jpg',23043981,67,'45.49567','-122.63856',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,105.00,3,90,90,4.94,17422378),(779,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17462225','Dog-Friendly Retro SE Portland 2-bedroom with yard','This clean, bright, and spacious house in SE Portland is a great place to relax after a day of exploring all of what PDX has to offer. The house is located in a cute old Portland neighborhood where coffee, food, and drinks are all within walking distance. Close to everything, yet removed enough to feel at home at the end of your day!','Some of the neighborhood gems within walking distance from the house are:<br />Local watering hole - Gladstone St Pub<br />Pizza shop and cocktails - Saint Pizza Lounge<br />Sandwich shop - Shut Up and Eat<br />Coffee shop - Coffee Beer, Starbucks<br />Parks - Kenilworth Park and Creston Park<br />Groceries & stuff - Walgreens, Trader Joe\'s, and Plaid Pantry.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTc0NjIyMjU%3D/original/771f8e81-d7a9-48df-a089-8b96bdfc0e86.png',1778883,67,'45.49184','-122.6212',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,120,25,4.68,17462225),(780,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17479457','Come stay with my cool cats!','I\'m Dan (he/him), and my cats and I love hosting!  <br /><br />I greatly enjoy meeting good, kind people from all over the world.  I strive to ensure your trip is safe, successful, and fun!<br /><br />I charge only a small $50 cleaning fee.  No other fees!<br /><br />LGBTQ+ ally!','Three Mexican restaurants and a Cambodian restaurant are within walking distance.  There are two grocery stores not far by car.  <br /><br />The Roseway business district is about 15 blocks away.  The vintage Roseway Theater has digital equipment and plays first-run movies.  Fairley\'s Pharmacy is across the street, with an old-school soda fountain and ice cream.  In the past year, two new coffee shops have moved into the area.  I really love The Red Gate, with bubble waffles.<br /><br />The Beamont District is relatively close also.  It is a very walkable area, with wonderful storefronts, restaurants, coffee shops, and gift shops.  Plenty of great restaurants!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c270c0f3-cfcd-4d33-85f1-78cd25a4f8b7.jpg',118408050,74,'45.545456','-122.572716',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,60.00,2,29,212,4.99,17479457),(781,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17498339','Large Private Home - King Bed','Ideal for corporate rentals and relocation housing! This updated and spacious 3600 sq ft home is close to downtown. Located within the city limits,  it\'s a short trip to the city center, OHSU, PCC Sylvania, Moda Center, Nike Campus and Intel. Transit station is .75 mile from home.<br /><br />THIS IS A MONTHLY RENTAL.  PLEASE ENTER 31 NIGHTS INTO THE DATES - THE LODGING TAXES OF APPROX. $2200 WILL CHANGE TO $0.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c934921e-0e44-4d00-b460-9fe1a39498c1.jpg',62992553,53,'45.44692','-122.72011',1,16,3.50,7.00,9.00,500.00,30,1125,2,5.00,17498339),(782,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17556602','NE Irvngtn Bungalow','Bottom floor (1500 sq ft) of charming 1906 bungalow in NE Irvington neighborhood.  2 BR, 1 BA. Short walk to street car, MAX, bus, and Broadway. Close to Mississippi, Alberta, N Williams districts and downtown and the Pearl. Great block and neighbors. It is where you want to be!','Historic residential neighborhood with beautiful tree-lined streets and plenty of gardens. Commercial strips, public transportation and city park close by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2193a891-4a52-4504-81d7-d685d181b4e9.jpg',444759,26,'45.54289','-122.65893',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,200.00,3,45,33,4.94,17556602),(783,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17577294','Bright Studio Near Portland\'s Favorite Restaurants','Impeccably clean, incredibly comfortable walker\'s paradise with hip design and a caring and responsive host.<br /><br />Relax in this garden condo built for AirB&B by two award winning interior designers. Sleep soundly in a new bed and block out the light with heavy curtains. Fantasize about Michelin Star Farmhouse Thai. Crave Tove cold-brew. Pine for Hazel Cafe biscuit sammiches. <br /><br />Then awake, and step outside. You\'re a short walk away from many of Portland\'s best restaurants, bars and shops.','The ideal place for a true Portland experience, this home sits in the heart of the Hawthorne Neighborhood. It is home to some most notable restaurants, cafes, shops and bars the city has to offer, such as:<br /><br />-- Blue Star Donuts<br />-- Fried Egg I’m In Love <br />-- Stumptown Coffee<br />-- Sapphire Hotel<br />-- Jackpot Records<br />-- Jam on Hawthorne<br />-- Martian Arts<br />-- Coava Coffee<br />-- Red Light<br />-- Chicken and Guns<br />-- Apizza Scholls<br />-- The Waffle Window<br />-- Powell\'s Book<br />-- El Cubo de Cuba<br />-- Crossroads Trading Co.<br />-- ¿Por Qué No?<br />-- Nakhon<br />-- Cup & Saucer<br />-- Potato Champion<br />-- The Gold Door<br />-- Gold Dust Meridian<br />-- Harlow<br />-- Nick\'s Coney Island<br />-- Chez Machin<br />-- Thanh Thao\'s<br />-- Cha-Cha-Cha<br />-- Pho Dalat<br />-- Happy Sparrow<br />-- Tov<br />-- ... and too many more to list!<br /><br />LOCAL DESTINATIONS: <br />------------------------------------<br /><br />- ½ mile from ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/91f8419d-b178-4741-90ec-f3f45c56477c.jpg',7635902,16,'45.51226','-122.63361',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,60.00,30,364,133,4.87,17577294),(784,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17593943','Ladd\'s Subtraction','(Please see updated Policy under \"The Space\")<br /><br />Great little basement apartment with a Queen bed located just a few blocks from Ladd\'s Addition. Get it? Super close to all the Clinton and Division St. bars and restaurants!','Inner SE Portland! Subtracted from Ladd\'s Addition and a few blocks from the Clinton neighborhood!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ffc851bd-8490-44fd-b866-075dd363ba58.jpg',16113117,25,'45.50255','-122.64399',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,75.00,2,28,121,4.72,17593943),(785,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17637225','Cozy home in the Alberta Arts District','Our house is located just three short blocks from Alberta street in the colorful Alberta Arts District, which has many wonderful restaurants, quirky boutiques and creative street art installations.<br /><br />Please note this post is for a full house - 3 bedrooms and 2 bathrooms; a downstairs bathroom with tub and shower, upstairs bathroom with shower.  Large great room, kitchen, laundry room, 600 sq. ft wraparound porch, and small fenced-in backyard.<br /><br />You will have the whole property to yourself.','The neighborhood is quaint, quiet, and historical (many houses were built in the period from 1880 - 1910, our house was built in 1904).<br /><br />The house is a 5 minute walk to bustling NE Alberta St, one of the \"hippest\" parts of the city.  Alberta St. offers a huge selection of restaurants, bars, boutiques, art projects, and plenty of local color.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-17637225/original/874a956c-4fa2-4a0d-b25e-bd33d1e0fe95.jpeg',5666531,14,'45.56086','-122.65385',1,6,2.00,3.00,3.00,90.00,30,1125,7,4.57,17637225),(786,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17652225','Clean & modern Concordia studio','- early check-in and late checkout times<br />- light-filled basement apartment<br />- full kitchen & dining<br />- tasteful furnishings<br />- private and peaceful <br />- centrally located','Welcome to Concordia, one of Rip City\'s most desirable neighborhoods! Here you’ll be nestled on a quiet street next to the University of Oregon campus, conveniently located only a few minutes from PDX airport by car; a half block from the bus stop (#17); and less than half a mile from groceries, pharmacy, and other essentials.<br /><br />Super walkable! Awesome local coffee roasters Extracto down the street, award-winning dining at Dame a five minute walk. The burgers at Wilder are the best in town. Walk down to Gabbiano\'s for awesome homestyle Italian or to Toy Shop Ramen, and another 1/4 mile to the Kennedy School—a converted elementary school with a movie theater, soaking pool, and a collection of bars and restaurants. Less than 10 minutes on foot to yoga, shopping, coffee, and a bakery at 30th and Killingsworth.<br /><br />Or . . . walk 15 minutes to famous Alberta Street to catch a show at the Alberta Rose Theater, get your licks at Salt and Straw Ice Cream, rooftop dining at the ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-17652225/original/f72344ac-5df9-4e0f-90ab-3aa39cabf7be.jpeg',92031924,1,'45.56783','-122.63879',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,100.00,1,12,238,4.89,17652225),(787,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17653916','The Fox Chase Inn Flat 2','The Fox Chase Flat is simple, clean, spacious with lots of natural sunlight. Located within a few hundred feet of some of Portland\'s best restaurants, bars, coffee shops, and markets. Only 10 minutes from Portland airport, 7 miles from the center of downtown.<br />A charming place to make yourself at home, while you explore all that Portland has to offer or just simply work from home.','The Fox Chase Addition neighborhood has a little of everything Portland has to offer.We are located within The Alberta Art District that has some of NE Portland\'s Best restaurants, best coffee shops, galleries, boutiques, parks and grocery stores.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-17653916/original/0d672771-8b1f-49cc-bf9a-de5eef5e69d9.jpeg',1213257,1,'45.56368','-122.63536',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,30,365,14,4.36,17653916),(788,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17655794','Foxchase Flat #1','1929 Folklore inspired Flat<br />Charming, cozy, lodging with old world look, tone, feel located in one of Portland\'s famed foodie enclaves. Just a 10 min drive for PDX and 15 min from downtown proper. A multitude of outstanding eateries, bars, shops, and galleries all with in close walking distance.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-17655794/original/8629fb2a-6958-40bc-9fe3-7f8dad89daaa.jpeg',1213257,1,'45.56318','-122.63623',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,126.00,1,1125,26,4.96,17655794),(789,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17669875','New Gorgeous Modern Apt in Historic Victorian','This modern ground-level apt has reclaimed wood accents, a kitchenette, new appliances and furniture, a luxurious shower, and comfy beds. A cozy, well-designed jumping off point for exploring Portland and its beautiful NW nature. Located at the Dekum triangle restaurants and shops including Breakside Brewery, 10 mins to airport, 15 to downtown, 5 to Alberta Arts, and an easy drive to the Columbia River Gorge or Mt Hood. Great for couples, adventurers, and business people. All are welcome here.','We are right around the corner from the original Breakside Brewery- with multiple award-winning beers, Firehouse restaurant- with delicious brick oven pizza and Italian food, Woodlawn coffee shop- a cozy neighborhood spot for good coffee, pastries and food, Oregon Public House- the nation\'s first non-profit bar, Tamale Boy- authentic Mexican cuisine, Bassotto Gelateria- Italian ice cream, Tough Luck - a new bar in town, The High Water Mark- bar and event space and 7.5 acre Woodlawn Park. Woodlawn neighborhood has a small town feel, but is minutes from the Alberta Arts district and a quick drive or bus to downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/596560c8-7b28-4524-a891-a9ff3ae56e39.jpg',103713628,45,'45.57255','-122.65732',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,100.00,7,120,175,4.89,17669875),(790,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17696910','Historic 3 BR Updated Condo in Alphabet District','Centrally located in Portland\'s NW Alphabet district. Surrounded by shops on 23rd and 21st Ave. Blocks from the Pearl District, downtown, Forest Park, entertainment, and restaurants. Good Sam hospital, streetcar line, and Salt & Straw are one block away. 1,000 SF condo in renovated historic building with windows on all sides, large living and dining rooms, remodeled kitchen and bathroom. Walk score of 97 and bike score of 96. Good for solo adventurers, business travelers, couples, or families.','The Alphabet district is an excellent place to visit while in Portland. This area is filled with shops, restaurants, and beautiful homes. The architecture is absolutely stunning and is mainly comprised of older homes that have been well maintained and newly restored. It\'s a great place to take a leisurely stroll while enjoying the beautiful views of the city.<br /><br />This district is also home to the ever so famous Salt & Straw Creamery. You cannot visit this part of town without experiencing a scoop of their amazing ice cream! There are tons of restaurants to choose from and the streets are filled with the most adorable mom and pop and boutique style stores. There are several parking garages around the area that charge a nominal fee.<br /><br />You might find yourself walking up and down some of the Portland hills as you pass through. Many of the streets are lined by beautiful trees and bright foliage. If you\'re visiting Portland and are looking for fun things to do, I would highly','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-17696910/original/2edfb950-7353-44fe-8e5c-3eac59097c29.jpeg',17932869,27,'45.52829','-122.69567',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,28,4.79,17696910),(791,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17714737','Queen Room w/ Private Bath at NW Portland Hostel','Experience Portland’s top-rated, family-owned hostel, in the vibrant Northwest District! Enjoy a FREE breakfast and explore nearby downtown attractions, Washington Park, the Rose and Japanese Gardens, and hiking trails. Join our daily free events like walking tours, tap tastings, live music, and trivia nights. For over 25 years, our mission has been to provide a welcoming, affordable, and safe space, connecting Portland with travelers worldwide and making a positive impact locally and beyond.','We are located in the Northwest district, just a few blocks from popular shops, cafes, pubs, cinemas, and some of the city\'s best restaurants. Many area attractions, including the Pearl District, downtown Portland, Saturday Market, Portland Farmers Market, Powell\'s Bookstore, art galleries, the Lan Su Chinese Garden, museums, the MLS Stadium, and Pioneer Square, are within walking distance. The Rose Gardens and Japanese Gardens are a short bus ride or a 25-minute walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTc3MTQ3Mzc%3D/original/9eb23dc4-dd95-44d6-be98-0a42ed4219c1.jpeg',2820851,27,'45.52542','-122.68933',2,2,4.00,1.00,1.00,102.00,1,365,52,4.90,17714737),(792,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17733906','BEST NEIGHBORHOOD IN PORTLAND','Completely furnished, modern, private. Located in friendly, close-in Northwest Portland. This central location with a 98 Walk Score and is next to some of the best restaurants, bars and cafes in town.  Full kitchen.  Private bath. Beats hotel pricing.','Close-in Northwest Portland- Nob Hill.<br /><br />This convenient location, with a 98 POINT WALK SCORE is blocks from trendy NW 23rd AVE, Dragonfly Coffee House, St. Honore Bakery, McMenamins Pub, a natural foods grocery store, the public library, as well as the post office. <br /><br />Window shop at all the lovely boutiques located just blocks away or hike/bike/run/explore the 80 miles of trails and over 5,000 acres of Forest Park; one of the largest urban parks in the United States! <br /><br />You can quickly and easily reach the Pearl District, the Brewery Blocks or Downtown Portland in minutes by foot, bike or streetcar; no need for a vehicle when living here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-17733906-unapproved/original/6d29406f-669d-4aca-b7f5-cc01624c3f3b.JPEG',10161853,27,'45.53536','-122.70287',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,53.00,30,800,31,4.74,17733906),(793,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17735080','Alberta Arts Urban Haven','A comfortable and spacious upstairs suite in an ideal Portland location—a<br />short drive from downtown and less than one block from the vibrant Alberta Arts district, where you’ll find excellent coffee shops, restaurants, bars, food carts, and more. Close enough to walk to everything in the neighborhood while still tucked away from the noise of Alberta Street. <br />Blocks away from a natural food co-op, bike rental, and bus stop w/direct service downtown. Free street parking, 20 minutes to PDX.','The Alberta Arts District<br />Driving through the neighborhoods of Northeast Portland, you suddenly stumble upon an oasis of unique restaurants, bars, boutiques, and art galleries. Buildings are decorated with colorful wall murals, a cyclist rides by on a two-story bicycle, and people of all backgrounds are sipping beer, coffee, and kombucha - welcome to the Alberta Arts District!<br />Where is Alberta Arts District?<br />East of MLK Jr. Blvd, the Alberta Arts District can be found on NE Alberta St. from 9th all the way to 33rd Street. The area has been gradually growing over recent years, so even if you\'ve been here before you are likely to see something new.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/14734096-17a2-4fa0-a31e-517e1e56447e.jpg',22498676,14,'45.55769','-122.65268',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,50.00,30,90,469,4.88,17735080),(794,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17749267','Hotel Style Studio Apartment - #X','Newly constructed modern townhouse. Located in the Overlook neighborhood in North Portland. Ground floor suite with its own entrance and is separate from the main house. Full bath. Fantastic location. Easy access to the Airport, Public Transport, Light rail, Convention Center, restaurants etc. Close to N. Mississippi, Alberta, I-5, Overlook. This space was designed to be a like a hotel suite, it does not have a kitchen. It does have a mini fridge. There is ample and safe street parking.','There is a green space next to the house for stretching your legs or walking your dog.<br />We are also located next to a convenience store for your convenience.<br />If you want to buy liquor the closest place is called North by Northeast, 4375 N Williams Ave, Portland, OR 97217<br />There is a dispensary nearby called Green Sky.<br /><br />Here are few food recommendations if you have the time.<br /><br />There is a bagel place two blocks away, Eisenhour Bagels. <br />I can highly recommend the the Japanese Cafe, Miho, three blocks away. The Alibi Room is across the street for Tiki Bar and Karaoke.<br />Broder Nord, also a great hip breakfast place. Tilt is down on Swan Island if you want giant burgers and fries.<br />There is a whole strip of bars, food carts and restaurants along N Mississippi Ave: Por Que No tacos, is great. Gravy is great for large breakfasts. <br /><br />Two of my favorites are Toro Bravo and Tasty and Sons, both run by John Gorham. <br />Best pizza; Life of Pie','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8ecaa374-6d99-40a0-9141-6cd06181c593.jpg',121088523,13,'45.55653','-122.6796',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,81.00,30,1125,67,4.91,17749267),(795,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17762473','The Magic House / Walk Score 93!','Everyone\'s safety is our top priority.  We are following Airbnb\'s enhanced cleaning guidelines, and our neighborhood is safe and peaceful.<br /><br />The Magic House is located in the heart of Hawthorne\'s charming restaurant and boutique district, three blocks to SE Hawthorne and SE Division.<br /><br />15 min to the airport, 10 min to downtown and convention center.   Driveway parking for easy load in and out.<br /><br />The house is comfortable for big groups.  A second unit is available in the backyard, booked separately.','We are located in one of the most beautiful, and hippest neighborhoods in Portland.<br /><br />With the center of both SE Hawthorne and SE Division St within 3 blocks, there is an abundance of restaurants, grocery stores, neighborhood strolling, boutique browsing and hiking options within walking distance.<br /><br />See a movie, or just step in to witness the beautiful and iconic McMenamin\'s Bagdad theater, accompanied by an incredible restaurant/bar/pool hall in the back called the \"Back Stage Bar\", at SE 37th and Hawthorne. It will give you a feel for classic Portland!<br /><br /><br />We are minutes from Mt Tabor park which has a lovely forest with walking trails sitting upon a dormant volcano, and we are 45 minutes to the spectacular 600 foot tall Multnomah waterfall in the gorgeous Columbia River Gorge scenic area.<br /><br />Division is the new up and coming Southeast neighborhood. With lots of modern architecture, new restaurants and shops you will get a feel for the freshest v','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c8b3ce99-4d50-456f-9132-fe6409f795cc.jpg',26822355,8,'45.50824','-122.62435',1,10,5.00,5.00,8.00,231.00,1,14,192,4.83,17762473),(796,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17789859','Upstairs bedroom, 1911 home near Reed, Trader Joes','Stay in the upstairs bedroom of our 1911 farmhouse in SE Portland, near Reed College and across from Trader Joes. The bedroom has a queen bed and a working space. Use communal areas, including: kitchen, living room for hanging out and movies; dining room. There\'s a 1st-floor bathroom (shared w/ other guest if there is one).<br /><br />We’re 15-minute walk to Gladstone pubs and restaurants, a short drive to Woodstock, Division St., the Hawthorne District, and more.<br /><br />Includes washer and dryer in basement.','We are in SE Portland, with awesome neighborhoods and shopping districts in every direction. Our small neighborhood boasts a couple authentic, old-Portland bars and restaurants on Gladstone, all within a 15-minute walk. Reed College is a leisurely half-mile walk away, and its quirky campus offers a beautiful nature trail. The Crystal Springs Rhododendron Garden is also close by. What’s more, Woodstock shops are just a mile south. Clinton Street, with its historic theater and bars, and Division Street, with its hot new restaurants, are a mile and a half to the north. Mt. Tabor, Belmont, and the Hawthorne District are also within a few minutes’ car ride.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b7952df1-3691-4644-9481-0d0004b60ace.jpg',8793178,61,'45.48799','-122.6244',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,1,30,58,5.00,17789859),(797,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17809720','Bright and modern studio.','Located near the Alberta Arts district with a lovely park a block away, you’ll enjoy original mid century modern furnishings and original artwork as a guest in my 100 year old home.','Very walkable with tons of great restaurants.  In a very quiet neighborhood','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3d8caecf-f6fa-4cfd-a9f7-889a609d66b2.jpg',495089,46,'45.55634','-122.62719',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,102.00,2,6,273,4.91,17809720),(798,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17825887','Best neighborhood in Portland- 15','Completely furnished, modern, private. Located in friendly, close-in Northwest Portland. This central location with a 98 Walk Score and is next to some of the best restaurants, bars and cafes in town.','Close-in Northwest Portland- Nob Hill.<br /><br />This convenient location, with a 98 POINT WALK SCORE is blocks from trendy NW 23rd AVE, Dragonfly Coffee House, St. Honore Bakery, McMenamins Pub, a natural foods grocery store, the public library, as well as the post office. <br /><br />Window shop at all the lovely boutiques located just blocks away or hike/bike/run/explore the 80 miles of trails and over 5,000 acres of Forest Park; one of the largest urban parks in the United States! <br /><br />You can quickly and easily reach the Pearl District, the Brewery Blocks or Downtown Portland in minutes by foot, bike or streetcar; no need for a vehicle when living here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-17825887/original/cf5be945-97dc-4959-9a61-0aa86ca55e5d.jpeg',121884165,27,'45.53652','-122.70214',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,57.00,30,1125,15,4.93,17825887),(799,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17847830','Williams Artists Studio - North','Bright and cheery sub-level apartment is tastefully furnished and sparkling clean.Located on a bustling block In the heart of one of Portlands hottest neighborhoods, surrounded by breweries, shops, restaurants & food carts. We are minutes from City Center via close public transportation, bike or car share. This space is 1 of 3 units at this property, one of which is owner occupied. Quite professional property, guests are asked to be =<PG-13. LGBTQ+ friendly. Find a different party place.','The fabulous Williams Corridor in NE Portland. Close in, first-rate public transportation, major north-south bike lanes, New Seasons grocery a block and a half walk. Award winning restaurants and indie shops on the immediate block & vicinity ... or stroll to Mississippi or Alberta for even more eclectic Portland food/drink/shops.<br /><br />Portland is all about neighborhoods and ours in Boise-Eliot is as charming and inviting as they come. Just east of the Willamette River, Boise-Eliot is an eclectic mix of traditional brick buildings, Victorian homes, and brand new ultra-modern structures coexisting happily in the very hip and popular North Portland.<br /><br />Restaurants, shops, New Seasons grocery, bars, food carts, yoga studios, tree-lined streets, coffee shops galore, and more - all within a block or two.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-17847830/original/d0b36a08-d9e9-465c-9f8c-0625142c931b.jpeg',1239203,9,'45.55091','-122.66576',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,88.00,2,180,302,4.93,17847830),(800,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17860056','Bar 3728','This is an open 850 sq ft. studio w/ a queen bed, living space with a modern smart TV & gas fireplace, bar/kitchenette, private entrance & bathroom.  The space is intended for solo travelers only.   I live in the Richmond neighborhood & am located 1 block from 37th & Division Street, which is surrounded by great restaurants & shops.  My home is a 1910 Bungalow & I’ve owned it for 24 years.','Richmond - One block south of Division.<br />Great for dining, shopping and walking to shops & parks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/df51cabb-cfbf-4797-9da7-c1090ddc4106.jpg',15081218,8,'45.50486','-122.62479',1,1,1.00,0.00,1.00,41.00,4,21,163,4.92,17860056),(801,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17866124','The Book House. Quiet Stay: Twin Bed with Balcony','Twin bed/private balcony. Close to Forest Park trailhead/St. John\'s Bridge/downtown St. Johns/Cathedral Park. New Seasons nearby. Close to pubs, restaurants, coffee in safe, friendly neighborhood. 13 blocks from University of Portland. Easy access to NW Portland and airport.<br /><br />Street parking.','Close to New Seasons, restaurants and pubs.  Fairly close to St. Johns and the terrific hiking and biking trails of Forest Park, Cathedral Park and beyond.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b5d11b5b-e725-4c4c-83f8-6c4c65efb186.jpg',42694776,60,'45.58444','-122.72919',2,1,1.50,1.00,2.00,58.00,1,7,182,4.88,17866124),(802,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17904315','Basement Apartment in North Portland','One bedroom apartment in the basement of our 1922 home. This private space has a living room, kitchenette, dining room table, bathroom and separate entrance. Located around the corner from a grocery store and a bus stop right in front of our house. We look forward to having you stay with us!','Welcome to North Portland! We do live on a very busy street; the plus side is we are within walking distance to a grocery store, coffee shop, restaurants and a convenience store is right across the street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/89695a23-6b48-4ffe-b311-7b68f3a1b295.jpg',12591253,51,'45.57663','-122.69579',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,31,178,4.92,17904315),(803,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17937829','Cozy Alley Cottage, Concordia/Alberta Arts, NE PDX','Come enjoy our beautiful detached cottage, in a Concordia alley 5 blocks from Alberta Street.  French doors lead onto your own private patio.  The fully stocked kitchen has everything you need.  The cottage is designed to be self sufficient, and full of natural light.  Take a stroll through the alleyways and wander through Alberta park to restaurants and coffee shops.  It is a very bike friendly neighborhood.  We are also connected by bus lines to downtown.','We live in the Concordia Neighborhood.  A short walk through Alberta Park takes you to Killingsworth and 15th  block where Pod\'nas, Hat Yai, a Vegan taco place and other restaurants and bars are.  Two more blocks south and you get to Alberta Street where between NE 13th all the way up to NE 30th there are lots of great bakeries and breakfast options.  Bollywood, Proud Mary’s and Fuel cafe are some of my favorites.  Our closest cafe, Kiss cafe, on Ainsworth, it has great breakfast burritos and outdoor seating. Feel free to ask us for other suggestions. There are also lots of local businesses open for shopping.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/14547311-dcdd-487e-b24f-e5cf4ed130f3.jpg',9180789,1,'45.56753','-122.64162',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,96.00,3,350,311,4.95,17937829),(804,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17966883','Concordia Fir Cabin','The ultimate Portland cozy place to stay (see reviews) Proximity to great pubs, top-rated restaurants, dispensaries, coffee & tea, airport, and much more!  The shopping/dining of Alberta St, Dekum St, 42nd Ave just blocks away. Queen size bed, eucalyptus hardwood floor, quality decor, turntable and extensive vinyl record collection, private yard, outdoor fire-pit, parking *ONLY* available Nov-May, heating/air, coffee maker/tea kettle, and microwave.','Our proximity to so many great places to get a meal, snack, drink, coffee, nearby parks, galleries, and more. We are also close enough to the airport and access to the highways should those be valuable to you. It\'s easy access to the fun to be had here in Portland from our property (NE, SE, NW, North Portland, and SW).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6f1af462-7112-447e-8a5c-b9155e9ac349.jpg',92867046,1,'45.56907','-122.63181',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,2,14,557,4.95,17966883),(805,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/17978703','Redwood House PDX','Three towering redwood trees create a secluded oasis in the heart of the super vibrant Division/Clinton Street neighborhood.  After exploring our great town, come home and relax in this historic-era bungalow with modern amenities.','The big ticket places to visit are of course Pok Pok, Salt & Straw and Blue Star Donuts, which are just a block away.  But there are so many awesome places within walking distance on Division Street, Clinton Street and Hawthorne Blvd, it\'s super fun to just explore - you can\'t go wrong!<br /><br />Downtown is 3 miles away.  Biking across the Hawthorne Bridge is not too daunting, otherwise it\'s a short drive into the center of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d0622cf3-92ce-4fe7-b1de-8fddc85eeff0.jpg',12223228,8,'45.50564','-122.63194',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,199.00,2,62,247,4.68,17978703),(806,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18005169','The Nehalem House w/hi-spd fiber-optic wifi+Roku!','This 1940\'s bungalow in the highly sought after Woodstock neighborhood of Southeast Portland, is a real charmer. We\'ve celebrated it\'s roots with true to era hardware, fixtures, custom porcelain tile, and oak flooring throughout. Dedicated fiber-optic Wi-Fi, Roku, and an alternate power source for peace of mind. No hard shut-offs in Winter storms! Stocked kitchen, luxury bedding (700+T.C.), cozy woodstove, and extras everywhere! Giant cedars, 16x20 patio, fruit trees, lilac, iris, BBQ, enjoy!','Established quiet neighborhood with friendly neighbors.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/85208a33-c9f0-457a-9c1e-338ace1bb6c5.jpg',123760860,38,'45.46478','-122.61769',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,219.00,30,1125,2,5.00,18005169),(807,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18009756','Hawthorne Apartment w/ Jacuzzi Tub & Kitchen','Light, bright and well-equipped one bedroom basement apartment offers you a quiet respite in an excellent location with a relaxing jetted jacuzzi tub that fits two! Just a block off of Hawthorne, restaurants, bars and shops are easy to find. If staying home is your thing - we\'ve got you covered there too! A 42\" TV in the living room is equipped with a RokuExpress, the one in the bedroom has a ChromeCast and both have antenna for watching local stations.','My home is situated in one of the best areas of SE Portland. Just a block off of the busy Hawthorne Blvd, you\'ll find shops, restaurants and bars just a quick walk away. This residential neighborhood is pretty quiet and tucked away but well-positioned for exploration!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ff5df43d-cd17-470f-83a9-4983de00c1a5.jpg',28583708,8,'45.51074','-122.63379',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,91.00,2,90,216,4.88,18009756),(808,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18023616','2 Primary Suites*Hawthorne/Division Area!','***When making a booking request please CONFIRM NO ONE IN THE GROUP SMOKES! No Exceptions. I am highly sensitive to secondhand smoke. Please confirm you have read the house rules and the \"Other Things To Note\" section when making a booking request.***','Live like a local!  Walk Score of 95! This is a wonderful and highly coveted, trendy Portland neighborhood with incredible restaurants, bars, brew pubs, wine bars and great tax free shopping at locally owned boutiques and vintage shops, all within walking distance.  The nearest coffee shop is a 3 minute walk away but there are several others within walking distance. The nearest restaurants and bars are also 3 minutes away but dozens within 5-20 minutes walk.  Plenty of great shops on both Hawthorne and Division! <br /><br />Nearby restaurants are some of the best in Portland!  Here is a list of a few great restaurants, brew pubs, cideries and bars that are walkable:<br /><br />* Matt\'s BBQ at Hinterland Food Cart pod<br />*Apizza Scholls<br />*Por Que No?<br />*Rangoon Bistro<br />*Kim Jong Grillin Food Cart<br />*Three Doors Down Italian - Upscale<br />*Salt and Straw<br />*Blue Star Donuts<br />*Pinolo Gelato<br />*Petite Provence<br />*Olympia Provisions<br />*Stumptown Coffee<br />','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-18023616/original/e1dbd79b-9945-4547-bb5d-23a2c7aebaef.jpeg',1096266,8,'45.50771','-122.61662',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,183.00,3,120,129,4.95,18023616),(809,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18034741','Bright, modern suite, close-in NE','Modern suite with lots of natural light and private entrance.  This comfortable 650 sq ft studio is nestled in the heart of Portland\'s hottest neighborhoods.  Walk to Williams Ave restaurants and cafes in 5 min, the Alberta arts district in 7 min, and the trendy Mississippi neighborhood in 10 min.<br /><br />It is conveniently located a 15 min drive from the airport, and you can bike, drive, or bus to downtown in only 15 minutes without getting on the freeways.','Close-in NE is one of the hottest locations in Portland and this AirBnB is located a short walk from it all.  You\'ll enjoy staying right between three bustling neighborhoods without the hassle of parking. The Williams Ave restaurants and bars are just 5 min on foot, the Alberta Arts District is 7 min on foot and the trendy Mississippi Ave restaurants just 10 min on foot.  These three neighborhoods offer amazing restaurants and bakeries, family friendly activities, as well as some of the most popular bars in town.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f30f8bcd-f595-4144-913c-19dbf1cc79fa.jpg',2021272,24,'45.55857','-122.66723',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,56.00,2,30,564,4.80,18034741),(810,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18074788','A tree house on a quiet street','The apartment has a private entrance to an entire floor of our 3-story home.  There are two comfortable bedrooms, living room and kitchen, with oversized windows to draw the outside in. Portland\'s incredible urban Forest Park trails are literally at our doorstep. And still, we are just over a two mile walk/drive to downtown shopping, dining, entertainment and much more!  We are also close to Portland State Univ and OHSU\'s medical school. It\'s a great location for either business or pleasure.','Our neighborhood is an older and quiet neighborhood of Portland.  It\'s great for walks and running.  We are on a hill and you can expect to have a mix of terrain when you are out.  We can direct you to many of the frequented routes--roads & trails, each with their own allure and challenge.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b44c89ea-5636-4566-80ad-de647164a7d4.jpg',17527121,54,'45.50131','-122.69638',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,150.00,2,7,130,4.98,18074788),(811,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18093210','Sellwood Garden Studio with Private Patio','New construction garden studio with private patio. Light filled, cozy, quiet & private. High ceilings, clerestory windows, skylight & sliding patio doors. Airy and light year-round. Well equipped kitchenette, queen size Murphy bed with real mattress, walk-in shower & plenty of counter space. Easy street parking in front. New Seasons Market, coffee, bagels, restaurants & shops all within walking distance. 5 blocks to the Willamette River and Sellwood Bridge. Neighborhood walk score of 90.','Sellwood-Westmoreland is a one of Portland\'s 95 neighborhoods. We are on the east side of the Willamette River. 10 mins from Reed College and 20 from Lewis & Clark. The neighborhood includes many small commercial areas including SE 13th Ave, just a block away. Our location and the neighborhood are very safe, with a walk score of 90. The Garden Studio is within easy walking distance of New Seasons Market, coffee houses, bakery, restaurants and food carts, wine shops, bars and brewpubs, antique shops and boutiques. There are bike shops, yoga studios, parks, and a movie theater. We\'re are just a 15 minute walk to the pedestrian and bike friendly Sellwood Bridge across the Willamette.  Check out our Guest Guidebook on arrival to see additional recommendations.. <br /><br />We are a few blocks walking/biking distance from Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge, the Springwater Corridor Trail, and the Willamette River. A walk to the bluff of Sellwood Park provides a stunning view across the Willamette ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-18093210/original/8c80fd79-2d59-48fd-9077-86e2411c8d66.jpg',32635358,20,'45.46294','-122.65531',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,3,14,282,4.95,18093210),(812,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18094561','Clean, Comfy, Modern Private Apartment','Lovely, light-filled, quiet, clean apartment with private entrance, full kitchen.  Architect-designed for style and comfort. Two bedrooms, comfortably houses 4 people (5 if someone sleeps on the couch!) in prime Alberta Arts location.<br /><br />Our apartment has a private entrance 20 feet from our front door and requires no interaction with us while checking-in or out, but we are nearby and happy to help with whatever you need.','Our \"walkability\" score is 86, 50 for transit and 97 for biking.<br /><br />The Alberta Street area is just two blocks away, which means you are within short walking distance of tons of interesting eateries, shops and bars.  Within 3 to 5 blocks you can find tasty thai, spanish, mexican, iraqi, irish, japanese, italian and vegan food, as well as some of the most delicious coffee and cocktails in town.<br /><br />We are also close to several key bus lines (download the Trimet app for easy planning) and are a fairly short Lyft/Uber ride to many other neighborhoods. While many guests rent a car, we have had quite a few do without and they\'ve had a great time.<br /><br />Downtown is the center of Portland, and home to Powell\'s and other must-see spots, but it\'s not necessarily the most charming area to stay. Portland is more a series of walkable neighborhoods with shopping, dining and more residential feeling. Our particular neighborhood is 10-15 minutes from downtown by car (unless it\'s r','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f6974bb3-9b05-4ba2-a83a-2158661cb94b.jpg',491984,1,'45.55855','-122.6328',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,116.00,1,1125,355,4.97,18094561),(813,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18136463','Classic Garden Bungalow in Overlook with Hot Tub','Come stay in a newly-restored Craftsman Bungalow on a beautiful property with lush gardens in the amazing neighborhood of Overlook. You have the whole house to yourself! <br /><br />The hot tub is in the private backyard, but easily reservable for your enjoyment! Your hosts are in the private backyard cottage and available for anything you might need during your stay!','Visit our village just around the corner! Pick up a warm focaccia at Milk Glass Market or indulge in an Old Fashioned at one of the best whiskey bars in the city, the Old Gold. There are numerous restaurants, bars, and coffee shops within walking distance of our home. Our favorites spots within a short walking distance include Stacks for a steaming cup of coffee amongst floor to ceiling books,  and the bright and fresh Mediterranean wraps at Spitz.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-18136463/original/76cf9bf3-4405-476a-a1c2-c454bc45947a.jpeg',11875534,13,'45.56284','-122.68937',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,210.00,4,60,186,4.97,18136463),(814,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18191700','ON Alberta Street: Private Loft w/ Rooftop!','OMG, you guys. This loft--literally located ON Alberta Street--has everything you could possibly need to have the best trip ever to Portland. Did I say it\'s located ON Alberta? It seriously is. You can walk out the door to multiple eating, drinking and exploring adventures. Plus there\'s a rooftop deck with views of Mount Saint Helens, too!','Vernon is one of Portland\'s hip neighborhoods that is located in close proximity to the Alberta Commercial Corridor, with restaurants, bars, coffee shops, theaters and awesome food carts! All you have to do is step outside this apartment and you are STEPS to some of Portland’s best dining, drinking and shopping!<br /><br />DRIVE TIMES TO LOCAL DESTINATIONS:<br />* Hawthorne: 15 minutes<br />* Division: 20 minutes<br />* Downtown: 10 minutes<br />* 23rd street: 13 minutes<br />* Sauvie Island: 34 minutes<br />* Wine Country: 43 minutes','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/407c44b0-f1b7-4418-941b-c8890f7eb2e1.jpg',109509841,14,'45.55918884277344','-122.65302276611328',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,103.00,30,1000,353,4.84,18191700),(815,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18238378','Spacious one bedroom suite next to Grant Park','This  900 square-foot suite is located in NE Portland, near the Hollywood District and next to Grant Park, with easy access to PDX.  <br /><br />The basement suite  has bath (walk-in shower), private bedroom, (plush queen bed),  office space,  microwave, fridge, utensils, toaster,  Keurig coffee maker, and table for two.  Relax in the separate living room, with a  large screen TV, recliner and sofa bed (single) (A single rollaway is available as well. )Secure free wifi too.','The Grant Park neighborhood is very walkable (scores 65 and 95 on bikeability). It is an older neighborhood with a number of styles of homes, from old English, to Tudors to old Portland. And, you will see a few newer homes interspersed. Large oak and maple trees line most streets and offer a canopy when walking. <br /><br />We are a 19 minute walk from the MAX (light rail) Blue Line, the MAX Green Line and the MAX Red Line at the Hollywood/NE 42nd Ave TC MAX Station stop.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a7e2d791-9e18-4ad3-92cb-7128339a84d5.jpg',1176871,33,'45.54172','-122.629',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,101.00,30,1125,220,4.95,18238378),(816,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18256025','Cozy, Convenient Sellwood Retreat','Beautiful, recently renovated, 2 bedroom apartment conveniently located in Sellwood. Walking distance to multiple coffee shops, restaurants, pubs, bus routes, Springwater hiking/biking trail, Oaks Bottom wildlife refuge, Sellwood library, Moreland theater, 2 grocery stores, Sellwood park and Oaks Park (amusment park and skating rink). A short hop to downtown Portland, OHSU and many other Portland attractions.   People from all backgrounds are welcome in our home.','Sellwood has something for everyone!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/70dfc33d-611b-4a57-b440-a01e927d2783.jpg',20395786,20,'45.47005','-122.65784',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,110.00,2,1125,372,4.97,18256025),(817,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18294608','Cozy Spa Sanctuary w/ Soaking Tub','Steps from shopping & dining on Division, we are the perfect home base for all your PDX adventures. We offer a cozy bedroom with comfy queen bed, washer/dryer, full gourmet kitchen, patio and Euro-style bathroom with rainfall shower head and clawfoot soaking tub. In the common area, you\'ll find an easily convertible queen sofa bed and a desk space with an iPad. TVs in both the bedroom and common area are equipped with Roku for streaming Netflix, Hulu, HBOMax and more. We can\'t wait to host you!<br /><br />Our garden apartment was lovingly crafted and furnished with guests in mind. We enjoy providing a welcoming space for travelers from all over the world and look forward to hosting you, too!<br /><br />You\'ll access the apartment via your private entrance equipped with a keyless lock for easy ins and outs. You\'ll notice your very own patio space just outside the entrance and once inside, you\'ll find the gourmet kitchen with all new appliances including a full-size fridge/freezer, gas r','Our neighborhood is incredibly walkable and right in the heart of SE PDX. Located just north of Division on a quiet, residential street, our house is perfectly positioned for your Portland explorations. With so many options for dining, coffee and shopping nearby, you may never want to leave the neighborhood; but if you do, getting around is super easy via the nearby transit stops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-18294608/original/704a1817-7470-47d6-b7e0-c16a70a0daea.jpeg',126524556,8,'45.507','-122.63032',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,139.00,2,1125,331,4.99,18294608),(818,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18303786','5+ bed Artsy Bungalow Inner SE Portland','Portland Flair - a great option for large families or groups.  This 2-story, artsy bungalow in hip SE PDX can comfortably sleep 4-10 people:  three bedrooms upstairs and  2 sofas in the common area.  Seated on a dead-end street, and with a driveway that can fit 2 of your cars, our home is not the average Airbnb in Portland. The bungalow has a wrap-around porch with a hammock, porch swing, back-deck with gas BBQ and a yard that wraps around 3 sides of the home.','We are located on a dead end street (safe and relatively quiet) in SE portland - with a Large grocery store 2 blocks away, a Trader Joe\'s, nail salon and Starbucks 4 blocks away.  Creston park with a playground, outdoor pool and lots of trees is only 2 blocks away. For the hip part of SE you will find hotspots on Division St (13 blocks away) and Hawthorne St (23 blocks) with lots of restaurants, boutiques, bars, food trucks, cinema, and talented buskers.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTgzMDM3ODY%3D/original/007bdade-cf87-45cd-81a2-29a112ec266b.jpeg',15063380,67,'45.4949','-122.61896',1,10,1.50,3.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,11,4.82,18303786),(819,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18308578','Urban Oasis in Irvington/Walk to Convention Center','Come enjoy the entire second floor master suite. Large, private 558\' Square-foot apartment sized room with high vaulted ceilings, beautiful local wood work, master bathroom tiled with travertine marble, jacuzzi and walk-in shower. Super convenient inner city location, by the Moda Center, offers easy access to downtown Portland, close in to Hip streets such as; North Mississippi, Alberta Arts District, North Williams and Vancouver Streets. This is a very bike and walk friendly part of Portland.','Location..Location..Location! <br />Located in close in NE Portland in the Historic Irvington Neighborhood. <br />~You are walking distance to the Moda Center, a block away from public transportation, minutes away from downtown. <br />~Popular North Mississippi area, North Williams and Vancouver streets, and the Alberta Arts District. All are a quick scoot away.<br />~Look forward to being surrounded by a vibrant restaurant culture, live music options and independent retailers.<br />~New Seasons is 10 blocks away and a locally owned wonderful grocery store. High quality food.<br />~Irving Park is 6 blocks away, wonderful trails, playgrounds, basketball and tennis courts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/712c6696-de39-489d-816f-1f737a78a3b7.jpg',63559052,26,'45.54017','-122.66036',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,200,122,4.99,18308578),(820,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18309571','The Nest/Portland.Peaceful.Fun','The Nest is situated on the second and third floors of this charming Old Portland home. The house is central to everything Eastside, boasting a walk score of 94! Belmont & Hawthorne have incredible eateries, bars and shopping only a few steps away. It is also very close to the heart of the Division, Stark, SE 28th & Burnside commercial districts. It\'s a 5 minute walk to Laurelhurst Park, voted the most beautiful park on the west coast, & only 2 miles from downtown, The Pearl and Mt. Tabor Park.','We are located in the Sunnyside neighborhood, sometimes referred to as the Hawthorne District. The House is located between SE Belmont St & Hawthorne Boulevard: Two of the hippest streets in the city. If you enjoy craft beer, wine, spirits, Cannabis, and food, this is the perfect location. SE Stark, SE 28th, E Burnside, and SE Division are easy walks from the Nest.<br /><br />Oh, and don\'t miss Laurelhurst Park, only a 5 minute walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/58a8ab76-977d-4681-9a33-297ab1fb3c63.jpg',121923954,16,'45.51659','-122.63304',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,56.00,1,30,449,4.94,18309571),(821,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18333679','Hawthorne Division Food Drink Tabor Wonderland','Relaxed + modern one bedroom basement apartment, fully separate from upstairs house. Comfortable for the urban dweller that would rather stay in a quaint neighborhood than downtown hotel, it\'s a great home-base for the traveller curious to explore Portland-- especially for the food lover! Located in quintessential Hawthorne/Mt. Tabor neighborhood. Just blocks from Mt. Tabor Park, restaurants, bars and bus lines. 15 minutes from airport. Naturally cool during summers heat and warm in the winter.','This apartment is the perfect launch pad for exploring Portland, especially Southeast. It is within walking distance of the Hawthorne, Belmont, Division neighborhoods and Mt. Tabor Park. <br /><br />Around the corner: Albina Press Coffee, Porque No? Tacos, Tabor Bread and Sapphire Hotel Bar.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/53e03c27-f60d-466b-9057-8f950cee3a8d.jpg',9931242,15,'45.51142','-122.60809',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,59.00,2,100,445,4.80,18333679),(822,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18357744','Spacious 3 Bedroom Apt Central Eastside Portland!','This is our mid century modern 3 bedroom apartment at the roots of Pine Manor. Recently remodeled clean and spacious! A Cozy, Private, and Quiet Space with a Modern tribal flare. Perfectly located in inner Southeast nearby Moda and Convention Center. Food carts and Voodoo Doughnut close by! Perfect for business trips, visiting family, catching a show or a place to land when relocating and looking for a new home in Portland Oregon. Family and pet friendly. We love Dogs! Dog Park nearby!','This neighborhood is an \"architecturally rich mix of compatible early 20th century styles\", notable for their \"continuity of scale, setback, orientation, and materials.\" Architectural styles represented include bungalow, craftsman, American Foursquare, Mission, Tudor, and Colonial Revival.<br /><br />Three bridges connect Buckman to neighborhoods in Southwest Portland across the Willamette: the Old Town Chinatown neighborhood via the Burnside Bridge, and Downtown Portland via the Morrison and Hawthorne Bridges.<br /><br />You can cross the Burnside Bridge on weekends into an open-air marketplace which features 250+ booths of handmade goods, artisanal cheeses, and local produce, sold by local Pacific Northwest artisans.<br /><br />The neighborhood also includes Lone Fir Cemetery with its many unmarked graves (1855), Colonel Summers Park, where community events and picnics are aplenty (1921), Buckman Community Garden (1980), and much of the Vera Katz Eastbank Esplanade (opened 2001).<br ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-18357744/original/188ad738-7ba0-47a0-a11d-9dc510ebd488.jpeg',103138695,32,'45.52006','-122.65075',1,6,1.00,3.00,3.00,112.00,2,120,149,4.74,18357744),(823,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18375485','Valentina\'s Little Sister','City view of Portland lighting up like a jewel at night...and on the other side, expansive green Hillside Park view. Beautifully crafted, modern one bedroom (within bones of 1926 Mediterranean family home named \"Valentina\") has ALL.  Two decks! Two levels! Hand-blown glass fixtures! Two big TVs! Custom floors! Every essential + more! Walking distance to NW 23rd Avenue shops/cafes and peace/serenity of Forest Park. Make your visit to Portland with this incomparable location in the NW hills!','Tasha Miller, a famed Portland singer (jazz/blues/soul/R&B), lives in Valentina with her family. Catch one of her shows and sleep under the same roof!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-18375485/original/e03f5bea-6838-4c44-8be2-8c6a1e1fefae.jpeg',127253367,79,'45.52675','-122.70887',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,3,1125,225,4.96,18375485),(824,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18379258','Historic Jacobberger House  Downtown Portland','This spacious 3000 sq foot hillside paradise awaits you as you discover the abundance of old world charm and architecture. This Stunning Craftsman is perched on the hill just steps to downtown Portland with stunning city and mountain views. Built in 1904 by Joseph Jacobberger this is a restored beautiful classic home.<br />This home makes an ideal \"no car needed location”.<br />All bedrooms provide exceptional views of the city and Mountains. All rooms passed safety Inspection and are  B&B Permit -LU-','Our Neighborhood<br /><br />Located in a quiet neighborhood, just blocks to downtown. Imagine being above it all with stunning city, mountain views and patio space to enjoy the perspective from the comforts of this spacious home. You’ll have a very special experience to remember here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-18379258/original/9b30a83d-75fd-454c-8ac9-0f79806fee76.jpeg',12846561,54,'45.50832','-122.68596',1,4,1.50,4.00,5.00,508.00,3,122,14,5.00,18379258),(825,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18395206','Exceptional East Moreland Guesthouse/ Reed College','We take Covid 19 safety standards seriously!  <br /><br />Artfully decorated street-level garden apartment in a quiet, residential neighborhood lined with 100 year old trees.  15 minute walk to Reed College and nearby hiking/cycling trails. Private garden patio, gas \'woodstove\' in the living room- lots of ambiance and comfort. Fully equipped kitchen. Enjoy the complimentary HBO/ Netflix.<br />We use nontoxic cleaning materials.  #superhost','Eastmoreland is a quiet,  100 year old tree lined neighborhood just a 15 minute walk to Reed College. We\'re close to several large parks for walking/hiking as well, e.g., The Rhododendron Garden and the 40 mile Spring Water Corridor and the Westmoreland Park (for picnics and has a salmon spring). Eastmoreland neighborhood borders the (public) Eastmoreland Golf Course and is close to the (private) Waverly Golf Club. We\'re in walking distance between the restaurant-rich Sellwood and Woodstock neighborhoods.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7cdfb1b7-5823-4159-8567-cede7bb14633.jpg',17292270,5,'45.4707','-122.6241',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,126.00,3,29,233,4.98,18395206),(826,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18410518','Victorian Parlor Room. Permit# 24ASTR-PER-00491','Gorgeous bedroom for one guest (no visitors), with shared bathroom in a beautifully restored Victorian home in SE Buckman neighborhood. On the edge of the Central Eastside Industrial area- close to downtown and many of Portland\'s best restaurants and bars. 1 mile from Convention Center. Great for business travelers. Please note, there is no kitchen access, but you do have an electric kettle, microwave and a mini fridge in the room.','On the edge of the SE Industrial neighborhood, we are just blocks from some of the best venues, cafes, bars and restaurants. 1.5 miles to downtown (Portland Saturday Market, Chinese Gardens, Shanghai Tunnels, Voodoo Donuts....); 1 mile from the Convention Center.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a989727a-c3ab-40e9-b37d-66084ddcce2c.jpg',56983408,32,'45.52198','-122.65332',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,2,14,319,4.96,18410518),(827,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18412868','Tiny, Serene Art Filled Treehouse','This tiny treehouse is in the apple tree in my lush backyard & is offered as if inflation didn\'t happen<br />EASY climb up to the tiny deck. Cozy & safe. Electricity, WiFi,  windows, doors, 2 tiny decks for merging into the tree. It’s small, but perfect for 1 or 2 (smaller types) to stretch out & have a peaceful sleep on comfy thick pads. Mini breakfast included. In S. Tabor near Mt. Tabor, Portlandish Areas, transport ect. Unique Listing! PLEASE READ ENTIRE DESCRIPTION BEFORE REQUESTING to Book  :-)','This neighborhood is in the heart of artsy SE, quiet and safe. This is very tree filled...like all of Portland...duh!, but South Tabor is great, because it is really close to beautiful Mt. Tabor, where you can go and hike in a forest. It\'s very close to public transportation, grocery and restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ccfcf8bd-c082-48d9-9322-9106968ed6a1.jpg',127584615,37,'45.49798','-122.58429',2,2,0.00,1.00,1.00,28.00,1,3,442,4.89,18412868),(828,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18433339','Bright, Comfy Division / Hawthorne Basement Studio','Private, spacious (> 500 sf) studio in daylight basement. Newly remodeled in 2017. The perfect home base for exploring southeast Portland!<br /><br />Walk to dozens of great restaurants, food carts, bars, coffee shops, thrift stores, cannabis dispensaries, and more on SE Division St and SE Hawthorne Blvd.','We live on a quiet street, but just a few blocks from one of Portland\'s hottest food scenes. Portland is a great food town, and SE Division is one of the best destinations, with pizza, Thai, tacos, Indian, sushi, Italian, Northwest cuisine and more.<br /><br />Divison, Hawthorne, and Belmont have tons of cool vintage stores, cute boutiques, and unique shops.<br /><br />Mt. Tabor Park, a 190-acre forested park on an extinct volcano is only a mile away. It has miles of hiking trails, and excellent views of the city from the top. A perfect place to jog, stroll, or take the kids for an adventure. We also have a playground less than a block away at Richmond Elementary School.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ad9fd61c-d6ab-42aa-8e47-170521a8e6f5.jpg',53953234,8,'45.50639','-122.62028',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,2,28,315,4.96,18433339),(829,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18434478','Charming FoPo Retreat, Self Check-in!','Welcome to my humble abode! It\'s been recently updated and squeaky clean. Please enjoy an entire floor of my home to yourselves. Come and go as you please with keypad access. I am happy to give you privacy or get more involved by giving you recommendations and advice on visiting our lovely city. If you have concerns or accommodation questions, please reach out, I usually respond within an hour.','A quiet and cozy residential pocket in the Foster-Powell (locals call it Fo-Po) neighborhood of Portland. Foster Street to the south has the coffee shops, antique stores, and bars you\'re looking for, and is within walking distance of the house! Even closer, Kern Park is right across the street, complete with a quaint playground and off-leash park surrounded by large (blossoming in the spring) trees. Walk south and explore the famous Portland Mercado or discover the large selection of popular food carts nearby.<br /><br />One mile north, you\'ll reach Mt Tabor Park. Summiting this volcanic landform gives you a great view of downtown Portland, spectacular at sunset. Other tourism hot spots, such as Division Street and Hawthorne Boulevard, are a 5-10 minute drive away. <br /><br />We are a 15 minute drive to Downtown Portland and less than 10 miles from PDX Airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/553ea9dc-7c38-4dd8-9c4a-b7276d6e020f.jpg',127777784,36,'45.49304','-122.59412',2,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,31,129,4.88,18434478),(830,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18447314','Beautifully Renovated 1910 Craftsman','This beautiful house is filled with light and features a bathroom with heated marble floors and a refinished clawfoot tub and shower. The guest room has a brand new full sized bed. The main bedroom has a brand new king sized bed. Located between Hawthorne and Division avenues the house is in walking distance to the city\'s best restaurants. Please note there is a basement apartment with a separate entrance in the back of the house. The apartment might be occupied during your stay.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b49b8374-62f0-4836-9d23-19ef1a7109de.jpg',77382200,8,'45.50648','-122.62491',1,3,1.00,2.00,2.00,185.00,30,50,15,4.93,18447314),(831,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18449084','Best Location in Portland! THE View','This quiet,cozy 1bd apartment offers so much to do in a one mile area. Walking distance from SouthWest Waterfront, Portland\'s Max,StreetCar,TriMet all coverge here at Tillikum Bridge. Dont pass up this gem,it won\'t last long.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ebc8923b-153d-4086-b6c8-947be8fbf686.jpg',57187286,22,'45.50473','-122.67737',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,0,1.00,18449084),(832,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18464402','St. Johns neighborhood, privacy and comfort','We are two blocks from downtown St. Johns, off the busy street, and a quick walk to restaurants and boutiques. The University of Portland is 2 miles away. Our home is a gold-certified back-yard habitat with native songbirds & plants. The patio is private, peaceful, and welcoming for guests. Along with a private bedroom and bathroom, guests have access to a shared kitchen and living room with TV.','St. Johns has several coffee shops and a variety of restaurants including, Thai, Mexican, Vegan, and Pizza among others. All are within a short walk. The neighborhood also hosts two movie theaters, a Farmers Market on Saturdays, and numerous boutiques. This is a up-and-coming neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/35392c31-9457-48f1-90db-98ff8ff6fa2c.jpg',48023979,58,'45.59427','-122.75673',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,1,30,156,4.88,18464402),(833,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18502484','Private Duplex, Fast Internet, Walk To It All','As longtime AirBnB users, we are happy to now be hosts! Our home is a charming, quiet 2 bedroom/1 Bath located in the heart of bustling Hawthorne, Belmont and Division neighborhoods. Walk or bike in any direction to some of the best restaurants, food carts, coffee shops and breweries Portland has to offer. Under 2 miles from the center of downtown (and Voodoo Donuts).<br /><br />City of Portland short-term rental permit number available upon request (AirBnB won\'t allow us to display it)','We are nestled in the middle of SE Portland\'s most vibrant neighborhoods - Belmont, Hawthorne and Division. There is an near endless variety of restaurant, coffee shops, breweries, food carts and bars in a one mile radius. Downtown is a few short miles and access to freeways is very close by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cec1290f-d280-4ec8-b8eb-44a1b9e08479.jpg',2322279,32,'45.51369','-122.64682',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,175.00,1,28,387,4.92,18502484),(834,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18507317','/// Brand new studio / on MAX line to airport','You\'ll feel right at home in our gorgeous, newly renovated, bright and cozy studio with private bathroom and kitchenette.  Our home is close to the 60th Avenue MAX light rail station, several bus lines, bike paths, and grocery stores. You’ll love our place because of the comfy queen sized bed and easy access to any part of town by rail, bus, bike, or car. We are two blocks away from a nice brewery and food cart pod. Our place is great for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers alike!','There are cafes, bars/restaurants, grocery stores, and parks (including a golf course) within walking distance. Rose City Park is an excellent location for access to the city or to set up a home base with easy access to the beautiful hiking trails and wilderness areas surrounding Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-18507317/original/d3d3feed-0dc2-4b3c-9648-44dac5ab186e.jpg',14513978,11,'45.53505','-122.59897',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,63.00,2,31,271,4.94,18507317),(835,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18565183','Artistic, Quiet, Comfortable Portland home.','Five minutes from the University of Portland. Near downtown Pearl District, Mississippi Avenue and Alberta area where there are lots of cafes, restaurants and cute unique retail stores. Lots of street parking near the house. Downstairs has a gas fireplace, 1/2 bath, kitchen & deck. Good heating/AC. Your private room and bathroom are upstairs.  With the coronavirus I provide hand sanitizer, Lysol and clean thoroughly. Excellent Wi-FI, USB ports &  laptop desk.','Quiet and safe neighborhood with mostly young families or people who have lived in the area for 20 years. Very close to the house are Columbia Park and Willamette street where lots of people walk, bicycle, and run. Close to Portland University as well. Nice community feeling.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-18565183/original/220cf756-5647-4d55-9532-82df5dd8b792.jpeg',128887124,57,'45.5794','-122.71786',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,30,60,91,4.99,18565183),(836,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18565742','Glamorous Suite w/Round Bed in SE','Glamorous remodeled Victorian home in the popular Southeast neighborhood. Comfortably fits 2, private living room, bedroom and bathroom the only shared space is the entry way. Within walking distance of the Hawthorne food carts, shops and restaurants including Pok Pok, Salt and Straw, Pine State Biscuits, the list goes on!! More photos coming soon!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9ca2ef33-3b23-48b2-aa7f-a2fdde7176fe.jpg',10385699,25,'45.50453','-122.65431',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,155.00,2,1125,193,4.94,18565742),(837,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18576618','ZEN HAUS. An inner SE Hawthorne/Division Studio.','LOCATION and COMFORT.  Zen Haus is an easy walk to the best shops, pubs, restaurants and amenities on Hawthorne and Division\'s \"restaurant row.\"  This detached, self-contained studio is thoughtfully designed and furnished to satisfy your desire for comfort, convenience, calm and glorious slumber.  Designed to accommodate both the holiday or business traveler, find your zen in Zen Haus.','ZEN HAUS is located in a quiet residential street midway between the concentrated business districts of SE Hawthorne Blvd. and SE Division Street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9de14f72-90c1-4312-bef5-877f4ed817e4.jpg',30883612,8,'45.50801','-122.62804',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,85.00,1,100,669,4.98,18576618),(838,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18586781','Close-in two bedroom apartment','Enjoy a stylish experience at this centrally-located two bedroom apartment.  This recently renovated upstairs apartment in a 1910 Craftsman home is located one mile from downtown Portland, within walking distance of OHSU, the tram, John\'s Landing, on several bus lines with easy freeway access.  Walking distances to several cafes and restaurants, the Willamette river trail, yet backing up to a lush green.<br /><br />Note:  The owners live downstairs with their friendly lab, but use a separate entrance.','Urban neighborhood, yet property backs up to a green space.  Easy bus access to downtown (1 mile to PSU), walking distance to OHSU (20 minutes), tram (20 minutes) & John\'s Landing (5 minutes).  Cafes and restuarants within 5-10 minute walk.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-18586781/original/e3f7b102-ef52-4958-9bcd-7b1d5fc259b2.jpeg',7187155,22,'45.489922592741166','-122.67950493449887',1,3,1.00,2.00,2.00,120.00,30,365,2,5.00,18586781),(839,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18603330','Mid-Mod Prescott Pad','Spacious, 600sqft, private basement studio with kitchenette and bath. Driveway parking, adjacent shared laundry. Close to the airport, on major bus lines. Host is attentive and responsive. Meticulous attention to detail means you will want for nothing during your stay. Enjoy luxurious amenities and a spotless, comfortable space.','About 10 minutes from the airport, my neighborhood is surprisingly quiet, considering my location on a busy street and bus line.<br />There is a great deli 2 short blocks away; they offer coffee, ice cream, salads, soups, sandwiches, pastries, beer, wine and sundries.  There\'s a wonderful old style café about 10 short blocks away; they are open for breakfast and lunch.  Grocery stores are nearby, as is a great old movie theater, park space, and good restaurants/bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1c16eaf3-3c0a-4f5f-91cc-bdb84a58c589.jpg',17022261,21,'45.55624','-122.58977',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,94.00,2,1125,171,4.95,18603330),(840,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18615313','Cool Green-built Modern Guest House near Alberta','A stylish and comfy place to stay. Modern and upcycled finishes, classic style. Self-check in. <br /><br />Located in fun Sabin neighborhood between NE Fremont and Alberta streets, everything you need is easy to reach: shops, restaurants, music venues, parks and groceries. You are minutes to Portland International Airport or downtown Portland. About an hour to the beach or mountains.<br /><br />Come relax in a clean and comfy home after enjoying the city,  nearby natural wonders or visiting family.','We are in the Sabin neighborhood just a few blocks north of Irvington and a few blocks south of Alberta Street. We are also nearby to North Williams where you can find a lot of great restaurants and cute shops. Our neighborhood is safe and quiet and diverse.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/df4b0439-4fe7-4bb8-aa71-714775e55bd6.jpg',2783158,6,'45.55201','-122.65471',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,5,1125,174,4.98,18615313),(841,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18618551','Relaxing retreat in sweet bungalow','Relax in retreat-like space with giant Doug firs/Cedars in backyard and organic garden in front, while still 5 mins from all city activity.<br /><br />Hardwood floors, high ceilings, fireplace, hot tub, outdoor shower, awesome location.<br /><br />One room has double bed, Casper mattress, two big windows, dresser, vanity, closet. Other has queen pullout couch w large windows & roku. Large couch in living room w/door.<br /><br />Easy public transportation. Good for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, small groups.','Roseway is awesome!<br /><br />5 mins to Alberta Arts District. 5-7 mins to airport. Easy access to Columbia River Gorge and highways to Mt Hood, Hood River, and winery adventures.<br /><br />We are close to amazing restaurants like Pizzeria Ottos, Kainos Coffee, Thai Seasons, lots of Pho shops, and BTU. Unicorn Burger food cart is 2 blocks away. Safeway and Walgreens are 4 blocks away for all your needs.<br /><br />And dont miss the baklava and growler pours at Ira\'s deli!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4183cee9-ba43-4352-ac35-66f12941cc04.jpg',2576419,39,'45.55347','-122.58692',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,182.00,30,1125,17,4.76,18618551),(842,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18618775','Fully Private Suite w. a Superhost +Alberta Arts!','...and did I mention: adorable?<br />A garden entrance brings you into your own PRIVATE, SEPARATE space within my cozy, colorful and bright Concordia/Alberta Arts home! All for you: bedroom, full bath & garden-facing breakfast room fully equipped for self-catering. The house is an easy walk to many NE Portland highlights that are also a take-out paradise, including: the Kennedy School, restaurants at Killingsworth/30th, and *amazing* Alberta Street. 10 min from Portland Int\'l Airport!','The house is just a block and a half from the fabulous Kennedy School, three blocks from the University of Oregon Portland campus,  and is a quick walk to the heart of unique, lively and very cool Alberta Street and the Alberta Arts neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/57edb217-8e22-47cc-badd-953a6bb151bb.jpg',129344634,1,'45.56721','-122.63102',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,71.00,1,14,340,4.91,18618775),(843,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18628799','Beautiful Arbor Lodge','Experience Portland in a beautifully furnished,  centrally located, bright and light 2 bedrooms 1 bath home in the Arbor Lodge neighborhood.<br /><br />***Please note: Because of the laws in Portland we are bound to 30 day minimum rentals only. This property is actually available INDEFINITELY from the AVAILABLE date for reservations. If your stay is longer than 30 days, we CAN accommodate you. Please sent me a request for your requested dates.','Arbor Lodge is the gem of North Portland. Beautiful and residential with 2 spacious, green parks. The house has a walking score of 85, and a bike score of 100. The location is within walkable distance to public transportation, both the Max Light Rail line, and the bus. New Seasons, Green Zebra, and Fred Meyer are all in close distance. Neighboring the communities include Alberta Arts, Kenton, Dekum Triangle and St. Johns. Its a quick drive or train ride to downtown, East Portland or Vancouver.<br /><br />The entire house, back yard, back deck, front porch and front yard are exclusively yours during your stay.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/770f335a-37ad-466f-89bc-d46ce63d24e8.jpg',36909902,51,'45.57568','-122.68879',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,99.00,30,1125,2,4.50,18628799),(844,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18630078','★ Walk to Belmont - 2-bed/1-bath - Walk Score: 95!','This home--designed by two top architects--is as dreamy as they come; you\'ll never want to leave, we guarantee it. With its Walk Score of 95, fully stocked kitchen, high-end beds, flat-screen televisions and brand new central air conditioning (Portland gets hot now, y\'all!), this home has all the comforts of a hotel plus more. Everything you could need is just steps from the door, and we encourage our guests to leave the car at home and bring comfy shoes: Portland is calling!','The Buckman neighborhood is one of Portland\'s most popular neighborhoods due to its plethora of cafes, restaurants, pubs and shops, just a stone\'s throw away. Buckman\'s Belmont & Hawthorne District is one of the most unique, and most sought-after areas in Southeast Portland. The area is known for its wonderful restored old Portland homes, liberal residents, and fun and funky feel. The street is lined with unique restaurants and shops, and has a definite Portland-local flair.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/47304a05-61f2-4125-945f-3e4f8161c241.jpg',129428891,32,'45.51669','-122.64118',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,109.00,30,1125,371,4.89,18630078),(845,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18630797','A modern stunner- steps to Belmont! Walk Score 95!','This home--designed by two top architects--is as dreamy as they come; you\'ll never want to leave, we guarantee it. With its Walk Score of 95, fully stocked kitchen, high-end beds, flat-screen televisions and brand new central air conditioning (Portland gets hot now, y\'all!), this home has all the comforts of a hotel plus more. Everything you could need is just steps from the door, and we encourage our guests to leave the car at home and bring comfy shoes: Portland is calling!','The Buckman neighborhood is one of Portland\'s most popular neighborhoods due to its plethora of cafes, restaurants, pubs and shops, just a stone\'s throw away. Buckman\'s Belmont & Hawthorne District is one of the most unique, and most sought-after areas in Southeast Portland. The area is known for its wonderful restored old Portland homes, liberal residents, and fun and funky feel. The street is lined with unique restaurants and shops, and has a definite Portland-local flair.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/14d81f51-5585-44ed-b93e-7a41ed5f243a.jpg',129435693,32,'45.51641','-122.6421',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,119.00,30,1125,344,4.92,18630797),(846,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18635638','Rose Garden Guest Suite w/ Private Entrance','A private modern, yet cozy guest suite with all the luxuries of home. Includes your own patio and view of a lovely Rose garden and Fig tree. Easy access from the airport, to downtown, to Mt. Hood, to Columbia Gorge, etc. Located on a quiet cul de sac next to Glendoveer golf course and it\'s lovely 2 mile nature trail.','Near Glendoveer Golf Course which has a beautiful hiking trail around it. It\'s a quiet neighborhood but fairly close to the airport, downtown and the gorge.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fbd4429e-3fa2-4f37-84e8-e2ab11fdb00b.jpg',129473003,63,'45.53223','-122.52872',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,55.00,2,14,425,4.91,18635638),(847,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18636900','Modern Luxury Apartment - Prize City Location!','Welcome to your Portland escape! 🌟 Our **Beautiful Modern Apartment** has a private entrance, comfy queen bed, and sofa bed for up to 4 guests! 🛏️📺 Chill with Netflix, Hulu, and more, or cook up a feast in our fully equipped kitchen. 🍳🎨 Stylish decor, great location near parks, shops, and food. We’re experienced Superhosts with 99% five-star reviews! ⭐️✨ Book now for a stay as amazing as Portland itself! 🚀🌟','Single-family homes with kids, pets, and a nearby park. Park in front of the apartment and leave your car for your stay. Safe and quiet family-oriented neighborhood close to all of Portland\'s best art districts, parks, restaurants, shops, and attractions. Rent nearby bikes, play in the park, stroll nearby art districts, and see what makes Portland the Jewel of the Pacific Northwest.<br /><br />› Quiet residential neighborhood.<br />› Wide streets and sidewalks.<br />› Easy and free street parking with no permits or meters.<br />› Large, mature trees and blooming flowers year-round.<br />› Families with kids of all ages walking dogs often.<br />› Unique mix of historical and modern homes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-18636900/original/d3ffae70-7632-48d7-a8d2-88025d71d338.jpeg',17733541,6,'45.55101013183594','-122.6549301147461',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,75.00,2,14,375,4.96,18636900),(848,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18653995','Lille Hus: Sweet backyard house in great location','Experience Portland like a local in one of the best locations. Comfortable, compact second story house with many stylish details.','We are located \"close in\" to downtown in Southeast Portland between Division and Clinton Streets where you will get a good taste of what makes Portland so \"weird\" and special. Apartment is two blocks from excellent local supermarket, a natural food co/op, and walking or biking distance to lots of unique shops, bars, and award wining restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/79ff7204-fc6d-4744-81ef-1f28dd9d40fa.jpg',1627089,25,'45.50479','-122.65007',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,95.00,14,1125,60,4.87,18653995),(849,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18672469','Newly Remodeled (Jan 2024) Open & Spacious Studio','Be one of the first guests to experience our newly remodeled (Jan 2024), open, and spacious (1,000 sq.ft+) basement studio with a private entrance.  Feel restful with your 2 comfy king beds. Feel productive using your gigabit fiber optic internet. Feel joyful experiencing your hi-fi entertainment system. Feel healthy enjoying home-cooked food from your kitchen. Feel peaceful strolling along our neighborhood\'s ridge walk. Feel clean with your updated bathroom and full-size laundry machines!','Roseway is a quiet and friendly neighborhood just a short walk from Rose City Golf Course and two large parks, Wellington and Glenhaven, including sports fields, picnic areas, a skate park, and lighted pathways for walkers, joggers, and bikers.  <br /><br />The historical and renovated Roseway Theatre is a perfect date night spot, located on Sandy Boulevard, also home to many coffee shops, restaurants, and stores.<br /><br />Safeway (open until 1:30 am) and Walgreens are also within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTg2NzI0Njk%3D/original/46f49210-494b-4250-917b-de26e54c6c76.jpeg',2936952,39,'45.543','-122.58934',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,99.00,2,31,79,4.92,18672469),(850,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18720958','Modern Studio Apt in Laurelhurst, Near Downtown','Located in the historic Laurelhurst neighborhood and minutes from downtown, our beautiful studio apartment (more like a 1 bedroom; there\'s a separate sleeping area) has everything you need to enjoy everything Portland has to offer. Easy walking distance to restaurants, bars, transportation, and Providence Portland Hospital. We embrace and celebrate diversity and we look forward to hosting other like-minded guests!','Laurelhurst is a beautiful well-established (most houses are from the 1910s and  1920s) neighborhood close to everything Portland has to offer. We have gorgeous tree-lined streets perfect for evening strolls, the 26-acre Laurelhurst park (which boasts ball fields, a small lake, playground, and picnic areas), shops, restaurants, bars, etc.; everything you need is within easy walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fcaf2304-a60f-4e53-b939-29ff6ef39a7c.jpg',4880727,23,'45.53041','-122.62989',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,87.00,2,4,239,4.98,18720958),(851,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18770616','Alberta Nest: Your Home Away From Home','Relax in our comfortable Alberta Nest guest house. The guest house is modern, bright and airy with one-bedroom. You will enjoy the high ceilings, French doors & skylights. It is a great home base for business or pleasure. We are steps away from the amazing Alberta Arts neighborhood with many cafes, breweries, restaurants, coffee shops, bike shops, galleries & boutiques. All are welcome at our guest house. LGBTQ+ friendly.','Amazing location! We are in the heart of the Alberta Arts District in Portland. The neighborhood centers on Alberta Street, and stretches from approximately MLK Jr. Blvd to 33rd Ave in the Northeast section of the city. We are steps away from many cafes, breweries, restaurants, coffee shops, bike shops, galleries & boutiques. One block from Salt & Straw Ice Cream & Proud Mary restaurant!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8b685b2f-7117-4632-a302-f1fac7cfbed7.jpg',21270012,29,'45.55934','-122.64532',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,82.00,1,24,430,5.00,18770616),(852,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18790208','Charming Home in Inner Southeast Portland','Sit back in a leather Eames chair for a moment of reading enveloped in the charming decor and mid-century furnishings of this restful home. Cook breakfast in a warm kitchen with gray-washed floors and dine at an umbrellaed table on the patio.<br /><br />The single two-bedroom house has a fenced backyard with grass and flowers. Both bedrooms are on the main floor.  There are NO shared spaces.  You have a private parking space in the driveway.','The house is set in a low-key residential area of Southeast Portland, one block from the trendy restaurants, cafes, and shops along SE Belmont Street. Take a stroll to Mt Tabor Park and walk along the leafy footpaths while admiring scenic views.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ba6ea47a-707b-46df-b7b0-2a37cab6cf18.jpg',2399422,16,'45.51619','-122.61817',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,170.00,1,1125,429,4.94,18790208),(853,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18803962','Modern Private Guesthouse in Historic Kenton','Private, modern guesthouse in the Historic Kenton neighborhood in North Portland. Walk 1/2 a block to Kenton Park and a few blocks to the Kenton business district with great shops and restaurants. The apartment offers light and bright interior with touches of Scandinavian design. Open floor plan from kitchen to living room. One bedroom, one bath, plus a full size sleeper couch. Free street parking in front. Do not park in the driveway please. 15-20 min to downtown.','The apartment is half a block from Kenton Park and a few blocks from the Kenton business district, which hosts many great restaurants and shops. There’s also easy access to the freeway and public transit. Walking distance to the Max train station for easy access to downtown and other parts of the city. The apartment is also close to the Adidas campus, Portland Expo Center, Delta Park,  and Portland International Raceway for folks coming into town for events at any of these locations.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/061f433d-2772-47fb-8e31-507502a5708e.jpg',31862405,55,'45.584251403808594','-122.69332885742188',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,72.00,2,15,299,4.94,18803962),(854,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18807994','Comfortable Home, Great Location','Classic Portland arts & crafts: Dark wainscoting in the living and dining rooms, high ceilings, spacious layout. This is our home, but we make it available when we travel. It is comfortable, and in a great location: A block from Hawthorne Blvd, and a few blocks from the popular Division Street and some of the best restaurants in town (Ava Gene\'s, Salt & Straw). A great way to explore Portland.','There are three great neighborhoods nearby. First, the Hawthorne District is classic Portland - a 1920s movie theater just a block away, a Powell\'s book store and coffeeshops and clothing stores. A few blocks further north is Belmont Street, with its pubs and cafes. And, a few blocks south is Division Street, with some of the city\'s most popular restaurants - Pok Pok, Bollywood, Ava Gene\'s and Salt & Straw.  <br /><br />There are also two of Portland\'s favorite parks nearby - Olmsted-designed Laurelhurst Park to the north, and Mt Tabor (with great views of the city and nice hiking) about a mile to the east.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2034e798-e61b-4b65-8428-49cb7f5bf06a.jpg',1153199,8,'45.51002','-122.62513',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,80.00,2,1125,18,4.94,18807994),(855,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18810464','Washington Park Suite - Near Rose Gardens','Our 90-year old colonial home is in the heart of Washington Park, walking distance to downtown & northwest Portland. We are just a block from the International Rose Test Gardens, Portland\'s number one tourist attraction. All of the park and hiking trails are easily accessible, and we are also very close to excellent restaurants and shopping. The bright, newly constructed garden suite features many thoughtful touches to make your stay comfortable. It\'s the perfect base for exploring Portland.','Arlington Heights, one of Portland’s most scenic neighborhoods, is just west of city center, with easy access to the spectacular Portland International Rose Test Gardens and all of the Washington Park attractions. Many of the streets offer access to the ten miles of trails in the 183-acre Hoyt Arboretum. Walk to the Japanese Gardens as well as to the Oregon Zoo. Downtown is within walking distance (all downhill), and you take the bus back if needed.  If you’re up for it, you can walk down to one of the many restaurants on Northwest 21st and 23rd Avenues and enjoy an evening meal. You just have to remember the uphill walk home.<br /><br />Arlington Heights is a veritable museum of architectural styles. Ranging from Victorian cottage to the latest contemporary dwellings, these homes are graced by lovely gardens and spectacular views. This is an old neighborhood with most of the homes built before 1939.<br /><br />Distance to:<br />International Rose Test Gardens - 1 block<br />Portland J','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-18810464/original/15c082aa-5a71-444f-8a84-82b9481df6e1.jpg',15422453,64,'45.52139','-122.7062',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,130.00,2,30,246,4.98,18810464),(856,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18887342','Tiny Farmhouse in the Heart of Belmont- Hawthorne','Whether you\'re in town for business or to explore the city, this is one of Portland\'s finest locations with a straight shot to downtown and mere blocks from Stumptown coffee, the restaurants/bars on Division, Belmont and Hawthorne, Biketown bike share, Mt. Tabor and Laurelhurst Park, New Season\'s, H-Mart, Powell\'s books and Bagdad theater.  This modern tiny house is tucked away in a quiet, peaceful neighborhood, and yet, right in the middle of everything a Portland visit requires.','Sunnyside is close to everything.  In between Belmont and Hawthorne you get to be in the middle of a quiet neighborhood, but blocks from so much fun.  Downtown is a ten minute bike ride.  Mt. Tabor is thirty or so blocks the other way.  You are 10 minutes from Sellwood.  10 minutes from Mississippi and Alberta.  But the neighborhood is so great you\'d be fine not to leave.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/924b557b-9400-4ca6-9690-fb1e6188389f.jpg',131613511,16,'45.51428','-122.63073',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,86.00,1,29,314,4.91,18887342),(857,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18932346','Retreat NW Portland One Bedroom','Welcome to your bright, spacious one bedroom Retreat tucked off bustling NW 23rd Ave in the heart of the restaurant and shopping mecca of PDX. Clean apartment with free access to W/D onsite and plenty of comfortable space to enjoy Portland to the fullest! Mid-stay cleaning service available-message me for details.','All the eating, drinking, shopping you could want are at your finger tips in NW Portland.  <br />Portland is a foodies paradise and this apartment offers easy access to all of it! St Honore Boulangerie french bakery, lunch of every style from food cart to sit-down, dinner theaters and dive bars, hand-made ice cream, classy pool halls...and that is just the beginning located just steps from your apartment door.  <br /><br />Shopping is top notch too.  Vintage jewelry, clothing boutiques galore, keepsakes and high-class home furnishings, and the list goes on.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-18932346/original/339e972b-4865-4aaa-bf6e-b2bf4ceaf906.jpeg',14540855,27,'45.53433','-122.69916',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,72.00,30,730,131,4.95,18932346),(858,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18945723','Airy Buckman Courtyard Guesthouse','Airy courtyard guesthouse in Inner Southeast Portland','We are on a residential street, an easy six-block walk to SE 28th and Burnside, one of the city’s best neighborhoods for dining out and nightlife. It\'s a vibrant, bustling neighborhood with lots to offer.<br /><br />Whole Foods Market and the Laurelhurst Theater anchor the neighborhood. Restaurants, bars, food carts, and boutiques abound (including Tusk, Boxer Ramen, Navarre, Angel Face, Guerro, Crema, and Fifty Licks, to name a few). Ken’s Artisan Pizza and Bamboo Sushi are a mere two blocks away.   We keep a binder of our favorite local spots to visit. <br /><br />Laurelhust Park -- one of Portland\'s loveliest -- is ten blocks east. Mount Tabor Park is a half hour walk on <br /><br />Within three miles you\'ll also reach Mount Tabor Park, the Hawthorne District, the Central Eastside, the Willamette River, and Downtown.<br /><br />Owen is a guidebook author and a fount of knowledge about Portland and Oregon.  He loves to give recommendations and help with itineraries, both in town or f','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0a9574fe-43f8-4baf-915f-7530374ab6a3.jpg',442446,32,'45.52068','-122.63792',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,200.00,2,1125,102,4.95,18945723),(859,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18948401','Comfy Room in Eclectic Victorian-31 day min no tax','A comfy private room with lock and key inside a charming 1896 Victorian building set up for Airbnb guests-like a mini hostel.  Out front is a popular Mexican food cart and 2 blocks away is trendy~NW 23rd Avenue-a 1.5 mile strip of coffee shops, restaurants and unique shops. A bus stop is 2 blocks away or use Uber/Lyft/car to get downtown in 6 minutes. Also Forest park Is only a 15 minute walk away.<br />Part of your fee goes to help Ukrainians🇺🇦. Your host lives on premises in a different apartment.','The NW Alphabet District (Slabtown) offers a variety of wonderful art, clothing, yoga/fitness, coffee, specialty shops, pubs, grocery stores and restaurants.  Walking down NW 23rd Avenue is a great way to interact with Native Portlanders. Take NW 23rd Avenue all the way to Burnside Street (turn left-East) then pass Powells books and other sights all the way to Voodoo donuts and explore the waterfront to get an even better feel of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1afec7ce-e457-472e-af42-96f04a8b4355.jpg',98202133,27,'45.5388','-122.697',2,1,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,31,365,699,4.93,18948401),(860,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18962310','Portland Sanctuary','Modern mid century boho chic two bedroom apartment unit in a gorgeous private craftsman bungalow home  built in 1910. The unit is spacious, cool and provides ample room for a cozy stay. You will find new appliances in both the bathroom and kitchen. Both bedrooms are outfitted with tempurpedic mattresses and clean linens and towels and accented with local Pendleton prints. Backyard is shared. We do have chickens in the backyard and if you like fresh eggs we are happy to drop off some off.','Piedmont is a perfect location right between key neighborhoods in the Northeast. You can walk over to Dekum Triangle where the famous local Breakside brewery is located or take a stroll to the Alberta Arts district which is peppered with shops and restaurants. Also a stone throw is the Boise neighborhood of Williams street  and very popular Mississippi street where there are plenty of music venues and restaurants. 15 minute uber ride and you can find yourself either in Southeast on the well known Hawthorne and Burnside streets. And last but not least 15 minutes and you are on the west side so really it\'s an ideal location to move from while in Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/82cb75a2-eb7c-4762-a9c1-3ef4485811ff.jpg',9078003,48,'45.56671027475282','-122.66214344873457',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,115.00,1,35,166,4.89,18962310),(861,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18976343','Industrial vibe studio in perfect location','Our cool detached studio offers a truly Portland experience. Industrial vibe with skylights and concrete floors. Funky outdoor hangout space. 1 queen bed (Tuft and Needle) and 1 queen size pullout couch. Basic kitchen. Private bathroom. Amazing location. Quiet residential neighborhood, 1 block to light rail, bike share, and the best bar in town. Walk/ride to Mississippi St. as well. 6 min drive to the Pearl District. A few blocks to the Skidmore Bluffs.<br />**pets are an additional $10 per night.','Quiet neighborhood, with very close access to everything you want/need in Portland.  Make sure to hit up the Skidmore bluffs for sunset.  Eisenhower bagels in the morning.  And the Alibi Tiki bar, if you\'re looking for a kitschy cocktail (with a great karaoke room in the back).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/97e8dc48-f135-4507-bc34-202c55d6b51f.jpg',7872197,13,'45.55571','-122.68427',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,99.00,2,1125,212,4.86,18976343),(862,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18977209','Sweet NE PDX 2-bed: Close to All','Welcome! We have a sweet 2-bed/1-ba that will be perfect for your visit: an in-law unit with private entrance, living/dining area, small kitchenette, 2 bedrooms and bath.  Quiet block with grocery, yoga, coffee, and restaurants to walk to!  The bluff is 2 blocks away-watch the sunrise/set there! 5 min from Alberta Arts & Beaumont (home of Pips donuts!), and 10 min from Hawthorne. NOTE: We are following all CDC guidelines in terms of disinfecting and sanitation in between guests to keep you safe.','Lovely neighborhood in the Rose City/Alameda area of NE Portland. Sidewalks and well-kept homes make this area feel inviting and friendly.  Its a great neighborhood for walking.  Safeway grocery store, yoga studio, several restaurants including pizza, Thai, & Mexican, Kainos coffee shop, Mom & Pop\'s wine store, and Roseway movie theater are all within walking distance. We are about 15 minutes from downtown, 5 minutes from Alberta Arts, 3 minutes from Beaumont/Fremont (home of Pip\'s donuts and Fire On the Mountain restaurant!), and 10 minutes from the Hawthorne/Belmont/Division area. About 7 minutes from airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/68eba040-ded7-4185-a597-b3b2539322ed.jpg',2760621,39,'45.54534','-122.5963',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,14,62,4.97,18977209),(863,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18996706','Portland Experience Awaits You!','Staying over 30 days *eliminates* the extra *fees* housing tax! This is a shared space in a quiet neighborhood duplex with off-street parking.  Multnomah Village (1 mile away) offers delicious restaurants, an art center, village coffee, bakeries, and shopping. PCC, 1 mile away. The #12 or #44 bus line (to downtown) is minutes away from your front door.   OHSU 30 min by bus. Uber, 10 min to City Center.  The kitchen is fully equipped for your inner chef!  $15 per night extra guest fee applies.','Barber World Market, for groceries, is within walking distance.  A walking pathway along Capital Hwy goes to Multnomah Village for restaurants and other activities.  The neighborhood is friendly and welcoming.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/171d2044-90b4-4cdf-b794-6ad1b3188a42.jpg',132519510,18,'45.45499','-122.71732',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,44.00,30,150,19,4.95,18996706),(864,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18996997','Bright, New Apartment in Hip & Accessible Kenton','Bright, garden-level, welcoming space located in hip North Portland.  Get to know the neighborhood or enjoy the easy access to downtown (15 mins), the airport (20 mins), or the great outdoors!  Residential setting with easy parking and quick access to what Portland (and the surrounding areas) have to offer.','Kenton is a thriving neighborhood in North Portland. Located \"on the peninsula,\" Kenton\'s downtown was known for its cattle district in the late 19th century but is currently packed with great restaurants (Swift & Union) and hip shops (Mantel). Enjoy a walk over to Columbia or Kenton park! Not far from us are the thriving St. John\'s area, Alberta Arts District, and Mississippi.  If you\'re in need of groceries there\'s a Green Zebra very close and a New Seasons or Fred Meyer within 2 miles.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7ab30c23-a2d8-455e-b86f-91044c7b29b2.jpg',11311261,55,'45.58342','-122.70337',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,93.00,1,15,432,4.97,18996997),(865,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/18999545','Brand New, Modern Apartment in Trendy NE PDX','The apartment is brand new, very clean, comfortable and modern. It is on the 1st floor of a 3 story townhouse. It is perfect for a small family getaway (public park w/ playground next door), business travel, or for a fun vacation. It is very close and walkable to several lively Portland areas (N Williams, Alberta Arts, Mississippi) and a quick drive to downtown PDX or the convention center. If you love visiting new cities and exploring the local area on foot, then you\'ll love this place!','The apartment in located in the King/Sabin neighborhood, walking distance to 4 different trendy Portland areas.  Close to two beautiful Portland parks.  4 blocks from MLK which has bakery/coffee shop- St. Beatrix and one of Portland\'s shining stars in the food scene- Cafe Olli.  10 minute walk to adorable N Williams Ave with dozens of restaurants and bars.  0.6 mile from the vibrant Alberta Arts district. 1 mile to N Mississippi Ave. 0.5 mile from Whole Foods Market or New Seasons Market for groceries. Also don\'t miss the King Farmer\'s Market every Sunday (10am-2pm) just a few blocks from our place from May-November!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dcd174a2-4297-4bf3-9e9c-cdb1a432443c.jpg',12222973,14,'45.55294','-122.65948',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,130,4.97,18999545),(866,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19019667','Alberta Arts Room - Wifi, TV, A/C - Great location','Lovely room with a large south-facing window, comfortable bed, mini fridge and microwave. Located in the vibrant and eclectic Alberta Arts neighborhood.','The house is located in the heart of the vibrant and eclectic Alberta district. Starting 3 blocks away, there are great places to eat like the Radio Room, Grilled Cheese Grill, Salt and Straw, Podnah\'s Pit (recent restaurant of the year), Random Order (named one of America\'s Best Pie Spots by Food&Wine), brew pubs, shopping, and live music venues.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/873e4166-1218-4bb6-9b17-5465273d831c.jpg',2236909,14,'45.56047','-122.65714',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,30,120,30,4.90,19019667),(867,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19049489','The Crow;s Nest @ The Gilman','A sweet little room in a hip, bike-friendly neighborhood. Just 2 miles from downtown, and close to everything you\'ve come here to experience! <br />Our home has a quirky mix of vintage, DIY, and theatre decor; reflecting our unconventional take on life.  We are a family of creatives who can serve up the inside scoop on Portland\'s arts & culture scene, along with breakfast. The Gilman is Safe Space devoted to hospitality, diversity, and the common good.','Portland\'s Kerns neighborhood, is just east of the Willamette River, combines urban convenience with a Bohemian, creative charm.  Our house is right on the cusp between North East and South East, within easy walking/cycling distance of oodles of Portland\'s top venues, attractions, restaurants, bars and shops; including Powell\'s, Voodoo Donuts, Revolution Hall, The Hollywood Theatre, Hawthorne, Belmont, and so much more!<br /><br />Walk Score: 90<br />Bike Score: 96<br />Transit Score: 64','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4a8bedbe-d312-4d28-b42e-c88ae5baa778.jpg',74852933,12,'45.52529','-122.64176',2,2,1.00,2.00,1.00,182.00,31,1125,1,5.00,19049489),(868,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19051513','Beautiful Basement Apartment in Contemporary Home','1,100 sqft apartment in a contemporary home in desirable NE Portland. Enter down the driveway and through the back gate. Lockbox on back door. Head downstairs. I live upstairs. Large bedroom with sitting area, living room, FULL kitchen, bathroom with double sinks, and laundry room. Minutes away from shops, restaurants, bars, and coffee shops in Beaumont Village on Fremont Street. Close to Alberta Arts District. Only 3.8 miles from the airport!','Family friendly. Young adults. Dog friendly. Bike Friendly. Walking distance to Fire on the Mountain (Best chicken wings in town!) and Mad Hanna, which is a noteworthy neighborhood bar. Minutes from Beaumont Village. Bike ride away from great restaurants and bars on NE 42nd and close to the Alberta Arts District and other desirable NE hot spots.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3aca3f03-5e6c-4b1d-a66a-9222360c46fa.jpg',132980319,39,'45.55237','-122.59546',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,81.00,2,1125,113,4.93,19051513),(869,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19102236','Private garden loft apartment','A private room and bath on its own floor of the house and own entrance with a semi-private hallway below, as in a duplex. There is a tea station and fridge and microwave but no kitchen access.   <br /><br /><br /><br />Great restaurants and cafes within walking distance at dekum triangle .1.7 miles to Alberta, Williams and Mississippi, fun north portland  walking streets.<br />cats on premises but not in the space!','We are walking distance to restaurants, cafe, brew pubs, yoga studio and park in the woodlawn  triangle area...<br />Woodlawn cafe is my personal<br />Favorite as is P and Q market. Eleven cafe is close also and faces south so sunnier <br /><br /><br />within a mile of arbor lodge new seasons, max line station and cafes and shops<br /><br /><br /><br />Also Peninsula park and rose gardens with   tennis courts and community center is a half mile , short bike ride away.<br /><br /><br /><br />Mississippi, Williams and Alberta street are a bike ride away and are fun streets to walk on','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/29ed62ce-71fc-4643-9971-43647dd74ba0.jpg',41333497,48,'45.57247','-122.66415',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,68.00,1,15,351,4.74,19102236),(870,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19120860','Hollywood Haven','Our home is an eclectic mix of things that make us happy. The basement studio is an extension of the same. We\'re told that it\'s comfortable and inviting. Close to so many of the great things that Portland has to offer, we think you\'ll find our place convenient and comfortable for your stay. Whether you just want to stay in the neighborhood, or wander into the city and beyond, you\'ll find yourself in a safe, easy, and accessible location.','The neighborhood is vibrant and safe. Close to much of what the city has to offer. There is plenty available on foot in the neighborhood - see the map I\'ve included of some of the highlights, in the photos.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/74eca602-c8fb-42d4-8f27-66d68f0e10a7.jpg',40607528,11,'45.53827','-122.61283',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,111.00,2,26,208,4.95,19120860),(871,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19138065','* *Stylish Backyard Studio + Private Patio* *','The Stylish Backyard Studio opens onto its own private covered veranda with plenty of spaces to sit and enjoy the peacefulness  of the grounds. The studio has contemporary furnishings and artwork, beamed ceilings, and a full bath with tub. You will sleep like a baby in the super comfy bed, with quality linens and an assortment of pillows. Easy and ample free parking ...and many little extras you may want while traveling help make your stay pleasant.','This is one of the most conveniently located areas in Portland! A lovely “pocket” neighborhood that is very quiet where you will only hear the crows and the squirrels. We are next to the beautiful Rocky Butte observation mountain. The Madison South neighborhood is also home to some of the best Vietnemese restaurants in the city! Nom nom. We\'re ten minutes from the airport, a straight shot down Sandy Blvd. to Downtown (15-20mins), Alberta Arts (10mins), with The Grotto grounds and beautiful Mount Tabor park also just minutes away. Very conveniently located to all the main streets and highways, but without the hassles, crime and noise you may encounter in busier neighborhoods. Serene spot to come home to after exploring our fair City of Roses!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-19138065/original/3a305248-883f-4fe9-96da-b2508602b561.jpeg',133774958,74,'45.5446','-122.57382',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,61.00,1,14,708,4.91,19138065),(872,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19139827','The Flying Whale-MountTabor.','You will have full reign of the top (street)level of the home. Host lives downstairs in the sun basement. You are the only ones who will enter through the front door, and you’ll have a reserved parking space in the double driveway. Your private space includes a double queen and king bedroom, a full bathroom with a jetted bath and shower, a fully equipped kitchen, dining/living room with wood burning fireplace and stunning views, a laundry room, a wrap around deck with outdoor table and chairs.','Mount Tabor is one of the most beautiful parks in the city. Our home is up on the hill, on a quiet residential street close to the trails. We are minutes away from the Montavilla neighborhood,which has amazing restaurants, cafes and the iconic Academy theater. We are close to fun Portlandia neighborhoods on Hawthorne and Belmont street with unique cafes, restaurants, theaters and bars, and walking distance to gorgeous trails through the park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1f9f4c73-01f2-4c44-bb31-50f6b5d6d21b.jpg',133785686,15,'45.5213','-122.58814',1,3,1.00,2.00,3.00,165.00,2,730,367,4.98,19139827),(873,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19175797','littlebluepdx','Stylish little house with lots of light and lots of garden! Clean, comfortable space where anyone could enjoy a relaxing vacation. A short walk to some of Portland’s favorite restaurants and bars! Littlebluepdx does not disappoint!','Awesome NE neighborhood with bars, coffee, restaurants, organic grocery store all in walking distance from our place.<br />Alberta Arts and Concordia are chock full of great places to hang!<br /><br />We encourage people to really dive into our neighborhood-we are literally in walking distance to some great food and bars! While it may feel like we are tucked away on a quiet alley way -a hop, skip and a jump to alberta street will certainly bring celebratory noise. Please click on the links of our neighborhood assets sent to you once booked-to really see the neighborhoods potential!<br /><br />Make sure you bring rain gear (fall, winter and spring) and comfortable shoes for exploring Portland! Renting a bike or taking a stroll can really bring out the best of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-19175797/original/868fdb7f-58de-4637-b55b-5070af741c47.jpeg',1792734,1,'45.563904','-122.635216',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,2,10,475,4.98,19175797),(874,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19195669','•1898UrbanVictorian Loft view near Convention Ctr.','*Renovated 1898 Neo-Classical Victorian 800 sq ft. view loft studio apartment. *Restaurant row featuring awarded LePigeon is five minute walk away. <br />*Near Convention Center, Lloyd Center shopping mall, movie theater.<br />*Streetcar 3 blocks away, Max Train 10 minute walk, buses to downtown 2 blocks, or walk across Burnside Bridge. <br />*Easy access to I-84 route to airport.<br />*Located in urban Central Industrial area, neighbors are businesses in smaller buildings. <br />*Urban noises. <br />*City and tree views.','*My 1898 home is one of the few remaining houses in what used to be a residential neighborhood. <br />*She has been lovingly restored her to more modern living but many details remain true to the period.<br />*The 1898 Urban Victorian is located in an area with the attendant urban noises associated with adjacent businesses that occur throughout the day and night including trains, car and truck and traffic noises. A nearby bakery sometimes has the smell of baking bread.<br />*A wide variety of restaurants are within walking distance. Recent nearby apartment construction has brought in more coffee shops and restaurants to explore.<br />*The house is located in area with light foot and car traffic during the day. After business hour,  the  traffic, people and parked cars are greatly reduced.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5ac75964-4bcf-4c42-b156-bc898f0864ed.jpg',134280900,12,'45.52578','-122.65812',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,140.00,1,1125,165,4.73,19195669),(875,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19197609','The artFlat / Portland.Peaceful. Fun','The artFlat is a two room (entire apt), including large kitchenette (no stove/oven) & bath, designed in our daylight basement. Nestled within a classic Portland foursquare, you will enjoy the  rich gallery atmosphere of The artFlat, decorated with original prints taken from around the world by your host, Holly.  We have carefully appointed the unit to maximize your comfort and enjoyment. The artFlat is located in the epicenter of everything Portland, quietly sitting on a tree-lined avenue.','artFlat, Portland is in the heart of the Inner Eastside; the part of town that defines Portland and gives it its reputation. We are one block from Hawthorne Blvd. and a short stroll to bustling SE Division St. <br /><br />Our walk-score is conservatively 89. <br /><br />While it is worthwhile and recommended to explore within a few mile radius that encompasses downtown, the Pearl District, Alberta Arts District, NW 23rd, Slabtown, Mississippi Ave, Burnside, NE 28th Ave, Washington Park, and the Willamette River, you could spend your entire visit within blocks of the artFlat and only scratch the surface of what the immediate neighborhood has to offer. From the artFlat you can walk or take a very short drive to Pok Pok, Salt & Straw, Bollywood Theater, Pine Street Biscuits, Porque no!, Ava Genes, multiple Food Cart Pods, Baghdad Theater, Music Millennium, Blue Star Donuts, Farma (most awarded cannabis dispensary), Helium Comedy Club, Sweet Hereafter, Powell\'s books, Whiskey Soda Lounge, ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3d7a8f2b-a03f-424c-b324-c16944f6757e.jpg',134299336,8,'45.5118','-122.63124',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,57.00,1,30,349,4.89,19197609),(876,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19208182','Rad Daylight Basement in 1959 Split Level Ranch','Recently renovated - and very cozy - daylight basement in a split level midcentury ranch style home. The entire basement floor is yours and includes a queen size bed, sitting area, fridge, microwave, etc. You\'ll be surrounded by ancient Doug Fir - wall to wall wood paneling / window framing - and midcentury decor. Centrally located in the inner SE quad, very close to downtown, Reed College, restaurants, bars and shops - Sellwood, Westmoreland, Division/Clinton, Hawthorne, Belmont/Mt. Tabor...','The neighborhood is located in the inner SE quadrant. It is centrally located, close to the Willamette river and the downtown area on the West side of town. Creston-Kenilworth is the name of the neighborhood and while it is close in, it is very quiet. Safe and sleepy, the neighborhood reminds me of the Division-Clinton neighborhood when I first moved to Portland nearly ten years ago. In all, the neighborhood is a great way to experience what it feels like to be a local, living in PDX. <br /><br />Gladstone Street is one of the primary neighborhood arteries nearby; just to the north of my house, it has a small cluster of restaurants and bars. I highly recommend C Bar at SE 28th and Gladstone. It always has a great selection of craft beer and the Chef\'s Burger on the menu is really, really good. The sushi place is so-so. I wouldn\'t recommend it.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-19208182/original/d888523b-d61b-48dc-b7f0-8bc0dfa7a421.jpg',22809489,67,'45.49084','-122.62768',2,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,49.00,1,15,554,4.97,19208182),(877,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19209341','Great, quiet neighborhood. 30 day minimum.','The house is located in the Mt Tabor neighborhood in SE Portland. There are some great restaurants within walking distance- Tabor Tavern,  Oly’s Pizza, and good Thai and Indonesian restaurants. <br />The bus is on the corner for a short ride to downtown.','My Tabor Tavern and  Oly’s Pizza are on the next block.  Grocery store is two short blocks. Thai food and Indonesian  are a 5 minute walk.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4cfe0179-46cc-4170-ab7f-b074b4cad588.jpg',106287972,15,'45.52255407254195','-122.60991125690482',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,30,90,1,5.00,19209341),(878,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19225029','Pet Friendly with Fast Wifi & Easy Parking','Furnished & stocked with everything you might need during your stay, our ground-floor apartment is the perfect space to call your home away from home in Portland!  It has a comfortable queen bed, spacious full bathroom with a large shower stall, washer & dryer, full kitchen with new appliances, lounge area with a Roku-equipped TV and even your own outdoor patio. Street parking is easy in our neighborhood and you’ll have easy access to I-405, I-5 plus, we’re just a 15 minute trip to downtown.','We\'re located just South of Alberta St and East of Martin Luther King Jr Blvd in the King neighborhood. It\'s a very walkable area with charming tree-lined streets, plenty of unrestricted parking and it\'s close to many transit stops, local retailers, coffee shops and restaurants.<br /><br />-- 4 blocks to Bushel & Peck bakeshop<br />-- 6 blocks to Whole Foods<br />-- 9 blocks to Williams food haven with Eem, Life of Pie, Lompoc and so many more!<br /><br />Though you may not even want to leave the neighborhood, you\'ll have easy access to lots of other fun areas of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b9e8d78c-b231-426c-998f-ae21c4157313.jpg',134574350,14,'45.5514','-122.65669',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,105.00,30,90,185,4.87,19225029),(879,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19246074','Full Private Apartment in Trendy Neighborhood','Cozy second floor apartment in charming vintage fourplex. Full kitchen (not a kitchenette) with gas range and coffee, tea, snacks. Small table for eating and corner desk for office work. Private bedroom with queen bed, and a couch futon in kitchen common area that folds into a bed if additional sleeping space is required. Perfect location for visitors interested in living in an authentic Portland neighborhood! High-speed 100Mbps wifi.','One block from Foster, a historically significant street with restaurants, coffee shops, bars with live music, vintage shops and the Portland Mercado. Foster Powell, or FoPo, is a neighborhood reminiscent of 1990s Portland: safe but rough around the edges with art galleries, taquerias, bike shops and record stores. You\'re also a short walk to Mt. Scott Community Center if you have a hankering for rollerskating, swimming, or working out!<br /><br />Foster Road comes from early resident Philip Foster, a prominent farmer and the brother-in-law of F.W. Pettygrove, one of Portland\'s founders. Powells Valley Road, named after the family of Jackson Powell who homesteaded land in the Gresham area in 1853, became Powell Boulevard.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/66bcd037-2c72-438b-825f-8ac937730a4d.jpg',29172616,65,'45.48831','-122.5947',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,42.00,31,1125,92,4.92,19246074),(880,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19247651','Multnomah Village Guest House','Just a block off of SW Portland\'s historic Multnomah Village on a quiet street.  This perfectly located guest house has everything you could need to enjoy Portland.  \"The Village\" is full of  boutique shops, outstanding restaurants, gorgeous parks as well as easy access to I-5 and the rest of Portland.  <br /><br />The guest house has a private entry, full bathroom and kitchen.  An easily operated and very light murphy bed (full/double bed), gas fireplace and smart TV provide space and comfort.','Known as “the village in the heart of Portland,” historic Multnomah Village delivers small town charm mere minutes from the city center. This is a quaint Southwest Portland suburb, where you can stroll down streets lined with charming cafés, galleries, bars and shops.  <br /><br />https://www.travelportland.com/article/multnomah-village/','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/343f3c51-bf7f-42c5-94de-da46e2d290cc.jpg',25278503,18,'45.4663','-122.71423',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,30,30,269,4.92,19247651),(881,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19273583','Sweet Hideaway in the trees, Mount Tabor','Sweet Hideaway is a little, cozy space for couples or solo travelers looking for a peaceful refuge in the trees, yet only a 10 minute drive to downtown. You will have your own entrance and enjoy a Tempurpedic queen bed, a smart TV, your private bathroom, a dining/kitchenette area with a bar table and stools, mini-fridge, microwave, toaster oven, coffee maker, tea, coffee, treats, utensils, a private table and chairs on the deck over the trees.  For  2+ night stay, free use of washer/dryer.','This is one of my favorite neighborhoods in Portland—a leisurely 10 minute walk to Mount Tabor Park and the trails and a 15 minute drive to down town Portland. We have concerts in Mount Tabor park every Tuesday night in the summer, and we border on the charming Montavilla neighborhood, where you\'ll find the iconic Academy Theater, great restaurants and cafes, and the Montavilla  farmer\'s market on Sundays. We are also close to Coquine, a farm to table neighborhood restaurant on SE Belmont and 69th, a nice walk through the treelined streets, and Mandala Yoga which offers a variety of yoga classes also on SE 69th and Belmont.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-19273583/original/8f8dae6b-b2d0-4328-9c8b-c3fde1cf7f01.jpg',133785686,15,'45.52068','-122.59036',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,67.00,1,730,805,4.98,19273583),(882,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19290369','Quaint Basement Studio w/ Hot Tub and Private Deck','This is a basement unit with separate entrance, bathroom and laundry area.  Inside the unit:  Queen size bed, full size couch, fire place, full bath (walk in shower only), washer + dryer, small fridge and microwave.  Outside the unit: large deck space, fire pit, and hot tub. <br /><br />**Please note this unit is below our living area there is some inherent noise due to foot traffic and our pups.  We do our best to be mindful of this but it\'s not a \"sound proof\" unit.  Most guests are good with this!!','Hayhurst is our hood! Quiet dead end street with mature trees and no busy traffic.  Located in the SW hills of Portland with greenways in front of the house and behind our back yard.  Close to the Hillsdale and Multnomah Village communities and 15 min drive to the south portion of Downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-19290369/original/3ad77699-e889-4e64-8413-ee333619f4bd.jpeg',16918919,17,'45.4832','-122.72932',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,30,538,4.83,19290369),(883,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19308293','Two Stories Guest Cottage  with Deck and Grill.','Close in. 31+ days is our best price. East view. Full + half bath. Washer Dryer. High speed, cable  and two TVs with DVR, one on each floor.  Balcony.  Dish washer. Small full  kitchen. Quiet heat pump. Shops and restaurants (world class) within walking distance. Large Deck for guest\'s use. Easy access to downtown via bus lines or car.  American Standard fold out couch turns into a high quality queen bed and there is queen in the single BDRM. Deck has a grill for summer months.','Residential family neighborhood. We often walk to restaurants, coffee shops, and grocery store.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/66fc3acb-3b0c-406c-a8dd-c1a1cfefbe06.jpg',16176539,8,'45.49864','-122.63291',1,4,1.50,1.00,2.00,99.00,3,1125,46,4.98,19308293),(884,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19366649','Convention Center/ Moda/ Eliot/ West Irvington','Street level 1910 duplex is a tranquil space with easy access to  inner Portland and all it has to offer. We love this city and hope you enjoy your stay.<br /><br />5 minute walk to Portland Streetcar.<br />5 minute walk to Nike bike rentals/Nike Factory Store<br />5 minute walk to Ox/Toro Bravo/ Wonder ballroom <br />15 minute walk to  Moda Center<br />15 minute walk to the Convention center.<br />15 minute walk to Emanuel hospital.<br />15 minute walk to Max light rail.<br />1.5 miles to downtown.<br />1.2 miles Pearl District.','The duplex is located in the Eliot/West Irvington neighborhood . Easy to get downtown and to other close in neighborhoods. 1 block to the bus and a 5 minute walk to the street car that loops around the central city. Max station to the airport is a 15 minute walk.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/db07816b-3bd9-43f1-b43f-db4e33e08550.jpg',135429095,26,'45.53851','-122.6604',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,86.00,2,1124,284,4.85,19366649),(885,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19384339','Cozy Private 800 sq. ft. Downstairs in St. John\'s!','Welcome to your Portland get away! This is a CLEAN large legally licensed and permitted space that is fully furnished, newly remodeled and updated! We are located in St. John\'s Oregon, the newest up and coming neighborhood with lot\'s of culture and happenings. We are also close to University of Portland!<br />About your stay:<br />We personally check in each guest and give you the code.<br />We can be available to speak with or if you prefer otherwise that is fine too!','More than 100 years ago, leafy St. Johns existed as a small, quiet town at the confluence of the Willamette and Columbia rivers. Today, the quaint North Portland neighborhood retains its small-town charm with its many locally owned shops, pubs and cafés. Pack a picnic blanket for an afternoon in Cathedral Park, cross the picturesque St. Johns Bridge and get ready to explore a lovely, lesser-known side of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9735cd7b-11bf-4664-979f-4e8783f63b39.jpg',135879197,58,'45.59366','-122.73515',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,2,27,165,4.93,19384339),(886,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19387985','Privacy & Peace steps from OHSU','Cozy bedroom in a private residence. Shared spaces are the full kitchen, full bathroom, washing/drying machine, patio and backyard overlooking Marquam nature park. Conveniently located 0.5mi from OHSU campus and 2mi from PSU and downtown. Short walk from bus line 8 with frequent service into town all day. Adjacent to huge network of hiking/running/biking routes as well as Healy Heights and Council Crest Parks.<br /><br />Public overnight parking available on street for guests (no cost).','Quiet neighborhood with peaceful vistas and many options for outdoor activities. The OHSU campus and a convenience store are half a mile down the hill and there are lots of parks and trails scattered around.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/45f7e5c1-f387-40e2-9f15-9976f5cfcbf5.jpg',9584819,30,'45.49689483642578','-122.69591522216797',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,1,30,53,4.91,19387985),(887,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19403380','Inviting Oasis By Division Street\'s Restaurant Row','Conveniently located off Division’s Restaurant Row. Private garden entrance. Well-appointed apartment, tidily maintained, full of natural light. Walking distance to famous restaurants and popular bars, cafés, and shops including Bollywood Theater, Stumptown, Salt & Straw, Kati Thai (vegan), Blue Star Donuts, and Broder Cafe\". Features equipped kitchen, relaxing living room, comfortable bedroom w/full bed, bright bathroom w/shower. Living room futon converts to full bed.','The house is located in one of the most popular areas of inner Southeast Portland, between Division and Clinton Streets. It\'s an easy walk to many restaurants, bars and small unique cafe\'s and shops on Division St, Clinton St, and Hawthorne Ave. This area, as the rest of Portland, is growing rapidly but is still a neighborhood full of charming, single-family houses with well maintained gardens.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-19403380/original/cdb80b8f-4e8f-47aa-aa0c-dc9462aa8099.jpg',136020511,25,'45.50411','-122.6363',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,101,4.99,19403380),(888,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19413838','Spacious, private SW hills HOUSE w free parking','Historic (1925) house with modern updates. Enjoy a balcony breakfast with city views. Ideally located to visit highlights like hip NW 23rd, the Timbers\' Providence Park, Powell\'s or the Japanese Garden, all ~1 mile away. Central air! GB wifi. Indoor fireplace & outdoor fire pit on wooded lot. You\'ll have the place to yourself. Note that the recent review mentioning a \"busy corner\" was left by a guest who tried to overstay the reservation. I\'ve added 4 new exterior pics debunking this.','Portland Heights has wonderful views into downtown Portland and large, wooded lots. Old Portland at its finest, and close to the happening locations on NW 23rd and downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a8c09d03-2cf6-489c-94a1-fd7fad0caae9.jpg',40426471,54,'45.51607','-122.69658',1,5,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,59,4.95,19413838),(889,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19460421','The LaunchPad: clean, mod, convenient guest house','DEEP DISINFECTING & CLEANING PRACTICES ARE USED AT OUR GUEST HOUSE.<br />Welcome to The LaunchPad - a small, yet efficient, self-contained guest house just 3 miles from the center of downtown. It is brand new, comfortable, clean, and uncluttered, with just a bit of a Space Age theme. This is a perfect place for one person or a couple to kick back and relax, or to use as your base camp while exploring Portland. We welcome guests from all backgrounds,  orientations, and planets.','The Launch Pad is located in Portland\'s Overlook neighborhood, a short walk to the Adidas campus and the bluff looking out at Forest Park across the river (especially pretty at night). Although our block is residential, an espresso bar is directly across the street, and right around the corner are  sushi, Thai, and Mexican restaurants, as well as a wine bar. The neighborhood is a mere 3 miles from the center of downtown Portland. We are close to the N. Mississippi neighborhood and the Alberta Arts district, both with their many shops and restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTk0NjA0MjE%3D/original/133e4d9d-36ee-4f33-b6d8-c48527d9c507.jpeg',3119225,13,'45.56226','-122.69506',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,69.00,3,60,171,4.96,19460421),(890,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19475518','Entire Cozy Apartment Studio in Hip Neighborhood','High speed wifi! Cozy studio apartment in charming vintage fourplex. Full bed with huge TV and comfy suede couch in common area. Fully equipped kitchen with gas oven/range and bathroom with shower and bathtub. Perfect location for visitors interested in living in an authentic Portland neighborhood!','One block from Foster, a historically significant street with restaurants, coffee shops, bars with live music, vintage shops and the Portland Mercado. Foster Powell, or FoPo, is a neighborhood reminiscent of 1990s Portland: safe but rough around the edges with art galleries, taquerias, bike shops and record stores. You\'re also a short walk to Mt. Scott Community Center if you have a hankering for rollerskating, swimming, or working out!<br /><br />Foster Road comes from early resident Philip Foster, a prominent farmer and the brother-in-law of F.W. Pettygrove, one of Portland\'s founders. Powells Valley Road, named after the family of Jackson Powell who homesteaded land in the Gresham area in 1853, became Powell Boulevard.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ec4bc878-f02b-4f80-b0c5-5a82dafbdb26.jpg',29172616,36,'45.48959','-122.59487',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,51.00,57,1125,94,4.84,19475518),(891,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19494240','Ultra Clean 2 Bedroom with HEPA Air Purifier','Gorgeous newly remodeled fully equipped 800 sq. ft. two bedroom BASEMENT APARTMENT with HEPA air purifier in North Portland three blocks from the MAX line for quick and direct access to downtown and the rest of the city. Enjoy our spacious home with private key-less entry that easily sleeps up to five guests. There is ample street parking in front our house as well as several restaurants, bars, grocery stores (New Seasons/Fred Meyer) just a short walk away.','We live in a residential neighborhood with all the benefits of city life. Fred Meyer grocery store is one and a half blocks away and New Seasons (great grocery store with breakfast/lunch/dinner cafe) is just four blocks. Arbor Lodge Coffee is on the corner of Rosa Parks and Interstate kitty corner to New Seasons parking lot. Satchel, a local marijuana dispensary, is a 3 minute walk behind our house on Interstate. Also, there is a Thai food cart called Long Do and the Look Long brew pub three blocks away. There are loads of great restaurants and bars in the nearby area. Peninsula Park, about a half mile from our house, is awesome and you can enjoy the huge beautiful rose garden in spring and summer. So much available in our area!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-19494240/original/6da85218-88ab-49dd-8551-0698ca5c80a9.jpeg',136858425,51,'45.57423','-122.68205',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,94.00,1,60,393,4.90,19494240),(892,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19519294','Cozy Modern Apartment on Alberta St','This newer basement space is modern, clean and equipped with a full range of amenities including a full kitchen with professional appliances.<br /><br />This space is perfect for couples, business travel or small families looking for a central home base from which to explore Portland or a quiet spot to relax. We are 20 minutes from the airport and 5-10 minutes from downtown, the Moda and convention centers and a number of fun neighborhoods full of restaurants and shops.','We are located right off of Alberta Street in the centrally-located Overlook neighborhood, just a short walk from the Mississippi/Boise shops and restaurants. It is a fairly quiet neighborhood with some background noise from the interstate close by and passersby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b26a5dc2-5451-4922-9b9b-52dc20a03187.jpg',7580556,13,'45.5581','-122.68051',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,40,356,4.91,19519294),(893,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19530684','Orchard View-Stucco','Pet Friendly. A Country in the City feeling, private acreage on 100 year old Orchard, a peaceful respite from City Life. <br />Or venture out, a 4 mile bike/drive to Portland Center & OHSU. Walk to Multnomah Village & Hillsdale for Food/Pubs & Shops. Easy access to the Willamette River & Pearl district.<br />Day trip the Columbia Gorge, Pacific Ocean, Wine Country, Cascade Mountains, Golf & Cultural events. For Couples, Solos, Business Travelers. Hosts offer as much, or as little, opinion as you seek!','The absolute quiet so near the inner city. Multnomah Village and Hillsdale, our desirable little towns within walking distance in both directions. Ours is the topmost property on the hill. Peaceful and charmingly slow paced.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/20b65a74-dc6b-41a6-bc5a-843a0334618d.jpg',28410788,17,'45.47727','-122.71508',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,123.00,30,365,85,4.71,19530684),(894,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19533599','Beautiful light-filled home in Irvington','Light-filled family home with three bedrooms and lots of open living space. <br /><br />Ideal location on a quiet, low traffic street in the Irvington historic district. Within walking distance of local coffee shops, bars and restaurants, close to public transport, and easy to get to downtown, the Pearl, Mississippi and Alberta Arts District.','Irvington is a friendly, residential neighborhood in NE Portland, with easy connections to the rest of the city. It’s a quiet, charming, tree-filled community populated by cyclists, dog walkers and kids playing basketball on the street.<br /><br />The neighborhood also contains the largest, most diverse, and intact collections of Queen Anne, Arts and Crafts, and Colonial Revival style residences in Oregon and was designated an historic district and added to the National Register of Historic Places in 2010.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2cd95fb2-b09a-4650-a1fb-23f5f58f1e2e.jpg',3630538,7,'45.53753','-122.64869',1,6,2.00,3.00,4.00,350.00,30,300,5,5.00,19533599),(895,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19545779','Alberta Loft','Beautiful, spacious one bedroom loft, down the street from the up and coming supper club & restaurant strip on 42nd ave, 5 minutes from the Alberta arts district, 5 minutes from wonderful Fremont street and only 12 minutes from the airport. Tucked into a quiet backyard on one of Portland\'s bike boulevards, the newly constructed 2 story Alberta Barn has gorgeous large windows, modern fully equipped kitchen, loft bedroom, full bath and a killer record collection!','Our neighborhood is called Cully, though most people clump us in with the Alberta Arts District since we are right on the edge nearest to it. In the past is was suburban farm land. The lots are narrow and deep. Perfect for large back or front yard gardens. Sidewalks and curbs are rare and we like it that way. Often after dinner you will find groups of folks walking down the middle of the street, off for a drink or ice-cream, or just out walking the dog, or duck. Yes, the neighbors walk their duck.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-19545779/original/979deced-7239-4047-82ef-14107079bf92.jpeg',11076206,21,'45.55752','-122.6167',1,3,1.50,1.00,1.00,98.00,2,60,185,5.00,19545779),(896,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19547625','The Tiny Big Guest House','The Tiny Big Guest House is a detached studio cottage, cozy, private, and well-insulated.<br /><br /><br /> It\'s conveniently located for access to downtown and a short distance to local destinations for Portland\'s food/drinking/coffee/bakery/dessert/boutique scene.  <br /><br />This a residential block where real people live with a wonderful group of diverse neighbors. <br /><br />We welcome ALL nationalities, religions, sexual orientations, & genders!','Our neighborhood is a diverse mix of single-family homes and apartments.  Close by are restaurants, a sweet juice bar, bakery, coffee shops, beer, wine bars, pubs with full food service, Mexican, Sushi, Pizza, and fast food.  A large food cart space is in the works near by, along with 600+ others around Portland.  Our family often walks to parks or to eat out nearby, and we enjoy running and biking in the neighborhood.<br /><br /><br />A 15-20 minute walk will bring you to Clinton and Division Streets, one of Portland\'s biggest restaurant scenes!  It\'s a 20-minute walk to our nearby stores (Safeway, Trader Joes, New Seasons), and of course everything is convenient by bike or car.  We\'re a 25-45 minute drive from the airport, depending on traffic.  Some guests have stayed with us for treatment at OHSU.<br /><br />There are many fantastic farmer\'s markets, some are year-round.<br /><br />Let us know if you\'re looking for anything in particular, we\'re happy to give recommendations!  Pleas','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c2d62db6-cb6f-4d73-9696-a4246a5b2dbf.jpg',415258,67,'45.49564','-122.63793',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,99.00,2,28,452,4.94,19547625),(897,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19553361','Patio Cottage for 1-2 w/kitchen & gas firepit','With its private entrance at the end of a secluded patio, this eco-friendly cottage is the ideal retreat for solo travelers or couples.<br /><br />In its super-quiet, colorfully decorated, chemical-free interior, you\'re just steps from the happening Alberta Arts District, Killingsworth Street, and Williams and Mississippi Avenues, all chock full of locally-owned shops, restaurants, pubs, and food cart pods of all kinds.','► The location of the Patio Cottage is unbeatable. <br />The airport and downtown Portland are just a short drive away, and Alberta Street, Williams Avenue, Mississippi Avenue, and Killingsworth Street are within walking distance, offering a plethora of locally owned restaurants, pubs, and shops.<br /><br />The central location of the Patio Cottage allows for easy exploration of the stunning Columbia Gorge and Oregon Coast.<br /><br />► GETTING AROUND IS A BREEZE!<br />    • Free on-street parking is usually available right in front of the house or elsewhere on the block.<br />    • The house is just 3 blocks from Everybody\'s Bike Rentals and Tours.<br />    •  1/2 block to Alberta Street, 1 block to Williams Ave.<br />    • Pleasant walk to the Alberta Cooperative Grocery, Cherry Sprout Produce, Natural Grocers, or New Seasons grocery.<br />    • 5-minute, tree-lined walk to KILLINGSWORTH STREET, with its 3-mile length of more bars and restaurants.<br />    • The airport is a 15-minut','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-19553361/original/8234e3b2-3586-414e-802f-928b2537508d.jpeg',6946676,24,'45.558284759521484','-122.66563415527344',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,1,21,183,4.90,19553361),(898,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19570342','Comfy Condo Downtown Portland 97201 Extended Stay','Extended stay in Portland?  Visiting or working in Portland from 31-90 days?  Check us out!   Sunny  corner condo in urban downtown Portland  for extended stays of minimum 31 days to 3 months. Near streetcar, light rail, bus. Walk to the Pearl!  Shopping, bookstores, theatres, museums, dining.  breweries, PSU. Dryer/washer in unit, small bedroom, queen bed, TV, Wi Fi.  No parking. Across from new apartment building with coffee shop & restaurant. A block from grocery. 90 min to beach or Mt Hood','In the Cultural District near museums, university, performing arts venues, grocery, shopping, dining, riverwalk. Very handy location! Farmers Market, PSU.  Nice mix of new and older buildings.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b81bb583-0546-43b1-b3a3-636110aa4ac9.jpg',21288777,44,'45.51576','-122.68536',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,31,90,8,4.88,19570342),(899,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19609470','Magic Caravan','Cozy, charming space in a lively neighborhood!  Bedroom is on the main floor. The space includes shower, toilet, sink, kitchenette, mini-fridge, table, couch, A/C, full length mirror. Projector has Guest Roku so bring your passwords for Netflix, etc. Two blocks from popular Mississippi Ave. Close to coffeeshops, restaurants, bars, food carts, the Max light rail, and Biketown bike rentals. Bike helmets available. Close-in Portland center.<br />Check in is 3pm, check out is 11am.','Mississippi Ave is just 2 blocks West of the cottage, this is a popular, funky, historic, and lively neighborhood full of shops, restaurants, food carts, bars, coffee and tea shops. Also walkable to Williams Ave neighborhood, just 6 blocks East of cottage. Alberta Arts District is a short bikeable distance to the East.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cb5b0a68-7c96-486b-aa0c-340846e108a5.jpg',1510664,9,'45.55275','-122.67202',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,60,320,5.00,19609470),(900,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19610033','Taylor Street Cottage','Enjoy this newly constructed one bedroom guest cottage with soaring ceilings, an open and airy floor plan, and upgraded finishes.  Our guests rave about the stylish furnishings, cozy feel, and location in one of SE Portland\'s great walking neighborhoods. The bedroom has a queen size bed with a premiere-quality fold-out couch in the living room. We are just blocks away from great Portland dining, shopping, and coffee shops.','Great residential neighborhood a couple of blocks from SE Belmont Street, walking distance to Hawthorne Street & SE Division Street. About 15 minutes to downtown, and about 30 minutes from the Airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a7beb0b3-f9f6-4621-9650-c509c0dd4790.jpg',137895170,16,'45.5155','-122.63575',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,83.00,1,29,477,4.95,19610033),(901,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19626637','Tranquil Little House W/ Hot Tub. Pets welcome : )','Very quiet & private studio/cabin in a peaceful, relaxing neighborhood. A Modern & comfortable design perfect for couples looking for a Portland getaway with safe, off-street parking. <br />We LOVE your pets & welcome them to stay with you!  Your first pet is free & any other pet is only an addition $25 . <br />The Tranquil Little House\" is Very Close to Woodstock Blvd, Reed College, Restaurants, Ice Cream Parlors, Dog Parks, Supermarkets & more. <br />Come explore Portland from this Tranquil Little House.','Great convenient location on very quiet street.<br />Trader Joes is 8 blocks away.<br />Starbucks is 8 blocks away.<br />Great restaurants, grocery stores, bars and much more on Woodstock blvd 12 blocks away. The excited Division St and Hawthorne Blvd are around 5 minutes drive.<br />Woodstock dog park is 2 blocks away.<br />Downtown is 15 minutes drive away without Traffic. 25 with traffic.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTk2MjY2Mzc%3D/original/cfbde960-c2f5-4799-90b4-dd8416a728d8.jpeg',4901178,38,'45.48745','-122.6137',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,48.00,30,120,783,4.85,19626637),(902,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19657817','Williams Designer Suite - South','Bright and cheery sub-level apartment is tastefully furnished and sparkling clean.Located on a bustling block In the heart of one of Portlands hottest neighborhoods, surrounded by breweries, shops, restaurants & food carts. We are minutes from City Center via close public transportation, bike or car share. This space is 1 of 3 units at this property, one of which is owner occupied. Quite professional property, guests are asked to be =<PG-13. LGBTQ+ friendly. Find a different party place.','The fabulous Williams Corridor in NE Portland. Close in, first-rate public transportation, major north-south bike lanes, New Seasons grocery a block and a half walk. Award winning restaurants and indie shops on the immediate block & vicinity ... or stroll to Mississippi or Alberta for even more eclectic Portland food/drink/shops. <br /><br />Portland is all about neighborhoods and ours in Boise-Eliot is as charming and inviting as they come. Just east of the Willamette River, Boise-Eliot is an eclectic mix of traditional brick buildings, Victorian homes, and brand new ultra-modern structures coexisting happily in the very hip and popular North Portland. <br /><br />Restaurants, shops, New Seasons grocery, bars, food carts, yoga studios, tree-lined streets, coffee shops galore, and more - all within a block or two.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b1579b37-3570-480a-a7f1-dc604cd7d9f8.jpg',1239203,9,'45.550971084972176','-122.66726993659198',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,2,180,228,4.89,19657817),(903,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19678795','Spacious 2 Bdrm In Popular SE Hawthorne','Relax in this spacious two bedroom house, only steps away from the popular Hawthorne St District and Divison St District which features Pok Pok, Salt & Straw, Bagdad Theatre, House of Vintage, Por Que No, Stumptown Coffee, Laurelhurst Park and more. Enjoy the large backyard, wifi & free street parking.','The house is located in the Hawthorne St District which features Pok Pok, Salt & Straw, Por Que No, Stumptown Coffee, Laurelhurst Park and more. Enjoy the large backyard, wifi & free street parking.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5ab1d637-4836-4011-9c77-241fe3e4c248.jpg',23400410,16,'45.51511','-122.62457',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,90.00,31,180,88,4.83,19678795),(904,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19683221','Savor the Laid-Back, Bohemian Feel at a Sunny Urban Abode','Enjoy private access to a bedroom and living room tastefully furnished featuring:<br /><br />A very comfortable pull-out couch; <br /><br />A brand new bathroom with shower and heated towel rack; <br /><br />A front-loading washer and dryer; <br /><br />Dishes, fridge, sink, coffee maker, microwave, ample counter space and a small dining table;<br /><br />Private WiFi network. <br /><br />We\'ve put a lot of love into making this place beautiful and comfortable. See our five star reviews!<br /><br />Late check-ins can be easily accommodated with a passcode door lock.<br /><br />We’d love you to make our studio your home base.<br /><br />Bring the family. Your comfy pull-out couch sleeps two more. <br /><br />Want a light snack between restaurants? Walk a few blocks to our local New Seasons grocery store. Use your kitchenette with fridge, microwave, coffee maker, sink, dishes and wood countertops. <br /><br />Recharge your travel wear with front loading European washer/dryer. <br /><br /','This sought-after district is home to dozens of restaurants and brew pubs within walking distance, while there\'s a Bike Town bike share station one block away for getting around town. The local New Seasons grocery store is a few blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4e76ab96-799f-4644-ab3f-1aa61e06d8db.jpg',417776,9,'45.5502','-122.66566',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,99.00,2,700,372,4.98,19683221),(905,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19723300','Castle like home in SW PDX, minutes to downtown!','Spend your vacation surrounded by the hills of Southwest Portland minutes away from Downtown. This home has great views to the west. Fully remodeled, huge vaulted ceilings in the living room.  BRAND NEW hot tub. Close to OMSI and OHSU.','Quiet neighborhood near Council Crest Park with great views over the city. Fairmount avenue is a 5 minute walk from the house and a popular destination for cyclists, walkers, and runners. Small, retro Hillsdale is a 5 minute drive with grocery, bars, coffeeshops, and the Portland staple, food carts!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-19723300/original/c785bfbb-7d70-473a-9435-7654df4fcf6f.jpeg',100656896,54,'45.49427432515024','-122.70378309143187',1,8,1.50,3.00,3.00,145.00,31,1125,105,4.60,19723300),(906,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19764369','Spacious, charming 1 bdrm, historic close-in NE','Well-appointed 600 sf, garden view, heated floors, private entry with courtyard, walk-in closet,  standing desk, w/d, bike/kayak storage.  <br />Walk historic neighborhood, 2 blocks to Whole Foods, public transport, bike rentals, cafes..10 blocks to Alberta arts.  <br />5G, no TV.  Quiet after 10pm.<br />1 dog probably ok - ask me.   No cats, we\'re allergic.<br />Message me about your party, and what you\'re up to in Portland','Enjoy the historic craftsmen and  gardens as well as plenty of action in Alberta Arts...great coffee and french pastry at 15th and Prescott','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-19764369/original/57223c90-995d-4831-8e4a-c8bc486d5332.jpeg',1895446,6,'45.54894','-122.64911',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,30,180,9,4.33,19764369),(907,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19764780','Parkrose Room','Private bathroom.  Ten minutes to PDX Airport! Convenient frugal accommodations.','Commercial area, some street/train noise.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/efb6b8c6-ab54-4d14-9634-e63573814b15.jpg',36382116,40,'45.55992','-122.55382',2,3,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,65,37,4.54,19764780),(908,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19769143','Two Bedroom Getaway NE Alberta Arts area: THE DUPE','We are in the NE Alberta Arts area with one off street parking spot in the driveway. Close-in, walkable location with easy access to dining, shopping, public transportation, Biketown rentals, farmer\'s market-pretty much all the best things about Portland are just a quick jaunt from your front door.  Enclosed front and backyards are lovely spots to enjoy your morning coffee, a drink or have a nice meal. Fully stocked kitchen with a dishwasher, and all the comforts for your home away from home.','We are located right off of Alberta Street and are also within an easy walk to the N Williams & N Mississippi areas. All have fantastic food, drink and shopping options. There is a Nike Biketown self service bike rental a block away that is on the Going street bike route, and Portland is a fantastic biking town!  The King school around the corner hosts one of the many Portland Farmer\'s Markets May-November, it also has a playground to keep the little ones entertained.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/41287c00-2c47-41ab-afab-9db0864660a1.jpg',139541066,14,'45.55808','-122.66069',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,62,4.81,19769143),(909,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19812267','Cozy, Beautiful Alberta Arts Apartment','We offer a two-bedroom in-law basement apartment, well-designed and newly constructed, quietly nestled just four blocks from the heart of the lively Alberta Arts district in the center of Northeast Portland. It features King-size Keetsa Pillow Top beds in each bedroom, a charming eat-in kitchen, a spacious bathroom with luxurious tiled shower/tub, washer-dryer in unit, private patio seating, antique glass doorknobs, thoughtful new and vintage furnishings.','The apartment is four blocks from bustling Alberta Street, so you can pop out for a delicious avocado toast at Proud Mary\'s, a scrumptious wrap at Bollywood Theater, crowd-pleasing ice cream at Salt & Straw, or melt-in-your-mouth pastries at La Petite Provence. And don’t forget to grab an artisanal latte at one of the many nearby coffee shops - Just Bob and Guilder are our favorites. <br /> <br />Our neighborhood is beautiful for walks - just blocks away from gorgeous Wilshire Park and shaded Alberta Park. Grab a rental bike for a lovely ride to our weekend Farmer’s Market at King School or to the Williams/Mississippi corridors to shop the boutiques. Or jump on the 17 bus one block away to head downtown. Ride-share cars, Ubers and Lyfts are usually less than 5 minutes away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-19812267/original/e384e7f1-f21f-45a8-86b2-333afa167ed4.jpg',31304088,19,'45.55499','-122.63816',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,73.00,4,1125,352,4.98,19812267),(910,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19820204','Pure Privacy for 2 in Multnomah Village','Secluded but welcoming, smoke-free, private-entrance, 1-bedroom apartment for 2 people. The apartment is within 3 blocks of historic and unique Multnomah Village. Access to shopping, restaurants, quick freeway access to downtown Portland (approximately 10 minutes), and close proximity to 2 community centers with work-out facilities. The apartment is also within 1.5 hours of beaches, wineries and the mountains if you seek activities that are a bit farther away.','Multnomah Village is one of the oldest neighborhoods in Portland. Developed from an 1800\'s land claim, the village got its own train depot in the early 1900\'s and was eventually annexed in 1950. Today it is a bustling community with an art center, shops, restaurants, a brew pub and its own historical society. There is a rich history of dairy farming and the former \"Red Electric\" train line reflected in subtle ways in and around the Village.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-19820204/original/02b5096b-881a-463b-b918-abfbe53a8ad3.png',137846612,18,'45.46833','-122.70695',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,111.00,2,28,216,4.99,19820204),(911,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19865184','1898UrbanVictorian Parlor Apt.near Convention Ctr.','*The Parlor Unit is located on the main floor of an 1898 Neo-Classical Victorian. <br />*Parlor guests have their own private entry from side porch. <br />*The original bay-windowed parlor consist of one large room encompassing the living area with couch, coffee table, chairs and desk and a sleeping area highlighted with queen bed. <br />*A separate kitchen has frig, gas range, microwave, sink, table and 2 chairs plus all items for preparing a meal. <br />*New vintage style bathroom has claw foot tub/shower combo.','*This 1898 home is one of the few remaining houses in what used to be a residential neighborhood. It is now a mixed use urban neighborhood housing  a teacher’s union, auction house, advertising company, state offices, urban lofts, meat distribution facility, cross fit gym and studios for a local art college. <br />*We have lovingly restored her to more modern living but many details remain true to the period. <br />*Home is located in an urban area with the attendant urban noises associated with adjacent businesses that occur throughout the day and night including trains, car and truck and traffic noises. <br />*A nearby bakery sometimes has the smell of baking bread. <br />* Many restaurants within walking distance. Recent apartment construction nearby has brought in more coffee shops and restaurants to explore. <br />*House is located in area with light foot and car traffic during the day. <br />*After business hours the traffic and parked cars are greatly reduced.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/beee199c-8ad9-4987-bc29-308a04962969.jpg',134280900,12,'45.52605','-122.65667',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,139.00,30,30,103,4.66,19865184),(912,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19880543','Hazelwood Haven: 1 BR w/private entrance & bath','Beautiful front bedroom with private bath & your own entrance. Private space - separate from the rest of the house.  Wood floor, lots of light. Clean, spacious & lovely.<br /><br />Convenient location, quiet neighborhood. 15 min drive downtown, 15 min drive to airport - Trimet MAX train is 4 blocks away, #20 bus is half a block away.<br /><br />This is our family home, all are welcome. Hate-free zone :)','The Hazelwood neighborhood is a nice area, with a library five blocks from the house, and a beautiful city park ten blocks away. There are a number of old Doug Firs on this street, and the neighbors are mainly families. Children in the neighborhood like to play on the unpaved road in front of the house and nearby homes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-19880543/original/ea0b045b-6f8b-4d28-a961-c2cca8a1a012.jpeg',63788073,63,'45.52064','-122.53362',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,49.00,30,1125,271,4.77,19880543),(913,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19890526','Entire Main Floor Bungalow - Min 30 Night Stay','The complete main floor of a Bungalow home in the Woodlawn neighborhood of Northeast Portland with 1 bedroom, 1 office w convertible sofa and 1 full bath. Perfect for work-from-home, with recently upgraded internet speed!   The bedroom has a luxury, queen-sized bed; bathroom has a lovely claw foot tub/shower.  Living and dining rooms are spacious, light and bright.  Kitchen is large and fully equipped. There\'s a full sized washer and dryer  for use during your stay.','The house is on a quiet, one-block street in a friendly, diverse residential neighborhood.  It\'s a 5 minute walk to fantastic restaurants, cafes, coffee shops, a bakery and a brewery.  There\'s a wonderful neighborhood park nearby.  A variety of grocery stores and food-cart pods are within a 1 mile radius.   <br /><br />The home\'s location in the inner Northeast part of the city also provides great access to everything Portland has to offer.  The Alberta Arts district is a pleasant 20 min walk away.    It\'s 15 minutes by car to the airport, downtown, the Pearl District, Forest Park or the Portland Japanese Garden and 30 minutes to the campuses of Nike or Intel.   It\'s also an easy 1  to 1  1/2 hour drive to spectacular scenery  of the Columbia River Gorge, Mt Hood, Mt St. Helens or the Oregon Coast.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-19890526/original/63e47c91-28db-4ce7-9bea-f4cec510b40e.jpeg',32601622,45,'45.57089','-122.65708',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,7,5.00,19890526),(914,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19910312','Private bedroom off Hawthorne Blvd Mt Tabor','Private room and bathroom in turn of the century bungalow off Hawthorne Blvd.<br />It is true location, location. Por Que No and A Pizza Scholls a stones throw away. Cana Connection across the street.<br />Both locations are open for take away or take out orders.','Extremely Desirable-neighborhood. Keep Portland WEIRD is the city Motto. It will not disappoint. You will be in the heart of the weirdness. Just open the front door. Bike lanes abound and top reviewed highly rated eating and drinking establishments for your foodie fix.<br />We have a bike to use for you. Sometimes 2 bikes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/07939e74-2d45-431d-b6bd-acabc7b73fab.jpg',90701654,8,'45.51159','-122.61483',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,2,30,179,4.91,19910312),(915,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19928912','Vintage-Modern Large Hawthorne Suite. A+ location','Live like a local; bring your walking shoes. You\'ll love the vibrant convenience of our location and the serene comfort of the apartment itself. We\'re an easy 20 minute Uber from the airport (PDX).  Explore all that Hawthorne, Division, Belmont and our lovely city and region have to offer. Our place is suitable for singles, couples, small groups, families and business travelers.','Close to everything! Truly the beating heart of SE Portland with the core of Hawthorne mere footsteps away. <br />Multiple coffee roasters and cafes (great for people watching) including one in a double-decker bus<br />Vintage and locally designed clothing shopping<br />Boutiques, a wonderful toy store and many novelty and gift shops<br />Restaurants within easy walking distance include vegan and vegetarian food, a famous donut shop, french pasteries, Thai, Vietnamese, Indian, Sushi, Pizza, fine and casual dining in abundance, multiple varied food-carts, two major grocery stores within blocks, too too many food options to name...<br />Several pubs, Cider bar, Cocktail lounge, happy-hours galore.<br />Division restaurant row <br />Belmont nightlife and boutique shops are each 8 blocks away<br /><br />Two Rental bike stations are within three blocks in two directions','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTk5Mjg5MTI%3D/original/269bd393-541f-4c38-b8c2-1549821b18cc.jpeg',1743188,8,'45.51178','-122.6319',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,99.00,2,28,298,4.90,19928912),(916,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19949395','TheBuffaloBee-Private Suite+Balcony-Clean & Quiet!','This unit was built recently, specifically for short term renters. It is a Private guest suite with a full kitchen for preparing meals or just coffee/tea which is provided. It is has all of the amenities you might need. My second story unit has a private entrance and is quiet. It is in a safe, friendly neighborhood. It has a beautiful elevated Queen bed. It has a great NW facing Balcony, that is covered and has a table and chairs. It is peaceful and thoughtfully furnished.','Arbor Lodge Neighborhood is very Walkable and has great access to Downtown, Kenton, St Johns areas. There is Arbor Lodge Park 3 blocks away and Kenton Park about 7 blocks away. The Kenton area has Coffee Shops, Restaurants, Unique Stores, Antique Shop, Liquor Store, Laundromat, a Convieneince Store, Bars and lots of Fun stuff to do!  The Famous Kenton Paul Bunyan Statue, which has a BRAND NEW Coat of Paint on him, is about a 5-10 minute walk away. .','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cbe1969b-d045-4f8a-bf99-9ee0d62acec4.jpg',11740189,51,'45.57515','-122.68669',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,81.00,3,29,168,4.98,19949395),(917,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/19952673','Portland Home with garden','Home with private back yard and off street parking. Plenty of space with 5 bedrooms, and a basement.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7c041922-0e2d-4549-a70f-a95114966074.jpg',20413267,19,'45.55001','-122.63231',1,7,2.50,5.00,5.00,275.00,30,1125,7,4.71,19952673),(918,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20001164','Alberta Arts Cob Oven Home','Welcome to Alberta Arts District--one of Portland\'s coolest neighborhoods. You can walk to art galleries, fine and casual dining, New Seasons grocery, the soaking pools, movies and bars at the Kennedy School or cook in our wood-fired cob pizza oven.','Excellent shopping and restaurants, art galleries. Kennedy school offers a Japanese soaking tub and movie theater.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5b300483-78e1-41ab-9e9f-6d0d658dbef3.jpg',7316008,1,'45.56022','-122.63343',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,90.00,30,1125,79,4.85,20001164),(919,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20027335','Bedroom in Hip Mississippi neighborhood home','Bedroom right in the middle of Mississippi neighborhood. Chill in living room or backyard, if you can peel yourself away from the tons of great restaurants, coffee shops, boutiques, & breweries nearby - Portland spirit!<br /><br />Public transit very close - both MAX & bus lines. About 10 min drive (and 20 min on bus) from Downtown hot spots like Powell\'s Books and Voodoo Donuts. Very close to other busy hangouts like N Williams Ave, Interstate, N Killingsworth and NE Alberta Street.','In the city that likes to “keep it weird,” Travel Portland has coined the phrase, \"You can, in Portland.\" North Portland is a prime example with delicious meals, tax-free shopping, one-of-a-kind bars and much more off the beaten path. Enjoy live music, tons of local shops, popular restaurants, breweries and great hang out spots on N. Mississippi Ave, one block from home. The many independent retailers of North Mississippi Avenue reflect Portland\'s eclectic tastes and DIY ethic. North Mississippi provides this vibrant neighborhood with ample watering holes and entertainment, one of the city\'s best concentrations of quality craft beers and brewpubs, and lots of yummy eateries.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/49cee141-d676-41ad-93cc-b4fdf6c38d18.jpg',3220022,9,'45.55001','-122.67587',2,1,2.00,1.00,1.00,39.00,14,1125,80,4.81,20027335),(920,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20035331','The Copper Flat - Walkable, Creative & Private!','Welcome to Copper Flat. Pull up a woven chair at the rose gold-accented bistro table and refuel for a day of exploring the historic Mississippi district. This zen ground-floor guest suite combines a pared-back color palette with quirky ornaments and eye-catching artwork. Accepting guests and implementing extra cleaning protocols. Excellent wireless internet speeds!<br /><br />We\'d love to have you. Book your stay today!','The Mississippi neighborhood has quickly become one of Portland\'s most coveted foodie areas, with such names as Por Que No, Ox, Gravy, Samurai Blue, and Mee Sen minutes from the doorstep. Great breweries, coffee shops and lots of shopping too! Portlands Original Food Carts are just a block away!!! Reach downtown in just minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/272921d0-aa21-469c-9d31-ed17b2922593.jpg',6416589,9,'45.55305','-122.67727',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,1,1125,736,4.96,20035331),(921,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20055813','Stylish North Portland home with beautiful view','Step into a Portland design magazine! Unobstructed Willamette River, bridge & Forest Park views from the kitchen, living room & back patios! Every inch of this home is bright, fresh and stylishly maximized.<br /><br />Steps from University of Portland, easy access to Downtown Portland, and an easy walk to the heart of St. Johns','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7055f1fb-7a67-429e-ae1a-7a081a067040.jpg',10514300,57,'45.58','-122.74061',1,6,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,1125,128,4.71,20055813),(922,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20057131','Piedmont Private Retreat','Located in North Portland\'s Piedmont Neighborhood, this newly constructed retreat has everything one would need while enjoying their time in Portland.   It\'s 780 square feet, two floors, and set back from the street with a private entrance.  High-end appliances, stainless steel countertops, local furniture and metalwork, queen bed, work space, full size washer & dryer, and A/C on both levels.  Walking distance to light rail, bus, restaurants, parks, grocery and more.','The newly constructed retreat is located in the Piedmont neighborhood. There are lots of single family houses and beautiful, historic Peninsula Park with a huge rose garden, sports fields, outdoor pool, playground and splash park. It\'s a 5-10 minute walk to public transportation, grocery stores, restaurants, and more.  The location is easily accessible from I-5 and functions as a convenient launching point for lots of local and regional site seeing/adventures.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/632cf373-4411-4e24-adf8-31d3b8d174b7.jpg',94888093,48,'45.57432','-122.67782',1,2,1.50,1.00,0.00,0.00,31,90,101,5.00,20057131),(923,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20067366','Restored Buckman Craftsman-your perfect home base`','Enjoy entire 1905 Old Portland house in Portland\'s historic, vibrant, walkable Buckman neighborhood, 20 blocks from downtown. Inside beautifully restored. Spacious, private decks. Walk to unique shops on Portland\'s eastside. Walk to award winning restaurants, PDX’s coffee, craft beer scene and dispensaries. Ocean, mountains, great wineries nearby. Super clean, warm and inviting inside and out. Perfectly cozy inside with professional espresso machine and a beautiful gas fired “wood stove.”','Buckman is a diverse neighborhood with many single family homes, loads of excellent restaurants, coffee shops and brew pubs.  It is a wonderful walking and biking neighborhood.  Public transportation is a few blocks away.  This is one of Portland’s famous walkable neighborhoods: within a short walkable distance you’ll find all your needs from medical care to excellent ethnic restaurants to coffee/pastry shops to affordable movie theaters to yummy craft ice cream. Hard to imagine you won’t find something wonderful to tickle your fancy.  There is even a quaint old movie theater nearby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-20067366/original/bcfa3adf-9d2c-41a7-a3bb-e70f1a616609.jpg',2644422,32,'45.51995','-122.64263',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,193.00,3,1125,214,4.99,20067366),(924,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20074833','Kelly\'s Cottage, A Modern SE Portland Guest House!','Welcome to Kelly\'s Cottage, a beautiful guest house in SE Portland, Oregon! It includes a private entrance and driveway to park your vehicle. <br />Enjoy your own private side yard with a grill - you can relax outside and barbecue if you\'d like. <br />Kelly\'s Cottage is a short drive from downtown Portland and only three blocks from public transportation (the MAX line and bus stops). <br />It was recently renovated and is newly furnished. <br />You will have security and privacy in this charming suite!','The property is located in Portland\'s Brooklyn neighborhood.<br /><br />Brooklyn is in a great location as it is in close proximity to some of Portland\'s most hip and popular neighborhoods such as Sellwood, Hawthorne and Clinton. Residents have plenty of coffee, pub and dining options just a stones throw away in most cases across several adjoining neighborhoods. <br /><br />Brooklyn is definitely a favorite and in-demand Portland neighborhood and feels very community friendly, safe and family focused.  Dog walkers, runners, babes in strollers and people of all sorts busy the streets.  Brooklyn, like most of its close-by sister neighborhoods, is fiercely independent and has a high number of locally owned businesses who thrive due to overwhelming local support.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/044e2209-aa6f-4546-8cdb-11a1f4ab6fd9.jpg',32292601,56,'45.49174','-122.6497',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,69.00,1,31,178,4.89,20074833),(925,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20124460','Cedar Grove Cottage with Superhost near Airport!','Bright, private, 2-bedroom guest suite on main level of home in a recently-remodeled bungalow 7-10 minutes from the airport. Quiet residential neighborhood close to public transport, the Grotto, Rocky Butte, and restaurants/shops on Sandy Blvd. Easy access to the Gorge hikes on 1-84! Two comfy queen mattresses. Modern full kitchen & appliances. Free access to shared laundry space. Distant view of Mt. St. Helens on a sunny day from the big, beautiful garden in the backyard.','Quiet, friendly neighborhood within walking distance to the gorgeous Grotto. Nearby public parks include Johnson Lake Property, Sacajawea City Park and Rocky Butte Natural Area (that\'s an extinct volcano)! You can catch a glimpse of Mount Saint Helens from the backyard and around the neighborhood on a cloudless day. Those with a car will enjoy quick, easy access to the beautiful Columbia River Gorge/Multnomah Falls area for endless hiking, as this listing is on the East side of town close to the I-84 freeway.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7f9d284a-f046-4881-b33f-e1649b6114a6.jpg',2215281,80,'45.55738','-122.57237',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,217,4.98,20124460),(926,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20133878','Executive Gem In the Heart of Hawthorne','Executive Gem in the Heart of Hawthorne and Belmont Arts and Restaurant District.  This is the ideal place to start your adventure in Portland.  Ideal for one or two people wanting to have longer stays in the city.','A neighborhood of shops along SE Hawthorne Boulevard. It\'s offbeat with overtones and undercurrents of funky.  Many restaurants, vintage clothing stores and breakfast locations.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/98697cb5-8c2c-4159-bcb3-fb3df4650804.jpg',2086378,32,'45.51424','-122.63817',1,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,123.00,4,31,101,5.00,20133878),(927,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20167870','Explore Portland on Foot from Your Modern Retreat','Welcome to The LoftHaus. Stroll through a luscious landscaped garden and past a bubbling fountain to reach this light-filled, creative living space. A roll-up glass garage door in the bedroom offers a connection with the outside world while flooding the room with natural light. Accepting guests and implementing extra cleaning protocols. Excellent wireless internet speeds!','The Mississippi neighborhood has quickly become one of Portland\'s most coveted foodie areas, with such names as Por Que No, Tasty and Sons, Ox, Gravy, Samurai Blue, and Mee Sen minutes from the doorstep. Great breweries, coffee shops and lots of shopping too! Portlands Original Food Carts are just a block away!!! Reach downtown in just minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6c4dec82-214e-4d0f-802b-3499c4c0072a.jpg',6416589,9,'45.55462','-122.67702',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,108.00,1,1125,839,4.97,20167870),(928,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20193247','Welcoming 1 bedrm eco tiny house near NE Alberta.','All are welcome to enjoy our sweet and eco-friendly tiny house. Nearby are NE Alberta, Williams and Mississippi Districts- high walkability score!! Enjoy organic bedding and towels, efficient cooling and heating, bamboo flooring, local/Fair Trade art- a cozy space for guests to enjoy Portland\'s best!  We (and our renters and their sweet dog, who sometimes is in the yard) live in the main house on the property. Try out tiny house living-Come enjoy our sweet place and welcome to Portland!','Our neighborhood is just plain old amazing. First, it is transit friendly- with several bus lines and the Max to connect you anywhere. What other city neighborhood has coffee shops, all kinds of ethnic food carts and restaurants, a library, art studios, is both walking and bike friendly, has Peninsula Park with stunning trees and roses, great diversity, a local grocery store, award winning restaurants all within minutes? It is also a 9 minute drive to Forest Park, USA\'s largest city forested park, by the way. Also, the Columbia Gorge and downtown are easily accessible. There is a City orange rental bike rack and a full bike rental shop a few blocks away. Explore bike friendly Portland or hop on the bus/Max (lightrail) -blocks away to zip downtown in minutes or walk just a few blocks to artsy Alberta/Mississippi neighborhood. (Our neighborhood rated high on walkability/bike-ability. ) Local food/sites: Great ethnic and vegan food carts at Piedmont Station, PCC Cascade Campus, Peninsula ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c057cb1e-3008-4e91-8cca-75e95644f63f.jpg',24551609,14,'45.56161','-122.66386',1,2,1.00,1.00,4.00,82.00,2,30,376,4.98,20193247),(929,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20195374','Private hot tub in beautiful Rose City','This freshly renovated 1-bedroom apartment offers you a relaxing retreat in the Rose City Park neighborhood, which is in the heart of the city with easy access to parks, nightlife, and downtown.','Rose City Park is a quiet residential neighborhood that is nestled beside the beautiful 18 hole Rose City Golf Course. There is a walking path around the golf course, which makes for a nice way to unwind and get some exercise. The walking path leads to Rose City Park which has a playground for little ones, tennis courts, basketball courts, and baseball/soccer fields. It is also a short walk over to Sandy Boulevard where you can visit local restaurants and bars, a grocery store, a local wine shop, urgent care, pharmacy, and other cute local businesses. NE Fremont St is a short 5 minute drive away which features countless boutique shops, restaurants, cafes, and bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cb9cbac2-635c-46f3-bbf8-b71ad11694f6.jpg',42731803,39,'45.54218','-122.59002',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,103.00,2,28,422,4.91,20195374),(930,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20211007','Luxurious Cape Cod in Central Eastside','Recently remodeled cozy cape cod with the entire upper floor for your use. Lot\'s of comfy furnishings including a memory foam bed and double futon, as well as a dinette, refrigerator/freezer, microwave and coffee, and a luxurious marble and tile bath.','The neighborhood is super quiet and friendly. Right between Burnside and Stark, you\'ll have easy access to shopping, the freeway, both Laurelhurst Park and Mt. Tabor, the amazing Hawthorne shopping experience, plus way too many incredible restaurants to choose from - many within walking distance. A QFC grocery store (with a Starbucks) is just 2 blocks away, and a Fred Meyer just a mile away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-20211007/original/adfad3cd-ea60-4e19-9a6a-27d28ecbcbf1.jpg',143962583,15,'45.52137','-122.6105',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,51.00,1,16,434,4.96,20211007),(931,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20214662','Quick\'s Cozy Cottage','Very nice one bedroom basement apartment.  It has refrigerator  and stove, and washer, and dryer.  On Mississippi Ave','www.mississippiave.com','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/843e5bff-faad-4e20-8023-d7e114e4b238.jpg',139135055,24,'45.558','-122.67728',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,2,1125,78,4.83,20214662),(932,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20254543','Handcrafted Hempcrete Home w/ Backyard Spa Oasis','Welcome to the basecamp tinyhouse, nestled in our spacious backyard oasis. You\'ll completely forget you\'re in the city! Perfect for one or two, the tinyhouse has a cozy bed, an office space, closet space, and a fully stocked kitchenette. Just out the front door, enjoy our covered outdoor bathroom, sauna, bathtubs, and fireplace. I built it all myself and would be delighted to share it’s magic with you!','The Portland Cully Neighborhood is a culturally diverse urban neighborhood with a mix of commercial and residential developments. There is a strong sense of community and active neighborhood involvement in fruitful and joyous collaboration.<br /><br />We are nestled conveniently between the airport and some of the weirdest (that\'s a good thing) spots in town. Our Cully neighborhood offers nice retreat after a busy day in the city. Less traffic, less hustle, more trees, and free parking ;)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjAyNTQ1NDM%3D/original/33369e6c-d6bf-4f37-9926-363b2f6e82d5.jpeg',15152314,21,'45.56111','-122.60371',1,2,2.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,730,286,4.93,20254543),(933,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20257538','Private Handcrafted Cottage','Stay in this stunning craftsman cottage that is brand new and where almost every detail was thoughtfully designed and uniquely handcrafted. The cottage is tucked away on the other side of the block from my home so you’ll have your own private entrance/driveway. Max light rail is 10 minutes away on foot, and you can walk to the heart of Mississippi in under 25. The unit also features many amenities, including high-speed Internet connection; flat screen TV; and a well-appointed kitchenette.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/45965d80-6950-4a18-ac9f-da4e8fd1fbe2.jpg',13376106,48,'45.57491','-122.67527',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,84.00,2,30,452,4.95,20257538),(934,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20270387','Old World Elegance-3 room suite, private entrance','Huge/200 sf. elegant bedroom with vaulted cedar ceiling and private entrance/French doors to patio,  bathroom with shower and  sitting room with a cozy table/workspace. French doors to back patio, private entrance. Queen bed, rocking chair, TV w/ premium channels,  mini fridge, microwave, snack basket,  electric kettle, french press coffee maker, coffee/tea bags/sugar, fresh milk, cold drinks,  mugs/bowls/plates/glasses, neighborhood guide.','I live in the Reed neighborhood, very near Sellwood/Westmoreland and Woodstock neighborhoods.  Both are trendy, thriving urban neighborhoods full of restaurants, bars, and shops, however we live between the two, and where we live it\'s quiet and serene. <br /><br />Our neighborhood is sometimes called \'Pleasantville\' by the neighbors. Houses are painted various colorful shades, and the neighbors are lovely and friendly. We are truly an oasis right the heart of quirky and eclectic Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20270387/original/9a0183fb-b31e-4aed-bfb2-bed7ac905414.png',5341424,61,'45.48309','-122.62939',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,55.00,1,15,235,4.97,20270387),(935,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20282301','NoPotel, comfortable guesthouse in Portland!','NoPotel is a newly built, contemporary space nestled in NoPo (that\'s North Portland for out-of-towners) in the hip, laid-back St. Johns area. We\'ve designed this work/live space with you and your comfort in mind. It\'s just a short walk to coffee shops, cafés and bars.','St. John’s has a rich and colorful history. It’s nestled about 10 mins north of the big city, 1.5 hrs from the coast, and 45 mins - 1.5 hrs from wine country, Mount Hood, and hiking/wine tasting in the Gorge. Although, not recommended doing hiking and wine tasting together! We’ve seen our small town of St. John\'s come alive over the past 10 years. There are pizza shops, coffee shops, bars, eateries, food carts, clothing consign shops, antique shops, and niche shops. There are three incredible classic Pacific NW parks within walking distance. We have two movie theaters in walking distance. One of the famous McMenamin\'s is here in town and offers dinner while you watch a movie. Every Saturday during seasonal months there\'s a Farmer\'s Market in the square where farmers, local artisans, musicians, and neighbors gather to mingle, eat and share their bounty.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/858ec536-e68b-4c5b-bece-df03dd8be008.jpg',16155383,58,'45.59394','-122.75073',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,97.00,2,26,326,4.97,20282301),(936,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20300889','★Modern Nob Hill Getaway★','Bright, spacious basement apartment located in beautiful, walkable Nob Hill. Close to many of Portland\'s finest coffee, donut, dining and ice cream establishments with easy public transport/ride share access to all of Portland’s great neighborhoods. This modern getaway has polished concrete floors, an open kitchen with stainless appliances, Portland-centric decorations and everything you need to enjoy your Pacific Northwest getaway! Perfect for a couple, a couple of couples or a small family.','The apartment is in a mixed residential neighborhood at the edge of Slabtown, Nob Hill and Wallace Park - only two blocks from Forest Park. Many of Portland\'s finest cafes, restaurants and bars are within a short walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6f7b6e31-c87d-410b-9a2e-811823679b8d.jpg',13008180,27,'45.5359','-122.70735',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,117.00,2,30,398,4.97,20300889),(937,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20308030','Mid Century Portland Sanctuary.','Modern mid century boho chic two bedroom unit in a gorgeous private craftsman bungalow home  built in 1906. The unit is spacious, cool and provides ample room for a cozy stay with a spacious porch and dining room.Both bedrooms are outfitted with tempurpedic mattresses and clean white linens and towels and accented with local Pendleton prints. Guests are free to share the spacious backyard which is landscaped with beautiful plants and furniture for you to feel right at home.','Piedmont is s perfect location right between key neighborhoods in the Northeast. You can walk over to Dekum Triangle where the famous local Breakside brewery is located or take a stroll to the Alberta Arts district which is peppered with shops and restaurants. Also a stone throw is the Boise neighborhood of Williams street  and very popular Mississippi street where there are plenty of music venues and restaurants. 15 minute uber ride and you can find yourself either in Southeast on the well known Hawthorne and Burnside streets. And last but not least 15 minutes and you are on the west side so really it\'s an ideal location to move from while in Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0ba4e331-3ac0-44d8-b250-5bb55b5c568a.jpg',9078003,14,'45.5647','-122.6626',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,446.00,1,1125,38,4.84,20308030),(938,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20322456','Bright new home near pubs, parks and University!','This new home compliments many of the bungalows built in University Park in the 1920\'s from the outside.  Inside a Master suite on the main floor is arranged peacefully in the back of the home.  A large flat yard with makes a great place to BBQ and hang out.  Upstairs provides a full bath with open layout providing a two queen beds with privacy screen as well as a full bed for children, work desk and plenty of windows.  Modern kitchen with with open living floor plan and table for 6.','This neighborhood is 7 miles from downtown Portland.  Its in the neighborhood for the University of Portland, a small, private school and is surrounded by parks and a short bike ridge to Forest Park the largest urban forest in the US.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7bf75728-f836-4bf4-8f4f-1c85528436b9.jpg',8955868,57,'45.579','-122.72125',1,5,2.00,2.00,4.00,100.00,30,730,29,4.72,20322456),(939,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20325722','Location, Location UofP','.5 block from University of Portland and bus line.  Cozy private room with your own dedicated bathroom and living room.  Shared common kitchen area.  Ideal for visiting parents, professors and anyone looking to enjoy the many activities.','University of Portland','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-20325722/original/31ef5e1f-d46d-460c-b03d-cd2b13a477d0.jpeg',22344380,57,'45.57618','-122.72537',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,30,365,2,5.00,20325722),(940,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20327118','Stylish Craftsman Close to Downtown','Welcome to the William B. Waters House, a 1911 gem just across the Fremont Bridge from downtown, combining new renovation and modern amenities with the charm and character of vintage Portland. The home is in the historic Irvington neighborhood, 5 minutes to downtown, 5 minutes to the hot Alberta Arts District, and 5 minutes to the equally trendy Mississippi street restaurants, cafes and bars.','The Williams Waters House provides the best of both worlds. We are uniquely situated very close to downtown and hip east side neighborhoods, while also being tucked away on a quiet residential street next to a park. Our neighborhood, Irvington, is  an upscale, historic, architecturally splendid area, great for quiet walks or for getting downtown in a heartbeat.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-20327118-unapproved/original/d1fbfa88-27f6-441d-a9ea-b9fbe4d07d6d.JPEG',509244,7,'45.54465','-122.65721',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,137.00,1,29,431,4.99,20327118),(941,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20328717','Elegant SE Portland/Reed College BLUE MOON SUITE','The Blue Moon Suite is a cool, comfortable and convenient apartment within a home to stay if you\'re visiting Reed College, are in Portland for business (downtown is only 15 mins away) or if you are just touring the city. We look forward to welcoming you into our home and aim to make your stay as comfortable as possible while taking your privacy seriously & offering private access to an elegantly decorated yet comfortable one bedroom lower level apartment with everything that you might need.','Reed College is literally a stone\'s throw from our door which makes staying at the Blue Moon Suite very convenient for anyone - parents, potential new students, guests of the College - to visit the campus.  Woodstock Blvd, in the opposite direction, offers great restaurants, shops and a mellow but fun night life.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c535acdb-8e24-41a8-8bbb-3a577b9800ed.jpg',98837449,5,'45.47899','-122.62475',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,118.00,2,60,384,4.98,20328717),(942,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20335993','★ Bright, New In-law suite in PDX, Alberta Arts','Welcome to Portland!  This comfortable walk-in 8-ft ceiling basement has lots of room and light.  With a thick queen mattress, stainless steel kitchen and private laundry, you will have all you need in this newly constructed home.  It is on a quiet cul-de-sac but minutes to the vibrant and hip Alberta Arts District.','Alberta Arts district is home for some of the best of Portland!  Admire the district\'s murals and funky flair while hitting favorite food destinations like Salt & Straw and Hat Yai.  We are also quite close to the exciting areas of Mississippi St and Williams St.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0de0af3e-5f46-403d-8ab5-6e8560bdfc5c.jpg',65297739,29,'45.56226','-122.6511',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,112.00,1,29,119,4.80,20335993),(943,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20354598','Tiny house- Studio','Our newly built 220sq foot tiny house is nested in our backyard surrounded by lots of green. It is very quiet as well as private.<br />It has a comfortable bedroom with ample natural light, heat/ ac unit, spacious bathroom and fully equipped kitchen.','Our neighborhood is super quiet and yet very easy to access from the airport, downtown and other places in the city. <br />There are two beautiful parks within walking distance and even a short nature hike at Reed canyon just 10 minutes away from us.<br />Grocery and specialty stores nearby-  New Seasons, Grand central bakery, Otto\'s ( German deli ), Trader Joe\'s, Starbucks, and main convenience stores are 6-12 blocks away. <br /><br />Restaurants and Coffee shops- We live super close to the following busier commercial areas, Division, Hawthorne, Foster-Powell streets where you\'ll find a very interesting variety of cuisines, second hand stores or other funky little shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/25322c6a-d1cd-4d0f-8e45-20bffb94ff57.jpg',3645233,67,'45.49178','-122.61359',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,81.00,1,1125,372,4.83,20354598),(944,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20387779','Cozy Hideaway: Walk to Pittock Mansion & trails','This modern and private mother-in-law suite has a full kitchen, bath, and your own entrance so you can come and go as you please. Our home is located in Forest Park, surrounded by beautiful trees, and only 5 minutes from downtown. Easy access to the Japanese Gardens, Washington Park, Oregon Zoo, the Portland Children\'s Museum, and walking distance to the historic Pittock Mansion (a great spot for picnics and views) and trails. We also have a quiet porch and garden for full relaxation.','The west hills are a quiet, serene area that provides convenience to downtown, the west suburbs, and wine country. Pittock Mansion is right around the corner from the house, which is a wonderful place to walk around or to just sit and take in the city. Additionally, Forest Park is filled with hiking trails which can lead you right into NW Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjAzODc3Nzk%3D/original/3205a187-1fcc-4b52-aa16-c03305100598.jpeg',2967070,79,'45.52145','-122.72066',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,115.00,2,1125,215,4.89,20387779),(945,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20404043','Heart of NW Portland - Near Crystal Balllroom','Welcome to this bright, comfortable, clean, fully-furnished studio apartment located in a quintessential 1920\'s building with all the charm of that era. <br /><br />Original porcelain sinks, tub, hardwood floors and penny tiles. We love the antique look and decorated it with vintage finds from all over Portland. <br /><br />It is very close to  Powell\'s Books, Crystal Ballroom, Brewery Blocks, the Pearl district, the Timber\'s Stadium.  Max train - 2 blocks away, bikes and scooters around the corner!','The neighborhood is amazing! You are 2-3 blocks away from the Pearl district which is the fanciest part of Portland with stores and the famous Powell\'s bookstore. There are a ton of cafes and restaurants, bars, and vegan spots nearby. <br /><br />To the west you are a 10 minute walk away from the entrance to the massive Washington Park where you can see both the Rose garden and Japanese Garden. There are tennis courts and spectacular views. <br /><br />The Northwest is sprinkled with funky old homes. M bar, on 21st, is a sweet nyc sized and reminiscent full bar with indoor and outdoor seating. Right down the street is art house cinema 21.  2 blocks up to 23rd avenue is Henry Higgins Boiled Bagels-- another reminiscent nyc jewish deli: white fish salad, fresh made bagels, etc. yum! Stroll along 23rd for the fancier shops and a ton of restaurant offerings.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/af01e37c-bd5d-4880-9266-43f83c727636.jpg',12299929,3,'45.52262','-122.6876',1,1,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,7,4.86,20404043),(946,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20420420','3BR/6 guest home in Sellwood - new winter pricing!','Comfortable 3 bedroom home in a great location, steps from restaurants, shopping, and public transport. You will not be disappointed! Our 1920s house is beautifully renovated and has a peaceful, private backyard for you to enjoy. We live in the best spot in Sellwood!  Step out the door and enjoy the convenience of many local amenities.  Want to stay in?  Our backyard is park-like, pleasant and private. Relax in the hammock, have a BBQ, or chill on the covered back porch. Maximum 6 guests/night.','Sellwood is one of the best neighborhoods in Portland.  It is a sweet little suburb located 15 minutes from downtown.  We have amazing dining, cool bars, a movie theater and nice walking space.  The house is located in a prime spot to take it all in!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20420420/original/e31b5bb2-918d-424e-8e2d-f8ca1a28e233.jpeg',46324976,20,'45.473341337808016','-122.65052036955608',1,6,2.00,3.00,3.00,275.00,5,179,31,4.97,20420420),(947,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20426737','Hawthorne Hood*Private Bath*Garden Suite*','*Please confirm you are a non-smoker and that you are amenable to the \"Other Things To Note\" info when you send a booking request.* <br /><br />Walk Score 93!  Beautiful home in the heart of one of the best dining areas in Portland! Dozens of restaurants within walking distance. Primary suite with private bathroom. Easy free street parking. No third party bookings allowed.<br /><br />I also rent out a second master suite upstairs just down the hall. It may be occupied during your stay.','93 Walk Score and 100 Bike Score! Live like a local! This is a wonderful and highly coveted Portland neighborhood with incredible restaurants, bars, brew pubs, wine bars and great tax free shopping at locally owned boutiques and vintage shops, all within between 3-20 minutes walking distance. The nearest coffee shop is a 3 minute walk away but there are several others nearby, <br />The nearest restaurant/bar is also 3 minutes away but dozens within 5-20 minutes walk.  Plenty of great shops on both Hawthorne and Division! There are countless options for dining.  Downtown is about 10 minutes by car, the airport is about 20 minutes by car.   My street is very quiet and parking is easy.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/302445e1-1f25-4f27-9842-2efd5738d885.jpg',1096266,8,'45.50598','-122.61499',2,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,66.00,1,27,78,4.99,20426737),(948,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20427061','2 BR Family Friendly Luxury Suite in SE Woodstock','Constructed in 2017, enjoy our spacious 800-square-foot, private lower level apartment in our 1910 arts and crafts home in cozy Woodstock neighborhood in inner SE Portland. A short walk to Woodstock restaurants and grocery stores. Close to Reed College, Sellwood, SE Division and SE Hawthorne shops and restaurants. A short 20 min drive into downtown Portland and one block away from public transit.  Comfortably sleeps up to 5 max. Height in some areas might inconvenience guests over 6\'.','Our home is situated on a very quiet street in the Woodstock Neighborhood. No traffic noise here!  We are walking distance (1/2 mile)  to 3 neighborhood grocery stores, 15 restaurants,  2 coffee shops and a bakery. There is plenty of creative and diverse Portland cuisine a short stroll from the house.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/addf4972-d991-4cca-8452-75114aff5163.jpg',21427983,38,'45.48464','-122.6185',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,119.00,1,30,477,4.95,20427061),(949,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20436612','Hot Tub, Secluded Getaway In the City.','Your own separate remodeled carriage house on unique lot. Hot tub nestled beneath tree canopy.  Large landscaped fenced yard.  Near University of Portland.  Beautiful light and surrounded by giant trees.   2 min walk to Mock Crest bluff and  views of city skyline.  Romantic getaway.  Clawfoot tub. Laundry in unit.  Perfect for longer stays.  Near Historic Kenton, Mississippi neighborhoods, Alberta Arts district, and St Johns. Walk to  restaurants, coffee. Easy access to 5N/5S. 20 min to airport','Some of the best views of the city skyline and forest park along Willamette bluff two minute walk away.  Near New Seasons, bars, restaurants, local coffee shops, Starbucks as well.  Two blocks from wooded Columbia park and public pool.  Quick and easy access on and off I-5. Walk to University of Portland campus.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ab3eb964-6850-4e0e-978a-eb6c2f60078d.jpg',119485170,57,'45.57723','-122.71601',1,5,1.00,1.00,2.00,160.00,1,1125,873,4.76,20436612),(950,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20461290','Upscale quiet 2BR (1400sf)near downtown,pool table','Private  2 bedroom basement suite is located in an upscale & serene residential neighborhood full of  beautiful scenery. <br />It has  15 steps that leads down the hill to the entrance. It\'s the perfect spot if you\'re looking for a quiet getaway with the convenience of being a close drive to downtown, Nike, Intel, St. Vincent hospital. You’ll love our place because of its forest retreat charm, comfortable beds, luxurious kitchenette/bar with granite slabs, pool table, and plenty of space (1400 sqt).','Forest Heights is a upscale neighborhood, nestled in the hills west of downtown Portland. It has a beautiful community park with an oversized pond and a plethora of views . It is considered to be one of Portland\'s more desirable neighborhoods.<br />The commute is great, being only a 12-15 min. commute to Downtown Portland and a 15 min. commute in the opposite direction into Silicon Forest (Nike, Intel, etc). It is close to numerous parks and over six miles of hiking trails, including Forest Park, the 14th largest city park in the country.<br />There is village shopping center with restaurants and a Starbucks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a0f454e3-a0e8-4d9a-a71d-f936550c893b.jpg',1674967,81,'45.54594','-122.77272',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,106.00,2,21,92,4.87,20461290);
INSERT INTO `listings` VALUES (951,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20469907','Charming Cottage in park like setting','This charming cottage is located in a peaceful park like setting.  It has two bedrooms. You can enjoy s\'mores around the outdoor wood burning fire table, or a nice meal  on the patio BBQ area. A short walk takes you to the Leach botanical gardens, only a block away.  This beautiful garden  just received a 12.5 million dollar renewal. There is lots of outdoor space and a fenced backyard for your pet. (Pet fees apply.)','Quiet tree lined neighborhood a few hundred yards from the beautiful Leach Botanical Gardens.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjA0Njk5MDc%3D/original/97a4725a-05f0-4e4d-b5e7-65d992b0de36.jpeg',39925570,77,'45.47529','-122.5374',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,89.00,30,180,13,5.00,20469907),(952,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20477753','Garden Sanctuary near Airport with Superhost!','Sparkling new remodel! A light-filled, cozy, private downstairs guest suite apartment within a classic bungalow home 7-10 min from the airport. Backyard garden entrance, stylish bedroom, bathroom, and kitchenette. Quiet residential neighborhood close to public transport, the Grotto, Rocky Butte, and restaurants/shops on Sandy Blvd. Easy access to hike the Gorge from 1-84. Access to shared laundry room; renters live upstairs. Distant view of Mt. St. Helens from the backyard garden.','Quiet, friendly neighborhood within walking distance to the gorgeous Grotto. Nearby public parks include Johnson Lake Property, Sacajawea City Park and Rocky Butte Natural Area (that\'s an extinct volcano)! You can catch a glimpse of Mount Saint Helens from the backyard and around the neighborhood on a cloudless day. Car renters will enjoy quick, easy access to the beautiful Columbia River Gorge/Multnomah Falls area for endless hiking, as this listing is on the East side of town close to the I-84 freeway.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/01118d15-e69a-4da5-890b-82c1deff8a37.jpg',2215281,80,'45.55702','-122.57053',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,310,4.97,20477753),(953,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20479122','PDX Art Deco Lounge ~ Local Eateries, Bars & Shops','If you\'re a fan of great food, craft beer, pour-over coffee, this is your place. My apartment is situated in the famous Buckman District - which neighbors many of Portland\'s top-rated restaurants and bars, vintage shops, and offers some of the best people-watching around.<br /><br />My place is great for couples, solo adventures, and business travelers. With a convenient home base within walking distance to the neighborhood hot spots, you can get an authentic taste of how the hipsters live in Stumptown.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors—no chain restaurants here! Enjoy vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or opt for an elegant night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />But Portland isn’t just for foodies. The vibrant indie spirit of Hawthorne is alive with a multitude of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques, making it a true hipster haven. Catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of recreation, head up to Mt. Tabor. This 196-acre city park, located atop a dormant volcano vent, offers miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of the city, providing a perfect escape into nature righ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20479122/original/63d009a0-b0d8-4fef-b289-3be5d0a0409e.jpeg',146196024,32,'45.51725','-122.64051',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,72.00,1,1125,632,4.79,20479122),(954,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20498898','Charming, Basement Retreat-Popular NW Portland, OR','! LOCATION*LOCATION*LOCATION !<br />2 Bed-1 Bath-\"Private Basement\" in the Heart of N.W. Portland. Charming, Freshly Renovated- with Private Back Entrance-Basement is separated from House by a Locked Door.  Small Private Patio w/Table & Chairs & a Lovely community lawn area next to the patio & a BBQ to enjoy at your leisure.  Walk to Restaurants, Downtown PDX Shops, Stores, Buses, Streetcar, Nike Bikes & the Max Rail. 2 Blocks from The Famous 23rd St. Shopping. Complimentary on Street Parking Passes.','Popular NW(Alphabet District)-Friendly Eclectic Neighborhood-within Walking Distance to Downtown Portland, Restaurants & Breweries, Grocery Stores, including Fred Meyer & Trader Joe’s. Movie Theatre’s (Cinema 21) & Parks(and Dog Parks too) as well as Portland’s Streetcar, the Max rail system & Nike Bikes all within walking distance as well.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d0749fc1-977c-4776-819f-998c596aaacc.jpg',146344153,27,'45.52695','-122.69404',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,194.00,30,1125,166,4.92,20498898),(955,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20501442','Sleeping Beauty in Northwest Alpha. Near trails!!','Situated in Portland\'s NW Alphabet District in a quiet, friendly neighborhood, this Sleeping Beauty is very cozy yet spacious with that impeccably clean quality you desire. It\'s perfect for a restful retreat after a big day of activity. <br /><br />If you enjoy relaxing outside,  please feel welcome on the lovely garden patio located just outside your door.','Portland is where you\'ll find some of the best food on the planet! With more than 50 restaurants within a mile of Your Sleeping Beauty and world class art, music, theater, sports and special events happening all through the year in this part of town. There is never a lack of something to do. Need suggestions for something special? We\'re happy to help, and there\'s always plenty of up-to-date literature on events and hot spots to help you plan your day.<br /><br />Get Next to Nature<br />For a big dose of natural wonder, walk three  blocks from The apartment to Macleay Park, which is part of the largest and most beautiful urban forest in the Pacific Northwest. Our Forest Park system boasts over 30 miles of connected hiking trails as well as car free dirt roads for the hearty bicycle crowd.<br /><br />Is That All?<br />Need more excuses to visit our little paradise? Check out: Portland\'s Soccer team The Timbers, local GOLF, killer shopping, farmers markets, seasonal festivals, biking, ple','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/04489c87-2d83-4915-becc-56ac744fe73b.jpg',51019210,27,'45.53751','-122.71481',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,86.00,2,29,290,4.92,20501442),(956,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20524089','West Hills Room #1','10min drive to downtown and easy access to two frequent bus lines.  Walking distance to food carts, shops, restaurants, & brewery.','Hillsdale neighborhood is wonderful!  Close to shops and restaurants. <br /><br />Walking distance:<br /><br />Gigi\'s Cafe which has amazing breakfast.  Homemade fried chicken and waffles are amazing.  Liege waffles too!<br /><br />Sugar and Spice Bakery have delicious pastries and they even have a separate store a couple doors down for cupcakes!<br /><br />Verde Cocina is not your ordinary Mexican food spot. They offer a high quality, traditional and healthy menu of farm-to-table items and Paleo options.  Very Portland!<br /><br />One word: Starbucks <br /><br />Craving beer?  Portland is internationally known for it\'s breweries!  Just walk down a couple blocks and you\'ll find Sasquatch Brewery!<br /><br />Food Carts: Portland is nationally known for its high quality and quantity of food carts. A few blocks away enjoy burgers, incredible bento, Thai food and the best grilled cheese sandwiches ever.<br /><br />Several other restaurants as well.<br /><br />Hiking, running and biking: Th','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20524089/original/6bf3ada5-4c45-46eb-97fe-7100c9fa9cc6.jpeg',153132135,31,'45.48033','-122.69923',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,37.00,1,365,247,4.68,20524089),(957,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20538927','Private Studio Apartment Close to Downtown','I am conveniently located 2 miles from downtown Portland.  Has a private bathroom  and private entrance. Comfortable for one or two people. High quality queen bed. Has access to a small deck that gets partial sun. Easy access to the public transportation and .5 miles to the nearest bus stop. Special care taken to sanitize the room. Dedicated high speed internet.','It is a peaceful neighborhood. It is well lit at night. We have a neighborhood watch program in place.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2c14b3c8-df1f-48d7-8e39-0cb151dd028c.jpg',44474897,22,'45.48995','-122.67847',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,30,60,609,4.95,20538927),(958,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20591246','Modern private room in quiet NE Neighborhood','The private space is located in the upper level inside our home with a shared entrance. There are 2 bedrooms and 1 bathroom. There is a small refrigerator, coffee/tea only - no microwave or kitchen use. It will be reserved for your exclusive use during your stay. If you book for 1 to 2 people you will have the use of 1 bedroom and bathroom. If you would like to utilize both bedrooms then book for 3 people. You will automatically be charged the $15 extra for the other room when you do this.','We are in a wonderful, quiet neighborhood just 2 blocks away from a park with tennis courts and playground. There are restaurants, coffee shops, food carts all within walking distance.  Walking paths nearby with beautiful views of golf course and Mt Hood. Close access to I-84 as well. Rose City Golf Course open to the public year round is within blocks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a036f6e2-a3f1-4433-9470-22c00ff5ebd4.jpg',23416496,11,'45.54162','-122.59845',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,49.00,2,14,270,4.93,20591246),(959,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20603233','Miller Street Sellwood Garden Apartment','Cozy one-bedroom basement apartment in a quiet neighborhood. Queen-bed. Decorated with art from my travels in Turkey, Colombia, China and Egypt with descriptions in the AirBNB binder. No stove but small refrigerator, microwave and toaster and sink.  Cabinet with plates, cups, silverware.  Board and card games in cabinet below the TV.  Have Hulu, Netflix, and Prime Video for your entertainment.  Your own washer-dryer in the unit.','Sellwood is a family-friendly neighborhood with sidewalks that take you to good restaurants and quality public transportation. There is a farmer\'s market on Wednesday-May to October-, New Seasons Organic Food Market close by, and breweries and wine bars.  Reed College is within a five-minute drive. Crystal Springs that flows through Westmoreland Park has been converted to a Salmon Sanctuary three blocks away. There is also a nature park for children that uses natural materials for kids to play on.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6717298c-c7c3-46e5-9d61-3a099db2aad6.jpg',109799233,20,'45.4657','-122.64413',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,79.00,2,14,328,4.95,20603233),(960,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20608009','Discounted entire apartment garden patio & parking','This is a bright and modern additional living space in my beautiful hilltop home. Located just 5 minutes from downtown Portland in the West Hills, close to the best that Portland has to offer. There is a separate staircase leading to a private entrance, with outdoor living space including edible garden. Walk outside and enjoy your own private deck and read a book in a lovely garden and water feature. Forested hiking trails are located within a few minutes\' walk.','A stones throw to OHSU.  5 minutes to the amazing Rose garden, Japanese Gardens, Lan Su (botanical) Chinese Garden, the Portland waterfront, Oregon Zoo, Council Crest Park, Pittock Mansion(best view of the city) Multnonah falls, Portland Art Museum, OMSI, OHSU,  Powells Books (largest independent chain of bookstores in the world), 31 microbreweries, shopping downtown (tax free), coffee shops, bakeries, famous Salt & Straw ice cream & fun Voodoo donuts, great variety of food carts, AMAZING restaurants, Portland has 6 James Beard awarded Chefs with restaurants.<br />Just 2 minutes to trail heads into the gorgeous Forest Park for hiking & running trail.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bef768c4-df3d-4a5d-98ab-ec2398c84121.jpg',147284022,54,'45.50683','-122.69772',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,130.00,1,300,73,4.96,20608009),(961,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20621667','Stare out at the Treetops on an Extinct Volcano Mountainside','Spend a few hours reclining in a canary-yellow Adirondack chair on the covered porch. Scandinavian styling in gray, white, and yellow creates an equally cheerful feel inside. A polished concrete shower and kitchen breakfast bar are cute additions.','The north slope of Mount Tabor is a great basecamp for exploring the city. Morning walks to the summit serve up epic mountain views. Stop by Coquine for some of the area\'s best food, and the Cheese Bar for artisanal cheese and beers.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-20621667/original/fcd44672-f98b-4766-85ea-04738a316035.jpg',552766,15,'45.52188','-122.59373',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,99.00,30,365,71,4.97,20621667),(962,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20678018','Cozy Haven in Spacious House w/ Backyard Spa Oasis','Welcome to Basecamp! A spacious, cozy community house where you can relax after your Portland adventures. This unique short-term room rental offers the perfect blend of privacy and community. As the only room we rent to short-term guests, you\'ll likely meet some of our fun-loving housemates who are happy to ensure you have a great stay.<br /><br />The skylight in the room has blinds and window has blackout curtains.','The Portland Cully Neighborhood is a culturally diverse urban neighborhood with a mix of commercial and residential development. There is a strong sense of community and active neighborhood involvement in fruitful and joyous collaboration.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjA2NzgwMTg%3D/original/c4807fa1-f1ed-43c9-b088-9974072e85e6.jpeg',15152314,21,'45.5569','-122.60039',2,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,59.00,1,730,30,5.00,20678018),(963,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20692714','A Viewpoint By The River','Located in the heart of John\'s Landing in SW Portland. Everything you could want is close by. Walk to the waterfront walking trails, parks, to downtown, the tram, south waterfront along the Willamette River. Hop on a variety of public transit/ available only a block or 2 away. The city center a 5 minute drive. There\'s great shops, coffee/cafe\'s, pubs and restaurants in the area and easy access to all areas of PDX. This is one of the most desirable, in demand, enjoyable neighborhoods in Portland!','This neighborhood is filled with great people and places. Your in the city but it\'s remarkably relaxed so it\'s a great place/area to unwind after a busy day. The house is close to the river for walking/biking, rent kayaks, etc. The city of Portland is like a mini SF or Seattle but easier to navigate,  known for their breweries, food carts, and outdoor activities that will keep you occupied in your free time.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20692714/original/4fbdcf2c-b5b4-44ee-9020-a7d32e77c531.jpeg',22613181,22,'45.48549','-122.6778',1,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,74.00,30,90,28,4.82,20692714),(964,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20709084','Amazing 1BR Granny Flat Nestled near Rocky Butte','This one bedroom \"granny\" flat apartment is light, bright and recently renovated. It\'s a great place to relax and get cozy yet be close enough to experience all that Portland has to offer. If you enjoy the snow and want to ski, snowboard or snowshoe the mountain is within an hour of Portland. Even better, if you don\'t want to drive you can catch the shuttle bus from the near by transit center up to the resorts.','The apartment is located in the Madison South neighborhood. It has easy access to both I-84 and I-205 and just minutes from Portland International Airport (PDX). It is located within the vicinity of Rockey Butte and the newly opened park, Gateway Green.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d071210b-eab2-401c-b1d5-ad3d3ecd47c7.jpg',148253043,74,'45.53719','-122.56731',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,2,29,297,4.97,20709084),(965,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20710225','Henry Hill Guest Loft - Private and Convenient','Design and vintage enthusiast homeowner created private guest loft space with comfort in mind.  Walking distance to Woodstock and Sellwood neighborhoods with coffee shops, restaurants, and vintage stores. Closer yet, only a four blocks to Reed College. Access the entrance through a shared walkway on a quiet tree lined street. Atop a short flight of stairs find a spacious room with a private bathroom. Well maintained, clean, and airy loft space feels like a respite from the world around you.','Known for its tree canopy, lush home gardens, and mix of architecture styles with first homes built in the early 1900\'s. Beautiful inner Southeast neighborhood where residents are often walking/biking/running and many times accompanied by their furry friends.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-20710225/original/9ff1d33c-0688-446e-a329-d7a8b5ae30ff.jpg',25514905,5,'45.476','-122.62664',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,5,106,4.92,20710225),(966,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20724782','HOTEL in a HOME in Beautiful MONTAVILLA','Located in the small, hip Montavilla neighborhood, truly provides an authentic \'Portland\' experience. Central location, close to PDX and 10 mins to downtown. An adorable 1920\'s house situated right off E. Burnside. Our lower unit is both contemporary and spacious with 800 sq ft that is brightly lit with ample windows, private bathroom, small kitchen, roomy entertainment area, and modern furnishings. Feels like a hotel with your own private entrance, great yard and seating for coffee in morning!','We are in an eclectic, cutting edge neighborhood that is home to an artistic and hip community. We have great restaurants, bars, and a retro movie theater that is all within walking distance. Mt Tabor is an extinct volcanic butte that is within a 10 minute walk from our house, it passes through beautiful neighborhoods along the way. The park itself is 196 acres with amazing views of Mt Hood as well as the city of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/66ca2459-382c-4b11-a6c6-4d17b20f3500.jpg',33616213,10,'45.52306','-122.58351',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,101.00,2,30,144,4.84,20724782),(967,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20729965','SE PDX Craftsman','Great, great inner Southeast Portland location. Great old craftsman in a prime location. Walking distance to restaurants, bars, breweries. Short walk to OMSI and the river. Light rail and biking trails close. A cheap Uber ride to the whole city!','Southeast is known for restaurants, bars, breweries, distillers, etc... You wont have a problem finding a great place to close to eat!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5456e7d3-4aa9-47e8-aa95-1c75f9a71d76.jpg',148452836,25,'45.50858','-122.65725',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,119.00,30,1125,290,4.87,20729965),(968,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20765126','Bright St. Johns bungalow with cozy gas fireplace','My clean, bright, urban oasis is your home away from home. Strong Wifi, a gas fireplace for unwinding at night,  Netflix+,  separate office, private backyard,  and quiet. 9-foot ceilings give you space. Walkable to New Seasons gourmet grocery; 5 min to a dog park; 20 min drive to downtown and 25 from airport.  Comfy queen-sized bed and a farmhouse kitchen with all the fixin\'s sweeten your stay. EV charger avail. My house is nice for singles and/or couples. 1 small, well behaved dog considered.','Historical St. John\'s is tucked away yet close to everything. It\'s kind of like it\'s own little town and has everything you might need. Sudra vegetarian restaurant,  pizza pubs, brewhouses, food carts, vintage stores, record stores, Cathedral Coffee, University of Portland campus, New Seasons grocery store, an old cinema with first-run films, McMenamins with beer, food and movies, dive bars, fancy bars, Kelly Point Park, Bybee and Smith Lakes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7069ddfe-1409-4039-aec2-ccf628c1fecc.jpg',2076827,60,'45.58715','-122.72437',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,1,1124,87,4.95,20765126),(969,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20786008','Sunnyside Wonderland - Coffee Shops, Bars & Parks','If you love great food, craft beer, and pour-over coffee, this is your spot. Located in the famous Buckman District, my apartment is near Portland\'s top-rated restaurants, bars, vintage shops, and offers some of the best people-watching around.<br /><br />Perfect for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers, my place is a convenient home base within walking distance of all the neighborhood hot spots. Experience an authentic taste of hipster life in Stumptown.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District puts you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors—no chain restaurants here! Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or enjoy a fancy night out at Castagna, all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />But Portland isn\'t just for foodies. The vibrant indie spirit thrives in Hawthorne, with plenty of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques to explore in this hipster haven. Catch a movie at the Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of recreation, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park on top of a dormant volcano vent. Here, you’ll find miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of the city. Enjoy the perfect blend of ur','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20786008/original/bb1dbd6c-99d8-4c36-90ae-337300880da0.jpeg',36435346,32,'45.5152','-122.6384',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,74.00,1,1125,674,4.79,20786008),(970,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20788623','Comfy SE Portland Apartment - Great Eats/Bars','If you\'re a fan of great food, craft beer, pour-over coffee, this is your place. My apartment is situated in the famous Buckman District - which neighbors many of Portland\'s top-rated restaurants and bars, vintage shops, and offers some of the best people-watching around.<br /><br />My place is great for couples, solo adventures, and business travelers. With a convenient home base within walking distance to the neighborhood hot spots, you can get an authentic taste of how the hipsters live in Stumptown.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors—no chain restaurants here! Enjoy vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or opt for an elegant night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />But Portland isn’t just for foodies. The vibrant indie spirit of Hawthorne is alive with a multitude of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques, making it a true hipster haven. Catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of recreation, head up to Mt. Tabor. This 196-acre city park, located atop a dormant volcano vent, offers miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of the city, providing a perfect escape into nature righ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20788623/original/661f71a6-b43a-49b0-b5ba-13b7852fa30c.jpeg',146196024,32,'45.515','-122.6402',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,72.00,1,1125,654,4.82,20788623),(971,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20799319','Modern Guest House in Hip NE Alberta/Williams','Built in the fall of 2017 this private guest house has great natural light and an open loft concept.   Upstairs master loft suite with 1.5 bathrooms with an additional pull out living room sleeping area.   Located in heart of NE Portland, you\'ll be walking distance to the well-known districts of Alberta St., Mississippi St, and N. Williams Corridor.   Just less than 2.5 miles from the Pearl District & Downtown Portland.  Experience the local, real Portland!  Completely separated and private.','NE Portland is a true slice of Portland that offers you a density of bars, restaurants, and shopping, while still feeling like you\'re experiencing a local neighborhood feel.    Explore NE Alberta St., N. Williams Corridor, walk to Mississippi Street and explore unique coffee shops, restaurants, and bars!  <br /><br />What makes this area great is that you\'re also only 2.5 miles from downtown Portland - so it\'s really easy to bike, take a bus, or an uber/lyft and be downtown within 10 to 15 minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20799319/original/0dc88551-3977-4b7f-a7c6-1f04dca89e87.jpeg',9996037,14,'45.55682','-122.66053',1,3,1.50,1.00,2.00,108.00,2,28,486,4.98,20799319),(972,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20805575','Mt Tabor Parkside Gem','Welcome to our 1 Bedroom/1 Bath home, abutting beautiful Mt. Tabor Park, where you can enjoy hiking, picnics, and nature right outside your door! Our home is dog-friendly, so feel free to bring your furry friend along for the trip.(fee added at checkout).Relax in our spacious clawfoot tub, or catch up on work with our fast and reliable WiFi.  Host are attentive and responsive and live on site. Book now and experience the charm and convenience of our home and the best that Portland has to offer!','Super safe and walkable neighborhood in southeast Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/12da659b-77f5-411b-834b-5792b71c8002.jpg',45465987,15,'45.51601','-122.5883',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,2,170,85,4.80,20805575),(973,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20811359','THE NEST:  Spacious 2 Story Home Sellwood-Moreland','Located in the heart of bustling Sellwood Moreland, this historic 2 story house has everything needed for a comfortable stay. Tastefully furnished 3 bedroom home with 1.5 bathrooms. Large tile entry, spacious living & dining room, kitchen, bar area, and half bath located on main floor. Full bath with shower & tub, and all bedrooms located upstairs on 2nd floor. Equipped with new mattresses & pillows, quality linens, cotton sheets, well appointed kitchen,  wifi, smart tv, movies, games, and more.','Nearby attractions within walking distance include: <br />Locally Owned Shops & Boutiques, Restaurants, Bars, QFC Grocery Store, Coffee Shops, Pizza, Doughnuts, Wine & Spirits, Antique Shopping, Salons, Spas & Barber Shop, Gyms, Dry-Cleaners, Banks, Post Office, FedEx, Farmers Market, Bike Shops with Rental & Repair, Movie Theater, Oaks Amusement Park & Roller Skating Rink, Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge, Reed College, Pioneer Wedding Chapel, Zoom+Care, Wilhelm Memorial, Willamette River, Several Public Parks, and Much More!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/730f21c5-67d3-4c02-9162-9950cae57e41.jpg',143163862,20,'45.47485','-122.65002',1,6,1.50,3.00,4.00,135.00,30,90,16,4.94,20811359),(974,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20818777','Discount! Craftsman bungalow w/ 1st class lodging!','You will love it! A full sized private bedroom within our house with down pillows and comforter in Queen sized sleigh bed! Surrounded by gorgeous antiques and vintage Japanese scrolls!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/092208ef-b806-4aa2-b6e4-868962b93a84.jpg',26679646,39,'45.54757','-122.59017',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,30,30,5,4.80,20818777),(975,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20831387','North Portland Studio Apartment','Private studio located in North Portland neighborhood.  Close to Max Light Rail (yellow) restaurants, coffee shops, grocery stores, and parks.  Easy access to the freeway.<br /><br />Perfect for traveling nurses: 1.6 miles to Legacy Emmanuel, 2.2 to Legacy Good Samaritan, 4.5 to OHSU and 5.6 to St. Vincent’s. <br /><br />2.2 miles away from Convention Center & Rose Quarter. 3.6 to Expo Center. <br /><br />Located adjacent to our home with private access. Full kitchen, washer/dryer, air conditioning, smart tv and wifi.','North Portland is historic yet ever-changing. Old historic homes mix with new condo’s and high-rises which brings an exciting mix of generations that include those born and raised in Portland and many new to this growing part of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0513303a-cf1e-42d0-b8df-eba1ec0f269d.jpg',111643457,13,'45.5646','-122.68521',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,2,1125,344,4.98,20831387),(976,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20836531','Quiet Artist\'s Condo in NW','This bright private condo near NW 23rd is perfect for 1 or 2 people looking for a cozy place to explore the city from. It\'s a quiet second story walkup filled with plants and sunlight, making it an ideal space for contemplative work, writing, and art.  It has large warehouse windows offering views of the vegetated courtyard, Fremont Bridge, and hummingbird feeders! Full kitchen amenities including a French press, rice cooker, waffle iron, pizza stone, and griddle.','NW 23rd and the Alphabet District is a lovely shopping street just a minutes walk away. Skip the lines at Bamboo Sushi and Salt & Straw by going at off peak hours like a local!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-20836531/original/ddaa7358-baa5-4d19-882c-ea315b5b4903.jpg',2145885,27,'45.52724','-122.69729',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,205.00,2,21,52,4.96,20836531),(977,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20850115','Charming & Spacious 5BR Home in SE Portland','This amazing home is conveniently located in SE Portland near all of the best restaurants, bars, shopping areas, and close proximity to downtown! Plenty of awesome spots within walking distance.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20850115/original/d090946e-da51-4342-9ce3-4d3fded5c726.jpeg',67834636,8,'45.49881','-122.61414',1,12,2.00,5.00,5.00,319.00,1,1125,527,4.70,20850115),(978,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20903576','Lovely Studio in Portland\'s Best Location','Prime location in the Portland area.<br />Across the street from the Portland streetcar and walking distance to many hip restaurants, shopping, cinema, the Medical Center,  Northwest 23rd and 21st avenues.<br /><br />Between the Nob Hill and the Pearl District. This is one of the best spots to be in the city if you are visiting looking for a permanent home or doing a residency at the hospital.<br />Beautiful brick building with the main areas recently renovated,  you will feel at home!','Located in one of the best and safest areas in Portland:  “The Alphabet District.” close to public transportation, downtown, sophisticated shopping, dining and leisurely strolls.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20903576/original/03e417aa-fce5-4107-aa6f-daa157af1037.jpeg',18925199,27,'45.52913','-122.69053',1,2,0.00,0.00,1.00,75.00,30,1125,23,4.74,20903576),(979,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20928656','The Overlook Nook','Tucked away in a quiet nook in the popular Overlook Neighborhood is one of Portland’s first ADUs - The Overlook Nook. Converted from an art studio garage, The Overlook Nook was grandfathered into the current regulations, so you’ll find it a bit more spacious than others in the area. Fun fact - the kitchen was built from the leftover set of The Real World Portland TV show. An easy walking distance to the TriMet MAX Light Rail and Bus, you’ll have no problem getting around in the city.','Have a picnic or a swing at Overlook Park. See the stunning views of Downtown Portland or watch an incredible sunset from the bluff at Mocks Crest Park. Explore nearby restaurants, food cart pods, cafes, pubs, and breweries along Historic Mississippi Avenue. All of these are within a short walking distance from our guesthouse.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3247e678-3a33-489e-adf0-8dcc228a4374.jpg',150440935,13,'45.55272','-122.68333',1,5,1.00,0.00,3.00,150.00,2,29,127,4.98,20928656),(980,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20935576','Ankeny Loft Just a Block From East Burnside','This pet-friendly ground floor apartment is in the heart of Portland\'s Southeast Laurelhurst neighborhood.  It\'s just 5 blocks away from a hub of amazing restaurants and Whole Foods Market. There are cafes, shops, breweries and parks all within walking distance and it\'s just one block off of the famous East Burnside Street.<br />Pet fee is $35 for one night; $50 for 2-7 nights. Higher fee with longer stays.','Located in the desirable Laurelhurst neighborhood, from here it\'s just steps to trendy shops, restaurants, and cafes. See new releases at a small movie theatre and taste beers at microbreweries. Parks and public transportation are also close.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-20935576/original/5112188e-13c8-442e-964e-6d5e8468262c.jpeg',49136460,32,'45.52227','-122.64121',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,81.00,1,240,381,4.93,20935576),(981,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20946576','Ground Level Walkout Modern Architecture Townhouse','Step into a private oasis in this exclusive flat. The guest unit features its own separate entrance, neutral grays with rustic wood accents, chic furnishings, and a secluded backyard garden patio with a dining space.<br /><br />Our hip space will be a perfect place for you to call your home while you explore restaurants, parks, and sights in Portland! Go out or stay in! We had fun decorating with a Portland theme and sourced much of the decor locally. Take advantage of the modern kitchen with gas stove and cook up some delicious meals with goodies from the local farmers market. Chill on the patio? Yes, there is secluded backyard patio. Get a good night sleep on the brand new Caspar queen size mattress and get your laundry done with the stacked washer/dryer.  Relax? Yes, Binge-watch your favorite TV shows on the smart flat-screen TV in the bedroom with Netflix, and Amazon Prime Video,​ and cable service. Stay cozy in the Fall/Winter with the radiant floor heating and cool in the summer ','The property is located in the Cathedral Park area close to St. Johns Bridge and the historical St. Johns neighborhood. Stroll and discover the charming shopping and dining options, as well as cafes, the local bar nightlife, and more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/61bbcff8-12da-4c84-b616-62f819777e89.jpg',1828909,42,'45.59426','-122.76254',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,103.00,30,365,123,4.91,20946576),(982,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20971758','NE Irving Park Cottage','Welcome to the Irving Park Neighborhood Cottage located within walking distance of NE Williams, Alberta Arts District and Mississippi Avenue in Portland, Oregon. Our quiet cottage sits in the back of our garden and offers privacy with your own stone patio with bistro table and chairs. There are many restaurants nearby and a large city park (Irving Park) 2 blocks away. Please reach out to us if you would like recommendations prior to your stay or have questions.','Our cottage is a short 10-minute walk to the fantastic shops and restaurants on NE Williams and NE Fremont. Mississippi and Alberta districts are a 20-minute walk from our location. Refer to the local guidebooks we provide and our list of recommended spots. Historic Irving Park is 2 blocks away and is a great place to picnic, exercise, play, or read a book under the trees.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjA5NzE3NTg%3D/original/52915b1b-ec35-41b5-b02f-c6036c67a965.jpeg',150888783,14,'45.55077','-122.65906',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,115.00,1,30,412,4.99,20971758),(983,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/20993707','Northwest Natural Habitat Getaway in SE Portland.','Fully sanitized between guests. Take refuge in a sunlit lower unit in the Laurelhurst area of Portland, well situated to restaurants, stores, access to downtown, as well as Mt Hood.  Unit was built from scratch in 2017, a NW Native habitat garden created in 2018, rain gardens/bioswales in 2019-2020. We\'re a yoga and meditation oriented house: quiet after 10 pm. I\'m up between 5:30 & 6, you may hear chanting. Space is not intended for parties. Light use of alcohol only. BIPOC & LGBTQ friendly.','Walking distance to quintessential Portland neighborhoods of Hawthorne, Division, Mt. Tabor, Laurelhurst, Burnside. Conveniently located between downtown and airport. Quiet neighborhood','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4e24ed2f-fc97-4a5e-9719-21aac17efffb.jpg',951583,52,'45.52171','-122.61536',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,95.00,3,1125,107,4.93,20993707),(984,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21013818','Loft Living Steps From Laurelhurst’s Hip Restaurant Scene','Tucked in one of Portland\'s trendiest neighborhoods, this pet friendly, new-build apartment oozes the kind of coolness the city is known for. Modern furniture and minimalist decor makes the most of the open-concept space. AC unit in bedroom cools the whole place.<br />Pet Friendly:','The famed corner of E 28th and Burnside beckons with its celebrated restaurants, bars and Whole Foods Market. Across the street, there are local eateries along with a wine shop and a few cafes. For a scenic bike ride, Laurelhurst park is nearby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a5ebae22-76cb-4116-9ec8-a1b71d6f4660.jpg',49136460,32,'45.52227','-122.64121',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,1,240,299,4.86,21013818),(985,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21021665','Open and Light upstairs apartment with fireplace','This is a second story 1 bdrm apartment in a very central location in NE Portland. Apartment is about 500 sq ft. <br />Great for walking to anything you could want - lots of restaurants, bars, parks, grocery stores.  Close to Convention Center, Max line, Mississippi Ave, N Williams Ave.  Lots of windows, a skylight, hardwood floors, stone countertops, full kitchen, fireplace and a small balcony.  <br />The apt is completely separate, but please keep the volume down out of respect for downstairs neighbors.','It is in close in NE Portland - it has a walkscore of 83 with dozens of restaurants, bars, coffee shops and stores within walking distance. There\'s a great grocery store (New Seasons) about 2 blocks away and it\'s right off two major bus lines. It\'s a 6 minute drive to downtown Portland, there are several huge parks within walking distance (with dog parks, tennis courts, playgrounds and basketball courts) as well and it\'s in a perfect place for biking. Several MAX train line stops is within a mile.   City bike share (Biketown) has two station within a couple of blocks where bikes can be rented by the hour or by the day.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/70472d6c-b747-4bdf-8ed1-399b693566e8.jpg',5053719,26,'45.54609','-122.66308',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1124,61,4.98,21021665),(986,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21029021','Private apartment in a Portland Charmer','In-law apartment built in 2017 with all the furnishings to make your stay easy and worry-free. This basement apartment has a lot of natural light with large bedroom windows. <br /><br />Perfect for business travelers, families, travelers with pets, or friends that want separate sleeping spaces but great common areas private from the hosts.<br /><br />We welcome pets for a fee of $40 per pet (limit of 2 pets).  We will request the appropriate pet fee if it is not automatically added to your reservation cost.','The Piedmont neighborhood is safe and family-friendly. There is a grocery store three blocks away, along with other shops and restaurants. Historic Mississippi and Alberta Arts Districts are one mile from our home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bd3d103f-3db6-4083-a1f8-50f9a8a0d299.jpg',7902031,48,'45.56976','-122.6765',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,85.00,1,1125,459,4.73,21029021),(987,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21039971','Marvelous Sunny Mississippi AC 1 Bedroom Apt MAX','Welcome to the Mississippi Apts. in N Portland, Oregon. This is a charming 1909 Craftsman  Duplex features spacious, sunny private 1 bedroom 1 bath apt w/ Smart TV/ AC  Located on the 2nd floor. Perfect work from home situation with amazing light! Perfect for a long term stay. There\'s a  large bedroom, comfy queen size bed, en suite bath tub &shower, spacious living room with plenty of room to relax or work.   Walk 2 blocks  Max Train yellow line.  10 min. to dwtn.  No Pets Free Street Parking','Street parking out front.   3 blocks from the heart of the Mississippi district, 5 min walk to the Williams/Vancouver corridor and New Seasons Market. Close to all the bars and restaurants North Portland has to offer.  <br />1 mile to Swan Island, walk to Addidas, Kaiser Permante, Legacy Emanuel, short 10 minute ride on the Max to downtown Portland. 2.2 Mile to Union Station (train station)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-21039971/original/dadd2c08-92a9-43d8-a24c-f633159efb50.jpeg',477663,13,'45.55283','-122.68007',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,72.00,31,120,45,4.89,21039971),(988,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21046136','Little Backyard Cottage','Live like a local in Arbor Lodge.  Charming backyard cottage. 400 sq ft of Mid century modern flair filled with natural light. Only two short blocks to Max yellow line, restaurants and New Seasons grocery.  Minutes to downtown.','Arbor Lodge is a North Portland neighborhood just minutes from downtown. It\'s a tree lined neighborhood close to Mississippi, Kenton, Alberta nightspots and Adidas.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/40e160d1-9413-4e4a-81ec-4035cba754b2.jpg',7391129,51,'45.57015','-122.68674',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,2,14,442,4.95,21046136),(989,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21052140','Trendy Hawthorne/Division*Walk Score 95!','Walk Score 95!!  In the heart of one of the best dining areas in Portland, walking distance to dozens of restaurants on Hawthorne & Division!<br /><br />***PLEASE READ!***When you send a booking request, confirm that have read my full listing description, \"other things to note section\", house rules and that no one in your party is a smoker.  I am very sensitive to secondhand smoke so if anyone is a smoker, do not send a request.','93 Walk Score and 100 Bike Score! Live like a local! This is a wonderful and highly coveted Portland neighborhood with incredible restaurants, bars, brew pubs, wine bars and great tax free shopping at locally owned boutiques and vintage shops, all within walking distance.  The nearest coffee shop is a 3 minute walk away but there are several others nearby, <br />The nearest restaurant/bar is also 3 minutes away but dozens within 5-20 minutes walk.  Plenty of great shops on both Hawthorne and Division! <br /> Downtown is about 3.5 miles by car, the airport is about 7.5 miles and the convention Center is about 4.5 miles by car.  I hope you enjoy our house and neighborhood as much as we do!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-21052140/original/27a542e7-ab53-4e37-bb8e-13af37c5a2ad.jpeg',1096266,8,'45.50645','-122.61521',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,1,5,59,4.98,21052140),(990,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21096045','Cozy Basement Apartment','Light-filled basement apartment with kitchen and bathroom. Perfect for 1-2 guests. Extremely cozy, clean, and comfortable. Our family lives upstairs, which can lead to a little noise. The apartment is below our home so we can only accommodate guests on the reservation.<br /><br /><br />The neighborhood is quiet but the Dekum Triangle is about 3 blocks away and is bustling with places to eat and drink.','The apartment is 4 blocks from the Dekum triangle in Woodlawn. Lots of places to get food, drinks, and there’s a charming park down the street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9a18f1c5-a7e4-4d53-89e2-7017a17e14c1.jpg',13240293,45,'45.56852','-122.6593',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,70.00,1,730,210,4.85,21096045),(991,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21113829','Lux Group Retreat','The Lux Group Retreat @ the previously known Travelers\' House is a private space centrally located in Portland for strolling, biking, and exploration. The unit is cosy for 5 but hosts 6 and is thoughtfully designed  relaxation nooks in each room. The apartment is attached to the 1900s \"Craftsperson\" and has three bedrooms, two bathrooms, a full kitchen, and dining/living room with Roku equipped HD projector lounge, bluetooth sound-bar, and a shared, but private backyard for grilling or hanging.','We are centrally located with access to great nightlife, breweries, and food options all within a short walk. The Historic Mississippi, Alberta Arts, and Williams Districts are at our doorstep. These neighborhoods are what makes Portland so special and different from other cities that only have nightlife in the downtown area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-21113829/original/b92fa33c-49d2-4db6-b06c-42ae27c203d2.jpeg',13604254,24,'45.55998','-122.67524',1,6,2.00,3.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,39,4.95,21113829),(992,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21135547','Upstairs Studio: kitchenette, private bathroom,','Charming, cozy, private & spacious upstairs studio space with shared entrance! Sorry men,  because there is a shared  entrance , I am currently only renting to women! This clean space allows you to cook basic things and make coffee/tea. It has a kitchenette and a private bathroom. It\'s in the heart of Foster-Powell, an up & coming old school quirky neighborhood and in walking distance of some of Portland\'s most trendy areas. Great for longterm stays. See our discounts.','Hip Portland meets old quirky Portland. There is much discussion about which is better these days. In Foster-Powell, you can enjoy both worlds --while being in the heart of old quirky Portland, you are only a short 10 block walk from some of Portlands hippest haunts, such as Division St. Also 1.5 miles from Hawthorne district, and 1 mile south of Mount Tabor, a great inner city hiking area. Without traffic, you can make it downtown in 10 minutes.  Foster -Powell, is an up and coming old school Portland neighborhood -with many great ethnic restaurants, bars,  local markets in walking distance, bus stops, and hikes nearby. This neighborhood is currently coming alive with lots of new businesses opening up.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/36a4eb31-0f36-4f9d-88bc-a54c98cdb6b9.jpg',1030342,36,'45.49548','-122.60139',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,7,90,74,4.95,21135547),(993,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21155236','Cozy Loft Studio','12/2- 1/3 Currently available! Welcome to our cozy retreat! Nestled in Woodstock, we\'re just moments from the lively Woodstock Avenue, embraced by free libraries and lush gardens. Reed College\'s serene campus invites leisurely strolls nearby. Venture a short distance to explore the vibrant southeast Division, Hawthorne, and Belmont neighborhoods, each boasting its own unique allure. Despite the nearby excitement, our street remains quiet and peaceful, offering a serene escape.','Woodstock is a quiet neighborhood, close to Reed University. There are big trees and beautiful gardens all around. We are one mile from both a Trader Joes and a New Seasons grocery store.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1ff8599c-fbc3-48b2-9683-580850b9c21d.jpg',7634865,38,'45.48709','-122.61317',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,55.00,30,1125,92,4.89,21155236),(994,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21155408','Alberta Arts 3 blocks to eats, bars & shops','Explore Alberta Arts 20 blocks of trending shops, restaurants, 420, bike rentals, and kids’ playground. <br /><br />Big groups can spread out across 3 floors in this renovated 1930 bungalow permitted for Airbnb:<br />* Kid friendly - 2 pack & plays, 2 high chairs, and more!<br />* 5 queen beds, 2 two twin sofa beds, and portable mattresses<br />* 4 smart TVs<br />* Blazing fast 1G wifi<br />* Fully stocked kitchen<br />* Central AC<br /><br />All of Portland is nearly 15 minutes in every direction (airport, Southeast, Downtown, Pearl).','Alberta Arts District is a trending, historic neighborhood in Northeast Portland.  Alberta Street is the heart of an arts, restaurant, and shopping district approximately 20 blocks long.  Your 3 block walk to Alberta Street will be through historic neighborhoods crammed with Craftsman houses, bike riders, and everything that makes Portland weird.<br /><br />WALK OUT THE FRONT DOOR!<br /><br />2 blocks away: local coffee, wine tasting, bakery, 420 and public park.<br /><br />3 blocks away: Alberta Street with 20 blocks of Yelp! 5 star restaurants and bars, Biketown rentals, food trucks, yoga, pay by day gym, and more!<br /><br />5 blocks away: Whole Foods, Starbucks, UPS store if you need to receive deliveries.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjExNTU0MDg%3D/original/b0d699ab-d698-44a1-b355-3caee24da44b.jpeg',26818733,6,'45.55666','-122.64859',1,8,2.00,4.00,6.00,198.00,2,1125,401,4.98,21155408),(995,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21186901','Concordia Retreat','A new (2010)  house designed and built by a Street of Dreams builder. We are close to Alberta St, New Seasons grocery, Kennedy School, Fernhill and Alberta parks. Backyard garden area. Clean and comfortable.','We\'re in a very walkable, bikeable neighborhood. Close to great variety of coffee shops,  natural grocery store, Alberta St, restaurants,  food carts, Kennedy School,  brewpubs, parks,  gardens, alleys and tennis courts. Close to bus routes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9dfb2d40-e3df-4947-be70-55279a2cfc50.jpg',6589054,1,'45.56773','-122.63565',2,1,1.50,1.00,1.00,65.00,30,1125,21,4.86,21186901),(996,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21187329','The University Park Art House','This spacious, comfortable well-appointed two-bedroom, one bath home is the perfect place to land in Portland!  A short walk from the U.of P., it is a launching pad for any neighborhood you’d like to explore in the city. Called the Art House, the 1924 bungalow showcases art and designer furniture by some of the area’s best artists.','This is among the closest vacation rentals to the University of Portland, so if you are a visiting professor or a parent visiting a student enrolled at the school, you couldn\'t find a closer place to stay.  There are two small parks within easy walking distance. The main portion of Columbia Park is a mile away with huge trees and walking paths and a pool and playgrounds. The neighborhood is close to downtown and to more bustling places with little shops and galleries (St. John\'s, Kenton, and Mississippi-Boise).  There are good restaurants nearby, on Lombard and Greeley.<br />University Park itself is a quiet green oasis. Many of the neighbors have lived here a long time. It\'s a peaceful place, and we are so excited to share it with you.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7e6aabb2-7337-4fb8-bd53-ebe39a02dd44.jpg',45434894,57,'45.57735','-122.72001',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,125.00,2,14,122,4.96,21187329),(997,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21298601','Modern Private Bungalow, king bed, soaking tub','Really quiet, private, 1 story, fully renovated modern apartment with secluded outdoor seating area, large soaking tub for 2, and separate shower. <br /><br />The apartment is a short walk to public transit to airport and downtown MAX line. <br /><br />GREAT FOR: Couples or individuals looking for a quite relaxing stay. Unusually quiet and private for Portland. No neighbor\'s windows looking into apartment, or outdoor patio space. <br /><br />NOT FOR LOUD PEOPLE/ GROUPS: Only mature, respectful guests to stay in my home.','My place is *not* right in the center of restaurants, bars and shops, if it was, parking would be really difficult. We are a few blocks off Glisan and 60th. It is a quiet street with lots of parking out front, and a few blocks from a supermarket, park, coffee and a cannabis shop. Its also really convenient to the MAX light rail. It\'s also easy to get to the highway for the airport and trips to the Gorge, etc.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8d4673d9-f3f1-4494-9b25-1f3a49abb921.jpg',89239158,52,'45.52807','-122.60075',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,78.00,2,90,393,4.93,21298601),(998,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21422556','Portland International Guesthouse - Room 1','Room #1 is a large, corner room on the main level (2nd floor) of the Guesthouse. It has 1 queen bed and 1 single bed.   It has 2 large windows, a bistro table and chair, large closet, an upholstered chair and ample floor space. A full bath is just steps from the Room #1 door.  Please see all 4 room listings for our Guesthouse and don\'t miss our 1 bedroom apartment (in same building as the Guesthouse) listed here on AirBnb!  Thank you.','The Guesthouse is located in Portland\'s historic Alphabet District also known as Nob Hill. Our neighborhood is the city\'s most charming and vibrant. We are within walking distance or a short transit ride Downtown, the Pearl District, Powell\'s Books and most of Portland\'s major cultural institutions.<br /><br />One can meander through the neighborhood streets lined with Victorian homes, NW 23rd and 21st Avenues lined with shops and restaurants or walk up to Washington Park and the amazing Japanese Gardens. From there, it is possible to access over 40 miles of hiking trails.<br /><br />Some of the Portland\'s best restaurants, coffee houses and cinemas are only a few blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c497f849-ae70-42e2-b4b6-e0efc4cbae39.jpg',2915808,27,'45.525718688964844','-122.69625854492188',2,2,2.00,1.00,2.00,105.00,1,20,96,4.92,21422556),(999,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21425869','“Pearl Pad” Grt. location, view & free EV Chging!','Enjoy your upscale condo with everything you need for a great stay.  Close to all....shops, riverwalk, parks, OHSU/Legacy medical facilities, and streetcar! But still quiet and relaxing.<br />Park in assigned spot w/free EV chg. & forget all about it!<br />Kitchen is super-stocked,<br />W/D, WIFI, Netflix, king size bed,<br />Queen sofa bed.  Balcony w/park view. <br />Linens, towels etc,  It’s a real house!<br /><br />While we have a 31 day minimum stay, please contact me for shorter or longer stays!<br /><br />No pets or smoking please!','Enjoy Ovations coffee, Fields and Tanner Parks, the river walk, All of the wine bars, REI store, Powell Books,<br />Anthropologie, food carts<br />Streetcar stop is half block away to take you to 23 rd St. District or the south waterfront!<br />Bike rentals at the park!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7076c4a4-f68f-4ec7-b475-2fe9266f8d47.jpg',10218720,2,'45.53257','-122.68132',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,150.00,31,100,8,5.00,21425869),(1000,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21430359','Truly Local Experience, Steps from Restaurant Row!','Are you a traveler who likes to be mere steps from the action, visiting as many restaurants, breweries, bars, shops and cafes as humanly possible when you travel? If so, this modern, private guesthouse apartment is for you! Throw on your trusty pair of Chuck Taylor\'s and head outside - literally everything you could want is steps from your front door. You can\'t get a better location for exploring PDX like a local! Then come home & recharge with friends and Netflix on the comfy sectional sofa.','The Buckman neighborhood is known to be one of Portland\'s hottest, hippest neighborhoods! With such celebrated SE streets as Hawthorne, Belmont and Burnside being smack dab in the middle of Buckman, there\'s no lack of things to do, see, explore, eat, and drink. Buckman is also right on the edge of NE Portland and all of its blossoming, charming entertainment/shopping districts. If all that is not enough, it is exactly 2 miles from the center of downtown Portland. Bring some comfy shoes, grab a couple coins for the bus lines or MAX light rail, and go on an epic Portland adventure. Prefer to explore the city on self-propelled wheels and discover why Portland is touted as one of the most bike-friendly cities in the country? Just walk around the corner from this house and pick up an orange \"Biketown\" city bike for a couple bucks. This neighborhood truly has it all and it is sure to be the perfect launching point for an amazing trip.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-21430359/original/ded518ee-669a-4020-9629-51aabc6c184f.jpeg',3519216,12,'45.52407','-122.63654',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,71.00,1,29,529,4.91,21430359),(1001,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21439433','Portland Classic - Parks, Eateries + Local Shops','If you love great food, craft beer, and pour-over coffee, this is your spot. Located in the famous Buckman District, my apartment is near Portland\'s top-rated restaurants, bars, vintage shops, and offers some of the best people-watching around.<br /><br />Perfect for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers, my place is a convenient home base within walking distance of all the neighborhood hot spots. Experience an authentic taste of hipster life in Stumptown.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District puts you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors—no chain restaurants here! Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or enjoy a fancy night out at Castagna, all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />But Portland isn\'t just for foodies. The vibrant indie spirit thrives in Hawthorne, with plenty of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques to explore in this hipster haven. Catch a movie at the Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of recreation, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park on top of a dormant volcano vent. Here, you’ll find miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of the city. Enjoy the perfect blend of ur','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-21439433/original/40b04505-1db7-454b-b050-abb116cd1bd6.jpeg',36435346,32,'45.51499','-122.64052',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,1,1125,604,4.77,21439433),(1002,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21459894','Portland is Pad with Speakeasy in basement','This chic mid-century cozy bungalow has all the modern updates of 2017 whiling keeping its charm from 1926. To the right there is a drinking/sitting area with a bar area to relax after a long day. Or choose to go left and snuggle up in a dangerously comfortable west elm sectional and watch a good movie/show on either Netflix, Hulu, or HBO. The kitchen is fully stocked with bar stools and a retro vibe.','A city suburban along with the serenity wildlife of being in the Pacific Northwest. A convenient location to explore the the Stark Street Bar/Restaurant Scenes and close to the airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/25081721-5dd9-41d2-a201-41d99aa0c7dd.jpg',33109623,10,'45.52188','-122.5711',1,6,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,165,4.85,21459894),(1003,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21470050','Adorable Grant Park basement apartment','Super cute 700sf basement studio apt 2.3 miles fr. downtown. Private entrance. Easy access to public transportation. 40 min drive to Columbia Gorge. <br />The apt is bright  and cozy w bdrm nook with queen bed. Walkable grocery stores/restaurants. Best if  looking for quiet place, not parties. New! Got a puppy in 2020 who is a little yappy when she hears you enter/exit','2.3 miles from downtown. Easy to Lyft or Uber around or take a bus or the Max. Within walking distance to great restaurants and grocery stores (one block away)<br /><br />40 minute drive to beautiful Columbia Gorge and Multnomah Falls. Great hiking options. Based on the distance I’ll tell you a few favorites! <br /><br />Other great sites close by around downtown Pittock Mansion, Washington Park, Japenese Gardens, The Pearl Portland Saturday Market <br /><br />Oregon coast is 90 minute drive<br /><br />My favorite places to walk:<br />-New Seasons market has great food. Try the Ramon bar or taco bar. One block away. Great grocery store as well. <br />-Sweet Basil is great thai food. Two blocks away. <br />-Blind Onion pizza. One street away. <br />-Nicolas. Mediterranean and Lebanese. One block away. Get the pita bread and hummus.<br />-Grant park<br />-Laurelhurst Park <br />-Starbucks four blocks away','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0b49a8e9-4dba-4212-9312-48ad444fff3d.jpg',28595712,33,'45.53622','-122.63048',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,52.00,2,1125,226,4.95,21470050),(1004,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21494223','Walkable 2BR | Central AC | Private W/D','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-21494223/original/a741f5e2-fd7e-45d5-955f-5ba98ca5dc83.jpeg',145210319,27,'45.53322','-122.69526',1,6,2.00,2.00,3.00,204.00,1,1125,89,4.38,21494223),(1005,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21502820','Dragonfly House','Live like a local in our beautiful one-bedroom craftsman home that blends modern design with century old architecture. This private space is located in trendy Kenton on a quiet street. The lushly landscaped front yard is a great place to sit and enjoy a cup of coffee, local beer, or a glass of wine. Cook your purchases from one of Portland’s many farmer’s markets in the full kitchen. Then get a great night’s sleep the comfy queen bed. Come see what makes Portland uniquely Portland!','Kenton is a trendy neighborhood in North Portland.  It has numerous restaurants, coffee shops, grocery and convenient stores, shops, pubs, and parks, etc.  The University of Portland is less than a mile away and we are 2.5 blocks from a Columbia Park.  Columbia Park has an indoor swimming pool, a children\'s play area, and many picnic tables.  Denver street is nearby with many options for food.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/252ffbe5-c49d-4031-964c-c1e76c6ac7ba.jpg',9268124,55,'45.57847','-122.70447',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,125.00,1,1125,87,4.97,21502820),(1006,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21506661','Woodstock Storybook Cottage','A 1937 Spanish revival that feels like a mountain cabin.  The living room boasts lofted ceilings and exposed beams with a grand fireplace.  Enjoy indoor/outdoor flow with direct access to backyard from the main living space.  Two good sized bedrooms with lots of light and an updated bathroom.  Portable A/C available for warmer days. Charming family neighborhood with easy access to Woodstock Park, New Seasons Market, Reed College, coffee and dining and much more.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-21506661/original/4544ef5c-3fe7-4a06-96ab-a558c75def9a.jpg',12556069,38,'45.48802','-122.61918',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,168.00,3,365,26,4.88,21506661),(1007,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21517694','Bright Contemporary Loft in The Pearl - 745 sq ft','This recently renovated loft is located in the heart of the Pearl District, steps away from top-rated restaurants, coffee shops, wine bars, art galleries, boutiques and more (walk score of 97!).','Portland streetcar stop: 1 block away<br />Drugstore: 1 block away<br />Healthy Mexican restaurant: downstairs<br />Portland Monthly Restaurant of the Year (Republica): 1.5 blocks away<br />Fresh baked cinnamon rolls: 2 blocks away<br />5 Coffee shops: 2-3 blocks away<br />24 Hour Fitness: 1 block away<br />Spa: 1 block away<br />Park: 2 blocks away<br />Nail salon: 3 blocks away<br />Grocery store: 5 blocks away','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/901f1f7c-5430-4d4b-906e-59b290d27cae.jpg',156366214,2,'45.528','-122.68359',1,4,1.00,0.00,1.00,120.00,31,1125,11,5.00,21517694),(1008,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21537748','Million-Dollar River View: light-filled downtown','Centrally located downtown overlooking the lively Riverplace Esplanade with lots of restaurants and boutiques right downstairs. We are making our second home available to you for that truly special extended stay.  The first thing you\'ll notice in this top floor corner unit is the light filling the rooms from the large East-facing windows. Enjoy the 180 degree view up and down the river where you can see SIX of Portland\'s famous bridges through the big windows in the living, dining and bedrooms.','Restaurants and more are right outside your door with easy access to OHSU, PSU, Keller Auditorium and waterfront parks, all within 5 blocks. Convenient to the Portland Streetcar (3 blocks away).<br /><br />Other nearby services include:<br /><br />- 24 Hour Fitness, OHSU Wellness & Fitness Center<br /><br />- Biketown bicycle rental station<br /><br />- PSU farmer\'s market on Saturdays<br /><br />- Jogging, biking & walking path right out front<br /><br />Events within walking distance:<br /><br />All Year<br /><br />Portland Farmers Market at PSU<br /><br />The Portland Saturday Market Waterfront Park<br /><br />February<br /><br />Portland International Film Festival Waterfront Park<br /><br />Portland Jazz Festival Waterfront Park<br /><br />May<br /><br />Cinco de Mayo Waterfront Park<br /><br />Rock n\' Roll Marathon Waterfront Park<br /><br />Rose Festival City Fair Waterfront Park<br /><br />Festival of Flowers Pioneer Courthouse Square<br /><br />June<br /><br />Starlight Parade','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/782bd7a2-ac30-440f-8986-e3dba6d28266.jpg',156366214,44,'45.5099','-122.67394',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,140.00,31,1125,3,5.00,21537748),(1009,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21566467','Stunning Victorian in the heart of Alberta Arts','Located in the heart of the Alberta arts district, this home has two spacious bedrooms, two fully renovated bathrooms and a dedicated office room. You are less than half a mile away from some of the best restaurants, bars and coffee shops in Portland (Key’s Lounge, Radio Room, Tin Shed, Bye & Bye) in a quaint neighborhood away from loud traffic. A 10 min drive to the Forest Park and 15 mins to the airport make this the perfect location for anyone looking for a truly local experience!','We\'re located in a quiet residential neighborhood which is less than a 5 minute walk to some great food carts and bars on Killingsworth St, including Key\'s Lounge. Other amenities that are within a 5-10 minute walk include the post office, two grocery stores, a gas station and multiple ATMs.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjE1NjY0Njc%3D/original/1cd3ed57-6234-4817-8a7e-d76e92abd1c5.jpeg',124649867,14,'45.56407','-122.65729',1,4,2.00,3.00,2.00,139.00,2,90,51,4.90,21566467),(1010,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21566921','Alberta Arts Apartment','Get ready for an unbeatable experience in the vibrant Alberta Arts District! Nestled beneath a charming Portland home, lies a brand new, exclusive apartment just for you. Indulge in the thrill of being just steps away from countless mouth-watering restaurants, trendy coffee shops, lively bars, eclectic galleries, and unique shops. Plus, with a grocery store right around the corner, you\'ll have everything you need for an unforgettable stay right at your fingertips!','We feel lucky to live in a neighborhood filled with great restaurants, a weekend farmers market, and friendly neighbors. You will be walking distance to parks, nightlife, and wonderful breakfast spots.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1675d3f6-6e57-482d-83af-c1c2b376ed40.jpg',124293,29,'45.56137','-122.64648',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,3,1125,248,4.98,21566921),(1011,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21579586','Huge Home with King Beds in Prime Spot with Views!','This architectural masterpiece is on a quiet and safe street while still within walking distance of Portland’s best areas for dining, drinking, and shopping. Lots of room for your entire group across 3 levels with multiple lounge/living spaces, a large open kitchen, 4 bedrooms with king beds and 1 bunkbed bedroom (each with a TV), plus 3.5 bathrooms for your convenience. Dine alfresco or relax on the beautiful back patio and enjoy east or west roof decks for viewing sunrises or sunsets.','The Boise-Eliot neighborhood is known to be one of Portland\'s hottest, hippest neighborhoods! With such well-known streets as Mississippi, Alberta and Williams being smack dab in the middle of Boise, there\'s no lack of things to do, see, explore, eat and drink. Bring some comfy shoes, grab a couple coins for the bus lines, and go on an epic Portland adventure - this neighborhood is sure to be the perfect host.<br /><br />FROM PORTLAND\'S MOST POPULAR NEIGHBORHOOD WEBSITE: <br /><br />\"Portland\'s Boise-Eliot neighborhood is one of the most unique and most popular Portland neighborhoods. Most locals know Boise-Eliot by a few names: Williams Avenue and Mississippi Avenue. While technically both part of the same neighborhood proper, these two streets have truly developed their own unique personality and feel with respect to the independent businesses that line their streets and the folks who frequent them.<br /><br />The Mississippi Ave neighborhood has changed radically in the last 10 year','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-21579586/original/8e4dccfd-6fe8-46f2-9e0d-2fe5896bb798.jpeg',37422309,14,'45.551559','-122.663864',1,10,3.50,5.00,5.00,281.00,2,1125,315,4.90,21579586),(1012,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21620813','Separate spacious guest house over garage.','We are located in the very popular Hosford-Abernathy neighborhood, within walking distance to some of Portland\'s finest restaurants and shopping. There is off street parking (with a power outlet for charging electric cars) available plus key less entry makes check-in a breeze. The bathroom floor is heated plus a TV in both the great room and bedroom. You have the entire place to yourself because it is detached from our primary house.','The Hosford-Abernathy neighborhood lies above Ladd\'s Addition and below Mt Tabor - all of these areas are high demand, highly popular areas to live.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1869b069-4628-4b35-b2fc-6564b2894699.jpg',6162657,25,'45.50791','-122.64097',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,148.00,3,21,195,5.00,21620813),(1013,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21622144','The Nest in Brooklyn. Love where you stay!','Well situated, modern space with a fenced backyard, deck, full kitchen, two bedrooms and two full bathrooms. Roku media player, TV and High speed internet included. About us: We are a Canadian-Hungarian couple who both grew up in the US. We all love to travel and host people from all over the world. If you are into outdoor sports, we are your resource to adventures around the area!<br />Note: A dog normally lives here. If you’re severely allergic to dogs, you may get a reaction.','We are just north of Sellwood (about a mile/20 min walk away), which has an abundance of cute shops, restaurants, and yoga studios, and is highly walkable. Also, it is three minutes from the Oaks Bottom bike path, and at the South end of the Brooklyn Neighborhood. It is easy to access main roads, or the tranquil park by the Willamette River.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-21622144/original/3a99af7c-55f0-459b-b0a3-893dfa94210f.jpeg',15310395,20,'45.48752','-122.6513',1,5,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,26,180,14,4.86,21622144),(1014,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21636682','Valentina\'s Tiny Brother...Tino!','Valentina\'s Little Brother, named Tino. The perfect little cedar tiny home escape (1-2 guest capacity) when spending time in the plentiful town of Portland!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-21636682/original/d906c27c-b5a4-4ca0-a794-511bdc73b0a7.jpeg',127253367,79,'45.52695','-122.70831',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,2,180,103,4.89,21636682),(1015,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21642481','Classic bungalow great location walkable Northeast','This home is a 1924 bungalow and has been completely restored.  The space is very light and bright due to the original windows, but has modern touches. The bathroom has plenty of space and updates such as heated floors. The bedrooms are cozy and have plenty of closet space.  Enjoy seating on two porches, one off the front of the house and the other off the kitchen. The house has heating and a/c. Please inquire about children under 12.  You will be the only guests at the home.','Our neighborhood is a nice \"slice of pie\" between the Hollywood, Beaumont and Rose City Park neighborhoods. We often feel like we live in an urban park due to the quiet, the birdsong, the abundance of plant life and the proximity to greenways and bike lanes. However, we can walk a couple blocks to Fire on the Mountain restaurant and brewer. From there, you can continue walking West on Fremont hitting many local favorites such as: Jim and Patty\'s Coffee Shop,   Amalfi\'s, Starbucks, Pip\'s Donuts, Prince Coffee, Grand Central Baking, and the Beaumont Market.  In the other direction toward Sandy, within 10 minutes, you will find Case Study Coffee,  Bake Shop, Cabezon,  and plenty of food carts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8d90c948-31b9-4be1-972c-1c9524b353c2.jpg',30438500,11,'45.544662653271445','-122.60534433264519',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,200.00,2,21,35,4.91,21642481),(1016,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21650064','Downtown One Bedroom Condo In Historic Building','Come enjoy Portland, Oregon in this downtown condo. Vintage charm updated for today\'s lifestyle. Prime Location, a walk score of 98. Just steps away from the Portland Art Museum, Pioneer Square, Portland State University, Farmers Market, Fantastic restaurants, Trendy food carts. Close to Jen-Weld Field, the home of the Portland Timbers.  Perfect for the out of town visitor, business traveler or extended stay guest. Ground floor unit with additional storage + bike storage in basement.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/28e6fe21-9df6-435a-914b-0f5726f9c738.jpg',25190618,44,'45.51475','-122.68572',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,68.00,30,1125,23,4.91,21650064),(1017,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21698361','Back Bedroom in Cozy, Artsy, St. Johns Bungalow','Comfy bedroom with full size bed in cheery, light infused home filled with oil paintings by host. Located in quaint and charming St. Johns with restaurants, shops and parks all within walking distance.  <br /><br />All guests much submit proof of  Covid-19 vaccinations.<br /><br />Please note I am LGBT-friendly and have no age, gender, racial or religious biases - everyone is welcome here!','St. Johns is an up and coming neighborhood 8.3 miles from downtown Portland. There are shops and restaurants serving local food and locally made goods. Just 3 blocks away is a food cart pod with a fire pit and outdoor market. Nearby Cathedral Park is beautifully located under the St Johns Bridge, right on the river. We have 2 cinemas within walking distance that serve food and beer in the theater.  A small local health club 3 blocks away offers day passes.  Easily accessible are 2 different bus stops that connect you to downtown and all the colorful and interesting neighborhoods around Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ddda288a-6fbf-4aae-abe1-4417d46f003e.jpg',13263099,58,'45.58846','-122.7443',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,3,28,62,4.89,21698361),(1018,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21739910','Beautiful guesthouse near restaurants, bars, shops','This two-level guest house is right in the heart of the vibrant Hawthorne neighborhood. Walk to restaurants, brewpubs, cafes, and shopping on nearby Hawthorne, Belmont and Division. The space is quiet and private with large windows, lots of wood and an elegant Pacific Northwest feel. Enjoy morning coffee or happy hour on your own patio. There’s free on-street parking and bike share is less than a block away. Perfect for singles and couples who want to experience everything Portland has to offer.','The Hawthorne neighborhood is one of Portland\'s vibrant, close-in neighborhoods. Walkable and friendly, the area features parks, restaurants, cafes, local shops and events.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b2522361-e382-41c8-a6e4-5b012c1e38dd.jpg',158343305,8,'45.51099','-122.63031',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,126.00,30,1125,74,4.99,21739910),(1019,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21742124','Convenient place for female only','The location is great. It is near to the airport PDX, it just 7 minutes by car. It is about 5 minutes to bus stops that have two lines. And there is a Winco (24 hours supermarket) just right across the street, it is about 5 minutes to get to Max station by bus. And also there are many stores and shops around. The movie theatre is about 15 minutes by car. You can enjoy the quiet and peaceful atmosphere here. Bathroom is right on the opposite. We accept woman only b\'cause  I have female student','My neighboors are friendly. and quite place.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/26e14c00-0715-4dd7-89e6-b477ae14e06a.jpg',148139307,35,'45.53516','-122.53952',2,1,1.00,2.00,2.00,40.00,30,365,12,4.92,21742124),(1020,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21752934','Pet friendly Montavilla Studio. Pets stay free!','Private studio with bath. Pet friendly with fenced patio. Montivilla neighborhood, ranked one of the top 10 coolest neighborhoods in the nation.<br /><br />Near airport, Mt Tabor, PCC, and Stark St. w/shops, pubs, restaurants, and theater. Easy access to public transit and freeways to get to heart of Portland or out to explore nature.<br /><br />A majority of our guests travel with pets, so for those with allergies or hair/fur concerns, this might not be a good fit!','Montivilla neighborhood, foot of Mt Tabor. Shops, bars, restaurants and second-run theater all within walking distance. Just a few blocks from PCC SE.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-21752934/original/058d3e56-5641-430a-aca0-3e0dc61f2d7f.jpg',37620967,10,'45.51037','-122.58314',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,1,1125,543,4.89,21752934),(1021,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21754288','New Classic Portland Guesthouse','Be one of the first to enjoy my beautiful, light filled, newly built 2 story, one bedroom guest house.  Furnished and decorated in classic Pacific Northwest Style. Located in a separate structure from my home sharing the same lot.   Private, 24 hour entry.  Ideally situated halfway between the airport and downtown in NE Portland. Walking distance to views of Mt. Hood above a wooded golf course and park teeming with wildlife.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c027f89a-b1cd-4754-9163-aaffb134f3b1.jpg',54808736,39,'45.54474639892578','-122.58920288085938',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,82.00,2,28,360,4.91,21754288),(1022,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21768930','The Butterfly Cottage','Beautifully built in 2017.  Very bright in all white with crown molding trim, high ceilings, and four skylights. There\'s not enough room to list all the great restaurants and places within walking distance or five minute drive on Hawthorne and Division: Grand Central Bakery, Jam, Castagna, Lardo, Waffle Window, Bagdad, Por Que No, Pok Pok, Salt & Straw.  New Seasons, Market of Choice, Safeway, and Fred Meyer are within walking distance. 30 minutes walk to downtown Portland.','We are located between two very prime east/west streets: Hawthorne and Division.  If you stayed here a month you could eat at a different place every night within about a mile.  Lots of choices.  If you need a quick coffee, snack, meal — a block and a half away on Hawthorne  is Grand Central Baking — bread, muffins, cookies, sandwiches, coffee.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a6d0af64-d4e8-40aa-9a44-ec9b20499c91.jpg',7409866,25,'45.51154','-122.64476',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,92.00,30,120,382,4.89,21768930),(1023,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21779678','NW 23RD AVE - Alphabet District','Stay in the heart of Portland\'s most coveted neighborhood NW 23rd Ave in the Alphabet District. Walking score of 98. Great access to loads of shops and restaurants. Condo is warm and spacious. You may not want to go home after experiencing this amazing place. Close to all of Portland main attractions.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-21779678/original/7b819cfa-4ca6-4535-92b1-1b86c97512b5.jpg',70330470,27,'45.5325','-122.69838',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,136.00,30,1125,65,4.86,21779678),(1024,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21784551','Underground Art Suite','Spacious underground art suite/apartment in the sunlit basement of our 1926 bungalow in the lively SE Foster Powell Neighborhood.<br />We partner with local artists to bring rotating artwork to the space. <br />Enjoy a relaxing guest suite with a private entrance, parking and access to nearby food carts, restaurants, bars, galleries, and shops featuring local wares art & food.<br />The space is a newly finished one bedroom modern guest suite with full kitchen, located in a quiet yet fun and funky neighborhood.','We know you will enjoy the local food and beverage scene that Portland is famous for.  Our neighborhood has coffee and breakfast spots, a Vietnamese bakery, food carts, good  sushi, a local brewery, Detroit style pizza, a  neighborhood grocery and dispensaries are all within a five minute walk.  The neighborhood has fun boutique shops featuring weird Portland finds, and the night scene includes the famous Devil’s Point and several bars that feature great food, craft cocktails, local beers, and live music.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-21784551-unapproved/original/53be5124-71f9-4bbd-aa42-86baf0ea4552.JPEG',50608466,36,'45.49616','-122.60446',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,120.00,1,31,427,4.96,21784551),(1025,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21786792','Super Quiet, Boutique Suite Guest Favorite','This well lit, 2 bedroom basement suite is perfect for 1-4 people. Each bedroom has one Queen sized bed. The full kitchen is well equipped and the full sized front loading washer and drier are quiet & convenient. Located in the Piedmont neighborhood of North Portland only minutes away from many restaurants, pubs, breweries and bars, it is also a close walk or bike ride to Legacy Emanuel Medical Center and Randall Children\'s Hospital making this a popular choice for locum tenens.','The Piedmont neighborhood is the ideal urban village. It boasts easy access to other popular Portland neighborhoods such as Humboldt, Alberta, Arbor Lodge, Boise, Eliot and Kenton, to name just a few.<br />While the Piedmont neighborhood may be farther north than other Portland neighborhoods, the area runs alongside the Max light rail train, allowing for a convenient commute to downtown Portland. The neighborhood acts as a launching point for full access to all that the city has to offer its residents. With a residential focus, the Piedmont area is community conscious. Unlike other rapidly evolving neighborhoods in Portland, Piedmont remains an old-time neighborhood filled with young families, singles, and long-established locals who celebrate their area with block parties and neighborhood association initiatives. An isolated pocket of neighborhood charm, there can be no doubt that Piedmont is a great place to live.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3272156a-fb75-455c-965e-094151be8395.jpg',58470243,48,'45.5760286','-122.6676401',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,200.00,30,1125,23,4.96,21786792),(1026,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21800129','Portland Home near Light Rail and Park','Great walking neighborhood just 6 short blocks to shops, eateries, bank, coffee, dry cleaners, groceries, hardware and more. Also kitty corner/across the street from Westmoreland park - a huge park with playground, softball, soccer/football, a huge duck pond, a casting pool and tons of green space. It is one block from the MAX light rail so easy to get around. There is a driveway and street parking as well. Please note this is our primary home so our things are here. Also, two sets of stairs.','There are shops, bars, and restaurants that are just a few short blocks away! The neighborhood is charming with older homes, tree-lined streets, and a park across the street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a1c525c0-43cf-4246-942c-c3cddcf03baa.jpg',2341031,20,'45.4734','-122.64246',1,4,3.00,2.00,1.00,155.00,2,1125,60,4.82,21800129),(1027,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21850631','Walkable Woodlawn Home','Whole home available in cute Woodlawn! (This is not a basement).  Home has AC! 5 minute walk to local brewery, cafe, city park, farmers market and more.  Easy access to downtown, Alberta Street or day trips out to the gorge.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fec7f4b9-e240-43d2-ae9c-4aad86ad1e69.jpg',5946065,45,'45.57428','-122.65305',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,19,4.79,21850631),(1028,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21861603','Guesthouse Among The Trees','Our Southeast Portland home is a newly constructed whole house rental. It is walking distance from the vibrant SE Division Street with bars and restaurants like Salt and Straw, Cicoria, Ava Gene\'s, Cibo, and Cat\'s Paw, etc. within a 5 minute walk. You’ll love our place because of the location, the quiet street and the lovely modern interior design. Oh and you\'ll have the whole place to yourself in a peaceful and quiet backyard.','Quiet neighborhood within walking distance of one of the hippest neighborhoods in Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/90d28253-31e5-4d6b-a2e6-bba50dcf2ee1.jpg',34691278,8,'45.50091','-122.6298',1,4,1.50,2.00,2.00,189.00,2,1125,208,4.95,21861603),(1029,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21863373','Piedmont Carriage House - Close in NE Portland','Studio apartment in the Piedmont neighborhood - walking distance to coffee shops, pubs, restaurants, shops, and parks. New apartment above our garage that was built with sustainability in mind.  People from all backgrounds are welcome!  We are taking extra safety precautions to disinfect all surfaces and have a one day buffer between guests.','We live in the historic Piedmont neighborhood and are within walking distance to Cafe Eleven coffee shop and the Dekum Triangle area featuring Woodlawn Coffee & Pastry, Good Neighbor Pizza, the Oregon Public House (world\'s 1st non-profit pub), Firehouse restaurant, and Breakside brewery, among others.<br /><br />It\'s also a short walk to businesses on Killingsworth Street, including In Other Words bookstore (featured on Portlandia), Turn Turn Turn/Flipside (music pub at night, coffee shop during the day, awesome all the time), and two vintage/salvage shops.<br /><br />There are food carts nearby on MLK Blvd and Killingsworth Street, which are a great option when the weather is nice. <br /><br />Both Woodlawn and Peninsula parks are within walking distance, and both have great playgrounds. Peninsula park\'s pool is open in the summer and its sunken rose garden dates to 1912.<br /><br />We are a short bike or car ride away from Alberta Street and Mississippi Street, which both have severa','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0c750ab0-cbcb-436f-9f10-792ab5ee2e36.jpg',1313392,48,'45.56718','-122.66461',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,80.00,2,30,244,4.96,21863373),(1030,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21869260','Cozy private studio-2 min walk to trendy AlbertaSt','Newly renovated basement studio in a craftsman classic house.   Alberta Arts district one block away, 2 minute walk: amazing restaurants, boutiques, food carts, organic grocery store, and a direct bus line to go to downtown (line 8- 25min).<br />15min drive from the airport (Uber/Lyft approx $16/18)','Many boutiques and galleries, restaurants for every budget on the trendy Alberta St. Also close to the up-and-coming Mississipi Avenue with lots of stores and bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ce29f278-4f7f-46be-b527-fda5139706cd.jpg',4426437,29,'45.56083','-122.65094',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,121.00,4,10,66,4.94,21869260),(1031,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21879052','Modern Studio in NE Portland (Piedmont)','Comfortable, no-smoking modern basement studio with private entrance, only minutes away from downtown and located in safe, quiet Piedmont neighborhood with plenty of on-street parking. Comfy queen size bed, private full bath and full kitchen with a full set of amenities, including 1Gb Internet service (wired and wireless). One or two adult guests. No infants or children please due to an abundance of caution regarding the stairs that lead to the space. No pets or animals of any kind allowed.','Piedmont is a quiet, family oriented neighborhood. There is a large city park a few blocks away with a beautiful rose garden, tennis courts and public pool. The trendy Alberta Arts and Mississippi neighborhoods are nearby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6ae2e23c-d03e-400b-8aa5-81475c1482e3.jpg',71495475,48,'45.56814','-122.6656',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,2,185,510,4.96,21879052),(1032,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21929069','Best neighborhood  @ Your Urban Nest','We are central to everything Portland has to offer. <br />We want you to feel right at home. We have practically everything & are willing to help if you need something special as we live right next door.  Our place is kid-friendly providing pack-n-play, toys, high chair, baby bath, books, games & have many DVD’s available upon request.<br />For additional fees - we can personally shop for groceries so that the fridge is stocked with what you need upon arrival.','We live close in to everything. Ten minute drive to downtown and to/from the airport. Close to public transportation. We are in the 90’s for both walking and biking score. We have a large park (Wilshire) at the end of the block, playground, baseball field, and running path. Located in NE Portland near well known areas such as Alberta, Mississippi, Fremont and Concordia. Tons of great shops, coffee, restaurants, grocery and night life all within walking distance','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d4f86e8e-9700-4b9a-919a-0225758f6a97.jpg',9724899,46,'45.55017','-122.62616',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,254,4.93,21929069),(1033,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21949191','Bright + cozy wood stove + holiday decor','*note: twin bunk beds photo coming asap! <br />* home for sale soon (great if you want to ‘try before you buy.’<br /><br />St. Johns is a secret Gem.  From our windows you can see the hills & mist of Forest Park, a large,  grassy lawn is great for children playing, and you\'re walking distance from the famous St. John\'s beer porch (live music-summer), grocery stores, boutiques, farmers\' markets, and direct transit lines into town.  *This is our family home* and we welcome you to enjoy it as you would your own.','- St. John\'s is a mecca for everything. You don\'t have to go into Portland if you don\'t want to. Cozy bars, walking distance from Forest Park hikes, 4 blocks from the farmer\'s market, and fun events/live music/festivals abound in Cathedral Park and in our little town. <br />- The St. John\'s bridge is famous, and you won\'t be able to stop admiring. <br />- Sauvie Island is the pick-your-own haven for everything in summer, the haunted maze leader in fall, and good for hikes and beaches year round...and just 5 minutes drive, or short bus ride. <br />- Downtown and the Pearl District are a short ride on the 16 (bus), or a 12 minute drive...busses also easily take you to famous Mississippi and Alberta areas, which are close to north Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b2194ca1-b20e-4266-b9d3-d165860dfd62.jpg',1397292,42,'45.5835','-122.74391',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,112.00,10,90,27,4.37,21949191),(1034,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21950255','morrison street eco house','Recently constructed, fully detached private garden guest house in a quiet, beautifully landscaped setting in a close-in to downtown neighborhood. Two bedrooms & master bath upstairs. Half bath downstairs. High end kitchen. One block to Belmont restaurants and shops and short walk to Laurelhurst Park & Hawthorne retail district.  Ideal for singles/couples, business travelers, two couples, or small families.','The neighborhood is close-in SE Belmont/Hawthorne, just steps away from Belmont\'s restaurants and bars and a short walk from the Hawthorne district\'s shops, bars, theaters, and restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c87adcf4-d7b4-4a76-8021-92bdf30e821e.jpg',129257796,16,'45.5163','-122.62553',1,4,1.50,2.00,2.00,202.00,2,45,54,4.98,21950255),(1035,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21957533','Little Green Garden Guesthouse','Our cheery, bright guesthouse in the North Tabor neighborhood is perfectly placed for exploring Portland. The 2-story house is simple, clean, and creatively designed.<br /><br />The first floor has a kitchen, comfy living room, and a projector for movies or youtube. The upstairs has a queen bed, full bath with rain shower and skylight, sitting area, and views into the treetops. The brick patio is shared with our main house and is warmly lit at night. When the rain stops, enjoy the cafe table and grill.','We\'re in Portland\'s North Tabor neighborhood. There\'s a city neighborhood feel here, and you can walk to several restaurants, coffee shops, and pubs. The guesthouse is walking distance to Trimet Max lightrail and Providence Hospital. The neighborhood is named for nearby Mt Tabor - a beautiful, wooded park and extinct volcano with the best views of Portland this side of the Willamette River.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-21957533/original/b7fd9565-00c5-4944-b12f-bd742eca1023.jpeg',1680036,52,'45.52632','-122.60464',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,193,4.99,21957533),(1036,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21983848','Spacious Studio Apartment Next to Reed College','Newly remodeled in December 2017, this clean and spacious studio apartment has wireless internet, a queen size bed, kitchenette, beautiful bathroom and a lovely private backyard setting.  It is in a quiet residential neighborhood with Reed College in the backyard.  Street parking is plentiful and light rail/bus access is nearby.  The  neighborhood offers excellent restaurants, grocery stores, and coffee<br />shops.  A popular brew pub and marijuana store are two blocks away.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d63e6490-168a-41c4-86f3-a565dc80e921.jpg',123234322,61,'45.48484','-122.62902',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,93.00,2,1125,230,4.96,21983848),(1037,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21996713','The Clinton Modern','The Clinton Modern is a clean and contemporary accommodation located in the heart of the famed Clinton/Division neighborhood in Portland, OR.  The neighborhood is itself embedded in the equally renown East Portland district, known for its dynamic food, rich cultural offerings, and quirky nightlife.  The locale is quiet yet conveniently accessible to all this great city has to offer.  If you\'re looking for a space to both adventure from and return to congregate with friends, look no further!','Our home is located in the culturally vibrant, inexhaustibly dynamic Clinton/Division neighborhood in Portland, OR.  It is completely walkable with an endless array of restaurants and boutique shops.  If you feel like cooking, you can walk either 2 blocks south to The People\'s Food Co-op or 2 blocks north to New Seasons.  Eating out? Try Jaqueline for the oyster happy hour or perhaps Quaintrelle for their Pacific Northwest inspired cuisine.  Time for dessert? FiftyLicks on Clinton is a must try.  A little further east is Portland\'s famed Division promenade featuring notables like Ava Jean\'s, Salt and Straw, and Bollywood Theatre.  The choices are literally endless.<br /><br />Tired of eating? Attend an event at the Tomorrow Theatre.  Catch a viewing of the longest, continuous showing of the Rocky Horror Picture show at the veritable Clinton Theatre.  Boutique shop at Xtabay\'s on Clinton or perhaps check out Langlitz Leathers on Division if motorcycle jackets are more your style.  The n','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/10cc9de5-51d9-4a1a-90fe-0a36ee2e9c7b.jpg',3917228,25,'45.50114','-122.64611',1,5,2.50,2.00,2.00,199.00,2,14,283,4.95,21996713),(1038,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/21997605','Bright and Comfortable St. Johns Apartment','Rent this one-bedroom, 500+ sq. ft. apartment in a super fun neighborhood with lots to walk to + quick access to the University of Portland, Forest Park, Sauvie Island, NW Portland/Pearl District/downtown, Vancouver,  four bus lines. The space has lots of windows, A/C, sleeps up to four, has a kitchenette + dining area.<br /><br />Well behaved + housebroken pets can be accommodated for an additional fee depending on the size, number of pets + length of stay.  Send Inquiry so I can respond with offer.','The apartment is in the awesome St. Johns neighborhood, and very close to many other neighborhoods (look up and explore Kenton, NW Portland, the Pearl District, University Park, Cathedral Park, and of course downtown)!<br /><br />We\'re near a fun food cart pod, and just a 10-minute walk to downtown St. Johns, where there are hip bars, dive bars, restaurants, shops, a farmer\'s market on Saturdays from May to October, two movie theaters, the historic St. Johns Bridge, two yoga studios, a gym, and more! Check out Eater Portland\'s #1 burrito at Tienda Santa Cruz, delicious vegan barbecue at Homegrown Smoker, Indian food at The Sudra, breakfast at John Street Cafe, trivia/bocce ball/ping pong at Leisure, live music at The Fixin\' To or Slims, coffee at Two Stroke Coffee or St. Johns Coffee Roasters, typewriter shopping at Ace Typewriter, record shopping at Vinyl Resting Place, sunset view from the middle of the St. Johns Bridge, ETC.!<br />Forest Park, just a few miles away, if you want to h','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/34bd2582-454c-436e-a55c-260ce1f3533f.jpg',126371404,58,'45.58814','-122.74318',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,123.00,30,1125,105,4.98,21997605),(1039,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22048494','Hawthorne Sunnyside Cottage','The cottage is a small, detached room with a full size bed, private bath, separate entrance, plus a beautiful patio with a relaxing seating area and fountain. Located between Hawthorne Blvd and Belmont St and a short walk to many restaurants, coffee shops, pubs, shopping, bus stops as well as Mount Tabor and Laurelhurst Parks. We welcome guests from all backgrounds, however the space is not suitable for pets or children. We don\'t charge a cleaning fee!!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cb582fca-9b85-4b25-9f5b-61e001c9b61f.jpg',10468278,16,'45.5136','-122.61371',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,1,7,886,4.96,22048494),(1040,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22088727','Bright & Colorful Home in SE Division Neighborhood','Relax and enjoy this peaceful place to stay in southeast Portland. There is a beautiful patio and backyard with grille, roses and other flowers. Inside there is a living room with lots of seating, a full kitchen, and one bathroom. There are two bedrooms upstairs, one with a queen bed and one with a full sized sofa bed. Come enjoy walking to shops and restaurants on nearby Division street or check out other great neighborhoods as well. The inner SE is a great hub for your Portland adventures!','Division Street is a 15 block stretch of restaurants, bars, coffee shops, and boutique stores. A few miles from downtown and north Portland, a very central place to call home for a few days. :)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7925fc02-03d0-454e-8a03-f43843d91f48.jpg',161360298,8,'45.49984','-122.62619',1,6,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,4,1125,25,4.88,22088727),(1041,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22108131','Portland Regency Moderne - an Artist’s Home','Maximalism meets jungalow glam in our best expression of modern Hollywood Regency for the Rose City. Hand-painted crane mural and gilded decor adorn this centrally-located, mid-century ranch artist’s home. Private access to 2BR + den/1BA home, includes a full kitchen, dining area, and sunset views of the West Hills from the front deck.','Peaceful Creston-Kenilworth neighborhood! Down the street from beautiful Creston Park. Close to Richmond neighborhood (Division / Hawthorne) and Reed College, easy walk to coffee shops, neighborhood restaurants and bars, and grocery stores (Trader Joe\'s 2 blocks away)! <br /><br />✓Walk Score: 94 - (Most errands can be accomplished on foot)<br />✓Transit Score: 54 - (Many nearby public transportation options)<br />✓Bike Score: 87 - (Mostly flat, good bike lanes)<br /><br />Several restaurants, cafes, bars and markets exist within a few block radius of the property:<br />✓Keeper Coffee Co<br />✓Trader Joes<br />✓Coffee Beer & Cutiee Buys vegan quick mart<br />✓Rocio\'s Mexican Restaurant<br />✓Hapa PDX Ramen & Whiskey<br />✓Holy Ghost Bar<br />✓28 Tigers Dumplings & Noodles<br />✓Electric Pizza Company <br />✓Natural Grocer<br />✓Safeway<br />✓Matcha Cafe Maiko<br />✓Studio One Theater<br />✓Gladstone St Woodfired Pizza<br />✓Gladstone Pub<br />✓Thunderbird Bar<br />✓Slingshot <br />✓Bro','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/853c19b7-c01a-44f3-bd9c-62482f894180.jpg',12801017,67,'45.49245461431203','-122.6201185670912',1,6,1.00,2.00,2.00,99.00,2,14,245,4.88,22108131),(1042,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22146883','The Comforts of Home in Alberta Arts (18-135432)','Up to 5 guests. Queen bed in the master bedroom & a memory foam queen sofa sleeper plus twin daybed in the living area.  A well-appointed kitchen and full laundry are within your fully separate apartment.<br /><br />3 blocks from Alberta Arts district (locally operated eateries, bars and shops) 10 min ride share to Convention Center, 15 min to airport. 5 miles to downtown','Quiet residential neighborhood only three blocks from Alberta Arts District eateries and entertainment.<br /><br />Whether your itinerary includes boutique and vintage shopping, a convention, a visit to Powell’s Books, a concert, a Blazers or Timbers game, or a visit to our excellent museums or zoo-they are all easily accessible from our close-in location.   <br /><br />Adventuresome travelers may enjoy a day trip to the region’s wine country to sample our excellent pinot noirs; explore the Columbia Gorge, hike or ski on Mount Hood, or plan a fishing trip from your home base.  <br /><br />Stumptown Central is perfect for couples, friends or families looking for a Portland getaway.  We welcome travelers of all backgrounds and experiences.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-22146883/original/64db4f1f-b8c6-4a5d-b5a4-41f106277901.jpg',13187107,19,'45.55505','-122.63877',1,5,1.00,1.00,5.00,115.00,3,28,184,4.97,22146883),(1043,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22164601','Sparkling New Studio in Ladd\'s Addition','Beautifully built in 2017, this impeccable, private studio situated above the garage was created with modern flair and design.  High end furnishings, very comfortable bed, beautiful kitchen and bath.  Located in the heart of Ladd\'s Addition, just steps from all that close-in SE has to offer. New Seasons and Market of Choice, wonderful restaurants on Hawthorne and Division, quirky antique stores, rose gardens. Walk to downtown within 15-20 minutes.  Street parking available.','We are located in Ladd\'s Addition which is Portland\'s oldest planned development. It is known for it\'s rose gardens and diagonal street pattern.<br /><br />It’s a short walk to  restaurants and shops on Hawthorne and Division. Ladd\'s is a 20-30 minute walk to downtown Portland.<br /><br />Three grocery stores within walking distance, Safeway (28th & Hawthorne), New Seasons (20th and Division), Market of Choice (12th & Morrison).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/506e11ab-7f7c-428c-9860-cf63ab624a10.jpg',22901192,25,'45.51084','-122.64913',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,128.00,2,1125,235,4.99,22164601),(1044,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22173141','Light filled basement apartment','Light filled basement apartment with 3 south facing egress windows. Open floor plan with full size eat in kitchen, gas range, full size fridge and apartment size dishwasher, lots of counter space. Queen size bed with quality bedding will offer a good nights rest. The bedroom has lots of closet and storage space. The large bathroom includes laundry and folding table, large vanity, and walk in tiled shower. Twin size built in daybed day with book shelves is a cozy space to spend a rainy day.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2b51b287-9ee3-470f-9b0f-9fc65651a18a.jpg',3228077,48,'45.57146','-122.66949',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,30,1125,6,5.00,22173141),(1045,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22228992','Modern Pearl Condo with Secure Reserved Parking','30 Day Minimum Rental<br /><br />Park Place in the Pearl <br /><br />Features include:<br /><br />- 1070 sf 5th floor unit<br />- Modern furniture <br />- Stainless steel appliances<br />- Fireplace<br />- Large master bedroom w/ Cal King Tempur-Pedic <br />- Large walk-in master closet<br />- Full double bed in 2nd bedroom/den<br />- Sleeper sofa<br />- Large bath w tub<br />- Balcony w BBQ grill<br />- Washer & Dryer<br />- 1-reserved parking space in a secured garage<br />- 55 inch Samsung Smart HDTV <br />- WiFi<br />- Concierge Service<br />- Utilities included<br />-$150 Cleaning/$300 Move in Fee','Fashionable and lively, the Pearl District is a shopping destination with hip brands, indie boutiques and the massive Powell\'s City of Books. Reclaimed warehouse space house the Pearl\'s many bars and restaurants, from craft breweries and artisan coffee shops to fine dining mainstays. Galleries showcase contemporary art, photography and glass works. In summer, families cool off in Jamieson Square\'s wading fountain.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3929c5d2-5feb-4d79-8272-e88149233d11.jpg',162425891,2,'45.53039','-122.68106',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,120.00,30,1125,3,5.00,22228992),(1046,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22229252','Greene & Greene Bungalow','Our Greene and Greene style bungalow is great for people who want to explore all that Portland has to offer, and want to do it from their own private home. Located between Alberta and Killingsworth, this home is within walking distance of some of Portland’s best restaurants, bars, and boutiques. This home is also within 15 minutes of downtown, the airport, and a half hour drive to the beautiful Gorge. Our home was built in 1906 and has been remodeled with modern appliances and amenities.','The neighborhood is extremely walkable, but the few blocks of buffer from Alberta and Killingsworth our street pretty quiet.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cf087e8b-518f-482c-be03-6b58a5bc12d4.jpg',49306713,14,'45.56113','-122.65793',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,30,11,4.64,22229252),(1047,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22280517','The Royal Scott Double Decker Bus','Our tiny home started life as a commuter bus in Manchester, England, in 1953, then did stints in San Francisco and Mt. St. Helens before finding a home as the Grilled Cheese Grill in Portland. Now it’s been reimagined as a mid century modern-inspired tiny home, with whimsical painting details from one of its former lives and fresh new handmade details that make it a cozy, inspiring stay. Find more on IG @smore.life','We are the gateway to hiking and visiting the Columbia Gorge, as well as all of Portland. Generally speaking, our place is about 15 minutes from anywhere you want to be in Portland. We are also an easy shot to and from the airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/93370530-d3e8-48ba-88bb-156ae550e84b.jpg',49871309,82,'45.54326','-122.53215',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,1,35,807,4.86,22280517),(1048,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22280827','Gem in the center of inner-Southeast','Beautifully-restored historic home in the Sunnyside neighborhood. With a very high walk  score, you\'re within blocks of restaurants, parks, food carts and more. The home has a newly remodeled kitchen and bathroom with custom closets and wide-plank pine floors. The relaxing  backyard includes tranquil ponds, covered gazebo, hot tub and seasonal garden. Well-behaved pets are welcome with a $50 pet fee. Unfortunately, we can no longer accommodate large groups or parties due to issues with noise.','Located between the beautiful Laurelhurst and Mt Tabor parks. Centrally located near the Belmont and Hawthorne neighborhoods providing tons of amenities within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c6cf3352-e55d-4601-a4bc-ed64431e3efb.jpg',162827036,16,'45.51766','-122.61592',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,175.00,2,1125,260,4.95,22280827),(1049,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22429780','The Magic Attic / Walk Score 93!','The Magic Attic is high in the heart of a charming restaurant and boutique district, 3 blocks to SE Hawthorne and Division.<br /><br />15 minutes to the airport, 9 to downtown or the convention center, with rental bikes and 4 bus stops within 2 blocks, and ample free street parking.<br /><br />The Magic House was Todji\'s sculpture studio for 17 years and is full of art.<br /><br />This is an entire attic with private bath.  The front door, stairway, 2nd floor hallway, and sculpture garden are shared space with other guests.','The Magic House is centrally located in one of the most beautiful, charming and safest neighborhoods in Portland. There is an abundance of restaurants, grocery stores, neighborhood strolling, boutique browsing and hiking options beginning within one block.<br /><br />See a movie, or just step in to witness the beautiful and iconic McMenamin\'s Bagdad theater, accompanied by an epic restaurant/bar/pool hall in the back called the \"Back Stage Bar\", at SE 37th and Hawthorne. It will give you a feel for classic Portland!<br /><br />We are minutes from Mt Tabor park which has a lovely forest with walking trails sitting upon a dormant volcano. We are 45 minutes to the spectacular 600 foot tall Multnomah waterfall in the gorgeous Columbia River Gorge scenic area (check to see if it has re-opened).<br /><br />Division Street is the new up and coming Southeast neighborhood. With lots of modern architecture, new restaurants and shops you will get a feel for the freshest vibe Portland has to offer','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/43e4813a-7b5e-4a90-b503-9dc53cd77ae9.jpg',26822355,8,'45.50882','-122.62333',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,36.00,1,7,63,4.92,22429780),(1050,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22436145','Alberta Arts: Beautiful Pet Friendly Private Home.','Clean and bright, this two-bedroom, one-bathroom house is in the heart of the Alberta Arts district. The inside is freshly painted with brand new windows making it light and bright, and the floors are refinished throughout. In the back, a fully fenced private backyard is secure for your pet and features a cedar deck with seating. The giant front porch is perfect to watch the festive and fun neighborhood. Walk to restaurants, coffee shops, bakeries, and the last Thursday art walk.','The Alberta Arts neighborhood is one of Portland\'s most exciting and walkable areas.  Restaurants, galleries, and local shops line Alberta Street and offer an excellent sense of what makes Portland such a great city. The Mississippi, Dekum, and Kenton neighborhoods each have their own flair, and are great fun to investigate, less than 10 minutes away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e8172f9f-6128-4795-bf0c-0a3a96f2a4d1.jpg',36909902,29,'45.56017','-122.64768',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,118.00,30,1125,8,4.75,22436145),(1051,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22437323','The Urban Cabin','Unique cabin style studio tucked away in quiet, up and coming Foster neighborhood. Walking distance to coffee shops and restaurants. Close to 3 major bus lines and light rail. Just 20 minutes from Portland International Airport, 10-12 minutes to Hawthorne, Division, and Woodstock neighborhoods, and 15 minutes to downtown Portland.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/37bcc306-770f-44b5-a799-066b4b5ffd45.jpg',127253983,36,'45.49326','-122.59907',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,55.00,30,30,108,4.97,22437323),(1052,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22443816','The Home With The Yellow Door/Alberta Arts','Best location ever. A stone throws away from epic Alberta Arts District (at 14th). Enjoy the best that Bohemian Portland has to offer all within walking distance. A foodie’s paradise. Cafes, bars, food carts, shops, yoga. Central to other Portland attractions. Cozy and stylish main floor of home with 2 bedrooms on main floor, living room, dining room and bath. Front porch/backyard<br /><br />Kitchenette with sink, hotplate, Airfryer/Convection Oven/Electric pressure cooker/micro/coffee/tea/toaster/fridge','In my opinion the best Bohemian/Cool/Hipster/Artsy areas in all of Portland….we are in the heart of it!!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-22443816/original/1637f0d1-db87-408e-bba9-92771aaf8e16.jpeg',1602024,14,'45.55841','-122.65198',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,89.00,1,500,680,4.81,22443816),(1053,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22449684','Rose City Guest House','Light and bright private guesthouse located behind our main house, features hardwood floors, quartz counter tops, heated tile bathroom floor and a beautiful patio to sit and relax on during those gorgeous PDX days! <br />We are located between the Hollywood and Beaumont neighborhoods so there are many restaurants, coffee shops and entertainment hotspots! Close proximity to downtown, the airport, as well as public transportation. Includes access to plenty of on street parking.','We are located in the Rose City Park neighborhood nestled between the Beaumont and Hollywood Districts. Most of the homes were built between 1912-1929. It is a great walking neighborhood with some hidden staircases along the ridge that is perfect for getting some downtown views and minutes to coffee shops, restaurants and groceries!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e513735c-ec7f-4c5c-b2fb-7d724bf13696.jpg',161634806,11,'45.54279','-122.61005',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,121.00,2,60,282,4.99,22449684),(1054,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22449916','Modern Studio w/ Patio in Quirky Kenton with AC','This modern, vibrant studio is detached from the main house and offers a private getaway for two that is in walking distance to Kenton neighborhood attractions and 10 min drive from Portland city center. All visitors from near and far welcome. This unit is pet free and smoke free.<br /><br />We are a young family of three living in the main house and look forward to hosting you.','We are located in an amazing NE Portland neighborhood called Kenton. It\'s a quirky district that feels at home in Portlandia. There are a ton of really cool coffee shops, bars, bakeries and brunch spots. A distinguishing feature is our historic Paul Bunyan statue on Denver street. It\'s a must see in this very walkable neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5b55dcc8-3a22-4f69-89e7-9c89a7b439db.jpg',33153648,55,'45.57857','-122.69876',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,388,4.87,22449916),(1055,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22450913','Urban Oasis on NW LoveJoy in the Pearl','Centrally located condominium located on the top floor of a classic brick building designed with comfort in mind. With stainless steel appliances, slate counter tops and wood floors, your temporary home away from home has been completely and tastefully remodeled. This fantastic Northwest location provides endless conveniences. The Portland Streetcar, just outside your door, will take you to downtown Portland or South Waterfront in minutes and connects you to the MAX light rail system.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/09972e31-8dd4-46c3-8900-f0f2dc34cfc3.jpg',25135442,27,'45.52949','-122.68925',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,70.00,30,1125,12,5.00,22450913),(1056,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22455628','Lovely location, Hot tub & Bikes','Welcome to your home away from home! You will have the whole house as your own. <br />We love our location in historic Irvington, a quiet neighborhood convenient to public transit, shops, & restaurants. <br />Secluded backyard has an outdoor eating area and hot tub. <br />Nice price for your visit to the City of Roses.<br />Check out our awesome reviews.','The old homes in our historic Irvington neighborhood make it a beautiful, friendly, and a joyful place for a stroll. You\'ll enjoy a short one-block walk to Broadway St. where you\'ll find  transit, shops and restaurants. Public transportation is within 1/2 block of the house.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/07a7e345-e6d5-46a6-9041-ce3303df7834.jpg',12516331,7,'45.5356','-122.64249',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,150.00,4,31,67,4.94,22455628),(1057,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22487403','BOHO Cozy Suite/Private Entrance mins from Alberta','LOCATION!! LOCATION!! LOCATION!!<br /><br />***Ideal for guest traveling for work, international guest and entrepreneurs.<br /><br />Welcome to the heart of NE Portland! Experience our trendy oasis that\'s walking distance to the popular, Alberta Art Street District where entertainment is endless. We are located just minutes away from some of the best shops, restaurants, and bars in the area.<br />This includes but is not limited to N. Williams and Mississippi Shopping areas.','RESTURANTS IN THE NEIBORHOOD INCLUDED<br /><br />TIN SHED GARDEN CAFE<br />PETITE PROVENCE<br />PINE STATE BISOUIT<br />RADIO ROOM<br />MCMENAMINS KENNEDY SCHOOL<br /><br />NEW SEASONS<br />WHOLE FOODS <br />5 MINS DRIVE AWAY<br /><br />76 GAS STATION 2 MIN DRIVE FOR YOUR CONVINCE','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-22487403/original/6a188076-ed0f-4a43-8c95-d786447152d8.jpeg',164911609,29,'45.56362','-122.65279',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,56.00,1,5,191,4.90,22487403),(1058,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22488209','Rose City Garden Retreat','Quaint guest cottage overlooking the garden. You will feel right at home in this tastefully appointed studio home featuring a gas dual fuel range, quartz counters, wood windows, skylights, marble bath with radiant floor heat and private patio space.  Steps to bus line, restaurants, grocery.  Located about 4 miles from downtown and 10 minutes from the airport and 5 minutes to Beaumont, Fremont, Hollywood Districts and 7 minutes to Alberta and Mississippi District.','Roseway is a centrally located neighborhood in the Northeast quadrant of the city.  Enjoy a walk around the neighborhood, including the Rose City Golf Course and views of Mt. Hood from the bluff on NE Sacramento Street. The golf course has a rich history.  As the story goes, the land it stands on was the first landing field for airplanes in the vicinity.   Enjoy dinner at Pizzeria Otto.  If you really want to get the flavor of yesteryear, stop by Fairley\'s pharmacy, home of one of the last functioning soda fountains in the state.  Locally owned and operated since 1913, it is like taking a step back in time with a large selection of malts, shakes, espresso, and phosphate sodas.<br /><br /><br />Just 20 blocks away is the Hollywood District, where you will find Whole Foods, Trader Joe\'s, 24-hour fitness, and the historic landmark Hollywood Theater.  The theater is now owned by a non-profit that celebrates film as art,  featuring 16mm & 35 mm screenings, and recently brought back 70mm for','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-22488209/original/97fa3b2f-577c-470b-bf81-1312c56bc3f4.jpeg',40729073,39,'45.54574','-122.59406',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,89.00,2,120,345,4.95,22488209),(1059,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22496767','Treetop Cedar Studio','Welcome :)<br />We offer you a beautiful and private treetop cedar studio space with a private entrance.  Enjoy the huge and unique Southeast treetops (Douglas Fir, Chestnut, Cedar, Apple, etc.) from your own private balcony with greenery and a bistro table.  The sunsets here are delightful! Whether you\'re traveling or looking for a spot to land for your staycation, you\'ve found it.','The Woodstock neighborhood where we are located is one of the fastest growing, up-and-coming neighborhoods in all of Portland; it\'s also one of the most walkable!  We\'ve included a binder of our favorite local spots and recommendations for how to spend any free time you might have.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-22496767/original/28a8e780-36ba-42d0-a2f2-12330591dac1.jpeg',41514066,69,'45.47528','-122.61213',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,98.00,1,365,302,4.93,22496767),(1060,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22568125','Roseway Basecamp  near PDX Airport','Entire bottom floor of cute 1927 NE Portland home in quiet Roseway neighborhood.  The space has a private separate entry and is not shared.  Full bathroom, two bedrooms, one with queen bed and the other with two twins.   Cable tv/Netflix, wifi, and kids games.   Mini fridge, microwave, coffee maker, washer/dryer, and city maps in unit.  Home is only eight minutes to the PDX airport.   Short walk to eats, bars, wine shop, grocery store, and boutique shops.  Wellington Park is only one block away.','A city park is only one block away and has open space to kick a ball around or just hang out.  There is also a playground for kids.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2810f8cd-caf5-4b25-a6ee-4150cf21a8fe.jpg',32163035,39,'45.55479','-122.5963',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,89.00,1,1125,333,4.81,22568125),(1061,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22599038','Portland International Guesthouse Room 2','Room #2 is our economy room.  It has 1 twin (single) bed, small chest of drawers, large mirror and a bookcase. There is a large window in the room facing west.   Please see all 4 room listings for our Guesthouse and don\'t miss our 1 bedroom apartment (in same building as the Guesthouse) listed here on AirBnb!  Thank you.','Ideally located in the heart of Portland’s most charming and vibrant neighborhood, travelers can easily walk to myriad shops, restaurants, cafes and bars, enjoy the beauty and serenity of the Japanese Garden and Washington Park, or hike over 40 miles of trails in Portland’s Forest Park, the largest natural urban park in the US.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-22599038/original/4a84e40f-f225-412d-a106-37e10115b5ac.jpeg',2915808,27,'45.525699615478516','-122.6963882446289',2,1,2.50,1.00,1.00,85.00,1,20,132,4.94,22599038),(1062,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22608587','Beautifully Crafted NE Portland ADU','Live in Portland\'s first Net Zero ADU! Built in 2017, this is a beautifully crafted, 2 story house with lots of natural light and the latest in eco-friendly design, materials, fixtures and technology. Situated in the backyard of the main house, a glass sliding door onto a covered stone patio extends the living space into the bird-friendly garden. Access is via a gated, paved pathway. 2 blocks from restaurants & shops on N Williams and centrally located with easy access to any part of town.','We live on a quiet block in close-in NE Portland with great neighbors, on the border of King and Boise Eliot neighborhoods. We are two blocks from Williams, which has a fun variety of excellent shops, restaurants, coffee shops, bakeries, wine bars and hangout spots. There is a New Seasons natural food focused grocery store six blocks away (Williams and Fremont). Mississippi Ave also has lots of great shops and restaurants and is a 10-15 minute walk from our house (0.6 mile). The popular Alberta Arts district is about a 20-30 minute walk or a quick bike ride away (a little over a mile).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5431c763-433d-4c1f-baab-c85675768c53.jpg',11122733,14,'45.5517','-122.66357',1,2,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,14,120,45,4.96,22608587),(1063,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22614995','Portland International Guesthouse Room 3','Room #3 has 1 queen bed, large closet, 1 large window, bistro table & chair set, chest of drawers and a comfy chair..  One full bath and one 1/2 bath along with our breakfast/common room are on the same floor as this room. Please see all 4 room listings for our Guesthouse and don\'t miss our 1 bedroom apartment (in same building as the Guesthouse) listed here on AirBnb!  Thank you.','The Guesthouse is located in Portland\'s historic Alphabet District also known as Nob Hill. Our neighborhood is the city\'s most charming and vibrant. We are within walking distance or a short transit ride Downtown, the Pearl District, Powell\'s Books and most of Portland\'s major cultural institutions.<br /><br />One can meander through the neighborhood streets lined with Victorian homes, NW 23rd and 21st Avenues lined with shops and restaurants or walk up to Washington Park and the amazing Japanese Gardens. From there, it is possible to access over 40 miles of hiking trails.<br /><br />Some of the Portland\'s best restaurants, coffee houses and cinemas are only a few blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-22614995/original/839e8c11-7d3d-40bd-83d9-019f8168a3d0.jpeg',2915808,27,'45.525699615478516','-122.6963882446289',2,2,3.50,1.00,1.00,93.00,1,20,136,4.92,22614995),(1064,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22615930','Portland International Guesthouse Room 4','Room #4 is a large room on the top floor (up 2 sets of stairs) of the Guesthouse.  It has 1 queen bed and 1 single bed and carries a max capacity of 2 people.  It has 2 large windows, small desk & chair, large closet, an upholstered chair and ample floor space.  One bath, with large, walk-in shower, and one 1/2 bath are on this floor, too. Please see all 4 room listings for our Guesthouse and don\'t miss our 1 bedroom apartment (in same building as the Guesthouse) listed here on AirBnb!','The Guesthouse is located in Portland\'s historic Alphabet District also known as Nob Hill. Our neighborhood is the city\'s most charming and vibrant. We are within walking distance or a short transit ride Downtown, the Pearl District, Powell\'s Books and most of Portland\'s major cultural institutions.<br /><br />One can meander through the neighborhood streets lined with Victorian homes, NW 23rd and 21st Avenues lined with shops and restaurants or walk up to Washington Park and the amazing Japanese Gardens. From there, it is possible to access over 40 miles of hiking trails.<br /><br />Some of the Portland\'s best restaurants, coffee houses and cinemas are only a few blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-22615930/original/633968b6-db7c-456d-9082-29ac77d74370.jpeg',2915808,27,'45.525699615478516','-122.6963882446289',2,2,2.50,1.00,2.00,100.00,1,20,113,4.93,22615930),(1065,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22618305','Minimalist apartment on the edge of Pearl','Impeccable one-bedroom apartment on the edge of the Pearl. Minimalist decor, luxury finishes. Fast wifi, with remote work needs in mind. <br /><br />10 to 15 minutes walk to bars, cafes in Pearl. Get to Powell\'s Books in 15 minutes and to downtown in 25 minutes, by foot.  OHSU by car in 15 min. 10-minute drive to NE bars on Mississippi. <br /><br />Standing desk for remote working. Parking space included, jacuzzi tub and seasonal pool access. 24 hour check-in, <br /><br />Only available for long-term, 30+ day stays.','Located at the edge of the Pearl, within 15 minutes walking distance to most bars and restaurants in the Pearl. 25 minutes to walk to downtown. Minutes to the river running trail by the waterfront and between 6-8 minutes to streetcar stations.<br /><br />It\'s a more quiet and residential area that offers the proximity to the waterfront.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/99fe2c00-3b6c-412b-aa8e-8e4909ed35f3.jpg',3285925,43,'45.5296','-122.67606',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,30,365,200,4.67,22618305),(1066,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22618697','Cozy Two Bedroom High Ceiling Daylight ADU','Relax with the whole family at this peaceful place on a quiet dead-end street but close to good dining and interesting shops. This is a family home with a separate 840 sqft. daylight apartment. Two separate bedrooms each with a queen sized bed and an easy pull-out queen sleeper in the main area allow for up to six guests. It\'s complete with a full kitchen and washer and dryer. The quiet backyard has outdoor seating and a wood fired hot tub. A few chickens provide us with fresh eggs.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-22618697/original/c542ddd5-8982-4860-876b-5d49cdd67809.jpeg',22042161,8,'45.50029','-122.62072',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,105.00,2,1125,70,4.99,22618697),(1067,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22654722','NE Portland studio with private courtyard','NE Portland kitchenette studio apartment with excellent proximity to both the airport (15 minute drive) and downtown Portland (20 min. drive).<br />The unit has a 70 walkscore, bus lines one block away, multiple restaurants in walking distance, in a chill neighborhood .<br />With lots of light, blue pine accents, cork flooring, 340 square feet of carefully designed interior space, and private courtyard, it feels like an updated cabin oasis.','This is a brand new 340 sq ft kitchenette studio apartment with excellent proximity to both PDX (15 minute drive) and downtown Portland (20 minute drive).<br />The unit has a 70 walkscore and is one block from two phenomenal restaurants, Tamale Boy** and Tough Luck* as well as Ranch Pizza**. Within a half-mile is Ps and Qs Market**, a European style market with great, hand-crafted food, and the Dekum Triangle, home to Good Neighbor Pizzeria*, Woodlawn Coffee*, Grand Army Tavern*, The Firehouse**, and nationally acclaimed Breakside Brewery**.<br />A five minute drive away is the Alberta Arts shopping district, where numerous dining and shopping options abound.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ecdaf869-07c2-423a-83a1-1b1e5a70068e.jpg',142027593,45,'45.57201','-122.64782',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,83.00,30,31,581,4.98,22654722),(1068,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22658710','The Hummingbird Suite','The Hummingbird Suite is a generous sized bedroom with great natural light. It features french doors, oriental rugs, vintage furnishings, and a soffet wall with curtains to allow visual privacy for a second bed. The front half of the room has a queen size bed and an arm chair; the back half has a full-sized bed and a velvet loveseat. A wardrobe and dresser complete the space.','Inner-Southeast Portland is one of Portland’s most vibrant neighborhoods.<br />It is extremely walkable/bikeable, and our home is just two blocks from one of Portland\'s great restaurant rows, filled with unique locally owned restaurants, coffeehouses, bars, food carts, pot shops, ice cream vendors, pizza joints, clothing retailers, yoga studios and yes, even an old-school hardware store. All of this just 15 minutes from downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjI2NTg3MTA%3D/original/31e87b02-6d3d-48d5-8eef-39f210c069b1.jpeg',45329606,8,'45.50327','-122.62739',2,2,2.00,1.00,2.00,48.00,3,90,327,4.93,22658710),(1069,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22659735','The Cyan Room','Th Cyan Room is a small private bedroom in our fully restored 1911 Old Portland home. It features a box beam ceiling, hardwood floors, an ample closet and dresser, as well as a queen bed and side chair. Our super-friendly cats may drop by to say hello during your stay.','Lots of good restaurants, coffee shops, bars, retail shopping, bakeries, gelato shops and even an old-school hardware store are within a couple blocks of our home. You’re also two blocks from public transportation and a reasonably priced electric bike rental. Our neighborhood is safe, walkable and bike-friendly. Lots of trees and lush greenery everywhere.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4c687391-bc2a-4eca-a668-3969b8acf11e.jpg',45329606,8,'45.50289','-122.62776',2,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,39.00,3,90,493,4.89,22659735),(1070,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22686855','1 BR in N. Mississippi Food and Arts District','Our house is an updated English Tudor style 3-bedroom/2-bathroom 1920\'s bungalow (1,800 sq. ft.) in the popular and hip Mississippi Food and Arts District in North Portland. The house is located on a quiet street within walking distance of Peninsula Park, New Season\'s and the city’s light rail public transit system. Award-winning restaurants, coffee shops, boutiques, live music and the Adidas Headquarters are near by. The house has immediate access to I-5 and is 5 minutes away from downtown.','The Historic Mississippi District is an example of quintessential Portland culture, combining creative originality and diversity with lots of independent energy.  Almost every business is locally owned and operated, including some of Portland\'s most talked about restaurants, coffee shops, brew pubs, and boutique clothing stores.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/aeb43100-2cad-4a7e-85c8-f14967481e5f.jpg',167221905,48,'45.56699','-122.67534',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,69.00,30,1125,197,4.96,22686855),(1071,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22689376','Bright + Cozy Guesthouse w/ Classic Portland Charm','This bright + open cozy guesthouse is imbued with creative style and classic Portland charm. With the perfect mix of vintage and modern, the space features work by local artists, plenty of greenery for plant lovers, a record/cd/radio player + a delightful walkout balcony for outdoor drinks or relaxing.','Located in a historic, vibrant, multi-cultural, socially-conscious NE Portland neighborhood. Nestled among N. Williams St, the Alberta Arts District, and N. Mississippi Ave, all with amazing shops and dining spots!<br /><br />Just over the Fremont Bridge from Forest Park, for incredible hikes and nature walks.<br /><br />Around the corner from Irving Park. Walking distance to Whole Foods and  New Seasons neighborhood grocery store.<br /><br />Minutes away from some of Portland\'s best live music venues. Favorite restaurants within walking distance include EEM, Kayos Ramen Bar, Life of Pie, and XLB. Also nearby is Porque No, with some of the best tacos in town. <br /><br />A few minutes to downtown, the Pearl, NW 23rd, Moda Center, the Convention Center, and the iconic Powell\'s Books.<br /><br />An hour and a half to the Coast and to Mt Hood. 45 minutes to the Columbia River Gorge. <br /><br />20 minutes by car to Portland International Airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-22689376/original/8e5f8d7a-0265-45d6-9f1f-2303514b8432.jpeg',27752797,26,'45.54516','-122.66002',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,145.00,30,365,25,5.00,22689376),(1072,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22693154','❤️ CLEAN ★ LUXURY OASIS ★ NEAR DOWNTOWN','☀ 10 Mins to downtown + Airport <br />☀ Free Private on-site parking <br />☀ Luxury queen bed • premium bedding<br />☀ Queen sleeper sofa in living room<br />☀ Fully stocked cook’s kitchen<br />☀ Large private patio<br />☀ Fire Pit + Gas BBQ<br />☀ Super Fast Wifi • USB charging outlets<br />☀ 65” 4K Smart TV<br />☀ Smart Home • Alexa equipped<br />☀ Nebia Spa shower<br />☀ Heated floors<br />☀ Steps from public transit<br />☀ Safe walkable neighborhood<br />☀ Bikes to explore Portland <br /><br />★☆Learn More Below & Experience Portland With Us!★☆','•  Located in the historic Laurelhurst/Tabor neighborhood <br />• Extremely safe <br />•  Fantastic quiet walkable neighborhood <br />•  A dream for bikers<br />•  Huge lush mature trees<br />•  Walking distance to public transit, awesome restaurants, bars & coffee shops<br />• A Starbucks 4 doors down','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a4bdc36f-8a0d-4739-940f-d03d53fe21f1.jpg',14008197,52,'45.52556','-122.61682',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,125.00,2,30,321,4.95,22693154),(1073,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22701360','2-bedroom Home - Modern-CLEAN! Close-in (日本語）','Enjoy this newer construction, private entry home.  One of Portland\'s hottest neighborhoods with streets such as Mississippi, Alberta and Williams - some of Portland\'s go to locations for shopping, exploring, eating and drinking.  Walk to restaurants, coffee, brew pubs, bakeries, boutiques, parks and more.  Less than 3 miles to Pearl District & downtown! 7 Miles from Portland International Airport.  Blocks from Emanuel and  Randall. Hosts speak Japanese.<br /><br />Free Street Parking!','Excellent Freeway access and public transportation make this place unique.  N. Williams is just a couple blocks away and N. Mississippi is a short walk.  Prefer to bike?   BIKETOWN is Portland\'s bike share program, launched in July 2016 with 1,000 bikes at 100 stations across downtown and several neighborhoods. The system is designed for quick trips with convenience in mind, and it’s a fun and affordable way to get around. There are two bike hubs just a few short blocks from our home.  Search Bike Town Portland to learn more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d2b1306d-290c-413f-8be6-500b516e17ee.jpg',6917563,9,'45.55086','-122.66478',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,120.00,1,28,223,4.96,22701360),(1074,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22727693','Woodstock Hideway, clean comfort, great location','Sparkling clean, completely private with contactless self-check in, comfy two queen bedroom garden apartment with full kitchen, bath, living room, and private patio in a quite, safe neighborhood.  Convenient to airport, i-205, i-5, Reed, Hawthorne District, Mt Tabor and downtown, it\'s a great spot to relax and explore Portland from.  Easy to get to and with plenty of street parking and easy public transit, you\'ll be in your new digs in no time.  And lots of great places to eat and drink nearby!','The blooming Woodstock neighborhood, which has two supermarkets, many pubs and restaurants, a bike shop, shopping, and many other amenities is a 15 minute walk.   We are also adjacent to the FoPo (Foster Powell) neighborhood, and with 5-7 minutes walk there are restaurants, local pubs, a bottle shop, a local market and much more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c7d02195-464f-4197-a21e-51676300bdde.jpg',24365988,38,'45.48864','-122.60367',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,125.00,3,29,168,4.98,22727693),(1075,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22732326','Architect-designed house in SE Portland’s MtTabor','Our modern guesthouse is a clean, private space filled with natural light.  The front gate opens into a private, landscaped courtyard landscaped with jasmine, a Japanese maple tree, rhododendrons, and ferns.  We are conveniently located near Mt Tabor Park that has walking trails and a spectacular view of the city.  We are also close to several popular neighborhoods with shops, cafés, and restaurants.  We welcome people of all backgrounds to stay here and enjoy beautiful Portland.','Mt Tabor neighborhood is best known for its beautiful city park, Mt Tabor Park, which is an extinct volcano about a 10-minute walk from here.  Walking paths guide you among majestic fir trees, and at the peak of Mt Tabor are panoramic views of the city and water reservoirs.  This is a destination for hikers, walkers, bikers, dog-walkers, and birders (Mt Tabor is along the path of many migratory birds).  Families with kids enjoy the playground located near the picnic shelters and information office.<br /><br />A couple of coffee shops are within walking distance of the guesthouse, as are several good restaurants and bars (Tabor Tavern, Caldera, Belmont Station).  The Cheese Bar on the corner of SE 60th and Belmont Street, is a nationally recognized cheese counter, and a great place to get a bite to eat and a drink.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-22732326-unapproved/original/a8320896-a48e-4898-9a04-45c871847a43.JPEG',6468837,15,'45.51988','-122.60383',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,135.00,1,60,338,4.98,22732326),(1076,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22733624','Central condo in downtown PDX','Bright top floor unit centrally located in downtown Portland. Beautiful refinished hardwood floors, antique touches, remodeled with new kitchen appliances and big windows to let in the sunshine. Nice living room space with large couch, a dining nook and walk in closet with ample storage space.<br /><br />Pet friendly.<br /><br />Location is key here with close proximity to NW 23rd, the pearl and just 10 minutes car ride to Beaverton (Nike and Columbia campuses).<br /><br />Street parking only available.','Close to shopping, some of the best Portland dining and just a few blocks from the freeway so getting around town is easy.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dd8124f7-ef00-414e-967c-0af068f34d4f.jpg',9111756,3,'45.52079','-122.68941',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,67.00,30,1125,21,4.67,22733624),(1077,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22733844','Duplex in Alberta Art District!','Newly remodeled duplex interior, finished hardwood floor in living and dining rooms,bathroom with tub, fully equipped kitchen, stove, new refrigerator, cable TV, central heating/A.C.  and internet/Wi-Fi. Located close to <br />Alberta Art District with many good restaurant close by, you will be tempted to dine out!  Alberta park just across the street, 5 min walk to Alberta St, 10 min from Airport, 10 min to downtown PDX, 10 min, <br />!!!HOST & FAMILY ALLERGIC TO DOGS & CATS!!!   NOT ALLOWED<br />PLEASE!!!','Alberta Art District, 4-5 min walk, Alberta Park Just Across the Street,','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-22733844-unapproved/original/333a8f5d-70da-4d5b-abc7-2e1fef964991.JPEG',63619764,14,'45.56239','-122.65716',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,175.00,2,22,57,4.98,22733844),(1078,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22776781','Tabor Cottage: Detached Guest House SE Portland','Mt. Tabor Cottage is a quiet, cozy, detached one bedroom house.with a private, fenced patio. In the South Tabor neighborhood, we are close to Mt. Tabor park and walking distance to several restaurants. It\'s a 15 minute car ride to the airport or about 17-20 minutes to downtown Portland and only a 5 -7 minute drive to Montavilla, Division St and Hawthorne Blvd restaurants, bars and shopping. Street parking is always available on the block, often next to property or within 150ft, 30 second walk!','Mt. Tabor Cottage is located in Portland\'s South Tabor neighborhood, home to Mt. Tabor, an extinct volcanic cinder cone.  The park surrounding Mt. Tabor includes numerous hiking trails, paved pathways, a playground, tennis and basketball courts, a visitor center, and plenty of views of the city and Mt. Hood. <br /><br />Mt. Tabor Cottage is also adjacent to the Jade District, which is home to a variety of Asian restaurants and unique international shopping.<br /><br />Take a 4-minute car ride to Montavilla, a fun neighborhood with plenty of places to go, including The Observatory restaurant, the Academy Theater, Montavilla Brewing and the Bipartisan Cafe. <br /><br />A 5-minute drive down SE Division leads to the beginning of Division Street restaurants, bars, and boutique shopping. Stop by Petite Provence for French pastries or a full breakfast, or enjoy a morning beverage at Stumptown Coffee Roasters. Go further west on Division to the Division/Clinton area, home to iconic restaurant','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-22776781/original/eb2ee162-7f85-4947-b60c-c9cb765e2262.jpg',168264312,37,'45.50329','-122.57912',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,2,10,419,4.95,22776781),(1079,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22808872','Cozy Murphy Bed Studio: Kitchenette near Hawthorne','Nestled between the bustling streets of Hawthorne & Division, this cozy studio is situated in the epicenter of the best SE Portland has to offer. A short walk through our charming neighborhood will get you to restaurants, bars, shops & more.','My house is situated in one of the best areas of SE Portland. Just a block off of the busy Hawthorne Blvd, you\'ll find shops, restaurants and bars just a quick walk away. This residential neighborhood is pretty quiet and tucked away but well-positioned for exploration!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/baaabff3-14a4-499a-8fd2-d3c32448406f.jpg',28583708,8,'45.51001','-122.63354',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,75.00,2,60,152,4.86,22808872),(1080,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22810044','Prime Location! Historic home available monthly','Light-filled private apartment: Top 2 floors of Victorian duplex in unbeatable spot, just off bustling NW 23rd Ave. Chef\'s kitchen, rain shower, A/C, in-unit laundry, one off-street parking spot & more! Month-to-month only.  30-day minimum.','The Neighborhood...<br />The neighborhood goes by many names - Northwest District, Nob Hill, Alphabet District are a few.  But whatever you call it, you\'ll find the best of everything Portland has to offer right here!   <br /><br />Within 3 blocks:<br />-  NW 23rd Ave (restaurants, shops, ice cream)<br />-  NW 21st Ave (bars & nightlife)<br />-  Trader Joe\'s grocery store<br />-  Centrally located<br />-  Street Car & Bus Stops (easy transfer to Max to/from Portland International Airport)<br /><br />Short walk to:<br />-  Timber\'s Stadium (Providence Park)<br />-  Providence Park Max Station<br />-  Fred Meyer, Zupan\'s, Walgreens, Starbucks<br />-  Parks, playgrounds, basketball courts & more<br />-  Forest Park (5,000 acre urban forest with hiking & biking trails)<br /><br />\"City Hike\" or 5-Minute Transit to:<br />-  Pearl District, Old Town, Downtown<br />-  Saturday/Sunday Market, Waterfront<br />-  Washington Park/Rose Garden<br />-  Oregon Zoo, Children\'s Museum, World Forestry C','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/72fe787c-846f-4256-ae8e-522e043f8b55.jpg',20727837,27,'45.5277','-122.69873',1,7,2.00,3.00,3.00,272.00,31,1125,194,4.95,22810044),(1081,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22813740','Charming South Tabor Apartment!','Charming, remodeled, clean one-bedroom basement apartment with some natural light. Private entrance and patio. In a quiet, safe SE neighborhood central for exploring Portland. Walk to Mt. Tabor Park. Furnished in mid-century style, with high-end cotton linens, bedding and towels; full kitchen and bathroom. Large flat-screen TV, full Cable, HBO, etc. Very reliable WiFi. We welcome all nationalities, ethnicities and creeds. We are LGBT-friendly!  We’re 420 friendly outside in the private patio.','Our South Tabor neighborhood is a good home-base from which to explore all the fun neighborhoods, restaurants, coffee shops and creative businesses that make Portland so exciting. We are minutes away from nearby SE Division and Clinton streets, as well as SE Hawthorne Boulevard. <br /><br />Our house is walking distance from pretty Mt. Tabor Park, an awesome park in Portland, well loved for walking (around 2 different reservoirs, with views) hiking trails (it\'s a volcano!) and scenic views - west to downtown and east to snow-covered Mt. Hood. We are close to Clinton park, next to the most beautiful high school - Lincoln High - (it looks like a movie set)!<br /><br />There are several nearby grocery stores nearby and great, affordable restaurants in the nearby Jade district. We are two minutes from one of the best Vietnamese soup places in the whole city that serves world class Pho. <br /><br />We’re less than 10 minutes drive from all the delicious restaurants, bakeries, bars and inter','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/39dc84ff-db2c-47b2-9d37-183a6f96b8cc.jpg',9691781,37,'45.49849','-122.58638',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,2,90,206,4.92,22813740),(1082,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22877200','Accessible, AIA-Award Winning, Urban Garden Oasis','A nurturing place with abundant light, garden views, & access to the best Portland food.<br /><br />“The best Airbnb I’ve ever stayed in!” - frequent guest comment. <br /><br />- American Institute of Architects Award to designer Webster Wilson<br />- Upscale amenities & European fixtures<br />- Quiet NoPo neighborhood tree-lined street, minutes from downtown <br />- Fully equipped kitchen w/ fresh local coffee<br />- Indoor & outdoor dining <br />- See photo captions for more details<br />- Trained Service Animals welcome; no pets nor ESAs','The Mock\'s Crest area is in the Arbor Lodge neighborhood and was built nearly a century ago. You\'ll see plenty of \"Old Portland\" style homes while staying close to all the main attractions downtown. We are about halfway between Interstate 5 and the thriving community of St. Johns, which is full of small shops, restaurants, breweries, Cathedral Park, and the iconic St. Johns Bridge. We are also 1 mile from University of Portland and a great place for parents and grandparents to stay during university events.<br /><br />Columbia Park is 2 blocks from our home and its giant fir trees provide shade for beautiful picnics all summer long. The Kenton Farmer\'s market is also within 2 miles (open Wednesday’s from June 6-September 25).<br /><br />If you’re looking for Farm to Table experiences, we can direct you to berry picking on nearby Sauvie Island or dinner in a field at one of their farms.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8db6f577-bda8-41ff-9d33-2de7be8ba202.jpg',19143593,51,'45.57653','-122.70664',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,135.00,2,30,474,4.99,22877200),(1083,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22886335','Relaxing retreat steps to OHSU & min from downtown','This bright, newly renovated home in the Southwest Hills is just minutes away from OHSU, Marquam Nature Trail, downtown Portland and Council Crest. The 2-bedroom flat provides plenty of space for guests, and also equipped with a full kitchen and bathroom with everything you\'ll need during your visit. Located in the quiet and historic Homestead neighborhood with free parking, this home is the perfect location for families and groups on their Portland vacation or business stay.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-22886335/original/1c1cccea-1fb5-4b41-a6a6-663403b08579.jpeg',70200278,30,'45.49724','-122.69295',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,119.00,1,1125,351,4.90,22886335),(1084,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22955191','Modern Alberta Arts Studio w/ King Bed, Best of NE','Modern studio with private entrance, perfect for couples and business travelers. Plush king-size bed, sitting area, kitchenette, and modern bathroom with essentials.<br /><br />Walkable neighborhood with awesome restaurants around the corner and the best of Alberta Street steps away. We\'re located just 15 minutes from the airport, and close to downtown.<br /><br />On parle français... Y también hablamos español.','We\'re on a quiet street in one of Portland\'s hottest, most walkable neighborhoods. As Travel Portland puts it, \"Independent and diverse, this Northeast Portland neighborhood teems with art, shopping and dining options.\"<br /><br />In keeping with the neighborhood’s diversity, the dining options offer food for every taste (vegan to carnivore), craving (foie gras to fried chicken) and budget (PBR to Dom Pérignon).<br /><br />Peppered with locally owned shops, cafés, bars and galleries, Alberta street (a short walk from our home) is famed for its monthly Last Thursday street fair, but offers entertaining options any day of the month.<br /><br />When you check in we\'ll send you a link to a map we created with our favorite haunts in the neighborhood and beyond.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9c6ee2e2-be3c-4924-83f0-437239734250.jpg',20705013,29,'45.56274','-122.64935',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,1,10,257,4.95,22955191),(1085,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23021927','Inner NE - Moda, Mississippi, Downtown','Great inner NE Portland location! Perfect for individual travelers or couples who are here to explore all this exciting city has to offer. We are close to downtown, the Williams corridor, Moda Center, Alberta Arts district, Mississippi Ave and Emanuel hospital; and within walking distance of many bars, breweries, restaurants, and music venues!','This is a busy and bustling inner NE Portland location with older beautiful homes and quick easy access to many amenities. There is close access the Williams corridor, Moda Center, Mississippi Ave., and the Alberta Art district. <br /><br />You can walk to some really great places to eat and drink in the area. We are just blocks from critically acclaimed restaurants like Ox and EEM. There are several craft  brew and cider houses very close by. Also nearby are an oyster house, ramen and a fabulous bakery.<br /><br />We are about 22 minutes from the airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-23021927/original/b1dc6bb8-6be3-4d21-8fa0-d2aad25a04a7.jpg',113106891,26,'45.54471','-122.66353',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,3,7,242,4.98,23021927),(1086,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23045959','Cozy, eclectic home near downtown','This spacious, cheerful home has everything you need for the perfect Portland getaway or extended stay. Two queen bedrooms are situated perfectly for privacy and the large sitting area makes for a cozy place for winding down and includes a comfy sofa.   A fully equipped kitchen and washer and dryer ensure you have everything you need.  Close to Downtown (10-min drive) with ample street parking, and a large private deck provides the perfect place to unwind.','John\'s Landing is a vibrant community of primarily residential homes nestled in between major arterial roads with restaurants, bars and shops. Located near the Willamette River, you\'ll enjoy a beautiful, paved walking trail connecting the area with downtown along the river -- perfect for walking, biking or running. Oh yeah, and Zupan\'s, an amazing grocery store, is just around the corner.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-23045959/original/2e209f4a-38ee-44d4-8810-98cc161f2b25.jpeg',7409866,22,'45.47045','-122.67251',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,81.00,30,60,123,4.86,23045959),(1087,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23063504','Bright Queen Bed Overlooking Courtyard','Need to extend your stay? Ask about adding 60 days, 90 days and more!<br /><br />Light and bright tropical vibe studio with comfy queen bed, private bathroom and kitchenette.<br /><br />Kitchenette: microwave, two burners, toaster oven, dorm-size fridge, sink, French press, coffee beans, dishes, etc!<br /><br />Walk in shower.<br /><br />3 mins to Mt Tabor.<br /><br />The studio is accessible through the garage and opens onto a shared courtyard.<br /><br />If traveling with a pet they must be accompanied by their humans at all times or in a crate. :-)','Quiet neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a70ddfab-1030-4bea-a27a-737aefa73186.jpg',8260857,37,'45.50388','-122.59061',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,120,222,4.73,23063504),(1088,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23094747','Modern Guest House in North Portland','Charming updated guest house in conveniently located North Portland.  Easy and quick access to the airport, downtown, the thriving Mississippi neighborhood, the University or Portland, and all of Portland\'s major attractions.<br />It’s a short walk to coffee shops & restaurants, and only a quarter mile to Adidas HQ.  This units enjoys easy access to both bus service and the MAX yellow train line.','Located in desirable Arbor Lodge in north Portland. <br />It\'s a quiet area and people comment what great sleep they have here! <br />This is a walkable neighborhood with Arbor Lodge Park four blocks away. <br />Beautiful University of Portland is 3 miles with an overlook of the Columbia River. <br />The Adidas campus is only about 5 blocks away.<br />Killingsworth street (half-block away) has several restaurants and coffee shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e2406324-2f84-4004-884b-e83cd48fd554.jpg',20418871,13,'45.56452','-122.69629',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,1,30,387,4.94,23094747),(1089,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23102673','University of Portland Oasis','Welcome to our beautiful, modern, 750 square ft one bedroom apartment. Our apartment has its own private entrance and is located on the lower level of our newer three story home. Our designated work space (desk, comfortable chair, WIFI, great lighting and office supplies) will be great for business travelers or anyone with a little work to do.','Our apartment is just a short walk to the University of Portland, and a 5 minute drive to the Adidas and Daimler headquarters. With close proximity to St. Johns and Kenton areas, and a 15-20 minute ride via bus or car to downtown Portland, Pearl District, Alberta Arts District, or Mississippi Avenue, you get a taste of Portland\'s small town charm with access to it\'s big city fun.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-23102673/original/b0884470-2db7-4750-904f-b7f1756020d7.jpeg',108079827,57,'45.57533','-122.72138',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,7,60,89,4.98,23102673),(1090,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23128043','Charming, Detached Studio!  Heart of Sellwood!','I have lived in Sellwood for over 20 years  and, in our opinion, it\'s by far the best place to be in Portland...  welcome!  If you are coming for work, to visit with family, or simply want to explore and relax, you are sure to find comfort while staying here in this BEAUTIFUL Sellwood Studio Space!  Everything you need is just a WALK away!','If you are not familiar with the charm and uniqueness of Sellwood, take some time to explore this place, and all that it has to offer.  The studio is in a peaceful, quiet neighborhood in the heart of Sellwood.<br /><br />To the north, only four houses away, is the infamous Sellwood Park.  Walk two more blocks and you are treated with one of the best views in Portland, overlooking a 140-acre Wetland with our city skyline off in the near distance.  And, the  fully operating, 1910 Oaks Amusement Park and Skating Rink are within a 10 minute walk settled along the Willamette River.<br /><br />The amazing Sellwood Park is a walk away; If you have time for a walk, this is a must!!! At the northend, you will find a trailhead that leads down and around the 140 acre wetland of Oaks Bottom. It\'s a beautiful mixture of forested trails, water, and wild life! Either walk out and back or make it a loop. Depending on your direction, you may walk past our old historic Oaks Chapel, the oldest, one-story','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/be26691f-821b-4be6-8f7a-9a33eeb3ce55.jpg',56540131,20,'45.46657','-122.66019',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,68.00,2,14,346,4.95,23128043),(1091,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23164577','Gorgeous Laurelhurst 2 bed home! Walk Score 93!','Welcome to The Laurelhurst Townhouse! You can\'t get much more central than this roomy, stylish home with a walk score of 93! Settle in and enjoy the airy, light-filled living area, the cozy bedrooms, and the backyard patio--and then head out for a night on the town. Walkable to a myriad of Portland\'s most famous restaurants, bars and shops, and only a few minutes away from downtown and the Pearl District.  Quiet and private,  the Laurelhurst Townhouse is a gem in the heart of it all!','Kerns, being relatively close-in to downtown Portland, is in a fairly urban area sprinkled with beautiful, large homes with period charm and details<br /><br />Kerns has many popular Portland restaurants and locally owned businesses, making this a  fun neighborhood to visit.  The nearby shops, bars, and restaurants along Burnside and 28th Avenue are some of the best in town. The Laurelhurst Theater is a great old classic theater for catching a movie. Kerns is also home to some of Portland\'s finest breweries!<br /><br />Kerns is considered to be urban, artsy, bike-friendly, green and eco-conscious.  This is a neighborhood of families, singles, and urbanites.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5931e87d-e2c5-4896-abe0-bc7198d75c52.jpg',7409866,12,'45.5243','-122.6338',1,4,1.50,2.00,2.00,135.00,2,30,305,4.95,23164577),(1092,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23255044','Gorgeous Irvington Apartment','Historic Irvington home, located on quiet, safe, tree lined street in the center of one of Portland\'s best neighborhoods. Your private apartment was recently renovated, and features stylish design, furnishings and a spacious, open layout. <br /><br />Walking/biking distance to the best restaurants, coffee shops and night life in the city. Close to public transportation.<br /><br />*There are two medium (30lb), very sweet dogs on the property.  Once in awhile they will bark, but they are harmless. Photos in listing.','Within walking distance of several great neighborhood shops, restaurants, bars and public transit.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7448a99f-82f6-442e-80ab-5fac2b518520.jpg',5755250,7,'45.54036','-122.65634',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,67.00,2,15,298,4.78,23255044),(1093,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23268451','Big Bright Private Home in Excellent  Alberta Area','Welcoming basement apartment in great NE Portland location. Well lit, windows in every room, spacious separate unit with private entrance. Perfect for those who want to explore Alberta, Killingsworth, Dekum\'s Triangle and Mississippi neighborhoods.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c214ab3f-bdc9-4e93-adac-56de112359d2.jpg',5769084,29,'45.56402','-122.6551',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,83.00,2,365,28,4.50,23268451),(1094,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23272254','Alberta Delight','Abundant natural night, quiet, affordable \'mother in law\' with separate entrance and private full bath(over 250ft\'). Tv(w/fire stick), kitchen appliances, eating table, prep space, refrigerator and queen bed. Across the street from Khunamokwst Park, close to 42nd Ave Business district, Beaumont Village, Alberta Arts district, Hollywood District which offer breweries, bakeries, and local shops, all while under 4 miles to PDX international airport(5 min) or Downtown(10 min)!','Cully is friendly, diverse and centrally located in NE Portland. Close to several coffee, grocer, restaurants(breweries/organic/Vegan/anything)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/366d30fb-0b3a-4584-98c0-3bb33a508ac2.jpg',50972958,21,'45.55871','-122.60848',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,70.00,30,60,260,4.83,23272254),(1095,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23273206','Viatorum Gallery At Hawthorne','This whimsical space is a private world of its own, safely tucked away in the thriving Hawthorne district. Thoughtfully curated by hosts to honor guests, neighbors, community and Earth! The space is deep cleaned,  aired out and disinfected in accordance with OSHA and the WHO for virus prevention.  An immersive art experience paired with thoughtful amenities, fun surprises and a warm welcoming atmosphere.','We live in the heart of the chic Hawthorne district, of Southeast Portland. An area rife with restaurants, cafes, coffee shops, thrift stores, modern mercantile and pop-up shops. We are half a block from the Historic Bagdad Theater and 4 metro bus lines, which also connect to Portland\'s light-rail train, MAX. We are approximately 30 minutes from PDX international airport by car and the same by MAX. We are within walking distance of Division, home of POK POK Thai and Bollywood India as well as Mt. Tabor, a caldera (inactive volcano) with unbeatable vistas at its peak.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-23273206/original/4676f60a-2720-44e4-bdc0-30d7f46a58f8.jpeg',140115987,8,'45.51011','-122.62492',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,112.00,1,14,712,4.90,23273206),(1096,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23309972','Cozy & Private Apartment in Portland\'s Montavilla!','Conveniently located, NEW & PRIVATE garden-level apartment bordering Montavilla & Mt. Tabor neighborhoods!<br /><br />Llama\'s Rest is a relaxed & fun 1 bedroom apartment equipped with the essentials needed to make your home base in Portland, Oregon. <br /><br />After a long day come home to a comfy KING bed, or make a delicious meal on the gas oven/range! <br /><br />Relax by the toasty fireplace or catch an iconic view of the city from Mount Tabor! <br /><br />Treat yourself to a local dinner and drinks or a movie on Stark street!','Llama\'s Rest is just a 5-minute walk from the shops, restaurants and bars on Montavilla\'s main street, SE Stark! <br /><br />Walk up the street and grab an ultra-local craft beer at Montavilla\'s own Brew Works or a special cocktail at Vintage Cocktail Lounge! Eat a gourmet dinner at Lazy Susan or pick up a breakfast bialy at White Rabbit. <br /><br />After a long day, you\'re sure to find a movie you like at The Academy. Admission is just $5 anytime and you can enjoy a pretty excellent selection of craft beers or kombucha too! <br /><br />There is no shortage of excellent coffee nearby either. Don\'t miss the very popular Bipartisan cafe, which also serves sandwiches and pies. If you\'ve got a sweet tooth, check out PDX Cookie Co for something truly unique. <br /><br />On NE Glisan street check out the new Rocket Empire Machine food court for Gigantic beer and a mix of food for every taste. Don\'t miss the best pizza ever at East Glisan or the glamorous Blank Slate bar. Desserts at DB Dess','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-23309972/original/081dab3c-edf6-4b88-9726-dd06b8e94798.jpeg',173567336,15,'45.51875','-122.58663',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,30,1125,33,5.00,23309972),(1097,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23328366','Sweet and Simple in Southeast!','Come home to a charming bungalow in the beautiful South Tabor neighborhood! Simple decor creates a serene living environment in this newly renovated basement apartment. The space is well-lit and outfitted with all the basic amenities; nothing fancy, but super comfy. This space is non-smoking and non-vaping, including tobacco, cannabis, incense.  We hope to make your stay in Portland fabulous!','This neighborhood is a gem: Mount Tabor within walking distance, a grassy field for strolling or lounging directly across the street, quiet residential streets on all sides for walks or jogs anytime.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/90ea5c1c-dd4f-4ed8-92f7-e1f904ead1d7.jpg',38610656,10,'45.5064','-122.58436',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,47.00,30,180,88,4.86,23328366),(1098,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23332931','Portland Airbnb Private Guesthouse, Alberta Arts','NE Portland Alberta Arts; cozy private guest house, sleeps 4. Dogs ok! AC, no cleaning chores. Full kitchen and bath/tub; courtyard with fire pit. Cathedral ceiling, exposed woodwork, local art.  Spiral staircase to loft with adjustable queen bed; comfortable pull-out sofa bed, sleeps two; washer/dryer; large desk/workspace; Kitchen w/ dishwasher, fridge, cooking supplies, oven, microwave.  Coffee, tea, seltzer and snacks supplied. Bluetooth radio, WiFi, and hard-wired Ethernet, TV/Roku/Netflix.','Our NE neighborhood is in the center of it all; we’re a short walk to the hip bars, restaurants, coffee shops, boutiques and art studios on Alberta Ave, Williams St, and Mississippi Ave. You won’t need a car to find that ultimate Portland coffee shop or bar with amazing cocktails, all within a 10-15 minute walk. Our green, leafy neighborhood makes for great strolls; beautiful Irving Park, a 10-minute walk away, has towering trees and quiet spots to hang out. We’re an easy bus ride downtown to Powells, the Art Museum, OMSI, and the Pearl District. You’ll find that our guesthouse makes a peaceful, quiet respite after a busy day.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e6fe2be2-6959-4b6e-98e8-2a0497e1b5d6.jpg',34537748,14,'45.553749084472656','-122.6602554321289',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,88.00,1,28,332,4.98,23332931),(1099,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23341097','*Walk to Alberta eats & drinks*Dog Park*Playground','Bright one-bedroom with private access and parking for 1 vehicle. Beautiful Alberta Park is just across the street and you’ll be within four blocks of Alberta Street and all the restaurants, shops, galleries, and nightlife it has to offer. Aside from the location, you’ll have a fully stocked kitchen with dishwasher, Roku TV, and washer and dryer.<br /><br />If you\'re traveling with a pup, read the full description. No cats (sorry!). Please reach out to discuss longer term stays (up to 30 days). Thanks!','Our neighborhood has everything you could want. Across the street, Alberta Park has an off-leash dog park, playground, trail, and open green spaces. We’re just a few blocks to Alberta hot spots like Salt n’ Straw and Bollywood Theater, and we’re even closer to Podnahs barbeque, Prospect bottle shop, and La Taq. Breakside brewing, Tamale Boy, and Pine State are other nearby reminders of Portland’s amazing food and drink scene. We’ll also share recommendations for nearby yoga studios and running and biking routes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/41732528-2c16-4884-b40d-3b4654a3b9b4.jpg',97623766,29,'45.56434','-122.64624',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,90.00,2,30,305,5.00,23341097),(1100,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23353382','The Sneakaway','Built to feel like a little touch of luxury, with the quaintness and quality of a craft home.  This place is a true sneak-away with a two person soaking tub, marble shower, king tempurpedic bed and a fully stocked kitchen. This open studio has 15 ft ceilings allowing ample sunlight and a large, light feeling. This house was designed and built by me my friends so no detail is overlooked or unintentional.  This was our labor of love for a year and Im so excited to now be able to share it.','An Excellent close in NE location.  Walkable and bike able to everywhere.  our neighborhood has a walking score of 98 because within ten minutes you can walk to the infamous Alberta Arts district (salt and straw, pine state biscuits, bollywood theatre etc), the Woodlawn neighborhood also known as the Dekum triangle (grand army tavern, the famous breakside brewery, tough luck bar,  woodlawn coffee, the weed shop, to name a few) , the Killingsworth corners (Le taq and Hat Yai two of our personal favorites ) yet, our house is not right smack in the middle of any of it, so you can have a very quite nights sleep. This means all the food, bars, shopping and coffee you could possibly desire are within a few minutes walk.  A major bus line to all parts of the city is about 1,000 feet from your door.  There is a grocery store within two blocks. Hop on a bike and your a ten minute ride from the Mississippi district, Williams street, and the max line to down town or anywhere else. Less than a ten','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-23353382/original/bb661904-825d-431f-9d44-30d2aaae5fe7.jpeg',86380272,14,'45.56505','-122.65812',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,106.00,2,20,528,4.97,23353382),(1101,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23358705','Creston Cutie - Close-in SE','Welcoming, comfortable home with full amenities located close-in in SE Portland.  Walking distance to bus lines, a great coffee shop, and a few local restaurants.  A stones throw to the hot southeast hang-outs of Division/Clinton streets, the Hawthorne district, and the Woodstock district.  Nearby is Reed College.  It\'s a short drive/ride to downtown Portland.  Guests of all backgrounds are welcome!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f2f159d8-f9c5-4755-a81c-aa80759b610d.jpg',18671930,67,'45.49372','-122.62579',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,60,6,5.00,23358705),(1102,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23376340','Pot-friendly 1 BR full APT w/ comfy Portland charm','Clean and private 1-bedroom (Q) apartment with well-stocked kitchen and bath, one block to Alberta Arts Main Street. Separate outdoor keyless entry to a daylight-basement in our 100+ year-old craftsman home ensures a contactless stay. Blackout bedroom curtains invite great sleep, and comfortable couch is also long enough to sleep on. All welcome! Cannabis friendly (outdoors only) covered patio. On a quiet dead-end road with free parking. Stays over 7 days can request access to laundry.','Alberta Arts District is a thriving business district of locally owned, black owned and women owned businesses. No national chain stores, not even a Starbucks. It is the home of the original locations of some of Portland\'s most recognized restaurants, including Salt & Straw, Bollywood Cafe and Barista. <br /><br />Walk to organic grocery, many hip shops, handmade and local art galleries, bars, music venues, parks, and bike rental. Check out our many murals and vibrant street art. <br /><br />Alberta is a very easy neighborhood to get around without a car, as is Portland in general. Though for a longer visit, if you want to see the natural areas outside of town, it\'s handy to have a car for a day or two.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/72408687-6864-4701-8944-7d2ecf35478f.jpg',31768062,29,'45.56008','-122.65055',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,87.00,1,29,269,4.98,23376340),(1103,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23391856','Thompson Street Guest Suite with Spacious Garden','Old Portland charm in a renovated central northeast Victorian home. Bright, private basement apartment with tall ceilings, separate garden entrance, large bedroom with queen size bed and your own bathroom. Spacious shared garden with outdoor dining table, gas grill and lawn. Perfect for enjoying the outdoors! Incredibly convenient location close to the Convention Center, Downtown and vibrant neighborhoods. Reliable, fast wifi with speeds up to 400mbps for zoom meetings, if you work from home.','The Eliot neighborhood of Portland is a beautiful residential neighborhood right off of city center. It offers the benefit of a relaxing residential community, with proximity to urban Portland.  We have many excellent restaurants within walking distance of our home including Ox, Sizzle Pie, Pine State Biscuits, Ex Novo and Bernstein\'s Bagels. For entertainment there are several music venues in the neighborhood such as the Wonder ballroom and the Moda center. Sports fans and music fans can walk to Blazers and Winterhawks games and concerts at the Moda Center.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-23391856/original/7cdbd94b-0cf9-427f-aa5f-3ede28b86469.jpeg',6034282,26,'45.53916','-122.66554',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,59.00,2,1125,265,4.94,23391856),(1104,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23395538','Vintage Loft Just off Alberta Street!','We’ve restored this spacious private guest suite from top to bottom, combining vintage charm with modern amenities and custom-built touches to welcome guests to our favorite part of Portland. With a huge bedroom and new queen bed, spotless bath with soaking tub, simple kitchenette and sitting room with tv and sofabed, plus one of Portland\'s most vibrant and walkable districts just outside the door, you\'ll find a perfect home base to explore PDX.','Our home is located in the heart of the Alberta Arts District which features a ton of public art, fun little independent shops, some of Portland\'s best dining and a ton of fabulous bars and pubs. If you ever wanted to live like a local in Portland, this is the place!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/734bd52c-455b-4b90-912a-f0b50e014891.jpg',65899399,14,'45.55884','-122.65489',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,2,21,235,4.93,23395538),(1105,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23398383','Tabor Retreat','Charming, woodsy, spacious one bedroom basement apartment. Large full kitchen, bathroom, washer and dryer, living room with gas fireplace insert.  Private, easy access, lighted entrance.  Convenient access by bus to downtown Portland and Airport. Includes beautifully landscaped grounds, patio, and access to Mt. Tabor park with running, biking, hiking trails and tennis courts.','Quiet neighborhood at Mt. Tabor Park','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/97540239-8e0c-44d4-9344-68f5a004c21a.jpg',25806993,15,'45.51548','-122.58983',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,94.00,30,1125,252,4.91,23398383),(1106,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23399594','Waterfront Pearl District Condo w/Parking, Hot Tub','Beautiful condo in downtown NW Portland, within a few minutes walk to the heart of the Pearl district and the best restaurants, coffee shops, and bars Portland has to offer!  The condo complex sits on the Willamette River with direct access to the riverfront pathway with endless biking and walking!  Free parking, cable TV/WiFi, swimming pool, and hot tub!','The Pearl District is an area of Portland, Oregon, formerly occupied by warehouses, light industry and railroad classification yards and now noted for its art galleries, upscale businesses and residences. The area has been undergoing significant urban renewal since the mid-1980s when it was reclassified as mixed use from industrial,[3] including the arrival of artists, the removal of a viaduct and construction of the Portland Streetcar. It now mostly consists of high-rise condominiums and warehouse-to-loft conversions.<br /><br />The increase of high-rise condominiums and warehouse-to-loft conversions was made evident with the construction of the Cosmopolitan on the Park building, which opened in Summer 2016. The Cosmopolitan on the Park residential building is now the tallest building in the Pearl District and the 8th tallest building in Portland, contributing to the changing Portland skyline.[4]<br /><br />The area is located just northwest of downtown between West Burnside Street on','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d2f94a6e-fbd8-48be-891a-2ebfcc5ecd70.jpg',12575059,43,'45.53105','-122.67488',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,30,360,20,4.85,23399594),(1107,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23399860','The Diamond','The Diamond is a rental in the heart of the Alberta Arts district of Portland, OR. The two floor unit is the pinnacle of comfort and modern aesthetic. From the simple, clean decor to the windows featuring an abundant garden, you will find our home is the beacon of relaxation and peace you are looking for.','Concordia is a beautiful neighborhood with all the amenities you need within walking distance. Night life, movie theaters, restaurants, public transportaion, wellness centers, and shopping are just a few of the modes of entertainment available to you.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4cb3fc41-3c05-4603-915b-6120eea215ed.jpg',4162970,1,'45.56198','-122.63079',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,60.00,1,1125,284,4.93,23399860),(1108,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23430717','Master Suite in Mississippi Food and Arts District','Our house is an updated English Tudor style 3-bedroom/2-bathroom 1920\'s bungalow (1,800 sq. ft.) in the popular and hip Mississippi Food and Arts District in North Portland. The house is located on a quiet street within walking distance of Peninsula Park, New Season\'s and the city’s light rail public transit system. Award-winning restaurants, coffee shops, boutiques, live music and the Adidas Headquarters are near by. The house has immediate access to I-5 and is 5 minutes away from downtown.','Close to award-winning restaurants, breweries, shops and a local organic grocery store.<br />Also walking distance to a historic park (rose garden) and light rail/public transit.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0a2b3995-d601-4665-870d-17f96d7ff570.jpg',167221905,48,'45.56721','-122.67555',2,3,1.00,1.00,3.00,119.00,30,1125,69,4.96,23430717),(1109,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23432574','Dwell - Solar Powered Living','Now Net Zero Energy!  Dwell has 18 solar panels that cover more electricity that the building uses!  New modern House with gourmet kitchen.  Enjoy the tile shower with endless hot water, smart tv, and cozy furniture.  Short walk to Woodstock village with Double Mountain Brewing, New Seasons. Easy access to public transportation, or sit back and relax on the patio with firepit.  Light and bright guest house and you have the place to yourself. There is a fenced yard that is pretty private.','Woodstock park, restaurants, shopping and bars are all a short walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/59809580-2f57-4753-83fa-4610e0e61c8f.jpg',14796564,69,'45.47271','-122.61301',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,104.00,1,1125,358,4.92,23432574),(1110,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23432611','Master Suite + 1 BR in N. Mississippi District.','Our house is an updated English Tudor style 3-bedroom/2-bathroom bungalow in the popular and hip Mississippi Food and Arts District.  <br /><br />Award-winning restaurants, breweries, coffee shops, boutiques, live music and the Adidas Headquarters are near by.<br /><br />The skylit master suite upstairs sleeps 3 (king bed + pull out) and has beautiful walk-in multi-head rain shower and walk in closet.<br /><br />The main floor room sleeps 2 and shares a bathroom with the resident host.<br /><br />Perfect for families or small groups.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/937c13e0-ec00-4f1d-9c6c-eb0debfc8b0e.jpg',167221905,48,'45.56726','-122.67537',2,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,189.00,30,1125,1,5.00,23432611),(1111,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23437533','The Nest Tiny Home & Garden /Alberta Arts District','Beautiful tranquil bright airy tiny modern studio cottage behind a 1911 craftsman home, on an unpaved side road in a lushly landscaped tranquil wooded garden. Feel the escape of glamping in the heart of the vibrant Alberta Arts district!<br />Amazing restaurants, bars, shopping, groceries & yoga all within blocks. Walk or bike everywhere! Bike lock-up behind the Nest. Kitchenette, cooktop, toaster oven, Fr.Press etc.<br />For long term stay options of 6 mos. or 1 year- please feel free to reach out to me','The Alberta arts neighborhood boasts some of the best restaurants, and enticing shops, coffee shops etc., in PDX. All within walking distance. Bike everywhere. You\'re in the heart of it. The Nest boasts a walk score of 87!! (Very walk-able), a bike score of 81!!(Very Bike-able) mass transit score of 50! (Good Transit)!<br />Heres a few of my local favs:<br />Tin shed is one of my dog Pepe\'s and my very favorite breakfast places. (Get there early to avoid a long wait, or shop across the street at Frock which carries many local designers and artisans work  while waiting.)<br />Yakuza (one block away- on restaurant row) has one of the best burgers around, not to mention their amazing Asian fusion food and delicious drinks. Happy hour- just go.<br />Salt & Straw- artisanal ice cream<br />Bollywood Theatre- Indian street food<br />Extracto coffee shop is just around the corner, and a beautiful bright airy space for working, chilling, or just waking up.<br />Alberta Rose Theater is a great v','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/afbd03ba-119f-4a16-a1eb-88793e8dbc5a.jpg',6153335,1,'45.5621','-122.63643',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,75.00,30,365,27,4.89,23437533),(1112,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23449418','Overlook BackShack','NOTE: Separate entrance. Great place for social distance!<br /><br />We have made this small space feel fun and cozy with bright colors, modern amenities, custom design elements, brand new construction and vintage furnishings. Bamboo floors and big windows give the single room a spaciousness that you would not expect in 220 square feet! <br /><br />We\'ve decorated with plants and art to create a totally unique and comfortable experience.','The Overlook BackShack is a cozy little cottage that used to be a single car garage, nestled in a friendly back yard. In a beautiful and quiet neighborhood close-in North Portland, it\'s a great little getaway for 2 people. We are a ten-minute walk from some of the best restaurants and shopping in Portland in the historic Mississippi district!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d4fc4cb5-8fc0-4221-b020-cdfaf15ee99b.jpg',4702475,13,'45.55444','-122.68777',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,3,29,342,4.91,23449418),(1113,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23499440','Private room/bath in  unique St Johns.','Walk to restaurants, food carts, groceries, brewpubs,  in the unique St Johns neighborhood in Portland.<br /> Access to freeway, airport,  downtown, local hospitals, Intel, Nike. <br />Bus #4 to MAX light rail or downtown. <br />31+ nights only, please. 1 person only.<br />Room is 10\'x10\'. Queen bed. Large closet. Small desk. Sheets, towels, dresser. Private bathroom in hall.<br />Shared common spaces.<br />Fully supplied kitchen. Dishwasher, microwave, pots & pans. Washer dryer in garage.<br /><br />NO PETS<br />Non smoking property','Quiet, urban, friendly neighborhood.<br />St Johns has beautiful parks (Cathedral and Pier). <br />10 minute walk to downtown St Johns with restaurants, library, bars, grocery stores, post office, food carts, movie theaters, etc. In spring/summer there is a nice farmers market on Saturday 9-1.<br />Bus #4 located around the corner takes you to MAX N Interstate or downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4b8404d3-9772-42bd-8d4f-848299ea82c5.jpg',4564432,58,'45.59476','-122.74548',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,31,180,13,4.92,23499440),(1114,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23546465','Private ensuite queen bedroom/bath in St Johns.','Walk to downtown St Johns restaurants, groceries, bars, food carts, and Cathedral Park.<br />Easy access to freeways for local hospitals, Intel or Nike. <br />Bus #4 around the corner to MAX.<br />Room is minimum 31+ nights only. <br />Queen bed in private bedroom 10\'x10\'. Large closet. Ensuite bath. Senior friendly walk in tub/ shower. <br />Sheets, towels, dresser, desk, bedside table, lamp.<br />Self catering, shared kitchen with dishwasher, microwave, coffeepot, etc. Washer/dryer in garage.<br />NON SMOKING<br />NO PETS<br />1 guest','St Johns has become a very popular neighborhood in North Portland. Bars, restaurants, and Cathedral Park are all walking distance from the property. However, there is still a small town vibe. People in St Johns are very friendly, don\'t forget to say hello. In spring and summer there is a farmers market on Saturdays 9-1. It was on the corner of N Charleston and N Central last year.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0f47649a-9589-4f18-bd7b-3dd8bfdd757a.jpg',4564432,58,'45.59406','-122.74384',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,31,180,8,5.00,23546465),(1115,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23565505','Close-In NE PDX','Newly remodeled ground floor apartment located in Old Portland\'s affluent Irvington neighborhood. Walk to concerts/ Trailblazer games. One block from hip bars and restaurants on Broadway blvd. Fully equipped kitchen, High-Speed internet, Smart TV, SleepNumber beds, wood burning fireplace, nice leather couches, and bright south facing windows. Good for couples, solo adventurers, work-cations, and families too.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/220255be-74fb-41d5-b332-68cb9735704d.jpg',83388023,7,'45.53629','-122.64171',1,5,1.50,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,99,49,4.67,23565505),(1116,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23609556','Bright House-share with Private Bath Near Airport','Two queen bedrooms with a private bathroom in beautiful craftsman style house in a NE Portland. Guests have use of private full bathroom and two queen bedrooms. Both rooms have a smart TV. Dedicated medium sized fridge, microwave and coffee maker are provided. <br /><br />Close to parks and hiking trails. Just 8 minutes to PDX and easy access to freeways. Laundry and ample parking.<br /><br />Short bike ride to Beaumont, Alberta and Hollywood districts with many shops & restaurants.<br /><br />Breakfast: $10 / guest.','Diverse and hip Northeast Portland is known for the Alberta Arts District, with quirky shops, galleries, hip eateries and the lively Last Thursday street fair. Live music acts play regularly in small, low-key bars, and at the renovated 1920s Alberta Rose Theatre. We are also close to the fashionable Hollywood and Beaumont areas with their many shops and restaurants. Breweries, brunch spots and artisan boutiques line North Mississippi and Williams avenues which are a bike ride away. The Grotto is a Catholic shrine with tranquil botanical gardens.<br /><br />A short drive or 45 minute bike ride to downtown and the famous Pearl district.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a64ae59c-a707-4ae5-a449-f403b7a1d122.jpg',25079470,39,'45.55244','-122.58446',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,100.00,30,1124,2,5.00,23609556),(1117,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23613685','Bike\'N\'Roll Cottage: Adventure & Relaxation','Bike \'N\' Roll Cottage: Bicycle Tourism, Healing Garden<br />See Portland by bike-Biking Score 95! <br /><br />GUESTS RAVE: \"I can bike everywhere!\"<br /><br />■ Beautiful 560 sf w/the details of a 100+ year-old Craftsman <br />■ Bright - lots of windows - high ceilings <br />■ Relax & rejuvenate in a tranquil, healing garden<br />■ Near bus & max train - so you can bicycle even farther! <br />■ 100s of shops, restaurants & everything you want to see within biking distance!<br />■ Ranked 2nd in the CNBC\'s most bicycle-friendly cities in the US!','Brooklyn is a unique working class neighborhood with beautiful 100 year old houses. We are near the Spring Water Corridor, the Rhododendron garden, West Moreland, Division Street, Brooklyn neighborhood park, Aladdin Theater, and Rose City Coffee.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjM2MTM2ODU%3D/original/3f3be555-f6f2-407c-9f42-18a0ed475ced.jpeg',53232555,56,'45.49332','-122.65498',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,125.00,1,28,101,4.77,23613685),(1118,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23626383','The Portland Oregon Dome!     w/ Elec Car Charging','This is an authentic geodesic dome, designed by Oregon Dome Inc. and built with the help of local theatrical lighting and set-design artists.  Licensed and permitted #16 214126 000 HO.  You can also use my Level 2 Car Charging','This is a friendly, wooded, quiet area in hilly Southwest Portland; very nice for suburban walking.  20 minutes to downtown by car.  A wonderful \"world-food\" market in walking distance.  If you like bicycling, you\'d better be fit - it\'s hilly!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9d0170f7-104c-421e-bcb4-6351fbdb40c0.jpg',51010038,83,'45.45378','-122.73157',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,60,106,4.94,23626383),(1119,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23634569','Charming Hawthorne/Belmont Family Home','This spacious, light filled, older Portland family home lies in the heart of the Hawthorne/Belmont neighborhood. It\'s a great location for enjoying local coffee shops, bookstores, parks, and lots of great restaurants and food carts.  I welcome singles, couples and families of all persuasions. I enjoy kids, so families are especially welcome. You\'ll share the space with my friendly kitty, Sophie.','This charming neighborhood of well-kept older Portland homes is a delight for walking and biking.  Most anything Portland has to offer- vintage shops, cheap movies, parks, and restaurants- is right outside your door. This neighborhood is a foodie paradise with food cart pods, all the way to top-notch restaurants. <br />We are a short walk to the 100 year old Laurelhurst park full of old growth fir trees and Mt Tabor park situated on top of an extinct volcano overlooking the city. <br />And there is always plenty of street parking.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-23634569/original/8ff93bdb-6157-4af4-9d8a-2df8ce888c5c.jpeg',7288374,16,'45.51497','-122.63352',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,20,31,4.94,23634569),(1120,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23668933','New, Modern Chef\'s Dream in Historic Turret House','This isn\'t your standard rental w/ IKEA furniture & misleading photos! The Turret House sits on a large corner lot in Portland\'s most beautiful neighborhood (Irvington) and surrounded by stunning homes and tree-canopied streets. Broadway street is 3 blocks away & offers some of Portland’s favorite restaurants, bars, coffee shops, bookstores, grocers, & dispensaries. My partner & I are professional designers and we worked hard to blend traditional Spanish Californian design w/ modern simplicity.','The Irvington neighborhood is one of the largest Historic Districts in the country and features some of the most beautiful homes in Portland dating back to the 1920\'s. It is an architectural dream that spans a large swath of Portland. Most of the neighborhood, including my streets, are lined with old growth deciduous trees that create gorgeous canopies of green. The property has 5 giant old growth trees that feel like quintessential Portland. <br /><br />The apartment is ideal for anyone wanting to access all the culture of the Eastside while staying in a tranquil setting with a BBQ, hammock, and patio. The apartment is 2 miles from downtown Portland and less than a mile from the Convention Center and Moda Center.<br /><br />If you like taking walks with your family, friends, or dog, you couldn\'t choose a better location for natural and architectural beauty.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e1d59004-cdd0-459d-903c-3ee3ffb95e41.jpg',373733,7,'45.537','-122.64324',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,73.00,1,1125,300,4.85,23668933),(1121,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23672354','Sun-filled Home in Buckman Neighborhood w/ 2BRs','If you\'re a fan of great food, craft beer, and pour-over coffee, this is your place. My home is situated in the famous Buckman District, near many of Portland\'s top-rated restaurants, bars, and vintage shops. Ideal for families, friend groups, and business travelers, my place provides a convenient home base within walking distance of neighborhood hotspots. Experience an authentic taste of how hipsters live in Stumptown from this ideal location.','Commonly known as \"Foodie Row,\" the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a diverse array of top-notch local flavors—no chain restaurants here! Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or opt for a fancy night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />Portland isn’t just for foodies. Hawthorne’s vibrant indie spirit is alive with an abundance of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques to explore, making it a true hipster haven. Catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of fun, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park atop a dormant volcano vent. Here, you’ll find miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of the city, perfect for a day of outdoor adven','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-23672354/original/86dc07d9-5570-4e2b-865c-af8c3f3d42c7.jpeg',177257126,12,'45.5218','-122.63728',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,130.00,2,1125,582,4.90,23672354),(1122,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23702620','Cozy Studio Apt, Close-In Heart of SE PDX Location','Cozy, first floor, studio right in the heart of the original Portlandia neighborhoods. Coffee shops, restaurants, bars, food, entertainment, and public transportation all within easy walking distance.','SE Portland is the neighborhood of art cars, unicyclists, old hippies, bearded lumbersexuals, coffee roasters, and cozy bars. Many, many excellent restaurants are nearby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c97c0387-b0ed-47a9-8440-1eaabc3c0a1b.jpg',2135334,16,'45.5178','-122.6342',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,44.00,1,1125,568,4.92,23702620),(1123,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23780161','Bright Queen Bedroom with Private Bath in NE','Private queen room in beautiful craftsman style house in a quiet NE Portland neighbourhood with full private full bathroom. Room has  TV, fridge, microwave and coffee maker. Close to parks, hiking trails and the Grotto. Just 8 minutes to PDX and easy access to freeways. Laundry available. <br /><br />Short bike ride to Beaumont, Alberta and Hollywood districts with many shops and restaurants.<br /><br />There is ample street parking.','Diverse and hip Northeast Portland is known for the Alberta Arts District, with quirky shops, galleries, hip eateries and the lively Last Thursday street fair. Live music acts play regularly in small, low-key bars, and at the renovated 1920s Alberta Rose Theatre. We are also close to the fashionable Hollywood and Beaumont areas with their many shops and restaurants. Breweries, brunch spots and artisan boutiques line North Mississippi and Williams avenues which are a bike ride away. The Grotto is a Catholic shrine with tranquil botanical gardens.<br /><br />A short drive or 45 minute bike ride to downtown and the famous Pearl district.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0823a220-8e09-4b4b-abaa-db882f7c70a5.jpg',25079470,39,'45.55125','-122.58619',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,99.00,30,1125,40,4.78,23780161),(1124,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23784002','Elegant Westside Townhouse near Downtown/Beaverton','Our spacious 1,500SF townhouse- just 10 minutes from downtown/The Pearl or Nike-is very well-equipped and beautifully decorated since we believe that a rental should look and live like a home.   The townhouse features a two-story living/dining room with fireplace; new fully-equipped kitchen ; large master bedroom/bath; guest bedroom/bath;  a fully-equipped loft study; high-speed Internet;  a 700SF tandem garage; a front deck with a BBQ and a separate shaded patio. We are child- and pet-friendly.','The townhouse is just two short blocks from the village center of Forest Heights, the most upscale, sustainable development in Portland that is very family- (and dog) friendly.  The village center has a very nice coffee shope--with a huge indoor/outdoor fireplace--a cleaners; Pizzacato, which features gourmet pizzas, a very reasonable nail salon; a small neighborhood grocery store and a nice restaurant.  A free shuttle to the Sunset transit center--with access to the MAX light rail, the Westside commuter train and buses-- leaves from the village every thirty minutes during the week.  <br /><br />Just three minutes away is a large neighborhood shopping center, with a very nice QBS grocery store, mailing service, liquor store and four restaurants.  And, of course, the delights of NW 23rd/21st, the Pearl District, and downtown Portland are less than 10 minutes away.  <br /><br />There are parks and trails throughout Forest Heights. We are just a couple of minutes away from Portland\'s wild','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-23784002/original/7c270ddf-60da-47ae-a051-4bf85aa3fc80.jpeg',98560,81,'45.53956','-122.78047',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,105.00,31,180,4,5.00,23784002),(1125,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23788761','30+Day Rental *Pet Friendly* Private Guesthouse','Immerse in local living! <br />Embrace this charming guesthouse – immaculate and minimalist. <br /><br />Ideal proximity to public transit, hospitals, downtown, and the airport, all seamlessly accessible through keyless entry. <br /><br />Enjoy exclusive use of the entire driveway and a fenced yard, perfect for your dog to play. <br />Experience Portland in a new purpose-built haven designed to elevate your stay.\"','The Rose City Park Neighborhood is located in NE Portland, safe and walkable neighborhood, easy access to public transportation or freeway access.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-23788761/original/54614d6b-9414-480c-b45f-fbfdf09ed7de.jpeg',178501752,11,'45.54436','-122.59708',1,2,0.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,30,1124,22,4.91,23788761),(1126,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23790599','Bright, modern, private home in lively SE Portland','Bright, modern, private studio casita in the heart of the Richmond neighborhood. Walk to fantastic restaurants, coffee shops, and parks. Just steps from public transportation and easy access to Portland\'s Biketown bikes.','The main thoroughfare in the Richmond neighborhood is Division Street, which has become known as Restaurant Row. It is a 60-second walk from the casita to the original Stumptown Coffee. Other favorite Portland restaurants, bars, and coffee shops such as Woodsman Tavern, Salt and Straw, Cibo,  Bollywood Theater, Xico, Petite Provence,  Blue Star Donuts, and more, are all in walking distance. We are also a short walk to Hawthorne Blvd. with many more restaurants and shops. A 15-minute walk and you can check out Mt. Tabor Park. Walk the park trails and get a great view of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-23790599/original/70e6827f-6154-457f-bf6e-c4e3ed4ff1c5.jpg',99241770,8,'45.50498','-122.61671',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,87.00,2,14,305,5.00,23790599),(1127,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23875080','Hollywood District Hideaway','This beautiful, hidden gem is centrally located in inner NE Portland. Walking distance to the Hollywood Transit Center Providence Hospital, Hollywood Farmer’s Market, Trader Joe’s, Whole Food Grocery Store and several eateries, the Treehouse is perfect for guests wanting to explore Portland on foot. The Treehouse is a fully detached unit located behind the main residence. It includes a separate bedroom with bathroom, full kitchen and large private deck to relax and enjoy a drink.','The Hollywood District is a small friendly neighborhood located in central NE Portland. We are within walking distance to several grocery stores, bars, shops and restaurants. Very close proximity ( walking distance) to Providence Medical center. Close to Maxrail transit. And just Minutes to Downtown and the airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5909fb71-e686-4025-852c-81fdc4b2ad37.jpg',1396103,84,'45.53382','-122.61588',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,103.00,1,26,438,4.83,23875080),(1128,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23908214','Private Inner SE Suite','Spacious lower level guest suite with private entrance. Equipped with a queen bed, full bath, living room, eating area and work station. Note: no full kitchen. Washer and dryer located in suite. <br /><br />The house is ideally located in inner SE Portland, walking distance to shops and restaurants on Division and Hawthorne. We are also just a short drive to downtown Portland (10-15 minutes). Great base for exploring all that Portland has to offer.','Shopping and restaurants nearby on SE Division and SE Hawthorne.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3a22b908-5e7d-423f-b6cf-0052180340f6.jpg',486872,8,'45.49925','-122.62093',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,1,28,282,4.88,23908214),(1129,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23961600','Cozy cottage close to it all in Northeast Portland','Cozy, new guest cottage in historic Irvington section of Northeast Portland. Our quiet, tree-lined neighborhood is an easy walk to shops, coffee, restaurants, pubs, public transit and the perfect base camp for seeing Portland, Mount Hood, the Oregon Coast, the Columbia River Gorge or wine country. This is also a great spot if you\'re in town for conferences at the Oregon Convention Center or Trail Blazers, Timbers games. Free street parking, near transit & a 15-minute cab ride from the airport.','Irvington is a tree-lined historic district in the heart of inner Northeast Portland. Quick access to downtown Portland, the Willamette River, Interstate 5 and 84. Walking distance to Alberta Arts District. An easy cab ride or mass transit ride to the Pearl District, downtown Portland, Oregon Convention Center, the Moda Center, Providence Park. We\'re about a 15-minute cab ride from Portland International Airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3776c6dd-d93d-4897-a29d-edb6b45de328.jpg',72165971,7,'45.54433','-122.64534',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,2,15,205,4.97,23961600),(1130,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/23976606','Oak Street Flat - a quiet, welcoming getaway','Nestled in a quiet neighborhood on the north slope of Mt. Tabor you’ll be staying in a serene & welcoming historic home. Oak Street Flat is the perfect getaway for families, international travelers, and those looking for direct access to the city\'s delights. Fully-outfitted and dappled in natural light, the complete kitchen and claw-foot tub allows you to recharge and relax. This spacious apartment is tucked between restaurants, bars and shops in the Belmont, Hawthorne & Hollywood districts.','The neighborhood is quiet and somewhat off the beaten path yet still with in walking distance of restaurants, bars, coffee shops, food carts and markets.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4911cde2-dd2e-487c-a263-e5e8d87b156c.jpg',21774902,15,'45.52025','-122.60517',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,58,4.93,23976606),(1131,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24022524','Irvington Basement Apartment','Basement apartment (475 square feet), with one bedroom with a king-sized bed, living room (with a pull-out queen-sized bed), kitchenette (sink, refrigerator, microwave, coffee maker), in Irvington, one of Portland\'s oldest neighborhoods.  About 20 blocks from the Oregon Convention Center, Moda Center, and easy access to downtown.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/40bf5b9a-00eb-44a8-822a-a5d5fba7a41e.jpg',18775566,7,'45.53566','-122.64074',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,110.00,2,10,116,4.98,24022524),(1132,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24055913','Grand Richmond Craftsman','This large, 1910 Grand Richmond Farmhouse/Craftsman home is full of character and history, and truly one if a kind. <br /><br />Home has two master bedrooms, each with an en-suite bathroom, large home office, home gym, formal dining room, eat in kitchen, separate parlor, living room, deck, 2 covered porches, and balconies off of each bedroom.<br /><br />Walk to many of Portland\'s trendy restaurants, food pods, and boutiques. StumpTown, Woodsman Tavern, Petit Provence, and more are just a few minutes away on foot.','The home is just a couple blocks off Division, walking distance from a number of great restaurants and shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f4b9a47b-c9ba-4c02-94bd-fa2d2d852402.jpg',1339136,8,'45.49974','-122.61115',1,5,3.00,2.00,3.00,200.00,31,180,1,4.00,24055913),(1133,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24074692','Xx  your  room','Beautiful accommodations in a historic neighborhood. Minutes to downtown! Spacious bedroom with queen bed, and queen sofa pull out.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a869222d-9688-414d-8e67-9c89e13ea01f.jpg',164140913,44,'45.52226','-122.68008',1,4,1.50,3.00,3.00,200.00,30,1125,0,1.00,24074692),(1134,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24120344','Mississippi SkyNest','Enjoy your own private suite in North Portland, two blocks off trendy Mississippi Ave. 5 minutes to downtown Portland, and 20 min to the airport, and shops, restaurants, breweries all within walking distance! My home has no pets at the moment and children on the main floor, but you have your own entrance and deck to create privacy and tranquility. I am so excited to share our master suite with you and offer suggestions on request for all the wonderful things Portland has to offer!','Please look up Mississippi Ave. Portland!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/57c50d87-1dad-4b8a-bb6a-77e3bb73095c.jpg',45297070,9,'45.54971','-122.67474',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,86.00,1,7,837,4.88,24120344),(1135,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24122545','Bright Cottage|Vintage Charm|AC|Off Street Parking','Make yourself at home in our fresh new charming guest cottage.  Lots of light,  well-equipped full kitchen, 2 private bedrooms, 1.5 bathrooms, cute dining nook, vintage styling, great privacy & AIR CONDITIONING set this spacious home apart.  5 min. from PDX airport, and 10-30 mins from downtown by car.  (dedicated off-street parking space)  Bus nearby/ 10 min walk to MAX transit center for light rail.  We love Montavilla - a true urban neighborhood with a fun mix of people, homes, parks & shops.','Our neighborhood is on the edge of up and coming Montavilla. It is a true working-class neighborhood with a variety of people.  While we have great access to routes to the whole city, especially for those with vehicles - and including public transit.  However, our immediate neighborhood is not the most walkable to eateries and shops. <br /><br />The Montavilla Community Center and Park are down the street, and a few streets over on Stark you\'ll find the historic Montavilla main street - with local eateries, coffee and tea shops, the Academy Theater and unique boutiques.  (Those are easiest to access with a vehicle - a bit far to walk to.) We are just a few blocks from Multnomah University, and welcome guests who are visiting the school.  <br /><br />Fred Meyer - a local one-stop shopping center for both groceries and goods,  is a less-than 15 minutes walk from the cottage, just across the street from the Gateway Transit Center.  You\'ll be able to find just about anything you need there','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2546c044-2fec-4aaf-b3ee-dc2cfbc5f120.jpg',97329823,10,'45.52682','-122.56809',1,4,1.50,2.00,2.00,111.00,3,29,353,4.99,24122545),(1136,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24138960','The Robin’s Nest - Modern Condo in heart of SE PDX','Welcome to the Robin\'s Nest!<br />Look no further for your monthly home away from home.<br />This modern 1-bedroom, 1-bath condo is in the heart of Southeast Portland. <br />Secure building with in-unit laundry, and a reserved garage parking space.<br />Located in the vibrant Sunnyside \"Belmont\" neighborhood, and just a couple blocks from Laurelhurst Park, near some of Portland’s best shops and restaurants. <br />And, the condo faces a quiet residential street, and fully stocked with everything you might need.','Our condo is in the heart of Southeast Portland.<br />We are just a couple blocks away from one of the city\'s most beautiful parks (Laurelhurst), complete with duck pond and jogging / walking path. Some local favorite spots within walking distance are Hoda’s, Stumptown Coffee, Accanto, Baghdad Theater, and Powells on Hawthorne, just to name a few!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-24138960/original/03bf15bf-c1ee-46b5-b2b0-e37d5384f112.jpeg',2393210,16,'45.51667','-122.62407',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,72.00,31,250,14,5.00,24138960),(1137,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24141003','Spacious 1-bed bsmt retreat; 20-min to city center','Charming 1923 SE Portland basement retreat! Private entrance, full bath (shower/tub), kitchen, bedroom & living space. Close to restaurants, food carts, bus lines & main hwy (downtown, beach, Mt Hood). Self-checkin, back patio access. <br />Read full description before booking!','This is a very walkable/transit friendly neighborhood...two blocks from Tri-Met bus #9 and a few blocks to bus #71. Walking distance to many amazing restaurants and food carts...Assembly Brewing, Slingshout Lounge, Nayar Taqueria, Steakadelphia, Thunderbird, Midpoint Cafe, An Xuyen Bakery, Siri Thai, Speedboat Coffee, Kainos Coffee, and so many more...<br />A short Biking distance to Portland Mercado, FoPo food carts, Mt. Tabor Park, and so much more!!!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-24141003-unapproved/original/dbe62ca3-2461-4694-ab17-984269c2b945.JPEG',181896912,36,'45.49667','-122.60157',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,75.00,2,7,168,4.94,24141003),(1138,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24160736','Sellwood Detached Apartment','This is a newer one bedroom apartment above our garage. You will be given the code for our keyless entry to make check in simple. Features include a fully equipped kitchen, one bedroom with a queen bed and walk-in closet, and full-size sofa bed in the living area. Neighborhood is very walkable with many shops and restaurants, grocery store and a park nearby. A short 4 mile bike ride to OHSU, downtown Portland and many sites.','Sellwood is very walkable and we are close to downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/13bb617a-be7b-484b-a18d-c3af868a7d4b.jpg',3587672,20,'45.467','-122.65589',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,80.00,2,60,207,4.96,24160736),(1139,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24270337','Cozy modern staycation workplace close to downtown','Entire space is very private.  Enjoy the cozy modern 1 bedroom queen bed, 2 large sofas that are comfortable to sleep on,  oversize soaking tub large walk-in closet , 2 TVs, Blue Ray player, stereo, gorgeous private garden with table seating & tranquil water, feature, & private entry.  5 minute drive to downtown, 2 minute walk to get to Forest Park trails. Several amazing restaurants just minutes away.  There is a pet fee or $40 each pet.  Preferably just one pet or the fee is $70 for two.','West Hills neighborhood above the city with spectacular views!  Minutes to trail head’s for hiking trails into Forest Park that go in, around & above the city.  Hike to the Oregon Zoo, Pittock Mansion (picnic tables & best views!) Hoyt Arboretum, Japanese Gardens &  Rose Gardens. safe walkable neighborhood (very pet friendly)   5 minutes from down town.  Shopping is tax free with several amazing coffee shops, bakeries, fabulous restaurants, breweries, brewery tours/city tours, street cars & bus & MAX (Metropolitan Area Express) access in multiple areas as well as Uber & Lyft (readily available within minutes).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5ae2caed-b9e3-4c8f-ae88-224f55af750c.jpg',147284022,54,'45.50498','-122.69894',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,134.00,1,1125,267,4.96,24270337),(1140,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24287314','Private 1BR, Central Eastside','Great location! Clean & furnished 1BR apt with W/D. Need a guest for 1-2 months possibly longer. Please DM for details! Please be over 21.<br /><br />*Note: While you can NOT hear people or voices in the apartment ( the whole building is REALLY quiet) the street noise below is rather noisy with trucks/Max trains going by occasionally.','Across the Willamette River from downtown, this area blends industrial Portland with new restaurants, microbreweries and riverside recreation. Ou can find more info and a video on the area searching: This Is Portland: Central Eastside.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-24287314/original/6785fc33-8e7e-455a-90b4-6a68275ce936.jpeg',31725411,12,'45.52406397776503','-122.662021363279',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,58.00,30,60,0,1.00,24287314),(1141,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24287588','Bryant St. Bungalow','This is a one bedroom condo with lots of light, kitchen, dining room, and living room. It\'s in a quiet part of town but near many restaurants. It\'s a 5-minute walk to grocery store and 3-minute walk to the Max Yellow Line. Ideal for a couple.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7c966f36-c84b-49c1-b56c-e3de6a70bb1c.jpg',73175514,51,'45.57337','-122.68163',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,2,1121,13,4.23,24287588),(1142,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24304038','Private remodeled historic home in heart of NW!','Enjoy your private apartment in a newly-remodeled Victorian rowhouse on the National Register of Historic Places! Stay in a peaceful neighborhood and walk to the best of downtown Portland - shops on NW 23rd, restaurants on NW 21st, the Pearl!','Tree-lined street in the heart of NW Portland, with interesting Portland architecture.  Go down three blocks to the Pearl, or up four to the shops, bars and restaurants of 21st Ave and then 23rd Ave. <br /><br />Portland is a safe place, but like any city, it is important to stay aware of your surroundings. We have homeless people in the area. If you want to walk (and you should!) you will run into homeless people just about everywhere, from the Pearl to Alphabet District, to North Portland. Leave them alone and they will generally do the same (except for asking for change). I support causes to help with homelessness, but I do not directly give handouts. Feel free to decline requests.   Let me know if you have any questions or concerns.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/982fe4f8-2b20-4d6b-8b97-74da24951f7f.jpg',46600469,27,'45.52719','-122.68961',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,145.00,2,30,263,4.87,24304038),(1143,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24338674','Sweet Quiet room in Sunny, Spacious Hawthorne home','My home is bright, sunny and spacious.  Your room is the green bedroom which has a comfy queen-sized bed and overlooks the backyard garden.  The decor is simple, clean, warm and welcoming, with houseplants scattered throughout.  There are parks, and tree-lined streets for walking just outside the door. I live here, with my very friendly cat,  Sophie.','This charming neighborhood of well-kept older Portland homes is a delight for walking and biking.  Most anything Portland has to offer- vintage shops, cheap movies, parks, and restaurants- is right outside your door. This neighborhood is a foodie paradise with food carts, highlighting hot, new local specialties, all the way to top-notch restaurants. <br />We are a short walk to the 100 year old Laurelhurst park full of old growth fir trees and Mt Tabor park situated on top of an extinct volcano overlooking the city. <br />And there is always plenty of street parking.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-24338674/original/72f870d0-6dc9-4bda-aaf5-038d915ac1aa.jpeg',7288374,16,'45.51376','-122.63255',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,53.00,1,14,121,4.97,24338674),(1144,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24358125','SW Portland Gem!','Perfection, a gem!. Gently lived in.  Top of line quality. All cherry hardwoods, incredible millwork, a master suite from the Four Seasons. This property is superior in every detail. 2 zone heat.The photos don\'t lie.<br />8 minutes to Downtown Portland and very close to shops.','Bridlemile’s location is perfect! It is close enough to downtown to commute easily- just a 10 minute drive- but it’s far enough out of Portland downtown area that it is very quiet and peaceful- very little traffic or noise. It takes just a little over 10 minutes to get into town. The lay of the land is gently rolling hills with lots of woodsey areas- a lot of the streets being windy and leading to a dead end- which helps keep the streets and neighborhoods quiet and peaceful and good for kids!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5f1d5131-76d5-4708-8671-d1ba79e826bb.jpg',42090658,70,'45.48839','-122.72595',1,5,2.50,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,1125,89,4.88,24358125),(1145,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24375929','Mount Tabor Hideaway','Mt Tabor Hideaway is a fully stand-alone guesthouse at the back of our lot. Located at the foot of Mt Tabor, near SE Division & 60th, enjoy privacy & comfort in it\'s bright, modern & clean space. 2 BR with 3/4 Ba on each level, full kitchen, heat & A/C. French doors lead to your private outdoor patio. Reliable high speed internet, 600 mbps. Small smart TV. Enjoy a misty morning, drizzly afternoon or evening walk in Mt Tabor Park in a friendly neighborhood.<br /><br />City permit # 18–1 37613–0 00–00 – HO','This is a friendly neighborhood with folks living with family on the same street: kids, working professionals, & older adults. We’re close to multiple bus lines. We’re close to the Hawthorne district, Restaurant Row on SE Division as well as the Jade district and Montavilla.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f3a0fd5e-dde3-41db-8c0e-5dabe76732d7.jpg',25375623,15,'45.50817','-122.59992',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,184.00,1,28,216,4.96,24375929),(1146,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24406806','Work & Live in Alberta Arts Farmhouse','Come spend the Holidays in our Beautiful 100 year old farmhouse that seamlessly blends old world charm with modern conveniences. This is a light-filled home sits a block from Alberta Arts Street and 3 blocks from Alberta Park. Great for families, with lots of flexible space.  Hi-speed Internet makes this a perfect place to work, or a tranquil retreat while looking for a forever home. Fenced backyard with grill for outdoor dining.','The Alberta Arts District is an historically eclectic and racially diverse part of Portland, long home to many artists and families.  The neighborhood has been gentrifying and that has brought many new shops and restaurants to the area.  There are wonderful parks with playgrounds within walking distance (Alberta Park and Wilshire Park), lots of coffee shops, cafes and boutiques.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/42fde29d-d072-4727-bc59-3f0c31114f39.jpg',56752027,1,'45.55983','-122.63959',1,6,2.00,3.00,4.00,128.00,30,180,55,4.93,24406806),(1147,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24414396','SE Modern PDX','Come home to a modern garden suite in SE Portland’s trendy Richmond neighborhood. We are centrally located a few blocks south of Division Street where you can find gourmet dining, shopping and entertainment destinations, and 15 minutes by car to all that downtown Portland has to offer.','Start your day with a stroll to the original Stumptown or stylish Good Coffee for your morning fix, and then walk over to Petite Provence for an indulgent pastry. Take a refreshing jog through Tabor Park and grab lunch nearby at any number of signature Portland restaurants including Pok Pok, Scottie’s, Por Que No, Broder Cafe…the list goes on. <br /><br />Choose between happy hour back on restaurant row, or cooking a healthy meal in your fully appointed kitchen with local organic ingredients from one of four grocery stores nearby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e07a5af5-26e6-4a19-8c4b-29504220cfb5.jpg',184330974,8,'45.50102','-122.61604',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,30,190,62,4.98,24414396),(1148,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24492134','Portland Nest Guesthouse','Your urban forest oasis awaits you at the Nest Guest House! This newly constructed, well appointed and restful apartment has all you need for a perfectly Portland getaway. <br />Wake up to birdsong, coffee/tea and snacks. Enjoy the outdoor space, garden views, and relax in luxurious comfort in your  730 sq. feet apt.<br />Very close to the airport, short walk to restaurants, food carts, grocery store and transit. Nearby neighborhoods (10 min.drive/20 min walk) Fremont St, Alberta Arts, 42nd St, Hollywood.','The Nest Guesthouse is two blocks from the center of the Cully neighborhood, with restaurants, grocery stores, coffee shops and more.  Long blocks encourage walkers and a nearby park provides outdoor community','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a235d96a-b36e-45c0-97cb-a846aaa07d58.jpg',50378629,21,'45.55769','-122.60496',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,95.00,3,90,133,4.95,24492134),(1149,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24499293','PDX Portland Garden Cottage','Beautiful modern 2 story guest cottage built in 2019. Located 2 blocks from the Adidas HQ Village and a few blocks from the MAX light rail, which takes you to the Moda Center, Veterans Memorial Coliseum, Convention Center and downtown in 5-15 minutes. Walk, bike or drive to the many cafes, shops and restaurants at nearby destination neighborhoods, including the Alberta Arts District (1.5 miles), Killingsworth St. (.4 miles). Williams District (.9 miles), and Mississippi Ave. (.5 mile).','The guest cottage is located in the Overlook neighborhood and is...<br />- A few blocks from the MAX (light rail), which will take you to the Moda Center, Veterans Memorial Coliseum, the Convention Center area, and downtown Portland in 5-10 minutes.<br />- Several grocery stores nearby<br />- 2 blocks away from the Adidas HQ Campus<br />- A nice walk or a very quick drive to several eating and shopping destinations - Alberta Arts District, Williams Ave. District, Mississippi Ave. and Killingsworth St.<br />- 10 minute drive to downtown <br />- 20 minute drive to Portland International Airport (PDX)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/337afe45-54cc-424a-adf5-ee19f64f4bff.jpg',185071931,13,'45.55891036987305','-122.68563079833984',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,99.00,3,18,377,4.99,24499293),(1150,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24519446','Modern  3bed/2bath Townhome Steps to Mississippi!','For those of you who love to be smack dab in the middle of the action, with every restaurant, bar, shop and cafe right outside your door, this professionally-managed, 2-story townhome, with its Walk Score of 95, is the perfect place to experience Portland by day, and comfortably lay your head at night. Located smack dab in the middle of Portland\'s most coveted area, Mississippi Street, this house is seriously a stone\'s throw from all of the action Portland has become famous for. Come stay!','The Mississippi neighborhood has quickly become one of Portland\'s most coveted foodie areas, with such names as ¿Por Qué No?, Tasty & Sons, Prost!, Gravy, Blue Star Donuts, Mee Sen Thai, Interurban and more just steps away from the house! And with easy access to the Overlook MAX station, getting downtown is super easy, too; be there in less than twenty minutes!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-24519446/original/04cf55d8-b393-4181-a1d9-b8250e2bd6a4.jpeg',111978787,9,'45.55039596557617','-122.67799377441406',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,99.00,30,1125,246,4.84,24519446),(1151,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24556478','Downtown Portland with a View','Experience authentic Portland in this beautiful, vintage gem. With a walk score of 96, we are in the heart of Portland, walking distance to NW 23rd and 21st, downtown and transit. With a view of downtown from the living room, our apartment is your doorstep to Portland!','We are in the heart of Portland in the historic Goose Hollow neighborhood, and are five minutes walk to the famous NW 23rd, known for shops, restaurants, bars and coffee shops. We are also a stone\'s throw from a couple of farmer\'s markets, as well as a Fred Meyer, a Zupan\'s and a Trader Joe\'s. Washington Park, at just a few blocks away, is essentially your backyard, and home to the Rose Garden, Japanese Garden, Arboretum, Zoo and more. If you are a soccer fan, we are two blocks from Providence Park. MAX train and bus within two blocks. Movie theaters, bookstores and more are within a ten minute walk.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a60b3413-de51-4ab7-9ca6-e8a47380c7f0.jpg',5302649,3,'45.52161','-122.69468',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,30,1125,22,5.00,24556478),(1152,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24582435','Private, clean garden cottage- great location!','Sparkling clean newer construction in the popular and centrally located Mississippi District.  Quiet, safe, cozy and private off street garden and home filled with natural light. Private entrance from the alley behind our house.  Fast Wifi for distance working.  Full kitchen. Accessible for wheelchairs/walkers.  Disinfecting thoroughly (by a nurse!) between guests. We strive to create a safe and welcoming space, so that all kind and considerate people can be comfortable in our new little home!','I kid you not when I say that we live in the best neighborhood to stay in when visiting Portland.  It is safe and quiet, yet just a few blocks to N. Mississippi Avenue and N. Williams Avenue, two of the most popular destinations in the city for tourists and locals alike.  Easy walk to numerous cafes/restaurants/bars/grocery stores/local boutiques.  We are one block away from a park that is great for little kids.  Our neighborhood is one of the most diverse in the city and has an interesting history to discover.  We are a 5-10 minute drive to Alberta Arts district and downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-24582435/original/34440158-7bed-4daa-ab7f-dd3b5dd35802.jpeg',6746145,9,'45.55186','-122.67121',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,92.00,2,90,241,4.97,24582435),(1153,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24607040','Huge house in the BEST location (99 walk score!)','Elegantly stylish flat located in the desirable NW area of Portland. This 2100 sq. ft. accommodation comprises the upper 2 floors of a historical Portland home. Walk to everything: public transit, coffee shops, restaurants, bars, Trader Joe’s, yoga/gyms, hiking trails. The Pearl District with its eclectic mix of shops, restaurants, and bars, is just blocks away. COVID clean and completely sanitized. <br />I know all the best places to eat/drink/and hangout, so you will have the insider\'s guide.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/80719b26-469d-4b8b-ab5d-4fa8d7f93e9c.jpg',3823371,27,'45.5263','-122.68994',1,5,2.00,3.00,5.00,507.00,30,180,84,4.98,24607040),(1154,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24608049','Stylish detached one bedroom in University Park.','This is a stylish and comfortable one bedroom apartment.  It is new construction and we have thought of almost everything.  It is full of natural light and spacious.  It is walking distance to the University of Portland, a cute cafe, and New Seasons grocery store.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b12a1cd9-efc5-44e5-a24e-cee240b18e44.jpg',3635384,57,'45.57941','-122.73477',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,177,4.94,24608049),(1155,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24623591','Scenic floating home in Portland\'s Columbia River','Relax in this floating home with views out each window of the water. It is very peaceful here on the water (no cars, leaf blowers to wake you). You have the entire lower floor with your own entry. Next door is Lotus Isle Park which we use as an off-leash dog park.','It is very peaceful here on the water. There are no cars, leaf blowers to wake you. the Portland International airport is only a few miles away and on some days the overhead traffic is about a mile away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0ba62ff9-27fc-44ee-ba4c-81150792859e.jpg',63093092,85,'45.60611343383789','-122.6747817993164',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,90,1125,18,4.89,24623591),(1156,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24635402','Charming Victorian One Bedroom - Heart of Downtown','Central and cozy vintage apartment in the heart of downtown Portland. The Streetcar and multiple bus lines are steps away, Portland State University and Portland\'s beautiful Park Blocks are one block from the apartment, and the Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall is within short walking distance. The kitchen is equipped for light cooking and there are plenty of comfortable blankets and towels. Laundry onsite. Enjoy everything the city has to offer from this central, private, and convenient apartment!','This is a very central downtown apartment, right next to Portland State University, the Art Museum, and Safeway. Coffee shops, restaurants, and bars are steps away. All of downtown is easily walkable from this location, and there are several public transit options right outside the door. It is a vibrant and bustling street, sure to give you an authentic and comfortable Portland experience.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2b8330c3-259d-4eb8-8485-766fba938490.jpg',186181978,44,'45.5153','-122.6852',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,31,90,128,4.79,24635402),(1157,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24652511','Downtown NW Portland Willamette Riverfront Condo!','This listing is for a 1 Bedroom Condo with reserved parking, located at NW Portland Waterfront next to the Steel Bridge.  Within close walking distance to; NW Pearl and Alphabet District, Chinatown, SW Downtown district, Tom McCall Waterfront Park, Steel & Broadway Bridges, Moda Center, Convention Center, Public Transit, etc. <br /><br />This condo is also conveniently located less than 100 feet from convenience/grocery store and massage parlor.<br /><br />Walk-ability Score 87.','3-5 minute walk to Tom McCall waterfront park. Two blocks from the main train and bus terminals.  The Old Town Tri-Met stop is only three blocks away.  Easy access to all of Portland and surrounding areas using the MAX light rail system. Portland Street Car and Bus Stop are also very close and easily walk-able. Union Station less than two blocks from condo.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-24652511/original/ee78e51b-7ee6-4b61-8eb6-741929cb68c8.jpeg',121596159,43,'45.52785','-122.67255',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,31,265,24,4.88,24652511),(1158,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24674950','pet friendly Pearl condo right on the river','Pet friendly with approval.Riverview! upscale ground floor condo for a booking of a month or longer at McCormick Pier. Book 31 nights or more  and you pay no city tax (You’ll save est $600). A dog walking/ foot path steps away. Easy Access to metro, OSHU, RiverWalk,Trains. Patrolled security,Designated Covered parking space. NOTE: Portland, like most coastal cities, is experiencing home deprived encampments. In the Old Town area this is most apparent near the burnside bridge and train station.','On the river but in the city. Walk score 95. Lots of restaurants in the pearl. Walk over the broadway bridge in 10 minutes to get to Moda center for sports events or walk to The Pearl’s great shops, bars and restaurants. There’s the famous Union Train station nearby (with a great jazz bar/ restaurant called Milfs) for trips to Seattle or LA . Yes, you will hear train horns at times during the day …and at nite! BUT, you are in the heart of Portland with a  view of the river, a pet friendly condo, a nature river walk and Bike/jogging path right outside your door! Note: Portland is currently doing it’s best to address the home deprived situation but be aware there is an encampment near the burnside bridge and train station near the post office.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f3879e09-3b33-42bc-bde4-a8f8331908df.jpg',48754857,43,'45.52684','-122.6718',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,81.00,30,365,22,4.77,24674950),(1159,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24676704','Tiny House in Alameda/Alberta Arts ~ Dog Friendly','Quaint Urban retreat located in the heart of NE Portland near the Alberta Arts District. Offers everything you could need for a relaxing, central stay!<br /><br />The home features bright, open concept living with a fully equipped kitchen, an inviting lounge with sofa bed, queen bedroom space, Smart 43\" TV, modern bathroom & café style dining that doubles as a workspace.<br />Steps from the vibrant Alberta Arts district and Fremont Place with Whole Foods, Rose City Book Pub, cafes, restaurants & so much more!','Prime Location ~ On the corner of NE 19th & Alameda Street in vibrant NE Portland.<br />The tiny home is located in the lovely Sabin neighborhood within walking distance to the popular Alberta Arts District, a vibrant neighborhood located just half a mile away. <br />The area is known for its lively art scene, unique shops, and diverse selection of restaurants where you can enjoy browsing the many art galleries and studios which feature the work of local artists and designers. On the last Thursday of every month, the neighborhood hosts an art walk, which draws large crowds and features live music, food vendors, and street performers.<br />In addition to its art scene, the Alberta Arts District is also home to a variety of shops and boutiques, offering everything from vintage clothing to handmade jewelry. The area is also known for its excellent dining options, with a wide range of restaurants featuring cuisine from around the world, as well as local favorites like pizza and craft beer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-24676704/original/5f5790af-d3ed-4016-a7c2-2f615c67047a.jpeg',186502539,6,'45.55258','-122.64533',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,102.00,2,1125,402,4.92,24676704),(1160,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24716882','Stunning Home in Alberta’s Art District','An artistic vintage inspired home in NE Portland-close to Alberta Arts district!Gracious host and well known painter/interior designer Trish Grantham has been collecting for a life time and showcases the beauty throughout her spacious 1907 home. Experience her space, or as people say a museum of sorts, in a laid back, artists\' home. 21 years in Portland, Trish will send you to the best hidden restaurants, shops, and venues. MUST LOVE PETS! 1 Cat and 2 small dogs (sometimes)! Loving and quiet!','The neighborhood is one of the best in town.  Walk to parks, cafes, grocery stores, bars, record stores, clothing shops, ice cream, and music venues in minutes!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/85b324ca-393e-4708-9d8f-6c7d2809507c.jpg',529068,24,'45.55802','-122.66991',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,30,1125,80,4.98,24716882),(1161,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24729306','Sanctuary in Historic Kenton','Sanctuary in Historic Kenton<br />Cute, clean, comfortable private guest suite. Huge queen bed, sectional sofa, private entrance, kitchenette, full bath. Convenient to everything Portland has to offer!','Located in historic Kenton just a short walk to great shops, bars, cafes, restaurants, Kenton park, the library, and the MAX Light Rail — everything you need within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-24729306-unapproved/original/fb7457d3-4224-4c42-aa0d-5872f8970574.JPEG',1538000,55,'45.5801','-122.69104',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,2,30,122,4.90,24729306),(1162,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24754870','Cozy Fireplace!Walk Alberta Arts~SilverStarCottage','Come stay in our sweet, new guesthouse!  This is NOT a basement space. It has a real bedroom (not a studio) & full kitchen. <br />The Silver Star cottage is in our backyard but very separate with its own city lane access.    Lots of beautiful wood and a cozy vibe.  We are 1 block from the fabulous Alberta Arts St. but far enough away that it\'s quiet here. Perfect!  Walk to shops & restaurants. Also easy to access anywhere in the city. There\'s a double-sized hide a bed couch in the airy living space.','The Alberta Arts neighborhood is a vibrant place with boutiques, fabulous restaurants, art galleries, ice cream shops, and, of course, many coffee shops.  We are close to The Kennedy School, Salt & Straw, Bollywood Theater, and even a soak & sauna space called Common Ground.  Portland International Airport (PDX) is 14 minutes by car.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cec27cae-90d6-4a4f-aa81-22819d94c611.jpg',11816483,1,'45.558','-122.63831',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,104.00,1,40,362,4.98,24754870),(1163,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24807587','Sellwood-Moreland Stand-Alone Bungalow','New Sellwood-Moreland bungalow in the heart of charming and historic neighborhood.  Completely separate from main house. Full kitchen, king-sized Tuft & Needle mattress, sofa-bed, cable TV, wi-fi.  A couple of blocks from coffee, bars, restaurants, grocery store and more.  Car optional: 2 blocks from bus & bike path.  Note: a spiral staircase connects the 2 floors. Quiet. neighborhood with easy street parking (note: driveway is for owners).  No smoking  or pets please.  Permit # 18-133329.','Here is a great short description of our neighborhood that sums it up, but there\'s SO MUCH more so we\'ve also listed several websites that will give you more specific information, guides, and history on Sellwood-Moreland. We\'ve also noted the necessary amenities that you can walk to (there\'s nothing you won\'t find). You will love it here!!<br /><br />\"Sellwood feels much less \"hipster\" and \"chic\" than say, Mississippi Ave, Alberta Arts or the Pearl-- but a definite, at ease kind of \'anything goes, all are welcome\' type of feeling is present on these streets.  Like most Portland neighborhoods, Sellwood and Moreland neighborhoods feel very self-sustaining.  Local grocery store New Seasons, many local coffee shops plus a few local coffee roasters make this community feel warm and a lot like its own small town.  Walking the streets in Sellwood and Moreland neighborhoods invokes a \"back in the good old days\" feeling.  This area is family friendly, walkable, and livable with a strong sense o','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f93c0ba5-848c-4dcd-a8b5-08e183893494.jpg',164973855,20,'45.47921','-122.65069',1,3,1.50,1.00,2.00,94.00,3,28,309,4.97,24807587),(1164,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24833444','Explore the City from the Heart of Hawthorne','Located in the vibrant Hawthorne District, our apartment is within walking distance of Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brewpubs, and distilleries. other services, such as banks and massage therapists, are also nearby.  Around a mile from downtown, you can easily use bikes, public bus services, or walk to explore the city. Our sleek, European-style interiors feature high-grade surfaces and finishes, offering comfort and elegance in one of Portland\'s most dynamic neighborhoods.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors, with no chain restaurants in sight! Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, indulge in delicious wings right around the corner at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or enjoy a fancy night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />Portland isn\'t just for foodies. Hawthorne boasts a vibrant indie spirit, with numerous made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques to explore in this hipster haven. Catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue, serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping isn’t your idea of fun, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park atop a dormant volcano vent. Here, you\'ll find miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-24833444/original/99628f59-4519-4a14-b7ab-c6ea62c818b5.jpeg',187734201,32,'45.51312','-122.64583',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,67.00,1,1125,564,4.88,24833444),(1165,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24835735','Artist’s garden apartment','Located in one of the best neighborhoods in Portland. This basement apartment is filled with light, spacious (900 square feet) and stays nice and cool in the summer. Hawthorne and Division Avenue are both in walking distance and contain the best restaurants, cafes and bars Portland has to offer. Ceiling is low in some areas I recommend those under 6 feet tall. :)','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-24835735/original/31ad73ff-ca79-4230-a853-6ed23bb5e740.jpg',77382200,8,'45.50742','-122.62559',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,115.00,5,130,85,4.98,24835735),(1166,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24895142','Tabor Rest','Welcome to Tabor Rest. <br /><br />You are steps from  Mt. Tabor Park, a walkable, urban forest. You\'re also close to Portland\'s iconic Hawthorne District. <br /><br />This is a quiet, safe and picturesque Mt. Tabor Neighborhood yet still near restaurants on Division St . You\'re walking distance from  coffee shops, bakeries, food carts and uniquely \'Portlandia\' adventures. <br /><br />Verdant views. Green design. Numerous architectural details and personal features.  <br /><br />We hope that you\'ll love it here. Welcome. Cheers!','Words are not enough!  Just check out  \'Mt Tabor Portland\' and look at some photos of our area. Our neighborhood is a unique enclave in the heart of SE Portland. We are a secluded area, yet right next to an amazing park and the culturally engaging Hawthorne District. We think that you\'ll  enjoy exploring the area. When we first moved here I thought \"This area is so beautiful  someone ought to film a movie here!\" And now, years later our neighborhood has been the set of several films and TV shows. We feel secure in our historic neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9df2cdc8-1f43-4323-8ed1-9a972032a565.jpg',4105484,15,'45.51189','-122.60423',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,30,90,19,5.00,24895142),(1167,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24916586','CDC Compliant | Meticulously Clean Private Flat','If you’re looking for a safe, rigorously sanitized, home base in Portland, we’ve got your back!<br /><br />We’re taking corona virus extremely seriously and have doubled down on our already meticulous cleaning practices (see past reviews & list of cleaning protocols in our photos section). We now provide CDC compliant deep cleaning between every guest, using only approved products. You will not find a cleaner place to stay on the west coast.<br /><br />Thanks for the interest and we look forward to hosting you!','We are in a quiet, residential neighborhood, with several great bars, restaurants, and cafes within easy walking distance (see our 5-minute walking map in photos). We\'re always happy to let you explore, but can also provide local recommendations for hidden gems.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-24916586/original/265eab7d-4134-4ecd-80f4-f6e0f2810aad.jpeg',4089776,13,'45.55891','-122.68567',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,73.00,2,30,273,4.99,24916586),(1168,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24917913','Quiet private garden oasis, parking+walk score 90','★Totally private & quiet cozy house, no shared walls! <br /><br />★ Serta Queen bed w/400 thread count linens<br /><br />★Extra beds (sofabed, air mattress)*<br /><br />★Off street parking in driveway<br /><br />★Large fenced-in gated yard <br /><br />★Quiet independent air conditioning/heat <br /><br />★Full sized kitchen! Fridge, oven, stove, microwave<br /><br />★ Washer/dryer<br /><br />★47\" Smart TV, blazing fast wifi<br /><br />★Keypad self-check in<br /><br />★Walk score 90, Biker\'s paradise 95! Great dining, movies, shops, parks<br /><br />*BEFORE BOOKING pet fees/extra beds are paid SEPARATELY👇','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/01dbf645-9da3-41bf-8513-212d4cbe92dc.jpg',10872163,8,'45.49944','-122.62219',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,107.00,2,28,301,4.83,24917913),(1169,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24922380','Richmond Cottage in St Johns, Portland','This light, bright cottage is located in the heart of the St Johns neighborhood in Portland. Full of charm it features loads of reclaimed wood with an industrial farmhouse vibe. Complete with a private deck, keyless entry, full kitchen with eat-in island and a sleeping loft with a queen sized bed.  It is a close walk to restaurants, coffee shops, bars and shopping. Easy access to downtown Portland, University of Portland, the airport and the rest that Portland has to offer.','St. Johns is a neighborhood of Portland, Oregon. Located in North Portland on the tip of the peninsula formed by the confluence of the Willamette and the Columbia Rivers, St. Johns sits north of Cathedral Park, which is home to the only suspension bridge in the Willamette Valley, the iconic St. Johns Bridge. St. Johns is described by locals as \"extremely friendly\", \"A town within a city...\" The post office, coffee shops, breakfast places, restaurants, movie theaters, grocery stores, and several parks, are all within walking distance for residents and guests.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a033d203-2a36-400c-a77a-3d361e367862.jpg',6989528,58,'45.59464','-122.74913',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,125.00,2,90,217,5.00,24922380),(1170,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24931930','Casa Blanca','Spacious and private mother-in-law apartment in brand new house in quiet North Portland University Park neighborhood. <br /><br />580 sq ft, ground-level apt. has private entrance, parking spot, full kitchen, and washer/dryer.  Perfect for extended stays. Also can sleep up to 4: bedroom has a queen bed and there\'s a queen sleeper sofa in living room.<br /><br />Just blocks from University of Portland. <br />Close to shops and nightlife in NE Portland and St John\'s.<br /><br />Host lives in the upper part of house with roommates.','just blocks to University of Portland as well as bars and nightlife, neighborhood is quiet and has authentic Portland character','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-24931930-unapproved/original/05f2b875-2490-4c65-b8c5-bc4257c4812b.JPEG',21443934,57,'45.57834','-122.72716',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,39,4.95,24931930),(1171,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24970240','The Award Winning Z-Haus','The Award winning Z-Haus in the Heart of P-Town!! As seen in Dwell magazine, Oregon Home magazine, Apartment Therapy, The Kitchn, & Renest this Award winning design by Waechter Architecture is 2800 square feet, comprised of a series of rooms connected by half flights of stairs with framed views & full of natural light. Ideally located near Williams Ave Dist, Alberta Dist, Mississippi Ave Dist, the Pearl Dist, & Downtown. New Seasons Market is 3 blocks away as are Nike bikes available to rent.','The neighborhood is vibrant and full of amenities- New Seasons grocery store is a 5-10min walk away, cafes, ice cream shops, breweries, & boutiques all immediately out your doorstep. Off street parking available at the house.  <br /><br />It is also possible to quickly and easily walk (ie: roughly 30-40 min to Powell’s Bookstore) or bike (approximately 10-15 min, also to Powell’s) to the Pearl Dist or downtown. <br /><br />Powell’s Books, Oregon Chinese Garden, shops & boutiques, Pioneer Place Mall, Movie theaters, Portland Saturday market, NW. 23rd Ave. & The Alphabet District shops and eateries, the list goes on. All at your finger tips!!<br /><br />Stay in or go out, either way you will greatly enjoy this beautiful house and this central location!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/14b32043-5531-4764-80ee-7a6d2df48aa2.jpg',188778344,9,'45.54927','-122.6645',1,8,2.50,3.00,4.00,399.00,30,1125,8,4.88,24970240),(1172,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24970358','Hawthorne Penthouse Retreat- Roof Deck & Food Pods','Located in the vibrant Hawthorne District, our apartment is within walking distance of Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brewpubs, and distilleries. other services such as banks and massage therapists are also nearby.  Around a mile from downtown, you can easily use bikes, public bus services, or walk to explore the city. Our sleek, European-style interiors feature high-grade surfaces and finishes, offering comfort and elegance in one of Portland\'s most dynamic neighborhoods.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors, with no chain restaurants in sight! Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, indulge in delicious wings right around the corner at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or enjoy a fancy night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjQ5NzAzNTg%3D/original/f0758532-735d-42cc-89ef-ad27e96bad0a.jpeg',187734201,25,'45.5121','-122.64733',1,8,2.00,4.00,5.00,265.00,1,1125,558,4.92,24970358),(1173,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24973125','Sage Guest House','Enjoy free parking adjacent to the Guest House!<br />Located steps from the Hawthorne District and nestled in the historic Ladd\'s Addition neighborhood, this guest house is near fine restaurants, coffee shops, entertainment venues, and food carts .  Stroll in the shade of century old Elm trees, and discover four public rose gardens located at the compass points within this 1890 neighborhood.','Ladd\'s Addition is Portland\'s oldest planned community (1891) and one of the oldest in the western United States. Located near Hawthorne Blvd, guests will find high quality restaurants, coffee shops, and entertainment venues on both Hawthorne Blvd and Division Street within a 15-minute walk. Offering a counterpoint to the active perimeter commercial streets, the quiet formal geometry of this neighborhood offers rose gardens at each of the compass points, and major avenues are lined with century old American Elms that converge on a central public lawn.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-24973125/original/a3fb372e-c27c-46ed-8020-0d5c240d95f4.jpeg',42173408,25,'45.51051','-122.64662',1,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,200.00,3,14,97,5.00,24973125),(1174,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24989575','Portland, Oregon Studio steps to OHSU','This lovely studio is adjacent to the Oregon Health Sciences University- OHSU campus. A completely private studio w a Queen-sized bed, TV w Roku, and wi-fi.<br /><br />Typically rented by medical & nursing students. <br />Parking is very difficult to find, and guests need to purchase a parking permit. It is very close to downtown I recommend not having a car, taking Lyft or Uber.<br /><br />Minimum rental is 30 days. <br />If you rent for 30 days you will pay $465 in taxes.<br />If you rent for 31 days you will pay zero in tax.','It is an area filled with medical, dental and nursing students.<br />It\'s on top of Marquam hill and rather isolated from nearby downtown.<br />There is great hiking super closeby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/36513c30-4d32-4814-8e50-6cde8367ddc8.jpg',375683,30,'45.49928','-122.69005',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,69.00,30,1125,26,4.77,24989575),(1175,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/24993362','Cute solar-powered basement studio apartment','A lovely studio basement apartment, completely powered by solar energy, in historic Sellwood-Moreland neighborhood. Close to antique shops, bike paths, hiking trails, and public transportation, all within 20 mins of downtown Portland!<br /><br />We\'re transplants from India and Singapore and world travelers who have put down roots in Portland. We have often benefited from the kindness of strangers on our travels, and want to pay it forward.<br /><br />Please note we have a kiddo and a dog, so expect noises!','We moved to Sellwood-Moreland after looking all over Portland for our ideal neighborhood! Sellwood-Moreland sits atop a bluff and overlooks a special natural area (Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge, a birder\'s paradise), has extreme bike-ability (hello Springwater Corridor - 40 miles of bike-only path circling Portland), access to parks (three!) and some hidden gems for restaurants and bars (including our own speakeasy!).<br /><br />Our home is a block from #19 and #70, buses that connect you to downtown and to the Orange max line. Our favorite feature is the Willamette River, which you can access from Sellwood Park, a 15 min walk from our home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e090021f-9fca-409f-ac67-754a60dff4bc.jpg',4687912,20,'45.47664','-122.64964',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,55.00,3,25,96,4.83,24993362),(1176,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25016760','Hawthorne Hideout*Heated floors* walk everywhere!','This custom one-bedroom basement apartment has full size ceilings and windows and all the comforts of home. Stellar location two blocks from Hawthorne Street. With a kitchenette, washer/dryer, 4K smart TV, and beautiful custom wood and tile throughout. There is radiant floor heating that keeps this space extra cozy in the winter, and cool in the summer. Perfect home base for exploring or working in Portland with or without a car. This space is friendly to all.','Our block has on street parking, but can sometimes get full, so parking may be up to a block away. This is one of the city’s most colorful and charming neighborhoods, full of destination restaurants, unique shops, parks and farmer’s markets. A bike share station is just a few blocks away, so a car isn’t always needed and many visitors and locals alike use public transportation. The nearest bus station is a 1/2 block away and you can walk to nearby, Hawthorne street, Division street and Belmont districts, Mount Tabor and Laurelhurst Parks.<br /><br />There are many great places to eat, drink and shop with in walking distance.  The famous Bagdad theater is 4 blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-25016760/original/7879948a-42e1-465c-a127-db282dc88292.jpg',2066656,16,'45.51318','-122.62326',1,3,1.00,1.00,3.00,94.00,2,28,300,4.99,25016760),(1177,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25037353','The Creative Oasis on Hawthorne','Located in the heart of the eclectic Hawthorne District, you\'ll be within walking distance of some of Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brew-pubs, distilleries, and craftspeople. If you want to explore another area of Portland, I\'m just over a mile from the West side via bike, walking, or frequent bus service. The place has been designed to create a sleek, soothing, and stylish feel, incorporating the highest-grade finishes.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of an incredible array of top-notch local flavors (no chain restaurants here!). Indulge in vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, savor wings right around the corner at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or opt for an elegant evening at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />Portland\'s charm extends beyond its culinary delights. The vibrant indie spirit of the Hawthorne area is alive with a multitude of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques, making it a true hipster haven. Catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping isn’t your preferred activity, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park atop a dormant volcano vent. Here, you’ll find miles of hiking trails and incredi','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25037353/original/db9fafd4-5ca3-4db2-9290-131223a564b4.jpeg',146196024,32,'45.51331','-122.64701',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,73.00,1,1125,586,4.91,25037353),(1178,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25052019','Modern Hawthorne Studio - Food Carts & Local Shops','My apartment building is located in the heart of the eclectic Hawthorne District, within walking distance to some of Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brew-pubs, distilleries, and artisan shops. You\'ll also find all necessary services, from banks to massage therapists, and it\'s just over a mile from downtown by bike, walking, or frequent bus service. The interiors are designed with a sleek, soothing European feel, incorporating the highest-grade surfaces and finishes.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District puts you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors (no chain restaurants here!). Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, dive into some wings at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or enjoy a fancy night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />Portland isn\'t just for foodies. The vibrant indie spirit of Hawthorne is alive with plenty of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques to explore in this hipster haven. Catch a movie at the Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews. If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of fun, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park on top of a dormant volcano vent, where you’ll find miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of the city. Enj','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25052019/original/2cc1e555-cea0-4643-915b-9133d91b57fb.jpeg',36435346,32,'45.51331','-122.64593',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,67.00,1,1125,445,4.87,25052019),(1179,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25057254','Chez MAK - Large condo w/ balcony over the Pearl','You won\'t find a better location!  Perfectly centered in Portland\'s trendy Pearl district.<br /><br />Gorgeous large condo with full balcony in the heart of downtown Portland.  Steps to restaurants, nightlife and public transportation.  About 15 minutes to all of the best Portland has to offer.','Heart of the Pearl.  A lively central neighborhood in Portland.  Close to downtown.  Walk to everything.<br /><br />Walk to Whole Foods and Safeway, one block from a Walgreens pharmacy.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7b8e9e76-07b9-40e9-aa8e-5d6542424152.jpg',189444467,2,'45.52655','-122.68341',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,49,4.96,25057254),(1180,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25082436','Victorian in Historic Irvington','Cozy one-bedroom basement apartment in the Daniel Olson House, a beautifully restored 1893 Victorian in the Irvington historic district of downtown Portland. Full kitchen, bath, and separate, gated entrance through back garden area. Located in thriving inner Northeast neighborhood, its a pleasant 3-block walk to shops, restaurants, cafes, and public transportation. On-street parking out front on quiet, tree-lined street that is dedicated bikeway.','Before there were bridges crossing the Willamette River that splits the city in two, Irvington was the first area to be settled on Portland\'s inner Eastside  It is a quiet, leafy, residential area that runs from 7th to 24th and is Portland\'s most architectually diverse  neighborhood. Our street (Tillamook) was the original \"Main Street\" and was the first to be graded, get plank sidewalks, and it even had a trolley running down it','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/54603083-2f58-4539-98bd-f7abdbbbad54.jpg',168608697,7,'45.5382','-122.65443',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,2,1125,232,4.91,25082436),(1181,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25099504','Alberta Arts Retreat with 4 bedrooms/3.5 baths','The Alberta Arts Retreat is located in the heart of the vibrant Alberta Arts area of Portland, within easy walking distance of great coffee shops, restaurants, boutiques, and parks. Guests appreciate the spacious house and comfortable outdoor spaces. The on-site resident, as required by the City of Portland for short term rentals, is in a separate apartment and is available for assistance, if needed. The perfect location for your Portland visit!','Portland is a city of great neighborhoods, and the Alberta Arts area is one of the most fun and exciting. In addition to all of the restaurants and shops, there are parks, bike rentals (the house is on the designated bike route), the Kennedy School for movies, and much more. The house is in a residential area, and we ask that our guests be considerate of the neighbors.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25099504/original/4869a6dc-3d00-44c3-a72a-715c8d7af110.jpeg',21467169,6,'45.55658','-122.65131',1,8,3.50,4.00,4.00,529.00,3,29,150,4.99,25099504),(1182,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25190815','The Vera Tiny Home at Slabtown Village','Slabtown Village is Portland’s first tiny home hotel to mix existing historical houses with high-end modern tiny homes to form a one-of-a-kind hotel experience.<br /><br />Each home is fully furnished and self-contained. All six homes come with light cooking options, shower, full bathroom amenities, complimentary tea and coffee, and an attached deck alongside outdoor areas.','Located on NW Overton Street between 18th and 19th Avenues. This trendy area, which boasts walkable streets, plentiful shopping, coffee, restaurants and art galleries, is within walking distance of many other local hot spots. From here, you can easily access downtown, the Pearl District, Nob Hill and Forest Park, either on foot, bike or via Portland Streetcar. But feel free to stay put — everything you need can be found in this lively, friendly neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0b35d039-0366-47dc-baee-845cb23414a8.jpg',190340428,27,'45.53195','-122.69041',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,134.00,1,1125,143,4.94,25190815),(1183,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25213433','Perfectly Crafted Oasis in The Heart of Portland','Step into this light-filled Northwest sanctuary, just moments from the light rail and surrounded by local favorites markets, bars, cafes, and restaurants. This custom-designed space features unique architectural touches, including exposed scissor trusses over the spacious great room that flows to a charming back deck. Relax in the authentic Japanese spa-inspired bathroom for a truly serene experience. Enjoy high-speed internet and a Smart TV with local channels for all your entertainment needs.','Stroll to and from Peninsula Park truly one of Portland\'s gems or walk to New Seasons to grab ingredients for your next mouthwatering meal','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjUyMTM0MzM%3D/original/716d4d95-344d-47de-a7be-bfcbe574e091.jpeg',52609760,51,'45.56812','-122.68443',1,3,1.50,1.00,2.00,125.00,5,730,58,4.88,25213433),(1184,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25223570','波特兰 温馨小站','Welcome to Portland. Our home is your home. We\'re trying to give you a cozy home. We have two rooms for you to choose from. Six cars can be parked at the door. Four cars can be parked in the shed. There are two very large halls. There are more than 16,000 pings in the yard behind. If you don\'t want to go anywhere, you can lie in the garden and sunbathe in the grass. You can also sit on the terrace at night to see the stars. Transportation is convenient here. The airport is here. Uber is here in a few minutes. Welcome you.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7a9d4a2c-ae31-4e37-9237-6200970103bc.jpg',20955447,78,'45.48851','-122.54856',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,30.00,30,1125,17,4.71,25223570),(1185,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25233729','Sunny Studio Apartment ~ Food Carts, Coffee & Bars','Perfectly nestled between North Portland’s most vibrant neighborhoods, our location offers unparalleled convenience. Walk to bustling bars, renowned restaurants, and lively shows on Williams, N Mississippi, and Alberta Streets. This brand-new building features high-end finishes, providing a luxurious retreat to unwind after exploring Portland. Enjoy modern interiors with stainless steel appliances, quartz countertops, and expansive windows. We look forward to welcoming you soon!','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of an incredible array of top-notch local flavors (no chain restaurants here!). Indulge in vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, savor wings right around the corner at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or opt for an elegant evening at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />Portland\'s charm extends beyond its culinary delights. The vibrant indie spirit of the Hawthorne area is alive with a multitude of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques, making it a true hipster haven. Catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping isn’t your preferred activity, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park atop a dormant volcano vent. Here, you’ll find miles of hiking trails and incredi','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25233729/original/dd472feb-452e-4f62-8921-0e9c00706ef4.jpeg',190656099,32,'45.51289','-122.64661',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,66.00,1,1125,537,4.91,25233729),(1186,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25263259','The Henry Tiny Home at Slabtown Village','Slabtown Village is Portland’s first tiny home hotel to mix existing historical houses with high-end modern tiny homes to form a one-of-a-kind hotel experience.<br /><br />Each home is fully furnished and self-contained. All homes come with light cooking options, shower, full bathroom amenities, complimentary tea and coffee, and an attached deck alongside outdoor areas.','Located on NW Overton Street between 18th and 19th Avenues. This trendy area, which boasts walkable streets, plentiful shopping, coffee, restaurants and art galleries, is within walking distance of many other local hot spots. From here, you can easily access downtown, the Pearl District, Nob Hill and Forest Park, either on foot, bike or via Portland Streetcar. But feel free to stay put — everything you need can be found in this lively, friendly neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b5fbbb98-1423-4e95-80dc-a24ea07719b7.jpg',190340428,27,'45.53195','-122.69041',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,141.00,1,29,153,4.96,25263259),(1187,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25263730','The Weidler Tiny Home at Slabtown Village','Slabtown Village is Portland’s first tiny home hotel to mix existing historical houses with high-end modern tiny homes to form a one-of-a-kind hotel experience.<br /><br />Each home is fully furnished and self-contained. All six homes come with light cooking options, shower, full bathroom amenities, complimentary tea and coffee, and an attached deck alongside outdoor areas.','Located on NW Overton Street between 18th and 19th Avenues. This trendy area, which boasts walkable streets, plentiful shopping, coffee, restaurants and art galleries, is within walking distance of many other local hot spots. From here, you can easily access downtown, the Pearl District, Nob Hill and Forest Park, either on foot, bike or via Portland Streetcar. But feel free to stay put — everything you need can be found in this lively, friendly neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/41a21631-c7b3-4cd8-bb1d-737de17148f0.jpg',190340428,27,'45.53153','-122.69002',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,141.00,1,29,164,4.96,25263730),(1188,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25265689','#SavorTabor','Gorgeous modern Mt Tabor guesthouse filled with natural light. This private space is perfect for a couple\'s long week or a family\'s extended stay.','Mt Tabor is the only volcano inside a major city in the U.S. The park is wonderful, with trails and trees covering every inch. The surrounding neighborhoods and major walking streets - Hawthorne, Belmont, Burnside and Division - have everything you could need or want.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bde518a6-a1d1-4b08-8cbf-2ed4b33a9f3b.jpg',20950189,15,'45.51868','-122.60467',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,149.00,2,29,428,4.97,25265689),(1189,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25282946','The Mothership: a city retreat in the heart of SE','The Mothership Motel is a tastefully renovated house in the heart of Foster-Powell neighborhood exclusively designed for Airbnb. Walk to Henry Higgins Bagels, and Piper Cafe, Bread & Roses Market for delicious organic produce, Hammer & Jacks toy store, Red Castle Games, LoveHive Yoga, Ginger Salon, The Portland Mercado, Tango Berretin, and so much more!   We live on the property so you may see us check the mail or see a friend walk through the side yard to the back house.','Our SE neighborhood is a mix of brand new modern homes, 1950s bungalows, and old plantation-style houses.  With lots of young families, this safe and trendy little pocket offers everything you need from libraries and play structures to hip restaurants and night life. You are walking distance to major bus lines, the PDX Bodega sub shop is across the street, Bread & Roses market (a neighborhood fav!) is only 2 blocks away, and there is so much more!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a35b7b33-0af9-4d08-b592-e9ffabd6250c.jpg',7409866,36,'45.49061','-122.59851',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,85.00,30,1125,261,4.90,25282946),(1190,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25283645','Modern, Sleek & Stylish: 2 blocks from Hawthorne!','Designed to appeal to the most discriminating traveler, this large, family-friendly, original Portland Craftsman home has been lovingly designed to be a true home-away-from-home. With its Chef\'s kitchen, pillow-top beds, three private bathrooms, formal dining room, flat screen TVs and modern touches, this house is fully ready to be the highlight of your upcoming trip to the Pacific Northwest. This home is professionally managed by a local company; send us a message-we\'re ready to book your stay!','Voted one of the best neighborhoods in Portland by Sunset Magazine, the Richmond neighborhood does not disappoint. Located between the bustling streets of Hawthorne and Division, this neighborhood is chock full of many of Portland\'s best restaurants, bars and shops while still maintaining the eclectic \"Keep Portland Weird\" aesthetic that it\'s become famous for. <br /><br />You can\'t get any closer to the action than at this house, which sits just steps from popular Hawthorne Boulevard, with some of the city\'s most heralded restaurants, cafes, shops and bars just a block away, such as:<br /><br />-- Albina Press<br />-- Sapphire Lounge<br />-- ¿Por Qué No?<br />-- Apizza Scholls<br />-- Harlow<br />-- Ruby Jewel<br />-- Space Room<br />-- Coava Coffee<br />-- Hawthorne Theatre<br />-- Crossroads Trading Co.<br />-- Buffalo Exchange<br />-- Powell’s Books on Hawthorne<br />-- New Seasons Market<br />-- ... and too many more to list!<br /><br />LOCAL DESTINATIONS: <br />------------------','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/68769b0b-b3b4-4001-a664-71bb1895c123.jpg',114699668,8,'45.50964','-122.61233',1,6,3.00,3.00,4.00,173.00,2,1124,167,4.86,25283645),(1191,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25297183','Light & Bright Guest Suite','Light, bright and luxurious private Guest Suite with living room, bedroom, bath and separate entrance. Close-in to downtown Portland and Hollywood neighborhood. Enjoy coffee and tea by the gas fireplace, relax in the bedroom with comfortable king-sized bed and pamper yourself in the spa-like bathroom with heated floors and towel warmer.','Our home is in a sweet neighborhood with easy access to downtown, the Hollywood district, Rose City Golf course and more. One of the best coffee shops in Portland is a 1/4 mile walk and we have a great neighborhood breakfast spot nearby also.<br /><br />Love hiking or skiing? Easy access to Mt. Hood, the Columbia Gorge, Hood River.<br /><br />Want to head downtown but avoid parking? A Max stop is about 1/2 mile walk or bus stops are even closer. <br /><br />Easy to get here via car, public transit or from the airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7458cfff-50df-4f6f-9c8a-069ad9d5477a.jpg',1858382,11,'45.53502','-122.60291',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,14,80,4.96,25297183),(1192,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25340898','South Tabor Modern Cottage','Enjoy our newly constructed, light-filled, two-story modern cottage; primely located in the South Tabor neighborhood of SE Portland. Private entrance, 24-hr keyless entry, easy street parking, private garden patio area and full amenities. <br /><br />Permitted short term-rental through the City of Portland. <br />Permit # listed in guest house','The cottage and our property is located in the South Tabor neighborhood of SE Portland. South Tabor is becoming a popular SE neighborhood and is a mix of families and folks that have lived in the neighborhood for decades. We are a short walk to Clinton Park (big open park and play area), Mt. Tabor (beautiful natural wooded area with trails, reservoirs, summer concerts, and kids play areas). Nearby eateries are: Pizzacato, Thai Sky Kitchen, Rain or Shine Coffee House, and the Scout Beer and Food Lot on SE 50th and Division. There is also a small grocery store with all the essentials, Green Zebra. A quick drive or bike and you will be in the heart of SE Division Street (Bollywood Theater, Salt and Straw, Xico, Kati Portland, Olympic Provisions, plus SO MANY MORE eateries and shops)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e9be9257-d11f-4948-af4f-32b15272d0f1.jpg',12447921,37,'45.50076','-122.59979',1,4,1.50,2.00,3.00,150.00,2,14,260,4.99,25340898),(1193,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25372936','Charming Craftsman Cottage','Restored 1920 cottage on a shared lot, quiet street just blocks to countless restaurants and shops on Mississippi St. and Williams corridor. Local health food and grocery store; Cherry Sprout also within walking distance.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25372936/original/c1226131-98f4-4fd5-8852-7922df1a6de9.jpeg',8138210,24,'45.5548','-122.67224',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,365,7,4.57,25372936),(1194,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25380832','Purely Portland  Bungalow. Patio. Near everything.','My sweet bungalow is a gem! My back yard is recovering from a recent construction project, so the ground is brown instead of green, but plants and birds still abound! Front patio seating allows you some privacy with trees and tall plants nestling the seating area while still having a view of the sunset. Both are truly an oasis. See \"The Space\" for details about my home!','Beaumont-Wilshire is the ideal place to stay! Lots of shops and restaurants with well-appointed outdoor seating, and without the crushing summer crowds. There is always parking within a few car lengths of my house. We have old school bars and burger joints, Thai fusion (Bang! Bang!), incredible outdoor seating and live music at the Amalfi’s, Jim & Patti\'s coffee, the ever-delicious Pips made-to-order donuts, sushi, Thai, and more! Beaumont Market is a quick 4 block walk up the strip, where you\'ll find everything you need, including a walk-in beer cooler ;). Hollywood, Alberta, and Mississippi districts are just a 5-10min bike or drive, but if you want to know where the locals go to avoid the crowds, I\'ll be happy to share! Walking this neighborhood, the shop-owners will greet you warmly and help you find whatever you need. You will experience the uniqueness of a very Portland neighborhood while feeling very much at home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25380832/original/105cd53b-e9e3-4343-9acf-f128493f1d1b.jpeg',7727691,46,'45.55073','-122.61516',2,1,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,49,4.92,25380832),(1195,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25406167','Charming Sellwood Getaway with Hot Tub','Charming Sellwood getaway, walking distance to restaurants, coffee shops, bars, groceries, antique stores, yoga, parks and public transportation. 1 BR, 1 BA with hardwood floors and full kitchen. Large yard with hot tub,  picnic table, and gas grill. Netflix, HULU, coffee and towels provided.','We love our neighborhood! We\'d be happy to give you recommendations on places to go when you\'re here. The following are some of our favorites, all within a few blocks/Moreland:<br />PDX Sliders<br />Holler (fried chicken, American food and arcade)<br />Oaks Bottom Public House (Lompoc Brewing)<br />Fetch Coffee; Awake Coffee; Starbucks, and more<br />Twisted (patisserie)<br />Nectar Frozen Yogurt<br />Kay\'s Bar<br />Saburos Sushi House<br />Limelight Restaurant & Bar<br />Classic Thai<br />Bible Club PDX (1920\'s themed Speakeasy with outdoor patio and live music)<br />Stars Antique Mall<br /><br />7 minute walk to Sellwood:<br />Jade restaurant<br />Reverand\'s BBQ<br />Thailana Thai Food<br />Bottle Shop (beer wine and food)<br />Blue Kangaroo<br />Many shops too!!!<br /><br />Other great places nearby:<br />Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge<br />Sellwood Park<br />Sellwood Riverfront Park (On the Willamette River)<br />West Moreland Park<br />Eastmoreland Golf Course<br />Crystal Springs Rh','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7cbeb5a9-ca25-4245-b0f0-f1ed4a4c3542.jpg',16996867,20,'45.47385','-122.65078',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,110.00,2,30,163,4.87,25406167),(1196,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25430968','Private Room, Bath & Entry in Northwest Portland','Have a peaceful and cozy stay at this Northwest Portland neighborhood location.  Within blocks of 23rd Ave shops and restaurants, and the Good Sam hospital.  Location offers many transportation options, free street parking and recreation. Located across from the street from Wallace Park, and a within a mile from various entrances of Forest Park.','In walking distance to many convenient shops, restaurants, and recreation!<br /><br />2 Block Radius<br />•Wallace Park (including Dog Park and Chapman School)<br />•Thurman St Restaurants and Cafes<br />•Post Office<br /><br />4 Block Radius<br />•Retail and Restaurants of 23rd Ave<br />•Multiple Coffee Shops & Bakeries<br />•New Seasons Market (Grocery)<br />•Bus and Streetcar Stops<br />•Legacy Good Samaritan Hospital/Medical Center<br /><br />6 Block Radius <br />•Pearl District<br />•Forest Park (for hiking and other recreation)<br /><br />Simple access to:<br />•Free neighborhood parking <br />•Freeway <br />•Max Train Station (30 walk) <br />•Pearl District, Downtown, Providence Park (30 walk) <br />•NW Hills for cycling','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-25430968/original/36a8b6f1-fc80-416d-af96-d462a016a8a5.jpg',191982844,27,'45.53527','-122.70282',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,82.00,1,1125,212,4.91,25430968),(1197,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25433422','Belmont District Garden Retreat','Winemaker\'s home with backyard garden retreat in the heart of hip inner SE Portland\'s Belmont District. Walk to nearby bars, coffee shops and restaurants or relax in the backyard garden with outdoor fireplace, grill and dining area. A ten minute drive to downtown and easily accessible by public transportation. Onsite parking space.','Sunnyside/Belmont is in the heart of inner, close in southeast Portland. Everything you could want as far as food, beer and wine is within walking distance along with Laurelhurst park - one of Portland\'s most beautiful city parks that has paths, tennis courts, a pond with ducks, a children\'s area, soccer field, basketball hoops and grand trees.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8f9af191-4c4a-474d-b5ed-b834ef24da05.jpg',50525845,16,'45.51787','-122.63086',1,4,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,7,28,17,4.88,25433422),(1198,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25443778','Westmoreland Retreat','This large bungalow is located in the heart of Westmoreland; it\'s a perfect family retreat. Spend your evening in our shaded, fully fenced, back yard while enjoying dinner off the barbecue.  If traveling with little ones, our home is set with toys, games, and books. Primary has king bed with on-suite bath. Twin rooms share a bath with claw foot tub. Double room is on 1st floor and uses the main bath. We are a short walk to Westmoreland Park, shops, restaurants, grocery store, bus and MAX line.','Westmoreland is a wonderful family friendly, highly walkable neighborhood. At our home you are steps away from weekly farmers market, shops, resturants, food carts, MAX line, busses, the Moreland movie theater, QFC and New Seasons grocery stores, Westmoreland and Sellwood parks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b1d2bc62-122b-45a6-90fe-8bae46e3bdfe.jpg',35257956,20,'45.47323','-122.64689',1,7,3.00,4.00,5.00,115.00,30,120,54,4.87,25443778),(1199,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25455464','Princeton House - Modern, private and comfortable','Enjoy this apartment with private entrance in our modern home built in 2018, decorated in a minimal style with a professional and contemporary design.<br />This home is a perfect PDX getaway for those wishing to be close to all  that Portland offers yet enjoy peace and quiet after a day exploring the city.  Fifteen minutes to downtown by car, walking distance to University of Portland and less than two miles from two funky Portland neighborhoods you won’t run out of things to do during your stay.','The house is on a quiet street in North Portland, or NoPo as locals call it. It is walking distance to the University of Portland, 15 minute drive to downtown and easy access to and from the airport.  We are near the bluff overlooking the Willamette River and the City. If you are a runner or biker, you won\'t be alone running/biking along Willamette Boulevard while taking in the views. Walk to our local coffee shop, bar and bottle/growler shop, or take a short drive, leisurely stroll or hop on Portland\'s shared electric scooters to find food cart pods, breweries, restaurants and more nearby. <br /><br />Located in University Park, you’re smack dab in the middle of two great historic neighborhoods: St. Johns to the west (about 2 miles away) and Kenton to the east (2.5 miles away) St. John’s was once a separate town and and is now home to funky boutiques, cafes, a natural grocer, two independent movie theaters, and a food cart pod with fire pit, beer garden and often local musicians. <br ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dab7b3c9-8080-4b39-8c21-8f34d2c4024e.jpg',192136110,57,'45.57737','-122.72199',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,101.00,30,30,271,4.89,25455464),(1200,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25539936','Portland Vintage Charm','This quiet charming vintage apartment comes fully furnished with lots of natural light & privacy.  Perfect for business professionals, traveling medical professionals, & guest professors with a secretary\'s desk, printer and Wifi.  Close to public transportation & Convention Center. The neighborhood is beautiful and perfect for leisurely strolls with intermittent stops to smell the roses. This rental has a 30 day minimum  stay up to 85 nights.','This residential neighborhood is quiet, 3 blocks to the grocery store, post office, restaurants and bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f91fd4ff-d8f1-444f-b43f-387cf6f27eb4.jpg',5337178,7,'45.53814','-122.65432',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,45.00,30,85,6,4.83,25539936),(1201,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25539996','Hideaway Suite, Heart of Inner SE','*No AC* Basement-level ADU stays very cool throughout summer. <br />This is a private ADU on the remodeled lower level of this Ladd\'s Addition bungalow. You\'ll have exclusive use of its kitchen, bathroom, living area (& a couch that converts to futon), a desk, and bedroom with a queen bed & walk-in closet. The living area provides space to relax after your adventures around town, with a cozy dining nook and seating for two. Your exclusive use of a washer & dryer are available in the laundry room.','This space is walkable to Restaurant Row and is smack between the happening \'hoods of Hawthorne and Division. It\'s also easy to navigate to downtown Portland, NE neighborhoods (Alberta Arts District, Kerns, and more) and Mt. Tabor via bus or bicycle.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3ad27bd0-222d-456b-be28-a9c33515e127.jpg',844971,25,'45.50734','-122.64452',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,138.00,1,28,137,4.96,25539996),(1202,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25546113','#StayinMyDistrict Sellwood Private Garden Casita','Stay in My District Sellwood! Experience a vibrant SE Portland neighborhood and live like a local! Known for it’s “walkability” and “friendly neighborhood feel”! Private Garden Casita located in the heart of Sellwood! Walk (3 blocks) to local hotspots, nightlife, dining, coffee, & boutique shops,  from your beautifully appointed Queen Studio Suite. Relax and enjoy a glass of wine or cup of coffee in the private garden oasis. Detached studio suite with private entrance to both yard and studio.','The Sellwood District is a popular Southeast Portland neighborhood. Historic Sellwood-Moreland boasts an array of shops, vintage vendors and restaurants, as well as a rambling wildlife refuge — all just minutes from downtown.  Sellwood is a popular destination neighborhood located in the City of Portland, situated on the east bank of the Willamette River near the southern tip of Ross Island. The house is located in the heart of everything and one could easily get by without a car and find tons to do within walking distance.<br /><br />The neighborhood offers specialty retail, antiques, grocery and hardware stores, banks, dry cleaners as well as tons of restaurants and a seasonal farmers market are concentrated in two historic commercial districts. <br /><br />Approximately two miles in length and a mile wide, the teardrop-shaped area is rich in natural and recreational amenities. This includes four public parks,Westmoreland, Sellwood, Sellwood Riverfront and Johnson Creek, hiking paths','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-25546113/original/3fe93277-fb52-47a8-92f1-51c9a76dd359.jpeg',3142393,20,'45.470665','-122.652672',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,51.00,1,28,317,4.90,25546113),(1203,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25585870','Charming 2BR in the Heart of NE Portland','Location, Location, Location! NE Portland is one of the most coveted areas of this beautiful city and my apartment is right in the heart of it all. Within blocks you can be at the Historic N Mississippi Ave, N Williams Ave, NE Alberta St (Alberta Arts District), and MLK! Restaurants and bars aplenty. Some notable include Por Que No, Tasty n Sons, Ned Ludd, Ecliptic Brewing, Life of Pie, Box Social, and so many more are all within walking distance of my apartment.','This apartment is located smack dab in the center of NE Portland. Within blocks you can be at any of the sought after shopping districts in the city such as the Alberta Arts District, Mississippi Ave, MLK, and Williams Ave. Hip and Trendy restaurants, bars, cafes, and food carts are all within steps of this apartment boasting a Walk Score of 92!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25585870/original/c13b1fe7-320b-4518-920c-73b20d72808f.jpeg',121226154,14,'45.55155','-122.66217',1,6,1.00,2.00,3.00,78.00,30,1125,498,4.81,25585870),(1204,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25593437','Bohemian Bungalow in the heart of SE','This open and bright home is the perfect way to unwind/recharge and enjoy the funky city of Portland like a local. It\'s conveniently located two blocks from SE 50th and Division St. There\'s no need for a car, some of Portland\'s best cafe\'s and eateries are just around the corner. If you are looking to venture a little further, the Hawthorne strip and Mt. Tabor Park are both less than a mile away. For those coming from the airport, the Bungalow is about a 20-min drive, and downtown is 15 min away','A safe interurban neighborhood with all of the best things Portland has to offer. World-class restaurants and food carts, popular bars, breweries, boutique shops, and city parks. If you can\'t find what you fancy nearby, chances are the thing you are looking for is less than a 15 min drive.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/53e2bd7c-9f20-470c-9a55-3528b6183b81.jpg',10375423,8,'45.50195','-122.61327',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,188,4.88,25593437),(1205,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25623999','Alberta Arts - Private, Full Kitchen, Fireplace','Central location, great for longer stays, up to 29 nights.<br /><br />Studio-style 1bed/1bath with gas fireplace, full kitchen,  2-headed shower. <br />Queen sized bed.   Fold out sofa.<br />Gas stove, dishwasher.   Washer/dryer.<br />WiFi.   TV with Roku to access your Netflix, AmazonPrime, etc.<br />ADA toilet, 32 - 36\" doors, and only a couple low steps.<br /><br />Easy access to Oregon Convention Center.   On TriMet #6 bus line.<br /><br />Please Note - this is a basement apartment with 6\'8\" ceilings.  Some areas soffited at approx 6\'2\".','Close-in NE Portland.   <br />Quick walk to restaurants & shops in Portland\'s Alberta Arts district.<br />Less than a mile from Mississippi & Williams Avenue areas and a two mile straight shot down to the Oregon Convention Center.<br />2 blocks from grocery.<br /><br />Portland is full of delicious food & drink, you can’t go wrong, no matter what you choose. <br />Here are some of my favorites, with distance from unit, in no particular order:<br />- Petite Provence.  ¾ mile.  1824 NE Alberta.  <br />Breakfast/lunch/dinner, bakery.  The most delicious croissants I’ve ever had, served with raspberry jam.   Love the corned beef hash for breakfast, and the small-plate selection for dinner.<br />- J&M Cafe.  2.5 miles.  537 SE Ash St.    <br />Breakfast/lunch.   Eclectic spins on scrambles and other breakfast standards.<br />- Grain & Gristle.   ¾ mile.  1473 NE Prescott.   <br />Dinner & drinks.   My favorite item is the  “Two-fer” .. 2 beers, and shareable entree with meat & veg.<br />- P','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-25623999-unapproved/original/7f1fe1a3-ade7-449f-8a9d-816512e7b7d9.JPEG',32534040,14,'45.5599','-122.66',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,78.00,2,29,144,4.96,25623999),(1206,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25630778','Spacious & Hip 1BR with All Access to NE Portland','Newly remodeled and spacious one bedroom apartment located within walking distance of NE Williams, Alberta Arts District, MLK street, and the Historic N Mississippi Ave - boasting a Walk Score of 92. NE Portland is the hippest area to be this summer and my apartment is right in the heart of it all. Enjoy fully stocked amenities, large kitchen, king bed, sleeper sofa, and walk-through closet. Includes blazing fast internet with access to 400 mbps speed.','Enjoy prime location with all access to NE Portland. Within blocks you can walk to Alberta Arts District, MLK street, Historic N Mississippi Ave, and N Williams Ave. Walk to the Nike Factory Store and easily pick up a Nike city bike to enjoy all the restaurants, cafes, bars, and food carts NE Portland has to offer. Oh and did we mention a Walk Score of 92?','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25630778/original/d4807838-05fd-467b-92be-09c84bfd4e53.jpeg',25328937,14,'45.55247','-122.65917',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,30,1125,426,4.81,25630778),(1207,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25670665','Bright Studio Apartment - Food Carts & Local Shops','My apartment building is in the vibrant heart of the eclectic Hawthorne District, walking distance to Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brew-pubs, distilleries, and artisanal shops. All necessary services, from banks to massage therapists, are nearby. Only a mile from downtown, you can easily access the city via bike, walking, or frequent bus service. The interiors feature a sleek, soothing European design with high grade surfaces and finishes for your comfort and style.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District puts you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors, with no chain restaurants in sight! Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, get messy with wings right around the corner at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or opt for a fancy night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />Portland isn\'t just for foodies; the vibrant indie spirit of Hawthorne is alive with plenty of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques to explore. Catch a movie at the Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews. If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of recreation, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park atop a dormant volcano vent, where you’ll find miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25670665/original/0f31aa8f-063d-49f0-976b-de32d6467cb2.jpeg',193265498,25,'45.51208','-122.64534',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,67.00,1,1125,627,4.85,25670665),(1208,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25683545','Fern Cabin','The Fern Cabin has everything to enjoy your Portland stay. There\'s a private bedroom, living space w/ (small) sleeper sofa/kitchen/table. Full bath & jetted tub. WiFi and cable. Heating/air conditioning keeps you comfortable all seasons. Fully equipped kitchen. Private patio. Cozy lodging for 4. Located in SE Portland between Hawthorne & Division close to Mt Tabor park. Shops, cafes, food carts & restaurants abound. walk to everything. $20 pet fee per night. Cannabis friendly, outside only.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1c8e65ce-8b98-4efe-ae36-47fbbbd7f479.jpg',115974453,8,'45.50751','-122.61451',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,81.00,1,1125,404,4.95,25683545),(1209,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25779089','Clean, Convenient & Comfortable - close to river','Clean, Convenient & Comfortable - Come enjoy a relaxing and stress free stay just blocks from the Willamette River and close to everything you want to do in and around Portland.<br /><br />Enjoy a bike ride, run, paddle-board or simple stroll down the waterfront path just 2 blocks from your door. Sellwood, Oaks Park, South Waterfront and downtown can all be accessed easily with or without a car (5 minutes w/car). Come enjoy all that PDX and John\'s Landing has to offer!','In John\'s Landing you are surrounded by anything you want to do. Water is 2 blocks away, Marquam Trail head 3 blocks, Willamette Park is 5 blocks and some of Portland\'s most iconic eateries, bars and coffee shops are just minutes away walking, riding or driving.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/531d06c0-797f-4c3f-9ef6-232b22a6bf22.jpg',1770572,22,'45.47964','-122.676',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,91.00,2,730,275,4.92,25779089),(1210,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25784996','Family Home + Park + Yurt + Close to heart of PDX!','Welcome to our charming family home nestled in the tranquil Southwest Portland neighborhood. This cozy home is ideal for families, especially those with boys, as well as couples seeking a peaceful getaway.<br /><br />Situated just across the street from a beautiful park, our home offers the perfect balance of suburban serenity and convenient access to downtown, which is only a 10-minute drive away.<br /><br />Inside, you\'ll find plenty of entertainment options to keep everyone happy!','We live in a quiet residential neighborhood that is extraordinarily family friendly. Great for walking and riding bikes. You are within walking distance of a few local favorites - Laughing Planet and Sunny’s Frozen Yogurt.  There is also a wonderful community center and local coffee shops nearby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjU3ODQ5OTY%3D/original/399dedd6-f76c-400e-9339-f5bf5f11717e.jpeg',19936260,17,'45.48049','-122.73066',1,7,2.50,2.00,3.00,222.00,2,1125,12,4.75,25784996),(1211,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25813668','Perfect Hawthorne 2BR - Food Carts & Vintage Shops','My apartment building is located in the heart of the heart of the eclectic Hawthorne District, walking distance to some of Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brew-pubs, distilleries, craftspeople, and all services from banks to massage therapists, and just over a mile from downtown via bike, walking, or frequent bus service. Interiors have been designed to create a sleek, soothing European feel, and incorporate the highest-grade surfaces and finishes.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District puts you within walking distance to a wide variety of top-notch local flavors (no chain restaurants here!) Make new friends over some vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, get messy with some wings right around the corner at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or opt for a fancy night out at Castagna - all within a 1.5 mile stretch. Portland isn\'t just for foodies. There’s vibrant indie spirit in Hawthorne, with lots of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques to explore here in hipster heaven. Or, catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews. If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of recreation, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park on top of a dormant volcano vent, where you’ll find miles of hiking trails and incredible pano','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25813668/original/5e150633-b0cf-43e9-8db1-d18028464ad1.jpeg',193973403,25,'45.51208','-122.64588',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,88.00,1,1125,572,4.88,25813668),(1212,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25828740','Casa Dolce Casa / Home Sweet Home in Alberta Arts','Welcome to my charming detached guest house, filled with touches inspired by my home country, Italy. Experience the quaint charm of a tiny house with the comfort and openness of a traditional home.<br />Stroll to Alberta Arts District\'s restaurants, bars, breweries, food cart pods, and unique local shops. Explore the Oregon Coast, local hikes, and wineries. <br />Public transport is nearby for city exploration, and the airport is just a 12-minute drive away.','We live in the heart of the Alberta Arts District, and the house is in a peaceful street walking distance to... everything! From May to September on the Last Thursday of the month, Alberta Street is closed to the vehicle traffic. Musicians and performers line the street, galleries hold their monthly openings and the street is filled with food vendors, live music, and kids’ activities.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/93317f82-2e15-4ba4-a040-6f6c151f74bd.jpg',176106,1,'45.56086','-122.64262',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,106.00,2,1125,222,4.98,25828740),(1213,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25839024','Modern Hawthorne Guesthouse - Close to Everything','A bright, stylish and modern home awaits you in the heart of Portland\'s Hawthorne District. Located only a few minutes from downtown but you may find yourself not wanting to leave the neighborhood. An easy stroll will take you to the Hawthorne, Division, and Belmont restaurant/shopping areas.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-25839024/original/1d472ca9-13c5-4065-af7c-5a8ebe3b9996.jpg',23432303,8,'45.51039','-122.62796',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,128.00,2,28,360,4.99,25839024),(1214,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25892907','Light and bright condo with free parking','Light and bright high rise condo in the heart of downtown.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c94929a4-03d6-4d77-8734-e946e8bf025e.jpg',32875749,44,'45.51096','-122.67856',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,30,1125,22,5.00,25892907),(1215,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25894908','Sweet Sellwood Studio','Super hosts!  Perfect Sellwood location. Near great restaurants, shops,  groceries & nature. Studio apartment has a modern funky feel,  lots of amenities, located in the basement of our classic 1905 bungalow.  Babies and older kids welcome. People love the comfort and decor!<br />Private entrance,  Washer and Dryer, queen size bed, queen sofa bed, writing table, fully equipped kitchenette for cooking,  great showerhead, marmoleum flooring. Well lit for night entry. Small patio in shared back yard.','Please inquire if you\'d like to book longer than availability states. Sellwood is a desirable walking neighborhood about 15 minutes from downtown, close to restaurants and shopping, bike trail, bird refuge and river!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6c44505c-eae7-4303-a399-81224196af63.jpg',9649928,20,'45.469799','-122.653801',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,130.00,2,1125,92,4.99,25894908),(1216,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25912642','Montavilla manor','Charming, pet friendly 2 bedroom, 1 bath in hip Montavilla neighborhood. <br /> Great restaurants, bars, breweries, coffee and movie theater just a 3 minute walk away.  Full use of space. Nice deck with views of Mt. Hood.  Large back yard with two fire pits, one gas and one wood. Use of grill for summer grillin\'. Easy access to downtown, 3 to 5 minute walk to two major bus lines that run late (one is 24 / 7).  Close to beautiful Mt. Tabor Park.  Please note I live in this property when not rented.','Hip Montavilla neighborhood close to beautiful Mt. Tabor Park, breweries, coffee, restaurants, bars, movie theater and more!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4d189f6a-722f-4582-a030-20d40c1f61e2.jpg',138761774,15,'45.51852','-122.58669',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,79.00,3,180,78,4.83,25912642),(1217,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25920079','Ne PDX modern ADU','Cozy & Beautiful  Modern daylight basement. Street Parking Available in front of the house  Non Smoking Home. The whole apartment unit with a Private entry. Has two Bed room. Full kitchen. one full bathroom and living room with a pull out bed .','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7cfe366a-aea6-41f5-a65c-d65e09424009.jpg',156967556,40,'45.5492','-122.54259',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,89.00,1,10,242,4.94,25920079),(1218,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25935157','The Bridgetown, safe escape, steps from NW 23rd Av','This classic remodeled home in the Alphabet district, just a block from the popular NW 23rd Ave is perfect for foodies, shoppers, & people watchers. Within the tree-lined, safe & comfortable neighborhood, you will find the Portland experience you are looking for. The entire city can be easily accessed with just a short walk, uber ride or via the streetcar/Max system.  Our home is centrally located in the heart of NW Portland, providing you with easy access to all of Portland\'s many attractions.','This rental property is located less than a block from the popular NW 23rd Ave and less than 3 block from NW 21st Ave, both of which are known for their boutique shops, endless retaurants, bars and coffee houses. You will be blocks from the up and coming Slabtown neighborhood and the high-end Pearl district. \"The Pearl\" is known for its Brewery blocks, art galleries, Powells bookstore and shops. Many of the top Portland attractions are in NW Portland - Forrest Park, Pttock Mansion, Powells Bookstore, Salt and Straw Ice Cream, Breweries and more. ***The property is not close to the goings-on near the federal building.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-25935157/original/66c26cd8-5cee-413a-b261-93cff1aa08d2.jpeg',54782133,27,'45.52839','-122.69951',1,8,2.00,4.00,5.00,110.00,30,365,229,4.95,25935157),(1219,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25940119','Just Call It Home *NE PDX Garden Retreat*','Relax in our spacious daylight basement guest suite, located just a few blocks from the hottest spots Portland has to offer! Enjoy our prime NE Portland location near delicious eateries and unique shopping.  Perfect for solo travelers, couples, friends, or family visiting the area for business or pleasure!<br /><br />Whole Foods, a bank and UPS Store are four blocks away.  Restaurants and parks are in every direction. Our quiet street is a biking and walking paradise.<br /><br />Our house is powered by the sun!','Our home is located on a quiet, residential street, but is mere minutes from many of the most entrancing neighborhoods in Portland. You can walk to Alberta, Killingsworth, Williams, or Fremont. You can also grab a Biketown bike rental and ride to Mississippi, Broadway, St. Johns, or even downtown! You could stop every few blocks and have a delicious coffee, donut, cheeseburger, or taco! :)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/36285f34-fa41-44a9-b29e-e550f46c37be.jpg',194980036,6,'45.55353','-122.65292',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,87.00,2,11,144,4.92,25940119),(1220,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25940445','Fabulous Vintage Craftsman, Best Location in PDX!','Our beautiful Craftsman Cottage in the center of Portland\'s most prime location is the perfect launchpad for any and all Portland vacations, business trips, & family reunions!<br /><br />The house has loads of thoughtful touches and is full of \'Portland Personality\' and the Mississippi/Williams corridor is home to countless shops, restaurants, and bars that could keep visitors busy for weeks!','This is a wonderful place to explore for artists and creative types looking to stay right where the action is! Just a few minutes from the max light rail and bus stops as well as walking distance to a plethora of other awesome neighborhoods, you really shouldn’t look any further. This is the best spot in town!<br /><br />Here are some suggestions for things to do in the Mississippi/Williams Neighborhood and a bit further a far :<br /><br />FOOD & DRINK - the following are all in walking distance (½ mi or much less)<br /><br />Most everything on Mississippi & Williams will more than satisfy if not blow you away. Here are some of our favorites:<br /><br />Grand Central Bakery (We have to start with this one because it’s so good and about a block from the house. Perfect for a quick morning and coffee and pastries. Try their soda bread if you an in town around St. Patrick’s Day. Strangely though, their neighbor SPIN, the cutest laundromat you’ve ever been in, has some of the best coffee in','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2de82e6d-818d-498e-8f2d-37599c763167.jpg',194952414,9,'45.54731','-122.67274',1,10,2.00,5.00,7.00,356.00,2,21,100,4.96,25940445),(1221,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25941316','Luxurious 3 Bed Condo Near Everything','Relax in a two-story condo perched above the street. Watch from your covered deck as hummingbirds flit through 100 year old trees, and hipsters pass by below. Sleep soundly in new beds and block out the light with heavy curtains.<br /><br />Then dream of Blue Star doughnuts. Fantasize over Waffle Window fried chicken & waffles. Crave Tove cold-brew. Pine over fluffy Hazel Cafe biscuit sammiches. Walk out the front door of your 2,000 square foot home onto famous Hawthorne Blvd, your city-sized food court!','This is it. One of the 5 most popular listings on AirB&B in Portland. You\'re in the absolute beating heart of the city, surrounded by the best shops and restaurants available. Most guests don\'t bring a car because you could spend a week walking and not get everywhere interesting near this house!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/faf8a8f3-190a-4ade-9447-723f0206d8e7.jpg',173625187,32,'45.51323','-122.63875',1,10,2.00,3.00,4.00,370.00,2,364,128,4.93,25941316),(1222,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25944358','LAURELHURST CHARMER, FAM-FRIENDLY|DEEP CLEAN!!','HISTORIC LAURELHURST!!<br />3 BLKS-MAX &TRADER JOE\'S<br />When you arrive, you will greeted with a quiet atmosphere of privacy and relaxation. On the first floor of our three story house, brand new, two-bedroom apartment, with private entrance and patio.  <br /><br />Ensuring your comfort, ALL APARTMENT SURFACES ARE DISINFECTED. The interior is replete with high end finishes of stainless steel appliances, granite counters, luxe towels, and soft, comfortable bedding wrapped up in classic modern interior.','Lisa and Frank’s house is located in the neighborhood of Laurelhurst in N.E. Portland, Oregon in the United States. Laurelhurst is one of the oldest neighborhoods in Portland. It is a uniquely designed neighborhood centered around 26 acre Laurelhurst park. It’s streets are punctuated with hundred year old elm trees. Many of the homes in this neighborhood were built in the early 1900’s. Our was built in 1913 and is a craftsman style bungalow. This neighborhood, with it’s beautiful streets is made for walking and taking in nature within an urban setting. It is a jewel in the middle of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bf237c1a-1417-473c-bb66-65cf7816f93d.jpg',195007597,23,'45.53013','-122.62391',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,97.00,1,180,144,4.92,25944358),(1223,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25947060','New Modern Buckman Charmer','New studio in the heart of Portland! Our new basement studio features a kitchenette, bathroom, sofa bed and queen size bed, with a separate entrance on the side of the house. We also include cable TV and WiFi with your visit. We are located across the street from a wonderful park with ample street parking. We are 1.5 miles from downtown and within walking distance to 100s of restaurants, bars and breweries in desirable inner southeast Portland (Hawthorne/Buckman Neighborhood).','Portland\'s oldest and popular eastside neighborhood with plenty within walking distance - multiple coffee shops, brunch spots, food trucks, breweries, and fine dining. We share some of our favorite places in the onsite guest book.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/de566958-3351-4d08-8156-b35b8795037d.jpg',4506845,32,'45.51385','-122.64727',1,4,1.00,1.00,4.00,95.00,1,1125,112,4.82,25947060),(1224,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/25986436','PDX private & spacious  2 bd room unit, with (EV)','Brand new, Modern, Daylight Basement. Privet entry. Privet parking space with Electric Vehicle charger station.   Fully equipped and staged unit.  Quiet & friendly neighborhood. located in a dead end street. Non smoking home.','Very friendly and quiet neighborhood in dead end street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/67975725-127b-4cc5-b50d-4b82e5157a96.jpg',156967556,35,'45.54181','-122.55502',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,98.00,14,1125,11,4.91,25986436),(1225,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26041396','Ladd\'s Addition Apartment in SE Portland','My Ladd\'s Addition apartment is well-positioned to allow you to explore Portland. Located in a quiet neighborhood halfway between the bustling streets of Hawthorne and Division; from here, you can easily walk to coffee shops, restaurants, bars, grocery stores, and a movie theater. Public transportation is readily available, as well as car, bike, and scooter shares. In just a few minutes, you can be downtown, the Moda center, the convention center, OMSI, or the waterfront esplanade.','The Ladd\'s Addition neighborhood is unique because of the unusual angled layout of the streets and the five public gardens throughout the neighborhood.  Each quadrant has its own rose garden.  In the center, the rhododendron garden often becomes an informal community gathering spot.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/26455180-9bf9-440a-85cd-d9d6ec811757.jpg',13080438,25,'45.50856','-122.64609',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,73.00,5,1125,148,4.99,26041396),(1226,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26062730','Retro Modern 1-Bedroom w/ 90 WalkScore','Located in the vibrant Hawthorne District, our apartment is within walking distance of Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brewpubs, and distilleries. other services, such as banks and massage therapists, are also nearby.  Around a mile from downtown, you can easily use bikes, public bus services, or walk to explore the city. Our sleek, European-style interiors feature high-grade surfaces and finishes, offering comfort and elegance in one of Portland\'s most dynamic neighborhoods.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors, with no chain restaurants in sight! Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, indulge in delicious wings right around the corner at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or enjoy a fancy night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />Portland isn\'t just for foodies. Hawthorne boasts a vibrant indie spirit, with numerous made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques to explore in this hipster haven. Catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue, serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping isn’t your idea of fun, head up to Mt. Tabor, a 196-acre city park atop a dormant volcano vent. Here, you\'ll find miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-26062730/original/0a680862-4807-4eb1-b8f3-ae39c127baee.jpeg',187734201,25,'45.51166','-122.64699',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,67.00,2,1125,471,4.90,26062730),(1227,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26101342','*Dec Deals* Bright & Cozy U of P Studio, Fast WiFi','Welcome to Modern Studio Oasis!<br /><br />Walk to University of Portland! Cozy 500 sqft apartment in University Park. Walk to bars, restaurants & transit.<br /><br />Full kitchen w/gas range, free laundry, and private entrance. Free street parking & no chore list!<br /><br />Tri-Met bus lines: 35 & 44<br /><br />* Downtown Portland: 7 mi<br />* Portland Airport: 6 mi<br />* Adidas offices: 3 mi<br />* Daimler/Freightliner offices: 4 mi<br />* Neighborhoods: St. Johns (1.5 mi), Kenton (2 mi), <br />* Mississippi (3 mi), Alberta Arts (4 mi)<br /><br />All are welcome!','THE NEIGHBORHOOD<br /><br />Our Airbnb in North Portland\'s University Park is a 5-minute drive to the Adidas and Daimler headquarters. Situated in a quiet section of the vibrant University Park neighborhood of North Portland or the 5th Quadrant as locals call it. <br /><br />Head across the street to our food cart pods, pizza shops, beer, and bottle shops, along with other bars and restaurants. <br /><br />Easily drive, take transit, or ride share to other parts of Portland.<br /><br />* <1 mile from New Seasons grocery store<br />* 1.4 miles to Fred Meyer store (groceries and more)<br />* 0.7 miles to Starbucks<br /><br />This is an excellent hub for outdoor recreation: If you are a runner, skateboarder, or biker, step out the front door and head South to the bluff just off Willamette Boulevard. It overlooks the Willamette River and offers impressive views of the City. <br /><br />* 5 miles away from hiking in Forest Park: the largest urban forested park in the United States.<br />* 5','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-26101342/original/1af77394-cc6e-4ed5-80cf-6c8aab505d7a.jpeg',76347703,57,'45.58024390644905','-122.7221510380317',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,78.00,1,28,278,4.81,26101342),(1228,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26131191','Classic Craftsman - King Beds - Steps to Hawthorne','This massive, classic Craftsman home-filled with better-than-hotel-quality king-sized beds--is located just steps from the famous Hawthorne District!  This original Craftsman has been professionally designed for the most particular of travelers, tucked away on a quiet block but right off one of Portland\'s most sought-after nightlife, dining & shopping districts.  Gather around the handcrafted wood dining table with friends, or unwind on the private back patio after checking out the neighborhood!','Voted one of the best neighborhoods in Portland by Sunset Magazine, the Richmond neighborhood does not disappoint. Located between the bustling streets of Hawthorne and Division, this neighborhood is chock full of many of Portland\'s best restaurants, bars and shops while still maintaining the eclectic \"Keep Portland Weird\" aesthetic that it\'s become famous for.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/39b0f862-44e3-4144-aff5-88eb134b73d1.jpg',114569265,8,'45.50992965698242','-122.6350326538086',1,10,3.00,5.00,6.00,203.00,2,1124,273,4.81,26131191),(1229,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26135619','Grant Park Haven in NE Portland','Welcome to Grant Park Haven, your home away from home.  Located in the beautiful Grant Park/Hollywood neighborhood of NE Portland, it offers easy access to downtown, public transportation, restaurants, pubs, shopping, entertainment, parks, a swimming pool, grocery stores, and the freeways. The one bedroom Airbnb is the day-lit, lower unit of a new Craftsman style house built in 2018. With a queen bed and a queen sofabed in the living area, there is space for 4 people total.  Everyone is welcome!','The neighborhood is beautiful, friendly, and quiet.  Many families have lived here for decades and know each other well so there is a strong sense of community.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-26135619/original/cf1ade67-9a4e-4d53-93a4-4b0553c080b7.jpeg',13281214,84,'45.53623','-122.62449',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,100.00,3,1125,179,4.96,26135619),(1230,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26170294','Award-Winning Guest House with Private Entrance','Featured in Dwell Magazine; Winner of “Best Whole House Design” by Oregon Home Magazine, this spacious urban garden retreat has one-bedroom with a luxurious king bed, full bathroom, and fully equipped kitchen. <br /><br />Tucked away in a tranquil urban oasis, the space is filled with natural light and boasts a private garden entrance. Wake up refreshed in the crisp, white bedroom and slide open the rustic barn door for a coffee on the patio of this zen retreat.','The property sits between the trendy Foster-Powell neighborhood and hip Division St in southeast Portland. Food carts, restaurants, shops, and grocery markets are all within walking distance or a short drive and there\'s easy access to public transit.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-26170294/original/c0e0ba66-9a7a-44b1-8e8d-608a542ee808.jpeg',101565574,36,'45.49582','-122.60117',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,126.00,2,28,322,4.99,26170294),(1231,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26171304','House with sauna and large yard','Recently remodeled 1950\'s bungalow. All hardwood flooring, natural light and open concept. The kitchen is fully stocked and great for family meals. Fully fenced backyard, garden with wood burning sauna and bright living space. House is ideal for multiple couples, business trips or a family visiting Portland.  Amazing authentic international foods walking distance from my home, bars, coffee shops, breakfast spots, library and parks.','Foster powell neighborhood is 15-20 minutes from the westside city center and a short walk to restaurants and bars including best dim sum in Portland and the mercado food carts. Within 1.5 miles of Mt. tabor park with dog park, Powell butte walking trails and easy access to freeway for day trips to Hood River or Mt Hood (within an hour).  Essex park with tennis courts and children play area with fountain is .4 miles away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0ff27501-03c0-4310-bef4-25cefd52d054.jpg',73663145,36,'45.49078','-122.58478',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,120.00,5,200,134,4.84,26171304),(1232,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26184695','PDX Central','We love this apartment and we think you will too! It\'s very spacious, fully stocked kitchen, fireplace, 700 square feet!<br /><br />Its bright, contemporary, you\'ll find everything you need and it\'s close to anywhere you\'d like to go in Portland, only 10 min to downtown and airport.<br /><br />Completely private and self contained in a quiet ne Portland neighborhood that\'s close to everything Portland has to offer!<br /><br />A great place to stay if you are sightseeing in Portland  or just for overflow of visiting family.','If you\'re coming to Portland to sightsee and explore Portland and surrounding areas you will love our neighborhood!<br />We are just 5 to 10 minutes from the airport close to bus and Max transportation.<br />And if you want to head east to the Columbia River Gorge Multnomah Falls Hood River the freeway entrance is just blocks away.<br />From downtown Portland the Pearl and Northwest 23rd neighborhoods we are a 10 minute drive.<br />if you want to take a day Excursion to the beautiful Oregon coast we are right by the freeway on-ramp and it\'s about an hour and 15 minute drive.<br />From our neighborhood you can also see both Mount Hood and Mount Saint Helens.<br /><br />And of course since we are a Portland Urban neighborhood there is plenty of shopping, farmers markets and great stores like new seasons and Trader Joe\'s not far away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/183d650b-d47e-44bb-8290-2589534556c3.jpg',190120922,40,'45.54935','-122.54253',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,76.00,2,28,268,4.97,26184695),(1233,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26193945','SW Portland Charming 2 bedroom - Dog Friendly','Welcome to the Holly Park House. This single family home has 2 bedrooms, bonus room  and one  bathroom.  A spacious kitchen is stocked with essentials. There are queen sized beds in the main bedroom and second bedroom and full (double) bed in bonus room. A smart TV with fast internet.  The dining room table seats 4. There is a window a/c unit.  Central heat.<br /><br />We accept dogs at this property. There is a separate pet fee for each dog.','West Portland Park is conveniently located a mile from I-5 and Capitol Highway. There is a bus stop on the end of the street.  Holly Park is located across from the house.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8d5ab727-f661-4ae5-b68f-3f6a1f676915.jpg',196865274,53,'45.44857','-122.72823',1,4,1.00,3.00,3.00,182.00,4,180,17,4.88,26193945),(1234,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26226110','The Going House','The entire top floor of the house is yours! This includes 2 bedrooms & a private living room both closed off by a door at the foot of the stairs.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-26226110/original/74c2db41-a941-4e51-93a2-8b3a32745a1e.jpeg',92131086,21,'45.55574','-122.60148',2,2,1.50,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,365,0,1.00,26226110),(1235,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26231050','Classic Bungalow in Hip North Portland - Long Term','4 Bedroom Long Term Stay Home in North Portland.  Classic Portland Bungalow with modern furniture, memory foam beds, a fully stocked modern kitchen, EV charging, dual remote workstations and a hot tub available for rent through Swimply app. The place is a short walk to Mississippi Ave, Alberta St,  Biketown Bike Share Station, Electric Scooter rentals, free parking and easy access to Trimet transit to explore all of Portland. Message me with questions or to book it.','Here are my suggestions for places to see and delicious food in Portland proper and within a few hours drive. Since Portland is known for Rain (and sometimes Sun), I\'m going to break this out into two categories. Rain and Sun. Also, check the Guidebook for a Map<br /><br />-TO DO- <br />---On a RAINY DAY------------------------------------<br />1. Brewery Tours<br />2. McMenamins Kennedy School<br />3. Shopping <br />4. Shows (Music/Theatre)<br />5. Powells City of Books<br />6. Donuts<br /><br />1. Brewery Tour: There\'s a free brewery tour at Widmer brewery. Fridays at 2:00pm & 3:00pm<br />Saturdays at 12:00pm, 1:00pm, 2:00pm & 3:00pm Sundays at 1:00pm & 2:00pm<br />RESERVATIONS REQUIRED / GROUP SIZES ARE LIMITED Online search to call the Widmer Brewery (Airbnb won\'t let me show the number) ext. 7201. Once your reservation is confirmed, please plan to meet your tour at the Widmer Brothers retail store prior to your tour start time. Close toed shoes are required to participate in our b','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/69205890/2df479dd_original.jpg',307635,24,'45.55796','-122.67216',1,5,1.00,4.00,5.00,176.00,30,365,15,5.00,26231050),(1236,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26272298','Stroll to Restaurants New Laurelhurst Loft','Step straight from the sidewalk into an easily accessible ground floor apartment.  Cedarwood Loft is in the desirable Laurelhurst neighborhood, with trendy shops, restaurants, cafes, a small movie theater, breweries, and parks. <br />East Burnside is one block away and has buses to take you right downtown.<br /> ** Pets are welcome with a pet fee of $50 per week.','Cedarwood Loft is in the desirable Laurelhurst neighborhood, steps away from trendy shops, restaurants, cafes, a small movie theater, breweries, and parks. There\'s easy biking, walking, parking, and public transportation close by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-26272298/original/193eb44e-23ff-42a7-9291-f6cb1292d5df.jpeg',49136460,32,'45.52225','-122.6434',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,31,240,386,4.92,26272298),(1237,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26300261','Woodstock Farmhouse','Modern farmhouse in the heart of Woodstock featuring 1 bedroom, 1 bathroom,  living room, a fully stocked kitchen, AC, and a private deck. This space is a new construction farmhouse with lots of privacy. Enjoy off street parking with a private garden path leading to your front door.  <br />Just a short walk to some of SE Portland\'s hottest spots including Double Mountain Brewing, New Seasons Market, Otto\'s Sausages,  Cloud City Ice Cream, Grand Central Bakery, The Woodstock Farmer\'s Market, and more.','The Woodstock neighborhood is family friendly and is boasting with activity. Take the short walk to access coffee shops, The Woodstock Farmer\'s Market, library, grocery, restaurants, shops, New Seasons Market (with rooftop seating), Cloud City Ice Cream, Grand Central Bakery, Otto\'s Sausages, Double Mountain Brewery, Sushi Shoko, and many other restaurants, shops, and bars.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6d94e14d-7a2f-4c17-b886-bc8bb757d3ae.jpg',62800380,69,'45.47344','-122.61291',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,135.00,1,30,263,4.94,26300261),(1238,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26301500','Deluxe 5★ Guest House ❤️ Close-in Convenience','Enjoy modern amenities and close-in convenience at our Craftsman home in historic Laurelhurst. This spacious retreat is private, easy living for business visitors, pleasure seekers, and family fun. It’s a pleasant stroll to the best restaurants and shops, plus instant access to public transport. Read our stellar reviews and book with confidence. 10 minutes to Downtown; 15 to airport','Ten minutes from Downtown and 15 minutes from the airport is only the beginning: Find yourself a few steps from the famous Olmsted-designed Laurelhurst Park\'s running trails, pond, and playground. <br /><br />Enjoy a short walk through tree-lined streets to 28th & Burnside\'s Restaurant Row, Belmont Street bars and eateries, and the famously infamous Hawthorne Boulevard. <br /><br />Or extend your trek by foot or bike to take in the forest plus city views at our neighborhood volcano — the stunning Mt. Tabor Park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-26301500/original/26847250-03e4-4757-bfd3-671bf4517d6a.jpeg',197760682,23,'45.52374','-122.62231',1,5,1.00,1.00,4.00,111.00,2,730,305,4.99,26301500),(1239,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26396810','Poolhouse of Portland Architectural Gem','Private guest house adjacent to Pietro Belluschi\'s \"Sutor House\", featured in Dec 2017 Dwell Magazine. Pool-house is 750 square feet, and features a master bedroom, full bath, living area with kitchenette, and access to and shared use (With our family) of the swimming pool in summer months (June, July, August). Surrounded by private wooded garden with Japanese plantings and water features. Located in Portland\'s West Hills, just minutes from Downtown.','Located in Portland\'s West Hills, the property sits on a private, 4 acre wooded estate. It is walking distance to the hiking trails of Washington Park, The Arboretum, and the Wildwood Trail, and very near to the Zoo and the Portland Japanese Garden. Downtown Portland is a 10-15 minute drive.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/59e1b2bc-9e0d-4e6a-aa6d-9f6608524c8f.jpg',7488923,62,'45.51627','-122.72766',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,225.00,2,14,91,4.90,26396810),(1240,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26441861','Perfect Portland getaway-Near everything-Patio','My sweet 1942 bungalow is a gem! A gas fireplace to keep you cozy on cool nights... Birds and plants to enjoy in the back yard... Flowers, herbs, and veggies to enjoy from the front patio. A comfy oasis just one block from a street that has lots of shops and restaurants!  <br /><br />Every dollar of the cleaning fee goes to the woman in the neighborhood who cleans the space. <br /><br />See \"The Space\" for more details about my home!','Beaumont-Wilshire is the ideal place to stay! Lots of shops and restaurants with well-appointed outdoor seating, and without the crushing summer crowds. There is always parking within a few car lengths of my house. We have old school bars and burger joints, Thai fusion (Bang! Bang!), incredible outdoor seating and live music at the Amalfi’s, Jim & Patti\'s coffee, the ever-delicious Pips made-to-order donuts, sushi, Thai, and more! Beaumont Market is a quick 4 block walk up the strip, where you\'ll find everything you need, including a walk-in beer cooler ;). Hollywood, Alberta, and Mississippi districts are just a 5-10min drive, but if you want to know where the locals go to avoid the crowds, I\'ll be happy to share! Walking this neighborhood, the shop-owners will greet you warmly and help you find whatever you need. You will experience the uniqueness of a very Portland neighborhood while feeling very much at home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-26441861/original/5f85970d-1822-4c39-a35f-93513e70d9ec.jpeg',7727691,46,'45.55058','-122.61622',2,1,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,35,4.94,26441861),(1241,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26452292','Dogwood Loft -cozy neighborhood, pet friendly','This pet-friendly ground floor apartment is in the heart of Portland\'s Southeast Laurelhurst neighborhood.  It\'s just 5 blocks away from a hub of amazing restaurants and Whole Foods Market. There are cafes, shops, breweries and parks all within walking distance and it\'s just one block off of the famous East Burnside Street.<br />Pet fee is $35 for one night; $50 for 2-7 nights. Higher fee with longer stays.','Plenty of restaurants, shops, cafes, breweries and grocery shopping are all within walking distance!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-26452292/original/5bf60661-1055-4d92-a443-2a50100cd1a9.jpeg',49136460,32,'45.522148','-122.639351',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,1,240,256,4.95,26452292),(1242,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26466422','Liebe Guesthouse - Cozy Home, Convenient Location','Nice and Private Guests\' Suite centrally located in Southeast Portland at a convenient location.<br /><br />_Walk to Foods, Shops, Pubs Public Transits. Short drive to PDX, Downtown<br />_Near OR-213, I-205, US-26,<br />_A Comfort of a home-away-from-home with a cozy living room, 2 bedrooms, a fully equipped kitchen and nice bathroom with washer/dryer.<br />_A perfect corporate rental and a comfortable stay for business travelers or guests needing an extended stay<br />_A nice place for friends, or family get together.','This property is located in a Lents Historic District near Eastport Plaza Shopping Center in an old established neighborhood in SE Portland. In recent years, this area has become a reviving and thriving multicultural community. This home is located close to many amenities that Portland has to offer. It is only a short drive to Downtown Portland and Portland International Airport. It is an excellent hub to many of Portland\'s Must See Neighborhoods, less than a ten-minute drive to many trendy places like Hawthorne District, Division/Clinton District, Montavilla Districts.<br /><br />The location is very accessible as it is near Portland Major Roads, Highways and Interstates. It also has easy access to Portland Suburban Cities East and South of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d7ad5a5d-ca31-4bf9-894e-2c54819f3679.jpg',12523076,72,'45.48613','-122.57694',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,99.00,30,180,13,4.54,26466422),(1243,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26534627','Sanctuary in Portland Long-term House Rental','Nestled in nature, my 1/3 acre property features waterfall, pond, seasonal creek & mature trees, creating a tranquil setting. The lovely cedar wood meditation cottage looks over creek & green space beyond. Located at the border of Portland and Lake Oswego. You can easily walk to Tryon Creek State Park and take a forest bath. New Seasons Market within walking distance as well.','This is an affluent residential neighborhood in SW Portland, borders Lake Oswego. 25 mins to PDX Airport and 12 mins to Downtown. You are right next to Tryon Creek State Park and New Seasons Market. Close to Lewis & Clark College.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/249fbc09-e231-468c-880d-b9aa5980c7ef.jpg',29763138,73,'45.43724','-122.69256',1,2,2.50,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,180,3,5.00,26534627),(1244,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26572629','Professionally Cleaned Modern Alberta Arts Apt','This is a new private apartment located in the Alberta Arts District. Walking distance to restaurants/bars, grocery and shopping. <br /><br />THE SPACE<br />The ground floor apartment has a private entrance. It is furnished with a Queen size memory foam bed, living room with a full size pull out bed, wall mounted flat screen tv with cable and streaming. There is a full size bathroom, walk-in closet, a large kitchenette, washer and dryer, table w/ stools. This place has everything!!','Alberta Arts is one of Portlands great neighborhoods. Outstanding food, drinks and shopping options are a short walk away. There are two large parks close by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/87e31900-8661-4920-adda-71116f642286.jpg',34926669,1,'45.55969','-122.63291',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,80.00,2,28,228,4.92,26572629),(1245,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26608214','Yurt Meadow Retreat - on farm by nature park','Pacific Yurt  nestled privately in farm/forest setting against acres of old growth in the nature park! Minutes from downtown you’ll see panoramic views of the city while watching the wildlife.  Relax under the \"moonroof\" and watch the stars by cricket song.  Unique features incl. raw wood interior, kitchenette, comfy bed  (bed warmers!) + heater, mini fridge,delights of house commons, hammocks. Shower under the trees in the yurts solo Bathhouse compost tiolet. Cozy hideaway all winter.','Powellhurst Gilbert is one of the most diverse neighborhoods in the city. We speak over 50 languages here! Backed by the majestic Powell Butte Nature Park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/41a6e52e-bda0-4f97-adb5-c80e1bc088a4.jpg',421792,78,'45.487993551240564','-122.51722253859043',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,1,12,707,4.92,26608214),(1246,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26642063','Burnside Studio: Explorer’s Oasis Near Everything!','This bright, comfortable, and clean fully-furnished studio apartment is in the best location for exploring downtown Portland. Please inquire about stays longer than 31 nights, we are happy to host guests for up to three months and you can extend your stay as you go so you only pay for one month at a time. The condo is currently available through February 2025.<br />My condo is very near to Powell\'s Books, Crystal Ballroom, the Brewery Blocks, the Pearl district, the Timber\'s Stadium and much more.','So close to everything! <br />Within .25 mile: <br />Walking distance to Powell’s Books (4 blocks), Timber’s stadium (6 blocks), and Crystal Ballroom (1 block). Close to shopping in the Pearl/Alphabet district, drinking at one of Portland’s many breweries, or eating at the best restaurants in the city. Easy on and off-highway access and only a couple blocks away from the MAX or streetcar. Check out our guide for our favorite spots.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2f71c60c-1bae-4766-b3f6-3d399b3b5ce7.jpg',1308879,27,'45.52330748047453','-122.68700595266634',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,100.00,30,120,66,4.91,26642063),(1247,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26705841','Charming and Bright  1920s Cottage in SE Portland','Our 800 sq. ft cottage in the Mt Scott-Arleta neighborhood features a recently remodeled kitchen and bath and new hickory floors. There are two bedrooms; one is set up as an office and does not have a bed. Fully fenced back yard w/ garden. Kitchen has gas range, 2-burner induction cooktop, stainless steel sink, fridge and dishwasher.  Laundry in basement. We are two blocks from the Portland Mercado food carts, Mt-Scott Rec Center, close to the Woodstock, Lents, Fo-Po and Hawthorne neighborhoods.','We are in SE Portland and the downtown area is easily accessible by bus or on surface streets.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2ec5ba95-171b-427a-952c-efb848b379fe.jpg',44119978,65,'45.48414','-122.58766',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,60,2,5.00,26705841),(1248,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26710860','Adorable Suite in Historic Isam White House','Adorable third floor suite in the historic Isam White House. Includes bedroom, kitchenette with microwave, hot water kettle, small fridge and private bathroom with tub/shower. This is one of the last grand mansions downtown that hasn\'t been converted to condos or offices. We are at the shopping and restaurant districts of Northwest 21st and 23rd Avenues. Walkability score of 97!','Northwest Portland, Nob Hill, also known as the Alphabet District offers sophisticated shopping, dining and people-watching. Victorians, Colonial Mansions, boutiques and restaurants line the streets of this neighborhood that\'s ideal for leisurely strolls, while the adjoining Forest Park was made for hikes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-26710860/original/70d5fd5a-1702-443a-a6ff-aaa58de854f5.jpeg',7409866,27,'45.52515','-122.69259',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,67.00,1,1125,312,4.90,26710860),(1249,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26716619','Garden view private room','Southeast Portland dukes it out with Northeast for most livable and likable neighborhoods.  South Tabor/FoPo is friendly and loaded with bars, cafes and the eastside\'s best park: Mount Tabor.  The bus line means easy access to downtown, if that\'s where you\'re headed. <br /><br />Our 1940\'s home is clean, and decorated with mid-century furniture. Your room is comfortable, with a queen sized bed, and close to the bathroom on the main level. <br /><br />Cold beer and/or morning coffee will greet you upon request!','Southeast Portland has it all. And if you can\'t find it here...grab an Uber, Lyft, or bus to the city center. This area is bike central, so that\'s an option as well! Ask about our free bike loaners!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f3a0df6b-42f4-4be2-96bf-a1016a88a7c5.jpg',2917007,37,'45.49889','-122.60515',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,30,30,26,5.00,26716619),(1250,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26717394','Dream Cottage! Springwater Bike/Walking Path!','Explore, recharge, dream in your own quiet & inspiring country-in-the-city cottage. Sellwood is a great riverside neighborhood, featured in Sunset’s Best Places to Live in the West. Set off on a bike path adventure or start your novel at the writer’s desk. Walk to coffee shops, restaurants & New Seasons Market grocery. Ideal for College visits: drive times, 10 min to Reed, 10 min to Lewis & Clark, 15 min to PSU. Note: PLEASE ASK about weekly or monthly discounts if you\'re planning extended stay!','Sunset Magazine described Sellwood as “a neighborhood blooming with chic boutiques, farm-fresh eats and garden inspiration.”<br /><br />Sellwood is a fantastic walking and biking neighborhood. We are in Southeast (SE) Portland just a block from the Willamette River which divides the city’s East and West sides. The beautiful, new Sellwood Bridge is a few blocks away. <br /><br />A bench for river viewing is at the end of our block and access to the river for kayaks or stand up paddle boards is minutes away (rentals just across the Sellwood Bridge.)<br /><br />Oaks Bottom wildlife refuge (10 minute walk from here) is superb for birdwatching with trails around a large pond and our yard attracts many kinds of birds including hummingbirds, goldfinches, woodpeckers, doves and owls.<br /><br />Family-friendly Oaks Park (10 minute walk) is one of the oldest amusement parks in the US. It has a new roller coaster, a 1911 carousel, rides for all ages, rollerskating rink and roller derby venue.<br','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/46e15283-1513-4abb-af8a-b79023e91c55.jpg',5190363,20,'45.45861','-122.65596',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,86.00,1,365,538,4.97,26717394),(1251,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26740129','Music-Themed House with a Hot Tub in SW Portland','Relive the golden age of rock and roll in a newly built contemporary-style house. Play classic albums while shooting pool or sit on a couch and strum an acoustic guitar. Barbecue on the back deck and cook meals indoors in a stunning gourmet kitchen. The garage has a treadmill, Peloton bike, dumbbell weights, foosball and four new bikes/helmets.','The house is walking distance to local restaurants, bars, and a fancy family-owned grocery store. It\'s right by Willamette Park, Sellwood Bridge, Lewis & Clark and Reed Colleges, and several corporate headquarters. A waterfront walking and biking trail leads into downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2dbda4d7-a54f-439c-bace-82089ef5fee6.jpg',13080376,22,'45.47162','-122.67371',1,6,3.00,3.00,3.00,450.00,2,30,249,4.97,26740129),(1252,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26820355','Large Studio in Historic Isam White House','Super Clean third floor suite in the historic Isam White House. Includes bed area, living and dining area, kitchenette with microwave, hot water kettle, dishes and small fridge and private bathroom with tub/shower. This is one of the last grand mansions downtown that hasn\'t been converted to condos or offices. We are at the shopping and restaurant districts of Northwest 21st and 23rd Avenues. Walkability score of 97!','Northwest Portland, Nob Hill, also known as the Alphabet District offers sophisticated shopping, dining and people-watching. Victorians, Colonial Mansions, boutiques and restaurants line the streets of this neighborhood that\'s ideal for leisurely strolls, while the adjoining Forest Park was made for hikes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-26820355/original/f405e23a-85c6-4015-81b8-f954324ade4a.jpeg',7409866,27,'45.52515','-122.6927',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,69.00,1,1125,344,4.92,26820355),(1253,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26846062','Cozy North Portland Urban Oasis','Super cute and spacious Art Deco private unit with large yard and easy access to St Johns, Overlook, and Portsmouth neighborhoods, as well as the University of Portland, and the Adidas campus. <br /><br />Across the street from Columbia Park and a short walk/drive to excellent bars, restaurants, coffee shops, and other venues.<br /><br />Quiet, relaxing locale perfect for up to four guests.','Portsmouth neighborhood is a quiet stretch of residential housing surrounding Lombard street, upon which many classic bars and restaurants can be found.<br /><br />Columbia Park, one of Portland’s best recreational locations is directly across the street and offers wide open spaces as well as a public pool.<br /><br />Nearby beautiful views of Portland from the bluffs.<br /><br />Close to the University of Portland and a quick jaunt to the Adidas campus.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-26846062/original/0b887378-cc40-438b-9773-cec676dda563.jpg',18835888,60,'45.58006','-122.71334',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,71.00,2,31,205,4.95,26846062),(1254,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26861615','Airy Bedroom in Friendly Neighborhood','Our house is on a biking street in NE Portland near Alberta, Fremont and 42nd. Enjoy your own comfortable room with a shared bathroom, kitchen and laundry. We\'re in the hub of PDX\'s co-housing/intentional communities, down the block from a park, walking distance to shops and restaurants! In fact we have a fantastic guide we wrote for our airBnB guests on what to do in PDX.<br /><br />If you are planning on coming with a pet please check in with me ahead of time.','The neighborhood is off Alberta. An easy bike ride to downtown Alberta. Off of Fremont Street and near 42nd Street. Walking distance to restaurants and grocery. It is in the heart of Portland\'s intentional/co-housing communities. There is Cully Grove across the street, a net zero community down the block is being built, Columbia Eco village is a few blocks away, Rogue Gardens is a block away. It\'s a great place to stay if you\'re curious about various styles of community living.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjY4NjE2MTU%3D/original/385491ba-252b-4fd1-a97d-4255d7297a47.jpeg',1326395,21,'45.55773','-122.61222',2,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,13,4.85,26861615),(1255,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26867237','University Park Garden Guest House','This beautiful newly built home is located in the quiet residential University Park neighborhood. Located within walking distance of a diverse offering of restaurants, bars, shops, and parks and only a short jaunt to the University of Portland makes this house a convenient place to stay while in Portland. It was thoughtfully designed with cathedral ceilings that allow for an ample amount of light.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/78418753-7b41-45e2-867b-af7ee9b65a46.jpg',50687779,57,'45.58266','-122.73639',1,4,1.50,2.00,2.00,190.00,2,1125,61,4.98,26867237),(1256,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26875345','Light and art-filled flat by park & restaurant row','Beautiful, sunlit, art-filled flat in the heart of one of Portland\'s best neighborhoods and restaurant destinations. Soak in the sun through floor-to-ceiling windows or from the deck or the roof. Stroll in Laurelhurst Park or historic Lone Pine Cemetery. Hop a bus or a scooter to downtown,  15 minutes away. Enjoy a pie at Ken\'s Artisan Pizza, ranked 3rd best in America by @50toppizza awards in Napoli or sample any of the 25+ restaurants, cafes, and bars within a short walk away.','You could spend a week here and not work your way through all the food options.  Grab coffee/pastries at Crema or Heart; lunch at Paadee or the food cart pod around the corner; dinner at Navarre, Ken\'s Artisan Pizza, Bamboo Sushi, Tusk, Laurelhurst Market, or Davenport;  see a movie at Laurelhurst Theater;  nightcap at Angel Face--all literally steps away. For serious cooks, the wonderful store, Providore, is less than a mile away. For convenience, Whole Foods is around the corner. The Central Eastside restaurant and bar options are a medium walk or scooter away. Downtown is a 15 minute bike, scooter or bus ride away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c2609e49-882a-40d2-bbea-ac589ceb8cc5.jpg',3239276,32,'45.52242','-122.63753',1,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,159.00,3,9,113,4.94,26875345),(1257,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26892495','Alberta Arts Stylish Studio w/ Private Entrance','We are located in the popular Alberta Arts District just steps from restaurants, coffee shops, art studios, music venues, and more.','A short walk brings you to the many attractions of Alberta Arts Neighborhood. Here are some of our favorite places! Please check out our guestbook for more recommendations.<br /><br />New Seasons Market<br />Salt & Straw Ice Cream<br />Extracto Coffee<br />Alberta Rose Theatre (music venue)<br /><br />EATERIES <br />Akasura Ramen <br />Bollywood Theatre ( an Indian street food restaurant)<br />Dame<br />Hot Yai<br />Petite Provence Cafe & Bakery<br />Pine State Biscuits Cafe<br />Tin Shed Garden Café<br />Urdanita Tapas Restaurant (just around the corner)<br />Yakuza Lounge<br />Wilder<br /><br />Common Ground Wellness Cooperative<br />McMenamins Kennedy School <br /><br /> For up to date information, we also suggest visiting “travelportland” on line. <br />Check out “Things to Do” for activities, attractions, and dining.  “Places to Visit,” among other things, has all the neighborhoods listed, including ours- the Alberta Arts District—which starts just around the corner from the studi','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9f98c02b-1691-4491-87cb-f620f7f637e0.jpg',11476964,1,'45.5601','-122.63292',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,90.00,2,14,215,4.91,26892495),(1258,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26892924','Queen Suite w/Fully Stocked Kitchen /New Mattress','Queen suite with unbeatable weekly and monthly rates.  Fully stocked kitchen.  Well lit.  Very flexible checkin/out.  Ideal for working remotely. <br />     Arrangements can be made to access clothes washer/dryer and complimentary detergent/fabric softener.  <br />     Walk to restaurants, breweries and parks.  Private entry and courtyard with sitting area.  Grocery stores within walking distance.  Fo-Po Neighborhood in Portland is walkable (score 87) & bikeable (score 99).','Foster Powell is an up and coming neighborhood.  There are two breweries within walking distance.  Also near by is pizza, food carts, Mexican, Hawaiian, Vietnamese, Thai, vegan, and coffee shops.   You can walk to most places, rent a bike from Biketown PDX or take the Max to the city center.  A map of the neighborhood self-guided garden tour and local murals is provided.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-26892924/original/d203c265-ac98-458d-bf40-24cc97aa0bac.jpeg',6236702,37,'45.49769','-122.59895',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,68.00,3,120,29,4.90,26892924),(1259,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26963386','Private 2 BR Basement Suite close to the airport','Just 5 minutes to the Airport, close to MAX and bus lines.  Only 15 minutes to downtown Portland. Remodeled Basement with high ceiling, big windows for lots of light.  Free parking on the street.  800 Sqft apartment and you have a private bathroom, kitchenette with a full-size refrigerator, microwave/convection oven, induction cook-top, and living room. All-natural organic latex mattress.  The shared laundry room is here for you if you need it. Our street is lined with beautiful trees.','We are just a few minutes from the Portland airport, Cascade Station shopping center, 5 great golf courses, the Columbia river and of course downtown Portland.  Easy access to I-205 gets you in and out quickly.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/eeb7587e-cc1a-4315-ae6c-13385371ec85.jpg',33471709,21,'45.55609','-122.57987',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,89.00,2,1125,188,4.88,26963386),(1260,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/26999260','Stellar Sellwood Carriage House','Whether your here for business or pleasure, come  and stay in one of Sunset Magazine\'s Best Places to Live in the West neighborhoods.  <br />A modern 650 sq. ft. 1-bedroom carriage house tucked in the heart of Sellwood is perfect for the solo guest or couples. Lots of natural light, hardwood floors, A/C, full equipped kitchen, plus washer/dryer - all within walking distance to restaurants, local attractions, and public transit.','Sellwood is a quaint walkable neighborhood within the Portland Metro area.  We are about 10-15 minutes from downtown.  The neighborhood is full of restaurants, food carts, coffee shops, retail stores, library, banks, and dessert shops.  This property is on a quiet street but within walking distance to many things.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2f44ec31-ae51-4603-8f0c-0941a63d8a45.jpg',203150897,20,'45.46595','-122.64364',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,134.00,5,45,97,5.00,26999260),(1261,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27054795','* Cozy, Clean + Dog Friendly Guest House in NE PDX','Our guest house was built new in 2018. It is clean (read the reviews!), quiet, very private and a comfortable place to call \"home\" while visiting in Portland. All ameninities to make your stay easy including a full kitchen, compact washer/dryer and air-conditioning. Lots of natural light from 3 large skylights - sleep masks provided for late sleepers. The location has easy access to freeways,  PDX airport (15 min.), and bike ways. Self check-in and free street parking always available.','We are located in a residential neighborhood in Northeast Portland. Not nearly as close to the freeway as depicted in the location photo!  We are closest to the Hollywood, Laurelhurst, Mt. Tabor and Rose City neighborhoods with very easy access to freeways and major streets like Burnside and Sandy Blvd. Max train stations are close by as well. Several grocery stores less than 5 minutes away - by car. Restaurants, a brewery with food carts and coffee just blocks away. A quick 5-15 minute drive to most of the hottest neighborhoods on the east side like Hawthorne Street, Division/Clinton, Mt. Tabor, Alberta, Montavilla and Laurelhurst. Easy access to downtown and convention centers. Providence Portland Medical Center is just a couple blocks away as well.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4acc14d6-768f-46cf-aec6-c32249af54e4.jpg',120016557,11,'45.52922','-122.60925',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,108.00,2,28,351,4.98,27054795),(1262,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27116658','The Yellow Door Bungalow Close-in SE Portland','Relaxed and modern 2 bedroom 2 bath SE bungalow. Great home base for travelers wanting to explore Portland. Located in the historic neighborhood of Sellwood. Walkable to restaurants, shops, amazing parks and close to the river front. On the beautiful Spring Water Corridor bike path and close to public max train. Full kitchen, remodeled home with new amenities yet all the original charm you want in an old house. Private front porch for lounging and shared spacious back yard. So much to offer!','In a nice residential neighborhood and only a few blocks from some great restaurants and shops. Short walk to Killer burger, 2 sushi places, Thai food, desert shop, mini mart and crêperie. Half mile from New Seasons Market, Food Carts & Starbucks (about 10-15 minutes walk). Half mile to the main drag of Sellwood which has awesome restaurants, coffee shops, salons, gift shops and more. Less than a mile away from main drag of Westmoreland which has more great shops, post office, FedEx, great restaurants, movie theatre & the historic “Antique Row.”  Some of the best parks in Portland close by- Westmoreland Park, Johnson Creek Park, Sellwood Park and Sellwood waterfront park with river access. In the dry months don’t miss historic Oaks Amusement  Park on the Sellwood waterfront and the Milwaukie Farmers market (short bike ride away). 5 miles from downtown Portland. Our list of favorite nearby attractions available in the unit.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b8102186-8c5e-4642-8cad-10615196d9c8.jpg',102525527,20,'45.46379','-122.64287',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,139.00,1,14,338,4.77,27116658),(1263,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27126083','Craftsman duplex in the heart of Southeast PDX','This is the upstairs unit in a beautiful Craftsman duplex with lots of natural light located centrally in Buckman (Southeast Portland). Great location on Stark St. that\'s a quick walk from concert venue Revolution Hall, many craft breweries, and a delightful vegan strip with food and shopping options!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/17279a13-e2eb-431d-a13c-10c4e6647e69.jpg',1978398,32,'45.51955','-122.64838',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,119.00,2,28,113,4.86,27126083),(1264,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27161519','Cozy NW Portland Condo - Private Entry','MAKE THIS YOUR HOME. <br />OR YOUR HOME AWAY FROM HOME!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b6be6c98-2eca-4a4a-9def-2c974f735557.jpg',983107,27,'45.53326','-122.69509',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,30,360,15,4.93,27161519),(1265,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27163639','Starla! Farm Stay Camper 20m to downtown!','Starla: enjoy a cozy bedroom (once an art studio) on our hobby farm.  Enjoy an easy park and stay with walking access to our farm (donkeys, alpacas, goats,pigs+) 600 acre nature park of Powell Butte.  An easy access bath in the main house + all outdoor common areas. Note: Starla has a coffee/tea station but (NO KITCHEN) radiant heat keeps it cozy and ask for more comforters.  It’s 50 steps to the main house shared guest bath. 100% NON SMOKING PROPERTY due to fire hazards near park.','Powell Butte Nature Park is our main Neigbor but we also are just above the spacious Gates Park which provides dog, frisbee, ball heaven.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7731454f-b297-415f-9fa6-770ef9c9a3e9.jpg',421792,77,'45.48737','-122.51657',2,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,55.00,31,1125,43,4.77,27163639),(1266,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27200563','Modern Design,  Beautiful Views, Private Deck','Come experience our little piece of Portland paradise! Make yourselves at home in our guesthouse, designed to feel like your home away from home. We take hosting seriously and as longtime airbnb guests ourselves, we hope to have learned a thing or two about  what makes for a comfortable stay. Expect to find a spotless place with everything you need - just like home, minus the clutter!','We are located in the Overlook neighborhood on Willamette Boulevard, popular among Portlanders for \'the bluffs\' which are known to have the best sunset views in town. Quiet and neighborhoody, lovely for walks, yet still countless delicious cafes, restaurants and great bars, (Old Gold, Milk Glass Market, La Bonita, Mee Dee Thai, SPITZ, and Barlow Tavern to name a few) all within a few blocks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-27200563/original/3135773a-3619-4711-8c29-c8e54fa6880f.jpg',328095,13,'45.56247','-122.69725',1,4,1.50,1.00,2.00,136.00,1,31,185,4.97,27200563),(1267,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27229222','Portland Bungalow','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-27229222/original/edcf142e-1e02-4293-825d-0a9321a47f4f.jpeg',205064625,20,'45.46122','-122.6545',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,150.00,5,14,18,5.00,27229222),(1268,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27231117','My Portland Launch Pad','Thank you for taking a look at The Pad! It\'s a cozy 1 bedroom home in Portland\'s popular Alberta neighborhood. I host along with Joe Lara and we strive to provide a comfortable and clean home that offers easy access to dining, shopping, cafes, bars and Alberta Park (located across the street).  The Pad is a 15 minute drive to the airport and downtown Portland. We\'re looking forward to your visit!','The Alberta Neighborhood is anchored by Alberta Arts District which is a 1-mile long district situated on Alberta St. There you\'ll find a wide range of restaurants, cafes, bars, galleries and a performing arts theater as well as boutique shopping, yoga studios, professional services and more. It\'s a walkable and vibrant community space that offers something for everyone. Even closer to home (2 blocks) is Killingsworth Street\'s dining district with excellent BBQ and Thai options as well as Piedmont Station Food Carts - lots of great choices at a reborn gas station - don\'t miss the  beer shack for a craftbrew and a seat in the beer garden.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d3b81885-392e-4b8c-b01f-b979d195d014.jpg',205079895,29,'45.56294','-122.64466',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,116,4.90,27231117),(1269,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27232169','Well-Preserved Quintessential 1922 Craftsman','If you love great food, craft beer, and the quirky charm of Portlandia, my four-bedroom apartment in Laurelhurst is perfect for you. This vibrant neighborhood is home to top restaurants, bars, vintage shops, and offers some of the best people-watching.<br /><br />With a convenient home base just steps from neighborhood hotspots, you can experience the authentic lifestyle of hipsters in Stumptown. Enjoy the unique blend of history, culture, and modern amenities that make Laurelhurst a true Portland gem.','Located in the heart of the vibrant Laurelhurst District, this neighborhood is a quintessential representation of Portland’s eclectic charm. Nestled on NE Glisan Street, you’ll find yourself immersed in a lively area known for its tree-lined streets, historic homes, and a welcoming community atmosphere.<br /><br />Laurelhurst is a food lover’s paradise, boasting some of Portland’s top-rated restaurants, cozy cafes, and trendy bars. Start your day with a handcrafted coffee from one of the many local coffee shops, then explore the diverse culinary scene, from food trucks to fine dining. The nearby Whole Foods and local farmers’ markets ensure you have access to fresh, organic ingredients for those nights you prefer to cook at home.<br /><br />For shopping enthusiasts, the neighborhood offers a variety of vintage boutiques, quirky shops, and independent bookstores. You’ll also enjoy the proximity to Laurelhurst Park, a beautiful urban oasis perfect for a morning jog, afternoon picnic, or ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27232169/original/cf7452da-7740-47f9-8c6f-a1ba9d92728b.jpeg',190656099,12,'45.52703','-122.63301',1,8,2.00,4.00,4.00,264.00,1,1125,406,4.87,27232169),(1270,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27232368','Underground Mid-Century Hideaway in Laurelhurst','If you love great food, craft beer, and the quirky charm of Portlandia, my four-bedroom apartment in Laurelhurst is perfect for you. This vibrant neighborhood is home to top restaurants, bars, vintage shops, and offers some of 