’s eclectic charm. Nestled on NE Glisan Street, you’ll find yourself immersed in a lively area known for its tree-lined streets, historic homes, and a welcoming community atmosphere.<br /><br />Laurelhurst is a food lover’s paradise, boasting some of Portland’s top-rated restaurants, cozy cafes, and trendy bars. Start your day with a handcrafted coffee from one of the many local coffee shops, then explore the diverse culinary scene, from food trucks to fine dining. The nearby Whole Foods and local farmers’ markets ensure you have access to fresh, organic ingredients for those nights you prefer to cook at home.<br /><br />For shopping enthusiasts, the neighborhood offers a variety of vintage boutiques, quirky shops, and independent bookstores. You’ll also enjoy the proximity to Laurelhurst Park, a beautiful urban oasis perfect for a morning jog, afternoon picnic, or ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27232517/original/d8dea11f-7c01-40ae-b2e8-3f686c59f692.jpeg',190656099,12,'45.52595','-122.63459',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,69.00,1,1125,538,4.77,27232517),(1273,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27232628','Urban Cabin Studio ~ Breweries & Local Eateries','If you love great food, craft beer, and the quirky charm of Portlandia, my four-bedroom apartment in Laurelhurst is perfect for you. This vibrant neighborhood is home to top restaurants, bars, vintage shops, and offers some of the best people-watching.<br /><br />With a convenient home base just steps from neighborhood hotspots, you can experience the authentic lifestyle of hipsters in Stumptown. Enjoy the unique blend of history, culture, and modern amenities that make Laurelhurst a true Portland gem.','Located in the heart of the vibrant Laurelhurst District, this neighborhood is a quintessential representation of Portland’s eclectic charm. Nestled on NE Glisan Street, you’ll find yourself immersed in a lively area known for its tree-lined streets, historic homes, and a welcoming community atmosphere.<br /><br />Laurelhurst is a food lover’s paradise, boasting some of Portland’s top-rated restaurants, cozy cafes, and trendy bars. Start your day with a handcrafted coffee from one of the many local coffee shops, then explore the diverse culinary scene, from food trucks to fine dining. The nearby Whole Foods and local farmers’ markets ensure you have access to fresh, organic ingredients for those nights you prefer to cook at home.<br /><br />For shopping enthusiasts, the neighborhood offers a variety of vintage boutiques, quirky shops, and independent bookstores. You’ll also enjoy the proximity to Laurelhurst Park, a beautiful urban oasis perfect for a morning jog, afternoon picnic, or ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27232628/original/bad1a4f6-f48c-4482-abd9-929ae305ddf3.jpeg',190656099,12,'45.52569','-122.63285',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,66.00,1,1125,651,4.85,27232628),(1274,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27262964','YeOldeTinyHouse/Alberta Arts/featured in Dwell','TINY HOUSE is loaded with charm,  rustic but refined urban oasis provides a fully equipped  home  base for Pacific Northwest adventures  (featured in Dwell Magazine’s top 17 PNW Dreamy Retreats and OREGON LIVE top Oregon tiny homes). Half a block from Alberta Arts District, 15 minute drive to the airport and downtown. Easy drive to Mt Hood, wineries and the Oregon coast.  Managed by owners onsite, not a management company and EASY checkout, no long list of things to do. Dedicated internet.','We have a guide of our local favorite places, but be sure to ask in advance if want any eating tips or activities, we love providing recommendations to make your trip the best it can be.<br /><br />15 minutes drive from airport and downtown.<br />There are dozens of wonderful bars and restaurants, food carts ( food carts are a big deal in Portland and very high quality) within walking distance. Also a small theater a few blocks away, cute stores, galleries. New Seasons grocery store and Walgreens is a few minutes drive away. We are easily accessible to freeways to head to wineries, Mt. Hood and the Columbia River Gorge (which now requires reservations).<br /><br />Many quests have noted even though we are in a buzzing and vibrant neighborhood, the tiny house is so quiet and peaceful','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/71889d59-628f-4314-be6f-c2e8cdd812cf.jpg',185187318,1,'45.55792','-122.63517',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,112.00,2,30,224,4.99,27262964),(1275,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27263238','Walk 2 Restaurants & Park, Private Entrance','If you feel like adventuring through Portland and want to base out of Southeast where you sit almost directly between Division and Hawthorne on 32nd, it is hard to find a better location than this one.  You have a private entrance on the side of the house that leads down to a newly converted basement. It is clean, neat, and has some wonderful amenities. Every single thing in this retreat is brand new.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-27263238/original/f39330b2-22f1-4d63-95d4-c1f170685160.jpeg',62261998,8,'45.50869','-122.63317',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,103.00,2,29,65,4.57,27263238),(1276,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27290594','Top Floor Apt in NW; Great space; longer stays','5-Star luxury in heart of Northwest. Great space. Great location.<br />Longer stays (30+ days) welcome. <br /><br />Top Floor Apt is newly renovated private space atop our 1899 house. There is  a separate entrance.  On a quiet street in NW  neighborhood. One block to Legacy Good Sam; five minutes to famous Forest Park.  Walk to bars, restaurants, shops, Powell\'s Books.<br /><br />Wood floors, compact kitchen, AC, skylights, big balcony','We think (hope) you\'ll agree that our house is in a perfect location for exploring all the many places worth checking out in our neighborhood and surrounding areas.    <br /><br />23rd Avenue is a block away, and deserves its reputation as the most popular commercial main street in the City.  It\'s a 15-block stretch  filled with restaurants, bars, coffee shops, St. Honore Bakery, Salt & Straw, two cannabis stores, Blue Star Donuts, three distilleries, a theater, a comedy club and a fun collection of stores (from funky Three Monkeys to Urban Outfitters to Pottery Barn -- and everything in between).   You\'ll also find street car and bus stops nearby, as well as several ebike rental kiosks along 23rd Avenue.   And those electric scooters are now all over our neighborhood. <br /><br />NW 21st Avenue is another commercial main street worth checking out.  It\'s got Cinema 21 - a great locally-owned movie theater - and bars and restaurants with a bit more active night-life scene than NW 23rd. ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/890a4ee0-1e6f-4e09-a49b-8d4dbb91470e.jpg',32155407,27,'45.52996','-122.70027',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,195.00,4,180,58,4.95,27290594),(1277,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27291927','Sanctuary In The City: Close to OHSU SW Portland','This listing is for SOLO FEMALES ONLY.   You will have your own private room and bathroom in the upstairs of my rowhouse while the rest of the space is shared with just me and my kitty Bodhi. <br /><br />Generally only doing long term bookings...have a brief opening for a few weeks the month of July!!!  <br /><br />BEST for super quiet and super clean/mindful solo females.','The John\'s Landing neighborhood in SW Portland is a mix of historic Victorian houses, condos, and apartments nestled amongst the trees! It’s away from the hustle and bustle of the city....so if you’re looking for action or Portlandia vibe...you won’t find it here and it is not walking distance to a grocery store but there are a few cafes within walking distance.  I\'m in a good central location to get to any part of Portland. <br /><br /><br /> For the most part it is very quiet and surrounded by natural beauty. At times, here and there (especially summer months) you may hear the sounds of city life as people come and go on the street. I\'ve designed the space and your room to help with this!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/38c5e959-e861-4530-9cfc-7e9b1e37b87e.jpg',71968406,22,'45.49','-122.68004',2,1,1.50,1.00,1.00,70.00,30,180,159,4.99,27291927),(1278,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27336194','NW| Architectural Gem| In Forest Park','Urban oasis IN Forest Park designed by John Storrs.  City + country living in Portland\'s most prestigious neighborhood. 1 .5 miles to NW 23rd Street shops.   Remodeled spa inspired bathrooms. West Elm furniture.  Gas fireplaces.  2 WFH dedicated spaces with high speed internet.  Forest Park trails steps from front door. <br /><br />NOTE:   Front door is up a flight of stairs.  2 story home.  <br />No large gatherings or parties permitted.<br />1 Dog max per stay.  No Cats.','“Hillside” “NW”.    Treehouse - you are in the forest among the trees, but 1.5 miles to NW 23rd & downtown.  Hiking steps from home in Forest Park.  Quiet, and serene location. <br /><br />Designed by midcentury architect John Storrs.  Home blends modern amenities with historical character.  John Storrs also designed: Salishan Lodge, Caitlin Gabel School;  Oregon College of Art & Design; and Sokol Blosser Winery in Dundee.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e8d162ae-c08d-4f41-ade9-cc42b95d7579.jpg',1912227,79,'45.53153','-122.71445',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,239.00,30,90,51,4.80,27336194),(1279,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27339264','2 Master Suites*Hawthorne/Division Area','Non-smokers only, please! Walk Score 95!! Perfect for friends traveling together on a moderate budget who want their own bedroom & bathroom! Two clean and spacious master suites in a SHARED house (host lives here, too).  Walk Score 95! Gorgeous shared home near hip Hawthorne & Division Streets! Walking distance to restaurant, shops and bars!  Hike up Mt Tabor for great city views!  Garden paradise to relax in.','95 Walk Score and 100 Bike Score!  Live like a local!  This is a wonderful and highly coveted Portland neighborhood with incredible restaurants, bars, brew pubs, wine bars and great tax free shopping at locally owned boutiques and vintage shops, all within walking distance.  The nearest coffee shop is a 3 minute walk away but there are several others nearby, The nearest restaurant/bar is also 3 minutes away but dozens within 5-20 minutes walk.  Plenty of great shops on both Hawthorne and Division! There are countless options for dining ranging from a delicious Korean BB food cart just around the corner to plenty of Thai restaurants, Indian at Bollywood Theater, Japanese, Italian at Cibo (great happy hour!), Landmark Saloon for casual outdoor drinking with a couple of food carts and good old fresh Northwestern cuisine made with locally sourced ingredients. <br /><br />Downtown is about 10 minutes by car, the airport is about 20 minutes by car.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6d0c93c4-3bb5-4f0e-947e-4fd15f3acd7b.jpg',1096266,8,'45.50762','-122.61548',2,4,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,1,7,1,5.00,27339264),(1280,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27342211','North Portland Hideaway, Pet Friendly','Adorable 550 square foot one-bedroom bungalow  in hot North Portland. Walk to transit, restaurants and shops. The house is tucked inside a lush yard full of trees--feels like an urban oasis. Queen bed in bedroom with a high-end Queen futon bed in living room. Full kitchen with all the essentials. Small, cute backyard for small or medium dogs.','Walk to downtown Kenton, with its small town feel and great restaurants. Transit: The MAX station, Trimet\'s yellow line is 3 blocks away near Paul Bunyan off of Denver and Interstate Ave. <br />Restaurant\'s: Posies( Bakery &Cafe), PoShines Cafe De La Soul, Derby(Breakfast/Lunch), Cultured Caveman (Paleo), Fino(Pizza/Salad), Prince Coffee, and Swift and Union( Seasonal American/craft beer). <br />Things to do: Public Library(Books, books, books>>), Disjecta(Not for profit arts organization), Bamboo Craftsman(Cool Bamboo fort to climb), Give and Take(Resale), Kenton Park, Kenton Club(Live music, Karaoke, and Card games), Sweet Science Boxing Gym,  Blue Ox tattoo, Bart\'s Barbershop, Kenton Liquor Store','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b78737c6-1305-4b43-914d-dc4073e1f1da.jpg',11674194,55,'45.58313','-122.68015',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,7,730,31,4.97,27342211),(1281,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27362354','Backyard Garden Retreat','Quiet Reed College neighborhood setting with beautiful backyard garden, pond, waterfall, surrounded by sequoias. 2 Minute walk to scenic hiking trail, 10 min walk to a glorious garden, 7 min drive to shopping/dining/golf in Sellwood or Hawthorne districts, 15 min drive to downtown.<br /><br />Adjustable queen bed, A/C; free Wi-Fi, TV with Netflix, Amazon Prime; wet-bar, coffee-maker, mini-fridge.<br /><br />Extra bed in backyard yurt (at $69/night charge)<br /><br />Enjoy an urban oasis, all from your own backyard!','Quiet neighborhood adjacent to Reed College. Easily walkable to parks, stores, restaurants, gardens, etc.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1411e95f-17ea-45da-8656-f7ca2898f686.jpg',176094166,61,'45.48392','-122.62876',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,79.00,2,14,186,4.99,27362354),(1282,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27370420','Great Portland location with river views','This furnished one bedroom condo is situated in the midst of expansive grounds with landscaping and courtyards.  Located on the streetcar line with easy access to Downtown, Shopping, Dining, Theater, Parks and more. Everything is right at your doorstep.The urban setting gives you easy access to the best of what Portland has to offer.<br /><br />Guest is required to sign a short term lease before check in','Great location for walking to parks, restaurants, theater, PSU','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2931b6ec-9964-456a-b0bc-cc6dda95e3ec.jpg',56493074,44,'45.51044','-122.67935',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,79.00,30,365,20,4.80,27370420),(1283,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27392364','NE Sanctuary - Beautiful Award-winning PDX Home','Newly built,  beautiful, modern, award winning home! Designed and built by local architect.  Very quiet and relaxing private escape across from a Zen center is 10 minutes to airport, 15 minutes to downtown, near 2  major highways located on major bicycle route. Close to the action but just out of the chaos. Full amenities, new granite Kitchen counter, king memory foam mattress, desk, 55\" smart TV, patio, AC, W/D, etc. Certified sustainable environmentally conscious green home. Great work space!!','Neighborhood is peaceful, safe and quiet, neighbors are great. The home has huge windows, skylights and a patio overlooking a large tranquil Zen Buddhist park directly across the street which is great to walk through.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27392364/original/1a40f039-a199-480f-94e2-84629b72296d.jpeg',19259335,74,'45.54424','-122.57584',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,98.00,1,28,451,4.89,27392364),(1284,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27463822','Stylish 2nd Floor Studio Great Location!','This small studio is perfect for the solo traveler with everything one would need to stay for awhile. Big beautiful 4 square windows look down on an urban forest with century old homes framing the neighborhood. It features a kitchen, full bed, walk in closet, with a spacious bathroom (shared) and clawfoot tub. Welcome!','The Irvington neighborhood, now only a 15 minute bike ride from downtown, was once a trolley-car suburb to the just-fully-developed West side. Designated a historic district by the National Register of Historic Places in 2010, Irvington is filled with early 20th century homes that have been preserved in their original states. Irvington has become a livable hub of Northeast Portland as a whole, with shops and restaurants of all kinds, within walking distance, surrounding the neighborhood. Irvington proper boasts more than a few community and culinary destinations of its own.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27463822/original/ad197da3-5bf1-4ca3-9da3-6a0970d90829.jpeg',13695963,7,'45.54193','-122.64889',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,35.00,30,365,37,4.86,27463822),(1285,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27548325','Central, Pet-Friendly Home Steps From Mississippi!','Located 2 blocks from Portland\'s famous Mississippi Street, start your day with a cup of local coffee and stroll down the street, checking out all the neighborhood has to offer - the endless supply of shops, restaurants, food carts, bars, yoga studios and salons is dizzying!  Pop back to our cozy home to relax and freshen up before heading back out to one of the many nearby restaurants, take in a band at Mississippi Studios, or just cozy in and enjoy a glass of wine with friends and family!','The Mississippi neighborhood has quickly become one of Portland\'s most coveted foodie areas, with such names as: EEM, ¿Por Qué No?, Tasty & Sons, Prost!, Gravy, Coco or Blue Star Donuts, Mee Sen Thai, Interurban and more just steps away from the house! And with easy access to the Overlook MAX station, getting downtown is super easy, too; be there in less than twenty minutes!<br /><br />Some of the homeowner’s favorite 5 to 15 minute walk recommendations are:<br />-Our favorite coffee: Fresh Pot or Albina Press<br />-Breakfast: Gravy,  Swee Dee Dee(open Wed-Sat 9am-9pm, check before heading out), Broder Norde <br />-Our favorite beer in the hood: tough call... Stormbreaker or Ecliptic for proximity as it\'s on -Mississippi, but Ex Novo (8 min drive or bike ride) wins our vote<br />-Cocktails: Interurban or Box Social (on Williams Ave)<br />-Thai food: Mee Sen<br />-Best burger: Ecliptic, close tie for 2nd with BarBar and Little Big Burger<br />-Date night food: EEM, The 1905 for Jazz, br','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/827115ee-eb9d-44bd-9ac1-030f8046f87b.jpg',6473368,9,'45.5529','-122.67808',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,150.00,1,1125,287,4.76,27548325),(1286,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27553121','Near Eastport Plaza, Short drive to PDX, Downtown','Nice & Private Guests\' Suite located centrally in SE Portland at a convenient location.<br />1. Walk to Foods, Shops, Pubs, Public Transits<br />2. Short drive to PDX, Downtown<br />3. Near Eastport Plaza, I-205, US-26, OR-213<br /><br />Guests will have a comfort of A Home-Away-From-Home with a Spacious  Master Bedroom, Cozy Living Room, Fully Equipped Kitchen, Nice Bath with Washer and Dryer.<br /><br />A Perfect Corporate Rental - A comfortable stay for Business Travelers, Guests needed an Extended-Stay.','This property is located in a Lents Historic District near Eastport Plaza Shopping Center in an old established neighborhood in SE Portland. In recent years, this area has become a reviving and thriving multicultural community. This home is located close to many amenities that Portland has to offer. It is only a short drive to Downtown Portland and Portland International Airport. It is an excellent hub to many of Portland\'s Must See Neighborhoods, less than a ten-minute drive to many trendy places like Hawthorne District, Division/Clinton District, Montavilla Districts.<br /><br />The location is very accessible as it is near Portland Major Roads, Highways and Interstates. It also has easy access to Portland Suburban Cities East and South of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e04b6857-367f-49e0-93dc-fd9a2aed6dc3.jpg',12523076,72,'45.48739','-122.5779',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,30,180,4,4.50,27553121),(1287,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27555604','Cascadia: Our reviews say it all!','Entire Home - 3 Beds, New Build.  Live like the locals in the historic artsy Piedmont neighborhood. A quiet and safe neighborhood minutes from the restaurants, bars and boutiques of Alberta, Mississippi, and Williams.  Perfect central location. 15 minutes South to Downtown Portland or North to Vancouver. Even quicker to MODA Center, Convention Center, Expo Center.  10 minutes to Portland International Raceway.  Just 20 minutes to the airport.','Piedmont is a historic Portland neighborhood first established in the late 1800s/early 1900s.  It includes Peninsula Park with it\'s sunken rose garden.  While Piedmont itself is almost entirely residential, it\'s central location is coveted for it\'s quick and easy access to arts, entertainment, nightlife, shopping, sporting events, and major festivals.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-27555604/original/07cdf048-e5a4-4e1c-8093-a40cfc388569.jpg',29196049,48,'45.56649','-122.66683',1,4,1.50,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,180,169,5.00,27555604),(1288,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27606267','Peaceful Apartment in the Heart of Portland','A stellar studio apartment in happening SE Portland. Apartment is attached to a house on a quiet dead end street. BUT... 1 block off trendy SE Division Street, and 8 blocks off SE Hawthorne Blvd. Just a couple blocks to Pinolo Gelato, Salt and Straw, Baghdad Theater and many other popular restaurants, bars and shops. On main bus line. St Parking. Apartment has a kitchenette, full bath, queen size bed, private entrance, private outdoor area, and everything needed for a relaxing stay in Portland.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27606267/original/5d54c69c-1cd2-47ef-9359-e143ef448c49.jpeg',208306655,8,'45.50592','-122.62597',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,79.00,2,1125,120,4.96,27606267),(1289,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27634146','Walk Everywhere from a Historic Home with AC','Wander beneath an old cedar tree to an updated Victorian house with air conditioning painted in burnished, fall-inspired hues. Green and wood tones accent the warm gray interiors equipped with an electric fireplace. A gallery wall features local and vintage art hangs above the velvet couch. Windows that soar to 10 foot-high ceilings capture leafy street views. Just a block away, explore the vibrant Mississippi arts district, brimming with dining, drinking, and shopping options.<br />18201638H0','There are 20 locally owned shops and 26 restaurants and bars on the historic Mississippi Ave business district just one block away! Check out mississippiave dotcom to see a list of everything located nearby! Stroll to amazing brunch or great BBQ, or walk to live music at Mississippi Studios','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-27634146/original/ca5162f7-0e55-4c7f-ac6c-4cfb00ffa839.jpeg',60300963,9,'45.55105','-122.67661',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,108.00,2,730,496,4.95,27634146),(1290,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27677098','Private Minimalist Architecture Guesthouse Loft','Step through double French doors into a modern guesthouse. Inspired by contemporary design and filled with light. The home features an open-to-above foyer, a mezzanine bedroom, exposed beams, wood finishes, polished concrete heated floors, and access to a shared backyard.<br /><br />Location, location, location.<br />This is a tastefully constructed guesthouse in the heart of the Kearns/Buckman neighborhood in NE Portland.<br />There is a fully equipped designer kitchen with all the amenities you may need: microwave, coffee maker, toaster, Bertazzoni gas range, Bosch refrigerator & dishwasher. The large living/dining room is spacious & bright. It has a radiant heated concrete floor and custom made furniture. There is a 47 inch Ultra HD smart TV with Comcast Cable and an American Leather queen size sofa sleeper with gel mattress for your use. <br /><br />The bedroom/loft has vaulted ceilings, a queen size, hand crafted, locally made Parklane bed with Italian bedding and a 40 inch smart ','The property is located in NE Portland, boasting close access to restaurants, bars, grocery stores, coffee shops, public transit, and much more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e61284ba-30f9-4eb9-9c6e-dff180031b02.jpg',208901740,12,'45.52381','-122.64609',1,4,1.50,1.00,2.00,119.00,2,1125,237,4.98,27677098),(1291,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27678727','Modern Architect-designed House','A modern  one bedroom house in a quiet neighborhood minutes to downtown and to the ultra-hip Missisippi, Williams and Alberta districts.  One block from a beautiful 16-acre park.  Sleeps 4.  Great for one or two couples or families with kids. No pets allowed','The house is in a safe and very prime location.  It\'s located right on the borderline between the historic Irvington neighborhood and the super hip Boise-Eliot neighborhood. Irving Park - a gorgeous 16-acre park - is just a block away.  Walk to a cute little neighborhood pub and cafe, to some of the finest restaurants in Portland (The Ox, Ned Ludd, Toro Bravo) or drive 5 minutes to the three coolest areas in Portland - The Mississippi district, Williams Street or the Alberta Arts district.  You are very close in to downtown and can get downtown or to the Pearl by car in less than 10 minutes and very easily by public transportation accessible just less than two blocks from the house.  Easy access to freeways for trips to the Columbia Gorge, Mt. Hood or to the coast. This listing does not allow pets of any kind - hosts are severely allergic and guests can be confident that the unit has never had a pet inside.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27678727/original/682c898e-854f-48e0-8804-1b8095408410.jpeg',13079204,26,'45.54655','-122.65916',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,90.00,1,29,306,4.91,27678727),(1292,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27679449','Pittock Getaway near Forest Park','Remodeled apartment in a great location for exploring nearby Pittock Mansion, Forest Park, Washington Park, Japanese Gardens, Portland Zoo and enjoying the city of Portland. The apartment includes  one bedroom, a living room and small kitchen. The first floor apartment is secure with its own private entrance. Access to NW Portland and Downtown by car, No.20 Trimet bus or a short uber/lyft from MAX station at Providence Park.  Free parking is available on the street.','Our house is nestled in the Forest Park area of Portland, 12 min drive from Downtown Portland, 8min drive from Powell\'s City of Books and only 5 min drive from the Alphabet District. The neighborhood is filled with individual family homes on the hillside approaching Pittock Mansion, which is a short 15min walk from the house. If you do not want a walk up the hill to Pittock Mansion it is a 2min drive.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27679449/original/3b8a0c21-1715-4adf-a970-7b96860fe75b.jpeg',48368540,79,'45.52107','-122.72219',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,120.00,3,28,138,4.91,27679449),(1293,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27697302','The Teal Door Bungalow Close-in SE Portland','Relaxed and modern upstairs studio apartment in a SE bungalow. Great home base for travelers wanting to explore Portland. Located in the historic neighborhood of Sellwood. Walkable to restaurants, shops, amazing parks and close to the river front. On the beautiful Spring Water Corridor bike path and close to public max train. Full kitchen, remodeled home with new amenities yet all the original charm you want in an old house. Shared spacious back yard. So much to offer!','In a nice residential neighborhood and only a few blocks from great restaurants and shops.  Short walk to Killer Burger, 2 sushi places, Thai food, desert shop, mini market and creperie.  Half mile from New Seasons Market, food carts and Starbucks (about a 10-15 min walk). Half mile to the main drag of Sellwood which has more awesome restaurants, coffee shops, salons, gift shops and more.  Less than a mile from the main drag of Westmoreland which has more great shops, a post office, FedEx, great restaurants, a movie theater & the historic “Antique Row.” Some of the best parks in Portland are close by- Westmoreland Park, Johnson Creek Park, Sellwood Park, Sellwood Waterfront Park with river access.   In the dry months don’t miss the historic Oaks Amusement Park on the Sellwood Waterfront and the Milwaukee Farmers Market (short bike ride away).  5 miles from downtown Portland. Our lists of our favorite nearby attractions are available in the unit.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2470973b-6374-495f-8c58-d12d697a5480.jpg',78379504,20,'45.46408','-122.64431',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,69.00,1,14,276,4.79,27697302),(1294,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27758553','Cool 2 Bdrm Division St Suite Central SE Location','Take some time to relax in this cool two bedroom basement suite, only steps away from the popular Division St\'s, Pok Pok, Salt & Straw, Bollywood Theatre, First Ever Stumptown Coffee, Broder Cafe and more. Enjoy the location, wifi & free street parking.','The neighborhood is quite yet two blocks from one of the most happening streets in SE.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0e2f5521-c342-4c72-89fd-e8bbba349286.jpg',23400410,25,'45.50292','-122.63653',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,74.00,31,180,34,4.82,27758553),(1295,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27764324','The Foody Farmhouse - Your best choice for PDX!','Rare gem. 2 bedroom.  Renovated farmhouse in the middle of the PDX food scene. Peaceful with privacy in the heart of the hip Kerns neighborhood- Rated 5th coolest on the planet! <br /><br />Steps to cafes, Whole Foods, Laurelhurst Theatre & some of PDX\'s best restaurants. Fast WIFI, Cable tv, Great beds, fully equipped modern kitchen, & fenced yard. Workspace. Quality furnishings. Filtered drinking water. AC. Professionally Cleaned. - BASEMENT APARTMENT NOT INCLUDED. PETS ARE $50 per stay','Our \"hipster\" neighborhood is full of chefs, wonderful award-winning eateries, fun bars & unique shops. There\'s a movie theater that serves food & drinks 3 blocks away. Whole Foods market 3 blocks away. Come experience the unique Old Portland vibe in a friendly neighborhood. Great people watching too.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27764324/original/c25a3bc5-687d-460d-9388-7db269626b3c.jpeg',48015500,12,'45.52548','-122.63595',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,140.00,2,30,320,4.94,27764324),(1296,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27783538','Alberta Arts Townhome','2 Bed, 2.5 Bath Alberta Arts Townhome. Enjoy this stunning townhome built in 2015. Contemporary cutting-edge design worthy of Dwell magazine. Located in Portland\'s popular Alberta Arts District - over 20 blocks of restaurants, bars, cafes, galleries, boutiques and Alberta Rose Theater.<br />-Hardwood floors <br />-Chef\'s kitchen w/ basic pantry supplies available. <br />-Roll-up garage door off kitchen to balcony bring\'s the outside in!','The house is located in the Alberta Arts District which is anchored by Northeast Alberta St. where guests will find an eclectic mix of restaurants, cafes, boutiques, shops, bars and a theater along 30 city blocks. This pedestrian friendly corridor is buzzing with activity all week long and particularly on the weekend when locals line-up for a table at one of the many delicious brunch restaurants. You’ll find everything from locally made ice cream and locally brewed beer to unique galleries, shops and many dining options.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27783538/original/f8bb8bcd-20cb-47d1-ac99-975775f7f9e6.jpeg',205079895,29,'45.56261','-122.64516',1,5,2.50,2.00,2.00,100.00,2,364,307,4.88,27783538),(1297,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27784464','5428 Unit A','IF YOU BOOK FOR 31 DAYS OR MORE YOU AVOID PAYING HUNDREDS OF $$ IN LODGING TAXES:<br />Newer, fully furnished studio unit one block from the interstate Max light rail line in North Portland. Comfy queen size bed, washer and dryer in unit, air conditioning, dishes, linens, towels, etc. Utilities included, power, water, trash, wifi, there is no cable television, but there is a smart tv. Sorry no pets','Great North Portland neighborhood close to public transit and multiple restaurants. New Seasons natural grocers nearby as well.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1f4c45a1-fd23-4db2-87b6-c029fd634799.jpg',770134,13,'45.56268','-122.68038',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,43.00,30,1125,10,5.00,27784464),(1298,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27787557','Back Porch Bungalow-2 guests, 1 bdrm, private bath','If you are looking to be centrally located the Back Porch Bungalow is just the ticket. This spacious guest suite with private entrance is perfect for anyone looking to explore the wonders of the Rose City.  Walking distance to a major commercial grocery store in one direction and natural grocery store in the other, Peninsula Park Rose Garden and  many hidden gems along the way. Very near to live music, a comedy club, food carts,  limited and full service restaurants. ','This independent and diverse NE Portland neighborhood teams art, shopping, and dining. Cult status food carts, pubs, taverns, vegan options and Portland\'s premier Alberta Rose Theater where acoustic music and art house films can be experienced. Topped with Alberta\'s colorful street fair the last Thursday of every month.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/76015b52-9290-4ee8-8e66-477918ed08e7.jpg',209826108,14,'45.56263','-122.6617',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,78.00,1,14,1061,4.80,27787557),(1299,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27856170','Spacious Studio steps to Belmont & Hawthorne','This incredibly spacious and open floor plan Studio is right near all the action! Within steps to SE Belmont St, a few blocks from Hawthorne Blvd, Division St., and so much more. You won\'t have any trouble finding awesome stuff to do, places to see, drink, eat, visit, etc.','SE Portland is a Foodie\'s paradise. Located a few blocks from Southeast Hawthorne Boulevard, Belmont boasts its own mix of vintage and indie shops, coffee houses, bars and food carts. Some of the best restaurants Portland has to offer can be found within a short walk from this property and neighborhood!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27856170/original/81e7af37-2a1f-49ab-bda6-b01824fef375.jpeg',9819141,32,'45.51579','-122.64236',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,67.00,1,1125,496,4.80,27856170),(1300,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/27856696','Charming 4BR/2BA Victorian in Heart of SE Portland','This bright and airy Victorian Home boasts 4 bedrooms and 2 full bathrooms perfect for a family or larger group traveling to Portland. Located steps from Belmont St, a few blocks from Hawthorne Blvd, Division St., and so much more! With a Walk Score of 88 you will find some of the most amazing places in Portland well within walking distance.','SE Portland is home to some of the best restaurants, hippest bars, parks, nightlife, and brunch spots Portland has to offer!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-27856696/original/d06891d7-ae9d-4f27-a08d-b986dba2aadf.jpeg',210219190,32,'45.51593','-122.64114',1,8,2.00,4.00,4.00,119.00,30,1125,376,4.79,27856696),(1301,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28002714','Zen themed private retreat in NW Portland.','Peaceful 900 sq. ft. apartment with private deck on  cul-de-sac at the edge of Forest Park. A short walk to the Alphabet District--Portland\'s trendy shopping and eating area. 1.5 miles from downtown. Spacious living area with well equipped kitchenette, dining area, large screen TV.  Large bedroom with new queen-sized bed, desk, and ample closet. Bathroom with shower/ bathtub.  Additional Japanese-style tatami room with queen-size futon available upon request for an additional $50.00/night.','Quiet, cul-de-sac street in  residential King\'s Heights with views of Mt. St. Helens, Mt. Rainier, Mt. Adams and the Willamette River. Mt. Hood is fully visible on the walk into town. There are many public staircases facilitating easy walking into town and entries to the Wildwood trail in Forest Park  taking you to various sites such as the Audubon Society, Pittock Mansion, and Washington Park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/216a19f5-ad72-4798-b389-e86c9dcddd0a.jpg',12319817,79,'45.531466105403595','-122.71173318398445',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,175.00,2,28,171,4.96,28002714),(1302,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28012054','Alberta Arts Oasis: Basil\'s Garden Room','Completely self-contained unit. Comfy, no smoking, light-filled room with a window view out onto the garden, private entrance on the drive, and a beautiful bathroom. Only entered to clean between guests, or upon request. Amenities include microwave, and mini fridge.<br /><br />All are welcome here!','This is an established residential neighborhood in the city. We are three blocks from the fun and busy Alberta Arts District. Theater, food, music, donuts, vegan, veggie, artisan shopping, you name it! New Seasons grocery is five blocks down the street. Fremont shopping district is also close by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/05eddb3f-b840-4c6a-b993-bfe4579ef1b4.jpg',132998741,46,'45.55703','-122.62949',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,1,30,499,4.97,28012054),(1303,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28073771','Posh Victorian Apt-Great location (31 day-no tax)','Gorgeous 1 bedroom apartment located in a in charming Victorian building with a popular Mexican food cart right out front and located just 2 blocks away from one of Portland\'s most popular areas~NW 23rd (Trendy-third) Avenue where you\'ll find a huge variety of coffee shops, restaurants and unique shops. A bus stop is 2 blocks away or get downtown in 6 minutes via car. Enjoy Forest Park-only a 10 minute walk away.','The NW Alphabet District offers a variety of wonderful art, clothing, yoga, coffee, specialty shops, pubs, grocery stores and restaurants.  Walking down NW 23rd Avenue is a great way to interact with Native Portlanders. Take NW 23rd Avenue all the way to Burnside Street (turn left-East) then pass Powells books and other sights all the way to Voodoo donuts and explore the waterfront to get an even better feel of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bf4a103e-e2f0-4959-8e19-15bce1dc6b24.jpg',98202133,27,'45.53837','-122.69786',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,31,730,160,4.96,28073771),(1304,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28101093','Modern urban condo in the center of everything','One bedroom bedroom condominium with a private, secured entry.  1 secured underground parking spot included.   Beautiful furnishings throughout and a private deck.  All utilities  including basic cable/wi-fi are included.  A Smart TV lets  you hook up to Hulu, Netflix.   Queen size bed comes with all linens. Bathroom comes with towels, hairdryer etc. Kitchen comes equipped with Stainless Steel Appliances, Dishwasher,  Washer/Dryer,Over Range Micro-Wave, Plates, Utensils, Pots, Pans etc','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/777f1f57-1f94-4138-9243-f0ebec569849.jpg',66668669,27,'45.5342','-122.69914',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,360,2,5.00,28101093),(1305,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28102068','AMAZING NEIGHBORHOOD IN PORTLAND!','Completely furnished, modern, private. Located in friendly, close-in Northwest Portland. This central location with a 98 Walk Score is next to some of the best restaurants, bars and cafes in town.  Full kitchen.  Private bath. Beats hotel pricing.','Close-in Northwest Portland- Nob Hill.<br /><br />This convenient location, with a 98 POINT WALK SCORE is blocks from trendy NW 23rd AVE, Dragonfly Coffee House, St. Honore Bakery, McMenamins Pub, Forest Park, a natural foods grocery store, the public library, as well as the post office. <br /><br />Window shop at all the lovely boutiques located just blocks away or hike/bike/run/explore the 80 miles of trails and over 5,000 acres of Forest Park; one of the largest urban parks in the United States! <br /><br />You can quickly and easily reach the Pearl District, the Brewery Blocks or Downtown Portland in minutes by foot, bike or streetcar; no need for a vehicle when living here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bc24fce6-b6df-48c7-8587-7b35992488ad.jpg',212276052,27,'45.53504','-122.70317',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,54.00,30,1125,15,4.13,28102068),(1306,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28103535','Executive Home-2Bed/1 BA (31 night minimum)','2 Bedroom/1 Bath Fully Furnished 1-level Single Family house!<br />The home is 3 blocks from Reed College, 4 blocks from Trader Joe\'s, 8 blocks to Crystal Springs and Eastmoreland golf course.  Also ~ 1 mile to Woodstock grocery stores, restaurants,  nightlife, etc.  <br />No car? Bus stop to downtown Portland across the street. No lodging tax for stays 31 days or longer!','Eastmoreland golf course, Crystal Springs, Woodstock Shopping and tree lined streets.  One of the SAFEST AREAS of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4f5b724e-7162-46cd-b80c-4ab152d039e1.jpg',6127388,61,'45.48344','-122.62637',1,3,1.00,2.00,2.00,90.00,31,120,0,1.00,28103535),(1307,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28151971','Handsome Craftsman Home in Heart of Hawthorne','Our beloved century old classic craftsman sits in the heart of Inner SE Portland and is half a block from Hawthorne Blvd. It\'s just steps away from vintage shops, bars, great restaurants, coffee shops, supermarkets (New Seasons and Fred Meyer), public transportation, and Powell\'s bookstore.','Hawthorne is one of the most vibrant and popular neighborhoods in Portland.  The area is known for its beautifully restored Old Portland homes, and the street is lined with locally owned restaurants and shops.  Hawthorne street itself is located between Division and Belmont St which are both lined with lots of amazing shops and eateries.  <br />Some of our favorites include Blue Star Donuts, Harlow, Waffle Window, and Powell\'s bookstore - all of which are within a block.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/425bfcff-2c1d-4275-acc2-b59e1d3f3514.jpg',405092,8,'45.51089','-122.6256',1,8,1.00,3.00,2.00,214.00,31,1125,80,4.99,28151971),(1308,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28153099','Yellow Door | Famous Mississippi Ave | Pool table','Voted best neighborhood in Portland for dining, food carts, bars, coffee and shopping! Welcome to Yellow Door, only one block behind the famous Mississippi Ave. Just a minute walk from all the action - we\'d argue being the best located Airbnb in Portland!<br /><br />This home has bright and spacious living areas. Two of the bedrooms have new and comfortable memory foam mattresses with high-quality sheets and pillows for a cozy night\'s sleep. There is also a third bedroom located downstairs.','Mississippi St. is famous for its unique bars, shops and restaurants. Enjoy wandering the neighborhood for some of the best food, coffee, cocktails and boutique shopping Portland has to offer! We are also just an 8 minute drive to Downtown Portland and 5 minutes from The Moda Center (home of the Trail Blazers).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-28153099/original/78af5ea1-8758-44a7-8cda-21378a03090c.jpeg',212650552,9,'45.55011','-122.67362',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,172.00,3,1125,170,4.95,28153099),(1309,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28188294','Modern 4BR Retreat w/Top Amenities in Prime Area','Welcome to your perfect getaway! This spacious 4-bedroom home accommodates 8 guests and boasts amenities like a fully-equipped kitchen, two living rooms, BBQ grill, and exercise equipment. Enjoy the serene backyard or relax on the patio. Nearby attractions include the Alberta Arts District, with its vibrant galleries and dining, and the scenic Peninsula Park Rose Garden. With free parking, WiFi, and essentials provided, your comfort is ensured. Book now for a memorable stay!','77 Walk Score (very walkable) / 56 Transit Score (good transit) / 100 Bike Score (biker\'s paradise)<br /><br />Piedmont is centrally located between Alberta, Mississippi, and Dekum, it\'s highly walkable. Piedmont is primarily a residential neighborhood that is near everything therefore offering the best of both worlds. It provides a peaceful living environment while ensuring easy access to essential amenities, services, and recreational opportunities.<br />The Piedmont neighborhood is a beautiful part of NE Portland and was one of the original suburbs. Peninsula Park is one of the oldest neighborhood parks in Portland and is home to the first public garden in the city. The rose garden is one of the most relaxing and picturesque green spaces in the area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/820b1bd2-25d0-4eb0-a9fa-622525b0db05.jpg',70094369,48,'45.56829','-122.6652',1,8,2.00,4.00,5.00,207.00,3,29,180,4.97,28188294),(1310,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28197448','1700+ Great Reviews! We make your choice easy','Read our reviews! We love helping people plan their visit to our city! Please be aware that unfortunately we cannot host guests with animals due to a resident\'s severe allergy.','When visiting Portland, where you stay is critical. You want to have easy access to everything. We have that. Our neighborhood is Sellwood- you can look it up online and see why it is such a desirable place to be. There are lots of antiques shops, coffee and tea houses, a Columbia Sportswear Outlet, restaurants, parks, bars, microbreweries and river access to the Willamette River all within a few blocks. We are also just minutes away from the bus and the MAX (light rail)that will take you right downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjgxOTc0NDg%3D/original/745de48b-bac9-4d77-a9b1-95f20d078e11.jpeg',8474325,20,'45.4642','-122.65305',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,1,21,66,4.94,28197448),(1311,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28226590','Daylight Basement CloseIn/Portlandia SE PDX','Come and stay in my daylight basement apartment shaded by my blueberry & herb sidewalk garden. Full remodel in the basement with a beautiful tile bathroom, gas fireplace, stained concrete floors, small exercise room, & touches of old Portland. My house is an old PDX style home in the heart of close-in SE Portland.','My house has a walking score of 92. It is within a 5 minute walk of some of the best coffee, beer, cider, and food carts in Portland. Mass transit is easy. There are two high-frequency bus lines within a couple blocks of my house and electric scooters scattered everywhere in my neighborhood. Both Free2Move (Jeeps) and Zipcars are plentiful and easy to find in my neighborhood. A large grocery store is 3 blocks away and downtown Portland is a 20 min walk across one of Portland\'s many bridges or a quick car, bus, bike, or scooter ride.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d8d9a74b-0da1-4c3d-80f6-07398cbcdee1.jpg',2135334,32,'45.51556','-122.65153',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,99.00,1,1125,419,4.92,28226590),(1312,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28253904','Chez Modern','Private modern guest house near Multnomah Village and Gabriel Park. Just 10 minutes from downtown Portland, tucked away in the SW hills on a forested half-acre property. Unit has a private driveway, a full kitchen, full bath, full laundry, 1 bedroom and a deep sofa. Heated floor, AC, rain shower. Walk or bike to bars, restaurants, shops, etc.','Known as “the village in the heart of Portland,” historic Multnomah Village delivers small town charm mere minutes from the city center. Take a stroll down streets lined with charming cafés, galleries, bars and shops. <br /><br />Also within walking distance is Gabriel Park - a 90.65-acre site with a baseball field, softball field, soccer field, basketball courts, tennis courts, skatepark, volleyball courts, disabled access play area, disabled access restrooms, dog off-leash area, paved and unpaved paths, reservable picnic sites, WiFi, and the Southwest Community Center! Which includes an indoor swimming pool, indoor basketball court, fitness room, gymnasium, rock climbing wall, weight room, kitchen, meeting room, party room, etc.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-28253904/original/2f35315c-a441-4bc8-86e4-8d22f037c743.jpeg',52327539,18,'45.46197411878365','-122.72215885164334',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,110.00,2,1125,220,4.93,28253904),(1313,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28257253','Cedar Grove','Cozy apartment in a vintage Craftsman bungalow.  Rose City Park, great neighborhood with restaurants and coffee shops in walking distance. <br />Travel to airport and freeways easily. <br />This a great spot to stay while exploring Portland.','This is a wooded neighborhood with lots of vegetation and interesting old houses. It\'s great for walking or riding a bike. There are bicycle rentals available 2 blocks from your spot. <br />Portland is divided into neighborhoods, each with its own theater, restaurants, stores. We are in Rose City Park, right up the hill from Hollywood. There are coffee shops, theaters, and restaurants nearby.  within 5 minutes are Safeway, Whole foods, Trader Joe\'s, New Seasons and Fred Meyer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1efcd0bc-fadc-47cc-979b-dcd9750587a3.jpg',24966798,11,'45.54425','-122.60149',1,4,1.00,1.00,4.00,85.00,5,1125,294,4.98,28257253),(1314,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28259767','Portland Hazelwood House','This cozy and spacious guest room is provided on your own floor with a play area, bathroom, kitchenette, TV room and laundry.  This Portland home is within a minute walk from the brand new Discovery Park, minutes walk to the grocery store, less than 10 minute walk to the train that takes you directly to and from the airport, downtown and all over Portland within 15-20 minutes.','Our neighborhood is a quiet, family-friendly and walkable neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9c8b43ad-37a4-487b-b966-e6c7b65e23e5.jpg',2801498,63,'45.53053','-122.554',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,2,90,132,4.92,28259767),(1315,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28284093','Private suite for 1–2 w/ secret patio & gas firepi','Overlooking a quiet, secluded patio, this eco-friendly retreat is perfect for solo travelers or couples. And it’s just steps from the vibrant Alberta Arts District, Killingsworth St, and Williams and Mississippi Avenues, with their breweries, bars, shops, food cart pods, and vegan eateries.<br /><br />For best rates and customer care and to see over 650 5-star reviews, discover the Patio Suite at the Portland Eco House.','LOCATION<br /><br />- The location of the Patio Suite is unbeatable. The airport and downtown Portland are just a short drive away, and Alberta Street, Williams Avenue, Mississippi Avenue, and Killingsworth Street are within walking distance, offering a plethora of locally owned restaurants, pubs, and shops.<br /><br />The central location of the Patio Suite allows for easy exploration of the stunning Columbia Gorge and Oregon Coast.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-28284093/original/cb66655c-b4a1-460a-a903-8e5b690adfbc.jpeg',6946676,24,'45.558284759521484','-122.66563415527344',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,1,21,130,4.90,28284093),(1316,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28293489','Bohemian Oasis ~ Food, Coffee & Craft Beer Lovers','If you\'re a fan of great food, craft beer, pour-over coffee, this is your place. My apartment is situated in the famous Buckman District - which neighbors many of Portland\'s top-rated restaurants and bars, vintage shops, and offers some of the best people-watching around.<br /><br />My place is great for couples, solo adventures, and business travelers. With a convenient home base within walking distance to the neighborhood hot spots, you can get an authentic taste of how the hipsters live in Stumptown.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors—no chain restaurants here! Enjoy vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or opt for an elegant night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />But Portland isn’t just for foodies. The vibrant indie spirit of Hawthorne is alive with a multitude of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques, making it a true hipster haven. Catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of recreation, head up to Mt. Tabor. This 196-acre city park, located atop a dormant volcano vent, offers miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of the city, providing a perfect escape into nature righ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-28293489/original/23be377b-f62c-4edb-8e96-a24968dd0017.jpeg',146196024,32,'45.51664','-122.64004',1,8,2.00,3.00,4.00,264.00,1,1125,540,4.88,28293489),(1317,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28307776','Margaux - Nostalgic Charmer in the Heart of PDX','Welcome to Margaux the Vintage Airstream!<br /><br />Originally built in 1969 and loving designed and restored in 2019, this light-filled space is packed with vintage character. Whether you\'re seeking to experience Portland\'s vibrant local culture, get lost in the famous PNW wilderness, or simply relax in our lush garden and take a dip in the hot tub, Margaux provides the perfect base for your Portland adventures. We can\'t wait to host you!','Welcome to the vibrant neighborhood of Foster-Powell in Southeast Portland! Nestled in the heart of the city, Foster-Powell offers a unique blend of urban energy and community charm.<br /><br />This neighborhood is known for its diverse community, eclectic mix of businesses, and welcoming atmosphere. Located just a few blocks from my property you\'ll find a variety of convenient amenities and exciting local destinations to explore. <br /><br />Grocery shopping is a breeze with Trader Joe\'s, New Seasons, Safeway, and Fred Meyer all within easy reach. <br /><br />When it comes to dining, The Mercado is a must-visit, offering a vibrant food hall experience with a variety of international flavors to choose from. Off the Griddle is perfect for a delicious breakfast or brunch, while Pizzeria Otto serves up mouthwatering wood-fired pizzas. Bar Carlo, 5 & Dime, Atlas Pizza, and Street Disco are my other walkable favorites! <br /><br />For coffee, tea, and pastries I recommend Carnelian Roasters','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/45bb3f7f-7173-4ce3-a3bb-07c7852cc7e2.jpg',4810546,36,'45.48745','-122.59009',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,50.00,1,30,448,4.89,28307776),(1318,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28340091','The Monta-Villa Garden Cottage — cats + chickens','Your cottage is private with views of the garden. It’s a unique tiny home that feels big with high ceilings, lots of natural light & warm accents. You have everything to cook most meals. There are plenty of local food, drink & shopping options nearby. Walk the neighborhood, see city highlights, visit parks, hike to falls, feed chickens, pick seasonal fruits & veggies, or just sit in the garden or covered patio with a book & a cat. This is your home away from home.','Portland is the gateway to many beautiful outdoor sites. Just a short drive away or grand views of the Columbia River Gorge, iconic waterfalls, abundant state parks, beaches, wine country, rolling countryside and more. Just ask and we can point you in the right direction. <br /><br />The true Portland experience is all about the neighborhoods and their bustling commercial cores with pubs, restaurants, shopping and more, surrounded by residential streets. <br /><br />The Montavilla neighborhood (named after the original Mt Tabor Village) is one of the top ten neighborhoods in the U.S. according to Lonely Planet. Montavilla has great restaurants, cafes, sweets shops, breweries, entertainment and shopping. Most within a 15-25 min walk. <br /><br />There are several commercial cores to explore surrounded by charming residential blocks. <br /><br />Several parks nearby have good hiking, playgrounds and golfing. <br /><br />Explore by foot, bike, bus, train or car. <br /><br />We are always ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-28340091/original/d4f3801b-c40b-465d-9b3d-4a4ac894008b.jpeg',1797565,10,'45.53430814710033','-122.58622370660305',1,3,1.00,1.00,4.00,73.00,2,45,398,4.97,28340091),(1319,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28386030','The Rose Room','Cute artsy house, not an apartment.  Close to number 6 bus line.  Street parking.  Walk to cafes. 5-8 minute bus ride to convention center.  <br />The Location is perfect, you can be almost anywhere in the city within 5-20 minutes.<br />The neighborhood is safe and there is plenty of street parking. <br /><br />NON SMOKERS  only  DO NOT REQUEST THIS ROOM IF YOU SMOKE CIGARETTES<br />1 person only  <br />Do not try to reserve for two people or have a guest in this room.','Neighborhood is safe.  It\'s peaceful and there is a good breakfast spot down the street and a sweet cafe. Nike outlet store is a a couple blocks away. Parking is easy on our street. Don\'t leave visible valuables in your car. Car break ins are a thing throughout Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-28386030/original/a57ad58b-50bf-4a27-8b56-d0ffcc781232.jpeg',2410278,26,'45.54382','-122.6612',2,1,1.00,1.00,0.00,45.00,1,6,105,4.91,28386030),(1320,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28433150','The Heart of Alberta Arts - Private Home','Located in the heart of the Alberta Arts District, this is a fully furnished, single-level home with an upstairs loft. Downstairs features a full kitchen, living area, washer-dryer, mud-room, and bathroom; upstairs is a queen bed, dresser, closets, and writing desk. Flat screen televisions on both levels with access to Hulu streaming services, a desktop computer, and a well-appointed kitchen with appliances and accessories for all your basic needs.','You can\'t get any closer than this bungalow to the bustling activity on NE Alberta, home to some of the Portland\'s most popular restaurants, cafes, shops and bars...<br /><br />~ Pine State Biscuits<br />~ Great Notion Brewing<br />~ Mole Mole Mexican Cuisine<br />~ GrindWitTryz<br />~ Ben & Esther’s Vegan Jewish Deli<br />~ Bollywood Theater<br />~ Akasaru Ramen<br />~ Proud Mary Cafe<br />~ The Hilt<br />~ Via Chicago Pizza<br />~ Salt & Straw Ice Cream<br />~ Bella Pizza<br />~ Angel\'s Donuts & Ice Cream (formerly Tonalli\'s Donuts)<br />~ Gumba<br />~ Case Study Coffee<br />~ Binks<br />~ Thai Noon<br />~ Baerlic Brewing<br />~ Hana Japanese Bistro<br />~ T.C. O’Learys<br />~ Tin Shed Garden Cafe<br />~ Petite Provence Boulangerie & Patisserie<br />~ Bamboo Sushi<br />~ Radio Room<br />~ Zilla Sake House<br />~ The Bye and Bye (vegan)<br />~ El Nutri Taqueria<br />~ The Hilt<br />~ New Seasons Market<br /><br />... and, with a WALK SCORE of 88 and BIKE SCORE of 99, our home\'s proxim','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7eb066dd-c199-441c-a7d1-f8d525a6f631.jpg',51953429,29,'45.55951','-122.6431',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,125.00,1,10,510,4.95,28433150),(1321,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28443494','The Belmont Birdhouse, Steps From Mt Tabor Park','This space is FOR ADULTS ONLY, perfect for couples or 2 singles.<br /><br />Assistance animals and pets are not accepted due to allergies.<br /><br />Rest and recharge in this thoughtfully designed, vintage inspired retreat. A clean, quiet, and comfortable space to relax and unwind after a day of exploring.<br /><br />Whether you decide to lounge around the house or head out for adventure, this home has the best of both worlds with everything you need in a great location.','Mt. Tabor Park is a quick 6 min walk from the house with beautiful natural forest trails. Great for running, hiking or forest bathing and has the best night time view of the city, in my opinion. The sunsets are magical!<br /><br />The Mt. Tabor neighborhood is quiet and one of the safest in Portland, great for strolling around and admiring the grand old Portland homes under towering old-growth evergreens. Mt Tabor is surrounded by Belmont, Hawthorne, Division, Laurelhurst, Foster/Powell(FOPO) & Montavilla districts to name a few. Each has its own unique culture and offers the best coffee shops, cafes, restaurants, shopping and nightlife that Southeast Portland has to offer. The nearby freeway is .8 miles from the house so you\'ll have quick and easy access to any other part of the city and beyond.<br /><br />DISTANCE TO LOCAL ATTRACTIONS: <br />* Stark Street Station Coffee: 2 blocks/5 min walk<br />* The Belwether Bar: 2 blocks/5 min walk<br />* Blind Onion Pizza: 1 block/2 min walk<br','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b19afc44-8c5c-45da-bdbc-c629fc1168c4.jpg',5941807,15,'45.51616','-122.60309',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,246.00,2,12,88,4.98,28443494),(1322,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28492222','Industrial 2nd Story Living W/Private Deck NE 28th','PERFECT FAMILY/GROUP SPOT! The space is over 1,400 SQ FT! The private deck is 250 Sq Ft.  Welcome to our cozy inner city loft-like space with open concept living and huge open kitchen dining area. <br /><br />Walk Score: 89<br />Bike Score: 97<br /><br />Could sleep 8. We offer two bedrooms and a bonus room/office with a sofa that pulls out into a twin mattress, two couches and a blow up mattress. <br /><br />The outdoor bistro lights give it the perfect ambience in the evening. Patio includes firepit, eating area & BBQ.','In the heart of Sullivan\'s Gulch. A nice park with large grass field and playset for kids is literally across the street. You are in the heart of NE PDX. Along 28th Ave you will find some of the best restaurants, coffee, and dessert! This location is within walking distance to major stores, parks, coffee shops, ice cream shops and more. Only minutes from I-84 and 9 mins from downtown driving.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/af9ac81a-5c78-44ce-895e-1cec86f89b32.jpg',106844415,4,'45.5331','-122.63714',1,5,1.00,3.00,3.00,135.00,1,28,213,4.86,28492222),(1323,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28493203','Multnomah Hidden Pond - stunning upscale romantic!','Our B&B is an *experience* and not just a place to spend the night.  Situated in the coveted neighborhood of Multnomah Village, this is a super romantic garden cottage style gem.  Here, you will feel like royalty sleeping in the carved mahogany four-poster QUEEN SIZE bed, embraced by an amazing mattress, and surrounded by designer bed colors, prints and toss pillows.  You will find a gorgeous,  top-notch tiled bathroom, a modern beautiful kitchen and many delightful surprises..','Quaint. Charming. A bit off-center and quintessentially Portland. Call it what you will, southwest Portland’s Multnomah Village is filled with character – as well as dozens of unique shops, galleries, restaurants, a wine bar and a brewpub.<br />Annual events include the Multnomah Days Parade and ensuing street fair on the 3rd Saturday in August, an afternoon Halloween in the Village and Holiday Gala on the First Friday and Saturday of December.  So get over here and see what all the fuss is about!<br />There is a very close-by gym in the Mittleman Jewish Community Center, located at 6651 SW Capitol Hwy.  It costs $15/day to use the gym.  Their hours are:  Mon-Thur 6am-10pm, Fri 6am-9pm and Sat-Sun 8am-6pm.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/83c8e014-1508-4772-9017-27402236d838.jpg',37575586,18,'45.47178','-122.70281',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,93.00,1,1125,351,4.92,28493203),(1324,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28564991','Willamette River View Condo Near Downtown Portland','Executive condo rental-<br />Spacious one bedroom condo with Willamette River view  <br /><br />Resort like setting with the convenience of downtown Portland, Lake Oswego and OHSU. Just five minutes from the hustle and bustle of the city.  Stroll along the river path just steps from your door.  Covered  patio with an unobstructed view of the river.  <br /><br />High speed internet. Access to sauna, pool and hot tub. Covered parking included. <br /><br />No smoking, no pets<br />Walking distant to neighborhood restaurants.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a07df484-90b1-40d6-a6a2-48e24cc268fd.jpg',127774398,22,'45.48661','-122.67395',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,180,1,5.00,28564991),(1325,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28663623','Cozy Studio in Brooklyn','COZY STUDIO in house with separate entrance. Cozy and quiet space in very convenient inner SE neighborhood. Convenient to bus and MAX trains to downtown or OHSU','The neighborhood is very quiet. The street is a dead end on both sides. We are walking distance to coffee shops, bars & restaurants. We are also close to OHSU and downtown is just across the river. Or if you’re looking for a little bit of nature, Oaks Bottom park is about 1 mile away - makes for a nice jog in the park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/36e9d4bc-b999-43e6-945d-5d8bfdf45650.jpg',176661808,56,'45.50072','-122.6602',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,85.00,2,1125,204,4.98,28663623),(1326,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28687064','Peaceful Humble Abode','Dog friendly home in one of the best neighborhoods in Portland!  One block from Fernhill Park (dog park, playground, tennis courts, track, playing fields).  Walking distance to KISS Coffee, the McMenamin\'s Kennedy School (movie theater, restaurants, bars, game room, soaking pool), New Season\'s Market, the Alberta Arts District as well as Extracto, Dame and Wilder.  Just a 10 minute drive to the airport, downtown, NW 23rd, SE Hawthorne and Division streets.  Private and quiet backyard!','So many places in the neighborhood that are accessible by bike, a short walk or a quick drive.  Fernhill Park is just a block away and has a playground, off-leash dog park, tennis courts, running track and playing fields.  A great coffee and breakfast place within walking distance is KISS coffee.  If you want to catch up a movie, soak in a heated pool all year round, grab drinks and food or play pool or shuffleboard, the McMenamin\'s Kennedy School is also within walking distance.  Family-owned New Season\'s Market is within walking distance as well as the Alberta Arts District and some other great places on Killingsworth and NE 30th.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-28687064/original/ed654351-417d-4ccc-89d6-f4faabf5531b.jpeg',168060332,1,'45.5682','-122.62597',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,20,4.85,28687064),(1327,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28720554','Little Gem House close to Mississippi & Williams','PLEASE READ our description and guidelines below to see if we’re a good fit. :)<br />My protocol: If you request to book, I will send a message with some points to confirm. Be available to respond about them within 24 hours (the time Airbnb allows for requests). Then I can either accept or decline your booking. Thanks!','We are a 7 minute walk to the Mississippi Ave food carts, restaurants, shops, music, bars. We are also about a 15 minute walk to The Williams District where more restaurants, bars and shopping are. The Alberta Arts district is about a 25 minute walk for more delicious food, art events, music and night life. The Max station is about a 15 minute walk, the bus station about a 5 minute walk and the city bike rental is a 7 minute walk away too. So much to do and see right nearby in walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6ec31b4c-5088-41fb-978e-4b85b22c645e.jpg',149028,24,'45.55732','-122.67267',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,125.00,2,28,55,4.96,28720554),(1328,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28833457','Stunning Artistic ADU in Gated In City Sanctuary','Stunning, modern, charming guest house in a gated sanctuary in inner city NE Portland in the popular Alberta/Cully neighborhood.   Tranquil, private and elegant location, close to stores, cafes, restaurants and bars.  \"Moondance\"  has the feel of an artist\'s studio, rather than the Hyatt.  Air conditioned. Gas Fireplace.  Clawfoot Tub. Exceptional gardens. Temperpedic King Size Bed.  Read the reviews! They say \"amazing!\"','Bordering on the iconic ALBERTA ARTS DISTRICT and close to multiple sources of transportation.  The Cully Neighborhood is becoming one of the most sought after places to live in Portland.  This is a quiet residential street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9caf1631-b36e-4689-810f-1110a840381d.jpg',217425750,21,'45.55581','-122.60954',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,76,4.93,28833457),(1329,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28869509','The Sunshine House (OHSU/South Waterfront area)','Cute, cheerful, and cozy apartment in our 1889 yellow Lair Hill Victorian home. 1 bedroom, 1 bath (746 sq ft) with a full kitchen, washer/dryer, and very speedy internet. Private setting on garden level with private entrance on the side. Suitable for up to 2 adults. 1 block from Gibbs St pedestrian bridge, OHSU, aerial tram, streetcar, and South Waterfront. Easy parking in front of the house. Perfect for short term OHSU people!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3ab5c17e-91f2-4da2-a281-3f8c5cfb0af0.jpg',994334,22,'45.50108','-122.67548',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,90,95,102,4.89,28869509),(1330,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28918730','Premium Waterfront Condo, Great Views, w/ Parking','Full one bedroom Condo, no Sharing.  Beautiful views of Willamette river with Secure Off-Street parking.   Walking distance to everywhere in the Pearl District, Waterfront, and Downtown Portland .  Condo is fully prepared for long stay guests including Washer and Dryer.  City bike rental places outside of complex as well. Unbeatable value.<br /><br />Outdoor Pool and Hot Tub are fully open now.  <br />*** The HOA has 30 night minimum stay requirement ** PLEASE BOOK FOR 31 DAYS TO AVOID TOURIST TAXES**','McCormick Pier Condos are spread between Broadway and Steel Bridges in the most prime waterfront area with easy access to Max Lightrail, lots of jogging and walking trails and close to shopping and awesome Pearl District restaurants and shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-28918730/original/3a3649b6-6613-43aa-85d5-466dc085726c.jpeg',27903183,43,'45.53119','-122.67515',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,30,1125,10,5.00,28918730),(1331,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28986964','The Wolf Den: cozy and clean apartment in NoPo','The Wolf Den is a cozy lower-level apartment (stairs/non ADA) offering a private, quiet respite within walking distance of Kenton neighborhood attractions. Get to know the neighborhood or enjoy easy access to Portland city center (15 minute drive, bus/bike routes), PDX airport (20 minute drive), or the great outdoors of the Pacific Northwest wonderland. Residential setting with easy, off-street parking, self check-in, and quick access to what Portland (and the surrounding areas) have to offer.','Kenton is a quaint neighborhood located in North Portland. Highlights include restaurants Po\'Shines Cafe, Swift and Union, Posie\'s Coffee and Bakery, Pizza Fino\'s and fun shopping like Mantel, Speck\'s Records, Kenton Antiques + Collectibles, Salvage Works, and Bamboo Craftsman. Up your Portland experience by getting a haircut and shave at Bart\'s Barbershop or a tattoo at The Hive Tattoo.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/41987277-b458-46b0-802b-55464152051e.jpg',5575780,55,'45.58202','-122.70166',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,2,31,53,4.98,28986964),(1332,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29126487','4B2bRemodel Craftsman:Porches/Town/Grant/Irvington','Welcome to \"Portlandia\" Remodel!  <br /><br />Portland requires 30 days+ rental and restrict Vacation Rentals so we are looking for a longer-term guest.<br /><br />Perfect Vacation, Temporary Housing, Executives, Traveling Nurses, Back-Up Home<br /><br />Walking Score of 90!  <br /><br />Biker\'s Paradise (92)<br /><br />Super cool Irvington neighborhood with:<br />-Broadway Street<br />-Restaurants & Bars<br />-Supermarkets & Shops <br />-Minutes to Downtown<br />-Rose Garden Arena<br />-Close to Transportation','In a super cool Irvington neighborhood that is 5-10 minutes to Downtown with: <br /> <br />- Broadway Streets <br /> <br />- Restaurants & Bars <br /> <br />- Supermarkets & Shops <br /> <br />- Minutes from Downtown <br /> <br />- Rose Garden Arena','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2d9a8bb6-94d0-41a8-91b4-d1461b90b420.jpg',2503251,33,'45.53595','-122.63387',1,16,2.00,5.00,14.00,120.00,30,730,4,5.00,29126487),(1333,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29129259','Cozy Camper in Wooded SW Neighborhood','Cozy camper space with access to a hip house.  It\'s like camping on the edge of the city- including having to walk to the toilet (only 30\').  Very near charming Multnomah Village,  lovely wooded and open parks, OHSU and VA.  10 minutes to downtown.','We are at the end of a dead end street with lots of beautiful trees around.  There\'s a grassy water tower park within a short walk.  And if you walk just a little further there is a wooded park with a stream running through it year round and a small playground. <br /><br />The charming Multnomah Village is 1 1/4 miles away with variety of restaurants, cafes and interesting small shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/516e14f6-0584-416e-aeb8-afc382ac3a7f.jpg',112893366,86,'45.45909','-122.7005',1,1,1.00,1.00,0.00,24.00,30,120,66,4.76,29129259),(1334,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29158406','*Spacious Centrally Located Basement Studio','This is a great home base for your northwest experience or a stop along the way as you travel through.  We are 15 minutes from the airport, downtown, and a few minutes from 1-5.  <br /><br />Ample street parking available.','What makes this neighborhood great is it is easy to access just about everything!<br />If you want to stay hyper-local:<br />- walk a few minutes to one of the best parks in the city, Penisula Park Rose Garden<br />- New Seasons Market and Fred Meyer are also within walking distance<br />- The lively Mississippi/Williams district is a mile south. There you will find award-winning restaurants, bars, live music, and shopping.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3c17d87c-62ae-4cb6-8c5f-ea692d80742d.jpg',155811819,48,'45.57417','-122.67712',1,4,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,2,30,100,4.90,29158406),(1335,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29159055','Traveler\'s Haven! Rated Top 7 Hospitable PDX Host','Our home is a welcome haven for families and professionals desiring a comfortable and meticulously clean place to work and be together. Feel at home in this smartly remodeled and spotless sanctuary filled with character for your Portland retreat. Steps from quaint Kenton Park and local restaurants, taprooms, and coffee shops. A short walk to the Max light rail station takes you downtown in 20 minutes. Conveniently located for day trips to the coast, mountains, and incredible waterfalls.','The historic town of Kenton in North Portland was built near the confluence of several rail lines, along the Columbia River, so shipping was very convenient for the businesses that settled here back in the day. Today, it is a lovely community with a vibrant history. Kenton\'s business district is a 7-minute walk from the house, offering your pick of restaurants, shops, and services, including a bank, library, bike shop, barber, tattoo shop, and post office. The quaint business district and idyllic park setting with walking paths and an impressive new playground make the Kenton neighborhood enjoyable for everyone.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-29159055/original/f3c49690-805c-46af-b163-cecad04a9d4d.jpeg',18479582,55,'45.58613','-122.69363',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,122.00,1,1125,231,4.99,29159055),(1336,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29159242','West End  Loft','This iconic building is designed by Skylab Architecture in Portland\'s West End. The West end has become one of the best destinations for dining and entertainment in the city. All within walking distance of most urban zones. The building hosts James Beard award winning Chef\'s Greg and Gaby\'s Bistro Agnes and Kask Bar, as well as Heart Coffee, And Gold and Arrow Salon. The walk up studio unit has a secure entry through a landscaped courtyard and features an outdoor patio','Dolly Olive Restaurant , Never Coffee, Multnomah Whiskey Library, Crystal Ballroom, Ace hotel, Poler, Powells Books, Bamboo Sushi, Whole Foods, and City Target are all nearby','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7adba9ac-7f00-4cf8-9e29-a5254435f0b6.jpg',210522729,44,'45.52185','-122.68348',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,150.00,30,1125,151,4.76,29159242),(1337,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29160603','The Sparrow on Pine ::: close in SE Portland','This cozy vintage home is classy & clean with refinished wood floors, warm wood & period lighting. Main level has a charming living room, gas fireplace, large kitchen, dining room, 2 bedrooms & 1 bath. Kitchen is well equipped-gas range, microhood, fridge, dishwasher. Downstairs hosts a large den, 1 bonus/office room, large storage room with laundry. Empty detached garage & coveted off-street parking in long driveway. Large yard/patio. Heating, cooling & Smart thermostat.','Amazing location in the center of the Eastside. All the good stuff is nearby--Laurelhurst Theater, some of the best restaurants in town (seriously), cart pods, Whole Foods market, great schools (Buckman/Hosford/Cleveland), breweries, Laurelhurst Park, Lone Fir Pioneer Cemetery, bike routes & easy transportation. Downtown commute?--no problem. Your only real decision will be which direction to head out the door for an excellent bite to eat.<br /><br />BUCKMAN NEIGHBORHOOD AMENITIES ~<br />GROCERY STORES:<br />0.4 miles to Whole Foods<br />0.7 miles to Providore Fine Foods<br />1.0 mile to Fred Meyers<br />1.7 miles to Trader Joe\'s<br /><br />COFFEE:<br />0.3 miles to Crema Coffee + Bakery<br />0.3 miles to Heart Coffee<br />0.4 miles to Starbucks<br /><br />RESTAURANTS & BARS:<br />0.2 miles to Screen Door<br />0.2 miles to Tusk<br />0.2 miles to Luce<br />0.2 miles to Ken\'s Artisan Pizza<br />0.2 miles to Bamboo Sushi<br />0.3 miles to Gorges Beer Co.<br />0.4 miles to The Goodfoot<br ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjkxNjA2MDM%3D/original/d8669dd4-aee9-483f-97ce-131c2ab6542d.jpeg',1197739,32,'45.52091','-122.64208',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,110.00,31,360,5,5.00,29160603),(1338,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29181876','Marianna Condo','This historic condominium has been tastefully updated and furnished with contemporary flair. It has a full kitchen with a small bar for dining. There is a laundry room with drawers for additional storage. The bathroom has a shower and clawfoot tub. Curtained glass doors to be bedroom can be opened if tenant prefers a studio space or closed if you prefer a private bedroom.  There a dedicated parking space in the lot behind the building and limited street parking. Easy walk to downtown and PSU.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6b889bf5-1a2f-4aef-8d32-c30