rd Homes Tour, Weird Portland United, HGTV\'s \"Look What I Did!\" & \"That\'s Clever!\", AOL\'s \"My Unique House,\" KGW-TV (Portland), KING-5 Evening (Seattle).','We are located in Southeast Portland, in the Mt. Scott-Arleta neighborhood.<br /><br />The house is a short walk from lovely Mt. Scott Park. We are close to up-and-coming SE Foster Road, the Lents neighborhood, and the Woodstock neighborhood. <br /><br />We\'re just a few blocks from Shango cannabis dispensary, Lion\'s Eye Tavern, Joy Teriyaki, Cha Lua Deli, Portland Mercado, and so much more.<br /><br />We are conveniently located near many transportation options, parks, restaurants, and shops, as you\'ll see in the Guidebook.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-29305336/original/0d327091-d1c3-4ddc-9764-3743f5d54d59.jpg',220757080,65,'45.48195','-122.57952',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,78.00,1,7,111,4.89,29305336),(1342,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29315790','North Portland Private Studio with Jacuzzi tub','Our studio offers a private entrance, for you to come and go as you please, with all the comforts of home you need. We are conveniently located near the Piedmont and Kenton neighborhoods in North Portland. We are also a short drive from the popular Mississippi, and Alberta Arts Districts. There are many restaurants, bars and public transportation all within walking distance.','We live in a cute, and safe neighborhood. There are restaurants, bars, coffee shops, and parks all within walking distance of our home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b6ea4471-d6f5-4f74-a028-e970236e84fe.jpg',29407157,48,'45.57601','-122.67146',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,63.00,2,30,411,4.95,29315790),(1343,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29335562','Spacious Basement Suite in SE Portland','Private basement suite including one bedroom, small bathroom, living room and kitchenette. Living room has couch, a handful of games and TV with Hulu and Netflix. The couch pulls out to a bed for quality lounging or additional sleeping space for extra guests. <br /><br />Private back entrance, accessed through side fence. Backyard, including fire pit, is available for guest use. Kitchenette includes full fridge, toaster oven, microwave, coffee maker, hot water kettle, and single induction burner.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e536c80a-ba2d-4996-a1d0-99cd9098573d.jpg',4540216,72,'45.47664','-122.57302',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,4,46,4.98,29335562),(1344,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29362623','Comfortable. Close to Downtown. Sleeps 4.','This 2-story 1690 sq. ft. townhome was built in 2012, and is equipped with central air. The first floor has an open floor plan with a living area, dining area with a table that expands to seat 10, kitchen, half bath, gas fireplace, and, washer/dryer. The living room opens to a pleasant deck with a natural gas grill and a bistro table. Both the living area and the master bedroom have a 55” HDTV with Dish Satellite.','The townhome is in a quiet residential neighborhood with access to major thoroughfares offering easy travel to shopping, restaurants, neighborhoods and many Portland attractions.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8ab45ab1-51fc-4a31-bdcf-bf380b86328e.jpg',26630104,31,'45.46599','-122.69752',1,4,2.50,2.00,2.00,110.00,30,80,18,5.00,29362623),(1345,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29362745','Modern Studio in 1920s Cottage at \'The Orchard.\'','I\'m a British Creative and have travelled the world,  before settling in the most beautiful place of all, Oregon. With a love of nature, mountains and adventures I have found our happy place here in our 1920s English-style home. We have written a manual to share with you all of our favourite places to eat, wineries, and trails to run in Portland.  Can\'t wait to have you come stay with us.','Multnomah Village<br />Known as “the village in the heart of Portland,” historic Multnomah Village delivers small town charm mere minutes from the city center. Hop aboard TriMet Bus 44 or take a walk to reach our quaint Southwest Portland suburb, where you can stroll down streets lined with charming cafés, galleries, bars and shops.<br /><br />EAT<br />Locals rejoiced when Portland’s beloved wood-fired pizza cart Tastebud chose Multnomah Village for its first brick-and-mortar location in 2015. Visit the cozy restaurant for seasonally inspired small plates, salads and pizzas piled with fresh ingredients like arugula raab, roasted celery root and local bee pollen. It’s a short walk from the house and the pizza is on par to something you would find in Rome. The pizzas are huge and the glasses of wine are very generous.<br />Wake up with a hot cup of coffee and a fresh croissant at Grand Central Bakery, known for its rustic breads, made-from-scratch pastries and hearty sandwiches. Another ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MjkzNjI3NDU%3D/original/524e5512-0ec1-454c-abd1-5b7f2814423f.png',9042332,18,'45.46183','-122.71856',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,90.00,30,60,94,4.91,29362745),(1346,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29415372','Cozy Private Guest House Close to Southeast\'s Best','Unwind and experience Portland through our cozy and comfortable Guest House equipped with a full kitchen. Just a few blocks from Mt Tabor Park, this abode is the perfect stop for the casual traveler and makes a great home-base for longer term renters','South Tabor is a beautiful neighborhood with plenty of nature, culture, and in a great location to experience all Portland has to offer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2512fcad-6386-44d9-a579-2f5a4ef13a8a.jpg',221580026,36,'45.4973','-122.60385',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,90,112,4.71,29415372),(1347,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29482554','Modern 1 B Grant Park/Hollywood','Newly built daylight lower level apartment with beautiful patio in the heart of vibrant NE Portland.  Perfect for 1-2 guests.  Modern high end finishes and natural light. Ideal location to explore everything Portland has to offer.  3 blocks from the Hollywood district with its iconic Hollywood Theater and Grant Park.  Walk to MAX, 4 grocery stores , bars & restaurants. On Saturdays the Hollywood Farmers Market is a bustling array of fresh produce, flowers and prepared foods.  Very walkable area.','Wonderful Grant Park neighborhood located just off the intersection of NE Broadway and Sandy Boulevards.  Walk to the park, restaurants or grocery stores.  This is an upscale neighborhood with owner occupied homes.  A wonderful place to recharge from your travels.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/257cf4fb-f41d-4195-9270-73f319c1bc72.jpg',294378,33,'45.53596','-122.62624',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,99.00,5,180,34,4.91,29482554),(1348,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29492921','Newly Built Guesthouse with Private Courtyard','Newly built one-bedroom guesthouse with charming private backyard in the popular Maplewood neighborhood. Light-filled, open floor plan with vaulted ceilings. Walk to Maplewood Coffee & Tea. Located 1 ½ miles from Multnomah Village, 3-4 miles from downtown Portland, Lewis & Clark College and OHSU, 7 miles from Nike. Easy day trips to the Oregon Coast, Columbia River Gorge, Mt Hood, and Yamhill County’s Wine Country.<br /><br />ASTR Permit #18-220704-HO','Maplewood Coffee & Tea is one block away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/270b44ac-9540-4b75-8613-823141857707.jpg',111041622,75,'45.47416','-122.73002',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,129.00,2,29,287,5.00,29492921),(1349,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29566252','Hawthorne Haven-Full kitchen, bathroom, & laundry','Our 400 sqare foot fully furnished studio is tucked away in the popular Hawthorne area of SE Portland.  Less than 10 min drive to downtown, with a walk score of 91 and a bike score of 99, the neighborhood is quiet but allows access to everything including groceries, dining, shopping, and entertainment. We are within walking distance to many of the most popular establishments in Portland.','Popular streets nearby include Hawthorne, Belmont, and Division. Several great dining options are available within walking distance, which include but aren’t limited to, excellent food cart pods. Favorite restaurants of locals and visitors alike include Jam, Por Que No, and Apizza Scholls. Enjoy a meal and movie at the historic Baghdad Theater or music performances at the famous Hawthorne Theater. You might also like shopping in several locally owned boutiques and gift shops right in town!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3c8861eb-fe54-4a8f-bcb5-b57ab13aca79.jpg',222596780,32,'45.51409','-122.63757',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,74.00,4,60,183,4.96,29566252),(1350,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29592050','Fresh & Modern, Spacious 1 Bed/1 Bath Condo','Large, modern 700 sq ft condo with private entrance & lots of natural light. Free washer & dryer, A/C, and king-size memory foam bed. <br /><br />Cook’s kitchen with quartz countertops & full size appliances.  Lovely outdoor stone patio with picnic table. <br /><br />We\'re excited to host you at our Earth Advantage energy efficient home that\'s convenient to downtown,  the airport, and many nearby restaurants. Just steps away from walking paths on Mt. Tabor with panoramic views!','This neighborhood is quiet and peaceful yet close to the amazing amenities that make Portland unique. Our community is safe with friendly neighbors. You can easily reach the many restaurants and bars on Division St and Hawthorne Ave. Mt Tabor is within walking distance and is a fantastic hike with views of the whole city that you won\'t want to miss.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f5565893-e9e8-43cd-8f8d-01be1bd1d1d0.jpg',19605982,37,'45.50507','-122.59567',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,68.00,2,1125,358,4.91,29592050),(1351,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29608767','Luxe private clean studio in Concordia by Alberta','This light-filled studio is the perfect place to call home while you explore all Portland has to offer. Just minutes away from the heart of the popular Alberta Arts district, you can explore restaurants and shops as you please. Downtown PDX and posh NW is a 15-minute drive away, and easily accessible by public transportation. Mount Hood, the Coast, and the Columbia River Gorge are close enough for a leisurely day trip. The airport is a short jaunt away.','We\'re within 10 miles of every single restaurant on Eater\'s \"best restaurants in Portland\" list:, and only 7 miles of every single restaurant on Eater\'s \"2018 hottest restaurants in Portland\" list.<br /><br />We are just four blocks from the iconic Kennedy School, which features a movie theater, soaking pool, and bar and restaurant options. We are steps from one of Portland’s best parks- perfect for when you want to take a leisurely stroll around the neighborhood.<br /><br />We are a quick 15-minute drive to the heart of downtown Portland, and just 30 minutes to the Columbia River Gorge.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/daa96e03-e892-4b28-9cbb-98799b93e12b.jpg',19594248,1,'45.56461','-122.62476',1,4,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,1,29,117,4.91,29608767),(1352,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29610737','Mid-Century Modern Ranch on Arbor Lodge Treeway','1952 Mid-century Scandi-modern Ranch in the heart of Arbor Lodge along Omaha Treeway. <br /><br />The home is bright, airy & stylish with newly renovated kitchen and bath. <br /><br />Thoughtfully appointed with new & vintage mid-century details, modern conveniences and local flair.','North Portland\'s Arbor Lodge is a blend of quiet residential with the convenience of nearby entertainment. <br /><br />Walkable to:<br />Parks (Arbor Lodge Park, Gammans City Park)<br />Groceries (New Seasons, couple of corner markets)<br />Coffee (Arbor Lodge Coffee, Blend, Grindhouse)<br />Food (mlk glass market, Sushi, Thai, Spitz, Pizza, Mexican, Backyard Social)<br />Drinks (Old Gold, Barlow Tavern, Backyard Social, Mac Wine Cellars, more!)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/800134b1-e688-40b3-9080-337f9c03b8ee.jpg',1777366,51,'45.56936','-122.69133',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,38,4.97,29610737),(1353,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29610811','Bright Loft','Bright loft in artist community: walking distance to MAX Lines, restaurants, bars, farmer\'s market, and shops.<br /><br />NOTE: Washer and dryer are located in the basement (there\'s an elevator).','*It is a 10-minute walk to the Montavilla Stark Street that is host to a farmer\'s market, restaurants, bars, and shops. <br />*Community rooftop deck. <br />*Community garden space. <br />*Art gallery space. Shared shop space. <br />*Milepost 5 condos are true live/work--live in it, run a business out of it, use it as studio space. <br />*Milepost 5 Lofts is a community designed for artists and creatives located in the Montavilla neighborhood. <br />*Additional studio space available to rent.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-29610811/original/e59865a7-41bf-415d-b04b-797f90f687e3.jpeg',85235637,10,'45.53007','-122.58005',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,94.00,180,730,0,1.00,29610811),(1354,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29687631','Close-in Private getaway in the trees.','Come relax in our private one bedroom fort inspiring house in the trees. Eclectic and creative, this stay is an entrance to the Portland experience. Cozy textiles for you to rest your head while natural light welcomes your mornings. Close to Alberta Arts District, Mississippi and Kenton; our neighborhood offers foodie-dining, unique shopping, casual night-life and more. All keeping you as adventurous as your hearts content. <br />#WoodlawnFort','Woodlawn is a diverse family neighborhood with a blend of schools, casual nightlife and a variety of restaurants. Blocks to the bus stop, park, food, drinks and church. Dekum Triangle, our neighborhood gathering spot, offers restaurants, a cafe, brewery, yoga, dance hall, cannabis store, and a vintage goods shop. This area also hosts our seasonal Woodlawn Farmer\'s Market! All of this within easy walking distance. <br /><br />Up the street is one of my every day faves, P\'s & Q\'s, a quant eclectic grocery/deli/cafe blend. Perfect for grabbing a bite or a bottle of wine and a loaf of local bread. Alberta Co-op (my fave) and Safeway is nearby for your larger grocery store needs. <br /><br />2 blocks away is the Woodlawn City Park: basketball courts, baseball field, playground, amphitheater style seating area, summertime water kid play feature. Wonderful park to organize small outdoor gatherings if you\'re in town to visit with others!<br /><br />Located close to the Alberta Arts District, M','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fa4ab1a3-f2b8-4a68-93bd-63ba6393a833.jpg',10954552,45,'45.57578','-122.64983',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,77.00,2,29,592,4.93,29687631),(1355,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29732656','Tucked Inn Cully','Lovely, light-filled, peaceful, spacious, newly built sanctuary cottage w/small enclosed, private backyard in quaint neighborhood.  <br />Amenities: heated concrete floors, queen bed, washer/dryer, rain shower, skylights, wifi, parking, workspace, TV, kitchen, fan, air conditioner, shared hot tub.<br />Walk/bike/bus to shops, bars & restaurants on Fremont & Sandy to enjoy the local fare and vibe.<br />By car: 10 min to PDX, 5-7 min to Hollywood & Alberta Districts, 15-20 min to Downtown, Pearl, NW Districts.','Surrounding Roseway/Cully neighborhood is garden-like and friendly with local spots and parks to walk to. Coffee options, food carts, breweries, outdoor bars, breakfast spots, take out food are all within walking distance (w/in 1 mile).  <br />Bike on beautiful, dedicated biking greenways to access neighborhoods throughout Portland.  Our neighborhood straddles new and old Portland - you will find a fun mix of new hot spots and older establishments.<br /><br />Within 1 Mile:  <br />Groceries: Safeway (Whole Foods and Trader Joes 1.5 miles away) <br /><br />Coffee & Bakery: Bison Coffee, Pip\'s, Jim & Patty\'s Coffee, Grand Central Bakery, Starbucks, Ben & Esther\'s Vegan Jewish Deli.<br /><br />Food: Peters, Fire on the Mountain, Bang Bang, Chaba Thai, Mekah Vietnamese, Red Sauce Pizza, Happy Day Juice, Hi-Top Tavern, Little Griddle, Amalfi\'s Italian, Noho\'s Hawaiian, Clyde\'s Prime Rib, Pizzeria Otto and much more!<br /><br />Vegans: There are numerous vegan options within a few miles radi','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f6e92ec4-1463-483a-86d3-c3f2d47c3047.jpg',189099,39,'45.55055','-122.59927',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,1,14,250,4.91,29732656),(1356,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29736134','Stunning Views--Hot tub--10 min to Downtown','Just 10 minutes from downtown, our 3000 sq ft newly remodeled home has great views of the Willamette River and Mt Hood and is close to Willamette Park, Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge, and the Willamette Greenway/Springwater Corridor. We are a short walk from popular restaurants, coffeeshops, food carts, brew pubs, wine shops, grocery stores, yoga studios, and more!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/655a419f-e367-48ab-aaee-c6b67aa40c4b.jpg',5223057,22,'45.47118','-122.67417',1,8,3.00,3.00,3.00,228.00,2,30,53,4.98,29736134),(1357,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29762350','Portland-Queen bed','Located in the Multnomah Village neighborhood of Portland Oregon, our historic 1914 home offers a private bedroom with comfortable queen bed on 2nd floor.','Our home sits on a safe street and is close to almost everything.  A couple blocks away is The shops and dining og Multnomah Village.  Gabriel Park with plenty of space to roam, playground, basketball court, and tennis courts is 1.5 miles away.  A short drive (10-15 minutes can take you almost anywhere in metro Portland) will take you to downtown, Hawthorne, Lake Oswego, the Alberta Arts district, Mississippi area, & more. Throughout Portland, there are numerous brewpubs, restaurants, shops, & more.  Also, the Convention Center is only 10 minutes away.  And, if you like to stroll, less than 1/2 mile away is many local restaurants, coffee shops, local bars, and some fun shops. Its also less than 1/4 mile to the bus stop which will take you into downtown &