public transportation and cafes an easy walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9ded4d4c-c0ff-4fd7-bc26-804868ac18ce.jpg',152202888,56,'45.50095','-122.66052',1,8,3.00,4.00,5.00,299.00,2,30,182,4.95,29827564),(1360,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29830843','Historic remodeled home in Laurelhurst Portland','Amazing Historical Laurelhurst Neighborhood  historical home! Built in 1914 and  Completely REBUILT and REMODELED LUXURY 3000 sq foot house with 5 bedrooms / 3.5 baths only 5 min from downtown Portland, and steps away from the famed Hollywood District. check with me on reservations or inquiries for any Portland concert venue / restaurant or bar! I provide discounts with MadHousePDX <br /><br />Open Floor plan w/ a gourmet kitchen & enormous island<br />Amazing outdoor deck for relaxing. <br />Ideal PDX experience!','Historic quiet ideal Portland neighborhood of Laurelhurst. One of the premiere areas to live and raise a family in the entire PDX metro area. With the quintessential feel of Portland, with various parks (Laurelhurst & Grant), the Hollywood shopping and eating district literally feet away, and immediate access to I-84 to explore and commute to any Portland / Oregon area within minutes. Keep in mind located in urban setting with outstanding transportation access! however backyard is susceptible to urban / road noise','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7d1d146c-f48d-4219-b0ff-9cece4f5dade.jpg',57471246,23,'45.53306','-122.62497',1,12,3.50,5.00,9.00,201.00,30,730,250,4.94,29830843),(1361,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29851448','Portland-KING bed','Located in the Multnomah Village neighborhood of Portland Oregon, our historic 1914 home offers a private bedroom with comfortable king bed on 2nd floor.','Our home sits on a safe street and is close to almost everything.  A couple blocks away is The shops and dining og Multnomah Village.  Gabriel Park with plenty of space to roam, playground, basketball court, and tennis courts is 1.5 miles away.  A short drive (10-15 minutes can take you almost anywhere in metro Portland) will take you to downtown, Hawthorne, Lake Oswego, the Alberta Arts district, Mississippi area, & more. Throughout Portland, there are numerous brewpubs, restaurants, shops, & more.  Also, the Convention Center is only 10 minutes away.  And, if you like to stroll, less than 1/2 mile away is many local restaurants, coffee shops, local bars, and some fun shops. Its also less than 1/4 mile to the bus stop which will take you into downtown & beyond.<br /><br />There are so many things happening in Portland.  Exploring & enjoying the Rose City is easy with the monthly neighborhood art walks, the numerous craft beer events (including the Oregon Brewers Festival (OBF)), and t','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2305e2e5-3d97-45ef-a50c-1d461081d640.jpg',9373771,18,'45.46545','-122.70578',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,51.00,2,90,423,4.84,29851448),(1362,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29860746','Master bedroom with private bath','Hello future guests...<br /><br />I offer a cozy room with a queen sized bed. The bathroom is private.  There is a microwave and refrigerator for you to use.  I also live in the home and am here if you need assistance or have questions.','There are many fast food places and restaurants.  There is also a few local grocery stores located nearby.  A movie theater and bowling is a quick 5 min drive.  Plenty to see and do in the area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9b02fab5-7a79-4a67-b71c-53444c67b375.jpg',71520174,87,'45.49959','-122.51064',2,1,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,7,4.71,29860746),(1363,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29884092','Private entrance, one bedroom unit in Woodstock','Private entrance to the remodeled basement apartment with full kitchen, washer and dryer, private bathroom with tub and shower, cozy bedroom with comfy full bed,  couch that converts to firm queen bed, beautiful fireplace, all the amenities of Woodstock within walking distance including bus lines, restaurants, coffee houses, pubs, parks, and city walks. There’s the beautiful Reed Canyon Nature Walk nearby as well for Hiking.','Close to Ate On Ate Hawaiian Restaurant, Proper Pint, I Heart Coffee, New Seasons, Double Mountain Brewery, Portland Fish Market, Nudi Asian Fusion, 2 Thai Restaurants, Laughing Planet, The Delta,  2 Bakeries including Grand Central,  The Heist Food Carts,  2 City Parks, bus lines 19, 10, 71. <br />10 minute drive to Downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/da76653c-4735-4e6f-9284-3a2dba155bb0.jpg',133425745,38,'45.48249','-122.60659',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,95.00,1,14,71,4.89,29884092),(1364,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29900173','Cozy, Artsy St Johns Bungalow','Cheery, light infused vintage home filled with host’s oil paintings. Access to quiet, beautiful no grass, backyard garden w/covered patio. Located in quaint  St. Johns- restaurants, shops, parks within walking distance. Close to bus!<br /><br />Fragrance free home,<br />COVID-19 safety practices are strictly practiced. <br /><br /> 2 bedrooms, front with a full mattress and the back, with queen (has the only air conditioner) <br /><br />2 air filters <br /><br />LGBT-friendly with no age, gender, racial or religious biases!','St. Johns is an up and coming neighborhood 8.3 miles from downtown Portland. There are shops and restaurants serving local food and locally made goods. Just 3 blocks away is a food cart pod with a fire pit and outdoor market. Nearby Cathedral Park is beautifully located under the St Johns Bridge, right on the river. We have 2 cinemas within walking distance that serve food and beer in the theater.  A small local health club 3 blocks away offers day passes.  Easily accessible are 3 different bus stops that connect you to downtown and all the colorful and interesting neighborhoods around Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/32b96cfc-9e2f-4271-9c62-58801c8eed6d.jpg',13263099,58,'45.58809','-122.74626',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,215.00,28,28,39,4.90,29900173),(1365,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29908188','Whole Home in NE Portland Alberta Arts','This 1910 home features 11-ft ceilings and lots of light. Take a short walk or bike ride to the Alberta Co-op to pick up local produce and ingredients to prepare dinner in the well-equipped kitchen. Too tired from exploring to cook? Grab something from one of the numerous food carts to bring home and enjoy at the large dining room table. Spend your evenings lounging on the covered back porch surrounded by lush landscaping or catching a show at The Alberta Rose Theater!','Walk score: 84 (Very Walkable)<br />Transit Score: 50 (Good Transit)<br />Bike Score: 81 (Very Bikeable)<br /><br />This home sits on the tree-lined Ainsworth Street in NE Portland. It is a short walk or bike ride to Killingsworth and Alberta Streets, which have too many restaurants, shops, galleries, etc. to name here! There are also several parks in the area, including one used as a location in season 2 of Netflix\'s American Vandal. There are also Safeway and Walgreens stores close by. I-5 is only a couple minutes drive away, and you can get to PDX or Downtown Portland in 15. <br /><br /><br />Check out more of the area here: http://albertamainst.org/shoplocal/visit/','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0037e4ca-f930-4956-beb4-d3923b264bd1.jpg',39165671,45,'45.56697','-122.65508',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,106.00,2,31,231,4.90,29908188),(1366,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29935310','The Empath Retreat in Hollywood','Welcome! <br /><br />This is bright and cozy apartment that is centrally located in Portland, Oregon. It overlooks the historic Hollywood Theater.  It is nestled atop a healing boutique on 42nd Ave.  <br /><br />This private space has a full kitchen, a soaking tub, laundry in the unit, and a new King Size bed.  There is an extra day-bed for comfort and TV watching.  <br /><br />It is located in the vibrant neighborhood of Hollywood: with a farmer’s market, groceries, and local favorites all within walking distance.','Walkability score of 94*  <br /><br />-centrally located in Northeast<br />-Trader Joe\'s, Whole Foods, and Grocery Outlet within a block! <br />-Hollywood Farmer\'s Market<br />-Hollywood Theater<br />-The famous Laurelwood Park, Grant Park, and Rose City Golf Course near<br />-Hollywood Transit Center and Max Station close by<br /><br />This is urban and has a lot of commuters and random houseless folks at times, so we recommend bringing bikes inside. That being said we have never had a problem!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9f52d6e6-1e7b-4bd7-944e-c3c8472791d2.jpg',13588271,84,'45.53644','-122.62089',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,93,4.95,29935310),(1367,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29983697','Irving Parlor-private guest wing for longer stays','Private guest wing in a historic  home with kitchenette, living/dining area and bathroom with a Japanese soaking tub. Originally built as servant\'s quarters in 1904, the Parlor shares an entry with the house, but functions like a separate apartment. “Mid-term” rental for 30+ days.<br /><br />The Parlor is in a sweet close-in NE Portland neighborhood. Walk or bike to Alberta Arts, Williams, Mississippi Ave, Whole Foods, and parks.<br /><br />Enjoy (shared) BBQ grill and hot tub in a private and shady backyard.','The King neighborhood is quintessential Portland with classic homes,  tree-lined streets, and summer Pedalpalooza rides down NE 7th ave. Less than 3 miles from downtown Portland, you can easily get to Mississippi Ave, Alberta Arts and Williams districts by foot or bike; and other east side hot spots by bike, electric scooter or transit.  Whole Foods and New Seasons are a 10-minute walk, Irving Park is just 2 blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/649f665b-2fb6-40d5-8ffb-f0830698c681.jpg',7512487,14,'45.55122','-122.65782',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,91.00,30,120,9,4.89,29983697),(1368,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29984761','Mt Tabor House Salmon Room','Cozy, energy efficient new construction for a better world. Located in the hip SE Hawthorne neighborhood on a quiet residential street and at the foot of Mt Tabor, this custom house provides a luxurious and convenient studio for relaxed stays and enjoyment of all that Portland has to offer.<br /><br />We designed this studio specifically for visitors who want the ease and security of a private entrance, the warmth (or coolness) of radiant-floor temperature control, and comfort.','Our house is on a classic Portland residential street, with well-maintained Portland craftsman houses, tree-lined and sidewalks. The sounds of children playing and practicing piano fill the afternoons. Weekday mornings see a parade of school kids walking to the neighborhood school, while adults walk one block to Albina Press, the best coffee shop in all of Portland. Salmon Street, the nearest intersection, is popular for runners and walkers heading to Mt Tabor Park. Traffic on Salmon St is very light, because it is not a through street for cars, but allows pedestrians and bikes to follow a path directly Mt Tabor. <br /><br />Just 2 blocks to the north or to the south are the commercial streets of Belmont and Hawthorne. Both are lined with food carts, coffee shops, restaurants, pubs, and convenience stores, as well as bike-share stations, banks, grocery stores, and theaters.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-29984761/original/99c8f319-9e2d-451f-b163-5e1da332fcf4.jpg',1172796,15,'45.51393','-122.61175',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,81.00,1,30,327,4.94,29984761),(1369,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29986189','Oscar\'s Perch - Fantastic & Private 1-BR','Private one-bedroom in NE Portland with a full kitchen, roomy bath with W&D, wi-fi, & parking. Bedroom has a queen bed; sofa converts to a queen bed. USB ports in kitchen & bedroom. <br /><br />Golf course, park, bike route, public trans., restaurants, wine shop, brewery, & grocery store all within several blocks.  Easy access to downtown and PDX. <br /><br />5% of the nightly rate will be donated to Gales Creek Camp for Kids with Type 1 Diabetes.<br /><br />We welcome and appreciate the diversity of our guests!','The Roseway neighborhood is home to one of Portland\'s top rated pizza restaurants and it is just down the street! Easy walk to grocery, brewpubs, restaurants, parks, and Oregon\'s newest marijuana shops. Near multiple large hospitals and medical clinics. You will enjoy our quiet neighborhood that is close to everything.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8577d54c-7753-42cf-bd5d-e1ef86faa63c.jpg',90414561,74,'45.5414','-122.59353',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,105.00,2,28,215,4.98,29986189),(1370,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/29989693','Perfect Portland Experience for up to 4 people!','Looking for the perfect Airbnb in Portland for up to 4 people? look no further.<br />Our property situates you in the heart of NE Portland, with restaurants, coffee shops, bars, and grocery stores all within 5 mins walk . The property is also 5-10 min drive away from the most popular and interesting parts of Portland. Additionally, The Shaver House is serviced with Business Class internet, with speeds around 100mbps (For those of you working remotely!).','The Shaver house neighborhood is amazing as you do not need a car to have everything you need. A 10 minute walk down Shaver St. and you are on Williams Ave with restaurants, bars, coffee, brewery,  grocery store and shopping. Both the Mississippi district and the Alberta Arts district are also only a few blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-29989693/original/79b275a0-275d-4b53-baab-004181d12b57.jpeg',18935456,14,'45.55109','-122.65966',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,94.00,2,28,103,4.85,29989693),(1371,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30039041','Market Street Guesthouse PDX','This is THE ONE! A perfect blend of upscale finishes, fixtures, and appliances in a beautiful and welcoming cottage. Soaring ceilings welcome the weary traveler into a space that offers fine linens, a fully stocked kitchen, two full baths with heated tile floors and a custom, versatile layout. No expense was spared building the space: the vibe is true Pacific NW, with wood trim, warmth and beauty all around. <br /><br />IDEAL walkable location smack dab amongst Portland\'s coolest neighborhood amenities!','The house is in the bohemian Hawthorne district. Grab a growler and a fancy donut. Shop for records, vintage clothing, and handmade items. Walk to the movies, drink beer in the theater, read at Powell\'s Books, and visit a 5-acre park within blocks.<br /><br />Please visit my guidebook for detailed recommendations for cafes, restaurants, things to do and more! https://www.airbnb.com/s/guidebooks?refinement_paths[]=/guidebooks/335463&share_channel=copy','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzAwMzkwNDE%3D/original/86c88968-5a32-4fac-848e-c9ff5137c209.jpeg',38307544,8,'45.51113','-122.62937',1,4,2.00,1.00,2.00,145.00,2,90,367,4.95,30039041),(1372,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30103421','Studio in the Pearl','My studio has amazing light looking east to the city. The outdoor patio with seating and BBQ complete the space.A full size kitchen with everything you need to create a wonderful entertaining area The studio lives larger than the square footage. Large bathroom with a nice shower. Couch under the loft bed making viewing the big screen TV for your streaming converts into a comfortable bed. You will want for nothing. Just bring your clothes and your toothbrush','The Pearl in Portland is just as it means. It is the gem in Portland. From my place there are so many brew pubs restaurants grocery stores shopping all within 5 minutes walk. Light rail is one block over that can take you all the way to Beaverton Washington and limited to the East side. Trimet, the bus system can be picked up most anywhere','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bf67ab2d-500c-4f29-96e1-e3ae12c75330.jpg',105882281,3,'45.52234','-122.68794',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,53.00,30,180,24,4.92,30103421),(1373,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30108841','Guesthouse in vibrant neighborhood, EV charger','Join us in the heart of the walkable Woodlawn neighborhood, and enjoy Portland life like a local from our light filled modern guest cottage!  The small house is completely free-standing and does not share any spaces or ventilation with the main house.   Contact free check-in and out. A comfortable space for small families or couples to enjoy your time in our friendly and vibrant community.  -NEW - Level 2 EV (Rivian) charger compatible with J1772 charging plug!','Woodlawn has been our home for 10 years, and we can\'t imagine a better place to live.  We can walk and bike to the market, great restaurants, a beautiful park and our neighborhood school.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ea8a1a76-0df6-4707-9520-66dd85220260.jpg',2682677,45,'45.57149','-122.64808',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,120.00,2,28,66,4.92,30108841),(1374,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30207076','Colorful, spacious, light-filled guesthouse on MAX','Welcome to Juniper House! We designed our backyard guesthouse to be a bright, cozy loft, full of sunlight, exposed wood, tasteful furnishings and colorful finishes.<br /><br />Enjoy a private, 600-sq-ft space with an outdoor patio in a quiet, close-in Portland neighborhood, just blocks from light rail and within walking distance to a wide variety of great restaurants and watering holes. Perfect for couples and longer stays.','The guesthouse is set back from a quiet street in a neighborhood with quality amenities: within a 10-minute walk you\'ll find a New Seasons Market (Portland\'s best local grocery chain), multiple coffee shops (the closest just three blocks away), and a plethora of restaurants and watering holes including Mio Sushi, Milk Glass Market (lunch takeout), Backyard Social (upscale bar), The Old Gold (pub grub), La Bonita (Mexican), Spitz (Mediterranean Street Food), Atomic Pizza, and a couple of bars.<br /><br />We\'re also a half-block from a designated bicycle boulevard, and four blocks from a light-rail stop that will take you downtown in 15 minutes. The Mississippi Avenue and Alberta Arts business districts are a short drive away.<br /><br />The neighborhood\'s small commercial nodes also feature a healthy mix of neighborhood-serving commercial (bike shop, yoga studio, hair salon, mini-mart, etc). The Peninsula Park Rose Garden is well worth a visit between May and October; it\'s a bit of a hi','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-30207076/original/d5c8c0bd-66ba-49cd-a910-77abc7862377.jpeg',1204761,13,'45.56385','-122.68603',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,119.00,4,28,277,5.00,30207076),(1375,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30224062','Convenient North Portland lower level studio','Modern and large lower level studio with separate entrance.   With 800 square feet of space, your own bathroom with walk in shower, studio style bedroom. Space for an air mattress for an extra sleeping area for greater than 2 guests.  Microwave, mini fridge, toaster oven, pub table with seating for two.  Also a  washer / dryer for those guests having longer stays and needing laundry.  <br />This Airbnb is fully permitted and safety inspected by City of Portland.','Portsmouth is a quiet neighborhood full of mostly single family homes and 3 blocks from Columbia park (a large park full of cedar trees and sport fields with a nice paved path all the way around). Kenton is a sweet little up and coming neighborhood about 1mile east with a few shops and restaurants.   We are within about 10- 20 minutes drive to just about anything in metro Portland.  <br />Nearby: <br />University of Portland<br />Cathedral and Pier parks<br />Forest Park - Our amazing 5,000 acre urban park.  Located just over the famous Portland gothic style bridge, circa 1931. <br />St John\'s Farmer\'s Market & food carts  <br />New Seasons, Green Zebra, Fred Meyers  <br />Nearby neighborhoods :: Kenton, St. John\'s, Mississippi, Pearl, NW 23rd, and Alberta Arts Districts for shopping, restaurants, galleries, arts, music, pubs.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/697a176f-1e99-41b4-ac90-65349767e917.jpg',128850,60,'45.584698560373454','-122.71058229939928',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,82.00,2,12,77,4.96,30224062),(1376,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30225296','Hip Local, Artsy Space. Walk to food, pubs & music','Your stylish, art filled, private, four room suite with 2 queen beds is located in the famous Buckman district surrounded by award winning restaurants, 8+ craft breweries 2 urban wineries, cafes and great places for brunch!<br />Walk 2-8 blocks = 4 brew pubs, 2 urban wineries, 20+ restaurants, vegan bakery, 4 live music venues, Revolution Hall, 2 rooftop deck bars, bakeries, grocery stores and a school playground/park.<br />15 blks to the river/Downtown. Moda Center, Convention Center','Great close in neighborhood with enough to do that you could spend your time in PDX without getting into your car. <br /><br />Walk 1-6 blocks to 2 neighborhood brew pubs, Enzo (an urban winery), Voodoo Doughnuts Too (their 2nd location - open 24 hours), 10 restaurants, a guitar shop with acoustic shows, a chocolate shop, 4 coffee shops, Revolution Hall for live concerts (+ amazing views at their rooftop bar overlooking the river with Downtown in the distance), fantastic late night menu at Nostrana (restaurant of the year), grab a drink while you wait at their futuristic wine bar next door, 7 bars, a sports bar and more / all within 6 blocks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bcbcf741-60d3-41ba-ad48-67683339b440.jpg',15346651,32,'45.52067277276538','-122.64999192755567',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,121.00,2,14,285,4.96,30225296),(1377,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30291459','Gem in heart of Beaumont-Wilshire','Ideal for families with young children. Baby gates, outlet covers, and potty chair available. TV is strapped to media stand in dining/living room. Bed 1 has trundle bed. Bed 2 has full futon bed and toddler bed with rail. Pack n\' play on site. Full bath on first floor. Upstairs master has queen bed and space for pack n\' play with private bath - double sink and walk-in shower. Clean washer/dryer in half-finished basement. Kitchen has 5-burner range and dishwasher. Backyard fenced for kids.','Located just off Fremont St., Starbucks, Grand Central Bakery, and Prince Coffee are all within a block. Enjoy great cocktails and food at NoHo Hawaiian, Thrive, and (old school) Italian at Almafi\'s. Blackbird Wine and Cheese, Batter, Red Sauce Pizza, and a host of other great eateries are all within blocks of our home. Beaumont Market is also within blocks, open late, and has everything you need to cook at home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/04b22577-fc28-485d-bc09-89ce51867561.jpg',22650127,46,'45.54936','-122.61619',1,6,2.00,3.00,3.00,130.00,31,120,14,5.00,30291459),(1378,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30296652','Cozy SouthWestern Art Cantina - Mississippi Dstrct','Bright, 1bed/1bath, back yard guest house. This converted garage ADU is packed with art and South West/Desert/Rustic/Latin vibes. Perfect for couples, solo adventurers and business travelers. The small house is a great location - it\'s 20 minutes from the airport & 8 minutes to downtown with ample free street parking and wi-fi. Walking distance to Albert and Mississippi districts. We are a five-minute walk to multiple coffee shops, restaurants, and bars including Sweedeedee, Saraveza & Red Fox','Three houses north of this cantina is the most beautiful rose garden and spacious park, enjoy a walk there during your stay. My two favorite coffee shops are Red E and Coffee House Five, both 5 minute walks south. There is the most lovely plant shops called Sollabee on the corner of Killingsworth and Albina, treat yourself and buy a cactus! One of the most talked about breakfasts in town is Sweedeedee, also walking distance on Albina. They often have a long line, so if you want a secret spot, head to the Bad Habit room on Killingsworth, there\'s never a line. Beyond a 5 minute walk, I would reccomend a stroll down Mississippi, start at the food cart lot on Skidmore and stroll south to Freemont, stopping at whatever shops and restaurants interest you.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/36bc2a5a-977f-4126-a6e1-1094a49e3306.jpg',638465,24,'45.56481','-122.67273',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,40,13,4.85,30296652),(1379,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30327746','Secluded Studio tucked away in N. Portland','Private studio getaway  — centrally located in N Portland, just a few blocks away from the University of Portland and a quick hop to the many food trucks, restaurants, coffee shops, and parks that St. Johns has to offer. Perfect for couples, visiting parents, solo adventurers and business travelers alike. You’ll love the King sized Casper mattress, stylish aesthetic, and seclusion you get with the studio. LGBTQI friendly. Smoke Free environment.<br /><br />Professionally cleaned with fair wages paid.','This area is bustling with character! It’s mostly older homes and new families, so most nights are pretty quiet. There’s a great local coffee cart a few blocks away, as well as Starbucks, several restaurants and taverns within walking distance. Local charm abound in this area!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-30327746/original/40529630-fae8-4650-83c4-d8c831bd0d42.jpeg',6358589,60,'45.58597','-122.72397',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,58.00,2,365,189,4.96,30327746),(1380,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30347658','The Conservatory | Walkscore 92 + Bikescore 100','This two-level private loft is hidden in a mezzanine garden courtyard located in the heart of north Mississippi Avenue. The grounds feature a 3-story bamboo garden and walking access to countless top restaurants, boutiques, boutique stores, and public transport to greater PDX attractions.','The only similarity the Mississippi neighborhood shares with other districts is that it is uniquely Portland. In fact, trying to describe it would be like trying to verbalize a color, but let’s say that it has a little bit of that ‘special something’ that comes to mind when thinking of PDX… a Mardi Gras parade of high school bands accompanied by unicyclists with flame throwers (yep), the annual Mississippi Street Fair (~45,000 people), a thoroughfare for the world naked bike ride, notorious music venues, outdoor movies with fire pits, over 12 great bars, food cart pods and great dining. This street celebrates 5 nights out of the week.<br /><br />More information<br />I encourage you to explore EaterPDX for a better idea of the local attractions, but know that there are many other things on this street. In my mind, here are the best features the street has to offer, and they’re all within a block or two of this residence:<br /><br />Coffee/Cannabis<br />* Nectar - for those that indulge','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bb58ab3a-1dd1-4529-bc16-94f1b8e2da9b.jpg',14970082,9,'45.55424','-122.67519',1,5,1.50,2.00,2.00,120.00,30,182,345,4.94,30347658),(1381,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30418830','The Westmoreland Nest','This 1 bedroom, 2nd floor apartment over our personal studio and garage has a key pad entry and is loaded with amenities including vaulted ceilings with 3 skylights throughout, a comfortable queen bed, full kitchen which includes dishes, pans and other accoutrements, a coffeemaker along with coffee, tea and a teapot, full bathroom, living room, washer/dryer, dishwasher, large balcony, WIFI, TV and Blu-Ray with Roku, DVD’s and a turntable that includes loads of vintage records.','We are located steps away from everything! Walk a block in one direction and you will find tons of shops, restaurants, gyms, yoga/excercise classes and bars. The Willamette River is a short distance away and we are surrounded by various parks and trails such as Springwater, Oaks Bottom and Reed Canyon.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6ed61089-ffc5-4040-9ed9-06e9f854e6d9.jpg',150768243,20,'45.47383','-122.64842',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,99.00,2,365,138,4.96,30418830),(1382,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30439436','Charming Vintage Cottage perfect for Families','Welcome to one of the best Southeast neighborhoods in Portland for families, friends and foodies. This quiet and cozy South Tabor home will keep you safe and snug. Near Division St. and the Hawthorne District, it\'s perfectly located, a short drive to all the fun but not in the thick of it.<br /><br />Relax at the backyard\'s patio dining table or pull one of the Adirondack chairs up to the fire pit.','South Tabor is a quiet residential neighborhood between the bustling streets of Division and Powell.  According to Travel Portland, “You could plan a week’s worth of meals on Southeast Division Street, the city’s hottest dining corridor, and still not hit all of the must-try restaurants.” <br /><br />This neighborhood is a sweet, middle class area (highly sought after for people looking to live or rent long-term), perfect for families or laid back groups who want a more authentic neighborhood experience. <br /><br />There are great restaurants and shops all within a 6 - 10 minute drive or ride from here. It\'s a great neighborhood to walk in, especially if you want to hike up to Mt. Tabor, but walking to the shops and restaurants nearby takes about 30 minutes. I always drive, Uber or Lyft wherever I want to go - it\'s only 10 minutes to all the East side fun, and not much longer to downtown.<br /><br />Fabulous food experiences: Pok Pok, Ava Gene\'s, Whiskey Soda Lounge, Bollywood Theater','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/739dc829-7644-4229-8d17-511f969caab4.jpg',58599742,37,'45.50191','-122.58966',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,167.00,3,730,89,4.97,30439436),(1383,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30442104','Stay in a Dorm Bed (Male) at NW Portland Hostel','Experience Portland’s top-rated, family-owned hostel, in the vibrant Northwest District! Enjoy a FREE breakfast and explore nearby downtown attractions, Washington Park, the Rose and Japanese Gardens, and hiking trails. Join our daily free events like walking tours, tap tastings, live music, and trivia nights. For over 25 years, our mission has been to provide a welcoming, affordable, and safe space, connecting Portland with travelers worldwide and making a positive impact locally and beyond.','We are located in the Northwest district, just a few blocks from popular shops, cafes, pubs, cinemas, and some of the city\'s best restaurants. Many area attractions, including the Pearl District, downtown Portland, Saturday Market, Portland Farmers Market, Powell\'s Bookstore, art galleries, the Lan Su Chinese Garden, museums, the MLS Stadium, and Pioneer Square, are within walking distance. The Rose Gardens and Japanese Gardens are a short bus ride or a 25-minute walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzA0NDIxMDQ%3D/original/41be6e74-058b-4ab1-9554-bb5b6b7d8e59.jpeg',2820851,27,'45.52502','-122.69015',3,1,4.00,1.00,4.00,40.00,1,1125,152,4.84,30442104),(1384,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30467974','Cozy Seclusion in North Portland','Sink into our recently renovated, super sylin’ basement studio with warm lighting, polished concrete floors, and reclaimed wood accents. With your own full kitchen, bathroom, sleeping, and chillin’ areas, you’ll be set to rest in between sight seeing and restaurant visiting. <br /><br />Our house is close to I-5, public transit and bike streets making getting to anywhere in Portland a breeze.  There’s also plenty within walking distance - Peninsula Park, several bars and  restaurants and shopping.','North Portland - the 5th quadrant - is quickly becoming a local favorite. There are parks within 1/2 mile north and south of the house, easy access to transit to bring you all over the city, family owned restaurants within walking distance, old houses and rich Portland history.<br /><br />Peninsula Park and its rose garden are .7 miles from the house. If you prefer a quicker walk, Farraghut park is only 4 blocks. There are more if you prefer a longer run, walk or bike ride.<br /><br />If restaurants are your thing, you can hop on a bike, bus or car and head down to Williams for a delicious breakfast and local coffee roasters, or down Alberta and Mississippi for any number of spots featuring food carts, coffee shops, food co-ops, bars and numerous restaurants. N and NE neighborhoods are accessible by a 10-15 min bus ride. Downtown is a 20-30 mins bus or light rail ride. (See \"getting around\" for a description of nearby transit - there are lots of choices!).<br /><br />If you prefer cook','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c2a27d49-f100-465e-b8a1-d4a798e03f54.jpg',8076457,48,'45.57706','-122.67255',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,69.00,30,1125,189,4.83,30467974),(1385,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30515475','Cute, modern studio in North Portland!','Cute studio apartment in a cute neighborhood! <br /><br />Newly renovated, stylishly furnished, clean, well-lit space with a queen bed, kitchenette and full bathroom. Eight-minute walk to the Kenton/N. Denver station on the light rail (Yellow line), which takes you right into downtown Portland. The neighborhood itself is charming and safe. We are a few blocks from restaurants, cafes, bars, shops and a beautiful park (with a great playground). <br /><br />We very much look forward to hosting you!','Kenton is a little gem of a neighborhood in North Portland. It is famous for its iconic Paul Bunyun statue. There are a few nice cafes (Posies, Presso Cafe), restaurants (Swift and Union, Fino Pizzeria, Poshines, Casa Maya) and a nice minimart. There are some good bars, too, like Parkside Bar, Kenton Station and, of course, the world-famous Kenton Club (also a live music venue). There is also a library and post office, plus some retail like very cool second-hand stores, a bike shop, a comic book shop, and Speck\'s records.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/58beeead-2f1a-4954-b656-76b6d2bcf06c.jpg',11886279,55,'45.58188','-122.69191',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,68.00,2,1125,287,4.94,30515475),(1386,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30591779','Private room in SE','Standard modern townhouse','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/de269390-6c2e-4ce6-a1a8-51e77d5a2750.jpg',204559,69,'45.47456','-122.58132',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,49.00,30,1125,6,5.00,30591779),(1387,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30676051','Light-filled charmer in the heart of Buckman!','Delightful two bedroom charmer in the heart of the thriving Buckman neighborhood!  Enjoy all the restaurants, bars, shops, parks, and close in neighborhoods that are all within walking distance! This 1920\"s bungalow has the vintage charm of the era but with the modern updates you will appreciate!  The kitchen was recently remodeled to the studs which includes stainless steel appliances, quartz counters and new cabinets.  The decor is stylish, eclectic, warm and inviting!  Hope to see you soon!','Smack dab in the middle of close in East Portland.  The house is 24 blocks east of the Willamette River and downtown Portland.  It is within walking distance of other popular close in neighborhoods, countless restaurant and bar options, parks, public transit, gourmet grocery stores, freeway access and much much more!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-30676051/original/043b15c5-b42c-4b36-a27a-99c17b67c331.jpeg',14855444,32,'45.521275','-122.641693',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,164.00,1,1125,145,4.90,30676051),(1388,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30676335','Relaxed Apartment in a Richmond Craftsman Home','Enjoy this beautifully designed (900 square foot) 2 bedroom with craftsman details while emphasizing clean and modern lines. Each bedroom is large and tastefully detailed with comfortable queen beds, full closets, and plenty of storage for your belongings. The beautiful bathroom has a walk-in, glass enclosed shower and double sink.   We have a  fully equipped kitchen with a counter top oven, microwave and a 4 top burner stove. We have a coffee maker, microwave and all the eating and cooking utensils that you need.  There is a 50\" 4K Smart TV flatscreen with Comcast cable and Wi-fi.<br /><br />This apartment has a private entrance at the back of the house. We will provide you with a private code when you book your stay.<br /><br />We are available to answer any questions and provide guidance and suggestions of places to go and adventures to have.<br /><br />Set in a Craftsman home in the Richmond neighborhood, this newly-remodeled apartment is steps away from renowned restaurants, trend','Set in a Craftsman home in the Richmond neighborhood, this newly-remodeled apartment is steps away from renowned restaurants, trendy boutiques, and buzzy cafes along Division Street. Fun fact: The View-Master was invented at this apartment in 1939.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7babf82f-a1f1-45b8-93a7-6bbcd90641fd.jpg',272956,8,'45.50329','-122.62081',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,153.00,2,180,195,4.98,30676335),(1389,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30793573','Welcome Home','This home is quiet, cozy & peaceful.  A completely renovated 100 year old farm house on nearly an acre of private fenced old orchard.  The space is very private, guests love the park like setting.  Situated near OHSU, Downtown Pdx, Lewis & Clark College.  Hillsdale, Multnomah & Gabriel Park are within walking distance.  You are near great restaurants, shopping & public transportation in a bike friendly city.  Popular day trips include Hood River, The Oregon Coast, Wine Country & Rivers.','Our quiet street is a popular walking route for neighbors heading to the village or getting exercise on the walk up our hill.  Gabriel Park, Multnomah Village & Hillsdale are all within walking distance as well as the Community Center where you\'ll find trails, sports courts, exercise classes, swimming pool, etc.<br /><br />Great restaurants, bars, coffee shops & local clothing, sustainable lifestyle & household goods, children\'s shops & pet specialty boutiques.  It\'s pretty much all right here.  No need to drive but downtown is less than 10 minutes away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9ad96e5d-dd5c-4148-8a06-68e29bda50c6.jpg',28410788,17,'45.4794','-122.71443',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,128.00,30,360,139,4.73,30793573),(1390,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30815455','Luxury Penthouse: City, Mountain & River Views','Discover our South Portland penthouse condo, where luxury meets comfort. Enjoy panoramic views of the city skyline, Mt. St. Helens, and the Willamette River from this bright, 1350 sq ft space. Perfect for leisure or work, our condo offers a spacious bedroom, office, and top amenities in a secure, family-friendly area. Steps away from shopping, dining, and transport, with secure parking included. Experience the best of Portland in style!','Johns Landing, nestled in South Portland, stands as a serene and unspoiled enclave amidst the bustling city. This neighborhood offers a peaceful, secure, and welcoming atmosphere, setting it apart from the busier, more crowded areas of Portland. Its strategic location provides unparalleled access to the city’s highlights, including OHSU, Lake Oswego, Downtown, and the serene Willamette River, complemented by ample streetside parking and effortless access to major highways like I-5 and I-84.<br /><br />Characterized by a community of professionals, retirees, and families, Johns Landing is distinguished by its absence of the hipster and homeless populations more commonly seen in other parts of the city. Instead, the neighborhood is a quiet, friendly area where great restaurants, coffee shops, and retail options abound, with the added luxury of Zupans upscale grocery store merely 200 feet from our doorstep. We’re always here to provide personalized recommendations to ensure you discover t','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-30815455/original/34e3d7a1-1d33-4026-8fc5-310588bea23f.jpeg',141166845,22,'45.47382','-122.67206',1,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,120.00,1,28,93,4.94,30815455),(1391,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30888456','Streetcar Lofts in the Heart of the Pearl','One bedroom loft  condo with floor to ceiling windows and access to private outdoor patio and community space. Located within walking distance to grocery stores, restaurants, coffee shops, banks, urgent care centers, art galleries, several parks and the streetcar. The queen sized wall bed has a Tempurpedic mattress. An additional queen sized cabinet bed has a memory foam mattress for  overnight quests. Washer and dryer in unit. Parking space in building. WIFI and hi-def smart TV. NONSMOKERS ONLY','Many great restaurants, Powell’s bookstore, Piazza Italia, The Hairy Lobster, Lovejoy Bakery, on streetcar line. There isn\'t a better location! Anything you need can be found within a mile radius of the condo; doctors, pilates, yoga, spas, hairdressers, drugstores, parks, hardware store, liquor store, grocery stores and on and on. You can walk downtown, to the Alphabet District and all around the Pearl.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bfac344d-7b5d-4d4c-9ae5-375702332562.jpg',21707201,2,'45.5293714091881','-122.68206230144166',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,95.00,30,1125,14,4.86,30888456),(1392,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30890318','Chic Portland Pad!','10% Discount for 7 days or more!!<br /><br />This sparkling clean, new, well-appointed, well-located private apartment will be the perfect launch for all your Portland adventures! You will have your own entrance, bedroom, full kitchen, and bathroom with room for up to 4 people (queen bed in bedroom & comfortable queen sofa bed in living area). Close to the MAX (20 min on foot) and bus (10 min). Free street parking is readily available. 5 min on foot to groceries, bars, and restaurants.','This apartment is in the classic Portland Sullivan\'s Gulch neighborhood within 5-minutes on foot to a Starbucks, tiki bar, local gourmet donuts, gourmet bagels, Irish Pub, and Mexican food (Cha Cha Cha).  Within 10-15 minutes by foot there are many restaurants on NE Broadway or NE 28th (German, Italian, Mexican, etc.). ATM, several banks and coin laundry just a short walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b7a93a2b-89f5-4775-9050-9303300a4000.jpg',6431,4,'45.53212','-122.63823',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,57.00,2,30,452,4.94,30890318),(1393,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30890964','Overlook Victorian Mansion (5 Bedroom 10 Guest)','This is an updated, turn-of-the century mansion located perfectly near downtown Portland.  Come experience an authentic Portland home in a spectacular location.<br /><br />Two blocks from Overlook Park, and within walking distance of Kaiser Permanente Interstate Hospital. <br /><br />1.8 Miles to Moda Center.  <br /><br />1 block from light rail transit (Overlook Park Maxx station).<br /><br />5 Car Maximum w/extra long driveway.<br /><br />Permit #: LU18-275778','The Overlook neighborhood is unique among upscale Portland neighborhoods.  There is very little traffic due to being located on a bluff (no through traffic).  Many restored mansions from a different era are scattered in this wonderful community.  If you love architecture, take a walk around the block.  Many neighbors have been been in this neighborhood for decades, and love the quiet atmosphere at this location.  Be respectful and quite when you are outside to maintain the peaceful nature of this neighborhood.  Loud groups with late-night activities and/or parties are not a good fit for this location.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b4521ad0-1037-4957-8918-7335c13dbf83.jpg',84575822,13,'45.55316','-122.68354',1,10,3.50,5.00,6.00,263.00,2,1123,154,4.88,30890964),(1394,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30892405','Studio House-Modern Cozy Gem!','The Walnut Studio House is named after the historic trees surrounding our neighborhood and is carefully designed to maximize your space and provide a relaxing get away. The neighborhood is surrounded by historic homes and trees.  Quiet and peaceful yet in the heart of Portland\'s action--a 20 minute community where everything you need is close by: a beautiful rose garden, locally owned restaurants and bars, food cart pods, shopping, theaters with music, shows and much more.','Quiet and peaceful in the heart of close in North Portland. The neighborhood is lined with historic homes and trees. Alberta, Williams and Mississippi districts are a short walk and full of lively restaurants, cafes, bars, theaters, shopping and more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-30892405/original/3d6b4c97-6aa4-4c63-a50f-af764f9d3c0f.jpeg',36670674,14,'45.56057','-122.6648',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,72.00,2,1125,362,4.97,30892405),(1395,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30909886','Stunning Portland Condo: Parking, River & Dining','Explore Portland in style! Our freshly renovated top-floor condo offers 2BR/2BA, breathtaking views, and a private deck. Enjoy the convenience of secured parking, complimentary WiFi, and a fully furnished space ready for your stay, whether it\'s for a night, a month, or longer. Perfectly situated near OHSU, Lewis & Clark, and major medical centers. Steps away from Zupans Market and Willamette River parks. Ideal for travelers seeking comfort and convenience in a prime location.','Nestled in the upscale and vibrant area of South Portland, our neighborhood serves as a beacon of urban charm combined with seamless access to Portland’s diverse offerings. Johns Landing, in particular, is a treasure trove of activities and scenic beauty. Willamette Park, with its sprawling lawns and riverfront access, offers an array of outdoor activities. From running trails to kayak and paddleboard rentals, and the boat launch, the park is a hub for those seeking adventure or relaxation by the water. The summer months bring the park to life with live concerts, frisbee golf, soccer games, and performances by local musicians, creating a vibrant community atmosphere.<br /><br />Just steps away from the condo, the waterfront paved path presents a picturesque route for exploring Portland\'s scenic vistas and is ideal for those who enjoy leisurely strolls or vigorous runs against the backdrop of the city’s waterfront.<br /><br />The culinary scene in our neighborhood is rich and varied, bo','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-30909886/original/e52e2722-6fad-417c-b0dc-c96e2ca46304.jpeg',25976548,22,'45.47224','-122.67412',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,100.00,1,180,162,4.90,30909886),(1396,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30980830','Business Travel Dream - Spacious, Luxurious 2 Bed','Relax - we thought of everything. Owned and built by a global business traveler, we designed this space to meet your needs with 24/7 check-in, black out curtains, coffee station and mobile charging docks for all devices. <br /><br />When you awake you\'re at the corner of Lyft and Uber and a 10 minute trip to most city destinations. In the evenings, you\'re surrounded by some of Portland\'s top restaurants from casual to five star and there is a supermarket 1 block away if you want to stock your own unit.','This is it. You\'re in the absolute beating heart of the city, surrounded by the best shops and restaurants available. Most guests don\'t bring a car because you could spend a week walking and not get everywhere interesting near this house!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3a823ee5-0795-431d-a175-8ffed31e2ac0.jpg',173625187,16,'45.51289','-122.63123',2,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,77.00,31,365,2,5.00,30980830),(1397,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/30986083','Eastmoreland Private Guest Suite by Reed College','Private Guest House Studio Apartment in one of SE Portland\'s historic neighborhoods - Eastmoreland.  With quick access to all the best things Portland has to offer.  Situated two blocks from Reed College entrance and a short walk to golfing, Sellwood, Westmoreland, and Woodstock restaurants as well as bus lines and the Trimet MAX Orange Line. If you are looking to explore the wonderful city of Portland, or if you are looking for a quiet comfortable tiny home retreat you have found your getaway!','Eastmoreland is a historic neighborhood located in central SE Portland, giving you access to the city life without being caught in the middle of the craziness. Our neighborhood was built in the early 20th century, and with it\'s stately homes and picturesque trees, it has truly stood the test of time! This neighborhood is great for walking around and exploring, having parks, Reed College, the Rhododendron Garden, and various coffee shops and breweries being just a few minutes walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a237d377-1390-41ff-8348-1170ea0aa72d.jpg',142326751,5,'45.47777','-122.62879',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,98.00,3,90,196,4.99,30986083),(1398,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31018961','Cozy Apt.. Walking distance to Moda & Convt Ctr!!!','PLEASE READ THROUGH THE ENTIRE LISTING & ALL REVIEWS. <br /><br />BASEMENT APARTMENT. <br /><br />Irvington District. One mile to the Moda Center, Convention Center, Memorial Colosseum. We are in walking distance to 2 grocery stores, a pharmacy,  a number of restaurants, & fast food chains. We are near the Oregon Zoo & OMSI.  The Oregon Coast Line, Mountain Range, Colombia Gorge, and other natural attractions are an hour and half away! We’re conveniently located for those looking to explore the Portland Metro area.','We’re located in the Historical Irvington District. A few blocks to Irvington Elementary School.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cca3d827-c09f-46ec-9815-304283f8a6a8.jpg',152120973,7,'45.540005','-122.657288',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,1,30,329,4.92,31018961),(1399,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31041507','MODERN, PRIVATE, AND FULLY FURNISHED SE GUESTHOUSE','Our modern, private, work-friendly guesthouse is conveniently located in the quiet SE residential neighborhood of Creston-Kenilworth.  Bus lines, Trader Joes, coffee shops and restaurants are all within short walking distance.  It\'s an easy commute to PDX Int\'l, and the Moda Ctr, Reed, Kaiser Sunnyslope, Gresham, Clackamas, and Woodstock are all conveniently located on the same side of the river.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2289e0f6-2e74-44e8-8f84-b120552af48f.jpg',231857120,38,'45.48995','-122.61965',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,31,190,71,4.99,31041507),(1400,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31207702','Concordia Guest Suite, NE Portland','This sophisticated, well appointed basement guest suite with private entrance and a lovely backyard oasis is located within walking and biking distance (one mile) from the Alberta Arts District. The shaded backyard with secret garden paths calls out to you to explore. Guests are welcome to use the gas grill, outdoor patio seating, or our fire table in the evenings. We invite you to sit and enjoy some local micro-brew or local Oregon wines while relaxing here.','The guest suite is a two minute walk from seven great restaurants and coffee shops. A five minute stretch will take you to great parks, and to the McMenamins Kennedy School, which has five bars, two restaurants, a soaking pool that is open to the public, and a theatre. Within a ten minute walk you are in the heart of the Alberta Arts district. Walk or use the bicycles provided to get to these amenities in just a few minutes, or go further to explore one of the most bike friendly cities in America. And with less than a 15 minute drive to the Portland International Airport, you can spend your time in the Rose City to the fullest, while staying at the Concordia Guest Suite.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-31207702/original/0c87f588-d5b9-4583-ad32-c23591f1a51d.jpeg',176371931,1,'45.56997','-122.63471',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,100.00,2,1125,103,4.96,31207702),(1401,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31224158','Irvington Place Moda & Convention center close','950 sq ft, newly remodeled  bright, spacious guest suite in historic neighborhood is walking distance to the Convention Center, Moda Center, shopping, restaurants and coffee shops. Great for family travel & vacation getaway. Shops, restaurants, and entertainment, MAX light-rail & Streetcar all just blocks away. You\'ll enjoy a private, beautifully appointed interior, newly updated kitchen and memory foam beds.  patio seating, grassy yard, fruit trees. Great for families, couples, biz travelers.','Irvington is a historic neighborhood in Portland, OR. It is filled with beautiful tree-lined streets, sidewalks for jogging or meandering about. Beautiful historic century-old homes abound and gardens in the spring, summer and fall overflow with flowers, fruit trees and shady big oaks, maples and evergreens.<br />While the neighborhood is safe and walkable your also just four blocks from groceries, shopping, restaurants, wine bars and more. We are “close in” to city center and near the major thoroughfares.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6b98da8d-91e1-42f7-8afe-3857bf235bb8.jpg',4426731,7,'45.53928','-122.65485',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,66.00,2,30,160,4.84,31224158),(1402,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31224577','Zen oasis near Mt. Tabor, private bath, fast Wi-Fi','Relax in the first-level bedroom of our North Tabor home, featuring a cozy Tuft & Needle mattress and a private bathroom. Reach downtown in 15 minutes or PDX Airport in 20 via MAX Light Rail. It\'s a quiet neighborhood, but only a 5-min walk to public transportation, coffee shop and grocery, 5 min to Providence Portland Medical Center and with easy freeway access. Semi-private entrance leads straight back to your room—no one else is using this floor of the house, only for entry/exit.','It\'s considered the \"North Tabor\" section of Portland and there are several coffee shops, restaurants, dispensaries, food carts, Trader Joe\'s and a Fred Meyer Marketplace nearby.<br /><br />FOOD CARTS, PARKS AND MORE:<br />Take a 10-minute walk or quick drive and you\'ll find Rocket Empire Machine: A brand new food hall featuring Gigantic Brewing, Alleamin African Kitchen (Somalian), Tierra del Sol (Oaxacan), The Pie Spot and Sea & River Sushi. Go in the other direction for The Barley Pod: A beer garden and food cart park featuring Bull Run Pizza, La Arepa (Venezualen Street Food), Hapa (Ramen), Poblano Pepper (Mexican Food), Bam Pow (Burgers), Namu (Korean/Hawai’ian), Yaba Yabaa (Falafel), Eat Well (Vegetarian/Vegan), Flew The Coop (Fried Chicken) and The Dark Side (Thai), centered around Baerlic Brewing.<br /><br />It\'s a beautiful walk through the neighborhood to Mt. Tabor: A unique park on an extinct volcano with a 360 degree view of the area, walking trails and steps through the tr','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-31224577/original/cfd60bb2-435f-415b-add4-da9cd5e2bc18.jpeg',1314197,52,'45.52802','-122.59735',2,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,82.00,1,16,187,4.97,31224577),(1403,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31224648','The peaceful treehouse in quiet neighborhood.','Each high-touch surface, down to the doorknob is sanitized with a bleach solution.<br />I  use an extensive cleaning checklist each time the house is cleaned in between guests.<br />I provide extra cleaning supplies, so you can clean as you stay.<br /><br />2 story house with exceptional light inside  and clean. Quiet neighborhood in the Montavila area with many cafe\'s, coffee houses, brew pubs and a second run movie theater within a 15 minute walk.','Close to parks, golf course, shopping, coffee shops, cafes, pubs, and second run movie theater.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/70c29afa-8113-432c-a2e8-1730a4b5e15b.jpg',28892696,10,'45.52935','-122.58697',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,120.00,3,29,92,4.96,31224648),(1404,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31261650','Cute + Cozy Cottage in Portland!','*Extended month to month bookings can be made past March so please reach out if interested.<br /><br />Welcome to Historic St. Johns! This 2 bedroom, 2 bathroom, cozy cottage is located in one of Portland\'s oldest, most historic neighborhoods. Complete with a full kitchen, comfortable furnishings, and beautiful front porch, this home is within walking distance to St. Johns\' quaint downtown, stunning Cathedral Park, and landmark bridge. University of Portland is also only a short distance away!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7069f7dc-741a-4b07-b2e1-192787dc4014.jpg',3588025,58,'45.59294','-122.74127',1,4,2.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,10,365,42,5.00,31261650),(1405,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31271674','Castle Estate in SW Portland minutes from Downtown','Beautiful CASTLE LIKE home with lots of character. Spend your vacation surrounded by the hills of Southwest Portland minutes away from Downtown Portland. Built in 2002, recently Fully remodeled, huge vaulted ceilings. 5 minutes away from downtown Portland. Five Large Bedrooms w/ 3+full baths,  fireplace, beautiful marble tile work, Hardwood floors, unusual custom finish work. Territorial Portland views, brick exterior, craftsman finished ceilings, 2 Jacuzzis, Sauna and a Hot Tub.','Inna’s home is located in Portland, Oregon, United States.<br />Quiet neighborhood near Council Crest Park with great views over the city. Fairmount avenue is a 5 minute walk from the house and a popular destination for cyclists, walkers, and runners. Small, retro Hillsdale is a 5 minute drive with grocery, bars, coffeeshops, and the Portland staple, food carts!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8c0d9a6e-d1cc-4746-95e5-a4d2143f4c7a.jpg',100656896,54,'45.49397','-122.70555',1,10,3.00,5.00,8.00,750.00,3,730,129,4.82,31271674),(1406,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31284993','Luxury Apartment For Rent','Your luxury home away from home!  This apartment feels as good as it looks.  You will sink into the pillow top mattress while being hugged by 500 thread count sheets and pillow cases and a hotel quality comforter.<br /><br />The perfect place for a small gathering, the sectional seats 5-7 people comfortably and the dining table along with the eating bar will seat up to eight breakfast, lunch, and/or dinner guests that you can cook for on the double oven gas stove.','You can walk to everything you could possible want.  You will be located four blocks from the Lloyd Center mall full of lots of shops and entertainment.  It has a ice rink for ice skating, a movie cinema that features all the latest movies, along with a host of restaurants, bars, book stores, hair and nail salons, shops,massage therapy parlor, and a whole lot more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/87603eae-edee-4f37-a849-fbe1ce7ef7ff.jpg',123968362,7,'45.53888','-122.65012',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,199.00,3,1125,1,5.00,31284993),(1407,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31290790','Casa Maggie Mae Stunning COZY AC Alberta Arts','LONG TERM Possible…<br /><br />NEW Central Heating & Air Conditioning throughout ENTIRE Home…<br /><br />SUPER FUN Location extremely close to two of Portland’s HIPPEST neighborhoods: Less than a mile away...Alberta Arts District & Mississippi Neighborhoods…<br /><br />The PERFECT HOME for a STAYCATION! GREAT WORK FROM HOME environment, FAST INTERNET! <br /><br />STARBUCKS,  Safeway Grocery Store, Walgreens, Popeye’s, pubs, and restaurants all within very close proximity to the home<br /><br />Casa Maggie Mae<br />Circa \"1925\" English Tudor Home…','THE LOCATION<br /><br />From the property\'s unbeatable location, you\'ll enjoy easy access to numerous popular Portland neighborhoods, including the Alberta Arts District and Mississippi Avenue. Both areas are filled with quaint shops, brew pubs, restaurants, and opportunities to take in the vibrant culture exuded here. Situated less than a mile away, entertainment in these communities is always right at your fingertips!<br /><br />You\'ll also be within arms reach of downtown Portland, the Rose City! Head out for a scrumptious meal with your family, then to the pristine Willamette River for a pleasant evening stroll along the water front. Additionally, a Safeway grocery store, Walgreen\'s and Starbucks are all within walking distance for your convenience. Your Northwest escapade starts here with this stupendous Portland vacation rental house!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fa28bbb2-07a7-4125-b763-6c3b67a23a13.jpg',19204617,48,'45.56813049316406','-122.66258239746094',1,6,1.50,3.00,4.00,110.00,30,150,44,4.91,31290790),(1408,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31291509','Large, Private Woodstock Suite','Enjoy your stay in our light, airy 800 square foot basement studio with private entrance.  The suite has a large bathroom, well-equipped kitchenette, closet, window seat/twin bed, queen bed, comfortable couch and easy chair.  Laundry and wi-fi are available for guest use.','The Woodstock neighborhood has many amenities.  Walk to restaurants, bars, grocery stores and coffee shops.  Close to Division Street, Foster-Powell, Sellwood, Reed College, The Rhododendron Garden, Eastmoreland Golf Course and the Springwater bicycle trail.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-31291509/original/55875487-73b3-4060-8879-e35fb2f6e555.jpg',234182512,38,'45.4782','-122.61199',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,3,30,149,4.97,31291509),(1409,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31338578','Little Cedar House  High Speed WIFI - Super Clean','5 year old detached guest house in Laurelhurst/North Tabor.  Bright and spacious with vaulted cedar ceilings.  Modern Industrial style with many eco-friendly features such as mini-split heat/ac, tankless water heater, and all-natural fiber area rugs and linens means fewer toxins and a low carbon footprint.   Situated near Laurelhurst and Mount Tabor parks with restaurants and amenities nearby.   We are also pet friendly and allow well-behaved dogs on leashes for a $30 fee per dog, per visit.','Awesome Portland location!  Walk to Starbucks, a mini mart, a pizza place and new Indonesian restaurant all within 1 block!  Beautiful tree-lined streets makes our neighborhood highly sought after. We also have several restaurants, pubs, food carts and shops within a mile.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d48ac08f-d4fb-48cc-83c4-8255a796b9bd.jpg',30942269,52,'45.52553','-122.61659',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,123.00,2,28,524,4.98,31338578),(1410,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31339668','Cozy NE Portland Neighborhood Studio, walkable!','This light and bright studio is the lower level of our family home in the Piedmont neighborhood of NE Portland. Enjoy your own entrance and private space. This open studio can accommodate two people with a soft and comfortable queen bed, an eating area with table and chairs, a private bathroom with tile shower, TV, and kitchenette.<br />While there is no shared space, please keep in mind you will hear footsteps or muffled voices from above at points throughout the day.','Our neighborhood in NE Portland is centrally located to SE, SW, and NW Portland neighborhoods. We are a quick 5 minute drive to the I-5 freeway and bridges to downtown. Our immediate neighborhood is residential, but is very walkable to Portland hot spots like Mississippi district, Alberta, Williams street, and the Dekum triangle. We are also within walking distance of a few amazing parks, like Peninsula Park and rose garden. Our location is truly central with the added bonus of a safe, family-oriented neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ad8221df-eff4-4036-82e3-ff3d4f04dec5.jpg',6933405,48,'45.569540782728076','-122.66302768199178',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,64.00,1,60,438,4.89,31339668),(1411,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31339935','Clean and Beautiful Inner SE Apartment','Location, location, location! This well-designed, comfortable 800 SF private entrance studio apartment offers quick walking access to the famous restaurants and bars on Division and Clinton. Fancy a trip to the mountain or coast? We are only 90 minutes away by car. Cooking at home is easy in the well-appointed kitchenette (microwave, induction hot plate, fridge, toaster/mini oven). Easy street parking and good public transport, car share, bike/scooter rental access.','The neighborhood is a sought after area; a five block walk from all the shops and restaurants on Division St. and well connected to public transport and public bike rentals. There is a great parks for kids within walking distance (Piccolo park, Powell Park, Kenilworth Park) and some excellent restaurants like Áve Gene\'s, Oma’s Takeaway, and Little T\'s American Bakery (a breakfast/lunch delight). There are some cool bars like the Imperial bottle shop and Richmond Lounge. And ice-cream at Salt N Straw is famous (go at 3PM for no line!)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e6d1163b-097a-4979-9093-ac8306144175.jpg',21441201,8,'45.50052','-122.63537',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,79.00,2,90,162,4.87,31339935),(1412,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31351647','Private bedroom, bathroom, and living area','An easy space to relax and recharge while you make the most of your Portland stay. <br />You\'ll be close to a variety of popular destinations while being just 6 miles from the airport.<br />Located in the Montavilla neighborhood, you’ll be about a half-mile from the bars, restaurants, and local charm of Stark St.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-31351647/original/e55bcc71-5e06-4a8e-84af-e55ade46a6ce.jpeg',19475324,10,'45.52172','-122.56985',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,60,80,13,4.92,31351647),(1413,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31360833','Cozy Kenton apartment with fireplace','This private basement apartment is clean, comfortable and calm -- a cozy home away from home. Located in the sweet Kenton neighborhood of north Portland, the space includes a bedroom with queen size bed, spacious living room with a gas fireplace and smart TV, fully equipped kitchen and full bath. The apartment is accessed via its own private, keyless entrance.','Kenton is a fantastic neighborhood to enjoy and explore. A sweet local grocery is four blocks away, three great parks are within a mile (Kenton, Columbia + Arbor Lodge), and plenty of restaurants, coffee shops and bars are also within walking distance (we\'re happy to recommend some of our favorite spots!).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-31360833/original/26e47126-c395-42d2-8821-60d95bf1cb82.jpeg',5433404,55,'45.58003','-122.69888',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,14,222,4.90,31360833),(1414,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31392149','Modern Mt. Tabor Home','Relaxed + modern house.  Comfortable for the urban dweller that would rather stay in a quaint neighborhood than a downtown hotel, it\'s a great home base for the traveler curious to explore Portland — especially for the food lover! Located in the quintessential Hawthorne/Mt. Tabor neighborhood. One block from Mt. Tabor Park Mt.Tabor dog park! with endless hiking trails, great restaurants, bars and bus lines to explore Portland. 15 minutes drive from the airport.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2a1d6a78-042e-4358-8771-a0a3f0807847.jpg',89919003,15,'45.50595','-122.60346',1,5,3.50,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,1125,14,5.00,31392149),(1415,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31394104','‘Well Rested’-Accessible & bright private studio','Converted detached garage into a new, bright, studio. I love hosting people from all parts of the world. I  live right next door, so I’m available if you need anything but I respect your privacy. <br /><br />*No stairs leading up to, or in the apartment<br />*Off street parking<br />*EV (electric vehicle) fast charging station<br />*Heated floors in bathroom<br />*Full kitchen<br />*55 inch Smart TV <br />*A/C<br />*Easy freeway access<br />*Close to public transportation','We are located in the Piedmont residential neighborhood in the North side of town. We are 4 blocks away from the beautiful Peninsula Park Rose Gardens.  We are 20 minutes drive from the airport, close to the freeway (I-5) and only a 5-10 minute drive from some of the popular streets in Portland like Alberta, Mississippi, and NW 23rd. We are also a 12-15 walk to the max train stop.<br /><br />Other:<br /><br />*New Seasons grocery market is a 15 minute walk.<br />*Dekum street has good eats and is a 15 minute walk.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/83d179a2-8055-42d4-b508-fb0675022506.jpg',3302285,48,'45.5729','-122.67088',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,89.00,2,27,335,4.98,31394104),(1416,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31446743','Immerse yourself into the center of NW Portland','The Irving Street Towers is a charming, heritage listed building built in 1910 that is located in one of the most desirable parts of NW Portland. The apartment is a private corner unit with lots of windows and character with exposed brick, a claw-foot tub and space to relax after exploring the city. Wifi, gas heating & a great working kitchen. If you don\'t feel like cooking, just walk out onto NW 21st & you have a wide range of gourmet restaurants and hip bars to choose from.','Exploring Portland is endless and this home is a great central location with the inner city feel but the ability to enjoy beautiful walks and be transformed. Forest Park is only 1.4miles from the apartment, with short and long trails to enjoy. One trail will lead you straight to the historic Pittock Mansion. The Japanese Gardens is only 1.1miles and well worth a visit, there is a charge for entry. Portland Saturday market is down along the water front, enjoy a stroll around & see many local designers.<br />For foodies, just outside your front door you will find an array of choices from Thai, Japanese, Indian, Frozen yogurt and great coffee. Endless places to find a drink & enjoy the happy hour prices.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-31446743/original/6c06fbe2-6559-4aad-9abf-07c5b448d2c6.jpeg',158074447,27,'45.5279','-122.69472',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,72.00,31,1125,21,4.67,31446743),(1417,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31447915','North Tabor hideaway w/ desk, fast Wi-Fi, near MAX','You\'ll be staying in a top floor bedroom in this lovely home in North Tabor. Be downtown in 15 minutes and to/from Portland Airport (PDX) within 20 minutes via MAX Light Rail. Three minutes to Providence Portland Medical Center. It\'s a quiet neighborhood, but only a 5-min walk to public transportation, coffee shop and grocery store, and with easy freeway access. Guests may use the light-filled living, kitchen and dining areas as well as the upstairs bathroom with heated floor.','It\'s considered the \"North Tabor\" section of Portland and there are several coffee shops, restaurants, dispensaries, food carts, Trader Joe\'s and a Fred Meyer Marketplace nearby.<br /><br />FOOD CARTS, PARKS AND MORE:<br />Take a 10-minute walk or quick drive and you\'ll find Rocket Empire Machine: A brand new food hall featuring Gigantic Brewing, Alleamin African Kitchen (Somalian), Tierra del Sol (Oaxacan), The Pie Spot and Sea & River Sushi. Go in the other direction for The Barley Pod: A beer garden and food cart park featuring Bull Run Pizza, La Arepa (Venezualen Street Food), Hapa (Ramen), Poblano Pepper (Mexican Food), Bam Pow (Burgers), Namu (Korean/Hawai’ian), Yaba Yabaa (Falafel), Eat Well (Vegetarian/Vegan), Flew The Coop (Fried Chicken) and The Dark Side (Thai), centered around Baerlic Brewing.<br /><br />It\'s a beautiful walk through the neighborhood to Mt. Tabor: A unique park on an extinct volcano with a 360 degree view of the area, walking trails and steps through the tr','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fa07eee1-e1a9-4654-bac9-b0c571bfcdc6.jpg',1314197,52,'45.52743','-122.59754',2,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,77.00,1,16,164,4.98,31447915),(1418,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31449268','Cute Studio*Division/Hawthorne*93WalkScore+Parking','Inside our cozy, 350 sqft guest suite you\'ll find everything you need for an excellent short-term stay! The comfy queen bed provides a restful night\'s sleep and the living room with 40\" TV is the perfect spot to enjoy Netflix or Hulu (your login required). <br /><br />If you\'re here for business, the work desk is a great place for laptop time and it\'s close to the efficiency kitchenette with microwave, mini-fridge & coffee maker -- essentials to get the day started off right! We can\'t wait to host you!','Nestled squarely in the Richmond neighborhood of SE Portland, our home is located on the corner of two residential streets. Just a few blocks away, you\'ll find some of Portland\'s best dining, coffee & shopping with Stumptown coffee, Petite Provence & Por Que No. Walk a little further to Salt & Straw, Blue Star Donut, Waffle Window & Bollywood Theater. You can truly live life like a local here!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/81feb139-5f5a-46d6-a5c8-eaa102d3c727.jpg',235588475,8,'45.50763','-122.61565',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,98.00,2,10,167,4.96,31449268),(1419,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31496329','Private Montavilla Mid-Century, Park-Like Setting','Private, daylight-basement 1300 sq ft guest-suite in a park-like setting, in the Montavilla neighborhood. <br />Cozy bedroom w/ king bed. <br />Large dining area &  living room w/ fireplace & large screen TV.  <br />Kitchenette w/ everything you need to make coffee, tea & simple meals (modern hot plate, Instant Pot, toaster). <br />Short walk to great dining, coffee shops, pubs & eclectic retail on Stark & Glisan Streets. <br />5 minute drive to beautiful Mount Tabor Park. 15 minutes to downtown Portland & the airport!','Montavilla is an eclectic, artsy, family-oriented, working class neighborhood in East Portland. There are lots of really great restaurants, bars, brew pubs, and retail shops a short, 5-10 minute walk down the street -but our property is tucked into a quiet residential street. <br />A 5-minute drive (or 20 minute walk) away,  Mount Tabor City Park is an extinct volcano with lots of walking/hiking/biking trails, amazing views both east and west (mountains, city), play grounds and concerts in the summer! There are also two smaller city park within a short walking distance (Montavilla Community Park and Berrydale Park). <br />There are many bus stops within several blocks of the house. <br />There are two Max light rail stations within 1 mile/20 minutes walk or a quick bus ride away. <br />There is yoga, acupuncture, naturopathic medicine, massage and chiropractic practices nearby and the nationally- acclaimed Dharma Rain Zen Center is a 6 minute drive! <br />We are also a quick drive to l','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4a6aba45-6b42-4823-b802-b7d4d8781914.jpg',19686646,10,'45.52294','-122.57575',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,120.00,2,120,57,4.96,31496329),(1420,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31519710','Desirable NE Alameda area-Apartment w/ Kitchen','This is close in Northeast Portland. 15 minutes to Airport. 10 Minutes to downtown. Walk to shops, restaurants & grocery store. Safe neighborhood. Easy street parking: Space is a spacious studio apartment with a Queen bed and couch that converts to a bed. Guests have their own Kitchen & Bathroom with a shower. Laundry available upon request. Co-Host lives upstairs. There may be a bit of noise from above.  We are available to give information or give you privacy.<br />Internet speeds up to 100 mbps.','Walkable to shops, restaurants and grocery. Bus line nearby. Alberta Street is just to the North. Hollywood District just to the South. The neighborhood is very family friendly and safe. It is quiet but very close to many Portland hot spots. We love to walk everywhere!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ea2ea6c1-f669-4f1f-ba7e-961306693e06.jpg',155027096,46,'45.5479','-122.62485',2,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,92.00,2,30,219,4.88,31519710),(1421,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31520770','Luxe Suites:15 mins PDXairport','Peaceful and centrally-located. Super hosts since January 2019.<br />- 15 mins from PDX airport, 82nd Jade district (great Asian restaurants)<br />- 20-25 mins to downtown, Moda Center, Japanese Garden, Chinese Garden, Happy Valley, Hawthorne District, Alberta, Vancouver<br />- 1 min toGlendoveer Golf Course <br />- 30 mins to Beaverton/Tigard, Multnomah Falls, Silverton Falls.<br />-<br />#19-111504-000-00-HO','We live in a quiet, established 1940s neighborhood on the Glendoveer Golf Course corridor. Hidden mid-century gems are two to three streets down.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cf239e7d-7fd0-498a-8a47-31fe1917a5fb.jpg',202400439,71,'45.53085','-122.5079',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,67.00,2,28,523,4.85,31520770),(1422,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31534539','Historic 4BR 2BA 2,000 Sq. Ft. Irvington Bungalow!','Located in one of the oldest and most beautiful historic neighborhoods in Central Portland, this charming 1927 Irvington Bungalow has  4 bedrooms, 2 bathrooms and 2,000 square feet of living space...plenty for everyone!  <br /><br />The home is conveniently located blocks from the Moda and Convention Centers and you can walk, bike, drive or Uber everywhere.   More than 100 coffee shops, pubs, restaurants and grocery stores are within a 15 minute walk  and downtown is just 16 minutes away by bike!','The tree-lined historic neighborhood is very walkable, with a beautiful park and tennis courts only two blocks away. The Lloyd Center Mall, Whole Foods and New Seasons grocery stores are a 15 minute walk and neighborhood pubs and coffee shops are around the corner. <br /><br />If you don\'t want to walk, there are so many other options to get around the city. Biketown bike rental is at the Nike outlet store five blocks away. If you want to travel longer distances, take the short 20 minute walk to the 7th Ave. Max light rail station. Or call a ride share to take the short 10 minute drive to Pioneer Courthouse Square and check out the downtown core. Rent a scooter and explore one of the many unique neighborhoods, including Hawthorn, Alberta Arts District  and funky Mississippi. Each vicinity has numerous boutique shops, antique stores and restaurants to easily fill a day.  <br /><br />With over 100 restaurants within one mile of the house you can try a new restaurant every night. Foodies ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzE1MzQ1Mzk%3D/original/5f16753b-f465-48c8-bd4c-e8949083cbf3.jpeg',236328262,7,'45.54508','-122.65681',1,8,2.00,4.00,5.00,268.00,2,29,103,4.98,31534539),(1423,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31539235','Stunning Modern Loft Apt w/Tons of Natural Light','A beautiful, modern getaway in the heart of SE Portland. The perfect spot for a weekend stay or a longer visit to Stumptown.','With a Walk Score of 91, the apartment is two blocks from happening Division Street - home to Portland\'s Restaurant Row, coffee shops, bakeries, shopping, New Seasons grocery store, a sweet little park, bike rentals, and more. It is also two blocks from the #4 bus route, which goes downtown. This is truly one of the best locations in town to get a real sense of Portland, with easy access to the rest of the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/89aed09e-0631-4210-b480-acfb45fffaa6.jpg',1608236,25,'45.50551','-122.64073',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,122.00,30,30,140,4.99,31539235),(1424,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31560228','The Urban Fern - Walk to Shops/MAX/Food!','Welcome to the Urban Fern!  <br />This light-filled 1920\'s bungalow was completely remodeled, combining vintage Portland charm with modern comfort & amenities. <br /><br />Perfect location in a close-in Portland neighborhood w great access to the city. On a major bike street just blocks from the MAX train, shops, restaurants,  parks, food carts, grocery & more. Walk/bike/train to everything you need!  Easy to get around w/out a car but if you bring one there is plenty of free street parking right out front.','Home is located in the Overlook neighborhood in North Portland.  Centrally located between the popular destinations of Downtown PDX, Alberta Arts, Mississippi Ave, Williams Corridor, Dekum Triangle & St John\'s making it the perfect base camp for exploring Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8d4858c6-e3cb-4e57-adf4-5edbb71b101b.jpg',11182438,13,'45.56539','-122.68662',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,82.00,1,90,272,4.94,31560228),(1425,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31568106','Beautiful Tiny House','This beautiful studio or \"Tiny House\" punches above its square footage with tall ceilings and tons of natural light, and comes equipped with all the modern amenities for a true Portland experience. Located on quiet, safe, tree lined street in the Historic Irvington neighborhood, the space lives big and features stylish design, furnishings and an open layout. Walking/biking distance to the best restaurants, coffee shops and night life in the city. Close to public transportation and PDX airport.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fd4285f5-8a06-4905-be67-269453a1196e.jpg',5755250,7,'45.53863','-122.65587',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,73.00,2,15,386,4.91,31568106),(1426,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31585548','The Urban Nook ~ Steps to Shops/Max/Food!','Welcome to the Urban Nook, a recently remodeled basement studio ~ a fun & cozy hotel alternative!  <br />Lower level of 1920\'s craftsman house on large private lot with separate entrance & easy parking.<br /><br />Super stellar location in a close-in Portland neighborhood with great access to the city. Located on a major bike street & just blocks from the MAX train, shops, restaurants, parks, rose garden, food carts, natural grocery, bike rental & more. Walk/bike/train to everything you need!','Home is located in the Overlook neighborhood in North Portland. Centrally located between the popular destinations of Downtown Pdx, Alberta Arts, Mississippi Ave, Williams Corridor, Dekum Triangle & St John\'s making it the perfect base camp for exploring Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0c3b356a-e055-4352-b6ec-fdbcfc389779.jpg',11182438,13,'45.56516','-122.68765',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,74.00,1,90,348,4.95,31585548),(1427,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31649731','Chic Guest House in the Heart of the City','This guest house boasts designer fixtures and finishes created to exude equal levels of style and comfort. White walls, herringbone wood floors, and tall vaulted ceilings create a natural and airy ambiance that flows throughout every room. 1-level, ADA-friendly, with walk-in curbless shower and plenty of space to maneuver in spa-like bathroom and throughout.  Our guests have full access to the private freestanding guest house, as well as the concrete patio just outside the unit.','The home is in Laurelhurst, one of Portland\'s oldest neighborhoods. It\'s a walkable area with great options for dining out, relaxing in a cafe, and going for strolls through the park. Public transport is nearby making it easy to explore the city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8b11e34f-5b21-4ed1-8c12-32386ab2b589.jpg',35082631,23,'45.53009','-122.62628',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,121.00,2,27,377,4.94,31649731),(1428,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31696875','Cozy Bungalow in SE Portland','This home is cozy and bright, quiet and restful. Located in south east Portland you can enjoy the lovely hikes and hot-springs south of Portland along the Clackamus River, while also being close to all the fun things the city has to offer. The house is about twenty minutes from downtown , five minutes from Woodstock, ten minutes from Hawthorn.  Our home comfortably sleeps six, but it also perfect for a couple. It is cute and welcoming, and is always kept very clean and tidy for our guests.','It\'s a quiet neighborhood with wide streets and friendly folks that tend to keep to themselves.  The Woodstock and Foster-Powell neighborhoods are around 5 minutes away and the Hawthorne, Division and Sellwood districts are all around 10 minutes away with plenty of restaurants, bars, movie theaters, music venues and shops.  Downtown is 15-20 minutes away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/52349ff5-5568-4316-bcfc-15c3159bffda.jpg',237714363,69,'45.46526','-122.60193',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,93.00,2,1125,283,4.78,31696875),(1429,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31717654','Industrial Pearl District Loft - Free Parking','Industrial studio loft in the heart of Portland’s Pearl District! Whether relocating or looking for temporary housing, this is an amazing place to enjoy the best of Portland. Walk to restaurants, bars, the river and more within minutes.','The Pearl District is centrally located and in easy walking distance to everything you\'ll need - great restaurants, bars, boutique fitness, parks and more. Located on the West Side of the river, this location makes for an easy commute out to Beaverton but is also only minutes across the bridge to the East side.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-31717654/original/1d9e1b64-2821-40a6-b0ae-a2847f782b00.jpeg',5241391,2,'45.52961','-122.68289',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,113.00,30,1125,2,5.00,31717654),(1430,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31837043','Cozy Mississippi St. Flat (Garden/AC/Parking)','Awesome Airbnb in one of Portland’s hottest neighborhoods!! <br /><br />Basement cozy private apartment with bedroom (queen) , large family room/that may be used as 2nd bedroom (futon couch) and (single bed cot upon request). Full bath with shower and laundry room.<br /><br />Gorgeous  kitchenette with wood countertop, cooktop, air fryer oven, fridge, micro.  Free tea, and coffee.<br /><br />Lovely garden area. Central location. Steps from historic Mississippi St and Williams Ave. Free parking','We love our neighborhood. We have lived here for 15 years. We love the walkability of it and the proximity to many areas in Portland. Mississippi Street is one of the most charming streets in Portland. Full of character and a mix of historic brick buildings as well as well blended newer buildings. Great restaurants, cafes, shops and a laid back and artsy atmosphere. Williams St is the bicycle highway of Portland with many highlights similar to Mississippi St.<br /><br />Within 5 min by car you can be in downtown Portland, in Alberta Arts District, and many other cool neighborhoods in central Portland. You can get to great trails for hiking within 5-10 min car ride and of course you can also go by bicycle with ease from the house. The neighborhood is very eclectic. The park near our house is very family friendly.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b123200c-202a-46b0-8bbd-b0485fbaf418.jpg',114337777,9,'45.54987','-122.66983',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,1,405,4.86,31837043),(1431,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31858709','Spotless Modern Steps from the Best Shops and Restaurants.','New Construction! Grab a snack from a local food cart and kick back under the backyard parasol with a good book. This light-flooded space blends crisp white decor with rich teal accents, cheerful pops of yellow, and calming abstract art for a well-rounded look. There is a mother-in-law suite in the basement of the house so no loud noise, large gatherings after 11 pm (quiet hours). There is a $50 cleaning fee for pets.<br /><br />I personally built this house and I have been an Airbnb host for over 2 years and love being able to offer my home to caring respectful guests.<br /><br />Guests rent the entire top unit/main house. This has a private entrance only accessible by guests.  Around the back of the house is a shared bbq, patio, tables, etc.<br /><br />Mississippi is a great area with plenty of places to eat, shop, see a show, go to a gallery, and relax on the patio and watch people bike by. There is a co-op 4 blocks away for groceries and a Whole Foods around 10 minutes\' walk away.<','Mississippi is a great area with plenty of places to eat, shop, see a show, go to a gallery, and relax on the patio and watch people bike by. There is a co-op 4 blocks away for groceries and a Whole Foods around 10 minutes\' walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/36740e16-2d4c-4312-87a5-c41fdd408ac2.jpg',6063183,24,'45.55674','-122.67433',1,8,3.00,4.00,4.00,265.00,1,90,306,4.96,31858709),(1432,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31861183','✨Stylish & Spacious Home in Bustling FoPo✨','Located in the heart of the vibrant Foster-Powell neighborhood (aka The Slice) in SE Portland. <br /><br />Chill out in our airy modern 2,400 sqft bi-level! Stay in a quiet neighborhood   just four blocks from Foster Road’s famous retail district with awesome boutique pizzerias, cafe, bars, corner stores and local gems.','The neighbors are quiet and respectful, and our street is not a thoroughfare, so there’s very little traffic.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ccd4f989-dd6a-49be-8344-703052014732.jpg',121932858,36,'45.49182','-122.5914',1,4,3.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,21,33,4.91,31861183),(1433,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31896442','Quiet, bright flat | Full kitchen, W/D, 1.5 baths','Welcome to our sunny studio on a quiet side street just one block off of Alberta Street. It\'s perfect for couples, small families or solo travelers looking to soak up the sights.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-31896442/original/1fc7e3cf-846e-44dd-8f02-87a38bc967c1.jpeg',5863705,14,'45.55855314858638','-122.65255211842944',1,2,1.50,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,200,15,5.00,31896442),(1434,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31950837','Cozy Johns Landing Studio!','Great location, Johns Landing, 1 mile from downtown, walking distance to OHSU, the river, shops, restaurants, nice neighborhood coffee shop and Starbucks. high speed internet.<br />Perfect for 2 maximum 3 guests.(please chose a different property if more than 3, the studio can’t accommodate more than 3)<br />This is a none smoking property.<br />Parking is free in the street where this property is, and almost always there is available space.','About 1 mile from downtown, walking distance to the river, coffee shops and restaurants!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9b93c8ed-cdfc-4832-8e60-e8ca8d9c5a55.jpg',65277088,22,'45.48242','-122.67626',1,3,1.00,0.00,0.00,89.00,1,1125,133,4.82,31950837),(1435,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31983387','1910 Historic Jessie Morehead House -98 WalkScore','Welcome to a Registered Historic Home designed by renowned architect William C. Knighton, situated on NW 21st Ave with a WalkScore of 98. Original woodwork, fixtures, and tasteful furnishings add timeless elegance to your stay.<br /><br />The unbeatable location puts you steps away from highly rated restaurants and bars. The only challenge will be deciding which spot to try first. Experience the perfect blend of historic charm and modern convenience in this architectural gem.','Nestled in the vibrant and historic Northwest District. This prime location offers a perfect blend of urban excitement and charming neighborhood vibes, making it an ideal spot for visitors looking to experience the best of Portland.<br /><br />The area around NW Everett St is renowned for its culinary delights. You’ll find an eclectic mix of top-rated restaurants, cozy cafes, and trendy bars within walking distance. From farm-to-table eateries and artisanal bakeries to international cuisine and food carts, there’s something to satisfy every palate. Don’t miss out on the local favorites like Salt & Straw for unique ice cream flavors and the iconic Blue Moon Tavern & Grill for a laid-back dining experience.<br /><br />Just a few blocks away is the bustling NW 23rd Avenue, a shopper\'s paradise lined with an array of boutiques, vintage stores, and specialty shops. Whether you\'re hunting for unique fashion pieces, handmade jewelry, or quirky gifts, you\'ll find plenty of treasures to bring h','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-31983387/original/4113dae6-8210-47a0-b76a-fd7d5d054e40.jpeg',88253867,27,'45.5252','-122.69371',1,8,2.50,3.00,4.00,278.00,1,365,384,4.87,31983387),(1436,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/31993074','The Green Door PDX: A European Inspired Cottage.','A bolthole created from passion by Kaemingk Design, The Green Door PDX was designed to provide a unique respite from the energy of Portland while being conveniently located only minutes from downtown and popular shopping/eating districts.  We have taken queues from Europe and built a traditional field cottage tucked into the landscape at the front of the property and surrounded it with mature greenery for an inviting welcome and ultimate privacy for our guests.','The Overlook neighborhood is unique and quiet yet close to all the authentic Portland hot spots. We are less than block from Adidas headquarters and less than 5 minute drive from Portland\'s Mississippi District, Alberta District and Williams Corridor.   Enjoy downtown in less than 10 minutes or walk only a few blocks to nearby favorites like Milk Glass Market, The Old Gold and Spitz.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2b0ede05-a6b3-4c6c-b059-40871ae52483.jpg',31143498,13,'45.5592','-122.69148',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,155.00,2,29,363,4.97,31993074),(1437,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32051260','2 Bedroom Basement Apartment in Arbor Lodge','Two bedroom apartment in the basement of our 1922 home. This private space has a living room, kitchenette, dining room table, bathroom and separate entrance. Located around the corner from a grocery store and a bus stop right in front of our house. We look forward to having you stay with us!','Welcome to North Portland! We do live on a very busy street; the plus side is we are within walking distance to a grocery store, restaurants and a convenience store is right across the street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6c92e39a-93f8-4155-a7e1-f51a9554bf83.jpg',12591253,51,'45.576599','-122.69577',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,1,31,36,4.92,32051260),(1438,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32103577','Attractive and Affordable Suite in Alberta Arts','This beautiful, brand new guest suite is perfectly located just North of Alberta street and provides everything you need for a comfortable place to come home to after a long day of exploring, eating and imbibing at all the amazing options Portland has to offer.','Historically known as the focal point of Portland culture, Alberta lives up to expectations and supplies residents and visitors with the best of Artistic Culture, Fine Dining, and Artisan shopping. On the last thursday of every month there is an art walk that features galleries and shops during the winter months, and array of local artisan vendors lining the streets in the summer months. Aside from the bustling urban culture, Alberta features charming residential areas just steps from the exciting bohemian culture.  Our home is walking distance to other attractions such as Alberta Park and Mcmenamins Kennedy school.  We are 25 miles to Multnomah falls, 65 miles to Mt. Hood, and 70 miles to Oregon Coast.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0335804a-bffb-450f-9754-c9d15b70a7e7.jpg',36981269,1,'45.56115','-122.63645',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,60.00,1,1125,750,4.94,32103577),(1439,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32147679','Charming Craftsman in NE Portland','Our home is located in the Alameda District in NE Portland. We live on a quiet, wide street that is within walking distance to the restaurants, bars and shops of Alberta Street, Killingsworth Street and Fremont Street. Our home gets wonderful light, has plenty of space for visitors and a dedicated area for kids!','Our home is central to the hot spots of NE Portland (Alberta, Killingsworth, Fremont). Guilder is our favorite coffee shop and it is only a 10 min walk away! They\'re friendly,  make wonderful espresso and good food, and there\'s a solid playground for kids nearby. Wilshire park is also a few blocks away, which has a dirt running loop that is about 1k long.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/eea96d44-f124-4c67-aea5-206fba15b193.jpg',4507214,19,'45.54974','-122.63412',1,6,3.00,4.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,0,1.00,32147679),(1440,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32165887','Relaxing Retreat at two rivers portland','Two rivers retreat is a cozy newly renovated unit with one queen and a twin perfect for two or three adults or a child in an amazing walkable neighborhood full of shopping and  dining. It is nestled on a quiet tree lined residential street.  It has everything you need whether you are visiting PDX for a few days or for an extended stay.','Fox Chase or the greater Concordia/ Alberta Arts neighborhood really has a bit of everything. Great food, coffee, yoga studio,local health food groceries, pet stores, bars, art,... really everything!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/70852c5a-a481-435b-961f-a7d0b7c4fbcc.jpg',13602640,1,'45.563846588134766','-122.6345443725586',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,102.00,1,1125,68,4.72,32165887),(1441,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32179649','Shipping Container Home in famous Alberta Arts!','Straight out of the pages of Dwell! Have a designer Portland experience in our luxury container home (and private deck and 2nd bedroom casita). Maximum minimalism, comfort & style. And just outside your door is dense and bustling Alberta Arts District full of boutiques, galleries, craft beer, oregon wines, street fairs all within walking distance. Plus nearby Mississippi Ave too. A perfect location, in a stylish modern architectural setting. It would be our pleasure to host you!','This text box can not contain how much there is to explore on Alberta St. (aka Alberta arts district): Search the web, you\'ll find galleries, coffee shops, microbrews, wine bars, authentic tacos, and food(!!) from low brow but delicious carts, to foodie favorites that put PDX food on the map: Aviary, Bollywood Theater, Bamboo Sushi, lots of vegetarian options abound on colorful Alberta, and when you\'re done exploring Alberta, go another 5 minutes to equally fun Mississippi Ave. Beyond that, you are 15 min from downtown, Powell\'s etc. 30 min from the Gorge, 90 to the coast, and 2 blocks to Portland\'s best organic grocery market: New Seasons. You are going to have a great stay in a fantastic location!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/abcd646e-1c14-4c75-bdf7-8e6431f3c543.jpg',241446961,1,'45.56101','-122.6277',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,96.00,2,1125,208,4.88,32179649),(1442,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32205876','Bright and Spacious NW 23rd Ave Vintage Apartment','Absolute best location in Portland\'s most sought after area, Nob Hill. Walk to numerous restaurants, bars, retail shops, high end grocery stores like New Seasons, yoga, and more. Just a 100 steps from the famous NW 23th Ave.  No better location in NW Portland, steps to everything.<br />Our gorgeous vintage apartment is almost 1000 sq. feet. The bedroom has a King bed , 2 TVs, high speed Wi-Fi.  Spacious living room  with lots of lounge area. Great for  long stays, large enough to be comfortable.','The Nob Hill neighborhood in NW Portland is Portland\'s most trendy in town, a perfect place to base out of while visiting Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-32205876/original/0d199456-6a99-4944-aaa2-2e478ed91e84.jpeg',241675301,27,'45.5314','-122.6972',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,120,1,4.00,32205876),(1443,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32335809','Spacious Guest House','Wonder why Portland is such a popular tourist destination? Come and stay at our 2BR, 1.5 Bath Portland guest house in King/Sabin Neighborhood. Comfortably blending modern touch with classic charm, the house is between up and coming Williams/Mississippi districts and bustling Alberta Arts-perfectly situated to give easy access to boutique and artisan shops, galleries, dozens of Portland’s best restaurants, bars and brewpubs while providing the best comfort and amenities.','We are in a great location! We live on a residential street within walking distance between Mississippi/Williams Avenues and Alberta Art Districts. Up-and-coming Mississippi/Williams Avenues feature a long stretch of stores, acclaimed eateries and bars. Albert Art District teems with art, shopping and diverse dining options. Both neighborhoods are just blocks away from our house. Our house is also 15 minutes drive to downtown or 10 minutes drive to Pearl District. Portland’s compact, walkable downtown offers easy access to great food, green spaces, cultural offerings and tax-free shopping. Browse the city’s most diverse mix of retail brands, see a show and grab a bite at a food cart or fine restaurant. The chic Pearl District features galleries and cultural institutions, as well as stylish shops and acclaimed eateries.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3458c5c4-863e-4e89-bc34-1a1040b06759.jpg',242772784,14,'45.55336','-122.65844',1,5,1.50,2.00,3.00,180.00,2,10,242,4.98,32335809),(1444,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32344212','Main House in Madison South','Enjoy your stay at this serene house in the Madison South neighborhood of NE Portland, where comfort and convenience meet! Located near the base of Rocky Butte, this rental house is perfect for your next stay, with its charming interior and peaceful surroundings.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-32344212/original/f3b192db-d7e4-4fb8-8a3c-57100a47b38b.jpg',33648860,74,'45.53598','-122.57592',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,28,48,4.92,32344212),(1445,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32380294','Quiet Retreat at the Heart of Inner SE Portland','A classic mid century brick home in the heart of some of the best restaurants and night life in Portland.  This comfortable home sleeps six with a sunny patio to enjoy, and peaceful yard with a giant Deodora Cedar tree. <br /><br />You’ll be located near 28th and Belmont on a picturesque residential street, with easy access to the Belmont district, 28th Avenue “Restaurant Row”,  Kerns, Burnside, Hawthorne, Division St/Clinton, Central Eastside districts, and a short bus ride to downtown and the Pearl','Located in inner SE Portland at the heart of some of the best restaurants, parks, and shops in Portland.  Located at the cross roads of the Belmont District, Buckman, Sunnyside, and Hawthorne neighborhoods, 28th Ave Restaurant Row, and near Burnside, Glisan, Hawthorne, Division, and Clinton.   Restaurants, shops, and entertainment are plentiful on all these streets. Downtown is about 2 miles to the west.<br /><br />Parks are close by, Colonial Summers, Laurelhurst, Sunnyside Environmental School, Mt Tabor, and the Eastbank Esplanade are all within walking distance depending on your energy.<br /><br />Some favorite neighborhood restaurants are Nostrana, Crema, Ken\'s Artisan Pizza, PaaDee, Screen Door, Navarre, Davenport, Baby Doll Pizza, Blutos, Cricket Cafe, Bread and Ink  ... and  there are many many more!<br /><br />Providence Portland Medical Center is 1.9 miles.<br />Legacy Emanuel Hospital and Health Center is 3.4 miles.<br />Good Samaritan Medical Center is 3.6 miles.<br />OHSU H','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e66622f4-5f19-4134-8a5b-a82cafb64427.jpg',243140548,16,'45.51731','-122.63678',1,6,2.00,3.00,4.00,175.00,7,1125,64,4.94,32380294),(1446,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32402731','Mid-Century 2 Bed/1Bath newly Remodeled Duplex!','This is a beautifully remodeled mid-century unit in a duplex, completely furnished with a fenced private side-yard and shared backyard. Hardwood floors, stacked washer & dryer, window coverings. Corner lot, single level, walking distance from New Seasons and all Woodstock has to offer! We just had the furniture professionally cleaned after the last guest and stocked the unit with toilet paper and paper towels to get you started.<br />No smoking in unit or on property, please!','Near Reed College, First Cup Coffee House, Laughing Planet, Delta Cafe, Lutz Tavern, and Cloud City Ice Cream. . . Great for couples, business travelers, and furry friends (pets).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8818eb81-1048-4869-84bb-300d1dbeb43d.jpg',111643390,65,'45.48047','-122.5961',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,72.00,30,180,25,4.72,32402731),(1447,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32423269','Convenient Mt. Tabor private bedroom and bath','Convenient private basement bedroom and adjacent private bath in Mt. Tabor neighborhood.  Walking distance to public transportation.   15 min to downtown Portland by car, 25 min by bus.  10-15 min walk to restaurants.  20 min walk or short bus ride to supermarket.  Well-traveled hosts with long experience in Portland available to answer questions.   We comply with all covid avoidance direction and maintain cleanliness.  Private keypad entry.  Bedroom features queen-size bed and extra sofa/bed.','Pleasant east Portland neighborhood within walking distance to the Hawthorne District\'s restaurants, stores, and theaters.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzI0MjMyNjk%3D/original/06e5654c-4ff0-4989-85c7-8ae1a7894db4.jpeg',238984344,15,'45.51492','-122.61009',2,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,50.00,1,1125,301,4.87,32423269),(1448,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32423425','\"THE 2509\"  Creative Arts and Living Space','An ideally located modern, 800sf active arts space/loft with 9ft ceilings,  large windows, movable furniture, separate sleeping quarters, bathroom with a shower, and a kitchenette, which is only rented out in the summer. There is an outdoor space with a bench, table and chairs, separate entrance, and easy accessibility to many urban amenities. Completed in 2019,  this is a unique space that combines the aesthetics of a loft-like creative space and the practicality of a modern living quarters.','Great walkable neighborhood with restaurants, coffee houses, stores, movie theatres, and other urban amenities reachable by foot within minutes. The neighborhood, Sullivan\'s Gulch, is an urban mixture of old, turn of the century one-family houses and <br />newer apartment buildings, and it is one of the closest neighborhoods to downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-32423425/original/6133ab3c-b575-41e3-b2f6-70a79a909e4f.jpeg',415758,4,'45.53305','-122.64006',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,1,31,45,4.98,32423425),(1449,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32448243','Tiny Humboldt House','Charming tiny house located perfectly between Mississippi, Alberta, and Williams neighborhoods.  Enjoy this cozy guesthouse which features work from local designers and is also showcased in Little House In The City.  Tiny Humboldt has also been featured in The New York Times.','Located just off the corner of N Alberta and N Albina St.  Walking distance to Mississippi Avenue, Alberta, and Williams shops and restaurants!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-32448243/original/fb4169a6-ba15-47bd-929a-338acf03e302.jpg',70062145,24,'45.55861','-122.67401',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,140.00,2,14,317,4.99,32448243),(1450,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32499085','Get away and relax at Sierra Cottage!','Sierra Cottage features two master suites in the heart of inner SE Portland.  You\'ll be steps away from trendy cafes, restaurants & shops of the SE Division Street / Richmond neighborhood. From Sierra Cottage you can walk, bike or ride share to all the neighborhood hot spots including downtown Portland, less than 2.5 miles away.','In our Richmond neighborhood, you are steps away from some of the best food and cuisine in the Pacific Northwest! Just down the street from our cottage are oodles of coffee shops, bakeries, cafes, food carts, fabulous restaurants, wine bars, cocktail bars, local craft beers - and my favorites:  hand made gelato, craft ice cream and frozen yogurt! Several convenience stores, natural food stores, local supermarkets and many shops are all within 15 blocks.  When you need to walk off all those calories, head east to Mt. Tabor city park (2.5 mi.) for a fabulous view of the city, or cross over one of Portland\'s many bridges into downtown, just 2.5 miles away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/64a54794-f8bf-4640-b558-03293f8ff06b.jpg',244187765,8,'45.50351','-122.62898',1,4,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,1125,39,5.00,32499085),(1451,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32506802','Amazing Upscale 3BR,WiFi,King Bed/Parking❤️','Charming house, trendy with an amazing open concept kitchen & heated floor bathroom. It has been thoughtfully decorated to make your stay comfortable, enjoyable and private. You can expect very clean, well appointed, cozy, spacious and turn- key accommodations. <br />It is the perfect alternative to a hotel, providing a cost savings, convenience, and all the comforts of a home. Ideal for corporate housing & families with relocation needs. Small service dogs ONLY upon request and approval.','This neighborhood doesn\'t get any better! You have the water front, parks, great restaurants, bars, coffee shops and stores all within walking distance, making it really convenient for all your needs and JUST MINUTES AWAY FROM DOWNTOWN! <br />Daily errands can be accomplished on a bike, there are bike lanes and trails, road connectivity to Downtown and most of the attractions in Portland.<br />Sellwood-Moreland is considered one of the best places to live in Oregon. It offers residents an urban feel. Many families and young professionals live in Sellwood-Moreland.<br />One of the best things about this very walkable neighborhood is how incredibly friendly, safe and clean it is!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2e8899ee-bbfd-4257-a6d5-e22bade96d52.jpg',213350724,20,'45.46474','-122.65962',1,5,1.00,3.00,3.00,189.00,30,365,9,5.00,32506802),(1452,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32607298','Beautiful 2-Bedroom in Alameda for Families','This clean and beautiful basement apartment with separate entrance features everything you need to enjoy a comfortable stay in Portland in the heart of the popular Alameda neighborhood. Enjoy a beautiful kitchen, 2 comfortable bedrooms, side patio, and easy access to public transit.','The Alameda neighborhood has shops, amazing restaurants, parks, and grocery stores all around it. You will get the true Portland experience staying here. We are right off of Klickitat Street which was the basis for many of Beverly Cleary\'s books. You can get a map of the three houses where Beverly Cleary lived in the neighborhood and of the school named after her down the road.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/70d7fef2-2f04-4221-9b39-1f1ef9a21f32.jpg',49957564,46,'45.54693','-122.62987',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,108.00,2,30,285,4.95,32607298),(1453,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32611548','Modern Charming House in the Heart of Division','A 1921 house, renovated with minimalist Scandinavian trends,  in a prime southeast Portland location. A five minute walk to Division Street where you can explore some of Portland\'s best restaurants, coffee shops and amazing micro-brews. Queen bed, walk in closet, modern chef\'s kitchen with gas range, wood burning fireplace, TV-room, espresso machine and bodum, washer/dryer and A/C. All the amenities and features you expect when renting a house.','Division Street neighborhood (Richmond) is lively and fun.  Numerous coffee shops, some of Portland\'s best restaurants, ice cream choices, eclectic micro-breweries.  Close to the Hawthorne\'s Powell\'s book store and iconic Bagdad Theatre.  Close to food truck and walking distance to parks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f3f291d5-6ea3-41c5-a0cf-6ce6ec2dbc7d.jpg',32902791,8,'45.50125','-122.63504',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,17,5.00,32611548),(1454,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32616529','The PitStop - 2bdrm, 4 guests, private bath','Come visit our great place to refuel your body and mind or drop your bags and go explore the beauty of Portland. We offer a private suite that includes 2 separate bedrooms and a living space with couch and TV. We also offer a private bath . 5 minutes from Alberta district and 5 minutes to Mississippi ave. Very close to the Portland Airport and downtown.','Our neighborhood has made a name for itself with its distinctive multi-cultural population, socially-conscious inhabitants, and one of the best farmers\' markets in town, located at King Elementary. The King Neighborhood is located along the major thoroughfare of Northeast Portland, Martin Luther King, Jr. Boulevard, also known as Highway 99. Providing easy access to the rest of Northeast, North, Southeast, and west Portland via several bridges, the King neighborhood is a thriving community perfect for commuting anywhere in the metropolitan area. The King neighborhood is home to several of the city\'s best restaurants, including Ned Ludd, Wayne\'s Chicago Red Hots, and the nearby N Williams and N Mississippi dining and shopping districts. King is also within walking distance to some of Portland\'s hippest up-and-coming neighborhoods.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9f3038dc-6104-4c50-949f-d1630ec4fb47.jpg',209826108,14,'45.56447','-122.66348',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,60.00,1,14,711,4.67,32616529),(1455,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32617426','Arbor Lodge Lodge- a relaxing oasis in the city','Architect designed Arbor Lodge cottage. Located in a quiet neighborhood 1/2 block from Arbor Lodge Park. The space is bright and gets a lot of natural light. I hope you find it comfortable and relaxing. It is also conveniently located to many nearby shops, grocery store, restaurants, pubs and transit connections (light rail and bus).','Arbor Lodge is a lovely neighborhood and there is a nice park right down the street. I enjoy walking, riding my bike and running in and around the neighborhood. There are plenty of amenities (organic grocery store, coffee shops, retail shops, restaurants and pubs) within a 10-15 minute walk, Adidas North American HQ (15 min walk). Located close to Historic North Mississippi district (2 miles), Alberta Arts District (2.5 miles), N. Williams corridor (2.5 miles), downtown (5 miles), Forest Park (10 min drive).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1b3921f7-a3c4-4117-b851-83f9ad6ff8b3.jpg',373547,51,'45.57031','-122.69281',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,71.00,2,1125,391,4.95,32617426),(1456,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32663622','1931 bungalow, 1BA, fireplace & yards. No pets.','Cozy old bungalow near great restaurants, breweries, farmers\' market. Walk to Mt. Tabor Park in minutes. Close to the airport, light rail, and bus routes. Secluded with lush vegetation. Front and backyard outdoor seating. Low-carbon-footprint house with recycling and food composting. One owner (myself) is generally home, but often away in the summer. I have a mellow short-haired cat, Luigi. Warning: steep attic steps to upstairs bedroom, sturdy hand railing. Upstairs level is 600 sq ft.','MONTAVILLA NEIGHBORHOOD: Lazy Susan Diner, Ya Hala Lebanese, The Observatory restaurant, Roscoe\'s taproom, Miyamoto Sushi, The Academy Theater, The Beer Bunker, Thatcher\'s, Mt. Tabor, Vintage Cocktail Lounge. Cool independent shops in the hood, and the best Asian restaurants in town; noodle and dumpling houses, and izakaya, etc. Easy to navigate and fun for walks. Great pizza parlor at East Glisan Lounge up the street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/71c6f9e9-748c-4bfa-abb0-6b0081536d75.jpg',9061399,10,'45.52258','-122.58149',1,1,1.00,2.00,3.00,90.00,30,31,8,4.63,32663622),(1457,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32701263','Modern Refuge aka The Glam Pad','New modern apartment in 1920\'s home with its own entrance and easy access to light rail in the Overlook neighborhood of North Portland.  The custom layout prioritizes efficiency and functionality and includes wifi, tv and full kitchen.  The one bedroom unit includes a sofa bed in living room to sleep up to 4 people.  Designed by Trace Salmon of Salmon Built. <br /><br />@glampadpdx','The Overlook neighborhood is in close proximity to several districts full of shops and restaurants such as Alberta and Mississippi streets but nearby is very quiet.  New Seasons grocery is a few blocks away as is the Peninsula Park rose garden.  On street parking is no problem and there is usually a spot directly in front.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/638cfbba-2482-4dbc-9e83-50815afb0026.jpg',9930480,13,'45.56415','-122.68154',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,89.00,1,1125,233,4.91,32701263),(1458,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32720937','Are You Ready to Explore Portland?','Sparkling clean home with a full kitchen!  <br /><br />A spacious, quiet & private bungalow in a thriving NE Portland neighborhood.  <br /><br />The perfect place relax and unwind.  This space is within walking distance to 2 grocery stores, multiple restaurants and Mt. Tabor Park.<br /><br />Enjoy a peaceful back deck to soak up some midday sun & a large front porch to people watch while you drink your morning coffee.','Nearby amenities include:<br />Starbucks<br />7 Virtues Coffee Shop<br />Tabor Tavern<br />Oly\'s Pizza<br />American Dream Pizza<br />Flying Pie Pizza<br />A&L Tavern<br />Leikam Brewery<br />QFC<br />Fred Meyer<br />2 gas stations<br />Providence Hospital','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-32720937/original/16e77810-80f7-458b-b53d-396eb1692c54.jpeg',154575784,52,'45.52402','-122.60461',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,102.00,2,30,146,4.92,32720937),(1459,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32722647','Stay in a Dorm Bed (Female) at NW Portland Hostel','Experience Portland’s top-rated, family-owned hostel, in the vibrant Northwest District! Enjoy a FREE breakfast and explore nearby downtown attractions, Washington Park, the Rose and Japanese Gardens, and hiking trails. Join our daily free events like walking tours, tap tastings, live music, and trivia nights. For over 25 years, our mission has been to provide a welcoming, affordable, and safe space, connecting Portland with travelers worldwide and making a positive impact locally and beyond.','We are located in the Northwest district, just a few blocks from popular shops, cafes, pubs, cinemas, and some of the city\'s best restaurants. Many area attractions, including the Pearl District, downtown Portland, Saturday Market, Portland Farmers Market, Powell\'s Bookstore, art galleries, the Lan Su Chinese Garden, museums, the MLS Stadium, and Pioneer Square, are within walking distance. The Rose Gardens and Japanese Gardens are a short bus ride or a 25-minute walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzI3MjI2NDc%3D/original/29005e4c-fd55-4bfd-bf34-e9dc9db8ddfa.jpeg',2820851,27,'45.52634','-122.68856',3,1,4.00,1.00,4.00,40.00,1,1125,213,4.82,32722647),(1460,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32723932','Urban Cabin on Mt Scott','Close to the city and close to nature, this is the best of both worlds! Tucked into forested Mt Scott on the edge of Portland, a very popular stay! 20 minutes from downtown and convention centers, 5 minutes from the freeway, 5 minutes from several food cart pods, 20 minutes from four major rivers, 30 minutes from the famous Columbia River Gorge waterfalls, and an hour from Mt Hood skiing and Timberline Lodge. Enjoy this entire guest house to yourself with shared driveway parking in front.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f91c9c24-bfa6-40ff-81f6-d3d8c34295b9.jpg',246070767,77,'45.47082909136234','-122.54257438307138',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,119.00,2,90,113,4.88,32723932),(1461,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32724894','Oculus House, a wood & stone neighborhood retreat','The Oculus House is a peaceful one bedroom house with a king size bed. It is located down a private alley in a quiet neighborhood. It’s open floor plan and high ceilings gives a balance of comfort and artistic appeal. There is a lounging loft which can be used as a sleeping space for agile children and adults.   We have designed the house to honor the era in which it was built  and elevate the aesthetic. The kitchen is well-stocked and the bathroom has a luxurious  jetted tub.','Portland\'s St. Johns neighborhood boasts one of the most beautiful bridges in the country, rising above Cathedral Park that borders a dock and beach on the Willamette River; the St. Johns Bridge ends at a trail-head to Forest Park, one of the largest parks within city-limits in the U.S. We are a few blocks from Pier Park, an old-growth forest with lovely walking paths. Pier Park includes a free skate park and a free public disc golf course. St. Johns has two independently-owned movie theaters, many excellent restaurants including one of the best food cart pods in Portland. The grit of Old St. Johns with its dive bars and unpretentious local hang-outs are a contrast to the boutiques,  coffee shops and hipster weed dispensaries laced throughout. Recommendations enthusiastically offered!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-32724894/original/f0be8e20-5102-4c97-a260-e06d0e119ec9.jpg',90662593,58,'45.59817','-122.75669',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,124.00,2,30,226,4.98,32724894),(1462,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32747089','Private Cozy One Bedroom Apartment','Our bright and cozy backyard guesthouse is a newly constructed modern detached ADU (aka small house) above our two car garage (Cars are not kept in the garage). Our guesthouse is located in an easy access  NE Location, with vaulted ceilings and spacious open-plan living area, cozy bedroom and modern bathroom.','The Guesthouse is located in the Sumner  neighborhood  located in Northeast Portland. It is bordered by the Cully, Parkrose, Madison South and Roseway neighborhoods, and on the North by Portland International Airport. The Grotto is few blocks away (10 minutes walk) and is an internationally- renowned Catholic shrine and botanical garden that provides a spiritual and peaceful retreat for everyone. If you feel like shopping (and YES, we don’t have sales tax), Cascade Station shopping center is only minutes away by car or by MAX (Metropolitan Area Express) light rail.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/31b73c58-bfd2-41c9-bc80-6e8664f38d54.jpg',73398160,80,'45.55814','-122.57094',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,98.00,3,730,64,4.97,32747089),(1463,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32748678','Quiet, Sparkling, Private, Fenced Garden Studio','Immaculate, Quiet Modern Studio<br />Cute Kitchenette with Toaster/Convection Oven, Microwave, Hot Plate<br />Tea/Coffee/Brita<br />Sm Refrigerator<br />Gorgeous Tile Bath<br />Large Private Garden area<br />Private entrance<br />Great for couples and Single travelers<br />This neighborhood is up and coming and it has a lot to offer<br />Walk to many choice eateries, Double Mountain Pub, Food Carts@Mercado Cafes<br /> all within 1 mile.<br />New Season\'s Roof top patio Market, Heart Coffee,<br />Yoga, Community Pool, excellent walking neighborhood','This neighborhood has a lot to offer, walk to<br />Brew pubs, Heart Coffee Cafes, New Seasons, Safeway, Cloud Ice Cream, Otto\'s Deli,  Dick\'s Paleo,  Nudi,  Otto\'s Pizza all within walking distance and much more on SE Foster, SE Woodstock, blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-32748678/original/bd8a330c-45e1-4611-86d2-2d1b7ef54e6c.jpeg',5627019,65,'45.48001','-122.59235',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,4,30,142,4.94,32748678),(1464,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32808619','Luxury &Location Kings Hill Walk Best of Urban PDX','Your Portland Pied-a-terre<br />In the historic General Beebe home is a renovated first floor level luxury living space - a light filled retreat! Gorgeous spa bathroom.<br />Located in quiet Kings Hill district below Washington Park, blocks from NW 23rd shops walk to downtown, Max , waterfront, urban and Forest Park hiking trails.<br />Approved by the City of Portland, meets all the requirements for safety.  Security system. No stove or oven but alternative cooking options and fully stocked housewares kitchen.','Quiet one way street just below Washington Park. Historic neighborhood.<br />Walk to Max lines, shopping, Timber stadium, hiking trails.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/72c73d35-e655-4b6d-bb02-43b05a4fa10b.jpg',25375592,3,'45.52095','-122.69543',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,159.00,2,14,134,4.93,32808619),(1465,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32851850','Home Away From Home Art Apartment (Hawthorn Area)','This apartment has its own entry, a very comfortable queen size bed in a basement studio setting.<br />The location is quiet yet right in the middle of two of the most desired locations, the Hawthorn and the Division street. There are cafes, coffee shops, cider houses, bars, shops, restaurants, grocery stores all within walking distance or bus. <br />There are 3 bus routes close by and street parking is never an issue.<br />The Kitchenette is very well stocked with most things you\'d need.','this location is truly ideal! Mt tabor park is close which is a small inactive volcano...an amazing place to hike around. There are limitless options for food, drink and shopping all within a short walk or bus. Some of my favorites are: Stumptown coffee, Common Grounds coffee house, New Seasons grocery, Paadee Thai food, Salt and Straw ice cream, Por Que no (taqueria), APizza Sholls, Miamotos sushi, Ava Gene\'s, Harlow, Xico, Bollywood Theatre, Saphire Hotel, Cibo.... the list goes on!! <br /> The apartment is in a wonderful quiet neighborhood that is called Richmond, voted in Sunset magazine as the #1 neighborhood in the US. It is quiet and quaint yet close to everything you will want. The apartment is filled with art and antiques and very cozy and warm in the winter and cool in the summer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bcd7ba89-3346-4668-a2bd-358a25f56e68.jpg',2034859,8,'45.50814','-122.61803',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,1,1125,330,4.92,32851850),(1466,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32895081','Peaceful and private','Set in SW Portland, only 5 miles from downtown.  Private and quiet in a park like setting.','Close to Gabriel Park and Multnomah Village- a popular spot with coffee shops, restaurants and unique shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-32895081/original/c261d003-c005-4a66-9914-7e18e33405f7.jpeg',69201599,17,'45.48492','-122.72242',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,1,30,164,4.88,32895081),(1467,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32900769','RAD home in hip SE available Oct 15. 30 day min','Close to all the SE hotspots (Division, Sellwood, Hawthorne, & more), minutes to downtown & a few blocks to the MAX for easy city exploring! This turn-of-the-century home is full of designer touches. The bedrooms offer high-quality linens, vintage furniture & large closets. The bathrooms feel luxurious with a soaking tub, a dual head shower & plush towels. The kitchen is fully stocked.  Enjoy the private backyard & driveway for off-street parking. Awesome monthly rates. 30 day minimum.','Historic Brooklyn neighborhood in hip SE Portland; House sits next to a coffee shop, convenience store, and across the street from a park. Close to Portland\'s best bars and restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1c281c39-d961-42b5-87e0-8f84e3127685.jpg',49136577,56,'45.49911','-122.65463',1,6,2.00,4.00,3.00,205.00,30,360,23,5.00,32900769),(1468,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32934768','Fulton Bungalow- in the heart of John\'s Landing','Welcome to the Fulton Bungalow, close to everything Portland offers. Enjoy Roku TV/high speed internet/wifi and 5 minutes proximity to downtown and Sellwood. This cheerful house is minutes from OHSU, Lewis & Clark, PSU, Reed College - perfect for traveling nurses, patients, professionals, or parents visiting their kids in college. Relax in the impeccable and private yard with a beautiful Japanese-inspired garden. Bright and fully-stocked gourmet kitchen with high-end wolf/sub-zero appliances.','The John\'s Landing/Corbett neighborhood is Portland\'s best kept secret. This area is quiet, quaint and very bikeable and walkable. You are two blocks to public transportation, minutes to Downtown by car, foot or bike. The Willamette Park, Jola Cafe, McMenamins Fulton House Pub and Zupans are all within minutes on foot. Willamette Park is also where you can access the Willamette River Greenway which lends a nautical feel to the scene with marina\'s, green spaces and boat launch access (bring your kayaks and stand up paddle boards!). The Greenway is also a super fun and accessible path for running and biking, all the way to downtown, Sellwood or South Waterfront.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/240924ef-a743-4250-b73a-ecde84674303.jpg',158873581,22,'45.47666','-122.67413',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,30,38,4.97,32934768),(1469,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32962790','Lewis and Clark Hide-A-Way Apartment','Private entrance apartment in Southwest Portland near Lewis & Clark College, OHSU, Multnomah Village and Hillsdale.  Large living room, full size kitchen. Extremely quite bedroom with queen bed, single roll away bed and pak-n-play bed available. Large outdoor patio space with barbeque, play structure for children, fire pit and fenced yard. Quiet neighborhood, walking distance to Moonlight grill, Chez Jose Mexican, Tokyroll sushi, Tryon creek sports bar. Walking distance to Tryon Creek.','The neighborhood is very quite area in the southwest hills. Our home is on the top of a low hill and there are no sidewalks but paved roads. Neighbors love to walk the hills for great exercise. Great walking access for dog walkers bikers. We are in walking distance to Tryon Creek Pub, Chez Jose Cafe, Market of Choice.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-32962790/original/fde26df4-2ebe-4f89-8a08-25ec0d64fa4c.jpg',4519200,49,'45.45635','-122.68064',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,74.00,2,730,234,4.99,32962790),(1470,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/32987079','Newly Built SE Division/Clinton Home w/ City Views','Our guest home is a newly built (March 2019),  two-bedroom home with backyard views of Portland. Located on the bike path next to Division St. you can Bike/Scooter/Walk to nearby coffee shops, food carts, restaurants and everything Portland has to offer.','The neighborhood is filled with 50s/60s styled midcentury homes, 2 blocks from SE Division. The original Stumptown Coffee shop is a 3 minute bike ride. Food Carts (Hinterland Food Carts & The Lot at Scout) are two blocks from the house right on SE Division St.  Definitely check out Apizza Scholls (~5 min bike ride).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/60ff6314-865c-4f70-aa43-f6b3acecbdd9.jpg',29487483,8,'45.5031','-122.60969',1,5,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,258,4.72,32987079),(1471,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33040869','Projector/Spacious/Airy ★ Walk to everything!','A modern-elegant 1000 sq ft guest suite, a few minute walk from a gorgeous, 26 acre park and all the restaurants, bars and shopping you could want. The space is complete with a private guest bedroom with luxury, organic bedding, private bath with locally-made products, a fully loaded kitchenette, an 8-seat dining table, a 100\" screen with access to every streaming service, lightning-fast wifi, and even a baby-grand piano! Perfect for couples, business travelers or families.','You know that kid in high school, who was so cool and interesting, but also really nice to everyone? You know how everyone just loved them and wanted to be friends with them? That\'s how we feel about Portland, and specifically our neighborhood. We geek out about our love of this city in a big, big way. <br />There is no where we\'d rather be than where we live, in Historic Laurelhurst.  We\'re on a very quiet, peaceful and friendly street, and yet are a few minute walk to superb coffee, food carts, restaurants, artisanal cocktails, and designer and vintage shopping, as well as a block away from 26 acre Laurelhurst Park, which was (fun fact!) designed by the same architects who designed Central Park. <br /><br />Want to explore more of Portland? We\'re located near easy public transportation or a few minutes drive to downtown Portland, the waterfront, and several museums. Alternatively, we have bikes and helmets for rental available - please enquire! Also, we\'re about 15 minutes drive to t','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f744acad-46bb-480f-9646-a6e626266c02.jpg',654280,23,'45.520450592041016','-122.61940002441406',1,6,1.00,1.00,2.00,71.00,1,29,393,4.90,33040869),(1472,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33094401','Luxurious Home For Up to 10 Guests (7 Queen Beds)','Welcome home away from home.  This very big, clean, beautiful house is waiting to be the best vacation home you have ever stayed in.','This neighborhood has everything within walking distance.  Coffee shops, bars, restaurants, movie theaters, ice skating, shopping at the mall, workout gyms, and a whole lot more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7ee46611-2bfd-4ee3-a59a-19d594be9282.jpg',123968362,7,'45.53859','-122.65021',1,10,1.50,4.00,7.00,600.00,2,1125,11,5.00,33094401),(1473,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33102414','Private light filled room in residential area.','Light filled 1 bedroom with foam queen bed and 2 inch foam topper. Quiet residential centralized  Sabin neighborhood near downtown, Broadway, Alberta, Mississippi and Williams neighborhoods & 2 blocks to TriMet Bus Service. The local area has a WalkScore of 87 out of 100 which is very walkable so some errands can be accomplished on foot.<br /><br />Near numerous parks, restaurants, bars & cafes.  Groceries nearby include Whole Foods (walking distance) along with New Seasons, Natural Grocers & Safeway.','Light filled 1 bedroom with with foam queen bed and 2 inch foam topper on tatami mat. Guests have typically been very comfortable.<br /><br />Excellent location near downtown, Broadway, Alberta, Mississippi and Williams neighborhoods & 2 blocks to TriMet Bus Service. The local area has a WalkScore of 87 out of 100 which is very walkable so some errands can be accomplished on foot.<br /><br />Our location is in the Sabin area near numerous parks, restaurants, bars & cafes.  Groceries nearby include Whole Foods along with New Seasons, Natural Grocers & Safeway.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cb60dbb0-62cf-4ef6-aaa3-cb3575e529a3.jpg',3519870,6,'45.55171','-122.65158',2,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,71.00,30,90,16,4.81,33102414),(1474,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33160496','Prescott House','New remodel house in 2019. All new in the house and security cameras outside the house.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b7e89599-9060-4bab-be51-ad5029562c64.jpg',249670904,40,'45.55624','-122.54461',1,5,2.00,2.00,2.00,173.00,2,1125,76,4.75,33160496),(1475,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33163017','Richmond Garden House','Enjoy a bottle of local wine on the house when check-in to the incredible Richmond Garden House. You\'ll get the entire house\'s finished space, large backyard w/ deck, grill & fire pit in this extremely clean, private space.<br /><br />Close to PDX’s most famous eateries in an awesome walkable neighborhood with easy parking, plenty of stores, conveniences & urban shopping.<br /><br />The home is full of comforts: premium bedding, stocked kitchen, high speed internet, gas fireplace, and great entertainment options.','The house is located between Division and Powell, near Cesar Chavez Blvd, within a walk or short 5 minute drive/bike ride/ride share trip from the trendiest neighborhoods around Hawthorne and Division in SE Portland. You’ll be close to many great shops, boutiques cafes and some of the most famous Portland restaurants and music venues. You\'re also just a 5-10 minute drive from supermarkets and big box stores. Though nearby and accessible to several busy and more industrial streets, the direct neighborhood is beautiful and safe with ample parking. Please note that SE Portland is oriented around residential neighborhoods with clusters of shops, restaurants and other commerce. There is plenty nearby and within a mile walk or 5-10 minute rideshare/cab, but its not a \'downtown\' area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c9dd7426-2ba7-460f-a207-3a295259c995.jpg',25566155,8,'45.49981','-122.61749',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,155.00,1,30,135,4.91,33163017),(1476,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33169341','Walker\'s Paradise','Come stay in our bright 1 bedroom daylight basement apartment. Our home was built in 1906 and is filled with character and charm, including a secret door disguised as a bookshelf. Located in between SE Belmont and Hawthorne, our home is walking distance to 100s of restaurants, shops, movie theaters and more. We are also blocks away from 2 bus lines that will take you downtown in 10 minutes. We live upstairs and are available if needed. Our ASTR Permit number is 20-109340-HO.','Some of our favorite spots just blocks away: Seasweets, The Bagdad Theater, Stumptown Coffee, Powell\'s Books, Fred Meyer, Ava Genes, Pinolo Gelato, Straight From NY Pizza, Laurelhurst Park and and so much more!!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c4f30028-f002-4b5c-ab15-f44986f451f7.jpg',249746109,16,'45.51423','-122.63474',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,91.00,2,1125,112,4.95,33169341),(1477,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33314579','Modern, bright house in the heart of Sellwood','Home  in one of the best neighborhoods in Portland. Warm and welcoming interiors. Living room has fireplace to keep you warm and cozy in the evenings. Kitchen has modern appliances. <br />Two bedrooms with and 1.5 baths  and stacking laundry. <br />Walk to restaurants, bars, coffee shops, Four Seasons grocery store! Take a walk in the beautiful Oaks Bottom Wildlife Refuge or bike your way to downtown Portland along the Willamette River trail. Both just blocks away.','Friendly neighborhood','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-33314579/original/69a978d4-90a9-4133-a116-8342967f8bf5.jpeg',103922819,20,'45.46507','-122.65734',1,5,1.50,2.00,3.00,145.00,30,1125,45,4.82,33314579),(1478,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33370307','Forested Escape Minutes from OHSU','Make yourself at home in this modern minimalist designed apartment. This newly constructed space is airy and bright, with french doors that open to a large private patio.  Quiet and serene this space has outdoor seating and even a hammock to fully relax in and take in the amazing, forested views.  This space is just minutes away from OHSU and downtown it\'s the perfect location for easy access to the heart of the city as well as The Zoo, The Japanese Gardens and The Rose Gardens.','Council Crest is one of Portland\'s oldest and most Please note we are located in the hills which is almost exclusively accessible by car. <br />Esteemed neighborhoods close to OHSU, the VA hospital, downtown Portland, Nike and lots of other businesses.<br /><br />Nearby Council Crest Park offers views of five different mountain peaks: Mt St Helens (catch it from the dining room or deck!), Mt. Hood, Mt Rainier, Mt Adams and Mt Jefferson.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c356f5a2-55d0-4817-a0f6-032e069147d1.jpg',1978398,54,'45.49997','-122.70192',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,109.00,2,90,179,4.54,33370307),(1479,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33394369','Garden Guesthouse - modern & private','Your entrance is 4307 SE Ivon St., please park in front of your entrance or along the hedge, so our neighbors parking spaces aren\'t taken.  Thank you','Within an easy walk you will find a variety of famous restaurants:  St. Honore, Bollywood, Petite Provence, Division Wines, Turning Peel…just to name a few.  Just two blocks away is Portland’s Original Stumptown Coffee.  Upscale shopping is available within 10 blocks on Division St. with Hawthorne Blvd. being only 8 blocks away.  The night life on Division varies from outdoor Pubs, Bars, Bands, and an amazing choice of eateries.   Six blocks west is Portland’s famous ice cream shop “Salt and Straw” and six blocks east is a wonderful Food Court with some of Portland’s award-winning food trucks.  You are in the center of everything and only 40 blocks from downtown Portland.  Transportation is a breeze for any destination with easy access to Uber and Lyft, taxis, rental bikes and a clean and efficient bus system.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0650e7a5-b94f-45db-96ba-9cca07d2acce.jpg',251575849,8,'45.5043361','-122.6177377',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,79.00,3,365,240,4.98,33394369),(1480,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33395999','Cozy Getaway w/Hot tub, Fireplace, Firepit & A/C','Our peaceful getaway house has everything you could need!  Inside is cozy with vaulted wood ceilings, hardwood floors, a fireplace, big screen TV, games, a fully stocked kitchen, claw-foot cast-iron bathtub, washer & dryer, two queen beds in separate bedrooms, and plenty of special extras to spoil our guests. Outside you have access to bikes, a BBQ, fire pit, 3-person hot tub, hammock, bistro table and new dining area w/umbrella outside and a garden. All close to transit & 10 mins from downtown!','Located a short walk away from restaurants and bars, 3 long blocks from Providence Portland, able to frequent the Hollywood area as well as a weekly Hollywood Farmers Market every Saturday.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ea13611d-f3e4-4787-9eb7-849ceac4c704.jpg',129582844,23,'45.53162','-122.62301',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,175.00,2,28,257,5.00,33395999),(1481,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33401196','Ken\'s airporter bungalow w/queen bed','Great for business-minded guests or tourists! The room has a separate entrance into the home, a shared bathroom and living room with other guests. 10 minutes (3.5 miles) to PDX. 15 minutes (6.5 miles) to downtown. Several restaurants are an easy walking distance.','Located near the Madison South and Gateway neighborhoods. Ten minutes to PDX by rideshare. Freeway (I84) is nearby for quick access to downtown by car or head to the Gorge. The Max 82nd stop is 5 minute walk, which takes you to the airport, downtown and all over the Metro area. Close to Rose City Golf Course and Rocky Butte.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b026b379-5979-477f-ba2b-149f50c69f32.jpg',94889798,74,'45.53979','-122.57872',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,36.00,1,21,664,4.52,33401196),(1482,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33469567','Luxury Home For Up to 10 Guests (8 Queen Beds)','As soon as you walk in you\'ll feel right at home away from home. This home is 3,200 square feet of luxury living.  The living room will welcome you right in and the formal dining room will seat up to 10 comfortably with an additional leaf allowing seating for two more dinner guests.  The gourmet kitchen has all top of the line commercial grade appliances with a separate butler\'s pantry.  The second floor has four bedrooms with seven  queen Serta pillow top mattress beds with luxury hotel linens.','This neighborhood has everything within walking distance.  Coffee shops, Bakeries, bars, restaurants, movie theaters, ice skating, shopping at the mall, workout gyms, and a whole lot more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fdc0a070-2174-4e8b-834a-a70fa73c20d8.jpg',123968362,7,'45.53867','-122.65149',1,10,2.50,5.00,8.00,750.00,2,1125,18,5.00,33469567),(1483,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33469666','Ken’s airporter bungalow w/double bed','Great for business-minded guests or tourists! The room has a separate entrance into the home, a shared bathroom and living room with other guests. 10 minutes (3.5 miles) to PDX. 15 minutes (6.5 miles) to downtown. Several restaurants are an easy walking distance.','Located near the Madison South and Gateway neighborhoods. Ten minutes to PDX by rideshare. Freeway (I84) is nearby for quick access to downtown by car or head to the Gorge. The Max 82nd stop is 5 minute walk, which takes you to the airport, downtown and all over the Metro area. Close to Rose City Golf Course and Rocky Butte.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b026b379-5979-477f-ba2b-149f50c69f32.jpg',94889798,74,'45.53863','-122.57895',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,36.00,1,21,617,4.47,33469666),(1484,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33474431','Bright Basement Space in superb SE location','Enjoy your stay in our spacious, modern basement apartment on a quiet street near vibrant Southeast Portland neighborhoods and one of Portland’s largest public parks. Within walking distance of this superb location you can experience much of what makes Portland and the Pacific Northwest such an attractive and exciting place to live or visit from the dining, shopping and nightlife to the splendor and beauty of the natural landscape.','On nearby Hawthorne, Belmont and Division streets you’ll discover a wealth of fantastic options for coffee, tea, shopping, dining, cinema, and nightlife including Portland’s famous Powell’s City of Books. To the east you can explore the 196 acre Mt. Tabor Park; a forested urban park built around an extinct volcano where you’ll experience the natural beauty of the Pacific Northwest.<br />What\'s Local? Here are a few ideas:<br /><br />Local Parks<br />Mt. Tabor Park Salmon St entrance .6mi<br />Laurelhurst Park 1.3mi<br /><br />Coffee, Bars and Restaurants<br />Albina Press - .3mi<br />Tabor Bread Cafe .3mi<br />Sapphire Hotel restaurant and bar .3mi<br />Por Que No? Taqueria .5mi<br />Russel St. BBQ .5mi<br />Pizzicato Pizza .6mi<br /><br />Belmont Food Carts .5mi<br />Division Food Carts .8mi<br />New Seasons Market & Grocery .8mi<br />QFC Grocery .7mi<br /><br />Fine Dining<br />Tasty & Daughters 1mi<br />Coquine 1mi<br /><br />Other<br />Bagdad Theater 1mi<br />Powell’s City of Books','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0dae3f71-124d-41ef-92c2-5109497d81b7.jpg',252219155,15,'45.51605','-122.60945',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,79.00,2,10,127,4.94,33474431),(1485,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33592675','South Tabor Tuckaway','Sweet portland home less than a mile from mount tabor park for your outdoor adventures and montavilla for your bars, restaurants and shops. Situated in the south tabor neighborhood directly on 80th and Division for quick access to 82nd, Powell, FoPo, Richmond and Hawthorne district. A perfect portland experience!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/abedc6ad-0d0d-4609-89a2-eff28f6658f9.jpg',65222350,37,'45.50304','-122.58175',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,99.00,30,1125,78,4.79,33592675),(1486,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33619387','“Dahlia’s Place” • Historic Private Studio','Our private second floor studio space nests on the middle floor in one of Portland\'s oldest historic buildings, built in 1880. Portland decorative style and designed to be spacious and cozy. <br /><br />Welcome to the center of our city. Two blocks from PSU, and just 1/2 block from the bus and MAX lines + Portland Street car. Directly above Phat Cart Cafe on main level and very popular Food Cart Pod right across the street. Just 4 blocks walk to the waterfront, and very easy on/off access to the highway.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0fc441c7-67cd-4e8d-8a9b-d0a5470cf5f7.jpg',28688984,44,'45.50912','-122.68232',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,730,29,4.72,33619387),(1487,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33621233','Enjoy an old farmhouse in a quiet neighborhood','You will be staying in the converted basement of my late 1800s house. The space includes a bathroom with shower, a kitchenette with fridge/freezer, microwave, and hotplate, a living room and 2 bedrooms. This South Tabor house is close to the airport and within a 9 block walk to 3 major bus routes that will take you anywhere you want to go. I live upstairs and am often available if you have questions. Enjoy sitting on the front porch  anytime. If it\'s a nice night, chances are I\'ll join you.','There are great coffee shops and restaurants within easy walking distance of this ideal location. If you like nature, take a walk up Mt. Tabor. The base is a short 6 blocks away. You can spend hours on the trails or enjoy one of the best views of Portland and Mt. Hood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/11e13bf1-ab7d-4d39-ae1b-f849a7c25252.jpg',145659006,37,'45.50268','-122.59688',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,109.00,2,12,112,4.81,33621233),(1488,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33689103','Walkable Apt Next to Restaurants, Bars, and Shops!','Welcome to Alberta Abode, your modern, spacious home in the walkable Alberta Arts District in Northeast, Portland! <br /><br />✓ Fully equipped kitchen for longer stays<br />✓Work from home desk + chair<br />✓Private washer & dryer<br />✓ Smart TV with 65in screen<br />✓ 5 minute walk to coffee shops, restaurants, boutiques & parks<br />✓ Fast, seamless WiFi<br />✓ Central Heating & Air<br />✓ Pet-friendly & non-smoking<br />✓ Free parking','It\'s hard to describe the Alberta Arts District and the surrounding neighborhoods in just a small typed box. <br /><br />The hype is real, you just need to go explore it and find out for yourself all what everyone\'s talking about! So many amazing restaurants, coffee shops, boutiques, craft breweries and other things to do that you\'ll never be bored.<br /><br />Just step outside this little haven and have tons of fun for as long as you stay!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzM2ODkxMDM%3D/original/9b851219-fc74-4660-980c-90f6d43304f8.jpeg',53371722,29,'45.560306549072266','-122.65093994140625',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,73.00,30,1125,445,4.87,33689103),(1489,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33773933','Contactless Clean Private Treetop Studio','Majestic, unattached and sparkling clean, treetop studio in vibrant, accessible, and friendly neighborhood.  New space whit lots of custom unique features. Great nearby restaurants, parks, coffee, and good vibes.<br /><br />On check out all we ask you to do is load the dishwasher and put dirty towels in one place.','We are just a few blocks from some of the best restaurants and coffee shops in Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a5fe7ad0-4e0d-4e67-ba33-bb079b1d36e8.jpg',24385374,1,'45.56662','-122.63681',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,93.00,1,30,557,4.98,33773933),(1490,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33782686','★ Clean, comfortable master bedroom  ★ patio','Peaceful, spacious and light double bedroom in secure 3-bed home on quiet street in safe SE Portland neighbourhood. Bus 19 to Downtown or a 15 minute drive, close to Woodstock and Mt Scott Park. 20 min drive from PDX. Original wood floors,  blackout blinds, front + back gardens, medium firm queen size mattress, a choice of pillows and door lock for peace of mind and privacy.  Luxurious shared bathroom and attractive rear covered patio for summer chilling. 50mbps internet. Sorry, no pets.','The area around Mount Scott Park, 0.5 miles away, is a classic slice of Southeast Portland which I love. Green trees, excellent coffee (at Space Monkey) and a brilliant recreation centre with cheap fitness classes, pilates, swimming and a hot tub looking out into the trees. I love that it\'s quiet, with no rowdy crowds or noisy through traffic coming past the house, yet the whole city is accessible. Woodstock is my next favourite place because of its clean-yet-vintage Portland feel. Portland Insight (under 5 minutes walk) is a good place for meditation or a massage. My favourite park in Portland is Mt Tabor, 2.5 miles away. Cartlandia, Heist and the Portland Mercado are the closest food cart pods.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-33782686/original/08a7e227-c058-4991-bc94-a18e2cbddaf0.jpeg',254586465,69,'45.4754','-122.59004',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,42.00,30,200,45,4.91,33782686),(1491,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33805610','Garden Apartment in the Heart of Portland','Beautiful and bright basement apartment with AC in relaxing Northeast Portland. The neighborhood has everything you could want with NE Williams Street a short walk away, easy access to the Rose Garden and the Convention Center, and a 10-minute bike ride to Powell\'s Books in downtown Portland. The community center across the street offers a full-sized pool and gym.<br /><br />Enter through your own gate into a backyard food forest, and enjoy a private entrance to your apartment. <br /><br />Easy checkout.','We love being so close to downtown but still being in a classic Portland neighborhood. We are blocks from some great Portland restaurants, good coffee, the Wonder Ballroom, etc. Across the street is the Matt Dishman Community Center, which has a pool, weight-room and a world-class boxing gym for a reasonable daily fee.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3a4be419-ade6-4ae5-9664-d215e6cf6dc7.jpg',5424140,26,'45.5412','-122.66342',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,102.00,2,30,85,4.95,33805610),(1492,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33807010','Studio with a VIEW - Access to Trails, OHSU','The Studio is perched on the southwest hills of Portland with an amazing view of Mt. Hood and the valley below. It requires a walk up 43 stairs to access but is worth every step. The Studio was built as a workspace for a local artist and provides an amazing view of Mt. Hood. Since converted to an escape from the normal urban confines of Portland. Easy access to downtown and walking distance to OHSU and the Veterans Hospital, it provides escape and accessibility. Did we mention the sunrise view!','We are hidden from the typical walking neighborhoods of Portland. With that comes amazing views and fantastic seclusion. Easily accessible to downtown Portland via car or public transit. We are just below the Terwilliger Parkway which provides a more gentle slope and miles of walking, running, or trail exploration.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/4fd62417-72c1-42b1-bc7c-0eb101a6ce1a.jpg',30415706,30,'45.49163','-122.68124',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,45,84,5.00,33807010),(1493,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33814266','Gorgeous private ADU on the edge of NE Laurelhurst','Private detached spacious 750 sq ft, 2 bedroom craftsman\'s bungalow centrally located on the inner east side in Kerns neighborhood right off 28th Ave. Spacious, bright, keyless entry, open dining and kitchen area with USB charging ports, with private bedrooms. Offering a perfect blend of old and new Portland.  Walkable to popular Portland restaurants and locally owned businesses, making this a  fun neighborhood to visit. <br />Perfect for couples, friends, families and overnight business','Relatively close-in to downtown Portland, with a heavy mix of commercial and residential. Do you love living in an urban setting centrally located in the heart of all the action? This is your place! <br />Some local attractions:<br />-Guero<br />-City State<br />-Stammtisch<br />-Matador<br />-Pollo Norte<br />-PImbeche<br />-28th Food cart pod<br />- Screen Door<br />- Ate oh Ate<br />-Laurelhurst Park<br />- Ole Ole<br />- Navarre<br />-Sudra<br />-Cheese & Crack Snack Shop<br />- Plaid Pantry<br />- Luce <br />And so many, more that the list goes on!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/994356d8-c4c1-448f-8fdc-c9415185a7eb.jpg',252680829,12,'45.52343','-122.63725',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,160.00,2,29,64,4.91,33814266),(1494,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33831038','Cedar Cabin  w/ Hot Tub & Garden Hawthorne','Two-story cedar cabin w/ covered deck, hot tub and secluded garden. An oasis of tranquility steps from one of Portland\'s most popular streets — house walls are double insulated. Downstairs: handcrafted fir beam ceiling, concrete floors, full kitchen. Light-filled bedroom plus single bed alcove upstairs. Bathroom has heated floors and two person waterfall shower.<br /><br />100 ft from Hawthorne Blvd and public transportation makes visiting Portland without a car a snap. This is an ADU behind owner\'s home.','Restaurants, boutiques, public transportation, gourmet grocery stores, bars, shops, music venues, parks... you name it, the Hawthorne District has it!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ec123aa3-cbe3-40c6-aaeb-bdc3a9d768c5.jpg',13162607,16,'45.51293','-122.62942',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,159.00,3,28,251,4.95,33831038),(1495,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33852871','SE Division Studio Apartment in Craftsman Home','New construction basement studio apartment in the heart of SE Division neighborhood. The space was designed with guests in mind: you will have your own laundry facilities, fast Wi-Fi, a heated bathroom and a kitchenette. Additionally, apartment has a separate entrance and keypad entry for your convenience. <br /><br />This apartment is 2 blocks from major Portland bus lines and has free street parking. Walk to SE Portland\'s Bollywood Theater, Apizza Scholls and more as you explore Portland\'s finest.','We love walking around our neighborhood for coffee or to socialize with friends in the evening. With Division and Hawthorne so close by, we find that most of our exploring happens pretty close to home.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8195259d-2eff-42be-ab0d-e6ffe52887ec.jpg',1458369,8,'45.50614','-122.62197',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,93.00,3,8,41,4.90,33852871),(1496,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33911444','Light-filled Cottage, cleaned  to CDC  standards','Dahlia Cottage is located in Southeast Portland, in the beautiful, quiet Eastmoreland neighborhood. A stand-alone home built in 2019 filled with beautiful natural light. A fully functional kitchen.  A beautiful relaxing living space. One bedroom (queen) on the main floor, a king bed in loft with ladder/handrails access.  Washer & dryer.  Full bath with walk-in shower.  A relaxing outdoor patio with table/chairs.   We clean and sanitize the cottage to meet current CDC guidelines.','Dahlia Cottage is located in our lovely, enchanted and quiet Eastmoreland neighborhood.  Take a walk through our picturesque neighborhood.  Enjoy the eclectic architecture, impressive trees and lush gardens.  Dahlia Cottage is centrally located so you can easily get to restaurant row on Division, Bagdad Theater on Hawthorne, Powells Books in the Pearl and Laurelwood Public House and Brewery in Westmoreland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7d78e8b4-140f-44dc-ab07-89d71403fe71.jpg',204626355,5,'45.47097','-122.62771',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,16,183,4.99,33911444),(1497,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33915285','Enjoy a bedroom in an old farmhouse near Mt. Tabor','You will be staying in the recently converted basement of my 1890s South Tabor house. Your space in the basement includes a private bedroom which sleeps up to 2 people. There is a private kitchenette, dining area, living area, and bathroom. You are close to the airport and within blocks of 3 major bus routes going anywhere the city. I live upstairs and am often available. Enjoy sitting on the front porch and if it\'s a nice night, chances are I\'ll join you.','There are great coffee shops and restaurants within easy walking distance of this ideal location. If you like nature, take a walk up Mt. Tabor. The base is a short 6 blocks away. You can spend hours on the trails or enjoy one of the best views of Portland and Mt. Hood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3a3f9ff2-0125-44e1-b24f-8e10557f3ac4.jpg',145659006,37,'45.5017','-122.59652',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,12,50,4.88,33915285),(1498,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/33915615','Cute bedroom in an old house close to Mt. Tabor.','You will be staying in the recently converted basement of my 1909 South Tabor house. Your space in the basement includes a private bedroom which sleeps up to 3 people. The kitchenette, dining area, living area, and bathroom will be private as well. You are close to the airport and within blocks of 3 major bus routes going anywhere the city. I live upstairs and am often available. Enjoy sitting on the front porch and if it\'s a nice night, chances are I\'ll join you.','There are great coffee shops and restaurants within easy walking distance of this ideal location. If you like nature, take a walk up Mt. Tabor. The base is a short 6 blocks away. You can spend hours on the trails or enjoy one of the best views of Portland and Mt. Hood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/aabb6733-c0e4-408d-a871-77eb2b422073.jpg',145659006,37,'45.50289','-122.59523',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,12,47,4.79,33915615),(1499,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34014563','Concordia Annex','Built in 2019, the Annex guesthouse is walking distance to the <br />Alberta Art District, University of Oregon (U ofO), Kennedy School, restaurants & specialty bars. Public transportation is near by.  15 minutes from Airport.<br />The Annex is filled with natural light flowing through cathedral windows.<br />Full Kitchen with cooking supplies, utensils, coffee and tea  options, <br />Private patio in the garden.','The Annex is a 5 minute walk East to McMenamins,  Kennedy School Hotel and restaurant.  <br />The NE Alberta Arts Street is a short walk South.  You have every choice of food and drink.<br />Tin Shed and Petit Provence are both great for breakfast or lunch.  <br />A variety of eating venues and bars are also on NE Killingsworth St.,  a short walk West through Alberta Park.  Podnahs is great for BBQ.<br />The Firehouse on NE Dekum Street is  less than a mile away.  They offer Italian, steaks and fish.<br />Strolling or biking East, down tree-lined Ainsworth St, is Fernhill Park.<br />Pick up coffee at Kiss  or at Extracto on your walk.<br />Concordia neighborhood is an open and caring community that we feel proud to be a part of.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/236dbc67-c8f7-4942-a391-a3e46fcba4f3.jpg',24306194,1,'45.56506','-122.63952',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,130.00,2,14,127,5.00,34014563),(1500,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34036628','Awesome location, fun 2BR Alberta Arts District','The Alberta Petite Hotel is a very nice relaxing house in a perfect walkable location on Alberta St and 24th with galleries, local shops, restaurants and entertainment. <br />This quaint space is a private daylight basement with its own external entrance, living area with TV, bathroom, dining area and kitchenette. Enjoy the outdoor sitting spaces for relaxing and people watching. One parking space.','Alberta Street is lined with cafes, restaurants, coffee shops, bars, music venues, a theater, boutique shops and street art. During the summer, get out and enjoy Last Thursdays on Alberta and the Alberta Street Fair - fun for the whole family. During the rest of the year explore the local neighborhood and eat at the plethora of delicious food establishments.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzQwMzY2Mjg%3D/original/a75a9aca-d5ee-4383-a180-7e8e9f465de4.jpeg',224911430,1,'45.55888','-122.64031',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,123.00,2,300,62,4.89,34036628),(1501,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34036884','Garden Oasis: Space & Comfort Steps to Hawthorne!','Exquisitely renovated daylight ground floor space, overflowing with charm and all the ammenties of home. This jungle oasis has two bright and airy bedrooms, bathroom and laundry closet, spacious living room for gathering and an efficiency kitchen, perfect for storing and heating up your leftovers from meals out at some of the best food Portland has to offer. Hundreds of local shops and delicious eateries are just a few blocks from this ideal jumping off point for an incredible Portland getaway!','Situated in the heart of Portland\'s hottest neighborhood! Hawthorne, Belmont, and Division streets converge creating a hotbed where eclectic Portland eateries and shopping thrive like the verdant cityscape surrounding it! Enjoy the best of what SE Portland has to offer right outside the front door of your epic Airbnb','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/509f21c6-7862-4506-aef5-70cc651ae333.jpg',257005682,16,'45.51445','-122.61876',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,93.00,2,29,205,4.96,34036884),(1502,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34064074','Charming Craftsman in Prime Hawthorne District','This 1924 craftsman is located in a quiet neighborhood in the heart of SE Portland. Walk/bike score 95. Only  minutes from downtown/waterfront, close day trip to Mt. Hood or the Oregon Coast. Located between Hawthorne and Division, both streets are known for cuisine and shopping. No need for a car, everything is within bus/walking/biking distance!! Outdoor opportunities are endless. Mt Tabor Park is 1 mile away and has great hiking trails and big dog park.  Yes, we are dog friendly too!','As one of the most entertaining neighborhoods in Portland, you will never get bored!! Hawthorne has a very friendly laid back vibe. We like to say \" keep Portland weird\" and even people watching can be quite fun. I am located off of Hawthorne though, so when you\'re done with the fun you can retreat to a neighborhood that is quiet and cozy. You will feel right at home!           <br /><br />Hiking/walking/biking nearby <br />	◦	Mt Tabor Park<br />	◦	Forest Park<br />	◦	Hawthorne St. <br />	◦	Division St.<br />	◦	Oaks Bottom<br />	◦	Reed College Canyon<br />	◦	Sellwood antiques<br /><br />Food<br />	◦	Por que no?<br />	◦	Food carts <br />        ◦	Paradox Cafe, vegan options<br />	◦	La Petit Provence<br />	◦	Horse Brass Pub<br />	◦	Waffle Window<br />	◦	Rovente pizza<br />	◦	Produce Row<br />	◦	Stump Town Coffee<br />	◦	Flying Pie Pizza<br />	◦	Pok Pok - tai<br /><br /><br />Bars<br />	◦	Space Room<br />	◦	Baghdad Pub with theater<br />	◦	Landmark Saloon - live music, younger crowd<br />','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cdef2a29-260a-4f80-85e5-f857ed8328ed.jpg',479684230,8,'45.50796','-122.61538',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,171.00,2,14,77,4.83,34064074),(1503,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34066774','Boho-Chic Private Haven: Alberta Arts District','Stylish and fun guest suite (1,000 square feet) with all the unique charm you expect from Portland and within walking distance to sought after restaurants, coffeeshops, bars, and shopping in the Alberta Arts District.','The Alberta Arts District boasts both high-end dining and affordable faves. Excellent coffee, beer, cocktails, and your choice from a gamut of highly sought after and top rated restaurants lie less than a block or two away from your door. We\'re a 10 minute ride from downtown Portland, and you have your pick of nightlife spots with Northeast bars and clubs just a few blocks away. Alberta Park is just across the street with a covered basketball court, bike jousting, tennis courts, jogging path, and off leash dog area. There is so much to explore just outside your door that you may not have any time for anywhere else in Portland!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/370db65a-d855-4ad2-8c15-0eb0c15654cb.jpg',22615259,29,'45.5633','-122.64698',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,106.00,2,60,124,4.91,34066774),(1504,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34091942','Laurelhurst English Cottage','Please be fully vaccinated before arrival.<br /><br />You will have the entire recently finished basement, including a large bed room, a media room and a private bathroom. New Queen Bed, bureaus and space for hanging clothes. There is a private entrance on the driveway side. If I am in town, you are welcome to use the kitchen and backyard. There is a wonderful deck under a large walnut tree in the back yard.','\" Restaurant Row\" is a roughly T-shaped dining and retail district four blocks from the house.  This diverse neighborhood comprises a slew of mostly food-related ventures along East Burnside Street from about 22nd to 28th avenues. Then, where Burnside meets 28th Avenue, you\'ll find several blocks of first-rate eateries as well as a handful of boutiques in either direction, heading north up to about Glisan Street and south down to about Stark Street. The historic Laurelhurst Theater anchors the intersection of 28th and Burnside, and top foodie haunts in these parts include Heart Coffee Roasters, Davenport, Screen Door, Tusk, Matador, Pambiche Cuban, Navarre, Alma Chocolate, Fifty Licks Ice Cream, PaaDee Thai, Laurelhurst Market, Crema Coffee & Bakery (and the small but excellent food-cart pod containing Wolf and Bear\'s for Middle Eastern food and Le Pantry for French bistro fare), Vino wine shop, Ken\'s Artisan Pizza, Bamboo Sushi, and Canteen vegan restaurant and juice bar.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/550707b7-8a3a-4dcb-9db7-526d78d007ba.jpg',22697835,12,'45.52111','-122.63234',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,14,99,4.95,34091942),(1505,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34121174','Standard Queen, Shared Baths at The Society Hotel','Take a trip back in time in a historic 1881 sailor\'s hotel! Lovingly restored former boarding rooms have been updated with modern amenities, including free ultra-high speed wi-fi, reading light and charging outlet, in-room sink, and Shared Baths.','Old Town/Chinatown is the historic heart of Portland. It\'s our Ellis Island, where immigrants of all stripes first came ashore, just a few blocks away at the river. Now you\'ll find festivals, the Saturday Market, music shows and clubs, restaurants, art galleries, and shopping, all within a few blocks of our location.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/fb71d1d8-ff79-4b50-8fcf-3c6f8b21edf9.jpg',1032014,43,'45.52531','-122.6748',4,2,3.00,1.00,1.00,76.00,1,28,757,4.72,34121174),(1506,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34122118','Premium Suite at The Society Hotel','Take a trip back in time in a historic 1881 sailor\'s hotel! Lovingly restored former boarding rooms have been updated with modern amenities, including free ultra-high speed wi-fi, reading light and charging outlet, en-suite bath, and 7-foot windows.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/08bfd3f8-00bc-42ab-9015-b7cf7a75723d.jpg',1032014,43,'45.52438','-122.67294',4,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,122.00,1,28,32,4.88,34122118),(1507,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34122310','Single Bunk Bed at The Society Hotel','The bunk room has been created as a nod to the hotel\'s creation as a safe place for sailors. You\'ll find the same thing in this space with 18\' ceilings- cozy, strong, and comfortable triple bunk beds.<br />All reserved guests must have a valid i.d and living address 50miles or more from Portland.<br /><br />Once you check in with our front desk you will be assigned a bunk bed for the full length of your stay. There are to be no changes with your bunk assignment unless otherwise worked out with our front desk.','Old Town is Portland\'s oldest neighborhood - the original epicenter of Portland, Oregon.  It has a colorful history and an equally colorful present! We are the epicenter of Portland\'s street fashion scene, the nightlife district, as well as a social services haven for those most in need.  So expect an eclectic mix from Old Town, and hopefully love it as much as we do!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c9038247-da91-4194-bb08-f2d0365cdbb0.jpg',1032014,43,'45.52505','-122.67286',4,1,3.00,1.00,2.00,36.00,1,7,1680,4.84,34122310),(1508,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34123277','Suite at The Society Hotel','Take a trip back in time in a historic 1881 sailor\'s hotel! Lovingly restored former boarding rooms have been updated with modern amenities, including free ultra-high speed wi-fi, reading light and charging outlet, en-suite bath, and 7-foot windows.','Old Town/Chinatown is the historic heart of Portland. It\'s our Ellis Island, where immigrants of all stripes first came ashore, just a few blocks away at the river. Now you\'ll find festivals, the Saturday Market, music shows and clubs, restaurants, art galleries, and shopping, all within a few blocks of our location.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/09b6b33e-b631-437e-a2a4-c93e8ebc314b.jpg',1032014,43,'45.52538','-122.67469',4,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,112.00,1,28,81,4.79,34123277),(1509,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34123760','Cedar House','Nestled in inner North/NE Portland, this cozy guest house sits between the vibrant Mississippi and Williams shopping districts and is just a short day trip to lovely hikes in the surrounding area. We\'re a quick bus ride from the center of town and a short walk to a wide variety of local shops and dining. High ceilings and plenty of natural light give this intimate space an airy, open feeling, making it an in-town sanctuary with easy access to public transport, bike lanes, and on-street parking.','This is a busy and bustling neighborhood, where you\'ll find a wide variety of amenities to suit most of your needs. There is plenty of retail and we\'re proud that many shops are local and independently owned, which usually means they will be filled with unique finds. Close by you\'ll encounter plenty of cafes, brew pubs, bars, and a variety of great eats - from finer dining to casual restaurants with excellent happy hours, to a variety of ethnic and fusion cuisines, to food carts and ice cream shops. Besides being a fine neighborhood for a jog on the quieter sides streets, you\'ll also find walkable access to a gym and to exercise classes like spinning/cycling, barre workouts, yoga studios, and a community center with indoor pool. We are within blocks of two city parks with a basket ball court and children\'s playground areas, and a slightly further walk from 2 larger parks featuring those amenities and more, including kids\' splash pads in summer, baseball diamonds, soccer fields, and, in','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-34123760/original/3d9550e2-654c-4bb0-b91a-bb5b516b7317.jpg',248930295,9,'45.55211','-122.66817',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,91.00,4,125,102,5.00,34123760),(1510,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34180606','New Home. 15m-airprt. 15m-DT. 40m-MT. 5m-lightrail','1 mile from Max Transit Center (gateway transit), blocks away from bus line, <br />6 miles from the Airport (10-15 min drive), <br />7 miles from downtown Portland (15 drive). Easy freeway access and off street parking. <br /><br />You’ll be 5 mins away from freeway access going both north and south (i205) and east and west (i84).  <br /><br />This place is completely remodeled and spotless! Comes with everything you need to be home away from home but yet close enough to everything you need to get to.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6cd15184-6557-4439-9bca-89b7f3b28d60.jpg',29167392,63,'45.52628','-122.55096',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,100.00,30,1125,50,4.84,34180606),(1511,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34229716','Modern Condo near Belmont and Laurelhurst','About 1400 sq ft three-story townhouse has an office with a fold out air bed and half bath on the entry level.  <br /><br />Second floor has a spacious fully equipped modern kitchen, dining room with seating for four and a cozy see-through gas fireplace.  The living room shares the other side of the cozy fireplace and you’ll also find a half bath on this level.<br /><br />3rd/top floor has 2bedrooms and 2 full baths.  Garage excluded.  Strret parking.','The Sunnyside neighborhood is located in Southeast Portland and is bordered by the Buckman, Kerns, Laurelhurst, Mount Tabor, and Richmond neighborhoods. <br /><br />This area also encompasses the Belmont District, which you can find here, and the northern half of the Hawthorne District, which you can find here.<br /><br />The large (32 acre)and beautiful Laurelhurst park is 5 blocks away and grocery/restaurants just 2 blocks away on Belmont.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-34229716/original/1137d8c2-b8c8-404e-a7b8-7e2a936d59f6.jpeg',135322695,16,'45.51767','-122.63133',1,4,3.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,6,160,11,4.73,34229716),(1512,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34230129','Dreamy Hawthorne 2 bed, 2 ba','Live like a local! Enjoy the vibrant Hawthorne District, just two blocks from your front door, or walk a few more blocks to buzzy Division Street or hip Belmont. An abundance of great food, craft beer, locally roasted coffee, vintage shops + great boutiques can be found here in the heart of Southeast Portland.','This two-bedroom unit is a welcoming space in the center of an historic neighborhood that boasts one of Portland’s most unique districts just outside the front door. Every amenity you could hope for is within walking distance from coffee to groceries, yoga to shopping.<br /><br />The eastside of Portland and especially the Hawthorne/Division area is a foodie paradise. There are literally countless options, from food trucks to fine dining and everything in between. Portland\'s beloved local grocer, New Seasons Market, is just a few blocks away. Many wonderful restaurants and food carts are open within blocks for takeout or patio dining. I\'m always happy to share recommendations if needed.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/687381fd-9004-4392-8590-fa016fe9c7e7.jpg',17378091,8,'45.50871','-122.63007',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,160.00,3,21,154,4.97,34230129),(1513,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34256753','Colorful Roseway Bungalow -classic Portland charm!','Colorful & relaxing: your stay is sure to be pleasant in this easy, convenient, cozy, and charming Roseway home. The 101-year-old house has queen bedrooms, and an upstairs lounge with double bed and futon (plus living room sofa bed.) The furnishings are fun and funky but never compromising comfort. You\'ll enjoy a large kitchen with lots of space, a big fridge, and a 6-burner Viking cooktop. Within a 10-minute walk you\'ll find some great restaurants, but you might just want to stay in!','House is right across the street from a grocery store and around the corner from a big and fun vintage thrift store. Excellent pizza, Vietnamese food, New York bagels, and delicious old-fashioned donuts are on the next block, as well as a very good wine shop. Of course there are several great parks nearby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b09a0110-f7c5-4ab4-b968-092abd3a2da8.jpg',369441,39,'45.54771','-122.59078',1,5,1.00,2.00,4.00,175.00,3,1125,72,4.99,34256753),(1514,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34284152','Gorgeous Art Home. Family, pets, friends, welcome.','Gorgeous 1927 craftsman home with modern updates and the artistic touch.<br /><br />I love my house.  It’s been thoughtfully decorated and designed to be bright, welcoming and inviting.   Your pet family is invited to join you, at no additional charge, kids have their own place to hang out.  Fenced backyard is a great way to have a private picnic and front yard gazebo is the best for making winter s’mores.<br /><br />I hope you are as comfortable here as I have been the past 7 years.','Maplewood is a beautiful residential neighborhood.  It’s safe and a great place for evening walks, family gatherings and easy Portland living. <br /><br />My house is 15 minutes from OHSU, 18 minutes from downtown Portland and walking distance to Sw Portlands favorite family and pet friendly park, Gabriel Park.<br /><br />It is just 2 miles from the quaint shopping and restaurant filled neighborhoods, Multnomah Village and Hillsdale.<br /><br />There are 2 coffee shops, a frozen yogurt and heathy burrito restaurant within 5 block of my home. Trader Joe’s is just 1.5 miles away.  New Seasons (higher end organic groceries) is 2 miles to the north Fred Meyer and Safeway are less than 8 minutes by car.<br /><br />The Maplewood neighborhood is the perfect blend of quiet residential and everything you need, close by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-34284152/original/43a8b547-fa7e-40f5-81ae-be15d591474c.jpeg',23083044,17,'45.47636','-122.73247',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,190.00,1,42,54,4.98,34284152),(1515,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34285685','Private St Johns bsmnt apt free off-street parking','Private newly-remodeled basement apartment with off-street parking and WiFi in funky St. Johns neighborhood. Guests have private entrance and can check themselves in with the keypad. Close to the University of Portland and downtown St. Johns, and across the street from a food cart pod with lots of dining options, as well as beer, wine, and cider. We\'re also across the street from a Fred Meyer grocery store and a block from New Seasons, a grocery/deli specializing in local and organic options.','St. Johns has its own downtown area about a mile from our home, with lots of options for coffee, dining, drinking, shopping, and entertainment. We have a farmer\'s market every Saturday during the summer. There are many parks within walking or biking distance. We\'re also only a 20-minute drive from downtown Portland and its endless options for eating, drinking, and entertainment. We\'re about an hour from the coast and 1.5 hours from Mt. Hood, with unlimited options in every direction for enjoying the outdoors.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d1000bfa-5f7c-47a1-843e-a08752349fe0.jpg',156237727,58,'45.58743','-122.73967',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,69.00,30,30,156,4.96,34285685),(1516,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34285799','Charming, private 2-level guesthouse-Woodstock','**No list of chores to do at the end of your stay!**<br /><br />Vaulted ceilings, fully private 2 level home. Chef’s kitchen, AC, patio, designer decor and architecture. Contact-less, private self checkin.<br /><br />New Guest House in quiet residential area, upscale Eastmoreland-15 mins from downtown Portland. One bedroom/one bath. Within 10 minutes’ walk is Woodstock Ave-full of cafes, bars, bakeries, and shopping. Ample parking on the street.','The house sits just between the Woodstock and Eastmoreland neighborhoods. Eastmoreland is an established area with intricate old Victorian and craftsman houses-a great place to take a wander. Woodstock is a fun, newly popular neighborhood with plenty of Portland charm—you’ll find breweries, a fish-n-chips window, a famous sausage BBQ joint, bakeries, New Seasons upscale grocery, and vintage shops. Woodstock Ave is approx. 7 blocks from the guest house. Eastmoreland Golf Course, the Rhododendron Garden, historic Sellwood and Reed College are also very close by.<br />Hot spots for Portland in general: Moda Center, The Rose Garden, The Oregon Zoo, Forest Park, The Japanese Garden, Multnomah Falls and so much more!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/283b1bbc-4f4b-465e-8cba-ff475b9b8a53.jpg',16627549,38,'45.47209','-122.61697',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,18,200,4.93,34285799),(1517,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34286860','Concordia home','A newer (2010)  house designed and built by a Street of Dreams builder. We are close to New Seasons grocery, Fernhill and Alberta parks, Alberta St, and Mc Menamin\'s Kennedy School. Backyard garden area for relaxing.  Clean, quiet and comfortable.','We\'re in a very walkable, bikeable neighborhood. Close to great variety of coffee shops,  natural grocery store, Alberta St, restaurants,  food carts, Kennedy School,  brewpubs, parks,  gardens, alleys and tennis courts. Close to bus routes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/54dc3018-e4f5-47da-b7ce-be3e736cf8d6.jpg',6589054,88,'45.57788','-122.63913',1,2,2.50,2.00,2.00,125.00,30,1125,14,4.71,34286860),(1518,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34291889','Modern Kenton home, with Hot Tub.','***CORONA VIRUS UPDATE**. ALL SURFACES (DOOR HANDLES ETC PROFESSIONALLY CLEANED AND SANITIZED BETWEEN ALL GUESTS AND ALL BEDDING BLEACHED!!<br /><br />Ultra modern, new construction single family home. Near Portland International Raceway.  Minutes to Alberta Arts District. Approx 10 min drive to downtown. Walk to Max light rail. Approximately 10-15 minute walk to Kenton shops, restaurants and bars.','Located in historic Kenton district of North Portland. Walk to Kenton shops, restaurants and pubs.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d11aaa07-f4b3-411c-bb13-d8a5e6173cdc.jpg',177429857,55,'45.58822','-122.70254',1,5,2.50,3.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,180,4.92,34291889),(1519,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34321950','Modern Spacious 2-BR Apartment with High Celings','This is a fantastic 2 BR apartment with a great kitchen and spacious living room/dining room.  The  apartment is situated with close proximity to many great eastside neighborhoods, and is only a few minutes from downtown.  <br /><br />The decor is mod-chic with a Portland flare.  The beds are comfortable and the kitchen is fully equipped.','We have a great bar one block south of the apartment called Culmination Brewing.  We have several excellent coffee shops within walking distance, including Nova, Coffee Quest, and Seven Virtues.  We have a small gourmet grocery store a few blocks away called Providore.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-34321950/original/192d9ccd-6c03-42d2-a5ed-5f257936ccb5.jpeg',1218855,12,'45.5294','-122.64256',1,6,1.00,2.00,3.00,68.00,30,365,233,4.91,34321950),(1520,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34333094','The Roomy Basement','This is a huge (appr. 1,000 sq. ft.) sized CLEAN and fully finished and furnished basement suite that is located near the airport.<br />It has a queen-size bed, private bathroom, and a large shower area. It has a sitting area, small fridge, microwave, 65\" Smart TV, and a pool table. All of the space that you see in the picture is included in your stay as \"private\" space (not shared).','I\'m close to the airport, a bike trail, and Glendoveer Golf Course.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0ad3b65b-6bd6-4856-a805-16771906a0f7.jpg',182053001,71,'45.54465','-122.49796',2,2,0.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,7,4.86,34333094),(1521,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34344012','Spacious Chic Apt | Luxe 2BD in Central Portland','This is a fantastic 2 BR apartment with a great kitchen and spacious living room/dining room.  The  apartment is situated with close proximity to many great Eastside neighborhoods, the Oregon Convention Center, the MAX Lloyd <br /> stop, and is only a few minutes from downtown.  <br /><br />Pet fee is $50/pet with a maximum of two pets.  When you book, please let me know how many pets you will be bringing.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-34344012/original/e0613279-d294-4244-8884-e72ae724e0cd.jpeg',1218855,4,'45.5306','-122.64396',1,6,1.00,2.00,3.00,62.00,30,365,304,4.90,34344012),(1522,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34355963','Centrally located house for large group','Oldest house on record in Porltnad per city records but newley remodeled house inside/out, walking and biking distance to everything, downtown Portland 0.5 miles,  Moda Center 1.8 miles, convention center 1.5 miles, OMSI 0.8 miles, Museums, Opera, all mode of transportation is just nearby, including Lloyd Center, etc..<br /><br />Very quiet at night, strategic location for a large group or families.','This is a very central location, you can walk and bike anywhere in east/west downtown Portland, 1.5 miles away. Hawthorne & Division street shops are just a hop, skip & a jump away. OMSI is a couple of blocks, 0.8 miles away. Also Convention Center is 1.5 miles away and Moda Center is 1.8 miles away','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-34355963/original/d03615d7-3c54-4fb6-9698-e010760be161.jpeg',258045340,25,'45.508369','-122.659538',1,11,2.00,5.00,6.00,395.00,30,1125,258,4.74,34355963),(1523,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34364995','Walk to Mt Tabor- Spacious, Rustic 2 bdr Duplex','What better place to enjoy your Pacific Northwest vacation than a stay in the heart of Portland? You will love having an entire one side of a duplex with a chic and spacious interior.  Numerous amenities will pamper you and just to think, it is all within a short walk to bus, max train, food, dispensaries, and to Mt Tabor. Tabor is an extinct volcano and is home to a beautiful park with stunning views of downtown Portland.  Mammoth fir trees and hiking paths make this a cool oasis in the summer.','We are very accessible to all public transportation and are within easy walking distance to food, dispensaries,  and fuel.  Interstate access to I-84 is 5 min away, and Portland International Airport is a 17 min drive.  <br />We are also located in a historic area.  Many years ago our property was an orchard, and just down the street, there is the historic Shogren house, built in 1904 by two sisters who became world famous dress designers, with many of their dresses becoming popular in Paris. They had created a style of dress more suitable for the Portland climate, which was practical, stylish and chic.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8bb5146b-06e1-455e-910e-d2416f5bc8c4.jpg',232864151,52,'45.52425','-122.60058',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,129.00,30,30,170,4.70,34364995),(1524,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34393230','Bohemian Bamboo Hideaway','Enjoy all the comforts of home in this secluded private apartment with views of the surrounding bamboo grove and  trees.  The bedroom has a queen size bed.  The space includes a glass room.  Cots can be set up for sleeping in it in the warmer months.<br /><br />To enter the space go through the gate at the end of the driveway  then through the backyard to enter at the glass room.','Mt. Tabor with it\'s hiking and biking trails, tennis courts and magnificent views is a short walk away. One can walk everywhere in my neighborhood.  There are many wonderful restaurants on Hawthorne and Belmont streets as well as numerous food carts which Portland is famous for.  It\'s an easy walk to New Seasons health food market and Fred Meyers larger everything store.  The library is close as well as Powell\'s book store.  There are a few small movie houses in the neighborhood and farmers markets.  Tabor bread is an excellent bakery using ancient grains and is around the block.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ba9defdf-cc7b-4271-aa75-97dfb2886b83.jpg',10437867,15,'45.51301857472373','-122.60997115138689',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,62.00,1,1125,128,4.92,34393230),(1525,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34394879','Portland Urban Lodge | Quiet | Walkable |  Near','Welcome to the Portland Urban Lodge, a cozy, newly remodeled home nestled in a quiet, friendly neighborhood with an off-street parking spot and ample on-street parking.<br /><br />With  two full bathrooms, a full kitchen and a kitchenette,  the Portland Urban Lodge boasts beautiful wood finishes, two televisions and modern lighting and controls.','Near 57th and Harold, just half a mile from the heart of the Woodstock neighborhood where you will find the park, Safeway, New Seasons, the Library, Grand Central bakery and many others.  Otto’s, an old-school sausage joint has an outdoor barbecue that has been serving up quality German sausage since 1929. With almost 90 years of service to the Woodstock neighborhood, you better believe this is a neighborhood hot spot! Other favorites include Nudi, Toast, Laughing Planet Café, and Ate-Oh-Ate Grill.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-34394879/original/f86cee08-b3b8-4076-9ee0-b015e139526a.jpeg',8876448,38,'45.48213','-122.60481',1,5,2.00,1.00,3.00,117.00,2,1125,87,4.82,34394879),(1526,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34410296','Laurelhurst Park Retreat, light-filled and fun.','A Portland classic in one of the city\'s most vibrant neighborhoods, our home provides a central location to explore and a quiet respite. We are across the street from historic Laurelhurst Park and walking distance to Whole Foods, Laurelhurst Theater and some of Portland\'s best restaurants, bars, and ice cream.','We live in the Laurelhurst neighborhood,  full of locally owned businesses including coffee houses, restaurants, bars, historic homes and Laurelhurst Park. There is a Whole Foods a few blocks away. We\'re within close walking distance to other popular commercial districts- SE Belmont and SE Hawthorne.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-34410296/original/f25f739a-d875-4b00-a3fd-49b3655bd2a8.jpg',1909916,23,'45.52166','-122.63134',1,5,1.50,2.00,2.00,320.00,3,10,44,5.00,34410296),(1527,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34421940','Happy Cozy Home','Be our guests! Our homey place can accommodate small to large groups.  We are located in walking distance of the new up and coming Killingsworth street and Alberta Art district. Home to restaurants, bars, art studios and more. Alberta park is also in walking distance. We’re located right next to the transit line that can take you to and from downtown or anywhere in Portland.','Alberta Art District','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/770fddab-fc42-4034-9ea7-6f8a47aed375.jpg',259852767,29,'45.56599','-122.64948',1,10,1.00,4.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,0,1.00,34421940),(1528,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34465871','Kenton Dreamin\' - 31+ day booking','This charming Old Portland home is a perfect place to enjoy the city. Available for stays of 30 days or more, it is perfect for traveling health care professionals or those looking for interim relocation housing.<br /><br />With an exterior garage and full basement, you\'ll have room to store your things and a fully furnished interior so you don\'t have to unpack!','Kenton is quaint a charming, a pocket neighborhood in North Portland. Quick to get to anywhere by public transit or driving.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/27ead861-2c99-45d6-9a07-8cc2d696f1ca.jpg',20410856,55,'45.58007','-122.68483',1,6,1.50,3.00,3.00,97.00,31,1125,20,5.00,34465871),(1529,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34477057','3 Master Suites - modern, clean, & comfortable!','We are steps away from the yellow line MAX light rail. Nearby are local neighborhood bars, restaurants, food carts, coffee shops and more. You\'ll have the entire house with a kitchen, eating area, washer/dryer and 3 private queen bedroom suites each with a 40\" Samsung Smart TV, quiet Mitsubishi heat/cool mini-splits, work desks & fast free Wifi. The detached garage (for use in warm weather only) has been converted to a semi-finished living room w/huge smart TV, wetbar, mini fridge, half bathroom','Located in the northern part of the Overlook neighborhood.  Killingsworth Street bars & restaurants are very close and Mississippi District is only one mile away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-34477057/original/4ed3faea-54fc-40c2-9404-11b8c495c2b7.jpeg',259462630,13,'45.56249','-122.68336',1,6,3.00,3.00,3.00,263.00,2,29,84,4.95,34477057),(1530,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34512519','Tranquil garden apt','Separate lush garden apartment located in quiet SW hills neighborhood 5 minutes to OHSU , NW 23rd, PSU. Walk to Council Crest park. Close to Zoo and Japanese Gardens.','We are within walking distance to Council Crest Park,which also has a fantastic view of Portland and surrounding mountains.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/03bf6294-4842-4132-87b6-bb184c0da5e2.jpg',66965972,54,'45.49539','-122.70741',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,89.00,1,14,79,4.96,34512519),(1531,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34535868','Beautiful \"Music Studio\" on the End of the Street','Sitting on a quiet cul-de-sac with views of the coastal mountain range everywhere, step onto a private deck that leads to a beautiful studio and bathroom. <br />Enjoy a fireplace, large TV with Roku and a kitchenette. <br />Stroll down to  historic Multnomah Village or Hillsdale for cafes, bars, restaurants, live music and shopping.<br />A drive to downtown Portland  is only 8 minutes or 2.5 miles to OHSU.<br />Not suitable for toddlers','Multnomah Village is a quaint area that is quiet yet still has an urban feel.  Eat at chains like Starbucks and Speilman\'s Bagels or dine at local restaurants like Tastebud, Las Palmas, Fat Kitty Ramen, Yala, Renner’s, or Sera Bellum Cupcakes.  Enjoy The French Quarter for delicious food trucks and John’s Market for every beer or wine choice you can imagine. Bookstores , candy, children\'s, gifts and clothing shops are all there to enjoy.  Walk through nature trails to Gabriel Park including the large dog park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8d68d347-b17d-4fa2-968f-c9bfe4c2c4bb.jpg',218234644,18,'45.4739875793457','-122.71049404144287',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,93.00,2,1125,168,4.86,34535868),(1532,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34543263','Luxe Tiny Home in Hyper-Walkable SE Neighborhood','Indulge in Portland\'s weirdness by staying in our cute and cozy Tiny Home!<br /><br />Located in the heart of \"SouthEast\", just south of Powell along Cesar Chavez, you\'re blocks away from the Division and Hawthorne strips. A foodie\'s dream on foot!<br /><br />Public transit gets you to downtown\'s SW quadrant in <15 minutes. Be sure to visit the historic Powell\'s Books and grab a slice at Sizzle Pie!<br /><br />When you\'re finished wandering, come home to your lovely loft and hunker down...or snuggle UP...your call ;-)','·       Walgreen’s 4 blocks  E on Holgate<br />·       Trader Joes 4 blocks E and 1 block S<br />·       Reed College campus and canyon walk 10” walk<br />·       Crystal Springs Rhododendron Garden 1 mile SW<br />·       Cute shops and eats walking distance on Woodstock, Division, and Clinton<br />·       Groceries: Safeway and Natural Grocers < 1 mile NE','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/26e50ca2-a7f7-4258-9a84-a87adde42d32.jpg',44352149,61,'45.48842','-122.6278',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,91.00,30,1125,45,4.91,34543263),(1533,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34546508','Best kept secret GEM studio apartment','Newly renovated private studio with street entrance basement suite. A block from Belmont street that  boasts  it’s own mix of vintage and indie shops, coffee houses, bars and food carts.  Many recreational unique dining option footsteps away like Slappy Cakes, walking distance to Laurelhurst Park and Mt. Tabor Park, an extinct Volcano with trails and panoramic City View,  few blocks from lively Hawthorne district. 15 minutes to Downtown area and 15-20 minutes to Portland Airport.','We are located in Sunnyside neighborhood, bordered on the north by Laurelhurst and Mt. Tabor. We are a block off Belmont  District, it is packed with history and fantastic shops and restaurants few minutes walk to eclectic Hawthorne and Division Street. Easy access to Downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9294626d-018c-42e9-90f8-fc29a566e041.jpg',103126489,16,'45.51473','-122.61322',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,65.00,4,60,131,4.96,34546508),(1534,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34569604','Loft in Kenton- Hot tub, MAX line, Weed friendly','House with 650 sq ft and patio to yourself. The loft, with vaulted ceilings and beautiful tile and woodwork throughout, is settled behind the main house, and includes a comfortable king bed, modern decor, fold down couch, well functioning kitchen, and access to hot tub. Kenton has great food, retail shops, and bars two blocks away, and guests are a short MAX train ride to Downtown.  LGBTQ+ and rec. marijuana friendly.  This home is not suitable for any guests under 18.   Please read pet policy.','Kenton is a very sweet, old Portland neighborhood.  We are 2 blocks from Denver Street.  Denver Street has a bit of everything - Restaurants, Library, Liquor Store, Weed Shop, Convenience Store, Vintage Shopping, New Boutiques, and Bars.  Walk 2 more blocks to Kenton Park to spend time in nature.  There is a cute pub right next to the park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cb806cd9-f0e2-48c9-8cca-37d833196b66.jpg',26073388,55,'45.58261','-122.68343',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,2,14,492,4.98,34569604),(1535,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34574625','Its a Wonderful Life','Wonderful 1911 Portland 4 square with southern exposure. The home is walking distance to cafes, restaurants, mass transportations, parks, and entertainment. It is also very close to the Oregon Convention Center, The Moda Center, and only 1 mile to city center.  THERE IS A ONE MONTH SECURITY DEPOSIT REQUIRED EQUAL TO ONE MONTHS RENT. THANK YOU','Wonderful historic neighborhood with nearby parks, cafes, restaurants, and close to light rail and The Convention Center.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzQ1NzQ2MjU%3D/original/ab307ec9-5256-4564-b027-169bf606ba1f.jpeg',13109128,7,'45.53578','-122.65242',1,6,2.00,4.00,4.00,150.00,30,110,0,1.00,34574625),(1536,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34698091','St. Johns Portland house close to UP.','Cozy, clean and modern 2 bedroom house in the St. John\'s Portland area. This newly remodeled single level house is a great gettaway place to stay in and relax or as a home base to explore the Portland area.  It is about a 5 minute drive to  University of Portland, Columbia Park, St. John\'s food trucks and many other pubs, coffee shops and restaurants. Hiking trails, parks close by and less then 10 minutes away from St. John\'s historic downtown.','The neighborhood  overall is quiet family friendly neighborhood. There is a train horn that you may or may not notice that is somewhat far away.  Sometimes its during the day and sometimes at night. It is at random times and some people don\'t notice it at all while others who do.  Friday morning is garbage day and the city\'s garbage and recycling trucks come by around 7am.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d41f5cc5-18ee-4f2e-b84f-4df9512c766e.jpg',53617916,60,'45.5857','-122.71134',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,199.00,2,365,28,4.75,34698091),(1537,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34724550','Hollywood Casa | Close to Light Rail & Bus','Welcome to Hollywood Casa,  a newly renovated guest suite with private entrance conveniently located in the heart of NE Portland. Within walking distance of Providence Medical Center, Trader Joe\'s, Whole Foods, farmer\'s market, light rail station,  restaurants, theaters, Laurelhurst Park, or a jog away from Mt. Tabor. 1BD/1bath unit with 700 sq. ft. of space, including full kitchen, washer/dryer, dining/workspace, bathroom,  living room, bedroom,  Roku TV, WiFi. Private, quiet, and cozy space.','Hollywood Casa is located on the boarder of Hollywood district and Rose City Park neighborhoods, and close proximity to Laurelhurst and North Tabor neighborhoods. You can enjoy Middle Eastern,  Cuban, Mexican, Malaysian, Italian, Chinese and many other cuisines nearby. The neighborhood is also very safe, walker and biker friendly.  Many nearby trails in Laurelhurst Park and Mt. Tabor Park allow for outdoor walks and running. Farmer\'s market in the center of the Hollywood neighborhood every Saturday.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-34724550/original/b81303d4-5c30-4894-8b4c-c38b18ded4ab.jpeg',23750692,11,'45.53195','-122.61372',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,88.00,1,29,227,4.93,34724550),(1538,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34751941','Designer curated Mississippi home NO CLEAN FEE','Blocks away from Mississippi Ave, this darling designer/ curator owned home is the perfect base for your Portland adventures. Recently renovated, this 1927 home features old Portland charm, contemporary finishes and art covering most every wall. Walkable to everything that Portland is renowned for: restaurants, breweries, coffee roasters, music venues and shops. Minutes from City Center via very close public transportation, bike or car share.<br />The basement in-law suite is owner occupied.','Walk 5 minutes to historic Mississippi Ave and discover one of the most hippest neighborhoods in Portland. On this street you can find world class restaurants and food carts, popular bars, breweries, and cannabis shops, if that\'s your bag (Just please don\'t smoke in the house). One of the best coffee shops in town, Albina Press, is two short blocks away and Victoria, a see and be seen bar with a large patio, is about 4 blocks away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-34751941/original/889f7ac6-c3fc-4ef0-868c-3292672063a2.jpeg',5603277,24,'45.55739','-122.67157',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,139.00,2,32,258,4.92,34751941),(1539,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34783771','Charming Laurelhurst Suite','Quiet comfy suite w/ full private bath in the charming Laurelhurst Park area.  Walk the neighborhood and enjoy the tree lined streets and charming 1930\'s Craftsman homes.','Centrally located on the hip Eastside of Portland, 15 minutes to downtown by bus or Max.  Laurelhurst Park is a block away and only a 15 minute walk to Belmont and the Hawthorne Districts.  Plenty of wonderful restaurants within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8a1466e8-58db-4b3d-9008-7aeae61e6d8c.jpg',88039293,23,'45.52024','-122.62235',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,2,9,138,4.91,34783771),(1540,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34793168','Rose City Park Retreat','Located in beautiful Rose City Park, our studio is built with our guests in mind. It is clean and bright with 16 ft vaulted ceilings and skylights. Every detail has been thought of to make this a comfortable and inviting experience while you explore all that Portland has to offer. <br /><br />Beautifully tiled shower. Bamboo sheets and plush down pillows. You are within walking distance of restaurants, parks, bars, and food carts along with public transportation. We are close to downtown and PDX airport.','We are close to public transportation. Restaurants are in walking distance as well. Rose City Park Golf course is in walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b5eb86ad-fa49-4fcd-accd-24a9824a3863.jpg',14513197,11,'45.53904','-122.60556',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,106.00,30,90,117,4.99,34793168),(1541,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34821661','Modern Urban Home in a Walker\'s Paradise','This modern one bedroom private entry unit is a walker and biker\'s paradise and is located just a few blocks away from NE Williams district and a short walk to NE Mississippi district. It has all of the comforts of home and is perfect for solo travelers, couples and colleagues, alike. The ultimate in modern comfort with a walk score of 95!!!  It located less than 3 miles away from downtown Portland/Pearl District and 7 miles from the PDX airport.','Other things to note<br />Check-in is 4PM or later. You will receive a personal code for 24 hour entry.<br /><br />Check-out is 11 AM<br /><br />We can sometimes be flexible for a later checkout or earlier check-in if requested in advance and depending on other guests.<br /><br />NO smoking or vaping is allowed anywhere on the premises. <br /><br />Sorry but we do not allow pets.<br /><br />If you don\'t mind - please kindly remove your shoes when entering the guest house.<br /><br />Parking on street only - Please do not park in the driveway AT ANY TIME - EVEN TEMPORARILY as it is a shared space with neighbors.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cd908324-9bd2-4c26-8734-9a8baa4a77d6.jpg',3700834,9,'45.55062','-122.66507',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,71.00,1,14,195,4.95,34821661),(1542,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34837777','Henriette House - Cozy, Artsy, Walkable & AC!','Step into this charming 1907 craftsman, nestled in the heart of Portland’s trendiest neighborhood. Just steps from breweries, shops, and top restaurants, it’s the ultimate spot to soak up local culture—or unwind in style. Relax in the sunny backyard with a game of cornhole, whip up meals in the fully stocked kitchen, or venture out to explore Portland and the stunning PNW wilderness nearby.<br /><br />We have cold AC and a warm, inclusive vibe—LGBTQ+ friendly!','This is my favorite neighborhood in Portland. This up-and-coming neighborhood has a new restaurant/bar popping up weekly and it has easy access to other fun areas of the city.  Brunch and patio season is what Portland is all about so take advantage of this sweet location for both!  Some of my favorites are: Interurban (brunch, dinner, and patio drinking), Por Que No (lunch/dinner), Radio Room (patio/drinks), Stormbreaker (patio/beer/cornhole), and Vendetta (patio/drinks).  There are also food carts a few blocks down on Vancouver and another pod on nearby Mississippi.  New Seasons is a quick walk or bike ride if you feel like stocking up on groceries for a night in.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-34837777/original/57605d31-4071-4775-8874-9d837e65008d.jpeg',6949748,9,'45.55348','-122.6666',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,125.00,1,170,264,4.98,34837777),(1543,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34866219','Bright and Open Modern Northeast Montavilla ADU','New construction. Open modern design. New furniture and bedding. Includes full kitchen with pots and pans spices and olive oil and vinegar. A Mr Coffee maker. TV with directv in each room. Back French patio doors to private yard and garden.','The neighborhood has too many good restaurants and coffee houses to list. My favorites are Bi Partisan Cafe and Fillmore Cafe. East Glisan Pizza is excellent. Roscoes, Hourglass (great fried chicken), Observatory restaurant. <br />Go for a 3 mile hike up to Mt Tabor and get a great view of downtown Portland and watch the sunset. <br />Bring your bikes and lock them up in the new bike shed.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/60b46d33-ed94-4035-85f3-28088fdea933.jpg',4580020,10,'45.52658','-122.58289',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,157.00,2,1125,76,4.88,34866219),(1544,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34935743','Chic Spa Central - Inner Eastside Gem','Enjoy your stay in our tenderly accommodating, self sufficient modern home.<br /><br />Take pleasure in being just minutes away from everything you need, in the heart of South East Portland and the Clinton & Division St. neighborhood.<br /><br />Then come home & slide into our hot tub and sauna before getting a beautiful nights rest.<br /><br />We are centrally located in Southeast Portland, very close to downtown / OHSU and within walking distance to many great areas including bike rentals, restaurants, bars & markets.','Take pleasure in being just minutes away from everything you need, in the heart of South East Portland and the Clinton & Division St. neighborhood.<br /><br />Stroll leisurely to countless trendy shops, great bars, award-winning restaurants, decadent coffee houses and more. Your place is just seconds away from one of the best organic local markets, a few blocks away from New Seasons, Clinton corner and relaxation at Löyly massage house. There are bikes you can rent around the corner and there are great bike paths all around this area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b50300d6-3769-4ce2-987e-7f228b8ca8a4.jpg',263251243,25,'45.5014','-122.64471',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,79.00,1,30,321,4.92,34935743),(1545,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/34936500','Modern Luxury | Central PDX | Spacious Apt','This is a fantastic 2 BR apartment with a great kitchen and spacious living room/dining room.  The  apartment is situated with close proximity to many great eastside neighborhoods, the Oregon Convention Center, the MAX Llyod train station, and is only a few minutes from downtown.  <br /><br />The decor is mod-chic with a Portland flare.  The beds are comfortable and the kitchen is fully equipped.','We are located in the very centrally located Kerns neighborhood.  Culmination Brewery serves great food and drink and is only a block away.  The Zipper has several amazing restaurants and is only a 10 minute walk from our place.  We have several coffee shops and tea shops nearby as well.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-34936500/original/b1c62523-16fc-4ce0-a41d-e9561010524b.jpeg',1218855,12,'45.52948','-122.6432',1,6,1.00,2.00,3.00,70.00,31,365,308,4.89,34936500),(1546,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35013488','Hip Homey Haven','This beautiful, ground level apartment of our home is located in the heart of the Alberta Arts district. This place is flooded with light & offers all the cozy comforts to serve as your home away. If you\'re feeling adventurous, take a short walk to Alberta St. where you\'ll find great coffee, delicious food, & an assortment of quirky shops. Loads of coffee local shops, pubs & restaurants within 2 blocks. 15 minute walk from Mississippi Ave & N. Williams St, 10 minute drive from downtown Portland!','Our neighborhood is surrounded by local shops and everyday bikers on Going Street. The Last Thursday of every month in the summer features pop-up shops that line Alberta Street, which makes for a great evening for exploring and finding unique collectibles.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/598f1f2d-bd11-4352-bb99-7fb9376453af.jpg',289998249,6,'45.55761','-122.65153',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,78.00,2,45,186,4.92,35013488),(1547,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35034572','Thought Incubator','Enjoy our private entry way studio carriage house located behind our main home in the middle of Piedmont. Right next to Peninsula park and the Rosa Parks MAX Station, you\'ll be a walk away from a rose garden picnic, and stops away from City Center. The walk-up studio is fit with a full sized bed, a day bed/couch, washer, dryer, and air conditioning. If you feel the need to use the full kitchen, stop by New Seasons located two blocks away, for some ingredients.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f10d2c08-5c0a-4e41-ace9-88bc21125a06.jpg',21101389,48,'45.57129','-122.6748',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,2,7,143,4.92,35034572),(1548,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35091759','Sellwood Haven- Private entrance','Welcome to our home! We built this guest space to host people from all over the world and we hope you love it as much as we do. A lot of care and thought went into this, so we hope you will appreciate all of the things we\'ve done to make our home yours when you stay with us.<br /><br />There are two great bedrooms with high ceilings and lots of light and fresh air. There is a common space with a reading nook, kitchenette, and a closet for your coats, bags, and all of the treasures you find to bring home.','Sellwood is one of the jewels of Portland. Check out our guidebook to see the many things our neighborhood has to offer!  It is a small scale neighborhood just south of the downtown core,  surrounded by all the beauty for which the Pacific Northwest is known. We live in the heart of the community and our walking score is 95. You can walk to great local coffee, restaurants, bars, shops, food carts, sushi, bottle shops, pubs, breweries, theaters, and parks. If you need to stock up there are grocery stores and other suppliers and two different parks. We also live very close to Oaks Bottom wildlife preserve with an amazing assortment of wildlife and easy fun walks. Springwater Corridor\'s southern entrance is just down the street for long runs or access to Portland bike routes and of course, the city itself! It\'s very easy to get into Portland for all of the culture, food, fun, and more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5fab4faf-bc5f-4fc3-a1b6-055cdc649b78.jpg',117204372,20,'45.46811','-122.65106',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,86.00,2,27,220,4.97,35091759),(1549,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35155827','Large contemporary in a historic train station','Built in 1906 and listed on the National Register of Historic Places, the building was originally the North Bank Railway station. Centrally located in the middle of the vibrant Pearl District and around the corner to galleries, cafés and boutiques (Walk Score of 98!) and within walking distance of downtown. Newly remodeled with all new contemporary furnishings and original artwork in a classic context. Two bedrooms and 2 ½ baths, garage, 2,584 square feet – sleeps 6 comfortably.','Located in the heart of the vibrant Pearl District, cafes, restaurants, boutiques and galleries are just around the corner.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5786d0e9-ecfb-460d-8765-e027079559b7.jpg',264765755,2,'45.52852','-122.68147',1,6,2.50,2.00,3.00,200.00,31,365,7,5.00,35155827),(1550,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35158304','Our Guesthouse - Alberta Park - 2 bedrooms (queen)','Our goal is for you to feel at home during your stay with the convenient location and amenities. You\'ll have the space all to yourself as you explore Portland and the surrounding areas or return to after visiting friends and family. Walk to excellent restaurants, call in a local delivery, or stay in and cook with a fully equipped kitchen. Restless kids (or adults) can grab a ball and explore the 16 acre park one block away.','Leave the car, go for a stroll (even if it\'s raining). Within 1/2 a mile you will find plenty of  well known local restaurants such as Salt & Straw, Hat Yai, Pine State Biscuits, and Tamale Boy, plus there are dozens of other 4+ star Yelp restaurants, coffee shops and bars within that same 1/2 mile.<br /><br />The park has baseball fields, playground, swings, basketball and tennis court and small nature path in addition to a running/walking trail around its circumference.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8bd82c11-83b3-470e-9dcd-96163e303487.jpg',8804265,29,'45.56414','-122.64751',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,156.00,1,1125,261,5.00,35158304),(1551,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35192098','Portland Vintage Hideaway','Portland Vintage Hideaway is a lovely, private, completely self-contained unit in our light-filled 1950\'s day-ranch basement. Enjoy 600+ sq.ft., queen bed with memory foam topper,  double sofa bed, TV with streaming, workspace area, wi-fi, and adorable fully appointed kitchenette! The private, gated garden and patio offer a serene and lovely setting in which to hang out for meals & enjoy a glass of wine. We accept a maximum of two dogs and there is a pet fee. Please see details in the listing.','We are a half a block from 90 acre Gabriel Park with an awesome dog park, tennis courts, hiking trails, baseball fields, kids play area. SW Community Center is at our end of Gabriel Park - only steps away - with two pools, hot tub, exercise, yoga, & dance classes, and beautifully equipped exercise/weight room.   You will find delightful Driftwood Coffee across the street. We are a block from delicious and healthy Laughing Planet restaurant as well as Sunny\'s Legendary fro-yo.  Multnomah Village is a 10-minute walk (cut through Gabriel Park) where you\'ll find an amazingly charming little village with restaurants, bars, coffee hangouts, Grand Central Baking Co., Umpqua Bank, Annie Blooms Books, clothing, gift, art, and antique shops.<br /> Portland city center is a quick 10-minute drive and the #1 city bus stops directly in front of your private entrance to Portland Vintage Hideaway!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b1e18259-8e5b-4e3e-8cef-bbf3282d1b13.jpg',26712397,75,'45.47548','-122.72449',1,4,1.00,1.00,4.00,64.00,2,183,184,4.88,35192098),(1552,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35220921','Historic House by University of Portland','Historic Updated House in the University Park neighborhood of North Portland.<br />Parking spots for 2 vehicles and plenty of free street parking available.<br />Multiple restaurants, bars and food carts blocks away.<br />Walking distance to the University of Portland and multiple bus lines.<br /><br />University of Portland - 0.5 miles<br />Adidas Headquarters - 2.5 miles<br />Expo Center - 4 miles<br />Swan Island Businesses - 4.5 miles<br />Moda / Convention Center - 6 miles<br />Downtown - 6.5 miles<br />Airport -  10 miles','The University of Portland is 5 blocks away.<br />Lots of local bars, restaurants and coffee shops with in a 10 minute walk','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-35220921/original/f3284549-5bbc-41ba-8c9e-a892185b64f1.jpeg',51858478,57,'45.5801','-122.72308',1,6,1.00,2.00,3.00,150.00,2,10,2,4.50,35220921),(1553,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35236468','Private Dog-Friendly Studio Near Downtown','Welcome to the Monkey Puzzle, your humble abode while exploring PDX ! Walk, bike or Uber to nearby Mississippi Street or Alberta Arts district, step across the street and take a leisurely walk around Peninsula Park, or take a quick drive eastward to explore the many waterfalls of the Columbia River Gorge. With a MAX stop within walking distance, freeway access a mere mile away, and a bus stop just steps from the front porch, this is a prime locale for your Portland vacation. No pet fees!','The original rose testing garden built in 1913 is just steps from our front door.  We are squeezed in between the bustling Mississippi Street and the Alberta Arts District.  Our neighborhood is close to many universities, colleges, and our block dead ends into a community college.  We are just a 10 minute drive from the City Center.   NE Portland in particular is known for its concert halls, local art, coffee shops, brunch spots, the Moda center/Rose Quarter.  You won\'t run out of things to do or places to walk/bike to while enjoying your stay!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-35236468/original/b24ba948-fd91-43cb-a94f-b0e001513026.jpeg',498934,24,'45.56081','-122.67145',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,125.00,1,100,545,4.86,35236468),(1554,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35287438','Gorgeous, Walkable, Spacious & Family Friendly!','Our home is within walking distance of fantastic coffee shops, restaurants, boutiques and movie theaters. We\'re a block away from Berrydale Park. Our kitchen is fully equipped and our master king bed is fantastically comfortable. We\'ve got three kids so in addition to the king bed in the master, we have a day bed in the office, bunk beds in the kid room and a baby crib in the nursery you are welcome to use with your family! Our kitchen is fully equipped.','Start your day out right with a walk to Hungry Heart where you can grab a cup of coffee and pastries. For a late morning brunch, hit up Lazy Susan. For lunch you can pick from pizza to sushi and everything in between. In the evening you can choose craft cocktails, tasty brews or fine wines. And it\'s all within an easy walk from our home!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/91387ed0-afc6-4826-8b48-01b822b5d984.jpg',793916,10,'45.51496','-122.56956',1,4,2.50,2.00,2.00,100.00,30,1125,1,5.00,35287438),(1555,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35301751','Private Studio adjacent to PSU, HistoricHafnerHaus','This listing is for a Private studio with a private entrance and full bath. The bathroom has a traditional claw foot style  bathtub and shower.<br /><br />There is a queen bed as well as a twin bed in the room and we can add a roll away for a fourth person upon request.<br /><br /> Please search \'The Historic Hafner Haus\' for pictures of the  bedrooms options.<br /><br />The full kitchen, formal dining room and living room are shared spaces but are available for your use as well as your private studio.','We are close to everything downtown. You might also be interested to know that there\'s a police rest stop in the church next door so it\'s a very safe neighborhood as well.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzUzMDE3NTE%3D/original/5c6a393d-0734-479a-b0ba-279a4b6c3974.jpeg',8207605,44,'45.51601','-122.688',1,4,1.00,0.00,3.00,48.00,30,33,39,4.79,35301751),(1556,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35317415','Private studio close in SE Clinton/Division','Welcome to our basement studio close in SE. Sits blocks away from Portland\'s popular Division and Clinton areas. Extremely close to some of the best neighborhoods, restaurants, bars and shopping Portland has to offer!<br />Private entrance, kitchenette, full bathroom, and bedroom. (Queen Tempur-pedic bed) Shared access to beautiful covered outside patio! Covered/secured area if you have a bike. free wi-fi, shared washer/dryer. We live on the upper levels of the home if anything is needed','We live close in SE and are walkable to so much! There are parks, coffee, tea, kava, beer, drinks, food, clothes, movies, books... so much so close. Public transit is everywhere and can take you to all parts of the city. It is a perfect location for exploring','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/48598634-70b1-4329-a570-c1bf8bc87a29.jpg',6484099,8,'45.49851','-122.62998',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,4,95,41,4.93,35317415),(1557,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35318813','Ash Street Loft- Urban chic, walk to downtown','Newly constructed attic loft on one of Buckman\'s historic streets. Downtown Portland is merely one mile away! Restaurants, entertainment and shopping within walking distance.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/100ff457-44f4-4fb6-b5a5-6466954bf440.jpg',27977619,32,'45.52054','-122.65354',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,90.00,2,1125,318,5.00,35318813),(1558,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35318843','Private guesthouse w/ yard, firepit, patio, loft','We built this cottage in 2019 using many reclaimed materials, and we hope you love it as much as we do. Located just one block from all the best North Portland has to offer; coffee shops, brunch spots, neighborhood bars and shops. Very easy access to public transit (light rail and bus) and only one exit from downtown. 15 minutes to the airport and 8 minutes to Forest Park. Includes a spacious private yard/patio and firepit.','We love the Humboldt Neighborhood just north of downtown Portland. There is an adorable grocery store three blocks away, Cherry Sprout. We also love the Wisconsin themed bar around the corner, Saraveza. 3 minute walk to the Killingsworth Food Carts and a 10 minute walk to Peninsula Park rose garden and Mississippi Street attractions. We are located very close to the freeway and public transit so getting anywhere in town is quick and easy.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dbb7fb9b-7670-4385-80ad-4877c1312b5c.jpg',448315275,24,'45.56225','-122.6767',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,74.00,2,730,165,4.95,35318843),(1559,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35387473','Lovely NE bright hideaway, walk to food/beer/shops','Welcome to your Portland Hideaway! This charming 2-bedroom, 1-bath home is the perfect base for exploring the city. Located in a vibrant neighborhood, you\'re just steps away from Portland\'s best bars, restaurants, shopping, and parks. Enjoy the convenience of nearby outdoor recreation, with hiking trails only a short drive away. The home features a fully equipped kitchen, cozy living area, and fast Wi-Fi. Whether you\'re here to relax or explore, this is the ideal spot to experience Portland!','We absolutely love this neighborhood, and we think you will too! Very walkable, with some great spots just 2 blocks away. Don\'t miss La Taq for some to-die-for brisket queso and margaritas. Hat Yai is the best lunch spot around, and Proud Mary will provide for all of your coffee needs. <br /><br />Alberta Park is just 4 blocks away, and has a great playground for the kiddos and plenty of green space for all!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0061bf1f-9697-4140-bee6-2d92bdcde740.jpg',8013108,29,'45.5648','-122.65126',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,135.00,2,1125,204,4.96,35387473),(1560,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35390383','The Travelers Nest','A perfect space for  solo travelers and couples, The Travelers Nest is a quiet apartment that is within walking distance to shops, restaurants & the arts districts of Belmont, Hawthorne & Division St.  We are also only a 5 min walk to Providence Hospital.  Drive a few minutes or take light rail to downtown, Washington Park, The Zoo, Rose Garden & Japanese Gardens.   We are Oregon natives and live upstairs & are ready to offer any advice to enhance your stay, yet give you the privacy you need.','Hike/Dine/Drink/Dance/Shop/Rest/Rinse/Repeat!<br />Quiet neighborhood on a bike street with easy access to parks, restaurants, bars, shopping, hiking, freeways and more.  It\'s a perfect place for those visiting loved ones at Providence Hospital as well where we are only a five minute walk away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cb93970b-d72e-4575-a81f-d970812435d4.jpg',5231006,52,'45.52607','-122.61123',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,52.00,3,14,67,4.97,35390383),(1561,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35418187','Cozy Yurt Getaway in Forest Park + Indoor Space.','Experience a unique retreat just 10-15 minutes from downtown Portland! Our spacious accommodations include a charming yurt and a cozy basement studio with a private entrance, small kitchen, library, and bathroom. Perfect for nature lovers, the yurt offers a serene escape with nearby hiking trails and gardens. The nearby neighborhood of St. Johns is great for a quick outing.<br /><br />Note: The Studio is a 50-yard walk from the yurt. For a smoother arrival, plan to settle in during daylight hours.','Enjoy miles of Forest Park trails, right outside the yurt door, with access to small towns with Northwest 23rd only 6 miles away.  <br /><br />Across the river is St Johns with lots of great coffee spots and places to eat.   We love Cathedral Park which gives you a great view of the bridge and a bit of river.   St Johns has a great food cart pod and many types of food.  <br /><br />West on Highway 30 is the small town of LInnton with a great Feed and Seed Store and two local taverns.  Further down the road is Sauvie\'s Island with many farm markets and river beaches.<br /><br />We are in Portland but the North Portland neighborhoods maintain their original roots and are fun places to walk around and explore. <br /><br />Our house is at the end of the road and is part of a small cluster of houses. The hill is winding and ends in the park.  The road is dirt in some places.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e7e9b457-4051-441d-9228-78dbfeee5c05.jpg',3005870,89,'45.58365','-122.7753',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,91.00,2,90,125,4.78,35418187),(1562,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35486590','The Booty House','A radical community house with a Portland following of its own.  Permaculture homebrewery featured on Vice\'s BeerLand, Musical instruments, giant garden, Ducks, and love galore.','Classic Portland on the edge of the ever encroaching gentrification.  Montevilla has bars and restaurants abound in walking and stumbling distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/012ab101-7cfd-4c88-9baa-1e7965142f95.jpg',16213970,10,'45.52873','-122.58766',2,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,39.00,1,30,127,4.96,35486590),(1563,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35519473','Heart of SE Portland Studio | A Quiet Haven','Welcome to Studio B! We are proud to offer our private studio nestled in the heart of Southeast Portland. Inside you will find accommodations designed to help our guests recharge and prepare for a full day exploring our beautiful city. Studio B offers a great landing point for where you want to be on your visit to PDX with close proximity to hotspots such as SE Clinton & Division St. Downtown is really accessible with light rail services nearby or a 5 minute UBER.<br /><br />We look forward to having you!','The Brooklyn neighborhood was orginally named \"Brookland\" by Giddeon Tibbets due to the rivers, creeks, and lakes on his property.<br /><br />Since those days of German influence, you can still find delicious food down the street at Edel Weiss deli. Rose City Coffee is right around the block and has a delightful and talented staff of baristas ready to take your order.<br /><br /> \"Today it is regarded as among southeast Portland\'s most desirable residential neighborhoods.\" - Wikipedia','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-35519473/original/b0068972-23af-42f4-8065-8232b1f0b644.jpeg',215058058,56,'45.49906158','-122.65305328',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,2,365,138,4.96,35519473),(1564,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35548744','Stylish Vintage Retreat: Art+Vinyl+Fenced Yard+BBQ','Restored 1940s gem!! Meticulously maintained, quintessential Portland.<br /><br />Enter a curated living space with hand-picked designer vintage furniture, contemporary art, oak floors, heat & A/C. Fully equipped kitchen w/Viking stove & custom island. Very private, fully-fenced backyard w/ BBQ, perfect for kids and pets! Garaged & driveway parking included.<br /><br />Unbeatable location: walk or bike to coffee, restaurants, bars, markets, Adidas HQ, & accessible to all Portland has to offer!','Overlook is very pretty, feels safe and has old growth trees that line many of the streets. It\'s a wonderful area with beautifully improved homes and neighborhoods.<br /><br />This area offers a secluded feeling, but still extremely convenient access to other local neighborhoods and the Max light rail train. Local businesses thrive here - a few standouts are Old Gold, Blend Coffee, Miho Sushi & Izakaya, Backyard Social, and The Overlook House. If you want shop like a local, head to New Seasons Market and Fred Meyer, and also check out the retail, vintage shops, and restaurant areas on nearby Belmont St. & Hawthorne Blvd., just a short drive away.<br /><br />Overlook offers very \"bikeable\" access to downtown Portland, great mass transit options via light rail and bus and is about a 5 minute drive to downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b906bf3e-37ac-43e9-87ad-d58457bab1e2.jpg',85513975,13,'45.56107','-122.6895',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,129.00,1,60,232,4.81,35548744),(1565,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35605973','Cozy Sunnyside Flat in Historic Home','Beautiful updated flat in a 1907 Portland 4 square.  You will have full private access to the first floor unit with front porch as well as the basement apartment.  The basement apartment has an extra bedroom and sitting area with television, bathroom and kitchenette. This historic home is located in the heart of historic Sunnyside.  Easy access to New Seasons and Fred Meyer Groceries and very short walk to Belmont and Hawthorne shopping districts.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d30ff18e-e1b4-4981-9ef8-c2231371b678.jpg',16783762,16,'45.5169','-122.62197',1,6,2.00,2.00,4.00,84.00,30,1125,2,5.00,35605973),(1566,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35612880','Hip Mid-Century Montavilla 2 bed pet friendly','Renovated Mid Century Montavilla duplex.  Back unit that stays cool, quiet and private.  Clean and bright with an eclectic mix of modern and vintage furnishings.    Newer appliances with dishwasher and lightly used W/D included.  Pet friendly with a private fenced backyard.  There are even garden beds if you want to grow fruits and veggies.  750 square feet that\'s nicely furnished with high speed internet and a smart TV.  We have added a portable air conditioner for summer!','Montavilla is a hip walkable area with coffee houses, bakeries, highly rated restaurants, an inexpensive movie theater and some quaint shops.  There is even a farmer\'s market once a week in the summer!  All within walking distance from your unit.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5dffa97e-9a7d-4356-91d8-5d87371ed0b2.jpg',30942269,10,'45.52573','-122.58465',1,3,1.00,2.00,2.00,95.00,30,1125,25,4.84,35612880),(1567,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35621697','Retro Modern 2-Bedroom w/ 90 WalkScore','Located in the vibrant Hawthorne District, our apartment is within walking distance of Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brewpubs, and distilleries. other services, such as banks and massage therapists, are also nearby.  Around a mile from downtown, you can easily use bikes, public bus services, or walk to explore the city. Our sleek, European-style interiors feature high-grade surfaces and finishes, offering comfort and elegance in one of Portland\'s most dynamic neighborhoods.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors, with no chain restaurants in sight! Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, indulge in delicious wings right around the corner at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or enjoy a fancy night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-35621697/original/d89287f6-5786-4d2f-aab3-67aab7d40fe5.jpeg',187734201,32,'45.51277','-122.64727',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,90.00,2,1125,440,4.86,35621697),(1568,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35682143','Beautiful SW Portland Room and Bathroom!','Great location in Southwest Portland for your comfort. Only 10 minutes to downtown, Beaverton, or Tigard. Close to three bus lines, 54, 56, and 55. Shopping and Restaurants within a short drive. Across the street from Hamilton Park. Great option for a long term stay or a work from home option. We are a fun family and if you need anything just ask! We have a small dog named Harley and he doesn’t bite :)','Near to Counsel Crest overlooking all of Portland','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/065af442-8787-4916-b8a4-c63f0a011f43.jpg',76418105,70,'45.48998','-122.72282',2,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,39.00,30,1125,63,4.83,35682143),(1569,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35682163','One Bedroom Retreat in the Heart of inner SE','This eclectic modern apartment sits on the ground level of our home, with the door down a private entrance hydrangea flanked walkway. <br /><br />New construction, appointed beautifully with all brand new appliances, including a washer & dryer.  Extremely well positioned for a short walk to concerts at Revolution Hall, bars, restaurants, coffee, grocery stores, all while on a quiet street with plenty of parking.','Buckman is an incredibly walkable neighborhood located squarely in the middle of Portland. Access to North, Deep SE, NW, and Downtown is incredibly easy.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0a8fd8aa-2abb-44de-a6cf-81efddb21760.jpg',1406738,32,'45.51806','-122.648',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,109.00,3,1125,24,4.96,35682163),(1570,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35793276','Walk Everywhere from a Historic Home with A/C','Step through a jasmine  archway into a timeless historic Portland residence with air conditioning, seamlessly blending historic charm with contemporary comforts. Rare off street parking in a vibrant area walking distance to outstanding restaurants and a short bike ride or drive to downtown. This home features charming details like wood floors and tin ceilings, alongside modern conveniences. Upstairs, the bedroom includes an attached second living room, ideal for movie nights or yoga sessions.','There are 20 locally owned shops and 26 restaurants and bars on the historic Mississippi Ave business district just one block away! Check out mississippiave dotcom to see a list of everything located nearby! Stroll to live music at Mississippi Studios and The 1905, walkable to yoga studios, Barre 3, and many classpass workout options.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-35793276/original/07032966-d022-4de7-91f2-1a713b1bf997.jpeg',60300963,9,'45.55138','-122.67667',1,2,1.50,1.00,1.00,199.00,3,90,35,4.89,35793276),(1571,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35849527','Spacious 5,000+ sq ft house, Close to PDX Airport','Custom Built Over 5,000 sq ft home. 5 Large bedrooms,  5 full baths, 2 wet-bars, 3 fireplaces, large family, living and dining rooms, Huge garage with table tennis, pool table, and other games. Hardwood floors in main living area and cozy carpet in the bedrooms. large TVs in every room, cozy sectional sofas and a large gourmet kitchen. The home is great for family\'s, small groups, vacationers and business travel.  A/C in every room. Huge back yard, tons of parking.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/443a3917-46f3-4312-b2bb-9d057b802edd.jpg',100656896,71,'45.53822','-122.49673',1,10,5.00,5.00,5.00,600.00,4,1125,64,4.83,35849527),(1572,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35912999','Hawthorne Apartment LLC','Private studio apartment on Hawthorne near Mount Tabor. Separate entrance ample street parking','Close to all the cafes, restaurants and shops on Hawthorne plus walk to Mount Tabor Park for spectacular city and mountain View’s','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6b3f06a1-e1c9-44c0-9475-f8354835fbc4.jpg',94623462,15,'45.5113','-122.60815',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,2,28,130,4.98,35912999),(1573,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/35999782','The Loft: Modern Open space in Southeast Portland','An open, airy, private, and stylish space located over a detached garage behind the main house. This is a great neighborhood that is close to public transportation and major roads. Easily walk to bike rentals, food carts, restaurants, local bars, and main shopping areas. We are looking to provide a safe and comfortable space. We love to give suggestions and recommendations on places and things to do while in Portland and Oregon.','This space is great for 1-2 people and comfortable but tight for 3 people.  We are in a quiet residential area within a growing city. Walkable to multiple food cart pods, bars, coffee shops, and some of the best restaurants in the city.  The area we live in is called Richmond but borders on Foster-Powell aka FoPo.  Clinton Park, Creston Park and Pool are both less than 0.5mi away. Mt. Tabor is 1 mi away, bike to Woodstock, and all of the new places coming up on Foster.  Also look up streets/neighborhoods:  Division, Hawthorne, Foster Ave (FoPo), Woodstock.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-35999782/original/7da75e95-def7-4534-b6ae-02706713c041.jpeg',488928,37,'45.49994','-122.60887',1,2,1.00,0.00,4.00,86.00,2,28,308,4.99,35999782),(1574,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36000696','Cute and Classic Montavilla House','Our home is a single family house built in 1904 in a calm but lively neighborhood at the foot of Mt. Tabor called Montavilla. The house is just a 5 minute walk to Stark St., the neighborhood\'s main street, with several bars, coffee shops, breweries, a movie theater, and a market. We have tried to preserve the house\'s original shape and feel, but at the same time make it comfortable and livable.','It is a very peaceful neighborhood but it also has many things to offer, depending on what you are looking for! Just a 5 minute walk from the house you\'ll find Stark St., with great coffee shops, an old school movie theater, a Sunday farmer\'s market and several restaurants, bars, and breweries. (There is one brewery right on our street, called \"Threshold\", which is our favorite, and is run by a Polish guy who makes the most amazing beer.) About a 15-20 minute walk from our house is a beautiful park located on top of an old volcano crater with beautiful city views and picnicking opportunities called Mount Tabor. We are about a 30 min bus ride/15 min taxi ride from Portland\'s downtown. We are also between 10 and 20 minutes in the car from other great Portland neighborhoods such as Hawthorne, Belmont, Foster/Powell, Kerns, Alberta, Williams, and Mississippi.  But really, Portland is fairly small, and we\'re pretty centrally located, so everything in the city will be fairly easily accessibl','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36000696/original/2998544f-ac33-425e-85f2-b33f45a56c2d.jpeg',103005225,10,'45.52268','-122.58324',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,60,14,4.93,36000696),(1575,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36001458','Newly-built Backyard Guest House near Mt Tabor','This newly-built additional dwelling unit (ADU) with high ceilings feels light, bright, and larger than it’s 495 square feet. Built-in décor is simple and modern, yet the furniture and kitchenware feels comfortable and eclectic. Immerse yourself in a deep bath in the Japanese-style ofuro; have a glass of wine on the patio underneath the apple tree outside the backdoor; relax on the couch with a book; or enjoy the heat or air-conditioning inside as you cook a meal in the well laid-out kitchen.','South Tabor is a pleasant, walkable neighborhood located in-between the dynamic neighborhoods of 82nd Ave. Jade District, Montavilla, Division Street and Foster-Powell (FoPo). Mt. Tabor Park, a lovely forested park, is just a half-mile walk away! (Entrances on SE 66th and SE 67th streets.) Stroll around the flat neighborhood on sidewalks, or hike up Tabor for more of a work-out under tall Douglas fir trees, and enjoy a gorgeous view of the City. <br /><br />Walk to nearby coffeeshops or to Thai, Chinese, Vietnamese, Peruvian, brewery/bars, pizzeria or Philly sandwich eateries—all within a half-mile. Feel free to ask your hosts for recommendations.<br /><br />If you want to walk, ride a bike, take the bus or drive just a little further (1-2 miles), the restaurants, food cart pods, and shops of Division and Hawthorne Streets, Montavilla, Foster-Powell neighborhood, and the 82nd Street/Jade District beckon. Grocery stores within a 2-mile radius include Winco, ABC Seafood Company, OM Seafo','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e823c9e6-25c0-4958-a80d-d368da6db493.jpg',200194273,37,'45.50011','-122.59669',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,31,200,13,5.00,36001458),(1576,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36075543','Modern Comfort | Stylish 2BD in heart of PDX','This is a fantastic 2 BR apartment with a great kitchen and spacious living room/dining room. The apartment is situated with close proximity to many great eastside neighborhoods, the Oregon Convention Center, the MAX Lloyd stop,  and is only a few minutes from downtown. The decor is mod-chic with a Portland flare. The beds are super comfortable and the kitchen is fully equipped!','We have a great brewery, Culmination Brewery just a block away.  There is a cool small grocery store/cafe/bakery called Providore not far, a tea shop called Jasmine Pearl, and a great food cart pod called the Zipper, all within walking distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36075543/original/c19c4716-2120-4a14-bec5-e211970585aa.jpeg',1218855,4,'45.53035','-122.64317',1,6,1.00,2.00,3.00,71.00,30,365,304,4.90,36075543),(1577,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36104735','#StayInMyDistrict St Johns Walk to dining & shops','Stay in My District Downtown St Johns. Walk to local dining & shopping. Forest Park is across the bridge, with miles of single track running, hiking & Mtn biking trails. Walk or bike to Downtown St Johns, Cathedral Park, 10 min. to Downtown Portland & Pearl District. 20 min to PDX. NEW basement apt designed with guest comfort in mind. Modern finishes and upgrades in this comfortable 900 ft.² featuring 2 bed / 1 bath. Sleeps up to 5. Kitchen, Washer/Dryer, Fireplace. FREE Parking, Roku Streaming/','The home is located in the heart of the historic \"St Johns\" neighborhood, in Portland OR. This neighborhood is a local favorite and a great place to experience the heart and soul of one of Portland’s favorite neighborhoods. The river and Forest Park to the West, Downtown Portland to the South, you will be in the center of the action! St Johns boasts quaint little coffee shops, restaurants and unique shopping. There are a variety of restaurants, pubs, breweries, candy/ice cream shops, bike shops, and a convenience store within 5 blocks of the home. Just across the bridge from Portland’s iconic Forest Park with miles of single track running, hiking and mtn biking trails. The Forest Park trail system connects all the way to NW Portland and Washington Park, home of the Oregon Zoo, Portland Japanese Garden and the Rose Garden. Only 10 minute drive to Downtown and 20 minute drive to the PDX Airport. St Johns is an eclectic North Portland neighborhood with it`s own town center and rich Histor','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-36104735/original/58cc0d8f-2cef-41f9-975a-6405dfa6a742.jpeg',3142393,42,'45.593632','-122.760269',1,5,1.00,1.00,3.00,65.00,1,60,294,4.85,36104735),(1578,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36199575','Hotel Rose, Stumptown Balcony King','The illuminating lights of the Hotel Rose neon sign let you know that you’ve arrived at one of Portland’s premier hotels. Hotel Rose is a place with a funky style and colorful interior design. We live by the motto of “Keep Portland Weird” and will give you a modern accommodation and setting to do the same.<br /><br />An amenity fee with Tax ($28.94 per day) will be charged upon arrival.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ea526688-4257-433f-8d46-67d86bf8e3ad.jpg',270114277,44,'45.51743','-122.67325',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,159.00,1,28,9,4.33,36199575),(1579,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36199672','Hotel Rose, Stumptown Balcony Two Doubles','The illuminating lights of the Hotel Rose neon sign let you know that you’ve arrived at one of Portland’s premier hotels. Hotel Rose is a place with a funky style and colorful interior design. We live by the motto of “Keep Portland Weird” and will give you a modern accommodation and setting to do the same.<br /><br />An amenity fee with Tax ($28.94 per day) will be charged upon arrival.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6436e5fc-5f14-4016-b222-87c021b4a0b8.jpg',270114277,44,'45.51743','-122.67325',2,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,157.00,1,28,7,4.43,36199672),(1580,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36199745','Hotel Rose, Cityscape King','The illuminating lights of the Hotel Rose neon sign lets you know that you’ve arrived at one of Portland’s premier hotels. Hotel Rose is a place 