,'https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1cc1fdb6-c0f6-4892-9df9-8eef07bed95e.jpg',270114277,44,'45.51743','-122.67325',2,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,128.00,1,28,114,4.63,36200927),(1590,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36207629','Hip & Cozy w/ Gorgeous Private Backyard','Our well-appointed home is a comfortable and safe place to hunker down. We welcome you to enjoy our private backyard, lush with trees and hanging lights, or curl up on the couch and log into your streaming services on our 50” Roku TV. Take walks in the quiet, blooming residential neighborhood. We’re a 12 minute drive to downtown. With excellent WiFi, comfortable beds, ample parking, and a well-equipped kitchen, this is the perfect home away from home.','Just 12 minutes to downtown Portland, our home is located in a quiet, residential neighborhood full of parks and charming homes. We\'re half a mile from Mississippi Avenue, home of some of the best restaurants, bars, music venues, and shops in Portland. We\'re also just a little over a mile from the Alberta Arts District, with galleries, venues, and unique shopping and dining experiences. We\'re also half a mile from the best karaoke joint in PDX, the Alibi Tiki Lounge.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3c28c207-2dee-456b-ab2a-ce949309109d.jpg',272318368,13,'45.55673','-122.68534',1,5,1.50,2.00,2.00,180.00,2,1125,146,4.85,36207629),(1591,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36309570','Moss Rock Retreat - Near Leach Botanical Garden!','Moss Rock Retreat is a peaceful tiny home surrounded by an acre of hillside gardens. Tucked behind the magical Leach Botanical Garden in a forested neighborhood, Moss Rock has the serenity of a mountain retreat - but is only 20 minutes from downtown and PDX. Come for respite from the busy world, a quiet workspace, a creative getaway, a romantic weekend, or to explore the natural beauty of Oregon - all are possible in the comfortable intimacy of Moss Rock Retreat.','The Moss Rock Retreat neighborhood is quiet, secluded, and forested. Think semi-rural. You might hear the occasional goat or chicken. You\'ll see and hear all kinds of birds, including hawks, owls, and sometimes eagles. We are just a few blocks from Foster Avenue, but it feels like a world away. Amenities such as stores and restaurants are definitely a drive, so a car (or frequent use of Lyft or Uber) is a must, unless you\'re a pro at public transportation (the nearest stop is a .5 mile walk).<br /><br />While commercial necessities require a car, nature is right out the door. Stroll around our lush, wild garden. Take an easy walk to Leach Botanical Garden, the Foster Floodplain Natural Area (a 63-acre reclaimed floodplain), to Zenger Farm (a working urban farm), or to the Springwater Corridor Trail.  <br /><br />A 5-minute drive takes you to the Ellis Street entrance of Powell Nature Butte for great hikes and a panoramic view of the surrounding mountain ranges, or to Scouter\'s Mountain','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5fae3726-2a5f-4c84-a7bf-4ab8bdc109fa.jpg',5524096,77,'45.47315','-122.53359',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,83.00,1,31,436,4.97,36309570),(1592,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36311422','Fresh Farmhouse Remodel in SE Portland 96BikeScore','Soak up the light in this sun-filled, freshly remodeled farmhouse. Originally a Sears kit house from the 1920s, this tasteful renovation preserves its original charm while incorporating modern touches. You\'ll fall in love with the refinished original hardwood floors, quartz countertops, new appliances, and restored vintage details. Just a short walk to Hub Brewery or a few blocks over to Division St, you\'ll find an endless array of eateries and drink spots to explore!','Our charming home is nestled in the idyllic Division/Clinton district, also known as the Hosford-Abernethy neighborhood on local maps. Just four blocks away lies the historic Ladd\'s Addition, known for its beautiful rose gardens and unique diagonal street layout. While our home is situated on a bustling street, walking one block north will bring you to a serene residential area.<br /><br />You\'ll be steps away from some of Portland\'s finest restaurants, eclectic shopping, and convenient grocery stores, all within easy walking distance. Enjoy the vibrant local culture with nearby cafes, boutiques, and farmers\' markets. The area is also well-served by public transit, making it easy to explore other parts of the city. Whether you\'re looking for a quiet stroll through tree-lined streets or an evening out at a trendy eatery, our neighborhood offers the perfect blend of urban excitement and residential tranquility.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36311422/original/6e3d1618-aeef-4eab-b6ae-51c9279263da.jpeg',273076012,56,'45.4983','-122.64165',1,8,2.00,4.00,4.00,265.00,1,365,396,4.78,36311422),(1593,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36357801','Sleek Modern Studio North Portland; Sleeps 4!','Industrial-modern studio with all the amenities, including green solar energy, luxurious plush queen bed AND queen sleeper-sofa bed, full kitchen, beautiful bathroom, laundry and outdoor front patio located across from large urban park.<br />Fully stocked kitchen and bathroom for all your home away from home needs.  Relax in the tranquil modern space and soak in the cool vibes of Portland.','Trenton park is across the street;  equipped with a brand new basketball court, open field to play and swing set.  The unit is a mile away from historic downtown Kenton with popular bars, restaurants, parks, shopping, etc.  <br />Experience Portland like a local while having your morning coffee or afternoon wine, watching the kids playing at the park. And, you may also get the true local Portland experience if there is an RV or two stationed at the park across the street. Welcome to Portland!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36357801/original/88866b11-7879-4dc2-96a6-93da2a72cfd4.jpeg',6326768,55,'45.58737','-122.70342',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,105.00,1,28,262,4.97,36357801),(1594,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36429217','Sanctuary in the City','This home offers a retreat: an experience of serenity and a centered state. With it\'s features of an outdoor sauna & cold plunge, clawfoot tub & salts, in & outdoor generous space with fireplaces, and the company of air-purifying plants--working from home finally feels peaceful. It is in a quiet neighborhood only 5 miles from the center of the city and offers a place to ease and rest between local and far-away adventures. Located 1 mile or less from essentials: max, bus, groceries, coffee, etc.','A quiet established neighborhood in North Portland--a mile away from the private University of Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36429217/original/298796cb-fd1c-4f6d-8a0a-bb35021c7d5a.jpeg',16297531,51,'45.57374','-122.70191',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,199.00,30,1125,54,4.94,36429217),(1595,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36523552','Embrace urban serenity in our North Tabor oasis!','Discover the perfect blend of tranquility & accessibility in our spacious North Tabor retreat, boasting two bedrooms with private bathrooms for your ultimate convenience. Reach downtown in 15 minutes or the airport in 20 via MAX light rail! Nestled in a quiet neighborhood, but only a 5-minute walk to public transport, coffee and grocery with easy freeway access to all areas. <br /><br />I normally rent private rooms when I\'m in town so please check my other listings for rave reviews from delighted guests.','It\'s considered the \"North Tabor\" section of Portland and there are several coffee shops, restaurants, dispensaries, food carts, Trader Joe\'s and a Fred Meyer Marketplace nearby.<br /><br />FOOD CARTS, PARKS AND MORE:<br />Endless options abound! Take a 10-minute walk or quick drive and you\'ll find Rocket Empire Machine: A brand new food hall featuring Gigantic Brewing, Alleamin African Kitchen (Somalian), Tierra del Sol (Oaxacan), The Pie Spot and Sea & River Sushi. Go in the other direction for The Barley Pod: A beer garden and food cart park featuring Bull Run Pizza, La Arepa (Venezualen Street Food), Hapa (Ramen), Poblano Pepper (Mexican Food), Bam Pow (Burgers), Namu (Korean/Hawai’ian), Yaba Yabaa (Falafel), Eat Well (Vegetarian/Vegan), Flew The Coop (Fried Chicken) and The Dark Side (Thai), centered around Baerlic Brewing.<br /><br />It\'s a beautiful walk through the neighborhood to Mt. Tabor: A unique park on an extinct volcano with a 360 degree view of the area, walking trails ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36523552/original/ff57c2be-3df8-4144-8404-2f11d87d7898.jpeg',1314197,52,'45.52952','-122.59947',1,5,2.50,2.00,2.00,369.00,3,9,8,5.00,36523552),(1596,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36558877','Contemporary Studio | Patio | W/D','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-36558877/original/b4593f05-49e3-4303-82f8-50c58826db54.jpeg',111797565,27,'45.52917','-122.70198',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,155.00,1,1125,11,4.45,36558877),(1597,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36560307','Airy Studio | Private Balcony | W/D | Great locale','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-36560307/original/86c1ab67-c98c-418f-90fe-3b2f484a7525.jpeg',111797565,19,'45.543765257238995','-122.62638798509971',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,125.00,1,1125,41,4.83,36560307),(1598,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36573110','#StayInMyDistrict Multnomah Village Modern Retreat','#StayinMy District Multnomah Village & Hillsdale! Tastefully designed with modern finishes & decor. This 1 bedroom daylight basement apartment is spacious, bright and newly remodeled. Located on the lower level of the Owner\'s Home, and carefully designed with guests comfort in mind. Full Kitchen, Washer/Dryer. FREE Parking in front of space. Nestled in the trees with a cozy outdoor space. DOG friendly with additional $50 fee per pet (up to 2).','This neighborhood is convenient to I-5, OHSU, and downtown. Approx 5-7 min to the OHSU campus. Beaverton, Tigard and Washington County are on the borders and minutes from the property. The home is located in the Multnomah Village District, known for its charming small town vibe. Multnomah Village has plentiful sidewalk cafes, bakeries and bookstores, and offers casual dining options like taverns, cozy American restaurants and traditional Italian eateries. In sprawling Gabriel Park, there are sports fields, a large skatepark and picnic areas. Stores selling women’s fashions, rustic home decor and antiques cluster around Southwest Capitol Highway. The Hillsdale neighborhood is also very close to the location and features plenty of dining, shopping and nightlife.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-36573110/original/327fa9d9-55dd-465c-9144-3f836119b5c8.jpeg',3142393,17,'45.48142623901367','-122.71266174316406',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,67.00,1,28,206,4.76,36573110),(1599,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36588815','WorldMark Portland Studio Deluxe','Ideally located in the center of two vibrant communities including downtown and Old Town Chinatown - WorldMark Portland Waterfront Park is in walking distance to almost everything Portland has to offer. The original downtown area is a bustling entertainment district, home to the famous Portland Saturday Market, Voodoo Doughnut, Lan Su Chinese Garden, and the Oregon Maritime Museum. You and your family will enjoy this unforgettable urban destination for all your traveling needs.','Enjoy a little retail therapy at Pioneer Place shopping mall or find your DIY dream at Crafty Wonderland. Indie boutiques and local brands reign supreme in the downtown area. Hungry? Get creative with everything from eclectic food trucks to black-tie seafood affairs. The Portland Saturday Market is also very popular and runs the gamut with live music, food and plenty of folk art. And speaking of art, the Portland Art Museum is an absolute must for those that are into Asian and Native American art. If the art of dance is more your style, book an evening at the Keller Auditorium for ballet or a live concert. For a city that prides itself with the motto, \"Keep Portland Weird\", there is never a shortage of things to do or see!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a184a1e2-79c2-4d2b-9622-c9d43efa2f27.jpg',266083019,43,'45.5206203','-122.6712424',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,365,0,1.00,36588815),(1600,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36588887','WorldMark Portland Studio Suite','Ideally located in the center of two vibrant communities including downtown and Old Town Chinatown - WorldMark Portland Waterfront Park is in walking distance to almost everything Portland has to offer. The original downtown area is a bustling entertainment district, home to the famous Portland Saturday Market, Voodoo Doughnut, Lan Su Chinese Garden, and the Oregon Maritime Museum. You and your family will enjoy this unforgettable urban destination for all your traveling needs.','Enjoy a little retail therapy at Pioneer Place shopping mall or find your DIY dream at Crafty Wonderland. Indie boutiques and local brands reign supreme in the downtown area. Hungry? Get creative with everything from eclectic food trucks to black-tie seafood affairs. The Portland Saturday Market is also very popular and runs the gamut with live music, food and plenty of folk art. And speaking of art, the Portland Art Museum is an absolute must for those that are into Asian and Native American art. If the art of dance is more your style, book an evening at the Keller Auditorium for ballet or a live concert. For a city that prides itself with the motto, \"Keep Portland Weird\", there is never a shortage of things to do or see!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5598e16f-9460-4630-bd45-3c0fdb3a17b6.jpg',266083019,43,'45.5206203','-122.6712424',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,365,0,1.00,36588887),(1601,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36593172','Modern - Private - Cozy - Guesthouse','Newly built two story 760 sq. ft. 2bed 1bath guest house!  The perfect luxury escape. Some features include zone control heating and air conditioning. A.C. blows cold. Fully stocked kitchen with dishwasher, stove, microwave, fridge, vaulted ceilings, maple hardwood floors, TV with NETFLIX,  Comfortable queen beds in each room. Windows offer natural light and views. Quiet neighborhood. The space is a stand alone private guest house with yard. You will love it! Updated faster wifi.','Woodstock is a vibrant, hip, and conveniently located neighborhood in Southeast Portland with a bustling strip of shops, restaurants and bars. Attractions include Heart Coffee, Double Mountain Brewery, New Seasons market, Proper Pint, Cloud City Ice Cream, Red Fox Vintage and the Delta Cafe, Tom Yum Thai Cuisine, Ate oh ate, Heart Roasters, Space Monkey Coffee, Otto\'s Sausages, and The Lutz.... Woodstock is near to Reed College, Division, Hawthorne, Sellwood and East Moreland. Also close to the Mt. Scott Community Center, including a large indoor pool, and the Portland Mercado and restaurants on Foster Rd.  15-20min to downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7adb33a4-590b-46d9-8781-ebcfa8f4ff97.jpg',30323140,65,'45.47685','-122.59995',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,67.00,2,180,165,4.87,36593172),(1602,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36643611','Daylight Basement w/ patio, AC, 2 BR in SE PDX','Mt Scott, daylight basement 2 BR in SE Portland. Private entrance, 1 bath w/ VERY small shower, dorm fridge, microwave, some essentials. Main entrance from your patio enters Queen BR. Unfenced backyard for wildlife to traverse, Mt St Helens view.  Quiet, clean, wake to birds, maybe deer in yard. 15 min to downtown or airport, 1/3 mi to #12 bus line, 5 min to food carts, neighborhood restaurants. Plenty of room to stretch out & relax. We find it\'s perfect for 2 adults & 1-2 kiddos or 2-4 adults.','Quiet natural setting. The east side of the property is a \"conservation zone\", descending to a small ravine, which deer frequently use as they travel from woodland areas. Stroll the street for excellent sunset views, a glimpse of downtown Portland and Mt St Helens.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MzY2NDM2MTE%3D/original/5e47ff6d-6709-420d-884a-05d7ed6e0536.jpeg',9195404,77,'45.46684','-122.54111',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,90.00,2,5,15,4.93,36643611),(1603,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36701090','Comfort!!   King room/Downtown/pearl','This room is inside a 3 bedroom 2 bathroom apartment and is bigger than the king rooms at the Nines hotel as well as hotel sentinel which are our only two 5 star hotels in Portland!!<br /><br />This place may not be suitable for everyone, seniors or older guest may not like the location/amenities.  Close to all the nightlife and business.  This place is for travelers who want to be in proximity to everything and not have to fuss over commute.   <br /><br />Portland is a walkable city so location = convenience!','Lots or things to do explore and see while in town.  <br />- If your a city person who likes to be where the action is and mingle and have fun conversations and hang with the locals<br /><br />- looking for outdoor adventures and scenery,   <br /><br />- In town for convention, business, classes, job interview <br /> This location is what your looking for! <br /><br /> NW 13th. The heart and strip of the pearl district (which looks like an emerald city)<br /><br />NW 23 is great for the ladies who like to shop and find exclusive clothing made by shop owners.  Also just another great street to explore<br /><br />Portland State University <br /><br />The restaurants and bars/breweries are close <br /><br />The moda center <br /><br />The convention center <br /><br />Roseland theater <br /><br />All the hotels downtown so it’s like staying in the same proximity for more comfort and better price<br /><br /><br />Fields park, tanner springs park, Jamison square are a must.  To start your e','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/639d9287-2ad4-4798-a62b-ab1015554b4c.jpg',231707604,2,'45.52721','-122.68066',2,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,101,4.80,36701090),(1604,'https://www.