e line Max train. Easy access to trendy SE neighborhoods, and Universities: You’re centrally located and sure to find lots to do, very close to the apt.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-36831192/original/951b5a79-173d-4d86-897d-1524846a87c3.jpeg',36442855,20,'45.4840843321233','-122.64703273773193',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,65.00,30,1125,100,4.88,36831192),(1610,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36836282','Charming Studio Near Great Food and Shopping','Perfect Portland hideaway! Fully equipped studio apartment situated within walking distance to Belmont and Hawthorne street, these areas offer some of the best of everything Portland has to offer! Numerous funky coffee shops, locally owned restaurants, boutiques, brewpubs and clothing shops. Fifteen minute to downtown Portland, the Rose and Japanese gardens, kayaking and endless hiking trails. Less than 2 hours to the beach or Mt Hood.  Keyless entry for those late night arrivals, wifi & cable.','This is a very walkable neighborhood for nearly everything you need; great local restaurants, funky coffee shops, brewpubs, local taverns to watch the game, shoot a game of pool or play shuffleboard, boutiques, second hand clothing stores, Baghdad theater, and Wunderland nickel arcade. If your driving downtown Portland is 15 minutes away. Short distance to the Rose Gardens, Japanese Gardens, Patrick Mansion, hiking trails and water activities! Rent a kayak or for something a little more thrilling book a jet boat ride on a hot summer day!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-36836282/original/ef59c929-4dbf-46ea-afb2-f1f3bdce2956.jpeg',147708508,16,'45.51506','-122.63421',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,90.00,1,7,105,4.75,36836282),(1611,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36850421','Urban Cabin Oasis with Hot Tub and Gated Parking','**Please read entire description before requesting to book. Thanks!**<br /><br />Nestled in a bustling urban/industrial setting, among trees and greenery in it\'s own private courtyard, this cabin is truly an oasis in the middle of the city! With a delicious pizza spot and dispensary literally next door, food carts less than a block away, bars, groceries and other food within a few blocks, this quirky little cabin will be the perfect spot to launch your Portland adventure!','The neighborhood definitely has an industrial vibe, with lots of commercial properties on all sides. There is a pizza place literally next door, food carts and fast food, bars, other restaurants, grocery stores and other amenities all within a few blocks! If you don\'t like what is available in this neighborhood, or you want to switch it up, however, there are many desirable neighborhoods flanking it on almost all sides!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ab88938f-53fd-4b0d-a8c7-9f7019f29e8d.jpg',18796965,48,'45.57743','-122.66139',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,207.00,3,16,96,4.90,36850421),(1612,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36868347','Misssissippi Street District - Private Unit','Historical Mississippi St District 1909 Victorian home with large back yard, parking, and a bar and a coffee shop 1 block away.','North Mississippi Avenue features a long stretch of stores, bars and restaurants; the acclaimed eateries and bars on up-and-coming North Williams are just half a mile away.<br />https://www.travelportland.com/collection/mississippiwilliams/','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36868347/original/502a7add-3106-4466-a9dd-ee9876b51af2.jpeg',277105198,24,'45.55761','-122.6754',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,149.00,1,30,4,4.75,36868347),(1613,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36874629','Two elegant private bedrooms near Reed College','Two private bedrooms,  sleeps 4, private bathroom to share, sitting room with a  table/chairs, dishes/cups/glasses/silverware/etc.  Main bdrm: vaulted ceiling, private entrance to back porch,  microwave, coffee maker, coffee, tea, sugar, ceiling fan, central AC. Smaller bedroom: small table and two chairs, comfy double bed. Bathroom: attached to main bedroom,  10 ft. from 2nd bedroom.  Access from 2nd bdrm to 1st bdroom is 10 feet down hallway, you may cross paths w/ host in hall on occasion.','We live right between two great neighborhoods  filled with restaurants, bars, and shops: Woodstock and Sellwood/Moreland. Each one is a five minute drive from our house. We are a five-minute walk to the Reed College campus, including its lovely wooded canyon, and a ten-minute walk to the renowned Crystal Springs Rhododendron Garden and Eastmoreland Golf Course.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36874629/original/a918e197-d581-4755-95a3-ac62d94db0a4.jpeg',5341424,61,'45.48315','-122.62738',2,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,70.00,2,9,62,4.97,36874629),(1614,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36876587','2 bedroom Clinton/Division apartment','Fun Modern Renovated 2 bedroom, 1 bathroom, full kitchen, full washer and dryer, private patio, in Triplex Unit in the Clinton Division Neighborhood.<br /><br />Great walking to restaurants and public transit, quiet neighborhood.<br /><br />Close to Reed College, OHSU, Downtown','We are steps away from the Clinton Division neighborhood.  Walk to many great Portland restaurants.  Easy walk to grocery stores or other is you need anything for your stay.<br /><br />This is a great close in location for those looking for longer stays.  We are on a bike boulevard  street and close to major bus and other transit lines.  Close to OHSU, Reed College, Downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1f720c19-6688-4b2c-b5d9-542f72d60551.jpg',5237519,25,'45.49871','-122.6364',1,4,1.00,2.00,3.00,128.00,30,1125,17,5.00,36876587),(1615,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36881772','Beautiful Large Home in PRIME Location!','This stylish restored 1908 (with AC!) Portland home is the perfect fit for anyone.  It has been designed for all of your home away from home needs. The kitchen offers a gas range, full refrigerator, and a dishwasher. Backyard is completely fenced and private for only your use, grill and deck included. There is also a washer/dryer in basement and all linens and kitchen wares are provided.','This neighborhood has everything you need with in walking distance.  If you have a car it is also close to freeway access.  Easily get to the I84  or take a bus which stops at the end of the block straight downtown over the bridge.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/501d2324-bd8a-4eb8-8351-b53e9bba887e.jpg',113311649,32,'45.52228','-122.65069',1,5,2.00,2.00,4.00,201.00,1,730,319,4.89,36881772),(1616,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36941749','★ Cute 2 bedroom home in SE Portland ★ patio','Light, quiet, one-level home  that\'s perfect for relaxing stays in Portland such as summer vacations, temporary remote working and relocation. House is in a quiet, clean, safe family occupied residential street with lovely helpful and respectful neighbors. House has AC and patio and garden lovely in summer. 15-20 minute drive to downtown, under 5 minutes to the shops and restaurants of Woodstock and 10 minutes drive from Mt Tabor. PDX airport is 8 miles / about a 20 minute drive. Sorry, no pets.','The area is a quiet, safe residential neighbourhood one mile east of Woodstock and close to Mt Scott Park.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f68f4a3a-5ca5-47ae-ab96-51530a3bd0ea.jpg',254586465,69,'45.47478','-122.5914',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,150.00,31,180,0,1.00,36941749),(1617,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36948215','Belmont Getaway','Enjoy quintessential Portland, peace, and privacy just steps away from popular Belmont District, Laurelhurst Park, and so much more.  This daylight basement apartment in our 1912 home is freshly remodeled and decorated with comfort in mind, using carefully curated mid-century and modern pieces.  Fully private entrance.  Suitable for up to 4 guests (2 in private bedroom, 2 more in living room with pull-out sofa).  Ample street front parking, and public transportation less than a block away.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2c41adfe-053d-4c8b-b251-6ebe02b1e464.jpg',159041849,16,'45.51605','-122.62466',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,114.00,1,14,171,5.00,36948215),(1618,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36949309','Charming 1909 farm style home.','This attractive, 1909 farm style home is ideally located on a wide, quiet street at the foot of Mt Tabor. Abundant shopping, eating and sightseeing within walking distance plus numerous bus routes within a block or two. 10-minute walk to Mt Tabor Park with hiking trails, an off-leash dog park and beautiful views of the city.<br />Smoking allowed on porches and in garden.','Easy walk to the Hawthorne and Division business districts and just a few blocks from Mt Tabor hiking trails and dog park, plus just a half block from the popular Tabor Bread bakery.<br />Two bedrooms with Queen beds, full kitchen, smart TV, private back yard and ample street parking.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36949309/original/c40d5257-3860-4a49-9a90-f9fd95599864.jpeg',245001079,15,'45.51061','-122.60982',1,4,1.50,2.00,2.00,119.00,5,30,14,5.00,36949309),(1619,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36975799','Blue Fopo House Upstairs Bedrooms','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/06263033-fd1e-4a7f-9960-c2cfd3647918.jpg',19252862,36,'45.49588','-122.6032',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,70.00,10,1125,2,5.00,36975799),(1620,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/36977618','Spacious Basement Suite','Newly built large bedroom with queen size bed and and private bath in basement level.  Close to Woodstock, Division, Hawthorne, and Foster/Powell neighborhoods.  Easy access to public transpiration and 15 minutes from downtown.','On a residential street with plenty of free street parking.  Walking distance to the Foster Street Food Carts.  Within a mile of Woodstock and Foster street restaurants, breweries, and shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-36977618/original/cd34ace1-686b-48f2-8bf8-e0c341af9cef.jpeg',33769719,67,'45.49119','-122.61208',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,88.00,1,6,119,4.98,36977618),(1621,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37014597','Bright, Quiet,  and Private Guest House','This charming 725 sq ft guest house is very light and bright; walkable to great parks and  restaurants! The entire house is yours with private entrance and covered patio. Fast wifi, comfortable living space, and very well-equipped kitchen make this an ideal home away from home. <br />This is an LGBTQ+ welcome & safe home.<br />Black Lives Matter.<br />Accessibility: 2 steps up to the house, safety rail in tub, uneven rock path','The guest house is located in the Mt. Scott-Arleta neighborhood—a quiet, residential setting. A 15min walk gets you to the up and coming “FoPo” area with a variety of locally-owned restaurants, breweries, shops, and cafés; including great bagels, pizza with gluten-free and vegan options, and many food carts to choose from. <br /><br />Also close by is the popular Woodstock neighborhood with lots of options for restaurants, grocery, and more. Reed College and Rhododendron Gardens make for lovely nearby strolls, as well as many parks and green spaces—including gorgeous Mt. Tabor and Powell Butte. You’ll be a short drive to the hip shops and restaurants of the Division and Hawthorne districts, and very near several main arteries to easily get you around [or out of] town. <br /><br />The Mt. Scott Community Center is just 5 blocks away and offers an indoor pool and gym, as well as an amazing park for picnicking. Guests can buy a punchcard without membership.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/43b70b43-870e-4e5f-8b2d-921b27e04b76.jpg',77990596,65,'45.4826','-122.59695',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,143.00,4,60,87,4.98,37014597),(1622,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37019919','Welcome to \"The Gladstone House\"  Enjoy your stay!','SUPER CLEAN 2 bedroom 1 bath. Brand new kitchen fully stocked.  Like new HOT TUB. FREE 2 car driveway parking.  Fully fenced private backyard.  I live in attached but completely seperate A.D.U.  I enter though the big gate. Close to restaurants, bars, breweries, golf courses, parks and bike trails. The coast or Mt. Hood are 1.5 hours away. Downtown is 10 minutes away.  Multnomah Falls is a half hour away.  Hood River is 1 hour.  Airport is a little over 20 minutes away.  Busses are easy.','It is a quiet neighborhood in a cozy part of town.  Close to parks, grocery stores, restaurants, bars, hiking, biking, 1.5 hours to coast or Mt. Hood, hour to Hood River.  10 minutes downtown.  A little over 20 minutes to the airport','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/174fa5e0-d22a-43b8-a32f-83acb5b67ab4.jpg',275151873,36,'45.49271','-122.59929',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,134.00,2,28,176,4.91,37019919),(1623,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37038333','Charming Laurelhurst Courtyard Garden Studio','During these unusual times I am very conscious about keeping keeping things scrupulously clean and am taking extra precautions to ensure my visitors safety. <br /><br />This new, light-filled separate guest studio in the historic Laurelhurst neighborhood is close to Laurelhurst park, shops, restaurants, and public transit—the perfect home base for exploring the city or reconnecting with friends and family . It is adjacent to a “sister” apartment for extra guests. <br /><br />To view:<br />www.airbnb.com/rooms/7306750?','This is an amazing neighborhood to explore because it’s literally 15 minutes to walk to some of the best restaurants and shops in the city. Some favorites include Screen Door for brunch, Ava Gene’s for dinner, and Pinolo for the best gelato. Beautiful Laurelhurst Park is only a few blocks away and the bus stop, also blocks away, will take you downtown to Powell’s Book store and many other interesting shops and restaurants. The apartment is conveniently close to the freeway and the Portland airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0f548689-49f4-4e73-a5b9-08e58eecbe0e.jpg',22112041,23,'45.5203','-122.61872',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,120.00,2,730,55,4.85,37038333),(1624,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37055597','Modern Design + Heated Floors, Close In w/ Parking','Newly built 800 sq. ft. guesthouse in Portland\'s iconic West Hills. Ten minutes to downtown and near freeway access. Serene and elegant, the guesthouse is well-appointed with designer furnishings, radiant-floor heating, and three generous balconies. Open the French doors and sip your coffee overlooking lush NW evergreens. Find inspiration in our dedicated workspace with vaulted ceilings and private views. Premium appliances, cable TV w/ HBO, high-speed WiFi & thoughtful amenities.','The guesthouse is located in Portland Heights, an iconic neighborhood in Portland\'s West Hills. It\'s a quiet, residential area, with beautiful old Portland homes and incredible views. Vista Springs Cafe, one of the last-standing genuine neighborhood restaurants in Portland, is a short walk through the neighborhood (0.2 miles from the house). We\'re less than a mile from the Marquam Nature Park - its several trails and breathtaking views wind through the West Hills and connect to OHSU and Council Crest. Only ten minutes to downtown by car, we\'re even nearer to Portland\'s renowned NW Alphabet District. There you\'ll find Zupan\'s, a premium grocery store with an excellent deli, and some of the best (sales tax free!) shopping the city has to offer. We\'re centrally located for easy access to all parts of the city, including nearby freeway entrances to Beaverton (Nike\'s World Headquarters) and Hillsboro (home of Intel).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-37055597/original/b961eb82-5f9c-4e34-bfe8-5d193efe8e01.jpeg',278674051,54,'45.50656','-122.69906',1,2,1.50,1.00,2.00,314.00,3,28,71,5.00,37055597),(1625,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37097929','Stylish, Comfy & Warm Guest Suite!','Enjoy Portland while staying in our private guest suite! We are the main residents of the property, and are excited to host you in our furnished guest space while you explore the city! This guest suite is located blocks from some of the best dining destinations in Portland - Alberta Arts District, and in close proximity to Killingsworth, Williams District and Mississippi District.  Whether you are traveling for business or vacation, our private guest space has all you need to recharge and relax.','Alberta Arts District is independent and diverse - teeming with art, shopping and some of the best dining options in PDX','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7b06f2b0-c463-4e07-8ed3-18bdc65b2f3e.jpg',1618,29,'45.56291909999999','-122.6518687',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,1,365,11,4.64,37097929),(1626,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37156272','Best of Hawthorne','We are in the heart of all the fun of the Hawthorne district.  Walk to the  movie house, pizza, sushi, burgers, vegetarian and Grand Central Bakery.  Visit the legendary Mcmenamin\'s Barley Mill tavern just down the street Walk to downtown in 30 minutes or take the bus or rent a scooter or bike (right around the corner).   Parks abound and great hiking is nearby in the City at the Columbia Gorge or on Mt. Hood.  3% of every booking fee is donated to support people who are homeless','The Hawthorne neighborhood reflects the best of Portland\'s urban Renaissance.  It\'s vibrant and quirky.  Fine dining if you want or affordable and delicious  food cart pods.  Distilleries, microbreweries and plain old pubs within a 30 minute walk or 10 minute bike, scooter or bus ride.  Parks abound close by. Movies, music and great shopping.  Just a great place to walk, bike or hang out.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2c55636f-db08-4444-9597-108824e38a56.jpg',3240723,25,'45.51206','-122.64263',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,120.00,2,28,229,4.95,37156272),(1627,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37213399','Classic Portland Pearl District Condo','Centrally located, this well-equipped condominium, located in a classic brick building, was designed with comfort and luxury in mind. With stainless steel appliances, slate counter tops and wood floors, your temporary home away from home has been completely and tastefully remodeled from the ground up.<br /><br />An assigned parking space is included.<br /><br />We provide cable, high speed internet, flat screen TV and DVD player. The gourmet kitchen is fully equipped for all your cooking and baking needs.','This fantastic Northwest Portland location provides endless conveniences. The Portland Streetcar, just outside your door, will take you to downtown Portland or South Waterfront in minutes and connects you to the MAX light rail system. Forest Park, the largest natural urban forest reserve in the U.S is located nearby and invites you to come and explore 5000 acres of hiking trails. <br /><br />Spend the day here or in the Columbia Gorge, hiking, biking, or kayaking, then return home for a quick shower and you are out the door to Portland\'s nightlife. Take in the symphony or get tickets to one of Portland\'s numerous live theater performances. Cinema 21, featuring independent films is just two short blocks away. You are blocks from numerous art galleries in the Pearl District and across the street from one of Portland\'s artist \'active spaces\'.  At the end of the day, you are a short walk or ride back to your urban oasis in the middle of it all.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1eea75b1-e34c-4855-bdb6-0dbe96683857.jpg',25135442,27,'45.52927','-122.69112',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,30,1125,5,4.60,37213399),(1628,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37241754','Luxury Loft ~ Bidet, Skylight & Bed for Royalty','*We offer a 15% weekly stay discount and 20% monthly stay discount.<br />*Photos of all businesses in this listing are < 1.0 mile away.<br />*All Races, Gender Identities, Sexual Orientations, Religions Welcome.<br /><br />Our family welcomes you to a slice of our Portland life. We live in a quiet residential neighborhood where the sounds you are most likely to encounter are the distant squawks of our backyard chickens, the pitter-patter of raindrops on the skylight, or the occasional children\'s squeal or dog bark.','We are located in the Richmond Neighborhood - an area surrounded by destination restaurants (Por Que No?, Apizza Scholls, Original Stumptown Coffee, Bollywood Theatre), boutique coffee shops (Common Grounds, Albina Press), independent gyms, record and music stores, and even an arcade. We are also home to a vibrant and hip shopping district that includes Buffalo Exchange, Crossroads Trading, Powell\'s Bookstore (annex), and a host of other toy, thrift, gift,  jewelry and spiritual shops sprinkled in between. Within a mile, you can also meet your basic needs with grocery stores, pharmacies, laundromats, and a UPS store. The nearest hospital is just over 1 mile away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/05db6433-4a1f-4c53-90ff-c7b63c63945d.jpg',280375947,8,'45.50919','-122.61443',1,4,1.00,0.00,2.00,77.00,3,1125,126,5.00,37241754),(1629,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37254170','Charming Craftsman  Perfect for Long Term Stays','Live like a local in Portland style in this two-bedroom craftsman bungalow with loads of charm and character. Centrally located off Lombard with easy access to historic Kenton and St John\'s neighborhoods with parks, restaurants, shops, and cafes!','Centrally located off Lombard with easy access to historic Kenton and St John\'s neighborhoods with parks, restaurants, shops, and cafes!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/57d40620-f89f-4ed6-8eac-cae143899f60.jpg',1828909,57,'45.57771','-122.71468',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,113.00,30,730,27,4.93,37254170),(1630,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37323635','Bright & Cozy Brooklyn Apartment | Full Kitchen','Welcome to the Brooklyn Neighborhood! We are proud to offer our private basement apartment nestled in the heart of SE PDX. Inside you will find accommodations designed to help our guests recharge & prepare for a full day exploring our beautiful city. You will find a great landing point for where you want to be on your visit with close proximity to hotspots such as SE Clinton & Division St. Downtown is really accessible with light rail nearby or a 5 minute UBER.  <br /><br />We look forward to having you!','The Brooklyn neighborhood was originally named \"Brookland\" by Giddeon Tibbets due to the rivers, creeks, and lakes on his property.<br /><br />Since those days of German influence, you can still find delicious food down the street at Edel Weiss deli. Rose City Coffee is right around the block and has a delightful and talented staff of baristas ready to take your order.<br /><br />\"Today it is regarded as among southeast Portland\'s most desirable residential neighborhoods.\" - Wikipedia','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-37323635/original/4289ed26-5a40-4e7d-81ce-56d6e206742f.jpeg',64846618,56,'45.49731445','-122.64955139',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,2,365,83,4.78,37323635),(1631,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37326607','Studio 47--private entry & patio--dog allowed','Studio style master bedroom with separate entry, private bathroom, patio & dedicated parking space. Kitchenette is stocked with microwave, mini-fridge, hot plate, Keurig, and many other essentials (see photos). Spa-like oversized shower. Roku enabled TV. In-room heater, overhead fan, & window A/C unit (in summer) allow you to adjust the temperature to your comfort level. Private patio lets you to relax in PNW style. Walkable to groceries & restaurants. One dog allowed & basic amenities provided.','Located in the Woodstock neighborhood on a quiet residential street. Only one mile from Reed College and two off-leash dog parks: Brentwood and Woodstock Parks. Walk to New Seasons, Safeway, Dick\'s Primal Burger, Double Mountain Brewery, and other restaurants, coffee shops, and bars. There\'s a local Farmers Market on Sundays from June to October in the Key Bank parking lot just down the street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7159ec1c-e1b9-42a0-a4c8-3ffd56b38f93.jpg',49879856,69,'45.47466','-122.61427',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,2,28,46,4.89,37326607),(1632,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37366706','The Division District Full Private Home','A walker\'s paradise with a WalkScore® of 98/100. If you\'re a big fan of great food, craft beer, pour-over coffee and Portlandia, this is your place. Our private and spacious three-bedroom home features five beds in a historic home at the heart of the eclectic SE Division District - home to many of Portland\'s top-rated restaurants and bars, vintage shops, and some of the best people-watching around.','Talk about location! This is often referred to as Foodie row. You are a hop skip and a jump away from to two hot streets in Portland (Hawthorne and Division). There are many shops and restaurants that you can get lost in! You will even find a coffee roaster inside a double-decker bus! If vintage shopping, lifestyle boutiques, and novelty gift shops are your thing, you\'ll need a could days to work through Division.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c0c1b03f-96c7-46d5-820b-8e4a23597d40.jpg',59272527,8,'45.50397','-122.62311',1,11,2.00,3.00,5.00,115.00,1,300,431,4.87,37366706),(1633,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37425670','Alberta Arts Rejuvenated 110-year old  Apartment','Lovely, craftsman, renovated 1907 Portland home. The main floor of a 3-level house is all yours to enjoy. An earthy, rough-tiled, slate floor, leads past an up-cycled timber roof truss, into the living room, with refurbished old-growth, fir floors and authentic ax mark blemishes. Once, a nearly abandoned old house, in a tough neighborhood, it now glows with rejuvenation inside and the vibrant, eccentric, internationally-recognized , Alberta Arts neighborhood a few blocks away.','The house is located in the heart of the vibrant Alberta district. Starting 3 blocks away, there are great restaurants, many of which have been reviewed favorably in national publications, coffee houses (like Random Order named one of America\'s Best Pie Spots by Food&Wine), brew pubs, internationally recognized ice cream shop (yes, ice cream!)--Salt and Straw, shopping and live entertainment.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ee816d88-0917-4680-bcfc-fcdec2abea57.jpg',2236909,14,'45.56113','-122.65789',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,30,120,25,4.84,37425670),(1634,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37430089','North Portland: Light-Filled Garden Contemporary','A quiet light-filled one-bedroom with full kitchen, bath and courtyard located in the Arbor Lodge neighborhood of close-in North Portland. Just a 10-15 minute drive to downtown and surrounding neighborhoods with popular eateries and shopping. Walker/Runner? Bring your shoes as we\'re a block off the bluff on Willamette Blvd. Enjoy the view of the city and on a clear day, you\'ll see Mt. Hood.  AC/Heat, wifi and a full kitchen. Green Zebra grocery and a few restaurants are within a 5-10 min walk.','Arbor Lodge is a quiet family-friendly neighborhood that is close to many things which makes it easy to get around the city.  We are 10-15 minute drive to downtown, Northwest 23rd, Pearl,  Mississippi/Williams, Alberta, St Johns. And, about 20 mins to Sauvies Island or the airport. U of P and the North America Adidas Campus is about a mile away. Public transportation is easy to get to either by bus or MAX. <br /><br />You can walk to grocery stores, the closest one being Green Zebra and a few restaurants such as King Burrito or Tuk Tuk (Thai restaurant). Take a longer walk towards Killingsworth and there you\'ll find Mio Sushi, Backyard Social, Atomic Pizza, Milk, Old Gold to name a few.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/abbcf4d5-cb7c-4c84-b9ea-3429d5beb7ca.jpg',282238879,51,'45.57122','-122.69863',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,5,1125,51,5.00,37430089),(1635,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37433452','Woodstock Family Home','Perfect when the extended family is traveling together. <br /><br />A 4-bedroom home to include a basement mother-in-law apartment providing privacy with a bedroom, living room, kitchen, and bathroom. <br /><br />Super bright, spacious house for a wonderfully relaxing stay in one of Portland’s best neighborhoods.','Our house is located in the Woodstock neighborhood about a five minute walk from Reed College. We have numerous restaurants, coffee shops, grocery stores within walking distance. We live one block away from two bus lines that will take you to downtown Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1bcecfbc-5119-4de1-b9ab-1d21bb6c1d75.jpg',3983058,38,'45.47903','-122.62237',1,9,3.50,4.00,4.00,216.00,1,30,39,5.00,37433452),(1636,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37457146','Fun 1 br+ HOUSE! Yard, Pets, Near Food/Bars/Park!','MOON HOUSE! A Private Portland 1 bedroom, small 1920\'s House with Yard. Close to Peninsula Park Rose Garden & near Mississippi, Williams and Alberta Districts. Walk to restaurants, food carts and bars. 10 min drive Downtown. Onsite W/D, big TV, full kitchen with gas range, WiFi. Driveway parking spot. Basement for your storage needs. Lovely front garden. Key pad entry after 3 pm, check out before 11 AM. Across from Polaris Hall and PCC. Eclectic and classic Portland!','Head to the Coffeehouse Five on Killingsworth to start your day, or in the other direction to Sweedeedee on Albina. Continue on and you\'ll find Prost!, a German beer hall and Portland\'s best food carts where Mississippi St begins. Bars, food, shopping, beer and lightbulbs (make sure to visit Sunlan lighting) all await you on Mississippi. <br /><br />Don\'t miss the Historic Peninsula Rose Garden on the opposite side of PCC! It is super close and a lovely place for a picnic or jog. Atlas pizza is a block away for your pizza and beer (or last minute dinner) needs. Solabee has all your houseplant and/or floral needs covered. Thai food, Pho, gyros, Mexican, burgers and Ethiopian-- all a block away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-37457146/original/c1c26aa4-2dd8-4c95-a703-6c170dab8847.jpeg',282537740,24,'45.56263','-122.67476',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,117.00,4,1125,65,4.94,37457146),(1637,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37508779','Dreamer #9–Just Steps from the Max','Our home is just a few years old, newer construction features two bedrooms and two bathrooms. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and a beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week. The local park has new playground and splash pad.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/496937c6-1734-4d35-af4f-db05074c45d7.jpg',6692974,55,'45.58296','-122.68431',1,6,2.00,2.00,2.00,165.00,30,1125,1,5.00,37508779),(1638,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37509421','Artist #5–Just Steps from the Max','Our home is just a few years old, newer construction features one bedroom and one bathroom. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and a beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week. The local park has a new playground and splash pad.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-37509421/original/a30d73d4-1feb-4483-af9a-95218eea7132.jpeg',6692974,55,'45.58335','-122.68241',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,104.00,30,1125,15,4.73,37509421),(1639,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37509738','Entertainer #4–Just Steps from the Max','Our home is just a few year old, newer construction features two bedrooms and two bathrooms. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/b1e04bd5-9008-46f5-93be-631700b7589e.jpg',6692974,55,'45.58499','-122.68456',1,6,2.00,2.00,2.00,124.00,30,1125,29,4.97,37509738),(1640,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37565004','Modern 4BR home in trendy Portland neighborhood','A walker\'s paradise with a WalkScore® of 92/100. If you\'re a big fan of great food, craft beer, pour-over coffee, etc. this is your place. Our fun home sits at the heart of the eclectic NE Alberta District - home to many of Portland\'s top-rated restaurants and bars, vintage shops, and some of the best people-watching around. With a convenient home base within walking distance to the neighborhood hot spots, you can get an authentic taste of how the hipsters live in Stumptown. No parties allowed!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/610b4782-0eef-4d53-8fd0-0c9137f804cc.jpg',283783090,14,'45.56217','-122.6631',1,11,2.50,4.00,6.00,142.00,1,1125,405,4.82,37565004),(1641,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37593569','1913 Bungalow in the Heart of Roseway','Our 1913 bungalow features a large front porch, newly updated kitchen, clean and modern decor, hardwood floors and lots of natural light! There is a beautiful little side deck surrounded by trees that makes a perfect spot for your morning coffee. The large, fenced backyard is perfect for dogs. We are located just 5 minutes from the airport in a walkable neighborhood with cafes, restaurants and a grocery store within a couple blocks. Please note this is a home, not solely an Airbnb rental.','The Roseway neighborhood is located just above the Rose City golf course and park, and walks along this path provide great views of Mt. Hood and towering Douglas firs. Within walking distance there are cafes (Kainos and Fresh Love are favorites), artisan pizza at Otto\'s, a great resale shop (Rerun) and a local Safeway for groceries. The Beaumont neighborhood with more bars and restaurants is a short drive or a walk up Fremont Street. Downtown is about a 15-20 minute drive.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-37593569/original/3fbe90ed-78d4-4078-b19f-37d554dc2c6f.jpeg',17054337,11,'45.53575','-122.6048',1,5,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,7,42,4.95,37593569),(1642,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37617910','★Spacious St Johns Hideout★Food/Bars, Shops, Parks','No Cleaning Fee! You\'ll have the privacy of your own floor in this roomy, bright finished basement apartment of our 1913 craftsman home in North Portland. <br /><br />We are located on a quiet street just a few blocks walk to many activities and eats around the funky St. Johns neighborhood. A lovely getaway for couples, singles, friends or families!<br /><br />Landmarks:<br />PDX Airport: 11 mi<br />City Center: 8 mi<br />Forest Park Ridge Trailhead : 1.3 mi<br />University of Portland: 2 mi','Walk to restaurants, shopping, movie theaters, bars and parks:<br />*Beautiful, relaxing Cathedral Park<br />*St. Johns Beer Porch with local taps and food carts pod<br />*West Coast Fitness gym with daily rates for walk-ins (4 blocks)<br />*St. Johns Twin Cinema<br />*Tienda Santa Cruz-Mexican restaurant and grocery<br />*Occidental Brewing, unique local German microbrewery<br />*Gabagool Italian (2 blocks)<br />*StormBreaker Brewing gastropub (5 blocks)<br />*McMenamin\'s St. Johns Theater & Pub<br />*Saturday Farmer\'s Market with lots of local produce and eats (May 18th through October 26th)<br />*Laundromat available (4 blocks)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-37617910/original/c69c1d1e-a29a-4cc5-b556-7861979ad829.jpeg',65785806,58,'45.58868','-122.74687',1,4,1.00,1.00,3.00,91.00,2,8,166,4.93,37617910),(1643,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37660495','Hotel Style Studio Apartment - #P','Newly constructed modern townhouse. Located in the Overlook neighborhood in North Portland. Ground floor suite with its own entrance and is separate from the main house. Full bath. Fantastic location. Easy access to the Airport, Public Transport, Light rail, Convention Center, restaurants etc. Close to N. Mississippi, Alberta, I-5, Overlook. This space was designed to be a like a hotel suite, with kitchenette; mini fridge, two burner cooktop, toaster oven. There is ample and safe street parking.','You are in the Overlook Neighborhood in North Portland.<br />Street parking is safe and hopefully plentiful.<br /><br />There is a Plaid Pantry convenience store across N Interstate for your convenience.<br /><br />If you want to buy hard liquor the closest place is called North by Northeast, 4375 N Williams Ave, Portland, OR 97217<br />There is a dispensary nearby called Green Sky.<br /><br />Here are few food recommendations if you have the time.<br /><br />A bagel place two blocks away, Eisenhower Bagels. <br />The Alibi Room is down the street and is a fun old school Tiki Bar and Karaoke.<br />Broder Nord, also a great hip breakfast place. <br />Tilt is down on Swan Island if you want giant burgers and fries.<br />There is a whole strip of bars, food carts and restaurants along N Mississippi Ave: Por Que No tacos, is great. Gravy is great for large breakfasts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/017ff6ed-7cd3-4829-9fa6-583744c3f146.jpg',121088523,13,'45.55736','-122.68183',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,82.00,30,180,19,4.63,37660495),(1644,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37660891','Private Bed and Bath in Roseway!','Your quiet bedroom and private bath is a 10 minute drive from the airport and downtown, close to public transportation, and fully stocked with all the necessities. There are plenty of places nearby to relax and eat, grab groceries, or just explore.','Primarily consisting of single-family homes with mature tree lines, the Roseway neighborhood makes for a peaceful getaway from the city. Nearby is the Rose City Golf Course, Kainos Coffee, plenty of pho, and more with easy access to Highways I-84 and I-205.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/15707612-8ae1-4c11-8a66-dcec53373b4d.jpg',21967638,39,'45.55089','-122.59387',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,1,18,98,4.98,37660891),(1645,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37693150','Multnomah Village Getaway','Come and stay right in the heart of one of Portland’s best neighborhoods - Multnomah Village! Enjoy a private studio right within walking distance of all the food trucks, restaurants, and shops the Village has to offer. We are conveniently located 5 miles from downtown and a short drive to the Zoo/OHSU. After exploring and eating your way through Portland make your way back to our newly renovated digs for free parking and a great night\'s sleep on a Casper mattress.','Multnomah Village is known for being Portland\'s best kept secret and it is as quaint and quirky as they come! Our space is within walking distance to all the restaurants, coffee shops, food trucks, and shops that the Village has to offer. You have to try Fat City\'s cinnamon roll french toast, Tastebud pizza has delicious wood fired pizza and the best Kale  Ceasar salad, and Yoshi\'s sushi is our favorite spot at the French Quarter. We have great trails, swimming, and tennis/basketball courts right around the corner at Gabriel Park. We are also  near the bus line and it\'s a quick trip to downtown, OHSU, and the Oregon Zoo. The village is cute, quirky, and safe. We love our neighborhood and are excited to show it off to you!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8c55dc6b-f6d4-4964-812e-6c74741f92f1.jpg',48377732,18,'45.46897','-122.71615',1,4,1.00,0.00,4.00,90.00,2,30,73,4.89,37693150),(1646,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37770353','Bright, Cozy Apt in Heart of North Portland','Newly built basement apartment with plenty of light in the heart of North Portland. Only a 5 min walk to 2 grocery stores and the Interstate MAX train for easy access to anywhere in Portland. Close to Kenton, Mississippi, and Dekum neighborhoods for plenty of bars, restaurants, food carts, and more!','Super easy access to the MAX line. This will take you to downtown, the Expo Center, the Moda Center, other MAX line connections, pretty much anywhere you want to go. Within walking distance there are 2 grocery stores, a great coffee shop, a few bars, a brewery, pizza, thai, and a cinnamon roll shop! For a quick bike ride, few dollar Lyft, or couple minute MAX ride the world is your oyster- super popular Mississippi neighborhood, Kenton, Dekum St., and N. Williams offer all kinds of cool bars, shops, eateries, historic neighborhood walks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/336be6ba-e6e3-4e37-8660-4ef6c7fac814.jpg',4135090,51,'45.57280349731445','-122.67955017089844',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,2,365,55,4.96,37770353),(1647,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37802604','Brand New, Open, Modern and Pet Friendly','Beautiful, brand new, completely private and separate house. Modern, clean, light-filled. Pet-friendly, private fenced yard. Climate controlled with central heat and air conditioning, laundry inside the house, a full kitchen including a dishwasher and gas range. Upstairs, a bonus sleeping loft includes a queen bed and can double as a den and/or workspace as needed. The yard is fully fenced and completely separate and private.','Arbor Lodge is a fantastic residential Portland neighborhood. Walk to two parks, restaurants, grocery stores, the bus and the Max. Easy commute to downtown Portland and Vancouver.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3513b223-a2cc-4792-9309-5fd5cdb6e88b.jpg',36909902,51,'45.57481','-122.68918',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,90.00,30,1125,4,5.00,37802604),(1648,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37870442','Cheerful 4 bedroom house with gym access','Relax with the whole family at this peaceful place to stay.<br />This listing is for short term rentals for a minimum of one (1) month.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-37870442/original/bf3f6382-a7db-4754-a014-2d5a7b5a36fd.jpeg',182183418,73,'45.44032','-122.70787',1,6,2.50,4.00,4.00,152.00,30,1125,3,5.00,37870442),(1649,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37880229','Two bedroom condo with a fully stocked kitchen!','No extra cleaning fee and flexible check-in/out time!<br /><br />Recently remodeled two bedroom condo. Well stocked kitchen, ready for you to make great meals! A washer in the unit and a dryer on site.<br /><br />For sleeping arrangements, a queen sized bed, trundle bed that can be either two twin beds or used as a king. The couch in the living room also folds out into a comfy full sized sleeper as well! Plenty of pillows, blankets and everything else.<br /><br />Dedicated parking spot as well as guest spots available.','Lake Oswego has a beautiful downtown area and you will be a short drive to Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1dab5d9c-9c51-4079-a023-647193bf05e6.jpg',19350780,73,'45.43725','-122.70818',1,3,1.00,2.00,4.00,72.00,30,130,19,4.84,37880229),(1650,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37904834','Three Wishes Studio','Three Wishes Studio is steps away from the heart of Southeast Division street, one of Portland\'s most vibrant neighborhoods.   This newly constructed studio apartment is full of amenities and designed with a modern aesthetic.  Located on a quiet side street with a private ground floor entry, Three Wishes is the perfect escape for couples or a small family.','World class dining and unique boutiques line Division street in a walkable setting that is easily connected to downtown via the 2 bus (located two blocks away.). Try BIKETOWN bikeshare for a tour of the Richmond and Hawthorne neighborhoods or stroll two blocks to restaurants including Ava Gene\'s, Pok Pok, Little Beast Brewery or Salt and Straw ice cream.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5fec8e45-2348-4dd7-8328-e2eca1e08f4e.jpg',285663945,8,'45.50523','-122.63024',1,3,1.00,0.00,2.00,109.00,2,30,147,4.88,37904834),(1651,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37918192','Artist\'s Urban Jungle Loft SE Portland (apartment)','This studio apartment stands where our garage used to be and is completely separate from our home, but there is one shared wall. The skylights offer neighborhood and sunrise views, plus lots of bright natural light.','I love our neighborhood! We\'re close to Clinton Park and Mt. Tabor, and there are several good coffee shops and restaurants/food carts around too,  just a quick hop over to Division and Hawthorne neighborhoods and attractions.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-37918192/original/26157d48-a236-462a-b697-6fefd2d6e7e8.jpeg',4484796,37,'45.49893','-122.60403',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,61.00,1,10,192,4.94,37918192),(1652,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37919008','Spacious and Bright Daylight Basement Apartment','Spacious 2-bedroom daylight basement apartment with great natural light and a private entrance. Ideal for guests who’d like to stay in a residential area with easy access to downtown Portland via public transit or car. Located in the Historic Kenton neighborhood of N. Portland, with public transit (MAX or bus), restaurants, coffee shops, and parks within easy walking distance.','Kenton is a historic neighborhood north of downtown Portland. A statue of Paul Bunyan stands at the front of our neighborhood. Posie\'s is a great coffee shop and has breakfast and lunch. Swift & Union and Fino are among a number of fine dinner spots in the neighborhood (with happy hours from 4pm-6pm).','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/89adc021-d199-4bfe-aa07-e773e7c6bc66.jpg',87625287,55,'45.58106','-122.69228',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,65.00,2,31,83,4.84,37919008),(1653,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37937007','Hawthorne - a block or 2 to just about everything!','Ask about longer stays Oct 2024 - Feb 2025.<br /><br />Awesome location - 1 block to Hawthorne, quick walk to Division. Food carts, outdoor patio bars, coffee shops, used clothing/records. The Bagdad, Salt & Straw, Por Que No - it\'s all here! Easily e-bike/e-scooter, bus or Uber to explore more of Portland!<br /><br />Cottage with patio garden.  Our walkable neighborhood is quiet & peaceful.<br /><br />Host lives onsite, downstairs in a separate living space.  Backyard is for host only.','Vibrant, hip , alternative, foodie culture.  Yep, that\'s the Hawthorne and Division Street vibe.  Families, good neighbors, community gardens - that\'s also Hawthorne.  It\'s a real neighborhood with people who live here and have a strong sense of community.  We like to go to the same food carts, bars, shops that you have been hearing about.  We live here for a reason - to live in one of the coolest neighborhoods in Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-37937007/original/adacdfa6-e3f7-4d9c-b89e-729a570b7ab2.jpeg',22122683,8,'45.50885','-122.62735',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,3,90,73,4.95,37937007),(1654,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37946533','Detached Private  - Spacious Bright Guesthouse','Gladstone Guesthouse is located in a neighborhood called the Foster-Powell area of South East Portland and 1 block from Kern Park.  Close to grocery stores, restaurants, I205 entrance mins away, downtown and airport are 15 mins in either direction.  Please don’t hesitate to ask for deals and discounts on long term stays.','Welcome to the FoPo neighborhood of Portland!  With a walking score of 76 this area has 2 parks, grocery stores, diverse choice of restaurants and food carts.  The Portland Mercando is within 15 minutes walking distance, offering Latin American food carts and a grocery store as well as a bar with indoor seating.  Just a block from there is a another food cart pod.   Kern park is just down the street and Essex park is a 9 minute walk away from the guesthouse.  Should you need to pick up a few amenities, we are less than a 4 minute car ride from stores like Winco Foods, SF Asian Supermarket, Walgreens and Wal-Mart.  Another 10 minute car ride away is Trader Joe’s, Fred Meyer’s and Whole Foods.<br /><br />The neighborhood is a great mix of family homes and conveniences.   The Foster-Powell neighborhood is full of a mix of different restaurants such as Korean, Vietnamese, Chinese, Middle Eastern, Indian, Mexican, etc. One of our favorite spots is off the Griddle which is great for not just','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/31d4bcd1-f7fd-4507-af52-82699be354d2.jpg',4139334,36,'45.49265','-122.5908',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,140.00,2,360,34,4.82,37946533),(1655,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37969468','Beautiful Updated Quiet Condo with Parking Stall!','This condo is located in one of the most desirable neighborhoods in Portland—Goose Hallow! With a 96 walk score, you’re a few minute walk to the Max/bus station, Providence Park, Washington Park, and the NW Alphabet district. Get the convenience of city living with the quiet comfort of a neighborhood. <br /><br />With \"all inclusive\" internet, electric, water, heat, private off-street parking, in-unit washer/dryer, walk-in closet, black-out shades, and fully stocked kitchen/bar equipment!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/224abce6-deb2-47e4-8e8c-82d68cc07b34.jpg',152882319,3,'45.51861','-122.69347',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,180,1125,3,5.00,37969468),(1656,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/37976543','Psychedelic Mandala Room at the Bold Bungalow PDX','Magical, spacious, mandala-filled room with king bed, desk, antique vanity, hardwood floor, space for yoga, meditation, relaxing, reading, and enjoying the hand-painted psychedelia on walls and ceiling. Enjoy the glow-in-the-dark and UV-reactive accents! <br /><br />Our unique art home has been featured on Atlas Obscura Experiences, Portland Weird Homes Tour, Weird Portland United, HGTV\'s \"Look What I Did!\" & \"That\'s Clever!\", KGW-TV (Portland), KING-5 Evening (Seattle).','We are located in Southeast Portland, in the Mt. Scott-Arleta neighborhood.<br /><br />The house is a short walk from lovely Mt. Scott Park. We are close to up-and-coming SE Foster Road, the Lents neighborhood, and the Woodstock neighborhood. <br /><br />We\'re just a few blocks from Shango cannabis dispensary, Lion\'s Eye Tavern, Joy Teriyaki, Cha Lua Deli, Portland Mercado, and so much more.<br /><br />We are conveniently located near many transportation options, parks, restaurants, and shops, as you\'ll see in the Guidebook.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-37976543/original/9a032a00-cb17-44e2-a0e3-88d6ccb73724.jpg',220757080,65,'45.48017','-122.58085',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,2,7,1,5.00,37976543),(1657,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38019727','Chill SE House','SE House for M-to-M Renter!  Our housemates are often Nurses, Students or Grads with jobs. We\'re friendly and welcome anyone who\'s respectful, tidy and responsible. We\'re all Covid conscious and vaccinated, no masks necessary at home though. We all come home to relax and chill.<br /><br />AMENITIES: There is fast internet (1000mbps), 2nd fridge in the garage,  (microwave, keurig, toaster, crockpot, instant pot, kitchen-aid, etc), workout equipment, street parking, a 110in. projector screen!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-38019727/original/1f2b5fbe-5df4-4224-8283-b9ee54227708.jpeg',12993408,69,'45.47453241375086','-122.58901664973756',2,1,1.50,1.00,1.00,34.00,30,180,0,1.00,38019727),(1658,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38027305','The Pasadena House, Private home minutes from pdx!','Quiet and private single-family  home tucked away just over ten minutes from downtown Portland, with convenient freeway access to all of Portland, and the many fun activities available to the Pacific Northwest.  The Pasadena House is a serene home for your family to relax in, located in the best spot to be your hub to all that Portland offers. Why cram into a hotel room when you and your family can enjoy a home. We hope you love the Pasadena House as much as we so and look forward to your stay!','The neighborhood the Pasadena House resides in is a family oriented area,  there is a great park within walking distance, and multiple options for more parks, entertainment, grocery and shopping all within 3-15 minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-38027305/original/8c60283e-ab8c-43c8-b28c-2ba1da273d03.jpeg',288537764,68,'45.44525','-122.73472',1,6,2.00,3.00,3.00,155.00,30,1112,13,4.92,38027305),(1659,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38131490','Precious Dash Space- 4 guests, 2bdrm, private bath','Life is short and people put get stuck in their routines .All to often they postpone things and forget to enjoy lifes journey. Using the excuse there\'s never enough time or money. <br />When it\'s all said and done life is basically a dash between when you\'re born and when you\'re gone. Some Dashes are long and others are short .<br /> Make your dash meaningful... <br />Drop everything, including your bags and go out and enjoy your life.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-38131490/original/6597e149-8884-456b-9877-71c51e3e33d1.jpeg',209826108,14,'45.56445','-122.6611',2,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,50.00,1,14,453,4.74,38131490),(1660,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38137124','SE Portland  private studio near Division','The remodeled 330 square studio is modern, colorful and boasts comfort with all the essentials - your home away from home.  Enjoy the open concept studio apartment, just a short stroll to SE Division’s trendiest restaurants, coffee shops, bars, and boutiques. You’ll feel right at home with a full kitchen, private entrance and patio, comfy queen bed with luxurious bedding, WiFi, smart TV, original artwork, plants, and deluxe towels.','Located in Portland’s South East Richmond neighborhood, we’re 4 blocks from SE Division, which has many restaurants, wine bars, brew pubs, and coffee shops. There\'s always a new spot sprouting up on SE Division - Salt and Straw ice cream, Bollywood Indian, Little Beast Brewing or SE Wine Collective.  Let\'s just say you won\'t be without great food or drink. <br /><br />Our quiet neighborhood retreat allows you to explore Portland all day, but retreat back in for the night.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/deb8ef5b-0bdb-440a-831d-91a6ee219a50.jpg',27703529,8,'45.49973','-122.62764',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,84.00,4,29,180,4.99,38137124),(1661,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38183354','The Kenton- The perfect Boutique Hotel','The Kenton is a customer forward boutique hotel that lends itself to the technology savvy world we live in without losing the person to person interaction we so desperately long for. With deep roots in the Kenton community, we have rejuvenated this 1962 era property into an Instagram worthy must see and stay destination. With over 5300sqft. of sleeping quarters, our redesigned hotel offers 18 unique Oregon themed murals designed by locally known artists.','We are located in the historic Kenton neighborhood surrounded by trendy restaurants and bars only a few steps away. Want to visit the Waterfront and Downtown? Simply jump on the MAX which stops in front of our hotel and enjoy the best of Portland!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6538b022-270c-4d8d-af5e-ef9a0eb502e3.jpg',290147674,55,'45.58241','-122.68425',2,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,4,4.00,38183354),(1662,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38188608','The Concordia Retreat','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/900f0676-2e1f-47ee-8c76-8edc4aa1b8ce.jpg',274097987,1,'45.56455','-122.63924',2,3,1.00,1.00,3.00,70.00,1,14,286,4.94,38188608),(1663,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38195185','WanderLuxe, Luxury+ Location +Walk to Food & Parks','WanderLuxe is a new, chic, guesthouse custom designed and built with you in mind. Want for nothing as you explore Portland with ease from your conveniently located home base. Walk a block to Wilshire Park for a picnic or a jog, catch a movie at McMenamins Kennedy School, eat at one of the dozens of neighborhood restaurants, or be just about anywhere in Portland in 15 minutes by car. <br /><br />Perfect for a romantic getaway, work trip, girls/guys trip, or just some much needed alone time.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/03f91cc4-66d3-4876-ac53-b87f56cda0e0.jpg',52253283,46,'45.55572','-122.62922',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,165.00,3,1125,88,4.98,38195185),(1664,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38262484','Small luxury studio apartment in the heart of FoPo','Luxurious, newly remodeled studio apartment in the heart of the Foster-Powell neighborhood.  Complete remodel in 2019 including king-sized latex memory foam bed, quiet heat/ac, beautiful kitchen with new custom ceramic counters, in-cabinet lighting, Miele dishwasher and touchless sink faucet.  Apartment is right on Foster Rd. within footsteps of great restaurants, bars, & a small grocery store.','The Foster-Powell neighborhood within walking distance of this apartment retains \"old-Portland\" charm, but has recently been undergoing a Renaissance.   The changes include a new brewpub, small boutique grocery store, 4 great pizza places, the Portland Mercado (which has great Latin-American inspired food carts), and others.  There are vegetarian/vegan dining options close by (within a short walk).   Of course, if learning to dance Argentine Tango has always been on you to-do list, you are adjacent to the famous Argentine Tango studio, Tango Berretin, which hosts frequent tango lessons and dances.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/77fbbd1b-64d1-4e6f-8c1e-088e10f965e0.jpg',83532914,36,'45.49079','-122.59747',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,31,60,10,5.00,38262484),(1665,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38263711','Cozy Piedmont Bungalow near Alberta, Mississippi','Location is ideal for all activities in Portland. A few blocks East to historic Woodlawn triangle with coffee, brews, food and dispensaries; a few blocks west to Peninsula Park and its lovely rose garden. Close to bus stops and MLK blvd. 10 minutes drive to airport and downtown. Close to Alberta and Mississippi districts.','Piedmont and Woodlawn neighborhoods are a beautiful part of historic North/Northeast Portland. Bus, walk and bike friendly along with Alberta, Mississippi and greater North/NE Portland. Peninsula park Rose garden is what made me fall in love with this neighborhood and then beautiful Woodlawn, Farragut and Alberta parks, all within a one mile radius. Within blocks are local food and drinks including a local favorite..Breakside Brewery and Oregon Public House non profit brew pub.<br />There is a Retrogame bar a few blocks from my house on MLK and Dekum, where you can play video games and have drinks; and the High Water Mark punk bar with good burgers and vegan options. Gram Central Station dispensary within few minutes walk, two coffee shops and grocery stores.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/65f88aea-f180-465f-963f-e49da81a60ec.jpg',25370041,48,'45.57169','-122.66478',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,50.00,1,4,71,4.86,38263711),(1666,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38264102','Light-filled Craftsman in trendy neighborhood','Come and enjoy my adorable 1913 Craftsman Bungalow. Nestled in a quiet, tree-lined street in historic Southeast Portland, this is the perfect place to experience the quaint neighborhoods of Portland. Perfectly set up for remote working with an office and adjustable standing desk, walking distance to some of Portland\'s best restaurants on Hawthorne and Division, and a 10 minute walk to gorgeous Mt Tabor Park. You will have the entire place to yourself to make it your home away from home.','Southeast Portland is one of the classic local neighborhoods of Portland. For dining out, some popular favorites within a short walk are Tasty and Daughters, Apizza Scholls, Porque No for delicious street tacos, and Tabor Bread for artisan breads. If you\'re a coffee connoisseur, you\'re in the right place. All within a short walk are Albina Press, the original Stumptown Coffee location, and Good Coffee. <br />Mt Tabor is a gorgeous park built on a dormant volcano with spectacular views of the city. It\'s a great spot for a picnic overlooking one of the reservoirs, or a hill run or ride amongst the Douglas Firs that cover the hill. <br />Venturing out a little further, you can be hiking in the forest in 15 minutes, carving it up in the snow on Mt Hood in 90 minutes, enjoying the wind-centric water sports in the Columbia River Gorge near Hood River in 60 minutes, or taking in Oregon\'s rugged coastline in 90 minutes.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/22067741-e998-49c2-98d2-404c97c51741.jpg',56432819,8,'45.50963','-122.61359',1,4,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,2,1125,56,4.95,38264102),(1667,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38292968','Art-filled Townhouse steps from NW 23rd Avenue','You\'ll love this modern 2-story townhouse on a residential street close to trendy NW 23rd/21st Avenues. Easy walk to cafés, restaurants, and organic groceries. Car/bus to Powell\'s Bookstore, Portland Art Museum, Forest Park, Japanese Garden. The Columbia Gorge & Willamette Valley wineries are 1 hour away. After an adventurous day, come home to a fully-equipped kitchen, room to relax, cook, or stream a movie. Two comfy bedrooms, each with private bath, truly make this a home away from home.','Private setting, five star walkability, tree-filled neighborhood!  Forest Park, with miles of hiking trails, is 1 mile away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-38292968/original/bac739bf-47de-43a3-bba9-342c573d0cf9.jpeg',7409866,27,'45.53497','-122.70147',1,4,2.50,2.00,2.00,170.00,1,60,65,4.97,38292968),(1668,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38299327','Su Casa','Su casa is a festive and cozy studio in a quiet residential neighborhood. The space has a full kitchen stocked with essentials. The bathroom is stocked with eco-friendly versions all your basic needs. Bring your Hulu, Amazon and Netflix passwords to watch your favorite shows. The space includes access to our large fenced backyard,  outfitted with a fire pit, BBQ, and outdoor games (cornhole and giant jenga) with plenty of seating (covered) to enjoy all four seasons in Portland\'s mild climate.','Dekum triangle, Alberta Arts District, N Williams Street, Mississippi District','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3e40ec3f-c920-4570-973e-465d89b52d53.jpg',150316808,48,'45.57055','-122.66597',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,11,5.00,38299327),(1669,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38319354','New, Private Guesthouse in Excellent Location','Enjoy this brand new, open, bright space! Sleep soundly in the queen bed, or on the sofa bed if you need the extra space. Full kitchen is ready for anything from prepping some of Portland\'s finest coffee to making dinner for your whole party (or maybe just heating up some of your leftovers from a delicious spot in the city!) Located less than a mile from Alberta St, Williams Ave, or Mississippi Ave - you\'ll always be close to the action! Enjoy NE Portland like a local!','Quiet, authentic NE Portland neighborhood. Enjoy walking to our favorite bakeshop, Bushel & Peck, or venture a few blocks further to explore some of the main NE business districts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a108ea35-2436-49c5-b86e-e9a40a6fae4a.jpg',2574467,14,'45.55087','-122.65835',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,87.00,3,21,139,4.91,38319354),(1670,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38319691','Dreamer #3-Just Steps from the Max (No Stairs)','Our home is just a few years old, newer construction features 2 bedrooms and 2 bathrooms. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week. Our neighborhood park is only a couple blocks away and has a new play structure and splash pad.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6b86911b-e39c-4db5-b789-6897a5f14d3f.jpg',6692974,55,'45.58299','-122.68408',1,6,2.00,2.00,2.00,137.00,30,1125,58,4.86,38319691),(1671,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38362548','Charming craftsman style Montavilla private suite','Located in SE Portland\'s East Tabor/Montavilla neighborhood, this Airbnb puts you 3 blocks from several delicious restaurants/bars, boutique shopping and a historic movie theater. OHSU, Portland State, Downtown, Pearl District and 23rd Avenue are all within a 15 minute drive. This spacious suite includes a private entrance, full kitchen, WiFi, air conditioning, a washer/dryer and a TV with Hulu, Disney and ESPN. For guests with a vehicle, there is also plenty of free street parking.','From several delicious restaurants to local breweries and bottle shops there\'s no shortage of great places to walk to. Whether you\'re into shopping at the boutique stores, catching a classic movie in the historic theater or walking up to Mt. Tabor Park to have a picnic while watching the sunset behind the downtown cityscape there\'s something for everyone in this neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d8cfdef1-726c-460a-a582-f0097a959157.jpg',2884284,10,'45.51773','-122.57742',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,105.00,30,730,170,4.96,38362548),(1672,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38385952','Central & spacious vintage flat','The Sunnyside Neighborhood is one of Portlands best.  Located in the center of all that is great about SE Portland, the Belmont/Hawthorne District has been compared to San Franciscos Haight Ashbury District with its many independently owned bars, restaurants, cafes and shops all nestled among Victorian and roaring 20s architecture.  Sunnyside is bordered by the Laurelhurst, Richmond, Buckman, Kerns, and Mt Tabor neighborhoods. Nature walks and the I5 are a stones throw away.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-38385952/original/2d46c223-f93a-4d22-a5d2-537053c79e57.jpeg',114861645,32,'45.516944091708666','-122.63838030752444',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,75.00,30,182,0,1.00,38385952),(1673,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38388475','Luxury Private King Apartment w/ Healthclub','Luxury apartment for the fitness enthusiast. Available for your 31+ day stay. Full health club membership included. New construction in 2018 on the lower level of this 1914 building. Stylishly decorated with original artwork. Very comfortable, lots of light, with plenty of space to relax. Feels like an oasis in the city. Pet friendly. Luxury bedroom with king bed and large walk-up closets.','A perfect location to experience one of Portland\'s oldest neighborhoods. So much is available when you stay here. St. Johns feels like a village on the edge of the city. Our community is located close to the Willamette River and is filled with locally owned shops, pubs, outdoor activities, and a wonderful riverfront park below the famous St. Johns Bridge.<br /><br />You will be surrounded by a huge array of fitness opportunities. The property features a hot yoga and barre studio on the main level. Right outside your window is a boot camp exercise yard with an obstacle course layout. Across the street is a 23,000 sf health club with yoga, Spinning, boxing, Zumba, senior fit classes, olympic lifting, Hydromassage, steam room, sauna, and more! All these health club options are included in your stay!<br /><br />Each apartment has free parking, air conditioning, weekly cleaning, washer/dryer, full kitchen, streaming and live TV, and WiFi.<br /><br />Many activities and venues are within eas','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/35e7d53d-019e-40bc-91d9-c1897642d7a3.jpg',13540222,58,'45.58785','-122.74382',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,30,180,7,5.00,38388475),(1674,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38433196','2-Bedroom Light & Bright St Johns Central House','Spacious, open & light-filled guest suite in the heart of St. Johns with easy 15-minute access to Portland (esp. North, NE and downtown). High ceilings & open floor plan. View from main bedroom feels like you\'re in a treehouse. Close to Farmers Market, food carts, Cathedral Park, library, Forest Park & more. Easy commute to downtown PDX. Walk score 90.','St. Johns is a wonderful neighborhood. Classic historic charm mixed with new shops and restaurants. You\'re a block from the library, the local park and several great coffee shops.  Iconic Cathedral Park with the gothic-inspired green bridge is a 10 minute walk. Sauvie Island is a close drive. The Fixin To (live music venue) is in walking distance. University of Portland is close.<br />Favorite walkable restaurants of ours include:  Gracie\'s aPizza, Bahn Mi Up and John Street Cafe. Lots of vegan options, too.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/025660d1-d28c-4c8c-8282-a5e630f85dae.jpg',59233279,58,'45.59033','-122.74879',1,4,1.50,2.00,3.00,127.00,1,1125,201,4.94,38433196),(1675,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38491322','Tidy Studio- Newly built in Foster Powell','Our small cozy studio has all the basic amenities you need to be comfortable during your stay in Portland.  Located in the heart of Foster Powell and a short walk to local restaurants, shops, coffee, parks, bus line and more!','Many popular spots within a short walk. Bread and Roses Market, Mercado food carts, Street Disco, Henry Higgins Bagels, Carnelian Coffee, Five and Dime, Pizzaria Otto, Assembly Brewing, Bar Maven, and more!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cc23ed89-12eb-4735-abe8-331c2c859a96.jpg',12056976,36,'45.49344','-122.59208',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,65.00,2,7,295,4.92,38491322),(1676,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38500509','Cozy Bedroom with great location  near MAX','This place is located in a convenient location within walking distance to shopping and transportation. 11 minutes a way from airport and 15 minutes away from downtown. You do not need a car. This is a very friendly environment.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/983f0594-3b9f-45fa-bd59-0f6e9f3801e3.jpg',96243932,63,'45.52743','-122.52076',2,1,2.00,1.00,1.00,30.00,30,1125,15,4.73,38500509),(1677,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38541570','Shipping Container tiny house with private patio','Stay in a one-of-a-kind Shipping Container Home!  <br />This unique tiny house, made from two 20\' shipping containers, sits in the heart of southeast Portland\'s trendy FoPo neighborhood. <br /><br />The Container Home is a well-designed mix of modern and industrial esthetics.  The studio layout features a kitchenette, spacious bathroom, queen bed, A/C, large back deck, television, internet, W/D...everything you need for a comfortable stay.','The Foster-Powell neighborhood, aka FoPo, is a bike- and pedestrian-friendly neighborhood, loaded with character and unique Portland establishments.  It\'s a vibrant community where you\'ll regularly hear children playing and wave to folks walking dogs and biking by.  <br /><br />Walk half a mile to Foster St, where you\'ll find the Portland Mercado food carts, Assembly Brewing, Carnelian coffee, Bread and Roses Market and many other bars, restaurants, and vintage shops.<br /><br />Walk 1 mile north to the base of iconic Mt Tabor Park.  Hike to the top and look out over SE Portland and across the river to downtown.  Mt. Tabor is perfect for a picnic, basking in the sun or full moon, or running stairs and trails.   <br /><br />For more trail running, hiking, and birdwatching drive 15min east to Powell Butte Nature Park - over 600 acres of meadowland and forest.  <br /><br />The Container House is <br />・15-20min drive to downtown Portland<br />・ 3min to I-205<br />・15min to the airport<br ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9fd3a5f7-bf75-474f-a897-d68fea03007e.jpg',88749047,36,'45.49531','-122.59083',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,81.00,4,730,124,4.99,38541570),(1678,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38671207','Airy & bright studio, amazing location','This private space can be found in a sweet residential neighborhood within walking distance to downtown (a mile), the Oregon Convention Center, shopping & entertainment galore   (Burnside, Belmont, Hawthorne), and more wonderful restaurants than we can count (Le Pigeon, Langbaan, Nong\'s Khao Man Gai, Screen Door, etc.); coffee shops (Heart, Crema, Floyd\'s); the Vegan Village (for all things Vegan) and even Voodoo Donuts. Bars, brew pubs, live music at Revolution Hall are all steps away.','Enjoy the comfort and excellent location of our peaceful guest house in the Buckman neighborhood.  This is the perfect spot from which to wander and explore Portland!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5cef3ae2-8982-4c41-9367-dc73c389b8af.jpg',774106,32,'45.52237','-122.64993',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,80.00,2,8,313,4.92,38671207),(1679,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38696366','Poca Cabana! A stylish and private tiny house!','The Poca Cabana is a carefully built, stylish, well thought out space. It’s clean and modern. We did all that we could to make it as comfortable and welcoming to stay in. We really hope you enjoy your time here!','Brooklyn is minutes from downtown and blocks from the public light rail transportation (MAX) line. The Aladdin Theater (a fabulous concert venue)  is right by us. We are minutes from OHSU and downtown by Max. This is a spot that is quiet for Portland but walking distance from all the bustle of Division and Hawthorne streets.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-38696366/original/4aaa09da-9c83-4899-ad90-5d53e995b4f4.jpeg',272145512,56,'45.49579','-122.65126',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,83.00,2,730,340,4.99,38696366),(1680,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38697954','Hillsdale Hideaway','Welcome to one of Portland\'s best neighborhoods, Hillsdale in Southwest Portland, Oregon!  <br /><br />Very walkable: 2-3 blocks to coffee, cafes, restaurants, food carts, & parks. Or take the car/bus for a short drive to downtown, Multnomah Village (I-5 , OHSU or wherever you\'re going in PDX.<br /><br />This bungalow is a private 1 bedroom space that has its own separate entrance, a kitchenette, living room, & dining area. The full bathroom has a shower/bathtub and plenty of room. <br /><br />We look forward to your visit!','We\'re only 2-3 blocks to the Hillsdale TownCenter! Tons of stuff to walk to - coffee shops, bagel shop, restaurants (Oak & Olive, Casa Colima, etc), breweries (McMenamins & Sasquatch), Hillsdale Food Cart Park, so much more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/83357264-56ce-462a-ad85-c71c3753ee71.jpg',1723786,31,'45.48056','-122.69802',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,30,180,16,4.44,38697954),(1681,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38699497','Close-in, private Overlook retreat.','The Overlook neighborhood is one of Portland\'s hidden gems.  Quiet, tree lined, yet only a few minutes from all the action Portland serves up.  Walk or ride to meals, brewpubs or shopping in the Mississippi and Williams districts. Hop a train (three blocks away) to downtown or The Pearl District. Or to unwind,  walk to Overlook or Mocks Crest parks for sweeping views of downtown Portland, Forest Park and the Willamette River.  Please read on to see if this space is the right fit for you.','What makes Overlook so special is its quiet charm amidst a teeming, vibrant, easily-accessed city.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-38699497-unapproved/original/87570c8e-7b4b-44ef-b776-36da9befdc9d.JPEG',9745512,13,'45.55014','-122.6836',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,72.00,1,1125,489,4.96,38699497),(1682,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38752729','✔︎✔︎ Tiny Garden Home ✔︎✔︎','This is a totally new and dedicated space. Lots of light, air conditioning and a mini kitchen. It is tiny, efficient and private. Come and go as you please.  Hawthorne/Belmont historic neighborhoods, lots shopping, restaurants and entertainment all within walking distance.  Level 2 EV charger is available.','My neighborhood is very very walkable (walk score 90).  Restaurants, shops, entertainment and so on.  Leave your car, travel on foot or rent a scooter/bike.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5582b5df-558b-4e91-833d-2eee52a0390f.jpg',44210890,8,'45.50707','-122.62256',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,46.00,4,30,369,4.83,38752729),(1683,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38776459','Light Filled Apartment SW Portland - King, Patio.','A quaint apartment with a private entrance to get some R & R. Surrounded by trees sunrise and golden hour here are magical!<br /><br />The apartment is near 3 different parks, close to several grocery stores and coffee shops. Multnomah Village is a little \"village\" within our larger city and 3 min away driving 10 min walking. <br /><br />Your own private patio, new washer and dryer. All furnishings provided by @artifactpdx','The neighborhood is in SW Portland and located between Hillsdale and Multnomah Village which are both very sweet communities full of local businesses. Its a 10-15 min walk to a beautiful park, Gabriel Park, and a ton of great food options! <br /><br />My favorite food options you can walk to: <br /><br />Maplewood Cafe (Best coffee shop//such an adorable space)<br />Baker & Spice (Best bakery!)<br />Verde Cocina (Amazing margaritas!)<br />Sasquatch (Brewery with great food)<br />Marco\'s (Great Breakfast)<br />Yalla (A MUST! Great Mediterranean)<br /><br /><br />Favorite stores:<br /><br />Consign Couture (my store!)<br />Pawsh Pet Cafe<br />Village Cheer<br />JP General<br />Indigo Traders <br />& so many more downtown Multnomah Village.<br /><br />We are a 10 min drive to: <br />OHSU<br />Downtown Portland<br />Beaverton<br />Bridgeport Village<br />Washington Square<br /><br />We are a 10-15 min drive to: <br />Lake Oswego<br />Close in SE Portland','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6Mzg3NzY0NTk%3D/original/01d0ed4b-ac94-4080-bafe-c4ae6a1d4aa8.jpeg',10525989,17,'45.4785','-122.70852',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,30,1125,47,4.91,38776459),(1684,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38848625','Light, Peaceful Mt Tabor Guest House on Hawthorne','A former schoolhouse located on a serene stretch of one of Portland\'s most vibrant streets. It is a comfortable private space with a cozy but open layout, vaulted ceilings and skylights to bring in the natural light. You\'ll be a few blocks from hiking trails and stunning city views from Mt. Tabor, as well as a short walk to Hawthorne, Division, and Belmont where you\'ll find the full array of urban amenities.','The Hawthorne district is a shining example of what makes Portland so great - nature walks, unique shops, top-notch restaurants, entertainment & nightlife are all walking distance from The Hawthorne Haven. Wondering where to go for dinner? Just ask - we love sharing local tips with out guests.<br /><br />Take a short walk to a 200 acre park centered around an extinct volcano and enjoy sweeping views of the city. Down the road eat tacos at Por Que No, have a romantic dinner at Sapphire Hotel, or unwind with some old school video games and pinball  at Quarterworld. Downtown is a short drive, bike ride or bus trip away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/89edef1a-382f-4133-b49b-15654ce660b5.jpg',7219122,15,'45.5115','-122.60392',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,64.00,30,120,29,4.59,38848625),(1685,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38901095','Rose City Garden Studio-Midterm rental discounts','Stylish lower-level studio with approximately 6 wide steps to the landing.  This retreat features, quartz counters, walnut shelves, a full-sized refrigerator, hardwood floors,  AC & heated tile floors.  Although this is a lower-level suite, it does have a good amount of light with a beautiful fir window on the south side and a full-light glass door on the east side of the house.  The entrance to the suite overlooks a lovely garden.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-38901095/original/0c19b158-4405-4d02-bfc7-09fe6be62949.jpeg',40729073,39,'45.54663','-122.59489',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,28,90,34,4.97,38901095),(1686,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38918275','WOW! Newly  Studio Apartment- Heart of Sellwood❤️','Stylish studio with an amazing open concept kitchen, heated floor bathroom and bluetooth speakers. It has been thoughtfully decorated to make your stay comfortable, enjoyable and private. You can expect very clean, well appointed, turn- key accommodations. <br />It is the perfect alternative to a hotel Jr. Suite with all the comforts of a home, private covered patio & backyard, providing a cost savings and convenience. Ideal for corporate housing, medical stays, work stays, or any relocation needs.','This neighborhood doesn\'t get any better! You have the water front, parks, great restaurants, bars, coffee shops and stores all within walking distance, making it really convenient for all your needs and JUST MINUTES AWAY FROM DOWNTOWN! <br />Daily errands can be accomplished on a bike, there are bike lanes and trails, road connectivity to Downtown and most of the attractions in Portland.<br />Sellwood-Moreland is considered one of the best places to live in Oregon. It offers residents an urban feel. Many families and young professionals live in Sellwood-Moreland.<br />One of the best things about this very walkable neighborhood is how incredibly friendly, safe and clean it is!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7c72c501-6143-4cd0-a27f-741658f0d7ea.jpg',213350724,20,'45.46452','-122.65922',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,30,730,12,4.92,38918275),(1687,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/38954210','The Portland Snu House','This completely unique Mandala home is a one-bedroom stand-alone house that is a perfect location to launch your Portland staycation or adventures from.  Light-drenched and cozy, this space features vaulted wooden ceilings, large skylights, and a gas fireplace.  Newly built, it offers a fully equipped kitchen and a private outdoor courtyard with a hot tub just off the bedroom.','Close to many things & easy access to everything Portland offers. The Alberta Arts District and the Williams corridor are a few blocks away, both bustling with things to do, but also quiet & tucked away. Within walking distance are local favorites like Eem, Salt & Straw, Bye & Bye, Mississippi Studios, Jinju Patisserie, & Kayo\'s Ramen Bar, to name a few. <br /><br />If you want to venture outside of the neighborhood, we are in close proximity to other communities that have their own unique offerings, like Hawthorne, Pearl District, Nob Hill, and Saint Johns.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/edd967e8-074b-4528-9c1e-8d948ad3282e.jpg',960864,14,'45.55193','-122.65934',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,2,29,228,4.97,38954210),(1688,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39037465','Burnside Suites: Luxurious 3rd Floor Apartment','This authentic, renovated space sits just2 floors above Dante’s, the legendary venue that\'s given Portland 24 years of live music, burlesque, and NY pizza. Come and check out hotspots like Voodoo Donut, Mary’s Club, or one of many food carts, and more. See our guidebook for more recommendations!  <br /><br />***WARNING*** This building is 119 years old, so you will hear the live shows from downstairs most nights, as well as other city noise (earplugs provided). If this doesn\'t dissuade you, then welcome!','With a walking and biking score of 99 and a transit score of 90, Burnside Suites is surrounded by amazing food, cocktails, and entertainment. A stone’s throw away is everything from dive bars and strip clubs to fine dining and cocktail lounges. Enjoy a stroll along the picturesque waterfront, or spend a rainy day roaming the vast Portland Art Museum. If you’re a fan of the outdoors, Forest Park has hiking trails for days (literally). If you enjoy nature in smaller doses, the Lan Su Chinese Garden and the Portland Japanese Garden are breathtaking oases in the City of Roses. The Portland Saturday Market is just three blocks away and is packed with local artist offerings. We’ve curated our own AirBnB Guidebook just for you, and includes all the places we’ve taken our own out of town friends and family.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39037465/original/ab526263-d96a-4155-9046-04399edc291a.jpeg',319750330,43,'45.5236','-122.67352',1,10,1.00,2.00,5.00,242.00,1,30,141,4.91,39037465),(1689,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39053512','Cozy Cottage in the City','Beautiful guest house on the east side. We keep calendar open for multi-week stays, but contact us if you have shorter trip requests. Hardwood floors, heated tile bathroom, AC. Large windows with southern light, plus wrap around deck and well landscaped yard. Well appointed kitchen. King bed and two bunk beds. A quiet retreat, with easy walking to restaurants and shopping, plus historic Laurelhurst and Mt. Tabor Parks. Ample public transport nearby.','We are centered in between 3 great neighborhoods--Mt Tabor, famous for a sprawling urban park with city views, historic reservoirs, and numerous trails and rec facilities. The Richmond neighborhood features Hawthorne and Divisions Street retail districts w everything from farm to table restaurants or tasty food trucks to hip shops or Powell\'s Book Annex. The historic Laurelhurst neighborhood has remarkable NW architecture and tree-lined streets, as well as the Olmsted-designed Laurelhurst Park where locals feed ducks, have picnics and do tai chi. All are in easy walking biking or driving distance.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-39053512-unapproved/original/b6ffc673-8024-441a-ad8e-ead073b4e75e.JPEG',11439956,16,'45.51725','-122.61396',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,25,90,44,5.00,39053512),(1690,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39090071','Find Foodie Bliss from Sunnyside Carriage House','Raise the blinds and let light fill two bedrooms with vaulted ceilings and a fully-equipped kitchen. Enjoy the warmth of heated bathroom floors. Share a growler on the recycled brick patio or have a soak in a 6-person hot tub. The carriage house is behind the main home and above the garage in the bohemian Sunnyside neighborhood. It is great for families, friends, and business groups.','Southeast Portland has a small town, city-within-a-city feel, which makes it great for the Airbnb experience. Grab a growler and a fancy donut. Shop for records, vintage clothing, and handmade items. Walk to the movies, have a beer and catch a movie in the historic Laurelhurst theater, read at Powell\'s Books, visit the historic Lone Fir Cemetery, take a walk in the 37-acre Laurelhurst Park and grab a meal at the Pod 28 food carts.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/108aeb11-ab97-4a9e-abed-e4c07813fb30.jpg',40890090,16,'45.5192','-122.63473',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,160.00,2,28,328,4.95,39090071),(1691,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39112551','Woodlawn Urban One Bedroom','Welcome to your home away from home! Nestled in the vibrant heart of the city, our newly renovated basement studio offers a tranquil escape from the hustle and bustle. Perfect for solo adventurers or couples, this intimate space combines modern comforts with a touch of rustic charm. <br /><br />This location is within walking distance to some of Portland’s most loved coffee shops and resturants. In less than a 30-minute drive, you can find yourself standing amongst 700+ year old trees.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39112551/original/5ca65194-2659-4dbd-b34b-936229741de9.jpeg',200142887,45,'45.57081','-122.65897',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,87.00,30,1125,2,5.00,39112551),(1692,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39168630','Charming 3 bed, 2 bath Portland/ Multnomah Village','Adorable 3 bedroom, 2 bathroom, 1420 sq ft, modern ranch with air-conditioning, well maintained front and private back yard, just 5 minute drive to downtown Portland\'s fabulous restaurants & nightlife.<br />Comfortable great room floor plan with vaulted ceilings and 5 skylights give the home a spacious feel. <br />Master bedroom and bathroom with shower, dual vanity and walk-in closet. 2 additional bedrooms that share a bathroom with bathtub and shower.','Multnomah Village is a very short walk (couple blocks) away and has shops, restaurants, pubs, salons, and other attractions. Close by parks and dog parks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/60b8c7df-8149-4310-b670-f41e1d6fcac4.jpg',623138,18,'45.46785','-122.70517',1,6,2.00,3.00,6.00,121.00,30,364,5,4.40,39168630),(1693,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39195215','Ladd\'s Lodge: 2BD Apartment in Prime Location','Welcome to Ladd\'s Lodge, a fully appointed basement apartment located in the heart of Portland\'s most livable neighborhood: Ladd\'s Addition. We offer a friendly location, an easy walk to some of Portland\'s finest restaurants, bars and attractions, and rigorous cleaning and disinfecting to protect our guests. With downtown Portland just ten minutes away by car or bus, and the other wonders of Oregon within easy reach, we hope that our home can be  your home when you visit our special city.','We are located in one of the most livable and delicious neighborhoods in Portland. Within a few blocks you have access to several great coffee shops, top-notch restaurants (Thai, Japanese, Mexican, Italian, Ethiopian, Vegetarian, Gastropubs, etc.), quaint bars, a brewery, cannabis shops, and Portland\'s finest grocery store.<br /><br />We\'ll provide guests with a local guide, which includes house rules and many recommendations for places to visit and explore.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/899c7bc8-6f44-43c2-a4fb-c11b5bfa7425.jpg',300761993,25,'45.50648','-122.64729',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,63.00,2,1125,254,4.92,39195215),(1694,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39200359','Modern Alberta Arts  apartment.','If you want to get a real taste of everything that Portland has to offer then our in-law apartment in the Alberta Arts neighborhood is the perfect place to land and start your adventure.','The Alberta neighborhood is perfect for walking to cafes, restaurants, shops, groceries, theaters and the Irvington, Fremont and Mississippi neighborhoods. Sample the delicious Portland food culture from vegan to omnivorous delights… and some of the best pie in the region!  Walk to a movie at the McMennamin\'s Kennedy School or catch some live music at the Alberta Street Pub or Alberta Rose Theater.  There are at least three beautiful parks (including a rose garden) within a 15 minute walk from our house.  If you\'re lucky enough to be here early Spring through late Fall and it\'s the last Thursday of the month, our neighborhood holds \"Last Thursday\" - a free wheeling street festival featuring musicians, singers, dancers, theatre, crafts, art, food and drink, stilt walkers, marching bands and circus performance; it may also feature mud wrestling, free advice booths, and free lavender - you never know what you\'re going to find, but you\'ll always have fun!<br /><br />A few nearby places:<br','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39200359/original/5c13285a-7cbd-436e-8b2d-d86b1f9fca56.jpeg',4580337,1,'45.55641','-122.63942',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,92.00,2,14,96,4.91,39200359),(1695,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39207853','Artist #8--Just Steps from the Max','Our home is just a few years old, newer construction features one bedroom and one bathroom. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week. Our neighborhood park is only a couple blocks away and has a new play structure and splash pad.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7475d2c5-d825-4384-ad7b-6500317b9814.jpg',6692974,55,'45.58435','-122.68395',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,112.00,30,1125,39,4.85,39207853),(1696,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39212010','Cottagecore vibes & everything you need','Your cozy home away from home in Portland! Centrally located in the Rose City Park neighborhood, a recent guest stated that “walking into the house felt like getting a warm hug.” Thoughtfully organized and fully stocked with everything you’ll need for a weekend visit or a month in town. Queen bed w/ memory foam mattress, full bathroom, kitchen, high speed internet, washer & dryer. Live plants and 10-foot vaulted ceilings. 10 min from PDX, 15 min from downtown, on bike routes and #12 bus.','Our studio is nestled in a quiet, highly walkway neighborhood. Just five blocks from Safeway, with numerous local restaurants and dispensaries within a five minute walk:  Pizzeria Otto, Thai Seasons, Pho Korner, Second Profession Brewing Company, Ohana Hawaiian Cafe, El Burrito Azteca, and several unique local coffee shops, just to name a few. The fully detached unit is set back from a picturesque residential street at the end of a long private driveway and offers complete privacy with keyless self-check in. Nest playground is just across the street, and Rosehips Yoga is less than one block away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-39212010/original/b4767e20-3fa8-4a27-a1b2-6ecbf483d1a3.jpeg',155798693,39,'45.54617','-122.59635',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,66.00,7,180,233,4.92,39212010),(1697,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39224415','Luxe|Clean|Contactless Alberta Daylight Apartment','Welcome to the NE PDX daylight apartment. Our charming centrally-located neighborhood is between Irving Park and Alberta. Easy access to N. Portland, Airport, Downtown, and all the fun & food the city has to offer. Enjoy a comfy, clean eco-luxe stay in a cute new apartment with premium amenities and a remote work setup.<br /><br />Happy to accommodate most anything guests need, just ask. Kitchen fully equipped with cooking gear and a microwave, one burner cooktop, electric skillet, fridge, and dishwasher.','Enjoy an ideal spot convenient to many awesome Portland neighborhoods, 405 and 84. In between Irving Park and Alberta Street, the apartment is convenient to a Whole Foods market and shopping center within walking distance on Fremont and 15th; shops, restaurants and cafes on Williams and Mississippi Avenues; and gas stations and grocery stores on MLK.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39224415/original/132a8e71-d923-4a51-bd74-f2a3a7ddc9e2.jpeg',46411027,6,'45.55312','-122.65481',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,82.00,4,730,139,4.79,39224415),(1698,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39233083','Cozy Sellwood Bungalow','This cozy bungalow is located on a corner lot in the charming quiet neighborhood of Sellwood. This is a great location just a short walk to local restaurants, bars, antiques, parks, & bike paths.<br />For those that want to explore Portland, Bus and Max Street Car are within walking distance, and it is an easy bike ride to downtown along Springwater Corridor.','Walkable, family friendly, two parks near by...','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39233083/original/f817e846-3256-4c59-8b29-868f7ee82b11.jpeg',13642877,20,'45.4665','-122.64423',1,3,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,3,14,77,5.00,39233083),(1699,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39246069','Farmhouse Apartment in Sweet Woodlawn','A fresh, bright lower level guest suite with a private entrance walking distance to breweries, coffee shops and beautiful parks. Cozy and clean, with a king size bed and spacious bathroom. Set under our gorgeous Victorian farmhouse. All are welcome!','Centrally located in a beautiful green neighborhood with different shops, coffee shops, bars just a few blocks in each direction.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ace4b2dd-959c-41aa-82e3-992ddac1c9d5.jpg',20913493,45,'45.57005','-122.6539',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,2,1125,35,4.66,39246069),(1700,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39270326','Cozy, private suite in the shade of Forest Park','Unique garden-level sanctuary in the hills of Willamette Heights.  Easy trail access to Forest Park providing miles of beautiful hiking, trail running, and mountain biking.  <br /><br />Coffee shops, food carts, bars, distilleries, breweries, restaurants and shops of trendy Slabtown and NW 23rd in under a mile.  <br /><br />Private deck and serene backyard with sunset views. Brand new queen bed. Private bathroom with full-sized tub.  Mini-Fridge and electric kettle with coffee and tea.  Table, couch & dresser.','Our neighborhood is a very safe residential area in the hills of Portland, Oregon. We are right across the street from Forest Park, one of the largest urban forests in the United States. As such, our neighborhood is often bustling with joggers, dog-walkers, and families out for hikes. People are very friendly here so don\'t be surprised if everyone you pass waves and calls out a hello.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-39270326/original/187f5d8e-a68b-4e2f-a48d-a1f257f3e3e7.jpg',11187732,50,'45.53562','-122.71918',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,110.00,2,15,138,4.95,39270326),(1701,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39279746','Artist #5–Just Steps from the Max','Our home is just a few years old, newer construction features one bedroom and one bathroom. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week. Our neighborhood park is only a couple blocks away and has a new play structure and splash pad.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1fe532c1-ed70-4fd4-a0ca-b67c