'Welcome to my childhood home! This is a historic house in SE Portland, one of the first built in the neighborhood in the early 1900s, the Concord grape vines in the backyard are over 100 yrs old! We recently renovated and refurnished the entire house, so you can expect beautiful modern furnishings, brand new appliances, the comfiest beds, and clean bright bathrooms. The location is super convenient, just a quick stroll from must visit Hawthorne and Division Streets.','The house is just a 15 min walk from popular Hawthorne and Division streets, and a quick stroll from local favorites Laurelhurst park and Mt.Tabor Park (great for a casual hike and you can get a view of the entire city and Mt.Hood from the top!). My favorite cafes, restaurants, and bars are within walking distance, but if you feel like staying in, you can also prepare your own meals using veggies from the backyard in our stunning and fully-equipped kitchen, and eat outside on our deck looking out into our beautiful garden (true \"farm to table\"!)','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/74b26006-4cbc-439b-b719-2db261af5c6b.jpg',20936849,52,'45.52122','-122.61304',1,5,2.50,2.00,3.00,288.00,2,1125,53,4.98,39781784),(1719,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39814914','Little Cabin in the City','Little cabin in the city. Two bedrooms, office with a sleeping space, kitchen, bathroom, living room and back yard are yours to enjoy privately. The basement and garage are host access only- but wont be accessed during your stay, and if you need a space for storage you are welcome to use either.','Mrs. Zumsteins coffee shop and bakery is right around the corner.  New Seasons Market is a 15 minute walk away.  Great bars and restaurants are less than three blocks away. Fernhill park is an 8 minute walk.  AND SO MUCH MORE!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39814914/original/d539511c-be94-4a4c-88e4-db51315dbdf1.jpeg',241947014,1,'45.55992','-122.62139',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,175.00,2,365,77,5.00,39814914),(1720,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39820322','Cora Street Retreat - 2 bedroom in Portland','Lovely Spacious two story Town Home  in a quiet Inner Southeast neighborhood<br />ALMOST 3 bedrooms: 2 extra large bedrooms (4 beds) and 2 1/2 baths<br />-Gas fireplace <br />-Smart TV<br />-Office nook with monitor <br />-Highspeed WI-FI <br />- Well stocked kitchen <br />- Master suite with king bed<br />-Large separated bedroom ( 2 bedrooms with a double door that opens between):<br />- Queen bed in one side<br />- Full and twin bunk in the other side<br />- Portable crib/play yard <br />- Laundry <br />-Central ducted heating. Zoned air conditioning','Our townhome is iin the Brooklyn neighborhood, with a neighborhood organic deli and a great Mexican restaurant just 2 1/2 blocks away. Food carts and Pok Pok are nearby, as well as the Aladin Theater, a Portland landmark, and the Brooklyn park with kids play structures. A short drive or bus ride will take you to the Sellwood/Westmoreland, or Clinton/Division neighborhoods with their own great eateries.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-39820322/original/657a282a-8c30-408e-bd35-d757918a4cee.jpeg',766064,56,'45.4914','-122.65284',1,5,2.50,2.00,4.00,254.00,2,1125,69,4.81,39820322),(1721,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39845797','Dreamer #9–Just Steps from the Max','Our home is just a few years old, newer construction features two bedrooms and two bathrooms. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and a beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week. The local park has new playground and splash pad.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/dc3c95e1-4ebe-452a-b5d0-f3762a6444d4.jpg',6692974,55,'45.58383','-122.68319',1,6,2.00,2.00,2.00,137.00,30,1125,59,4.86,39845797),(1722,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39846092','Dreamer #6–Just Steps from the Max','Our home is just a few years old, the newer construction features two bedrooms and two bathrooms. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and a beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week. The local park has new playground and splash pad.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2fae822b-0cb9-486d-b130-18db92f9f605.jpg',6692974,55,'45.58254','-122.68303',1,6,2.00,2.00,2.00,137.00,30,1125,19,4.95,39846092),(1723,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39846186','Entertainer #4–Just Steps from the Max','Our home is just a few years old, newer construction features two bedrooms and two bathrooms. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39846186/original/03040cf2-0eb5-4890-b4a1-cd87b2269c4a.jpeg',6692974,55,'45.58254','-122.68437',1,6,2.00,2.00,2.00,124.00,30,1125,52,4.88,39846186),(1724,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39846286','Dreamer #3-Just Steps from the Max (No Stairs)','Our home is just a couple years old, newer construction features 2 bedrooms and 2 bathrooms. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week. Our neighborhood park is only a couple blocks away and has a new play structure and splash pad.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39846286/original/000a9dd9-1330-490d-985a-9d95ab185e3f.jpeg',6692974,55,'45.58455','-122.68382',1,6,2.00,2.00,2.00,97.00,30,1125,42,4.83,39846286),(1725,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39846406','Strategist-Just Steps from the Max','Our home is just a few years old, newer construction features one bedroom and one bathroom. Only steps away from the Max/Train-experience Portland like a native rather than a visitor. Situated in North Portland aka NOPO-the Kenton Neighborhood is true Portlandia. A two minute walk puts you in Kenton Historical District with plenty of shops, pubs, restaurants, and a beautiful park.','Our neighborhood is special because it\'s right off the Max Line (public light rail), but still feels like a Portland neighborhood.  We are only steps from some of our favorite places to eat, or grab happy hour. In season there is also a farmers market once a week. The neighborhood park has a new playground and splash pad.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39846406/original/2d9907ad-bae7-45b0-a6aa-2f0cf544ef10.jpeg',6692974,55,'45.58433','-122.68379',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,99.00,30,1125,21,4.90,39846406),(1726,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39874259','Private Room in Kenton - North Portland','Relax in this calm stylish space in the North Portland Kenton Neighborhood. Great for short trips or extended stays. Dedicated work space in room for students or remote work.  <br /><br />Original 1910 home with updated kitchen, and bathroom. Hardwood floors and tile throughout, central air, in unit washer/dryer, free onsite parking. Big well-maintained backyard with covered seating area.','Located in North Portland in the Historic Kenton Neighborhood. Close the the Kenton business district of Denver Avenue where there are coffee shops, bars, and restaurants. Easy access to Max light rail and two bus lines. Close to Adidas headquarters, University of Portland, Expo Center, and the neighborhoods of St Johns, University Park, Portsmouth, and Arbor Lodge.  15 minute drive to airport and 10 minutes to downtown.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-39874259/original/a9696edf-1baf-4160-8e09-fe549f03e35c.jpeg',45233333,55,'45.58830205071735','-122.7008104942146',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,48.00,2,120,35,5.00,39874259),(1727,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39924964','Cute and Comfy in Downtown Kenton in N. Portland!','Cozy, cute, studio apartment located in the heart of Kenton neighborhood with private entrance.  Four blocks to max light rail (yellow line).  Minutes to downtown Portland, PDX airport, and downtown Vancouver.   Easy freeway access (I-5).   Restaurants, bars, and boutiques steps from your door.  Beautiful covered outdoor patio space.  Clean stylished interior for a comfortable and relaxing stay.  Kitchenette and private washer and dryer in unit.','Your choice of coffee shops close by,  we like Posies which is locally owned and has fresh baked pastries. Many great restaurants steps away including Swift and Union (refined American food, craft beer, and house cocktails),  PoShines (soul food), Pizza Fino (Italian), Derby (breakfast, lunch, and cocktails), Parkside pub (cozy fireside pub with standard food and drinks).  Nearby Bars include World Famous Kenton Club, Kenton Station (casual neighborhood bar), and  Mayfly Taproom and Bottle shop. Beautiful Kenton park blocks away.  Check out the giant Paul Bunyan statue at the edge of downtown Kenton district.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/56d62624-06be-494e-b8d9-d35283c0f6cd.jpg',17783032,55,'45.58028','-122.68774',1,3,1.00,0.00,1.00,59.00,30,99,57,4.93,39924964),(1728,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39925806','Tiny home away from home','20 minutes from the PDX airport; 5 minutes from the Woodstock area; one stop away from Clackamas Town Center; walking distance from food carts and public transportation;  tucked behind the house that looks like an Andes Mint; your very own cozy space.  Great getaway in a tiny home away from home.','Glenwood park is right around the corner; Lents Park, the home of the Portland Pickles, is minutes away; or head down the Springwater Corridor to Cartlandia about a mile away.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/18b9fde4-e727-417f-945c-f3fb2db0e2c8.jpg',241041292,72,'45.47491','-122.57549',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,1,5.00,39925806),(1729,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39943647','PDX Airport TownHome','We invite you to our home the PDX Airport townhome.This is a 2bed rooms and 2 private bathrooms, a cozy living room with a balcony (cannabis friendly) and a cute little kitchen. We have a nice park 1block over, We are close to the airport about 5 minutes away. 20mins from downtown and close to shopping. We are near the Troutdale outlets, the gorge and also close to grocery stores and gas stations like Costco. I hope you enjoy your stay!','We are located near everything take a drive around town an enjoy what Portland has to offer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/11e7f945-705f-47e5-a242-c63c3123c1ed.jpg',307898087,71,'45.55045','-122.5017',1,4,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,30,9,4.56,39943647),(1730,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39969259','Spring Garden Suite: private, green & cozy retreat','Wind down in a peaceful neighborhood setting just 10 minutes from downtown Portland and a 10-minute walk from quaint Multnomah Village — we invite you to enjoy our private, cozy, garden-level apartment.','Multnomah Village has a little bit of everything you need — good restaurants, awesome pizza, a great bakery, coffee, a fantastic beer selection, and a growing food cart pod. There are a number of parks within walking distance from those with interactive play areas to quiet trails. <br />In the summer we have an abundance of fruit and vegetables growing on the property. The gardens remain lush from April through October and sometimes surprise us with an extra-long season. From the top of the hill, you can get an amazing view of Mt. Hood on clear days.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-39969259/original/a6957b88-24f9-4842-a0bd-2112b0f9a31f.jpeg',807266,18,'45.45901','-122.71411',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,86.00,2,14,65,4.82,39969259),(1731,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/39975940','Private Greenhouse Suite for 1 or 2 Guests','Elegant, private king bedroom suite with magical private greenhouse, private entrance, desk and ensuite bathroom. Enjoy radiant tile floor heat, charming greenhouse seating nook, spacious 2-person shower and an amenities cabinet with microwave, mini-fridge, teakettle & flatware - ideal for simple breakfasts or reheated leftovers. This spacious room is ideal for 1 or 2 guests who want an entirely separate private space and charming \"interior garden\" porch, but who don\'t need a full kitchen.','Food in our immediate walkable neighborhood is generally awesome, with some restricted hours and interior seating owing to the pandemic (call ahead for the latest): #1: Ps & Qs Market: Go for lunch or dinner any day, or brunch on the weekends; go early in your stay, because you\'ll want to return for more. This is a hipster bodega, with a deli case and full kitchen, like a Vermont country store. It\'s a hit through Portland, and people travel to our neighborhood just to eat there. 5 blocks away. #2: Woodlawn Cafe and Bakery: Super baristas and pastries. Also serving artisanal breakfast and lunch plates until about 5 or 6pm. 3 blocks away. #3: Breakside Brewery: This might be number 1 if you\'re a beer fan, as it is a famous regional brewery with decent brewpub cuisine. 3 blocks away. #4: Tamale Boy: Awesome and unique Mexican food, specializing in tamales, but with a broad menu. 8 blocks away, and adjoined by a decent gelato place and a funky meed bar. #5: Firehouse Restaurant: Upscale It','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/70c4d27f-b1c9-42f3-ab92-e2ae35256b17.jpg',7358871,45,'45.57051','-122.65544',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,87.00,1,18,386,4.95,39975940),(1732,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40009844','Walk & Transit Bliss! Car Optional, Fly-n-Ride Apt','Location 98% Easily explore Portland! Car optional (PDX✈ transit: $2.80/person) bright, quiet 950sf apartment with ample free parking. Walk to Convention & Moda Centers, shops, cafés, food carts, breweries/pubs, with transit via Streetcars, 3 MAX light rail lines, Buses, and E-bikes steps away.  In historic Irvington with keypad entry, a private office, fast Wi-Fi 6, FULL kitchen & bath. This private level-up on a hotel is perfect for friends, families, and remote work for any length of stay.','[✔] 𝗣𝘂𝗯𝗹𝗶𝗰 𝗧𝗿𝗮𝗻𝘀𝗶𝘁 𝗯𝗼𝘅 𝗼𝗻 𝘁𝗵𝗲 ❞𝗪𝗵𝗲𝗿𝗲 𝘆𝗼𝘂’𝗹𝗹 𝗯𝗲.❞ 𝗺𝗮𝗽 to see nearby fixed transit if your viewing device shows it.<br /><br />We are located in the beautiful, quiet historic Irvington neighborhood, and very close to the happening NE Broadway corridor, the Oregon Convention Center, Moda Center, 3 light rail MAX lines and core Portland circling streetcars. <br /><br />Irvington is a classic tree-lined neighborhood with lovely parks, homes and gardens. Platted in the late 1880s and named a National Register Historic District (Oregon’s largest), Irvington is like a walk back in time containing the work of many of Portland’s most talented early 20th-century architects with  the largest collection of Queen Anne, Arts and Crafts, and Colonial Revival style homes in Oregon. While bustling NE Broadway has a slew of great local stores, restaurants, cafés, coffee shops and pubs, as well as must-have amenities like a grocery store, a pharmacy, dry cleaner, US Post Office, FedEx Print & Ship, hardwa','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6NDAwMDk4NDQ%3D/original/5382cfc1-a8c1-4fde-90ba-bf060f52748a.png',137104652,7,'45.53605','-122.65674',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,105.00,30,60,109,4.92,40009844),(1733,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40031934','Cheerful Irvington Apt - Walk to MAX & Shops','Our basement apartment is located in Irvington, a beautiful historical neighborhood 7 minutes from downtown. You would not need a car as you can walk to the MAX train station (5-7 minutes) and be in downtown in 7 minutes. We furnished our space  with a comfortable brand new bed and sleeper sofa. The decoration is very unique with a mixture of local and Hawaiian art. We give our guest total privacy but we are available for questions and tips.','Irvington is one of the  oldest neighborhoods in Portland, the largest historic district in Oregon where 85 percent of 2,800 properties retain their original appearance. There are beautiful old trees and Victorian mansions close by, worth a walking tour even in the rain.  You will see some of the old beautiful homes built in the early days in late 1800’s that still remained intact. We are within walk distance form MAX train station, Lloyd Center (Mall),  10 minutes walk from Blazer\'s Stadium, restaurants, coffee shops, stores and public parks -  Irving park is my favorite.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/eadfc99c-a493-4764-8349-65911ed5e086.jpg',13285949,7,'45.5394','-122.65293',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,57.00,3,27,93,4.87,40031934),(1734,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40094761','Northeast Portland, J&J Home stay','Come and relax in our charming urban craftsman home near the NE Portland Alberta Arts District.  The 1100 square foot space is full of character and artistic touches.  The house contains custom stained glass windows, mosaic murals, has a newly remodeled bathroom and remodeled kitchen, two bedrooms (both with queen beds),  comfy living room, dining room, office space, large front porch and garden patio for lazy mornings or lounging in the afternoon-evening hours.','Our neighborhood is in an urban setting with a park directly across the street from the house featuring a farmer\'s market every Sunday from May to Nov.<br />The Portland Bike Share System is located directly in front of the house.<br />Within walking distance: Alberta Street is 3 blocks away and is known as the Alberta Arts District. It offers a vibrant scene with several restaurants; food carts coffee shops, brewpubs, art galleries, and popular retail shops. <br />Williams Street is 6 blocks away, the most recent up-and-coming area offering additional choices of coffee shops, restaurants, brewpubs, and shops. <br />A little further away (17 blocks) is Mississippi Avenue, providing a long stretch of popular restaurants, live music, breweries, bars, retail shops, food carts, donuts, and coffee shops.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-40094761-unapproved/original/13b2c360-2959-40b2-95b6-51347cb2d249.JPEG',19929626,14,'45.55526','-122.66057',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,200.00,3,1125,37,5.00,40094761),(1735,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40096810','a little urban oasis','Welcome to Portland... to our breweries, exotic food options and all the artisan shops/ galleries your heart desires! While we can\'t promise sunshine, \"a little oasis\" will ensure your senses are heightened and remain in relaxed, vacation mode, even as the rains fall. This newly renovated, lighted-filled, 2nd story studio was inspired by our favorite mexican surf town and curated by experienced world travelers  to greet you with stunning aesthetics and optimal functionality.','The guest suite is located in the historic Irvington district- filled with stately homes, old trees and glorious strolls waiting to be had.  Just to the south is Broadway Street hosting a rich menu of ethnic eateries. The Lloyd District and mall are .5 miles away and connect with Portland’s light rail. One stop west:  Convention Center, one more: Moda Center (concerts/Trailblazers), one more: Old Town/Saturday market. Very central and super convenient location!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-40096810/original/feb51219-c93c-44a5-82cb-05159a223d2a.jpeg',13818089,7,'45.53667','-122.6534',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,70.00,1,1125,379,4.93,40096810),(1736,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40098476','Private & Cozy Casita','Private unattached ADU, new, cute and comfortable, light and bright, off-street parking, quiet neighborhood, close to public transportation, 10 minutes from downtown, hiking trails, parks, near Portland Community College, one hour to the beach, one hour to Mt Hood. Portland is known for its good food, breweries, wineries, coffee shops, shopping, all close by.','We are close to public transportation, 10 minutes from downtown, lots of hiking trails, parks, near Portland Community College, one hour to the beach, one hour to Mt Hood. Portland is known for its good food, breweries, wineries, coffee shops, shopping, all close by.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-40098476/original/f8234e39-89e7-4f5c-a28c-6c70d7ef0b3e.jpg',237669885,68,'45.44204','-122.72751',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,97.00,1,30,557,4.97,40098476),(1737,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40122072','Charming home in safe beautiful area - fenced yard','It is a comfortable home, in a convenient, safe, beautiful neighbourhood. Most things are on the ground level, master bedroom suite and second bedroom, laundry, garage, deck, living dining room, greeting room, all on the ground level. One step to go in the houe from the front entrance, also one step from garage to go inside the laundry room, then hallway. <br /><br />Lots of trails to hike or walk or jog right inside the neighbourhood. <br /><br />Please note pet fee is $15 per pet per night.','Nice neighbourhood in north west of Portland OR. With around 2000 households in it, the Forest Heights HOA is the second largest HOA in the state of Oregon. The neighbourhood is on hills, previously part of Forest Park, many trails still existing inside the neighbourhood and got maintained nicely by the HOA. <br /><br />Furnished, fenced, master on main, parks, trails, kids friendly, pets friendly ... beautiful and updated home in Forest Heights, the premier neighborhood in Portland. The home has 4 bedrooms, 3 full bathrooms, open plan kitchen, dining and entertainment areas. The home has beautiful views of the NW hills. backed by green space making it very private. The backyard is fully fenced if you do have pets or young children. The home is situated on cul de sac which makes it extra safe since it is hard to gt there unless you use the address and follow GPS. It is walking distance to Millpond Park, and a quaint village center (Coffee Shop, Pizzicato, American Hero Cafe, STEM Child','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-40122072/original/32889dd9-51dc-455e-b378-b79e1f10f827.jpeg',70796747,81,'45.5327892','-122.7768752',1,9,3.00,4.00,5.00,205.00,30,360,3,5.00,40122072),(1738,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40122336','Enchanting Old Portland Home ~ 92 WalkScore','This enchanting victorian-style home is nestled in the heart of SE Portland, right between Hawthorne and Division! Walk a block in one direction and you are at famous Portland restaurants such as Pine State Biscuits and Genie\'s Cafe, but walk a block in a different direction and you\'re at some of Portland\'s best breweries and beer spots. That includes Ladd Taphouse, Baerlic Brewing, Apex, and Grixsen.','This neighborhood is the best location on the East side of Portland. Within minutes you can be in downtown Portland, but at the same time can be on popular streets such as Hawthorne and Division by just walking a few blocks.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-40122336-unapproved/original/ffbe2ca1-fbe5-4c43-8520-7bb693e7260e.JPEG',120600285,25,'45.50564','-122.6546',1,8,1.00,3.00,4.00,204.00,2,1125,403,4.81,40122336),(1739,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40136778','📚🗺🐈‍⬛ Local History Museum in Historic Albina','Built in 1895 in the Historic Albina neighborhood, our home has oft been described as a local history library full of maps and books to help you get the most local flavor possible during your stay in Portland.<br /><br />As a seventh-generation Oregonian, I’ve hosted travelers from all seven continents, and am excited to share this local knowledge with everyone who comes into our home.','Located on a quiet neighborhood greenway (a traffic calmed bicycle route) and just two blocks from the vibrant N Williams corridor, this location enjoys a relaxed neighborhood atmosphere with countless shops, restaurants, and other destinations only blocks away. We’re in the heart of Historic Albina, one of the most diverse parts of town with a rich, multicultural history.<br /><br />In addition to our location within a historically Black neighborhood, we also acknowledge that we currently occupy land once home to village sites of the Multnomah, Cowlitz, Kathlamet, Clackamas, Molalla, Wasco, Chinook, Tualatin, Kalapuya, and many other Tribes who made their homes along the so-called Columbia and Willamette Rivers.<br /><br />Through practices of settler colonialism, some lands promised by the 1855 Treaty of Kalapuya were later stolen, yet the treaty and subsequent legal victories upheld enduring tribal sovereignty in these lands. We pay our respect to Tribal elders both past and present','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-40136778/original/09e29ebe-2b9e-4b0a-86d1-228908416f47.jpg',6877671,9,'45.55051','-122.66389',2,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,1,27,73,4.90,40136778),(1740,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40138718','Modern & Spacious 4BR in Central SE PDX!','This tastefully renovated SE Portland charmer is near delicious food and trendy bars! Within steps from booming Foster-Powell, minutes away from SE Division St., Hawthorne, and so much more. You won’t have any trouble finding awesome stuff to do, places to see, drink, eat, visit, etc.','SE Portland is a Foodie’s paradise. Located a block from Foster Rd, Foster-Powell boasts its own mix of cafés, bars, food carts, and vintage shops. Experience what true Portland is all about within a short walk from this property and neighborhood!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-40138718/original/f6e53960-34bc-40f8-ab08-d2039630ff3e.jpeg',51832729,36,'45.49251','-122.60178',1,10,1.50,4.00,5.00,264.00,1,1125,290,4.72,40138718),(1741,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40200097','Casa Chica PDX','A mini house in the Rose City Park neighborhood of the City of Roses that will make you feel right at home. Casa Chica is full of natural light, and a short walk away from Portland-caliber coffee, a local brewery, wood-fired pizza, bagels made fresh daily, a Mom n\' Pop wine shop, an independent movie theater, two beautiful parks, groceries, and the best Vietnamese food in Portland (in our opinion). Follow us on Instagram for more photos, tips, and info: @casachicapdx','Casa Chica is nestled in a quiet, historic neighborhood  near a main thoroughfare--NE Sandy Boulevard. Sandy is home to Rose Hips Movement (yoga/dance studio)--4 mins walking), Kainos Coffee (6 mins walking), Pizzeria Otto (with an unbeatable happy hour deal; 6 mins walking), Phở MeKha Restaurant (8 mins walking), and the Arrowwood Restaurant and sister business Second Profession Brewing Company (10 mins walking). Nearby you\'ll also find vintage shopping, a skatepark, two lush parks, a golf course, a public library, and a Safeway grocery store nearby.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9c4a313e-fed4-4d0c-8051-85549c863edc.jpg',2205701,11,'45.54267','-122.59684',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,64.00,1,1125,766,4.92,40200097),(1742,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40231423','Hawthorne apartment LLC two bedroom','','Close to all the cafes, restaurants and shops on Hawthorne plus walk to Mount Tabor Park for spectacular city and mountain  views','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c9386b34-2fc1-473c-a316-8a52a5b870a9.jpg',94623462,15,'45.51066','-122.608',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,109.00,2,28,34,4.88,40231423),(1743,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40265884','Dog Friendly Motor Lodge, One King Bed','Bring your bestie! Four-legged family members are welcome at the Jupiter. We apply a one time $45 pet cleaning fee at Check-in and will explain our pet policy to you if you plan to bring your pup.<br /><br />Jupiter Hotel is a locally owned and operated, renovated, 1970\'s style motor lodge. Doug Fir Lounge is on site, with great food and beverage options and a music venue with performances most nights. Night owl? Early riser? You’ll feel at home here.','In the heart of the inner east side cultural district, Jupiter is surrounded by great places to eat, drink, shop and explore. We are a few blocks from the Burnside Bridge which can take you into the heart of downtown Portland or to enjoy the Riverfront walkways and the Saturday Market.<br /><br />On site, in addition to Doug Fir Lounge, we also have Hey Love, which is an all-encompassing bar/restaurant/lounge/indoor jungle/neighborhood escape/all day hangout spot with hours ranging from 3:00 PM to 1:00 AM depending on the day. <br /><br />Our neighborhood has locally owned boutiques, great food and beverages, as well as multiple venues for live performances.  We are also a short jaunt form the Moda Center and the Convention Center.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-40265884/original/74ec4c43-5674-433f-8e8a-9ec160ae07a7.jpeg',8873069,32,'45.52179','-122.65636',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,209.00,30,1125,2,4.00,40265884),(1744,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40352164','Easy & Cozy Extended Stay (30-day min)','Quiet neighborhood great for extended business travel or other longer-term stays with separate entrance and off-street parking spot. Cozy fully-furnished, 1-bedroom apartment, with stocked kitchen, dining table, and living room with sofa bed.  Includes flatscreen TV with Roku for streaming (subscriptions not included). Easy to get most places w/ PDX airport 2.7 miles away, nearby highway entrances for I-205 & I-84, downtown Portland 6 miles away, and bus lines and the Max line a few blocks away.','Our house is one block away from The Grotto which has beautiful gardens to visit most times of the year and holds a huge light festival between Thanksgiving and New Years Day (google for more info).  If you\'re planning your stay in late November or December, you can expect more traffic on our quiet street than usual.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1a7369f2-f63b-4e03-a4cc-5ff98d4dc423.jpg',30290883,80,'45.55378','-122.57105',1,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,90.00,30,1125,9,4.78,40352164),(1745,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40369611','Light-filled Garden House (Alberta Arts)','Staying at 5615B can be an immersion or an escape. Our cozy, bright, clean, and custom space is Portland like whoa. Step around the corner for an amazing breakfast, take the bus straight downtown for the day, then have a locavore dinner on Alberta street and maybe hit our fav late night spot for queso and tequila after visiting the only hip hop pot shop in the city. Or, build a steady rhythm of cooking in and snuggling up while you get to know the animals and plants that call our garden home.','Alberta park is our home away from home. The Alberta Coop has the best eggs available in Portland, and the best sourdough English muffins (Dos Hermanos shoutout!) If you need something in the middle of the night (or a slurpy anytime), 7-11 is close. Right around the corner is the best Thai fried chicken I can\'t even. Vegan food and great drinks at our best queer bar is a short walk away. So much shopping on Alberta - vintage, resale, and new. You can walk to a great yoga studio (I teach there). Multiple saltwater soaking pools within walking distance. And the bus downtown takes 20 minutes. If you want to drive or bike, it\'s 15 minutes. There\'s plenty of on-street parking, and I\'ll tell you how to get to all the farmers markets.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/44e3fc47-c9cc-4425-8b45-120d11e7f4cd.jpg',20335532,29,'45.56262','-122.64998',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,3,30,31,4.94,40369611),(1746,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40378860','Charming Home to Yourself','Awaken to an entire home to yourself and step into our back yard patio for a cup of coffee. Our freshly remodeled home sits in the quaint neighborhood between the heart of St. John’s and the University of Portland. Enjoy sightseeing at Cathedral Park/St. Johns bridge, enjoy the local shops & restaurants a short walk away. Then cozy up in our quiet escape amongst the city. Our kitchen has everything you need to cook all of your meals here. Or if you prefer food trucks are within walking distance','Our house sits in a conveniently located quiet neighborhood. A short walk from Cathedral Coffee, the St Johns Beer Porch and food carts, and Fred Myer. A perfect place to stay for someone visiting University of Portland, the Adidas Campus, St. Johns, Forrest Park or Portland in general.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/aa369368-607d-4067-8e5e-f59ba050c9e0.jpg',18749328,42,'45.58456','-122.74193',1,4,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,34,4.38,40378860),(1747,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40400460','Modern Stylish 2 BR in Historic St. Johns','Wake up in this sun-drenched Loft and drink in the light.  Exposed beams & modern furnishings create an eclectic space that our guests love. Dig into our vinyl collection and enjoy the record player during your stay. Spacious feel with ultra-high ceilings and open floor plan. <br /> A Portland classic, St Johns offers a dynamic taste of city life with small town charm.<br /><br />***The loft sits above a music shop that is open to the public 12-5:30pm Tue-Sun.','Enjoy the many great restaurants, coffee shops, breweries, and unique local shops within walking distance.  Steps away from the St Johns plaza which hosts Farmer\'s Market, art fairs and other seasonal fun.  Immerse yourself in Portland food cart culture and enjoy live music at one of three venues. Cyclists, hikers and kayakers will love the proximity to trails and rivers. Easy access to other Portland neighborhoods and main attractions','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/0404ae84-1e7d-4ab3-af26-d619c186c92c.jpg',221421926,58,'45.59083195278738','-122.75394765575254',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,127.00,2,180,23,4.96,40400460),(1748,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40407224','Alberta Street Hideaway','This charming studio is clean and cozy with reliable wireless internet. The space is great for couples, solo adventures and business travelers. The building is a 1906 mixed-use bungalow. The main level of this house has been converted into a commercial space. The current business is a boutique hair salon. The entire lower level of the home is the Hideaway with private entrance to this 880sq ft. gem.','Enjoy this perfect urban hideaway retreat. Nestled right in the heart of the Alberta Arts District, which has a multitude of bars, restaurants, coffee shops, locally owned boutiques and galleries stretching over 20 blocks. Enjoy Portland\'s best ice cream at Salt & Straw located on 21st. Great ramen at Boxer Ramen located on 20th. Brunch is a must at the Tin Shed on 14th. Local Co-Op Grocery store located on the corner of 15th. Check out the Historic McMenamins Kennedy School Theater.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2c251cc5-429a-46ac-96c1-80812fda46d0.jpg',43716054,14,'45.55976','-122.6533',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,69.00,30,180,9,4.78,40407224),(1749,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40414540','Comfy & Cozy 2 Bedroom Portland Flat','If you\'re a big fan of great food, craft beer, pour-over coffee and Portlandia, this is your place. Our private and spacious two-bedroom apartment sits in the heart of the eclectic Burnside District - home to many of Portland\'s top-rated restaurants and bars, vintage shops, and some of the best people-watching around.<br /><br />With a convenient home base within walking distance to the neighborhood hot spots, you can get an authentic taste of how the hipsters live in Stumptown.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7545dc14-9755-4b5c-ac2f-85dcf66271ab.jpg',310753989,12,'45.52339','-122.63352',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,71.00,1,360,348,4.71,40414540),(1750,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40435487','Charmingly Warm PDX Flat in Trendy SE','If you\'re a big fan of great food, craft beer, pour-over coffee and Portlandia, this is your place. Our private and spacious two-bedroom apartment sits in the heart of the eclectic Burnside District - home to many of Portland\'s top-rated restaurants and bars, vintage shops, and some of the best people-watching around.<br /><br />With a convenient home base within walking distance to the neighborhood hot spots, you can get an authentic taste of how the hipsters live in Stumptown.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6NDA0MzU0ODc%3D/original/058f066a-d100-4165-a04c-c9757bf6b895.jpeg',310753989,12,'45.52179','-122.6331',1,5,1.00,2.00,2.00,64.00,1,360,308,4.78,40435487),(1751,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40451310','#StayInMyDistrict Raleigh Hills Serene Havens Nest','Stay in My District Raleigh Hills! Convenient to Shopping, Dining & Entertainment. Single level guest home is spacious, bright and tastefully appointed. Nestled down a private driveway on a quiet culdesac, w/ all the conveniences of the City. Close to SW Beaverton Hillsdale Hghwy & US 26, 15 min downtown PDX. This NEW private guest house is a cozy 500 ft.², with King bed/ sofa bed /1 bath. Sleeps up to 4. Full Kitchen, Washer/Dryer, FREE Parking, Smart TV & WIFI.','Raleigh Hills is located in the southwest hills with Beaverton to the west, West Slope to the north, and Progress and Garden Home to the south. It is a safe, quiet neighborhood in the hills with beautiful established landscape. There is tons of shopping, dining and entertainment in the surrounding areas. Downtown Beaverton, Hillsdale, Multnomah Village and Canyon Road are all within 5 min and have plenty of amenities. This is a suburb of Portland with beautiful parks and convenient to all Portland amenities, but would not be considered a “walkable” neighborhood. <br />Washington Park, home of the Oregon Zoo, Portland Japanese Garden and the Rose Garden are 5 min drive from the property.  Only 15 minute drive to Downtown and 30 minute drive to the PDX Airport.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-40451310/original/b076d70d-a9d0-450f-a05f-099a1a677fd5.jpeg',3142393,70,'45.488529205322266','-122.74200439453125',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,75.00,1,25,165,4.96,40451310),(1752,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40468274','Light & Bright N. Portland Studio!','This cozy and comfortable studio is close to classic Portland eateries, taverns, and markets like Drunken Noodle, New Seasons Market, Cathedral Coffee, Sundown Pub, and food carts. We are also within walking distance to several parks that are fun for kids.<br /><br />You’ll love my place because of the well appointed kitchen and the super comfy bed. My place is good for couples, solo adventurers, business travelers, and families.','Our North Portland neighborhood is growing like crazy. New eating and drinking spots are popping up all the time. There are 2 coffee shops, a pizza place, a mexican place, a great seafood place, and 2 or 3 taverns within a 5 minute walk from your basement studio. There are 2 old time movie theaters that serve beer and food and a great food cart pod close by for an authentic Portland experience.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7bcc623f-283a-416a-b2a6-f684ec98dac3.jpg',35707797,60,'45.58569','-122.72445',1,2,1.00,0.00,2.00,61.00,1,90,61,4.93,40468274),(1753,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40600913','Gem in Prime Location','If you want to avoid paying City tax book for 31 days or more.','Prime location, the unit is in the middle of everything. <br /><br />Grocery Stores :<br />- Trader Joe’s<br />- New Seasons Market <br />- Whole Foods<br />- Fred Meyer<br />- Safeway <br />- Zupans<br /><br />Many Cafes, Restaurants & Bars Around <br />Few of my favorite <br /><br />COFFEE <br />- Good Coffee<br />- Barista (2 locations, both walking dist.)<br />- Ken’s Artisan Bakery (also, great pastries and bread) <br />- St Honoré Bakery <br /><br /><br />RESTAURANTS <br /><br />- Mama Bird<br />- Papa Haydn (also check out their desserts, especially Bacana Dolce)<br />- The Fireside<br /><br /><br />BARS <br />- Cafe Mingo bar and restaurant <br />- Jo Bar & Rotisserie <br /><br /><br />PLACES OF INTEREST close by<br /><br />- Providence Park (Portland Timber’s) <br />- Forest Park (many trails to hike, one of largest urban parks in the USA) <br />- Portland Japaneese Garden <br />- Rose Garden <br />- Pittock Mansion (might need to drive, gorgeous view of the city and can tour ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e16c10df-6a27-4cab-a45b-fce14f5999df.jpg',20828305,27,'45.53035','-122.69619',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,72.00,30,1125,35,4.54,40600913),(1754,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40602080','NE Portland Private Entry Studio-Walking Distance','1 block off of NE Williams avenue: A cool and trendy place to soak up your authentic Portland experience! Coffee shops, the BEST restaurants around, Bars, workout studios, shopping, CoCo Donuts and more. <br /><br />Studio space includes private separate entrance, backyard patio for your using, Kitchen (Fridge/freezer, toaster, microwave), en suite bathroom with shower, queen size bed, and large flat screen TV. WIFI included.<br /><br />Happy to give recommendations for a good time!','North Portland is home to some of the coolest places in town.<br />Restaurants:<br />Award winning EEM- a thai-bbq tropical fusion to die for by some of the top dogs in town.<br />XLB, life of pie, EaT oyster bar, Kayo\'s Ramen bar<br />Snacks/ Coffee shops/ Bars<br />CoCo donuts, Either/Or, the box social, hopworks,Compass coffee roasting, Jinju Pattiserie, What\'s the scoop','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/6181719d-864c-45bd-a701-dad26ce1c873.jpg',22901192,9,'45.55266','-122.66649',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,76.00,1,15,346,4.94,40602080),(1755,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40639783','ECO-CONSCIOUS PEACEFUL HIDEAWAY TRENDY N. WILLIAMS','Quiet & cozy 2 BR apt for travelers/visitors desiring a healthy eco-consciously designed space.  <br />Our newly constructed, light-flooded basement is nestled on a quiet street close to Alberta and Mississippi Art Districts.  <br />A great home base for exploration; downtown, Alberta/Mississippi,  around the block on N. Williams Blvd.  Catch a yoga class, sip Portland’s famous coffee, peruse local shops or independent book stores, eat at one of dozens of restaurants and food cart pods.','We are on the east side of the river.  Most of the protests and demonstrations have been on the west side near the federal building in SW Portland.  This residential neighborhood is currently very quiet and safe.  <br /><br />Looking for exercise?  Electric and regular bike rentals are just blocks away. Peninsula and Alberta Parks are great to walk in or walk to if you want a 30-45 minute walk each way.  Peninsula is my favorite when the roses are in bloom, however if heading across the river you can get public transportation to the Rose Garden in Washington Park.  There are also great hiking trails in Forest Park. <br /><br />You may have come to Portland to eat; after all this is Portland, usually near the top of the list for most restaurants per capita!  Ethiopian, Indian, Vegan, Italian, Mediterranean, Thai, Mexican, Distilleries- all here in the neighborhood .    No matter which part of Portland you are exploring you will have choice.   <br /><br />If your trip is more about pampe','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/pro_photo_tool/Hosting-40639783-unapproved/original/084614df-8850-44fe-a2ad-19879006726f.JPEG',121280844,24,'45.5549','-122.66477',1,3,1.00,2.00,2.00,109.00,30,30,65,4.94,40639783),(1756,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40640474','Old Portland Charm, Perfect Southeast Location','This spacious, light-filled condo is in a building built in 1910, but it has been rehabbed and has a modern interior. The leaded windows, hardwood floors, and tree-lined neighborhood give you a taste of old Portland, but with modern comfort and convenience.<br />The furnishings are tastefully modern with mid-century (but not too kitschy) touches.<br />The location is excellent, with quick access by bicycle, bus or foot to downtown, Hawthorne, and many shops, restaurants and breweries.','Although the condo and furnishings are beautiful, the best thing about the condo is its location. It is in the Buckman neighborhood of Portland, a block from Hawthorne Avenue. Many popular shops, restaurants and breweries are within easy walking distance. One mile brings you to the heart of the lively Hawthorne District, with more shops and restaurants. In the opposite direction, one mile brings you to the Downtown area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1b6079ec-26ea-41e0-8450-e0634c651785.jpg',400281,32,'45.51353','-122.65097',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,30,90,16,5.00,40640474),(1757,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40672806','NE Cozy Home - Beautiful Home away from Home!','Newly remodeled, fully furnished, private, quiet,  2 bed, 1 bath stand alone home . Utilities included! Modernized open floor plan. Full kitchen, modern appliances, NEW washer/dryer, smart TV, Wifi, air conditioning, outdoor deck seating area, covered off street parking. Remodel designed and built by local architect. Cozy , quiet, across from Zen center. 10 minutes to airport, 15 minutes to downtown, near two major highways, on major bicycle route. Close to the action but just out of the chaos.','The neighborhood is family oriented, quiet and safe. The neighbors are friendly and supportive of the Airbnb. Please be friendly and respectful back to maintain our good standing in the neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-40672806/original/e1b19469-115f-46e8-ac3b-70d6f1857450.jpeg',19259335,74,'45.54411','-122.57675',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,75.00,30,365,15,4.80,40672806),(1758,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40695568','Modern Urban Retreat + Sauna','Our modern urban guest house is a completely private space, accessible by a separate walkway, and has an outdoor patio. We designed the space to be light-filled, feel cozy yet roomy, fitting a lot into a small space. Vaulted ceilings, a ceiling fan, full kitchen, bathroom, a bed alcove with a comfy queen mattress and soft bedding and lots of extra touches.<br />Our 335 sq ft guest house is fitted with all you\'ll need for your time in Portland.','This location is one of the best in the city - so much that makes Portland - Portland is located within minutes walking in any direction. Food, drinks, parks, open space, food carts, bustling neighborhood centers of Hawthorne, Division and Montavilla. Extremely walkable neighborhood full of families and small businesses.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/bcbc9585-ce60-41f8-a8a1-7002541270bf.jpg',8183063,15,'45.50822','-122.61082',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,100.00,2,29,138,4.95,40695568),(1759,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40706580','HeartofHawthorne MidCentury Dream 95 WalkScore 3BR','Live out your mid-century modern dream in this newly renovated Southeast charmer. Perfectly situated in the heart of Hawthorne, you can walk to the best shows, thrift shops, and restaurants in seconds. My home was thoughtfully renovated with an emphasis on living local: the floors, cabinets, and cabinet pulls were all manufactured here in the Northwest using sustainable practices!','Hawthorne, often hailed as the Heart of Portland, truly lives up to its reputation. This vibrant neighborhood boasts some of the city\'s best restaurants, concert venues, and vintage thrift stores, all lining the bustling streets. You could easily spend your entire trip exploring these few blocks and never run out of exciting options.<br /><br />The dining scene in Hawthorne is unparalleled, offering a diverse array of culinary delights. From farm-to-table eateries and trendy brunch spots to food carts serving global cuisines, there’s something to satisfy every palate. Don’t miss out on iconic local favorites like Apizza Scholls and Por Qué No.<br /><br />Music lovers will appreciate the live music venues scattered throughout the area, featuring both local talents and touring artists. Catch an intimate show at the historic Aladdin Theater or groove to the beats at the cozy Hawthorne Theatre.<br /><br />For those who love to shop, Hawthorne is a treasure trove of unique finds. Wander thr','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-40706580/original/267770b7-7aa1-4d5e-9ab3-adcd0a47be7a.jpeg',88253867,16,'45.51331','-122.61984',1,6,2.00,3.00,3.00,178.00,1,365,467,4.89,40706580),(1760,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40726828','Hip & Spacious: Mt. Tabor Haven with Hot Tub!','Come stay at Tabor Haven, a unique apartment in southeast Portland with mid-century charm and all the amenities of home! Tabor Haven rests at the base of an ancient volcano, surrounded by a beautiful city park located in the heart of the Montavilla neighborhood. Delicious restaurants, local shopping, unique bars and breweries a few blocks away! You’ll have it all nearby plus a quiet retreat to retire to in the evenings. Explore the best of Portland with our spacious apartment as your home base!','Montavilla is primarily a quiet residential area. Our Airbnb is located on a residential street but walking distance to many shops, restaurants and attractions. The heart of Montavilla neighborhood is just a short 10 minute walk from the house. This is a super hot area with many bars, restaurants, coffee shops and a theater. And if Montavilla doesn\'t suit your fancy Hawthorne, Division and Belmont restaurants and shops are only a couple miles away, the options are endless!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/1ed4b7b4-2304-4638-88ae-3bdb4f13d054.jpg',316013466,10,'45.5117','-122.58179',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,93.00,2,29,162,4.92,40726828),(1761,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40755790','The Woodstock Guest House','Perfect for families and professionals, our newly renovated guest house is a great place to relax after a hard day of work or play. Get an excellent night’s sleep on the memory foam mattresses. Enjoy the steam in the enormous walk-in shower. Kick back on the patio with a brew from Double Mountain Taproom. Create a gourmet meal with produce from the Portland Farmer’s Market. Snuggle up by the fire with a good book from Powell’s. Unwind at the Woodstock Guest House by booking today!','Woodstock is one of Portland’s oldest and most walkable neighborhoods. You can easily walk to Reed Lake (and Reed College), as well as access several grocery stores, coffee shops, and restaurants. With easy access to public transit and extraordinarily bike-friendly streets, Woodstock is considered to be the quintessential Portland Neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-40755790/original/89a85ba6-0ae9-4afa-8fca-d43a806a9af9.jpeg',4967953,38,'45.48122','-122.61285',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,200.00,7,60,96,4.98,40755790),(1762,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40758385','Urban Hideaway','Bright, spacious, and thoughtfully designed basement apartment.','Located in the Reed/Woodstock neighborhood, where there are plenty of parks, gardens, a golf course, and the Reed College campus. You’ll be a block from one of the best coffee shops in town, along with a Trader Joes, and Walgreens. Woodstock street is a half mile from the apartment and provides great food, bars, coffee, and shopping. The Sellwood neighborhood is 1.5 miles from the apartment as well, and plays host to numerous options for food and shopping.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/364e3bc5-3b6a-48c1-bf8d-f173ba03ddb1.jpg',31648101,38,'45.48759','-122.62125',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,75.00,3,730,197,4.91,40758385),(1763,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40775816','Ancillary Dreams','In a garden behind our home, a comfortable bed beckons, sharing its visions through a very large window. Complete privacy and tranquility envelop this little cottage, that is nestled ever so quietly between two of Portland’s most walkable and desired districts, celebrated as Southeast Hawthorne & Division.  … an urban retreat from your day to day life, you’ll want to call home during your stay.','Ancillary Dreams couldn\'t be located in a more perfect spot to experience what gives Portland it\'s reputation. It is situated three blocks from SE Hawthrone Blvd and five blocks from SE Division. Either direction are a short walk to the following establishments: Pok Pok, Bollywood Theater, Harlow, Fried Egg Love, Blue Star Donuts, Salt & Straw, Ava Gene\'s, Farmhouse Kitchen, Olympia Provisions, The Waffle Window, Baghdad Theater, Cubo, Whiskey Soda Lounge, and many many other phenomenal places. We are close to two outstanding parks within a mile or so, both Laurelhurst and Mt Tabor boast crazy accolades. One has won an award for most beautiful park on the West Coast and the later is an inner city volcanic cinder cone complete with reservoirs and 360 degree views of the city and Mt Hood. While all of this excitement is happening nearby you are all the while tucked into a beautiful, walkable, safe, and very quiet neighborhood.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3ab6d57d-659d-468a-bc15-a370c3d8337b.jpg',714512,8,'45.51','-122.63008',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,74.00,1,30,155,4.90,40775816),(1764,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40780172','Sabin Guest House','Built in 2019, this architecturally-designed space is warm and modern, with good natural light for a comfortable home base during your travels.<br /><br />We’re located on a quiet street in the King/Sabin neighborhood that’s just a short walk to great restaurants, shops, parks and a grocery store down the street. With a strong emphasis on locally made furniture and art, the ADU feels rooted in place. There’s also a small outdoor patio and rain garden in front.<br /><br />Thanks for looking!','We’re in the King/Sabin neighborhood very close to excellent parks, transit and local restaurants.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3a586f5f-026d-4e8e-86e6-77a31d9abebd.jpg',35830853,6,'45.55297','-122.655',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,132.00,4,100,127,4.94,40780172),(1765,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40787863','Bridgetown Bungalow: The perfect cozy getaway!','Come retreat from the city in this gorgeous studio designed with a modern art deco flair and rustic cabin comfort. The cozy interior features a vaulted ceiling with original timber beams, craftsman trim, reclaimed wood accents, loft with a library ladder, a heated bathroom floor and walk-in shower. The full kitchen provides all the amenities you\'ll need for cooking & baking including basics like pots, pans, utensils, spices, oils, small appliances and several coffee-making options.','The Bungalow is located in the thriving & diverse Montavilla neighborhood of NE Portland with several coffee shops, breweries, cafes, bakeries, grocers, and food trucks within walking distance or a short drive. Some of our walkable neighborhood favorites about 3/4 of a mile away are Fressen Artisan Bakery, East Glisan Pizza, and Blank Slate cocktail bar. Two of Portland\'s best outdoor eating spots are within a mile from the bungalow! The Barley Pod food truck pod featuring Baerlic Brewery & a huge variety of cuisine is a short drive down NE Halsey (on NE 60th), and newly opened in 2020 is the much-anticipated Rocket Empire Machine food hall (on NE Glisan & 70th) featuring Gigantic Brewing & a variety of food stalls including the delectable Pie Spot. There is also a wide array of international cuisine in the neighborhood including Vietnamese, Thai, Lebanese, Mexican, and a Halal market.  <br /><br />If it\'s wide open spaces you want, we have several within 2 miles of our home! Mt. Tabor','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/f12a44ed-1adc-46f2-bf18-90a0f93caea0.jpg',7611748,10,'45.53224','-122.58596',1,5,1.00,0.00,2.00,95.00,2,1125,333,4.98,40787863),(1766,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40803769','Peaceful Loft - Close to shops, Train & Downtown','Our peaceful detached apartment is located in Irvington, a beautiful historical neighborhood 7 minutes from downtown. You would not need a car as you can walk to the MAX train station. We furnished our space with a comfortable brand new king size bed and full size sleeper sofa. Bedding & duvet cover washed every time. The decoration is tropical inspired art and from Hawaii. There is a cute and equipped kitchenette with coffee maker, tea make, microwave, dishwasher electric range for small meals.','Irvington is one of the oldest neighborhoods in Portland, the largest historic district in Oregon where 85 percent of 2,800 properties retain their original appearance. There are beautiful old trees and Victorian mansions close by, worth a walking tour even in the rain. You will see some of the old beautiful homes built in the early days in late 1800’s that still remained intact. We are within walk distance form MAX train station, Lloyd Center (Mall), 10 minutes walk from Blazer\'s Stadium, restaurants, coffee shops, stores and public parks - Irving park is my favorite.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/59f6f4fd-6b08-4597-bdb8-3ed6c919e1ef.jpg',13285949,7,'45.53875','-122.6533',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,67.00,3,31,195,4.95,40803769),(1767,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40822541','Retro NoPo Duplex One Bedroom','One-bedroom unit in duplex-style home in NoPo.<br /><br />Offered fully furnished with all utilities and wifi included for rental of 30-120 days. Washer/dryer and additional storage on site. On-street parking or alley access parking is available. <br /><br />Easily walkable to public transit (MAX) many grocery stores (Fred Meyer & New Seasons) and I-5 access for commuting!','Ideally situated between Kenton, Arbor Lodge, Overlook & Piedmont neighborhoods. So much to explore!<br />Posies Bakery & Cafe, Po\'Shines Cafe, Cultured Caveman, <br />Tehuana Oaxacan Cuisine, Peninsula Park & Rose Garden, just to name a few.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9ad7ffc0-b933-4acd-adc1-871f2478f42e.jpg',20410856,51,'45.57268','-122.67939',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,45.00,30,1125,23,4.83,40822541),(1768,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40847662','Thurman Street Loft','Our loft is located right in the heartbeat of Portland\'s greatest neighborhood - NW 23rd and Thurman. Surrounded by the cities best restaurants, shops, coffee houses, bars and grocery stores. Cozy, modern and perfect for your Uptown stay. Welcome!','AWESOME DAY ACTIVITIES<br /><br />Colombia River Gorge Scenic FALLS: If you drive out on I 84, there are multiple falls along the way. (about 30 min away)<br /><br />-Multnomah Falls is a must see. <br />You can park at Bridal Veil and take a short hike along the road, which is fun and it takes you to Multnomah Falls. Also, there’s a mile hike to the top of Multnomah that’s amazing.<br />-Bridal Veil Falls<br />-Latourell Falls (our favorite waterfall. It’s a short hike to the waterfall)<br />-Swimming holes at Dougan Falls & Naked Falls in Washington. (amazing!!! Go during the week, it’s about 45 min away)<br />-Day Hike at Forest Park!!<br />Park at the Lower Mcleay Trail head, and head up the path. You will see a bridge above you called Thurman Street Bridge above you. <br />-Pittock Mansion has amazing views, you can actually hike up to it from Forest Park trails.<br />-Portland Rose Garden <br />-The Zoo<br />-Powell’s Book Store<br />-Overlook Park (amazing views of the city, bri','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/a53b6a60-9980-4bc8-b2c4-7b4f286367c9.jpg',317918819,27,'45.53455','-122.70007',1,6,2.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,31,1125,14,4.86,40847662),(1769,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40864982','Amazing location, family friendly in Alberta Arts','7 bedroom design haven steps from trendy Alberta Arts District in Portland, Oregon!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-40864982/original/4f66bba1-84a4-4a7f-97b5-27dcd4949340.jpeg',1150082,29,'45.56026','-122.65043',1,15,3.50,7.00,8.00,550.00,1,1125,31,5.00,40864982),(1770,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40865331','Sleeps 20!- amazing architecture + location','9 bedrooms with eco modern style, perfect for large groups, walking distance from cool and artistic Mississippi District.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/76520953-ff69-4259-b274-f219a1f2417e.jpg',1150082,24,'45.55606','-122.67614',1,16,5.00,9.00,9.00,708.00,1,1125,41,5.00,40865331),(1771,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40870837','Portland\'s White House B&B - Jack & Jackie','Welcome to Portland\'s White House, one of the Rose City\'s most luxurious and elegant historic homes that now houses a high-end bed & breakfast. Dating back to 1911 when it was originally built for wealthy lumber baron Robert Lytle and his family, the neoclassical mansion is situated in the heart of the exclusive Irvington neighborhood with lots of restaurants, shopping and public transportation within walking distance.','Portland\'s White House is centrally located whether you are here on vacation or for business. Lloyd Center, the Convention Center and MODA Center are mere minutes away and the exciting downtown and Pearl districts are just over the bridge. The Japanese Gardens, Washington Park with its Rose Garden, Chinatown, Oregon Zoo, Mt. Hood, Timberline Lodge where \"The Shining\" was filmed and plenty of shopping on trendy NW 23 Ave, in downtown or on the Eastside\'s North Mississippi and NE Alberta streets.<br /><br />Those who appreciate top-notch cuisine, fine wines, microbrews, and craft cocktails are in for a real treat as Portland boasts the greatest number of critically acclaimed restaurants, wineries, microbreweries and bars per capita than any other city in the nation. We also count scores of Food Network stars and James Beard award winners whose creativity has kept the city front and center on the epicurean scene.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/13bfe484-91bc-4de5-910b-d8a8a2b116e8.jpg',318184666,7,'45.53623','-122.64341',2,3,1.50,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,365,0,1.00,40870837),(1772,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/40873497','Portland\'s White House B&B - George & Martha','Welcome to Portland\'s White House, one of the Rose City\'s most luxurious and elegant historic homes that now houses a high-end bed & breakfast. Dating back to 1911 when it was originally built for wealthy lumber baron Robert Lytle and his family, the neoclassical mansion is situated in the heart of the exclusive Irvington neighborhood with lots of restaurants, shopping and public transportation within walking distance.','Portland\'s White House is centrally located whether you are here on vacation or for business. Lloyd Center, the Convention Center and MODA Center are mere minutes away and the exciting downtown and Pearl districts are just over the bridge. The Japanese Gardens, Washington Park with its Rose Garden, Chinatown, Oregon Zoo, Mt. Hood, Timberline Lodge where \"The Shining\" was filmed and plenty of shopping on trendy NW 23 Ave, in downtown or on the Eastside\'s North Mississippi and NE Alberta streets.<br /><br />Those who appreciate top-notch cuisine, fine wines, microbrews, and craft cocktails are in for a real treat as Portland boasts the greatest number of critically acclaimed restaurants, wineries, microbreweries and bars per capita than any other city in the nation. We also count scores of Food Network stars and James Beard award winners whose creativity has kept the city front and center on the epicurean scene.','https://a0.m