nd more)<br />0.7 miles to Starbucks <br /><br />This is an excellent hub for outdoor recreation: <br />5 miles away from hiking in Forest Park: the largest urban forested park in the United States.  <br />5 miles away from the Smith and Bybee Wetlands natural area: one of the largest urban wetlands in the United States<br /><br />Further away:<br />The Columbia Gorge National Scenic area is less than 40 minutes away<br />Timberline Lodge on Mount Hood is less than 90 minutes away (make dinner reservations in their Cascade Dining Room for your visit)<br />Cannon Beach is just over 90 minutes away and is home to a gorgeous coastal beach, famous for the Haystack Ro','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/312d3a29-58a0-4d59-ab23-f004eecb6410.jpg',998681,57,'45.57768','-122.7196',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,135.00,3,29,203,5.00,41839542),(1820,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/41932344','Best neighborhood in Portland!!!25','A quiet, perfectly located studio for visiting Portland\'s best spots. Beautiful Forest Park and NW 23rd - with all its fantastic food and shops - are a few minutes away (by foot) and Powell\'s, downtown Portland, the Rose Garden, and really anywhere else you\'d like to visit are easy to get to by bike, public transport, or car. Our place is equipped with a full kitchen so you can enjoy meals at home with all the amazing produce Oregon has to offer.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/c7a2c574-eb95-4ca9-a6e6-530a8d668228.jpg',326526800,27,'45.53633','-122.70142',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,60.00,30,365,5,4.60,41932344),(1821,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/41935714','Charming One Bedroom Near Great Food and Shopping','Perfect Portland hideaway! Fully equipped 1 bedroom apartment situated within walking distance to Belmont & Hawthorne street, these areas offer some of the best of everything Portland has to offer! Numerous funky coffee shops, locally owned restaurants, boutiques, brewpubs and clothing shops. Fifteen minute to downtown Portland, the Rose and Japanese gardens, kayaking and endless hiking trails. Less than 2 hours to the beach or Mt Hood.  Keyless entry for those late night arrivals, wifi & cable.','This is a very walkable neighborhood for nearly everything you need; great local restaurants, funky coffee shops, brewpubs, local taverns to watch the game, shoot a game of pool or play shuffleboard, boutiques, second hand clothing stores, Baghdad theater, and Wunderland nickel arcade. If your driving downtown Portland is 15 minutes away. Short distance to the Rose Gardens, Japanese Gardens, Patrick Mansion, hiking trails and water activities! Rent a kayak or for something a little more thrilling book a jet boat ride on a hot summer day!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-41935714/original/f7ca04ca-6ef8-404a-b382-7fdcca315bbd.jpeg',147708508,16,'45.51484','-122.63379',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,85.00,1,14,94,4.80,41935714),(1822,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42018596','Your PDX Destination home away from home','Welcome to PDX Destination! Our 1919 luxury cottage is a gem in Alameda neighborhood. Located in the center of Portland, this family friendly neighborhood will provide you with a quiet space to rejuvenate while giving you access to all that Portland has to offer. This home encompasses the old charm of early 20th century housing and is updated with modern conveniences. Luxury linens, appliances and furniture will keep you comfortable after exploring the beauty of the Pacific Northwest.','This is one of the safest, prestigious and loveliest neighborhoods in Portland and Portland’s surrounding area. There is a park behind Alameda Elementary school which is located one block away from our home. A wonderful coffee shop called Guilders is located four blocks away. Lucca (an Italian restaurant) is situated right across the street from Guilders. There is a Whole Foods, Starbucks, and a local coffee shop thirteen blocks down the street.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/2cfbe109-0e80-409d-bb84-ee7f356755aa.jpg',233209184,19,'45.54763','-122.63654',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,295.00,2,21,48,4.98,42018596),(1823,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42045234','Barbie Pink Portland Home 15 minutes from Airport','This quaint and colorful home is nestled on a quiet block, under tall trees with a massive backyard! With plenty of room to spread out, this home is perfect for both families or friends traveling together. It sleeps 5 comfortably - if you’re ok sharing a room. The primary room sleeps 2 in a comfy queen-sized bed. The guest room sleeps 3 with a queen-sized bed and a comfy full-sized daybed. Enjoy A/C in the living room and primary room.','Sitting between two main roads my neighborhood is tree-lined, safe, and quiet. It\'s a block away from a couple of big box grocery stores: Ride Aid, Fred Meyer, and Grocery Outlet. There\'s fast food and Starbucks within walking distance as well. There is great stuff on Division that’s less than a 10 minute drive - Hinterland foodcarts featuring Matt’s BBQ tacos and Burger Stevens to name a few. There’s Stumptown for coffee, Woodsman Tavern for oysters, Salt & Straw for ice cream and Bollywood Theatre for Indian also on Division just minutes away by car. All the fun stuff in SE Portland is 20 minutes or less by car!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6NDIwNDUyMzQ%3D/original/051c8322-087e-4dbd-b544-2d5b8b54b826.jpeg',273386591,78,'45.49966281734936','-122.5434657705945',1,5,2.00,2.00,3.00,165.00,2,7,11,5.00,42045234),(1824,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42063871','Vintage Charm in Vibrant Walkable Neighborhood','Charming, diminutive one-bedroom, one-bath 1923 Craftsman bungalow with natural wood finishes, lovely light and a lush backyard garden. You\'ll be perfectly situated to walk, bike, hop on the bus or drive wherever you need to go from this centrally-located home. Just steps from dozens of restaurants, cafes and breweries. Newly renovated, this cottage is situated in a peaceful garden with greenery, birds and seasonal beauty all around, in one of the most walkable of Portland neighborhoods.','In addition to walkable, green, tree-lined streets and parks, this little house is within easy walking distance (2-10 minutes) of myriad great businesses: artisinal coffee joints, restaurants including casual and elegant, vegan, two favorite pizza places (Ken’s and Babydoll), many international/regional restaurants, several ice cream shops, Whole Foods, an Italian grocer, hair dressers, healthcare, a hippie spa, live music/dancing (Revolution Hall, the Laurelthirst and the Goodfoot), breweries, wine/gift/tchotchke shops, and a beloved vintage movie theater and pub.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-42063871/original/420faa3c-f4fa-4e3c-b8c9-87c1edd8e5ae.jpeg',26919028,32,'45.5224','-122.63958',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,87.00,30,1125,7,5.00,42063871),(1825,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42100767','Beautiful Large MidCentury Modern Home SW Portland','This beautiful 3600 sq. ft. modern home is tucked away in a secluded part of SW Portland, yet only ten minutes from downtown Portland.  Big open spaces inside and out are perfect for larger gatherings.','Beautiful SW Portland, near Jackson Middle School','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/55421985/3d9a98a5_original.jpg',4121479,41,'45.45235','-122.70148',1,7,3.00,4.00,5.00,500.00,30,60,1,5.00,42100767),(1826,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42143191','Charming Classic Ladd\'s/Hawthorne Gem','You will stay in an historic neighborhood with 100 year old trees, in a home with character and beauty fitting of this lovely, walkable and friendly part of Portland called Ladd\'s Addition, where it intersects with Hawthorne Blvd.   Steps from restaurants, food carts, pubs, coffee houses, bike rentals, a comedy club and more!  Vintage shopping? Yes. <br />Easy public transit? Yes. You can also spend time relaxing;there is a modern kitchen, living and dining room, and even a piano if you like to play.','Ladd\'s Addition is the  oldest neighborhood in Portland.  It is unique in design, with the streets arranged like the spokes of a wheel.  There is one main circle(Ladd circle) and four rose gardens, North, South, East, and West.  It is a wonderful neighborhood for a stroll!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-42143191/original/ab538a71-5da9-4c6c-8e4c-4ee490740ec6.jpeg',13351238,25,'45.51182','-122.65075',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,86.00,1,1125,377,4.87,42143191),(1827,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42171568','Newly Renovated Historic Home with Garden Oasis','Relax in this spacious urban Oasis just steps from trendy Mississippi and Williams avenues. Virtually next door to Mississippi Studios and  Stormbreaker Brewery. <br />Be downtown or to NW in 5 minutes. <br />Enjoy the yard and patio or relax in the hammock and help yourself to fresh produce from the garden.<br />Ample free street parking. <br />Fast WiFi, plenty of space and privacy to work remotely or just relax.<br /><br />Ring cameras at Front and Back doors.','Extremely walkable. Mississippi ave is filled with local restaurants, breweries,  food carts, shops, and cafes.  Laid back vibe.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-42171568/original/a60e2b7d-7f0b-4774-8bcc-d8e2a2a6947f.jpg',15451664,9,'45.54936','-122.67674',1,4,2.00,2.00,2.00,171.00,2,200,82,4.96,42171568),(1828,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42207396','Mid-Century Apartment on Hawthorne ~ Thrift & Eat','Located in the vibrant Hawthorne District, our apartment is within walking distance of Portland\'s best restaurants, cafes, bookstores, brewpubs, and distilleries. other services, such as banks and massage therapists, are also nearby.  Around a mile from downtown, you can easily use bikes, public bus services, or walk to explore the city. Our sleek, European-style interiors feature high-grade surfaces and finishes, offering comfort and elegance in one of Portland\'s most dynamic neighborhoods.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors, with no chain restaurants in sight! Make new friends over vegan poutine fries and grilled PB&Js at the Cartopia food cart pod, indulge in delicious wings right around the corner at Fire on the Mountain, share a pie at Apizza Scholls (consistently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or enjoy a fancy night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-42207396/original/86c46f35-3b67-4dfc-8c29-388ef629555b.jpeg',187734201,32,'45.51278','-122.64745',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,89.00,1,1125,420,4.88,42207396),(1829,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42221300','A Hollywood Haven Pet Friendly Walkable','This cozy dwelling in the Hollywood district is well lit, with plenty of windows to let in a warm natural light and multiple sconces adorning the walls. Includes a private fenced yard, a full kitchen, washer and dryer and one off street parking place.  In the neighborhood is a farmers market, Trader Joe\'s, Whole Foods, several parks, the iconic Hollywood Theater, fabulous restaurants and pubs, (Moon and Sixpence and New Deal Cafe being my favorites), and many fantastic small businesses to visit.','Our neighborhood is safe, very walkable, pet friendly, and beautiful as so many people plant flower and vegetable gardens. There are several beautiful parks within walking distance, the eclectic Hollywood Theater and many fantastic restaurants bars and coffee shops to choose from, most offering vegan and gluten-free options. Staying in the Hollywood District puts you in the hub of Portland with many spectacular sights, interesting venues and exciting experiences just moments away; The Washington Park Arboretium, Mount Tabor, The Colmbia Gorge waterfalls (Ainsworth is my favourite dog friendly camping spot as you can visit five waterfalls on one trail), and The Grotto are some of my favorite spots.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d5daf451-a7c9-4ee3-9600-c75e17e23875.jpg',59546078,11,'45.53342','-122.61401',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,125.00,30,1125,25,4.72,42221300),(1830,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42224566','Mt. Tabor Cottage : Cozy modern studio in SE PDX.','** We have a brand new queen size bed!!**<br /><br />We are located just a couple of blocks from beautiful Mt Tabor Park in SE Portland. The space has your own private entry and is a detached guest house just next to our main house. It is a light and bright lofty space with a super comfy queen-size sofa bed, table and chairs, restroom and shower. There is also a small kitchenette (with a mini fridge, microwave, coffee maker and tea set up.) On a clear day, we have a great view of Mt. Hood from our street!','We love SE Stark street just a few blocks from here. Check out the bipartisan coffee shop, Redwood room, The Observatory and the Academy Theater. There are a number of great shops on that nearby strip. We are also close to the fabulous restaurant Coquine, one of Portland\'s finest restaurants - you may need a reservation. We are not far from restaurant row on SE Division street and the fun other neighborhoods in SE - Hawthorne street, Belmont street, etc. We are about a 15 minute drive to downtown, depending on traffic of course.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-42224566/original/1aad85e7-aa74-4452-bf62-a155bbd3db15.jpeg',6298174,15,'45.51153','-122.58771',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,95.00,3,90,95,4.84,42224566),(1831,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42227113','Sunwashed Hollywood Studio','Winter never comes in this sunwashed abode. Enjoy the clean, modern furnishings, glass walls, and simple layout. Come home to everything you need to work or play: efficiency kitchen, fast internet,  and art & plants to inspire your space. <br /><br />Centrally located, with quick access to downtown, food trucks & restaurants a couple blocks away, a park across the street, and the shops of Hollywood less than a mile away.<br /><br />We use local, fair trade, organic and eco products whenever possible.','Our location is perfect for busy bees! I love going for runs or hikes at nearby Mount Tabor (1.5 mile run/drive). For PDX-proud craft coffee and bakery delights, I head to Seven Virtues (.5 miles) or Kainos coffee (1 mile). You\'ll find delightful thai, Mediterranean, Hawaiian/Korean, Colombian, Mexican, burgers, pizza and more at the food trucks at 60th & Halsey! Grab a beer from Baerlic Brewery and enjoy their COVID-compliant heated outdoor patio.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-42227113/original/dd390f4e-96aa-45ad-bdb6-a44ae4ea1de3.jpeg',28829879,11,'45.53446','-122.60384',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,148,4.82,42227113),(1832,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42309241','UofP/Adidas! Live in stylish comfort and privacy','Hello! I\'ve designed the space for students and travelers who need a private guest suite for longer term stays (30+ days). You have everything you need in terms of bath accessories, bed linens, kitchen utensils, laundry supplies and more. There is a 55 inch SmartTV. Cable TV isn’t available. The ADU has its own tankless water heater. Enjoy your private entrance, patio and garden arbors and secure bike storage. Tenants upstairs have 2 dogs and you will hear them on occasion.','The neighborhood is quiet with a mix of  young and older.  There are great views along Willamette Blvd with a short walking distance to N. Killingsworth where you\'ll find some great restaurants.  Arbor Lodge is a highly sought after area, because it’s quiet and centrally located.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/8a04472e-550d-4c90-8e35-1cbba201cd17.jpg',88040415,51,'45.57355','-122.69655',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,30,365,16,5.00,42309241),(1833,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42311940','CDC Compliant - Meticulously Clean Private Cottage','If you’re looking for a safe, rigorously sanitized, home base in Portland, we’ve got your back!<br /><br />We’re taking corona virus extremely seriously and have doubled down on our already meticulous cleaning practices (see past reviews & list of cleaning protocols in our photos section). We now provide CDC compliant deep cleaning between every guest, using only approved products. You will not find a cleaner place to stay on the west coast.<br /><br />Thanks for your interest and we look forward to hosting you!','We are in a quiet, residential neighborhood, with several great bars, restaurants, and cafes within easy walking distance (see our 5-minute walking map in photos). We\'re always happy to let you explore, but can also provide local recommendations for hidden gems.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/15beffb4-7e2d-41ad-85e6-d5d54dc3c67b.jpg',4089776,13,'45.5585','-122.68678',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,68.00,2,30,281,5.00,42311940),(1834,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42313191','South Tabor Stay-Private Large 2 Bedroom Apt','South Tabor Stay is your large 2 bed/1 bath basement apt. We offer a cozy private space with 3 queen beds, stocked kitchen and washer/dryer. Walk to Mt. Tabor Park, drive to SE Division St or Hawthorne Blvd restaurants and shops in minutes. Downtown Portland is a 15 min drive. We are located near Powell Blvd. for easy, quick grocery and food options. Ample free street parking. Keyless entry, self check-in in a clean remodeled basement apt.','Welcome to the South Tabor neighborhood! Our location is a perfect base for adventurers, hikers, city explorers or those who want a quiet, peaceful, cozy, comfortable home away from home. We are a 15 min walk to Mt. Tabor Park (about 3/4 of a mile or drive mins directly to the visitor center), 15 mins to Powell Butte Nature Park and 20 mins to Multnomah Falls and the Columbia Gorge/Vista House and endless hikes and waterfalls. We are a quiet residential neighborhood located right off of Powell Blvd filled with the easiest access to everything.<br /><br />Chinese Seafood Restaurant is across the street from the apt with local pubs & great Mexican store (El Campesino) right around the corner. <br /><br />Parking is super easy on our street-directly in front of the apt. Our quiet and safe street dead-ends at Mt. Tabor Park and Division Street. 82nd Ave and the Jade District is minutes drive away with affordable options for coffee, restaurants, shopping, and groceries. Downtown is a 15 min','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ec60f707-22ae-4c1e-be2a-5efa0f270234.jpg',63796820,37,'45.49861','-122.5943',1,5,1.00,2.00,3.00,129.00,2,28,134,4.99,42313191),(1835,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42315604','The Portland A-frame','Dramatic Mt Hood views at this West Portland Park A-Frame Chalet. With mid-century modern features and space galore, you\'ve never seen an A-frame quite like this. Soaring ceilings w/ exposed beams, skylights, original hardwood floors & 2 fireplaces. Eat-in kitchen w/ stainless appliances and options for dining indoor or al fresco. You\'ll feel like you\'re tucked into a mountainside, while having the convenience of living in the city.','West Portland Park is a lush and beautiful neighborhood with a several natural areas within walking distance from the house, and a 6 minute drive to Tryon Creek Park which has lots of hiking trails. It is a quiet and safe neighborhood (which is why you will feel like you\'re on a mountain retreat), but just a short 10-15 minute drive to downtown Portland, 6 minute drive to Multnomah Village, a 10 minute drive to Wholefoods and other shopping.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/9ebdaa9a-a82a-43e8-b363-fd3316cb1a88.jpg',10472485,53,'45.44861','-122.7193',1,6,2.50,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,2,5.00,42315604),(1836,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42353977','KEX Portland-Standard Queen Ensuite','Our Standard Queen Ensuite Room is a cozy European-style room, offering a comfortable place to lay your head after a day of adventures in Portland. It features a single queen bed uniquely designed with repurposed headboards from vintage fireplace mantels, a wall mounted Smart TV and a small desk. This room has a private bathroom located ensuite, with a stand-up tiled shower. The size of the room is about 150 - 170 sq ft.','KEX is just across the Willamette River from downtown, only a 10 minute walk across the Burnside Bridge.  In addition to being close to downtown, the Central Eastside neighborhood where KEX is located is filled with great restaurants, coffee, shopping and more.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/d8dc06cf-a0fa-4a1d-b480-8d1632fa8f36.jpg',325943042,12,'45.52327','-122.66208',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,136.00,1,28,25,4.88,42353977),(1837,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42362446','Marquam Hill Private Guest Room.','This private room for 1 or 2 guests is in the walk-out basement of our home. Convenient location, just minutes driving from downtown Portland, up in the hills surrounded by forest. Great place from which to explore Portland, the coast, Willamette Wine Country, Columbia Gorge and Mt. Hood area!  You have your own entrance reached by going down flight of steps. Walking distance to the VA and OHSU hospitals Marquam Hill campus. Please read house rules before booking. Permitted with Portland.','It is a quiet dead end street. Any direction you walk it includes uphill or downhill. I do not recommend staying here without a car unless you have specific things to do like a doctor’s visit or visiting someone in the hospitals. It is very easy to go for wonderful walks with great views of the Willamette River and Mt. Hood.  There are no restaurants or stores nearby that don’t involve walking downhill and back uphill','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/e1d38d36-28cc-4a09-b37a-a327e602950e.jpg',79151801,30,'45.4937','-122.68099',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,65.00,1,6,260,4.91,42362446),(1838,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42380321','Best Neighborhood in Town! 11','NORTHWEST PORTLAND: Completely furnished studio in a beautiful Mediterranean building located in friendly, close-in Northwest Portland. <br />This convenient location with a 98 Walk Score is close to some of the best restaurants, bars and cafes in town.','Close-in Northwest Portland- Nob Hill.<br /><br />This convenient location, with a 98 POINT WALK SCORE is blocks from trendy NW 23rd AVE, Dragonfly Coffee House, St. Honore Bakery, McMenamins Pub, a natural foods grocery store, the public library, as well as the post office. <br /><br />Window shop at all the lovely boutiques located just blocks away or hike/bike/run/explore the 80 miles of trails and over 5,000 acres of Forest Park; one of the largest urban parks in the United States! <br /><br />You can quickly and easily reach the Pearl District, the Brewery Blocks or Downtown Portland in minutes by foot, bike or streetcar; no need for a vehicle when living here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7c29bc29-dbc2-4147-8889-ef604705c9f3.jpg',322907763,27,'45.53694','-122.70172',1,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,58.00,30,365,9,4.33,42380321),(1839,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42383821','Modern Living w/hot tub in Alberta Arts District','Big Blue Box on the outside, light-filled modern comfort within! This spacious 3-story loft is an excellent place to experience what our amazing city has to offer. The BBB is a short walk to Killingsworth and Alberta Streets, parks, bike routes, numerous restaurants and shops. Available from 30 days to 90 nights or longer, it is perfect for an extended stay or business traveler.','This home sits on the tree-lined Ainsworth Street in NE Portland. It is a short walk or bike ride to Killingsworth and Alberta Streets, which have too many restaurants, shops, galleries, etc. to name here! There are also several parks in the area, including one used as a location in season 2 of Netflix\'s American Vandal. There are also Safeway and Walgreens stores close by. I-5 is only a couple minutes drive away, and you can get to PDX or Downtown Portland in 15.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ce05e2bc-c4d4-44d3-a666-146891efe160.jpg',39165671,29,'45.56526','-122.65377',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,94.00,30,90,85,4.85,42383821),(1840,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42416190','The Fern Cottage','Come enjoy Portland Oregon and explore our beautiful city! Grab a donut at Blue Star Donuts, stop at Salt and Straw for delicious ice cream or enjoy a delicious dinner on Mississippi. Spend some quality time in your tiny home on a quiet street with a lovely urban garden.','Arbor Lodge has many great places to eat, cute shops to check out and lots of activities to enjoy the Portland scene. We are walking distance to Kenton which has lots of places to get food and explore. Mississippi and Alberta are also close which have great places to explore.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-42416190/original/82fe1558-404c-4b23-bb05-5af6211cc787.jpeg',7409866,51,'45.57282','-122.68852',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,68.00,1,90,100,4.84,42416190),(1841,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42436031','Portland Riverside Condo at McCormick Pier','Downtown Portland condo right on the Willamette River.  Parking space available with rental of the unit.  Easy access to walk along the river and walk to the Pearl District, Old Town, Chinatown, and Waterfront Park.  Less than a 5 minute walk to the Old Town light rail (MAX) which goes directly to the airport.<br /><br />Communal pool and jacuzzi.  BBQ pits right on the river.<br /><br />Two different desks with monitors for doing remote work.  Wifi included, two TVs and a full kitchen.<br /><br />HVAC unit with A/C.','Literally steps to the Waterfront where Saturday market occurs every Saturday and Sunday. 15 minute walk to the Pearl District.  5 minute walk to Old Town/Chinatown.  Great restaurants and bars all in the area.  Moda Center is a 20 minute walk across the Steel Bridge for NBA games, concerts and other events.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/91a1b2c5-9ca1-4be2-a069-2ef7eb849b88.jpg',100676307,43,'45.52631','-122.67114',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,85.00,30,90,7,5.00,42436031),(1842,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42468070','Remodeled 1 BR Alberta Arts Guest Suite','Carefully cleaned and sanitized before your arrival.  We take every precaution when preparing the apartment for your stay to ensure you have a healthy and happy stay!<br /><br />Newly remodeled 1 BR basement guest suite (private entrance, no shared spaces) in the heart of the Alberta Arts district!  All new furnishings in a newly remodeled guest suite one block away from some of the best restaurants, art, bars, and shops in the Pacific NW.','One block away from the heart of Alberta Arts!  World Class restaurants, bars, and shops are all within a few blocks!!  Salt & Straw, Pine State Biscuits, Ciao Vito, The Waffle Window, Thai Noon, Cruzroom...  More food than you can eat in one vacation. <br /><br />Equally close to both downtown and the airport, Alberta Arts is the perfect central location for your Portland getaway.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-42468070/original/23baa3fe-8423-436a-b444-52a8f32855ea.jpeg',42701935,1,'45.56086','-122.64066',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,58.00,2,30,317,4.93,42468070),(1843,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42477015','WELCOME TO URBAN TREEHAUS','Premier Portland West Hills neighborhood just above downtown Portland, easy access to Beaverton/Hillsboro. PRIVATE DETACHED studio home with separate access and private deck. Local access into 200 acres of lush hiking trails. UPSCALE FINISHES: quality mattress, desk/chair, wood floor, full kitchen, quiet Bosch dishwasher, Jennair oven. Limestone bathroom. Full size front load washer/dryer. Parking space. Lots of windows with private tree views. BRIGHT, BEAUTIFUL & EXTRA CLEAN recently built!','Premier West Hills Location Near Pittock Mansion. Private access into renowned Washington Park trail network.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6NDI0NzcwMTU%3D/original/87d66a25-d0e8-4417-9faa-221efe6607d3.jpeg',191661378,62,'45.51738','-122.72159',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,83.00,30,730,0,1.00,42477015),(1844,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42488022','Portlands gem in the city','A+ as indicated by a 92 walk score. Its convenient to everywhere in town and to freeways to get you out of town. Recently remodeled with high end finishes. Small complex with private outdoor space.','Close to down in the hottest neighborhood. Lots of bars, restaurants and grocery all in walking distance','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/82973536-5063-4692-bb21-b8de155a580a.jpg',8680367,32,'45.51633','-122.65302',1,4,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,9,4.33,42488022),(1845,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42488541','Two bedroom Remodeled Gem','A+ location as indicated by the 92 walk score. Walking distance to bars, restaurants, and a amazing grocery. Convenient to downtown, public transit in any direction, and freeway access or to the light rail','Buckman is the hot neighborhood at the moment because of its proximity to everything and world class restaurants in close proximity','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/aaf62412-2d63-411c-96da-12c9d2bbbbb8.jpg',8680367,32,'45.51633','-122.65302',1,8,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,6,4.00,42488541),(1846,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42601276','Roseway Getaway - New Modern Private Home','Newly built and spacious modern home!  Entire spacious house is just for you alone,  enjoy the privacy.  Designed and built by local award winning architect! This cozy,  relaxing private escape has great access to the city. 10 minutes to airport, 15 minutes to downtown and near two major freeways. Close to the action yet just off the beaten path. Full amenities,  Kitchen, dining, queen memory foam mattress,  washer/dryer, 45\" smart TV with WIFI,  AC split unit, W/D,  Excellent private workspace.','The home is nestled in the wonderful Roseway neighborhood of NE Portland.  There are parks and green spaces all within 5 minute walk of the house.  Neighborhood is quiet, peaceful and full of wonderful neighbors. Off the beaten path yet near all the action, the home is very conveniently located.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-42601276/original/dd0f73fd-4afd-42f6-aa3a-76c4bc504904.jpeg',148312450,39,'45.55013','-122.58674',1,3,1.00,1.00,1.00,84.00,1,60,260,4.97,42601276),(1847,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42619371','Comfortable room, desk & FireTV - Monthly discount','\"Alder\"<br /><br />Sunny private room in the quiet St. John\'s neighborhood in North Portland and walking distance to brewpubs, restaurants, food carts, coffee shops, movie theaters and the St. John\'s bridge.<br />Room has a desk and internet TV and a comfortable queen bed.<br />House has keyless coded entry. Monthly discounts.<br /><br />Portland has a occupancy tax if the rental is less than 31 days so if you want to save approximately 200 dollars of tax, book for  31+ days !','At 5-10 min walking distance are the beautiful St. John\'s bridge, McMenamins , Soma Kombucha Speakeasy, Occidental brewing company, Stormbreaker brewpub,  St. John\'s twin theaters, many local  food carts offering delicious, diverse and affordable food options and numerous other restaurants and coffee shops. Right across the iconic St. John\'s bridge is Forest Park,  a 5100 acre park with numerous hiking and biking trails.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/5c1ac644-5a27-4ca6-8102-8667977808e5.jpg',8587273,58,'45.59045','-122.74738',2,1,1.00,1.00,1.00,45.00,30,180,13,5.00,42619371),(1848,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42623805','BEST NEIGHBORHOOD IN TOWN! 14','NORTHWEST PORTLAND: Completely furnished studio in a beautiful Mediterranean building located in friendly, close-in Northwest Portland. <br />This convenient location with a 98 Walk Score is close to some of the best restaurants, bars and cafes in town.','Close-in Northwest Portland- Nob Hill.<br /><br />This convenient location, with a 98 POINT WALK SCORE is blocks from trendy NW 23rd AVE, Dragonfly Coffee House, St. Honore Bakery, McMenamins Pub, a natural foods grocery store, the public library, as well as the post office. <br /><br />Window shop at all the lovely boutiques located just blocks away or hike/bike/run/explore the 80 miles of trails and over 5,000 acres of Forest Park; one of the largest urban parks in the United States! <br /><br />You can quickly and easily reach the Pearl District, the Brewery Blocks or Downtown Portland in minutes by foot, bike or streetcar; no need for a vehicle when living here.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/cf9d84f3-896b-47ec-9143-6b66dfddc89b.jpg',322907763,27,'45.53556','-122.70313',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,58.00,30,365,2,5.00,42623805),(1849,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42636202','Jewell\'s Landing floating home','Beautiful floating home on the front row with gorgeous, unobstructed views. Amazing sunsets & stargazing from the 2nd story 280sq ft master deck, outdoor dining, hot tub, BBQ, lounge chairs and more<br /><br />New comfy memory foam beds, smart TVs and a fully-equipped modern chef\'s kitchen with everything you could need<br /><br />2 Kayaks on site with lifejacket<br /><br />Enjoy the city of Portland while living the peaceful river life It\'s a 5-10 minute drive or ride-share to NE, North Portland or Alberta Arts District','Floating home neighborhood','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-42636202/original/80649923-99af-4744-910d-1605cc157258.jpeg',73445044,85,'45.60626','-122.67432',1,4,1.50,2.00,3.00,130.00,30,1125,5,5.00,42636202),(1850,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/42693147','BEST NEIGHBORHOOD IN TOWN - 23','NORTHWEST PORTLAND: Completely furnished studio in a beautiful Mediterranean building located in friendly, close-in Northwest Portland. <br />This convenient location with a 98 Walk Score is close to some of the best restaurants, bars and cafes in town.','Close-in Northwest Portland- Nob Hill.<br /><br />This convenient location, with a 98 POINT WALK SCORE is blocks from trendy NW 23rd AVE, Dragonfly Coffee House, St. Honore Bakery, McMenamins Pub, a natural foods grocery store, the public library, as well as the post office. <br /><br />Window shop at all the lovely boutiques located just blocks away or hike/bike/run/explore the 80 miles of trails and over 5,000 acres of Forest Park;