ated in a secure and quiet building a block from Providence Park, steps from Forest Park, and too many restaurants, grocery stores and iconic landmarks to list (Powell\'s Books, Japanese Rose Garden, Portland Art Museum)! With a walk score of 98 and a Max transit center a block away, access to the area is convenient and the space is ready for you to relax!','Goose Hollow is a historical downtown Portland neighborhood nestled between the hills leading to Forest Park and the Pearl Arts District.  Less than a mile from the waterfront and a short hop over the Burnside Bridge which leads to the East side of Portland, in itself  a wonderful area.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/143c97d7-13ed-47ea-9ced-386f16d88847.jpg',8118413,3,'45.52102','-122.68738',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,65.00,30,1125,9,5.00,552459643994124868),(2478,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/552837525666012664','The Raynes House ~ Explorers & Remote Workers','Newly built townhome with everything you could imagine to make your Portland trip effortless. With high end finishes and tasteful design, falling in love is merely a formality. Explore Portland\'s exceptional restaurant scene, or dine in with the beautiful chef\'s kitchen and luxurious appliances.','Located in the heart of the charming Rose City Park neighborhood, this vibrant area perfectly captures the eclectic spirit of Portland, offering a delightful mix of residential tranquility and urban convenience.<br /><br />The Rose City Park neighborhood is known for its tree-lined streets, historic homes, and friendly atmosphere. Just a short stroll from your doorstep, you’ll find a variety of local amenities that showcase Portland\'s unique charm. Enjoy a leisurely walk to nearby cafes, bakeries, and boutique shops that add a personal touch to your daily errands.<br /><br />Food enthusiasts will love the diverse dining options available within walking distance. Whether you\'re craving farm-to-table cuisine, international flavors, or a classic Portland food cart 