6','-122.60486',1,8,2.50,3.00,4.00,265.00,30,365,153,4.84,552848042925497266),(2480,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/553013219005188623','#StayinMyDistrict Pendelton Place Walk to Mt Tabor','#StayinMyDistrict Richmond Pendleton Place. Walk to Mt. Tabor, local shopping & dining! Live like a local while experiencing this popular Portland District! 4 blocks to shopping & dining in between SE Division and SE Powell, 6 blocks to Mt Tabor Park for hiking & great views! Street level basement apartment with both rustic & modern furnishings to create a comfortable and charming space! Historic 1 bed/1bath (+sofa bed) King Suite, Full Kitchen, Dedicated Workspace, WIFI, & FREE Street parking!','Safe, residential, tree-lined street in Portland\'s hottest neighborhood! Lovely and quiet, but just a few blocks from the newest section built up on Division St! A short walk will take you to food cart pods in two directions (50th and Division St. and Carts on Foster.) Also Green Zebra grocery, Plaid Pantry (convenience store), Good Coffee, Fern Kitchen, Petite Provence Patisserie, North Bar, Landmark Saloon, Los Gorditos, Bete Lukas (Ethiopian), Tokio Table (Japanese Hibachi), Siri Thai, and so much more! Keep walking west on Division, and you will hit everything on Portland\'s \"Restaurant Row\", including Tasty and Daughters, Pok Pok, Ava Gene\'s Salt n Straw, etc! The Richmond district is one of the most exciting and diverse neighborhoods in Southeast Portland. A longer stroll will take you to the Hawthorne District, which is not technically a designated neighborhood- but the locals all know where it is. The Hawthorne area is packed with trendy shops, restaurants, cafes, book stores, t','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-553013219005188623/original/e77499a0-2199-4f70-b7cb-73fa21f94969.jpeg',3142393,8,'45.50024','-122.61084',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,55.00,1,28,94,4.73,553013219005188623),(2481,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/554324491193620283','Cheerful 2 bedroom home, w/fireplace and office','Monthly rental. Cozy ranch style home (duplex), fully furnished 2bdrm/1.5 bath duplex w/ extra office space. Comfortably set up for long term rental for travel nurses and travel professionals. Full kitchen with all you need for cooking, comfortable furniture,  laundry room with washer/dryer private back yard. In NE Portland\'s Woodlawn neighborhood. Great neighborhood. .Walking distance to coffee shops, restaurants and park. Near Alberta arts district. Within 10 miles of most area hospitals.','NE Portland, Woodlwan neighborhood. Near coffee shops, restaurants and park. Great walking neighborhood. Alberta Arts district 15 minute walk or 5 minute drive. Travel nurses, most of Portland\'s hospitals are withing 8-10 miles','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-554324491193620283/original/1dfefbf9-8126-48b3-9575-e03ccd7844d7.jpeg',6827749,45,'45.57062','-122.64904',1,4,1.50,2.00,2.00,100.00,30,300,2,5.00,554324491193620283),(2482,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/554482307665275377','Private Alberta Arts Guest Home','Take it easy at this unique & tranquil private urban getaway. Our tiny home is a functional, rustic, open-concept studio. Set back on a quiet street with no shared walls or spaces, our studio provides quiet solitude while the bustle of many bars, restaurants, food carts and shops is just a few blocks away. Due to the nature of the space it has some quirks and may be best for younger people, solo travelers, and those without mobility issues. Please see description for details.','Alberta Arts District and Killingworth Street have many restaurants, bars, shops, and food carts that are easy to get to. Alberta Park is lovely and just seven blocks away. There is a laundromat five blocks away on Killingsworth and 6th Ave - Walnut Park Cleaners.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-554482307665275377/original/abe9a59b-a861-4529-8d30-809a0e29aa90.jpeg',184659909,29,'45.56532','-122.65499',1,2,1.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,30,31,51,4.94,554482307665275377),(2483,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/555642234041458343','Cozy Mt. Scott oasis with a view','Unique home on a private estate on the side of Mt Scott with an amazing view of the city.  5 minutes to Trader Joes, and great restaurants, yet feels like you are away from it all.   This home comes with 2 bedrooms, one King size bed and one Queen bed.  There are 2 bathrooms and one deep soaker tub.  Off street parking and hiking trails very close by make this a very fun place for outdoor lovers.  Huge windows in the living room and bedroom creates a wonderful ambience.','Mt Scott','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/7b38b803-dce4-46a3-bc45-6d609fd291c6.jpg',5192007,72,'45.460979979587805','-122.5655954915285',1,2,2.00,2.00,2.00,115.00,90,180,0,1.00,555642234041458343),(2484,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/555817839422284025','Custom North Tabor Farmhouse ~ Gym + Chefs Kitchen','Newly built townhome with everything you could imagine to make your Portland trip effortless. With high end finishes and tasteful design, falling in love is merely a formality. Explore Portland\'s exceptional restaurant scene, or dine in with the beautiful chef\'s kitchen and luxurious appliances.','Located in the heart of the charming Rose City Park neighborhood, this vibrant area perfectly captures the eclectic spirit of Portland, offering a delightful mix of residential tranquility and urban convenience.<br /><br />The Rose City Park neighborhood is known for its tree-lined streets, historic homes, and friendly atmosphere. Just a short stroll from your doorstep, you’ll find a variety of local amenities that showcase Portland\'s unique charm. Enjoy a leisurely walk to nearby cafes, bakeries, and boutique shops that add a personal touch to your daily errands.<br /><br />Food enthusiasts will love the diverse dining options available within walking distance. Whether you\'re craving farm-to-table cuisine, international flavors, or a classic Portland food cart experience, you\'ll find it all nearby