plore the renowned International Rose Test and Japanese Gardens, stroll the meandering trails of Forest Park, and visit the enchanting Pittock Mansion. You can also enjoy the hotel\'s signature amenities, such as a pop-up cinema, a mini-golf course, and a cocktail lounge. Whether you are looking for a romantic getaway, a business trip, or a family vac','- Providence Park - 0.2 miles; <br />- Powell\'s City of Books - 0.4 miles; <br />- Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall - 0.5 miles; <br />- Portland Art Museum - 0.5 miles; <br />- Lan Su Chinese Garden - 0.9 miles; <br />- International Rose Test Garden - 1.6 miles; <br />- Oregon Museum of Science and Industry - 1.7 miles; <br />- Washington Park - 2.2 miles; <br />- Pittock Mansion - 2.3 miles; <br />- The Grotto - 6.8 miles; <br />- Portland International Airport - 9.7 miles.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-863170116040578307/original/a4446544-41aa-4a13-a8c2-4770308d94af.png',174792040,3,'45.521','-122.68776',4,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,0,1.00,863170116040578307),(3205,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/863278276027894402','King Size Bed in Portland for Monthly Lease','Our home is nestled in the popular Buckman neighborhood — just a few blocks from Laurelhurst Theater. It\'s a two-story house that has been decorated in a modern Sonoma style with upscale design touches (we\'re architects) like crystal glassware and a Samsung Frame TV.<br /><br />It will comfortably fit 2 people in one king bed. However, the office has a pair of twin beds that can be used for kids, if you\'re travelling with family.','Our home is just steps from some of the best that Portland has to offer — from coffee shops to cocktail bars to the best movie theater in town. Whole Foods is nearby (we walk there all the time) and our main neighborhood, Laurelhurst, is dotted with excellent places for sushi, ice cream, and cocktails. Kenn\'s Artisan Pizza is just around the corner and was recently named the #2 best pizza place on EARTH.<br /><br />More broadly, we are 20 minutes from the Airport and 5 minutes from Downtown. Our preference is a 30 day stay, which is why we offer significant discounts for those who wish to stay longer.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-863278276027894402/original/e0390dab-ff73-4422-b119-ed11b81247ef.jpeg',23087686,32,'45.51847908107404','-122.6396800131576',1,2,1.00,2.00,0.00,0.00,30,60,0,1.00,863278276027894402),(3206,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/864485328754597191','Cute on a budget!','This cute little room w/ its own bathroom is perfect for you if:<br /><br />    - you\'re on a budget & looking for a clean, simple, affordable place to stay<br />    - you like old houses w/ character<br />    - you\'re looking for a very walkable/bikeable neighborhood <br />    - you\'re ok with hearing noise upstairs, where we live with our three-year old who likes to run around & is not always quiet :)<br /><br />Note: This listing is for a room & bathroom w/ its own separate/side entrance. It does not have a kitchen.','Southeast Portland is cute and walkable, and we\'re super close to Mt. Tabor, which we think is the most beautiful park of all (even more so than Forest Park, which is also stunning.) We\'re in walking distance to four grocery stores (Whole Foods, Safeway, Fred Meyer, and New Seasons), and several amazing restaurants and coffee shops. Plus bus lines down Belmont or Hawthorne.<br /><br />Our house is a craftsman from the early 1900s and so are most of the other houses nearby--we love walking by them and adoring their charm and character.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-864485328754597191/original/a901aeb3-863a-43d0-a2f5-626daec3f747.jpeg',4935076,16,'45.51372','-122.63327',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,55.00,2,730,56,4.77,864485328754597191),(3207,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/865096351459731670','Super Walkable Hillsdale Home','Super walkable Hillsdale home ready for families or a small group. It\'s on a big lot behind another house so it\'s really private. It consists of three bedrooms (one king, queen bunks, & a twin), a full office with printer, kitchen, and a living room with a  smart TV. We\'re right in the heart of Hillsdale so you are a 3 minute walk to over 10 different restaurants. There are 2 parks within a 10 minute walk and the local library. We have on-site parking and are a 2 block walk to a major bus line.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-865096351459731670/original/0b602f77-972e-4e40-be41-b0b87f261cba.jpeg',29819283,31,'45.480011249214705','-122.69655977114381',1,6,1.00,3.00,0.00,0.00,30,365,0,1.00,865096351459731670),(3208,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/865926000216939252','Art-Deco Inspired Guest Suite','Experience an unforgettable stay in a stunning private guest suite (with private entrance) that pays homage to the iconic art-deco period. Perfect for couples or solo travelers, our peaceful retreat provides a queen size bed,  Wi-Fi, smart TV, & a makeup vanity that doubles as a desk for remote working.  Conveniently located 5 minute walk from Division St or a quick a 15 minute drive to any main attraction in Portland.  Book now & experience the magic of this special space!','You\'ll be staying in a vibrant and bustling neighborhood with easy access to Division St and Hawthorne Blvd, two of the most popular destinations in the city.<br /><br />Getting around the neighborhood is a breeze, with excellent public transportation options and access to Nike\'s electric bicycles. And when you\'re ready to explore other parts of the city, the nearest MAX light rail station or busses are just a short walk away for a trip to downtown.<br /><br />Division St is known for its trendy boutiques and specialty shops. You\'ll find a variety of unique clothing stores, artisanal gift shops, and even a store dedicated to succulents! When it\'s time to refuel, Division St has a plethora of dining options. For breakfast, try Pine State Biscuits, famous for their Southern-style biscuits and gravy. For lunch or dinner, head to Bollywood Theater for some of the best Indian street food in the city. Or, if you\'re in the mood for some delicious Thai cuisine, check out Kati. <br /><br />Hawt','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-865926000216939252/original/c47691cd-fd24-4fd1-bd41-2f4bbeafd0cc.jpeg',25667842,8,'45.50015980375358','-122.63256302371714',1,3,1.00,1.00,2.00,79.00,2,28,74,4.92,865926000216939252),(3209,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/865945198947434343','Entire Beautiful Victorian in Overlook! 30 day min','Restored 1890 Victorian house, quiet close-in overlook neighborhood in Portland.   3 great bedrooms and 3 full bathrooms.  2 living rooms with TVs.  Chefs kitchen with butler pantry.  10 foot ceilings and all the charm of an old house , but all the upgrades of a modern new house. Fenced Yard and dog door.<br />30 day minimum stay only!','I know all the neighbors, they are great and helpful','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/99431493-d326-414c-b711-25dbcaa2fa24.jpg',509275508,13,'45.5596','-122.68616',1,4,3.00,3.00,3.00,110.00,30,120,5,5.00,865945198947434343),(3210,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/866654780514435855','Near to Oregon Zoo! Spacious Bedroom! Pet Friendly','Our hotel is situated in the downtown of Portland only minutes away from exciting locations such as International Rose Test Garden and Powell’s City of Books. Ideal for a fun vacation, the area provides an amazing selection of activities for guests to enjoy. Feast your eyes on lifelike artworks at the Portland Art Museum, experience nature at the Oregon Zoo or go for an entertaining concert at Moda Center. The list of what to engage in is endless and there’s something for everyone!','- Portland Art Museum – 0.4 miles <br />- International Rose Test Garden – 1.4 miles <br />- Oregon Zoo – 1.9 miles <br />- Tom McCall Waterfront Park – 0.4 miles <br />- Oregon History Museum – 0.4 miles <br />- Portland Classical Chinese Garden – 0.4 miles <br />- Portland Japanese Garden – 1.4 miles <br />- World Forestry Discovery Museum – 2 miles <br />- U.S. Bancorp Tower – 0.2 miles <br />- Portland International Airport – 6 miles <br />- Johnson Creek – 5.6 miles <br />- O’Bryant Square – 0.1 miles','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-866654780514435855/original/bb1fcd93-6488-4659-bced-fccd2fcc56c1.png',174792040,44,'45.52101','-122.67835',4,2,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,30,1125,3,3.33,866654780514435855),(3211,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/866715379618734502','Groovy on Glisan','','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-866715379618734502/original/e1c710f2-f83d-44b9-a15a-e53ac5c72258.jpeg',509450167,23,'45.527153131815844','-122.61863034163586',2,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,55.00,30,365,0,1.00,866715379618734502),(3212,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/867315556858008375','Cozy Suite in Arbor Lodge','Unwind and enjoy the city in our cozy and clean basement guest suite, conveniently located in a great neighborhood! We encourage you to read the whole listing to make sure our place is the right fit for  your stay. <br /><br />We live above the suite on the main floor of the house and we\'re excited for you to use our private basement guest space as a comfortable home base for your trip to Portland.','Get to know the lovely Arbor Lodge neighborhood! Great for strolls and just a 10 minute walk from Rose Parks Max Station, which provides direct transportation to Moda Center and downtown Portland in 10-15 minutes.<br /><br />Historic Kenton Neighborhood is a seven minute drive north. Great area for casual dining.<br /><br />Grindhouse Coffee and La Burrito Azteca are four blocks away for amazing coffee and breakfast burritos.<br /><br />6 minute drive from Mississippi Ave. Amazing area for live music at Mississippi Studios, delicious food at Prost or Interurban or Por Que No or Uchu Sushi, local art, some shopping, and great people watching.<br /><br />10 minute walk or 3 minute drive to New Seasons Market for all of your personal care, snacks, buffet needs. You can hop on the Max, or drive 5 minutes NE to Fred Meyers supermarket for anything you need.<br /><br />5 minute walk from Arbor Lodge Park.<br /><br />Local Spots<br />-Grindhouse Coffee<br />-Backyard Social<br />-Arbor Beer L','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6ODY3MzE1NTU2ODU4MDA4Mzc1/original/79298afa-9303-4a38-a5fd-c51780b5073b.jpeg',56078136,51,'45.56861','-122.69074',1,4,1.00,1.00,2.00,65.00,2,50,47,4.74,867315556858008375),(3213,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/867538135621907399','Sadie\'s Slice of Portland Charm','Step into a slice of Portland history with our charming studio apartment in the heart of SE Portland\'s dynamic Division/Clinton neighborhood. Housed within a stunning 1906 Craftsman, this cozy apartment boasts a wraparound porch and a fascinating backstory as the former home of Sadie Dibble Ross. A lifelong Portlander, she was actively involved in the community and lived here with her family until 1933. Walk to stylish shops, cafes, and restaurants and experience Portland living at its finest.','Southeast Division and Clinton Streets are some of Portland’s most iconic food destinations. Wander, snack, sip and shop. Some food for thought...<br />*Bollywood Theater<br />*Kim Jon Grillin<br />*Ruthie\'s<br />*Oma\'s Hideaway<br />*La Moule<br />*Jaqueline<br />*Broder<br />...just to name a few!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-867538135621907399/original/6b359da7-5b4c-45b1-ae0b-597a72549ff6.jpeg',158074447,8,'45.50276383717362','-122.63294084348637',1,2,1.00,0.00,1.00,77.00,31,93,6,5.00,867538135621907399),(3214,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/867593258576533950','Modern cozy heaven - full independent appartment','sit back and relax. This modern apartment is the perfect place to call home. Located in a quiet neighborhood, it is close to dining and commuting options, making it ideal for those who want to be close to the action. Inside, the apartment is cozy and inviting, with plenty of natural light and modern amenities. The kitchen is fully equipped with stainless steel appliances, and the living room is spacious and comfortable.  <br />Min. stay 28 d. extendable up to 3 mths. Message me if calendar is blocked','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-867593258576533950/original/37e7f56c-b3db-4dbc-b3d1-3f3a2d19ad16.jpeg',20275483,13,'45.56248','-122.6875',1,3,1.00,1.00,0.00,0.00,20,90,13,5.00,867593258576533950),(3215,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/867654779094903220','A+ Neighborhood SE PDX Queen Anne Cottage','Sweet Queen-Anne in bike/pedestrian centric Hosford-Abernethy neighborhood. Close to  Division and Hawthorn with easy access to downtown. Make your way Broder Cafe for a most delicious breakfast, walk through leafy Ladd\'s Addition enjoying the beautiful rose gardens and unique street layout, then stop at the New Seasons market for some supplies and relax in the lovely garden before heading for a massage at the spa a block away and then dinner at a choice of 3+ great special spots within a block.','You’ve hit the quirky PDX jackpot with a fantastic blend of Old Portland charm and New Portland variety at your fingertips. And if you’re visiting the neighborhood from another part of the city or somewhere else in the world, brace yourself for a full double dose of everything that keeps Portland fantastic.  Clinton/Division Neighborhood, one of Portland\'s signature destinations and a walk-able hotspot. Featuring a nationally renown restaurant scene, it is also known for it\'s boutique shops, friendly residents & beautiful gardens. Close by are Hawthorne & Belmont, and a short drive will get you to Downtown, Reed and other city destinations.”','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-867654779094903220/original/57524e6d-0222-4bc7-8ce3-e0c0b9be2e84.jpeg',52252008,25,'45.50322860000001','-122.6458944',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,158.00,30,365,53,4.87,867654779094903220),(3216,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/868403072892660655','Renovated John\'s Landing Bungalow','Enjoy a stylish & peaceful experience at this centrally-located historic bungalow. Completely renovated and on a dead end corner lot, this home offers relaxation and space; all while being minutes to downtown Portland and 1.3 miles from OHSU. Walking distance to shops, restaurants, and Willamette Park. Enjoy Kayaking, paddle boarding, yoga in the park, la cross and much more!','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-868403072892660655/original/19040edf-9a36-47d9-a54c-59b0ffe9de32.jpeg',323829992,22,'45.47399','-122.67356',1,8,2.00,4.00,5.00,190.00,30,365,0,1.00,868403072892660655),(3217,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/869131332756468753','El Oasis','El Oasis is a perfect get away for anyone looking for an urban-suburban experience. A converted basement to 1bedroom apartment, its versatility has something for everyone. Sitting on a hilltop, El oasis provides a central refuge for small families, couples, friends or even a solo trip. Central to coffee shops, bars, restaurants & the beautiful Mt. Tabor, El Oasis has something for everyone. We hope you love it as much as we do!','The North Tabor neighborhood is located in Portland\'s central eastside. It is bordered on the north by Rose City Park, on the west by Laurelhurst, on the south by Mt. Tabor, and on the east by Montavilla.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/3950ba1d-ca78-402d-8c14-a7dd236e412e.jpg',504645540,52,'45.52626306580342','-122.59995764133348',1,4,1.00,1.00,1.00,99.00,2,365,71,4.79,869131332756468753),(3218,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/869638024944793827','2 bed, 2.5 bath Alberta / Mississipi Dream Home!','This 2 bed, 2.5 bath home is sandwhiched right in between Alberta and Missisippi! Walk to your favorite restaurant, brewery, or cafe or discover a new one! Portland\'s restaurant of the year, multiple 4.5+ star yelp-reviewed dining establishments, parks, and bike routes are all in the area! <br /><br />Perfect for professionals, traveling nurses, couples transitioning between homes, and med school students!<br /><br />**NOTE: this unit sits directly above a 1 bed, 1 bath apartment with its own private entrance.','','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-869638024944793827/original/3ff730c8-7be7-47d3-8f31-229bd2bf8b39.jpeg',77828962,24,'45.55575','-122.66746',1,3,2.50,2.00,2.00,225.00,90,180,0,1.00,869638024944793827),(3219,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/870316809473416299','Windows Galore - Heart of Pearl!','Enjoy a stylish experience at this centrally-located corner one bedroom. <br /><br />This gorgeous place in the heart of The Pearl offers easy access to fashionable retail spots, excellent dining venues, endless entertainment and quick walk to Safeway or Whole Foods.  Nearby attractions include Powell\'s City of Books, Portland Art Museum, Roseland Theater, and Lan Su Chinese Garden. During your stay, you\'ll love the contemporary design, floor-to-ceiling windows, airy bedroom, and in unit washer/dryer.','The walkable, vibrant Pearl District of Portland is an excellent place for your temporary/long term stay. This gorgeous apartment in the heart of the city offers easy access to fashionable retail spots, excellent dining venues, and endless entertainment. Just a few blocks away, you\'ll find Jamison Square, Union Station, and a variety of local eateries Kure, JoJo, Irving Street Tapas, Brix Tavern, Piazza Italia. You can reach convenient grocery shopping at Whole Foods, and Safeway. Nearby attractions include Powell\'s City of Books, Portland Art Museum, Roseland Theater, and Lan Su Chinese Garden.  Every First Thursday The Pearl hosts an artist street market.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-870316809473416299/original/8bd87c09-13f0-4278-bf80-37aae19ad6b8.jpeg',41852577,2,'45.5287869','-122.6846317',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,90.00,31,365,2,5.00,870316809473416299),(3220,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/870604175096902996','Condo in the heart of Nob Hill NW','Delightful light & bright 3rd-floor condo in the heart of the Alphabet District. 1927 is full of charm and timeless updates. Secure storage unit and bike storage included—steps to fabulous shops, restaurants, studios, parks, grocery stores, and a movie theatre. Near the Zoo, Rose, and Japanese Gardens, 2 minute walk to a hospital. Also washer/dryer, dishwasher, high-speed internet, and built-ins.','Northwest Portland’s historic Victorian homes reimagined as boutiques, galleries, theaters and restaurants exude Old Portland charm in this walkable neighborhood that’s close to the Pearl District, Old Town Chinatown and downtown Portland —as well as Forest Park, with its 70 miles (113 km) of trails to explore in Portland’s west hills.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6ODcwNjA0MTc1MDk2OTAyOTk2/original/4ce10077-7377-484d-a286-9562fd8c35c5.jpeg',510247615,27,'45.52841098777242','-122.69422764603272',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,80.00,30,365,2,5.00,870604175096902996),(3221,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/871238042431556186','The Kenilworth Guest House','Showcased in the Modern Home tour of Portland, this newly built ADU is the amazing creation of Portland architect Webster Wilson.  A private, airy and elegant oasis set in urban Portland.  A glass house with intentional frosted glass to ensure privacy.  Escape and experience the elegant grace of this unique guesthouse.  Threading the needle of a city lot, the Kenilworth House lives along side a 1905 Victorian, where the host resides.','Friendly and walkable Creston Kenilworth neighborhood.  Excellent Kenilworth park down the block.  Diners choice of food and drink on Gladstone!','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/airflow/Hosting-871238042431556186/original/d17152e7-8117-4bfc-97a1-68e62a236c65.jpg',510394122,67,'45.49307352738117','-122.63394898973804',1,4,1.00,2.00,2.00,190.00,2,28,87,4.98,871238042431556186),(3222,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/871721529181150283','Relax in Style at a Boutique Hotel with Signature!','This vintage-inspired boutiq