g Sellwood-Moreland district - Perfect for the Portland aficionado who loves hand-crafted cocktails, eclectic shops, and live local music, making it the ideal location for those looking to experience the unique culture of Portland.<br /><br />The studio features a comfortable queen bed, full bath and kitchenette. The space is designed to be comfortable and inviting with quirky décor and plenty of natural light.','Located along the Crystal Springs Creek, the property is a rare gem in Sellwood-Moreland neighborhood, dubbed the Mayberry of Portland, you’ll enjoy walking to our neighborhood coffee shop, award-winning bakery, Sellwood saloon, and the best Thai restaurant in town. <br /><br />We are also just a short bike-ride away from the Moreland movie theater, eclectic shopping districts with local eateries, and historic Oaks Park Amusement Park and Skating Rink. While you\'re in town, consider visiting the Japanese Garden, hiking in Forest Park, picking berries at Topaz Farm on Sauvie Island, or paddling along the Willamette River. <br /><br />Whether you’re looking for a romantic getaway or a solo adventure, our charming tiny house is the perfect place to call home during your stay in Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-885124970398557753/original/6fb1dbe4-360a-40d3-b648-80dd97f18c8e.jpeg',39378828,20,'45.46197','-122.64195',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,59.00,1,30,70,4.91,885124970398557753),(3279,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/886952564101590976','Sunstone House, Sunny, Desk, Safe, transit/dining','Contact us today about our unique urban retreat, where extended stays of 31 days or longer are a breeze! Nestled in the heart of the vibrant city, our cozy oasis is the perfect home away from home for medical professionals, digital nomads, and business travelers on extended assignments. Whether you\'re seeking a comfortable space for work or a peaceful haven to unwind after a long day, our inviting living space is ready to cater to your needs during your extended stay.','The Kenton, Arbor Lodge, and Portsmouth neighborhoods are found in North Portland, south of St. Johns and on the peninsula between the Willamette and Columbia Rivers. North Portland has access to parks, quieter urban neighborhoods, excellent public transit options. Living in Kenton offers residents a dense suburban feel. In Kenton there are a lot of bars, restaurants, coffee shops, and parks. Many families and young professionals live in Kenton.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6ODg2OTUyNTY0MTAxNTkwOTc2/original/1699b41e-88f2-4def-b020-cd553bec682d.jpeg',493461219,55,'45.57916254335364','-122.70050743406806',2,2,2.00,1.00,1.00,34.00,30,180,6,5.00,886952564101590976),(3280,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/886983212436759181','Minutes to Portland Art Museum! Parking!','Located in downtown Portland, this property offers easy access to all attractions, including the Oregon History Museum, Portland Art Museum, Portland University, and Providence Park. The MAX Light Rail Station is just nearby, providing easy access to the Moda Center, the Oregon Convention Center, and Portland International Airport. No matter what time of year you choose to visit Portland, there’s always something new to experience!','- Pioneer Courthouse Square  - 0.2 mile; <br />- Classical Chinese Garden  - 0.5 mile; <br />- Lan Su Chinese Garden  - 0.5 mile; <br />- Oregon History Museum  - 0.5 mile; <br />- Portland Art Museum  - 0.5 miles; <br />- Tom McCall Waterfront Park – 0.5 mile; <br />- Oregon Museum of Science and Industry – 1.4 miles; <br />- Washington Park International Rose Test Gardens – 1.9 miles; <br />- Oregon Zoo – 2.9 miles; <br />- World Forestry Discovery Museum – 3.0 miles; <br />- Portland International Airport – 6 miles; <br />- Johnson Creek – 4.0 miles; <br />- Vancouver Waterfront – 8.8 miles; <br />- Pearson Air Museum – 9.4 miles.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/prohost-api/Hosting-886983212436759181/original/767007f8-