lled 1920\'s bungalow was completely remodeled, combining vintage Portland charm with modern comfort and amenities. Perfect location in a close-in Portland neighborhood with great access to the city. On a major bike street just blocks from the MAX train, shops, restaurants, food carts grocery & more. Walk/bike/train to everything you need! Easy to get around w/out a car but also plenty of free street parking & off street parking in the driveway.','Home is located in the Overlook neighborhood in North Portland.  Centrally located between the popular destinations of Downtown PDX, Alberta Arts, Mississippi Ave, Williams Corridor, Dekum Triangle & St John\'s making it the perfect base camp for exploring Portland.','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/ec13cf5d-0f2c-4b7c-9028-3a1520404203.jpg',11182438,13,'45.565316321716445','-122.68671160304713',1,5,2.00,2.00,4.00,178.00,1,28,9,5.00,948588166133141058),(3417,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/948722280357366372','King Beds. Games. Best Area with 95 Walk Score.','Enjoy your stay at the \"Vibrant Victorian\" a renovated and modernized early 1900s home. Many areas for relaxing, multiple dining areas, and even two kitchens! Two bedrooms have king beds and there are three full baths. Kids of all ages can play retro game on the arcade machine. Stay in the best area — an easy walk to many of the most compelling neighborhoods with award-winning restaurants, fun bars, and interesting local shops. Just a short drive to downtown, key sights, and the airport.','The Boise neighborhood is sometimes referred to as \"Boise-Eliot\" and is located on the east side of the Willamette River.<br /><br />Portland\'s Boise-Eliot neighborhood is one of the most unique and most popular Portland neighborhoods. Most locals know Boise-Eliot by a few names: Williams Avenue and Mississippi Avenue. While technically both part of the same neighborhood proper, these two streets have truly developed their own unique personality and feel with respect to the independent businesses that line their streets and the folks who frequent them.<br /><br />Our neighborhood prizes diversity, independence and entrepreneurialism. Locals know each other and support their local businesses. A mix of renters and owners, singletons and families.<br /><br />In Boise-Eliot you\'ll discover independent retail and boutiques. Around the corner from the home (3 blocks and less away) are the award-winning Eem (Thai BBQ), Life of Pie (pizza), La Cocina (Mexican), XLB (Chinese), EaT (oyster bar),','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-948722280357366372/original/485a2b24-9ccb-4967-842e-173b98cc3026.jpeg',37422309,9,'45.55008','-122.66877',1,10,3.00,5.00,6.00,256.00,2,28,45,4.98,948722280357366372),(3418,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/949148236424023110','Quiet Room in Quiet Neighborhood','This is a room and shared bathroom (across the hall) in a 2bed/2bath apartment located in the beautiful, quiet Woodstock neighborhood; close to Woodstock Park and Reed College. It is 10min walking distance to Trader Joe\'s, the library, New Seasons, Safeway, Bi-Mart, Walgreens and a large variety of restaurants. Streets are not often traveled so a walk or run in the park for fresh air and exercise is easy. Bus routes are easily accessible.<br />**On Sundays, Checkout: 9:00 a.m. Check-in: 7:30 p.m.','Food Carts abound for a quick bite in multi-cultural varieties! Restaurants: Thai, Japanese, Chinese, Organic, Gluten Free, Bakery, Southern American fare + much more options abound! Hardware Store, Medical Services, Retail Stores just a few blocks away.<br /><br />Close to: Crystal Springs Rhododendron Garden, Reed College, Reed College Canyon for hiking, Eastmoreland Golf Course, Portland Waterfront, Springwater Corridor','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-949148236424023110/original/291cf763-b800-43cc-a567-3d82da2418be.jpeg',96996221,38,'45.48635384650204','-122.61227047925644',2,2,1.00,1.00,2.00,60.00,2,730,3,3.67,949148236424023110),(3419,'https: