g in Stumptown.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors—no chain restaurants here! Whether you\'re a foodie, a nature enthusiast, or someone who loves exploring unique shops, the Hawthorne/Buckmantently voted Portland’s favorite pizza), or opt for an elegant night out at Castagna—all within a 1.5-mile stretch.<br /><br />But Portland isn’t just for foodies. The vibrant indie spirit of Hawthorne is alive with a multitude of made-in-Oregon shops and boutiques, making it a true hipster haven. Catch a movie at Bagdad Theater and Pub, a revamped 1920s theater turned view-and-brew venue serving local McMenamins food and microbrews.<br /><br />If bar hopping through neighborhoods isn’t your idea of recreation, head up to Mt. Tabor. This 196-acre city park, located atop a dormant volcano vent, offers miles of hiking trails and incredible panoramic views of the city, providing a perfect escape into nature righ','https://a0.muscache.com/pictures/miso/Hosting-1213079392080802798/original/84a6c1ef-181b-46f3-b6f2-f59d90a5dd0c.jpeg',592522307,15,'45.50746','-122.61113',1,2,1.00,1.00,1.00,79.00,1,365,16,4.69,1213079392080802798),(4170,'https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1213080176618382968','Mt Tabor Retreat ~ Local Eateries ~ Shops ~ Bars','If you\'re a fan of great food, craft beer, and pour-over coffee, this is your place. My apartment is situated right between Hawthorne and Division, near Mount Tabor—close to many of Portland\'s top-rated restaurants, bars, shops, and coffee spots.<br /><br />Perfect for couples, solo adventurers, and business travelers, my place offers a convenient home base within walking distance to the neighborhood\'s hot spots. You can get an authentic taste of living in Stumptown from this ideal location.','Commonly known as “Foodie Row,” the Hawthorne/Buckman District places you within walking distance of a wide variety of top-notch local flavors—no chain 